<node id="&quot;WORKPEOPLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES/PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workpeople are the individuals employed by the Contractor who require passes to access the site or portions thereof, indicating their status as laborers in the worksite context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f19199388ebb0416790d9140af888a4f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1209}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TESTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tests are a method used to examine, measure, or evaluate the quality of materials and workmanship as required by the Contract or ordered by the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 277}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 954}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub-clause (2) is an event where the Contractor must provide assistance for examining, measuring, or testing any work and samples of materials before incorporation into the Works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 259}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 937}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub-clause (a) is an event where any expense relating to examinations, measurements, or tests ordered by the Maintenance Surveyor that show materials or workmanship are not in accordance with the Contract will be borne by the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 263}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 950}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub-clause (b) is an event where if a series of tests on any part of the Works indicate that the Contractor has failed to comply with the requirements, then the expense of complying with this Clause will be borne by the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1209}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (C)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub-clause (c) is an event where if any test or series of tests show that the Contractor has failed to comply with the Contract's requirements, then further or other tests as approved by the Maintenance Surveyor will be carried out at the Contractor's expense."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Access refers to the right granted to the Maintenance Surveyor and his authorized persons to enter various locations including the Works, Site, workshops, and places where materials or manufactured articles are stored or prepared by the Contractor or sub-contractors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 259}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 937}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE [GCCBWT] 45&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub-clause [gccbwt] 45 is an event that grants access rights to the Maintenance Surveyor and his authorized persons at all times on the Works, Site, workshops, and places where materials or manufactured articles are stored or prepared by the Contractor or sub-contractors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 263}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 950}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAUSE 46 (1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Clause 46(1) describes an event where work cannot be covered up without prior approval from the Maintenance Surveyor or their Representative, requiring full opportunity for examination before covering up."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAUSE 47 (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Clause 47(2) details another event involving uncovering and making openings in Works as directed by the Maintenance Surveyor, with responsibilities to reinstate parts of the Works accordingly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The term 'Maintenance Surveyor’s Order' is used in context of instructions or authorizations given by the Maintenance Surveyor for work execution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 934}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKS COMPLETION TIME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Works Completion Time refers to the duration within which works are expected to be completed, subject to possible extensions as per Clause 53."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1209}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NORMAL WORKING HOURS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Normal Working Hours are standard working times, outside which work requires permission from the Maintenance Surveyor unless it prevents injury or damage."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1209}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINUOUS WORKING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Continuous Working refers to the requirement by the Maintenance Surveyor to perform tasks 24 hours per day, as specified in Clause 52."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXTENSION OF TIME FOR COMPLETION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Extension of Time for Completion is a provision allowing delays due to unforeseen circumstances or orders from the Maintenance Surveyor, subject to notice and documentation requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCLEMENT WEATHER CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Inclement weather conditions are considered as an event that can cause delays in the progress of works, affecting the ability to proceed with construction activities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STORM SIGNAL NO. 8 OR ABOVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hoisting a storm signal no. 8 or above is a specific condition indicating severe weather that could lead to work suspension and subsequent delay."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAUSE 5, CLAUSE 63, CLAUSE 57 (2) (A) TO (D), CLAUSE 63&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These clauses refer to specific conditions or events under which delays can be justified for an extension of time. They include instructions from the Maintenance Surveyor and variations in work orders."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UTILITY UNDERTAKING, DULY CONSTITUTED AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Utility undertakings or other duly constituted authorities are organizations that may impact construction by failing to commence or complete necessary works on schedule, potentially causing delays if not addressed proactively by the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE, PORTION OF SITE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The site and its portions refer to specific areas where work is being carried out. Delays can occur due to issues related to access or conditions at these locations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1209}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAUSE 57 (2)(A) TO (D)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These clauses describe specific circumstances under which the contractor may not be entitled to an extension, such as suspension caused by certain events or conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f5f6be589350c8e73f0a57d60397f9eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR (CLAUSE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The organization known as the Maintenance Surveyor is responsible for overseeing work progress, granting extensions of time, and instructing on necessary steps to expedite work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-671cf14fabde451a853f4cb49e6a812f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1209}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GENERAL HOLIDAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"General Holidays are days when work is not expected to proceed as per standard contract terms, impacting the completion timeline."&lt;SEP&gt;"General holidays are days off that may affect the deadlines for submitting statements or lists, as specified within the contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-87f722c8522f822c2e90eb078db141b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE OFFICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Site Offices are locations where contractors provide services such as offices and latrines until all outstanding works are completed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Site offices are temporary structures built on-site to serve as administrative centers for project management and coordination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Site offices are temporary structures or facilities constructed on a building site for administrative purposes during the construction phase."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0c2d16f0534b8f7a9f0c286e3e24591&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e519122ccc2d577ad6723a71d0f9b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daaffb786a24be963871c47c40b85efb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 803}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPLETION CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Completion Certificate is a document issued by the Maintenance Surveyor certifying that certain parts of the works have been completed to satisfaction and can be used permanently."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 262}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 948}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUSPENSION ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Suspension Orders are directives from the Maintenance Surveyor instructing the Contractor to halt work for specific reasons, such as weather conditions or contractor defaults."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 276}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAUSE 59(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Clause 59(2) is a reference within the contract that defines certain exclusions from the term 'Works', indicating specific tasks not covered under this clause."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GROUND REINSTATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ground reinstatement refers to the process of restoring any disturbed ground after construction, which may or may not be included in a Certificate of Completion depending on its explicit mention."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUSPENSION LASTING MORE THAN 90 DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is an event where work suspension exceeds 90 days, potentially triggering specific conditions and considerations within the contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 276}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUSPENSION OF WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Suspension of Works refers to a situation where the progress of the Works is halted for more than 90 days on the order of the Maintenance Surveyor without permission to resume work within 90 days, potentially allowing the Contractor to serve notice and proceed with the works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d204e5d2ccca14fb7f49bf493cc0bdb1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 262}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 948}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY REINSTATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Temporary reinstatement is a process involving the making good of any defects or imperfections in the temporary restoration of highways, roads, or ways until permanent reinstatement can be carried out by an appropriate authority or another party."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERMANENT REINSTATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Permanent reinstatement refers to the final and complete repair work that may be undertaken by a relevant authority after the Maintenance Period has ended or when full occupation of the site is taken for permanent works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1209}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFECT, IMPERFECTION OR FAULT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These terms refer to issues that may arise in the work of permanent reinstatement which need investigation and rectification as per contractual obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c58277d66887ed610fbaec73a4e8d85b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1209}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VARIATION ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Variation Order is an action taken under Clause 63(2) that changes the scope of work or terms of the contract, potentially affecting both parties involved in the Nominated Sub-contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Variation Order, issued in writing and signed by the Maintenance Surveyor, authorizes changes to work or materials detailed in a Works Order."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-62865738eafa658463c1c26212a98b20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 277}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 954}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIFICATION OR SCHEDULE OF RATES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Specification or Schedule of Rates are documents detailing the rates for standard materials and works, which may be varied according to specific clauses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d72604c877ec1b265cace0cc38e4690d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VARIATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Variations refer to changes in work form, character, quality, or any different work/material not detailed in the Specification or Schedule of Rates that require agreement on new rates between parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d72604c877ec1b265cace0cc38e4690d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1209}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DAYWORK BASIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Daywork Basis is a method for paying for work executed as per specific orders where payment is made based on time worked rather than pre-agreed rates."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d72604c877ec1b265cace0cc38e4690d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE'S CHECK FACILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the ability of the Maintenance Surveyor's representative to verify the accuracy of submitted documents by checking time and materials."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DRAWINGS, SPECIFICATION, DETAILS OR LEVELS FROM THE MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are documents provided by the Maintenance Surveyor that guide the Contractor's work on the project."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAUSE 51&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Clause 51 is a reference to an agreement within the contract specifying timeframes for completion of works, which can be extended with approval from the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 263}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 950}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S OPINION ON REIMBURSEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Maintenance Surveyor has discretion in determining if and how expenditures should be reimbursed when progress is affected by certain factors beyond the Contractor’s control."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISTURBANCE OF THE PROGRESS OF THE WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to situations where work is delayed due to issues such as lack of instructions from the Maintenance Surveyor, which can impact the Contractor's ability to be reimbursed for their efforts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WRITTEN APPLICATION BY THE CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Contractor must formally request consideration if they believe progress has been affected and are not being adequately compensated."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTOR’S PROPOSED DAYWORK ACTIVITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ACTIVITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to specific tasks or work that the Contractor plans to carry out, which need prior notification for verification by the Maintenance Surveyor's representative."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 263}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 950}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REIMBURSEMENT OF EXPENDITURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The process through which the Contractor seeks financial compensation for their work when progress is affected as outlined in the contract terms and conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1209}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT 51&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Clause 51 of the Contract likely outlines timelines and deadlines for completion of works which can affect progress and claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 275}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIM NOTICE PERIOD (28 DAYS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The claim notice period is an event where the Contractor must notify the Maintenance Surveyor within 28 days if they intend to make a higher rate or additional payment claim."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 267}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UTILITY UNDERTAKING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Utility Undertaking, not engaged by the Employer, refers to entities that provide essential services such as water, electricity, gas, etc., and are excluded from certain claims under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 275}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DRAWINGS, SPECIFICATIONS, DETAILS OR LEVELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are technical documents provided by the Maintenance Surveyor that guide the Contractor on how to perform their tasks accurately."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 933}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INGRESS/EGRESS CHANGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Changes in ingress or egress refer to modifications in access points which can affect work progress and claims under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 275}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT, SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The General and Special Conditions of Contract are documents that outline terms and conditions applicable to both parties involved in the agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (2) CLAUSE 64, SUB-CLAUSE (2) CLAUSE 65&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These sub-clauses likely pertain to specific procedures for notifying higher rates or additional payments under certain clauses of the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 267}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTEMPORARY RECORDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contemporary records are detailed documentation kept by the Contractor that support any claims made, ensuring accuracy and traceability in claim processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 270}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIM PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Claim Process is a series of steps followed when making claims under the contract, including notification periods and record-keeping requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UTILITY UNDERTAKING NOT ENGAGED BY EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to entities providing essential services that are not contracted directly by the Employer, thus their actions do not affect claims under certain conditions of the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTUAL OBLIGATIONS AND PROVISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These refer to specific clauses in the Contract that outline obligations, procedures for claim handling, and other relevant provisions affecting both parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKS COMPLETION TIMELINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Works Completion Timeline is a critical aspect of the contract specifying deadlines and milestones for completing work according to the agreed terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTUAL INSTRUCTIONS AND DECISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Instructions and decisions from the Maintenance Surveyor are crucial in guiding the Contractor's actions, affecting progress and claims under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATERIAL DELIVERY DELAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Late delivery of materials by the Employer can impact work progress and may be a valid reason for claiming additional costs or time extensions according to certain clauses of the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK METHODOLOGY CHANGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Changes in construction sequence, method, timing as specified in Works Order affect how work is executed and claims are processed under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTUAL CLAIMS PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The procedure for making contractual claims involves specific notice periods, documentation requirements, and steps to be followed by both parties involved in the agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 267}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK ORDER MODIFICATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Modifications to Work Orders can significantly impact work progress and may necessitate additional costs or time extensions as outlined in certain clauses of the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 267}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTUAL COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Compliance with contractual terms, conditions, and procedures is essential for both parties involved in ensuring fair claim handling and dispute resolution processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 270}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIM DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documentation requirements ensure that claims are supported by accurate records, facilitating fair evaluation of claims under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 270}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTUAL DISPUTE RESOLUTION MECHANISMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dispute resolution mechanisms outlined in the Contract provide a structured approach for resolving disagreements and ensuring fairness between parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK EXECUTION IMPACT FACTORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Factors such as progress of works, material delivery delays, work methodology changes, etc., can impact claim handling processes under certain clauses of the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 267}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTUAL PERFORMANCE METRICS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Performance metrics outlined in the Contract help measure and evaluate the Contractor's performance against agreed terms and conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIM NOTIFICATION PERIODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Notification periods for claims ensure timely communication of intentions to claim, allowing both parties sufficient time to address potential disputes or additional costs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 270}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTUAL OBLIGATIONS AND RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Obligations and rights defined in the Contract provide a framework for understanding responsibilities and entitlements under various clauses affecting claims handling processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK INGRESS/EGRESS MODIFICATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Modifications to work ingress/egress can impact access points, potentially affecting claim handling procedures as outlined in certain clauses of the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 275}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTUAL CLAIM HANDLING PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Claim handling procedures defined in the Contract provide a structured approach for processing claims and resolving disputes between parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 267}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK EXECUTION TIMELINE ADJUSTMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjustments to work execution timelines can impact claim handling processes, requiring adherence to specific clauses of the contract that address delays or changes affecting progress and costs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Special Conditions of Contract provide additional or specific terms beyond the general ones, which may include claim provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1209}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Claim is a legal demand for compensation or other relief that can be pursued through arbitral proceedings, subject to reasonable time constraints."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Claim is an event where a Contractor seeks additional payment under contract conditions, subject to certain procedural requirements and timelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"A claim is a formal request made to the Commissioner or Court for payment of funeral and medical attendance expenses based on specific criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Claim and counter-claim are mentioned in relation to defenses, suggesting events where parties present their arguments before an arbitral tribunal or court."&lt;SEP&gt;"Claim and counter-claim are mentioned in relation to defenses, suggesting products or tools used in legal proceedings such as arbitration and court cases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-854d00c33e69aed0258675abc1e2d264&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c4488b1327869fe2b0410a202e25b48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2e37a06f23a289862428e2457ce5863</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 936}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Notice is an official document that must be displayed in workplaces according to Occupational Safety Officer's requirements. It can pertain to various aspects such as ordinance operations, installed plants/substances, and commercial/industrial activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Notice here refers to any written communication that might be used in an attempt to limit warranty obligations, which is also subject to the provisions outlined."&lt;SEP&gt;"Notice here refers to formal written communications required by law or regulation, used as a means of serving information and ensuring compliance with legal obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Notice is a document required by law for reporting workplace accidents when certain conditions are met, containing detailed information about the incident and relevant parties involved."&lt;SEP&gt;"Notice is a form of communication that can be given in writing or otherwise and includes other forms of notifications, as mentioned in the ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Notice is an event where a party informs another of their rights or obligations under the contract, such as payment due dates or compliance requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Notice refers to notifications given under Section 43D, which trigger payment obligations for wage arrears as per legal responsibilities of the total contractor and previous subcontractors."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Notice is a formal communication required by the Contractor to initiate a claim process, detailing their intention to seek additional payment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58cf55b6baed9ac9a3c4052538486aa3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f7e01a5307e145a0563e90666073bf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14526d01cdd531d1142f16c1d5e43367&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2333b3d2deec0b227d514b0090b44838&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af77be8b003511c35b7551f4285bb427&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6f1b0342117fba0657cd9deb544e402</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 138}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 606}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECORDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Records are documents or data kept by the Contractor for supporting claims, which must be contemporary and reasonably necessary as per contract conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1209}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRST INTERIM ACCOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The First Interim Account is a financial document submitted by the Contractor to provide details of the sum claimed so far and grounds thereof, sent within a reasonable time after giving notice to the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FURTHER UP-TO-DATE ACCOUNTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Further Up-to-Date Accounts are periodic financial documents provided by the Contractor at intervals requested by the Maintenance Surveyor, detailing accumulated totals of claims and additional grounds for such claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Nominated Sub-contractors are organizations that provide work, materials, or services in connection with the works. They have obligations to the Contractor which can be assigned to the Employer after the maintenance period if they extend beyond it."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nominated Sub-contractors are selected by the Employer to execute specific works or supply goods, subject to terms provided in standard forms unless otherwise specified by the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR (CLAUSE 69)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Maintenance Surveyor has the authority to instruct different terms for sub-contracts when necessary, overriding standard forms if required by specific project needs or circumstances."&lt;SEP&gt;"When instructed, the Maintenance Surveyor may direct the Contractor to enter into sub-contracts with different terms from those in the standard form provided by the Employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STANDARD FORM OF SUB-CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY, PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Standard Form of Sub-contract is a template document used for entering into agreements with Nominated Sub-contractors unless otherwise specified by the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTOR'S OBLIGATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Contractor must adhere to both contractual and sub-contractual obligations, ensuring consistency in their performance with the Employer’s directives and maintaining detailed records of claims and work execution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S INSTRUCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Instructions given by the Maintenance Surveyor to enter into a sub-contract are events that trigger certain obligations and actions under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 259}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 938}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONTRACT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Sub-contract is a specific type of agreement between parties, often involving different terms from standard forms and potentially leading to additional expenditure for the Contractor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sub-contracts are agreements entered into by the Contractor to execute specific portions of the works, incorporating certain clauses related to plant management and cost recovery."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 259}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 938}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTOR'S OBJECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Objections raised by the Contractor against Nominated Sub-contractors are events that can affect contractual obligations and actions taken by both parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1209}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S INSTRUCTION UNDER CLAUSE 68(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This specific event involves instructions given by the Maintenance Surveyor to enter into a sub-contract, which triggers certain conditions for the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 259}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 938}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S INSTRUCTION UNDER CLAUSE 69(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Instructions given by the Maintenance Surveyor regarding a sub-contract with different terms from standard forms, leading to potential additional expenditure for the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 259}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 938}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;QUOTATIONS, INVOICES, VOUCHERS AND RECEIPTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are documents that provide financial details related to expenditures in respect of Nominated Sub-contractors, required by the Maintenance Surveyor as per Clause 70(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Nominated Sub-Contractors are entities contracted to perform specific tasks under a main nominated sub-contractor. They may also have their own sub-contractors and share liability for employee wages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nominated Sub-contractors are organizations or individuals contracted by the Contractor to perform specific tasks or supply goods/services."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1373b3be58ae445e60a533999b71823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79b86e6b5d2c9cc7cc776e8be6a979bb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 260}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 944}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Maintenance Surveyor certificate is a document that certifies payments due for work executed or materials/supplies provided by Nominated Sub-contractors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1373b3be58ae445e60a533999b71823</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 260}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 944}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLUES 79, 80, AND 81&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are specific clauses in the contract that detail procedures related to issuing certificates regarding payments to Nominated Sub-contractors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1373b3be58ae445e60a533999b71823</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT AND TEMPORARY BUILDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Constructional plant and temporary buildings owned by the Contractor become property of the Employer upon being brought onto the site but can be removed by the Contractor at any time unless prohibited in writing by the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATERIALS FOR INCORPORATION IN WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Materials owned by the Contractor that are to be incorporated into the works vest in the Employer once delivered to the site and cannot be removed without prior written consent from the Maintenance Surveyor, except as surplus upon completion of the works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY BUILDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Temporary Buildings are structures erected on-site that can be removed after completion of work, also owned by the Contractor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary Buildings are structures used during construction that may become the property of the Employer if not completed by the Contractor within specified terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary buildings are structures erected on-site for short-term use, which must be removed after completion of works unless specifically allowed to remain or complete outstanding work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3df24d7cf0a0114d43ffbcf5d5c71fd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 259}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 939}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SURPLUS MATERIALS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Surplus materials are those not required upon or prior to the completion of works and may revert in ownership back to the Contractor if found surplus but can also be sold by the Employer with proceeds going towards the Contractor after deducting charges and expenses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 932}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1209}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIRE OR HIRE-PURCHASE AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These refer to financial arrangements for acquiring constructional plant through leasing or purchase with periodic payments, managed under specific contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 259}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 938}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOSS OF OR DAMAGE TO CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event pertains to the potential loss or damage of equipment that has become property of the Employer and is covered by specific clauses ensuring no liability for such losses unless stated otherwise in Clause 23."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 268}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBMISSIONS* FOR PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The process involves submitting signed copies of payment requests after completion of measurement on each Works Order, subject to checking and correction by the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 268}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIMENSION BOOK(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dimension Books are documents prepared by the Contractor and checked by the Maintenance Surveyor that detail the dimensions of work executed under a Works Order."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dimension Books are technical documentation supplied by the Contractor to detail completed work, which must be accompanied by necessary vouchers or receipts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dimension books are documents that must be submitted for full and final measurement of work executed under a Works Order."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dimension books are technical documents that detail measurements and specifications for construction projects, used in verifying claims and correcting values."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8130c8086938f6df2d05cdf9fb7e405c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77cf568578b8488d566bb45f92f61c0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ff1f20b792fbc8d1bdd961c49e1244</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 262}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 946}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CERTIFICATES FOR PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Certificates for Payment are formal documents issued by the Maintenance Surveyor certifying the correct value of completed works, which then go to the Employer for payment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12ff1f20b792fbc8d1bdd961c49e1244</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 262}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 949}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPENDIX TO THE FORM OF TENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Appendix contains a standard base charge and an amount threshold used in determining how detailed measurements need to be provided with Complaint Chits."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Appendix contains specific details, such as payment schedules and conditions, related to Works Orders."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77cf568578b8488d566bb45f92f61c0d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 262}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 946}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKS ORDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Works Orders are documents that detail specific tasks or projects for which payments may be made, often related to construction or maintenance work."&lt;SEP&gt;"Works Orders are specific instructions or tasks issued under a contract that detail particular work requirements for the Contractor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Works Orders refer to specific orders or instructions issued by the Employer for work to be carried out, which are part of the overall contract between parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8130c8086938f6df2d05cdf9fb7e405c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5e827172d85d4fce202f234f783e044</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 934}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPLAINT CHITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Complaint Chits refer to formal complaints or issues raised by the Contractor regarding the Works Orders or any discrepancies found during batch checking processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8130c8086938f6df2d05cdf9fb7e405c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 934}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPENDIX TO FORM OF TENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Appendix to Form of Tender provides additional details, likely including payment schedules and other relevant information for the works order process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8130c8086938f6df2d05cdf9fb7e405c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 198}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 735}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interim Payments are calculated and paid out according to specific rules outlined in this document, serving as a form of compensation during an interim period before final assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interim Payments are temporary payments made during a project or process, subject to final settlement and potentially surcharges if not paid within the specified period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interim Payments refer to temporary financial assistance provided before the final determination of compensation, which may be deducted from the total amount if paid prior to the issuance of the Certificate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interim payments are made during the progress of work under certain conditions, typically not exceeding 80% of the estimated value of completed permanent works."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interim payments refer to partial payments made during the execution of works orders, subject to certain conditions and schedules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interim payments are temporary financial arrangements made under Certificates of Interim Payment or Review Certificates, used as part of the overall payment process but not final compensation amounts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9a6dfc79f4a9de7dba162e137dcffd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f817e1f2a5b13a0586c36573c6eea5b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0a0053e7177c68e160847406a3692d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d03bb282f99bcf0993cd32ec58e1edb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8130c8086938f6df2d05cdf9fb7e405c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 198}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 735}]</data>
</node>
