<node id="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">An Arbitrator is a neutral third-party individual appointed or agreed upon by disputing parties to resolve their disputes through arbitration. The primary role of an Arbitrator involves making impartial and binding decisions based on evidence and arguments presented during the proceedings. They are part of an arbitral tribunal that can include other arbitrators, with each member having specific powers and responsibilities defined within agreements or default rules.

The Arbitrator has the authority to hear evidence from witnesses, including those like the Maintenance Surveyor who provide relevant information. In certain circumstances, they may also have the power to appoint themselves in disputes where no agreement exists between parties. They can act as both an arbiter and a mediator under specific conditions, potentially staying arbitral proceedings for mediation purposes.

The Arbitrator's mandate is subject to termination based on various conditions such as inability to act or resignation, with provisions outlined in relevant articles (e.g., Articles 13-14 of the UNCITRAL Model Law). They are responsible for handling confidential information obtained during arbitration and must ensure fairness by properly notifying their appointment.

In some cases, an Arbitrator may be appointed by courts or other authorities to maintain independence and impartiality. Their role is crucial in resolving disputes between parties according to agreed-upon rules of procedure, with the authority to open up, review, and revise decisions made during arbitration proceedings (except for specific clauses). The term "Arbitrator" also encompasses a presiding arbitrator within an arbitral tribunal.

The description provided includes both Chinese and English terms. In this summary, we have focused on the comprehensive role of an Arbitrator as described in the given descriptions, ensuring clarity and coherence across all aspects mentioned.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-63fa361a4bbae312d93826ee30bf2182&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea943fe3338aa88e6573bf715e772abd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a820d49f72ef3eeb5be9d057a9cb248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7aaf6f770f217f1e2eb977b5ec34ad19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af79dae94b8a0756fefbbf0f811ebd51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6cff72e41603eed38553fb4f306a008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0165ce281c7667854e6df58da6d1a76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d869f809c494e89028b24de4ba24f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-963f917b5a00c96d5b43bd1832480a19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d58ad3e1c6ef21463d303a3e0c4d6ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522c43aa0cb7d424d1da1c5b00c65777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff2369343594485564382d2d30ba3755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da3d7a01706de39cd849092deef8b9b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38b4dba8dcefb2d368c753859f749fd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-367745ea1d4a071f6e58849b6c7523ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dd6cc93acdd87603565c28f0e5d9386&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e105b81cb8e7429af8bdd848fcb41de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51d1d77716a000d59a4c18879a262e96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750</data>
