<node id="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3c3394a6b72977677a8a437b4151b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92c85875b0985afcab2ef9a7ace52829&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23a60b107acb436d1472e4d6fcca723b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d5ac982d50689641df03f0066401a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85bf5f4c0ed4aaf7faca3a4817c0b647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b297641c5fc96a9b02649fb896184fdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d5bf4b80d4916179a3f7d858e7175b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66cccec6ac7d06fb5417245d5fe5f3b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea83763b873f6b32742c132cbac8d568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-106089b31da6304da0bc926c63d44161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-057cc616cb8b855799f3fcacf937e222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70cdeeb8eece52f9eaa0ef190c0b61e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-852d5344329889ebbea0dad97630dd26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7881ceecf94346279b299fee8d79193&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da2837c3b5e351b2e1c63635e1c0a663</data>
  <data key="d1">The Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (Cap. 59) is a comprehensive legal document governing industrial activities and safety standards within Hong Kong, forming part of the broader regulatory framework for site safety or environmental offenses. This ordinance defines terms related to industrial undertakings and outlines specific powers granted to officers responsible for ensuring compliance with regulations. It encompasses various aspects including employment conditions, workplace safety, inspections, examinations, and the circumstances under which an employer can dismiss an employee without just cause.

The document establishes roles such as inspectors or occupational safety officers who are tasked with overseeing factory operations and industrial practices in the region. The ordinance also addresses provisions related to disclosure offenses and may influence compensation awards for wrongful dismissal cases. Overall, Cap. 59 serves as a critical legal framework that regulates industrial undertakings, ensuring safe working conditions and compliance with relevant regulations in Hong Kong's manufacturing sector.</data>
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 146}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 640}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1160}]</data>
</node>
