  <data key="d0">"AMENDMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"event"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a1f612e80bc33b548b5b253bf3e3dac0</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELLING CONTRACT PARTY DEALING AS CONSUMER (DEALS AS CONSUMER)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The party involved in a selling contract who is not operating within their business and does not represent themselves as such, while the other party operates in a business context, can be considered to deal as a consumer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a1f612e80bc33b548b5b253bf3e3dac0</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSUMER TRANSACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to transactions where one of the parties acts as a consumer rather than a business entity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a1f612e80bc33b548b5b253bf3e3dac0</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PURCHASER NOT DEALING AS CONSUMER (NOT DEALS AS CONSUMER)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A purchaser who is not considered to be dealing as a consumer, such as in auction or competitive bidding scenarios."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a1f612e80bc33b548b5b253bf3e3dac0</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;A PARTY TO A CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A party to a contract of sale refers to the buyer or seller in a sales contract, who neither makes the contract in the course of a business nor holds themselves out as doing so."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 744}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANOTHER PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON/ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Another party can refer to either the buyer or seller in a sales contract, where one is making the contract in the course of a business and the other is not."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 744}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOODS PASSING UNDER OR IN PURSUANCE OF THE CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Goods are items being sold in a contract, which are typically of a type ordinarily supplied for private use or consumption."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 744}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Contract of Sale is an agreement between parties where one party agrees to sell and the other to buy certain goods or services."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Contract of Sale is an agreement between parties where one transfers or agrees to transfer ownership of goods for monetary consideration. It can be absolute or conditional based on specific terms and conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Contract of Sale refers to an agreement where goods are sold and purchased, with terms regarding conditions and warranties."&lt;SEP&gt;"A contract of sale is an agreement where one party sells and another buys goods, with implications on quality and fitness as per legal statutes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A contract of sale is an event where goods are sold under the terms specified by law, which can be established in various ways including writing, orally, partly written and partly oral, or through implied agreements based on parties' behavior. It does not affect corporate laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contract of sale is a legal agreement between parties for the exchange of goods with specified payment conditions and obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contract of sale is an agreement where one party transfers ownership of goods to another party in exchange for money, often within the context of business transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contract of sale refers to an agreement between parties for the transfer or sale of goods, which can be either unconditional or conditional."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to an agreement between parties where one party sells goods or services to another, with specific terms and conditions regarding fulfillment and warranties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c537dc0fa7ed6ca01860ee51729f49a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a93975688247d3b9e7a757c9ac99d011&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6898f338d8c873d727625cb55234a222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7899f94c0b8fd41924e069cd239cc724&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8e3424a8a5275e58cb410e4ea0f205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-777ee0ce7b06539972a14723dda21238</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 746}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSUMER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A consumer is someone dealing under normal circumstances, where liability cannot be excluded or restricted regarding goods' correspondence with description or sample, or their quality or fitness for any particular purpose."&lt;SEP&gt;"A consumer refers to an individual dealing with a service provider, whose agreement to submit future differences to arbitration can only be enforced under specific conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A consumer refers to someone who purchases goods primarily for personal use rather than commercial purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Consumer is a type of person who engages in transactions under certain conditions specified by law."&lt;SEP&gt;"Consumer is an individual who enters into a contract under specific conditions, such as dealing with another party's standard terms of business."&lt;SEP&gt;"Consumer refers to a person who purchases goods or services primarily for personal use rather than commercial purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca4a2a9fbbaee42187b60b84f640f8f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a2e2728ed9206072fd11eab3f6ceb87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0093428c9e5c24b975d1827e057247c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9caec393d81747f82a0bc36401fbbd53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-872dd343c6e35c900d1e080217da3c6c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 744}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A business is an organization involved in commercial, industrial, or professional activities for profit."&lt;SEP&gt;"Business includes a trade or profession and any like activity carried on by a person."&lt;SEP&gt;"Business includes any industry or profession, and similar activities engaged by individuals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Business includes professions, as well as public institutions, public authorities, duties of various committees or similar bodies appointed by the Chief Executive or Government."&lt;SEP&gt;"Business is an activity engaged in producing and selling goods, providing services, etc., with the aim of making profits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Business refers to a commercial enterprise or entity for which the employee was working before the death of the deceased employer, and its ownership might pass to a personal representative."&lt;SEP&gt;"Business refers to a profession, the activities of public bodies, authorities, boards, commissions, and other entities appointed by the Chief Executive or Government. It includes both personal business operations and those conducted on behalf of others."&lt;SEP&gt;"Business refers to commercial activities or enterprises where goods are supplied for private use or consumption, distinguishing it from personal dealings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Business refers to commercial enterprises that may undergo ownership changes affecting their employees' contracts as per legal provisions mentioned."&lt;SEP&gt;"Business refers to commercial or industrial enterprises that may be impacted by decisions regarding construction noise permits affecting their operational hours and methods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fee7842314099c25edf5106ebd221850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65134d6c88195bfcc2ac0100392eb0d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-405702086caa260fb0fa6bf8fac677c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ddecf99bc0bca06387d96224afeaf4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac6eb040e98e92757cf6e4d3f0473e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aa5c7bec2bb945d36bb333255416d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a67530e0a9df975682238097b18b864&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85644a914cfa94d353943cc7d1724450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35333cbaccd9be2f64c80f729f9d5ffb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 744}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An auction is a process where goods are put up for sale by public competitive bidding, typically concluding with the fall of the hammer or another customary manner."&lt;SEP&gt;"An auction is a public sale where goods are sold to the highest bidder, often used in business transactions and not considered consumer dealing as per subsection (2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32292d53bc2adbfdb992bdf0fe946e4a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 758}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELLING CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A selling contract is a specific type of contract where ownership of goods is transferred from seller to buyer in exchange for payment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 746}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALE AND AGREEMENT TO SELL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Sale and Agreement to Sell refers to the transfer of property in goods from seller to buyer under certain conditions or at a future time."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a93975688247d3b9e7a757c9ac99d011</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 747}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGREEMENT TO SELL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Agreement to Sell becomes a sale when the time elapses or specified conditions are fulfilled, allowing property in goods to be transferred from seller to buyer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a93975688247d3b9e7a757c9ac99d011</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 747}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CAPACITY TO BUY AND SELL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Capacity to buy and sell is a legal concept regulated by general law concerning capacity to contract and transfer property. It includes the obligation of an infant or minor to pay a reasonable price for necessaries, which are goods suitable to their condition in life and actual requirements at the time of sale."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Capacity to Buy and Sell refers to the legal ability to enter into contracts for buying and selling. It is regulated by general laws concerning capacity to contract, transfer, and acquire property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c537dc0fa7ed6ca01860ee51729f49a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a93975688247d3b9e7a757c9ac99d011</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INFANT OR MINOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Infant or Minor refers to individuals who are under a certain age and may have limited contractual capacity due to their age or mental state."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a93975688247d3b9e7a757c9ac99d011</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NECESSARIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Necessaries refer to goods that are appropriate for the condition in life of an infant or minor and meet their current needs when sold and delivered. They must be paid a reasonable price by such individuals if they lack capacity to contract due to mental incapacity or drunkenness."&lt;SEP&gt;"Necessaries refer to goods that are essential for the lifestyle of an individual, such as food, clothing, and shelter, which must be paid for at reasonable prices by infants or minors who receive them."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c537dc0fa7ed6ca01860ee51729f49a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a93975688247d3b9e7a757c9ac99d011</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FORMALITIES OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Formalities of contract include the methods for making a sale agreement, which can be in writing (with or without seals), orally, partly written and partly oral, or inferred from parties' actions. This section does not affect laws concerning corporations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c537dc0fa7ed6ca01860ee51729f49a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 746}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CORPORATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Corporations refer to legal entities that are distinct from their owners and have the capacity to enter into contracts under specific laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c537dc0fa7ed6ca01860ee51729f49a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;现货或期货&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"现货指的是卖方拥有或管理的货物，而期货则是指在签订销售合同时由卖方制造或获取的货物。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c537dc0fa7ed6ca01860ee51729f49a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 746}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;有事件&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An event that may or may not occur, which can affect the seller's ability to obtain goods. This term is used in legal contexts where future events determine contractual obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c537dc0fa7ed6ca01860ee51729f49a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 746}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXISTING OR FUTURE GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Existing or future goods refers to items that can be owned by the seller either as current inventory or those manufactured/acquired after contract signing. In this context, 'future goods' are significant in trade agreements and contracts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da0594a6faf073110e696a64d93f3508</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINGENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A contingency is an event which may or may not happen, affecting the acquisition of future goods by the seller."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da0594a6faf073110e696a64d93f3508</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT FOR SALE OF SPECIFIC GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONTRACT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a trade agreement involving unique items. The contract can be valid even if the goods have perished without the seller's knowledge at the time of signing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da0594a6faf073110e696a64d93f3508</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOODS WHICH HAVE PERISHED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Specific goods that perish before being sold but after an agreement is made are considered void in contracts, indicating their significance and impact on trade agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da0594a6faf073110e696a64d93f3508</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RISK TRANSFER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The risk of damage or loss in goods transfers from the seller to the buyer when certain conditions are met."&lt;SEP&gt;"The risk of loss or damage to the goods transfers from the seller to the buyer once the goods perish before sale, affecting the validity of the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7fbaa0d66e947840f2ec3483b78cc0fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0594a6faf073110e696a64d93f3508</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGREEMENT TO SELL SPECIFIC GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An agreement to sell specific goods is established between the seller and buyer, which can be determined by contract or through mutual dealings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7fbaa0d66e947840f2ec3483b78cc0fb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REASONABLE PRICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A reasonable price is a fact-dependent issue, determined by individual circumstances and can be set by mutual agreement or through market valuation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7fbaa0d66e947840f2ec3483b78cc0fb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRD-PARTY VALUATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Third-party valuation refers to the process where an independent party assesses the value of goods for pricing purposes in sales agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7fbaa0d66e947840f2ec3483b78cc0fb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRD PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Third Party refers to an entity that valuates goods, which may be prevented from doing so due to fault by either the seller or buyer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A third party is any entity other than the employer that may be involved in recovering damages, particularly when it involves employees initiating legal actions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A third party refers to any individual or entity other than the employer who might have legal liability for causing injury leading to compensation claims."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Third Party refers to a person other than the employer, who is legally liable to pay damages to the employee in respect of an injury caused by circumstances creating such liability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Third Party is someone other than the employer from whom an employee may have recovered compensation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e2828dcd3a1acc333b703677e12c2630&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5264a8fa197e6ad59c59c71f8b3763e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f8e345be219d3fc366dc62469796daf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e72191ab4edd091f82585ac0b7be851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddbe221813d2b91715360a8a16979bab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 130}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALE CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A sale contract refers to an agreement between parties where one party agrees to sell a product or service to another for a specified price."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sale contract is an agreement between parties to sell and buy goods, with conditions governing the transfer of ownership and risk. The validity can be affected by various factors including fault in delayed delivery or special laws granting selling rights."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Sale Contract is a document specifying terms of sale and conditions for both parties involved in the transaction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2828dcd3a1acc333b703677e12c2630&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-200bd4845769007ce451fb6541f74f39</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 130}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT TERMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Payment Terms refer to stipulations regarding when payment should be made, which are not necessarily essential elements unless explicitly stated otherwise."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e2828dcd3a1acc333b703677e12c2630</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CALENDAR MONTH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Calendar Month is a unit of time defined by the Gregorian calendar system and used in contracts for standardization purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e2828dcd3a1acc333b703677e12c2630</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDITIONS AND WARRANTIES CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conditions and Warranties Clause refers to provisions within sale agreements that specify terms under which goods are sold, including conditions and warranties provided by the seller."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e2828dcd3a1acc333b703677e12c2630</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TIME STIPULATIONS CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Time Stipulations Clause pertains to legal clauses in contracts specifying timeframes for actions such as payment, with certain stipulations regarding their importance depending on contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e2828dcd3a1acc333b703677e12c2630</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FACIE CALENDAR MONTH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Facie Calendar Month refers to a specific period in time used for certain legal or financial purposes, though no detailed description is provided in this text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-777ee0ce7b06539972a14723dda21238</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 746}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDITION TO BE TREATED AS WARRANTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A condition that can be treated as a warranty when breached by the seller, allowing the buyer to claim damages rather than terminate the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-777ee0ce7b06539972a14723dda21238</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 746}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDITION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conditions in a contract refer to stipulations that must be fulfilled by the seller before the buyer can accept the goods; their breach may lead to different consequences depending on how they are classified within the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6898f338d8c873d727625cb55234a222</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 746}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPUDIATED CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Repudiation occurs when one party declares they will not fulfill their contractual obligations, leading to termination of the agreement under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6898f338d8c873d727625cb55234a222</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 205}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPOSSIBILITY OR OTHER LEGAL EXCUSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal excuses such as impossibility can excuse the fulfillment of a condition or warranty in a contract without affecting its validity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6898f338d8c873d727625cb55234a222</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 753}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OWNERSHIP LIABILITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ownership liabilities refer to implied responsibilities related to property rights and their transfer, ensuring that goods are free from undisclosed encumbrances at the time of sale."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6898f338d8c873d727625cb55234a222</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 205}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Goods are items being traded and subject to the provisions regarding stoppage in transitu when an insolvent buyer fails to fulfill payment obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Goods are items being traded between the seller and buyer under specific contractual terms related to ownership and delivery risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Goods refer to items as defined under the Sale of Goods Ordinance (Cap. 26), indicating a legal context related to commercial transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Goods refer to items being sold in transactions, which can be inspected and accepted or rejected based on certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Goods refer to items being sold that may or may not be owned by the seller. The transfer of ownership is conditional based on various factors such as fault in delayed delivery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Goods refer to items being traded between seller and buyer in contractual agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Goods refer to items being traded under the terms of the contract between the Seller and the Buyer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Goods refer to items being transported under specific terms and conditions, including their status as being in transit or delivered."&lt;SEP&gt;"Goods refer to items for sale that may involve complex ownership and sales dynamics as described in the Ordinance and related laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"Goods refer to items of commerce that can be sold and used privately, often subject to specific legal protections when a consumer is involved in the transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Goods refer to items that have been sold but may still be in the possession of the seller or newly acquired by a buyer under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Goods refer to products or items being sold and covered under warranty terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Goods refer to the items being sold in the contract of sale."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3460a8b3f83d1862f966932908fad7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-019dad10da4fa0e0f55e19465cb7641c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-535dface6286d8bede9ae8225e2d5326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69fc897b8b9dfae677db802b05a78337&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-405702086caa260fb0fa6bf8fac677c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3304fe02529acf61f5b7a297e0a498dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aa5c7bec2bb945d36bb333255416d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34bc94419b349addb3ca3738887910de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09f76424c00042dab76ada9f73a18154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2262a3a4061aab5ab97a1077b67a5057&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-097842d27813c438fcbfa56e8eef5ca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 214}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 761}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY TRANSFER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property transfer refers to the legal concept that defines when ownership or rights over goods are transferred from seller to buyer, based on contract terms, intentions, and circumstances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property transfer refers to the process where ownership or right to goods is passed from seller to buyer, subject to certain conditions and guarantees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-57cd738c9ff0713f532a9b12760d5197&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 866}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPLIED CONDITION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Implied condition denotes a legal obligation that arises by implication rather than express agreement in the contract of sale."&lt;SEP&gt;"Implied condition refers to an underlying assumption or understanding not explicitly stated but understood by both parties involved in a transaction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5228b6166ae5f3bb9be72928713eb4f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 215}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 766}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TITLE GUARANTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Title guarantee is an implied undertaking ensuring the seller has the right to sell and transfer ownership without encumbrances as disclosed or known to the buyer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 215}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 766}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELLER'S RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Seller's rights refer to the legal entitlement of the seller to sell goods, which includes having a clear title free from undisclosed encumbrances at the time of contract and during property transfer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUYER'S PEACEABLE POSSESSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Buyer's peaceable possession is an implied condition ensuring that once ownership transfers, the buyer will have undisturbed control over the goods unless such disturbance arises from disclosed or known encumbrances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRD PARTY CLAIMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Third party claims refer to potential interference in the buyer's peaceable possession of goods by parties other than the seller, who may have rights based on undisclosed or unknown encumbrances at the time of contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTUAL INTENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contractual intent refers to the mutual understanding and expectations between the parties involved in a sale agreement regarding the transfer of goods and associated legal obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPLIED WARRANTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Implied warranty is an inherent guarantee that arises from the nature of the contract, ensuring certain conditions are met without explicit mention in the terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISCLOSURE REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Disclosure requirement is a procedural technology or rule for disclosing situations that might affect an arbitrator's independence and impartiality."&lt;SEP&gt;"Disclosure requirement refers to the obligation on the seller to disclose all known encumbrances or interests affecting the title before property transfer occurs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Disclosure Requirement mandates that an individual who might be nominated for appointment as an Adjudicator must disclose any potential conflicts of interest and provide written assurance about their independence and impartiality before being appointed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-40b68681ecca6bd68067e789107e9bdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6cff72e41603eed38553fb4f306a008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 852}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL OBLIGATIONS OF SELLERS AND BUYERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal obligations of sellers and buyers encompass a range of implied conditions, warranties, and guarantees that protect both parties' rights during the sale process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 852}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY PASSING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property passing refers to the legal transfer of ownership or right over goods from seller to buyer as stipulated in the contract of sale."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPLIED CONDITION ON THE PART OF THE SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An implied condition that in the case of a sale, the seller has a right to sell the goods and will have such rights at the time when property is to pass. In an agreement to sell, it implies he will have those rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7fc73f93b207fb939f0a65e3152d73dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPLIED WARRANTY ON THE GOODS BEING FREE FROM CHARGE OR ENCUMBRANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An implied warranty that the goods are not subject to any undisclosed charges or encumbrances and will remain so until property is to pass. It also implies quiet possession of the goods except as may be disturbed by the owner or other entitled parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7fc73f93b207fb939f0a65e3152d73dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE WITH INTENTION TO TRANSFER ONLY SUCH TITLE AS A THIRD PERSON HAS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A contract where there's an implied warranty that all known charges not disclosed have been made known and no one claiming under the seller, third party, or any undisclosed charge will disturb quiet possession."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7fc73f93b207fb939f0a65e3152d73dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHARGE OR ENCUMBRANCE DISCLOSURE REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Requirement for disclosing known charges to the buyer before contract is made. Warranty that neither the seller nor a third person can disturb the buyer's quiet possession of goods except as disclosed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7fc73f93b207fb939f0a65e3152d73dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALE BY DESCRIPTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sale by description refers to a type of transaction where goods are sold based on their description, with implied conditions that the goods must correspond with this description. If both sample and description are used in selling, all goods should match the description as well."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5228b6166ae5f3bb9be72928713eb4f7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 215}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 766}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAMPLE SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sample sale is a type of selling where goods are sold based on samples, with the requirement that all items must match the sample provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5228b6166ae5f3bb9be72928713eb4f7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 215}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 766}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;QUALITY AND FITNESS FOR PURPOSE GUARANTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Quality and fitness for purpose guarantee refers to implied conditions regarding the quality of supplied goods and their suitability for specific purposes. The seller is assumed to provide goods in a merchantable condition unless otherwise specified in the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5228b6166ae5f3bb9be72928713eb4f7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 215}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 766}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIFIC PURPOSE SUITABILITY GUARANTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Specific purpose suitability guarantee refers to conditions implied in contracts where the seller is assumed to provide goods suitable for particular uses or purposes unless explicitly stated otherwise."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5228b6166ae5f3bb9be72928713eb4f7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 215}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 766}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS OPERATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY,ACTIVITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Business Operation pertains to the ongoing activities and operations conducted by businesses as part of their regular business practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Business operation refers to the conduct of commercial activities where goods are sold and certain implied conditions or warranties apply regarding their quality and suitability for a specific purpose."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-183ae686da520342fd44ebd9847a6fdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 212}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTUAL SUPPLY OF GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contractual supply of goods refers to the sale of products under business operations, with certain implied conditions or warranties concerning their quality and suitability for use."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-183ae686da520342fd44ebd9847a6fdf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 212}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIFIC PURPOSE GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Specific purpose goods are items sold based on a buyer's specific intended use, implying that they must be suitable for such purposes unless unreasonable to rely on the seller’s expertise or judgment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-183ae686da520342fd44ebd9847a6fdf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 212}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 16&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 16 refers to a legal section that provides conditions and warranties regarding goods supplied under a contract of sale."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-abd61364920843014789da67b81b39a5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 215}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 764}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPLIED CONDITION OR WARRANTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Implied condition or warranty is a legal concept referring to the circumstances in which there are any implied terms about the quality or fitness for purpose of goods sold, except as specified by specific conditions and buyer's knowledge."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-abd61364920843014789da67b81b39a5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 215}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 764}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFECTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Defects refer to flaws or issues in a product that could lead to loss or damage if not properly addressed through warranty provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Defects refer to specific issues with goods that can be pointed out by the seller and which would negate any implied condition of merchantable quality, provided these defects are drawn to the buyer's attention before or at the time of contract formation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-abd61364920843014789da67b81b39a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2333b3d2deec0b227d514b0090b44838</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 215}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 764}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUYER’S KNOWLEDGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The buyer's knowledge refers to situations where a buyer is aware of specific issues with goods prior to entering into a contract, which can affect the applicability of implied conditions and warranties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-abd61364920843014789da67b81b39a5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 215}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 764}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;QUALITY OR FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This concept refers to the implied conditions in contracts of sale ensuring goods meet certain standards, either being merchantable or fit for specific purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 746}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOODS SUPPLIED UNDER A CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Goods sold in contracts are subject to conditions ensuring their merchantability or suitability for specific purposes unless certain exceptions apply."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 215}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 765}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFECTS SPECIFICALLY DRAWN TO THE BUYER'S ATTENTION BEFORE THE CONTRACT IS MADE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Defects are noted by the seller prior to the contract, exempting them from implied conditions regarding those specific issues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUYER EXAMINES THE GOODS BEFORE THE CONTRACT IS MADE AND DEFECTS WHICH THAT EXAMINATION OUGHT TO REVEAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The buyer's inspection of goods for obvious flaws before signing a contract exempts the seller from certain implied conditions related to these defects."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT FOR SALE BY SAMPLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A sales agreement based on samples implies quality standards, but only as far as apparent defects in those samples are concerned."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTICULAR PURPOSE FOR WHICH GOODS ARE BEING BOUGHT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The buyer's specific use of the goods can influence implied conditions regarding their fitness for that particular application."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 746}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;USAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Usage refers to established practices or customs in business transactions, which may be used to imply certain terms and conditions into contracts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALE BY A PERSON WHO IN THE COURSE OF A BUSINESS IS ACTING AS AGENT FOR ANOTHER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This describes an intermediary selling goods on behalf of someone else, with implications similar to direct sales but considering agency roles."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRINCIPAL IN THE COURSE OF A BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The principal refers to the original seller or supplier who is conducting business activities through their agent."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PURCHASE PRICE OR PART OF IT IS PAYABLE BY INSTALMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Payment terms involving installments can affect how implied conditions are applied in sales contracts, including references to the person handling initial negotiations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANTECEDENT NEGOTIATIONS (事先商议)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Antecedent negotiations refer to preliminary discussions or agreements that may influence the final contract and its terms, especially regarding who is responsible for certain actions during transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALE BY SAMPLE AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Sale by Sample Agreement is a contract where goods are sold based on a sample, with implied conditions regarding the quality and fitness of the bulk goods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7899f94c0b8fd41924e069cd239cc724</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 746}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1174}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANTECEDENT NEGOTIATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Antecedent negotiations refer to any prior discussions or arrangements that induced the buyer to enter into an agreement or promoted the transaction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7899f94c0b8fd41924e069cd239cc724</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 746}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1174}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;QUALITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The quality and fitness for a particular purpose of goods supplied under a contract of sale are not implied unless specified, according to relevant sections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7899f94c0b8fd41924e069cd239cc724</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 746}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1174}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALE BY SAMPLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sale by sample is a commercial practice where the quality of bulk goods must correspond with the sample and provides conditions for implied warranties regarding the goods' quality."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-57cd738c9ff0713f532a9b12760d5197</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 866}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;確定意向的規則&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"確定意向的規則是一系列法律條款，用來確定雙方在交易中的權利和義務。這些規則涉及貨品產權轉移、付款日期以及賣方對貨品處理的要求等內容。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6c550597a3052a5b04c9cf13a1394b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;規則1&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"規則1是關於當訂立不附帶條件的合約時，特定貨品的產權在合同簽署時即刻轉移到買方手中。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6c550597a3052a5b04c9cf13a1394b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;規則2&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"規則2描述了賣方必須對特定貨品進行處理使其達到可交付狀態的情況下，直到賣方完成這些處理並通知買方之前，產權不會轉移給買方。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6c550597a3052a5b04c9cf13a1394b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;規則3&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"規則3涉及當訂立合約售賣處於可交付狀態的特定貨品但需要進行稱量、量度或測試以確定貨價的情況，直到這些處理完成並通知買方後產權才轉移。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6c550597a3052a5b04c9cf13a1394b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;規則4&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"規則4描述了當貨品是按有待同意或'售賣或退回'原則或其他類似條款交付給買方時的情況，規定在特定條件下產權的轉移時間點。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6c550597a3052a5b04c9cf13a1394b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;移給買方&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"移給買方是指货物所有权转移给买方的事件，具体条件和时间取决于买卖双方的具体协议。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4919d9417efe70a24558dc1ea463f973</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;合理時間&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"合理時間是一个事实问题，指的是在没有明确退回期限的情况下，货物所有权转移到买方所需的时间长度。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4919d9417efe70a24558dc1ea463f973</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;規則5. (1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"規則5. (1) 描述了订立合同并凭货品说明售卖未确定的货品或期货的具体条款和条件。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4919d9417efe70a24558dc1ea463f973</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;規則5. (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"規則5. (2) 规定了卖方依据合约将货物交付给买方或承运人或其他受寄人的具体条款，以及在何种情况下货物所有权转移给买方。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4919d9417efe70a24558dc1ea463f973</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RULE 1.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rule 1 是关于特定状态下的无条件合同的具体规则，规定了在这种情况下货物的所有权何时转移到买家手中。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4919d9417efe70a24558dc1ea463f973</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RULE 2.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rule 2 规定了卖方在将货物交付给买方或承运人时的义务和责任，并明确了在此过程中货物所有权转移的时间点。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4919d9417efe70a24558dc1ea463f973</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RULE 2&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rule 2 describes a scenario where property in specific goods does not pass to the buyer until the seller has done something with them and the buyer is notified."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e602b76f9699cca512b4176568443c48</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RULE 3&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rule 3 outlines conditions under which property in specific, deliverable state goods do not pass to the buyer until certain acts are completed and notice given."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e602b76f9699cca512b4176568443c48</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RULE 4&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rule 4 details circumstances where property passes to the buyer upon approval or acceptance of delivered goods on approval terms, or after a reasonable time if no action is taken by the buyer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e602b76f9699cca512b4176568443c48</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RULE 5 (1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rule 5(1) explains that when unascertained or future goods are appropriated to the contract and assent given, property in those goods passes to the buyer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e602b76f9699cca512b4176568443c48</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RULE 5 (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rule 5(2) states that if the seller delivers goods for transmission without reserving disposal rights, they have unconditionally appropriated them to the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e602b76f9699cca512b4176568443c48</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNASCERTAINED OR FUTURE GOODS BY DESCRIPTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Unascertained or future goods by description refers to items not yet fully defined but agreed upon in a sale contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e602b76f9699cca512b4176568443c48</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPROPRIATION OF GOODS TO THE CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The act of appropriating specific, deliverable state goods to the contract is described as transferring property rights from seller to buyer under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e602b76f9699cca512b4176568443c48</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;保留貨品處置權&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"保留貨品處置權 refers to the legal concept where a seller retains control over delivered goods until specific terms are met, often seen in business and contract law studies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e602b76f9699cca512b4176568443c48</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CARRIER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Carrier is an entity responsible for transporting goods from one location to another according to the agreed-upon terms of delivery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carrier refers to a transportation entity that can receive goods for transmission, often mentioned alongside other bailees such as warehouses or storage facilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-08fbcc9c2ce9e3d4f773cc495db19495&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3304fe02529acf61f5b7a297e0a498dd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 752}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BAILEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A bailee, or custodian, can also hold goods for a buyer and yet allow the seller's right of lien to apply."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bailee is an organization or individual who holds goods on behalf of the seller or buyer, typically involved in temporary custody and transfer processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-08fbcc9c2ce9e3d4f773cc495db19495&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83a8d937e2b926da0d7047a5288d8ae8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 216}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 768}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESERVATION OF RIGHT OF DISPOSAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The concept involves retaining control over goods until certain conditions are met, affecting property rights even after initial delivery to a buyer or carrier."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-08fbcc9c2ce9e3d4f773cc495db19495</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 750}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1175}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BILL OF LADING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Bill of Lading is a document that evidences the receipt of goods by a carrier and serves as evidence of title in some cases, often used for transferring ownership during shipping processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-08fbcc9c2ce9e3d4f773cc495db19495</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 752}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY IN THE GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY/MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property in the goods refers to legal ownership of the goods, which can be transferred based on certain conditions outlined in the contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property in the goods refers to ownership rights over the items being sold, which can be transferred according to contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c8e3424a8a5275e58cb410e4ea0f205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34bc94419b349addb3ca3738887910de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 751}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1177}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RISK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Risk is a concept that describes potential losses or uncertainties associated with the transfer and delivery of goods between parties under specific contractual terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk is associated with ownership of goods; it shifts from the seller to the buyer upon transfer of property unless delivery has been delayed due to fault."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34bc94419b349addb3ca3738887910de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;風險表面與產權同時轉移&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This phrase refers to an event where risk and property rights are transferred simultaneously, as per Chinese legal context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-34bc94419b349addb3ca3738887910de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 207}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;貨品&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Goods are items being traded between the seller and buyer under specific contractual terms related to ownership and delivery risks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-34bc94419b349addb3ca3738887910de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY IN THE GOODS (CHINESE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property in the goods refers to legal ownership of the goods, which can be transferred based on certain conditions outlined in the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-34bc94419b349addb3ca3738887910de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 207}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;風險 (RISK) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Risk is a concept that describes potential losses or uncertainties associated with the transfer and delivery of goods between parties under specific contractual terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-34bc94419b349addb3ca3738887910de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property here refers to the legal title and rights over goods, which can be transferred from the seller to the buyer under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property refers to assets that are owned or in possession of parties involved in the arbitration, relevant for determining the scope and nature of disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 918}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DELIVERY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Delivery refers to the act or process by which goods are transferred, and its timing can affect risk and title transfer conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELLER'S AUTHORITY TO SELL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The seller’s authority to sell is a key factor in determining the buyer's ownership of the goods. If the seller lacks this authority, the buyer may not acquire better title than what the seller had."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 775}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON/ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Owner refers to the organization or individual who owns the property and may be informed about potential delays in construction work or supply of related goods and services."&lt;SEP&gt;"Owner refers to the rightful holder of goods who can authorize or consent to their sale. The nature and extent of ownership influence the transfer conditions between seller and buyer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Owner is mentioned as someone who might be notified about the claiming party's intention to delay work or supply."&lt;SEP&gt;"The owner refers to the individual or entity that owns the property subject to construction work and may be notified about delays."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89690e148d95bff497042548ed9e3555&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a39eb07c8451fb1542c2fcc4877cecdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d229505b95cc3e576d9ad034318c66d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 775}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE FACTORS ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 48)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Factors Ordinance provides legal provisions that may affect the surface owner's ability to act as if they were the true owner, potentially impacting title transfers in certain circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGENTS REGULATIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 48)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This ordinance affects the validity of sale contracts where a person acts on behalf of another without explicit authority but may still be treated as if they had such authority under specific legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A court order may be made to restrict the employer's right to make deductions as specified in Section 32."&lt;SEP&gt;"A court order may override normal sale contract provisions, affecting how title is transferred between seller and buyer under specific circumstances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Any court order that limits the deductions made by employers is mentioned but no specific details about such orders are provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"Court Order here refers to legal commands issued by courts that are used for comparison with emergency relief provided by an emergency arbitrator in terms of enforceability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Court Order refers to an order issued by the court, which can be requested by employers, persons named in the Certificate, or ECAFB."&lt;SEP&gt;"Court orders can modify the intervals of periodical payments, ensuring flexibility in payment schedules."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0b8e9edfab8c32d5cea9270e6f74ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9335a6eed209eaa686a730c45ba54a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bad177b227e380cc066abb25e6c2cf7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2e37a06f23a289862428e2457ce5863&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad963d62d75768847794433df9caf4b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 410}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1114}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SURFACE OWNERSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT/PROPERTY LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Surface ownership refers to the apparent or outward appearance of ownership that can be different from true legal ownership. This concept affects how goods are treated in certain legal contexts, especially when sold by unauthorized persons."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRUE OWNERSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT/PROPERTY LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"True ownership is the actual and rightful possession of property, which may differ from surface ownership. The distinction can impact title transfers between seller and buyer under specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL AUTHORITY TO SELL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT/LEGAL RIGHT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal authority to sell refers to the rights granted by an owner or through other legal means that allow a person to sell goods on their behalf, which is crucial in determining title transfers between seller and buyer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 918}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TITLE TRANSFER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/CONTRACT CLAUSE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Title transfer involves the formal change of ownership from one party (seller) to another (buyer), with conditions that may affect when this occurs based on factors such as fault in delayed delivery or other legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 918}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RISK ASSUMPTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT/LEGAL RIGHT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Risk assumption refers to the shift in responsibility for loss of goods from seller to buyer upon transfer of title, which can be conditional and affected by various factors including fault in delayed delivery."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 918}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAULT IN DELAYED DELIVERY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/CONDITION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fault in delayed delivery is a condition that affects risk assumption and the validity of sale contracts. If either party's fault causes delay, the goods are at the risk of the party responsible for such fault until title transfer occurs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMERCE LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY/LEGAL FIELD"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Commerce law governs commercial transactions including sales agreements, ownership transfers, and related legal rights and obligations between parties involved in commerce activities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMERCIAL TRANSACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/CONTRACT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Commercial transaction refers to the exchange of goods or services for consideration. The text discusses conditions under which such a transaction can occur legally and how risks are transferred from seller to buyer based on various factors including fault in delayed delivery."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL REGULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY/LEGAL FIELD"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal regulations, particularly those found in the Factors Ordinance (Chapter 48) and Agents Regulations Ordinance (Cap. 48), affect how commercial transactions are conducted and the rights of parties involved, especially when dealing with unauthorized sales or surface ownership."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 918}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMERCE ACTIVITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY/LEGAL FIELD"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Commerce activities include buying and selling goods as described in the text, where legal provisions determine conditions for title transfer, risk assumption, and other aspects related to commercial transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 130}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL PROVISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal provisions are specific laws or regulations that govern how commerce is conducted. The text mentions several such provisions affecting the sale of goods by unauthorized persons and conditions for title transfer and risk assumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal provisions refer to laws or sections within a legal document that outline rules for employee dismissal and re-engagement as described in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 833}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMERCE REGULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY/LEGAL FIELD"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Commerce regulations, including those found in various ordinances like the Factors Ordinance (Chapter 48) and Agents Regulations Ordinance (Cap. 48), provide frameworks within which commercial transactions must be conducted to ensure legal compliance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMERCIAL SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/CONTRACT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Commercial sale is a transaction where goods are sold for consideration, with conditions governing the transfer of ownership and risk as described in the text. The nature of such sales can vary based on factors like fault in delayed delivery or legal provisions affecting surface versus true ownership."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMERCE PRACTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY/LEGAL FIELD"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Commerce practices include standard procedures for conducting commercial transactions, which may be influenced by various laws and regulations as described in the text. These practices ensure that sales are conducted fairly and legally between parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal Compliance involves adherence to laws and regulations related to workplace incidents, ensuring proper reporting and handling of accidents as required by law."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal Compliance refers to adherence to laws and regulations governing business transactions, including payment claims and responses. It ensures that all parties act within legal boundaries."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal Compliance refers to adherence to laws and regulations governing dispute resolution processes, ensuring that all actions taken during arbitration proceedings are in line with legal standards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal compliance is a key aspect discussed, ensuring that employers adhere to statutory requirements regarding employee leave and alternative holiday arrangements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal compliance refers to adherence to legal requirements for employment contracts and dismissals as described in the text, particularly related to Sections 31T, 9, 10 of 1992 s. 62."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal compliance refers to adherence to relevant laws and regulations governing commerce activities such as those discussed, ensuring fair transactions and protecting rights of all parties involved in commercial dealings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98b9cc96db8e2ffdc374754939531431&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adbe757d90ad335b39fd280c5f650025</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 151}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 657}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FACTORS ORDINANCE (CAP. 48)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Factors Ordinance (Cap. 48) is an enactment that allows the apparent owner of goods to dispose of them as if they were the true owner, despite potential ownership issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"This refers to a specific piece of legislation in Hong Kong defining 'mercantile agent', which is not directly an entity but contextually relevant here."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-097842d27813c438fcbfa56e8eef5ca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 303}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 992}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHOP OR MARKET&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A shop or market in Hong Kong operates under the ordinary course of business, providing a setting for open sales subject to certain legal conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-097842d27813c438fcbfa56e8eef5ca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 213}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT OF COMPETENT JURISDICTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A court with authority to make decisions regarding sales and ownership disputes, ensuring legal validity through judicial processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-097842d27813c438fcbfa56e8eef5ca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 209}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC MARKET&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Public markets in Hong Kong are places where goods can be openly sold as part of their regular business operations, subject to specific legal protections for buyers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-097842d27813c438fcbfa56e8eef5ca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 213}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELLER'S VOIDABLE TITLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A seller's voidable title refers to ownership that is potentially invalid but not yet nullified at the time of sale, impacting the buyer's acquisition rights under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-097842d27813c438fcbfa56e8eef5ca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 213}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALE UNDER VOIDABLE TITLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event of selling goods with a voidable title involves legal complexities where buyers may still acquire good ownership despite potential issues in seller's authority."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-097842d27813c438fcbfa56e8eef5ca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 214}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 761}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VOIDABLE TITLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Voidable title is an ownership status that can be invalidated but isn't yet nullified, affecting the sale and transfer of goods according to specific legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-097842d27813c438fcbfa56e8eef5ca4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 209}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLEDGE OR OTHER DISPOSALS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These refer to actions like pledging (using as collateral</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a502d54239df6738cd72e46d8d4377e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELLER'S DEFECTIVE TITLE KNOWLEDGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This concept relates to the seller's awareness (or lack thereof</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a502d54239df6738cd72e46d8d4377e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELLER OR BUYER IN POSSESSION AFTER SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Seller or buyer in possession after sale refers to a situation where goods are sold and the seller continues to possess them or their documents of title, or when a new buyer obtains possession with consent from the original seller."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2262a3a4061aab5ab97a1077b67a5057</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 214}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 762}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTS OF TITLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documents of title are instruments used for transferring ownership, such as bills of lading or other legal documents related to goods transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2262a3a4061aab5ab97a1077b67a5057</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 214}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 761}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMERCIAL AGENT (MERCANTILE AGENT)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A commercial agent is a person who acts on behalf of another in business dealings and can be involved in the delivery or transfer of goods under certain conditions without affecting their legal status as an authorized representative."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2262a3a4061aab5ab97a1077b67a5057</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 214}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 762}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LIEN OR OTHER RIGHT OF THE ORIGINAL SELLER IN RESPECT OF THE GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to any claim by the original seller over the goods, such as a lien, which could affect subsequent transactions if not resolved properly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2262a3a4061aab5ab97a1077b67a5057</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 214}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 762}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MERCANTILE AGENT (商業代理人)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A mercantile agent, as defined by the Factors Ordinance, has implications for understanding possession and transfer of goods in commercial transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOODS OR DOCUMENTS OF TITLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These refer to physical products or documents that serve as evidence of ownership over such products, which are central to the discussion on delivery and transfer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALE AGREEMENT (售賣合約)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONTRACT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The sale agreement outlines the terms under which goods will be transferred from seller to buyer, including responsibilities for both parties regarding payment and delivery."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DELIVERY OF GOODS (交付貨品)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the act of transferring possession of goods from the seller to the buyer as per the terms agreed in the sale contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 756}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT FOR GOODS (支付貨價)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The payment event involves the transfer of funds by the buyer to the seller, which is concurrent with the delivery of goods and forms part of the overall transaction process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 756}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POSSESSION TRANSFER (管有交予)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This describes the act where ownership or control over goods changes hands from one party to another as a result of sale, involving both physical transfer and legal recognition of new ownership status."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 750}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1175}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT PERFORMANCE (合同履行)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The performance aspect involves adherence by both parties—seller in delivering the goods and buyer in accepting them and making payment according to the terms agreed upon in their contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPEALED 52 OF 1987 S. 45&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This indicates a specific section within an ordinance that has been repealed, affecting certain aspects related to commercial transactions and agent responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART III (第III部)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SECTION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to the third part of the document which deals with detailed rules on contract performance including delivery and payment conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERFORMANCE OF CONTRACT (合同的履行)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This term encompasses all actions taken by both parties in fulfilling their obligations under a sale agreement, particularly focusing on timely and proper execution of the transaction terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 750}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1176}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALE AGREEMENT TERMS (售賣合約條款)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONTRACT条款"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are specific conditions outlined within the contract that govern how goods will be delivered to and accepted by the buyer, including payment obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 750}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1176}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONCURRENT CONDITIONS (同時履行的條件)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This concept refers to situations where both delivery of goods and receipt of payment must occur simultaneously for a sale agreement to be validly concluded without one party's obligation being contingent on the other’s performance first."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGREEMENT (議定)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGREEMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Any additional agreements between parties that may modify standard terms, such as conditions of delivery and payment beyond what is stipulated in a basic sale agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OWNERSHIP TRANSFER (所有权转移)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This involves the legal change from one party to another regarding who has rightful control over goods or documents representing ownership rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMERCIAL TRANSACTION (商業交易)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A broader term encompassing all activities related to buying and selling of goods, including delivery, payment, and transfer of legal title as described in the document."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HONG KONG LEGISLATION (香港立法)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers broadly to laws applicable within Hong Kong that govern commercial transactions, such as those related to sale agreements and mercantile agents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FACTORS ORDINANCE ( FACTORS 条例)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a specific piece of legislation in Hong Kong defining roles like 'mercantile agent', which impacts how goods are transferred under certain conditions without direct seller involvement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOOD FAITH TRANSFER (善意转让)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to the transfer or delivery of goods to someone who is unaware and acting in good faith, potentially absolving original sellers from claims if such a transfer occurs legally."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OWNER CONSENT (所有人同意)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONSENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Involves obtaining consent from the owner for certain actions like transferring possession or documents of title related to goods as part of commercial transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 751}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1177}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENT OF TITLE (单据或所有权证明文件)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documents that serve as evidence of ownership over specific items, often used in transfer and sale processes without direct physical delivery of the item itself."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALE CONTRACT (售賣合同)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONTRACT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A formal agreement between a seller and buyer detailing terms for exchange of goods or services including payment obligations and conditions for delivery."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT OBLIGATION (付款义务)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"OBLIGATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The financial responsibility of the buyer to make timely payments as per agreed-upon terms in a sale contract, which is often concurrent with receiving delivered goods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 754}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOODS DELIVERY PREPARATION (货物交付准备)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Preparation by sellers to ensure they are ready and willing to deliver goods upon request from buyers according to the terms of their agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 754}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUYER ACCEPTANCE RESPONSIBILITY (买家接受责任)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"OBLIGATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The duty of the buyer to accept delivered goods in accordance with contract terms, which is often linked with making corresponding payments for those goods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELLER'S DELIVERY READINESS (卖方交付准备度)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to sellers ensuring they are prepared and willing to deliver goods as per the agreed-upon conditions in a sale contract, including readiness to transfer possession of items or documents representing ownership."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT FOR GOODS PROCESS (货物付款流程)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCEDURE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The process by which buyers make payments corresponding to delivered goods according to terms set out in their sales agreement with sellers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 751}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1178}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DELIVERY RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Delivery Rules are a set of guidelines for when and how goods should be delivered in exchange for payment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-048787341fb4d01340940003ad08182c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELLER'S PLACE OF BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Seller's Place of Business is the location where the seller conducts their business, which serves as the default delivery point unless otherwise specified by contract or agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The seller's place of business is the location where delivery takes place if the seller has one. If not, it defaults to his residence."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-048787341fb4d01340940003ad08182c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d46459d50da26f6edb3bcb2bd876ab7d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRD PARTY POSSESSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Third Party Possession refers to a situation where goods are held by someone other than the buyer and seller, affecting when and how delivery can be made."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-048787341fb4d01340940003ad08182c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRD PERSON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A third person holds goods on behalf of either the buyer or the seller and must acknowledge this for a valid delivery from the seller to the buyer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d46459d50da26f6edb3bcb2bd876ab7d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REASONABLE TIME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Reasonable Time refers to any time during which an inspection can be carried out without requiring a warrant, as specified in the regulatory framework for Employment Agencies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reasonable time is a term indicating that certain actions or requests can be made at any point within normal business hours or operational periods, ensuring transparency and accountability in the regulatory framework for employment agencies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reasonable time is defined within the context for entering and searching premises or places where there may be evidence of an offence under this Part, implying normal operational hours but not necessarily limited to them."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reasonable time is determined based on circumstances, indicating flexibility in deadlines but requiring prompt action."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reasonable time refers to a period during which inspections can be conducted without requiring a warrant, implying normal operational hours but not necessarily limited to them."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reasonable time refers to a period of time determined based on facts and circumstances, as mentioned in the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-067e7bd64c7c5b9cd0bc7a9d57842457&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4b0005d3a0274c239ac28577960774&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-409891bfe2bfb21a0731ddceffe7a7d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee0cf79121cc26199f0bf5c4d14a8ce8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d46459d50da26f6edb3bcb2bd876ab7d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 147}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 644}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELLER'S EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The seller must bear all costs and incidental expenses related to putting goods into a deliverable state before delivery."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d46459d50da26f6edb3bcb2bd876ab7d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 147}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 644}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUYER'S REFUSAL OF GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"If the quantity delivered by the seller is less than agreed, the buyer can refuse receipt. If accepted, payment should be made at the contract rate for that quantity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d46459d50da26f6edb3bcb2bd876ab7d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELLER'S OVER-DELIVERY HANDLING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"When the quantity of goods delivered exceeds what was contracted, the buyer has options to accept part or all and reject excess, with full payment required if accepting all."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d46459d50da26f6edb3bcb2bd876ab7d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT RATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contract Rate is a term used in the context of payment for goods delivered as per the agreement, indicating the agreed-upon price or value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contract rates are pricing terms agreed upon in sales contracts for specific quantities of goods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-09f76424c00042dab76ada9f73a18154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d46459d50da26f6edb3bcb2bd876ab7d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 750}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1175}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;USAGE OF TRADE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Usage of Trade refers to industry practices that may override specific terms outlined in the contract if applicable."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-09f76424c00042dab76ada9f73a18154</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 751}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1177}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERIODIC DELIVERY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Periodic Delivery refers to a situation where goods are delivered in installments, which is subject to specific conditions outlined in the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-09f76424c00042dab76ada9f73a18154</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 750}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1175}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DELIVERY BY INSTALMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Delivery by instalments refers to the process of delivering goods in multiple installments which are separately paid for. The breach of this contract can be either a repudiation of the whole contract or a severable breach giving rise to compensation claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7711a5fb09f26ba7ae910773ed7d5cf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;交付承運人&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Delivery by carrier involves handing over goods to a carrier appointed by the seller, which is considered as delivering the goods to the buyer. The terms and conditions with the carrier must be reasonable considering the nature of the goods and other circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7711a5fb09f26ba7ae910773ed7d5cf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RISK OF DETERIORATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT/MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Risk of deterioration refers to the potential damage or loss in value that may occur during transit, which must be managed by either the seller or buyer based on their agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19b288c9efaa7bb08b81764887c880c5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 751}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1177}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEA TRANSIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sea transit is a specific type of transportation where goods are transported via sea and involves risks such as weather conditions, piracy, etc., which can affect the condition of the goods during delivery."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19b288c9efaa7bb08b81764887c880c5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 750}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1175}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISTANT PLACE DELIVERY RISK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT/MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Risk associated with delivering goods to a distant location entails additional considerations for risk management beyond just sea transit, including potential delays and other logistical issues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19b288c9efaa7bb08b81764887c880c5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 751}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1177}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RIGHT OF EXAMINING GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The right of examining goods is an industry practice or legal requirement that allows the buyer to inspect delivered items to ensure they meet contractual specifications. This process helps in dispute resolution and quality control."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19b288c9efaa7bb08b81764887c880c5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 750}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1175}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCEPTANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Acceptance is a significant event where the buyer officially acknowledges receipt of goods after examination."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-535dface6286d8bede9ae8225e2d5326</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 750}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1175}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXAMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Examination involves checking if the delivered goods meet contract specifications, crucial for determining acceptance or rejection."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-535dface6286d8bede9ae8225e2d5326</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 750}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1175}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (1) describes the conditions under which a buyer is deemed to have accepted goods after delivery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (1) in this context refers to specific legal provisions that ensure continuity and enforcement of rights despite a party's death, impacting how arbitration agreements are managed posthumously."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (1) is a legal provision that addresses the liability of directors, managers, secretaries, or similar individuals for offenses committed by an organization with their consent,纵容或疏忽。"&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (1) is a legal provision that outlines the requirement for noise abatement notices served by The Authority."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (1) outlines the primary obligation of employers to ensure employee safety and health at work through various means such as providing safe plant and systems, making necessary arrangements for safety, offering information, instruction, training, supervision, maintaining a safe workplace, and ensuring a safe working environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (1) refers to a legal proceeding where a court may order the disclosure of names, identities, secrets, or processes under specific conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (1) refers to requirements that an employer must include truthfully in a statement under subsection (1), which are not further specified in this context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (1) refers to the amount required by reference to the number of employees in relation to whom the policy is in force and in accordance with the Fourth Schedule."&lt;SEP&gt;"The event refers to the circumstances where an employee's contract of employment is not renewed and they are not re-engaged under a new contract, as mentioned in section 31D(2)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The event refers to the legal subsection that outlines requirements for employers and insurers."&lt;SEP&gt;"subsection (1) is a part of the regulation detailing how holiday pay should be handled, specifically stating that no payment in lieu of grant of a holiday can be made except as specified."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-82a3bfa1b02f074277b3b1a27f3afcb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8565a0dde3a6e724288267c5d06fe0dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d1a5d83703c47f3bc06048ecc6e08a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13ee9a92c0574802dd2767b6923aabc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f10185e6fc563260f4e1f20ab8c394fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6401943df7f64de20cb83d590f559418&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33baa15beb160832b6e2302162f04d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8903577fbeb26a0f144927da3a1efb7c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 156}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 666}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A legal provision specifying the categories of employers who must maintain records as per Part X regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (2) details additional circumstances where acceptance of goods by a buyer may be delayed, particularly if they have not examined them yet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (2) is a provision that addresses the liability of partners in a partnership who are involved with offenses committed by other partners or those managing the business, and it can also be attributed to their negligence. It was added in 2018 under section 10."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (2) is an event or clause in the text that specifies exceptions to certain parts of a regulation, particularly concerning state employments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (2) lists specific cases where employers fail to comply with Subsection (1), including failing to provide or maintain safe plant and systems of work, making necessary arrangements for safety in connection with the use, handling, storage, or transport of substances, providing insufficient information, instruction, training, supervision, maintaining an unsafe workplace, and providing a working environment that is not safe."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (2) outlines conditions under which delay in resolving a claim is considered unreasonable."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (2) outlines the penalties for an employer who contravenes subsection (1), including fines and imprisonment terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The event refers to a further legal subsection detailing penalties for contravention of the main section."&lt;SEP&gt;"The event related to subsection (2) involves specifying dates for various types of payments and leaves, including overtime pay, maternity leave, paternity leave, severance payment, long service payment, sickness allowance, holiday pay, and annual leave."&lt;SEP&gt;"subsection (2) outlines a specific event or condition that affects gratuity or benefit reduction, involving years of service and pre/post-transition portions."&lt;SEP&gt;"subsection (2) refers to a specific part of the legal text that outlines conditions for recoverable damages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f93037749b5c82c21a4dffe24495861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8565a0dde3a6e724288267c5d06fe0dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d1a5d83703c47f3bc06048ecc6e08a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13ee9a92c0574802dd2767b6923aabc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc495e2347a322a5aaa3ff390e7601c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b785a6d2d7fe1aa9d111846965f88378&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5368f346dbcfde8d0b6c8190b98be08d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15fe91e28bec496f95bc0e2d20ab50c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8903577fbeb26a0f144927da3a1efb7c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 158}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 671}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (3) clarifies that the consumer's right to rely on subsection (2)'s provisions cannot be waived or lost through agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (3) describes penalties for employers who fail to comply with Subsection (1), including fines of up to $3,000,000 on summary conviction and up to $10,000,000 on conviction on indictment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (3) is a legal provision that employers must not contravene without reasonable excuse; otherwise, they commit an offense and are liable to a fine."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (3) is a provision that continues from subsections (1) and (2), providing further details on the offenses related to corporate or partnership misconduct. It was added in 2018 under section 10."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (3) is part of the legal provision detailing the period during which leave can be taken, starting from four weeks before the expected delivery date and ending 14 weeks after the actual delivery date."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (3) outlines the process for an employee to request a compliant statement from their employer if they have not been provided one within a week of receiving notice."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (3) pertains to another legal proceeding involving the disclosure of secrets or processes as required by justice."&lt;SEP&gt;"subsection (3) describes an event where the aggregate amount of qualifying items is reduced by the post-transition portion of the long service payment under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-82a3bfa1b02f074277b3b1a27f3afcb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13ee9a92c0574802dd2767b6923aabc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f10185e6fc563260f4e1f20ab8c394fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b785a6d2d7fe1aa9d111846965f88378&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f18d7b28f469093dbda2666fad1b8f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baa998ea27b6baa036c2807f3cddf020&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8903577fbeb26a0f144927da3a1efb7c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 157}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 669}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (4)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (4) describes an event where The Authority can cancel or vary requirements in a previously issued Noise Abatement Notice."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (4) provides additional context and clarification for the application of previous sections, addressing how legal principles should apply when a new owner offers renewal or re-engagement to an employee who has previously worked under different ownership."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (4) provides details on how to interpret and apply section 31C(2)'s provisions when dealing with offers made by a new owner, ensuring that certain conditions are met during such transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (4) specifies penalties for employers who intentionally, knowingly, or recklessly fail to comply with Subsection (1), including fines of up to $3,000,000 and imprisonment for 6 months on summary conviction, and fines of up to $10,000,000 and imprisonment for 2 years on conviction on indictment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (4) states conditions under which a buyer is deemed to have accepted goods, even if they retain them without informing the seller of rejection within a reasonable time."&lt;SEP&gt;"subsection (4) provides details on the inclusion of interest in compensation awards based on specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92eb9fce002800330c9f680d468f081b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5368f346dbcfde8d0b6c8190b98be08d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8903577fbeb26a0f144927da3a1efb7c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 159}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (5)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (5) describes the power of the Court to exercise authority if an arbitral tribunal cannot be established or does not exist."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (5) is another legal provision detailing the specified payment date on which a sum becomes payable if the employer fails to reinstate or re-engage the employee as ordered by an award. It was added in 2018 under section 10."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (5) outlines factors considered in determining whether 'reasonable time' has elapsed for subsection (4)'s application."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (5) outlines the penalties for committing an offense as defined in subsections (a) and (b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37eade578e866e449433b5cf2ef5311c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13ee9a92c0574802dd2767b6923aabc1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 160}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 673}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (6)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (6) describes an event where non-compliance with requirements in a Noise Abatement Notice results in committing an offense."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (6) details the special powers of the High Court in relation to arbitration proceedings outside Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (6) specifies that a buyer is not deemed to have accepted goods merely because they are delivered under a sub-sale or other disposition without the buyer's explicit acceptance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 162}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPLACED 85 OF 1994 S. 6&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to an amendment replacing section 6 from Act 85 of 1994, indicating changes in legal provisions over time."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 160}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 674}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (3) (CHINESE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (3) in Chinese states that a buyer's right not to return rejected goods cannot be waived by agreement or otherwise."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 160}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 674}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (1) (CHINESE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (1) in Chinese describes the conditions for acceptance of delivered goods, similar to its English counterpart."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 160}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 674}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (2) (CHINESE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (2) in Chinese details additional circumstances where a buyer may delay accepting goods after delivery without examination."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 160}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 674}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (4) (CHINESE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (4) in Chinese states conditions under which a buyer is deemed to have accepted delivered goods, even if they retain them without informing the seller of rejection within a reasonable time."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 160}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 674}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (5) (CHINESE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (5) in Chinese outlines factors considered in determining whether 'reasonable time' has elapsed for subsection (4)'s application."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 160}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 674}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (6) (CHINESE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (6) in Chinese specifies that a buyer is not deemed to have accepted goods merely because they are delivered under a sub-sale or other disposition without the buyer's explicit acceptance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 160}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 674}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT REPUDIATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Repudiation of the contract occurs when the buyer neglects or refuses to take delivery, which is equivalent to terminating the agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-019dad10da4fa0e0f55e19465cb7641c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 751}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1177}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNPAID SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Unpaid Seller is a party in the transaction who has not yet received payment for goods delivered, and retains certain rights such as stoppage in transitu."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Unpaid Seller is the party who has parted with possession of goods and retains the right to stop them in transitu when the buyer becomes insolvent."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unpaid Seller refers to a seller who has not received full payment for the goods, which can include scenarios where the price has not been paid or tendered in full, or when a negotiable instrument is accepted as conditional payment but the condition is not fulfilled."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unpaid seller represents the party who has sold goods but hasn't yet received payment and exercises rights such as lien, retention, or stoppage in transitu."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3460a8b3f83d1862f966932908fad7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae57bca98959e6dd3d2fc2d9ac1ea95e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-019d766805b0f1dd881f70eeb98bba2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c25cd0589b8a4d3c22c97ec5d8feb564</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BILL OF EXCHANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Bill of Exchange is a negotiable instrument used in conditional payment scenarios, which can be accepted but may not fulfill its conditions due to dishonor or other reasons."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c25cd0589b8a4d3c22c97ec5d8feb564</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSIGNOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Consignor refers to the person who sends goods for transportation and may also be responsible for paying the price directly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c25cd0589b8a4d3c22c97ec5d8feb564</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Agent can refer to a representative of the seller, such as one who endorses a bill of lading or handles other aspects related to the sale of goods."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Agent is someone authorized to act for another person (the principal) and may be held responsible for actions taken within the scope of their authority."&lt;SEP&gt;"An agent is mentioned as someone who may be in possession of goods on behalf of another party but still allows the seller to exercise their lien rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-83a8d937e2b926da0d7047a5288d8ae8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6afb8943a99ee7bf996b0ce17c18a04b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c25cd0589b8a4d3c22c97ec5d8feb564</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNPAID SELLER'S LIEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The term 'unpaid seller's lien' refers to a legal right of an unpaid seller who is in possession of the goods, allowing them to retain those goods until payment or tender of the price under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unpaid seller's lien is a legal right that allows the seller to retain possession of goods until payment for those goods is made. It applies in situations where credit terms are not specified or have expired."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-83a8d937e2b926da0d7047a5288d8ae8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d30dda660ca1f229dc1755fad3c1ac13</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 216}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 768}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STOPPAGE IN TRANSITU&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Stoppage in transitu is a legal term indicating that an unpaid seller can regain possession and retain the goods during transportation if the buyer becomes insolvent, until payment or tender of the price is made."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stoppage in transitu is an event where the seller can detain goods during transportation after parting with their physical possession, typically when the buyer becomes insolvent and the property has passed to them."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d30dda660ca1f229dc1755fad3c1ac13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64fb15ad53f00752c5f21028f6ffe501</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 216}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 769}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CREDIT SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A credit sale is mentioned as one type of transaction where the term of credit has expired, leading to the seller's right to retain possession of the goods until payment or tender of the price."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-83a8d937e2b926da0d7047a5288d8ae8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 216}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 768}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART DELIVERY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event 'part delivery' refers to the situation where an unpaid seller has already delivered some but not all of the goods, which affects their rights regarding the remaining items."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-83a8d937e2b926da0d7047a5288d8ae8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGREEMENT TO WAIVE LIEN OR RETENTION RIGHT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An agreement to waive the lien or retention right is mentioned as a condition under which the seller may lose their rights over the remainder of the goods if part delivery was made in such circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-83a8d937e2b926da0d7047a5288d8ae8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CARRIER OR BAILEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A carrier or bailee, who handles the transportation or custody of goods on behalf of another party, can still allow the seller's lien to apply even when they are managing the goods for a buyer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-83a8d937e2b926da0d7047a5288d8ae8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 216}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 768}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION OF LIEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event refers to the situation where an unpaid seller loses their right of retention or lien on goods under certain conditions, such as delivering them to a carrier for transmission to the buyer without reserving disposal rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-64fb15ad53f00752c5f21028f6ffe501</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 216}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 769}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;途中停運&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"途 中 停 運 (Stoppage in transitu) refers to a legal right where an unpaid seller can regain possession and retain goods during transportation if the buyer becomes insolvent, until payment or tender of the price is made."&lt;SEP&gt;"途中的停止运输指的是在特定条件下，货物可以被暂停运送，直到进一步指示或条件满足为止。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-64fb15ad53f00752c5f21028f6ffe501&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3304fe02529acf61f5b7a297e0a498dd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 216}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 769}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;途中停運權&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"途 中 停 運 權 (Right of stoppage in transitu) allows an unpaid seller to regain possession and retain goods during transportation if the buyer becomes insolvent, until payment or tender of the price is made."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-64fb15ad53f00752c5f21028f6ffe501</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 216}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 769}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAND TRANSPORT PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Land transport period refers to a specific time frame when goods are being transported by land, which can be relevant in legal contexts involving stoppage and lien rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-64fb15ad53f00752c5f21028f6ffe501</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 216}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 769}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSOLVENT BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Insolvent Buyer refers to a person or entity that cannot meet its financial obligations, leading to the rights of stopping goods in transitu for the unpaid seller."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3460a8b3f83d1862f966932908fad7a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELLER'S RIGHT OF STOPPING GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Seller's Right of Stopping Goods is a legal event where the seller can reclaim possession of goods during transit if the buyer becomes insolvent, until full payment or tender of price is made."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3460a8b3f83d1862f966932908fad7a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 214}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 763}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAND CARRIER/SEA CARRIER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Land Carrier or Sea Carrier refers to entities responsible for transporting goods by land or sea and are involved in the process of delivering goods to the buyer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3460a8b3f83d1862f966932908fad7a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 214}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 763}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUYER'S AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Buyer's Agent is a person authorized by the buyer to receive deliveries on their behalf, mentioned in relation to part delivery of goods."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Buyer's Agent is a representative acting on behalf of the buyer, possibly involved in receiving or managing the delivery of goods during transit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3460a8b3f83d1862f966932908fad7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-019d766805b0f1dd881f70eeb98bba2c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DELIVERY LOCATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Delivery Location refers to the designated place where goods are expected to be delivered and signifies the end of transport for legal purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3460a8b3f83d1862f966932908fad7a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 214}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 763}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRANSPORTATION PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Transportation Period is a defined time frame during which goods are in transit, subject to specific conditions regarding stoppage rights and delivery obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3460a8b3f83d1862f966932908fad7a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 214}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 763}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DURATION OF TRANSIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event refers to the period during which goods are in transit from delivery to a carrier until final delivery or other specified conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3304fe02529acf61f5b7a297e0a498dd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 214}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 761}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHIP CHARTERED BY THE BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A ship chartered by the buyer refers to a specific mode of transportation for goods under contract with the buyer's agreement and is subject to carrier responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3304fe02529acf61f5b7a297e0a498dd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 214}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 761}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MASTER AS A CARRIER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Master, acting as a Carrier, has the responsibility to transport goods according to contractual agreements without wrongful refusal or delay in delivery."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3304fe02529acf61f5b7a297e0a498dd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 214}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 761}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGENT OF THE BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Agent of the Buyer is someone authorized by the buyer to act on their behalf for specific transactions related to the purchase and receipt of goods during transit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3304fe02529acf61f5b7a297e0a498dd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 214}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 761}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;未獲付款的賣方&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"未获付款的卖方是指那些尚未收到货款但仍保留对货物的实际控制权，并有权根据合同条款采取行动的一方。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3304fe02529acf61f5b7a297e0a498dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;實際管有&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"实际管有指的是在特定情况下，一方能够实际控制和管理货物的状态，这可能影响到运输过程中的权利与义务分配。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3304fe02529acf61f5b7a297e0a498dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;向管有貨品&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"向管有货品是指另一方被授权管理和控制已交付的货物，涉及相关责任和权益的转移或维持。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3304fe02529acf61f5b7a297e0a498dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CARRIER OR OTHER BAILEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Carrier or Other Bailee refers to entities that have physical possession of the goods during transportation, including carriers and storage facilities where goods are held before delivery."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-019d766805b0f1dd881f70eeb98bba2c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRINCIPAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Principal refers to an entity or individual who has given authority to another (the agent) and must be informed about stoppage in transitu for it to be effective."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-019d766805b0f1dd881f70eeb98bba2c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELLER'S AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Seller's Agent is a person authorized by the seller, possibly involved in re-delivery of goods as per the seller’s instructions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-019d766805b0f1dd881f70eeb98bba2c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RE-SALE BY BUYER OR SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Re-sale by Buyer or Seller refers to situations where either party sells the goods again after an initial transaction, which can affect the rights and obligations between parties regarding stoppage in transitu."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to situations where a buyer or seller resells the goods, impacting legal rights related to ownership and control."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1e7e0254dd707b1e5c7c10449fc028e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-019d766805b0f1dd881f70eeb98bba2c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 208}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNPAID SELLER'S RIGHT OF LIEN OR RETENTION OR STOPPAGE IN TRANSITU&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The unpaid seller's rights include the ability to retain goods until payment is made, and to stop the shipment if payment is not received. These are legal mechanisms used primarily in commercial transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"This refers to legal rights related to goods delivery and ownership transfer, which are crucial for understanding the dynamics between buyers and sellers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1e7e0254dd707b1e5c7c10449fc028e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-200bd4845769007ce451fb6541f74f39</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 51}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 420}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUYER OR SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to individuals involved in transactions of goods, with specific roles such as making sales or disposals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1e7e0254dd707b1e5c7c10449fc028e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 51}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 420}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CARRIER OR OTHER BAILEE IN POSSESSION OF THE GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to entities responsible for transporting goods and holding them on behalf of others until delivery is made."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1e7e0254dd707b1e5c7c10449fc028e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 51}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 420}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENT OF TITLE TO GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to documents that serve as evidence of ownership over goods, which can be transferred legally between parties involved in transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1e7e0254dd707b1e5c7c10449fc028e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 51}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 420}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUYER'S GOOD FAITH AND VALUABLE CONSIDERATION TRANSFER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event describes the situation where goods are transferred from a buyer who has taken them in good faith and with valuable consideration, which affects the unpaid seller’s rights of lien or retention or stoppage in transitu."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-200bd4845769007ce451fb6541f74f39</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 51}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 419}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLEDGE OR OTHER DISPOSITION FOR VALUE TRANSFER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A pledge or other disposition for value refers to situations where goods are transferred under a contract that involves security interests. The unpaid seller's right can only be exercised subject to the rights of the transferee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-200bd4845769007ce451fb6541f74f39</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 51}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 419}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALE REVOCATION DUE TO LIEN EXERCISE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event describes scenarios in which the sale is not generally rescinded by the exercise of lien or stoppage in transitu, but there are exceptions where such actions can lead to contract cancellation if certain conditions are met."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-200bd4845769007ce451fb6541f74f39</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 51}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 419}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALE NOT RESCINDED DUE TO LIEN EXERCISE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event describes that a sale is not generally rescinded by the mere exercise of an unpaid seller's right of lien or retention or stoppage in transitu, unless specified otherwise under this section."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-200bd4845769007ce451fb6541f74f39</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESALE AFTER LIEN EXERCISE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"After exercising their rights of lien or retention or stoppage in transitu, if the goods are resold by the unpaid seller to a new buyer who takes them in good faith and for valuable consideration, it affects the original buyer's rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-200bd4845769007ce451fb6541f74f39</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 51}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 420}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALE CONTRACT NOT RESCINDED DUE TO PERISHABLE NATURE OF GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"If the goods are of a perishable nature or if the unpaid seller notifies the buyer of their intention to resell before payment is made and within a reasonable time, then the original sale can be rescinded by the unpaid seller."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-200bd4845769007ce451fb6541f74f39</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 51}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 419}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELLER'S RESERVATION OF RIGHT TO RESALE FOR SECURITY PURPOSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"If the seller reserves the right to resale as a security measure against non-performance by the buyer, and resells after such non-performance occurs, it may lead to cancellation of the original sale contract but does not affect any claims for damages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-200bd4845769007ce451fb6541f74f39</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 51}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 419}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALE NOT GENERALLY RESCINDED BY LIEN OR STOPPAGE IN TRANSITU&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to a legal situation where a contract of sale is not typically canceled due to an unpaid seller's exercise of their right of lien, retention, or stoppage in transitu."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae57bca98959e6dd3d2fc2d9ac1ea95e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUYER ACQUIRES A GOOD TITLE THERETO AS AGAINST THE ORIGINAL BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event describes that when an unpaid seller re-sells goods after exercising their right of lien or retention, the new buyer gains a valid claim over those goods compared to the initial buyer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae57bca98959e6dd3d2fc2d9ac1ea95e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RE-SELL THE GOODS AND RECOVER FROM THE ORIGINAL BUYER DAMAGES FOR ANY LOSS OCCASIONED BY HIS BREACH OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to an unpaid seller's right to re-sell goods after exercising lien or retention, and subsequently seek compensation from the first buyer if there is a loss due to their non-compliance with the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae57bca98959e6dd3d2fc2d9ac1ea95e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WHERE THE GOODS ARE OF A PERISHABLE NATURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONDITION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This condition specifies that when goods are easily spoiled or deteriorate quickly, an unpaid seller may re-sell them and claim damages from the original buyer if they fail to pay within a reasonable time."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae57bca98959e6dd3d2fc2d9ac1ea95e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNPAID SELLER GIVES NOTICE TO THE BUYER OF HIS INTENTION TO RE-SELL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event describes that when goods are perishable or when an unpaid seller notifies the buyer about their intent to resell, and the buyer fails to pay in a timely manner, the seller can proceed with resale."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae57bca98959e6dd3d2fc2d9ac1ea95e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WHERE THE BUYER DOES NOT WITHIN A REASONABLE TIME PAY OR TENDER THE PRICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONDITION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This condition indicates that if the buyer doesn't promptly provide payment after being notified of an intention to re-sell perishable goods, the unpaid seller may resell and seek damages for any resulting losses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae57bca98959e6dd3d2fc2d9ac1ea95e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WHERE THE SELLER EXPRESSLY RESERVES A RIGHT OF RE-SALE IN CASE THE BUYER SHOULD MAKE DEFAULT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONDITION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This condition states that if a seller explicitly retains the right to resale upon buyer's default, they can proceed with such action without rescinding the original contract entirely but still have grounds for seeking damages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae57bca98959e6dd3d2fc2d9ac1ea95e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACTIONS FOR BREACH OF THE CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These actions refer to legal proceedings initiated by a seller against a buyer who has breached their contractual obligations regarding payment or delivery of goods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae57bca98959e6dd3d2fc2d9ac1ea95e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REMEDIES OF SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Remedies of seller are various legal tools and methods available to the party selling goods, including rights like lien, retention, stoppage in transitu, resale, and claims for damages when a buyer breaches contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae57bca98959e6dd3d2fc2d9ac1ea95e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY HAS PASSED TO THE BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event describes that under certain conditions of sale, ownership or property rights over goods have transferred from seller to buyer even before physical delivery."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae57bca98959e6dd3d2fc2d9ac1ea95e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUYER WRONGFULLY NEGLECTS OR REFUSES TO PAY FOR THE GOODS ACCORDING TO CONTRACT TERMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONDITION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This condition specifies situations where a buyer fails to make payment as per agreed-upon contractual obligations, constituting wrongful behavior and justifying legal action by the seller."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae57bca98959e6dd3d2fc2d9ac1ea95e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACTION FOR PRICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Action for price refers to a legal proceeding initiated by the seller against the buyer when payment terms are not met according to contract stipulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c8e3424a8a5275e58cb410e4ea0f205</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 751}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1177}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DAMAGES FOR NON-ACCEPTANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Damages for non-acceptance is an event where the seller can sue the buyer for losses due to the refusal or neglect of accepting and paying for goods, based on contractual terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Damages for non-acceptance refers to the legal action a seller can take against a buyer who wrongfully neglects or refuses to accept and pay for the goods, seeking compensation based on estimated loss."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c93fa5b9277d567b2558365e758a282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8e3424a8a5275e58cb410e4ea0f205</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 755}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARKET PRICE/TIMES PRICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS/SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Market price or times price refers to the current value of goods in an available market, used as a basis for calculating damages when there is no specific acceptance time agreed upon."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c8e3424a8a5275e58cb410e4ea0f205</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 755}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REMEDIES OF BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Remedies of buyer is a concept related to actions available to a buyer in case of non-acceptance of goods by the seller."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c93fa5b9277d567b2558365e758a282</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 750}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1175}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DAMAGES FOR NON-DELIVERY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Damages for non-delivery refers to the legal action a buyer can take against a seller who wrongfully neglects or refuses to deliver the goods, seeking compensation based on estimated loss."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c93fa5b9277d567b2558365e758a282</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 751}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1177}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARKET PRICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Market price refers to the current value at which goods can be bought or sold in an available market, used as a basis for calculating damages when there is no fixed time for acceptance or delivery."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c93fa5b9277d567b2558365e758a282</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 750}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1175}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIFIC PERFORMANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY/EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Specific performance is a legal remedy where the court orders one party to carry out their contractual obligations rather than providing monetary compensation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fed27e8241086925853de29390c3f116</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 751}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1177}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DAMAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Damages are monetary compensation claimed by the buyer against the seller due to breach of warranty."&lt;SEP&gt;"Damages refer to any compensation that can be claimed by employees who sustain bodily injuries during their employment due to workplace accidents, excluding claims under this Ordinance, and the interest payable on such damages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Damages refer to financial compensation for losses incurred due to breach of contract, which can be calculated based on market prices or estimated loss."&lt;SEP&gt;"Damages refer to financial losses that may result if a temporary measure is not ordered and are considered in determining whether such a measure should be granted."&lt;SEP&gt;"Damages represent the legal remedy where the buyer can seek compensation due to breach of warranty conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-69fc897b8b9dfae677db802b05a78337&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fed27e8241086925853de29390c3f116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed869807b046c3698e2d9492883a3d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7266eb6e2df511d14420717ab492d463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8630302d71316afe5c4d5a0aacb23fcb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 344}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1031}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GUARANTEE CLAUSE VIOLATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Guarantee clause violation refers to a situation where the seller breaches a warranty in the contract, and the buyer may choose to treat it as such even if not explicitly stated."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fed27e8241086925853de29390c3f116</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT JUDGMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY/EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court judgment is an event or legal decision made by the court regarding specific performance or compensation for breach of contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fed27e8241086925853de29390c3f116</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Price refers to the monetary value assigned to goods or services, which may be adjusted based on warranty breaches."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-69fc897b8b9dfae677db802b05a78337</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 750}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1175}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BREACH OF WARRANTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Breach of warranty refers to a violation in the quality or condition of goods sold, leading to potential legal actions for damages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed869807b046c3698e2d9492883a3d9e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 344}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1034}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTEREST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interest is a financial term referring to the cost of borrowing money or the income from lending it, often calculated as a percentage of the principal amount."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interest is an amount payable for the use of money over time, calculated based on the judgment rate as determined by the Chief Justice."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interest refers to financial compensation awarded by the Arbitral Tribunal on certain payments or amounts as specified in the arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8edbd1c4d3b35d7faddb32b978e73e29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed869807b046c3698e2d9492883a3d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a7d382b60c68c418d8128c80396b687</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1204}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIAL DAMAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Special damages are specific monetary compensation for particular losses such as medical expenses and lost wages resulting directly from an injury or breach of contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed869807b046c3698e2d9492883a3d9e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1204}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The buyer is a party in a transaction who purchases goods or services, potentially claiming damages if the seller breaches warranty terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed869807b046c3698e2d9492883a3d9e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The seller is a party in a transaction responsible for providing goods or services and ensuring they meet specified quality standards as per contractual warranties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed869807b046c3698e2d9492883a3d9e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;《管制免責條款條例》(第71章)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"《管制免責條款條例》(第71章) is a regulation that governs the terms under which liability can be waived or limited in sales contracts, affecting how warranties and conditions are handled."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed869807b046c3698e2d9492883a3d9e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 344}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1034}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPPLEMENTARY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Supplementary refers to additional provisions or explanations added to an ordinance or law for clarification or further detail."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supplementary refers to additional provisions that support or clarify other sections in legal documents, such as those found in Part IX of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-990bd24369be2bc2f9bdd440773f2e19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed869807b046c3698e2d9492883a3d9e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 344}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1034}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTROL OF EXEMPTION CLAUSES ORDINANCE (CAP. 71)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Control of Exemption Clauses Ordinance is a legal document that may affect the negation or variation of implied terms by express agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5c4b0005d3a0274c239ac28577960774</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 748}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RIGHT, ETC., CAN BE ENFORCED THROUGH LITIGATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This statement indicates that any rights, responsibilities or legal liabilities published under this ordinance can be enforced through litigation unless otherwise specified by the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5c4b0005d3a0274c239ac28577960774</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 147}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 644}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RIGHT, ETC.&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rights, duties, and liabilities are legal concepts enforceable through litigation as stated by the Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed2ef74a32a03501189b4ee2f1d7da9e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUCTION SALE&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An auction is a public event where goods or property are sold to the highest bidder under the hammer of an auctioneer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed2ef74a32a03501189b4ee2f1d7da9e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BIDDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A bidder is an individual who participates in an auction to purchase items being sold through competitive bidding."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-32292d53bc2adbfdb992bdf0fe946e4a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 759}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUCTIONEER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An auctioneer is the person who conducts the auction, manages bidding processes, and announces when the sale is complete."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-32292d53bc2adbfdb992bdf0fe946e4a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 758}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HAMMER FALL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The fall of the hammer signifies the completion of an auction where bids have been finalized."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-32292d53bc2adbfdb992bdf0fe946e4a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BID RETRACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Until the announcement of the completion of the auction, any bidder may retract their bid."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-32292d53bc2adbfdb992bdf0fe946e4a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 759}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESERVE PRICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A reserve price is a minimum selling price that must be met for an item to sell at an auction; if not reached, the sale can be withdrawn or conducted privately."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-32292d53bc2adbfdb992bdf0fe946e4a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 206}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 751}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1177}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BANKRUPTCY RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bankruptcy rules continue to apply to sales contracts even under this legislation, ensuring certain protections and procedures are maintained in case of seller insolvency."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-32292d53bc2adbfdb992bdf0fe946e4a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 758}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMON LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Common Law refers to the body of law derived from judicial decisions and customs rather than statutes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Common law principles, including commercial laws, continue to apply unless explicitly overridden by the provisions of this statute, covering areas such as agency rights, fraud, misrepresentation, coercion, or other grounds for contract invalidation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2554ffe0d55bbe29aef6808731a595f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32292d53bc2adbfdb992bdf0fe946e4a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 757}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALE OF GOODS (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1977&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Sale of Goods (Amendment) Ordinance 1977 refers to a specific legal document that amends the existing laws related to the sale of goods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9ff930ec7eb83b579d28ddffeafb904</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 310}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BANKRUPTCY RULES RELATING TO CONTRACTS OF SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bankruptcy rules relating to contracts of sale are mentioned as continuing to apply, indicating their relevance and ongoing use in legal contexts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9ff930ec7eb83b579d28ddffeafb904</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 310}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMON LAW INCLUDING THE LAW MERCHANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The common law, particularly the law merchant, continues to apply where not inconsistent with this Ordinance, highlighting its integration into existing legal frameworks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9ff930ec7eb83b579d28ddffeafb904</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 310}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RULES RELATING TO THE LAW OF PRINCIPAL AND AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Specific rules related to the law of principal and agent continue to apply, showing their importance in contract law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9ff930ec7eb83b579d28ddffeafb904</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 310}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FRAUD, MISREPRESENTATION, DURESS OR COERCION, MISTAKE, OR OTHER INVALIDATING CAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rules regarding fraud, misrepresentation, duress, etc., are mentioned as continuing to apply, indicating the ongoing relevance of these legal concepts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9ff930ec7eb83b579d28ddffeafb904</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 310}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BILLS OF SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bills of sale refer to documents evidencing the transfer of ownership or title of property, which are mentioned as enactments that continue to apply despite changes in other parts of the Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"References to bills of sale indicate their continued applicability in certain contexts despite changes in other laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9ff930ec7eb83b579d28ddffeafb904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd505e56ed8f7c2a002ed11a0086e732</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 310}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTS FOR THE SALE OF GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contracts for the sale of goods are subject to specific rules and continue to be governed by existing legal frameworks, showing ongoing relevance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9ff930ec7eb83b579d28ddffeafb904</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 310}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALE OF GOODS (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1977 (58 OF 1977)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to an amendment made in 1977 that modifies certain provisions of the original Ordinance, but its specific changes are not detailed."&lt;SEP&gt;"This product is a legal document that amends and updates existing laws related to the sale of goods, but its specific details are not provided in this text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd505e56ed8f7c2a002ed11a0086e732</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 310}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Employees' Compensation Ordinance is a legal document aimed at providing compensation to employees injured during their employment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employees' Compensation Ordinance is the base legislation that was amended by various ordinances over time, including those from 1982 and 1988."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1183805b5e096e72ad7ed819d31ac70a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52f2dcf46c7d731442f86d90c2b5ddd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 386}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CAP. 282&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cap. 282 refers to the chapter or instrument number of the Employees' Compensation Ordinance in Hong Kong legislation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1183805b5e096e72ad7ed819d31ac70a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 386}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1953年A160號政府公告&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"1953年A160號政府公告 is an official gazette notice issued on 1 December 1953, marking the initial publication of the Employees' Compensation Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1183805b5e096e72ad7ed819d31ac70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;[1 DECEMBER 1953]&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The date [1 December 1953] marks the specific day when the first official gazette notice was issued for the Employees' Compensation Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1183805b5e096e72ad7ed819d31ac70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRELIMINARY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Preliminary is a section title indicating introductory or background information in legal documents, such as the Employees' Compensation Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Preliminary section provides an overview or introduction to the ordinance, including its short title and purpose."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Preliminary section provides introductory information and context for the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1183805b5e096e72ad7ed819d31ac70a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4f6f1173170ce4ac811fedab280f3b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb7fcd5200d5f794a363f07e5ee2dc70</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 386}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK INJURY COMPENSATION CLAIM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Work injury compensation claim pertains to legal proceedings for seeking compensation due to injuries sustained at work, where the court may treat a worker as if they were working under a valid employment or apprenticeship contract even when such contracts are deemed illegal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b89c4e47ed400d96906517cf8d97057f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAMILY MEMBER OF EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Family members of an employee include those who can represent the deceased employee in legal proceedings regarding compensation for work-related injuries, including their legal heirs and representatives appointed by the Chief Executive Officer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b89c4e47ed400d96906517cf8d97057f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;雇主&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"雇主也是接受评估的对象之一，与雇员一同接收由普通评委会或特别评委会发出的证明书。"&lt;SEP&gt;"雇主是指提供工作并支付报酬的实体，在此上下文中涉及终止合同的情况。"&lt;SEP&gt;"雇主是指雇佣了工人的企业或个人，负责支付工资和遵守相关劳动法规。"&lt;SEP&gt;"雇主是指雇用人员的组织或个人。"&lt;SEP&gt;"雇主是接受通知並可能要求提供醫生證明書的人或組織。"&lt;SEP&gt;"雇主是负责支付因员工去世所产生的相关费用的一方，在规定的时间内必须完成付款义务。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1009cd645f2a253ea46bb7c8dd54bc47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-737d4df7f01f646261bb3f23aa0c6c79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f5c32e3a6975f5012a9f880a409dd60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb31bef1e8dd24810a075920d4fb5602&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3451e297aa0bd05f84186c235d841d44</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 93}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 496}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;意外&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"意外指在工作期间因工遭遇的身体受伤事件。"&lt;SEP&gt;"意外指的是在工作过程中发生的事故或事件，可能影响到员工的安全和健康。"&lt;SEP&gt;"意外指突发事件或事故，可能导致员工死亡或受伤。"&lt;SEP&gt;"意外是指事故或突发事件，文中的事件涉及支付补偿的问题。"&lt;SEP&gt;"意外是指雇员在执行工作职责过程中遭遇的事故，在香港境内与境外之间、或者在香港以外的地方与其他地方之间的交通工具使用中发生的。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8d6f58db2bf906e62e1287ce399d4434&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdb83d21468796679ea45d3ca07b4e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae344452d3fef20d9a84a14e26b325a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f5c32e3a6975f5012a9f880a409dd60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-686d30ddd39f8474a0c88cb4aa604f1c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 88}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 494}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;保險單&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"保險單是彌償僱主就僱員損傷所負的法律責任的一種金融產品。"&lt;SEP&gt;"保險單是用于保障员工在工作过程中可能发生的意外伤害的保险合同，涉及金额和条款的具体规定。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4f5c32e3a6975f5012a9f880a409dd60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-269d623b6606eba8ac3002fec6213eae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 71}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 456}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1127}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第40(1)條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"第40(1)條是指與僱主投保相关的法律规定。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4f5c32e3a6975f5012a9f880a409dd60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;合同&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"合同指的是任何形式的劳动合同或学徒合同，包括明示和暗示、口头和书面形式。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4f5c32e3a6975f5012a9f880a409dd60</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 71}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 456}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1126}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;行政長官&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"行政長官是指具有委任权力的人，在此上下文中可能指有权任命代表雇员家庭成员行事的人。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4f5c32e3a6975f5012a9f880a409dd60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;4. MEANING OF EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Meaning of employee是指对雇员定义的解释和说明。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4f5c32e3a6975f5012a9f880a409dd60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot; (僱員)">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee refers to any person who has entered into or works under a contract of service or apprenticeship with an employer, except for specific exceptions such as casual workers, outworkers, and family members residing with the employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d8a5d1112f976dfc9d2cfe7182bd06d2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OUTWORKER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An individual who works outside a regular employment setting, often associated with piecework or contract-based work."&lt;SEP&gt;"Outworker is a type of employee who works outside the main workplace and may be subject to different employment laws regarding severance payments during layoffs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Outworker refers to a person who performs工序 in their home or another location not controlled by the employer, involving assembly, cleaning, washing, modification, decoration, processing, or repair of items for sale."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-700cb0251acd9df09975828a3d0f4f1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8e2655c247e96affa05132d650c897b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-590222e3ba7f541e965c6d035076bb63</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 572}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1138}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COHABITEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cohabitee is defined as someone living with an employee at the time of an accident, akin to a spouse."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-700cb0251acd9df09975828a3d0f4f1d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 572}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1138}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EARNINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Earnings denote any wages paid in cash by employers and any benefits that can be valued monetarily."&lt;SEP&gt;"Earnings refer to income or wages received by employees, which can potentially be used to pay for insurance premiums related to the employer’s legal liabilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-700cb0251acd9df09975828a3d0f4f1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd33f100307534902fe4100976fabc93</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 575}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSURANCE POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A financial product that provides coverage for potential liabilities arising from employee injuries during employment."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Insurance Policy is a document that provides coverage and protection against financial losses, particularly in cases of damage or injury."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Insurance Policy is a document that provides coverage for liabilities, and it governs how claims can be made against the insured person or entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Insurance Policy is mentioned in the context of covering an employer's legal liability, indicating its importance for employment contracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Insurance Policy is required for employees under the total contractor and must cover liabilities up to a specified amount as outlined in the Fourth Schedule."&lt;SEP&gt;"An insurance policy is a financial product that provides coverage for certain conditions or events, such as accidents at construction sites."&lt;SEP&gt;"An insurance policy issued for the purposes of this Part is a product that covers employees' injuries arising out of and in the course of their employment."&lt;SEP&gt;"An insurance policy, which is the subject of legal requirements and provisions for inclusion of specific data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance Policy is a type of product, specifically mentioned in the text and related to the commissioner's requirements for inspection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance policy is the document that provides coverage for various risks or liabilities related to employment and legal responsibilities of employers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance policy refers to a contract between an insurer and the insured party that covers certain risks or liabilities. It is mentioned in relation to claims and legal proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance policy refers to a contract that indemnifies the employer against liability in respect of personal injuries caused by accidents during employment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance policy refers to a document that provides coverage for various risks, particularly in the context of workplace injuries and legal responsibilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance policy refers to the type of coverage required under subsections (1), (1B), and (1C) for employees' safety and compensation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb529b0707db1b4e516f08ed3339967d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f93037749b5c82c21a4dffe24495861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8565a0dde3a6e724288267c5d06fe0dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d1a5d83703c47f3bc06048ecc6e08a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6157228e3518a3c9dd66f98867aa8a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9b169ef4b1de04369879d234076f1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff7a7ad14c10761bcb15431ef57d8f8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f50ffa55ee49cc2d1e6b1641b82f27dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2fbd733817e8b83d49f91e4a4cbe908&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ead5337f34ae6c6d3adbc5b06e2bc74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab8247f4347839df18b680f569571c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a384314fa98b789ae4d76d79c9eae831&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-700cb0251acd9df09975828a3d0f4f1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca74ec0b128bebdd8deb74d88fe33613</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 572}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1139}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;同居者&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"同居者是指在有关意外发生时与该雇员共同生活如同其妻子或丈夫的人。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-033e8a760f87ee7c1653db65ace61bb6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;收入&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"收入指雇主以现金付给雇员的任何工资,以及可作金钱估值的任何优惠或利益,包括雇员因意外而失去享有的任何由雇主所提供的食物、燃料或宿舍的价值;亦指超时工作付款或所作工作的其他特别酬金,不论是以花红、津贴或其他形式发放,而属固定性质者或为惯常执行的工作而发放者,而受雇从事的工作因其性质以致习惯地给予和收取小费的习惯是公开和公认的,并得雇主认可的,则亦包括小费：但并不包括间歇性超时工作的酬金、临时非经常性的得款、交通津贴的价值、交通特惠的价值、雇主为雇员的退休金或公积金所分担的供款或付给雇员以应付其受雇从事工作性质所需的特别开支的款项。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-033e8a760f87ee7c1653db65ace61bb6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;次承判商&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"次承判商是分包合同中的承包方，可能需要向总承判商转交通知。"&lt;SEP&gt;"次承判商是指——(a)任何与总承判商订立合同（不论是明订或隐含的）以为总承判商所承担进行的全部或部分工作的人；及(b)任何订立合同（不论是明订或隐含的）以为(a)段所指的次承判商所承担进行的全部或部分工作的其他人。"&lt;SEP&gt;"次承判商是指进行全部或部分工作的承包商。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-86c763b37e9e3638b9a073d36c6b4de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-033e8a760f87ee7c1653db65ace61bb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb7e4af89a52e25a6a1e9f29341b95ad</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;完全喪失工作能力&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"完全喪失工作能力是指暂时或永久丧失工作能力,并因如此丧失工作能力而使雇员无能力担任在引致如此丧失工作能力的意外发生时他有能力担任的工作。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-033e8a760f87ee7c1653db65ace61bb6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;完全喪失工作能力 (TOTAL INCAPACITY)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"完全喪失工作能力指的是暂时或永久丧失工作能力，并因如此丧失工作能力而使雇员无能力担任在引致如此丧失工作能力的意外发生时他有能力受雇担任的任何工作者。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb7e4af89a52e25a6a1e9f29341b95ad</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;法院 (COURT)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Court refers to the Court of First Instance or District Court."&lt;SEP&gt;"法院是指与区域法院或其他法庭相关的法律程序中进行裁决的地方，包括区域法院、其他法庭或审裁处以及处长（视情况而定）。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce595edca85b7cf2be310394d2ac094c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb7e4af89a52e25a6a1e9f29341b95ad</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;保險公司 (INSURANCE COMPANY)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"保險公司指的是在香港经营意外保险业务的人，包括根据《保险业条例》(第41章)第8条获授权经营该条例附表1第3部所指明的保险业务类别中类別13的公司。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb7e4af89a52e25a6a1e9f29341b95ad</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;保險人 (INSURER)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"保險人指的是在香港经营意外保险业务的人，包括根据《保险业条例》(第41章)第8条获授权经营该条例附表1第3部所指明的保险业务类别中类別13的公司。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb7e4af89a52e25a6a1e9f29341b95ad</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;區域法院 (REGIONAL COURT)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"區域法院是指与区域法院相关的法律程序进行的地方，包括区域法院本身和其他相关机构。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb7e4af89a52e25a6a1e9f29341b95ad</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;處長 (CHIEF EXECUTIVE OFFICER, CEO)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"處長指的是在某些情况下负责对追讨补偿作出裁定的人。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb7e4af89a52e25a6a1e9f29341b95ad</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;勞合社 (LLOYD'S OF LONDON)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"勞合社是指一个位于联合王国的承保人组织，通常指劳埃德保险市场。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb7e4af89a52e25a6a1e9f29341b95ad</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;意外保險業務 (ACCIDENT INSURANCE BUSINESS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"意外保險业务指的是与意外相关的保险服务和产品。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb7e4af89a52e25a6a1e9f29341b95ad</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;《保險業條例》(第41章) (INSURANCE ORDINANCE, CAP. 41)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"《保險業條例》是一部在香港规范保险公司经营行为的法规，包括授权、监管等内容。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb7e4af89a52e25a6a1e9f29341b95ad</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;區域法院追討補償程序 (REGIONAL COURT DEBT RECOVERY PROCEEDINGS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"區域法院追討補償程序指的是在区域法院进行的法律程序，用于追讨补偿款。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb7e4af89a52e25a6a1e9f29341b95ad</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;社會科學 (SOCIAL SCIENCES)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"社會科學涵盖了与社会、人类行为和互动相关的学科领域，在此文本中没有具体提及。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb7e4af89a52e25a6a1e9f29341b95ad</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;數學 (MATHEMATICS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"數學在法律文本中的应用主要体现在数字和计算上，但在此段落中未有明确的数学概念或公式出现。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb7e4af89a52e25a6a1e9f29341b95ad</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSURANCE AUTHORITY OF HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Insurance Authority of Hong Kong is an organization responsible for regulating insurers and insurance activities in the region."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0394a6f179167fe6215a7bbf41cc871e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOCIETY OF LLOYD'S&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Society of Lloyd's, also known as Lloyd's, is a well-known insurer organization based in the United Kingdom."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0394a6f179167fe6215a7bbf41cc871e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REVIEW CERTIFICATE OF COMPENSATION ASSESSMENT FOR FATAL CASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Review Certificate of Compensation Assessment for Fatal Case is an updated version of the original certificate after review, confirming or varying the initial determination."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Review Certificate of Compensation Assessment for Fatal Case is another type of official document that may be issued during the review process related to fatal case compensation assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A review certificate that reassesses the compensation in fatal cases, also serving as a basis for determining payment amounts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Similar to a Certificate of Compensation Assessment, this document reviews and possibly revises the assessment of compensation in fatal cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Similar to the previous certificate but indicates a review process for fatal case compensation assessments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Review Certificate of Compensation Assessment for Fatal Case serves as an additional or revised assessment document when reviewing compensation claims in fatal cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"This product refers to a document issued according to Section 6D(6)(c) that reviews and assesses compensation for fatal cases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9e62cff17ccfc412cc70505158f5a23e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0394a6f179167fe6215a7bbf41cc871e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d87e36b5ad46db41c716cf2910faa95c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f817e1f2a5b13a0586c36573c6eea5b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12b83ce1e2c205caa4f85bb97a5c7967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf9822f57c8a8c75b294d17dfa49f864&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0a0053e7177c68e160847406a3692d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 198}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 736}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF COMPENSATION ASSESSMENT FOR FATAL CASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Certificate is a formal document issued by the Commissioner detailing the assessment of compensation in fatal cases, to be sent to relevant parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Certificate of Compensation Assessment for Fatal Case is a document issued by the Commissioner that details the assessment of compensation in fatal cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Certificate of Compensation Assessment for Fatal Case is an official document issued as part of the process to assess and determine eligibility for fatal case compensation under the Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Certificate of Compensation Assessment for Fatal Case is a document used to determine the compensation amount in fatal cases, detailing the distribution rules and procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Certificate of Compensation Assessment for Fatal Case is an official document used to assess and determine final compensation amounts following a fatal case, likely related to workplace accidents or deaths."&lt;SEP&gt;"The event is a specific document that assesses compensation in fatal cases, which affects the cessation of interim payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"This certificate is issued after a fatal case and serves as grounds for objection within 30 days from its issue date."&lt;SEP&gt;"This document assesses the amount of compensation due in fatal cases and triggers payment obligations from the employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is a document used in assessing compensation for fatal cases, which influences when interim payments can be made."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is a specific document used in the determination process, particularly relevant when dealing with fatal cases and compensation claims."&lt;SEP&gt;"This product is another type of document, issued based on Section 6B(1)(b), used to assess compensation for fatal cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"This technology or document assesses compensation in fatal cases and is used to determine payment periods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9a6dfc79f4a9de7dba162e137dcffd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e62cff17ccfc412cc70505158f5a23e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0394a6f179167fe6215a7bbf41cc871e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d87e36b5ad46db41c716cf2910faa95c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eff0ca72356f89bbfc64201ec755179c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f817e1f2a5b13a0586c36573c6eea5b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12b83ce1e2c205caa4f85bb97a5c7967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-330946d46297f253a2618e1b8da8fb4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bb18157fba38057f130a7b17e656fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf9822f57c8a8c75b294d17dfa49f864&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a66ccff5f4b1f0435e3a62cb416f252b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0a0053e7177c68e160847406a3692d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 198}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 736}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAMILY MEMBER (MEMBER OF THE FAMILY)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Family Member includes a spouse or cohabitant, children, parents, grandparents, and other relatives who have lived in the same household with the employee within 24 months prior to an incident."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0394a6f179167fe6215a7bbf41cc871e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE COMPENSATION (SPECIAL ASSESSMENT) BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This organization is established according to Section 16E for special compensation assessments of employees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0394a6f179167fe6215a7bbf41cc871e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORDINARY ASSESSMENT BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Ordinary Assessment Board is a body whose decision or assessment can be appealed to the District Court, involved in making evaluations related to appeals under specific sections such as 16A, 16F, 16G, and 16GA."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Ordinary Assessment Board is a group appointed under section 16D(2) for assessing claims for compensation according to specific procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Ordinary Assessment Board is involved in certifying periods of absence for total temporary incapacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ordinary Assessment Board is another type of assessment board involved in determining the extent of an employee's loss of earning capacity due to injuries."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ordinary Assessment Board is a body mentioned in the text that issues certificates and can be involved in assessments or evaluations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ordinary Assessment Board is a body responsible for issuing assessments and certificates in relation to claims, as described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ordinary Assessment Board is a body responsible for reviewing assessments, particularly in cases where the assessment was made under ignorance or based on false information."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ordinary Assessment Board is a body that may be involved in assessing the earnings of an employee after an accident causing injury, but it's not obliged to consider these actual earnings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ordinary Assessment Board is a committee appointed under Section 16D for employee compensation assessments, as amended by Ordinance No. 76 of 1982."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ordinary Assessment Board is a committee that makes assessments according to section 16D(5) of the relevant regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ordinary Assessment Board is an organization that issues certificates under section 16F, which are relevant in determining the actions of employers regarding employees with incapacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ordinary Assessment Board is another organization that issues certificates under section 16F, which are cancelled upon the issuance of a certificate by the Special Assessment Board as per subsection (7)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ordinary Assessment Board is responsible for assessments under section 16D(5), reviewing objections from employers or employees, and issuing relevant certificates."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ordinary Assessment Board reviews assessments, confirms or varies them based on employee or employer objections, and issues certificates accordingly."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is another type of board appointed under Section 16D, whose members may join the Special Assessment Boards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-514e0a6ffa9d391d835f484bdbaa5724&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7788fe09e12252d0bb714e4f775b4322&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0512d455417ff415dc742891f2498109&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21097621f6720ea0958fecf07d8dcf43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f281684938925901a68a287ea35fbc44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aa6a1ecbb96f241ec693e9b7796d393&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779a6ebdcf1cc3fbd67a4dc22862c59e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3ba6e4c8e42988a064ffe8e2ff8f96e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb0545d506978169e320db3a0cda4273&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da37f195f3ad2a893b50923a13911e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-038abcb26f772c8f77b5ead3c3b7177c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-924ba54f67533a1228efb89110dcadb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bad177b227e380cc066abb25e6c2cf7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f5ab2145d9ab1c03798719541af19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eeedbfd93d66d01580f5f057b6a2dfb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 140}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 619}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1156}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTIAL INCAPACITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Partial Incapacity refers to a condition where an employee has some but not full loss of work capacity after an accident. It affects how and if periodical payments can be reduced or terminated based on their income changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Partial Incapacity refers to a temporary reduction in earning capacity due to an accident at the time of employment; permanent incapacity includes disfigurement and involves current or future earning capacity reductions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f281684938925901a68a287ea35fbc44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea6d20dfaa02a409f86af6c45c243e0a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 140}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 624}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FUNERAL EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Funeral Expenses are costs related to the burial or cremation of an employee and can be claimed by individuals who paid for them."&lt;SEP&gt;"Funeral Expenses are events related to the costs associated with a deceased employee's funeral."&lt;SEP&gt;"Funeral Expenses are part of the compensation according to specific provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Funeral Expenses are the costs associated with a deceased employee's funeral, which must be considered in calculating total liability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Funeral Expenses refer to the costs associated with the burial or cremation of a deceased person, which may be covered under certain compensation arrangements for fatal cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Funeral expenses are amounts that may be recovered or distributed according to specific legal provisions in fatal incident cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Funeral expenses are costs associated with arranging a funeral service for an employee."&lt;SEP&gt;"Funeral expenses refer to the reasonable costs associated with a deceased employee's funeral and medical attendance, which are specified for compensation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0bd0b12255f92625b40e8341bf78636d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3fbc4f46edd3e4f207893d46b3cad06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2b2485fa1ca142d969f0703e2e3861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aaf035b8724e14296be4849afc0b0d7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-932bd52b3e4a92915c346a0ad3c1fd7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-266c63bff8f647150f70f543690f359f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b99b710a13a074eee4b0551f5e725be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2e37a06f23a289862428e2457ce5863</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 181}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDICAL FEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Medical Fees are included in the compensation, subject to certain regulatory conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0bd0b12255f92625b40e8341bf78636d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 720}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1169}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WAGES OR SALARIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wages or salaries may be compensated based on clauses 16I(3) and 36MA of relevant regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0bd0b12255f92625b40e8341bf78636d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Temporary Payment is a type of payment added according to amendments in the law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0bd0b12255f92625b40e8341bf78636d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADDITIONAL FEES OR INTEREST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Additional fees or interest may be charged on top of compensation as specified by certain clauses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0bd0b12255f92625b40e8341bf78636d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTERED DENTIST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Registered Dentist has its meaning given in section 2(1) of the Dental Registration Ordinance (Cap. 156)."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Registered Dentist is a dental professional who can be involved in certain medical examinations according to labor laws and related provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Registered Dentist is a dental professional who can provide certificates for legal purposes related to employee incapacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Registered Dentist is a medical practitioner who provides dental care and treatment. In the context of this text, it refers to someone whose certificate can support an application for changes in periodical payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Registered Dentist is a professional who has been registered under the Dentists Registration Ordinance (Cap. 156)."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Registered Dentist is mentioned in the context of issuing certificates under certain conditions related to employee health."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Registered Dentist specializes in dental care and can be part of the board for evaluating prosthetic needs related to dentistry."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Registered Dentist specializes in dental care and treatment, often supervising or providing services related to oral health."&lt;SEP&gt;"A registered dentist can certify periods of absence from duty, contributing to the determination of total temporary incapacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"A registered dentist is another healthcare professional who may be authorized to provide certificates for sickness days under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A registered dentist offers dental care services, which may be included within the description of medical treatment covered by an employer's agreement to provide free medical treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A registered dentist provides dental services and can issue certificates for incapability due to injury or illness affecting the mouth area."&lt;SEP&gt;"Registered Dentist is an individual qualified by law to diagnose, treat, and prevent diseases of the teeth and mouth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Registered dentist is a professional who conducts dental examinations, named by the employer for employees under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The term 'registered dentist' has the same meaning as that provided for under Subsection 2(1) of Article 2 of the Dental Registration Ordinance (Cap.156) in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af55493786feba6de502e98ed832cde8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89f7731524d41ce9b762132c808abd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd0b12255f92625b40e8341bf78636d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-966009ce5701084bfffbbea532d598a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8b48e83da24f4750fe34f6e53c34ac0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908f80036493cf02a5dd6da247a2a7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-150ac34f962a55c7a622046976949d60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1ed02e78cf2ee9e321f22dbe3ba84b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea6d20dfaa02a409f86af6c45c243e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1faa1664ffe65d577dff74396c2e0ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60357a5d0f946dc1e998d1bea10860b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5f66bf87b244d8c901c733042ddc26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a67530e0a9df975682238097b18b864&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bad177b227e380cc066abb25e6c2cf7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af043de8381bfd2d54ddf7a99fe8b0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 111}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 567}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTERED PHYSIOTHERAPIST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Registered Physiotherapist refers to a physiotherapist who is registered as such under the Professional Allied Health Workers Ordinance (Cap. 359)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0bd0b12255f92625b40e8341bf78636d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTERED CHIROPRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Registered Chiropractor has its meaning given in section 2 of the Chiropractors Registration Ordinance (Cap. 428)."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Registered Chiropractor specializes in spinal manipulation and other manual therapies for the treatment of musculoskeletal conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A registered chiropractor is a professional with the meaning given by Article 2 of The Chiropractic Registration Ordinance (Chapter 428)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af55493786feba6de502e98ed832cde8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd0b12255f92625b40e8341bf78636d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7266eb6e2df511d14420717ab492d463</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 183}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTERED OCCUPATIONAL THERAPIST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Registered Occupational Therapist refers to an occupational therapist who is registered as such under relevant regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"A registered occupational therapist refers to an occupational therapist who has been professionally registered under The Specialist Medical Profession Ordinance (Chapter 359)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0bd0b12255f92625b40e8341bf78636d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7266eb6e2df511d14420717ab492d463</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 183}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCIDENT INSURANCE BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY, SERVICE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Accident insurance business refers to the business of entering into an insurance contract which insures employers against legal liability for bodily injuries sustained by employees during their employment due to work-related accidents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to a specific type of insurance business regulated under the Insurance Ordinance (Cap. 41)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6fe38763521cd6ea4535e1c682771715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7266eb6e2df511d14420717ab492d463</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 344}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1030}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE CHIROPRACTIC REGISTRATION ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 428)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY,INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Chiropractic Registration Ordinance is a legal document that defines the meaning of 'registered chiropractor' and regulates related professional practices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7266eb6e2df511d14420717ab492d463</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 183}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE SPECIALIST MEDICAL PROFESSION ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 359)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY,INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Specialist Medical Profession Ordinance is a legal framework for registering occupational therapists and regulating their professional activities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7266eb6e2df511d14420717ab492d463</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 183}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE MEDICAL REGISTRATION ORDINANCE (CAP.161)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY,INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Medical Registration Ordinance defines the registration of medical practitioners and regulates related practices according to its provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7266eb6e2df511d14420717ab492d463</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 111}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 564}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1136}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 29(A) OF THE MEDICAL REGISTRATION ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This article specifies conditions under which a doctor can be deemed as registered even if not formally listed in the register."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7266eb6e2df511d14420717ab492d463</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 111}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 564}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1136}]</data>
</node>
