<node id="&quot;ECAFB (EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ASSISTANCE FUND BOARD)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ECAFB, established by Section 3(1) of the Employees' Compensation Assistance Ordinance (Cap. 365), is responsible for managing funds related to employee compensation assistance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-033087b2f1fb0d32b2faddaa41f6e432</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 252}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT OF APPRENTICESHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A contract of apprenticeship includes trainee contracts or probationary worker contracts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-033087b2f1fb0d32b2faddaa41f6e432</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 116}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRINCIPAL CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Principal Contractor is a party in construction projects who receives notice from employees of sub-contractors regarding unpaid wages and must forward this information to superior sub-contractors if known."&lt;SEP&gt;"A principal contractor enters into a contract directly with an owner or occupier, or their authorized representatives, for performing work."&lt;SEP&gt;"A principal contractor is a person or entity that takes out an insurance policy as per section 40(1B)."&lt;SEP&gt;"A principal contractor refers to an entity responsible for performing construction work and must comply with specific insurance requirements as outlined in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Contractor refers to a person who directly contracts with the owner or occupier of property, or an agent or approved architect, surveyor, or civil, urban, or structural engineer, to perform any works on behalf of the owner or occupant."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Contractor refers to any person or entity engaged in trade or business that contracts with a Sub-Contractor for work execution. They are liable for the compensation of employees working under sub-contractors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Contractor refers to the main entity responsible for contracting work and paying wages, which can also claim contributions or deductions as described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal contractor is an entity mentioned in relation to sub-contractors and accident reporting procedures according to workplace safety regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal contractor is an entity that takes out a specific insurance policy as mentioned in subsection (1B)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal contractor is the primary contracting entity in a construction or project management context, responsible for overseeing sub-contractors and ensuring compliance with contractual obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal contractor refers to the person mentioned in Section 24 as such a contractor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to a principal contractor who may receive notices under section 43D or 43H."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Principal Contractor is responsible for paying wages of employees when subcontractors fail to do so within the specified period, as per the regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The principal contractor is an organization that has contracted to perform certain works and may subcontract these tasks to other parties such as main nominated sub-contractors or nominated sub-contractors."&lt;SEP&gt;"The principal contractor is another organizational entity that may need to provide particulars if it's related to a subcontractor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c648be5705790613057129f42ce74462&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09e282cd999f281d4422d40832df059c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d1a5d83703c47f3bc06048ecc6e08a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd3149c252f1ac5ec61e07c2fc936cbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1766fce0308d4fb774b3b29e83cb45eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1082e0d73690e2409d13d0dfdf0e64c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-033087b2f1fb0d32b2faddaa41f6e432&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca6a3d09e67d65c6e2efdbaf610d6291&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bfdf4a9968aec09594f73a07cdf18d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa4e81ff5495fa19b7b8105fa63909b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af77be8b003511c35b7551f4285bb427&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cb98b63e05e5bcca889147b0b338ac8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93a1fe97f228ec755ced3c31d6506c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb529b0707db1b4e516f08ed3339967d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92743ab978843e283d6914a0d34ee3ea</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 254}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 923}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An interim payment is a temporary compensation, determined according to Section 6C(1)(a) of certain regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-033087b2f1fb0d32b2faddaa41f6e432</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 252}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REVIEW CERTIFICATE OF INTERIM PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A review certificate for an interim payment issued under Section 6C(11)(c) of relevant laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"Another type of product, which is a review certificate for making interim payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Review Certificate of Interim Payment is a document issued according to Section 6C(11)(c), used for interim payment review."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Review Certificate of Interim Payment serves a similar purpose as the Certificate of Interim Payment but may be issued after reconsideration or review, possibly due to changes in information or conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9a6dfc79f4a9de7dba162e137dcffd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf9822f57c8a8c75b294d17dfa49f864&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-033087b2f1fb0d32b2faddaa41f6e432&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550180dac5a100738db953050f3d47b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 252}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF INTERIM PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A certificate for an interim payment issued according to Section 6C(1)(b) of certain regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"A certificate issued by the Commissioner detailing the determination and payment terms for interim compensation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A product that is used to make interim payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Certificate of Interim Payment is a document issued according to Section 6C(1)(b) for interim payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Certificate of Interim Payment is a document issued by the Commissioner, containing financial information related to interim payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Certificate of Interim Payment is an official document used for interim payment calculations in certain circumstances, particularly related to employee compensation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b9a6dfc79f4a9de7dba162e137dcffd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-033087b2f1fb0d32b2faddaa41f6e432&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bb18157fba38057f130a7b17e656fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf9822f57c8a8c75b294d17dfa49f864&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d03bb282f99bcf0993cd32ec58e1edb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550180dac5a100738db953050f3d47b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 252}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REVIEW CERTIFICATE FOR FUNERAL AND MEDICAL ATTENDANCE EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A review version of the certificate mentioned above, indicating a re-evaluation or reassessment process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Another type of certificate, similar to the previous one but possibly with updated information or corrections."&lt;SEP&gt;"Review Certificate for Funeral and Medical Attendance Expenses is a document issued according to Section 6E(12)(c), used for reviewing funeral and medical expenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is another type of certificate that may be used in certain circumstances, possibly for re-evaluation or additional details regarding the initial certificate."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9e62cff17ccfc412cc70505158f5a23e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550180dac5a100738db953050f3d47b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aaf035b8724e14296be4849afc0b0d7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2e37a06f23a289862428e2457ce5863</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 197}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 732}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CERTIFICATE FOR FUNERAL AND MEDICAL ATTENDANCE EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A product that is issued by the Commissioner containing details related to funeral and medical attendance expenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Certificate for Funeral and Medical Attendance Expenses is a document issued according to Section 6E(1)(b) related to funeral and medical attendance expenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"This document is used in determining expenses related to funeral and medical attendance, part of the broader claim determination process."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is a certificate issued by an employer or relevant authority detailing expenses related to funeral services and medical attendance on an employee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9e62cff17ccfc412cc70505158f5a23e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550180dac5a100738db953050f3d47b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aaf035b8724e14296be4849afc0b0d7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2e37a06f23a289862428e2457ce5863</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 197}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 732}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL DISEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A health condition that arises from work-related factors and is listed in specific regulations, requiring reporting to authorities."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Occupational Disease is a health condition that arises out of or in connection with employment, as defined and regulated by relevant laws and schedules."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Occupational disease is a health condition that arises out of employment and can be reported by a medical practitioner to the Commissioner."&lt;SEP&gt;"An occupational disease is defined as an illness resulting from work-related factors, and its cause might be presumed based on the employee's employment history until contrary evidence is provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"Occupational Disease refers to any disease specified in Column 2 of Schedule 2, as well as its recurrence and sequelae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Occupational Disease refers to illnesses or conditions resulting from work-related factors and can be used in legal contexts where compensation may apply."&lt;SEP&gt;"Occupational disease is a health problem caused by working conditions, which can lead to loss of work capacity or death as mentioned in this text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Occupational disease refers to an illness contracted due to work-related factors and used for determining liability and compensation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Occupational diseases refer to illnesses that may affect employees due to their work environment, which can be considered in determining liability and insurance coverage."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8bab0fa8e650dc6d58da85c05c8bf94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09e282cd999f281d4422d40832df059c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d781ae6a3974dcd155b4f5b736d6161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05288c51fb6c9855d3f031e51b7e2be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a364dde1ed8396d855ac25cb593a8ce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55b9afafd03eeeed71ede32974cead3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e7d6d62033f777323f252b1d52645d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082f06bd634567bd06a50adf127eb9eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550180dac5a100738db953050f3d47b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 738}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDICAL TREATMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Medical Treatment is the treatment provided by registered doctors, dentists, traditional Chinese medicine practitioners, physiotherapists or occupational therapists, or under their supervision. It can be in a hospital or other places for employees injured at work and treated during working hours."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-550180dac5a100738db953050f3d47b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 111}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 567}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SCHEDULE 2&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A schedule that lists specific types of constructions, including those related to transportation infrastructure such as walkways, roads, railways, etc., which may or may not be included in certain contexts but are distinct from the definition of residential units."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appendix 2 is a schedule providing criteria for the validation of certain standards in legal disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Schedule 2 is a document containing provisions that apply to arbitration agreements under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Schedule 2 is a part of the ordinance that contains detailed rules or criteria related to certain sections (2-7), possibly involving social science considerations in legal contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Schedule 2 is an industry document that lists specific diseases related to occupational health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Schedule 2 refers to specific matters that courts or arbitrators should consider when determining reasonableness in contract terms, though its exact content is not provided here."&lt;SEP&gt;"Schedule 2 specifies occupational diseases that must be notified to the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51792815fbdf7d62aebbf3740d5c33b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05288c51fb6c9855d3f031e51b7e2be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ad741dbed5c956a0e2be863adf9b077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e40e8a615669f7f3c43f8171f5d7b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-236f00f9bfd67b3814958a8c6ddf9450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550180dac5a100738db953050f3d47b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5ff7ccd88e0bf1fa24f736784b46e37</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOSPITAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A hospital is defined under The Private Medical Institutions Ordinance and does not include residential units as per section 2(1)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hospital is a facility providing patient care services including medical diagnosis, treatment, and nursing care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hospital is a place where employees can receive medical treatment as an in-patient or out-patient."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hospital is the location where some employees may stay for medical examinations, distinguishing it from other settings such as clinics or private practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hospital refers to a medical facility where patients receive treatment and is central in the context of medical expenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hospital refers to a medical institution where patients are admitted for treatment and care. In the text, it is mentioned in relation to employees being checked or staying overnight."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hospital refers to an institution providing healthcare services, as mentioned in section 33(6)(a) of the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hospital refers to any private hospital licensed under the Private Medical Institutions Ordinance (Cap. 633) that is in force, hospitals as defined by this ordinance, government-operated hospitals, military hospitals, and public hospitals under the Hospital Authority条例(Cap. 113), or Hong Kong Chinese Medicine Hospital as defined under Section 2(5) of the Traditional Chinese Medicine Ordinance (Cap. 655);"&lt;SEP&gt;"Hospital refers to government-run hospitals or specialist clinics, military hospitals, public hospitals under the Hospital Authority Ordinance (Cap. 113), and Hong Kong Chinese Medicine Hospital as defined in Article 2(5) of the Traditional Chinese Medicine Ordinance (Cap. 655). Additionally, it includes any hospital licensed by the Private Medical Institutions Ordinance (Cap. 633&lt;SEP&gt;"Hospital refers to healthcare facilities maintained by the Government, military hospitals, public hospitals within the meaning of the Hospital Authority Ordinance (Cap. 113), The Chinese Medicine Hospital of Hong Kong, or those licensed under the Private Healthcare Facilities Ordinance (Cap. 633)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Hospital is mentioned as the place where registered doctors, registered Chinese medicine practitioners, or registered dentists may issue certificates on the day of issuance if an employee is a hospital in-patient."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b89f7731524d41ce9b762132c808abd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba7e2407b8844aba128e42ffefa2f5d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f158408c588106f3a0fd30a322902be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60efa76430de6c8c3995f39eeee4cc13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34eee1f014b609a8808be1cb2bff9b39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-178a551bcbbb140ed32885ff11a760d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5f66bf87b244d8c901c733042ddc26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcd2a26e931b9fa624c25b0caadbcdb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51d776901078e225f9c3c73c7879b5ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af043de8381bfd2d54ddf7a99fe8b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d88128975194421da26a5cd7caa858a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 345}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1035}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1218}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDICAL EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Medical Expenses refer to financial compensation for medical treatment related to work-related injuries as mandated by labor laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical Expenses refer to the financial obligations of an employer towards covering the cost of medical treatment for employees' personal injuries, including specific provisions related to medicines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical expenses are costs related to medical care provided for the employee, which can also be involved in compensation distribution under certain sections of a law."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical expenses are products or services related to healthcare costs which may be covered under certain conditions as determined by the Commissioner."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical expenses include charges for registered doctors, registered traditional Chinese medicine practitioners, registered dentists, registered chiropractors, registered physiotherapists or occupational therapists; surgical fees and therapy fees; nursing costs; hospitalization costs as an in-patient at hospitals; and under certain conditions, the cost of medicines, treatment items, and medicinal dressings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical expenses include the cost of various types of treatments provided by registered practitioners, as detailed in subsections (5) and (5A)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-150ac34f962a55c7a622046976949d60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-226a5e625c1a8d9a1eec41b16cf5ab0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f5fe723dc66b1a35b256f0fbcfd9642&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-266c63bff8f647150f70f543690f359f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d88128975194421da26a5cd7caa858a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbcb1ef289ad456f0c48fcfc25edb43d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 111}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 566}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRIVATE MEDICAL INSTITUTIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 633)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Private Medical Institutions Ordinance (Cap. 633) is a legal framework governing private medical institutions in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d88128975194421da26a5cd7caa858a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 345}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1035}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1218}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOSPITAL AUTHORITY条例(CAP. 113)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Hospital Authority is an organization responsible for public hospitals and healthcare services in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d88128975194421da26a5cd7caa858a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 345}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1035}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1218}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRADITIONAL CHINESE MEDICINE ORDINANCE (CAP. 655)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Traditional Chinese Medicine Ordinance (Cap. 655) regulates traditional Chinese medicine practices in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d88128975194421da26a5cd7caa858a0</data>
