<node id="&quot;第(5)(B)款&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"第(5)(b)款是关于处长有权拒绝批准协议并说明理由，同时可将该协议退回雇主进行修订的规定。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ad03aa80581d9d78c4971adade589820</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE REQUIRING ATTENTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Employee is a person who has suffered permanent incapacity due to injury and requires continuous assistance for essential actions of life."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-21c14cf842653359f26af3af94b35c1f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 829}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Agreement is a formal document or arrangement between the employer and the injured employee, approved by the Commissioner, which outlines terms for providing necessary attention and associated compensation."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Agreement is a written document between an employee and employer, reducing or waiving the right to compensation for injuries caused by old age, serious physical defects, or infirmity in employment."&lt;SEP&gt;"An agreement refers to a contract or arrangement between parties that may be subject to cancellation based on specific criteria such as fraud or misrepresentation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-21c14cf842653359f26af3af94b35c1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1683d49752acaec3491f38a426aac742&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-691e0bbfff602acd26ed9f7e9579a105</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 608}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1144}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERMANENT INCAPACITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Permanent Incapacity contrasts with temporary incapacity, indicating an inability to return to work indefinitely."&lt;SEP&gt;"Permanent Incapacity is an event where an employee's work capacity is significantly and permanently affected by an accident, leading to changes in their periodical payments according to specific sections of the ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Permanent Incapacity refers to a state where an individual's ability to perform essential actions of life is permanently impaired due to injury or illness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-21c14cf842653359f26af3af94b35c1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70e316f848fd5f9f0f6efb5f28f0e45b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea6d20dfaa02a409f86af6c45c243e0a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 432}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ATTENTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SERVICE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Attention in this context refers to the continuous care and assistance required by individuals with permanent incapacity, which can be provided either as a lump sum payment or through periodical payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-21c14cf842653359f26af3af94b35c1f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 829}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LUMP SUM PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PAYMENT METHOD"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Lump Sum Payment is a single, fixed amount of compensation calculated based on the probable duration and cost of necessary attention for an employee with permanent incapacity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-21c14cf842653359f26af3af94b35c1f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 100}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 521}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERIODICAL PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Periodical Payments are recurring financial benefits provided to employees during temporary incapacity, which may be redeemed as a lump sum if the employee leaves Hong Kong for residing outside."&lt;SEP&gt;"Periodical Payments are recurring financial contributions made over time to cover ongoing costs associated with providing necessary attention to employees with permanent incapacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Periodical payments are calculated based on the difference between pre-accident earnings and current or potential future earnings during temporary incapacity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-21c14cf842653359f26af3af94b35c1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70e316f848fd5f9f0f6efb5f28f0e45b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bad177b227e380cc066abb25e6c2cf7d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 100}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 521}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;L.N.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"L.N. is a legal notation or reference used to cite specific laws or sections within legislation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-caf4b3f0aa7e762095c32496aac13d2b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1995 S. 4&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Amended 1 of 1995 s. 4 refers to an amendment made in the year 1995, section 4, which has been amended multiple times."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-caf4b3f0aa7e762095c32496aac13d2b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FREE MEDICAL TREATMENT AS AN IN-PATIENT IN A HOSPITAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a specific condition under which no compensation will be payable, indicating medical treatment received within hospital premises without cost."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-caf4b3f0aa7e762095c32496aac13d2b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 537}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPENDIX 1 DAMAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appendix 1 Damage refers to specific injuries listed in Appendix 1 that determine compensation rates for permanent partial loss of work capacity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-68ef0e8f1f38a0c8885d599e4ee4a20e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 820}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERMANENT TOTAL DISABILITY COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Permanent Total Disability Compensation is the outcome or result when an injury leads to a complete and irreversible loss of work ability, determining the amount of compensation based on specific percentages as per Appendix 1."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-68ef0e8f1f38a0c8885d599e4ee4a20e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 820}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MULTIPLE APPENDICES DAMAGE COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Compensation for multiple injuries listed in Appendix 1 involves summing up individual compensation amounts related to each injury."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-68ef0e8f1f38a0c8885d599e4ee4a20e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERMANENT PARTIAL DISABILITY COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Permanent Partial Disability Compensation is the outcome or result when an injury leads to a partial and irreversible loss of work ability, determining the amount of compensation based on specific percentages as per Appendix 1 for injuries not listed in it."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-68ef0e8f1f38a0c8885d599e4ee4a20e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;永久地完全喪失工作能力的情況&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"永久地完全喪失工作能力的情況指的是因某种损失导致员工无法继续从事任何工作的状态。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;某百分率而定出的補償額&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"某百分率而定出的补偿额是根据某个与员工在当时有能力受雇担任的工作方面因该项损伤永久丧失赚取收入能力的情况相称的比例来确定的赔偿金额。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;部分身體受傷&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"部分身体受伤指的是身体的一部分未完全丧失功能，但因此导致了永久性的收入损失情况。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;百分率&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A rate or percentage used in calculating compensation for various injuries as per the legal text provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"Percentage rate in this context likely refers to a quantifiable measure related to injury severity, recovery rates, or other statistical data in the field of medicine or rehabilitation."&lt;SEP&gt;"百分率是一个与员工因该项损伤永久导致的丧失赚取收入能力情况相称的比例，用于计算赔偿金额。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe10bdcc6509915c50dbde896f285728&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3900ed248a8474ab2f01af53f32e5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;附表1就該部分身體的喪失所指明的有關百分率&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"附表1就该部分身体的丧失所指明的相关百分率是指在特定情况下，根据受伤部位确定的具体比例。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;附表1及附註所指明的百分率計算比例&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"附表1及附注所指明的百分率计算比例是指在特定情况下，根据附表和附注确定的具体赔偿比例。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;一項或多項損傷(不論是否附表1所指明者)引致永久地部分喪失工作能力&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"一项或多项损伤（不论是否在附表1中明确指出）导致了永久的部分丧失工作能力，指的是因某种损失而导致员工无法完全从事工作的状态。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;按第(1)款而就該項或多項損傷指明或評估的喪失賺取收入能力的百分率,因僱員的特別情況而會實&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"按照第（1）款对某项或多项目损伤所确定或评估的丧失赚取收入能力的比例，由于员工的具体情况可能会有所不同。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;損傷(不論是否附表1所指明者)引致永久地部分喪失工作能力&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"损伤（不论是否在附表1中明确指出）导致了永久的部分丧失工作能力，指的是因某种损失而导致员工无法完全从事工作的状态。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 78}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;特別情況&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"特别情况是指与特定员工的具体状况相关的因素，可能会影响赔偿金额的计算方式和结果。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;工作能力&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"工作能力是指员工在特定岗位上能够完成工作的程度，与收入获取直接相关。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 71}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 456}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1126}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;收入能力&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"收入能力指的是个人或企业在一定时期内通过劳动或其他方式获得经济收益的能力。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 78}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;損失賺取收入能力情況&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"损失赚取收入能力情况是指因某种损伤导致员工永久性丧失获取收入的能力的状态。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 78}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;附表1&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"附表1 refers to an appendix table related to the compensation percentages for different types of injuries in workers' compensation ordinances."&lt;SEP&gt;"附表1是用于列出和定义特定情况下需要赔偿的具体损伤类型及相关百分率的表格或文件。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d1ddc182c8f11077e959dbc0ab877a19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 76}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;附註&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"附注是用于补充解释和提供额外信息的说明文字，在这里涉及到百分率计算的具体比例和其他相关细节。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1973年第4號第2條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"1973年第4号第2条是指在特定法律或法规中对某一条款的规定，用于补充和修改之前的规则。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1964年第19號第7條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"1964年第19号第7条规定了关于赔偿金额计算的具体比例和其他相关细节。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1980年第44號第15條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"1980年第44号第15条是对之前规定进行修订和补充的条款，用于进一步明确或调整赔偿金额计算的具体比例和其他相关细节。"&lt;SEP&gt;"This refers to an amendment or revision made in 1980 that established initial requirements for medical examination and treatment after accidents involving employees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60357a5d0f946dc1e998d1bea10860b6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 590}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1978年第4號第3條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"1978年第4号第3条规定了在特定情况下百分率不能超过附表中规定的具体比例，用于限制和规范赔偿金额的计算方式。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1985年第49號第4條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"1985年第49号第4条是对之前规定进行修订或替代的新条款，用于进一步明确或调整特定情况下百分率的具体应用和计算方法。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;損失賺取收入能力情況,須按某百分率評估&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"损失赚取收入能力情况须按照某个百分率进行评估，以确定赔偿金额的大小。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;僱員的特別情況&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"雇员的特殊情况指的是与员工个人状况相关的因素，可能会影响其收入能力和工作能力的情况评估结果。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERMANENT PARTIAL INCAPACITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Permanent Partial Incapacity refers to a level of incapacity that is less than total but still permanent, used in calculating compensation percentages when special circumstances apply."&lt;SEP&gt;"Permanent partial incapacity refers to a condition where an individual experiences a permanent but not total loss of work ability, resulting from injury."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-062631c2ee8edb363f6cc234fa986a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d80227f925bf1b081dc41765e6e6934</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 716}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRST SCHEDULE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"First Schedule is a part of the document that outlines various injury scenarios and their corresponding compensation percentages for loss of earning capacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"First Schedule is a reference document that lists specific injuries and the corresponding percentages for compensation in cases of permanent total incapacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"First Schedule is mentioned as containing specified injuries and their corresponding percentages of loss of earning capacity for permanent total incapacity cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"The First Schedule is a document that specifies injuries and their corresponding percentages for calculating loss of earning capacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The First Schedule mentioned here contains provisions that deem an employee to be in continuous employment under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The First Schedule, also known as ss. 3 &amp; 75, deals with continuous employment conditions and their determination under certain circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e976980f19e9ab89febaf65027fa503e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-062631c2ee8edb363f6cc234fa986a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779a6ebdcf1cc3fbd67a4dc22862c59e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3639cabcc91a09d2612cb06c302addd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f16e9e25a3dbce715e72ac73a5f618f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d80227f925bf1b081dc41765e6e6934</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 717}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOSS OF EARNING CAPACITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loss of Earning Capacity measures the financial impact on an employee's ability to earn income after sustaining injuries."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loss of Earning Capacity refers to the reduction in income potential resulting from an injury, used as a basis for calculating compensation percentages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loss of Earning Capacity refers to the reduction in income potential resulting from an injury, which is assessed by assessment boards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loss of earning capacity assesses the long-term impact on an employee's ability to earn income after sustaining injuries in an accident."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loss of earning capacity is a social science concept that measures the reduction in income due to disability or injury."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loss of earning capacity is an attribute used in assessing the percentage of permanent incapacity due to injury."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loss of earning capacity refers to the percentage loss prescribed in a schedule for partial or total incapacity, used in compensation calculations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb828f2a7eae180f120101c1cd23e327&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-062631c2ee8edb363f6cc234fa986a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1b7183db745ed54dff547be6105981a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779a6ebdcf1cc3fbd67a4dc22862c59e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f30d14d75a76f9e89eb6fe137661d148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f5ab2145d9ab1c03798719541af19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d80227f925bf1b081dc41765e6e6934</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 715}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRST SCHEDULE (AMENDED 76 OF 1982 S. 6)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The amendment on 76 of 1982 s. 6 added specific provisions related to the calculation of compensation based on injuries and their impact on earning capacity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d80227f925bf1b081dc41765e6e6934</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 715}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S QUALIFICATIONS AND EXPERIENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The employee's qualifications, previous training, and experience are considered factors in assessing the loss of earning capacity for injuries not specified in the First Schedule."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d80227f925bf1b081dc41765e6e6934</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 715}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE EARNED AFTER THE ACCIDENT CAUSING THE INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to employees who suffer injuries due to accidents and whose post-accident earnings are potentially relevant for compensation calculations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb0545d506978169e320db3a0cda4273</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACTUAL EARNINGS OF THE EMPLOYEE EARNED AFTER THE ACCIDENT CAUSING THE INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These refer to specific financial outcomes or income generated by an employee following a workplace accident, which may be considered in certain legal contexts regarding compensation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb0545d506978169e320db3a0cda4273</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY TOTAL DISABILITY COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the compensation provided for temporary total loss of work capacity due to injury from accidents. The amount is calculated based on income differences before and after the incident."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb0545d506978169e320db3a0cda4273</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTERED DOCTOR, REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER, REGISTERED DENTIST, ORDINARY ASSESSMENT BOARD OR SPECIAL ASSESSMENT BOARD CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are entities that can provide certificates for absences deemed necessary due to injuries from accidents, which may be considered as periods of temporary total loss of work capacity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb0545d506978169e320db3a0cda4273</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PROFESSIONAL CERTIFICATES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Certificates issued by registered medical professionals confirming the necessity of absence due to injury from an accident are used in determining compensation for temporary total disability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb0545d506978169e320db3a0cda4273</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT INCOME CALCULATION METHODOLOGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a method for calculating employment income, specifically focusing on monthly earnings before and after an accident causing injury. It is crucial for determining the amount of compensation under certain legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb0545d506978169e320db3a0cda4273</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY PARTIAL DISABILITY COMPENSATION MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This mechanism deals with situations where employees suffer partial loss of work capacity temporarily due to accidents, providing a framework for calculating appropriate compensation based on income differences."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb0545d506978169e320db3a0cda4273</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT OR APPRENTICESHIP AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are legal documents that define the terms and conditions under which an employee is employed. They are relevant in determining the base salary against which post-accident earnings are compared for compensation purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb0545d506978169e320db3a0cda4273</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPENSATION PAYMENT DATE CALCULATION MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This mechanism outlines how the dates of payment for compensation should align with the dates on which employees would have been paid had they continued working under their original employment or apprenticeship agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb0545d506978169e320db3a0cda4273</data>
</node>
