</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY INCAPACITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Temporary Incapacity is a period during which an employee cannot work due to illness or injury, for which compensation may be payable under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary Incapacity refers to a period of reduced ability to work due to illness or injury that is expected to last less than permanently but longer than just a short term."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary incapacity for which compensation is payable under section 10 of the Employees' Compensation Ordinance (Cap. 282) pertains to situations where an employee cannot work due to a temporary health condition, and are entitled to receive compensation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary incapacity is a condition where the employee cannot perform their usual duties due to illness or other temporary reasons, for which compensation may be payable under section 10 of the Employees' Compensation Ordinance (Cap. 282)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary incapacity refers to a situation where an employee is unable to work due to injury from an accident for a limited period of time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary incapacity refers to the period during which an employee cannot work after suffering from an accident, and it can extend beyond 24 months under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-70e316f848fd5f9f0f6efb5f28f0e45b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d14b62c50b2a0a92ac73c8ef0642fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1b7183db745ed54dff547be6105981a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f99b49d1daa84b1f278cb269b06646d1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 100}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 523}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 7 OR 9&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sections 7 and 9 are provisions that apply when permanent incapacity occurs, determining the lump sum payable in such cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sections 7 or 9 of the Ordinance are applicable when an accident results in permanent incapacity, determining specific actions to be taken regarding periodical payments and employment status."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-70e316f848fd5f9f0f6efb5f28f0e45b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1ed02e78cf2ee9e321f22dbe3ba84b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 311}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SMALL CLAIMS TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Small Claims Tribunal is a specific court established under the Small Claims Tribunal Ordinance (Cap. 338) for resolving civil debts below a certain jurisdictional limit."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Small Claims Tribunal is an institution established under the Small Claims Tribunal Ordinance (Cap. 338) where disputes can be resolved regarding small civil debts, including those related to medical expenses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f5fe723dc66b1a35b256f0fbcfd9642&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af55493786feba6de502e98ed832cde8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 142}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 625}]</data>
</node>
