  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Occupational Therapist helps individuals with injuries or disabilities to improve their ability to perform daily activities through various therapeutic techniques."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af55493786feba6de502e98ed832cde8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 111}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 564}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1136}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISTRICT COURT ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to an unspecified ordinance related to the District Court's jurisdiction and procedures, which may be relevant when dealing with larger compensation claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af55493786feba6de502e98ed832cde8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER (OUTSIDE HONG KONG)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Registered Medical Practitioner operating outside of Hong Kong is a medical professional who can supervise or provide treatment under certain conditions related to work-related injuries abroad."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af55493786feba6de502e98ed832cde8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 595}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER'S LIABILITY FOR WORK-RELATED INJURIES ABROAD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to the legal responsibility an employer may have in paying for medical expenses incurred by employees due to work-related injuries outside of Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af55493786feba6de502e98ed832cde8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 595}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1995&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT, LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Employees' Compensation (Amendment) Ordinance 1995 is a legal document that provides amendments to the existing employees compensation laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employees' Compensation (Amendment) Ordinance 1995 is a piece of legislation that contains transitional provisions affecting the operation of other ordinances."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is a specific piece of legislation mentioned that outlines conditions under which employers are or are not liable to pay medical expenses for employees injured outside Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b6ccfc41c467ba461a212761d1ed82e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d8e006856fc24f02eba931eaf4c63a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c507c410ec255631812c63bb0a5d8bf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 557}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCIDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Accident in this context likely refers to any incident that results in injury and necessitates attendance at assessments by employees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Accident is an event that occurs in the course of employment and can lead to inquiries or prosecutions under this ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Accidents are events that occur at workplaces, leading to employee incapacity or injuries, which must be reported according to specific timelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Accident is an unexpected event that causes personal injury during employment outside Hong Kong as described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Accident is the event that leads to permanent incapacity or temporary changes in an employee's work capacity, which can result in modifications of periodical payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"An accident includes incidents that occur due to a single identifiable event or a series of events. In cases involving occupational diseases, it can be considered as multiple separate accidents if more than one employee's work incapacity or death is not attributable to the same sudden and recognizable incident."&lt;SEP&gt;"An accident is an event that results in either the death of an employee or their total or partial incapacity, triggering notification requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"An accident is defined as any event that causes a detrimental impact on health, including situations where the victim cannot work for at least 3 days."&lt;SEP&gt;"An event related to an incident occurring during work hours or as a result of workplace conditions leading to potential legal actions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f45f6c1c93d50d9cf7dd1bef9a6ec44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdcb847cbe822aecbab442ce9430887f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea6d20dfaa02a409f86af6c45c243e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d8e006856fc24f02eba931eaf4c63a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e37def8625e820a47ed5130364eb70d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5742863cc938d9f9470985855601b925&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab861803e98b52f9a42ed6d058e8b49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80bd6fbaafa695488034148c221f9cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e87bb6b8feb2f7d365e7f2290bc5e29c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 557}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYERS'">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employers' refers to organizations or entities responsible for paying medical expenses under certain conditions as described in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c507c410ec255631812c63bb0a5d8bf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEES'">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employees' are individuals who may receive medical treatment outside Hong Kong and whose employment is related to their injuries, according to the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c507c410ec255631812c63bb0a5d8bf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDICAL EXPENSES'">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Medical Expenses refer to costs associated with providing medical treatment for employees injured outside of Hong Kong, as described in the legal context provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c507c410ec255631812c63bb0a5d8bf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMISSIONER'">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Commissioner refers to an official who issues certificates stating the amount of such medical expenses, as described in section 10B(1)(b) of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c507c410ec255631812c63bb0a5d8bf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTERED DOCTORS AND DENTISTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to medical professionals registered under the Pharmacy and Poisons Ordinance (Cap. 138), who can prescribe drugs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6781f980c6134c143f1e75549acfb5a6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LICENSED RETAILER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to individuals or entities holding a retailer license issued under the Chinese Medicine Ordinance (Cap. 549) section 114, authorized to sell traditional Chinese medicines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6781f980c6134c143f1e75549acfb5a6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to medical professionals registered under the Chinese Medicine Ordinal (Cap. 549), including those who can prescribe traditional Chinese medicine products or materials."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6781f980c6134c143f1e75549acfb5a6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRESCRIPTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A document issued by a registered doctor or dentist that includes specific details such as patient name, medicine names/doses, and date of issue."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a9f135881cefdec226e999451dec41e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 111}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 565}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTERED DOCTOR/DENTIST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Person holding a license to practice medicine or dentistry under the Chinese Medicine Ordinance (Cap. 549), who can provide prescriptions for drugs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a9f135881cefdec226e999451dec41e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 111}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 565}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;中醫&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"中醫是指注册中医师，负责开具处方并提供医疗服务。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e7838850b120bb3976756876786fd0f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;處方藥物&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"處方藥物指的是根据医生处方销售的药物，包括商品名或药名及剂量等信息。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e7838850b120bb3976756876786fd0f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;中成藥 (PROPRIETARY CHINESE MEDICINE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"中成藥是指具有《中醫藥條例》(第549章)第2條給予該詞的涵義的產品，通常指已經註冊或被視為已註冊的中成藥。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e7838850b120bb3976756876786fd0f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;中藥材 (CHINESE HERBAL MEDICINE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"中藥材是指《中醫藥條例》(第549章)附表1或2指明的中草药，或者华人惯常作药用的其他源于植物、动物或矿物的物料。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e7838850b120bb3976756876786fd0f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;收據 (RECEIPT)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"收據指的是銷售處方藥物時出具的憑證，顯示銷售日期及所售藥品名稱、份量和價格等信息。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e7838850b120bb3976756876786fd0f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;病人&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"病人是指获得处方药物的人，在文本中多次提及需要显示病人的姓名。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e7838850b120bb3976756876786fd0f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;註冊中醫 (REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"注册中医是具有合法执业资格的医生，负责开具中药处方并提供医疗服务。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e7838850b120bb3976756876786fd0f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;銷售處方藥物的人 (PRESCRIPTION DRUG SELLER)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"销售处方药物的人是指在文本中提到需要显示其姓名或名称及地址的人员，通常指药房工作人员或其他药品销售人员。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e7838850b120bb3976756876786fd0f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;《中醫藥條例》(第549章) (CHINESE MEDICINE ORDINANCE, CHAPTER 549)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"《中醫藥條例》是香港地区关于中医药管理的法规，规定了中药、中医处方等相关内容。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e7838850b120bb3976756876786fd0f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2006年第16號第15條 (AMENDMENT OF THE CHINESE MEDICINE ORDINANCE, NO. 16 OF 2006, SECTION 15)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
