</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S ACCIDENT DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee's accident date marks the event when an employee suffers an incident that affects their earnings calculation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c59e0c04b442ca3e395d9315796d6817</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 312}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREVIOUS 12 MONTHS OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The previous 12 months of employment is a period used to calculate monthly earnings, reflecting economic and social science principles related to remuneration over time."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c59e0c04b442ca3e395d9315796d6817</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 312}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY INCAPACITY BEYOND THE 12-MONTH PERIOD AFTER THE DATE OF ACCIDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Temporary incapacity extending beyond 12 months from the accident date is an event that triggers a different method for calculating monthly earnings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c59e0c04b442ca3e395d9315796d6817</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 312}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSUMER PRICE INDEX&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Consumer Price Index (CPI) is used as a measure to adjust earnings in certain circumstances, reflecting economic and social science principles related to inflation and cost of living adjustments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c59e0c04b442ca3e395d9315796d6817</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;24 MONTHS OR SUCH FURTHER PERIOD ALLOWED BY THE COURT UNDER SECTION 10(5)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to temporary incapacity extending beyond 24 months from the accident date, potentially adjusted by a court order as per Section 10(5), impacting earnings calculation methods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c59e0c04b442ca3e395d9315796d6817</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AVERAGE RATE OF INCREASE IN RESPECT OF THE EARNINGS OF OTHER PERSONS OF SIMILAR EARNING CAPACITY EMPLOYED BY THE EMPLOYER IN SIMILAR EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This phrase describes a method for calculating future earnings based on historical increases in wages for similarly situated employees within the same organization and job category."&lt;SEP&gt;"This refers to an economic and social science concept used for calculating average wage growth, which is applied when determining employee earnings post-accident."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c59e0c04b442ca3e395d9315796d6817&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f99b49d1daa84b1f278cb269b06646d1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RATE OF INCREASE IN THE CONSUMER PRICE INDEX AT THE END OF A 12-MONTH PERIOD AFTER THE DATE OF ACCIDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to an economic and social science concept used for adjusting wages based on inflation, as measured by changes in the Consumer Price Index over time."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c59e0c04b442ca3e395d9315796d6817</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT ORDER UNDER SECTION 10(5)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A court order allowing a further period beyond 24 months post-accident is an event that can extend the timeframe for calculating earnings based on specific legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c59e0c04b442ca3e395d9315796d6817</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 312}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSUMER PRICE INDEX REPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Consumer Price Index Report is a document published by the Commissioner for Census and Statistics that compiles and publishes the consumer price index as CPI(A)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f99b49d1daa84b1f278cb269b06646d1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMISSIONER FOR CENSUS AND STATISTICS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Commissioner for Census and Statistics is an organization responsible for compiling and publishing the consumer price index in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f99b49d1daa84b1f278cb269b06646d1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSUMER PRICE INDEX (消費物價指數)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Consumer Price Index refers to a measure of average changes over time in the prices paid by consumers for a market basket of consumption goods and services, used here as a basis for adjusting earnings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f99b49d1daa84b1f278cb269b06646d1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 10(5)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 10(5) is part of a legal section that may allow further periods beyond 24 months for temporary incapacity due to an accident."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f99b49d1daa84b1f278cb269b06646d1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 6, 7, 9 OR 10&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sections 6, 7, 9, or 10 are legal sections that may be used to compute the earnings of an employee during temporary incapacity beyond a specific period after an accident."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f99b49d1daa84b1f278cb269b06646d1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SIMILAR EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Similar employment refers to jobs with comparable nature and conditions where other employees have similar earning capacities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f99b49d1daa84b1f278cb269b06646d1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONTHLY EARNINGS OF AN EMPLOYEE AT THE TIME OF THE ACCIDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Monthly earnings refer to the regular income received by an employee before suffering from temporary incapacity due to an accident."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f99b49d1daa84b1f278cb269b06646d1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;24-MONTH PERIOD AFTER THE DATE OF THE ACCIDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A 24-month period is a specific timeframe used in legal calculations for determining future earnings based on past wage growth or inflation adjustments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f99b49d1daa84b1f278cb269b06646d1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AVERAGE MONTHLY AMOUNT WHICH, DURING THE 12 MONTHS PREVIOUS TO THE ACCIDENT, WAS BEING EARNED BY A PERSON OF SIMILAR EARNING CAPACITY IN THE SAME GRADE EMPLOYED AT THE SAME WORK BY THE SAME EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This phrase describes another method for calculating earnings based on historical wage data from similarly situated employees within the same organization and job category."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f99b49d1daa84b1f278cb269b06646d1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAME CLASS OF EMPLOYMENT AND IN THE SAME DISTRICT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Same class of employment and in the same district refer to jobs with similar nature, conditions, and geographical location where other employees have comparable earning capacities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f99b49d1daa84b1f278cb269b06646d1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SIXTH SCHEDULE, SECTION 11(5)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Sixth Schedule is a reference to an unspecified document containing specific monetary values used for calculations in the context of compensation assessments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db28cd6b23bdc6eed33984863e98ca47</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 303}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 992}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot; (OR &quot;ACT&quot;)">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to a legal framework or set of rules governing compensation assessment, though not named explicitly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db28cd6b23bdc6eed33984863e98ca47</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 11(5)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 11(5) is a reference within an ordinance specifying an amount per month for the purposes of earnings calculation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ba63e9eb3fbb2c29ada4788ed0dbf715</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 287}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FULL TIME EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Full time employment refers to a type of job that involves working for at least 40 hours during a minimum period of 5 days in any one week, as defined by the legal provision."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-435a72f0a09b4a0be544ae91d6f3f83f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 371}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1072}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 40&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 40 is a legal provision that outlines conditions under which adjudication proceedings can be terminated and new ones initiated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 40 is a regulation that imposes an obligation on employers to insure for amounts exceeding the coverage limits specified in their policies, even if such excess insurance is not required by the policy itself."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 40 is part of a set of regulations requiring an employer to provide sufficient information about concurrent contracts of service for an employee's earnings calculation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-435a72f0a09b4a0be544ae91d6f3f83f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10132a194a7ccd2dae34efb474098db1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19b1bce23dbf161109b02b0e7ddc678</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 371}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1072}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (7A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (7A) requires employees to provide written information upon the request of their employers regarding concurrent contracts of service, enabling compliance with section 40."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-435a72f0a09b4a0be544ae91d6f3f83f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 371}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1072}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (7B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (7B) specifies that subsection (7) does not apply if an employee fails to comply with subsection (7A)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-435a72f0a09b4a0be544ae91d6f3f83f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (8)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (8) describes an event where providing misleading or false statements in notifications to The Authority can result in committing another offense and facing a fine at level 5."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (8) mandates employers to furnish a written list of earnings within 14 days after receiving a request from the employee or Commissioner for calculating monthly earnings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-435a72f0a09b4a0be544ae91d6f3f83f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 371}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1072}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (9)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (9) imposes an obligation on employers who contravene subsection (8), making them liable to a fine at level 3 if they do so without reasonable excuse."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsection (9) refers to the main requirement or duty of an employer, which, if not complied with, leads to additional charges as per Section 13(3)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-435a72f0a09b4a0be544ae91d6f3f83f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffbe5c02e6f3e1420b13f54196f78358</data>
