<node id="&quot;44 OF 1980 S. 15&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Amendments made in 1980, Section 15, further clarified conditions under which an employee's refusal to undergo a medical examination would not affect their right to compensation for occupational diseases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Another reference to the same amendment that sets out conditions for when a Court can review and make decisions regarding periodical payments after an accident, based on changes in employee work capacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"This amendment from 1980 under section 15 is noted as having been amended over time but remains a significant reference point in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is a reference to another amendment in 1980 that provides additional context and conditions for the termination or reduction of periodical payments based on employee work capacity."</data>
