<node id="&quot;SECTION 10&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 10 is referenced but not detailed in the provided text, implying it may contain additional termination clauses or provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 10 likely pertains to provisions regarding compensation that may be affected by agreement cancellations or other actions taken by the Commissioner."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 10 outlines lump sum payments that can be invested, applied, or otherwise dealt with for the benefit of the recipient as determined by the Court."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 10 refers to a legal provision related to periodical payments by the employer in respect of injuries."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 10 refers to a specific condition or event that defines an exception where control does not apply."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 10 refers to a specific part of the Ordinance that deals with the payment of compensation, which is relevant in determining when an employer can terminate contracts or give notice regarding temporary incapacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 10 refers to an event where compensation is payable under the Employees' Compensation Ordinance (Cap. 282) for a day of absence from work due to temporary incapacity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7788fe09e12252d0bb714e4f775b4322&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bdac67e9c03ff3905f24c9ae12c304&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5b551a4a483944d6cf3179909e4812f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d88cda6d2e850ba77bbd055819688849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb8be73ac22c1010a0cf86f8afb0c798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-691e0bbfff602acd26ed9f7e9579a105</data>
