</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 16A(10)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 16A(10)(b) outlines an additional surcharge applicable after three months from the expiry of the payment period, as per Section 13(3)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ffbe5c02e6f3e1420b13f54196f78358</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 377}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OFFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An offence committed by employers who fail to comply with Subsection (1) as described in Subsections (3) and (4)."&lt;SEP&gt;"An offence is defined as any violation of the regulations regarding noise emission compliance by importing, manufacturing, supplying, or failing to equip a product with prescribed markings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Offence is a term used in legal contexts, referring to actions that violate laws and may result in penalties such as fines or imprisonment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Offence refers to a criminal act as defined in the text, such as resisting, obstructing, delaying public officers, and providing false information during identity checks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Offence refers to a violation of the law or regulation that may be subject to strict liability as per the amendment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Offence refers to an employer's failure without reasonable excuse to comply with sections 9, 10 or 12, which is punishable by a fine at level 6 according to subsection (12)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Offence refers to criminal actions committed by an employer who fails to comply with legal obligations regarding written statements or includes false information in such documents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Offences are violations of regulations concerning the operation of employment agencies as described in Part XIII of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e43310bb8a059a1a014c1ba9a611877f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-950a35becf4c52961439921c1e246ea5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb1255c2f5701b5ef025263ed94bd7e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ead5337f34ae6c6d3adbc5b06e2bc74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-990bd24369be2bc2f9bdd440773f2e19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffbe5c02e6f3e1420b13f54196f78358&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8903577fbeb26a0f144927da3a1efb7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-312b267feca3c2a25982c678db5c0527</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 405}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1101}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINE AT LEVEL 6&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Fine at Level 6 is a monetary penalty defined by legal standards, with specifics not provided in this text but typically associated with more serious offenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Fine at Level 6 refers to a monetary penalty that can be imposed on individuals or organizations who fail to comply with occupational safety regulations and requirements outlined by the Occupational Safety Officer, where 'level 6' is likely denoting a specific amount based on local legal standards."&lt;SEP&gt;"A fine at a specific regulatory level, indicating a monetary penalty for initial conviction related to product usage and emissions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A fine at level 6 indicates the severity of penalties imposed on employers who violate labor laws related to trade unions and employee rights under the Trade Unions Ordinance (Cap. 332&lt;SEP&gt;"A fine at level 6 is a monetary penalty associated with certain offenses under the legal provisions mentioned."&lt;SEP&gt;"A fine at level 6 is another type of penalty, more severe than the fine at level 5, which can be applied to repeat offenders who contravene conditions or limitations."&lt;SEP&gt;"A fine of a specific level, indicating a monetary penalty for first-time offenders as per amendment E.R. 2 of 2021."&lt;SEP&gt;"A fine of a specific level, indicating a monetary penalty for first-time offenders."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fine at Level 6 is a monetary penalty determined by the legal framework, typically corresponding to a fixed amount or multiple thereof based on the severity and nature of the offense."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fine at level 6 is the penalty imposed on employers who commit an offence as defined in section 13(12), indicating a specific monetary amount for such violations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to a legal consequence or penalty that may be imposed on an employer who contravenes certain provisions, not an actual event but a potential outcome of non-compliance."&lt;SEP&gt;"This refers to a specific fine amount, which is defined by legal standards but not detailed here."&lt;SEP&gt;"罚款级别6表示首次被判犯有此罪行时的处罚标准。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58cf55b6baed9ac9a3c4052538486aa3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad689dd49be1734c5e08c5a4e747265&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed8223cf90d5d4646feb10ec51169ca9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59eee484f73e813248a005b2d6fef14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7a153c57e6b577c1b46cd329273673a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cbc913a82bac150b6a4b08953fa04d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c62e4d3b32ca7459c870b08308d480ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-767fcab98a545fabc81b28e3a6ad1ac3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37eade578e866e449433b5cf2ef5311c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffbe5c02e6f3e1420b13f54196f78358&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb269a993727b98b029449c2f2612dff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 398}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1090}]</data>
</node>
