<node id="&quot;1992年第64號第4條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL PROVISION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This specific section (1992 Year 64, Section 4) is mentioned as an amendment to existing laws or regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-691e0bbfff602acd26ed9f7e9579a105</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER'S COMPENSATION(GENERAL ASSESSMENT) COMMITTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Employer's Compensation(General Assessment) Committee is a body established by the Secretary for administrative purposes related to employee compensation assessments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-691e0bbfff602acd26ed9f7e9579a105</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 289}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 963}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION (ORDINARY ASSESSMENT) COMMITTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Employees' Compensation (Ordinary Assessment) Committee is a committee established to assess claims related to employee injuries, determining the percentage of permanent loss of earning capacity and the period of absence required."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-259358639f98ae3f9ccaff8ed680037d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECRETARY FOR LABOUR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Secretary for Labour refers to an official who oversees labor-related matters and appoints members to the Employees' Compensation (Ordinary Assessment) Committee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-259358639f98ae3f9ccaff8ed680037d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTERED DOCTORS, REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONERS, OR REGISTERED DENTISTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These roles refer to medical professionals required as members of the Employees' Compensation (Ordinary Assessment) Committee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-259358639f98ae3f9ccaff8ed680037d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SENIOR LABOUR OFFICER OR LABOUR OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This role refers to a government official who can be appointed as a member of the Employees' Compensation (Ordinary Assessment) Committee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-259358639f98ae3f9ccaff8ed680037d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION (ORDINARY ASSESSMENT) BOARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employees' Compensation (Ordinary Assessment) Boards are organizations appointed by the Commissioner to assess claims for compensation related to employee injuries."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb828f2a7eae180f120101c1cd23e327</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 140}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 620}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 9(1A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 9(1A) is a specific clause that may trigger referral to a Special Assessment Board if applicable."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 9(1A) is another legislative reference mentioned in relation to claims for compensation and its application in assessment reviews."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da37f195f3ad2a893b50923a13911e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb828f2a7eae180f120101c1cd23e327</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LABOUR OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Labour Officer is involved in the assessment and handling of claims related to employee compensation, often part of labor-related roles."&lt;SEP&gt;"An officer from the labour department that can be a member of an Ordinary Assessment Board and also participate in a Special Assessment Board as per section 16D(2)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Labour Officers are members of the Ordinary Assessment Boards, either Senior or regular, and contribute to assessing claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-419f5ab2145d9ab1c03798719541af19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0512d455417ff415dc742891f2498109&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb828f2a7eae180f120101c1cd23e327</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 140}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 620}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDICAL PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A medical practitioner examines employees, suspects or reports findings/suspicions of occupational diseases to the Commissioner."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical practitioners provide medical services and can notify certain information under the conditions specified by section 15 of another ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Registered Medical Practitioners are members of the Ordinary Assessment Boards who assess injuries related to medical conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05288c51fb6c9855d3f031e51b7e2be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da2837c3b5e351b2e1c63635e1c0a663&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb828f2a7eae180f120101c1cd23e327</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 614}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Registered Chinese Medicine Practitioners are members of the Ordinary Assessment Boards who assess injuries related to traditional Chinese medicine conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb828f2a7eae180f120101c1cd23e327</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 178}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 715}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1982年第76號第14條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a specific amendment or addition made in 1982 that added provisions for these boards."&lt;SEP&gt;"This refers to another amendment made in 1982, which is part of the legal context governing certificates. It does not represent an organization or person but indicates changes in regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-514e0a6ffa9d391d835f484bdbaa5724&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb828f2a7eae180f120101c1cd23e327</data>
