<node id="&quot;REGIONAL COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Regional Court refers to a specific type of court mentioned for determining compensation claims and associated matters."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Regional Court is mentioned as having the authority to investigate, determine issues, and exercise all powers of a court in its civil proceedings under the Regional Courts Ordinance (Cap. 336)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Regional Court is mentioned as having the authority to make orders with certain powers and effects according to this regulation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Regional Court is where decisions are made by judges regarding employers and guarantors, including orders for imprisonment or release based on compliance with court commands."&lt;SEP&gt;"The regional court is mentioned as a place where appeals can be lodged against certain decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d68cfffcc2e250c3bcedc1cbea93ab48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51aca9ef532467f1fd709d3d772f4ca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe2fc373a4f6caf645c752f135c7582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baa998ea27b6baa036c2807f3cddf020&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd413c3e0e2d3c065b140491b75c8888</data>
