<node id="&quot;PERIODICAL PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT, TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Periodical Payment is a type of financial arrangement made for employees due to accidents, which may be reviewed or modified by the Court based on their work capacity. It involves regular payments over time."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea6d20dfaa02a409f86af6c45c243e0a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 585}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;16 OF 2006 S. 18&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES, MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a specific section and amendment date (2006) that modifies the provisions related to periodical payments and their review process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea6d20dfaa02a409f86af6c45c243e0a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;55 OF 1969 S. 16&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS, SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A reference to an earlier amendment in 1969 that provides context for changes made later (2006) regarding periodical payments and their review process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea6d20dfaa02a409f86af6c45c243e0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;76 OF 1982 S. 17&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES, MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is another reference to an amendment in 1982 that further modifies the provisions related to periodical payments and their review process."&lt;SEP&gt;"This section provides additional context to the review process for periodical payments and how it is influenced by changes in an employee's work capacity after an accident."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea6d20dfaa02a409f86af6c45c243e0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;36 OF 1996 S. 17&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS, SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A later amendment in 1996 that continues to modify the provisions for periodical payments based on employee work capacity after an accident."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea6d20dfaa02a409f86af6c45c243e0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;10(5), 16(4) &amp; 19(3)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES, MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are specific sections within a larger ordinance that provide exceptions to the general rules regarding the termination or reduction of periodical payments. They indicate conditions under which certain actions can be taken without court intervention."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea6d20dfaa02a409f86af6c45c243e0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;11 OF 1995 S. 7, 9&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES, MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These sections provide specific conditions for the application of different provisions when an accident results in permanent incapacity, affecting how periodical payments are handled based on the severity and nature of the incapacity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea6d20dfaa02a409f86af6c45c243e0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;17 OF 1969 S. 17&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES, MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This section provides conditions for when a Court can review and make decisions regarding periodical payments after an accident, based on changes in employee work capacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"This section provides conditions for when and how Court reviews regarding periodical payments after an accident are conducted based on changes in employee work capacity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea6d20dfaa02a409f86af6c45c243e0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECOVERY OF INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The recovery of income by an employee is considered as part of the criteria to determine whether their periodical payment can be reduced or terminated. It involves assessing if and how much the employee's earnings have increased after an accident."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea6d20dfaa02a409f86af6c45c243e0a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 432}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEATH OF EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Death of employee refers to the event where an employee passes away, triggering certain benefits or payments from employers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The death of an employee is a significant event that can lead to the termination of periodical payments as per specific sections within the ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The death of an employee is also covered under section 31M, with its effects detailed in Part II of the Third Schedule."&lt;SEP&gt;"The event refers to an employee's death which affects their employment contract and related rights."&lt;SEP&gt;"The event refers to an employee's death, which triggers specific provisions under employment protection laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e5131fef8ae89d5a0f48b17c1599d19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2f5d9b3d656df85c08982a8986732f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ed372c34a6ff55010cb2f16481f447c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea6d20dfaa02a409f86af6c45c243e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33baa15beb160832b6e2302162f04d3</data>
