</node>
<node id="&quot;TOTAL承判商&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Total Contractor refers to a principal contractor in the context of subcontracting arrangements, responsible for overall project management and payment obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Total承判商 is mentioned in the text but not fully translated, likely referring to the main contractor or principal contractor responsible for the overall project."&lt;SEP&gt;"Total承判商 refers to a principal contractor who enters into contracts with sub-contractors within their industry or business operations, but the exact translation and role are unclear from the provided text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Total承判商 refers to the primary contracting entity mentioned in sections 43C, 43G, and 43K."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a544f1422493c38b567ef610eadf02d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f62200ffc7f6236194042490c461241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af77be8b003511c35b7551f4285bb427&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b14e71147144e9b2f455f7918c813637</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 86}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB承判商&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub承判商 is mentioned as entities that enter into agreements with total承判商 for specific projects or purposes in a construction context. The term 'sub-contractor' implies an organizational structure within business operations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f62200ffc7f6236194042490c461241</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 86}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TOTAL CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Total Contractor is an entity involved in construction work and has contractual obligations with subcontractors regarding wage payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Total Contractor refers to a principal contractor who enters into an agreement with a subcontractor for the execution of work, either wholly or in part, and is responsible for paying compensation as per legal requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Total Contractor refers to the main contractor who is responsible for providing compensation when necessary, and can be pursued directly by employees in certain circumstances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Total Contractor refers to the primary contractor who is responsible for employment conditions and must ensure compulsory insurance coverage as per regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Total contractor is the main construction company responsible for carrying out building works and ensuring legal liabilities are covered by insurance policies as per regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f7e01a5307e145a0563e90666073bf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ad747843ea1e53c58713c22b928c5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdcb847cbe822aecbab442ce9430887f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dea5aae61ffe2f36c7ee939e119437c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6157228e3518a3c9dd66f98867aa8a6e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 251}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 922}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL LIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal Liability refers to the responsibility of a total contractor towards its employees and those hired by subcontractors, ensuring they receive appropriate compensation as per legal standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2ad747843ea1e53c58713c22b928c5ed</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 251}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 922}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTIFICATION REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Notification Requirement is a process where employees must send written notifications to the total contractor before making claims, containing details such as personal information, employment location, and injury specifics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Notification requirement is an event where employers are mandated to inform their employees about any changes or elections regarding the calculation method for annual leave, ensuring transparency and compliance with labor laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5dea5aae61ffe2f36c7ee939e119437c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 599}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE款額&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The款額 refers to a compensation amount that cannot exceed the damage compensation that would be awarded if not for this regulation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4a5734a3528df7505e20e5f0156116bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;法律程序&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"法律程序 refers to legal procedures for seeking damage compensation by employees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4a5734a3528df7505e20e5f0156116bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;彌償款項&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"彌償款項 means compensation payments that may be required under certain circumstances, such as after an accident notification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4a5734a3528df7505e20e5f0156116bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal Procedure refers to the process of enforcing compliance with improvement notices through legal means if employers or occupiers fail to comply within the specified period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal procedure is an event involving legal actions and processes, such as filing a lawsuit or arbitrating disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal procedure is the process described where documents are presented before a court, leading to their acceptance as evidence without further proof under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal procedures are mentioned as part of the process for handling compensation claims, indicating formal methods and documentation involved."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal procedures are systematic processes used within the legal system to initiate, conduct, and conclude cases related to offenses against this Ordinance; they involve formal steps such as filing complaints or laying information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal procedures refer to formal processes and actions conducted in court, including but not limited to trials, hearings, and appeals, governed by specific regulations under this Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal procedures refer to formal processes conducted by courts or other legal authorities where evidence is presented and testimonies are given in relation to the enforcement of specific legislation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal procedures refer to formal processes conducted in accordance with the law, particularly those involving insurance policies issued for employers' liability towards their employees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-01f73d3a0eb5a63d428e456a11dad9c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5264a8fa197e6ad59c59c71f8b3763e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddee27cc5f92142cd2814225d68af96b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9b169ef4b1de04369879d234076f1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bf4100b4fcbad386ad1781e51770f26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f10185e6fc563260f4e1f20ab8c394fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-211e080c19540ebafb0dc80d25b20e46</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 826}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STATUTE OF LIMITATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Statute of limitations refers to the time frame within which legal proceedings can be initiated, impacting the validity of certain actions or claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5264a8fa197e6ad59c59c71f8b3763e7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 824}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT OF FIRST INSTANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Court of First Instance has the authority to grant interim measures in arbitration proceedings taking place or about to take place in Hong Kong or elsewhere, subject to certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Court of First Instance is mentioned as a location for civil proceedings, providing context for witness immunities and privileges."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Court of First Instance is mentioned as having the power to inquire into alleged contempt and punish individuals accordingly."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Court of First Instance is one of the courts where an employee can take proceedings against the third party to recover damages."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Court of First Instance refers to the primary court in Hong Kong where civil cases are heard, providing witnesses with certain privileges and immunities as mentioned."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Court of First Instance refers to the primary court where legal cases are initially heard and decided upon."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d2fe562ab74fde36758e6db7f158f71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d187f5859fc0e151b7a45dda2b23c53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ed6bb61c777b6fe07e21fb258ca9224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fd04bf2888da55881f593f9613b44e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e72191ab4edd091f82585ac0b7be851</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 291}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 978}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 16A CERTIFICATE DETERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 16A certificate determination is an event where the amount of damages or compensation is determined by a certificate, which affects the calculation of compensation under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f8e345be219d3fc366dc62469796daf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 16CA SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 16CA settlement agreement refers to an event where claims for compensation are settled through mutual agreement between parties involved in proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f8e345be219d3fc366dc62469796daf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF COMPENSATION ASSESSMENT FOR FATAL CASE OR REVIEW CERTIFICATE OF COMPENSATION ASSESSMENT FOR FATAL CASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These certificates are documents that provide a formal assessment and determination regarding the amount of compensation due, particularly in fatal cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"These certificates are used in fatal cases to assess and determine compensation amounts, either initially or upon review."</data>
