<node id="&quot;CIVIL LIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Civil Liability refers to potential legal consequences for acts or omissions under good faith performance of functions as outlined in the Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Civil Liability refers to the legal responsibility of an employer for any injury caused by their negligence or wrongful acts towards employees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Civil liability refers to the potential for a person to face legal consequences under civil law, which is not incurred solely due to contravening workplace codes of practice but can be influenced by court decisions regarding their relevance in specific cases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3aa4260f473f5ab1bb0de261f78fc6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1901c04f5d127d84848a2cd1cbc4a1bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
