</node>
<node id="&quot;DAMAGES AWARDED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Damages Awarded are civil penalties determined in actions at common law or under other enactments, which may be reduced based on compensation paid according to the Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3aa4260f473f5ab1bb0de261f78fc6e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER'S LIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employer's Liability is the legal obligation of an employer for injuries caused by their negligence or wrongful acts towards employees, independent of this Ordinance but subject to reduction from awarded damages."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employer is responsible for paying the cost of supplying and fitting a prosthesis or surgical appliance to an injured employee, as outlined in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The event refers to a legal responsibility that employers may have towards employees who are injured at work and require prosthetic or surgical appliances."&lt;SEP&gt;"This concept refers to financial obligations imposed on employers, which can be covered by insurance policies and subject to legal proceedings as mentioned in section 36LA or 44."&lt;SEP&gt;"This refers to legal responsibilities of an employer towards their employees, particularly concerning injuries sustained at work, which are covered by insurance policies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3aa4260f473f5ab1bb0de261f78fc6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-194bd276c174598edc7fcf0c6886ead7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10132a194a7ccd2dae34efb474098db1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6157228e3518a3c9dd66f98867aa8a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c526fd9477b77161e84c476f0017da6e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 371}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1069}]</data>
</node>
