<node id="&quot;HONG KONG SHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Hong Kong ship refers to any vessel registered or licensed in Hong Kong, as defined by relevant laws such as the Merchant Shipping (Seamen) Ordinance (Cap. 478) or the Navigation and Harbours Ordinance (Cap. 313)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hong Kong ship is a specific type of vessel operating under the jurisdiction of Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hong Kong ship refers to any ship or vessel registered or licensed in Hong Kong, which is a legal term defining the scope of application for certain regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-21a9118870da5f24590e5c8c51628539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4d76a0b22237a0d626c699347fd4848&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fe09d9921bb58d6dfaa46f122e1840f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 304}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1001}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ship is defined as part of the technology and product category here, referring to vessels used on water, specifically within the context of merchant shipping laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ship refers to a vessel used in maritime transport, with its definition varying based on specific legal contexts such as the Merchant Shipping Act 1894 or other shipping regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f4d76a0b22237a0d626c699347fd4848&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fe09d9921bb58d6dfaa46f122e1840f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 304}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 999}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VESSEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The term 'vessel' has the same meaning as provided in section 2 of the Shipping and Port Control Ordinance (Cap. 313), as amended by Law Notice No. 150 of 2014."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vessel is another term for ship, often interchangeably used and defined similarly under various maritime laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vessel means a ship as defined in section 2 of the Shipping and Port Control Ordinance (Cap. 313)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vessel refers to a ship or boat, which is a technological term in this legal context related to maritime law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4d76a0b22237a0d626c699347fd4848&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126e18663d810ba6b83365ff30027a71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fe09d9921bb58d6dfaa46f122e1840f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 304}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1000}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEAFARER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Seafarer denotes individuals working on ships and vessels, including roles such as crew members, which are crucial for the operation of Hong Kong registered ships."&lt;SEP&gt;"Seafarer refers to individuals working on ships and is defined by the Merchant Shipping (Seafarers) Ordinance (Chapter 478 of Hong Kong)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Seafarer refers to individuals working on ships or vessels in a professional capacity, including but not limited to crew members like sailors or officers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Seafarers are crew members serving on ships registered in Hong Kong or under a specific ordinance related to seafaring agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f4d76a0b22237a0d626c699347fd4848&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49920e3fc93948bee580896f50d6da6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fe09d9921bb58d6dfaa46f122e1840f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-786c67dfb1439b58fce397c3168c9e29</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 304}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 999}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MASTER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Master is the term for the ship's captain or commander who has overall responsibility and authority over the vessel during its operation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Master refers to the captain or commander of a ship, an important person in maritime operations and employment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Master refers to the captain or ship's commander who has overall responsibility for its navigation and safety, a key person in maritime operations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-21a9118870da5f24590e5c8c51628539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4d76a0b22237a0d626c699347fd4848&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fe09d9921bb58d6dfaa46f122e1840f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 304}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1000}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE MERCHANT SHIPPING (SEAMEN) ORDINANCE (CAP. 478)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This ordinance provides specific regulations concerning seafarers, including their rights and responsibilities as defined under Hong Kong's maritime laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7fe09d9921bb58d6dfaa46f122e1840f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 304}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1000}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NAVIGATION AND HARBOURS ORDINANCE (CAP. 313)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Navigation and Harbours Ordinance governs the management of ports and harbors in Hong Kong, which is relevant to ship operations and seafarer activities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7fe09d9921bb58d6dfaa46f122e1840f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 304}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 999}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL PROCEEDINGS INVOLVING SHIPS AND SEAFARERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal proceedings related to maritime matters such as evidence rules for trials concerning ships or seafarers are governed by specific legal acts like the Merchant Shipping Act 1894."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7fe09d9921bb58d6dfaa46f122e1840f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 304}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 999}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CEMETERY FEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cemetery fees refer to payments made for burial services, which may be covered under certain maritime laws if a shipowner is responsible for such expenses as per local regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7fe09d9921bb58d6dfaa46f122e1840f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 304}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1001}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE MERCHANT SHIPPING ACT 1894 (TRANSLATED)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This act provides the legal framework and rules related to merchant shipping practices in Hong Kong, including evidence admissibility standards under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7fe09d9921bb58d6dfaa46f122e1840f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 304}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1000}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT ON HONG KONG SHIPS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The act outlines the conditions under which individuals can be considered employees of Hong Kong-registered vessels for legal purposes, extending beyond traditional roles like captain or crew members to include various personnel involved in ship operations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7fe09d9921bb58d6dfaa46f122e1840f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MERCHANT SHIPPING ACT 1894&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The 'Merchant Shipping Act 1894' is a legal document, though not an entity in the traditional sense, it refers to a specific piece of legislation governing maritime matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-21a9118870da5f24590e5c8c51628539</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 305}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;《1894年商船法令》&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"《1894年商船法令》 is another translation for 'Merchant Shipping Act 1894', referring to the same legal document."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-21a9118870da5f24590e5c8c51628539</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 305}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEAFARERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Seafarers are crew members working on ships, including officers and ratings, involved in various aspects of ship operation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-21a9118870da5f24590e5c8c51628539</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 304}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1000}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEPOSITION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A product here means the written statement of testimony given on oath by a witness, which can be used as evidence after being certified and signed by an authorized person."&lt;SEP&gt;"Deposition is a legal document where testimony is recorded, often used in maritime law proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8875aca5fc071476a8bdfdd21f6d729c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21a9118870da5f24590e5c8c51628539</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MERCHANT SHIPPING (SEAFARERS) ORDINANCE (CAP. 478)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Merchant Shipping (Seafarers) Ordinance (Cap. 478) is a regulation concerning seafarer agreements and the ships registered in Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Merchant Shipping (Seafarers) Ordinance is a legal document defining the term 'seafarer' for purposes of compensation and related regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is a legal document that regulates maritime employment and may be related to the licensing of certain types of employment agencies as per the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is an organization that defines legal terms related to seafarers within Hong Kong's shipping laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f4d76a0b22237a0d626c699347fd4848&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3b8b40b208f0fb021cf679f8d096916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d21c68431de960cb287d0f1ae3444dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-786c67dfb1439b58fce397c3168c9e29</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 304}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 999}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCIDENT CAUSING PERSONAL INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Accident causing personal injury refers to incidents that result in harm or loss of work capacity for seafarers while on duty."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-49920e3fc93948bee580896f50d6da6a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 47}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 394}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MASTER OF THE SHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Master of the ship refers to the captain or person in charge on board who can receive notices and claims as if they were the employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-49920e3fc93948bee580896f50d6da6a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HONG KONG SHIPS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hong Kong ships are defined by specific criteria set out in section 29(4) of relevant ordinances, indicating vessels registered under Hong Kong laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-49920e3fc93948bee580896f50d6da6a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 304}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 999}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE OF ACCIDENT AND CLAIM FOR COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A notice of accident and claim for compensation must be given to the ship's master, but under certain conditions, this may not be necessary."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d21c68431de960cb287d0f1ae3444dc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEAFARER (海員)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Seafarers are individuals working on ships, with specific legal definitions and rights as outlined in relevant ordinances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d21c68431de960cb287d0f1ae3444dc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPENSATION APPLICATION FOR SEAFARER DEATH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Applications for compensation due to the death of a seafarer must be made within 2 years after the death or 2 years after the ship's presumed loss with all hands lost."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d21c68431de960cb287d0f1ae3444dc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHIP LOST WITH ALL HANDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The phrase 'ship lost with all hands' refers to a situation where a vessel has sunk and everyone on board is believed dead, impacting compensation timelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d21c68431de960cb287d0f1ae3444dc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WITNESS EVIDENCE OUTSIDE HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Evidence from witnesses outside of Hong Kong can be accepted in legal proceedings related to incidents occurring elsewhere, provided certain conditions are met."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d21c68431de960cb287d0f1ae3444dc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JUDGE OR MAGISTRATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Judges and magistrates have the authority to accept witness statements under specific circumstances as evidence in court cases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d21c68431de960cb287d0f1ae3444dc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BRITISH CONSUL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"British consuls can administer oaths for witnesses outside of Hong Kong, allowing their sworn statements or certified copies to be used as legal evidence."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d21c68431de960cb287d0f1ae3444dc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TESTIMONY OF WITNESS OUTSIDE HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event refers to the process where a deposition made by a witness outside Hong Kong is admitted as evidence in proceedings under this Ordinance related to injuries occurring outside Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8875aca5fc071476a8bdfdd21f6d729c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JUSTICE OR MAGISTRATE IN HER MAJESTY'S DOMINIONS OR IN ANY PLACE WHERE HER MAJESTY EXERCISES JURISDICTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This organization refers to judicial officers who have the authority to administer oaths outside Hong Kong, including justices or magistrates within British territories or places under British jurisdiction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8875aca5fc071476a8bdfdd21f6d729c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BRITISH CONSULAR OFFICER ELSEWHERE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A person here is a consular officer of Britain stationed in locations other than those mentioned above, authorized to administer oaths for depositions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8875aca5fc071476a8bdfdd21f6d729c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;范围适用&quot;(RANGE APPLICABILITY)">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event refers to the application scope where this ordinance applies to employees who are injured outside Hong Kong during their work period and whose employment contract was made in Hong Kong with an employer carrying on business in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8875aca5fc071476a8bdfdd21f6d729c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;外地补偿&quot;(FOREIGN COMPENSATION)">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A product here means the compensation given by law of a place where injury occurred, paid to employees when injuries happen outside Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8875aca5fc071476a8bdfdd21f6d729c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;经营业务的人&quot;(PERSON CARRYING ON BUSINESS)">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This organization refers to entities engaged in commercial activities within or beyond Hong Kong as defined under The Business Registration Ordinance (Cap. 310) of Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8875aca5fc071476a8bdfdd21f6d729c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 185}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOREIGN COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Foreign compensation refers to payments made by entities outside Hong Kong, which may affect the amount of compensation payable under this Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Foreign compensation refers to the compensation paid to an employee for injuries sustained outside Hong Kong, under the laws of that place."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8308cea0d5fc5589bf46df7d1755b30d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3b44850af90a02b11f7716520e896fe</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 438}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERSON CARRYING ON BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Person carrying on business means a company or individual operating in Hong Kong as defined by the Business Registration Ordinance (Cap. 310)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8308cea0d5fc5589bf46df7d1755b30d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 438}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS REGISTRATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 310)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Business Registration Ordinance (Cap. 310) defines terms related to business operations in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8308cea0d5fc5589bf46df7d1755b30d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 303}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 996}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERSONAL INJURY BY ACCIDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Personal injury by accident refers to injuries sustained by an employee due to unforeseen incidents while performing their job duties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3b44850af90a02b11f7716520e896fe</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CIVIL DEBT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A civil debt is a legal obligation for an employee to repay any overpaid compensation to their employer as per the terms set out in the ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A civil debt refers to any sum awarded under subsection (6)(e) that shall be enforceable as such."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3b44850af90a02b11f7716520e896fe</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 967}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1211}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT OR AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Any contract or agreement, whether made before or after the effective date of this ordinance, where an employee waives their right to work-related injury compensation from the employer is considered invalid if it attempts to exempt or reduce legal liability for payment under the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3b44850af90a02b11f7716520e896fe</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGEING OR SEVERE PHYSICAL DEFECTS/DISABILITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The condition of employees who are particularly prone to accidents due to aging or severe physical defects/disabilities, which may affect their employment contracts and compensation rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3b44850af90a02b11f7716520e896fe</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTING OUT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contracting out refers to the act where an employee relinquishes any right to compensation from an employer for personal injury by accident arising out of and in the course of his employment, which is null and void unless certain conditions are met."&lt;SEP&gt;"This event involves clauses in employment contracts that attempt to nullify or reduce employee rights and benefits as provided by an ordinance, which are declared void."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-117a12d3025ead7fc5f26f4bb1ca96c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1683d49752acaec3491f38a426aac742</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 725}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OLD AGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Old Age is a demographic condition that may affect the likelihood and severity of accidents at work, leading to potential reductions or relinquishments of compensation rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1683d49752acaec3491f38a426aac742</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SERIOUS PHYSICAL DEFECTS OR INFIRMITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Serious Physical Defects or Infirmity are conditions that increase the risk of workplace accidents and may lead to reduced or waived compensation rights under certain agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1683d49752acaec3491f38a426aac742</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Occupational Diseases refers to health issues arising from work-related exposures, including physical agents and other sensitizing substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Occupational Diseases refers to illnesses caused by work-related factors, which are covered under compensation laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e00fdf9b02a058deef2e0c53efa1c4d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 188}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPENSATION FOR OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Compensation for Occupational Diseases is a legal provision that ensures workers with occupational diseases receive appropriate financial support and benefits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e00fdf9b02a058deef2e0c53efa1c4d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 608}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1144}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOSS OF WORK CAPACITY OR DEATH DUE TO OCCUPATIONAL DISEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loss of work capacity or death due to occupational disease refers to the situation where an employee becomes unable to work or dies because of a disease caused by their job, which can trigger compensation claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8bab0fa8e650dc6d58da85c05c8bf94</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 720}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1169}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE EMPLOYER WHO LAST EMPLOYED THE EMPLOYEE ENGAGED IN SUCH WORK BEFORE THE OCCURRENCE OF LOSS OF WORKING CAPACITY OR DEATH WITHIN A SPECIFIED PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The organization is responsible for providing information about other employers who have previously employed the same worker during that time frame, and may be liable to share compensation payments if it can prove the employee did not contract an occupational disease while under its employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-65a9f0efd50c34c4817bca268994887b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 880}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE EMPLOYER CLAIMING ANOTHER EMPLOYER AS A PARTY IN LEGAL PROCEEDINGS REGARDING COMPENSATION CLAIMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The organization refers to any previous employers who last employed the worker engaged in such work before the occurrence of loss of working capacity or death within a specified period, and may be liable for sharing payment if it can prove that the employee did not contract an occupational disease while under its employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-65a9f0efd50c34c4817bca268994887b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 880}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Court is an entity that can grant leave under section 84 for enforcement and may set aside an award if a challenge is upheld."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Court refers to a judicial body that can enter judgment and grant or refuse enforcement applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Court refers to a judicial body that has jurisdiction over interim measures in arbitral proceedings, particularly those outside Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Court refers to the judicial body that can grant or refuse leave for emergency relief."&lt;SEP&gt;"The organization refers to courts which decide on shared liability in compensation claims without prior agreement between parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3161c0abf732689fd0fb63c291711d64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65a9f0efd50c34c4817bca268994887b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6100d8c7e7c5fa3f9af262a8c8cb68f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80fae333d21f2886ed576bdc768e41f7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 879}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE WHO CONTRACTED A WORK-RELATED ILLNESS OR INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A person whose health is affected by the nature of their employment and may seek legal action for compensation based on occupational diseases developed during specified periods of employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-65a9f0efd50c34c4817bca268994887b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 880}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAMILY MEMBERS OF AN EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Family members are mentioned as potentially providing information or support in cases where employees need to disclose details about previous employers, highlighting the social dynamics involved in workplace health issues and legal proceedings related thereto."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-65a9f0efd50c34c4817bca268994887b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 880}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE PROCESS BY WHICH AN ILLNESS DEVELOPS GRADUALLY DUE TO EXPOSURE IN A PARTICULAR TYPE OF JOB&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This describes scenarios where occupational diseases develop slowly over time as a result of continuous work-related exposures, influencing liability determinations among multiple employers involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-65a9f0efd50c34c4817bca268994887b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 880}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPENSATION FOR OCCUPATIONAL DISEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Compensation for Occupational Disease refers to a legal entitlement provided under certain conditions related to an occupational disease resulting in incapacity or death."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b9afafd03eeeed71ede32974cead3e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 739}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT WITHIN THE PRESCRIBED PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment within the Prescribed Period is a specific timeframe during which employment must have occurred, as defined by law, for compensation claims due to occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b9afafd03eeeed71ede32974cead3e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER WHO LAST EMPLOYED THE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Employer who Last Employed the Employee is an organization that, during a specific period before the occurrence of incapacity or death due to an occupational disease, was responsible for the employee's employment and thus could be liable for compensation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b9afafd03eeeed71ede32974cead3e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 739}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE’S EARNINGS UNDER THE EMPLOYER FROM WHOM COMPENSATION IS RECOVERABLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee’s Earnings Under the Employer from Whom Compensation Is Recoverable refers to the financial remuneration an employee received, which is used as a basis for calculating compensation in cases of occupational disease."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b9afafd03eeeed71ede32974cead3e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 739}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE GIVEN BY THE EMPLOYER TO THE EMPLOYEE OR FAMILY MEMBERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Notice Given by the Employer to the Employee or Family Members is a formal communication required under certain conditions related to claims of occupational diseases, indicating that an employee has become incapacitated or died due to such a disease."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b9afafd03eeeed71ede32974cead3e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WILFUL AND INTENT TO DECEIVE REPRESENTATION IN WRITING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wilful and Intent to Deceive Representation in Writing is a legal concept where an individual intentionally misrepresents their health status, which can affect the eligibility for compensation related to occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55b9afafd03eeeed71ede32974cead3e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 739}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER FROM WHOM THE COMPENSATION IS RECOVERABLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The employer from whom the compensation is recoverable refers to the last employer during the prescribed period immediately preceding the incapacity or death, as determined by the nature of the employment and disease."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a364dde1ed8396d855ac25cb593a8ce7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 197}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 733}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE OF INCAPACITY OR DEATH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Notice of incapacity or death is the formal communication given by the employee's family to the last employer during the prescribed period, indicating a change in employment status."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a364dde1ed8396d855ac25cb593a8ce7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 197}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 733}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISEASE WAS NOT CONTRACTED WHILST THE EMPLOYEE WAS IN HIS EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event describes a situation where it is proven that the occupational disease was not contracted during the last employer's period of employment, absolving them from full responsibility but potentially making other employers liable for contributions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a364dde1ed8396d855ac25cb593a8ce7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 197}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 733}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OTHER EMPLOYERS WHO EMPLOYED HIM IN SUCH EMPLOYMENT DURING SUCH PERIOD AS HE OR THEY MAY POSSESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Other employers are those who have also employed the employee within the prescribed period preceding incapacity or death, and their information is required to be provided by the employee's family for potential contribution towards compensation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a364dde1ed8396d855ac25cb593a8ce7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 197}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 733}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRADE, INDUSTRY OR PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Trade, industry, or process are specific fields where employees may suffer from occupational diseases and claim compensation according to the law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-338f6b52974bc08baebc662da42c4477</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTERED DOCTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Registered Doctor is a medical professional who can issue certificates according to their practice."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Registered Doctor, along with Registered Chinese Medicine Practitioner and Registered Dentist, can issue certificates when employees have reasonable grounds for refusing treatment or are hospitalized patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"A registered doctor is involved in conducting pre-employment health checks for employees as required by employers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to a professional healthcare provider authorized by law to practice medicine in Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"Registered Doctor is a medical professional mentioned in the text with specific registration requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4f158408c588106f3a0fd30a322902be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-194bd276c174598edc7fcf0c6886ead7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5f66bf87b244d8c901c733042ddc26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcd2a26e931b9fa624c25b0caadbcdb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-338f6b52974bc08baebc662da42c4477</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 345}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1035}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1217}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECOND SCHEDULE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to a secondary schedule attached, likely containing additional details or formats related to the main document."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Schedule refers to an annexure that lists industries, trades, and processes related to occupational diseases for which presumptions can be made about their causes based on employment history."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Second Schedule deals with procedures for apprehending an absconding employer, indicating its relevance in labor and employment law contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Second Schedule is mentioned in relation to the period within which an employee must have been employed before a presumed occupational disease can be established."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Second Schedule refers to specific procedures and conditions that apply when an application is made by an employee regarding wage arrears or other moneys owed, detailing the process for issuing a warrant."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd0362fbf5661d142ff4aeefe27aea79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3b75037d48822c36000fbac9c3ce438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e7d6d62033f777323f252b1d52645d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6c5efdd1d212ba3c8e515e418526d4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082f06bd634567bd06a50adf127eb9eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 429}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDUSTRY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Industries specified in the schedules are subject to pre-employment medical examination requirements as per regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Industry refers to a group of businesses engaged in the production or distribution of goods. It can be transferred from one entity to another as described in Article 5."&lt;SEP&gt;"Industry refers to sectors specified in the Second Schedule where employees may be presumed to have contracted an occupational disease due to their work nature."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-65134d6c88195bfcc2ac0100392eb0d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-082f06bd634567bd06a50adf127eb9eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e7d6d62033f777323f252b1d52645d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 738}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Processes mentioned in the schedules pertain to specific work activities where employees may be at risk of occupational diseases, necessitating mandatory medical examinations before employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-28e7d6d62033f777323f252b1d52645d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Ordinance is the name of an important piece of legislation related to employment rights and responsibilities in Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employment Ordinance is a legal document aimed at protecting employee wages and regulating general conditions of employment. It was first enacted on 27 September 1968."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employment Ordinance is a legal document or regulation that outlines the process for applying for a warrant to recover wages."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employment Ordinance is a legal document that outlines the rules and regulations for employment in Hong Kong, including provisions related to debt recovery from employers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employment Ordinance is a legal document that provides guidelines and regulations for employment matters in Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employment Ordinance outlines regulations regarding pre-employment medical examinations and compensation for occupational diseases."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employment Ordinance refers to a legal document or set of regulations governing employment in Hong Kong, specifically mentioned for its Schedule 2 Part I paragraph 5 related to security requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employment Ordinance refers to the broader legal framework governing employment rights and protections, including sections related to dismissals and contract variations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-74275f2bcd7afd62cd2b27056407d1e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67218fecb16f152219fae29882c0cc1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b88142ce6c5ae26fdcafd8cc6d03845&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d580b5b472939d182c05bf201c52ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78c6c93b249203abfbdb5ba16af8eb78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cbd71f092df4f0f0a3f86b5141618df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edaba831bd1e0154426defdca143f061&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e7d6d62033f777323f252b1d52645d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 330}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;16 OF 2006 S. 19&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Amendments to the Employment Ordinance in 2006, Section 19, specify details about pre-employment medical examination requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-28e7d6d62033f777323f252b1d52645d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;19 OF 1964 S. 5&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The amendment in 1964, Section 5, added provisions regarding the refusal to undergo a medical examination and its implications for compensation claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-28e7d6d62033f777323f252b1d52645d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE INJURY OR ILLNESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Injuries or illnesses related to work can lead to loss of employment and may be subject to specific regulations regarding medical examinations, documentation, and compensation claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-28e7d6d62033f777323f252b1d52645d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 738}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRE-EMPLOYMENT HEALTH CHECK REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The technology involved in pre-employment health checks includes the methods and procedures used by registered practitioners for conducting these mandatory examinations before an employee starts work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-28e7d6d62033f777323f252b1d52645d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATHEMATICS OF RISK ASSESSMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Risk assessments related to workplace injuries or illnesses involve mathematical calculations to determine probabilities, risks, and potential outcomes associated with occupational health issues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-28e7d6d62033f777323f252b1d52645d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOCIAL SCIENCES IN OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The social sciences contribute to understanding the psychological and sociological factors that influence employee behavior regarding pre-employment medical examinations and their rights under labor laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-28e7d6d62033f777323f252b1d52645d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRADE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Trade is another term for industries or processes listed in the Second Schedule that are associated with specific occupational diseases and presumptions about their causes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-082f06bd634567bd06a50adf127eb9eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 738}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT HISTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment History pertains to an individual's work experience, which can be relevant when determining if a disease is due to one's occupation as per legal provisions regarding occupational health and safety."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employment History refers to a record of past employment, which includes details about each period of work and the wages earned during that time."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-082f06bd634567bd06a50adf127eb9eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe986d49a20cfdf5d43e02699374c050</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRESUMPTION OF CAUSE FOR OCCUPATIONAL DISEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The presumption that the nature of employment caused an occupational disease until contrary proof is provided, based on schedules like Second Schedule."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-082f06bd634567bd06a50adf127eb9eb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT FROM 1964 S.5 AND AMENDMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legislative amendments starting with section 5 of Act No. 19 in 1964 and subsequent revisions up to 1980, which established the framework for presumptions about occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-082f06bd634567bd06a50adf127eb9eb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NON-OCCUPATIONAL DISEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A disease that is not considered an occupational disease under this legislation but may be related to accidents or other non-work-related incidents causing bodily injury."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-082f06bd634567bd06a50adf127eb9eb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPENSATION RIGHTS FOR EMPLOYEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employees have the right to seek compensation for diseases, including those deemed as occupational and non-occupational based on specific legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-082f06bd634567bd06a50adf127eb9eb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL DEAFNESS (COMPENSATION) ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Occupational Deafness (Compensation) Ordinance is an ordinance related to compensation for noise-induced deafness in occupational settings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6577b4d90591dfe2444055a054a19ef4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 201}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 742}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROSTHESES AND SURGICAL APPLIANCES BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Prostheses and Surgical Appliances Board, or simply the Board, is a committee appointed under section 36M(1) of relevant legislation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Prostheses and Surgical Appliances Board consists of registered medical practitioners, Chinese medicine practitioners, dentists, and an Occupational Health Officer. Its functions include determining the necessity and cost of prostheses or surgical appliances for injured employees."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Prostheses and Surgical Appliances Board is an organization appointed by the Director to evaluate the necessity of prosthetic devices or surgical appliances, their costs, and issue certificates based on these evaluations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6577b4d90591dfe2444055a054a19ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38b1c51d4d144335e7ee22a31484c537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-966009ce5701084bfffbbea532d598a8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 201}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 742}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEALTH署长 (DIRECTOR)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Director of Health oversees health-related matters as per the legislative amendments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6577b4d90591dfe2444055a054a19ef4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 201}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 742}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROSTHESIS (义制品人体器官)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Prostheses are artificial items that replace parts of the body removed or amputated due to injury, serving a restorative function."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6577b4d90591dfe2444055a054a19ef4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 201}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 741}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SURGICAL APPLIANCE (外科器具)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Surgical appliance refers to any artificial item used to support directly or indirectly the structure or function of a part of the body impaired by an injury, as defined in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgical appliances are artificial devices used to support damaged bodily structures or functions directly or indirectly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6577b4d90591dfe2444055a054a19ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-427b651b5a2a0a36734fd93776b2efbd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 201}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 741}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART IIIA部&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part IIIA of the legislation deals with regulations and definitions related to prostheses and surgical appliances, indicating an industry focus on medical devices and health services."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6577b4d90591dfe2444055a054a19ef4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIRECTOR OF HEALTH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Director of Health refers to a position responsible for health-related matters, as mentioned in the context of amendments and additions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-427b651b5a2a0a36734fd93776b2efbd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 201}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 741}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROSTHESIS (義製人體器官)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Prosthesis is an artificial item that replaces parts of the body removed or amputated due to injury, according to legal definitions provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-427b651b5a2a0a36734fd93776b2efbd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 201}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 741}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROSTHESIS OR SURGICAL APPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Prosthesis or Surgical Appliance is a medical device required by an injured employee as a result of his injury, which the Employer must pay for according to the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prostheses and surgical appliances are medical devices that may be covered by legal provisions related to their supply and fitting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prostheses and surgical appliances are medical devices that may be required by an employee, for which costs need to be paid as per regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prostheses or surgical appliances are medical devices that may be fitted to replace missing parts of the human body, requiring assessment for their durability, replacement needs, and costs over a 10-year period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prostheses or surgical appliances are medical devices that may be supplied and fitted to employees, with costs covered by employers under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prosthesis or surgical appliance refers to artificial limbs, organs, or devices used for medical purposes as mentioned in sections 36B and 36I."&lt;SEP&gt;"These refer to artificial body parts or surgical equipment provided for injured employees according to sections 36B and 36I, which require their normal maintenance and replacement."&lt;SEP&gt;"These refer to medical devices such as artificial limbs, organs, or other surgical equipment needed by an employee due to workplace injuries."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5980c15d89bdf2ef4857f80a2f6b149c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdcbcb18d7b9887f495f81165f5fb4fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-607cc87ad2d00618b2e8b6ad160e563d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-194bd276c174598edc7fcf0c6886ead7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39a2bf80964aaaae8baf6e4ab980412a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c526fd9477b77161e84c476f0017da6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e62d63292a05cf6bb5e6be00c591105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72e470440b916fe7d89e88eb4a51cf95</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 115}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMITTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An organization that may approve or certify certain medical treatments and appliances as per legal provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Committee is responsible for assessing the costs related to prosthetic organs or surgical devices, including their supply, fitting, and maintenance over a 10-year period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eea091e3d60115d9c86a868057c8f1d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-194bd276c174598edc7fcf0c6886ead7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 371}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1070}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROSTHETIC DEVICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Artificial body parts such as limbs, organs, etc., used to replace missing or damaged body parts due to injury or illness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-194bd276c174598edc7fcf0c6886ead7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 115}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SURGICAL APPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A surgical appliance is another type of medical device that may be necessary for an injured employee and requires assessment by the Prostheses and Surgical Appliances Board."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical devices used in surgical procedures for treatment and recovery from injuries or illnesses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-38b1c51d4d144335e7ee22a31484c537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-194bd276c174598edc7fcf0c6886ead7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 201}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 742}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER, REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER, REGISTERED DENTIST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are professionals who can certify that a prosthesis or surgical appliance is required and has been supplied and fitted as per section 2(c)(i) of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c526fd9477b77161e84c476f0017da6e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 371}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1069}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Board refers to a governing body responsible for assessing and certifying the necessity and cost of prostheses or surgical appliances."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Board assesses the total amount under section 36M(2)(c) and (3), indicating it's a regulatory or administrative body with specific duties."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Board certifies whether a prosthesis or surgical appliance is manufactured, on sale in Hong Kong, and meets other specified criteria before approving payment by the Employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Board issues certificates under section 36M(4) supporting requests for payment made by the Director on behalf of claims under section 36B."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Board refers to an organization that approves the payment for medical treatments outside Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Board refers to an organizational body that can issue notices requiring employees to attend for examinations or assessments under section 36M."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5980c15d89bdf2ef4857f80a2f6b149c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdcbcb18d7b9887f495f81165f5fb4fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-607cc87ad2d00618b2e8b6ad160e563d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39a2bf80964aaaae8baf6e4ab980412a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-786468d759a9a7b3ea39a79ba530682c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c526fd9477b77161e84c476f0017da6e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 370}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1064}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;36B&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 36B is a provision that outlines the employer's liability to pay for certain medical expenses, including those related to prosthesis or surgical appliance fitting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5980c15d89bdf2ef4857f80a2f6b149c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;36C&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 36C sets limits on the amount of costs employers are liable to pay under Section 36B, specifically in relation to accidents and their associated treatments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5980c15d89bdf2ef4857f80a2f6b149c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 36B&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 36B is a legal provision related to the supply and fitting of prostheses or surgical appliances under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 36B is an event or regulation that outlines the employer's liability to pay costs related to accidents involving employees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 36B pertains to supplying and fitting prostheses or surgical appliances, suggesting this is related to medical technology or equipment management."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6e62d63292a05cf6bb5e6be00c591105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e2e52d53aa59764f7b51002074a7ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdcbcb18d7b9887f495f81165f5fb4fc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 115}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 36C&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 36C is part of the Sixth Schedule that specifies additional compensation amounts in terms of monetary values or percentages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 36C specifies the limit of the employer's liability under Section 36B in terms of monetary amounts and accident cases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c5e2e52d53aa59764f7b51002074a7ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-463028737c14d4a1b81570efedfe747c</data>
