<node id="&quot;COMPANY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Company can apply for the operation of a Vocational Introduction Office if it meets certain conditions, such as being associated with the holder of the license."&lt;SEP&gt;"A company can be held guilty of an offense if it is proved that the offense was committed with the consent or connivance of any director, manager, secretary, or other similar officer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A company can have related persons such as directors, managers, secretaries, and other similar officers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A company is an entity that can be issued with a licence or certificate of exemption and may experience changes in management, as described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"A company refers to a legal entity formed by individuals engaged in commercial, industrial, or other business activities. In this context, it can be any corporate body."&lt;SEP&gt;"A corporate entity involved in employment and contract renewal processes under various legal sections."&lt;SEP&gt;"Company refers to a business entity, as defined by the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622), and can be subsidiary or associated with other companies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Company refers to an entity defined under the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622) in Hong Kong, which has specific meanings for terms like subsidiary as per sections 32B, 32C, and 32D."&lt;SEP&gt;"Company refers to the term as defined in the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622) under Section 2(1</data>
