<node id="&quot;GROUP OF COMPANIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A group of companies refers to multiple entities operating together, which are covered under the provisions of Section 40(1C)."&lt;SEP&gt;"A group of companies refers to multiple related organizations that can collectively take out an insurance policy covering all members' liabilities as specified in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Group of companies has the same definition as 'company' according to the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622) under Section 2(1&lt;SEP&gt;"Group of companies refers to a collective entity that may take out an insurance policy together for compliance with subsection (1C)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Group of companies refers to a company group with the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-09e282cd999f281d4422d40832df059c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d1a5d83703c47f3bc06048ecc6e08a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b577aefb31326e0dd35b3e4acfd2057&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fae8b17287c09754a8180334dba81fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb529b0707db1b4e516f08ed3339967d</data>
