<node id="&quot;SUBSIDIARY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A subsidiary company that may be covered by its parent's insurance and can become liable for employee compensation under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A subsidiary has the meaning given in Section 15 of the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622&lt;SEP&gt;"A subsidiary of the holding company, insured under the same policy as the holding company, which may become liable for paying compensation or damages due to an employee's injury during employment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsidiary has the meaning given by section 15 of the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622) for that Ordinance's purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsidiary is an organization that is controlled by another company through ownership of voting shares or similar means, according to the definition in section 15 of the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c766b49f034ebbb22f19aa37de351708&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b577aefb31326e0dd35b3e4acfd2057&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fae8b17287c09754a8180334dba81fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2fbd733817e8b83d49f91e4a4cbe908&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d06ee4edd39803f9b252b767c726ef91</data>
