<node id="&quot;FOURTH SCHEDULE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fourth Schedule is a part of the legal document that outlines rules and rates related to medical expenses for employees in hospitals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourth Schedule refers to an appendix or schedule in a document, detailing insurance cover for certain conditions as per section 40(1)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Fourth Schedule is a document that specifies the applicable amount for insurance policies related to employer's liabilities as per legal requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Fourth Schedule is a reference document that specifies the applicable amount for insurance policies required by law."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Fourth Schedule is another section of the legal document that provides additional details or modifications related to claims by personal representatives for deceased employees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ba7e2407b8844aba128e42ffefa2f5d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09e282cd999f281d4422d40832df059c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da53ed52a17c537de0b1301ebe9c9aa8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6157228e3518a3c9dd66f98867aa8a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb529b0707db1b4e516f08ed3339967d</data>
