</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 42&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 42 refers to another part of legislation that may affect the rights and procedures for recovering claims from an insurer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f50ffa55ee49cc2d1e6b1641b82f27dc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 437}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISCLAIM LIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Disclaiming Liability is a legal action where the insurer renounces its responsibility under the insurance policy, potentially allowing direct proceedings against them without first suing the insured person."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f50ffa55ee49cc2d1e6b1641b82f27dc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 437}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE OR OTHER PERSON HAVING A CLAIM AGAINST THE PERSON INSURED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This describes individuals who have claims against the insured, including employees and others."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-740adc792b975b3e69e6b1a7c25c776a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 574}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTROL COMPANY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Control company refers to a parent company in a corporate structure where it has legal responsibilities towards its subsidiaries regarding employee compensation for work-related injuries."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-740adc792b975b3e69e6b1a7c25c776a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 251}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 922}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSIDIARY COMPANY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsidiary company is an entity that is a subsidiary of another company according to the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622) in Hong Kong as defined in section 15 for implementing relevant provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsidiary company is an organization that operates under the control of another larger entity, known as the parent or controlling company."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-740adc792b975b3e69e6b1a7c25c776a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c28e990fb442886ba69eb65de9d2282</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 335}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPENSATION OR DAMAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financial products or services related to the payment of compensation or damages due to workplace accidents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2fbd733817e8b83d49f91e4a4cbe908</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 332}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;40(1C) CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A specific legal provision under the insurance regulation which outlines conditions and responsibilities related to holding companies and their insured subsidiaries."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2fbd733817e8b83d49f91e4a4cbe908</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 332}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;A POLICY OF INSURANCE TAKEN OUT BY A GROUP OF COMPANIES PURSUANT TO SECTION 40(1C)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is an insurance product covering employees' compensation or damages under specific conditions, as described in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c766b49f034ebbb22f19aa37de351708</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 332}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S EMPLOYER BEING A SUBSIDIARY OF A HOLDING COMPANY WHICH IS ALSO INSURED UNDER THE POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON, ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An individual or an entity working within a subsidiary that has insurance coverage through their parent holding company."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c766b49f034ebbb22f19aa37de351708</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 334}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1023}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSPECTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An individual or a group of individuals authorized to inspect non-residential premises and ensure compliance with relevant regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inspector refers to a role defined by the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (Cap. 59), which can be taken to mean certain individuals before the commencement of this section."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3c3394a6b72977677a8a437b4151b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c766b49f034ebbb22f19aa37de351708</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 146}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 640}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1161}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSPECTOR'S AUTHORIZATION DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT, TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An official document that allows authorized personnel to enter and inspect non-residential premises without a warrant, as described in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c766b49f034ebbb22f19aa37de351708</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 146}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 640}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1161}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NON-RESIDENTIAL PREMISES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Premises where employees are working but which do not qualify as residential areas, subject to inspection by authorized officials."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c766b49f034ebbb22f19aa37de351708</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER OF AN EMPLOYEE WHO IS EMPLOYED BY A SUBSIDIARY INSURED UNDER A POLICY OF INSURANCE TAKEN OUT BY A GROUP OF COMPANIES PURSUANT TO SECTION 40(1C)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION, PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An entity or individual that employs someone whose compensation may be covered by the insurance policy mentioned in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c766b49f034ebbb22f19aa37de351708</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECORD OR DOCUMENT RELATED TO EMPLOYEES' COMPLIANCE WITH REGULATIONS WITHIN NON-RESIDENTIAL PREMISES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT, TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documents or records kept at a workplace that are relevant for ensuring employee compliance with specific regulations, as required by inspectors according to the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c766b49f034ebbb22f19aa37de351708</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MANAGEMENT OF A NON-RESIDENTIAL PREMISE OR ITS APPARENT MANAGER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON, ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The person in charge of managing a non-residential premises and overseeing employees' activities within it, who may be requested to provide information during an inspection."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c766b49f034ebbb22f19aa37de351708</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEPUTY COMMISSIONER FOR LABOUR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Deputy Commissioner for Labour is an organizational role within the Labour Department, second in command after the Commissioner."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Deputy Commissioner for Labour works under the Commissioner, likely handling labor-related matters in addition to general administrative duties."&lt;SEP&gt;"A deputy commissioner designated by the Commissioner to conduct formal inquiries into workplace accidents or dangerous occurrences."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1dbb46e60da08be769a0481277a08538&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ae9a7e8f27b80b32998caf906ca2a86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12cbce1945bd7c28729e716e02489760</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 610}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1152}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASSISTANT COMMISSIONER FOR LABOUR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Assistant Commissioner for Labour also supports the Commissioner and may handle specific tasks related to labor issues or other areas as assigned by the Commissioner."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Assistant Commissioner for Labour is another organizational role within the Labour Department, assisting the Commissioner and Deputies in their duties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6ae9a7e8f27b80b32998caf906ca2a86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12cbce1945bd7c28729e716e02489760</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 610}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1153}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LABOUR DEPARTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Labour Department advises on matters necessary for carrying out the purposes of this ordinance, particularly in relation to employment and labor regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Department is an organization responsible for enforcing workplace regulations and conducting inspections as described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Department is an organization that authorizes officers to bring prosecutions under certain conditions as per the text provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Department is an organization that issues and manages workplace codes of practice, providing them for public inspection during office hours."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Department is an organization where the Commissioner keeps a register of exemptions and ensures public access to it."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Department is an organization where the Commissioner's head office is located, providing workplace codes of practice for public inspection without charge during ordinary business hours."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Department is mentioned as having officers authorized by the Commissioner to conduct prosecutions under section 43P."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Department is responsible for issuing workplace codes and subsidiary legislation related to work practices and safety."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Department refers to an organization responsible for labor-related matters, including inspections related to workplace conditions and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de69b2333ff7d9bb2dd79e072a634503&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fabbc3eeb929a4a143a6817fd7b457aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b297641c5fc96a9b02649fb896184fdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ae9a7e8f27b80b32998caf906ca2a86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1833f1af069fda07edd900b2ad5d51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fd592d376d0854e1e9f902478b9ced3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c09a594dc48c807d71b9bc97e24d4b0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beb3c1a7d6211fc1cac75a7aeaaff11f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 609}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1148}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREMISES OF AN EMPLOYER WHERE PERSONS ARE EMPLOYED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These refer to workplaces or premises owned by employers where employees work, subject to inspection under relevant laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6ae9a7e8f27b80b32998caf906ca2a86</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 608}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1144}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;40TH SECTION CRIME EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The 40th section crime evidence pertains to potential criminal activities that may be found within residential premises, which could trigger an inspection by a judge based on sworn complaints."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6ae9a7e8f27b80b32998caf906ca2a86</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 608}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1144}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CIRCUIT JUDGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Circuit Judge is a judicial officer who can issue warrants based on sworn complaints regarding reasonable grounds of suspicion about the occurrence or ongoing incidents of offenses under this Ordinance or evidence that may pertain to such offenses in certain locations."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Circuit Judge, in this context, is a judicial officer who can issue warrants based on sworn information regarding potential evidence of offenses within residential premises."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12cbce1945bd7c28729e716e02489760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c09a594dc48c807d71b9bc97e24d4b0f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 609}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1149}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESIDENTIAL PREMISES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Residential Premises are the specific locations where inspections and checks may be conducted by authorities as per legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12cbce1945bd7c28729e716e02489760</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 610}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1153}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSURANCE POLICY, COVER NOTE OR OTHER DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These documents pertain to insurance-related paperwork that can be inspected during residential premises inspections for employees working in such places."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12cbce1945bd7c28729e716e02489760</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 610}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1153}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 40 OFFENSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 40 Offense refers to a specific type of crime or violation that may be found within the scope of residential premises as per legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12cbce1945bd7c28729e716e02489760</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 610}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1153}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSPECTION AND EXAMINATION EVENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event involves inspections and examinations conducted by authorities, particularly focusing on residential areas for potential violations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12cbce1945bd7c28729e716e02489760</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 610}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1152}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COVER NOTE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cover notes are documents related to policies of insurance that may also need to be produced according to the notice from the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bfb4e2ef783a3573d88736c7ce485115</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSPECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Inspection is a formal process conducted by authorized public officers to ensure compliance with regulations governing employment agencies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inspection refers to the process where The Commissioner checks or examines documents produced by employers as per their notice."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inspection refers to the process where the Commissioner checks or reviews the provided documents as per the notice issued by them."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5ead5337f34ae6c6d3adbc5b06e2bc74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee0cf79121cc26199f0bf5c4d14a8ce8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfb4e2ef783a3573d88736c7ce485115</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 147}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 644}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Commissioner has the authority to refuse issuing or renewing a licence, and can revoke a licence based on reasonable grounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner is an entity with the authority to issue notices requiring employers to produce documents for inspection."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner is an individual who has the authority to grant, withdraw, and enforce regulations related to exemptions for employment agencies."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner is an individual with the authority to amend certain schedules, as mentioned in section (6)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner refers to a government official responsible for issuing licenses, certificates of exemption, and codes of practice related to employment agencies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-950a35becf4c52961439921c1e246ea5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ead5337f34ae6c6d3adbc5b06e2bc74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1780efd8ae08a5db55e3f208ec193d60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e75048e9ce4b436dfa55abbe5d61e73f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602c441cf667030bb7c11323e7c28f43</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 147}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 645}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1162}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMISSIONER'S NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A notice issued by the Commissioner requiring employers to produce specific documents for inspection, which includes policies of insurance and other relevant records."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5ead5337f34ae6c6d3adbc5b06e2bc74</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 147}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 645}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1162}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A document that is accepted as evidence without further proof in court proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Document is a product that can be produced in arbitration, subject to certain conditions as stated in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Document refers to any document or article that may be required by The Commissioner from an employer as per the notice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5ead5337f34ae6c6d3adbc5b06e2bc74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d32c74af47d4bd7932dd3de0fb1f8ae1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 315}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONVICTION UPON INDICTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conviction upon Indictment refers to the process where an employer can be convicted of an offence through a formal trial by jury, which carries specific penalties including fine at level 6 and imprisonment for two years."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5ead5337f34ae6c6d3adbc5b06e2bc74</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 405}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1101}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUMMARY CONVICTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A type of criminal proceeding where the accused pleads guilty to a lesser charge without going through a full trial, potentially leading to fines as penalties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Summary Conviction is another legal term referring to a less serious form of criminal prosecution that does not involve a jury but can still result in fines or short-term imprisonment, as mentioned with specific penalties in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Summary conviction refers to the process of quickly determining guilt in minor criminal cases, which can result in fines and imprisonment as described by specific sections within legislation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5ead5337f34ae6c6d3adbc5b06e2bc74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd33f100307534902fe4100976fabc93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0812f6740fa10908c6c96dfb7b577a49</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 405}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1104}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HINDRANCE AND OBSTRUCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hindrance and Obstruction refers to actions by any person who interferes with The Commissioner's ability to exercise their powers of inspection, which is considered an offence carrying a fine at level 5 as per the law mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5ead5337f34ae6c6d3adbc5b06e2bc74</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 147}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 645}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1162}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BODY CORPORATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Body Corporate refers to an organization or entity managed by directors who are responsible for its operations and compliance with laws such as the Noise Control Ordinance (Cap. 400)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Body Corporate is a term used in the text to refer to companies and other organizations established as legal entities under Hong Kong law or elsewhere."&lt;SEP&gt;"Body Corporate refers to a legal entity that can be aggrieved by certain decisions made by the Secretary, such as registration refusals or cancellations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Body Corporate refers to a legal entity that can commit offenses under sections 63B or 63C. Directors, managers, secretaries, and other similar officers of the body corporate may be held liable for such offenses due to their consent, connivance, or neglect."&lt;SEP&gt;"Body Corporate refers to an entity that can commit offenses under section 43P and includes directors, managers, secretaries, or other similar officers who may be held liable for such actions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Body Corporate refers to an entity that operates businesses and has a registered office, subject to specific service procedures outlined for legal documents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Body Corporate refers to any company or other body corporate incorporated in Hong Kong or elsewhere, excluding corporations registered under the Building Management Ordinance (Cap. 344)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Body Corporate refers to companies or other organizations incorporated in Hong Kong or elsewhere, excluding those registered under the Building Management Ordinance (Cap. 344)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Body corporate is a legal entity managed by its members, and it can commit offenses under certain conditions related to premium increase notices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Body corporate is an organization incorporated under the law of a place outside Hong Kong or one whose central management and control is exercised outside Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"Body corporate refers to a company or entity that may be subject to the management practices of directors and officers as described in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-606c291ea5ee675ad86390a5e98aaec1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a825b77831d51f05d63ae1b415705940&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594b3f94b09a41a66ac58f172b6c0c83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89bbff8bbf3f0985059cdccf2a6fe747&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa06844e99812b2f5f3eb2b64f82eb38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-effb99400ad285817b5c201e84a15ab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c560e10db0daa7f51fa59f7a6b462aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd34572cc7a7c12a47fc15cbaf1c545c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a6827e6d05ee12b48810a8b5429419c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6127a28d22b5d9d9145842f6c4caba9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aae626926134b8ac6b7cded959f0e21a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 373}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1074}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIRECTOR, MANAGER, SECRETARY OR SIMILAR OFFICER OR MAIN AGENT OF THE BODY CORPORATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These roles within a body corporate are individuals who may be held responsible for committing an offense if they consent to, connive at, or neglect their duties regarding premium increases as per regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-aa06844e99812b2f5f3eb2b64f82eb38</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 373}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1074}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEMBER OF THE BODY CORPORATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Members of a body corporate can manage it and thus might be involved in offenses related to premium increase notifications under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-aa06844e99812b2f5f3eb2b64f82eb38</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 373}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1074}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Ordinance refers to a legal document or legislation, possibly the Arbitration Ordinance of Hong Kong, which governs aspects of arbitration within its jurisdiction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ordinance refers to a set of regulations or laws governing certain construction contracts and their subcontracts, particularly those involving significant values."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ordinance refers to an unspecified piece of legislation that contains sections governing various organizations and conditions for offenses related to noise and other activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ordinance refers to an unspecified set of rules and regulations governing compensation payments and their enforceability."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Regional Court Ordinance (Chapter 336) provides qualifications for judges who can be appointed as chairpersons, reflecting legal standards governing judicial appointments in Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"The product refers to a legal document or ordinance that has been amended and revised multiple times, focusing on regulations related to employment agencies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7c9d82cf88dd3738b34743e6dd94bc9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679d548673cb77dcfe447573286cf62e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66157f73d78c8a042051d0b5db5e4492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c1c54aae15fa21fd2f3fa9a3916e793&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-471ea86899263b19957a8682c15503f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8d055b17ca5d7c4bc065dbbfefc9360</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 722}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AIDED PERSON WITHIN THE MEANING OF THE LEGAL AID ORDINANCE (CAP. 91)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Aided person is defined by the Legal Aid Ordinance, subject to specific financial obligations related to legal aid contributions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-679d548673cb77dcfe447573286cf62e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 721}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIRECTOR OF LEGAL AID&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Director of Legal Aid holds a role overseeing legal assistance programs and has rights over compensation under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Director of Legal Aid is mentioned as benefiting from the first charge on compensation, indicating a role in overseeing legal aid contributions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd33f100307534902fe4100976fabc93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679d548673cb77dcfe447573286cf62e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 722}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL AID ORDINANCE (CAP. 91)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal Aid Ordinance (Cap. 91) refers to an organization or legislation that provides for legal aid and its provisions are mentioned regarding the first charge on compensation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Legal Aid Ordinance is a piece of legislation providing for the administration and provision of legal aid, with specific provisions affecting compensation payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd33f100307534902fe4100976fabc93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679d548673cb77dcfe447573286cf62e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 722}]</data>
</node>
