</node>
<node id="&quot;INSURANCE PREMIUM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Insurance premium refers to the cost of an insurance policy that may be deducted from earnings as part of an employer's liability for paying compensation under certain provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd33f100307534902fe4100976fabc93</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 575}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JUDICIAL OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Judicial officer refers to individuals, like judges or magistrates, who preside over courts and make decisions on cases related to insurance premium deductions and employer-employee disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Judicial officers refer to individuals such as the president of the tribunal or a judicial officer and their representatives who issue certificates."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2e830aa0329b87250f2426040cef8661&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd33f100307534902fe4100976fabc93</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1190}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CRIMINAL OFFENSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Criminal offense refers to actions that violate legal statutes, such as making unauthorized deductions from employee earnings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The criminal offense is the act of providing false information to the Secretary in certain circumstances, which can lead to penalties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d8d055b17ca5d7c4bc065dbbfefc9360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd33f100307534902fe4100976fabc93</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 405}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1104}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINE AT LEVEL 3 AND IMPRISONMENT FOR 6 MONTHS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This phrase describes the penalties an employer faces if convicted of a criminal offense related to insurance premium deductions. It is a specific form of punishment prescribed by law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd33f100307534902fe4100976fabc93</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 405}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1104}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;44 OF 1980 S. 15, 76 OF 1982 S. 29, 63 OF 1992 S. 16, AND 52 OF 2000 S. 23&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are specific legal amendments or sections that have modified the original text over time, indicating changes in laws related to insurance premium deductions and employer responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd33f100307534902fe4100976fabc93</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 303}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 992}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;47. DEDUCTION OF INSURANCE PREMIUMS FROM EARNINGS TO BE AN OFFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a title for a section within legislation stating that it is illegal for employers to deduct insurance premiums from employee earnings without proper authorization or legal basis."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd33f100307534902fe4100976fabc93</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 575}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT OR MAGISTRATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court or Magistrate is an entity that can impose fines and order compensation for employees when employers are convicted under section 63A(5)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Court or Magistrate refers to judicial bodies that can impose penalties, including fines and imprisonment, on employers convicted under subsection (1) of section 47."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5742863cc938d9f9470985855601b925&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b965639f18b2c29c5f672b6067f9d701</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 315}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPRISONMENT FOR 6 MONTHS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Imprisonment for 6 months refers to a potential criminal sentence that can be imposed on employers convicted of offences under section 47(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b965639f18b2c29c5f672b6067f9d701</data>
