</node>
<node id="&quot;CHIEF JUSTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Chief Justice is a high-ranking judicial officer who has the authority to determine the judgment rates used in arbitration cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chief Justice is a high-ranking judicial officer who has the authority to make Rules of Court, ensuring that these rules align with the broader legal framework and objectives."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chief Justice is responsible for determining the rate of interest under section 49(1)(b) (Interest on judgments) of the High Court Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chief Justice's approval is required for the HKIAC to make rules, indicating a role in governance or oversight of the center."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chief Justice's prior approval is required before any rules are made, indicating their significant role in this process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-01f73d3a0eb5a63d428e456a11dad9c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-678280ae191a89f40bc665d65f091cbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3450bee90618bb17df6c3522ce7aa42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd8b5a6b74d6568cda4bfce7dd132460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a7d382b60c68c418d8128c80396b687</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 235}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 872}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RULES OF COURT FOR REGULATING PROCEEDINGS BEFORE THE COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are specific guidelines or procedures established by the Chief Justice to manage court proceedings as per the Ordinance's provisions."</data>
