  <data key="d1">"This entity refers to specific measures and practices implemented within industries exposed to risks from electromagnetic radiation or ionizing particles, aimed at mitigating potential health hazards for workers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f30d14d75a76f9e89eb6fe137661d148</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEALTH IMPACT STUDIES ON OCCUPATIONAL EXPOSURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are research efforts focused on understanding the long-term effects of occupational exposures to physical factors like electromagnetic radiation and ionizing particles on worker health."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f30d14d75a76f9e89eb6fe137661d148</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This entity refers to industry-specific guidelines designed to ensure workplace safety, particularly in environments where workers may be exposed to risks from electromagnetic or ionizing particle exposure."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f30d14d75a76f9e89eb6fe137661d148</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPENSATION POLICIES FOR OCCUPATIONAL INJURIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are the formalized procedures and policies established by organizations or governments to provide financial support to individuals suffering from work-related injuries, including those caused by physical factors like radiation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f30d14d75a76f9e89eb6fe137661d148</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL HEALTH MONITORING PROGRAMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This entity refers to systematic programs designed to monitor workers' health over time in environments where they may be exposed to occupational hazards such as electromagnetic or ionizing particles."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f30d14d75a76f9e89eb6fe137661d148</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RADIATION SAFETY TRAINING FOR EMPLOYEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are educational and training programs aimed at informing and preparing employees about the risks associated with radiation exposure, proper handling procedures, and emergency response measures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f30d14d75a76f9e89eb6fe137661d148</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL HEALTH STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The text describes standards and practices aimed at ensuring occupational health, reflecting industry efforts to manage risks associated with hazardous substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text describes standards for ensuring worker safety in occupations involving hazardous substances, indicating a technological approach to managing these risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"This entity refers to established industry-wide or government-mandated standards for ensuring safe working conditions in environments where workers may be exposed to physical factors like electromagnetic radiation or ionizing particles."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f30d14d75a76f9e89eb6fe137661d148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94a1139425d270c7317d6d6a1dd6e020</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RADIATION PROTECTION EQUIPMENT AND PROTOCOLS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are the specific tools, devices, and procedures used to protect workers from harmful exposure to radiation in their work environment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f30d14d75a76f9e89eb6fe137661d148</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL HEALTH RESEARCH INSTITUTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This entity refers to organizations dedicated to researching occupational health issues, including those related to physical factors like electromagnetic or ionizing particles, with the goal of improving worker safety and health outcomes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f30d14d75a76f9e89eb6fe137661d148</data>
</node>
