  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">"Inflammation or ulceration of the mucous membrane of the upper respiratory tract or mouth due to exposure to dust, liquid, or gas."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-491fe17f0698fd111d0bfee1d246c18a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;鼻腔或相關氣竇的癌癥(鼻癌)&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">"Nasal cancer caused by exposure to dust, liquid, or gas in occupations related to the manufacture or repair of wooden products, shoes, or shoe accessories."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-491fe17f0698fd111d0bfee1d246c18a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;棉屑沉着病&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">"Disease due to exposure to cotton dust in occupations involving such exposure."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-491fe17f0698fd111d0bfee1d246c18a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;職業性哮喘病&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">"Occupational asthma caused by exposure to substances that can irritate or sensitize the respiratory system, including isocyanates, certain metal compounds, fumes from epoxy resin hardeners containing adipic acid anhydride, terephthalic acid anhydride, and tetramethylenediamine, smoke from rosin used as soldering flux, formaldehyde, proteases, or animals and insects for research or educational purposes in laboratories."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-491fe17f0698fd111d0bfee1d246c18a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;大麥、燕麥、黑麥、小麥或玉米的播種、栽植、收割、弄乾、處理、磨粉、運送或貯存&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">"Exposure to dust from the handling, drying, processing, grinding, transportation or storage of wheat, barley, rye, oats or corn."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-491fe17f0698fd111d0bfee1d246c18a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ELECTRO-MAGNETIC RADIATIONS (OTHER THAN RADIANT HEAT)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Electro-magnetic radiations are a type of technology that can cause skin or subcutaneous tissue inflammation due to prolonged exposure in certain occupations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IONISING PARTICLES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ionising particles are another form of technology that, when exposed for long periods, can lead to blood dyscrasia and other health issues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEAT CATARACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Heat cataract is a specific occupational disease caused by frequent or prolonged exposure to rays from molten or red-hot material in certain occupations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heat cataract is an occupational disease resulting from frequent or long-term exposure to the light emitted by molten or hot substances in quarries."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98d195ac6ea8e6425cbc78e7f365cca6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DYSBARISM, INCLUDING DECOMPRESSION SICKNESS, BAROTRAUMA AND OSTEONECROSIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dysbarism encompasses various health issues arising from compressed or rarefied air or other gases exposure, affecting the joints over a period of one year in some cases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTHRITIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arthritis is a medical condition that can be an occupational disease for those engaged in repetitive movements involving handwriting, typing, etc., with a prescribed observation period of five years."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBCUTANEOUS CELLULITIS OF THE HAND (BEAT HAND)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONDITION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subcutaneous cellulitis of the hand is a condition arising from severe or prolonged friction or pressure on the hand, commonly associated with occupations involving manual labour."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subcutaneous cellulitis of the hand is a specific health issue caused by severe or prolonged friction or pressure on the hands in manual labor occupations, leading to inflammation and infection."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b65ba7ca0b25e8b8db22e6c1edfd463f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BURSITIS OR SUBCUTANEOUS CELLULITIS ARISING AT OR ABOUT THE KNEE DUE TO SEVERE OR PROLONGED EXTERNAL FRICTION OR PRESSURE AT OR ABOUT THE KNEE (BEAT KNEE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONDITION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This condition involves bursitis or subcutaneous cellulitis of the knee, caused by occupations involving manual labour and severe or prolonged external friction or pressure on the knee."&lt;SEP&gt;"This condition is a result of severe or prolonged external friction or pressure on the knees in manual labor occupations, leading to inflammation and infection."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b65ba7ca0b25e8b8db22e6c1edfd463f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MANUAL LABOUR CAUSING SEVERE OR PROLONGED FRICTION OR PRESSURE ON THE HAND&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Manual labour involving significant physical strain can lead to various occupational diseases such as subcutaneous cellulitis of the hand (Beat hand)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MANUAL LABOUR CAUSING SEVERE OR PROLONGED EXTERNAL FRICTION OR PRESSURE AT OR ABOUT THE KNEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This type of manual work is associated with conditions like bursitis or subcutaneous cellulitis arising at or about the knee due to repeated stress and strain."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPRESSED OR RAREFIED AIR OR OTHER GASES OR GASEOUS MIXTURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Exposure to compressed or rarefied air or other gases can lead to dysbarism, including decompression sickness, barotrauma, and osteonecrosis."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RADIANT HEAT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Radiant heat is a form of electromagnetic radiation that does not cause skin diseases but may be associated with other occupational health issues in certain industries."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INFLAMMATION, ULCERATION OR MALIGNANT DISEASE OF THE SKIN OR SUBCUTANEOUS TISSUES OR OF THE BONES, OR BLOOD DYSCRASIA, OR CATARACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are potential health outcomes from exposure to specific physical agents such as electro-magnetic radiations other than radiant heat and ionising particles."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPETITIVE MOVEMENTS OF THE FINGERS, HAND OR ARM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Occupational diseases can arise from prolonged repetitive motions in industries like typing or handwriting, leading to conditions like cramp of the hand or forearm due to repetitive movements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CRAMP OF THE HAND OR FOREARM DUE TO REPETITIVE MOVEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a specific occupational disease resulting from long-term repetitive motion tasks such as writing or typing in various industries."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES (編輯修訂——2018年第1號編輯修訂紀錄)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The term 'Occupational Diseases' is updated and revised according to the 2018 Edition, indicating ongoing updates in occupational health regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK期间吸入的敏化物質 (ANY OTHER SENSITIZING SUBSTANCES DURING WORK HOURS) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are substances that can cause respiratory or skin issues when inhaled during working hours and may be associated with various occupations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;穀粉或粉末的運送或貯存 (TRANSPORTATION OR STORAGE OF GRAIN FLOUR OR POWDER)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This industry involves the handling, transportation, and storage of grain products such as oatmeal, rye, wheat, or corn."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;穀麥、小麥或玉米的播種、栽植、收割、弄乾、處理、磨粉、運送或貯存 (SOWING, PLANTING, HARVESTING, DRYING, PROCESSING, GRINDING OF OATS, BARLEY, WHEAT, OR CORN)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This industry encompasses the entire process from growing to storing various grains and their derivatives."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;塵埃 (DUST) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dust is a byproduct of grain processing that can cause respiratory issues when inhaled, particularly during activities like grinding or handling grain products."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FLAMMABLE DUST EXPLOSION RISK (可燃性粉尘爆炸风险)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The text does not explicitly mention this term but implies the potential for dust explosions in grain processing industries due to flammable properties of certain grains and their derivatives."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;穀物 (GRAINS) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Grains such as oats, barley, wheat, or corn are primary products processed and stored by this industry."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;工作期間吸入的敏化物質 (SENSITIZING SUBSTANCES INHALED DURING WORK HOURS) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These substances can cause allergic reactions or other health issues when inhaled during working hours, affecting various occupations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES (由1983年第386號法律公告代替。由1987年第52號法律公告修訂;由1991年第397號法律公告修訂;由1993年第410號法律公告修訂)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The term 'Occupational Diseases' is revised and updated according to multiple legal announcements, indicating ongoing regulatory changes in occupational health."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES (FORMAT CHANGES—E.R. 1 OF 2018) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This indicates that the regulations on Occupational Diseases have been formatted or restructured as per the 2018 Edition, reflecting updated guidelines and standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a173f515c3a7b233c06630f4bb889f7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BURSITIS OR SUBCUTANEOUS CELLULITIS ARISING AT OR ABOUT THE ELBOW DUE TO SEVERE OR PROLONGED EXTERNAL FRICTION OR PRESSURE AT OR ABOUT THE ELBOW (BEAT ELBOW)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONDITION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This condition involves bursitis or subcutaneous cellulitis of the elbow, caused by occupations involving manual labour and severe or prolonged external friction or pressure on the elbow."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b65ba7ca0b25e8b8db22e6c1edfd463f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRAUMATIC INFLAMMATION OF THE TENDONS OF THE HAND OR FOREARM (INCLUDING ELBOW), OR OF THE ASSOCIATED TENDON SHEATHS (AMENDED L.N. 146 OF 1999)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONDITION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This condition refers to traumatic inflammation affecting the tendons in the hand, forearm, and elbow areas, often due to frequent or repeated movements involving manual labour."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b65ba7ca0b25e8b8db22e6c1edfd463f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CARPAL TUNNEL SYNDROME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Carpal tunnel syndrome affects workers using hand-held powered tools that vibrate, excluding those solely hand-powered, added by L.N. 147 of 1999."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carpal tunnel syndrome is a repetitive strain injury caused by the use of hand-held powered tools that vibrate, affecting the wrist and hand area in occupations requiring such activities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b65ba7ca0b25e8b8db22e6c1edfd463f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7306865e35ebfb2e70b787c62738f5ca</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANTHRAX&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DISEASE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Anthrax is a disease contracted through contact with infected animals or handling animal products and residues associated with specific occupational risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anthrax is an infectious disease caused by contact with infected animals or handling animal products, posing risks to various occupational groups including those involved in agriculture and veterinary services."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da23b5f81dd13162b08cf24c13ec97da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65ba7ca0b25e8b8db22e6c1edfd463f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GLANDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DISEASE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Glanders is a zoonotic bacterial infection transmitted from equine animals to humans through direct contact, affecting occupations involving the care of horses or their carcasses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glanders is an infectious disease that can be transmitted by contact with equine animals or their carcasses, posing risk to certain occupations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da23b5f81dd13162b08cf24c13ec97da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65ba7ca0b25e8b8db22e6c1edfd463f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INFECTION BY LEPTOSPIRA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leptospirosis infections occur in occupational settings where there is exposure to rats, field mice, voles, dogs, and bovine animals or their meat products, posing risks for workers in agriculture and related fields."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b65ba7ca0b25e8b8db22e6c1edfd463f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FARMER'S LUNG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONDITION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A pulmonary disease caused by inhaling dust from mouldy hay or other vegetable produce, commonly found in agricultural, horticultural, forestry, loading/unloading/storage of such materials, or handling bagasse work environments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Farmer's Lung is an occupational disease related to inhaling dust from moldy hay, often affecting farmers and those involved in agriculture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Farmer's lung is a respiratory condition caused by inhaling dust from mouldy hay or other vegetable produce, affecting agricultural workers who are exposed to such environments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da23b5f81dd13162b08cf24c13ec97da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65ba7ca0b25e8b8db22e6c1edfd463f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1413ab0c72d29c4bf80b03987aaff3dd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONTHS&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">DURATION</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to a period during which certain conditions must be met before an event can occur."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BOVINE ANIMALS&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">"In the context of occupational health, refers to cattle and other related species that may carry or transmit diseases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PIGS&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to swine and their management in agricultural settings which can be a source of various infections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MOULDY HAY&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">PRODUCT</data>
  <data key="d1">"Agricultural product that has become infested with mold, potentially containing spores causing farmer's lung when inhaled."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FARMER'S LUNG&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">"An occupational disease caused by inhaling dust from mouldy hay or similar produce, characterized by respiratory symptoms and gas exchange defects."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGRICULTURE&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">INDUSTRY</data>
  <data key="d1">"The sector involved in farming crops and raising livestock, where workers may be exposed to various hazards including farmer's lung."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HORTICULTURE&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">INDUSTRY</data>
  <data key="d1">"The cultivation of plants for food or other purposes, potentially involving exposure risks similar to those found in agriculture."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FORESTRY&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">INDUSTRY</data>
  <data key="d1">"The management and use of forests for timber production, paper products, and other forest resources where workers may be exposed to dust from mouldy vegetable produce."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOADING OR UNLOADING&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">ACTIVITY</data>
  <data key="d1">"Activities related to the movement of goods in storage facilities that can expose workers to harmful substances like mold spores."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HANDLING IN STORAGE&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">ACTIVITY</data>
  <data key="d1">"The process of managing and storing agricultural products, which may involve exposure risks such as those from mouldy hay."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BAGASSE&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">PRODUCT</data>
  <data key="d1">"A by-product of sugarcane processing that can be a source of dust and potential respiratory hazards when handled improperly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PULMONARY DISEASE&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">"Respiratory conditions affecting the lungs, including farmer's lung caused by inhaling mold spores from hay or similar products."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MOULDY VEGETABLE PRODUCE&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">PRODUCT</data>
  <data key="d1">"A broad category of plant materials that have become infested with mold and can pose respiratory risks when inhaled as dust."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATION INVOLVING EXPOSURE TO THE DUST OF MOULDY HAY OR OTHER MOULDY VEGETABLE PRODUCE&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to jobs where workers are at risk of inhaling harmful spores from mold-infested plant materials, leading to conditions like farmer's lung."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGRICULTURE, HORTICULTURE OR FORESTRY&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">INDUSTRY</data>
  <data key="d1">"Industries involved in the cultivation and management of plants and animals that can expose workers to various occupational health risks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOADING OR UNLOADING OR HANDLING IN STORAGE SUCH HAY OR OTHER VEGETABLE PRODUCE&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">ACTIVITY</data>
  <data key="d1">"Activities related to moving and storing agricultural products, which may involve exposure to mold spores from infested materials."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HANDLING BAGASSE&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">ACTIVITY</data>
  <data key="d1">"The process of managing the by-products of sugarcane processing that can pose respiratory hazards when inhaled as dust."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1 YEAR&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">DURATION</data>
  <data key="d1">"A period of time specified for certain occupational health risks, indicating a timeframe during which exposure must be managed or monitored."&lt;SEP&gt;"A period specified for occupational health risks related to brucellosis, indicating a timeframe during which exposure must be managed or monitored."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;B5&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">"Infection by organisms of the genus brucella, an occupational disease associated with contact with infected animals and their products in various occupations involving such exposures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANIMALS INFECTED BY BRUCELLA&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">"Livestock or other animals carrying Brucella bacteria that can transmit infections to humans through direct contact or handling of carcasses, untreated products, laboratory specimens, or vaccines containing the organism."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;B6&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tuberculosis as an occupational disease associated with close and frequent contact with sources of tuberculosis infection in various occupations involving such exposures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDICAL TREATMENT OR NURSING OF A PERSON SUFFERING FROM TUBERCULOSIS&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
  <data key="d1">"Occupational activities related to the care and management of patients with tuberculosis, which can expose healthcare workers to airborne pathogens."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3ce3b452a4c4d63ae5162c1b37835b4e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;6 MONTHS&quot;|">
  <data key="d0">DURATION</data>
  <data key="d1">"A period specified for occupational health risks associated with parenterally contracted viral hepatitis, indicating a timeframe during which exposure must be managed or monitored."</data>
