  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cap 282 RTF is a document that provides detailed rules for apportioning compensation to eligible family members, with specific clauses addressing different types of family relationships."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6942b65bc123e327e9f90372813c148</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPENSATION PAYABLE TO ELIGIBLE MEMBERS OF THE FAMILY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event refers to the process or action of distributing compensation according to predefined criteria outlined in legal documents such as Cap 282 RTF (14-05-2026)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6942b65bc123e327e9f90372813c148</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPORTIONMENT OF COMPENSATION PAYABLE TO ELIGIBLE MEMBERS OF THE FAMILY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event refers to the process or action of distributing compensation according to predefined criteria outlined in legal documents such as Cap 282 RTF (14-05-2026)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6942b65bc123e327e9f90372813c148</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 729}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPOUSES OR COHABITEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Spouses or Cohabitees are considered as eligible members for family compensation, and their share is determined based on various scenarios involving other family members."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spouses or cohabitees are eligible family members who receive a portion of compensation, with varying percentages depending on the presence of other family members."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spouses or cohabitees are eligible family members who receive a portion of the compensation based on their status within the family structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spouses or cohabitees are individuals who may be entitled to receive a share of the compensation if they are the only eligible family members, according to the legal provisions outlined in Cap 282 RTF (14-05-2026)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spouses or cohabitees are individuals who share a domestic relationship, receiving 50% of the compensation if they are the only eligible members of the family."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6942b65bc123e327e9f90372813c148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1938a0bb46ac68b6b87f8f976a10b061&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4cada5f5bf4ec8ceba652ad11f10a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf83ce681b3c9c2ca889e6e5ad2a0c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44ee098d72c3cfdd3e201662ed838d22</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 728}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHILDREN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Children are also considered as eligible members for family compensation, with shares allocated according to the presence of other family members such as parents or grandparents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Children are another category of family members who may receive a portion of the compensation, receiving 45% in one scenario where other categories do not apply."&lt;SEP&gt;"Children are eligible family members who, along with other relatives, may receive a portion of the compensation depending on the presence and number of other relatives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Children are eligible members of the family who receive 75% or 50% of the compensation in equal amounts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Children are mentioned as a category that receives 95% or 75% of the compensation depending on other family members' presence or absence, indicating their significant role in inheritance and support distributions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Children are not directly compensated but their presence affects how compensation is distributed among other relatives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Children can be considered as one of the categories of eligible family members who may receive equal shares of compensation if they are the only ones entitled, based on legal provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Children receive a portion (45%) of the remaining 20% and 95% of the total compensation under different scenarios, showing their central position within the family structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Children receive different percentages of compensation based on their familial context and other eligible members present in the family."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-498a60e85a08494b75272ed277c81a05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6942b65bc123e327e9f90372813c148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e900da43d00f655414f15ad83d97a3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1938a0bb46ac68b6b87f8f976a10b061&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4cada5f5bf4ec8ceba652ad11f10a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3729eccee563b08b3baf022dfb8e0b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf83ce681b3c9c2ca889e6e5ad2a0c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44ee098d72c3cfdd3e201662ed838d22</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 727}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Parents are a category of eligible family members under certain conditions where other relatives like grandparents or cohabitees do not apply. Compensation is distributed according to specific rules outlined in Cap 282 RTF (14-05-2026)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parents are mentioned as recipients of 70% and 80% of compensation in different scenarios, indicating their significant role within the family structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parents are mentioned as recipients of a portion of the compensation when there are no grandparents or great-grandparents present."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parents can be part of the distribution of compensation if there are no grandparents present, receiving 70% of the 20%, or in combination with grandparents where they receive an additional 30%."&lt;SEP&gt;"The term 'parents' refers to the parents of an individual, involved in receiving a share of the distribution under specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-498a60e85a08494b75272ed277c81a05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ec65cd13e12d5661e764484d0e10bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6942b65bc123e327e9f90372813c148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1938a0bb46ac68b6b87f8f976a10b061&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e900da43d00f655414f15ad83d97a3a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 726}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GRANDPARENTS, AND GREAT-GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Grandparents and great-grandparents are also considered eligible family members under certain conditions. The distribution of compensation among them is governed by specific rules outlined in Cap 282 RTF (14-05-2026)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6942b65bc123e327e9f90372813c148</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 729}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OTHER FAMILY MEMBERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Other family members include siblings and in-laws who can also be recipients of compensation under certain conditions, reflecting a broader social structure within families."&lt;SEP&gt;"Other family members refer to relatives other than spouses, cohabitants, parents, grandparents, and great-grandparents. The text describes the distribution of compensation among these individuals based on their relationship status."&lt;SEP&gt;"Other family members who do not fall into the categories of spouses, cohabitees, children, parents, or grandparents may also be eligible for compensation. The distribution is governed by specific rules outlined in Cap 282 RTF (14-05-2026)."&lt;SEP&gt;"This includes other relatives or close associates within the family who receive their portion from the remaining 5% of the distribution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e900da43d00f655414f15ad83d97a3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ec65cd13e12d5661e764484d0e10bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3729eccee563b08b3baf022dfb8e0b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6942b65bc123e327e9f90372813c148</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 727}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL PROVISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal provisions are rules and regulations outlined in sections such as 6, 7, 32A(1)(c), 32B(3), and 32C that govern employment contracts and business ownership changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal provisions outlined in the text pertain to statutory holidays, alternative days off, and employer-employee communication regarding these matters."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal provisions refer to the set of guidelines and laws that dictate how compensation should be distributed among eligible family members, as detailed in documents such as Cap 282 RTF (14-05-2026) and E.R. 1 of 2018."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9ddecf99bc0bca06387d96224afeaf4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6942b65bc123e327e9f90372813c148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adbe757d90ad335b39fd280c5f650025</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 171}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 707}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CAP 282 RTF (14-05-2026)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cap 282 RTF (14-05-2026) is a legal document or regulation that outlines the rules for distributing compensation among family members."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cap 282 RTF (14-05-2026) is the reference document providing legal guidelines for family compensation based on different scenarios involving eligible members."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cap 282 RTF is a legal document that provides the framework for distributing compensation to eligible family members, with specific rules and clauses governing different scenarios."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is a legal document or regulation, providing detailed rules on the distribution of compensation among family members in certain scenarios."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c4cada5f5bf4ec8ceba652ad11f10a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf83ce681b3c9c2ca889e6e5ad2a0c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6942b65bc123e327e9f90372813c148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44ee098d72c3cfdd3e201662ed838d22</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 728}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPENSATION DISTRIBUTION RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Compensation distribution rules are the guidelines and procedures that determine how financial compensation is allocated among eligible family members, as outlined in legal documents such as Cap 282 RTF (14-05-2026) and E.R. 1 of 2018."&lt;SEP&gt;"The rules describe how compensation is distributed among different types of family members, detailing percentages and conditions for payment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The rules for distributing compensation among eligible family members are described in detail, outlining various scenarios based on who is present or absent from the household."&lt;SEP&gt;"These rules detail the distribution of compensation among family members in different scenarios, including parents, grandparents, and great-grandparents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c4cada5f5bf4ec8ceba652ad11f10a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498a60e85a08494b75272ed277c81a05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e900da43d00f655414f15ad83d97a3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6942b65bc123e327e9f90372813c148</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 727}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAMILY RELATIONSHIPS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Family relationships refer to the various types of familial connections that can qualify individuals for receiving financial compensation under legal provisions such as Cap 282 RTF (14-05-2026)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6942b65bc123e327e9f90372813c148</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCIAL COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financial compensation refers to the monetary awards or payments provided to eligible family members according to specific rules outlined in documents like Cap 282 RTF (14-05-2026) and E.R. 1 of 2018."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6942b65bc123e327e9f90372813c148</data>
</node>
