<node id="&quot;COMPENSATION ALLOCATION PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Compensation allocation process refers to the procedure or method by which financial compensation is distributed according to legal provisions outlined in documents such as Cap 282 RTF (14-05-2026</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6942b65bc123e327e9f90372813c148</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 729}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARENTS OR GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Parents or Grandparents are part of the family structure that can receive compensation, and their share is calculated based on specific conditions involving spouses, cohabitees, and children."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parents or grandparents are eligible family members who share in the distribution of compensation based on their status within the family structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parents or grandparents can be part of the distribution, with varying percentages depending on whether only children are present or if there are also spouses/cohabitees or other family members involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c4cada5f5bf4ec8ceba652ad11f10a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf83ce681b3c9c2ca889e6e5ad2a0c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44ee098d72c3cfdd3e201662ed838d22</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 728}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENGLISH AND TRADITIONAL CHINESE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"English and Traditional Chinese are languages in which the Cap 282 RTF document is available, indicating its accessibility to both English-speaking and Chinese-speaking populations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf83ce681b3c9c2ca889e6e5ad2a0c3b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 720}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1170}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAMILY COMPENSATION GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The guidelines for family compensation outlined in the text detail how payments should be distributed among different eligible members based on their relationship status within the family."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf83ce681b3c9c2ca889e6e5ad2a0c3b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 720}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1169}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAMILY MEMBERS ELIGIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The concept of eligible family members refers to those who are entitled to receive portions of compensation based on specific conditions and relationships within the family structure."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c4cada5f5bf4ec8ceba652ad11f10a00</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 728}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Grandparents can be part of the distribution of compensation when parents are not eligible for a larger share; specifically, they receive 30% of the 20% if there are no parents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1938a0bb46ac68b6b87f8f976a10b061</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 726}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OTHER MEMBERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Other members refer to any eligible relatives that fall outside the specific categories mentioned (spouses/cohabitees, parents, grandparents, and children), who receive a fixed 5% of the compensation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1938a0bb46ac68b6b87f8f976a10b061</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 726}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARENTS OR GRANDPARENTS, OR ANY COMBINATION THEREOF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Parents and/or grandparents form a group that can be compensated based on their presence, with specific percentages allocated to them depending on family composition."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 186}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OTHER MEMBERS WHO ARE NOT SPOUSES OR COHABITEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Other non-spouse/non-cohabitant family members receive 5% of the compensation in equal amounts when they are the only eligible members."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 186}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEVENTH SCHEDULE ADDED 52 OF 2000 S. 28&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The addition of Section 28 in Regulation 52 of 2000, which amends the compensation distribution rules based on family composition and eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 720}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1169}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAMILY MEMBERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Family members are categorized into different groups (children, parents, grandparents) for specific compensation distributions according to legal regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 186}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;配偶或同居者或其任何組合&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Spouses or cohabitees form a group that can be compensated based on their presence, with 50% of the compensation allocated to them when they are eligible members."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spouses or cohabitees form another category of family members who receive 50% of the compensation in equal amounts when they are eligible, with a different distribution method if grandparents are also present."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 186}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;子女&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Children again refer to those receiving 50% of the compensation in equal amounts under certain conditions where only children and non-spouse/non-cohabitant family members are eligible."&lt;SEP&gt;"Children receive 50% of the compensation in equal amounts when they are the only eligible family members."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 186}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;合資格家庭成員為或合資格家庭成員包括&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The term refers to a group that can include parents, grandparents, or their combinations as eligible recipients of compensation based on specific conditions and percentages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 186}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GRANDPARENTS AND GREAT-GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Grandparents and great-grandparents are mentioned as recipients of a portion of the compensation, with specific conditions on their share based on the absence of parents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-498a60e85a08494b75272ed277c81a05</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 726}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPOUSES OR COHABITANTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Spouses or cohabitants are mentioned as receiving 50% of the compensation when they are the only eligible family members, indicating their significant role in the household."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spouses or cohabitants are mentioned as receiving 95% of the compensation in certain scenarios involving only them and other family members."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e900da43d00f655414f15ad83d97a3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498a60e85a08494b75272ed277c81a05</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 727}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GRANDPARENTS OR GREAT-GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Grandparents or great-grandparents receive a portion (30%) of the remaining 20% of compensation when other relatives are involved, highlighting their importance as well."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to the grandparents or great-grandparents who receive a portion of the distribution in certain scenarios."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e900da43d00f655414f15ad83d97a3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ec65cd13e12d5661e764484d0e10bd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 726}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARENTS, GRANDPARENTS, GREAT-GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FAMILY RELATIONSHIPS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Parents, grandparents, and great-grandparents are mentioned as a category that can receive portions of the compensation if certain conditions apply, highlighting their importance in family structures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3729eccee563b08b3baf022dfb8e0b5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 727}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NO PARENTS SITUATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event refers to the scenario where there are no parents, and it involves distributing 100% of a certain amount among grandparents or great-grandparents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-23ec65cd13e12d5661e764484d0e10bd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 726}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;95TH PERCENTILE'S 70%&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This represents 70% of the 95th percentile, which is to be distributed evenly among parents in any other situation except where there are no parents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-23ec65cd13e12d5661e764484d0e10bd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 726}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;95TH PERCENTILE'S 30%&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This represents 30% of the 95th percentile, which is to be distributed evenly among grandparents or great-grandparents when there are no parents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-23ec65cd13e12d5661e764484d0e10bd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 726}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REMAINING 5%&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The remaining 5% is to be distributed evenly among other family members."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-23ec65cd13e12d5661e764484d0e10bd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 184}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 727}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISE CONTROL ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Noise Control Ordinance is a legal document aimed at preventing, minimizing, and abating noise. It includes the appointment of a Noise Control Authority and outlines its powers and duties related to noise control."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5d00b09a8462e6600243e76883c57569</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 378}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISE CONTROL AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Noise Control Authority is an appointed public officer responsible for controlling noisy activities in accordance with relevant ordinances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Noise Control Authority is an organization appointed under the Noise Control Ordinance with specific powers and responsibilities in controlling noise."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Noise Control Authority is an organization appointed under section 3(1) of the Noise Control Ordinance (Cap. 400), responsible for advising on proceedings related to noise control violations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce50382ff024b176dc7ebf19fb5b68d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d00b09a8462e6600243e76883c57569&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-606c291ea5ee675ad86390a5e98aaec1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 378}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPEAL BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appeal Board is a body established to hear appeals related to noise permits or other regulatory matters."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appeal Board is an organization constituted under section 21, tasked with determining appeals under this Part."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appeal Board is an organization that can be appealed to if one feels aggrieved by decisions regarding noise permits, such as denial or conditions imposed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appeal Board is the body that accepts appeals against decisions made by the Authority regarding construction noise permits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appeal Board refers to a committee established according to Section 21, which handles appeals related to noise control matters."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appeal Board refers to a committee established under Section 21, which handles appeals according to relevant regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appeal Board refers to a group of individuals responsible for hearing appeals and making determinations before the Court of Appeal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appeal Board refers to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal established under Article 5 of the Administrative Review Commission Ordinance (Cap. 442) and is involved in matters related to employee safety and health."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Appeal Board is a body consisting of the Chairman and members appointed from a panel for hearing appeals under this Part."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Appeal Board is a body that hears appeals and has powers similar to those of a court, including receiving evidence on oath, admitting statements, summoning witnesses, confirming decisions, making awards for costs, and dealing with contempt."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Appeal Board is a body where witnesses are entitled to immunities and privileges similar to those in civil proceedings before the Court of First Instance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Appeal Board is an organization that handles appeals against decisions made by the Commissioner regarding workplace accidents or notifications, providing a mechanism for employers or occupiers to challenge such decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Appeal Board is an organization where appeals can be made against service of notices by Authority under section 13 or 16."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Appeal Board is mentioned in the context of regulating appeals, suggesting it handles disputes related to regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Appeal Board is the Administrative Appeals Board established under section 5 of the Administrative Appeals Board Ordinance (Cap. 442)."&lt;SEP&gt;"上訴委員會是指根据第21条成立的上訴委員會。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c65da5be1610c7210df4b6d277a43ffa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf98c13106216ee2990969e11aafbee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c6fd01455af1494e4efe451e7933dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cee1a453a83b87002df2318ef0eb78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8d52a1038b5b838fbe9231f59cfc74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60c17dd78d73fb0b81ce0ba9e3153396&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a461efee858ab690fe058321b8a0025&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d107bfd5d6737d06b2fc1d377e10585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ed6bb61c777b6fe07e21fb258ca9224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7741f07cb911e2c57e64574afd3fe8e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3645bfc30781435fa7015192a9be351c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d00b09a8462e6600243e76883c57569&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7249fad978915b4915d01ecac03019f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35333cbaccd9be2f64c80f729f9d5ffb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56e97ce586530c13a293f392668859be</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 291}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 976}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHIEF EXECUTIVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Chief Executive is an individual who can give directions to public officers under this Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chief Executive是指有权批准或延长决议期限的人。"&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chief Executive has the authority to publish orders amending parts of schedules in the Gazette, as evidenced by amendments made under Section 68 and related provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chief Executive is a high-ranking government official with the power to give directions regarding the exercise of powers, functions, or duties by public officers under this Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chief Executive is an individual who has the authority to appoint dates for the coming into operation of different provisions in this Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chief Executive is an individual who has the authority to make regulations with certain conditions, as mentioned in section 1 of the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chief Executive is mentioned as someone who may appoint individuals, including District Judges, to act as Chairman when the original Chairman cannot perform his functions due to certain reasons."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chief Executive is responsible for appointing members of the Appeal Board and a Chairman according to certain qualifications."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chief Executive is the head of the executive branch of government in Hong Kong and has significant authority over legal matters, including those related to international conventions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chief Executive refers to the highest executive official of a certain administrative region who has the authority to appoint officials such as Noise Control Authorities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-553752aa230afc1ddedc93862b70955f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c65da5be1610c7210df4b6d277a43ffa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c6fd01455af1494e4efe451e7933dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66c75321ad1bdf83283c50d27bc8b7e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-603a9b33a6e3900af70fd439592326ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e804bc54b158b7b2826228aa81b5372e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce50382ff024b176dc7ebf19fb5b68d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5218a05714fc8de44f54bb46fbf020e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa88f4f6c68bdcdf602f197a3d1b3c60</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 291}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 976}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC PLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Public Place includes — (a) Any public street, wharf or park; (b) Railway's permanent passage; (c) Any part of the waters or a publicly navigable waterway; (d) Any portion of airspace over Hong Kong; and (e) Any other place where entry is permitted by any person without payment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public Place includes any area open to the public, where noise from various activities like games and business operations could disturb others."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public place encompasses public streets, piers, gardens, railway permanent ways, territorial sea, publicly navigable waterways, airspace above Hong Kong, or any other accessible location without payment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public place includes any public street, pier, public garden, permanent way of a railway, territorial sea, publicly navigable waterway, and airspace above Hong Kong where people are entitled to access."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public places include areas accessible to the general public and may be subject to different noise control measures compared to domestic or construction sites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public places include various areas such as docks, avenues, streets, roads, lanes, alleys, wards, waterways, beaches, passages, trails, paths, parks, country parks, public gardens and other locations that are either government or private property. However, it excludes certain types of premises used for business purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c6fd01455af1494e4efe451e7933dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1740b8b8c7e777efdccf16fb8d3a59de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126e18663d810ba6b83365ff30027a71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a0b3234913f2437002d1d69a535cc59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 293}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 981}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHAIRMAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Chairman is a key figure in the composition of the Appeal Board, responsible for determining questions of law and having a casting vote in case of equality of votes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chairman is an individual appointed with specific functions during his term, such as appointing persons to hear appeals."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chairman is the person appointed as the head of the Appeal Board according to Section 20(2)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chairman refers to a person who can determine forms or matters of practice or procedure not provided for in this Ordinance and has specific roles during absences or incapacitation."&lt;SEP&gt;"主席指的是根据第20(2)条任命的上訴委員會主席。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf98c13106216ee2990969e11aafbee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c6fd01455af1494e4efe451e7933dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d107bfd5d6737d06b2fc1d377e10585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60c17dd78d73fb0b81ce0ba9e3153396</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 291}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 976}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PILING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Piling refers to a specific type of construction work involving percussive piling which does not require cancellation under certain public interest conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Piling refers to any engineering work involving driving, pressing down, screwing in, spiral drilling, drilling, jetting, vibration, pouring or other methods for sinking piles into the ground or forming piles on-site. It also includes works related to piling used as foundation purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-14c6fd01455af1494e4efe451e7933dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d7aa41ab04a649aeb83e8611a7626ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 299}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 988}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Place here generally refers to any location that may be entered by the authorized officer for various purposes related to law enforcement and inspection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Place refers to any location whether it is on land or water."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-14c6fd01455af1494e4efe451e7933dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8024a8a38a1cf4faa9e3a31112f97d7c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 314}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1003}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOMESTIC USE PREMISES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Domestic use premises refer to places where residential activities take place, which are not covered by the definition of public places as mentioned above."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-14c6fd01455af1494e4efe451e7933dd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 314}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1003}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;局長 (SECRETARY)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"局長指環境及生態局局長，是一個具體的人員角色。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;地方 (PLACE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"地方指任何地方,不論該地方是在陸上或水上，是一個地理上的概念。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;住用處所 (DOMESTIC PREMISES)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"住用處所指全部或主要作居住用途,並且作為獨立住戶單位的任何處所;及由酒店或公寓管理人租予客人的任何酒店或公寓部分，是一個特定的生活空間概念。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;車輛 (VEHICLE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"車輛的涵義與《道路交通條例》(第374章)中該詞的涵義相同,是指交通工具。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;侵擾者 (INTRUDER)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"侵擾者指任何未獲許可而干擾任何處所或車輛的人，是一個行為上的角色描述。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;侵擾者警報系統 (INTRUDER ALARM SYSTEM)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"侵擾者警報系統指一個藉發出由侵擾者觸發的可聽信號以作有侵擾者的警告的警報系統，是一種安全技術。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;建築工程 (CONSTRUCTION WORK)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ACTIVITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"建築工程包括任何建築、拆卸、重建、支撐、改建、維修或修葺整個或部分建築物、拱形結構、橋樑、煙囪、船塢、圍板、遮蔽處、隧道、牆，是一種施工活動。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;建築工程&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"建築工程是指一系列涉及建造、拆卸等工作的施工活动，包括但不限于建筑物、桥梁和其他结构的建设或维修。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fcb1392a3c356025d7c364794c01ff7a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;建築地盤&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"建築地盤指的是进行建筑工程项目的地方。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fcb1392a3c356025d7c364794c01ff7a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;建築噪音許可證&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"建築噪音許可證是一种产品或工具，用于批准在特定时间段内进行可能产生噪音的建筑工程活动。"&lt;SEP&gt;"建築噪音許可證是一种根据第8(1)条发放的许可证，用于控制和管理施工过程中的噪声问题。"&lt;SEP&gt;"建築噪音許可證是一种用于建筑施工时控制噪音排放的产品或文件，确保符合相关法规要求。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75a63fc1bac46279a18763a5809259bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9053b5bb875d947585293b13bbe5f25e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcb1392a3c356025d7c364794c01ff7a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;指定範圍&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"指定范围是指根据第8A条规定设立的一个特定区域。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fcb1392a3c356025d7c364794c01ff7a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;登記車主&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"登记车主持有车辆的合法权利，其定义与《道路交通条例》(第374章)中对该词的规定相同。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fcb1392a3c356025d7c364794c01ff7a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;煩擾&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"煩擾指的是令人感到不悦或困扰的行为或情况，在此文本中可能涉及施工噪音等问题。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fcb1392a3c356025d7c364794c01ff7a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISE PERMIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Noise Permit is a document allowing construction activities to proceed during specific hours on non-public holidays."&lt;SEP&gt;"Noise Permit is a document or authorization required for certain activities, such as construction work involving noise."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-56e97ce586530c13a293f392668859be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7741f07cb911e2c57e64574afd3fe8e3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 291}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 975}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DESIGNATED AREA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Designated Area is a region established by the Secretary through notices published in the Gazette, subject to further technical memorandums regarding noise regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Designated Area refers to the area established under Section 8A; it is used in the context of noise control regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"指定范围指的是根据第8A条建立的区域。（1994年第2号修订）"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d107bfd5d6737d06b2fc1d377e10585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56e97ce586530c13a293f392668859be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86dd5816dd56bd7bc4f23ec93e31f0f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 299}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 988}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTERED OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Registered Owner has a meaning consistent with its definition in The Road Traffic Ordinance (Cap. 374), referring to the owner who registered the vehicle or property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-56e97ce586530c13a293f392668859be</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 291}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 975}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERCUSSIVE PILING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Percussive Piling is a method of driving piles into the ground using percussive devices and may be subject to specific guidelines as per Technical Memorandums."&lt;SEP&gt;"Percussive Piling is a specific type of construction activity subject to conditions stated in the written notice issued by the Authority when granting a permit."&lt;SEP&gt;"Percussive Piling is a specific type of construction activity that involves using equipment to drive piles into the ground by repeated blows and may require special permits due to its noisy nature."&lt;SEP&gt;"Percussive Piling is a type of pile driving operation using direct or indirect hammering, other impacts to drive piles into the ground; it includes operations with drop hammers, diesel hammers, double-action hammers, single-action hammers, internal drop hammers, pneumatic hammers, steam hammers, and other impact devices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Percussive piling is a method of driving piles into the ground using repeated blows, often requiring specific timing to avoid disturbing business operations during certain hours."&lt;SEP&gt;"Percussive piling refers to a method of pile driving where an impact hammer strikes the pile, often generating significant noise and requiring specific permits or time restrictions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4bda701f7b69fa34380775a0f86642cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c80a5edef13387c70f1ddbc0ac7e4acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72a00cd6e89601305d8b400d5eef9c21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35333cbaccd9be2f64c80f729f9d5ffb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56e97ce586530c13a293f392668859be</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 971}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1214}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PILE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pile refers to any structure driven into the ground or formed in it such as a board, column, post, tube, or caisson; it also includes structures called 'driven piles', 'spiral auger piles', 'in-situ cast piles', 'composite piles', 'sand piles', 'board piles', 'bored piles', and any other form of pile."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-56e97ce586530c13a293f392668859be</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 299}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 988}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POWERED MECHANICAL EQUIPMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT, TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Powered Mechanical Equipment refers to machines or devices driven by electrical, chemical, or thermal energy; it includes machinery that uses compressed air, steam, or hydraulic power as the primary means for generating mechanical action."&lt;SEP&gt;"Powered mechanical equipment includes machinery and tools used in construction activities with power sources."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-56e97ce586530c13a293f392668859be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d7aa41ab04a649aeb83e8611a7626ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 299}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 991}]</data>
</node>
