  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"使用与或用于上述操作的机械、设备、工具、器具和材料。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d107bfd5d6737d06b2fc1d377e10585</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 799}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SCREW PILE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Screw pile is a type of foundation element driven into the ground by screwing or augering, often used in construction and engineering projects."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eddefd61217d789ac2863952eb4183a7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CAST-IN-PLACE PILE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cast-in-place pile refers to piles that are formed directly at their location within the ground through pouring concrete, commonly used for stable foundations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eddefd61217d789ac2863952eb4183a7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPOSITE PILE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Composite pile is a type of foundation element combining different materials or methods to enhance its performance and stability in various soil conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eddefd61217d789ac2863952eb4183a7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAND PILE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sand pile involves the use of sand as part of construction techniques, often used for temporary support structures or specific engineering applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eddefd61217d789ac2863952eb4183a7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHEET PILE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sheet pile is a method involving long interlocking steel sheets driven into the ground to form walls and provide support in excavation sites or coastal areas."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eddefd61217d789ac2863952eb4183a7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORED PILE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bored pile involves drilling holes in the ground, often reinforced with concrete, used for deep foundations in various soil conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eddefd61217d789ac2863952eb4183a7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CAISSON PILE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Caisson pile is a type of foundation element constructed by sinking watertight chambers into the ground and then filling them to create stable support structures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eddefd61217d789ac2863952eb4183a7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PILING (打樁工程)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Piling or '打樁工程' involves various methods for driving piles in the ground, including hammering, jacking, screwing, augering, boring, jetting, vibrating, and casting. It is a construction technique used to provide stable foundations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eddefd61217d789ac2863952eb4183a7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLACE (地方)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Place or '地方' refers to any location on land or water where work related to piling may occur, including various public spaces such as streets, parks, and beaches."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eddefd61217d789ac2863952eb4183a7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POWERED MECHANICAL EQUIPMENT (機動設備)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Powered mechanical equipment includes machines driven by electrical, chemical, thermal energy, compressed air, steam, hydraulic means, or any other form of power used in construction activities including piling operations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eddefd61217d789ac2863952eb4183a7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC PLACE (公眾地方)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Public places include various areas accessible to the public such as streets, parks, and beaches. These are defined under specific legal contexts but exclude certain commercial or social spaces."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eddefd61217d789ac2863952eb4183a7</data>
</node>
