<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION SITES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction Sites are places where building activities take place, subject to noise regulations as described in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-309604fa3106e70bedbe6af0b9f1e7a3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 295}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUILDING NOISE PERMIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Building Noise Permit is a document issued by the Supervisor allowing certain activities related to construction, subject to specific conditions and fees."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Building Noise Permit is a document required for construction sites during specific hours and on public holidays, ensuring compliance with noise regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Building Noise Permit is a document that regulates noise levels during construction activities and can be renewed or modified under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"建筑噪音许可证是一种允许在特定条件下进行施工的官方文件或授权。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5cbc913a82bac150b6a4b08953fa04d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-870a1a55ba8a2e008f20db40471921e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3df2a801b8139ee63d424aaec7ccaaa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-309604fa3106e70bedbe6af0b9f1e7a3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 295}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;撞擊式打樁工程&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"撞擊式打樁工程是一种特定类型的建筑工程活动，在此文本中提及需要建筑噪音许可证，并可能受到条件限制。"&lt;SEP&gt;"撞擊式打樁工程是一项涉及使用锤击方式进行桩基础施工的技术活动。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75a63fc1bac46279a18763a5809259bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9053b5bb875d947585293b13bbe5f25e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;公眾假日&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"公眾假日是指特定的公众假期，这些日子在法律和规定中被指定为休息日或特殊日期。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75a63fc1bac46279a18763a5809259bb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;非公眾假日&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"非公眾假日指的是除了公众假日之外的所有其他工作日。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75a63fc1bac46279a18763a5809259bb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISE FROM CONSTRUCTION SITES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Noise from construction sites is a specific type of event where regulations apply regarding the use of powered mechanical equipment and percussive piling at certain times."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c80a5edef13387c70f1ddbc0ac7e4acd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 796}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1183}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OWNER, TENANT OR OCCUPIER OF DOMESTIC PREMISES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Owner, tenant, or occupier of domestic premises refers to individuals who have the authority to perform construction work in their own residences without specific permits during permitted times and with limited equipment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 796}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1183}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISE REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Noise regulations are rules and laws that govern the levels of noise allowed during construction activities, often requiring specific permits for certain types of work such as percussive piling."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 971}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1214}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;$200,000 FINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A $200,000 fine is a severe monetary penalty imposed for repeated offenses related to construction noise violations, reflecting the seriousness with which such infractions are treated in legal and social contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"A $200,000 fine is the maximum financial penalty that may be levied as a result of subsequent convictions for non-compliance with noise abatement notices or related offenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"This refers to the second or subsequent conviction fine according to the amendment in 1994 s. 9."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5997efc3513d7a18a8e6ffade96f199b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 398}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1087}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DAILY FINE OF $20,000&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A daily fine of $20,000 is a continuous penalty applied for each day an offense continues, emphasizing strict enforcement and deterrence against ongoing violations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PORTABLE POWERED MECHANICAL EQUIPMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Portable powered mechanical equipment refers to handheld tools or devices used in construction that are not fixed or supported by any means other than being held manually."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION NOISE PERMIT REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction noise permit regulations refer to the legal and administrative frameworks governing the issuance, conditions, and enforcement of permits related to construction activities to control noise levels."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OFFENSE UNDER THIS SECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An offense under this section is a violation of noise regulations during construction, which can result in fines and legal penalties for individuals or entities involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION WORK WITHOUT PERMIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ACTIVITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction work performed without the necessary permits falls under specific regulatory categories that define when such activities are permissible and what conditions must be met to avoid criminal charges."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISE CONTROL MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Noise control measures are implied in the context of managing and regulating noise during construction activities through specific permit conditions or refusal processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Noise control measures refer to strategies, regulations, and practices implemented to manage and reduce noise levels during construction activities, often including the requirement for specific permits or time restrictions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-35333cbaccd9be2f64c80f729f9d5ffb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A comprehensive system of laws, regulations, and agreements governing employment practices, including reengagement scenarios as described."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal framework encompasses the set of laws, ordinances, and regulations that govern the recognition, enforcement, and execution of arbitral proceedings in Hong Kong or other jurisdictions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal framework encompasses the set of laws, regulations, and administrative procedures that govern various aspects related to construction work, including noise control measures and penalties for violations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal framework encompasses the set of laws, regulations, and principles that govern employment contracts and changes in business ownership, providing structured guidelines for how these events should be managed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal frameworks are comprehensive sets of laws, regulations, and procedures designed to govern specific areas such as international trade law, arbitration, evidence collection, etc., ensuring fair and consistent application across different jurisdictions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Legal Framework encompasses all laws and procedures governing dispute resolution in the context of construction contracts as described throughout this text, including nomination processes for arbitrators and timelines for initiating new adjudications."&lt;SEP&gt;"The legal framework encompasses the set of rules, statutes, and procedures that govern employment disputes and wage protection as described in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b57ac243904d2f7c387b12d47bb079b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71350626a55fa7b808223b0a1848a949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b219a4ff887909dc5fdeb24191ca220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 25}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 328}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION ACTIVITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY,ACTIVITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction Activities refer to work or projects involving building structures or infrastructure that may generate noise disturbances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Construction activities refer to any operations or processes involved in building or altering structures, which may be subject to specific regulatory controls regarding noise levels and permit requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Construction activities refer to the processes and operations involved in building structures, which are regulated by permits like the construction noise permit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-35333cbaccd9be2f64c80f729f9d5ffb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 25}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 328}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION PERMIT REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction permit requirements refer to the specific conditions and documentation needed for obtaining a permit that authorizes certain types of construction work, particularly in relation to noise levels and times of operation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISE REGULATIONS ENFORCEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Noise regulations enforcement refers to the processes and mechanisms by which authorities ensure compliance with laws and rules governing noise during construction activities, including penalties for violations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION WORK TIME RESTRICTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction work time restrictions refer to specific periods of the day or night when certain types of noisy construction activities are permitted or prohibited based on regulatory requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 971}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1214}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL PENALTIES FOR NOISE VIOLATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal penalties for noise violations include fines and other sanctions imposed by authorities for breaches of laws related to noise control during construction, reflecting the legal framework's emphasis on compliance and enforcement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION EQUIPMENT USAGE RESTRICTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction equipment usage restrictions refer to limitations placed on the types and quantities of machinery that can be used in certain conditions or times, particularly those related to noise control during construction activities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 971}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1214}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISE POLLUTION PREVENTION MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Noise pollution prevention measures are strategies and practices implemented to minimize the impact of noise from construction activities on surrounding areas, often including permit requirements for specific types of work or times of day."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION SITE REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction site regulations encompass a range of rules and guidelines governing various aspects of construction operations, including those related to noise control measures and the issuance of permits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISE PERMIT CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Noise permit conditions refer to specific requirements that must be met for obtaining or maintaining a permit authorizing certain types of noisy construction activities, often including time restrictions and equipment limitations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION NOISE CONTROL MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction noise control measures are strategies and practices implemented by regulatory bodies to manage and reduce the impact of noise from construction sites on surrounding areas, often involving permit requirements for specific types of work or times of day."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL ENFORCEMENT MECHANISMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal enforcement mechanisms refer to the processes and procedures used by authorities to ensure compliance with laws related to construction activities, including those concerning noise control measures and permits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 323}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISE REGULATIONS IMPLEMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Noise regulations implementation refers to the practical application of legal frameworks governing noise during construction activities, often involving permit requirements for specific types of work or times of day."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 323}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISE CONTROL REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Noise Control Regulations are rules or laws that regulate noise levels in construction work to prevent environmental and community disturbances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3df2a801b8139ee63d424aaec7ccaaa2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPERVISOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Supervisor is mentioned as someone who receives instructions from the Appeal Committee regarding the supervision of certain functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Supervisor is an individual or entity responsible for issuing Noise Control Permits and enforcing noise-related laws and regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Supervisor refers to the individual who oversees the issuance, modification, and revocation of Building Noise Permits based on specific criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"The supervisor refers to an individual or entity responsible for receiving and verifying notifications regarding noise compliance, playing a key role in enforcing regulatory measures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1740b8b8c7e777efdccf16fb8d3a59de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b856945c331d2adb7af607cfc2cd9f8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-870a1a55ba8a2e008f20db40471921e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3df2a801b8139ee63d424aaec7ccaaa2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 295}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNICAL MEMORANDUM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Technical Memorandum is a document issued by the Authority that sets out principles, procedures, guidelines, standards and limits for different types of percussive devices used in construction sites."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Technical Memorandum is a document issued under section 9(1) or 10(1), its contents are not to be questioned in any appeal under this Part."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Technical Memorandum, as referenced in the text, serves as a guideline for supervisors when considering applications for Noise Control Permits under Section 9(1)."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Technical Memorandum, issued under Section 9(1) or 10(1), contains content that cannot be questioned during an appeal hearing according to regulation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A technical memorandum is a document that may contain detailed information or instructions related to technology and its usage. It can be subject to revisions and legislative processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Technical Memorandums are documents setting principles, procedures, guidelines, standards and limits for predicting, measuring, assessing construction site noise, issuing permits, imposing conditions on permits, and determining compliance with permit conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Technical Memorandum是根据第9或10节发布的技术备忘录，在发布后需提交给立法会会议，并可能被修正。"&lt;SEP&gt;"Technical memoranda are documents issued under section 10 that define areas considered as noise sensitive receivers for the purpose of issuing abatement notices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Technical memorandum refers to documents issued by the Authority that provide technical guidelines and regulations for specific areas such as designated zones."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf98c13106216ee2990969e11aafbee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66c75321ad1bdf83283c50d27bc8b7e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3df2a801b8139ee63d424aaec7ccaaa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1740b8b8c7e777efdccf16fb8d3a59de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b856945c331d2adb7af607cfc2cd9f8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72a00cd6e89601305d8b400d5eef9c21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a89fc961d4c4ccbebf98c5fc224109&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d7aa41ab04a649aeb83e8611a7626ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 967}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1211}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISE FROM CONSTRUCTION WORK CONTRARY TO REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to carrying out construction work that violates noise control regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3df2a801b8139ee63d424aaec7ccaaa2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRST CONVICTION FINE AT LEVEL 6&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A first-time offender is liable for a fine of Level 6, as per the legal provision mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The event of first conviction for violating noise control regulations results in a fine at level 6 as per the law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e980522a1add368d13a641e842c93a83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3df2a801b8139ee63d424aaec7ccaaa2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECOND OR SUBSEQUENT CONVICTION FINE OF $200,000&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the penalty imposed upon second or subsequent convictions for violations related to construction work and noise control regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3df2a801b8139ee63d424aaec7ccaaa2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINUED OFFENCE FINE DAILY $20,000&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"In cases where an offence continues, a fine of $20,000 is levied daily until the violation ceases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3df2a801b8139ee63d424aaec7ccaaa2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;技術備忘錄&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"技術備忘錄是指根据第9(1)条不时发出的技术文件，用于指导建筑噪音许可证的申请和发放过程。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9053b5bb875d947585293b13bbe5f25e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;監督&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"監督是一个职位或角色，负责监督公职人员的行为是否符合规定，并在必要时向政務司司長报告违规情况。"&lt;SEP&gt;"監督是指负责监督和审批建筑噪音许可证的人或机构，在此文本中具体指的是相关监管人员。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9053b5bb875d947585293b13bbe5f25e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87b463683890ea692cb1904bcc74ba11</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;申請人&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"申請人是申请建築噪音許可證的个人或组织，文中提到他们可以提交申请并收到许可或拒绝的通知书。"&lt;SEP&gt;"申请人在文本中指代的是提出申请的个人或实体，具体身份未明。"&lt;SEP&gt;"申请人是指提出申请的个人或实体，具体身份未明。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9053b5bb875d947585293b13bbe5f25e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b88142ce6c5ae26fdcafd8cc6d03845</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 94}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REVOCATION OF BUILDING NOISE PERMIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Revocation of Building Noise Permit is an event where a permit can be withdrawn if certain conditions are violated or due to misleading application information."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-870a1a55ba8a2e008f20db40471921e5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 295}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNICAL MEMORANDA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Technical Memoranda are documents detailing standards or limits for noise, which can be amended by the Legislative Council and affect noise regulation policies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Technical Memoranda are documents issued by the Secretary that provide guidelines and standards related to noise regulations in specific areas or the entire territory."&lt;SEP&gt;"Technical Memoranda are documents issued from time to time under section 9(1) that guide the Authority in considering applications for construction noise permits, setting principles, procedures, and standards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Technical Memoranda are documents issued from time to time under section 9(1) that set out principles, procedures, guidelines, standards, and limits for issuing permits. They influence permit issuance decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Technical Memoranda are documents issued under section 10 that contain standards or limits prescribed for the purposes of regulating noise levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Technical Memoranda are documents setting out principles, procedures, guidelines, standards and limits for measuring and assessing noise from various sources, as well as issuing abatement notices. They also provide guidance on whether such notices are being complied with."&lt;SEP&gt;"Technical Memoranda are documents that may be amended by the Legislative Council, with their implementation dates determined based on certain conditions related to resolution passage or expiration of specific periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Technical Memoranda provide technical guidelines and support for issuing construction noise permits under specific conditions as outlined in section 9(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9af0d61962337f7b194e565a06d8c298&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac0836d4d9cd8980aca2b9281cb718a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c46d2bc84b41a7759d92a2cdbd5b2891&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bda701f7b69fa34380775a0f86642cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86dd5816dd56bd7bc4f23ec93e31f0f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bc7b3a739542b0651749e63bbf9e5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e7556ee34515464c79e90674823db90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 298}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 985}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPLICATION FOR CONSTRUCTION NOISE PERMIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Application for Construction Noise Permit is a formal request made in prescribed form and manner accompanied by a fee, submitted to the Authority for consideration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c46d2bc84b41a7759d92a2cdbd5b2891</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 971}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1213}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPLICANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Applicant refers to a party initiating proceedings before an arbitral tribunal, similar to Claimant but possibly used more broadly for any type of application made within the context of arbitration."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Applicant refers to the employer or occupier who may apply for the review of a suspension notice within 14 days after receiving it."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Applicant is an individual or entity seeking a construction noise permit, who will receive written notice regarding the decision on their application."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Applicant is the individual or entity applying for a warrant under the Employment Ordinance, seeking recovery of owed wages from their former employer who intends to leave Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Applicant refers to one party in a dispute who initiates arbitration proceedings and must submit an application as per regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The applicant, an employee, initiates the application under section 67 of the Employment Ordinance to seek a warrant against their employer who has allegedly failed to pay wages or other entitlements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-67218fecb16f152219fae29882c0cc1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bda701f7b69fa34380775a0f86642cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78c6c93b249203abfbdb5ba16af8eb78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8247282749bd85cb6d48e946a81b3c1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39b02ac25884a8c6102243f2b93f0c03</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 292}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC INTEREST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT, SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Public interest is the overarching concern that may necessitate actions by the Authority beyond regular permit conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d7aa41ab04a649aeb83e8611a7626ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 971}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1213}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CANCELLATION OF CONSTRUCTION NOISE PERMIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cancellation of a construction noise permit refers to the action taken by the Authority when certain conditions are met as outlined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d7aa41ab04a649aeb83e8611a7626ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 967}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1211}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMENDMENT OR VARIATION OF CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Amendment or variation of conditions involves changes made to an existing construction noise permit based on specific criteria such as contravention of conditions, misleading information, etc."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d7aa41ab04a649aeb83e8611a7626ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 967}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1211}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPOSITION OF NEW CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Imposition of new conditions refers to the Authority adding additional requirements to a construction noise permit when necessary."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d7aa41ab04a649aeb83e8611a7626ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 967}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1211}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIFIED LOCATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Specified location is any particular place where certain actions related to the construction noise permit are required, such as displaying the permit or limiting equipment usage."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d7aa41ab04a649aeb83e8611a7626ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 971}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1213}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAXIMUM NOISE LEVELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY, MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maximum noise levels refer to specific decibel limits that must not be exceeded at designated locations during specified times."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d7aa41ab04a649aeb83e8611a7626ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 299}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 991}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIFIED TIME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT, MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Specified time is a particular period during which certain construction activities are allowed or restricted based on permit conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d7aa41ab04a649aeb83e8611a7626ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 796}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1183}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIFIED RANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION, CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Specified range is an area defined by the Authority where certain rules or conditions apply, often related to noise management in construction activities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d7aa41ab04a649aeb83e8611a7626ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 144}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 638}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HONG KONG TERRITORY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hong Kong territory refers to the broader geographical and administrative context within which technical memorandums may be issued for different areas including specified ranges."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Hong Kong Territory refers to the entire region under consideration for noise regulations as detailed in Technical Memoranda."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-86dd5816dd56bd7bc4f23ec93e31f0f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d7aa41ab04a649aeb83e8611a7626ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 144}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 638}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISE REGULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Noise regulation refers to guidelines and standards for managing construction site noises as detailed in Technical Memoranda."&lt;SEP&gt;"The term 'noise regulation' refers to a set of rules and procedures for controlling noise levels as outlined in Chapter 400, which includes the issuance of notices by appointed officers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a63521ff775998da1314db4dd547a7d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86dd5816dd56bd7bc4f23ec93e31f0f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 144}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 638}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUILDING SITE NOISE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Building Site Noise is a specific type of noise regulated by the Secretary through technical memorandums, involving prediction, measurement, evaluation, issuance of permits, conditions application and enforcement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-86dd5816dd56bd7bc4f23ec93e31f0f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 299}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 988}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERCUSSIVE DEVICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Percussive Devices are types of equipment used in percussive piling and may be subject to different principles, procedures, guidelines, standards and limits as per the Technical Memorandums."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-72a00cd6e89601305d8b400d5eef9c21</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 971}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1214}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNICAL MEMORANDUM (NOISE FROM PLACES OTHER THAN DOMESTIC PREMISES, PUBLIC PLACES OR CONSTRUCTION SITES)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is another type of Technical Memorandum that specifies the measurement and assessment of noises from places outside domestic premises, public places, or construction sites."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-71a89fc961d4c4ccbebf98c5fc224109</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 381}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISE EMANATING FROM PLACES OTHER THAN DOMESTIC PREMISES, PUBLIC PLACES OR CONSTRUCTION SITES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the occurrence of noises in locations outside domestic premises, public places, or construction sites that are regulated by specific Technical Memoranda."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-71a89fc961d4c4ccbebf98c5fc224109</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 381}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNICAL MEMORANDUM (NOISE MEASUREMENT)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A specific type of Technical Memorandum that outlines the procedures, guidelines, standards, and limits for measuring and assessing noises in places other than domestic premises, public places or construction sites."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-71a89fc961d4c4ccbebf98c5fc224109</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 320}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPERVISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Supervision refers to an overseeing body that has authority over public officers, including granting them certain powers through authorization documents."&lt;SEP&gt;"The role of supervision is performed by an individual who ensures compliance with noise reduction notifications based on Technical Memoranda during the measurement and assessment process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The term 'supervision' refers to the authority responsible for overseeing notifications and their delivery methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"监督指的是有权拒发建筑噪音许可或者批准相关活动的人，其行为可能影响到上诉人的权益。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5cbc913a82bac150b6a4b08953fa04d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a63521ff775998da1314db4dd547a7d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60c17dd78d73fb0b81ce0ba9e3153396&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a89fc961d4c4ccbebf98c5fc224109</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 320}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1997年第362號法律公告&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This legal notice made revisions to existing regulations, including changes related to technical memorandums for noise management in various locations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-71a89fc961d4c4ccbebf98c5fc224109</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1999年第78號第7條修訂&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This revision updated the provisions regarding Technical Memoranda and their availability for public inspection at government offices during business hours."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-71a89fc961d4c4ccbebf98c5fc224109</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGISLATIVE COUNCIL (LEGCO)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Legislative Council is a location where technical memorandums related to noise are submitted for review, and decisions can be made regarding their revisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ac0836d4d9cd8980aca2b9281cb718a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 376}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CIRCULATION IN THE GAZETTE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Circulating Technical Memoranda in the Gazette is an event that ensures public awareness of these documents through official publication."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ac0836d4d9cd8980aca2b9281cb718a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 298}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 985}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBMISSION TO LEGISLATIVE COUNCIL MEETING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Submitting Technical Memoranda to a Legislative Council meeting for review and potential revision is an important procedural step involving legislative oversight."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ac0836d4d9cd8980aca2b9281cb718a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 376}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DECISION-MAKING PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A decision-making process involves deliberations and resolutions by members of the Legislative Council regarding the revisions or extensions of Technical Memoranda."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE LONG官&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Administrative Long官 refers to a high-ranking official in Hong Kong's administration who is part of decision-making processes related to international legal agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Administrative Long官 refers to an official who has the authority to grant extensions or allowances for certain procedures, such as publishing in the gazette."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Administrative Long官 refers to the Chief Executive who has the power to enact regulations with the Executive Council."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2237564658a1150599559d04fcf04a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-603a9b33a6e3900af70fd439592326ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 155}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 663}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GAZETTE PUBLICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gazette publication is a formal process where decisions and resolutions are officially recorded and made public after being passed by the Legislative Council within 14 days of passage or an extended period granted by the Administrative Long官."&lt;SEP&gt;"Publication of specified forms in the Gazette is an event where the Commissioner disseminates official documents for public knowledge."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe986d49a20cfdf5d43e02699374c050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 607}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGISLATIVE SESSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION,ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A legislative session refers to the meetings held by the Legislative Council for conducting official business. It includes specific dates and agendas as per procedural rules."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROCEDURAL RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Procedural rules are guidelines that govern how decisions or actions should be carried out, particularly in legislative processes such as those involving Technical Memoranda."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REVISION OF TECHNICAL MEMORANDUM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The revision of a technical memorandum involves changes made to the document based on decision-making and approval by the Legislative Council."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXTENSION OF DEADLINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An extension of deadline refers to postponing the original due date for actions related to Technical Memoranda, as decided upon by legislative bodies or administrative officials."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRST MEETING AFTER EXTENSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The first meeting after an extension is a specific session held following any delays in scheduling, where decisions and discussions continue regarding Technical Memoranda."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECOND LEGISLATIVE SITTING OF THE NEXT SESSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the second sitting or meeting within the next legislative session, which could be crucial for further deliberations on technical memorandums after initial extensions have been made."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRST MEETING AFTER EXTENSION (NEXT SESSION)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The first meeting following an extension in a new legislative session is where discussions and decisions continue regarding Technical Memoranda that were initially delayed or extended."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESOLUTION BY LEGISLATIVE COUNCIL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A resolution passed by the Legislative Council involves formal decisions on matters such as extending deadlines for technical memorandums, ensuring all procedural steps are followed in legislative processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;14-DAY PERIOD FOR PUBLICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The 14-day period is a specific timeframe within which resolutions and decisions must be published officially after being passed by the Legislative Council."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 607}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE LONG官'S AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON,ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Administrative Long官 has authority over certain procedural matters such as granting extensions for gazette publications or other administrative processes related to legislative actions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNICAL MEMORANDUM ISSUANCE PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The process of issuing a technical memorandum involves multiple steps including decision-making, revisions, and formal publication through the Legislative Council and relevant authorities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGISLATIVE SESSION CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Calculating legislative sessions for time-related decisions such as deadlines or extensions involves specific dates and procedural rules that must be adhered to in order to ensure proper functioning of the legislative body."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNICAL MEMORANDUM DECISION-MAKING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The decision-making process related to technical memorandums includes various steps from initial issuance through revisions, extensions, and final publication or approval by the Legislative Council."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGISLATIVE PROCEDURE RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Procedural rules in legislation govern how decisions are made regarding Technical Memoranda, including timelines for actions such as issuing, revising, extending deadlines, and publishing through official channels."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNICAL MEMORANDUM EXTENSION MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The mechanism for extending the deadline of a technical memorandum involves formal decision-making processes within legislative bodies to ensure compliance with procedural rules and administrative guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGISLATIVE COUNCIL MEETING DATES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Meeting dates of the Legislative Council are specific times when decisions on Technical Memoranda can be made, including initial issuances, revisions, extensions, and final publications or approvals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNICAL MEMORANDUM REVISION TIMELINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The timeline for revising a technical memorandum involves multiple steps from initial issuance through various stages of decision-making, extension requests, and formal publication processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE PROCEDURES FOR TECHNICAL MEMORANDA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Administrative procedures related to technical memorandums include guidelines on how decisions are made regarding revisions, extensions, deadlines, and final publications through legislative bodies and relevant authorities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNICAL MEMORANDUM DECISION PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The decision process for a technical memorandum involves multiple stages including issuance, revision, extension requests, and formal publication or approval by the Legislative Council following specific procedural rules."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGISLATIVE BODY AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION,PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Authority of legislative bodies such as the Legislative Council includes making decisions on Technical Memoranda, extending deadlines, issuing revisions, and ensuring proper procedures are followed in all related processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNICAL MEMORANDUM PUBLICATION MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The publication mechanism for a technical memorandum involves formal steps including issuance, revision, extension requests, decision-making by legislative bodies, and final publication through official channels such as the gazette."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROCEDURAL GUIDELINES FOR TECHNICAL MEMORANDA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Guidelines on procedural matters related to technical memorandums include rules for issuing, revising, extending deadlines, decision-making processes within legislative bodies, and final publication or approval through official channels."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNICAL MEMORANDUM DECISION-MAKING AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON,ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Decision-making authority over Technical Memoranda involves formal procedures managed by the Legislative Council and relevant administrative officials to ensure compliance with procedural rules and guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGISLATIVE PROCESS FOR TECHNICAL MEMORANDUMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The legislative process for technical memorandums includes stages such as issuance, revision, extension requests, decision-making by the Legislative Council, and final publication or approval through official channels following specific procedural rules."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d890da037d9bf78ea552ca6dad1de5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;立法會會議&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"立法會會議是指在應用於計算時間時，指立法會開始舉行會議的日期。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66c75321ad1bdf83283c50d27bc8b7e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITTING OF THE LEGISLATIVE COUNCIL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"sitting of the Legislative Council是立法会会议的特定时段，在此期间可能审议技术备忘录并作出相关决定。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66c75321ad1bdf83283c50d27bc8b7e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 972}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SESSION OF THE LEGISLATIVE COUNCIL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"session of the Legislative Council是立法会会议的一个时间段，在此期间进行正式的议事活动。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66c75321ad1bdf83283c50d27bc8b7e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISE REDUCTION NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Noise reduction notices are formal communications sent to individuals responsible for generating noise that instruct them on reducing it according to specified standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e7556ee34515464c79e90674823db90</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 298}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 985}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;发出噪音地方的业主、租户、占用人或掌管人&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the individuals or entities responsible for a place where noise is emitted and are subject to noise reduction notifications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae9659112e4d17d9b06e19d0d8a43760</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;消减噪音通知书&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Noise Reduction Notice is a document that instructs recipients on how to reduce noise within specified periods and conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae9659112e4d17d9b06e19d0d8a43760</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;监督&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Supervision refers to the authority or individual responsible for overseeing compliance with noise reduction notices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae9659112e4d17d9b06e19d0d8a43760</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISE ABATEMENT NOTICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Noise abatement notices are documents issued by an authority to address noise issues, indicating a regulatory tool used in managing and controlling noise pollution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1740b8b8c7e777efdccf16fb8d3a59de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 967}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1210}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 13(1)(B) NOT YET IN OPERATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event refers to a specific clause within legislation that has not yet come into effect, indicating ongoing legal processes or pending regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1740b8b8c7e777efdccf16fb8d3a59de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 969}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOMESTIC PREMISES, PUBLIC PLACE, CONSTRUCTION SITE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These locations are specified as exceptions where noise abatement notices do not apply, highlighting the scope and limitations of such notifications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1740b8b8c7e777efdccf16fb8d3a59de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRST TIME CONVICTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"First time conviction refers to a legal outcome when someone is found guilty for the first offense under certain regulations, with specific penalties outlined."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1740b8b8c7e777efdccf16fb8d3a59de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 295}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECOND OR SUBSEQUENT CONVICTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Second or subsequent convictions refer to repeated offenses leading to increased penalties as specified in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1740b8b8c7e777efdccf16fb8d3a59de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 295}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CRIME OF NON-COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CRIME"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The crime of non-compliance refers to actions that violate noise abatement notices, punishable by fines and potential daily incremental penalties for ongoing violations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1740b8b8c7e777efdccf16fb8d3a59de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BOOKED WRITTEN NOTIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A written notification is a document required under certain clauses to inform the supervisor about compliance with specific regulations or standards related to noise management."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1740b8b8c7e777efdccf16fb8d3a59de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1994 YEAR 2 ORDINANCE AMENDMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event denotes changes made to the legislation in 1994 through the second ordinance amendment, indicating historical legal modifications related to noise control regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1740b8b8c7e777efdccf16fb8d3a59de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 969}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2021 YEAR 2 EDIT RECORD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The document refers to an edit record from 2021 that updates or modifies existing laws and regulations concerning noise abatement notices and associated penalties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1740b8b8c7e777efdccf16fb8d3a59de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 969}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISE ABATEMENT NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Noise Abatement Notice is a document served by The Authority to control the operation of certain systems, particularly those causing noise disturbances."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Noise Abatement Notice is an official document served by the Authority to require individuals or entities to reduce noise levels and comply with specific standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9af0d61962337f7b194e565a06d8c298</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 162}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISE SENSITIVE RECEIVER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Noise Sensitive Receiver is a place where any person, other than the source of the noise, may experience annoyance due to excessive noise."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9af0d61962337f7b194e565a06d8c298</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 298}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 985}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLANT, MACHINERY, VEHICLE, EQUIPMENT OR PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are specific sources that can generate noise and must be operated in accordance with conditions specified in a Noise Abatement Notice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9af0d61962337f7b194e565a06d8c298</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 162}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Authority is an organization that can authorize public officers to exercise certain powers as specified in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Authority is an organization that can issue and revise codes of practice for industries, providing guidance on good management practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Authority is an organization that can serve noise abatement notices and cancel or vary requirements therein."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddc943ee0b925d64ce2ff3b4b8fcc772&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f02d6ddba7929fb360049bae6cab88e4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 144}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 637}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTRUDER ALARM SYSTEMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Intruder Alarm Systems are security devices that trigger audible signals when activated and are subject to regulations regarding their operation to minimize noise disturbance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTROL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Control refers to the management or supervision of Intruder Alarm Systems, ensuring they comply with specified operational requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;21 DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"21 days is the minimum period from when a notice takes effect until it becomes enforceable after being served on any person."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 162}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OFFENCE UNDER SUBSECTION (6)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Offence under Subsection (6) is the act of failing to comply with any requirement in a Noise Abatement Notice, which can lead to legal consequences including fines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (7)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (7)(a) describes an event where first conviction for non-compliance results in a fine at level 6."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 294}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 984}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (7)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (7)(b) describes an event where subsequent convictions result in significantly higher fines, up to $200,000."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 398}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1087}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINE OF $20,000 PER DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Fine of $20,000 per day is the penalty for continuing non-compliance after an initial conviction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 162}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTRUDER ALARM SYSTEMS NOISE ABATEMENT NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Intruder Alarm Systems Noise Abatement Notice is a specific type of notice issued by The Authority regarding the operation of intruder alarm systems to minimize noise disturbance, subject to detailed regulations and penalties for non-compliance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTRUDER ALARM SYSTEM INSTALLATION CONTROL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The role involves managing Intruder Alarm Systems in such a way that they comply with noise abatement requirements within 15 minutes of triggering an alarm signal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUTOMATIC DEVICE FOR SIGNAL STOPPAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Automatic Device is required to stop any audible signals from intruder alarm systems after being triggered, ensuring compliance with noise regulations and minimizing disturbance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;15 MINUTES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"15 minutes is the maximum time allowed for an automatic device to stop any audible signal emitted by an Intruder Alarm System once it has been activated."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;$20,000 DAILY FINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A $20,000 daily fine is the additional financial penalty that can be imposed if an offense continues after initial conviction for non-compliance with noise abatement notices or related offenses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MISLEADING STATEMENT OFFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Making a misleading statement in notifications to The Authority regarding compliance with Noise Abatement Notices is considered an offense and can result in fines at level 5 as part of the legal consequences for non-compliance or false reporting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 371}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1072}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTRUDER ALARM SYSTEMS REGULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Intruder Alarm Systems Regulations are a set of guidelines and requirements established by The Authority to control noise emissions from these systems, ensuring compliance through various enforcement mechanisms including fines and penalties for non-compliance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTRUDER ALARM SYSTEM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An intruder alarm system is a device designed to detect and alert of unauthorized access or intrusion, often with audible signals. It can be installed in premises, vehicles, or nearby locations."&lt;SEP&gt;"An intruder alarm system is a device installed in vehicles to prevent unauthorized access and emit audible signals when triggered by direct physical contact with the vehicle. It must comply with specific regulations regarding signal emission and cessation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db5cb02beaa944fb9a1df344fab4d2a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e18098fcb5747dd72313d5ee7912acb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 299}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 989}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VEHICLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A vehicle is a mobile device used for transportation and can have an intruder alarm system installed inside it."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db5cb02beaa944fb9a1df344fab4d2a9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 375}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTRATION OWNER OF VEHICLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The registration owner of a vehicle refers to the individual or entity that legally owns the vehicle and has responsibilities related to its intruder alarm system."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db5cb02beaa944fb9a1df344fab4d2a9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 299}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 989}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIRECT SUBSTANTIAL CONTACT WITH VEHICLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES,MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Direct substantial contact with vehicle is defined as any interaction that physically touches or significantly affects the vehicle, which can trigger an audible signal from the intruder alarm system."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db5cb02beaa944fb9a1df344fab4d2a9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 375}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOISY PRODUCTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Noisy Products are items or devices that emit sound levels higher than prescribed limits, subject to regulatory control under relevant laws and regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Noisy products are items that produce excessive noise and may be regulated under specific standards or laws designed to control such emissions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0549d4328512324b45d1f4f3e4461ed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e18098fcb5747dd72313d5ee7912acb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 299}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 990}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATION ON INTRUDER ALARM SYSTEMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The regulation on intruder alarm systems is a set of rules governing the installation, operation, and compliance with certain conditions for these devices in vehicles. It ensures that alarms are effective but also considerate to avoid unnecessary disturbances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2e18098fcb5747dd72313d5ee7912acb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 299}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 989}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTROL OF NOISY PRODUCTS REGULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Control of Noisy Products regulation refers to a set of standards or laws designed to manage the production and sale of products that generate excessive noise, ensuring they meet certain criteria for environmental protection and public health."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2e18098fcb5747dd72313d5ee7912acb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 373}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1073}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTROL OF NOISY PRODUCTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Control of Noisy Products refers to the regulation and management of products that produce noise exceeding specified standards in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0549d4328512324b45d1f4f3e4461ed4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 299}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 990}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS OPERATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Business Operations refer to commercial activities involving the importation, manufacture, supply, offer for sale, or display of regulated noisy products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Business operations refer to the activities conducted by businesses, potentially affected by decisions regarding construction noise permits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0549d4328512324b45d1f4f3e4461ed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35333cbaccd9be2f64c80f729f9d5ffb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 299}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 990}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;犯罪&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"犯罪指的是违反相关规定的行动，可能导致法律惩罚。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2027fc353aa43ba4dd84704864f404ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;產品&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"产品是指为施行本部而订明的产品，可能涉及安装有特定指示牌、标签或其他与发出噪音有关的标志的产品。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2027fc353aa43ba4dd84704864f404ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;訂明的指示牌、標籤或標誌&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
