<node id="&quot;NOISE CONTROL MEASURES IMPLEMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Noise control measures implementation refers to the practical application of guidelines or terms provided in Technical Memoranda issued under section 9(1) for controlling construction site noise levels."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-35333cbaccd9be2f64c80f729f9d5ffb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS OPERATIONS IMPACT ANALYSIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Business operations impact analysis is a process that evaluates how decisions on construction noise permits may affect business activities, including operational hours and methods during specific times or days."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-35333cbaccd9be2f64c80f729f9d5ffb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERMIT ISSUANCE PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCEDURE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Permit issuance procedures refer to the formal processes through which applications for construction noise permits are evaluated by the Authority before issuing, amending, varying, or canceling such permits related to percussive piling activities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-35333cbaccd9be2f64c80f729f9d5ffb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS OPERATIONS DURING HOLIDAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Business operations during holidays refers to how businesses may be impacted differently on days when specific construction noise permit restrictions do not apply due to being general holidays."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-35333cbaccd9be2f64c80f729f9d5ffb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 798}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERMIT CANCELLATION PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCEDURE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Permit cancellation procedures refer to the formal processes through which a previously issued construction noise permit can be canceled by the Authority, including grounds for such cancellations and potential impacts on business operations during specific times or days."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-35333cbaccd9be2f64c80f729f9d5ffb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS CONTINUITY PLANNING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Business continuity planning involves strategies and actions taken by businesses to ensure operational stability despite disruptions from decisions on construction noise permits affecting their activities during specific hours or days."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-35333cbaccd9be2f64c80f729f9d5ffb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 291}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 979}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPELLANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Appellant refers to any person who wishes to appeal under this section, facing potential economic hardship or other conditions that allow them to challenge a notice."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Appellant refers to the party seeking an appeal against decisions related to construction noise permits or their conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"While not explicitly mentioned, 'appellant' can be inferred as another term for a party making a claim in an arbitration context, similar to respondent but from the opposing perspective."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7c9d82cf88dd3738b34743e6dd94bc9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 296}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPELLATE COMMITTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appeal Commission refers to the committee or organization where appeals against authority decisions are heard."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 296}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 8 NOTICE OF DECISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Section 8 Notice of Decision is a formal notification sent to the appellant regarding the authority's decision on their application or permit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 973}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNICAL MEMORANDA UNDER SECTION 9(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These documents provide technical guidelines and support for issuing construction noise permits as per specific conditions outlined in section 9(1)."&lt;SEP&gt;"These documents provide technical guidelines for issuing construction noise permits and are referenced in relation to the validity of notices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 296}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 13 NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Section 13 Notice is a formal notification sent under specific conditions as outlined in section 13(1) or (4)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 296}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 16 NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Section 16 Notice is another type of formal notification that can be issued under the terms specified in sections 16(1)(a) and (b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 296}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPERVISORY AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Supervisory Authority refers to the body responsible for overseeing compliance with regulations related to construction noise permits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 971}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1213}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNICAL MEMORANDA UNDER SECTION 10(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These documents provide technical guidelines for sending notifications according to specific conditions outlined in section 10(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 973}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTIFICATION DELIVERY ISSUES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES,CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Issues related to the delivery of notices and their compliance with specified formats or content."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 13 NOTICE UNDER (C)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Section 13(1)(c) Notice is a specific type of notification sent based on certain conditions as outlined in section 13(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 16 NOTICE UNDER (A) OR (B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Section 16(1)(a) or (b) Notice is a specific type of notification sent based on certain conditions as outlined in section 16."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPELLANT'S BUSINESS OPERATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY,ACTIVITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The appellant’s business operations are the core activities and practices conducted by the party appealing against decisions related to construction noise permits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ECONOMIC HARDSHIP DUE TO COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES,CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This concept refers to financial difficulties that could arise from compliance with permit conditions or decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 212}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTIFICATION FORMAT ISSUES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES,CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Issues related to the format or content of notices and their compliance with specified standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ECONOMIC HARDSHIP DUE TO PERMIT CANCELLATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES,CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This concept refers to financial difficulties that could arise from the cancellation or non-issuance of a permit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ECONOMIC HARDSHIP DUE TO NON-COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES,CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This concept refers to financial difficulties that could arise from non-compliance with permit conditions or decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ECONOMIC HARDSHIP DUE TO PERMIT CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES,CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This concept refers to financial difficulties that could arise from specific conditions attached to a permit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ECONOMIC HARDSHIP DUE TO PERMIT REFUSAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES,CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This concept refers to financial difficulties that could arise from a refusal to issue or cancel a permit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNICAL MEMORANDA ISSUED UNDER SECTION 10(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Technical Memoranda are documents that provide grounds for the service of a notice under section 13(1)(c)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a461efee858ab690fe058321b8a0025</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 291}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 976}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 13 OR 16&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL PROVISION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sections 13 and 16 are legal provisions that describe the service of notices and the grounds for appeal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a461efee858ab690fe058321b8a0025</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 291}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 976}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPEAL COMMISSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Appeal Commission is an organization responsible for deciding on appeals according to the provisions of a certain section."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Appeal Commission is an organization where parties can appeal decisions made by the Commissioner regarding suspension notices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7c9d82cf88dd3738b34743e6dd94bc9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8247282749bd85cb6d48e946a81b3c1e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 296}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE OF APPEAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Notice of Appeal is the prescribed form and manner in which an appellant lodges their appeal within 21 days after receiving a related notice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7c9d82cf88dd3738b34743e6dd94bc9e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 296}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE CHIEF OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Administrative Chief Officer appoints members to the Appeal Commission, including the chairman and other commissioners."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7c9d82cf88dd3738b34743e6dd94bc9e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGIONAL COURT JUDGE QUALIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A person qualified as a Regional Court Judge according to The Regional Court Ordinance (Chapter 336 of Laws of Hong Kong) is eligible for appointment as the chairman of the Appeal Commission."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7c9d82cf88dd3738b34743e6dd94bc9e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPEAL COMMISSION CHAIRPERSON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The chairperson of the Appeal Commission, appointed by the Administrative Chief Officer from qualified Regional Court Judges, leads the commission in hearing and deciding on appeals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7c9d82cf88dd3738b34743e6dd94bc9e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMISSION MEMBERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A group of people appointed by the Administrative Chief Officer to serve as members of the Appeal Commission for hearing appeals according to specific provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7c9d82cf88dd3738b34743e6dd94bc9e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC INTEREST STATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The notice may contain a statement indicating that suspension in its operation would be contrary to public interest, affecting the decision on whether to suspend the notice's operation during an appeal process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7c9d82cf88dd3738b34743e6dd94bc9e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 296}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE SUSPENSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Suspension of the notice's operation is considered if it does not harm public interest and can be lifted once the appeal is resolved or abandoned."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7c9d82cf88dd3738b34743e6dd94bc9e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE 1998 AMENDMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Amendments made in 1998 to certain provisions, including changes related to appointment terms of commission members."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7c9d82cf88dd3738b34743e6dd94bc9e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2024 AMENDMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Further amendments introduced in 2024 affecting the composition and operation of the Appeal Commission."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7c9d82cf88dd3738b34743e6dd94bc9e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE CHIEF OFFICER'S APPOINTMENT POWER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Administrative Chief Officer has the authority to appoint members of the Appeal Commission, including its chairman and other commissioners, based on relevant qualifications and criteria."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7c9d82cf88dd3738b34743e6dd94bc9e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERM OF OFFICE FOR COMMISSIONERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Commissioners have a term limit of 3 years but can be reappointed, indicating structured tenure management within the commission structure."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7c9d82cf88dd3738b34743e6dd94bc9e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISTRICT JUDGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A District Judge is a judicial officer who can issue warrants in accordance with the Second Schedule, particularly for applications related to wage arrears or other moneys owed under employment contracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"A District Judge is a judicial officer who handles applications under certain paragraphs of the Employment Ordinance, such as those involving sureties and bonds."&lt;SEP&gt;"A District Judge is a judicial officer who has the authority to issue warrants, hear applications, and make orders regarding employers who are suspected of evading debt payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"A District Judge is a judicial officer who will hear and decide on the case brought against the employer regarding security requirements under the Employment Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A District Judge is an individual qualified under Section 5 of the District Court Ordinance (Cap. 336) who can be appointed to act as Chairman when necessary."&lt;SEP&gt;"District Judge is a legal authority that can be called upon regarding employment disputes or payments as per the text's conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"District Judge is a role qualified for appointment as the Chairman of the Appeal Board according to the District Court Ordinance (Cap. 336)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The District Judge is responsible for ordering bonds, discharging warrants, and releasing employers or sureties based on certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-86f4348a1c4677448f8348eacdd112bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c65da5be1610c7210df4b6d277a43ffa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74275f2bcd7afd62cd2b27056407d1e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3b75037d48822c36000fbac9c3ce438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb63fc0b243ea63257ead6ec4cad1834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af8bb2bf50613f2cddc9c821004e6e7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edaba831bd1e0154426defdca143f061&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 333}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1020}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPEAL COMMITTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Appeal Committee is responsible for hearing appeals related to the exercise of functions granted by this regulation, issuing instructions to supervisors who must comply with these instructions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b856945c331d2adb7af607cfc2cd9f8b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 295}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPEAL HEARING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Appeal Hearing is a process where the Appeal Committee hears appeals related to specific decisions or regulations and can determine, overturn, or change those decisions as well as decide on litigation fees in a fair manner."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b856945c331d2adb7af607cfc2cd9f8b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 295}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;上诉委员会&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"上诉委员会是一个有权审理和确定、推翻或变更针对决定或规定的上诉案件的机构。它还负责处理藐视法庭的行为，并可以向原审法院提交证据以证明某人犯有藐视法庭罪。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-252ecead925f3c7e306c921cf96537d5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;原审法院&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"原审法院是与上诉委员会平行的一个司法机构，负责审理和判决由上诉委员会转来的案件中的诉讼费用问题以及处理有关藐视法庭的指控。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-252ecead925f3c7e306c921cf96537d5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;证人&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"证人在上诉过程中扮演重要角色，他们可以被正式传唤作证，并享有在原审法院中出席民事程序聆讯时所享有的豁免和特权。如果拒绝履行职责，则可能被视为藐视法庭。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-252ecead925f3c7e306c921cf96537d5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;藐视法庭罪&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"藐视法庭罪是指个人或实体违反法庭命令、规则或其他法律义务的行为，上诉委员会可以向原审法院提交证据以证明某人犯有此罪，并由原审法院进行审理和判决。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-252ecead925f3c7e306c921cf96537d5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT OF LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Court of Law is mentioned as a reference point for evidence admissibility rules that may not apply during adjudication proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Court of Law is referenced as a comparison for admissibility standards, where evidence and statements may differ in what can be admitted before the Appeal Board."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d30ea89e5165c3d71c14d8648bf53596&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf98c13106216ee2990969e11aafbee7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 804}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1185}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 5 OF THE DISTRICT COURT ORDINANCE (CAP. 336)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 5 of this ordinance is used to qualify individuals appointed by the Chief Executive to act as Chairman, providing a legal basis for their appointment and functions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 21(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 21(1) refers to a provision that appoints individuals to hear appeals under this Part, with potential replacements if the original appointee cannot perform his functions due to certain reasons."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 20(4)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 20(4) is referenced as part of the panel from which a replacement can be appointed for an individual who cannot continue performing their duties, ensuring continuity in appeal hearings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPPLEMENTARY PROVISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Supplementary Provisions are amendments or additions to existing laws that provide further details on how specific roles and procedures should be handled."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 21(1) OF THE ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This section is part of a legal document providing rules for appointing individuals to hear appeals, with potential replacements if necessary."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 20(4) OF THE ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This section provides details on the panel from which replacements can be appointed when an individual cannot continue performing their duties as part of appeal hearings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PANEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Panel mentioned in Section 20(4) is a group of individuals who may be called upon to replace someone unable to perform their functions, ensuring the continuity and proper functioning of legal proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 291}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 976}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPOINTING AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The authority that can appoint individuals as Chairman or District Judges includes both the Chief Executive and those qualified under Section 5 of the District Court Ordinance (Cap. 336)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 291}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 976}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 20(4) OF THE ORDINANCE - PANEL MEMBERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The panel members mentioned in this section are individuals who can be appointed to replace others, ensuring that legal proceedings continue smoothly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPEAL HEARING CONTINUITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ensuring continuity during appeal hearings is a key aspect of the provisions discussed, especially when dealing with absences or incapacitation of key personnel such as Chairmen and appointed individuals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 291}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 977}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGIONAL COURT (CAP. 336)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Regional Court mentioned in Section 5 refers to a legal body where District Judges are qualified for appointment, indicating its importance in the judicial system."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISTRICT JUDGE APPOINTMENT PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The process of appointing individuals as District Judges under Section 5 of the District Court Ordinance (Cap. 336) is described, highlighting qualifications and roles involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPEAL BOARD HEARING PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCEDURE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Procedures for hearings before the Appeal Board are outlined, including immunities and privileges granted to witnesses similar to those in civil proceedings at the Court of First Instance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 291}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 977}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUTHORIZED OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Authorized Officer is a person who has the power to exercise certain powers and serve notices, conduct measurements, inspections, tests, affix labels, and enter premises with or without consent."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Authorized Officer refers to a person who can enter places without warrant under certain conditions, such as believing an offense has been or is being committed."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Authorized officer refers to a person who has been given authority by The Authority to perform specific functions and exercises certain powers under this Part."&lt;SEP&gt;"An authorized officer is a public official who has been given permission by the Authority to handle complaints or information related to offenses against the Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddc943ee0b925d64ce2ff3b4b8fcc772&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddee27cc5f92142cd2814225d68af96b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8024a8a38a1cf4faa9e3a31112f97d7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7d7ad99b2b6121e30cb678dc647a4a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 314}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1002}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTRATION OF PERSONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 177)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Registration of Persons Ordinance (Cap. 177) is a legal document that provides for the issuance of identity cards, which are used to verify personal information during an inspection."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Registration of Persons Ordinance (Cap. 177) is a piece of legislation that issues identity cards, which public officers are required to produce under section 25(2)(b)."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is a specific piece of legislation that authorizes identity cards for inspection by an authorized officer as part of their functions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddc943ee0b925d64ce2ff3b4b8fcc772&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e43310bb8a059a1a014c1ba9a611877f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7d7ad99b2b6121e30cb678dc647a4a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 314}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1002}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENTERING AND INSPECTING POWERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Entering and inspecting powers refer to the authority granted to authorized personnel as described in section 25. This includes entering places without a warrant or with one, based on certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddc943ee0b925d64ce2ff3b4b8fcc772</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 322}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1012}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1215}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLACE OF OFFENSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Place of offense is any location where an offense under this ordinance has occurred or is currently happening, as determined by the authorized personnel.")</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddc943ee0b925d64ce2ff3b4b8fcc772</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 314}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1002}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OBJECTS FOR PROOF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Objects for proof are items that can be found in a place and used to prove or strongly suggest that an offense under this ordinance has taken place."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddc943ee0b925d64ce2ff3b4b8fcc772</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 314}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1002}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEASUREMENT, INSPECTION, TESTING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These refer to the actions of measuring, inspecting, or testing at a location as part of determining whether an offense under this ordinance has occurred. These activities are conducted by authorized personnel based on their reasonable belief that such actions are necessary."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddc943ee0b925d64ce2ff3b4b8fcc772</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 322}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1012}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1215}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OBSERVATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Observation refers to the act of observing and documenting any relevant information or evidence at a location, which can be part of the process for determining if an offense under this ordinance has occurred."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddc943ee0b925d64ce2ff3b4b8fcc772</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 314}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1002}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 13(1) NOTICE DELIVERY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event involves delivering notices according to section 13(1), likely related to informing individuals or entities about potential offenses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddc943ee0b925d64ce2ff3b4b8fcc772</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 322}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1012}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1215}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 16(1) NOTICE DELIVERY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to the delivery of notifications under section 16(1), possibly for similar purposes as mentioned in Section 13(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddc943ee0b925d64ce2ff3b4b8fcc772</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 314}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1002}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATHEMATICS (QUANTIFICATION)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The term 'quantification' here likely relates to numerical or statistical methods used by authorized personnel to assess the likelihood of offenses based on data collected during inspections and observations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddc943ee0b925d64ce2ff3b4b8fcc772</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 322}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1012}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1215}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOCIAL SCIENCES (BEHAVIORAL STUDIES)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These studies could involve analyzing human behavior, interactions, and social dynamics in relation to compliance with ordinances or regulations as observed by authorized personnel."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddc943ee0b925d64ce2ff3b4b8fcc772</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 314}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1002}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HUMAN RIGHTS COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This concept involves ensuring that the actions of authorized officers comply with relevant human rights standards while exercising their powers under this ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddc943ee0b925d64ce2ff3b4b8fcc772</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 322}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1012}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1215}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The legal authority refers to the formal and procedural framework established by sections 24, 25, etc., which defines how public officers can exercise their duties in a lawful manner."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddc943ee0b925d64ce2ff3b4b8fcc772</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 314}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1002}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OFFENCE AGAINST THIS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Offence against this Ordinance is an event where a violation of certain regulations or laws has occurred, which can include committing an offense or having evidence that such an offense is being committed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8024a8a38a1cf4faa9e3a31112f97d7c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 314}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1002}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WRITTEN AUTHORIZATION UNDER SECTION 24&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Written Authorization under section 24 refers to the document issued by authorities allowing officers to enter places without a warrant for specific purposes related to law enforcement and inspection."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8024a8a38a1cf4faa9e3a31112f97d7c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 314}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1002}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 13(1), 13(4), 16(1) OR 16(3)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These sections refer to events where notices can be served, indicating potential legal actions or inspections related to offenses against the Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8024a8a38a1cf4faa9e3a31112f97d7c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 314}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1002}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OBSERVATION AND MONITORING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ACTIVITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Observation and Monitoring refer to the continuous watch or surveillance of certain actions or conditions related to potential offenses against the Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8024a8a38a1cf4faa9e3a31112f97d7c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 314}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1002}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAGISTRATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Magistrate has the authority to issue a warrant authorizing an Occupational Safety Officer to enter premises with necessary force under specific conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Magistrate issues warrants based on information provided under oath regarding potential offenses against an ordinance or possession of evidence related to such offenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"A magistrate has the authority to issue a warrant authorizing searches in domestic premises if satisfied by information on oath that there may be found any evidence of an offense under this Part."&lt;SEP&gt;"A magistrate is a judicial officer who can issue warrants based on information provided by oath, allowing officers to enter premises for inspection if there's reasonable suspicion of an offense or evidence thereof."&lt;SEP&gt;"Magistrates are individuals who preside over court proceedings and have the power to make orders based on what they consider just."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9dd5fc5d6041ac2cbd3c37735096a0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7d7ad99b2b6121e30cb678dc647a4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-106089b31da6304da0bc926c63d44161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3282c20ec28d4bb14aec7fe4e4eafbe8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-029d1e15c5db53ebcfd1168d7ac7bbab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 146}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 639}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IDENTITY CARD ISSUED UNDER THE REGISTRATION OF PERSONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 177)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Identity Card refers to a specific product or item—such as a document—that is issued according to the provisions of the Registration of Persons Ordinance and used for identity verification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e43310bb8a059a1a014c1ba9a611877f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 322}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1012}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1215}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WARRANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Warrant is a legal document that authorizes public officers to conduct inspections of employment agencies' places of business when necessary."&lt;SEP&gt;"A warrant is a document issued by a District Judge ordering an employer to be apprehended if there is probable cause for believing that they intend to leave Hong Kong with the intent of evading payment of debts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Warrant is an official authorization that allows public officers to enter certain places, which continues in force until its purpose has been satisfied."&lt;SEP&gt;"Warrant refers to a document issued by the District Judge that requires payment or action from the employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-86f4348a1c4677448f8348eacdd112bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee0cf79121cc26199f0bf5c4d14a8ce8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e43310bb8a059a1a014c1ba9a611877f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb63fc0b243ea63257ead6ec4cad1834</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 333}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1019}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 25&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 25 refers to a specific legal provision or event where the powers of public officers are exercised and inspected identities as per the Registration of Persons Ordinance (Cap. 177)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e43310bb8a059a1a014c1ba9a611877f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WILFUL RESISTANCE, OBSTRUCTION OR DELAY BY A PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wilful resistance, obstruction or delay refers to actions taken against the exercise of powers conferred by section 25 by any public officer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47304134f07a5f479481f92c36a5c012</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAILURE WITHOUT REASONABLE EXCUSE TO COMPLY WITH REQUIREMENTS MADE BY A PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Failure without reasonable excuse is an event where a person fails to comply with lawful demands from a public officer, which could lead to legal consequences."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47304134f07a5f479481f92c36a5c012</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRODUCTION OF INCORRECT OR INACCURATE DRAWINGS, RECORDS OR DOCUMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Production of incorrect or inaccurate drawings, records or documents refers to the act of providing false information in compliance with section 25 requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47304134f07a5f479481f92c36a5c012</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WILFUL OR RECKLESS GIVING OF INCORRECT INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wilful or reckless giving of incorrect information is an event where a person intentionally or recklessly provides misinformation as required by section 25, which can result in legal penalties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47304134f07a5f479481f92c36a5c012</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WITHHOLDING OF RELEVANT INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Withholding of relevant information refers to the act of failing to provide necessary details when requested under section 25, potentially leading to criminal charges."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47304134f07a5f479481f92c36a5c012</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINE AT LEVEL 5 FOR OFFENCES COMMITTED UNDER SECTION 26&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PENALTY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A fine at level 5 is a penalty imposed on individuals who commit offenses as defined in section 26 of the regulation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47304134f07a5f479481f92c36a5c012</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATION MAKING POWER OF THE SECRETARY FOR ENVIRONMENT AFTER CONSULTATION WITH THE ENVIRONMENTAL CONSULTATIVE COMMITTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The organization mentioned here refers to the Environmental Consultative Committee, which advises the Secretary for Environment regarding regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47304134f07a5f479481f92c36a5c012</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECRETARY FOR ENVIRONMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The person referred to as 'Secretary for Environment' is an official who has regulatory powers and consults with committees like the Environmental Consultative Committee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47304134f07a5f479481f92c36a5c012</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL CONSULTATIVE COMMITTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Environmental Consultative Committee is a body that advises the Secretary for Environment on matters related to environmental regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47304134f07a5f479481f92c36a5c012</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATION MAKING POWER UNDER SECTION 27(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Regulation-making power refers to the authority granted by section 27(1) allowing the Secretary for Environment, after consultation with relevant bodies, to create specific rules and procedures as needed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47304134f07a5f479481f92c36a5c012</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPEALS AGAINST REGULATIONS MADE UNDER SECTION IV OF THE REGULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appeals against regulations are events where individuals or organizations can challenge decisions made by public officers in relation to environmental regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47304134f07a5f479481f92c36a5c012</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VARIOUS FEES FOR DIFFERENT SITUATIONS AS PER SECTION 27(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Various fees refer to the diverse charges that may be imposed under different circumstances, as outlined in section 27(2) of the regulation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47304134f07a5f479481f92c36a5c012</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATION MAKING POWER TO SET OUT GENERAL PROVISIONS FOR EFFECTIVE IMPLEMENTATION AND ACHIEVEMENT OF OBJECTIVES UNDER SECTION 27(3)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Regulation-making power includes setting up broad guidelines that ensure efficient enforcement and attainment of legislative goals, as stated in section 27(3)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47304134f07a5f479481f92c36a5c012</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMENDMENT E.R. 2 OF 2021&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Amendment E.R. 2 of 2021 refers to a specific legal change made on February 4, 2021, which has updated the regulation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47304134f07a5f479481f92c36a5c012</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART VI - MISCELLANEOUS REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part VI is a section in the document that deals with miscellaneous regulations and provisions not covered elsewhere."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47304134f07a5f479481f92c36a5c012</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATION MAKING POWER OF THE SECRETARY FOR ENVIRONMENT UNDER PART VI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The organization mentioned here refers to the regulatory authority vested in the Secretary for Environment, as detailed in Part VI of the regulation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47304134f07a5f479481f92c36a5c012</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MISCELLANEOUS PROVISIONS AND REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Miscellaneous provisions refer to various rules and stipulations that are not specifically categorized elsewhere but form part of the overall legal framework established by the regulation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47304134f07a5f479481f92c36a5c012</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATION MAKING POWER FOR EFFECTIVE IMPLEMENTATION UNDER PART VI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Regulation-making power includes creating measures aimed at ensuring efficient execution of environmental policies, as outlined in Part VI."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47304134f07a5f479481f92c36a5c012</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE SECRETARY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Secretary is an official who has the authority to make regulations after consulting with the Advisory Council on the Environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The person referred to as the 'Secretary' is a public official responsible for overseeing employment agencies and related activities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3645bfc30781435fa7015192a9be351c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8d055b17ca5d7c4bc065dbbfefc9360</data>
