</node>
<node id="&quot;PURPOSE OF THE ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event involves ensuring employee safety and health, detailing measures that make workplaces safer, and improving regulations on hazardous processes, equipment, and substances in work environments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb7fcd5200d5f794a363f07e5ee2dc70</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 386}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE PURPOSES OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event outlines several objectives, including ensuring workplace safety and health, prescribing measures for a safer work environment, improving standards for hazardous processes, plant, and substances, and generally enhancing the overall safety and health aspects of working environments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-61cee1a453a83b87002df2318ef0eb78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 153}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 658}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Workplace Code of Practice refers to a work guideline issued under Section 40(1), and also includes any revised version of such guidelines if they have been modified."&lt;SEP&gt;"A workplace code of practice is a document that provides guidelines for ensuring the safety and health of employees, as well as additional responsibilities on employers, employees, or non-employer premises occupiers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A workplace code of practice is a document that provides guidelines for practices in work environments, which becomes effective upon publication in the Gazette and can be amended or revoked with similar procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workplace Code of Practice is a code of practice issued under section 40(1) and includes any amendments made to it."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-71e44b452a884e51f90079ec8a9ac88f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126e18663d810ba6b83365ff30027a71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 389}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1083}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC ANALYST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Public Analyst is a person who performs analyses on samples provided by an Occupational Safety Officer and can provide analysis results documented in certificates."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Public Analyst is an individual responsible for analyzing samples submitted to them by Occupational Safety Officers as part of their duties under this Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Public Analyst performs analysis on the sample parts submitted for examination by an Occupational Safety Officer. Their certificate of results is admissible in legal proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Public Analyst refers to Government Chemist, Government Pathologist, or any analyst appointed in writing by the Chief Executive for implementing this Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public analyst includes Government Chemist, Government Pathologist, and analysts appointed by the Chief Executive for this Ordinance purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4c1ae5b0a8aff1b3116e95deba9e3ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce083c97323a19a9162d045f2002c1d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b491d14ac4486a01edd1dfafab97ca07</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 631}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DANGEROUS OCCURRENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Dangerous Occurrence is an incident of a type specified in Schedule 1."&lt;SEP&gt;"A dangerous occurrence refers to events specified in Schedule 1 that are considered hazardous."&lt;SEP&gt;"Any incident that poses a risk or hazard in the workplace, requiring immediate reporting to ensure safety measures are taken."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7249fad978915b4915d01ecac03019f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d781ae6a3974dcd155b4f5b736d6161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 631}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPIER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Occupier is an individual or organization that uses premises where a workplace is located, potentially subject to improvement notices if there are violations."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Occupier is someone who has control or responsibility over premises where a workplace is located. This could be an individual or an organization."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Occupier, with respect to any premises or workplace, includes anyone who has control over such premises or workplace, particularly including persons applicable under clauses (5) and (6)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Occupier includes any person having control over premises or workplace, including those specified in subsections (5) and (6)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Occupier is a person who occupies or uses business premises, potentially liable for breaches arising from their actions or omissions within those premises."&lt;SEP&gt;"Occupier is an organization or individual responsible for maintaining and ensuring safety in premises where workplaces are located."&lt;SEP&gt;"Occupier refers to the individual or entity that has control over and is responsible for maintaining the condition of a workplace."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Occupier refers to the person or entity that has control over a workplace, which can be either an employer or another party."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3717bfa1a0a429ae82cff6583f9ffc97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3af7b8f9d9569fddb32c031c5ec0dbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bec6b7a4bfd3c0c262594492fc624e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0a0ae0d06f82179e57847e5fde58901&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbb962605c6a7e5085bf69519da702fe</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 561}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Plant includes machinery, equipment, appliances, furniture, furnishings, and fittings used in the workplace."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plant refers to machinery, equipment, tools, furniture, fittings, installations and devices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 299}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 991}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IDENTITY CARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Identity Card is issued according to the Registration of Persons Ordinance (Chapter 177)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Identity Card is a document that can be requested by the officer from any person found on the premises if they reasonably suspect an offense against this Ordinance has been committed or could be provided as evidence of such an offense."&lt;SEP&gt;"Identity card is an identity document issued under the Registration of Persons Ordinance, used for identification purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Identity card refers to official identification documents issued by the government, as mentioned in the context of legal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4c1ae5b0a8aff1b3116e95deba9e3ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7249fad978915b4915d01ecac03019f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 151}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 656}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BODILY INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bodily Injury includes harm caused to health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bodily injury refers to harm caused to health."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 299}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 991}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSTANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Substance refers to a natural or artificial substance, whether in the form of a solid, liquid, gas, or vapor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Substance refers to natural or artificial matter, in any state of solid, liquid, gas or vapor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Substance refers to natural or artificial substances, regardless of their state—solid, liquid, gas, or vapor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126e18663d810ba6b83365ff30027a71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 631}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACTIVITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Activity includes operations and processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Activity involves operations and procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 628}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECORD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Record includes data recorded electronically."&lt;SEP&gt;"Record includes data recorded in electronic form."&lt;SEP&gt;"Record includes information stored in electronic form for documentation purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Record refers to information recorded in electronic form."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126e18663d810ba6b83365ff30027a71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 631}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERSON RESPONSIBLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"For any workplace, a Person Responsible refers to the individual or entity accountable for work-related matters."&lt;SEP&gt;"For any workplace, the term 'person responsible' has the meaning given by paragraph (2) of this provision."&lt;SEP&gt;"Person responsible in relation to a workplace means an individual designated by subsection (2) for occupational safety and health responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 151}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 656}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOMESTIC SERVANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A domestic servant is a person employed within a household, as defined in the Employment Ordinance (Cap. 57)."&lt;SEP&gt;"A domestic servant is an employee who works in a private household as if the household were a business and the maintenance of the household were the carrying on of that business by the employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Domestic servant includes gardeners, drivers, boatmen, and similar private servants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Domestic servant is a person employed in or connected with a private household for personal services, whose role can be affected by changes due to the death of the employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Domestic servant refers to a natural person working as a domestic helper, defined under the Employment Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Domestic servant refers to individuals employed in private households and are subject to specific provisions of employment laws as if their work were a business operation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The term 'domestic servant' is defined in the Employment Ordinance (Cap. 57)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b40910fef9ba5e880f9a32ae794f8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a79efc9c7d5b3c5051c209e7d8238e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9546d09d8137ba2697ee36074c84b498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae8f763a371efa17099b990f69f8b4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7249fad978915b4915d01ecac03019f3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 587}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPROVEMENT NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Improvement Notice is a formal notice issued by the Commissioner requiring employers or occupiers to remedy contraventions within a specified period or refrain from continuing or repeating them."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Improvement Notice is a formal written notice issued by the Commissioner to an employer or occupier requiring them to remedy workplace violations within a specified period."&lt;SEP&gt;"An improvement notice is a notification sent under section 9."&lt;SEP&gt;"Improvement notice is a formal notification served under section 9 to address issues related to workplace safety or conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70cdeeb8eece52f9eaa0ef190c0b61e0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 652}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUSPENSION NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Suspension Notice is a document issued by authorities, which can be reviewed and potentially revoked or varied based on certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Suspension Notice is a document issued by the Commissioner to employers or occupiers when there is an imminent risk of death or serious bodily injury due to activities, conditions, or uses on premises. It directs certain actions not to be undertaken while it remains in force."&lt;SEP&gt;"A suspension notice is a notification sent under section 10."&lt;SEP&gt;"A suspension notice is an official document issued by the Commissioner, which can be amended or suspended based on certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Suspension Notice is a notice served under section 10."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126e18663d810ba6b83365ff30027a71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8247282749bd85cb6d48e946a81b3c1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05baa7711eb26dcfef62e1a9f005bfc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbb962605c6a7e5085bf69519da702fe</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 608}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1147}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FUNCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Function includes both power and duty in the context of occupational safety regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Function includes powers and duties related to specific roles or responsibilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Function includes powers and responsibilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Function refers to the powers and responsibilities assigned or exercised by an entity, as defined under specific legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6028b01799478cec839282a4d1179b1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7249fad978915b4915d01ecac03019f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 151}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 656}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SERIOUS BODILY INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"For any person, serious bodily injury includes harm leading the injured party into a hospital or clinic for treatment or observation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serious Bodily Injury refers to significant physical damage resulting from a workplace accident, necessitating immediate reporting and medical attention."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serious bodily injury includes any bodily injury that results in the person's admission at a hospital or clinic for treatment or observation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serious bodily injury refers to any physical harm that requires hospital or clinic treatment, observation, and is considered a severe legal offense."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126e18663d810ba6b83365ff30027a71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bec6b7a4bfd3c0c262594492fc624e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 151}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 655}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OFFENCE OF STRICT LIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An offence of strict liability is any offense that fits the description provided—no proof is required from the prosecution regarding the defendant's state of mind at the time of committing the act when prosecuting such an offense."&lt;SEP&gt;"Offence of strict liability is a legal term where the prosecution does not need to prove intent, knowledge, or recklessness on behalf of the defendant."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 151}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 656}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STRICT LIABILITY OFFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Strict liability offence means any crime where the prosecution does not need to prove the defendant's intent, knowledge of the act, or negligence in committing the criminal act."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bec6b7a4bfd3c0c262594492fc624e7b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 561}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK-RELATED DANGER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Work-related danger includes dangers attributable to the manner in which business operations are conducted, dangers from equipment or substances used under circumstances related to such operations, and conditions of places where these uses occur."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bec6b7a4bfd3c0c262594492fc624e7b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 151}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 655}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TIME AT WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Time at work refers to when a person is actually present at their workplace. However, if someone travels by a vehicle defined in section (b) as part of the transport service for non-employees under similar conditions, they are not considered to be working."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bec6b7a4bfd3c0c262594492fc624e7b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 151}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 655}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Work here refers to tasks or projects that are contracted out, typically in the construction industry based on context clues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Work refers to work as an employee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af77be8b003511c35b7551f4285bb427&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126e18663d810ba6b83365ff30027a71</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RISKS ARISING OUT OF ACTIVITIES AT WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Risks associated with work activities are considered in this Ordinance and include risks related to how undertakings are conducted, plant safety, etc."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-126e18663d810ba6b83365ff30027a71</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 631}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDEPENDENT CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Independent contractors are self-employed individuals who may be subject to the Ordinance when acting as employers or occupiers of a workplace."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3717bfa1a0a429ae82cff6583f9ffc97</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 561}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELF-EMPLOYED PERSON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Self-employed persons, like independent contractors, can be covered by the Ordinance in their capacity as employers or occupiers of premises containing workplaces."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3717bfa1a0a429ae82cff6583f9ffc97</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 561}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDEPENDENT CONTRACTORS AND SELF-EMPLOYED PERSONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to individuals who work independently as employers or occupiers of premises where workplaces are located."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cbf739f28af13fb255489857524eaf50</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 322}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1010}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEES SAFETY AND HEALTH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Safety and Health at work refers to the social science concept related to protecting workers from physical, mental, and psychological harm in their workplace."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9e5937ed8f53f94669beb412edc19a99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 65}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 451}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATIONS ON EMPLOYEE SAFETY AND HEALTH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The regulations mentioned are legal frameworks ensuring employers provide necessary guidance, training, supervision, maintaining a safe working environment, and providing access routes that do not endanger health."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9e5937ed8f53f94669beb412edc19a99</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKING ENVIRONMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The working environment provided by employers, which should be safe and without risks to health as far as reasonably practicable."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8903577fbeb26a0f144927da3a1efb7c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 157}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 669}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAFETY AND HEALTH AT WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ensuring the safety and health of employees during work activities involves multiple factors such as plant and systems of work, arrangements for use, handling, storage or transport of substances, information, instruction, training, supervision, maintenance of workplace conditions, and provision of access to and egress from the workplace."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8903577fbeb26a0f144927da3a1efb7c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPIER OF PREMISES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Occupier of Premises refers to individuals or entities responsible for ensuring safety and health conditions in a workplace."&lt;SEP&gt;"The occupier of premises is responsible for ensuring the safety and health of persons employed at those premises, facing potential fines or imprisonment if non-compliance occurs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The occupier of premises refers to the person who is believed by an officer to be in charge of a workplace."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a215b7541a9d5eb966c5aa9ffed5374&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0812f6740fa10908c6c96dfb7b577a49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 146}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 642}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPRISONMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Imprisonment refers to the potential legal consequence of criminal conviction related to breaches of workplace safety laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a215b7541a9d5eb966c5aa9ffed5374</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 146}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 642}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee's employer controls the workplace where an employee works but does not necessarily manage it directly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0812f6740fa10908c6c96dfb7b577a49</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 146}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 642}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLANT OR SUBSTANCES KEPT AT PREMISES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY/PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are equipment or materials stored on the premises which must be safe and without risks to health as far as reasonably practicable."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0812f6740fa10908c6c96dfb7b577a49</data>
