  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Safety and Health Regulations are rules and standards designed to protect workers' safety and health in the workplace."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d0a0ae0d06f82179e57847e5fde58901</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 561}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE VIOLATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace Violations refer to actions that contravene regulations set forth in ordinances such as the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (Cap. 59)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 652}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REASONABLE PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Reasonable Period is a time frame determined by the Commissioner after considering relevant provisions, within which an employer or occupier must remedy violations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 826}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REASONABLE GROUNDS FOR NON-COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Reasonable Grounds for Non-Compliance are conditions that, when proven by an employer or occupier, can serve as a valid defense against charges of non-compliance with improvement notices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;400,000 HKD AND 12 MONTHS IMPRISONMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PENALTY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A penalty of $400,000 in fines and up to 12 months' imprisonment is the maximum punishment for employers or occupiers who fail to comply with improvement notices without reasonable grounds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace Regulations encompass a set of guidelines and standards established for ensuring safe and healthy working conditions in factories and industrial settings, enforced through ordinances like Cap. 59."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPROVEMENT NOTICE PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Improvement Notice Procedure refers to the formal process by which the Commissioner issues notices requiring employers or occupiers to address violations within specified timeframes, often involving written documentation and legal procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Law is a branch of law that governs the relationship between employees and employers, including workplace regulations and enforcement mechanisms like improvement notices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employment Law refers to the legal framework governing employer-employee relationships including provisions on entitlements like annual leave and other related benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employment law is a body of regulations that governs employment relationships, including how contracts are renewed or re-engaged after significant organizational changes such as ownership transfers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employment law refers to a set of regulations that govern employment relationships, including conditions for termination and compensation such as terminal payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text discusses various aspects of employment law including wage protection, civil debt recovery, and measures against absconding employers which fall within the domain of social sciences related to labor relations and legal studies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a1958590510250b6ab53b0fe3e4cc53e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b57ac243904d2f7c387b12d47bb079b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 154}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL HEALTH AND SAFETY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Occupational Health and Safety refers to practices aimed at protecting workers from physical, chemical, or biological hazards in their work environment, which are regulated by ordinances such as Cap. 59."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FACTORIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Factories refer to industrial establishments where goods are manufactured on a large scale and can be subject to workplace regulations under the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (Cap. 59)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Industrial Undertakings include various types of businesses engaged in manufacturing or processing activities, which are regulated by ordinances such as Cap. 59 to ensure safe and healthy working conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE INSPECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Workplace Inspection is a formal assessment conducted by authorities like the Commissioner to check for compliance with workplace regulations and identify any violations that may require improvement notices."&lt;SEP&gt;"A workplace inspection by public officers can trigger certain legal obligations regarding disclosure of details about the inspected site or its occupants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entering and inspecting workplaces is an event that can be performed by Occupational Safety Officers under certain conditions as described in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e25506f50e901e7cebe325e56cdc3f67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7f5c7774940469ec261850f6dbd6b83</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1159}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPIER'S RESPONSIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Occupier's Responsibility involves ensuring adherence to workplace regulations, including responding appropriately to improvement notices issued by the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER'S COMPLIANCE OBLIGATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employer's Compliance Obligations refer to the legal and ethical duties of employers to comply with workplace regulations, which are crucial for maintaining a safe and healthy work environment as per social science research on labor relations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATORY ENFORCEMENT MECHANISMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Regulatory Enforcement Mechanisms include processes such as issuing improvement notices and legal penalties aimed at ensuring compliance with workplace regulations like those outlined in the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (Cap. 59)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace Safety Standards are quantitative measures used to assess and ensure safe working conditions, often based on mathematical models and statistical analysis of workplace hazards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPROVEMENT NOTICE COMPLIANCE MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Improvement Notice Compliance Mechanism is a process that involves issuing formal warnings and penalties for non-compliance with workplace regulations to ensure adherence to safety standards and legal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 323}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Standards are the minimum conditions of employment required by law, including those related to health and safety in the workplace as enforced through mechanisms like improvement notices issued by authorities such as the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE COMPLIANCE MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Workplace Compliance Mechanism is a system designed to ensure that employers and occupiers adhere to regulations governing safe working conditions, often involving formal notifications and penalties for non-compliance like improvement notices issued by authorities such as the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Occupational Safety Regulations are laws and guidelines designed to protect workers from hazards in their work environment, which are enforced through mechanisms like improvement notices issued by authorities such as the Commissioner."&lt;SEP&gt;"Occupational Safety Regulations are legal guidelines and procedures for ensuring workplace safety, including requirements for accident notifications and documentation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text provides details on safety regulations for various occupations involving hazardous substances, indicating a technological approach to managing these risks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94a1139425d270c7317d6d6a1dd6e020</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON,ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employer or Occupier refers to individuals or organizations who are subject to and may apply for review of a Suspension Notice issued under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employers and occupiers are entities that may receive a suspension notice and are subject to potential fines for non-compliance with such notices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employers or occupiers are roles that can be affected by decisions made by the Commissioner and have the right to appeal these decisions through the Appeal Board."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to individuals or organizations responsible for compliance with industrial safety regulations as outlined in the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (Cap. 59)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8247282749bd85cb6d48e946a81b3c1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05baa7711eb26dcfef62e1a9f005bfc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8d52a1038b5b838fbe9231f59cfc74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70cdeeb8eece52f9eaa0ef190c0b61e0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 650}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPROVEMENT NOTICE COMPLIANCE FAILURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event of an employer or occupier failing to comply with a requirement specified in an improvement notice without reasonable excuse, leading to potential legal consequences."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-70cdeeb8eece52f9eaa0ef190c0b61e0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 651}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY SUSPENSION ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Temporary Suspension Order is issued by the Commissioner when there is an immediate danger of death or serious bodily harm due to activities at a workplace location or conditions and usage of equipment or substances in that location."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-70cdeeb8eece52f9eaa0ef190c0b61e0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 651}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;僱主或佔用人&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON/ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"僱主或佔用人指的是负责处所的雇主或占用人，涉及到发出暂时停工通知书的相关事宜。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f4dd58ad4c9957f63fe03ad87123a328</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 468}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;暫時停工通知書&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"暫時停工通知書是一种书面文件，用于指示在特定期间内不得进行某些活动或使用某些场所、作业装置或物质，并指出产生危险的事宜。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f4dd58ad4c9957f63fe03ad87123a328</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 468}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY RISK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,INDUSTRY,SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Workplace Safety Risk is an imminent risk of death or serious bodily injury that can arise from activities, conditions, or uses on premises. It is a critical factor in determining whether to issue a suspension notice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbb962605c6a7e5085bf69519da702fe</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 628}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMMINENT RISK OF DEATH OR SERIOUS BODILY INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An imminent risk refers to a situation that poses an immediate threat of severe harm or fatal consequences."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05baa7711eb26dcfef62e1a9f005bfc8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 608}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1147}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINE OF $1,000,000 AND TO IMPRISONMENT FOR 12 MONTHS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This describes the legal penalties imposed on employers or occupiers who contravene a suspension notice knowingly and intentionally."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05baa7711eb26dcfef62e1a9f005bfc8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FURTHER FINE OF $100,000 FOR EACH DAY OR PART OF A DAY DURING WHICH THE OFFENDER CONTINUES THE CONTRAVENTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Additional fines are levied daily if an employer or occupier continues to violate a suspension notice after conviction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05baa7711eb26dcfef62e1a9f005bfc8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY STOP NOTICE REVIEW RIGHTS OF EMPLOYERS AND OCCUPIERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the right of employers and occupiers to apply for a review within 28 days of receiving a temporary stop notice, with specific requirements for their application."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05baa7711eb26dcfef62e1a9f005bfc8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 653}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPLICATION FOR REVIEW OF TEMPORARY STOP NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An application for review is a formal request submitted by an employer or occupier to the Commissioner regarding a temporary stop notice they have received."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05baa7711eb26dcfef62e1a9f005bfc8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;14 DAYS PERIOD AFTER RECEIVING THE APPLICATION FOR REVIEW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the time frame within which the Commissioner must make a decision on an application for reviewing a temporary stop notice, typically 14 days from receipt."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05baa7711eb26dcfef62e1a9f005bfc8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMISSIONER'S DECISION NOTIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Commissioner is required to notify the applicant in writing of their decision regarding the review of a temporary stop notice within a reasonable time after making the decision."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05baa7711eb26dcfef62e1a9f005bfc8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 653}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RIGHT OF EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER TO HAVE SUSPENSION NOTICE REVIEWED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event involves the process where an Employer or Occupier applies for a review of a Suspension Notice within 28 days after receiving it, and the Commissioner determines whether to confirm, revoke, or vary the notice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8247282749bd85cb6d48e946a81b3c1e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 650}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RIGHT OF EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER TO APPEAL AGAINST DECISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event involves the process where an Employer or Occupier can appeal decisions made by the Commissioner within 28 days after receiving written notification of such a decision."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8247282749bd85cb6d48e946a81b3c1e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 650}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DECISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Decision refers to determinations made by the Commissioner regarding Suspension Notices, which may involve confirmation, revocation, or variation based on applications for review."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8247282749bd85cb6d48e946a81b3c1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY WORK STOPPAGE NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Temporary Work Stoppage Notice is a document that can be issued and potentially revoked under certain conditions as outlined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8247282749bd85cb6d48e946a81b3c1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATHEMATICS (TIME FRAMES)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The text involves specific time frames such as 14 days for review applications, which are mathematical intervals used to define procedural timelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Time frames such as 5 working days and 7 working days mentioned in the text are used to define deadlines for various actions during dispute resolution processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7ad6aa79a150340c8a28d98a0e6b1a24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8247282749bd85cb6d48e946a81b3c1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOCIAL SCIENCES (REGULATION AND COMPLIANCE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This text deals with the regulation of workplace safety through suspension notices and appeals processes, reflecting social science concepts related to compliance and administrative law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8247282749bd85cb6d48e946a81b3c1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTIFICATION OF SUSPENSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Notification of suspension is a document that can be modified by the Appeal Board based on certain conditions continuing to exist and directions being unreasonable."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bc8d52a1038b5b838fbe9231f59cfc74</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 149}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 650}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENTS OR OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace accidents or occupational diseases are events related to health issues arising from work environments, which fall under the scope of Part IV dealing with such matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bc8d52a1038b5b838fbe9231f59cfc74</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 617}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK LOCATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Work locations refer to physical places where employees perform their duties and can be sites for workplace accidents or other incidents covered by relevant regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bc8d52a1038b5b838fbe9231f59cfc74</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 617}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENTS AND OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace Accidents and Occupational Diseases refers to incidents that occur at the workplace, including injuries or deaths of employees, which require reporting according to specific regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 151}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 654}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace Accidents are incidents that occur in the course of employment, potentially causing harm or death to employees, which must be reported according to specific regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOST WORK CAPACITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lost Work Capacity is the condition where an employee becomes unable to perform their job duties due to injuries sustained in a workplace incident, requiring further documentation for legal compliance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDUSTRIAL ACTIVITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Industrial Activities refer to the types of work or business operations carried out at a specific location, such as manufacturing, services, etc."&lt;SEP&gt;"Industrial Activities refer to the various operations and processes carried out at a work location that may lead to accidents or incidents needing reporting as per regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 151}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 654}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY DEPARTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Occupational Safety Department is a governmental or organizational body responsible for enforcing safety regulations and managing reports of workplace incidents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 151}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 654}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Injury refers to injuries sustained by employees during their work, which may require reporting according to occupational safety laws and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL HEALTH AND SAFETY ACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Occupational Health and Safety Act is a legal framework that mandates the reporting of workplace accidents and incidents, ensuring employee protection and compliance with safety standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE INCIDENT REPORTING SYSTEM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Workplace Incident Reporting System is an organized method for documenting and managing reports of workplace accidents to ensure proper handling and follow-up according to legal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1158}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Occupational Safety Measures are actions or policies implemented by employers to prevent workplace incidents, including procedures for reporting such events as required by law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 151}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 654}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE ENVIRONMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Workplace Environment refers to the physical and operational conditions at a work location that may contribute to accidents or require documentation according to occupational safety regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDUSTRIAL ACTIVITIES DETAILS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Details of Industrial Activities include specific information about operations, processes, and activities conducted in a workplace which are relevant for reporting incidents as per legal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 151}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 654}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY TRAINING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Occupational Safety Training is educational programs designed to inform employees about safety practices and procedures, including the importance of accident reporting according to regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 151}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 654}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE INCIDENT DOCUMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace Incident Documentation refers to detailed records kept by employers for incidents that occur at work locations, which are crucial for compliance with occupational health and safety laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER TRAINING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Training for Occupational Safety Officers includes education on how to effectively manage workplace incident reports and ensure proper handling of accidents according to legal standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT INJURY REPORTING REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal requirements mandate the reporting of employment injuries, including specific details that must be documented in accordance with occupational safety regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1158}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Occupational Safety Compliance involves ensuring adherence to all legal and regulatory standards related to workplace incidents, including proper documentation and handling as required by law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE INCIDENT NOTIFICATION PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Procedures for Workplace Incident Notification are formal steps taken by employers to report accidents according to occupational safety regulations, ensuring timely and accurate information is provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY REGULATIONS ENFORCEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Enforcement of Occupational Safety Regulations involves the monitoring and implementation of laws related to workplace incidents, including the reporting requirements for such events as mandated by legal standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE INCIDENT REPORTING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Guidelines for Workplace Incident Reporting provide detailed instructions on how to properly document and notify authorities about accidents occurring at work locations according to occupational safety regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY COMPLIANCE PROGRAMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Compliance Programs in Occupational Safety are initiatives designed to ensure that employers adhere to all legal requirements related to workplace incidents, including proper reporting procedures as mandated by law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE INCIDENT MANAGEMENT SYSTEM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Workplace Incident Management System is a tool or process used by organizations to manage and document reports of accidents occurring at work locations according to occupational safety regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1158}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER CERTIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Certification for Occupational Safety Officers involves formal training and assessment processes ensuring that individuals are qualified to handle workplace incident reporting as required by legal standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE INCIDENT REPORTING FORMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Forms for Workplace Incident Reporting are standardized documents used by employers to document accidents according to occupational safety regulations, facilitating accurate and timely information submission."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY TRAINING PROGRAMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Training Programs in Occupational Safety include educational initiatives aimed at informing employees about proper accident reporting procedures as required by legal standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE INCIDENT DOCUMENTATION STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Standards for Workplace Incident Documentation outline the specific details and formats that must be followed when documenting accidents according to occupational safety regulations, ensuring compliance with legal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 151}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 654}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY COMPLIANCE AUDITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Audits of Occupational Safety Compliance involve systematic evaluations of organizations' adherence to all relevant laws and regulations related to workplace incidents, including proper reporting procedures as mandated by legal standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 151}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 654}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERSON RESPONSIBLE FOR WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The person responsible for a workplace is an individual who must notify accidents according to specific regulations outlined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e87bb6b8feb2f7d365e7f2290bc5e29c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER'S MAIN BUSINESS ADDRESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The employer's main business address, if not the location of occupancy, refers to where the primary operations are conducted by the company."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e87bb6b8feb2f7d365e7f2290bc5e29c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE INJURED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee injured includes details such as name, address, gender, identity card number (if known), and occupation (if applicable)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e87bb6b8feb2f7d365e7f2290bc5e29c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 38}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 362}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDUSTRIAL ACTIVITIES AT WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ACTIVITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Details of industrial activities conducted at the workplace are required to be reported in case of an accident."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e87bb6b8feb2f7d365e7f2290bc5e29c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEATH REPORT AFTER INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"If an injured employee dies following a notification or report, the responsible person must inform a safety officer and local police within 24 hours of learning about the death."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e87bb6b8feb2f7d365e7f2290bc5e29c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 38}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 362}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PENALTY FOR NON-COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Non-compliance with reporting regulations is considered a crime punishable by up to Level 6 fines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e87bb6b8feb2f7d365e7f2290bc5e29c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCAPACITATED (丧失工作能力)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Incapacitation refers to the permanent or temporary loss of work capability due to an accident, where the victim would otherwise be able to perform their job if not for the incident."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e87bb6b8feb2f7d365e7f2290bc5e29c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPIER OF THE PREMISES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Occupier of the Premises refers to an organization that owns or manages the premises where work takes place, such as a company or business entity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 153}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 658}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCIDENT NOTIFICATION REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Accident Notification Requirement outlines specific conditions under which an accident must be reported to an Occupational Safety Officer within 24 hours or 7 days, depending on circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1158}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMERCIAL ACTIVITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Commercial Activities are similar to industrial activities but may pertain more broadly to trade and service provision within a workplace setting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 153}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 658}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OTHER ACTIVITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Other Activities refer to any non-industrial or commercial operations that might be conducted at the workplace, such as research, administration, etc."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 153}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 658}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IDENTITY CARD NUMBER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Identity Card Number is a unique numerical identifier assigned by authorities for identification purposes in legal and administrative contexts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGE (IF KNOWN)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Age of an individual, if known, can be relevant to understanding the demographics or characteristics of employees involved in workplace incidents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEATH NOTIFICATION REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Death Notification Requirement specifies that within 24 hours after becoming aware of a death resulting from an accident, the responsible party must report it to both Occupational Safety Officers and relevant authorities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1158}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCAPACITATION REPORTING REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Incapacitation Reporting Requirement mandates reporting any accidents causing incapacitation for more than 3 days within 7 days of the incident, even if not initially fatal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1158}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POLICE STATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Police Station is where reports of accidents need to be submitted if the victim dies within 24 hours after the incident."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cbbad1d728178af8a023898a237d258a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1158}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DANGEROUS ACCIDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Dangerous Accident refers to any event that detrimentally affects a person's health and must be reported according to specific regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dangerous accident refers to incidents such as machinery disintegration, crane failures (excluding broken chains), and explosions or fires that cause structural damage or disrupt normal operations at work locations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cbbad1d728178af8a023898a237d258a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ca77e785253c5f3aca0053cf386383c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 38}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 363}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCAPACITATED (喪失工作能力)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Incapacitation means the victim is unable to work in any capacity for at least 3 days due to an accident, impacting their ability to perform job functions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cbbad1d728178af8a023898a237d258a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 38}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 362}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPIER OF RELEVANT PREMISES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The occupier refers to the person responsible for a workplace where an accident occurs and is required to report such incidents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d781ae6a3974dcd155b4f5b736d6161</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 153}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 658}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY DAMAGE OR DESTRUCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Damage or destruction of property resulting from an accident at the workplace, which must be reported as part of the incident details."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d781ae6a3974dcd155b4f5b736d6161</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1158}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CIRCUMSTANCES OF OCCURRENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The context and conditions surrounding a dangerous event that need to be documented for proper investigation and analysis."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d781ae6a3974dcd155b4f5b736d6161</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1158}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A medical professional who, upon examination or post-mortem inspection of an employee or former employee, may discover or suspect the presence of occupational diseases as defined in regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d781ae6a3974dcd155b4f5b736d6161</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 740}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER OR FORMER EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The individual being examined by a doctor for potential signs of occupational illness, either currently employed or previously employed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d781ae6a3974dcd155b4f5b736d6161</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 740}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SCHEDULE 2 DISEASES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Specific occupational illnesses detailed in Schedule 2 of relevant regulations, which must be reported by doctors upon discovery or suspicion."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d781ae6a3974dcd155b4f5b736d6161</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 740}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SCHEDULE 3 EXPOSURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace conditions and factors listed in Schedule 3 that may contribute to the development of occupational diseases, necessitating reporting when suspected as a cause."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d781ae6a3974dcd155b4f5b736d6161</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 740}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COLUMN 3&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Column 3 in Schedule 2 lists occupations associated with specific occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05288c51fb6c9855d3f031e51b7e2be3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 738}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FORM PROVIDED OR APPROVED BY THE COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The form used for notifications must be provided or approved by the Commissioner and is required for written submissions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05288c51fb6c9855d3f031e51b7e2be3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 614}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INFORMAL INQUIRY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Informal inquiry into workplace accidents is conducted by an occupational safety officer and reported back to the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-05288c51fb6c9855d3f031e51b7e2be3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 47}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 396}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENT OR DANGEROUS OCCURRENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Workplace Accident or Dangerous Occurrence refers to incidents that may involve injuries or other harmful situations occurring at work locations and are subject to investigation by designated officers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19f640b139895da0133f304114aeb8fc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 633}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INQUIRY INTO WORKPLACE ACCIDENT OR DANGEROUS OCCURRENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Inquiry into a Workplace Accident or Dangerous Occurrence is an informal process conducted by the Occupational Safety Officer to determine causes and circumstances of such incidents, with findings reported back to the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19f640b139895da0133f304114aeb8fc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 633}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LABOR BUREAU&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Labor Bureau is mentioned as a possible employer for the Occupational Safety Officers who conduct inquiries."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 610}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1151}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WITNESSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Witnesses are individuals who can be questioned during an inquiry and required to attend in writing or provide documents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Witnesses are individuals who may be examined on oath and directed to attend an inquiry to give evidence or produce documents, enjoying similar privileges as civil law witnesses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Witnesses are individuals who provide evidence during arbitral proceedings as described by section (8)(b) and (c)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1dbb46e60da08be769a0481277a08538&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 610}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1151}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CIVIL LEGAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Civil Legal Proceedings refer to the legal process involving evidence and testimonies in a civil case."&lt;SEP&gt;"Civil legal proceedings are mentioned as a context where certain labor law clauses do not apply according to specific amendments in legislation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Civil legal proceedings refer to the context where certain evidence cannot be compelled, such as documents that a person is not required to produce in civil court proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5074da09c4f82109b976a4c8a7a052fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602a52838c03cef3777006bf2a44b72e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 105}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INVESTIGATION OF ACCIDENTS OR DANGEROUS OCCURRENCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An investigation into accidents or dangerous occurrences, whether involving death or bodily injury, must follow specific procedures and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE INCIDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Workplace Incident refers to an accident that occurs at a work location, which may be the subject of formal inquiries as per the regulation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISIONS FOR INQUIRY TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"RULE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The provisions allow for the termination of an inquiry if certain conditions are met, such as unavailability or unwillingness to provide information from relevant parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 105}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE OF TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A written notice must be given by the Occupational Safety Officer to the Commissioner upon terminating an inquiry, stating the reasons for the termination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Notice of Termination is a formal communication from one party to another indicating their intention to end a contractual agreement, triggering specific obligations under different sections."&lt;SEP&gt;"Notice of termination is when an employer informs an employee that their contract will be terminated and specifies the date by which they must leave their employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a40a9600dcdabbcf7b1de20226238a1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 537}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISIONS FOR INQUIRY INITIATION AND CONDUCT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"RULE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The provisions detail how inquiries can be initiated (by a report or at the discretion of the officer) and conducted by questioning witnesses and requesting evidence."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CIVIL LEGAL EVIDENCE RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Evidence rules in civil legal proceedings are referenced, indicating that certain types of evidence cannot be compelled during an inquiry as they would not be required in a court setting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISIONS FOR INQUIRY CONDUCT WITHOUT CONSTRAINTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"RULE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The officer conducting the inquiry is not bound by normal evidence rules and can gather any relevant evidence deemed necessary to determine the circumstances of the incident."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REASONS FOR NON-ATTENDANCE OR REFUSAL TO PROVIDE EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REASON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"There are specific reasons why a person may be unable or unwilling to provide information, such as lack of reasonable excuse for not attending an inquiry when required."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 537}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVINCIAL COMMISSIONER OR DEPUTY PROVINCIAL COMMISSIONER OF LABOUR DEPARTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Provincial Commissioner or Deputy Provincial Commissioner of Labour Department is an official who can gather evidence without being bound by evidence rules during an inquiry."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5074da09c4f82109b976a4c8a7a052fb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 311}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVIDING FALSE INFORMATION DURING INQUIRY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Providing False Information During Inquiry is the act of giving false information during an inquiry, which constitutes a crime under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5074da09c4f82109b976a4c8a7a052fb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 105}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CRIMINAL LEGAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Criminal Legal Proceedings refer to legal processes related to criminal cases, where evidence and testimonies are used in court proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5074da09c4f82109b976a4c8a7a052fb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 105}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WITNESS PROTECTION DURING INQUIRY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Witness Protection During Inquiry refers to the rights of witnesses during an inquiry, including their protection from self-incrimination as per civil law procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5074da09c4f82109b976a4c8a7a052fb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 105}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FORMAL INQUIRY INTO WORKPLACE ACCIDENT OR DANGEROUS OCCURRENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A formal inquiry conducted by the Commissioner into workplace accidents or dangerous occurrences, involving examination of witnesses and parties on oath."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1dbb46e60da08be769a0481277a08538</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 610}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1152}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CIVIL PROCEEDINGS BEFORE A COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to the legal proceedings in court where certain rights and obligations related to witness testimony apply, such as the right not to be compelled to produce documents that could not be produced in regular civil cases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1dbb46e60da08be769a0481277a08538</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 610}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1152}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CORONIAL INQUEST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A coronial inquest is a formal investigation into the circumstances surrounding a death, often to determine the cause and manner of death."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d187f5859fc0e151b7a45dda2b23c53</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 291}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 978}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INQUIRY UNDER SECTION 17&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An inquiry under section 17 refers to a specific type of legal proceeding aimed at investigating certain deaths or incidents as outlined in the relevant legislation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d187f5859fc0e151b7a45dda2b23c53</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 291}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 978}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CRIMES ORDINANCE (CAP. 200)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Crimes Ordinance (Cap. 200) is a piece of legislation that outlines criminal offenses and penalties, including perjury."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d187f5859fc0e151b7a45dda2b23c53</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 291}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 978}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CORONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 14)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Coroners Ordinance (Cap. 14</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92c85875b0985afcab2ef9a7ace52829</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 146}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 640}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1160}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEALTH OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Health Officer is mentioned as one of the persons also considered an Occupational Safety Officer in addition to those appointed or authorized by the Commissioner."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Health Officer is mentioned in the text but does not have detailed roles described. They are associated with production requirements for certificates of authority."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health Officer is another role that qualifies as an Occupational Safety Officer, according to the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3c3394a6b72977677a8a437b4151b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea83763b873f6b32742c132cbac8d568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7f5c7774940469ec261850f6dbd6b83</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 608}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1144}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;督察&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"督察是指在《工廠及工業經營條例》(第59章)中被定义的角色，在此段落之前担任该角色的人被视为职业安全主任。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3c3394a6b72977677a8a437b4151b9d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 93}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 498}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;衞生主任&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"衞生主任是另一类根据文本规定可视为职业安全主任的人员。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3c3394a6b72977677a8a437b4151b9d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 93}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 498}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;职业安全主任&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"职业安全主任 refers to the role of an officer who investigates incidents, provides information, and conducts tests related to occupational health and safety."&lt;SEP&gt;"职业安全主任是根据条例被赋予特定职责的角色，可以由处长任命或视作已任命的人员。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3c3394a6b72977677a8a437b4151b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f30bd1959d14cc825d9dc1909b7819e3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 93}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 498}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUTHORITY CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Authority Certificate is issued by the Commissioner to each Occupational Safety Officer, detailing their name and functions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea83763b873f6b32742c132cbac8d568</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 632}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXERCISE OR PERFORMANCE OF FUNCTIONS BY OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event involves occupational safety officers exercising or performing their duties as described in the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea83763b873f6b32742c132cbac8d568</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 632}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Certificate of Authority is a document issued to an Occupational Safety Officer, stating that they are authorized to perform certain functions under the law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea83763b873f6b32742c132cbac8d568</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY DIRECTIVE 22&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Occupational Safety Directive 22 is a regulation that outlines the conditions under which an Occupational Safety Officer can enter premises and perform specific tasks related to workplace safety inspections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98d2094275e74c7538edf07aca95a54a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 628}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREMISES OCCUPIER OR APPARENT MANAGER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION,LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Premises Occupier or Apparent Manager refers to either the owner or apparent controller of a location where an Occupational Safety Officer may require access or information."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b491d14ac4486a01edd1dfafab97ca07</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1158}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAMPLE ANALYSIS PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY,PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Sample Analysis Procedure involves dividing the sample into three parts for different purposes: one given to the requester, another sent to a public analyst, and one retained for future comparison."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b491d14ac4486a01edd1dfafab97ca07</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 631}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 22 PREMISES ENTRY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 22 allows an occupational safety officer to enter certain premises for the purpose of conducting inspections or investigations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed932e3526aee6a4abf0328b0cfd58ca</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 630}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article evidence refers to any item that may be seized by a safety officer as potential proof of a violation, such as unsafe equipment or materials."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed932e3526aee6a4abf0328b0cfd58ca</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 630}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLANT EXAMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Plant examination involves testing and inspecting machinery or substances found on the premises for compliance with safety standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed932e3526aee6a4abf0328b0cfd58ca</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 630}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ATMOSPHERIC TESTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Atmospheric tests are conducted to determine the environmental conditions, such as air quality, in the workplace."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed932e3526aee6a4abf0328b0cfd58ca</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 630}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LABOR DEPARTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Labor Department is an organization that oversees occupational safety and health regulations and can provide documents for review by officers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed932e3526aee6a4abf0328b0cfd58ca</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 22&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 22 is a legal provision that allows an Occupational Safety Officer to enter premises for conducting various safety-related functions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c4c1ae5b0a8aff1b3116e95deba9e3ee</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1158}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE OF EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Article of Evidence refers to any item seized by the officer which they reasonably believe could be evidence of a contravention of this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c4c1ae5b0a8aff1b3116e95deba9e3ee</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 631}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLANT OR SUBSTANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Plant or Substance are terms used for equipment and materials found on premises that may need testing or examination by an Occupational Safety Officer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c4c1ae5b0a8aff1b3116e95deba9e3ee</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1158}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ATMOSPHERIC CONDITION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Atmospheric Condition refers to the environmental factors tested by the officer, such as air quality in the workplace."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c4c1ae5b0a8aff1b3116e95deba9e3ee</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1158}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE OR AGENT OF OCCUPIER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Employee or Agent of Occupier are individuals who may be required to provide assistance and facilities for an Occupational Safety Officer's functions on premises."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c4c1ae5b0a8aff1b3116e95deba9e3ee</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1158}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECORDS RELATING TO SAFETY OR HEALTH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Records are documents under control of employees that may provide information about safety and health conditions at a workplace, which can be requested by the officer for inspection if not in English or Chinese language, they must also produce a statement setting out their contents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c4c1ae5b0a8aff1b3116e95deba9e3ee</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1158}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAMPLE DIVISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event involves dividing a sample into three more or less equal parts as per regulations, with one part given to the requester and another sent to a public analyst for analysis."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce083c97323a19a9162d045f2002c1d4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMERCIAL USE OFFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,CRIME"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A person who uses the results of sample analysis for commercial purposes without proper authorization commits an offence and can be fined up to level 4 upon conviction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce083c97323a19a9162d045f2002c1d4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECORD RETENTION BY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ACTIVITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Occupational Safety Officer may retain records or statements taken from a person, either for copying or as evidence in potential legal proceedings against violations of the Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce083c97323a19a9162d045f2002c1d4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRAVENTION OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to a violation of the ordinance being discussed, which can result in legal consequences if not addressed properly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1158}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INFORMATION THAT MAY IDENTIFY THE OCCUPIER OF PREMISES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The product here is information that could help identify who controls or occupies certain premises, relevant for workplace inspections and compliance checks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 146}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 639}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REQUEST MADE TO A PERSON UNDER SUBSECTION (1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event involves an officer making a request to someone they believe has pertinent information about the occupier of a workplace."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FALSE OR MISLEADING INFORMATION PROVIDED BY A PERSON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A person who provides incorrect or deceptive information in response to an officer's request can be considered guilty of an offense under subsection (2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 146}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 639}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OFFENCE AND LIABILITY ON CONVICTION TO A FINE AT LEVEL 6&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event describes the legal consequence for providing false or misleading information, which is punishable by a specific monetary penalty."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REASONABLE EXCUSE FOR REFUSING COMPLIANCE WITH A REQUEST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A reasonable excuse refers to valid reasons that might exempt someone from complying with an officer's request under subsection (3)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIMING INFORMATION PROVIDED MAY TEND TO INCRIMINATE THE PERSON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event involves a person claiming their right not to provide certain information due to potential self-incrimination, as outlined in section 25 of the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POWER CONFERRED BY THIS SECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The technology here refers to the legal authority granted under the section for officers to make requests and enforce compliance with workplace regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE ENTERED IN ACCORDANCE WITH SECTION 22&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This location is a premise that has been legally accessed by an occupational safety officer as per Section 22 of the ordinance, allowing them to conduct inspections or request information."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;職業安全主任&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The person referred to here is an occupational safety officer who can make requests for workplace compliance and inspection according to local regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 153}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 658}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;負責人&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A responsible party, in charge of a work location as per the ordinance, may be required by officers to display certain notices or provide information about their activities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;告示&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Notices are documents that must be displayed at workplaces according to the ordinance, informing employees and visitors about safety measures, equipment usage, and other relevant matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;本條例的實施&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The implementation of this regulation is a key aspect of workplace compliance as described in section 25 of the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESPONSIBLE PERSON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Responsible Person refers to an organization or individual accountable for managing workspaces where specific notices need to be displayed according to Occupational Safety Officer's requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58cf55b6baed9ac9a3c4052538486aa3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 138}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 606}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMERCIAL ACTIVITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Commercial Activity refers to any business-related operation conducted within a workplace that may require specific notices for compliance with occupational safety regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58cf55b6baed9ac9a3c4052538486aa3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 153}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 658}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDUSTRIAL ACTIVITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Industrial Activity is similar to commercial activity but specifically pertains to manufacturing or production processes taking place in the workspace, which also requires relevant notices as per Occupational Safety Officer's guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58cf55b6baed9ac9a3c4052538486aa3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 153}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 658}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2023 S. 76&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The amendment of section 76 in 2023 refers to legislative changes made to the relevant occupational safety regulations, which may have updated or modified existing requirements for notice display and compliance with Occupational Safety Officer's directives."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58cf55b6baed9ac9a3c4052538486aa3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPLAY PERIOD REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Display Period Requirement is a specific instruction given by an Occupational Safety Officer that mandates how long (at least 12 months) the notices must be displayed in the workplace, ensuring continuous awareness of safety regulations and compliance obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58cf55b6baed9ac9a3c4052538486aa3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 138}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 606}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMENDED 5 OF 2023 S. 76&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The amendment on 5th June, 2023, section 76 is referenced as a source of changes in the legal text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe4c625e0d88b6c7ccc901d0d7b85932</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1157}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2023年第5號第77條修訂&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to an amendment made on July 7, 2023, which revised certain provisions related to offenses and penalties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe4c625e0d88b6c7ccc901d0d7b85932</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 627}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1157}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Public Officers are individuals who may not bear personal legal responsibility for certain acts done or omitted in good faith according to the regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public officers are individuals or groups authorized by law, including those mentioned in section (e) of the ordinance, who have functions, duties, and powers related to enforcing this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0cd5c7a6a9ef486d89da782949b23d31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23a60b107acb436d1472e4d6fcca723b</data>
