</node>
<node id="&quot;21(3)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 21(3)(a) is a clause that allows public officers or assisting persons under specific conditions, potentially relating to occupational safety functions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0cd5c7a6a9ef486d89da782949b23d31</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 629}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMENDED 5 OF 2023 S. 77&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The amendment on 5th of 2023 section 77 modifies the original text regarding offenses related to preventing or intimidating Occupational Safety Officers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0cd5c7a6a9ef486d89da782949b23d31</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 629}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMENDED 5 OF 2023 S. 78&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The amendment on 5th of 2023 section 78 modifies the original text regarding impersonating an occupational safety officer, making it a criminal offense."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0cd5c7a6a9ef486d89da782949b23d31</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 143}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 629}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISCLOSURE OF COMPLAINT DETAILS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Disclosing the identity or information related to a complainant without proper authorization is considered an offense, especially if it involves violations of specific ordinances such as those concerning factory and industrial operations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e25506f50e901e7cebe325e56cdc3f67</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 318}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPLAINANT'S IDENTITY PROTECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The text discusses measures to protect the identity and privacy of complainants, especially in cases involving industrial regulations, which is a social science concern related to legal practices and public safety."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e25506f50e901e7cebe325e56cdc3f67</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 318}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FACTORY AND INDUSTRIAL OPERATIONS ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 59)">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This ordinance regulates factory operations and industrial activities, impacting workplace inspections and the handling of complaints about such violations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e25506f50e901e7cebe325e56cdc3f67</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER'S LIABILITY FOR EMPLOYEE DISCLOSURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The text also addresses potential liabilities that employers may face if their employees disclose sensitive information without proper authorization, which is a social science consideration in labor law and corporate governance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e25506f50e901e7cebe325e56cdc3f67</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 318}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;A PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A public officer is someone who commits an offense by disclosing certain information without lawful authority, such as the name of or any identifying information about a person who has made a complaint regarding a contravention of specific ordinances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6d5bf4b80d4916179a3f7d858e7175b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 317}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPLAINT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A complaint refers to allegations of a contravention related to the Ordinance or the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (Cap. 59)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Complaint is an event where a person alleges a contravention of this Ordinance, leading public officers to take action or become aware of such violations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6d5bf4b80d4916179a3f7d858e7175b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-029d1e15c5db53ebcfd1168d7ac7bbab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 317}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPLAINT INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Complaint information includes details that could identify or name someone who has made a complaint regarding contraventions under specific ordinances, which can be sensitive and confidential."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6d5bf4b80d4916179a3f7d858e7175b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 317}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPIER OF A WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Occupiers of workplaces include those responsible for the management and operation of workspaces where employees perform their duties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da2837c3b5e351b2e1c63635e1c0a663</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEVEL 4 FINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A conviction for an offense against the section results in a financial penalty at level 4 as specified in the amended text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da2837c3b5e351b2e1c63635e1c0a663</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINE LEVEL 4&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS,SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fine Level 4 refers to a specific monetary penalty as determined by the court or regulatory body for offenses against certain sections of law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e7881ceecf94346279b299fee8d79193</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINE LEVEL 5&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A specific level of fine mentioned for offenses related to employment agencies, indicating a monetary penalty system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fine Level 5 is another specific monetary penalty, higher than Fine Level 4, imposed for different types of offenses in workplace safety and labor laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d8d055b17ca5d7c4bc065dbbfefc9360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7881ceecf94346279b299fee8d79193</data>
