</node>
<node id="&quot;FINE LEVEL 6&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS,SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fine Level 6 represents the highest fine level mentioned, indicating a more serious offense or violation of regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e7881ceecf94346279b299fee8d79193</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHARGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A charge imposed by an employer on any of the employer's employees for anything done under this Ordinance constitutes an offense."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-77530b0513e9222b2220609d22541c30</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 294}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 984}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE EMPLOYEE AID&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Providing or receiving aid to a workplace employee in respect of illness or injury is described as a legal action that cannot be obstructed without lawful authority."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-77530b0513e9222b2220609d22541c30</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 294}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 984}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTIMIDATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Intimidation, along with other acts or omissions, can lead to the prevention, obstruction, or delay of aid given to an employee at a workplace and carries penalties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-77530b0513e9222b2220609d22541c30</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTNER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Partner in a business entity who consents to, or facilitates, the commission of an offense described in this Ordinance is also held criminally responsible for it."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-77530b0513e9222b2220609d22541c30</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 370}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1066}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A firm can also be held guilty of an offense if it is proved that the offense was committed with the consent or connivance of a partner in the firm or any person concerned in its management."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feeece6356508f661dcb4d399a15acfe</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIRECTOR, MANAGER, SECRETARY OR OTHER SIMILAR OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These individuals are considered to have committed the same crime as their company if they consented to, were complicit in, or neglected duties leading to an offense by a company."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feeece6356508f661dcb4d399a15acfe</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 334}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1021}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTNER IN THE FIRM OR ANY PERSON CONCERNED IN ITS MANAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Partners and those involved in managing a firm can be held guilty of the same crime as their firm if they consented to, were complicit in, or neglected duties leading to an offense by the firm."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feeece6356508f661dcb4d399a15acfe</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 334}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1021}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATION SAFETY INSPECTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An occupation safety inspector is authorized to prosecute offenses under this Ordinance on behalf of the Secretary."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feeece6356508f661dcb4d399a15acfe</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CIRCUIT COURT JUDGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Circuit Court Judge will hear cases where the offense can be tried summarily under section 1(1A) of this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feeece6356508f661dcb4d399a15acfe</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CRIMINAL PROCEEDINGS (SUMMARY)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to criminal cases that can be tried summarily by magistrates as per the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-20f049d1d30f5c16c93c8bc30a7dab75</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 316}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1005}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;9 MONTHS DEADLINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a specific time period mentioned for prosecution deadlines in relation to certain offenses under this ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-20f049d1d30f5c16c93c8bc30a7dab75</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 316}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1005}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE (CAP. 227)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Magistrates Ordinance is a legal document that has been replaced by new provisions regarding prosecution deadlines for summary offences."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd366107b74e436e9991d1102531645e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUMMARY OFFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Summary offence refers to a minor criminal offense that can be tried in a simplified procedure, as mentioned in the context of prosecution deadlines and evidentiary matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd366107b74e436e9991d1102531645e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDICTABLE OFFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Indictable offence is a more serious crime that may be tried summarily or upon indictment, depending on the circumstances, according to new provisions discussed in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd366107b74e436e9991d1102531645e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROSECUTION DEADLINE (9 MONTHS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The prosecution deadline for summary offences and certain indictable offences under this Ordinance is 9 months from the date of commission, as per newly added sections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd366107b74e436e9991d1102531645e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPIER OF PREMISES WHERE A SPECIFIED WORKPLACE IS LOCATED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to individuals or entities that are in charge of specific work locations mentioned in summons for offences against this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd366107b74e436e9991d1102531645e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER-EMPLOYEE RELATIONSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The concept of employer-employee relationship is discussed in the text, focusing on legal evidence related to employment status and responsibilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text describes various legal provisions affecting employers' obligations towards employees during statutory and alternative holiday arrangements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-adbe757d90ad335b39fd280c5f650025&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d0bd5cc3392e5c0de523f5bb0536a64</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 249}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 913}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The term 'evidence' is used in the text to refer to legal documentation related to employment status, indicating its role in proving or disproving certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d0bd5cc3392e5c0de523f5bb0536a64</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 249}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 913}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ONUS ON DEFENDANT TO PROVE CERTAIN MATTERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event involves the burden of proof for a defendant in cases where compliance with requirements or obligations is not practicable or reasonable, or steps have been taken to comply."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85bf5f4c0ed4aaf7faca3a4817c0b647</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 146}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 641}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERSON NOT LIABLE TO BE PROSECUTED TWICE FOR SAME ACT OR OMISSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event describes that a person cannot be prosecuted twice under the same act or omission if they have already been convicted or acquitted according to another ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85bf5f4c0ed4aaf7faca3a4817c0b647</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 146}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 641}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT'S ORDER FOR FINANCIAL DATA SUBMISSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event involves a court ordering convicted individuals to submit business revenue data to determine their operational scale, in compliance with legal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85bf5f4c0ed4aaf7faca3a4817c0b647</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 146}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 641}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TAX ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 112)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Tax Ordinance (Chapter 112) refers to a specific piece of legislation that requires the submission of tax returns as part of the financial reporting process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f2783fda0cba2d6f90774b999de29ee5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 303}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 992}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCOUNTING AND FINANCIAL REPORTING BUREAU ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 588)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Accounting and Financial Reporting Bureau Ordinance (Chapter 588) is an organization responsible for defining professional accountants, which plays a role in auditing business turnover data."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f2783fda0cba2d6f90774b999de29ee5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 303}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 992}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROFESSIONAL ACCOUNTANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Professional Accountant refers to someone who has been defined by the Accounting and Financial Reporting Bureau Ordinance as required to audit financial statements, indicating their expertise in financial matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f2783fda0cba2d6f90774b999de29ee5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 825}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONVICTED PERSON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Convicted Person is a term used for individuals who have been found guilty of offenses under specific regulations, highlighting legal and social science contexts related to criminal behavior and its consequences."&lt;SEP&gt;"Convicted person refers to individuals who have been found guilty of crimes and are subject to legal proceedings regarding fines or other penalties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f2783fda0cba2d6f90774b999de29ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5997b47960ac46dfe44d6417d759c76</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 825}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TURNOVER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Turnover refers to the financial metric that measures business income from primary activities in Hong Kong, indicating a quantitative aspect of financial reporting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f2783fda0cba2d6f90774b999de29ee5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 825}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;被定罪人士&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"被定罪人士指循公訴程序被裁定犯本條例所訂罪行的僱主或處所佔用人。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19a5c38f633f907e9f2b2434dc908877</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;營業額&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"營業額指符合以下說明的收入:從某被定罪人士在香港進行的主要業務活動所得,並於香港產生或來自香港,但不包括附帶地產生或性質極其特殊的收入。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19a5c38f633f907e9f2b2434dc908877</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;年份&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"年份在這裡指的是被定罪人士的財政年度，如果沒有財政年度則為公曆年。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19a5c38f633f907e9f2b2434dc908877</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;法庭命令&quot;(COURT TO ORDER CONVICTED PERSON TO GIVE FINANCIAL INFORMATION)">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"法庭命令被定罪人士提供營業額信息以確定其業務規模。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19a5c38f633f907e9f2b2434dc908877</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;利润稅回報&quot;(RETURN FURNISHED BY THE CONVICTED PERSON FOR PROFITS TAX UNDER SECTION 51(1) OF THE INLAND REVENUE ORDINANCE (CAP. 112))">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"利润稅回報是指被定罪人士根據《入息徵收條例》第51(1)條提供的營業額信息。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19a5c38f633f907e9f2b2434dc908877</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;審計報告&quot;(DOCUMENT CONTAINING THE TURNOVER INFORMATION OF THE CONVICTED PERSON'S BUSINESS THAT HAS BEEN AUDITED BY A CERTIFIED PUBLIC ACCOUNTANT (PRACTISING))">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"審計報告是指由註冊公共会计師（實習）審核的被定罪人士業務營業額信息文件。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19a5c38f633f907e9f2b2434dc908877</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;法庭進一步命令&quot;(COURT MAY FURTHER ORDER THE CONVICTED PERSON TO GIVE ANY OTHER FINANCIAL INFORMATION THAT THE COURT CONSIDERS RELEVANT IN DETERMINING THE SCALE OF OPERATION OF THE CONVICTED PERSON)">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"法庭可以根據需要命令被定罪人士提供其他相關的財務信息以確定其業務規模。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19a5c38f633f907e9f2b2434dc908877</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;犯罪行為&quot;(OFFENCE UNDER THIS ORDINANCE)">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"犯罪行為是指本條例下被裁定犯下的罪行，涉及僱主或處所佔用人。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19a5c38f633f907e9f2b2434dc908877</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;香港&quot;(HONG KONG)">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"香港是營業額產生地點和收入來源地。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19a5c38f633f907e9f2b2434dc908877</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TURNOVER (營業額)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Turnover, or 营业额 in Chinese, refers to the revenue arising from principal business activities carried out by a convicted person within Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f5997b47960ac46dfe44d6417d759c76</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 825}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;YEAR (年份)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Year here means either the financial year of a convicted person or, if they do not have a financial year, a calendar year."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f5997b47960ac46dfe44d6417d759c76</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE CODES AND SUBSIDIARY LEGISLATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace Codes and Subsidiary Legislation refers to regulations related to workplace codes in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f5997b47960ac46dfe44d6417d759c76</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCIAL YEAR (財務年)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financial Year is the period used for preparing financial statements, either a calendar year or specific accounting periods as defined by an organization."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f5997b47960ac46dfe44d6417d759c76</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 825}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINE (罰款)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fine refers to monetary penalties imposed on convicted persons based on their operational scale and other relevant factors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f5997b47960ac46dfe44d6417d759c76</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE CODES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace Codes refer to guidelines issued by authorities for occupational safety or health, which can include approved rules, standards, regulations, specifications, or clauses from recognized bodies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fabbc3eeb929a4a143a6817fd7b457aa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 609}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1148}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CIRCULATION OF INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The circulation of information includes the publication in the Gazette about the issuance, revision or cancellation of workplace codes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fabbc3eeb929a4a143a6817fd7b457aa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC ACCESS TO DOCUMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Public access is free for reviewing all workplace work guidelines available at the Labour Department's main office during regular working hours."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fabbc3eeb929a4a143a6817fd7b457aa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE CODES OF PRACTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace Codes of Practice are documents issued by the Labour Department providing guidance on occupational safety and health in workplaces."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workplace codes of practice are documents that provide guidelines for safe and healthy work environments, which can be inspected at the head office of the Labour Department without charge during ordinary business hours."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1833f1af069fda07edd900b2ad5d51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 609}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1148}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Code of Practice is a document issued by an authorized body that provides guidance or standards in certain areas such as arbitration or third-party funding of arbitration."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Code of Practice refers to guidelines issued by regulatory bodies that employment agencies must follow. Non-compliance can result in denial or revocation of a license."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Code of Practice refers to the code issued under Division 4 and as amended from time to time."&lt;SEP&gt;"A set of guidelines that outlines specific practices and standards for third party funders in relation to arbitration funding activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Code of Practice refers to a set of guidelines for third party funders, detailing requirements such as capital minimums, conflict resolution procedures, and complaint handling mechanisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Code of Practice refers to a set of practices and standards expected from lawyers entering into ORFS agreements for arbitration. It can be issued, published, amended or revoked by the Authorized Body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Code of Practice refers to guidelines or standards that may be issued by the authorized body, which can influence legal proceedings and compliance obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Code of practice refers to specific regulations issued by authorities to guide certain behaviors or practices, often published in the Gazette."&lt;SEP&gt;"The code of practice outlines practices and standards for third party funders to comply with when engaging in activities related to third party funding of arbitrations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-087a07092efc881959ad458909cb8527&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24bcba17e89155ad11eeca80dd981ea9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff1392eccc9ea622ef0b3868092fcd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a96252983055863ad83c00cacd5a42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c30afb3b53c21887cbdb5f0083639960&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8d110ed10ec7ab18c6afd6141aca4b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d30f0221d62ed77d081c1e001cb1f4e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 413}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1120}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURTROOM PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Courtroom procedures refer to legal processes where workplace codes of practice may be considered relevant evidence in civil or criminal cases involving disputes over their applicability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 389}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1084}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CRIMINAL LIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Criminal liability pertains to the possibility that someone may face criminal charges as a result of violating certain laws, which is not directly related to contravention of workplace codes of practice but can be considered by courts when determining relevant evidence in legal proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 371}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1069}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal procedures refer to formal processes conducted within the judicial system where parties present their cases and evidence before a court, which may involve considering the relevance of workplace codes of practice as evidence."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CIVIL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Civil law refers to legal systems that deal with private rights and obligations between individuals or organizations, such as those related to civil liability in cases involving contravention of workplace codes of practice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CRIMINAL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Criminal law pertains to the body of laws dealing with conduct deemed harmful to society, which may be relevant when considering criminal charges that could arise from violations not directly related to workplace codes but influenced by court decisions in legal proceedings involving such matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK ENVIRONMENT SAFETY AND HEALTH GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace codes of practice are part of industry standards aimed at ensuring the safety and health of workers, providing detailed guidance on practices that must be followed to prevent accidents and ensure a safe working environment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 141}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC INSPECTION WITHOUT CHARGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Public inspection without charge refers to the policy allowing members of the public to access workplace codes of practice for free during ordinary business hours at the head office of the Labour Department, promoting transparency and accessibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RELEVANT EVIDENCE IN LEGAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Relevant evidence in legal proceedings includes documents or information that can be used by either party to support their case before a court, such as workplace codes of practice which may be considered when determining the applicability and relevance of certain laws or regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace safety guidelines are detailed instructions provided in workplace codes of practice that aim to ensure the health and well-being of employees, often including specific measures for preventing accidents and maintaining a safe working environment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 389}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1085}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal evidence refers to information or objects used by parties in legal proceedings to support their claims or defenses, such as workplace codes of practice which can be admitted into court as relevant documents when determining the applicability and relevance of certain laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 389}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1085}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE HEALTH GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace health guidelines are part of safety protocols outlined in workplace codes of practice that focus on maintaining good physical and mental well-being among employees, often including provisions for ergonomics, hygiene, and stress management."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 389}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1084}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL SYSTEM PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal system procedures refer to the formal processes and rules governing how legal cases are handled within a judicial framework, which may involve considering workplace codes of practice as relevant evidence in civil or criminal proceedings involving disputes over their applicability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 141}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are workplace safety regulations which must be given precedence over other types of regulations according to the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workplace safety regulations are established to ensure adequate facilities for treating injuries from workplace accidents, eliminate and avoid dangers in the workplace, maintain hygiene conditions, prevent fires, regulate activities involving hazardous substances or machinery, conduct physical examinations of employees, report details about the workplace to relevant authorities, assess risks associated with workplace activities, and manage various preventive measures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workplace safety regulations refer to the set of guidelines and standards established by authorities like the Labour Department that aim to ensure a safe working environment, often including specific measures for preventing accidents and ensuring employee well-being through workplace codes of practice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b74f875ef514e4d7940f5dbe0d7910e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fd592d376d0854e1e9f902478b9ced3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 47}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 395}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE HEALTH REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace health regulations are part of safety protocols outlined in workplace codes of practice that focus on maintaining good physical and mental well-being among employees, often including provisions for ergonomics, hygiene, and stress management to ensure a healthy working environment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENT PREVENTION MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace accident prevention measures are specific actions outlined in workplace codes of practice that aim to reduce the risk of accidents at work through various safety protocols and guidelines designed to protect employees from harm."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL PROCEEDINGS INVOLVING DISPUTES OVER APPLICABILITY OF LAWS OR REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal proceedings involving disputes over the applicability of laws or regulations may include cases where workplace codes of practice are considered relevant evidence, as courts determine whether certain provisions apply to specific situations and how they should be interpreted."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 389}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1084}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace safety measures refer to a range of actions and protocols established in workplace codes of practice that aim to ensure the health and well-being of employees, often including emergency procedures, first aid provisions, and regular safety training sessions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 141}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE HYGIENE GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace hygiene guidelines are part of safety protocols outlined in workplace codes of practice that focus on maintaining a clean and healthy environment to prevent the spread of diseases among employees, often including specific measures for cleaning, sanitation, and personal hygiene."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE ERGONOMICS STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace ergonomics standards are guidelines established in workplace codes of practice that focus on designing work environments and equipment to fit the physical capabilities of employees, reducing strain and improving overall comfort and productivity at work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 389}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1085}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHIEF SECRETARY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Chief Secretary refers to an official who has the authority to make regulations concerning workplace safety and health as well as additional responsibilities on employers, employees, or non-employer premises occupiers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-71e44b452a884e51f90079ec8a9ac88f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 389}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1083}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAFETY FACILITIES FOR INJURIES FROM ACCIDENTS AT WORK LOCATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Safety facilities designed to treat physical injuries caused by incidents occurring in the workplace are required to be provided according to regulations made under the authority of the Chief Secretary."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-71e44b452a884e51f90079ec8a9ac88f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 389}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1083}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HAZARDS AND POTENTIAL HAZARDS IN WORK LOCATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hazards and potential dangers that may arise for employees at their workplaces need to be eliminated or avoided as per regulations made by the Chief Secretary."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-71e44b452a884e51f90079ec8a9ac88f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 44}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 389}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1083}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRE PREVENTION MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fire prevention measures include providing adequate escape routes to protect workers from the consequences of fires."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b74f875ef514e4d7940f5dbe0d7910e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 47}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 395}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HYGIENE MAINTENANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hygiene maintenance refers to keeping the workplace in a clean and healthy condition as per regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b74f875ef514e4d7940f5dbe0d7910e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 47}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 395}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HAZARDOUS SUBSTANCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hazardous substances are materials that can be stored or used at workplaces, subject to specific regulations for safety reasons."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b74f875ef514e4d7940f5dbe0d7910e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 47}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 395}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MACHINERY OPERATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Machinery operations refer to the use and operation of specified types of equipment in the workplace, which may require special management according to regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b74f875ef514e4d7940f5dbe0d7910e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 47}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 395}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PHYSICAL EXAMINATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Physical examinations are conducted for employees working at workplaces as part of health and safety measures, with records kept accordingly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b74f875ef514e4d7940f5dbe0d7910e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 47}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 395}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPORTING DETAILS ABOUT THE WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace authorities must report detailed information about their work locations to relevant regulatory bodies and notify them of any changes in these details."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b74f875ef514e4d7940f5dbe0d7910e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 47}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 395}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RISK ASSESSMENT FOR WORKPLACE ACTIVITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Risk assessments are performed on various activities conducted at workplaces to determine the level of danger they pose to employee safety or health, guiding preventive measures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b74f875ef514e4d7940f5dbe0d7910e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 47}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 395}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;立法会&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"立法会 is a legislative body that must approve regulations established by the处长 (Director)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f30bd1959d14cc825d9dc1909b7819e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;规例&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"规例 refers to regulations or rules concerning workplace safety, which can be applied, adopted, or incorporated into any publication."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f30bd1959d14cc825d9dc1909b7819e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAFETY AND HEALTH OF EMPLOYEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ensuring the Safety and Health of Employees refers to measures taken to protect workers from hazards in their work environment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d004c27b0c530c46d0712f3eb4a62419</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 155}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 662}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYERS AND EMPLOYEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employers and employees are parties involved who must adhere to additional responsibilities as imposed by regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d004c27b0c530c46d0712f3eb4a62419</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPIERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Occupiers refer to individuals or entities that have control over a workplace, including employers and property owners."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d004c27b0c530c46d0712f3eb4a62419</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATIONS (CONTINUED)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Continued from the previous entry, these regulations can cover various aspects of employee safety and health, additional responsibilities, and occupational conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Further regulations can specify the application scope, exceptions, or factors affecting their implementation in different scenarios."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d004c27b0c530c46d0712f3eb4a62419</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace Safety involves measures to protect employees from physical or mental harm in their work environment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d004c27b0c530c46d0712f3eb4a62419</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADDITIONAL RESPONSIBILITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Additional Responsibilities refer to extra duties imposed on employers and employees beyond basic job requirements, often aimed at improving workplace conditions and safety."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d004c27b0c530c46d0712f3eb4a62419</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Occupational Conditions pertain to the overall environment in which work is performed, including physical, mental, and social aspects that affect employee well-being."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d004c27b0c530c46d0712f3eb4a62419</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STRICT LEGAL LIABILITY OFFENCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Strict legal liability offences are crimes for which criminal intent or negligence does not need to be proven; they can be established based on the act alone."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d004c27b0c530c46d0712f3eb4a62419</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PENALTIES AND SENTENCING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The text outlines potential penalties, including fines up to $400,000 and imprisonment terms of up to 12 months for certain offences."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d004c27b0c530c46d0712f3eb4a62419</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIFFERENT FACTORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These refer to various conditions under which regulations may apply differently, such as types of offenses and circumstances surrounding them."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d004c27b0c530c46d0712f3eb4a62419</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STRICT LEGAL LIABILITY CRIMES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Crimes that are considered strict legal liability require no proof of intent or negligence; they can be established based on the act alone."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d004c27b0c530c46d0712f3eb4a62419</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPRISONMENT TERMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The text specifies potential imprisonment terms for certain offenses, up to 12 months as an additional penalty or in lieu of a fine."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d004c27b0c530c46d0712f3eb4a62419</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATIONS (FINAL)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Final regulations can cover the application and enforcement details, including decisions by specified individuals or groups on various matters related to compliance and oversight."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d004c27b0c530c46d0712f3eb4a62419</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPLIANCE AND OVERSIGHT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Compliance refers to adherence to established rules and standards, while oversight involves monitoring and ensuring that these are followed correctly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d004c27b0c530c46d0712f3eb4a62419</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employees are individuals who work under the employer's contract and may be entitled to annual leave based on the chosen leave year or pro rata basis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employees are the workers who may be at risk of accidents or health issues in the workplace."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employees refer to individuals working at workplaces who could potentially be exposed to substances that pose a risk of absorption or bodily injury."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employees refer to the workers of a specific employer and are involved in wage disputes regarding partial payments or deductions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2cd54f63250a5891c0ad271003ffd081&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a519085f972ab451b135f99083dc3b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38f5270b24602bceb3522785e4ed41d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 65}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 449}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAFETY AND HEALTH STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Safety and Health Standards refer to the measures put in place by regulations to protect employees from harm during work activities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1a519085f972ab451b135f99083dc3b5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 65}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 451}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplaces are the sites where activities are assessed to determine risks to employee safety or health, records are kept, and tests may be conducted."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2cd54f63250a5891c0ad271003ffd081</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 618}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSTANCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Substances include materials used in the workplace which may cause risks such as absorption and bodily injuries when improperly handled."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2cd54f63250a5891c0ad271003ffd081</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 618}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BIOCHEMICAL TESTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Biochemical tests are specified medical examinations to detect substance absorption or bodily injury at workplaces."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2cd54f63250a5891c0ad271003ffd081</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 65}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 449}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BIOLOGICAL TESTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Biological tests, similar to biochemical tests, are used for detecting and investigating cases of substance absorption or bodily injuries in the workplace."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2cd54f63250a5891c0ad271003ffd081</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 65}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 449}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDICAL EXAMINATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Medical examinations are part of the measures taken when there is a risk of absorbing any substance at workplaces or bodily injury from using substances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2cd54f63250a5891c0ad271003ffd081</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 65}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 449}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Occupational safety officers provide information to employers and other persons in specified circumstances, conduct investigations, and may be involved in appeals processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2cd54f63250a5891c0ad271003ffd081</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 618}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STRICT LIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Strict liability refers to a situation where an individual can be held liable for committing an offence regardless of intent or negligence."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-990bd24369be2bc2f9bdd440773f2e19</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 843}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFENDANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Defendant is a party against whom legal action or claims are made in court proceedings, representing one side of the dispute within that context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Defendant is the person who may commit an offence intentionally, recklessly, or with knowledge of all ingredients of the offence as per subsection (7)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-990bd24369be2bc2f9bdd440773f2e19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 843}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SENTENCE OF IMPRISONMENT FOR A PERIOD OF NOT MORE THAN 12 MONTHS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sentence refers to a legal punishment that can be imposed under certain regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-990bd24369be2bc2f9bdd440773f2e19</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 405}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1102}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SCHEDULES 1 OR 2&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Schedules are documents that can be amended by the Commissioner, adding new items or replacing existing ones for specific purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-990bd24369be2bc2f9bdd440773f2e19</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 144}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 636}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXEMPTION FROM THE IMPLEMENTATION OF ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Exemption is a situation where an individual can be granted relief from certain regulations under specific conditions as per section 44(1) and (2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-990bd24369be2bc2f9bdd440773f2e19</data>
