  <data key="d2">chunk-a99af9933148a4cfe141c19ede6d5607</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;魯氏菌的實驗樣本或疫苗&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to experimental samples or vaccines containing Brucella, a type of bacteria."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e298de9a3d303228555899208700c934</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;醫治或護理結核病患者,或提供該項醫治或護理的附帶服務&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This describes the role of treating or caring for patients with tuberculosis, including ancillary services related to their treatment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e298de9a3d303228555899208700c934</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;照料結核病患者(而該等病患者是因其身體或精神虛弱而需接受照料的)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the care provided to weak and frail tuberculosis patients who require assistance due to physical or mental weakness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e298de9a3d303228555899208700c934</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;以研究工作者身分進行與結核病有關的研究工作&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This describes researchers engaged in studying tuberculosis-related topics."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e298de9a3d303228555899208700c934</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;病毒性肝炎的病源&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the sources of viral hepatitis mentioned in occupational health contexts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e298de9a3d303228555899208700c934</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;人類血液或人類血液產品&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are human blood or its products, which can be involved in the transmission of diseases like viral hepatitis."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e298de9a3d303228555899208700c934</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;受豬型鏈球菌感染的豬隻&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are pigs infected with swine brucellosis, which can be a source of infection for workers involved in their handling."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e298de9a3d303228555899208700c934</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;飼鳥病/鸚鵡熱感染的鳥類、其遺體或未經處理的產品&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are birds infected with psittacosis or ornithosis, including their carcasses and untreated products that can pose a risk to workers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e298de9a3d303228555899208700c934</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;使用或處理鉛、鉛化合物或含鉛物質的職業&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are occupations involving the use, handling, or processing of lead, its compounds, or materials containing lead."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e298de9a3d303228555899208700c934</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;暴露於鉛、鉛化合物或含鉛物質的煙霧、塵埃或蒸汽中的職業&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This describes jobs where workers are exposed to the smoke, dust, or vapor of lead, its compounds, or materials containing lead."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e298de9a3d303228555899208700c934</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAD POISONING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lead Poisoning is caused by the use or handling of lead or exposure to its fumes, dust, or vapour in any occupation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lead poisoning refers to the condition resulting from exposure to lead or its compounds, typically in occupational settings involving their use or handling."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f5e945da6ee5d967219134968ca6996b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed1726f93d2592bda71cc16ae18fc7a2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MANGANESE POISONING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Manganese Poisoning results from occupations involving the use or handling of manganese or exposure to its fumes, dust, or vapour."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manganese poisoning involves exposure to manganese or its compounds through occupations where they are used or handled."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f5e945da6ee5d967219134968ca6996b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed1726f93d2592bda71cc16ae18fc7a2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PHOSPHORUS POISONING (INORGANIC AND ORGANIC)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Phosphorus poisoning, whether inorganic or due to the anticholinesterase or pseudo-anticholinesterase effects of organic phosphorus compounds, occurs in occupations involving their use or handling."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed1726f93d2592bda71cc16ae18fc7a2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARSENIC POISONING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arsenic Poisoning happens due to the use or handling of arsenic or exposure to its fumes, dust, or vapour in any occupation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arsenic poisoning involves exposure to arsenic or its compounds through occupational settings where they are used or handled."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f5e945da6ee5d967219134968ca6996b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed1726f93d2592bda71cc16ae18fc7a2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MERCURY POISONING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mercury Poisoning is caused by occupations involving the use or handling of mercury or exposure to its fumes, dust, or vapour."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mercury poisoning refers to the condition resulting from exposure to mercury or its compounds, typically in occupations involving their use or handling."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f5e945da6ee5d967219134968ca6996b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed1726f93d2592bda71cc16ae18fc7a2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CARBON DISULFIDE POISONING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Carbon disulfide poisoning occurs in occupational settings where it is used or handled."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed1726f93d2592bda71cc16ae18fc7a2</data>
</node>
