</node>
<node id="&quot;分娩&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"分娩是指产下婴儿的过程，由1970年第5号第3条增补。"&lt;SEP&gt;"分娩是指怀孕结束并生产的过程，可能是自然分娩或其他方式终止妊娠。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fb31bef1e8dd24810a075920d4fb5602&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ac9460414e7dd9f37d9cef5c1c9b1a5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 83}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 485}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;代替假日&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"代替假日指的是因某些原因替代法定或其他指定假期的情况。"&lt;SEP&gt;"代替假日指的是根据第39(3)条给予或即将给予的假期，由1973年第39号第2条增补，并于1997年第137号第2条修订。"&lt;SEP&gt;"代替假日是僱主可以選擇的一種替代休假方式，用於補充法定假日或其他特定情況下的假期安排。"&lt;SEP&gt;"代替假日是指当原定日期不适合时，通过协商确定的一个替代假期的日子。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5ac9460414e7dd9f37d9cef5c1c9b1a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d9186420295a7ef185edec447e7f6b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e7cedd297868cbefbc6ffea9f8b7a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7430d09345738519e0c07e81b09c47d1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 194}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;另定假日&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"另定假日指的是根据第39(2)及(2A)条给予或即将给予的假期，由1973年第39号第2条增补，并于1997年第137号第2条修订。"&lt;SEP&gt;"另定假日是由雇主和员工双方商议决定的特定日子，在某些情况下可以作为法定或代替假日之外的选择。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5ac9460414e7dd9f37d9cef5c1c9b1a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7430d09345738519e0c07e81b09c47d1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 194}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;外发工&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"外发工是指由他人发出物品或物料，在自己家中或其他不受该人控制或管理的场所进行工序以获得付款或报酬的人，这些工序包括装配、清理等。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5ac9460414e7dd9f37d9cef5c1c9b1a5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 52}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;僱傭合約完成或終止時付給的酬金&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"僱傭合約完成或终止时付给的酬金是指在雇佣合同结束时给予员工的一笔款项。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5ac9460414e7dd9f37d9cef5c1c9b1a5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 195}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;工資期&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"工資期指的是根据雇佣合同或根据第22条有工资支付的期间。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5ac9460414e7dd9f37d9cef5c1c9b1a5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DANGEROUS DRUG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A dangerous drug has the meaning given by the Dangerous Drugs Ordinance (Cap.134&lt;SEP&gt;"Dangerous Drug has the meaning assigned to it in the Dangerous Drugs Ordinance (Cap. 134)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fee7842314099c25edf5106ebd221850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a66612db010d80c91ad3aa4fb718df84</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 203}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 744}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Relevant Date is a term used in relation to employment termination, defining specific dates based on different scenarios such as notice expiration, payment in lieu of notice, contract expiry, retirement date, or the employee's death."&lt;SEP&gt;"Relevant Date is defined as the date of termination of employment or the effective date when an employer changes the terms of an employee's contract, depending on the context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Relevant date is a key reference point in determining when an offer must be made, accepted, or rejected by the employee before it affects their contract rights."&lt;SEP&gt;"The relevant date for terminating employment — (a) if termination of employment is notified under section 6, it refers to the date when the notice expires; (b) if termination of employment is given with a notice-in-lieu-of-notice payment under section 7, it refers to the last day on which wages are paid; (c) if an employee terminates his or her contract without giving notice or notice in lieu thereof as provided for in section 10, then such date shall be the effective date of termination of employment; (d&lt;SEP&gt;"The relevant date is a specific point in time from which periods are calculated for making claims and extending deadlines, mentioned multiple times but not explicitly defined here."&lt;SEP&gt;"The relevant date is a specific point in time from which the 3-month period for claims begins, as mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The relevant date is a term used in section 31N to refer to the starting point for calculating whether an employee has made their claim within the stipulated period of three months, which can be extended by the Secretary with agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The relevant date is not explicitly defined but likely refers to a specific time frame for making claims or taking actions related to an employee who has died."&lt;SEP&gt;"The relevant date marks a specific point of time when an employee's contract might be terminated or renewed according to the conditions outlined."&lt;SEP&gt;"The relevant date refers to a specific day mentioned in the context of an employee's contract termination or offer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The term 'relevant date' refers to a specific day in relation to which certain conditions and offers must be made by the employer before an employee can claim severance payment, often tied to termination dates."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d536cf1eacc47eb2d3812dd2faa34e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e5f55eef00b5211e8c9c5c06c4bde96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff6ba65a2b6882ca144f894790a0cc18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908f80036493cf02a5dd6da247a2a7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da53ed52a17c537de0b1301ebe9c9aa8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adb3767092cbae0c3a6518107e6865b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a40a9600dcdabbcf7b1de20226238a1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4803dc099d05bf6f05b27d07f8429783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33baa15beb160832b6e2302162f04d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d06ee4edd39803f9b252b767c726ef91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a66612db010d80c91ad3aa4fb718df84</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 535}]</data>
</node>
