<node id="&quot;法定假日&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Statutory holiday is the holiday specified by Section 39(1) of relevant laws, indicating official holidays with specific dates as defined by legislation."&lt;SEP&gt;"法定假日是指按照法律规定设立的假期。"&lt;SEP&gt;"法定假日是指根据法律规定设立的假期，包括农历新年、劳动节等。"&lt;SEP&gt;"法定假日是指根据法律规定设立的假期，通常在这些日子雇主需要支付额外工资或提供其他福利。"&lt;SEP&gt;"法定假日是指根據法律或政府規定的節日，通常涉及休息和公共活動。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efb469411694660c1a6d57f27eeccd3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e7cedd297868cbefbc6ffea9f8b7a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dc88cb5a70d0e4c2d56e0663d5e01f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d9186420295a7ef185edec447e7f6b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7430d09345738519e0c07e81b09c47d1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 191}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 731}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1172}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;长期服务金&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Long service payment refers to the compensation that employers must pay according to Section 31R or can be claimed by eligible individuals under Section 31RA, related to employee benefits and rights."&lt;SEP&gt;"Long service payments refer to financial compensation provided by employers to long-serving employees based on their years of service."&lt;SEP&gt;"長期服務金是指根據特定條件和規定計算出的一種補償，用於處理僱員在某些情況下的超額部分。"&lt;SEP&gt;"长期服务金是一种因雇佣合同的执行而产生的补偿，可以是多笔按服务年资支付的酬金、雇主供款的职业退休计划利益或强积金计划权益。"&lt;SEP&gt;"长期服务金是一种支付给因雇员死亡而有权获得的款项，与服务年资相关联。"&lt;SEP&gt;"长期服务金是一种支付给符合条件员工的产品或福利，通常在员工去世时发放。"&lt;SEP&gt;"长期服务金是一种补偿形式，在特定条件下支付给员工，体现了雇佣合同的终止或变更时的一种经济补偿机制。"&lt;SEP&gt;"长期服务金是一种补偿机制，根据员工的工作日数和工资计算得出。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efb469411694660c1a6d57f27eeccd3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3af8cb7f383ac57c1ab02ce86bc0393f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fb9bafd0cba5b9cfa67282f7c70bf83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39ff31ef4fdbcf84c8c1f1a297094829&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a3ec4e0b16148270927aaef6bc6cb14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efde970dacc8f16ccdb4b94374b28042&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-985c71a2aa2037adf4ce25fd3c8c12de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23d51c29b119b65758639275d4ba4446</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 168}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 696}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;青年&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Young person is a term used in social science contexts referring to someone who has reached the age of 15 but is not yet 18, often associated with studies on youth development or legal ages for certain activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"青年指年滿15歲但未滿18歲的個人，涉及法律和社會保障方面的定義。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efb469411694660c1a6d57f27eeccd3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e03073aa0f6abdf5280f21aa17a6bbf7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;後嗣&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Issue refers to the children of deceased employees, regardless of whether they have reached adulthood, used in social and legal contexts related to inheritance rights and benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"後嗣是指已故僱員的子女，在某些情況下包括繼子女、領養子女等，與家庭法學相關。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efb469411694660c1a6d57f27eeccd3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e03073aa0f6abdf5280f21aa17a6bbf7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;長期服務金&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"長期服務金是指向有權領取的人支付的一種福利產品，與僱傭關係相關。"&lt;SEP&gt;"長期服務金是指因雇员去世而产生的补偿，基于服务年资计算。"&lt;SEP&gt;"長期服務金是指根據僱傭條例規定，在僱員工作滿一定年限後可獲得的一筆一次性補償金。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e03073aa0f6abdf5280f21aa17a6bbf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90c0794da631cfd39500d26a03a02ecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f522c2b4fb2af18c29efee69dde9f663</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 55}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 427}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1122}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;《婚姻制度改革條例》(第178章)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"《婚姻制度改革條例》是另一部法律文件，與婚姻法規及相關變革有關。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e03073aa0f6abdf5280f21aa17a6bbf7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 55}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 427}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1122}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;指明僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"指明僱員是指符合特定條件的僱員，在此段落中提及的是第31ZEA(2)(a)、(b)及，但具體內容未完全列出。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e03073aa0f6abdf5280f21aa17a6bbf7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 55}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 427}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1122}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPOUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Spouse refers to the legally married person of a married employee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b40910fef9ba5e880f9a32ae794f8b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 587}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WEEK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A week refers to a period of seven days used for calculating work hours and determining eligibility for certain contracts or benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Week, in reference to clause 11 and parts VA and VB, denotes a period from midnight on Saturday evening to midnight on the following Saturday evening."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b40910fef9ba5e880f9a32ae794f8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d9929bbede2eb72d013426b56ad4e6c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 504}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MISCARRIAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Miscarriage refers to the expulsion of an unborn fetus within 24 weeks of pregnancy that cannot survive after birth."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b40910fef9ba5e880f9a32ae794f8b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 112}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 569}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sickness Allowance is a benefit provided to employees who are absent from work due to illness or certain medical conditions, such as pregnancy-related issues and miscarriages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness Allowance is a form of paid leave provided by employers for sick employees as per section 33, which can be considered part of the broader employment benefits package."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness Allowance is a form of payment provided to employees who are unable to work due to illness or injury, including during maternity leave if specified by law."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness Allowance refers to benefits provided by employers to their employees who are sick, as detailed in Part VII of the relevant ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness Allowance refers to financial compensation provided to employees for sick leave as per labor regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness Allowance refers to the monetary benefit provided by employers to employees who are unable to work due to illness, calculated based on their average wages over a specified period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness allowance is a form of financial support given by employers to employees who are sick."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness allowance is another specific type of entitlement that can be considered as a product or benefit for employees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness allowance is defined by clause 33 and pertains to sick pay as specified in the relevant regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness allowance is money paid to employees who are unable to work due to illness or injury, as per the labor contract and regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness allowance refers to a sum equivalent to four-fifths of the daily average wages earned by an employee during specified periods before becoming sick or injured, provided certain conditions are met."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness allowance refers to financial support provided during periods when an employee is unable to work due to illness or injury, which can be part of terminal payments if applicable."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness allowance refers to the financial compensation provided by employers for sick leave as per the regulations outlined in this section."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8b40910fef9ba5e880f9a32ae794f8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7550fdff3623ae221e2d156f6ce5cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c96e8be9052d451fbf9a64ace39448d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5c7df56b94c0c429230f0546be40142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d46f6e07563bbf79e567c647ecf4fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdc4a39840a667a7878ee99d632412a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-323c200d08170c4d996dbd247312e21a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5e29cfe8eddddf302f5a14076a67a7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1c30b39b26dc22df210f2ea63b93552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af043de8381bfd2d54ddf7a99fe8b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f729e4dc4d8c13592d31110960bc5996</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 112}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 569}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SICKNESS DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A sickness day refers to a day when an employee is absent from work due to injury or illness, including days off required under The Ordinance No. 599 provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness Day is a leave period that does not count towards wage calculations for termination agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness Day is a period during which an employee takes leave due to illness, as documented in their record-keeping system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness Day is a type of leave taken by the employee due to temporary incapacity for which compensation may be payable under section 10 of the Employees' Compensation Ordinance (Cap. 282)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness Day is an absence from work due to illness, during which the employee may be entitled to sick leave or sickness allowance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness day is the term used for days when an employee is unable to work due to illness, which can be subject to certain conditions as defined in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness day refers to a period during which an employee takes leave due to illness, for which sickness allowance may be payable under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness day refers to a period during which an employee takes time off due to illness, often with the need for medical certification in some contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness day refers to the period during which an employee is unable to work due to illness and may be entitled to paid leave as per company policies or legal frameworks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness days are paid leave given to employees when they are unable to work due to illness, ensuring that they can recover without financial hardship."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sickness days refer to time off work due to illness or medical reasons."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e6ca8ea4c3347749e50a0bfdf049de28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b40910fef9ba5e880f9a32ae794f8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89f7731524d41ce9b762132c808abd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d14b62c50b2a0a92ac73c8ef0642fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fef56ddac89c58276c95d49a4ad2fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af043de8381bfd2d54ddf7a99fe8b0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 100}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 520}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cease refers to the permanent or temporary stopping of operations as per parts VA, VB, Annex 3, and Annex 6; the term 'diminish' has a corresponding meaning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cease, in relation to Part VA, Part VB, the Third Schedule and the Sixth Schedule, means cease either permanently or temporarily and from whatsoever cause. Diminish has a corresponding meaning."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fee7842314099c25edf5106ebd221850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b40910fef9ba5e880f9a32ae794f8b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 13}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOLIDAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A holiday is another term for a designated day off that may be used in conjunction with paternity leave according to the text provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"Holiday denotes periods off from work as defined in subsequent clauses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Holiday is a non-working day that may be designated by law or company policy and can include public holidays as well as personal days."&lt;SEP&gt;"Holiday is a non-working day that may be included in the terms and conditions of an employee's contract, affecting its termination or renewal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Holiday is a non-working day that may be part of an employee's annual leave package or granted separately as per company policy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Holiday is an official or unofficial leave day, recognized under the BAA for inclusion in wage calculations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Holiday refers to a non-working day that employees are given as part of their annual leave entitlements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Holiday refers to days when employees are entitled to rest and do not work but may receive some form of compensation or benefit."&lt;SEP&gt;"Holiday refers to specific days designated as non-working days or public holidays that are part of an employee's entitlements beyond regular work hours."&lt;SEP&gt;"Holidays are non-working days that may be provided by employers, often for public celebrations or personal observances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b40910fef9ba5e880f9a32ae794f8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccf624f83121089caf9f8fb044043303&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63d3371d1b762c2013adc08da9c549f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c54e7deea495212bab465e4af100b7ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fef56ddac89c58276c95d49a4ad2fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 504}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;另有定假日&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"另行规定的假日，具体指由雇主或相关机构额外设定的休假时间。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e7cedd297868cbefbc6ffea9f8b7a8f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 191}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 731}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1172}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第39(4)條規定給予僱員的假日&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"根据第39条第4款规定给予员工的休假，具体指由雇主按照法律规定提供的额外假期。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e7cedd297868cbefbc6ffea9f8b7a8f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 191}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 731}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1172}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;法定节假日薪酬&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"法定节假日薪酬是指根据相关法律法规规定的在法定节假日工作的薪资待遇。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e7cedd297868cbefbc6ffea9f8b7a8f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 481}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;強制性公積金計劃&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Strong积金计划 is a type of industry-related financial plan that may affect the calculation or deduction of long service payments as mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"強制性公積金計劃指的是根据《强制性公積金計劃條例》(第485章)注册的公积金计划，由雇主和雇员共同缴纳一定比例的资金到个人账户中。"&lt;SEP&gt;"強制性公積金計劃是指中国政府要求所有雇主为其雇员设立的强制性公积金制度，此处也指代一个具体的组织实体。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-233de206d4d440690ca3d19bf8ddb77c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e7cedd297868cbefbc6ffea9f8b7a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f522c2b4fb2af18c29efee69dde9f663</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 55}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 426}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;產假&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"產假是为怀孕和分娩后的女性员工提供的假期，分为多个时间段计算总天数。"&lt;SEP&gt;"產假是女性员工在产假期间的权利和福利。"&lt;SEP&gt;"產假是指女性僱員因懷孕和生產而享有的休假期間。"&lt;SEP&gt;"產假是指女性员工因怀孕或分娩而按照相关条例缺勤的时间段。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fb31bef1e8dd24810a075920d4fb5602&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e7cedd297868cbefbc6ffea9f8b7a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb1fa32929a7020d65f293e8c9d7dd58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75ec5cbcc26a69d2fa91ff3cd7cec100</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 83}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 486}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;產假薪酬&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"產假薪酬指的是根据相关规定给予产假期间的薪资待遇。"&lt;SEP&gt;"產假薪酬是女性僱員在休產假期間可獲得的補償金額。"&lt;SEP&gt;"產假薪酬是指女性员工在产假期间应得的工资补偿，根据其最近12个月或较短时期的平均每日收入计算四分之五。"&lt;SEP&gt;"產假薪酬是指根据相关条款支付给因产假而调离粗重、危险或有害工作的员工的款项。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e7cedd297868cbefbc6ffea9f8b7a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5d9d61caba55ae3f9dfd2940ae47cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 481}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;《第599章》規定&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL REGULATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These refer to regulations under Chapter 599 of the laws of Hong Kong that govern various aspects of employment such as leaves and compensations."&lt;SEP&gt;"《第599章》规定是指列于附表12第一部分中的、对活动范围施加限制的规定，具体指与劳动关系相关的条例和细则。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e7cedd297868cbefbc6ffea9f8b7a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9d7bf328eb68da98c29ac72b529085</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;處長 (COMMISSIONER)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"处长指的是劳工处处长，并包括副处长及助理处长，在处理劳动事务时具有相应的权力和职责。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e7cedd297868cbefbc6ffea9f8b7a8f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;閉廠 (LOCK-OUT)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"闭厂是指根据《职工会条例》(第332章)第二条给予该词的含义，即雇主因某些原因暂时或永久停止运营的行为。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e7cedd297868cbefbc6ffea9f8b7a8f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOCK-OUT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lock-out has the meaning given by Section 2 of the Employment Ordinance (Cap.332) in Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lock-out refers to a situation where an employer stops work, typically as part of industrial action or due to financial difficulties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd0362fbf5661d142ff4aeefe27aea79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a67530e0a9df975682238097b18b864</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1093}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Labour Tribunal is a specialized tribunal that handles disputes related to employment, including cases where an order of reinstatement or reengagement may be issued."&lt;SEP&gt;"Labour Tribunal is a judicial body where claims regarding labor disputes, including those concerning severance payments, can be filed according to Part 4 of the Labour Tribunal Ordinance (Cap. 25)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Labour Tribunal is a part of the organization responsible for making awards of compensation, alongside the court."&lt;SEP&gt;"Labour Tribunal is an organization involved in resolving disputes related to employee dismissals and other labor matters, as described within the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Labour Tribunal is an organization that handles labor disputes and makes judgments in accordance with relevant laws and regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Labour Tribunal is established under Section 3 of the Labour Relations Commission Ordinance (Cap.25) in Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"Labour Tribunal is part of the Labor and Industrial Relations Tribunal, handling labor-related disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Labour Tribunal refers to a location or institution where labor disputes are adjudicated, as mentioned in the context of filing claims under the Labour Tribunal Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Tribunal handles disputes related to employment and wages according to the text provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Tribunal is a body that handles claims according to Part 4 of the Labour Tribunal Ordinance (Cap. 25)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Tribunal is a judicial body responsible for resolving disputes related to employment rights and conditions in Hong Kong as per Cap. 25 of the Ordinances."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Tribunal is a legal body mentioned in the text, involved in making awards and settlements related to employment disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Tribunal is a specialized tribunal for labor disputes, which considers circumstances such as employment length when deciding cases involving employee rights."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Tribunal is an organization responsible for resolving labor-related claims and disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Tribunal is an organization that can make orders regarding the terms of re-engagement or reinstatement in employment disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Tribunal is an organization that, along with the court, has the authority to make awards of terminal payments under specific conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Tribunal is another organizational body that decides on orders of reinstatement or re-engagement, similar to the court's role."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b27a008edb9bce1c0b390190fc14d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9277263fe4be5c215993320cc63c410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d580b5b472939d182c05bf201c52ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f6302661df10aad972a6e63a05f0aa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cec848f1858ebf48439b7f8f5961be4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adb3767092cbae0c3a6518107e6865b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d4bd265e2aa3d3a8af55fbca1b13963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4803dc099d05bf6f05b27d07f8429783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4254cc0d21afce88f6eb9b8c9366f7cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a67530e0a9df975682238097b18b864&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee588c56ed96e2cbc4dc5b9474b0fa9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2200d76e6cc5397e7868136950dfb19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f17d41b36a40e80f45f0f635b4ad7eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc2894a439737cb35869b760804ff684&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93a1fe97f228ec755ced3c31d6506c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68f0496b4d3967e4dee08ee2a743063</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 833}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (VOLUNTARY) MPFS BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An employer-funded voluntary MPFS benefit is a type of financial compensation related to an employee's years of service and subject to repayment under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"An employer-funded voluntary contribution to a Mandatory Provident Fund Scheme for an employee is considered a specific type of benefit, defined by sections 2(1) and 4 of the relevant legislation."&lt;SEP&gt;"For a particular employee, the employer-funded (voluntary) MPFS benefit refers to the accumulated right that meets certain descriptions — specifically, from a mandatory provident fund scheme."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2193ccb19ec3e792d874a92951eae0f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e70ac051c2f0b62b1c78481493c78790&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a67530e0a9df975682238097b18b864</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 177}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED MPFS BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employer-Funded MPFS Benefit refers to the vested interest in a voluntary Mandatory Provident Fund Scheme (MPFS) for an employee, attributable to voluntary contributions made by the employer as defined under Section 2(1) of the Mandatory Provident Fund Schemes Ordinance (Cap. 485)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employer-funded MPFS benefit refers to either an employer-funded (mandatory) MPFS benefit or an employer-funded (voluntary) MPFS benefit for a specified employee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d0dd3aa2554b81fa47ed2eec0f056d25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e7d4bbfd9a7f73f2810843d3a9e9fa2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 176}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 714}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED NON-EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An employer-funded non-exempt ORS benefit is a type of employee benefit that does not fall under specific exemptions, as defined in section 3 of the relevant legislation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employer-Funded Non-Exempt ORS Benefit refers to an occupational retirement plan benefit for an employee that is funded by the employer and not exempt as defined under Section 3 of the amendment from the Fourth Ordinance (No.4) in 2022."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e70ac051c2f0b62b1c78481493c78790&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e7d4bbfd9a7f73f2810843d3a9e9fa2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 177}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED SPECIFIED ORS BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employer-Funded Specified ORS Benefit refers to an occupational retirement plan benefit for an employee that is either a non-exempt or specified exempt contribution from the employer as defined under Section 3 of the amendment from the Fourth Ordinance (No.4) in 2022."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e7d4bbfd9a7f73f2810843d3a9e9fa2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 177}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED PRESCRIBED PORTION EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employer-Funded Prescribed Portion Exempt ORS Benefit refers to a specific type of exempt occupational retirement plan benefit for an employee as defined under Section (5) in the amendment from the Fourth Ordinance (No.4) in 2022."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e7d4bbfd9a7f73f2810843d3a9e9fa2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 177}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employer-Funded Exempt ORS Benefit refers to a specific type of exempt occupational retirement plan benefit for an employee as defined under Section (4) in the amendment from the Fourth Ordinance (No.4) in 2022."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employer-funded exempt ORS benefit refers to the benefits provided by an employer in a occupational retirement plan (ORS) that are exempt from certain regulations, as specified under relevant clauses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-28b2163160f25fa57988c0b4d0c740cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e7d4bbfd9a7f73f2810843d3a9e9fa2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 581}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1140}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED ORS BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Employer-Funded ORS Benefit refers to financial benefits provided by employers under occupational retirement schemes, potentially subject to specific conditions and calculations as outlined in the ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employer-Funded ORS Benefit refers to a general occupational retirement plan benefit for an employee that is funded by the employer as defined under the amendment from the Fourth Ordinance (No.4) in 2022."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e43ce81a5e24ba44cc5896e9318ba422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e7d4bbfd9a7f73f2810843d3a9e9fa2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 176}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 712}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MANDATORY PROVIDENT FUND SCHEME (MPFS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Mandatory Provident Fund Scheme (MPFS) is a statutory retirement savings scheme for employees, managed by an authorized trustee as defined under the Mandatory Provident Fund Schemes Ordinance (Cap. 485)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e7d4bbfd9a7f73f2810843d3a9e9fa2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 176}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 714}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOURTH ORDINANCE (NO.4)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Fourth Ordinance (No.4) is a legislative amendment that introduced specific definitions and classifications for employer-funded occupational retirement plan benefits as of the date it was enacted."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5e7d4bbfd9a7f73f2810843d3a9e9fa2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 177}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECOGNIZED SCHEME OF MEDICAL TREATMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Recognized Scheme of Medical Treatment is a medical treatment scheme operated by an employer and approved by the Director for this Ordinance under section 34(1)."&lt;SEP&gt;"A recognized scheme of medical treatment is a plan operated by an employer that provides employees with reasonable out-patient medical treatment without expense to the employee, as approved by the Director."&lt;SEP&gt;"Recognized Scheme of Medical Treatment refers to a formal healthcare program that may be operated by the employer, requiring specific registered practitioners for issuing certificates related to employee attendance at medical examinations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Recognized Scheme of Medical Treatment refers to the specific medical services covered under an employer's health insurance or benefit plan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Recognized scheme of medical treatment is a formal healthcare program authorized by employers that covers certain types of medical treatments for employees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Recognized scheme of medical treatment is a healthcare plan provided by employers that has been approved under Section 34(1) of relevant regulations, and is used to implement this regulation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b89f7731524d41ce9b762132c808abd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908f80036493cf02a5dd6da247a2a7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4af496fc2b1c26e3d6bca76a4b99c25f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcd2a26e931b9fa624c25b0caadbcdb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28b2163160f25fa57988c0b4d0c740cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af043de8381bfd2d54ddf7a99fe8b0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 111}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 567}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STRIKE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Strike has the meaning given by Section 2 of the Trade Union Ordinance (Cap. 332) and is defined under relevant amendments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Strike is defined here as a form of collective action by workers who stop working in order to gain certain rights or benefits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-28b2163160f25fa57988c0b4d0c740cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd0362fbf5661d142ff4aeefe27aea79</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1093}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL RETIREMENT SCHEME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Occupational Retirement Scheme is a type of financial product or benefit provided by an employer for the long-term savings and investment needs of employees in relation to their retirement."&lt;SEP&gt;"An occupational retirement scheme is a plan or arrangement providing benefits based on length of service, excluding mandatory provident fund schemes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Occupational retirement scheme refers to a plan or arrangement where benefits are paid according to service years upon an employee's retirement, death, loss of capacity, or termination of employment, excluding Mandatory Provident Fund schemes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da3daa00f8a571e7a58b273ea6df48ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28b2163160f25fa57988c0b4d0c740cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-765d51e319fa417bcf02401654532054</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 581}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1140}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;職業退休計劃&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"職業退休計劃是一种由管理人管理和运营的职业养老金计划，在此上下文中指代一种具体的组织实体。"&lt;SEP&gt;"職業退休計劃是指一項計劃或安排，根據該計劃，在僱員退休、去世、喪失行為能力或終止服務時，須就僱員支付按服務年資支付的利益。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b97ce5993df5b6616c6c24d7afbaa008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f522c2b4fb2af18c29efee69dde9f663</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 54}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 423}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;轉制日&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"轉制日指《2022年僱傭及退休計劃法例(抵銷安排)(修訂)條例》開始實施的日期。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b97ce5993df5b6616c6c24d7afbaa008</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 54}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 423}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;續訂&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"續訂包括延長，而凡提述續訂合約之處，亦須據此解釋。"&lt;SEP&gt;"續訂是指在特定情况下，由已故僱主的遗产权利继承人续签劳动合同的行为或事件。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b97ce5993df5b6616c6c24d7afbaa008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad6d0a2eed4fbaf59a6253fe84df6ac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 54}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 423}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;疾病津貼&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Disease allowance is a benefit provided by the employer under the recognized medical plan, which can be used to cover costs related to treatments from registered practitioners."&lt;SEP&gt;"疾病津貼是一种根据法律规定或合同约定，因员工生病而给予的一种补偿。它通常与超时工作薪酬的计算无关，除非特定条件下其平均款额达到一定比例。"&lt;SEP&gt;"疾病津貼是一种由雇主提供的福利，用于支付患病员工的带薪假期。"&lt;SEP&gt;"疾病津貼是指因病假而获得的经济补偿。"&lt;SEP&gt;"疾病津贴是雇主在员工因病假期间应支付的一种福利或补偿。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73492d2774f700c9b55459d33fea445f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede40d11dd383fafe8000e746a4c43b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61c622614f8a7b3173a59e39171f674c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7b8e86ee38adbfe875f0b9f94a17519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f7b047f9f55a2ab249abdbcd1a65d36</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 85}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 488}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;假日薪酬&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"假日薪酬是基于法律或合同规定，在法定节假日工作的额外报酬。它可能根据具体的法律规定来确定发放条件和金额。"&lt;SEP&gt;"假日薪酬是指根據第 VIII 部須支付的與休假日相關的補償。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c82c895f7b30d4831c428126a0af9486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7b8e86ee38adbfe875f0b9f94a17519</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 85}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 488}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;超时工作薪酬&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"超时工作薪酬是指员工在正常工作时间之外的工作所获得的补偿，通常按照一定的比例计算。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d7b8e86ee38adbfe875f0b9f94a17519</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 85}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 488}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;A&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A is a variable representing the reference amount in the formula A = B × C × 5% × 12."&lt;SEP&gt;"A is a variable representing the reference amount in the formula, which calculates the exempted occupational pension benefit based on the employee's final average relevant income and service years."&lt;SEP&gt;"A represents the reference amount for calculating ORS benefits, derived from multiplying the employee's final average monthly relevant income by their years of service at 5% per year."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b4faa824234e05596e1018cdb0e9f8e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ebf8163b69d6052462eecc2153a2260&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf9c100a1957a664aeaa3ecb305d4386</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;B&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"B denotes the employee's final average monthly relevant income, which is a key factor in determining the reference amount for ORS benefit calculations."&lt;SEP&gt;"B is a variable representing the employee's final monthly average relevant income in the formula for calculating the exempted occupational pension benefit."&lt;SEP&gt;"B represents the final average monthly relevant income of an employee, which is crucial for calculating the exempted occupational pension benefits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b4faa824234e05596e1018cdb0e9f8e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ebf8163b69d6052462eecc2153a2260&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf9c100a1957a664aeaa3ecb305d4386</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;C&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"C indicates the years of service (proportionally calculated if less than a year) of an employee in determining the amount of exempted occupational pension benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"C is a variable indicating the employee's service years (proportionally calculated if less than one year) in the formula to calculate the exempted occupational pension benefit, where employer contributions are excluded from the occupational pension plan benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"C represents the number of years (and pro rata for an incomplete year) of service to which the employer-funded exempt ORS benefit is attributable, used as another critical component in calculating the benefit amount."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b4faa824234e05596e1018cdb0e9f8e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ebf8163b69d6052462eecc2153a2260&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf9c100a1957a664aeaa3ecb305d4386</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 173}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;僱主供款豁免職業退休計劃利益&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"僱主供款豁免職業退休計劃利益 refers to the part of the employer's contribution that is exempted under an occupational retirement plan, based on specific conditions and formulas."&lt;SEP&gt;"僱主供款豁免職業退休計劃利益是指根據某職業退休計劃,須就僱員支付的有關僱主供款豁免職業退休計劃的利益。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b4faa824234e05596e1018cdb0e9f8e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf9c100a1957a664aeaa3ecb305d4386</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;《強制性公積金計劃條例》(第485章)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Mandatory Provident Fund Schemes Ordinance (Cap. 485) is a Hong Kong legislation that provides for the establishment of mandatory provident funds and related matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9c100a1957a664aeaa3ecb305d4386</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;職業退休计划&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"職業退休计划 refers to an occupational pension scheme designed to provide retirement benefits to employees, often regulated by specific laws or regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9c100a1957a664aeaa3ecb305d4386</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;免職業退休計劃利益&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"免職業退休計劃利益是指根據某職業退休計劃,須就僱員支付有關的僱主供款豁免職業退休計劃的利益。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b4faa824234e05596e1018cdb0e9f8e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;強制性公積金計劃(豁免)規例&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"強制性公積金計劃(豁免)規例是指附屬法例B,用於界定某些特定的職業退休计划。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b4faa824234e05596e1018cdb0e9f8e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;最終每月平均有關入息&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"最終每月平均有關入息指根據某職業退休計劃或相關規定計算得出的僱員最後一段時間內的平均月收入,用於確定豁免職業退休計劃的利益額度。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b4faa824234e05596e1018cdb0e9f8e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;編輯附註:实施日期:2025年5月1日。&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"編輯附註指出了該條款或規定將在2025年5月1日正式生效。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b4faa824234e05596e1018cdb0e9f8e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ALTERNATIVE HOLIDAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Alternative Holiday refers to a holiday granted or to be granted under section 39(2) and (2A)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alternative holidays allow employers to reschedule statutory holidays within a 60-day window if they notify employees in advance as per the regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"An alternative holiday is a day that can be substituted for a statutory holiday if the employee cannot work due to personal reasons, ensuring they still receive time off as mandated by law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fee7842314099c25edf5106ebd221850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aed3ae0b98488b1b913e6b49db19fee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adbe757d90ad335b39fd280c5f650025</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 97}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 509}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Annual Leave Pay is required by this Ordinance to be paid in respect of a period of annual leave and any sum required to be paid under section 41D."&lt;SEP&gt;"Annual Leave Pay refers to the wages paid by an employer in respect of a day of annual leave taken by an employee, which may be reduced based on certain conditions as specified in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Annual leave pay is a form of compensation provided by an employer to employees for unused vacation days when their employment ends."&lt;SEP&gt;"Annual leave pay is a specific type of entitlement defined in the legal document, representing a product or benefit provided by employers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Annual leave pay is compensation provided to employees under certain conditions related to their employment and entitlements during periods when they are not actively working but have earned leave time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Annual leave pay is the compensation an employee would receive if their contract of employment were terminated on a specific day, calculated according to Section 41C."&lt;SEP&gt;"Annual leave pay is the compensation provided by an employer for the period during which an employee takes their annual leave."&lt;SEP&gt;"Annual leave pay refers to financial benefits provided during annual leave periods, which can be part of the total package of terminal payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fee7842314099c25edf5106ebd221850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74bf264f43f2a8be1c1c6d9a90273b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7dbc6cb0d2646456eacee5097d668ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed2004c9e59e7e54ef6756f3c59d039a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c46e076b844c67b6ef12faaaccec1c4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1c30b39b26dc22df210f2ea63b93552</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 129}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 580}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CAP. 599 REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cap. 599 Requirement means a requirement set out in Part 1 of Schedule 12 that imposes a restriction on movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cap. 599 Requirement refers to specific health and safety regulations mandated by the government, which can affect work attendance during annual leave."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cap. 599 Requirement refers to specific regulations that may limit an employee's actions and affect employment terms, necessitating compliance from the employee which can impact their job security or contract conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cap. 599 requirement refers to a set of regulations or guidelines enforced by the government, impacting employee work status."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fee7842314099c25edf5106ebd221850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6297aac0b94f77cc5b93128ce6315ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63d3371d1b762c2013adc08da9c549f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8b48e83da24f4750fe34f6e53c34ac0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 13}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHILD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Child means a person under the age of 15 years."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fee7842314099c25edf5106ebd221850</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 98}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 514}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONFINEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Confinement means the delivery of a child."&lt;SEP&gt;"Confinement refers to the actual delivery process, which can be used as an alternative starting point for maternity leave if it occurs before the scheduled commencement date determined by section 12AA."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fee7842314099c25edf5106ebd221850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8d3158e721c74f203da21b92ec49085</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 98}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 514}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DANGEROUS DRUG (危險藥物)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A dangerous drug refers to substances defined under the Dangerous Drugs Ordinance (Cap. 134)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIRECTOR (署長) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Director of Health is a specific role within an organization, responsible for health-related matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOMESTIC SERVANT (家庭傭工)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A domestic servant includes various roles such as garden servants, chauffeurs, and boat-boys, among others who provide personal services to employers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE (僱員) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An employee is a person covered by the provisions of this Ordinance, specifically those outlined in section 4."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER (僱主) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The employer refers to any individual or entity that has entered into a contract of employment with an employee and includes their duly authorized agents, managers, or factors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT (僱主供款豁免職業退休計劃利益)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a type of employer-funded benefit under the Occupational Retirement Schemes Ordinance that does not require tax exemption for both parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED NON-EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT (僱主供款非豁免職業退休計劃利益) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are benefits provided by an employer to employees, which do not qualify as exempted under the Occupational Retirement Schemes Ordinance and thus may be subject to tax."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED ORS BENEFIT (僱主供款職業退休計劃利益)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This term refers to benefits provided by employers that are payable upon retirement, death, incapacity or termination of service, attributable to employer contributions under the Occupational Retirement Schemes Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (PRESCRIBED PORTION) EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT (僱主供款(訂明部分)豁免職業退休計劃利益)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a specific type of employer-funded benefit that qualifies for tax exemption under the Occupational Retirement Schemes Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (SPECIFIED) ORS BENEFIT (僱主供款(指明)職業退休計劃利益)">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are benefits provided by employers, which may or may not be exempted from taxation according to specific criteria under the Occupational Retirement Schemes Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (PRESCRIBED PORTION) EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to an employer-funded part of an ORS benefit that falls under specified exemptions, as mentioned in subsection (5) of the same section."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e70ac051c2f0b62b1c78481493c78790</data>
