<node id="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Statutory Holiday is a day off work that employees are entitled to according to laws and regulations, specifically mentioned in relation to Chinese New Year days."&lt;SEP&gt;"Statutory Holiday refers to days off that are legally recognized and should not be considered as normal working days when determining layoffs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Statutory holiday is a non-working day designated by law, which also does not count towards normal working days in the context of lay-off determination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Statutory holiday refers to official public holidays recognized by law, which employees are entitled to take off with pay or without pay depending on local regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Statutory holidays are days off that employees are entitled to according to laws or regulations, as mentioned in section 39(4)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0aed3ae0b98488b1b913e6b49db19fee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8e2655c247e96affa05132d650c897b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e70ac051c2f0b62b1c78481493c78790&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2138132720286ddae5a4634e3cd8c8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f729e4dc4d8c13592d31110960bc5996</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 97}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 509}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOLIDAY PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Holiday pay is a form of compensation for time off taken by employees as mandated by law or company policy, included in the scope of terminal payments under this Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Holiday pay is the compensation provided by an employer for statutory holidays, alternative holidays, substituted holidays, and other days on which an employee must be granted a holiday, as defined in section 40."&lt;SEP&gt;"Holiday pay is yet another specific type of entitlement defined in the legal document, representing a product or benefit provided by employers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e70ac051c2f0b62b1c78481493c78790&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1c30b39b26dc22df210f2ea63b93552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 97}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 509}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ISSUE (後嗣) MEANS A CHILD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The term 'issue' refers to the children of a deceased employee, including step-children and adopted children by the employee, but not those adopted by another person unless under specific legal conditions as per section 5(1) of the Adoption Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e70ac051c2f0b62b1c78481493c78790</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MANDATORY PROVIDENT FUND SCHEMES ORDINANCE (CAP. 485)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Mandatory Provident Fund Schemes Ordinance Cap. 485 is a legal document that mandates the establishment of provident funds for employees and sets out rules related to contributions, benefits, and management."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is a piece of legislation that defines mandatory provident fund schemes and their operations, including contributions from employers as mentioned in section 2(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e70ac051c2f0b62b1c78481493c78790&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da3daa00f8a571e7a58b273ea6df48ea</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 177}]</data>
</node>
