<node id="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Paternity Leave is a period of absence from work provided to male employees when their partner gives birth, allowing them time to bond with the new family member."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity Leave is a right for male employees under certain conditions as defined in Part IIIA of the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity Leave is a type of leave provided to male employees when their partner gives birth, often included in the broader category of family-related leaves distinct from regular annual leave."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity Leave is a type of leave taken by an employee for the purpose of caring for a newborn child."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity Leave is a type of leave that an employee can take in relation to the birth of their child, subject to certain notification requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity Leave is another form of leave affecting the wage calculations for employee termination agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity Leave is the leave provided for in Part IIIA, specifically related to paternity rights and responsibilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity Leave refers to a type of leave that an employee can take in addition to rest days, holidays and annual leave when they are expecting a child."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity Leave refers to the entitlement of a male employee to take leave in respect of the birth of his child, subject to certain conditions and regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity Leave refers to the leave provided for fathers after the birth of their child."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity leave allows fathers to take time off work following the birth of their child, often for bonding purposes and sharing parental responsibilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity leave is a type of leave an employee can take, as per the legal requirements mentioned."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity leave is a type of leave for male employees related to the birth or adoption of their child, also considered part of wages under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity leave refers to a period during which a father can take time off work due to the birth of his child, highlighting its importance in family-related policies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity leave refers to the entitlement of a male employee to take time off work for the purpose of caring for his newborn child."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity leave refers to the period when a father takes time off work following the birth of his child, often with the purpose of bonding with the newborn."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aed3ae0b98488b1b913e6b49db19fee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d14b62c50b2a0a92ac73c8ef0642fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb89bd87e81559e9820333c42f3f0c6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908f80036493cf02a5dd6da247a2a7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c54e7deea495212bab465e4af100b7ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bab24c47d69b1c9fe7a8b2d862514c83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fef56ddac89c58276c95d49a4ad2fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-885c65878619106b2d2b302114a64bb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-570e52321eeb26a637fff48779e8695d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8a8ba58e2f04dd4f35b5bed0e044673</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 500}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Paternity Leave Pay is a benefit given to male employees for taking care of their newborn child, reflecting an extension of parental leave policies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity Leave Pay is a form of compensation provided by employers to employees taking paternity leave, as mandated by labor laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity Leave Pay is a form of compensation provided to employees who take paternity leave, as outlined in specific sections and conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity Leave Pay refers to the pay an employee receives during their paternity leave period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity leave pay is a type of compensation for paternity leave, which may be included in terminal payments if applicable."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity leave pay refers to the payment provided by an employer during a father's leave related to the birth of their child, specifically in cases outside Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f8f154dd34baff54c016b669ab2da5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908f80036493cf02a5dd6da247a2a7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6320bd8af6a47ec4d774b02d5588447a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d4bd265e2aa3d3a8af55fbca1b13963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4881be1a6d6d318bb1047aad7c99da</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 600}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT WITHOUT NOTICE OR PAYMENT IN LIEU&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the termination of employment without prior notice or compensation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 406}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DATE ON WHICH TERMINATION TAKES EFFECT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The date when the termination officially becomes effective after being notified to the employee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 406}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIXED TERM EXPIRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event occurs where an employee's contract is for a fixed period, and that period ends naturally without renewal or extension."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 406}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RETIREMENT AT SPECIFIED AGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The retirement of an employee upon reaching the pre-specified age as stated in their continuous employment contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE DEATH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee death is a specific event where the gratuity or benefit must be deducted from the long service payment according to certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employee death refers to a situation where an employee has passed away, triggering various entitlements and benefits for certain individuals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employee death refers to an event where the death of an employee triggers certain legal and financial implications, including long-service payments and deductions from such payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The event refers to an employee passing away, triggering various financial and legal obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"This event refers to the unfortunate passing of an employed individual, triggering specific legal and procedural actions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54addea578982eb79d7f3048cf09c6a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21b404a5b0d354defe8dd03eb692b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dabef41d299eda51d77087c2ca170398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b66ec28db0dbcb16e24e4d4df0ef35a2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 175}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DATE OF TERMINATION OTHER THAN ORDINANCE PROVISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The date when an employee's contract is terminated outside the stipulated procedures outlined in this ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENEWAL (續訂)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Renewal includes extension, and any reference to renewing a contract shall be construed accordingly. This term pertains to extending or revalidating contracts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REST DAY (休息日) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A rest day is defined as a continuous period of at least 24 hours during which an employee can abstain from work, as specified under Part IV of the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT (遣散費)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This term refers to the financial compensation provided by employers to employees upon termination of their employment contract, specifically mentioned in section 31B(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1095}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE (疾病津貼) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The sickness allowance is a form of payment provided for under section 33 to cover the costs associated with an employee's illness or injury."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SICKNESS DAY (病假日)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A sickness day refers to a day when an employee cannot work due to being unfit because of injury or sickness, and it also includes days required by Cap. 599 regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIFIED EMPLOYEE (指明僱員) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This term identifies employees who meet the conditions outlined in section 31ZEA(2)(a), (b), and (c)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPOUSE (配偶)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"In relation to a married employee, this refers to the legally recognized spouse of that individual."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spouse refers to the person lawfully married to a given employee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1095}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY (法定假日) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A statutory holiday is any day officially designated as a public or official holiday under section 39 of the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY (法定假日)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Statutory Holiday is defined as holidays specified in section 39(1) of relevant legislation, indicating official days off with legal recognition."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1095}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STRIKE (罷工)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Strike has the meaning assigned by Section 2 of the Trade Unions Ordinance (Cap. 332), referring to a collective action where employees stop work in protest or negotiation, typically involving trade unions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1093}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSTITUTED HOLIDAY (代替假日)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Substituted Holiday is described as a type of leave granted under Section 39(3) and can be seen more like an alternative to statutory holidays provided by employers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1095}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TIPS AND SERVICE CHARGES (小費及服務費)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tips and Service Charges are defined in relation to wages, indicating sums received directly or indirectly from customers that the employer recognizes as part of employee remuneration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1095}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRANSITION DATE (轉制日)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Transition Date refers specifically to the implementation day of the Employment and Retirement Schemes Legislation Amendment Ordinance 2022, which is crucial for changes in employment schemes effective from this date."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1095}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WAGE PERIOD (工資期)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wage Period denotes a specific time frame during which wages are payable under an employee's contract or as stipulated by section 22 of relevant legislation, essential for calculating and paying remuneration accurately."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wage period refers to the specific timeframe over which wages are calculated and paid, an important social science concept in labor economics."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45d3d232b5b9df510faacc808489eadb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1095}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wages are monetary compensation paid by employers, including various types of payments as specified in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wages encompass all forms of monetary compensation received in exchange for work done according to the terms outlined under an employment contract or as per Section 22. This includes various allowances, bonuses, commissions, and overtime pay but excludes certain specified items."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wages is a mathematical term used to describe monetary compensation for work performed, often subject to legal regulations like those found in the Minimum Wage Ordinance (Cap. 608)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wages refer to monetary compensation provided by an organization, which includes any sum paid by an employer as part of their employment contract or legal entitlements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wages refer to the monetary compensation paid for work performed, including overtime pay under certain conditions as defined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-681c7e69874ff6c2cdf180f0fb0d44f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d3d232b5b9df510faacc808489eadb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e220e0c7587651abe976f081881efeb5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1097}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Trade Union Ordinance Cap. 332 provides definitions for terms related to trade unions in Hong Kong and assigns meanings that are legally binding, including the definition of 'strike' mentioned earlier."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Trade Unions Ordinance (Cap. 332&lt;SEP&gt;"The Trade Unions Ordinance (Cap. 332) defines the terms 'lock-out' and 'strike', providing legal context for these events."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Trade Unions Ordinance (Cap. 332) is a legal document that outlines the provisions for forming and registering trade unions in accordance with certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Trade Unions Ordinance (Cap. 332) is a piece of legislation that defines the terms 'lock-out' and 'strike', providing legal context for these events."&lt;SEP&gt;"This ordinance regulates trade unions in Hong Kong, setting out the rights and responsibilities of both employers and workers within unionized environments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd0362fbf5661d142ff4aeefe27aea79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a6c178897818a8c58b6d17f59790314&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06d23d2b54047f6e0d92f6798bcab7c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb269a993727b98b029449c2f2612dff</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1093}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;星期&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"星期指的是为了第11节和第VA及VB部分的目的，从周六晚上午夜到下一个周六晚上午夜之间的时期。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a82f354bd72ecc759d4ab4ed34bac3db</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 479}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1132}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION OF A CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Termination of a contract of employment refers to the end of an employee's contractual relationship with their employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT UNDER PART IIA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"End of Year Payment is a specific type of payment made at the conclusion of a financial period as defined in Part IIA."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY UNDER PART III&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maternity Leave Pay refers to payments provided during maternity leave, as specified in Part III."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE PAY UNDER PART IIIA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Paternity Leave Pay is a payment made for paternity leave, defined in Part IIIA."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT UNDER PART VA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Severance Payment involves compensation provided to an employee upon termination of employment as per the provisions of Part VA."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT UNDER PART VB&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Long Service Payment is a type of benefit paid for long-term service, defined in Part VB."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE UNDER PART VII&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sickness Allowance refers to payments made during an employee's sickness period as per the provisions of Part VII."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOLIDAY PAY UNDER PART VIII&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Holiday Pay is a payment provided for holidays or time off, according to the regulations in Part VIII."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY UNDER PART VIIIA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Annual Leave Pay involves payments related to annual leave as defined by Part VIIIA."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WEEK (星期)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Week refers to a period between Saturday night and the following Saturday night, used for certain calculations in this context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;YOUNG PERSON (青年) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Young Person means an individual who has reached 15 years of age but is under 18 years old."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (2A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event related to subsection (2A) involves specifying the date for termination of employment in certain circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9dc495e2347a322a5aaa3ff390e7601c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (2B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event related to subsection (2B) involves overriding the default date specified by subsection (2) when an employee's contract is terminated by payment in lieu of notice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9dc495e2347a322a5aaa3ff390e7601c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 538}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Termination of Employment refers to the act of ending a worker-employer relationship, with its meaning consistent across different sections and provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Termination of Employment refers to the end or cessation of an employee's work relationship with the employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Termination of employment is an event where the employer may end the relationship with an employee under certain conditions related to their fitness for specific work activities and can be subject to determination by a Commissioner."&lt;SEP&gt;"Termination of employment refers to the legal act of ending an employee's contract, which can be done through dismissal, layoff, or other specified circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9dc495e2347a322a5aaa3ff390e7601c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f5ddfc5b519fcf524c4d9bd233c4e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d06ee4edd39803f9b252b767c726ef91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea6b2c9739d4904eac9e0c6be6072cb9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 538}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISMISSAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Dismissal refers to the act of terminating employment by the employer without valid reasons unless such reasons are shown, as per Section 32K."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dismissal is a specific event where an employee is terminated from their job without notice."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dismissal is an event where an employee's employment is terminated by the employer for various reasons, which can affect entitlements such as long service payment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dismissal is the act of terminating an employee's employment contract without their consent under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dismissal refers to the termination of an employee's contract, often subject to specific conditions and policies as outlined in labor laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dismissal refers to the termination of an employment contract by the employer without just cause, which can lead to legal challenges and remedies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-01e8dd2cd7216b43532ed7037814b54b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc495e2347a322a5aaa3ff390e7601c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc0e662ccd81354d4e411a146aa85d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a40a9600dcdabbcf7b1de20226238a1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66cccec6ac7d06fb5417245d5fe5f3b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdbd130fa51f2bbf4428aee9c45795cb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 108}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 550}]</data>
</node>
