</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Notice Period refers to the duration within which a party must provide notice before terminating a contract as per legal requirements and agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Notice period is a specified time frame within which an employee or employer must provide notice before terminating the contract, with minimum requirements outlined in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Notice period is an event during which an employee must leave before the expiration of a notice unless specific conditions are met, such as prior consent or payment in lieu."&lt;SEP&gt;"Notice period refers to the time an employee must remain with their employer after receiving dismissal or renewal notices, as described in section 6."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9ddecf99bc0bca06387d96224afeaf4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f355da3b0eddd390953ffae58fee2099&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e5f55eef00b5211e8c9c5c06c4bde96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 586}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROBATIONARY EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Probationary employment refers to a trial period during which both parties can assess suitability for permanent employment, often subject to specific termination conditions as described."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f355da3b0eddd390953ffae58fee2099</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WAGES (月)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wages refer to monetary compensation for work performed, where 'month' means a period starting from the day notice is given or employment begins, ending at the end of the corresponding date in the following month."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f355da3b0eddd390953ffae58fee2099</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 98}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 510}]</data>
</node>
