  <data key="d2">chunk-8625c1304f36a12d07cc0b6f8faf08b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAVE WITH THE AGREEMENT OF HIS EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to days off that are agreed upon between an employee and their employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8625c1304f36a12d07cc0b6f8faf08b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 479}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1132}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NORMAL WORKING DAY ON WHICH THE EMPLOYEE IS NOT PROVIDED WITH WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A normal working day on which the employee is not provided with work refers to a situation where an employee works but does not receive any tasks or assignments, often leading to partial pay for that day."&lt;SEP&gt;"This describes a normal working day where the employee does not receive any work, often referred to as unpaid leave or stand-by duty."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8625c1304f36a12d07cc0b6f8faf08b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1097}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DAY OF ABSENCE FROM WORK DUE TO TEMPORARY INCAPACITY FOR WHICH COMPENSATION IS PAYABLE UNDER SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to a day when an employee cannot work temporarily and is entitled to compensation as per the Employees' Compensation Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"This refers to a specific type of leave where an employee is absent and entitled to compensation as per the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a63ef432e83e1ac4184a66b9247423f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8625c1304f36a12d07cc0b6f8faf08b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 404}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1098}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION WITHOUT NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Termination Without Notice is a legal scenario allowing employers to end employment contracts immediately under certain conditions as outlined in sections 9 and 10."&lt;SEP&gt;"This event refers to the act of ending a contract of employment without providing formal notice as stipulated under certain circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8625c1304f36a12d07cc0b6f8faf08b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 588}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 6&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 6 is a reference to another part of a legal document that provides notice procedures related to contract termination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 6 is a reference within a legal document that outlines conditions for terminating a contract of employment without notice."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 6 is an amendment event that occurred in 2022, affecting the interpretation and application of certain clauses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 6 refers to a legal provision that outlines notice periods for termination of employment contracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 6 refers to a legal provision that outlines terms related to termination and notice periods for employees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9e5f55eef00b5211e8c9c5c06c4bde96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3a3f0edfa08a61dbd46b52c9f94d56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ddecf99bc0bca06387d96224afeaf4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8cb52dd4a9b2981de387c70ee06f029</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 100}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 524}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 15&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 15 is a reference within the legal document that sets constraints on when payment must be made for progress payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 15 is another reference in the same legal context, potentially outlining additional terms or conditions related to termination agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ad2f770d3edd7fc8b6985f3040077779&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 226}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 33&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 33 is a reference in the legal text where jurisdictional issues are addressed, determining whether an adjudicator has authority over a dispute."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 33 is a referenced section that may contain specific provisions affecting the ability to terminate contracts of employment without notice."&lt;SEP&gt;"This section is referenced in relation to the adjudicator's jurisdiction over payment disputes under this Part."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f4f0cfcab0e9f6d5a958dc7286fe8aad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e089cfc832db9c43bb24baa7baf3ed42</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 226}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE TERMINATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee Termination Agreement refers to an agreement between parties in a contract of employment for terminating the contract, which involves financial compensation calculations based on work duration and wages earned."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 100}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 524}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REST DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A rest day is a non-working day provided by employers as part of an employee's benefits package or employment contract, intended to ensure employees have adequate downtime."&lt;SEP&gt;"A rest day is a specific type of day on which an employee can take leave, as per legal requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest Day is a day off provided by employers for employees' rest and relaxation, separate from but often included in the calculation of annual leave days."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest Day refers to a day off where wages may not be considered in calculating compensation during contract terminations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest Day refers to a non-working day designated for employee relaxation and recuperation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest Day refers to any normal working day when an employee is not provided with work, which can be considered as part of their leave period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest Day refers to days designated for rest and relaxation, often included within the annual leave entitlements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest Day refers to days designated for rest as part of labor regulations, which can affect employment contract terminations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest Day refers to days when employees are entitled to rest and do not work but may receive some form of compensation or benefit."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest day is a non-working day that an employee can take as part of their employment benefits or personal days."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest day is a non-working day that should not be considered as part of normal working days when determining if an employee has been laid off."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest day is the designated non-working day for employees as per labor laws or agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest day refers to a designated non-working day provided to employees, as mandated by labor laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest day refers to a non-working day provided by employers as part of employee benefits and included in wage calculations according to BAA regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest day refers to a non-working day provided for employees as part of labor regulations, ensuring them time off within a week's period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest days are non-working days provided by employers, typically for the well-being of employees but not specified as physical locations in this context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccf624f83121089caf9f8fb044043303&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aed3ae0b98488b1b913e6b49db19fee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d14b62c50b2a0a92ac73c8ef0642fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-393f577c90dd494cee38d1bc9bc80592&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63d3371d1b762c2013adc08da9c549f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c54e7deea495212bab465e4af100b7ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fef56ddac89c58276c95d49a4ad2fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6511dbd5eb2121ae41cf477a6c2b2884&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2138132720286ddae5a4634e3cd8c8f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 97}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 507}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOLIDAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Holiday or Annual Leave are periods of time off where wages may be disregarded in the calculation of compensation during contract terminations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Holiday or Annual Leave refers to any leave taken by an employee, including paternity leave, rest day, sickness day, and other types of leave as specified in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 101}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 532}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY INCAPACITY COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Temporary Incapacity Compensation is a form of payment provided under section 10 of the Employees' Compensation Ordinance (Cap. 282) that affects wage calculations for termination agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 100}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 524}]</data>
</node>
