<node id="&quot;SECTION 11(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 11(2) is mentioned without details, suggesting it might pertain to specific conditions for terminating a contract of employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 101}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 526}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPER NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Proper Notice refers to the formal and legally required notification period before termination as specified in section 6."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 289}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 964}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE GIVEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Notice Given is an event where one party formally notifies another of their intention to terminate a contract, which triggers payment obligations under certain sections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 289}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 964}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DATE OF TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Date of Termination refers to the specific date when a contract ends as per legal provisions and notice periods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 537}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DAILY AVERAGE OR MONTHLY AVERAGE OF WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Daily Average or Monthly Average of Wages is calculated for purposes of payment under termination clauses, reflecting an arithmetic mean based on earnings over time."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 289}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 964}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION OF THE CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Termination of the Contract refers to the act of ending an employment relationship as per legal provisions and agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Termination of the contract refers to the legal act of ending a contractual agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 101}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 525}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE PARTICIPATION IN STRIKE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee Participation in Strike refers to an event where employees engage in collective action against the employer, which cannot be grounds for termination according to section 2(2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FALSELY DISOBEDIENT EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Falsely Disobedient Employee refers to an individual who, despite not being genuinely disobedient or insubordinate, is terminated based on a false accusation of misconduct according to section 9(a)(i)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNLAWFUL TERMINATION DUE TO STRIKE PARTICIPATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Unlawful Termination Due to Strike Participation refers to the prohibition against terminating employment contracts solely because an employee has participated in a lawful strike, as stated in section 2(2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FRAUDULENT OR DISLOYAL BEHAVIOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fraudulent or Disloyal Behavior is defined under section 9(a)(iii) and can be grounds for immediate termination without notice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 588}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPEATED NEGLIGENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Repeated Negligence, as outlined in section 9(a)(iv), refers to consistent failure to perform job duties properly and can justify termination without notice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OTHER LAWFUL REASONS FOR TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Other Lawful Reasons for Termination includes any valid grounds beyond those explicitly listed that may allow an employer to terminate a contract immediately, as per section 9(b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMENDMENT OF SECTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Amendment of Sections refers to the legal process by which existing provisions are modified or updated, as indicated in the text with references to amendments made in 2007 and 1975."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STATUTORY LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Statutory Law is a body of rules created through legislation that governs employment contracts and termination procedures, including provisions mentioned in sections 7, 9, 10, etc., as detailed in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT RELATIONSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Relationship refers to the legal and contractual bond between an employer and employee that can be terminated under specific conditions outlined by statutory law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT OBLIGATIONS UPON TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Payment Obligations Upon Termination are financial responsibilities incurred when a contract is ended, as detailed in sections 7 and other relevant provisions of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 537}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AN EMPLOYER MAY TERMINATE A CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT WITHOUT NOTICE OR PAYMENT IN LIEU&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to the situation where an employer can terminate a contract of employment without giving notice under certain conditions, such as employee misconduct."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b266f7ca95da19a8651bff75bd855a0c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE, IN RELATION TO HIS EMPLOYMENT— (I) WILFULLY DISOBEYS A LAWFUL AND REASONABLE ORDER; (II) MISCONDUCTS HIMSELF, SUCH CONDUCT BEING INCONSISTENT WITH THE DUE AND FAITHFUL DISCHARGE OF HIS DUTIES; (III) IS GUILTY OF FRAUD OR DISHONESTY; OR (IV) IS HABITUALLY NEGLECTFUL IN HIS DUTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This person refers to an employee who engages in specific behaviors that justify termination by the employer without notice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b266f7ca95da19a8651bff75bd855a0c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE FACT THAT AN EMPLOYEE TAKES PART IN A STRIKE DOES NOT ENTITLE HIS EMPLOYER TO TERMINATE UNDER SUBSECTION (1) THE EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event describes a situation where participating in a strike is not grounds for an employer to terminate an employee's contract without notice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b266f7ca95da19a8651bff75bd855a0c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE CAN WITHOUT GIVING NOTIFICATION OR SUBSTITUTE NOTIFICATION MONEY TERMINATE THE EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT — (A) EMPLOYEE REASONABLY FEARS THAT HIS BODY WILL BE SUBJECTED TO VIOLENCE OR DISEASE HARM, AND THERE IS NO EXPLICIT OR IMPLIED TERM IN THE EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT INDICATING SUCH A SITUATION; (AA) EMPLOYEE — (I) HAS BEEN EMPLOYED FOR AT LEAST 5 YEARS UNDER THE TERMS OF THE CONTRACT; AND (II) RECEIVES A CERTIFICATE FROM A REGISTERED DOCTOR OR TRADITIONAL CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER AS SPECIFIED BY THE SECRETARY ACCORDING TO SECTION 49, STATING THAT HE IS PERMANENTLY UNSUITABLE FOR HIS POSITION DUE TO REASONS STATED IN THE CERTIFICATE.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to situations where an employee can terminate their employment contract without notice if they reasonably fear violence or disease harm, or are deemed medically unfit after a certain period of service."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b266f7ca95da19a8651bff75bd855a0c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION OF CONTRACT WITHOUT NOTICE BY EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This organization is referring to the legal framework under which employers have the right to terminate contracts without notice for specific reasons."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b266f7ca95da19a8651bff75bd855a0c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PHYSICAL DANGER BY VIOLENCE OR DISEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Physical danger by violence or disease is an event where the employee reasonably fears harm, not covered in their contract of employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-515a3738f6ebf19e3d7fa78e01d28be6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 581}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1141}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ILL-TREATMENT BY EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ill-treatment by employer refers to a situation where employees are subjected to mistreatment from their employers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-515a3738f6ebf19e3d7fa78e01d28be6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 581}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1141}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 7 TERMINATION CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Section 7 termination clause is a legal provision allowing for contract termination under certain conditions without notice or payment in lieu of notice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2554ffe0d55bbe29aef6808731a595f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 760}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 23 WAGES PAYMENT CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Section 23 wages payment clause specifies the timeline within which wages should be paid, and failure to do so can lead to contract termination according to common law principles."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2554ffe0d55bbe29aef6808731a595f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 757}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT TERMINATION WITHOUT NOTICE OR PAYMENT IN LIEU OF NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event involves an employee terminating their employment contract without notice or payment in lieu of notice under specific conditions as stipulated by the law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2554ffe0d55bbe29aef6808731a595f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 760}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;14-DAY SUSPENSION CLAUSE FOR EMPLOYERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The 14-day suspension clause allows employers to suspend employees' work for up to 14 days based on certain grounds, without giving prior notice or payment in lieu of notice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2554ffe0d55bbe29aef6808731a595f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 211}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 757}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第9條終止�ORDINATES合約&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"第9条终止劳动合同是雇主要暂停雇佣关系的一个理由，涉及合同解除的事件。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-be5f720af1dc189f9088eb832b2b0cfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 71}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 462}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;刑事检控&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"刑事检控是指员工因雇佣引起或与雇佣有关的事宜遭受到的法律程序，可能影响其工作状态。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-be5f720af1dc189f9088eb832b2b0cfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 71}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 462}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUSPENSION FROM EMPLOYMENT IN CERTAIN CASES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"某些情况下暂停雇佣关系是一个事件描述，涉及雇主根据特定条件暂时停用雇员的情况。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-be5f720af1dc189f9088eb832b2b0cfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 71}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 462}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CRIMINAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Criminal Proceedings are legal actions initiated against an employee that could lead to termination if found guilty, and may also result in a suspension pending the outcome of these proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-098ca6bfb60006d76569bead63917ebd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAY-OFF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lay-off is a term used for temporarily reducing or stopping work without notice as agreed upon in the contract or implied from it, with limitations on duration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lay-off refers to a situation where an employee is not provided with work, and it can affect their remuneration and rights regarding severance pay."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-098ca6bfb60006d76569bead63917ebd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2138132720286ddae5a4634e3cd8c8f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 97}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 508}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NORMAL WORKING DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Normal Working Days refer to standard working periods that are quantified mathematically for calculating lay-offs and suspension durations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normal working days are the standard number of workdays used in calculations related to employee remuneration and lay-offs, typically 4 consecutive weeks or 26 consecutive weeks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-098ca6bfb60006d76569bead63917ebd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2138132720286ddae5a4634e3cd8c8f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 97}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 508}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"End of Year Payment is a financial compensation provided by an employer at the end of a year or employment period, as specified in the contract or otherwise calculated based on profits."&lt;SEP&gt;"End of Year Payment is a type of compensation that can be provided by employers to employees based on the terms and conditions of their continuous contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"End of Year Payment is an event where employees receive payments at the end of a fiscal or calendar year, often including bonuses or other benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"End of Year Payment refers to any annual remuneration of a contractual nature, regardless of its name such as 'thirteenth month salary', 'fourteenth month salary', 'double salary', or 'year-end bonus', but excludes any gift-based or discretionary annual payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"End of year payment is a compensation provided by employers typically around the end of the fiscal or calendar year, which may be affected by working on rest days under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"End of year payment is a financial compensation due to employees at the end of a specified period according to their employment contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"End of year payment is a type of compensation that might be included in terminal payments, typically related to annual bonuses or similar financial benefits due at the end of an employment period."&lt;SEP&gt;"End of year payment refers to any annual payment or bonus that is contractual in nature, excluding those that are gratuitous or discretionary."&lt;SEP&gt;"End of year payment refers to financial benefits or bonuses due to employees at the end of the fiscal year according to certain provisions in the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d4bd265e2aa3d3a8af55fbca1b13963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb1b0eee63da6475bd592efac352092a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1bb383ea19375cfe6d50e66dce88dd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43b4560ca9a773332d0b2bf256551f4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6511dbd5eb2121ae41cf477a6c2b2884&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adfd6c1ac1062c58ce3404e61a7b9509&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a365e751a6908c5178b1168febad9bcd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 399}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1091}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPORTION OF THE END OF YEAR PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Proportion of the End of Year Payment is a term used to describe part of an end-of-year payment as calculated under Rule 11F, which involves mathematical calculations and definitions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fb1b0eee63da6475bd592efac352092a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 399}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1091}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LUNAR YEAR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Lunar Year is used as the default payment period when no specific term is mentioned in the employment contract, indicating its significance in determining compensation periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lunar Year refers to the Chinese lunar calendar year that ends just before Lunar New Year's Day."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fb1b0eee63da6475bd592efac352092a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adfd6c1ac1062c58ce3404e61a7b9509</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 402}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNUAL BONUS PAYMENT DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Annual Bonus Payment Date refers to the date when year-end bonuses are scheduled to be paid according to Section 11E(1) or (2), or partially paid according to Sections 11F(3) or (4)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9fff8612fdefb52ed816a2d4502b87bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 593}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE, PATERNITY LEAVE, REST DAY, SICK LEAVE, HOLIDAY, ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are types of leave that do not affect the calculation of an employee's average monthly earnings over a period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9fff8612fdefb52ed816a2d4502b87bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 593}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPENSATION FOR TEMPORARY LOSS OF WORK CAPACITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to compensation provided by the Employment Ordinance (Cap. 282) under Section 10 when employees temporarily lose their ability to work and are absent from work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9fff8612fdefb52ed816a2d4502b87bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 593}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRTEENTH MONTH PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Thirteenth month payment is a type of end of year payment mentioned but not further detailed here."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thirteenth month payment refers to an annual payment or bonus that is contractual in nature."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 399}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1092}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOURTEENTH MONTH PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fourteenth month payment is another variant of the end of year payment, also not elaborated on in this text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourteenth month payment, like thirteenth month payment, is another term for a similar annual payment or bonus of a contractual nature."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 399}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1092}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOUBLE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Double pay also refers to an annual payment or bonus that is considered part of the contractual obligations between employer and employee."&lt;SEP&gt;"Double pay is a form of annual payment or bonus mentioned but lacks specific details here."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 399}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1092}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;END OF YEAR BONUS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"End of year bonus is included as part of the end of year payment, specifically noted for its contractual nature."&lt;SEP&gt;"End of year bonus, like thirteenth month payment, fourteenth month payment, and double pay, denotes a specific type of annual payment or bonus with contractual nature."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 399}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1092}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GRATUITOUS NATURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gratuitous nature refers to payments or bonuses that are not required by contract and can be given at the employer's discretion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gratuitous nature refers to payments that are not part of the contractual obligations between employer and employee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 399}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1091}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISCRETIONARY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Discretionary indicates that certain payments may only be made based on the employer's decision, rather than being a contractual obligation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 399}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1091}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;12-MONTH PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A 12-month period is used as a reference for calculating wages or bonuses in this context, specifically mentioned when discussing average monthly earnings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAME INDUSTRY OR OCCUPATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Same industry or occupation refers to the comparison group used for wage calculation if direct comparators are not available within the same employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAME REGION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Same region is specified as a factor in determining average monthly earnings when comparing wages from different employers but within the same geographical area."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISCRETION OF THE EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Discretion of the employer pertains to annual payments or bonuses that may be paid at the sole decision-making power of the employer, which is distinct from those with a contractual nature."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LUNAR NEW YEAR'S DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lunar New Year's Day is a statutory holiday, with the fourth day of Lunar New Year observed if it falls on a Sunday."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lunar New Year's Day marks an important event in Chinese lunar calendar and is used as reference for certain legal terms like 'lunar year'"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f7138b70fc0e22900e2a496ae78b23</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 35}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 358}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1063}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHINESE LUNAR YEAR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Chinese lunar year refers to a specific type of calendrical system, distinct from the Gregorian calendar."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 35}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 358}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1063}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT PERIOD (酬金期)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Payment period or '酬金期' is defined by section 11C and pertains to the timeframe for annual payments or bonuses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPORTION OF THE END OF YEAR PAYMENT (部分年終酬金)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Proportion of the end of year payment, as calculated in accordance with section 11F, refers to a specific part of an employee's annual bonus that is subject to certain calculations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 399}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1092}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAVE TAKEN BY THE EMPLOYEE WITH THE AGREEMENT OF HIS EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leave taken by the employee with the agreement of his employer pertains to days when employees can take time off from their jobs after obtaining permission from their employers."&lt;SEP&gt;"This event refers to a leave period agreed upon between an employee and their employer, which may also impact wage calculations."&lt;SEP&gt;"This refers to periods during which an employee may not be paid their full wages due to agreed-upon leaves."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5e29cfe8eddddf302f5a14076a67a7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84eda1f018d06824b6b2e9602213349f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 404}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1100}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY INCAPACITY FOR WHICH COMPENSATION IS PAYABLE UNDER SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Temporary incapacity refers to a situation where an employee cannot work due to illness or injury, and they are entitled to receive compensation as per Section 10 of the Employees' Compensation Ordinance (Cap. 282)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary incapacity refers to a situation where an employee cannot work due to temporary health issues and may be entitled to receive compensation as per Section 10 of the Employees' Compensation Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"This event involves a period when an employee's absence from work due to temporary incapacity results in them receiving compensation as per Section 10 of the Employees' Compensation Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5e29cfe8eddddf302f5a14076a67a7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84eda1f018d06824b6b2e9602213349f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 404}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1100}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FULL MONTH'S WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Full month's wages refer to the average monthly earnings calculated over a period, typically 12 months or less if the employee has been with the company for a shorter duration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 399}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1092}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;工資 (WAGES)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wages include any sum paid by an employer in respect of various types of leave and absences as mentioned above, indicating that wages are broadly defined to cover different forms of compensation provided by the employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"工資是指雇主支付给员工的报酬，包括工资、津贴和其他形式的薪酬。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6401943df7f64de20cb83d590f559418</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 156}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 667}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;12 MONTHS IMMEDIATELY BEFORE THE DAY ON WHICH THE END OF YEAR PAYMENT BECOMES DUE TO THE EMPLOYEE UNDER SECTION 11E(1) OR (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to the period used for calculating full month's wages, specifically mentioning a timeframe of 12 months prior to when an annual bonus is due."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IF THE EMPLOYEE HAS BEEN EMPLOYED BY THE EMPLOYER CONCERNED FOR A PERIOD SHORTER THAN 12 MONTHS IMMEDIATELY BEFORE THE DUE DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to situations where employees have not worked with their current employers long enough to cover a full year, thus using a different calculation method."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Employees' Compensation Ordinance (Cap. 282) is a legal document that provides guidelines for employee compensation and benefits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-96a39d49ad205c3ba703c46117f4dff9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE, PATERNITY LEAVE, REST DAY, SICKNESS DAY, HOLIDAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are periods during which an employee may not be paid their full wages due to personal reasons such as maternity/paternity leave, taking a rest day, being sick, having a holiday, or using annual leave."&lt;SEP&gt;"These are types of leave taken by employees which may affect the calculation of wages as per the ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"These are types of leave that may result in an employee not being paid wages or full wages during a certain period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-96a39d49ad205c3ba703c46117f4dff9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84eda1f018d06824b6b2e9602213349f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd469871354ff220088ed4c17affde45</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT PERIOD CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The process involves calculating an employee's average monthly wage over a period, considering various factors such as leaves and absences."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-96a39d49ad205c3ba703c46117f4dff9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONTHLY AVERAGE WAGE CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY,MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the method of determining an employee’s average monthly earnings by disregarding certain periods or wages as specified in the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-96a39d49ad205c3ba703c46117f4dff9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAME WORK, SAME TRADE OR OCCUPATION, SAME DISTRICT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY,SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These terms refer to criteria used for calculating compensation when direct comparison with the specific employee is not possible due to impracticality."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-96a39d49ad205c3ba703c46117f4dff9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE AMOUNT MAY BE CALCULATED BY REFERENCE TO THE WAGES EARNED BY A PERSON WHO WAS EMPLOYED AT THE SAME WORK BY THE SAME EMPLOYER DURING THE PERIOD OF 12 MONTHS IMMEDIATELY BEFORE THE DUE DAY, OR, IF THERE IS NO SUCH PERSON, BY A PERSON WHO WAS EMPLOYED IN THE SAME TRADE OR OCCUPATION AND AT THE SAME WORK IN THE SAME DISTRICT DURING THE PERIOD OF 12 MONTHS IMMEDIATELY BEFORE THE DUE DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a method for calculating wages based on previous employment data within specific parameters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0741b5ccf934d17c6a23c8ca19677d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;僱傭合約中有相反的書面條款或條件&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to conditions or terms in an employment contract that contradict the presumption of annual payments not being gratuitous and not payable at discretion, indicating legal considerations affecting wage determination."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0741b5ccf934d17c6a23c8ca19677d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;推定每年酬金或年度花紅不屬賞贈性質和不是僅由僱主酌情付給的&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a presumption that annual payments or bonuses are not gratuitous and cannot be given at the employer's discretion, reflecting legal interpretations of employment contracts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0741b5ccf934d17c6a23c8ca19677d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第(1)款不適用於在本條的生效日期前訂立的任何僱傭合約&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This clause states that subsection (1)'s presumption does not apply to any employment contract made before the effective date of this section, indicating a temporal limitation on legal presumptions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0741b5ccf934d17c6a23c8ca19677d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;編輯附註:生效日期: 1997年6月27日&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This editorial note provides an official declaration about when certain provisions in legislation come into effect, impacting the application of laws and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0741b5ccf934d17c6a23c8ca19677d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IT SHALL BE PRESUMED THAT AN ANNUAL PAYMENT OR ANNUAL BONUS IS NOT OF A GRATUITOUS NATURE AND IS NOT PAYABLE ONLY AT THE DISCRETION OF THE EMPLOYER UNLESS THERE IS A WRITTEN TERM OR CONDITION IN THE CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT TO THE CONTRARY&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to legal provisions for presuming non-gratuitous payments based on specific conditions within an employment agreement, indicating formalized methods of wage determination."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0741b5ccf934d17c6a23c8ca19677d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANY OPPOSITE AGREEMENTS AND EXCEPT AS OTHERWISE PROVIDED BY SUBSECTION (2)&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to exceptions in the application of certain clauses due to existing agreements or other provisions, highlighting legal nuances affecting contract interpretation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0741b5ccf934d17c6a23c8ca19677d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;除有任何相反的協議及除第(2)款另有規定外，根據連續性合約受僱的僱員&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to employees under continuous contracts who may be entitled to annual bonuses based on the terms of their employment contract, whether written or implied."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0741b5ccf934d17c6a23c8ca19677d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;本部適用於該僱員&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This indicates that certain provisions apply specifically to these types of employed individuals as defined by legal agreements and conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0741b5ccf934d17c6a23c8ca19677d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON, ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Continuous Contract Employee refers to an employee who has been employed under a continuous contract for at least one month and qualifies for specific sick leave benefit calculations according to the provisions mentioned."&lt;SEP&gt;"Continuous Contract Employee refers to an employee under a continuous contract who may be entitled to an end-of-year payment as per the terms or conditions of their employment agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-adfd6c1ac1062c58ce3404e61a7b9509&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aca44109366b72f73416de7630e4bed5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 402}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGREEMENT TO CONTRARY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Agreement to Contrary refers to any agreement made by parties involved in employment contracts that might affect the application of certain sections or parts of a contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-adfd6c1ac1062c58ce3404e61a7b9509</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 558}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 11F PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 11F Payment is a specific type of payment under section 11F, which pertains to the proportion of end-of-year payments as per employment contracts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-adfd6c1ac1062c58ce3404e61a7b9509</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 558}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPORTION OF END-YEAR PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Proportion of End-Year Payment refers to a part or share of an employee's end-of-year payment that might be subject to certain conditions in their contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-adfd6c1ac1062c58ce3404e61a7b9509</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 581}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1140}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNUAL END-OF-YEAR PAYMENT AMOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Annual End-of-Year Payment Amount refers to the total or partial amount of end-of-year payments an employee might receive based on their continuous contract and any specified terms within it."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-adfd6c1ac1062c58ce3404e61a7b9509</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 402}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAME EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to the same organization that employs the female employee, indicating continuity within the same company or entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Same Employer refers to the organization that has continuously employed an employee throughout a payment period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a1bb383ea19375cfe6d50e66dce88dd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 399}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1091}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROFIT CALCULATION DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Profit Calculation Date refers to the specific date when an employer determines their profits, which can affect the calculation or payment timing of the end-of-year payment if it is based on profit margins."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a1bb383ea19375cfe6d50e66dce88dd1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 399}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1091}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROFITS OF THE EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Profits of the employer refers to the earnings or net income generated by an organization after deducting all expenses, costs, and taxes from its total revenue."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-43b4560ca9a773332d0b2bf256551f4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 399}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1091}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART-YEAR BONUS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part-Year Bonus refers to the portion of year-end bonus that an employee is entitled to if they are not employed by a single employer throughout the entire bonus period but have been employed for at least three months."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02218e873b9a55b35f3e34874d7090d6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 101}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 529}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROBATION PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Probation Period refers to a term in an employment contract that might be excluded from the three-month period used for calculating part-year bonuses."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is a defined period during which an employee's employment can be terminated without following the normal procedures if certain conditions are met, as specified in subsection (1A)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02218e873b9a55b35f3e34874d7090d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5aaa252a172d6b006af917dc91a91759</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 101}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 529}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BONUS PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bonus Period is a specific time frame during which an employee's eligibility for year-end bonuses is determined. "</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02218e873b9a55b35f3e34874d7090d6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1997 YEAR 74TH AMENDMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This amendment refers to changes made in the 1997, 74th regulation that affect how part-year bonuses are calculated."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02218e873b9a55b35f3e34874d7090d6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2001 YEAR 7TH AMENDMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This amendment refers to additional regulations introduced in 2001, specifically affecting conditions under which part-year bonus calculations apply or do not apply. "</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02218e873b9a55b35f3e34874d7090d6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;部分年終酬金&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"部分年年终奖金是根据雇佣合同和服务期间计算的，用于支付给员工的一部分工资。"</data>
