</node>
<node id="&quot;FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Female Employee is a person who may take maternity leave after confirming her pregnancy with a medical certificate, subject to specific notice requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Female Employee is an employee who is entitled to maternity leave pay under specific conditions related to pregnancy and childbirth."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Female Employee refers to a specific category of employee who may be entitled to maternity leave pay under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Female Employee refers to an individual who is employed under a continuous contract and may be entitled to maternity leave after childbirth."&lt;SEP&gt;"A female employee is mentioned in the text, giving notice of pregnancy and intention to take maternity leave under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A female employee is the subject of specific provisions regarding wages, leave, and compensation during termination or maternity leave."&lt;SEP&gt;"A female worker who is protected under labor laws against unfair dismissal during her pregnancy period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Female employee is a person who may be required to provide medical certificates related to her expected date of confinement or the actual date of confinement as part of the process for taking maternity leave."&lt;SEP&gt;"Female employee refers to a person who is entitled to maternity leave under specific conditions, such as continuous employment for at least 40 weeks before the commencement of her leave."&lt;SEP&gt;"Female employees are individuals who may receive paid sick leave days or pre-natal check-up attendance certificates as per regulations, highlighting their role within the context of workplace health policies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Female employees are mentioned in the context of pregnancy, childbirth, and miscarriage related leave policies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-681c7e69874ff6c2cdf180f0fb0d44f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4646eb80519916bd0464a8b522d48735&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5001d950d1e5de5921648ae860af7539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78df2b99fcbe4aa2c71fdce1f79d338c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9112f21c7d8a89e9880b92acfce9ecd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60efa76430de6c8c3995f39eeee4cc13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-635fb659aa7fe54dd44ec966f454cd08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505a565a05fcfbf53c86377d50356a49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d6f22e03ef794b224e1918ddd3fee77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8d3158e721c74f203da21b92ec49085</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 98}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 511}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 12AA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 12AA is a provision that determines the start date for calculating maternity leave periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 12AA refers to an amendment that provides additional conditions for the commencement of maternity leave, including continuous employment for at least 40 weeks before the date of her commencement of maternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-681c7e69874ff6c2cdf180f0fb0d44f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8d3158e721c74f203da21b92ec49085</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 98}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 514}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDICAL CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Medical Certificate is used by female employees to confirm their pregnancy and notify employers of their intention to take maternity leave."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical Certificate is an official document issued by a healthcare professional certifying medical conditions, treatments received, and other health-related information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical certificate is a document produced by healthcare professionals that specifies the expected or actual date of confinement or certifies illness or disability related to maternity leave."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical certificate is another type of document issued by authorities that can be used to prove the delivery or death of an infant under certain circumstances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical certificates are mentioned as documents that can be submitted by employees for certain purposes related to pregnancy and work allocation adjustments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b89f7731524d41ce9b762132c808abd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9112f21c7d8a89e9880b92acfce9ecd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6320bd8af6a47ec4d774b02d5588447a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53400793123be7f8846d77b56748e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505a565a05fcfbf53c86377d50356a49</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 112}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 568}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREGNANCY CONFIRMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event of Pregnancy Confirmation involves the issuance of a medical certificate that confirms a woman's pregnancy, triggering notice obligations under the regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-505a565a05fcfbf53c86377d50356a49</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 98}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 511}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REST DAY OR HOLIDAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rest Day or Holiday refers to days off, which may overlap with holidays and are considered in the context of maternity leave."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest day or holiday are specific days that may be included in the calculation of annual leave and can affect its duration according to certain sections mentioned."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest day or holiday indicates specific days when employment might end and the rules for renewal or re-engagement apply as described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest day or holiday is a non-working day, often designated by local laws or company policies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest days and holidays are periods during which employees do not work, as mentioned in the text for special considerations regarding dismissal dates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest days or holidays are specific dates, typically non-working days, where references to a relevant date should be construed as the next working day according to legal provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest days or holidays are specified as exceptions where relevant dates may shift, impacting legal interpretations of employment terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d536cf1eacc47eb2d3812dd2faa34e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44e57b1615ed5c8b1f49eb6a6ecd4472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e5f55eef00b5211e8c9c5c06c4bde96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a40a9600dcdabbcf7b1de20226238a1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bef47a255f1eda2d15380bce3341cd94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1ba134cba7bc0ad2b2ef34e757e78d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 536}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maternity Leave Pay is a form of compensation provided during maternity leave as part of employee benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maternity Leave Pay is a product provided to female employees during their maternity period as part of labor rights and benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maternity Leave Pay is a type of compensation provided to employees during their maternity leave as per specific regulations and guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maternity Leave Pay is a type of payment provided to female employees during their maternity leave period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maternity Leave Pay is the financial compensation given to female employees for taking maternity leave, as required by regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maternity Leave Pay refers to the payment made during maternity leave, which cannot be replaced by other payments according to section 15C."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maternity Leave Pay refers to the payment provided during maternity leave, specifically mentioned as a component of severance pay."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maternity leave pay is a financial benefit provided by the employer to the female employee during her maternity leave, subject to specific conditions of employment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maternity leave pay is a sum of money paid by an employer to a female employee during her maternity leave, subject to certain conditions and reductions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maternity leave pay is a type of compensation provided to employees during their maternity leave."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maternity leave pay refers to financial compensation provided for a female employee's maternity leave, subject to certain conditions and legal provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maternity leave pay refers to the financial compensation provided during maternity leave, with a maximum amount of $80,000 specified for the latter period of maternity leave."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maternity leave pay refers to the monetary benefit provided during maternity leave as part of the employee's entitlements under this Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maternity leave pay refers to the payment made by an employer to a female employee during her maternity leave, calculated at four-fifths of the daily average wages earned before the leave."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-681c7e69874ff6c2cdf180f0fb0d44f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4646eb80519916bd0464a8b522d48735&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5b551a4a483944d6cf3179909e4812f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5001d950d1e5de5921648ae860af7539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd0362fbf5661d142ff4aeefe27aea79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78df2b99fcbe4aa2c71fdce1f79d338c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7550fdff3623ae221e2d156f6ce5cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d4bd265e2aa3d3a8af55fbca1b13963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d46f6e07563bbf79e567c647ecf4fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bef47a255f1eda2d15380bce3341cd94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f5ddfc5b519fcf524c4d9bd233c4e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d6f22e03ef794b224e1918ddd3fee77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-885c65878619106b2d2b302114a64bb2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 99}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 515}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Any leave taken with the agreement of his employer is considered a valid form of leave under the given context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employer Agreement refers to the agreement between an employer and employee, which influences decisions regarding leave commencement dates."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text discusses the calculation of wages for employees under specific conditions, such as taking leave or temporary incapacity. This can be considered a form of technology in labor law and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bef47a255f1eda2d15380bce3341cd94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd2478b6eecc304c9feadaf2ffde1109</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 99}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 518}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXPECTED DATE OF CONFINEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Expected Date of Confinement marks the anticipated start date for childbirth, which influences leave scheduling."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bef47a255f1eda2d15380bce3341cd94</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 98}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 512}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCTORS' CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Doctors' Certificate is a document that may be required in certain contexts but not fully detailed here; it pertains to medical certification related to employment and health matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bef47a255f1eda2d15380bce3341cd94</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 98}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 512}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCTORS' CERTIFICATES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Doctors' certificates are medical documents issued by registered doctors, registered Chinese medicine practitioners, or midwives for various purposes such as maternity leave, sick leaves, etc."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-911f250d278d47d4c7dfd5e35d124637</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 98}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 510}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MIDWIFE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Midwives are health professionals trained to provide care during pregnancy, childbirth, and the postpartum period. They can be registered under specific sections of the Midwives Registration Ordinance (Cap. 162)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Midwives are registered healthcare professionals who provide care during childbirth and can be involved in certain health-related decisions or practices within a recognized framework."&lt;SEP&gt;"Midwives are registered professionals mentioned as part of the medical profession, specifically regulated by the Midwifery Registration Ordinance (Cap. 162)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Midwives, whether registered under section 8 or deemed to be registered under section 25 of the Midwives Registration Ordinance (Cap. 162), are authorized to issue specific medical certificates as per the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcd2a26e931b9fa624c25b0caadbcdb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f158408c588106f3a0fd30a322902be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11184ac38e9ff98017a8ef0f47064dc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 345}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1038}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 12(4) OR (6)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 12(4) or (6) refers to a legal provision that outlines conditions under which certain types of medical certificates can be issued by registered professionals, including midwives in some cases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 111}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 564}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1136}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 12AA&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 12AA is another legal section mentioned for issuing specific medical certificates related to maternity leave and other purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 15AA&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 15AA, though not detailed in the text provided, likely pertains to a similar set of conditions or procedures as sections referenced above regarding issuance of medical certificates for specific purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDICAL CERTIFICATE&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Medical certificates are documents issued by registered professionals that serve various legal and administrative functions related to health and employment matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A registered Chinese medicine practitioner is a professional who can issue certain types of medical certificates, as specified in the text provided for different sections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MIDWIVES REGISTRATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 162)&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Midwives Registration Ordinance (Cap. 162) is an organization or legal framework that regulates midwifery practice and registration, including provisions related to issuing medical certificates."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Female employees are the recipients of certain rights regarding maternity leave wages as outlined in the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employers have responsibilities towards female employees, including providing paid maternity leave under specific conditions and issuing relevant certificates if required."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAID MATERNITY LEAVE&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Paid maternity leave is a benefit that can be granted to female employees based on certain conditions as outlined in the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT ORDINANCE (CAP. 27)&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Employment Ordinance (Cap. 27) likely refers to broader legal frameworks governing employment rights and benefits, including those related to maternity leave wages mentioned in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A continuous contract is a type of employment agreement that may be relevant for determining eligibility for certain benefits like paid maternity leave as per the conditions specified in the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1997 YEAR 73 ORDINANCE AMENDMENT (S.6)&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The amendment to the ordinance in 1997, specifically S.6 of that year, has modified certain provisions related to eligibility for paid maternity leave and other benefits as mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1995 YEAR 5 ORDINANCE AMENDMENT (S.4)&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The amendment in 1995, specifically S.4 of that year, has also impacted the conditions under which certain employment rights can be exercised or enforced as per the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;12(2)(A) DECISION&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A specific decision made according to section 12(2)(a), likely related to determining eligibility for maternity leave and associated benefits, is mentioned in the context of issuing relevant certificates or providing wages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 16 OF MIDWIVES REGISTRATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 162)&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 16 of this ordinance has implications on who can be registered as a midwife and thus authorized to issue certain medical certificates, impacting the overall process described in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 8 REGISTRATION&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Registration under section 8 is another specific condition or procedure that must be met for individuals like midwives to be eligible to issue certain types of medical certificates as per the regulations mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 25 REGISTRATION&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 25 registration, similar to section 8 but possibly with different conditions or requirements, is another pathway for individuals like midwives to be authorized to issue certain types of medical certificates as per the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINUOUS EMPLOYMENT REQUIREMENT&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The continuous employment requirement mentioned in point (a) refers to a condition that must be met by female employees before they can qualify for specific benefits like paid maternity leave and related certificates, impacting their rights under certain legal provisions as outlined."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTIFICATION REQUIREMENTS&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Notification requirements specified in points (b), (c) refer to procedural steps that must be followed by employers or employees before certain benefits can be granted or specific actions taken regarding maternity leave and related certificates, impacting the overall process as described."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION OF REGISTRATION&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The termination of registration mentioned in point (d) likely refers to a situation where an individual's eligibility for issuing certain types of medical certificates may be affected if they no longer meet specific conditions or requirements, impacting the overall process as described."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT RIGHTS AND BENEFITS&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The text discusses various aspects related to employment rights and benefits, particularly focusing on maternity leave wages and associated medical certificates, reflecting broader social science considerations around labor laws and employee welfare."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE WAGES&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maternity leave wages are a specific type of benefit provided by employers under certain conditions as outlined in the text, impacting both employees' rights and employer responsibilities related to employment benefits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINUOUS EMPLOYMENT PERIOD&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A continuous employment period is mentioned as one of the requirements for female employees to qualify for specific benefits like paid maternity leave wages, reflecting broader concepts around labor laws and employee welfare as discussed in the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTIFICATION COMPLIANCE&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Compliance with notification procedures by employers or employees is a key aspect of ensuring eligibility for certain employment rights and benefits related to maternity leave and associated certificates, impacting both parties' actions and responsibilities as described."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;休息日&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"休息日在某些情况下可以替代法定假日或其他特定日期的安排中起到关键作用，并且必须符合相关法规的要求。"&lt;SEP&gt;"休息日在某些情况下可以替代法定假日或其他特定日期，具体取决于相关法规和双方协议。"&lt;SEP&gt;"休息日指的是法律规定的工作之外的休假时间，员工在此期间无需工作并可获得相应报酬。"&lt;SEP&gt;"休息日是员工可以不工作的日子，通常不会获得工资。"&lt;SEP&gt;"休息日是指雇员有权享受的非工作日，通常用于恢复和放松。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7430d09345738519e0c07e81b09c47d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f7b047f9f55a2ab249abdbcd1a65d36</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 85}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 489}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;病假日&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"病假日是员工因为生病需要休养的日子，期间可能不会获得全额工资或没有工作。"&lt;SEP&gt;"病假日是指因健康原因需要休养的日子，在此期间雇员可以享受带薪或无薪假期。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 85}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 489}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;年假&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"年假是指员工在应享有假期的时间内未被给予该假期，而在该期间结束后继续雇佣的情况下，雇主需支付的补偿或提供有薪休假。"&lt;SEP&gt;"年假是每年给予员工一定天数的休假，用于休息和度假，通常可以获得相应的工资补偿。"&lt;SEP&gt;"年假是雇员每年可以享受的一段时间休假，通常在这些期间不会提供日常工资。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c777bc9929cfa20260878316c3ec4ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 71}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 456}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1128}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;《僱員補償條例》(第282章)第10條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a legal provision under the Employment Compensation Ordinance (Cap. 282), Section 10, which outlines conditions for compensation when an employee temporarily loses work capacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"根据《僱員補償條例》，雇员因暂时丧失工作能力缺勤时可获得的补偿，涉及计算和支付的具体条款。"&lt;SEP&gt;"根據此條款，僱主需向因工作受傷或患病的僱員支付補償金額。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b95a210c7fca53b1bea2e9c19744745</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;正常工作日&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Normal workdays are the days when employees perform their regular duties, as opposed to holidays or other types of leave."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normal working day refers to the standard days when an employee performs regular duties and earns wages according to usual conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normal working days are those where an employee performs their regular duties and receives full pay, which can be considered for wage calculations under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"正常工作日在這裡指的是女性僱員通常工作的日子，用於計算工資平均值。"&lt;SEP&gt;"正常工作日指的是僱主通常安排的工作日子，是計算假期和補償的重要基準。"&lt;SEP&gt;"正常工作日是指员工通常工作的日子，在此期间他们需要完成工作任务并获取工资报酬。"&lt;SEP&gt;"正常工作日是指员工通常工作的日子，在这些天里他们会被提供工作任务，并且会得到工资。"&lt;SEP&gt;"正常工作日是雇员通常需要工作的日子，这些天他们应该获得工资。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b95a210c7fca53b1bea2e9c19744745&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab559340de48ae6d55e82984ae48a4f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6957d2ae600df45cdcfeef087031ad45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8f159cb841c798f1b18dd22fda97160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14678de8548f803294fa05856c13dfc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 478}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;暫時喪失工作能力&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"暂时丧失工作能力指的是雇员因健康或其他原因无法继续从事其常规工作的情况，可能影响其工资支付和福利待遇。"&lt;SEP&gt;"這是一種健康狀況，導致女性僱員無法正常上班，影響工資平均值計算方式。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;緊接其產假開始日期之前的12個月期間&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"紧接产假开始前的一年时间范围，在此期间内员工的工资收入用于计算产假薪酬。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 477}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;較短的期間&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A shorter period than 12 months during which an employee was employed, used for calculating the average monthly wage when the employment duration is less than a year."&lt;SEP&gt;"较短的时间段指的是雇员在最近一年中实际受僱于有关雇主的具体时长，可能少于12个月。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b95a210c7fca53b1bea2e9c19744745</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 477}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;不放產假亦不會工作&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"这种情况描述了即使没有产假安排，员工也可能因其他原因无法工作的日子，在这种情况下无需支付产假薪酬。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;僱主通常無須就該日支付工資&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This statement reflects social science principles related to labor relations where employers may not be required to pay wages on certain days, such as rest days or when employees are absent without work provided by the employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"这表明在某些特定情况下，雇主可能不需要为该天支付工资，例如节假日或特殊安排的休息日等。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9d7bf328eb68da98c29ac72b529085</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;产假&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"产假 is a period of leave provided by employers for female employees after childbirth, often accompanied by pay."&lt;SEP&gt;"产假是指女性雇员因生育而暂时离开工作岗位的一种假期。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47f5ddfc5b519fcf524c4d9bd233c4e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 85}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 489}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;假日&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"假日是指法定的休息日或其他非正常工作的日子。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 85}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 489}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;《员工补偿条例》(第282章)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"《员工补偿条例》是一部法律文件，规定了因工伤或其他原因导致暂时丧失工作能力时的赔偿条款。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;每日平均款额&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"每日平均款额是指在计算产假薪酬时用来确定支付金额的一个数学概念。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;产假薪酬&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"产假薪酬是指因女性员工休产假而支付的补偿或福利产品。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 477}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;12個月或較短的期間&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"12個月或较短期间是指计算产假薪酬时所参考的时间段长度。"&lt;SEP&gt;"這是一個時間範圍，用於計算女性僱員在特定時期內所賺取的工資平均值。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;正常工作日所賺取的數額的一個分數&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"正常工作日所赚取的数额的一个分数是指在某些情况下，雇员可能只获得其日常工资的一部分或全部未支付。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 477}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;同一僱主從事同樣工作的人&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"同一僱主从事同样工作的人指的是在同一雇主下进行相同工作的其他员工，他们的工资可以作为参考来计算产假薪酬。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;附表1A中的指明的款额&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"附表1A中指明的款额是根据本条规定计算产假薪酬时的一个参考标准。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-752073f001b8e7d22967a0f26dd04e44</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第3E条&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"第3E条增补了关于产假末段期间支付的产假薪酬最高限额的规定。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-752073f001b8e7d22967a0f26dd04e44</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第12(2)(A)条&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"第12(2)(a)条涉及女性雇员在未经雇主许可的情况下为另一雇主工作的情况，规定其丧失获得该段时间产假薪酬的权利。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-752073f001b8e7d22967a0f26dd04e44</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第7号第6条&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"第7号第6条增补了关于计算某女性雇员所赚取的工资每日平均款额的规定。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-752073f001b8e7d22967a0f26dd04e44</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1997年第73号第6条修訂&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"1997年第73号第6条规定了产假薪酬支付的相关规定，并进行了修订，包括废除某些条款和修改其他条款。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-752073f001b8e7d22967a0f26dd04e44</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2007年第7号第6条增补&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"2007年第7号第6条对计算某女性雇员所赚取的工资每日平均款额的规定进行了增补。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-752073f001b8e7d22967a0f26dd04e44</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2020年第13号第6条修訂&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"2020年第13号第6条对产假末段期间支付的产假薪酬最高限额规定进行了修订。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-752073f001b8e7d22967a0f26dd04e44</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;雇傭合約或任何其他協議&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"雇佣合同或其他协议中的条款可能影响女性雇员在产假期间获得的报酬，具体取决于这些合同和协议的具体内容。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-752073f001b8e7d22967a0f26dd04e44</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 12(2)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 12(2)(a) refers to a legal provision that defines when an employee is entitled to maternity leave pay based on continuous employment and notice given by the employee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-681c7e69874ff6c2cdf180f0fb0d44f7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 99}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 515}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;40 WEEKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"40 weeks is a specific period of time used as a condition for female employees to be eligible for paid maternity leave under certain circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-681c7e69874ff6c2cdf180f0fb0d44f7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 97}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 505}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE UNDER SECTION 12(4) OR (5)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Notice under Section 12(4) or (5) refers to formal notification given by an employee regarding their intention to take maternity leave, which is a condition for eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-681c7e69874ff6c2cdf180f0fb0d44f7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 98}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 514}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 12(6) OR (7)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 12(6) or (7) refers to requirements that the employer may impose on employees before they can be eligible for paid maternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-681c7e69874ff6c2cdf180f0fb0d44f7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 98}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 514}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DAILY AVERAGE OF THE WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The daily average of the wages is calculated over a period of 12 months or a shorter period if the employee has been employed for less than that time, considering various factors such as unpaid days due to leave and temporary incapacity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5b551a4a483944d6cf3179909e4812f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 100}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 523}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 12(4), (5)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sections 12(4) and (5) are events or requirements that an employee must comply with before receiving certain benefits such as notice under these sections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5b551a4a483944d6cf3179909e4812f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 12(6), (7)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sections 12(6) and (7) are events or requirements related to compliance by the employee's employer after giving notice under section 12(4) or (5)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5b551a4a483944d6cf3179909e4812f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 99}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 515}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 3A, 3B, 3C&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sections 3A, 3B, and 3C are events that define how maternity leave pay is calculated based on the employee's wages over a specified period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5b551a4a483944d6cf3179909e4812f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 3E&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 3E is an event or requirement related to the calculation of maternity leave pay under section 3A and may provide additional conditions or exclusions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5b551a4a483944d6cf3179909e4812f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 99}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 515}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEES COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Employees' Compensation Ordinance (Cap. 282) provides the framework for calculating wages and benefits, including compensation for temporary incapacity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5001d950d1e5de5921648ae860af7539</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 98}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 511}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRADE OR OCCUPATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Trade or Occupation refers to specific types of work and professions that are used as a reference point for calculating wages during maternity leave pay calculations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5001d950d1e5de5921648ae860af7539</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 138}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 604}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISTRICT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"District is a geographical area often used in legal contexts, such as determining the relevant employment market for wage calculation purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5001d950d1e5de5921648ae860af7539</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 99}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 515}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SCHEDULE 1A&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Schedule 1A contains the amount specified for maternity leave pay, which can be amended by the Commissioner as per section (8)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78df2b99fcbe4aa2c71fdce1f79d338c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 98}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 511}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LATTER PERIOD OF MATERNITY LEAVE (產假末段期間)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Latter Period of Maternity Leave refers to a specific phase during maternity leave, defined as the time after the first 10 weeks and up until the end of the leave when an employee is expected to return to work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78df2b99fcbe4aa2c71fdce1f79d338c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 99}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 519}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;懷孕僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to female employees who are pregnant, indicating their specific status in the workforce."&lt;SEP&gt;"懷孕僱員 (Pregnant Employee) refers to a female employee who has informed her employer about her pregnancy, which triggers certain employment benefits and protections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78df2b99fcbe4aa2c71fdce1f79d338c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 99}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 519}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LABOR LAWS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Labor Laws are legal frameworks governing employment relationships, setting standards for wages, working conditions, termination procedures, and other aspects of the employer-employee relationship."&lt;SEP&gt;"Labor laws refer to the legal framework governing employer-employee relationships and include provisions for termination of contracts, wages, and other rights and obligations between parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602a52838c03cef3777006bf2a44b72e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 97}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 505}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1995年第103號第26條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"這條修訂指出了女性僱員在僱傭合約終止後獲得額外款項的情況，並規定計算方式。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2007年第7號第7條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"這條修正案替换了有關12個月或較短期間內工資平均款額的計算方法。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1981年第22號第5條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"這條增補規定女性僱員有權獲得產假薪酬，並增加了14星期的產假薪酬。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;產假、休息日、病假日、假日或年假&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"這些假期是女性僱員可能會放取的日子，影響每月平均款額的計算方式。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;暫時喪失工作能力以致缺勤&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"此事件是指因健康原因導致的缺席，影響每月平均款額的計算方式。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;補償&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"補償在此指僱主需支付給女性僱員的各種款項，包括終止僱傭合約後的補償和產假薪酬等。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 71}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 464}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;《僱員補償條例》(第282章)第10條會獲付補償&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"根据《雇员补偿条例》，员工因某些原因未能获得工资或全部工资时，可以得到补偿。"&lt;SEP&gt;"根據此規定，因工作受傷或患病的僱員可獲得補償金額。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c12a66b5fa9d29ed0b0dc7f747de3d29</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;放取任何產假、休息日、病假日、假日或年假&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"這些假期是女性僱員可能會使用的時間段，影響工資平均值計算方式。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 478}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;僱主同意下放取任何假期&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to leave taken with the employer's approval. It highlights the flexibility in holiday arrangements and employee rights within labor laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"此事件是指在僱主同意的情況下，女性僱員可以放取假期待遇。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9d7bf328eb68da98c29ac72b529085</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 476}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1129}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;14星期的產假薪酬&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"這是一種特定的補償形式，用於女性僱員在休完產假後獲得的额外薪酬。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 477}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;放取任何假期&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"此事件是指女性僱員可能會使用的各種假期，影響工資平均值計算方式。"&lt;SEP&gt;"此条款指的是在雇主同意下放取的假期，涉及社会学和劳动法的相关规定。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c12a66b5fa9d29ed0b0dc7f747de3d29</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 476}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1129}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;因正常工作日不獲其僱主提供工作&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"這是一種情況，指在正常工作日中，女性僱員未被安排工作的事件，影響工資平均值計算方式。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 478}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;产假、休息日、病假日、假日或年假&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are types of leave or holidays that employees can take according to labor laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ab559340de48ae6d55e82984ae48a4f0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 480}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREGNANT EMPLOYEE'S EMPLOYMENT TERMINATION PROHIBITION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to a set of rules prohibiting employers from terminating the continuous contracts of pregnant employees under certain conditions, as detailed in subsections (1)(a) and (b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5aaa252a172d6b006af917dc91a91759</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 106}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 543}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A product or agreement between an employer and employee that is not terminated for reasons other than those specified by law, such as pregnancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Continuous Contract of Employment is a type of employment agreement that does not have a fixed end date, and its terms may be subject to specific conditions as outlined in subsections (2) and (3)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bb3d86d7a750daf3fdfd492ec75be8b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5aaa252a172d6b006af917dc91a91759</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 106}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 543}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 9 TERMINATION PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a specific legal process outlined in Section 9 of the relevant legislation which must be followed when terminating employment contracts under normal circumstances, especially during maternity leave or probation periods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5aaa252a172d6b006af917dc91a91759</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 106}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 543}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER WHO TERMINATES CONTINUOUS CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT OF A PREGNANT EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This entity refers to an organization that may terminate the employment contract of a pregnant employee, potentially violating labor laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 306}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)(A) OR (B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are legal provisions indicating circumstances under which an employer's termination action is considered non-compliant with section 9 regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 306}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAVE TAKEN WITH AGREEMENT OF EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to days when an employee takes leave that has been agreed upon by the employer, not necessarily a physical location but an event in the workplace."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1097}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NORMAL WORKING DAY WITHOUT WORK PROVIDED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A normal working day on which no work is given to the employee, indicating a situation where wages are still due even if there's no productive activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"A situation where employees are present at their normal working day but do not receive any work from employers, thus no wage is earned on that day."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1096}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY INCAPACITY FOR COMPENSATION UNDER SECTION 10 OF EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Temporary incapacity leading to compensation as per specific labor laws, indicating a medical condition that affects work and entitles the employee to benefits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1097}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRAVENES SUBSECTION (1)(A) OR (B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This describes an action by an employer that violates legal provisions regarding termination of employment contracts during pregnancy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUM WHICH WOULD HAVE BEEN PAYABLE IF CONTRACT HAD BEEN TERMINATED BY EMPLOYER UNDER SECTION 7&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the monetary compensation that an employee might receive if their employment was legally and properly terminated according to Section 7, but in this case, it is not due."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 306}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONTHLY AVERAGE OF WAGES EARNED DURING SPECIFIED PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A calculation method used to determine additional financial compensation for wrongful termination, based on the employee's earnings over a defined time frame."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE IS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This phrase indicates that further details about the status or condition of an employed individual are forthcoming but not specified in this excerpt."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 98}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 511}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event of employment contract termination is referenced in calculating severance payments and related benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"The termination of an employee's contract by their employer due to violations of certain clauses, with conditions affecting applicability as per legal amendments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d6f22e03ef794b224e1918ddd3fee77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4646eb80519916bd0464a8b522d48735</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 104}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 540}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a procedural method for calculating wages, not an actual technology but a legal provision."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 398}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1089}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONTHLY AVERAGE OF THE WAGES EARNED BY A FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"It is a product or result derived from wage calculations over time, specifically related to female employees' earnings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 398}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1089}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;12 MONTHS IMMEDIATELY BEFORE THE DATE OF TERMINATION OF THE EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a specific period in time relative to an event (termination), not a physical location but a temporal one."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 398}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1089}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;12 MONTHS IMMEDIATELY BEFORE THE DATE OF TERMINATION OF THE EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT (FOR NO SUCH PERSON)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Another temporal reference for comparison when there is no suitable person to refer to in terms of time period."</data>
