  <data key="d1">"Maternity Leave Compensation refers to the compensation provided during maternity leave according to specific provisions of employment laws and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-df8fc6081be757641b05c1766ffacd20</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 138}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 604}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT PERIOD WITHOUT FULL WAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Any period where wages are not fully paid for any reason except those specified (excluding periods)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 504}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SICK LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sick Leave is a type of leave that allows an employee to take time off due to illness, which does not result in the loss of wages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 504}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY LOSS OF WORK CAPACITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Temporary loss of work capacity refers to a condition where an employee cannot perform their duties due to illness or injury and may be entitled to compensation under the Employment Injury Compensation Ordinance (Cap. 282)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1096}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT INJURY COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Employment Injury Compensation Ordinance is a legal framework that provides for compensation in cases of temporary loss of work capacity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1096}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DAILY AVERAGE WAGE CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Calculation method used to determine the daily average wage, considering various factors and conditions as specified by law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAME EMPLOYER SAME JOB EMPLOYEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to employees who are employed under the same employer and perform similar jobs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAME REGION SAME INDUSTRY OR PROFESSION SAME JOB EMPLOYEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to employees in the same region, industry, or profession performing similar jobs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT OR OTHER AGREEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to agreements between employers and employees that may affect wage calculations as specified by law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 98}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 510}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIFIED DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Specified date refers to the day on which the Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 2022 was published in the Gazette, marking a key point of reference for entitlements under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The specified date refers to a specific point in time related to paternity leave, used for calculating wages."&lt;SEP&gt;"The specified date refers to the effective date of certain provisions in a regulation or law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6ee37a79b0dc57f162b791dd8b859ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60efa76430de6c8c3995f39eeee4cc13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a43725922c10caf8be455ef54288f1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 169}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 699}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE PAY RATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The paternity leave pay rate is a calculation method based on four-fifths of the employee's average daily wages, determined over a specified period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6ee37a79b0dc57f162b791dd8b859ce</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 138}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 604}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AVERAGE DAILY WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Average daily wages are calculated by excluding certain periods where full or no wages were paid due to various reasons such as leaves and sickness days. "&lt;SEP&gt;"Average daily wages refers to the calculation of wages for a specified period, not exceeding $22,500 over a certain number of months."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6ee37a79b0dc57f162b791dd8b859ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-515212436640c28d5f467b8b10ac11d7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 169}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 699}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RATE OF PATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The rate of paternity leave pay is a specific event in the context of calculating compensation for paternity leave based on average daily wages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f6ee37a79b0dc57f162b791dd8b859ce</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 169}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 699}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AVERAGE DAILY WAGES CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event involves calculating the average daily wages of an employee without considering certain periods or days where no full wages were paid due to specific reasons."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-61c50955c5e42baad9d032d0022c3d46</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 100}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 523}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE, REST DAY, SICKNESS DAY, HOLIDAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are concepts that refer to different types of leaves and days during which the calculation of average daily wages is excluded."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-61c50955c5e42baad9d032d0022c3d46</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 100}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 523}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BIRTH CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A birth certificate is a formal document issued by authorities that records the birth of an infant, serving as proof of identity and other legal purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A birth certificate is an official document that records the details of a child's birth, including date, place, and parents' names."&lt;SEP&gt;"Birth certificate is a document issued by authorities that proves the birth of an infant, and in some cases, identifies the father."&lt;SEP&gt;"Birth certificate is a document required for parental leave related to the birth of an infant in Hong Kong, as per relevant regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f2c1776c3e340075487202946fbb11cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6320bd8af6a47ec4d774b02d5588447a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bab24c47d69b1c9fe7a8b2d862514c83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11184ac38e9ff98017a8ef0f47064dc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 111}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 564}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1137}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCTOR'S CERTIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Doctor's certification is a document needed when the child born has died or there is no birth certificate issued under the Registration of Births and Deaths Ordinance (Cap. 174) for the infant, required by employers in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f2c1776c3e340075487202946fbb11cb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 98}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 510}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MIDWIVES REGISTRATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 162)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Midwives Registration Ordinance (Cap. 162) is an organization or regulation that governs the registration of midwives and related legal requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Midwives Registration Ordinance is a legal document that regulates midwifery practice and registration in Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Midwives Registration Ordinance is a legal document that regulates midwifery practice in Hong Kong, including registration and certification requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-73492d2774f700c9b55459d33fea445f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bab24c47d69b1c9fe7a8b2d862514c83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11184ac38e9ff98017a8ef0f47064dc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 111}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 564}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1136}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BIRTHS AND DEATHS REGISTRATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 174)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Births and Deaths Registration Ordinance is another legal document responsible for the registration of births and deaths in Hong Kong, which issues birth certificates."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f11184ac38e9ff98017a8ef0f47064dc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 111}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 564}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1137}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE PAY: BIRTH IN HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Paternity Leave Pay for Births in Hong Kong refers to the policy or practice allowing fathers to take paid leave when their children are born in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f11184ac38e9ff98017a8ef0f47064dc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 429}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;15K. 與侍產假薪酬有關的所需文件&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This document is related to the required documents for paternity leave benefits, detailing what needs to be provided by employees to employers regarding their leave and associated payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bab24c47d69b1c9fe7a8b2d862514c83</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;15H(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 15H(b) refers to specific provisions within a regulation or law concerning paternity leave for infants born outside Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bab24c47d69b1c9fe7a8b2d862514c83</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEATH CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A death certificate is an official document issued by authorities that records the death of an infant, serving as proof in legal and administrative matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bab24c47d69b1c9fe7a8b2d862514c83</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 111}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 564}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1137}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WRITTEN STATEMENT FROM EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An written statement from an employee is a personal declaration provided to support claims or verify information related to paternity leave and associated benefits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bab24c47d69b1c9fe7a8b2d862514c83</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 500}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WRITTEN STATEMENT SIGNED BY EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A written statement from the employee, stating their relationship as father and the status of the child's birth/death if no other documents are available."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6320bd8af6a47ec4d774b02d5588447a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 429}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDICAL CERTIFICATE OR DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Medical Certificate or Document is a document required by employers, stating that the employee is the father and providing information about the health status of the newborn."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SERVICE LEAVE COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Service Leave Compensation refers to the financial benefit provided by employers during service leave, such as paternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REQUISITE DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Requisite Document is a term used in legal documents and policies that outlines specific requirements for employees to receive certain benefits like service leave compensation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 499}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;12 MONTHS AFTER THE FIRST DAY ON WHICH THE EMPLOYEE TAKES PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a time period of 12 months after an employee starts taking paternity leave, during which they must provide required documents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 499}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;6 MONTHS AFTER CESSATION OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is the timeframe within which employees who have stopped working need to submit necessary documents if not done earlier."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 499}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;15J OR 15K CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These clauses are part of a legal document that outlines specific requirements for providing paternity leave and related compensation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAID PARENTAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Paid Parental Leave is the financial benefit provided to employees during their leave, ensuring they receive wages while on paternity or maternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;7 DAYS AFTER CESSATION OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a period of 7 days after an employee stops working where certain documents must be submitted if not done within the initial timeframe."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 499}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Payment Day is when employers are required to pay employees for their service leave, such as paternity leave, based on the submission of necessary documents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SERVICE LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Service Leave refers to any type of paid or unpaid leave provided by an employer during which an employee does not work but may still receive pay under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT RELATIONSHIP TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The termination of employment relationship is a significant event that affects the submission deadlines for necessary documents related to service leave and compensation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 499}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REQUISITE DOCUMENT (所需文件)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Requisite Document refers to the necessary paperwork required by employers for employees claiming paternity leave pay, mentioned under section 15J or 15K."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f4881be1a6d6d318bb1047aad7c99da</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 600}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 15J OR 15K&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sections 15J and 15K are parts of an industry regulation that detail requirements for employees taking paternity leave and the documentation needed to claim pay."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f4881be1a6d6d318bb1047aad7c99da</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 600}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CESSATION (停止受僱)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Cessation is a specific event where employment ends, which affects when and how paternity leave pay can be claimed according to section 15L."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f4881be1a6d6d318bb1047aad7c99da</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAVE DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Leave Day refers to the specific day on which an employee takes paternity leave, triggering obligations for the employer regarding payment of leave pay."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f8f154dd34baff54c016b669ab2da5c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 15L&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 15L is a legal provision that outlines how employers must calculate and provide paternity leave compensation according to labor laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 15L is a legal provision that outlines the payment terms for paternity leave, ensuring employees receive appropriate compensation during their leave period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f8f154dd34baff54c016b669ab2da5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aed3ae0b98488b1b913e6b49db19fee</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 500}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 15M(4)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 15M(4) describes the scenario where an employer may deduct previously paid paternity leave pay if certain conditions are met, such as non-provision of required documents within a specified timeframe."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f8f154dd34baff54c016b669ab2da5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第5級罰款&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"第5級罰款 indicates a specific level of fine prescribed by law for criminal offenses, here referring to the potential financial penalty for employers who violate labor regulations concerning paternity leave pay."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f8f154dd34baff54c016b669ab2da5c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;E.R. 3 OF 2017&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"E.R. 3 of 2017 indicates an editorial revision made in 2017 to the format or structure of certain sections, likely affecting how they are presented or interpreted."&lt;SEP&gt;"E.R. 3 of 2017 refers to the format changes made in 2017, indicating an event where legal documents were edited and revised."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is an editorial revision record indicating changes made in the edition released on March 3, 2017."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-768a2ada446405fddb705e41250aee16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-985c71a2aa2037adf4ce25fd3c8c12de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aed3ae0b98488b1b913e6b49db19fee</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSTITUTED HOLIDAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A substituted holiday allows an employee to take leave on another date instead of a statutory holiday when it falls on their rest day or for other valid reasons, maintaining compliance with labor laws regarding days off."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0aed3ae0b98488b1b913e6b49db19fee</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 97}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 507}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EVERY EMPLOYEE WHO HAS BEEN EMPLOYED BY THE SAME EMPLOYER UNDER A CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Every employee continuously employed by one employer is entitled to at least 1 rest day every 7 days."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eeab579ddc2235f2e1503e95ddb7809</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY, OR ALTERNATIVE HOLIDAY OR SUBSTITUTED HOLIDAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Statutory holidays, alternative holidays, and substituted holidays are additional entitlements for employees apart from the required rest days."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eeab579ddc2235f2e1503e95ddb7809</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GRANT OF REST DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event involves granting rest days to employees as per labor laws and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eeab579ddc2235f2e1503e95ddb7809</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1976年第71號第4條修訂&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Amendments made in 1976, specifically the fourth clause of the seventh十一号法令，修订了关于休息日的规定。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8eeab579ddc2235f2e1503e95ddb7809</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;僱主指定的休息日&quot;">
