<node id="&quot;BANKING ORDINANCE (CAP. 155)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Banking Ordinance defines banks and sets conditions under which they can receive or share information for reasonable commercial purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Banking Ordinance is a piece of legislation that defines the meaning of 'any bank' in relation to long service payments, indicating its role in financial regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Banking Ordinance (Cap. 155) defines banks, which are relevant in the context of paying wages into an employee's bank account."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Banking Ordinance is a legal document defining the meaning of banks under Hong Kong's financial regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Banking Ordinance is a legal document governing banking activities and money lending under reasonable commercial purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Banking Ordinance is the legal framework governing banking activities in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79816614535478a4c5093238ccf5e99a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b2609f36389403179e27bcc11b4123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ad535185a1489332f643fec100e338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11d596f17d04a1402f9a7eda05284076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aa1d2d981153f366e07b9a78ba0c7ce</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 694}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BANK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bank refers to financial institutions mentioned as a place where wages can be deposited into an employee’s account according to section 2 of the Banking Ordinance (Cap. 155)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 694}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OFFICE OR OTHER PLACE CUSTOMARILY USED BY THE EMPLOYER FOR THE PURPOSE OF PAYMENT OF WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a specific office or place where employers usually make wage payments, distinct from the employee's regular work location."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 294}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 983}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHEQUE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cheque is mentioned as one method through which wages can be paid by an employer with the consent of the employee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 694}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONEY ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Money Order, similar to a postal order, is another financial instrument used for payment and mentioned in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 694}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DULY APPOINTED AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Duly Appointed Agent refers to an individual designated by the employee who can receive wages on their behalf."&lt;SEP&gt;"Duly appointed agent refers to an individual designated by the person entitled to receive payment, highlighting their role as a recipient's representative."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aa1d2d981153f366e07b9a78ba0c7ce</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 164}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 680}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENTERTAINMENT VENUE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Entertainment Venue is a place where payment of wages cannot be made according to regulation, as specified in section 27(a) of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CASH-SWEEPS EVENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cash-Sweeps Event refers to an activity or location where cash-based lottery games are held and payments cannot be made there due to regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIXED ODDS BETTING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fixed Odds Betting is a type of gambling activity mentioned as one place where wages cannot be paid according to the text, specifically in section 27(b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARI-MUTUEL BETTING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pari-Mutuel Betting refers to another form of gambling activity that falls under cash-based lottery games and is listed as a location where payments are not allowed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VENUE SELLING INTOXICATING LIQUOR OR DANGEROUS DRUGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Venue Selling Intoxicating Liquor or Dangerous Drugs is a place where payment cannot be made, according to section 27(c) of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RETAIL STORE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Retail Store is mentioned as one type of location where payments are not allowed for wages, unless the employee works there, which would make it an exception."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BETTING DUTY ORDINANCE (CAP. 108)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Betting Duty Ordinance (Cap. 108) is a legal document that regulates cash-sweeps, fixed odds betting or pari-mutuel betting and provides authorization for their organization or conduct."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Betting Duty Ordinance is a legal framework that regulates betting activities in the jurisdiction it applies to."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-23e0ef850c878d1bb32d1dab35a67bc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2d24bb03fc40b38ed1a8c0cbcdbd963</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 29}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHOP OR STORE FOR THE RETAIL SALE OF MERCHANDISE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A shop or store for the retail sale of merchandise refers to specific locations where wages cannot be paid according to certain regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-23e0ef850c878d1bb32d1dab35a67bc7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 29}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTOXICATING LIQUOR OR ANY DANGEROUS DRUG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Intoxicating liquor or any dangerous drug are products that, if sold in a place, would prohibit payment of wages there."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-23e0ef850c878d1bb32d1dab35a67bc7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 29}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLACE OF AMUSEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A place of amusement is a location where wages cannot be paid according to the regulations mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-23e0ef850c878d1bb32d1dab35a67bc7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 29}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOOD, ACCOMMODATION OR OTHER ALLOWANCES OR PRIVILEGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Food, accommodation, or other allowances or privileges are benefits that can be provided in addition to wages as part of an employment contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-23e0ef850c878d1bb32d1dab35a67bc7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTOXICATING LIQUOR, DANGEROUS DRUG, TICKET OR OTHER SUBSTITUTE FOR TICKET&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Intoxicating liquor, dangerous drugs, tickets, or any substitutes for tickets are prohibited from being used as remuneration according to the regulations mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-23e0ef850c878d1bb32d1dab35a67bc7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 581}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1140}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CASH-SWEEP, FIXED ODDS BETTING OR PARI-MUTUEL BETTING ORGANIZED OR CONDUCTED WITH PERMISSION UNDER THE BETTING DUTY ORDINANCE (CAP. 108)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are types of betting events regulated by the Betting Duty Ordinance as they require authorization for organization or conduct."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a2d24bb03fc40b38ed1a8c0cbcdbd963</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 29}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT OR AGREEMENT IN CONSIDERATION OF A CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This describes an employment relationship where terms, including those related to wage usage, can be legally binding between employer and employee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a2d24bb03fc40b38ed1a8c0cbcdbd963</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 118}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGREEMENT AS TO MANNER OF SPENDING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Agreements regarding the use or expenditure of wages are prohibited under labor laws to ensure employees have autonomy over their earnings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a2d24bb03fc40b38ed1a8c0cbcdbd963</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 118}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER OPENING SHOPS FOR SALE OF COMMODITIES TO EMPLOYEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employers may provide goods and services to employees through retail establishments, but cannot impose conditions on purchase as a term of employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a2d24bb03fc40b38ed1a8c0cbcdbd963</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REASONABLE GROUNDS TO BELIEVE IN THE ABILITY TO PAY WAGES AT DUE DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This concept refers to an employer's assurance that they can meet their financial obligations for paying employee salaries when due without undue delay or difficulty."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a2d24bb03fc40b38ed1a8c0cbcdbd963</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 118}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT, RENEWAL, OR CONTINUATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment contracts involve the terms and conditions of work between employers and employees, including provisions related to wage payments and employment duration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a2d24bb03fc40b38ed1a8c0cbcdbd963</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 118}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER NOT TO ENTER INTO CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT WITHOUT REASONABLE BELIEF THAT HE CAN PAY WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to the situation where an employer enters into a contract of employment without a reasonable belief in their ability to pay wages, which is illegal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9809ad52a0fec55dacd101bbfec86fa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT AS EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Contract of Employment as Employer is described here as a legal agreement between an individual and an organization or person acting on behalf of the employer regarding terms and conditions of employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9809ad52a0fec55dacd101bbfec86fa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Severance Payments are financial compensation provided to employees who have been laid off, which is part of labor rights protection measures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9809ad52a0fec55dacd101bbfec86fa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART VA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A specific part of an ordinance that provides rules for situations where an employee dies before a notice period expires, affecting contract terminations and renewals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Part VA is an industry-specific section that undergoes modifications as indicated in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Part VA refers to a specific section in the document that deals with severance payments and related matters."&lt;SEP&gt;"Part is another reference to sections of the legal framework defining entitlements but does not represent an independent entity here."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d0dd3aa2554b81fa47ed2eec0f056d25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9809ad52a0fec55dacd101bbfec86fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1c30b39b26dc22df210f2ea63b93552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2f5d9b3d656df85c08982a8986732f4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 117}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPEALED 76 OF 1985 S. 4&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event indicates that a particular clause or regulation was repealed on April 30, 1985, which had implications for the terms of employment contracts and severance payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d9809ad52a0fec55dacd101bbfec86fa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 97}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 505}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REDUNDANCY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Redundancy in this context refers to situations within organizations where positions become unnecessary, leading to employees being released from their contracts based on specific conditions outlined in legal sections."&lt;SEP&gt;"Redundancy is a situation where an employee's position becomes obsolete due to changes in business operations, leading to their dismissal or layoff."&lt;SEP&gt;"Redundancy is defined as one or other of the facts specified in section 31B(2), where an employee's contract is not renewed and they are not re-engaged due to circumstances wholly or mainly attributable to these facts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Redundancy refers to a situation where an employee's position becomes unnecessary, leading to their dismissal as part of organizational restructuring."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33baa15beb160832b6e2302162f04d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9546d09d8137ba2697ee36074c84b498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a783557f86fea333101af802aa41e0a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 584}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAYOFF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Layoff is the act of temporarily or permanently stopping work for employees within certain conditions specified by law."&lt;SEP&gt;"Layoff refers to an event where employees are temporarily or permanently dismissed without severance pay, and its duration is crucial for determining certain rights such as severance payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Layoff refers to the act of temporarily suspending an employee from work within the meaning of section 31E as per employment laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9546d09d8137ba2697ee36074c84b498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8e2655c247e96affa05132d650c897b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 584}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Employment Agreement refers to the legal agreement between an employer and employee, which may be subject to restrictions by employment agencies as per regulatory requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employment Agreement refers to a legal document that outlines the terms and conditions between an employer and employee, including rights and obligations during employment and termination."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf1cb5b59a9e111ec611acd3b69ca0ea</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 145}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRIVATE HOUSEHOLD WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Private Household Work involves individuals employed in domestic settings such as cleaning, cooking, or childcare within private residences, often regulated by specific labor laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 584}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAMILY ERMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Family Employee refers to a person who is hired for work related to maintaining and operating a household, typically with different employment conditions compared to regular employees in the business sector."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS OPERATION STOPPING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Business Operation Stopping refers to situations where an employer decides or plans to cease operations of certain businesses that employ specific workers, leading to potential layoffs and severance payments for those affected."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JOB DEMAND REDUCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Job Demand Reduction occurs when the need for a particular type of work in a business location diminishes, potentially resulting in job losses or restructuring efforts by employers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL OBLIGATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal Obligations refer to the duties and responsibilities that organizations have towards their employees under labor laws, including provisions for severance payments during redundancies or layoffs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 690}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1168}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;U.K.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The U.K. refers to the United Kingdom and is cited as a source for legal provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The U.K. refers to the United Kingdom and is mentioned as a reference for legal sections."&lt;SEP&gt;"The U.K. refers to the United Kingdom, a location where legal provisions are discussed in this context."&lt;SEP&gt;"U.K. (United Kingdom) is referenced in the context of legal comparison or reference for similar provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"U.K. refers to the United Kingdom, a country where certain employment laws and regulations are applicable."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8271f6bc492f9ae5ef71b7e98a92bd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9546d09d8137ba2697ee36074c84b498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-985c71a2aa2037adf4ce25fd3c8c12de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfd284d26c8ac23ba53544b4fe799168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-723308f570a274e7e8ac1a555c11b81b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 59}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 446}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 31G&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 31G is being modified to specify the calculation of severance payment amounts based on pre-transition employment period years and wages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 31G outlines the method for calculating severance payments as per employment laws in U.K."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d0dd3aa2554b81fa47ed2eec0f056d25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9546d09d8137ba2697ee36074c84b498</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 117}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS CESSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Business cessation is a concept where an employer ceases or intends to cease carrying on business for which the employee was employed, leading to potential dismissal or layoff."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9546d09d8137ba2697ee36074c84b498</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 117}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1965 C. 62 SS. 1 &amp; 19(1) U.K.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the source or reference for certain sections in the United Kingdom's employment laws, indicating where specific provisions can be found."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9546d09d8137ba2697ee36074c84b498</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 59}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 446}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2000年第51號第3條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a reference to an amendment made in 2000 that revised section 3 of the relevant law, impacting certain aspects of employment rights and obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9546d09d8137ba2697ee36074c84b498</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 59}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 446}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT TERMINATION CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The clause discusses the conditions under which an employer can terminate an employment contract without notice or severance pay due to employee misconduct."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-18f452820ec690c39e359260ee75e592</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 40}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 365}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEVERANCE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Severance Pay refers to compensation given to a terminated employee, but in certain cases as described, it may not be applicable."&lt;SEP&gt;"Severance pay refers to the monetary compensation provided by an employer to an employee upon termination of employment, calculated based on years of service."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-18f452820ec690c39e359260ee75e592&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3acaae72bbbda2c87c57f32876a632e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 40}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 365}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT RENEWAL OFFER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An employment contract renewal offer is made by the employer before 7 days from the relevant date, and if rejected unreasonably by the employee, no severance pay will be given."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employment contract renewal offer refers to the proposal made by an employer to continue or rehire an employee, which can affect their employment status and benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employment Contract Renewal Offer refers to the offer made by Rongxin or its successor to renew an employee's contract, which can be accepted or rejected by the employee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-18f452820ec690c39e359260ee75e592&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cb0098fa2f01839bce9b10d85c36181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bb14977455cfee69d96555a42dffb40</data>
