<node id="&quot;ORS BENEFITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ORS (Occupational Retirement Scheme) Benefits are employer-funded retirement savings plans that may be held in mandatory provident fund schemes or paid directly to the employee as part of severance payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORS benefits are employer-funded benefits related to long service payments or retirement plans."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORS benefits are employer-funded benefits that may be subject to reduction under certain legal provisions and conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORS benefits are employer-funded occupational retirement scheme benefits that may be paid to an employee based on their length of service."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORS benefits are employer-funded retirement savings plans that may be specified as part of the long service payment calculation."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORS benefits are employer-funded retirement savings plans, which can be either voluntary (specified) ORS benefits or basic portion exempt ORS benefits as mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORS benefits are employer-funded retirement scheme benefits that may be payable to a beneficiary after an employee's death, as per the terms of a contract or agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORS benefits refer to employer-funded (specified) ORS benefits that could be paid to employees and might affect the calculation of long service payment."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORS benefits refer to employer-funded Occupational Retirement Savings (ORS) plans or schemes provided as part of an employment package."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORS benefits refer to employer-funded occupational retirement plan benefits that are exempt from certain deductions."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORS benefits refer to employer-funded occupational retirement scheme benefits, which are subject to certain conditions regarding service years and severance payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORS benefits refers to a type of benefit or advantage that is exempted in certain situations."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORS benefits refers to employer-funded (specified) ORS benefits that may be paid or held in respect of an employee, which can affect the calculation of severance payment."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORS benefits是雇主资助（指定）的职业退休计划福利。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a23958c5eb862b357e8540d3c4c5afd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-233de206d4d440690ca3d19bf8ddb77c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e5131fef8ae89d5a0f48b17c1599d19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad13daf2441a168160e4226aa7ac493d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c317132f5543388aa4ec358d54fbcf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b785a6d2d7fe1aa9d111846965f88378&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d634411e44f3153b1f3217349599619c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c87228f0b6f2f82336ca7700cb45e5d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16880dc0f6b710adfcdbea0c6c5c09ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60278fe3510d3896a76c8ed45d034e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd899e03ecc067de0edd74af6740db7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dabef41d299eda51d77087c2ca170398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db531f9fed0b652cc40ad79eb2a48c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622dec92f9d3c73f201fbdc4fab3be5f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 165}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 687}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"MPFS (Medical and Personal Financial Security) Benefits refer to health, personal financial security, and other related benefits funded by employers, often held in mandatory provident funds or paid out during severance periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPFS benefits are employer-funded (voluntary) MPFS benefits held in mandatory provident fund schemes, which may also impact the long service payment amount."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPFS benefits are employer-funded (voluntary) MPFS benefits that may be held in mandatory provident fund schemes and can impact the severance payment for an employee."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPFS benefits are employer-funded (voluntary, basic portion, and mandatory) benefits under a specified scheme."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPFS benefits are employer-funded mandatory benefits mentioned, which include various types such as employment contract-based payments and occupational pension plan interests."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPFS benefits refer to employer-funded Medical Premium Funding Scheme (MPFS) benefits provided as part of an employment package."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPFS benefits refer to employer-funded benefits under the Mandatory Provident Fund Schemes, including pre-transition and post-transition portions."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPFS benefits refer to employer-funded mandatory provident fund scheme benefits that can be paid out upon the death of an employee (Person A) and are payable to beneficiaries like Person B under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPFS benefits refer to employer-funded mandatory provident fund schemes within specific strong积金计划中雇主供款的强制性公积金权益。"&lt;SEP&gt;"MPFS benefits refer to mandatory provident fund schemes' employer-funded benefits held in respect of an employee, also subject to specific conditions related to service years and severance payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPFS benefits refer to mandatory provident fund schemes' employer-funded benefits held or paid in respect of the employee, related to their years of service."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPFS benefits refer to mandatory provident fund schemes, which are a type of financial benefit related to an employee's years of service and used in calculating reductions for long service payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPFS benefits, including both voluntary and mandatory portions, can also be affected by the legal provisions outlined in this text."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPFS benefits是雇主资助（自愿）的强制性职业养老基金方案中的利益或权益。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a23958c5eb862b357e8540d3c4c5afd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-233de206d4d440690ca3d19bf8ddb77c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e5131fef8ae89d5a0f48b17c1599d19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad13daf2441a168160e4226aa7ac493d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c317132f5543388aa4ec358d54fbcf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b785a6d2d7fe1aa9d111846965f88378&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d634411e44f3153b1f3217349599619c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c87228f0b6f2f82336ca7700cb45e5d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16880dc0f6b710adfcdbea0c6c5c09ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60278fe3510d3896a76c8ed45d034e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd899e03ecc067de0edd74af6740db7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dabef41d299eda51d77087c2ca170398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db531f9fed0b652cc40ad79eb2a48c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622dec92f9d3c73f201fbdc4fab3be5f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 165}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 689}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GRATUITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gratuities are financial benefits provided to employees based on their length of service, which may be reduced by severance payments under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gratuities are payments made to an employee for length of service, which may be subject to reduction when calculating long service payment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gratuities are payments made to employees based on their years of service as part of the contract of employment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gratuities are payments made to employees due to their length of service and can affect the calculation of severance payment when they meet specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5c317132f5543388aa4ec358d54fbcf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c24d050bd3e4419e71408fc656cab32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad13daf2441a168160e4226aa7ac493d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60278fe3510d3896a76c8ed45d034e51</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 164}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 682}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee's Contract of Employment is the legal document outlining the terms and conditions between an employee and their employer, which can be renewed or re-engaged under specific circumstances as per section 31C(2)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employee's contract of employment is a document governing the terms and conditions between an employer and employee as per the amended legislation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employee's contract of employment is a legal document outlining terms and conditions between employer and employee before any changes occur due to business ownership shifts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employee's contract of employment is a legal document outlining the terms and conditions under which an employee works for their employer, including potential changes due to business ownership transfers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employee's contract of employment is a legal document that outlines terms and conditions related to gratuities and other benefits paid based on length of service."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employee's contract of employment is a legal document that outlines the terms and conditions under which an employee works, including provisions for gratuities based on length of service."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employee's contract of employment refers to the agreement between an employer and employee that outlines their terms and conditions, which can be varied or terminated under certain circumstances."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employee's Contract of Employment is a document outlining terms and conditions, including gratuities based on length of service and ORS/MPFS benefits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-781090deea1d567c616cff8f0c0ae1ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c317132f5543388aa4ec358d54fbcf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a365e751a6908c5178b1168febad9bcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92eb9fce002800330c9f680d468f081b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16880dc0f6b710adfcdbea0c6c5c09ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60278fe3510d3896a76c8ed45d034e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc2894a439737cb35869b760804ff684</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 171}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 709}]</data>
</node>
