</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 31D(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 31D(2) is a clause that may be applied when new owners renew employment contracts on behalf of previous owners, as if the original contract was maintained by the former owner."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 31D(2) refers to a provision that allows for renewal of employment contracts or re-engagement under new contracts as if by the previous owner without substitution, but its specific content is not provided here."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 31D(2) refers to the circumstances where an employee's contract of employment is not renewed and they are not re-engaged under a new contract, which can be attributed to redundancy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8cb52dd4a9b2981de387c70ee06f029&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33baa15beb160832b6e2302162f04d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be5c7596bb8e4301da4cc603ef1a2b55</data>
