<node id="&quot;SECTION 31C(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 31C(2) is a legal provision that outlines the conditions under which an employee's contract can be renewed or re-engaged by a new owner after refusing an offer from the previous owner."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92eb9fce002800330c9f680d468f081b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 159}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS CHANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Business Change refers to any alteration or transfer of ownership within a company, which can trigger provisions such as those outlined in sections 31C and 31K."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92eb9fce002800330c9f680d468f081b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 171}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 706}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT RENEWAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contract Renewal is the process by which an employee's contract may be extended under new conditions after refusing an offer from the previous owner, subject to certain legal stipulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92eb9fce002800330c9f680d468f081b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RE-ENGAGEMENT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Re-Engagement of Employment refers to a situation where an employee can be brought back into work with different terms due to changes in ownership as per section 31C(2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92eb9fce002800330c9f680d468f081b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;U.K. LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The U.K. Law, specifically the provisions mentioned (section 31C and its context), form a part of social science studies on labor relations and legal frameworks governing employment contracts in the United Kingdom."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92eb9fce002800330c9f680d468f081b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 159}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;相聯公司&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"相聯公司 refers to associated companies that are related through ownership or control and can be considered as part of the same corporate group."&lt;SEP&gt;"相聯公司在香港法律中指与某家公司有紧密联系的其他公司，这些公司的所有权或控制权可能部分或全部由同一集团持有。在本段落中，它涉及到业务变更和雇佣合同续签的相关规定。"&lt;SEP&gt;"相聯公司是指与另一家公司有紧密联系的公司，通常包括附属公司或同属一家母公司的其他子公司。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92eb9fce002800330c9f680d468f081b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc7050cecd4e7d8b17b6622358415e8f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1965 C. 62 S. 13 U.K.&quot;}">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL PROVISION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a reference to section 13 in schedule 62 from an Act passed in 1965, United Kingdom."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;相聯公司 (1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to associated companies that are related through ownership or control and can be considered as part of the same corporate group in relation to clause 1 of section 31K."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 71}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 455}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1124}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;前擁有人&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON/ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"前擁有人 is a term used for previous owners, which could refer either to an individual person or an organization depending on context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;新擁有人&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON/ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"新擁有人 is a term used for new owners, which could refer either to an individual person or an organization depending on context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第31B(2)條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL PROVISION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to section 31B clause 2 of the relevant legal document, likely defining certain conditions related to employment termination."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 83}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 483}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;僱用公司&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"僱用公司 is a term used for employing companies in this context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;附屬公司&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"附屬公司 refers to subsidiary companies that are owned or controlled by another company, often part of the same corporate group."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;解僱&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"解僱 is a term used for termination of employment in this context."&lt;SEP&gt;"解僱指的是终止与员工的雇佣关系的行为，在特定条件下可以被重新定义为续订合同或再次聘用。"&lt;SEP&gt;"解僱是終止僱傭合約的一種情況，可能涉及支付代通知金或其他補償。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c82c895f7b30d4831c428126a0af9486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad6d0a2eed4fbaf59a6253fe84df6ac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 83}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 483}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;僱主的變更&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"僱主的變更 is a term used for change in employer, indicating that the employment period may still count as continuous even if the company changes according to clause 4 of section 31K."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 71}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 456}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1126}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第三间公司&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"第三间公司 refers to the third party or intermediate parent company that owns both associated companies in question."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASSOCIATED COMPANIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Associated companies are entities where one company is a subsidiary of another, or both are subsidiaries of a third party, and this relationship affects the interpretation and application of sections 32B, 32C, and 32D as per section 32E."&lt;SEP&gt;"Associated companies refer to a situation where one company is a subsidiary of another, or both are subsidiaries of the same third party."&lt;SEP&gt;"Associated companies refer to two or more companies that are related through ownership and control, often used in labor law contexts where re-engagement and dismissal policies apply."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2351949864b29078618f803ef4d2c6cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c28e990fb442886ba69eb65de9d2282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01e8dd2cd7216b43532ed7037814b54b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 335}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPANY (第622章)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Company refers to a legal entity formed for business purposes under the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622) of Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-01e8dd2cd7216b43532ed7037814b54b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 335}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSIDIARY (第15條)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsidiary, as defined in Section 15 of the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622), refers to a company that is controlled by another company known as its parent company."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-01e8dd2cd7216b43532ed7037814b54b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 335}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Re-engagement is another term for reinstatement, referring to the process of re-establishing employment with a former employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Re-engagement is the process where employees are offered new employment by their current or another associated company after being dismissed from their previous role."&lt;SEP&gt;"Re-engagement refers to the act of re-employing an individual, which could lead to certain sums being awarded as entitlements under specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1c30b39b26dc22df210f2ea63b93552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01e8dd2cd7216b43532ed7037814b54b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 337}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSIDIARY (附屬公司)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsidiary means a company that is controlled by another company, as defined in the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsidiary means an organization that is controlled or owned by another company, specifically as defined under the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622) for legal purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2351949864b29078618f803ef4d2c6cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 336}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1026}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASSOCIATED COMPANIES (相聯公司)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Associated companies are organizations where one is a subsidiary of the other, or both share common ownership through a third party company, as per the definition in the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 336}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1025}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT (僱傭合約)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT, TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Contract refers to the agreement between an employer and employee outlining terms and conditions of work, which can be subject to various terminations or renewals as described in legal contexts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTUAL TERMINATION (合同终止)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contractual Termination is a formal end to a contract due to specific actions by the employer or events affecting the employment, which can be legally defined and enforced."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL RULES (法律規則)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal Rules refer to regulations and laws that govern business operations, including employment contracts and terminations as described in legal contexts within company relationships."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION OF CONTRACT (合同終止)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Termination of Contract is the formal end of a contractual agreement due to specific conditions or events affecting the relationship between parties involved, particularly relevant in employment law and business operations as described here."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT RELATIONSHIP (僱傭關係)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Relationship refers to the dynamic interaction between an employer and employee, which can be influenced by various legal and operational factors affecting contract terms and conditions of work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIRE (聘用)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hire refers to the act of bringing someone into an organization's workforce, which can be subject to various conditions affecting contract terms or employment relationships as described here."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENEWAL OF CONTRACT (續約)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Renewal of Contract is a process where existing contractual agreements are extended for another term, often involving the same parties but with potential changes in conditions and obligations as described within employment law contexts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT RENEWAL (僱傭合約續訂)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Contract Renewal is the process of extending an existing contractual agreement between employer and employee for another term, often involving review and potential changes in terms or conditions as described within legal contexts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 26}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTINUITY (僱傭關係連續性)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Continuity refers to the uninterrupted nature of an employment relationship over time, which can be affected by various factors including contract renewals and terminations as described in legal contexts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSIDIARY COMPANY (附屬公司)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsidiary Company is a business entity that is controlled or owned by another larger organization, often referred to within the context of corporate structures and employment relationships as defined under relevant laws and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARENT COMPANY (母公司)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Parent Company refers to an organization that controls or owns one or more subsidiary companies, playing a central role in determining associated business operations and employment dynamics as described within legal contexts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 336}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1026}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRD PARTY OWNERSHIP (第三方擁有權)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Third Party Ownership is the situation where multiple organizations share common control through a third-party entity, influencing their relationships and interactions particularly relevant in corporate structures and employment law as detailed here."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTUAL AGREEMENT (合同協議)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Contractual Agreement is an agreement between parties involved in a construction project that outlines terms, including payment obligations, and other conditions related to the work being performed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contractual Agreement is a formal document outlining terms and conditions of an employment relationship or other business operations, which can be subject to various changes or terminations as detailed in relevant laws and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 26}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL REGULATION (法律規範)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal Regulation encompasses all laws, statutes, and regulations governing legal relationships, dispute resolutions, and their enforcement within a jurisdiction or internationally."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal Regulation is a set of laws or guidelines governing business operations, particularly relevant to employment contracts and terminations within corporate structures as detailed here."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efd35e44f40ed90831a05d2c28acb9a5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 26}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT RELATIONSHIP DYNAMICS (僱傭關係動態)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Relationship Dynamics refers to the evolving nature of an employment relationship over time, which can be influenced by various factors including contract renewals and terminations within corporate structures as described in legal contexts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 336}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1025}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL DEFINITION (法律定義)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal Definition refers to specific terms or concepts outlined by laws and regulations that govern business operations, including employment contracts and terminations as described within legal contexts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION BY THE EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Termination by the Employer refers to the act where an organization ends its contractual relationship with an employee based on specific conditions outlined in legal sections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a783557f86fea333101af802aa41e0a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISMISSAL BY REASON OF REDUNDANCY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dismissal by Reason of Redundancy is a situation where an employee's contract is not renewed and they are considered dismissed due to the business needs or restructuring as per legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a783557f86fea333101af802aa41e0a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 581}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1140}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 31B(2)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 31B(2)(a) refers to the employer ceasing or intending to cease carrying on the business, which can be construed as including a reference to any person who has power to dispose of the business in consequence of an act or event."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d33baa15beb160832b6e2302162f04d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 170}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 705}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEATH OF EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Death of Employer refers to the event where an employee's employer passes away, triggering specific legal provisions under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The death of an employer is a significant event that can affect the employment contract, potentially leading to its termination under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The death of the employer is mentioned in section 31M and its effect is described by Part I of the Third Schedule, which applies specifically to this situation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The event refers to the death of an employer which impacts legal rights and obligations under employment protection laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d33baa15beb160832b6e2302162f04d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96ecd392e516343d8ffd40e3611e0e8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c826449cd8715ca847fb4ea3433d8bf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbef4b639390d1d66289078a98204ee1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 170}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 705}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIM FOR REDUNDANCY PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Claiming for redundancy payment refers to a situation where an employee has not been re-engaged and their contract was not renewed due to circumstances described by sections 31D(2) and 31B(2), unless certain conditions are met, such as the agreement on or prior notification of the claim."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d33baa15beb160832b6e2302162f04d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 535}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REDUNDANCY PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Redundancy payment is a financial compensation provided under certain conditions as described in section 31N when an employee's contract is not renewed and they are not re-engaged due to redundancy circumstances, unless specific conditions such as prior agreement or notification have been met."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d33baa15beb160832b6e2302162f04d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 373}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1073}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTRAR OF THE MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Registrar of the Minor Employment Claims Adjudication Board is an organization responsible for handling claims under Part 4 of the Minor Employment Claims Adjudication Board Ordinance (Cap. 453)."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is an organizational role within the government responsible for managing minor employment claim adjudications according to procedures outlined by Cap. 453, Ordinance on Minor Employment Claims Adjudication Board."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-11d596f17d04a1402f9a7eda05284076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9277263fe4be5c215993320cc63c410</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 339}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD ORDINANCE (CAP. 453)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION, LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This ordinance establishes procedures for minor employment claims adjudication, including filing and processing of severance payment claims by employees to the Minor Employment Claims Adjudication Board."&lt;SEP&gt;"This ordinance establishes the Minor Employment Claims Adjudication Board to handle disputes related to minor employees in Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"This ordinance provides rules and procedures for handling minor employment claims through the Minor Employment Claims Adjudication Board."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-11d596f17d04a1402f9a7eda05284076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9277263fe4be5c215993320cc63c410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06d23d2b54047f6e0d92f6798bcab7c8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 339}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (CAP. 25)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Labour Tribunal Ordinance is a legal document that outlines procedures for resolving disputes between employers and employees, including conciliation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Tribunal Ordinance is a legal framework for resolving disputes between employers and employees in Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Tribunal Ordinance is a piece of legislation that includes provisions for resolving disputes and claims related to employment rights in Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Tribunal Ordinance outlines the framework for labor disputes to be adjudicated by the Labour Tribunal."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Tribunal Ordinance sets out rules and processes related to labour disputes in Hong Kong, providing a framework for filing claims with the Labour Tribunal regarding severance payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Tribunal is an organization established under the Labour Tribunal Ordinance (Cap. 25</data>
