<node id="&quot;ISSUE OF THE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Issue of the employee includes children, grandchildren, etc., who can inherit rights to a long service payment in specific circumstances where no spouse is present."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 32}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARENT OF THE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The parent of an employee refers to the parents or guardians of the employee who may be entitled to receive a long service payment if there are no surviving spouse or issue."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 32}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERSONAL REPRESENTATIVE OF THE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Personal representative is a term for someone appointed by law, such as an executor or administrator, who can claim rights on behalf of the deceased employee when no other eligible person exists."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 32}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RELEVANT EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Relevant employer is the organization where an employee was employed at the time of death, responsible for processing applications for long service payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPLICATION IN THE FORM SPECIFIED BY THE COMMISSIONER UNDER SECTION 49&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The application process involves submitting an official document as required by the Commissioner, which must be completed within a specific timeframe to claim long service payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;30 DAYS BEGINNING ON THE DAY NEXT FOLLOWING THE DATE OF DEATH OF THE EMPLOYEE OR WITHIN SUCH EXTENDED PERIOD AS THE COMMISSIONER MAY ALLOW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to the deadline for submitting an application, which is 30 days from the date of death, with possible extensions granted by the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MINOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Minor refers to a legal status where individuals under a certain age are considered not fully capable and may require guardianship or representation in various matters including long service payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GUARDIAN OF THAT PERSON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Guardian is an individual appointed by law, such as a parent or legal guardian, who can make decisions on behalf of minors regarding applications for long service payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT TO WHICH HE IS ENTITLED—WHERE THE PERSON SO ENTITLED IS A SPOUSE, NOT LATER THAN 7 DAYS AFTER THE RECEIPT OF THE APPLICATION; OR WHERE THE PERSON SO ENTITLED IS AN ISSUE OR PARENT, WITHIN SUCH TIME AS MAY BE AGREED UPON BY THE EMPLOYER AND THE APPLICANT.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event describes when long service payments are to be made—within 7 days for spouses, with a flexible timeline for other eligible individuals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 32}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1988年第52號第6條增補&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The location refers to the specific legal amendment or section in Hong Kong's labor laws that outlines these provisions regarding long service payments and employee benefits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMENDED 105 OF 1991 S. 3; 74 OF 1997 S. 11&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These events refer to specific amendments made in the laws, indicating changes or updates to the provisions regarding long service payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPEALED 74 OF 1997 S. 11&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to a section that was repealed from the law, no longer applicable in this context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE DIES AND HE HAD BEEN AT THE TIME OF HIS DEATH EMPLOYED UNDER A CONTINUOUS CONTRACT FOR NOT LESS THAN 5 YEARS OF SERVICE ON THE DATE OF HIS DEATH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event describes the condition where an employee must have worked continuously for five or more years to be eligible for long service payments upon their death."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 164}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 680}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT CALCULATED IN ACCORDANCE WITH SECTION 31V(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The technology here refers to a specific method of calculating the amount of long service payment based on predefined rules or formulas outlined in another part of the law."&lt;SEP&gt;"The technology here refers to the specific method of calculating long service payments based on predefined rules or formulas outlined elsewhere in the law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMISSIONER MAY EXTEND THE TIME FOR SERVING AN APPLICATION UNDER SUBSECTION (2) ALTHOUGH THE APPLICATION FOR EXTENSION IS NOT MADE UNTIL AFTER THE EXPIRATION OF THE PERIOD OF 30 DAYS AFTER THE DATE OF DEATH OF AN EMPLOYEE.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event describes a provision allowing extensions to be granted by the Commissioner, even if the request comes late."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WHERE THE PERSON SO ENTITLED IS A SPOUSE, NOT LATER THAN 7 DAYS AFTER THE RECEIPT OF THE APPLICATION; OR WHERE THE PERSON SO ENTITLED IS AN ISSUE OR PARENT, WITHIN SUCH TIME AS MAY BE AGREED UPON BY THE EMPLOYER AND THE APPLICANT.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event describes the timeline for payment when different eligible recipients are involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WHERE A MINOR'S APPLICATION UNDER SUBSECTION (2) SHALL BE MADE BY THE GUARDIAN OF THAT PERSON.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The social science concept here is guardianship, which involves legal representation and decision-making on behalf of minors in various contexts including financial matters like long service payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GUARDIAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Guardian refers to an individual responsible for making applications on behalf of a minor, as mentioned in the context of subsection (2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e9d410c88421aeae56a47aedb79d008e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRIVATE HOUSEHOLD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A private household is described as an environment where domestic servants are employed and treated like employees in a business context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Private household refers to a domestic setting where an employee might work as a domestic servant and could be impacted by legal provisions after the owner's death."&lt;SEP&gt;"Private household refers to a residential setting where employees work and live in connection with the maintenance of that residence by its owner-employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a79efc9c7d5b3c5051c209e7d8238e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9d410c88421aeae56a47aedb79d008e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae8f763a371efa17099b990f69f8b4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 587}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAMILY SERVANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Family servant refers to an individual employed in a private household setting, similar to domestic servants but with specific legal application details provided by section 31Z of the relevant legislation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e9d410c88421aeae56a47aedb79d008e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOUSEHOLD BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Household business is a concept where a private residence operates as if it were a commercial entity for employment purposes, maintaining and managing its employees according to employer responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e9d410c88421aeae56a47aedb79d008e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LONG-TERM SERVICE MONEY ENTITLEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Long-term service money entitlement refers to the right of an employee, specifically a domestic servant, to receive compensation upon termination of employment after a certain period of service."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dae8f763a371efa17099b990f69f8b4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 587}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION NOTICE OR GARDEN LEAVE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Termination notice or garden leave payment is an event where an employer terminates an employee's contract without providing prior notice or paying the equivalent amount as a substitute notice period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dae8f763a371efa17099b990f69f8b4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE BEHAVIOR LEADING TO TERMINATION WITHOUT NOTICE OR GARDEN LEAVE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee behavior that allows for immediate termination without giving notice or substituting with a garden leave payment is considered, indicating specific grounds under which an employee might be dismissed immediately."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dae8f763a371efa17099b990f69f8b4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 587}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LONG-TERM SERVICE BONUS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Long-term service bonus is a financial benefit that employees may be entitled to if they are unfairly dismissed under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Long-term service bonus refers to a financial benefit provided to employees based on their years of service, with certain deductions as per specified conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1bb14977455cfee69d96555a42dffb40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3950c75e15e51a9aa6482b52fbd5f985</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 124}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 51 OF 2000 S. 5&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 51 of 2000 s. 5 is the amendment date and section number indicating changes to a legal provision."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e3a3f0edfa08a61dbd46b52c9f94d56a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 306}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 31T(1)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 31T(1)(b) is a legal provision under which an employee may be dismissed by their employer, triggering considerations for renewal or re-engagement offers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 31T(1)(b) is a specific clause under which employees may be dismissed, and it's used as a basis for determining long service payments in certain circumstances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 31T(1)(b) specifies another condition for considering an employee's contract as terminated due to the expiration of a fixed-term employment agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e3a3f0edfa08a61dbd46b52c9f94d56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c8faaa89696bb97daf5c16e2354ab6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff6ba65a2b6882ca144f894790a0cc18</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 535}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENEWAL OR RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Renewal or re-engagement of a contract involves extending or starting a new employment agreement after the death of the original employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Renewal or re-engagement refers to an offer made by the employer to continue employment with different terms and conditions, which could affect the employee's entitlement to a long service payment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e17f3710da650d1e14713613a2dff129&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff6ba65a2b6882ca144f894790a0cc18</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 690}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1167}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT FOR A FIXED TERM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contract for a fixed term refers to the specific type of employment agreement that has a defined end date and can lead to conditions for renewal or termination based on certain criteria."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ff6ba65a2b6882ca144f894790a0cc18</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 535}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 31R(1)(A)(II)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 31R(1)(a)(ii) is a legal provision that allows an employee to terminate their contract under certain conditions, which will be regarded as termination by the employee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6c8faaa89696bb97daf5c16e2354ab6f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 534}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;4 OF 2022 S. 7&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Amended a section in the law, indicating changes or updates to existing regulations related to employment contracts and terminations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6c8faaa89696bb97daf5c16e2354ab6f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 31T(1)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 31T(1)(a) outlines conditions under which an employee can be considered terminated by their employer without notice or compensation, based on the non-compliance with contract termination clauses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6c8faaa89696bb97daf5c16e2354ab6f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 536}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 31T(2)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 31T(2)(a) states that an employee cannot be considered terminated if their contract is renewed or they are rehired under similar terms immediately after the original contract's end date, thus maintaining continuity of employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6c8faaa89696bb97daf5c16e2354ab6f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 31T(2)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 31T(2)(b) further clarifies that a renewal or rehire occurring shortly after the termination of an existing agreement does not constitute a new termination event, preserving the original employment status."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6c8faaa89696bb97daf5c16e2354ab6f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 536}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REST DAY OR HOLIDAY&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to specific times when employment contracts may end due to legal provisions related to rest days and holidays without immediate rehire implications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6c8faaa89696bb97daf5c16e2354ab6f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE DISMISSAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee dismissal refers to an event where an employer terminates an employee's employment, potentially leading to reinstatement or re-engagement orders."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employee dismissal refers to the termination of an employee's contract by their employer, which can occur under specific conditions outlined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a2200d76e6cc5397e7868136950dfb19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 833}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT RENEWAL OR RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contract renewal or re-engagement refers to situations where an employee's contract is extended or they are hired again under new terms, which can prevent dismissal according to certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 9 OF 1992 S. 62&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a legal provision that outlines conditions under which an employer can terminate an employee's contract without notice or payment in lieu, but it is not directly related to any specific entity type mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 10 OF 1992 S. 62&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to another legal provision that outlines circumstances under which an employee can terminate their contract without notice or payment in lieu due to the employer's conduct, but it is not directly related to any specific entity type mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 31R AND 31RA OF 1988 S. 52&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These sections are legal provisions that provide exceptions for certain types of employees as described, but they do not directly relate to any specific entity type mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE TERMINATION WITHOUT NOTICE OR PAYMENT IN LIEU&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This describes a situation where an employee can terminate their contract without needing notice or compensation due to the employer's actions, according to Section 10 of 1992 s. 62."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RE-ENGAGEMENT UNDER NEW CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Re-engagement under a new contract is an event where an employee is hired again by the same employer but with different terms as described in the text, which can prevent dismissal according to certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 536}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 31T OF 1988 S. 52&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This section outlines specific circumstances under which an employee is considered dismissed by their employer and provides exceptions for contract renewals or re-engagements, but it does not directly relate to any specific entity type mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 536}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 31U OF 1988 S. 52&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This section specifies that certain types of employees are exempt from the provisions outlined in Sections 31R and 31RA, but it does not directly relate to any specific entity type mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION OF EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Termination of Employment Contract refers to the end of an employer-employee relationship due to various reasons, which can affect entitlements such as sickness allowance payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Termination of employment contract is an event where an employer ends an employee's contract, which can occur on rest days or holidays according to specific conditions outlined in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Termination of employment contract is an event where an employer ends an employee’s contractual relationship, potentially leading to severance payment obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Termination of employment contract is an event where an employer formally ends a worker's agreement to provide services, often due to changes in the company's structure or ownership."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5d2b28a0cc543e1f646cbc0388c9eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 695}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENEWAL OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Renewal of contract refers to extending an existing employment agreement as described in the text, which can prevent dismissal under certain circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 338}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RE-ENGAGEMENT BY SAME EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Re-engagement by the same employer is a situation where an employee is hired again with the original employer but possibly under new terms, preventing dismissal according to specific conditions outlined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE CONDUCT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee conduct refers to actions by employees, such as terminating their contract without notice or payment in lieu due to employer's misconduct according to Section 10 of 1992 s. 62."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER'S CONDUCT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employer's conduct refers to actions taken by employers that can lead to employee termination under certain conditions as described in the text, particularly related to Sections 31T and 10 of 1992 s. 62."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 536}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL EXCEPTION FOR EMPLOYEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal exceptions for employees refer to specific circumstances where laws provide protections or exemptions from standard dismissal procedures as described in the text, particularly related to Sections 31R and 31RA of 1988 s. 52."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL PROVISION APPLICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Application of legal provisions refers to how specific laws are applied in different scenarios such as contract renewals or re-engagements, which can affect employee dismissal according to the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT EXPIRATION WITHOUT RENEWAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contract expiration without renewal is an event where a fixed-term employment contract ends and is not extended, leading to potential termination of employment under certain conditions as described in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL TERMINOLOGY&quot;">
