<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S ENTITLEMENT TO EMPLOYMENT PROTECTION (32A) - CONDITION B&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Condition b under Section 32A refers to another specific situation for seeking remedies based on actions taken by an employee before dismissal, as outlined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-14c0e0b770ad5a127f415b9e1dc1b2e8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S ENTITLEMENT TO EMPLOYMENT PROTECTION (32A) - CONDITION C&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Condition c under Section 32A describes yet another scenario where employees can seek remedies if dismissed due to certain activities they engaged in prior to their termination, as detailed in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-14c0e0b770ad5a127f415b9e1dc1b2e8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT FOR A PERIOD OF NOT LESS THAN 24 MONTHS ENDING WITH THE RELEVANT DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a condition related to employment duration but does not fit into any other specified category directly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4f1489ce71ef2c2d18cbecd427f12202</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISMISSAL BY THE EMPLOYER BECAUSE THE EMPLOYER INTENDS TO EXTINGUISH OR REDUCE ANY RIGHT, BENEFIT OR PROTECTION CONFERRED OR TO BE CONFERRED UPON THE EMPLOYEE BY THIS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This describes an event where an employee can seek remedies if dismissed for a specific reason related to rights reduction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4f1489ce71ef2c2d18cbecd427f12202</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER, WITHOUT HIS CONSENT AND, IN THE ABSENCE OF AN EXPRESS TERM IN HIS CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT WHICH SO PERMITS, VARIES THE TERMS OF HIS CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT BECAUSE THE EMPLOYER INTENDS TO EXTINGUISH OR REDUCE ANY RIGHT, BENEFIT OR PROTECTION CONFERRED OR TO BE CONFERRED UPON THE EMPLOYEE BY THIS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This describes another event where an employee can seek remedies if their contract is varied without consent for a specific reason related to rights reduction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4f1489ce71ef2c2d18cbecd427f12202</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISMISSED BY THE EMPLOYER OTHER THAN FOR A VALID REASON WITHIN THE MEANING OF SECTION 32K AND IN CONTRAVENTION OF— (I) SECTION 15(1), 21B(2)(B), 33(4B) OR 72B(1); (II) SECTION 6 OF THE FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59); OR (III) SECTION 48 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This describes an event where an employee can seek remedies if dismissed for a reason not covered by valid reasons under section 32K and in contravention of specific sections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4f1489ce71ef2c2d18cbecd427f12202</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VALID REASON IS SHOWN FOR THAT DISMISSAL WITHIN THE MEANING OF SECTION 32K&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a concept where an employer can show a valid reason for dismissing an employee, which would negate the event described under (1)(a)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4f1489ce71ef2c2d18cbecd427f12202</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 32K&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 32K outlines conditions for variations to terms of contracts and valid reasons required for such changes. It also defines what constitutes a 'valid reason' for variation or dismissal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66cccec6ac7d06fb5417245d5fe5f3b9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 108}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 550}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 21B(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 21B(1) refers to rights vested in an employee that cannot be extinguished without valid reasons, as mentioned under subsection (4)(a)(i)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66cccec6ac7d06fb5417245d5fe5f3b9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 72B(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 72B(1) pertains to actions by employees which do not require showing a reason for termination according to the text in subsection (4)(a)(ii). It is part of the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66cccec6ac7d06fb5417245d5fe5f3b9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 6 OF FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This section, part of Cap. 59, is referenced as an example where employees' actions do not require showing a reason for termination according to the text in subsection (4)(a)(iii)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66cccec6ac7d06fb5417245d5fe5f3b9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISMISSAL&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Dismissal refers to the act of terminating an employee's contract without following certain procedures as stipulated in the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (Cap. 59)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Employee is a person who works for another individual or organization under agreed terms, particularly relevant to legal protections against wrongful dismissal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Employer refers to the entity that hires and manages employees according to labor laws and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 6&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Section 6 is a specific clause within the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (Cap. 59) that outlines conditions under which an employee can be dismissed without contravening legal protections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 32A(1)(A)&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Section 32A(1)(a) is a specific clause within the ordinance that defines circumstances in which an employee may be considered wrongfully dismissed, particularly when their right to severance pay or long service bonus is terminated."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 9&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Section 9 of the ordinance outlines conditions for terminating employment contracts without notice or compensation as stipulated by law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 10&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Section 10 of the ordinance provides terms under which an employee may terminate their contract without giving notice, affecting the employer's ability to dismiss them legally."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Employment contract is a legal agreement between an employer and an employee that outlines the conditions of employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Termination refers to the act of ending an employment relationship, which can be subject to specific regulations as outlined in labor laws like the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (Cap. 59)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE PERIOD&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Notice period is a legal term that refers to the time frame during which an employer must provide notice of termination or pay equivalent compensation, as stipulated in labor laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSEQUENT EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT RENEWAL&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Subsequent employment contract renewal involves extending the terms of an existing employment agreement, potentially affecting legal protections against wrongful dismissal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RE-EMPLOYMENT UNDER A NEW CONTRACT&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Re-employment under a new contract refers to hiring an employee again after their previous contract has ended, which can impact legal rights and obligations as defined by labor laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LONG SERVICE BONUS&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Long service bonus is a financial benefit provided to employees for long-term service with the same employer, often regulated under employment law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEVERANCE PAY&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Severance pay is compensation given to an employee upon termination of their contract, as mandated by labor laws like the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (Cap. 59)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WRONGFUL DISMISSAL&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Wrongful dismissal occurs when an employer terminates an employment relationship in contravention of legal protections, as outlined by ordinances such as the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (Cap. 59)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL PROTECTION&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Legal protection refers to the safeguards provided under labor laws that prevent wrongful dismissal and ensure fair treatment of employees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONCILIATION AND ARBITRATION SERVICES&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Conciliation and arbitration services are organizations or bodies responsible for resolving disputes between employers and employees, often mandated by labor laws to provide a mechanism for dispute resolution without litigation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LABOR LAW ENFORCEMENT AGENCY&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Labor law enforcement agencies are governmental entities tasked with enforcing compliance with employment regulations, including the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (Cap. 59)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONCILIATION SERVICE&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Conciliation services refer to processes or mechanisms designed to facilitate dispute resolution between employers and employees through negotiation and mediation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCESS&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Arbitration is a legal procedure where an impartial third party makes a binding decision on a labor dispute, often used as an alternative to litigation for resolving employment-related conflicts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONCILIATION AND ARBITRATION MECHANISM&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Conciliation and arbitration mechanisms are formal processes designed to resolve disputes between employers and employees through negotiation or third-party decision-making, ensuring fair treatment under labor laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LABOR DISPUTE RESOLUTION PROCESS&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Labor dispute resolution processes involve methods for resolving conflicts between employers and employees, often including conciliation, arbitration, and other forms of alternative dispute resolution (ADR)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONCILIATION SERVICE PROVIDER&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Conciliation service providers are entities that offer services to facilitate the resolution of labor disputes through negotiation or mediation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION BODY&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Arbitration bodies are organizations responsible for making binding decisions on labor disputes, often serving as an alternative to court litigation in resolving employment-related conflicts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONCILIATION AND ARBITRATION SERVICE PROVIDER&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Conciliation and arbitration service providers offer a range of dispute resolution services designed to help employers and employees resolve their differences without resorting to legal action."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LABOR LAW COMPLIANCE OFFICER&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Labor law compliance officers are individuals responsible for ensuring that an organization adheres to labor laws, including the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (Cap. 59), by providing guidance on legal requirements and conducting audits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LABOR INSPECTOR&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">)"Labor inspectors are officials responsible for enforcing compliance with labor laws, investigating complaints of violations, and ensuring that employers adhere to regulations protecting employees' rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 32A(1)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 32A(1)(a) is part of a legal provision that deals with conditions under which an employee's dismissal does not constitute termination for the purposes of certain severance payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f107e63d68c2fdb52424f9892f32be51</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 42}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;32C&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 32C refers to another clause within the same legal document that deals with general exemptions from obtaining remedies in certain circumstances. "</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-44e57b1615ed5c8b1f49eb6a6ecd4472</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;續訂或新訂合約(視屬何情況而定)的條文&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The terms of the renewed or new contract (as applicable), which are likely detailed conditions and clauses within an employment agreement, play a crucial role in determining rights and obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"續訂或新訂合約(視屬何情況而定)的條文指的是在特定情况下，劳动合同条款可能发生变化并影响员工的权利和义务。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-44e57b1615ed5c8b1f49eb6a6ecd4472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad6d0a2eed4fbaf59a6253fe84df6ac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 71}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 460}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;合理地拒絕該項要約&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Reasonable refusal of an offer refers to actions taken by employees that are considered fair or justified under the circumstances. "</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-44e57b1615ed5c8b1f49eb6a6ecd4472</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 71}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 460}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENEWAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Renewal refers to extending the existing contract of employment with new terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b8714cccfc72c7380caa9903fb713cd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 581}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1140}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RE-ENGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Re-engage means offering a new contract for an employee who was previously employed but is now being considered again under different conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b8714cccfc72c7380caa9903fb713cd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REMEDIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Remedies refer to legal or other forms of compensation that may be available if the terms of employment are not met as per certain provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b8714cccfc72c7380caa9903fb713cd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 582}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RIGHT TO REMEDIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Right to remedies is a concept in labor law which outlines the conditions under which an employee can seek legal recourse for breaches of contract or unfair treatment by the employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b8714cccfc72c7380caa9903fb713cd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;32C. GENERAL EXCLUSIONS FROM RIGHT TO REMEDIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This section describes general exceptions where employees do not have a right to remedies as per specific provisions in labor law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b8714cccfc72c7380caa9903fb713cd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 582}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;32A(1)(C)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a specific circumstance under section 32A where subsections (1) to (3) do not apply for employee dismissal cases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9ddecf99bc0bca06387d96224afeaf4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 171}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 707}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREDECESSOR OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Predecessor owner refers to a person who was previously responsible for a certain business before its ownership changed.""</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9ddecf99bc0bca06387d96224afeaf4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 171}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 706}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;32B(3)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 32B(3) refers to another specific clause in the text related to employment contract renewals or re-employment following business ownership changes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9ddecf99bc0bca06387d96224afeaf4c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;32C(1)">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a legal provision that outlines conditions under which an employee's offer for renewed employment can be refused, as mentioned in part of section 32C."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9ddecf99bc0bca06387d96224afeaf4c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;32C(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 32C(2) refers to another specific clause related to the refusal of a new employment contract or re-employment offer by an employee after business ownership changes, as mentioned in part of section 32C."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9ddecf99bc0bca06387d96224afeaf4c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL TERMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal terms such as 'termination,' 'notice period,' and 'payment in lieu' are used to describe the conditions under which employment relationships can be altered, reflecting mathematical logic applied to legal scenarios."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9ddecf99bc0bca06387d96224afeaf4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 171}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 707}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RONGXIN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rongxin is a company involved in business ownership changes and employment contracts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1cb0098fa2f01839bce9b10d85c36181</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 171}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 706}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FORMER OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Former Owner refers to the previous owner of the business before the change in ownership."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1cb0098fa2f01839bce9b10d85c36181</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 171}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 706}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENEWAL OR RE-ENGAGEMENT BY THE PREVIOUS OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Renewal or re-engagement by the previous owner is an event where the original employer continues the employee's contract after ownership changes, substituting themselves for the new owner in the agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 25}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 328}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OFFER TO RENEW OR RE-ENGAGE UNDER A NEW CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Offer to renew or re-engage under a new contract of employment is an event where the new owner proposes continuing the employee's work relationship, substituting themselves for the previous owner in the agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 171}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 709}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REFUSAL OF OFFER BY THE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refusal of offer by the employee refers to the social and psychological aspect of a worker declining a proposed change or continuation of their employment contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 171}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 709}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 32B(3)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 32B(3) is part of a legal framework that outlines specific conditions under which an employee's contract can be renewed after business ownership changes, without substituting the new owner for the previous one."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 25}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 328}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 32C(1) OR (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 32C(1) or (2) is an event that applies when certain conditions related to employee termination are met, as described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 32C(1) or (2) is part of a legal framework that outlines specific conditions under which an employee's refusal to accept changes in their contract can be handled after business ownership changes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1896582b740b6a3f00c9bfa592f3ab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 171}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 709}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS OWNERSHIP TRANSFERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Business ownership transfers refer to changes in the control or possession of a business entity from one party to another, which can significantly impact employment contracts and relationships within the organization."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 170}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 703}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT RENEWAL/RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment contract renewal/re-engagement refers to legal processes where an employee's existing agreement with their employer is extended or re-established after a change in business ownership."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employment Contract Renewal/Re-engagement refers to situations where an employee's contract is renewed or they are re-employed by a personal representative of the deceased employer within 4 weeks post-death, potentially avoiding dismissal status."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fbef4b639390d1d66289078a98204ee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 170}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 703}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSTITUTION OF NEW OWNER FOR PREVIOUS OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Substitution of new owner for previous owner refers to scenarios where legal documents are updated to reflect a change in business control, potentially affecting employee relationships and contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 25}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 328}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LIKE OFFER MADE BY THE PREVIOUS OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Like offer made by the previous owner is an event that mirrors conditions from before ownership changes, used as a reference point for handling similar situations after such transfers have occurred."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 171}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 709}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOUBLE AGREEMENT ON CONTRACT RENEWAL/RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Double agreement on contract renewal/re-engagement refers to instances where both the previous and new owners agree to continue an employee's work relationship, maintaining continuity despite changes in business control."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS RESTRUCTURING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Business restructuring refers to the process of changing the structure and control of an organization, which can include transferring business ownership and impacting existing employment arrangements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL PRINCIPLES FOR CONTRACT MANAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal principles for contract management are guidelines that ensure fair treatment in renewing or re-engaging employees after significant organizational changes like business ownership transfers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 170}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 703}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT RELATIONSHIP CONTINUITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment relationship continuity refers to the ongoing nature of an employee's work arrangement, which must be maintained despite changes in business control and ownership."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE RIGHTS PROTECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee rights protection is a principle that ensures employees are not unfairly impacted by organizational changes such as business ownership transfers, safeguarding their employment conditions and benefits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL COMPLIANCE DURING CONTRACT RENEWAL/RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal compliance during contract renewal/re-engagement refers to the adherence to legal standards when updating or re-establishing employee contracts after significant organizational changes like business ownership transfers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT LAW PRINCIPLES FOR CONTINUITY OF EMPLOYMENT RELATIONSHIPS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment law principles for continuity of employment relationships are guidelines that ensure ongoing stability in an employer-employee relationship, even when there is a change in the controlling entity or ownership structure."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS CONTROL CHANGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Business control changes refer to shifts in who has ultimate authority over a business, which can significantly impact how employment contracts are managed and renewed after such transfers have occurred."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT MANAGEMENT DURING ORGANIZATIONAL CHANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment contract management during organizational change refers to the process of handling employee agreements when there is a significant shift in an organization's structure or control, including changes in business ownership and related legal implications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORK FOR EMPLOYMENT CONTRACTS AFTER BUSINESS TRANSFERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal framework for employment contracts after business transfers provides structured guidelines on how to manage and renew existing employee agreements when there is a change in the controlling entity of an organization."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 170}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 703}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 32C(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 32C(1) is a legal provision that deals with the refusal of an offer by an employee after a change in ownership, and its effect on previous conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8bab69b3c78835240d5782d563ec35c1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 32C(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 32C(2) is another part of Section 32C dealing with similar provisions as (1), but under different circumstances or for a different case."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8bab69b3c78835240d5782d563ec35c1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OFFER BY THE NEW OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An offer made by the new owner in relation to an employee's contract, which may involve renewing or creating a new contract of employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8bab69b3c78835240d5782d563ec35c1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REFUSAL OF THE OFFER BY THE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The act of an employee refusing an offer from the new owner regarding their contract of employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8bab69b3c78835240d5782d563ec35c1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 32E(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 32E(1) is a provision that defines the term 'company' as including its associated or affiliated companies, impacting how certain clauses apply when dealing with business transfers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8bab69b3c78835240d5782d563ec35c1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RELATED COMPANY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Any company that is associated or affiliated with the main company, as defined by Section 32E(1), which can be considered for certain provisions related to business transfers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8bab69b3c78835240d5782d563ec35c1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 334}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1021}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE EMPLOYER (COMPANY)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The employer referred to here is an organization that can be a company or its associated companies according to the provisions in sections 32B, 32C, and 32D of relevant ordinances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2c28e990fb442886ba69eb65de9d2282</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 335}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREVIOUS OWNER (COMPANY)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Previous owner refers to a former entity owning shares or controlling rights over another company which is now owned by a new entity as per section 32E(2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2c28e990fb442886ba69eb65de9d2282</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 335}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEW OWNER (COMPANY)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"New owner refers to the current entity that has acquired ownership or control of a previously owned company, affecting the interpretation and application of sections 32B, 32C, and 32D as per section 32E(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2c28e990fb442886ba69eb65de9d2282</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 335}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE COMPANIES ORDINANCE (CAP. 622)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622) is a Hong Kong law that defines the terms 'company' and 'subsidiary', which are crucial for understanding sections 32B, 32C, and 32D as per section 32E(4)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2c28e990fb442886ba69eb65de9d2282</data>
