  <data key="d0">"LEGAL DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Eighth Schedule is a legal reference that defines the effect of an employer's or employee's death in certain parts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-adb3767092cbae0c3a6518107e6865b5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART I OF THE EIGHTH SCHEDULE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SECTION OF LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part I of the Eighth Schedule refers to specific provisions related to the death of an employer, as mentioned in relation to Part II for employees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-adb3767092cbae0c3a6518107e6865b5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART II OF THE EIGHTH SCHEDULE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SECTION OF LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part II of the Eighth Schedule pertains to the death of an employee and its legal implications, contrasting with Part I which covers employers' deaths."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-adb3767092cbae0c3a6518107e6865b5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPEALED 51 OF 2000 S. 4&quot;">
