</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (4BAB)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (4BAB) is an event in the legal text that modifies the application of another subsection, specifically excluding civil proceedings from its scope."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ec139f7ebf5b8697a790c183eb4ae20d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (4BB)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (4BB) defines a specific offense and penalty for contravening certain employment termination rules related to sickness days."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ec139f7ebf5b8697a790c183eb4ae20d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (4C)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This subsection outlines the employer's obligation to pay sickness allowance even after terminating an employee’s contract due to illness, ensuring continuous benefits despite the termination of employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ec139f7ebf5b8697a790c183eb4ae20d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AN EMPLOYER SHALL NOT BE LIABLE TO PAY SICKNESS ALLOWANCE TO AN EMPLOYEE IN RESPECT OF ANY SICKNESS DAY—&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This entity refers to a legal or organizational context where employers have specific conditions under which they are exempt from paying sickness allowances, based on medical certification and the opinion of healthcare professionals."</data>
