  <data key="d1">"This indicates another legal revision made in 2022, further updating regulations related to employment and leave policies. It reflects ongoing efforts to improve labor rights and protections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de9d7bf328eb68da98c29ac72b529085</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 476}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1131}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEES'&lt; LEAVE TYPES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leave types mentioned include maternity leave, paternity leave, rest days, sick leave, holidays, and annual leave. These are events that affect the calculation of wages for employees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd2478b6eecc304c9feadaf2ffde1109</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Employment Compensation Ordinance (Cap 282) is a product or regulation providing compensation to employees who temporarily lose work capacity, affecting wage calculations during such periods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd2478b6eecc304c9feadaf2ffde1109</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 99}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 518}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DAILY AVERAGE EARNINGS CALCULATION METHODOLOGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the method of calculating daily average earnings for an employee based on recent wages. It can be considered a technological process in labor law and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd2478b6eecc304c9feadaf2ffde1109</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 99}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 518}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAVE AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leave Agreement refers to an arrangement between employer and employee where leave can be taken with prior approval from the employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;12 MONTHS PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TIME FRAME"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The 12-month period is used as a reference for calculating sickness allowance, starting from the day before the employee's first sick leave or the actual sick leave date."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SICKNESS DAY CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The process for calculating the daily rate of sickness allowance involves taking four-fifths of an employee's average wages over a 12-month period before their sick leave date or first sick leave, whichever is applicable."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 138}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 604}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPENSATION UNDER SECTION 10&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Compensation Under Section 10 is a provision in the Employees' Compensation Ordinance (Cap. 282) that outlines conditions and amounts for workers’ compensation, including temporary incapacity benefits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE DEDUCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sickness Allowance Deduction involves subtracting any payments made by an employer to the employee during their sick leave from the total sickness allowance amount due, ensuring accurate and fair benefit distribution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2014 AMENDMENT S. 10&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Amendment of Section 10 in 2014 updated provisions related to wages and leaves, impacting how sick leave benefits are calculated for employees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2007 AMENDMENT S. 10&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Amendment of Section 10 in 2007 further refined the rules around sick leave and its associated allowances, enhancing employee protections and benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Amendment of Section 10 in 2007 revised the calculation method for sickness allowance based on a 12-month average wage, aligning with updated labor laws and practices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1984 AMENDMENT S. 15&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Amendment of Section 15 in 1984 added provisions related to sickness allowance for terminated employees, ensuring continuity in benefit provision even after employment ends."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;35. RATE OF SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REGULATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rate of Sickness Allowance is a specific regulation that defines how sickness allowance should be calculated for employees based on their average wages over the 12 months preceding their sick leave period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 100}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 522}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SICK LEAVE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sick Leave Payment refers to monetary benefits provided by employers during an employee's absence due to illness, subject to specific conditions and calculations as outlined in labor laws and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;21 OF 2014 S. 10&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Amendment of Section 10 in 2014 updated the criteria for including various types of leave (maternity, paternity, rest days) when calculating sickness allowance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;7 OF 2007 S. 10&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Amendment of Section 10 in 2007 further detailed the calculation method for sick leaves and their associated allowances, ensuring fair distribution based on average wages over a specified period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;35(4) PAYMENT FROM EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Payment From Employer refers to any compensation or benefits provided by an employer during an employee's absence, which may affect the final amount of sickness allowance due after considering such payments in calculations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
