  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Record Keeping Requirement is an organizational process mandated by law for employers to maintain detailed records about their employees' sickness days and allowances as part of compliance with labor regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f5c7df56b94c0c429230f0546be40142</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (1A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (1A) specifies the format in which accumulated paid sick leave should be recorded, integrating legal and social science principles for employee welfare management."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f5c7df56b94c0c429230f0546be40142</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;36 DAYS LIMITATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The 36 days limitation is a numerical constraint within the record-keeping system that ensures the total accumulation of paid sickness days does not exceed this threshold at any given time, reflecting mathematical and regulatory considerations in employee benefits management."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f5c7df56b94c0c429230f0546be40142</data>
