<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT TERMINATION RECORD ACCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event allows employees to access their records even after termination of employment for a period of 2 months, highlighting the importance of maintaining accurate and accessible documentation post-termination as per labor laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f5c7df56b94c0c429230f0546be40142</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISCREPANCY IN RECORDS HANDLING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"In case employers fail to maintain proper records or if such records are lost or destroyed, employees retain their rights under Section 33 for paid sick leave even after receiving sickness allowances, emphasizing the social science and legal aspects of employee rights protection."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f5c7df56b94c0c429230f0546be40142</data>
</node>
