</node>
<node id="&quot;APPROPRIATE DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The appropriate day is defined as either the first day of a shutdown related to annual leave entitlement, or the end of the last leave year for an employee without such entitlement. It can also be the commencement date of employment if there are no leave years."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-547fc5c5737727c52b8d88a47acddc1e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 502}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINAL EMPLOYMENT PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The final employment period is defined as starting from the appropriate day and ending on the termination of employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-547fc5c5737727c52b8d88a47acddc1e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 502}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAVE YEAR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A leave year, unless context otherwise requires, means any 12-month period commencing either at the first day of a shutdown related to annual leave entitlement or the commencement date of employment. It can also start from an anniversary of such days."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leave Year refers to a specific period during which an employee's entitlement to annual leave is calculated, typically 12 months."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leave Year refers to the calendar year in which an employee's entitlement to annual leave accrues based on their continuous contract duration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leave year is a period used to calculate entitlements for annual leave, typically 12 months, but not necessarily so according to this text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leave year refers to a period during which an employee's eligibility for annual leave is calculated based on continuous service duration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leave year refers to the 12-month period chosen or determined by an employer for calculating annual leave entitlements of their employees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e9e62e9c51234e7e58e65ee8d9b2c47e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f562ef17ff451340f1810793e3d7491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-547fc5c5737727c52b8d88a47acddc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1ba134cba7bc0ad2b2ef34e757e78d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 502}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTIONAL LEAVE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Notional leave pay is an amount calculated as if the employee's contract of employment had terminated on a specific day, used to determine annual leave pay."&lt;SEP&gt;"Notional leave pay refers to a hypothetical calculation of leave pay, though no specific definition is provided in this text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-547fc5c5737727c52b8d88a47acddc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed2004c9e59e7e54ef6756f3c59d039a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 129}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 580}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 41C&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 41C refers to a section in legislation that provides methods for calculating amounts related to employment contracts and leave payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed2004c9e59e7e54ef6756f3c59d039a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 129}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 580}]</data>
</node>
