  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"1990 Year refers to the year when this regulation was first implemented, marking the start date for certain provisions and definitions within the context of employment laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2014 AMENDMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"2014 Amendment is a specific event where changes were made to the regulations regarding annual leave, specifically concerning the number of years an employee must be in continuous contract before qualifying for certain benefits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Period refers to the duration of time during which an individual is employed under a continuous contract, impacting their eligibility and entitlements such as annual leave."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 97}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 505}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT REGULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Regulation refers to the set of rules and policies governing employment terms including benefits like annual leave, which are subject to change over time as seen with amendments in 2014."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINUOUS SERVICE REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Continuous Service Requirement is a condition that must be met for an employee to qualify for certain benefits such as annual leave, defined here as at least one year of continuous employment without interruption."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAID TIME OFF (PTO)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Paid Time Off is a broader category of paid leaves that includes various types such as annual leave, sick leave, personal days, etc., which are collectively managed by employers to ensure employees have sufficient time off for rest and other needs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATION AMENDMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Regulation Amendment refers to changes made to existing laws or regulations governing employment practices, specifically here concerning updates to how annual leave is calculated based on years of continuous service."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT TERM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Term refers to the duration and conditions under which an employee works for a company, impacting their eligibility for various benefits including annual leave."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee Benefit is any advantage or service provided by employers to employees as part of their compensation package beyond just salary, such as paid leaves like annual leave."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAVE ENTITLEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leave Entitlement refers to the right an employee has to take time off work for various reasons including personal or family needs, which is regulated by employment laws and company policies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leave entitlement denotes the amount of annual leave that an employee is entitled to according to company policies and legal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7dbc6cb0d2646456eacee5097d668ff</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 501}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT PRACTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Practice encompasses all aspects of how employers manage their workforce, including provisions on leave entitlements like annual leave as part of broader human resource management strategies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Annual Leave Calculation refers to the method by which paid time off is determined for employees based on factors such as years of continuous service and other conditions outlined in employment regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT REGULATION AMENDMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Regulation Amendment is a specific event where changes are made to existing laws or policies governing employee benefits, here specifically affecting how annual leave is calculated for different periods of continuous service."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 154}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee Rights refer to the legal protections and entitlements afforded to workers under employment law, including provisions on paid leaves like annual leave which are subject to change through regulatory amendments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT LAW AMENDMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Law Amendment is a formal process where existing laws or regulations governing employee rights and benefits such as annual leave undergo changes to reflect new policies or address emerging issues in the workplace."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINUOUS SERVICE REQUIREMENT FOR ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Continuous Service Requirement for Annual Leave refers to the specific period of uninterrupted employment an employee must have before they are eligible to receive paid time off such as annual leave, which is a key factor in determining their benefits under employment regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE ENTITLEMENT CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Annual Leave Entitlement Calculation involves the process by which employers determine how many days of annual leave an employee can accrue based on factors like years of continuous service and other conditions outlined in company policies or employment laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT TERM FOR ANNUAL LEAVE ELIGIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Term for Annual Leave Eligibility refers to the duration of time during which an employee must be employed under a continuous contract before they become eligible for certain benefits such as annual leave, which is defined here in terms of years and months."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TABLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Table mentioned here likely contains specific details about the calculation of annual leave entitlements, such as periods and corresponding days off."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e1ba134cba7bc0ad2b2ef34e757e78d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 501}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;14 DAYS'">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"14 days' notice refers to the minimum required written notice an employer must give before granting a period of annual leave, unless otherwise agreed by both parties."</data>
