</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 41F&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL PROVISION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 41F pertains to notice requirements for business closures, which can impact the granting and taking of annual leave according to specific legal guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 41F refers to a specific legal section that governs the conditions under which a business can be closed down without affecting certain employees' leave entitlements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b63d3371d1b762c2013adc08da9c549f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13c30dec17d1cd754d99b0830f49589c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 501}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE ENTITLEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Annual leave entitlement is related to the number of days an employee can take off, which varies based on their period of employment and is granted in addition to other leaves such as rest days, holidays, maternity leave, and paternity leave."&lt;SEP&gt;"Annual leave entitlement is the right granted to employees under certain conditions and policies, allowing them time off work with pay or without pay as per company policy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13c30dec17d1cd754d99b0830f49589c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 129}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 579}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REST DAYS, HOLIDAYS, MATERNITY LEAVE, AND PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are types of leave that employees can take under the Ordinance, distinct from annual leave."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-13c30dec17d1cd754d99b0830f49589c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 129}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 579}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TABLE (1990-2014)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Table outlines specific rules for determining the number of days' annual leave an employee is entitled to based on their period of employment, starting from 1990 and amended in 2014."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-13c30dec17d1cd754d99b0830f49589c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 129}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 579}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMON HOLIDAY YEAR SELECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event refers to the process of selecting a common 12-month period for calculating annual leave, which is decided by employers and affects all employees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a7a96ed62715f51c591ee8559b48c831</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE PERIOD OF 1 MONTH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Notice period of one month is a technology or method used by employers to inform their employees about changes in holiday year selection policies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a7a96ed62715f51c591ee8559b48c831</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;假期&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"假期在这里指的是员工享有的休息时间，是一种福利产品或技术的体现。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b1de7cbb89da3f1adf715fabc5ea88cf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 476}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1130}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;41F條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"41F條是香港劳工法的一部分，规定了关于员工年假的具体条款和条件。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b1de7cbb89da3f1adf715fabc5ea88cf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 73}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 472}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OPTION FOR COMMON LEAVE YEAR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Option for common leave year是指雇主选择使用一个共同的假期年度来计算所有雇员的年假，这是一种管理上的技术或行业实践。"&lt;SEP&gt;"The event refers to an optional policy allowing employers to choose a 12-month period as the leave year for calculating annual leave."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b1de7cbb89da3f1adf715fabc5ea88cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 73}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 472}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;12 MONTH PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"12 month period指的是由僱主确定的一个为期一年的时间段，用于计算员工的年假数量和安排。"&lt;SEP&gt;"A 12-month period is a specific timeframe used by employers for calculating employees' annual leave, which can be elected as per the option provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b1de7cbb89da3f1adf715fabc5ea88cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 73}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 472}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMON LEAVE YEAR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Common leave year is a standardized approach provided as an option, allowing employers to calculate and manage employee's annual leave more uniformly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CALENDAR DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Calendar days are units of time used in the calculation for determining pro rata annual leave entitlements based on the number of days worked or employed within a specific period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRO RATA BASIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pro rata basis is a method of calculating something, such as an employee's leave entitlement, in proportion to their time spent working during the relevant period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNIVERSARY OF DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Anniversary of day refers to the date that marks one year since a specific event or commencement, used for calculation purposes within this context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAVE YEAR DETERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leave year determination refers to the process of selecting a 12-month period for calculating annual leave based on specific criteria provided by employers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WRITTEN NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Written notice refers to a formal communication in writing that must be provided by employers to notify their employees of election decisions related to leave year determination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Written notice refers to a formal communication method used in legal and business contexts, detailing the termination of agreements and relevant dates."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eac62f2f1327a829e40a168eae3df71e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 411}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1117}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSPICUOUS PLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conspicuous place refers to a visible area within the workplace designated for posting important information like election intentions related to leave year determination."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPORTIONATE BASIS CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Proportionate basis calculation is a method of determining an employee's entitlements, such as annual leave, based on their time worked or employed within the relevant period compared to a full 12-month cycle."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAVE YEAR COMMENCEMENT DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leave year commencement date refers to the specific day from which an employer starts using a chosen 12-month period for calculating annual leave entitlements of their employees, marking the beginning of this new calculation method."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE CONSULTATION REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee consultation requirement is an event where employers must seek input or agreement from their employees before finalizing any changes to company policies related to annual leave calculations and management."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAVE ENTITLEMENT COMBINATION OPTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leave entitlement combination option refers to a policy allowing employees to combine their pro rata calculated leave with the next full leave year, providing flexibility in managing their time off work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE CALCULATION METHOD CHANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Annual leave calculation method change is an event where employers can alter how they calculate annual leave for all employees within a specific 12-month period, impacting the entitlements and management of employee leaves."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAVE YEAR DETERMINATION PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leave year determination process refers to the systematic approach or procedure used by employers to select and implement a 12-month period for calculating annual leave based on certain criteria provided in company policies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 73}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 472}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPORTIONATE BASIS CALCULATION METHOD CHANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Proportionate basis calculation method change is an event where the way of determining employee's entitlements, such as annual leave, changes to a more flexible and proportional approach based on their time worked or employed within the relevant period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAVE YEAR DETERMINATION CRITERIA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leave year determination criteria are specific conditions or standards that employers must follow when selecting a 12-month period for calculating annual leave entitlements of employees, ensuring fairness and consistency in policy application."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE CALCULATION METHOD CHANGE PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Annual leave calculation method change process refers to the procedural steps involved in altering how employers calculate annual leave based on a chosen 12-month period for all their employees, including notification requirements and employee consultation processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAVE YEAR DETERMINATION POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leave year determination policy is an official document or set of guidelines that outlines the process and criteria for selecting a specific 12-month period to calculate annual leave entitlements for employees within an organization."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 599}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE CALCULATION METHOD CHANGE EVENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Annual leave calculation method change event refers to any instance where employers decide to modify their approach or policy regarding how they determine and manage employee's annual leave based on a chosen 12-month period, impacting the entitlements of all employees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAVE YEAR DETERMINATION PROCESS IMPLEMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leave year determination process implementation is the actual execution or application of the systematic method used by employers to select and use a specific 12-month period for calculating annual leave based on company policies and guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE CALCULATION METHOD CHANGE IMPACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Annual leave calculation method change impact refers to the effects or consequences that result from altering how an organization calculates and manages its employees' annual leave, including changes in entitlements, management practices, and employee satisfaction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAVE YEAR DETERMINATION POLICY IMPLEMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leave year determination policy implementation is the process of putting into effect the official document or set of guidelines that outline the method for selecting a 12-month period to calculate annual leave based on company policies and standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRO RATA PORTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pro rata portion refers to a fractional part of something, in this case, the pro-rated annual leave based on the number of days worked since the start of employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e7dbc6cb0d2646456eacee5097d668ff</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 501}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;每日年假薪酬額&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Daily annual leave salary refers to the daily average amount of money calculated based on wages earned in the period preceding the annual leave, as per regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6957d2ae600df45cdcfeef087031ad45</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 476}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1130}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;僱員補償條例(第282章)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Employees' Compensation Ordinance (Cap. 282) is a regulation in Hong Kong that provides compensation for employees who are temporarily unable to work due to injury or illness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7bf34bf4406f6219987d03f2fb1fb1f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 479}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1133}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY RATE CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Calculating the daily rate of annual leave pay involves averaging wages over a period, considering various factors such as maternity/paternity leaves, sickness days, etc., to determine the appropriate compensation for an employee's absence."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5cf406b3b427b0e2efe01c3ec1bb9db4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE CALCULATION METHODOLOGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A method for calculating the daily average of the wages earned by an employee during annual leave based on employment history or similar roles in the same district."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT TERMINATION DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The date of termination of a contract of employment is used as a reference point for calculating certain benefits, such as annual leave pay."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 101}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 532}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SAME TRADE OR OCCUPATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A person employed in the same trade or occupation refers to someone with similar job roles and responsibilities within the same industry."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 101}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 530}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY REDUCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The annual leave pay is reduced by a sum of money paid by the employer for an employee's day of annual leave, as specified in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 101}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 528}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT DISTRICT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The district where an employee works and similar roles are considered when calculating certain benefits such as annual leave pay."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 101}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 527}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY CALCULATION METHODOLOGY (2007)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A method for calculating the daily average of wages earned by an employee during their annual leave was replaced and amended as per section 14 of Replaced 7 of 2007 s. 14."&lt;SEP&gt;"A method for calculating the daily average of wages earned by an employee during their annual leave, based on employment history or similar roles in the same district, was replaced as per section 14 of Replaced 7 of 2007 s. 14."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT STOP DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The date when an employee's employment is stopped and they are no longer considered for certain benefits such as annual leave pay, as specified in the text."</data>
