</node>
<node id="&quot;BUILDING WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Building Works refers to the construction, land leveling, reconstruction, maintenance (including repairs and exterior cleaning), renovation, alteration or demolition of any building, wharf, dock, bridge, elevated road, other structures; or any harbor or port engineering, reclamation work, roads, tunnels, sewers, drains, wells, or waterworks facilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Building works encompass all aspects of constructing or modifying buildings, from design through completion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Building works encompass the construction, site formation, reconstruction, maintenance (including redecoration and external cleaning), repairs, alteration or demolition of buildings, structures, ports, roads, tunnels, sewers, drains, wells, waterworks, and related installations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1766fce0308d4fb774b3b29e83cb45eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa4e81ff5495fa19b7b8105fa63909b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cb98b63e05e5bcca889147b0b338ac8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 255}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 927}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY OWNER OR OCCUPIER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property Owner or Occupier is a person who owns or occupies a property and may enter into contracts with main contractors for construction work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0cb98b63e05e5bcca889147b0b338ac8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 260}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 942}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARCHITECT, SURVEYOR, CIVIL ENGINEER, URBAN PLANNER, STRUCTURAL ENGINEER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROFESSIONALS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These professionals can designate nominated sub-contractors to perform specific tasks related to building works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0cb98b63e05e5bcca889147b0b338ac8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 260}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 942}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAIN NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Main Nominated Sub-Contractor is an organization that may receive information requests from employees regarding wage payments by the employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A main nominated sub-contractor is an individual or entity that directly enters into a contract with a principal contractor to undertake some or all of the works."&lt;SEP&gt;"Main Nominated Sub-Contractor refers to an organization responsible for receiving and forwarding notices regarding unpaid wages from employees of subordinate sub-contractors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Main Nominated Sub-Contractor refers to the primary contractor who has a contract with the employee and is liable for their wages within certain limitations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Main Nominated Sub-Contractor refers to the primary contractor who has agreed to perform specific work, and whose employees' wages must be paid if not by them directly."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to the main nominated sub-contractor who may receive requests under section 43E or 43I."&lt;SEP&gt;"The main nominated sub-contractor is the primary contractor within a hierarchy of subcontractors, potentially liable for certain actions if not properly communicated with by other sub-contractors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4c013f3a5fdc373a096e8c9e39e597f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a160d4a92860e123b37153b47528d3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1766fce0308d4fb774b3b29e83cb45eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79b86e6b5d2c9cc7cc776e8be6a979bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14526d01cdd531d1142f16c1d5e43367&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93a1fe97f228ec755ced3c31d6506c86</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 260}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 942}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECLAMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Reclamation refers to the process of reclaiming land from bodies of water for development purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1766fce0308d4fb774b3b29e83cb45eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 255}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 927}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ROAD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Roads are part of building works that involve construction or maintenance activities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1766fce0308d4fb774b3b29e83cb45eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 255}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 927}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TUNNEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tunnels are part of the works used for sewage treatment or water supply systems, highlighting their role in creating underground passages for various utilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tunnels, as a component of building works, refer to underground passages constructed through mountains or beneath bodies of water for transportation purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1766fce0308d4fb774b3b29e83cb45eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3f4b114096d8c9274040421c00bf9ac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 255}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 928}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEWER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sewers are part of the infrastructure included in building works that involve drainage systems and sanitation facilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1766fce0308d4fb774b3b29e83cb45eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 255}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 927}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DRAIN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Drains, as a component of building works, refer to channels or pipes for removing water from an area."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1766fce0308d4fb774b3b29e83cb45eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 255}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 927}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WELL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wells are part of the infrastructure included in building works that involve groundwater extraction and management facilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1766fce0308d4fb774b3b29e83cb45eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 255}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 927}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WATERWORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Waterworks include structures, systems, and processes related to water supply, treatment, distribution, and management as part of building works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1766fce0308d4fb774b3b29e83cb45eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 255}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 927}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OWNER OR OCCUPIER OF PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Owner or Occupier of Property is the party from whom a principal contractor typically contracts to perform work on property they own or occupy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-aa4e81ff5495fa19b7b8105fa63909b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 253}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGENT OR AUTHORIZED ARCHITECT, SURVEYOR OR CIVIL, MUNICIPAL OR STRUCTURAL ENGINEER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are individuals or organizations authorized by an owner or occupier to act as their representative in contracting for and supervising the performance of work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-aa4e81ff5495fa19b7b8105fa63909b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 253}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTOR (次承判商)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A sub-contractor is a person who enters into a contract with a principal contractor to perform part of the contracted work, or another sub-contractor's work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-aa4e81ff5495fa19b7b8105fa63909b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 254}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 925}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR (指定次承判商)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A nominated sub-contractor is specifically selected by an owner or occupier and their authorized representatives to perform certain parts of the work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-aa4e81ff5495fa19b7b8105fa63909b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 253}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK (工作)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Work refers to building works, including both construction activities and manual labor related to such projects."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-aa4e81ff5495fa19b7b8105fa63909b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 255}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 927}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPERIOR SUB-CONTRACTOR (上级次承判商)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A superior sub-contractor is a sub-contractor who further subcontracts part of the work they contracted to perform to another sub-contractor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-aa4e81ff5495fa19b7b8105fa63909b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 254}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 925}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPERIOR NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR (上级指定次承判商)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A superior nominated sub-contractor is a nominated sub-contractor who further subcontracts part of their work to another nominated sub-contractor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-aa4e81ff5495fa19b7b8105fa63909b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 253}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SMALL CLAIMS TRIBUNAL FOR WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Small Claims Tribunal for Wages is an arbitration body where claims regarding wage disputes can be lodged by employees or their representatives, leading to judgments that may affect payment obligations under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f7e01a5307e145a0563e90666073bf5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 138}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 606}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPERIOR SUB-CONTRACTOR(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Superior Sub-contractors are involved in joint and several liability with the principal contractor for paying wages of certain employees, depending on their relationship with the sub-contractor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c648be5705790613057129f42ce74462</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 254}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 923}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTOR(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub-contractors may be responsible for paying wages to their employed staff if they fail to do so within the specified period, subject to conditions outlined in the regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c648be5705790613057129f42ce74462</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 254}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 923}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON/ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee(s) are individuals employed by the employer, mentioned in relation to payment obligations and potential first contact for work-related matters."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employees are individuals who work under sub-contractors and whose wages need to be paid by principal contractors or superior sub-contractors as per the regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af8bb2bf50613f2cddc9c821004e6e7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c648be5705790613057129f42ce74462</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE UNDER SECTION 43D&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Notice Under Section 43D is a formal notification that triggers the payment obligation within 30 days, if not already met."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c648be5705790613057129f42ce74462</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 254}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 923}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRINCIPAL CONTRACTOR OR SUPERIOR SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Principal Contractor or Superior Sub-Contractor refers to entities responsible for paying wages, either directly or through a subcontracting arrangement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Principal Contractor or Superior Sub-Contractor refers to the entity that pays contributions or deducts sums by way of set-off, and is responsible for paying wages under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a544f1422493c38b567ef610eadf02d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26bf6e9b9c68841eec3e4308ce698c89</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 254}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 926}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK DETAILS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Work Details refer to the specific tasks or work performed by employees, which are relevant for wage claims and dispute resolution processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a544f1422493c38b567ef610eadf02d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE BY EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event is the process where an employee notifies the principal contractor about unpaid wages, which triggers subsequent actions and responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1082e0d73690e2409d13d0dfdf0e64c6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 254}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 923}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE OF A SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee of a sub-contractor refers to individuals employed by organizations that are sub-contracting work under larger contracts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af77be8b003511c35b7551f4285bb427</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 254}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 924}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPERIOR SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Superior Sub-Contractor is an organization that may receive payments from a principal contractor and has the right to make claims or deductions according to the terms outlined."&lt;SEP&gt;"Superior sub-contractor refers to a higher-level subcontractor within a hierarchy of contract work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af77be8b003511c35b7551f4285bb427&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bfdf4a9968aec09594f73a07cdf18d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 254}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 924}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONVICTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conviction refers to the legal process resulting in someone being found guilty of a crime and sentenced accordingly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af77be8b003511c35b7551f4285bb427</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 254}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 923}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;書面要求&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Written request is an event where a party formally communicates with another in writing, often for the purpose of requesting information or services."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-af77be8b003511c35b7551f4285bb427</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 138}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 604}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SET-OFF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Set-Off is a financial mechanism allowing deductions from one party's payment due to another based on mutual agreements or legal rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8bfdf4a9968aec09594f73a07cdf18d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 254}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 924}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee's Wages are payments made to employees as compensation for their work, which can be deemed as a product in terms of legal responsibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-26bf6e9b9c68841eec3e4308ce698c89</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTED WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub-Contracted Work is the task or project that has been subcontracted from one organization to another, involving payment and employment responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-26bf6e9b9c68841eec3e4308ce698c89</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 254}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 926}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SETTLEMENT UNDER SUBSECTION (2)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Settlement Under Subsection (2)(b) refers to a legal action where sums due are deducted by a principal contractor or superior sub-contractor as set-off against other obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-26bf6e9b9c68841eec3e4308ce698c89</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE OF WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee of Wages is an individual who has been employed under the terms and conditions specified in the contract, with rights to receive payment for their work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-26bf6e9b9c68841eec3e4308ce698c89</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAIN SUB-CONTRACTOR OR SUPERIOR SUB-CONTRACTOR'S LEGAL RESPONSIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Main Sub-Contractor or Superior Sub-Contractor's Legal Responsibility involves the obligations of these entities towards paying wages and fulfilling contractual agreements as per relevant laws and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-26bf6e9b9c68841eec3e4308ce698c89</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WAGES DUE TO EMPLOYEES UNDER SECTION 43C&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wages Due to Employees Under Section 43C are payments that must be made by a principal contractor or superior sub-contractor according to the terms of employment, as defined in legal sections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-26bf6e9b9c68841eec3e4308ce698c89</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR'S EMPLOYEES' WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Nominated Sub-Contractor's Employees' Wages refer to the compensation owed to workers employed by a specific subcontractor under an agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-26bf6e9b9c68841eec3e4308ce698c89</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL RESPONSIBILITY FOR WAGE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal Responsibility for Wage Payment is the obligation of entities, such as principal contractors or superior sub-contractors, to ensure timely and proper payment of wages according to legal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-26bf6e9b9c68841eec3e4308ce698c89</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK ON WHICH THE EMPLOYEE WAS EMPLOYED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Work On Which The Employee Was Employed refers to the specific tasks or projects where an individual is engaged in their employment contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-26bf6e9b9c68841eec3e4308ce698c89</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRST CONTACT WITH SUB-CONTRACTOR'S EMPLOYEES'">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"First Contact With Sub-Contractor's Employees' involves initial interactions and agreements regarding wage payments between principal contractors, superior sub-contractors, and the employees they employ or subcontract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-26bf6e9b9c68841eec3e4308ce698c89</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPERIOR NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Superior Nominated Sub-Contractors are higher-level contractors who, along with the direct employer (nominated sub-contractor), are jointly responsible for paying employees' wages if not paid by the main contractor or their immediate sub-contractor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Superior Nominated Sub-Contractors are organizations that, in a hierarchy of sub-contracting relationships, have higher positions and can also be requested for information or payment by employees regarding wage issues with the employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79b86e6b5d2c9cc7cc776e8be6a979bb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 260}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 943}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEES OF NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employees of Nominated Sub-Contractors refer to individuals who work under a specific contracted organization and whose wages may be payable by higher-level contractors in certain circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-79b86e6b5d2c9cc7cc776e8be6a979bb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 260}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 943}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE OF THE BUILDING WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Site of the Building Works is the physical location where construction activities are taking place, relevant for determining employment relatedness according to the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-79b86e6b5d2c9cc7cc776e8be6a979bb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 260}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 943}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SMALL AMOUNT SALARY DISPUTE ARBITRATION OFFICE OR LABOR AND WELFARE TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Small Amount Salary Dispute Arbitration Office or Labor and Welfare Tribunal refers to bodies that can make judgments on wage claims of employees in disputes with their employers, as mentioned for determining payment timelines when a claim is made."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-79b86e6b5d2c9cc7cc776e8be6a979bb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 138}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 604}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPERIOR NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Superior Nominated Sub-Contractors are secondary contractors jointly responsible, along with the main nominated sub-contractor, for paying employees' wages under specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a160d4a92860e123b37153b47528d3e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 260}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 942}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE OF BUILDING WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Site of Building Works is the physical location where construction work takes place, relevant for determining wage liability based on employment site."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a160d4a92860e123b37153b47528d3e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE UNDER SECTION 43H&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Notice Under Section 43H is a formal notification sent by an employee within the specified period if they have not received their due wages from the main nominated sub-contractor, initiating potential legal action for wage claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a160d4a92860e123b37153b47528d3e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 138}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 604}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE OF A NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee of a Nominated Sub-Contractor refers to individuals employed under a sub-contracting arrangement where their wages might not be paid within specified periods and they are required to send notices regarding unpaid wages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4c013f3a5fdc373a096e8c9e39e597f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 260}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 942}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPERIOR NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A superior nominated sub-contractor is a party that has been designated by the employer to perform work or pay wages, and can claim contributions from other parties or make deductions for certain purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Superior Nominated Sub-Contractor is an organization that may receive copies of notices from main nominated sub-contractors about employees' wage issues, as per the regulations mentioned in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4c013f3a5fdc373a096e8c9e39e597f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be3c1325ae6d7ddc996c9ba2b65c0d1d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;43G&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 43G is part of the legislation that outlines specific conditions for wage payments under certain circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-14526d01cdd531d1142f16c1d5e43367</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 260}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 942}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1988年第24號第2條修訂;由1995年第103號第17及26條修訂&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These amendments refer to changes made in 1988 and 1995 that have updated or modified the legislation related to wage payments and notice serving."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-14526d01cdd531d1142f16c1d5e43367</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 591}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;43I. 僱主應僱員要求提供資料的規定&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 43I is a provision in the law requiring employers, particularly nominated sub-contractors, to provide certain information upon request from employees regarding wage payments and compliance with legal obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-14526d01cdd531d1142f16c1d5e43367</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 591}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;43G CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The 43G Clause is an event where a main nominated sub-contractor pays wages to an employee on behalf of their actual employer, creating a debt relationship between them."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 260}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 940}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTING RELATIONSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Sub-Contracting Relationship refers to the business arrangement among multiple organizations in which each is responsible for specific tasks or work segments under a larger project."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 135}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;43J CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The 43J Clause is an event where a main nominated sub-contractor can pursue wage payments from other parties involved in the sub-contracting relationship, either through sharing costs or deductions from future payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 260}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 941}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTOR DEBT RELATIONSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Sub-Contractor Debt Relationship refers to financial obligations among multiple organizations within a sub-contracting network where each party may owe money to another based on the work performed and paid for by others in the chain of contracts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 260}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 940}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL OBLIGATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Legal Obligations refer to the responsibilities and duties that organizations, individuals, or entities have under legal frameworks such as labor laws and contractual agreements regarding wage payments and information provision."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WAGE PAYMENT MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Wage Payment Mechanism is a system or process through which wages are paid from one party to another in the context of sub-contracting relationships, often involving multiple layers of organizations with varying roles and responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 135}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK SEGMENT TRANSFER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Work Segment Transfer refers to the division of a larger project into smaller tasks or segments that are assigned to different parties in a sub-contracting relationship, each responsible for specific parts of the overall work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT DEDUCTION MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Payment Deduction Mechanism is a process where payments made by one party can be used to offset debts or obligations owed by another party within a sub-contracting network, often involving complex financial arrangements and agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 260}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 941}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL FINE FOR NON-COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Legal Fine for Non-Compliance is an event where organizations that fail to comply with legal requirements regarding information provision or wage payments face penalties such as fines imposed by relevant authorities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 260}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 941}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTION HIERARCHY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Sub-Contraction Hierarchy refers to the organizational structure within a sub-contracting network, detailing the relationships and responsibilities among different levels of organizations involved in project execution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE RIGHTS PROTECTION MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Employee Rights Protection Mechanism is a set of legal and procedural measures designed to safeguard employees' rights regarding wage payments, information access, and other related matters within sub-contracting relationships."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 135}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTOR NETWORK DYNAMICS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Sub-Contractor Network Dynamics refers to the complex interactions and dependencies among multiple organizations in a sub-contracting network, influencing their roles, responsibilities, and financial arrangements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORK FOR SUB-CONTRACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Legal Framework for Sub-Contraction is a set of laws, regulations, and guidelines that govern the relationships among organizations in sub-contracting networks, including wage payments, information provision, and other related matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WAGE PAYMENT DISPUTE RESOLUTION MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Wage Payment Dispute Resolution Mechanism is a process or system designed to resolve disputes regarding wage payments within sub-contracting relationships, often involving mediation, arbitration, or legal proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 260}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 940}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTOR INFORMATION SHARING REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Sub-Contractor Information Sharing Requirement refers to the obligation of organizations in a sub-contracting network to share relevant information with employees when wage payments are not made by their direct employer but by another party within the network."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTION RISK MANAGEMENT MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Sub-Contraction Risk Management Mechanism is a set of strategies and practices designed to mitigate risks associated with sub-contracting relationships, including financial, legal, and operational risks related to wage payments and information provision."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTOR DEBT RESOLUTION MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Sub-Contractor Debt Resolution Mechanism is a process or system designed to resolve debt obligations among organizations in sub-contracting networks, often involving financial arrangements such as payment deductions and sharing of costs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 260}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 941}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTION CONTRACTUAL AGREEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub-Contraction Contractual Agreements are formal legal documents that outline the terms and conditions between parties involved in a sub-contracting relationship, including responsibilities for wage payments, information provision, and other related matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE INFORMATION ACCESS RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Employee Information Access Rights refer to the rights of employees within a sub-contracting network to access relevant information regarding their wages and payment status from multiple parties involved in the project execution process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTOR FINANCIAL RESPONSIBILITY MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Sub-Contractor Financial Responsibility Mechanism is a system or framework that defines financial responsibilities among organizations within sub-contracting networks, ensuring accountability for wage payments and other related financial obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL COMPLIANCE MONITORING MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Legal Compliance Monitoring Mechanism refers to the processes and systems in place to ensure compliance with legal requirements regarding sub-contracting relationships, including wage payments, information provision, and other related matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTOR NETWORK GOVERNANCE STRUCTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Sub-Contractor Network Governance Structure is a framework that outlines the rules, regulations, and procedures governing the interactions among organizations within sub-contracting networks, ensuring transparency, accountability, and effective management of relationships."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;前判次承判商&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"前判次承判商 is a subcontractor that operates under certain provisions of section 43C or 43G as mentioned in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b14e71147144e9b2f455f7918c813637</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 86}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;前判指定次承判商&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"前判指定次承判商 refers to a designated subcontractor according to Section 43G, involved in wage payments and set-offs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b14e71147144e9b2f455f7918c813637</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 71}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 455}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1124}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第43C條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 43C refers to a specific clause related to wage payment by principal contractors mentioned in the document."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b14e71147144e9b2f455f7918c813637</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第43G條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 43G is another specific clause concerning wage payments made by superior nominated sub-contractors, as described in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b14e71147144e9b2f455f7918c813637</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第43F(1)及43J(1)條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sections 43F(1) and 43J(1) are clauses that may affect the cessation of employer's liability for wages paid by principal contractors or sub-contractors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b14e71147144e9b2f455f7918c813637</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;通知書的送達&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Service of notice is a process described in Section 43L, detailing methods and conditions under which notices can be delivered to relevant parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b14e71147144e9b2f455f7918c813637</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 86}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;面交上述人士&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNIQUE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Face-to-face delivery refers to the method mentioned in section 43L(1)(a) for serving a notice or requirement on an individual or entity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b14e71147144e9b2f455f7918c813637</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;留在上述人士的通常地址、最後為人所知住址或營業地址&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNIQUE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leaving at the usual address, last known residence, or business address is another method of service as described in section 43L(1)(b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b14e71147144e9b2f455f7918c813637</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;以掛號郵遞方式寄往上述人士(B)段所提述的任何地址&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNIQUE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sending by registered post to the addresses mentioned in (b) refers to a third method of service as described in section 43L(1)(c)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b14e71147144e9b2f455f7918c813637</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 86}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;留於該處所之日送達&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The notice or requirement is deemed delivered on the day it was left at the specified address, according to section 43L(2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b14e71147144e9b2f455f7918c813637</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 86}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTERED POST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Registered post is a method by which documents may be served, involving sending them through an official postal system with proof of delivery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Used for sending documents by registered post, ensuring a formal method of service."</data>
