  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to specific rights that must be paid according to certain sections of laws, including wages, year-end bonuses, maternity leave pay, paternity leave pay, severance payments, long-service bonus, sickness benefits, holiday allowances, annual leave allowances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c14c658fc7f9efe67addd18c3054ce6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第IXB部的释义 (DEFINITIONS IN PART IXB)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to the definitions section of Part IXB which explains key terms and their legal implications within a specific context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c14c658fc7f9efe67addd18c3054ce6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LABOR AND INDUSTRIAL RELATIONS TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Labor and Industrial Relations Tribunal refers to a body responsible for resolving disputes between employers and employees, including the Labour Department's Labour Tribunal and the Small Claims Tribunal for Wage Disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b27a008edb9bce1c0b390190fc14d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SMALL CLAIMS TRIBUNAL FOR WAGE DISPUTES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Small Claims Tribunal for Wage Disputes is another component of the Labor and Industrial Relations Tribunal, dealing with wage-related claims that are relatively small in amount."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b27a008edb9bce1c0b390190fc14d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT TERMINATION COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Contract Termination Compensation refers to payments made upon termination of an employment contract under specific conditions as outlined by legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b27a008edb9bce1c0b390190fc14d8a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A body responsible for making awards or decisions that can lead to presumptions being made about individuals involved with the organization's management and operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Tribunal refers to the arbitral body that decides on objections and issues orders such as preliminary orders and interim measures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tribunal refers to a body that makes awards against the body corporate, which can influence presumptions of liability under section 43P for its officers and partners."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tribunal refers to a body that makes decisions and awards, often in legal proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tribunal refers to the Labour Tribunal or Minor Employment Claims Adjudication Board, which are organizations responsible for resolving disputes and making judgments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tribunal refers to the arbitral tribunal that has jurisdiction over disputes and can order provisional measures or preliminary orders."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4667827d445ebb505094eb4b58494cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-effb99400ad285817b5c201e84a15ab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6778be16322ee3f645a000f95b6d6e2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f295ffb815631fda7aa87257db86215&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-570101da2940bef859df7e44c939408a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d4bd265e2aa3d3a8af55fbca1b13963</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 380}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1079}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTRAR OF LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Registrar of the Labour Tribunal is a person who has specific roles in relation to the Labour Tribunal, such as managing cases and issuing documents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6d4bd265e2aa3d3a8af55fbca1b13963</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 380}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1079}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTRAR OF MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Registrar of the Minor Employment Claims Adjudication Board is a person with similar responsibilities but related specifically to the Minor Employment Claims Adjudication Board."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6d4bd265e2aa3d3a8af55fbca1b13963</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 380}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1079}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WAGES OR ANY OTHER SUM PAYABLE UNDER SECTION 23, 24 OR 25&quot;">
