</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDITIONS OF SERVICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This concept refers to the terms under which employees will be employed, including details like wages and working periods as mentioned in section 44(1)(a)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de69b2333ff7d9bb2dd79e072a634503</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 609}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1148}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERSON ENTERING EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A person who is joining the workforce under certain conditions as communicated by the employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6cdefd54629d3267d124166ba92131ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WAGES AND WAGE PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The wages refer to the monetary compensation for labor, and the wage period indicates when these payments are made."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6cdefd54629d3267d124166ba92131ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 107}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 547}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT OR PROPORTION THEREOF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a financial benefit provided at the end of the fiscal year, which may be in full or partial form based on specific conditions as per Part IIA."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6cdefd54629d3267d124166ba92131ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 107}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 547}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE PERIOD FOR TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The notice period required to terminate an employment contract is a procedural aspect that ensures smooth transition and compliance with legal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6cdefd54629d3267d124166ba92131ae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 101}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 526}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTELLIGIBLE METHOD OF COMMUNICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The intelligible method refers to a clear and understandable way in which information about employment terms are communicated to employees before they start work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6cdefd54629d3267d124166ba92131ae</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL REQUIREMENTS AND COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ensuring legal compliance through proper communication of terms before employment starts involves understanding and adhering to relevant laws and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6cdefd54629d3267d124166ba92131ae</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INFORMATION PROVISION PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The information provision process is a systematic approach by employers to ensure all necessary details about the job are communicated clearly to potential employees prior to their start date."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6cdefd54629d3267d124166ba92131ae</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BOOK 48 OF 1984, SECTION 25&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to specific legal amendments or provisions that have been enacted in a particular year and section, impacting how employment terms must be communicated."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6cdefd54629d3267d124166ba92131ae</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WRITTEN REQUEST FOR INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A written request from the employee seeking detailed information about their prospective job before starting work is an important step ensuring all necessary details are provided by the employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6cdefd54629d3267d124166ba92131ae</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE IN WRITING CONTAINING CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a formal, documented notice that must be given to employees outlining key terms and conditions of employment as required by law or regulation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6cdefd54629d3267d124166ba92131ae</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT SIGNING PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The contract signing process is the legal procedure through which an employment agreement becomes binding between employer and employee after all necessary details have been communicated and agreed upon."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6cdefd54629d3267d124166ba92131ae</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT LEGISLATION COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ensuring that all aspects of employment, from initial communication to final agreements, comply with relevant laws and regulations is crucial for maintaining fair labor practices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6cdefd54629d3267d124166ba92131ae</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROCEDURAL REQUIREMENTS FOR CONTRACTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The procedural requirements for creating an employment contract include specific steps such as signing or legal validation processes that ensure the agreement is valid and enforceable."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6cdefd54629d3267d124166ba92131ae</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNICATION METHODS BEFORE EMPLOYMENT START DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Effective communication strategies used by employers to inform employees about their terms of employment prior to starting work are essential for setting clear expectations and ensuring mutual understanding between parties involved in an employment relationship."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6cdefd54629d3267d124166ba92131ae</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT TERMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contract Terms refer to the specific agreements and conditions outlined in contracts, which arbitral tribunals are required to take into account when making decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contract Terms refer to the specific agreements between an employer and employee regarding their rights and obligations in the workplace."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contract terms refer to agreements between parties that may attempt to limit legal responsibilities but are subject to certain sections of the Sale of Goods Ordinance (Cap. 26)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1093ec98fdeda43f43128129d5d24cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eddc386a4530fb8f47bfa480b977ad29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 102}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPLACE CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workplace Conditions refer to the physical and social environment where employees perform their work, including safety measures, working hours, and other relevant factors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1093ec98fdeda43f43128129d5d24cf9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 101}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 526}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EVERY EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Every employer refers to the entity responsible for informing employees of changes in their employment conditions and wage details."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-36d63c63cafeb631b985e26ad3fb4262</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WRITTEN AMENDMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Written amendment refers to the formal written changes made to the employment contract that need to be communicated to employees as per legal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-36d63c63cafeb631b985e26ad3fb4262</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 134}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 581}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1140}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WAGE PERIOD CONCERNED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wage period concerned refers to specific time intervals during which wages are calculated and paid out, such as weekly, monthly, etc., for the purpose of providing accurate wage details to employees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-36d63c63cafeb631b985e26ad3fb4262</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;44 &amp; 45 CLAUSES CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The terms 'conditions' in reference to Clauses 44 and 45 include salary rates, overtime pay rates, and any allowances or bonuses that can be calculated on a piecework, hourly, daily, weekly basis, or other methods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-36d63c63cafeb631b985e26ad3fb4262</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WAGE DETAILS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wage details refer to the specific information related to an employee's earnings including regular wages and overtime income, which are crucial for transparency in employment terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-36d63c63cafeb631b985e26ad3fb4262</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;46 CLAUSE CONDITIONS &amp; WAGE DETAILS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Clause 46 specifies that the conditions must include rates of pay, overtime rates, and any allowances or bonuses calculated on various bases such as piecework, hourly, daily, weekly, etc., while detailing what constitutes wages earned including overtime income."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-36d63c63cafeb631b985e26ad3fb4262</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMENDMENT 41 OF 190 S.20&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The amendment refers to a legal change or update made in the year 1990 that affects how employers must inform employees about changes in their employment conditions and wage details."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-36d63c63cafeb631b985e26ad3fb4262</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROCEDURES TO VALIDATE AMENDMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Procedures to validate amendments refer to formal processes required for confirming written changes to an employment contract, ensuring they are legally binding before being communicated to the employee."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-36d63c63cafeb631b985e26ad3fb4262</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RATE OF WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The rate at which employees are paid, calculated by piece, job, hour, day, week, etc., for compliance purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f15fe91e28bec496f95bc0e2d20ab50c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 559}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OVERTIME RATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The rate applied to the additional hours worked beyond regular working hours, as part of wage calculations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f15fe91e28bec496f95bc0e2d20ab50c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 559}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ALLOWANCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Additional payments or benefits provided to employees in addition to their base wages, which may be included in total earnings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f15fe91e28bec496f95bc0e2d20ab50c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 559}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OVERTIME EARNINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Earnings received by an employee for working overtime hours beyond the standard work schedule."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f15fe91e28bec496f95bc0e2d20ab50c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 559}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEDUCTIONS FROM WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Amounts deducted from employees' wages, along with reasons for such deductions as required by regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f15fe91e28bec496f95bc0e2d20ab50c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 559}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECORDS OF EMPLOYEES'">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Detailed records maintained by employers regarding their employees, including personal information and financial details like earnings and deductions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f15fe91e28bec496f95bc0e2d20ab50c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FORMAT CHANGES—E.R. 3 OF 2015&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A specific event or update in the format requirements for record-keeping as per a government directive."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f15fe91e28bec496f95bc0e2d20ab50c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECORDS TO BE KEPT BY EMPLOYERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The obligation on employers to maintain certain records, including employee details and financial transactions, to comply with labor regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f15fe91e28bec496f95bc0e2d20ab50c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART X&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A section or part of a regulatory framework that outlines specific requirements for employer-employee relations, particularly concerning record-keeping and compliance measures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f15fe91e28bec496f95bc0e2d20ab50c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 158}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 671}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CABINET GAZETTE ANNOUNCEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An official announcement in the gazette by a government authority, such as the Secretary, to specify certain classes or types of employers required to keep specific records."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f15fe91e28bec496f95bc0e2d20ab50c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EVERY EMPLOYER WHO IS A MEMBER OF A CLASS SPECIFIED UNDER SUBSECTION (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to employers categorized into specific classes as defined by the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0409e534977d79adcbe523886e26b9cc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECORDS IN SUCH FORM AS MAY BE SPECIFIED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are specific forms or records that employers must keep according to the Commissioner's specifications for compliance with Part X."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0409e534977d79adcbe523886e26b9cc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE IN THE GAZETTE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a public announcement made by the Commissioner through the gazette to specify classes of employers or provide other important information."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0409e534977d79adcbe523886e26b9cc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 608}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1144}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER OR CLASS OF EMPLOYERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION,NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These refer to individual employers and groups of employers that are required to submit returns as specified by the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0409e534977d79adcbe523886e26b9cc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RETURNS IN SUCH FORM AND AT SUCH TIMES AS HE MAY IN ANY SUCH NOTICE DIRECT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to specific formats and timing for submitting reports or records as directed by the Commissioner through notices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0409e534977d79adcbe523886e26b9cc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INFORMATION OR PARTICULARS IN RESPECT OF A TIME OR PERIOD MORE THAN 6 MONTHS IMMEDIATELY PRECEDING THE DATE OF THE NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS,SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This specifies that employers are not required to provide information about events or details from more than six months prior to the notice date."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0409e534977d79adcbe523886e26b9cc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COPIES OF ANY SUCH FORM SHALL BE SUPPLIED TO AN EMPLOYER FREE OF CHARGE ON APPLICATION TO THE COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Commissioner is obligated to supply copies of specified forms without cost upon request by employers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0409e534977d79adcbe523886e26b9cc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSENT FORM, REQUEST FORM, NOTICE, CERTIFICATE, APPLICATION FORM, RECORD OR RETURN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are various types of documents that the Commissioner can specify in terms of format for compliance with this ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0409e534977d79adcbe523886e26b9cc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 144}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 636}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;1988年第52號第15條修訂&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,MATHEMATICS,SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This indicates that certain provisions of this ordinance have been amended in 1988 through the 15th amendment to Ordinance No. 52."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0409e534977d79adcbe523886e26b9cc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER OR CLASS OF EMPLOYERS (FOR APPLICATION FOR FORM)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION,NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These refer to specific groups or individual employers who may apply for free forms from the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0409e534977d79adcbe523886e26b9cc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT RECORDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Records are detailed records that must be maintained by employers, containing information about employees' wages and employment history over a period of 12 months or more."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe986d49a20cfdf5d43e02699374c050</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK RECORD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Work Record is the specific term used for documents detailing an employee's wage periods and payments as required under section 49A(1) and (1A)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe986d49a20cfdf5d43e02699374c050</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS PREMISES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Business Premises are where employers must keep records as specified in section 49A(2)(a), indicating the physical location for maintaining such documents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Business Premises is the last known business location of a party involved in a construction contract, utilized as a point of contact for document service."&lt;SEP&gt;"Business Premises refers to the physical location where an employment agency conducts its operations and must display its license prominently."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-22aad013b6ace7041cfc26259ab41c0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db7c4caf2703152da21b6fa8c5646ce3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe986d49a20cfdf5d43e02699374c050</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 370}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1067}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;6-MONTH PERIOD AFTER CESSATION OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TIME PERIOD"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a specific duration, six months, during which employer-maintained wage records must be retained even after an employee's termination as per section 49A(2)(b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe986d49a20cfdf5d43e02699374c050</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE NAME AND DETAILS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are the details that need to be included in employment records for each individual employee, specifically their name according to section 49A(3)(a), indicating a requirement related to personal identification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe986d49a20cfdf5d43e02699374c050</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;假及假日&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"假及假日指的是特定期间内的休息时间，通常包括法定节假日和公司规定的假期。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ffd253a6ffc2d98305e581075ce59a38</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 75}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;《最低工資條例》(第608章)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"《最低工資條例》(第608章)是一部法律文件或条例，用于规定最低工资标准及相关细节。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ffd253a6ffc2d98305e581075ce59a38</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;實習學員&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"實習學員是指那些通过实习课程获得工作经验的学生或个人。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ffd253a6ffc2d98305e581075ce59a38</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;工作經驗學員&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"工作經驗學員指的是正在修讀與其職業相關的課程並獲得實際工作經驗的人士。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ffd253a6ffc2d98305e581075ce59a38</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;某機構&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"某機構指的是在特定情况下，如实习安排中提到的机构，可能是一家教育机构或其他类型的组织。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ffd253a6ffc2d98305e581075ce59a38</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 75}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE MINIMUM WAGES ORDINANCE (CAP. 608)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Minimum Wages Ordinance (Cap. 608) is a legal document that defines the minimum wage and related regulations in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb72900ee9c54337fb981f2f7d6cc6a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 138}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 605}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPENDIX 9&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appendix 9 refers to an appendix that can be revised by the Secretary through gazette notifications, detailing specific provisions or conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb72900ee9c54337fb981f2f7d6cc6a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 373}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1073}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKING HOURS (HOURS WORKED)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Working Hours is a concept defined in labor regulations and has implications for wage calculation and employee rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb72900ee9c54337fb981f2f7d6cc6a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 138}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 605}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WAGE PERIOD (WAGE PERIOD)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wage Period is a defined time frame within which wages are calculated, often tied to specific dates or cycles as stipulated in labor regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb72900ee9c54337fb981f2f7d6cc6a0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 138}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 605}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIFIED PERIOD (SPECIFIED PERIOD)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Specified Period refers to the duration relevant for certain employees based on their pre-privatization employment periods, used in calculating working hours and wages under specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb72900ee9c54337fb981f2f7d6cc6a0</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WAGE RECORD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Wage record is a document that records the wages paid and the employee's wage periods for each employee during their employment history."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3e6409377b6b4bbb92085773b4d5b79e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT RECORD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment record is another term used to describe documents containing an individual's work history, including details of wages and payment periods over 12 months of employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3e6409377b6b4bbb92085773b4d5b79e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;L.N. 34 OF 1990&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"L.N. 34 of 1990 is a legal notice that amended the requirements for employers to keep wage records, indicating changes in regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3e6409377b6b4bbb92085773b4d5b79e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;7 OF 2007 S. 16&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Amendment on 7 of 2007 s. 16 refers to specific provisions within a legal document that further defined or modified the requirements for wage and employment records keeping."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3e6409377b6b4bbb92085773b4d5b79e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;4 OF 2022 S. 17&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The addition in 4 of 2022 s. 17 introduced new subsections related to specified employees, expanding the scope of record-keeping requirements for employers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3e6409377b6b4bbb92085773b4d5b79e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLACE OF BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A place of business refers to a physical location where a party conducts its operations, which can influence the determination of jurisdiction in arbitration cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Place of Business is the physical location where an employer conducts their operations or maintains records related to employee wages and employment details."&lt;SEP&gt;"Place of business is a location where an entity conducts its operations, often used in the context of receiving written communications according to Article 3 of UNCITRAL Model Law."&lt;SEP&gt;"Place of business is an entity's operational location that can be used in determining the applicability and scope of this Law, particularly when parties operate from different locations across state borders."&lt;SEP&gt;"Place of business refers to the physical location where an employment agency operates and must display its licence prominently."&lt;SEP&gt;"Place of business refers to the physical location where an employment agency operates, which can change according to certain procedures as outlined in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Place of Business refers to the physical location where an Employment Agency operates from, which may be inspected by authorized public officers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e027acdec4c66c21703cf2589ec26926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b820d3fdcb65775124275159131a823e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee0cf79121cc26199f0bf5c4d14a8ce8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a98fdad24b6b0148ebf6a921fbf604fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-526d89a1459376fe55b0af078fc2a455&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff957c4b25c4b72be5b7c3c1525b4deb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8e07a1a35f0f2dbd1d061a1e93c29e0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 244}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 909}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MINIMUM WAGE ORDINANCE (CAP. 608)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Minimum Wage Ordinance (Cap. 608) is an organization or regulation that defines terms like 'hours worked', 'wage period', and 'wages' for employment purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Minimum Wage Ordinance (Cap. 608) defines key terms such as hours worked, wage period, and wages used in other contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Minimum Wage Ordinance (Cap. 608) is a legal document that sets minimum wage standards for employees in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1780efd8ae08a5db55e3f208ec193d60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d3d232b5b9df510faacc808489eadb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8e07a1a35f0f2dbd1d061a1e93c29e0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1094}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE, SICK LEAVE, MATERNITY LEAVE, PATERNITY LEAVE AND HOLIDAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are types of leave entitlements provided to employees as part of their employment benefits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d8e07a1a35f0f2dbd1d061a1e93c29e0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT (PART IIA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The End of Year Payment under Part IIA is a financial benefit mandated by law for certain categories of employees in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d8e07a1a35f0f2dbd1d061a1e93c29e0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE PERIOD FOR TERMINATION OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Notice period refers to the time an employee or employer must provide before ending an employment contract, ensuring smooth transition and compliance with labor laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d8e07a1a35f0f2dbd1d061a1e93c29e0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 552}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NINTH SCHEDULE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ninth Schedule refers to a specific part of legislation that can be amended by the Commissioner."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ninth Schedule refers to a document that can be amended by the Commissioner, likely containing specific details required in records of employee wages and work periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ninth Schedule refers to a legal document containing specific monetary caps and other provisions, such as those for keeping records of hours worked.""</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1896582b740b6a3f00c9bfa592f3ab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1780efd8ae08a5db55e3f208ec193d60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d3d232b5b9df510faacc808489eadb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 147}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 645}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1164}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOURS WORKED (工作時數)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hours worked is a mathematical concept used to measure time spent on tasks or employment, often related to calculating wages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45d3d232b5b9df510faacc808489eadb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 48}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 400}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1094}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIFIED EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Specified employee is an individual whose employment period determines the 'specified period' for certain calculations or definitions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1780efd8ae08a5db55e3f208ec193d60</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 106}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 544}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRE-TRANSITION EMPLOYMENT PERIOD (轉制前僱傭期)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pre-transition employment period refers to a specific timeframe before a transition date, which can vary based on the length of an employee's initial employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1780efd8ae08a5db55e3f208ec193d60</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 106}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 545}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WHOLE EMPLOYMENT PERIOD (整段僱傭期)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Whole employment period is defined as the total duration of an employee’s continuous engagement with their employer, used in determining certain periods or calculations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1780efd8ae08a5db55e3f208ec193d60</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 106}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 545}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT AGENCIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Agencies refer to organizations licensed or exempted under the relevant sections for providing job placement services."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employment Agencies refers to a system or practice of matching job seekers with employers, often facilitated through an organization."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0fbb70bb06a25c64d5b60d4ef9c96b1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2237564658a1150599559d04fcf04a08</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 300}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RELATED PERSON (相關人士)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A related person can refer to a director, manager, secretary, or other similar officer in relation to a company."&lt;SEP&gt;"A related person in the context of a company includes its directors, managers, secretaries, and other similar individuals; for partners in a partnership, it includes other partners or those involved in managing the partnership."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0fbb70bb06a25c64d5b60d4ef9c96b1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a12f68db2756f89b8999b59583f0a9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 336}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1024}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASSOCIATE (相關人士)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An associate is defined based on whether the person is an entity such as a company or partner. It involves related persons of that entity and individuals employed by them."&lt;SEP&gt;"Associate refers to individuals related to the person, including employees in specific cases like companies or partnerships."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0fbb70bb06a25c64d5b60d4ef9c96b1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a12f68db2756f89b8999b59583f0a9b</data>
