  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These sections are parts of a legal document that were in force before being amended by the Employment (Amendment) (No. 2) Ordinance 2018 and now form part of what is referred to as 'former provisions'."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-992f49fad60f9ac3ba8440de8738ff52</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATERIAL DATE (關鍵日期)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Material Date refers to a specific point in time that determines which legal provision applies to an employee's claim under Part VIA, based on whether the event occurred before or after certain specified dates."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-992f49fad60f9ac3ba8440de8738ff52</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE DISMISSED IN ANY OF THE CIRCUMSTANCES MENTIONED IN SECTION 32A(1)(A) OR (C)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to employees who are dismissed due to specific conditions outlined in Section 32A, which affects how their dismissal date is determined for legal claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-992f49fad60f9ac3ba8440de8738ff52</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER HAS NOTIFIED THE EMPLOYEE OF THE DISMISSAL BEFORE IT TOOK EFFECT—THE DATE ON WHICH THE EMPLOYEE WAS NOTIFIED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This describes a scenario where an employer informs an employee about a dismissal prior to its effective date, and in such cases, the material date is when the notification was received."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-992f49fad60f9ac3ba8440de8738ff52</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISMISSAL TOOK EFFECT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The actual occurrence of the termination of employment as per legal terms, which may differ from the date of notification if not specified otherwise."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-992f49fad60f9ac3ba8440de8738ff52</data>
</node>
