</node>
<node id="&quot;STRIKES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Strikes refer to a work stoppage by employees, usually organized for collective bargaining or protest against working conditions. They are defined under the Trade Union Ordinance (Cap. 332)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-65134d6c88195bfcc2ac0100392eb0d3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOCK-OUTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lock-outs involve employers stopping operations and refusing entry to workers, often as a response to strikes or other labor disputes. Defined in The Employment Ordinance (Cap. 599) and the Trade Union Ordinance (Cap. 332)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-65134d6c88195bfcc2ac0100392eb0d3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OPERATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An operation here refers to the process of transferring ownership or control within a business context as described in Article 5."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-65134d6c88195bfcc2ac0100392eb0d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 101}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 531}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT PERIOD CONTINUITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The concept of employment period continuity is maintained even when there are changes such as transfers between employers, as stated in Articles 4 and 5."</data>
