</node>
<node id="&quot;FIFTH SCHEDULE (REPEALED SINCE JUNE 27, 1998)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Fifth Schedule was repealed from June 27, 1998. Its contents before the repeal are provided in a table format detailing long service payments for employees based on their age and years of service."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a5e77a632eea87bc5c9d8f63b609eb9c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TABLE (COLUMN 1: AGE; COLUMN 2: YEARS OF SERVICE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Table provides details about long service payments to employees, categorizing them by age and years of service. It is a product or document used in the legal framework for compensation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a5e77a632eea87bc5c9d8f63b609eb9c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEATH OF EMPLOYER—LONG SERVICE PAYMENTS (FORMAT CHANGES—E.R. 3 OF 2017)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Death of Employer—Long Service Payments ordinance, with format changes effective from E.R. 3 of 2017, deals with long service payments to employees in the event of their employer's death."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a5e77a632eea87bc5c9d8f63b609eb9c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER'S DEATH (FORMAT CHANGES)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event refers to the legal provisions related to handling situations where an employer dies, including changes made in 2017 regarding format and payment procedures for long service payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a5e77a632eea87bc5c9d8f63b609eb9c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEATH OF EMPLOYER—LONG SERVICE PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Death of Employer—Long Service Payments is an event related to the termination and payment policies for employees when their employer passes away, involving legal provisions and conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bbdbf6e636df660b4b25abee0836e54e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER'S ESTATE REPRESENTATIVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Employer's Estate Representative refers to a person appointed by the deceased employer who manages the estate and can renew or rehire an employee after the death of the employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bbdbf6e636df660b4b25abee0836e54e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT RENEWAL/RE-EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employment Contract Renewal/Re-employment is an event where contracts are renewed or new ones are signed by the Employer's Estate Representative, potentially affecting employment status and long service payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bbdbf6e636df660b4b25abee0836e54e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINUOUS EMPLOYMENT PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Continuous Employment Period refers to a period of uninterrupted work that may be considered for long service payment calculations even after the death of an employer if renewed or re-employment occurs within four weeks from the date of death."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bbdbf6e636df660b4b25abee0836e54e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CAP 57 RTF (14-05-2026)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cap 57 RTF is a specific piece of legislation or legal document that outlines the rights and obligations related to employment contracts after an employer's death, effective from May 14, 2026."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cap 57 RTF is legislation or legal document that outlines specific provisions related to employment contracts and the rights of employees after their employer's death, effective from May 14, 2026."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is a reference to the Employment Ordinance of Hong Kong, specifically version dated May 14, 2026, which outlines legal protections and rights for employees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c826449cd8715ca847fb4ea3433d8bf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85644a914cfa94d353943cc7d1724450</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 170}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 702}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 31Z&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 31Z refers to a clause in Cap 57 RTF that deals with changes in business ownership and its impact on employee contracts after the employer's death."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85644a914cfa94d353943cc7d1724450</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 170}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 702}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 31ZB&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 31ZB is another legal provision within Cap 57 RTF, used to treat the death of an employer as a termination event for employment purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85644a914cfa94d353943cc7d1724450</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 170}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 702}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART VB OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part VB of this Ordinance is a legal provision that outlines rules and responsibilities related to employment and long service payments in certain contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Part VB refers to specific sections or provisions in legislation that deal with certain aspects of employee rights and business operations after the death of an employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85644a914cfa94d353943cc7d1724450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2419e9b08cdfdf99b66599d9de26ba7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 170}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 702}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 31R OR 31RA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sections 31R and 31RA are legal clauses within Cap 57 RTF that specify conditions for continuous employment service, which may be affected by changes in business ownership after the death of an employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85644a914cfa94d353943cc7d1724450</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 170}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 702}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT FOR THE REQUISITE NUMBER OF YEARS OF SERVICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A continuous contract for a specific period refers to uninterrupted employment over a defined timeframe, crucial for determining eligibility under certain legal provisions like 31R or 31RA."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85644a914cfa94d353943cc7d1724450</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENEWAL OR RE-ENGAGEMENT TAKING EFFECT NOT LATER THAN 4 WEEKS AFTER THE DEATH OF THE DECEASED EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to a situation where an employee's contract is renewed by a personal representative within four weeks following the death of their original employer, which can affect how employment continuity and service years are calculated."&lt;SEP&gt;"This event refers to when an employee's contract is renewed by a personal representative within four weeks following the death of their original employer, which can affect how employment continuity and service years are calculated."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85644a914cfa94d353943cc7d1724450</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERVAL BETWEEN THE DEATH AND THE DATE ON WHICH THE RENEWAL OR RE-ENGAGEMENT TAKES EFFECT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This interval refers to the period from when an employee's employer dies until a new contract is renewed by a personal representative, during which time employment continuity may be considered for certain legal purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85644a914cfa94d353943cc7d1724450</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NUMBER OF YEARS OF SERVICE SPECIFIED IN SECTION 31R OR 31RA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the specific number of continuous years required under sections 31R and 31RA, which are used to determine eligibility for certain benefits or rights related to employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85644a914cfa94d353943cc7d1724450</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WEEK WHICH FALLS WITHIN THAT INTERVAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A week during this period is considered significant as it can affect the calculation of continuous service years under legal provisions like 31R and 31RA, impacting an employee's eligibility for certain benefits or rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85644a914cfa94d353943cc7d1724450</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT RENEWAL BY A PERSONAL REPRESENTATIVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to the act where a new employment agreement is signed with a personal representative of the deceased employer within four weeks after their death, which can affect how an employee's service years are counted for legal purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85644a914cfa94d353943cc7d1724450</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RE-ENGAGEMENT UNDER A NEW CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT BY SUCH A PERSONAL REPRESENTATIVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to the situation where an employee is rehired or given a new contract after their original employer has died, with this action being taken by a personal representative."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85644a914cfa94d353943cc7d1724450</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TREATMENT AS NOT HAVING BEEN DISMISSED BY REASON OF A RENEWAL OR RE-ENGAGEMENT TAKING EFFECT AFTER THE DEATH OF THE DECEASED EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to a legal scenario where an employee is considered not dismissed due to their contract being renewed or them being rehired within four weeks following the death of their original employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85644a914cfa94d353943cc7d1724450</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TREATMENT AS HAVING BEEN EMPLOYED UNDER A CONTINUOUS CONTRACT FOR THE REQUISITE NUMBER OF YEARS OF SERVICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to how an employee's employment is treated in terms of continuity and length, which can affect eligibility for certain benefits or rights under legal provisions like 31R or 31RA."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85644a914cfa94d353943cc7d1724450</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 589}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1142}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TREATMENT AS NOT BEING BROKEN BY ANY WEEK WHICH FALLS WITHIN THAT INTERVAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to how the continuity of an employee's service is treated during a specific period, ensuring it remains uninterrupted for legal purposes even if there are breaks in employment due to changes after their employer's death."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85644a914cfa94d353943cc7d1724450</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEATH OF THE DECEASED EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event refers to the passing away of a business owner or employer, which triggers certain legal actions and obligations regarding their employees' contracts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85644a914cfa94d353943cc7d1724450</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 170}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 704}]</data>
</node>
