<node id="&quot;CONVENTION AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Convention Award refers to a decision made under international conventions, which can be enforced either through legal proceedings or according to specific procedures outlined by relevant laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Convention award is a decision made by an arbitrator or arbitral tribunal based on the terms of an arbitration agreement, often binding on the parties involved."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Convention award is a legal decision that may be enforced or refused based on certain conditions as outlined in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Convention award refers to an arbitration award that falls under the scope of certain international conventions, though not explicitly detailed in this text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Convention award refers to an arbitration decision made in a country or territory outside mainland China, where that country or territory is a party to the New York Convention."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3136488efa6b0856e563bdafbaaa1633&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-603a9b33a6e3900af70fd439592326ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38b4dba8dcefb2d368c753859f749fd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4494c24ec2905c2010570a5a5156b75e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 819}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A dispute is a disagreement between parties over rights, obligations, or other matters which may lead to legal action if not resolved amicably."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dispute includes differences and disagreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e027acdec4c66c21703cf2589ec26926</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 784}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HKIAC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"HKIAC refers to the Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre, which makes appointments of arbitrators as per the ordinance mentioned."&lt;SEP&gt;"HKIAC refers to the Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre, which plays a role in appointing arbitrators when parties fail to agree on an appointment procedure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre (HKIAC) is an incorporated limited liability company established under the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 32) in force at the relevant time."&lt;SEP&gt;"The HKIAC (Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre) is an institution that decides the number of arbitrators in certain arbitration cases if parties fail to agree and section 1 of Schedule 2 does not apply."&lt;SEP&gt;"The HKIAC is an organization that may appoint a mediator in arbitration proceedings and has the authority to make such appointments under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre is an organization that can establish rules to facilitate its own operations and perform certain judicial or arbitral functions as specified by relevant laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-95a4de41db58b9a101c75606869df8f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-678280ae191a89f40bc665d65f091cbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d812128591f21f04c27e6ee77e7d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dd6cc93acdd87603565c28f0e5d9386</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 235}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 872}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEW YORK CONVENTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"New York Convention refers to a convention that defines conditions and methods of becoming a party state, with provisions on enforcement and recognition by specified organizations or entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The New York Convention is the 'Convention on the Recognition and Enforcement of Foreign Arbitral Awards' signed in New York on June 10, 1958."&lt;SEP&gt;"The New York Convention refers to the Convention on the Recognition and Enforcement of Foreign Arbitral Awards, signed at New York on 10 June 1958."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ed6ba602b145c3cd359dd6dda74e3b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 819}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMISSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Commission refers to the United Nations Commission on International Trade Law (UNCITRAL)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commission refers to a governing body that has the authority to adopt legal definitions and agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commission refers to the United Nations Commission on International Trade Law (UNCITRAL)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commission refers to the body that adopted certain provisions related to interim measures and preliminary orders for arbitration processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6028b01799478cec839282a4d1179b1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d56571b98ba26116ef651214c379b2f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 243}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 904}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONVENTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Convention refers to the 1958 International Convention on Recognition and Enforcement of Foreign Arbitral Awards signed in New York."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6028b01799478cec839282a4d1179b1b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 783}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1181}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MACAO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Macao is mentioned as part of China other than Hong Kong and Taiwan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Macao is the jurisdiction from which Macao Awards originate, involving arbitration decisions that can be enforced in Hong Kong under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Macao refers to Macao Special Administrative Region of China."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6028b01799478cec839282a4d1179b1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec95a82e50ec8c3adae1748b384fca48</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 843}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MACAO AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Macao Award is an arbitral award made in accordance with the laws of Macao."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Macao Award is an arbitration decision that can be enforced in Hong Kong under specific conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Macao award is a legal decision that can be enforced under certain conditions and requires evidence such as the original or certified copy of the award and agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Macao award is a legal decision that may be enforced under certain conditions, but can also be set aside or suspended by a competent authority of Macao or under the law of Macao."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Macao award refers to a decision made by an arbitration tribunal in Macau that is recognized and enforceable under certain conditions within Hong Kong, as detailed in the relevant sections of the ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Macao award refers to arbitration awards related to Macao, distinct from those in Hong Kong and the Mainland."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a8178e8eb442ffa0ed10eccd55c6223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3136488efa6b0856e563bdafbaaa1633&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec95a82e50ec8c3adae1748b384fca48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6028b01799478cec839282a4d1179b1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53aea00b88989df2a0f5c9c8eaf66aa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 64}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Interim Measure is a temporary action taken by the arbitral tribunal, which can be modified, suspended, or terminated based on applications from parties or in exceptional circumstances. It involves providing appropriate guarantees as required."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Interim Measure is a temporary order or direction issued during arbitration proceedings that can affect cost assessments and payment orders."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Interim Measure is a temporary order or direction that can be included as part of the commands or directions made by an arbitral tribunal, which may include measures taken before final judgment to preserve rights and obligations between parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Interim Measure is a temporary order or directive issued during arbitration proceedings to preserve the status quo or protect rights until final resolution. It can be enforced by competent courts under specific circumstances."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Interim Measure refers to temporary actions taken by the Arbitral Tribunal in response to a dispute before a final decision is made."&lt;SEP&gt;"An interim measure is a temporary action requested before a final decision and includes directives not to frustrate the purpose of such measures as outlined under Article 17B(2)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interim Measure refers to a temporary order issued by the arbitral tribunal in response to a request from one party. It can include actions like preventing certain behaviors until the final decision is made."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interim measure in this context likely refers to temporary orders or actions taken during arbitration proceedings that are akin to interim measures in legal contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interim measure is a product or tool used within arbitral proceedings as described by sections 39 to 42."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interim measure refers to a temporary order or directive granted by The Court in relation to arbitral proceedings, which may include injunctions but excludes orders under section 60."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interim measures are temporary actions taken by arbitration tribunals or courts, as defined under specific legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-610c6dec3dfd2d606eea19c4dfbadfa7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4667827d445ebb505094eb4b58494cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a8aef97985d67c64a247cd4ac0838cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6028b01799478cec839282a4d1179b1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae42208132627b8d5ff98d4e7966f28e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6127a28d22b5d9d9145842f6c4caba9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6100d8c7e7c5fa3f9af262a8c8cb68f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44743bbc15d45a8109ce653b3d495eca</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 897}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1207}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE OF PROTECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Interim Measure of Protection is a court-issued measure requested by parties before or during arbitral proceedings to provide temporary relief until the final decision is made."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interim protective measures are a type of interim measure with a focus on providing immediate protection to parties involved in disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6028b01799478cec839282a4d1179b1b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 161}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE OLD ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Old Ordinance refers to the repealed Arbitration Ordinance (Chapter 341) that was replaced by new legislation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6028b01799478cec839282a4d1179b1b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMISSION (貿法委)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Commission refers to the United Nations Commission on International Trade Law, which deals with international trade law matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 875}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1195}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONVENTION AWARD (公約裁決)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Convention Award is an arbitral decision made in a State or territory that is party to the New York Convention but not China or any part of it."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 881}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1197}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT (原訟法庭)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Court refers to the Court of First Instance of the High Court, which handles initial legal proceedings and cases before higher courts in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 786}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE (爭議)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Dispute is a difference or disagreement between parties that may be resolved through arbitration or other means."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FUNCTION (職能)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Function includes powers and duties, referring to the roles and responsibilities of individuals or entities in legal proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HKIAC (香港國際仲裁中心)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The HKIAC is the Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre, a company incorporated under the Companies Ordinance as a guarantee limited entity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 881}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1197}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE (臨時措施)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Interim Measure is a temporary order granted by an arbitral tribunal or court to protect parties' interests during arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 786}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MACAO (澳門)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Macao refers to the Macao Special Administrative Region, part of China with its own legal system and autonomy in certain areas."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MACAO AWARD (澳門裁決)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Macao Award is an arbitral decision made according to Macao's arbitration law within its territory."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 881}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1197}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINLAND (內地)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Mainland refers to the part of China excluding Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 783}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1181}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINLAND AWARD (內地裁決)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Mainland Award is an arbitral decision made in accordance with the Arbitration Law of the People's Republic of China within its territory."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 881}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1197}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDIATION (調解)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mediation is a process where a neutral third party assists disputing parties to reach a voluntary agreement, often used as an alternative or preliminary step before arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 784}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINLAND CHINA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mainland refers to the part of China excluding Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 843}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION LAW OF THE PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Arbitration Law of the People's Republic of China is a legal framework for arbitration proceedings in Mainland China."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 819}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 341)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Arbitration Ordinance (Cap. 341) is a repealed ordinance that was replaced by the new arbitration laws mentioned in this text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TAIWAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Taiwan is part of China, separate from Hong Kong and Macao."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 429}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIM OR COUNTER-CLAIM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Claim or Counter-claim is a legal action made in an arbitration proceeding, where one party makes a claim against another and the other may counter-claim."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 843}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration Rules are procedural guidelines that parties agree to follow during their arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration Rules are the guidelines used for appointing and operating Emergency Arbitrators, including those from permanent arbitral institutions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration Rules are the procedural guidelines that govern how emergency arbitrations and related enforcement actions should be conducted."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0813ab9a59ae553fa1d3747bf42131f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad963d62d75768847794433df9caf4b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 410}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1113}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Defence is a legal argument presented in response to a claim or counter-claim made by the opposing party in an arbitration proceeding."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 53 AND SECTION 68 OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sections 53 and 68 refer to specific provisions within the ordinance that have special conditions for application, such as not applying to counter-claims or defences to counter-claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 429}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 53 OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 53 refers to a provision in the ordinance that applies specifically to claims and may also apply to counter-claims under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 429}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 68 OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 68 refers to another specific provision within the ordinance, distinct from Section 53, which has its own set of application rules."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SCHEDULE 1 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ON INTERNATIONAL COMMERCIAL ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Schedule 1 contains the full text of the UNCITRAL Model Law on International Commercial Arbitration as adopted and amended by the Commission, providing a detailed framework for international commercial arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 429}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMISSION ON UNCITRAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Commission refers to the United Nations Commission on International Trade Law (UNCITRAL) which is responsible for developing legal texts such as the Model Law on International Commercial Arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 429}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONCILIATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conciliation, included in mediation, is a process where parties attempt to resolve disputes through negotiation and compromise without formal arbitration or litigation processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 429}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPEALED ORDINANCE (CAP. 341)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Repealed Ordinance (Cap. 341) refers to the previous Arbitration Ordinance that was replaced by new laws and regulations mentioned in this text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 429}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COUNTER-CLAIMANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Counter-claimant is a party who makes a counter-claim against the original claimant in an arbitration proceeding, presenting their own legal action or defense to the initial claim."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Arbitration Proceeding is the formal process through which parties resolve their dispute before an arbitral tribunal according to agreed-upon rules and procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Arbitration proceeding is a process where disputes between parties are resolved through an arbitral tribunal following specific rules and agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration Proceeding is a process where disputes are resolved through arbitration, involving rights or legal responsibilities related to intellectual property (IP)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration Proceeding refers to the process where an arbitral tribunal makes decisions on disputes, often involving the calculation of interest on awarded amounts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration proceeding is a process in which disputes are resolved through binding decisions made by an arbitrator or arbitral tribunal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration proceeding is an event where disputes between parties are resolved through a tribunal as described by various sections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2b2fac04904854d200ea9c9161cb98c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b2687bf72645c6f4d1292a242f8ee55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a7d382b60c68c418d8128c80396b687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6eef98cdb7cf96d52a56e0103910d67</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 62}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERNATIONAL COMMERCIAL ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"International Commercial Arbitration is a specialized form of dispute resolution used for commercial transactions across borders, governed by international laws and practices such as those outlined in UNCITRAL Model Law."&lt;SEP&gt;"This refers to a specialized field dealing with commercial disputes between parties from different countries, often resolved through arbitration rather than traditional court systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"This term refers to a specific type of arbitration involving commercial disputes between parties from different countries. It is governed by rules and procedures designed to ensure fair resolution of such conflicts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-603a9b33a6e3900af70fd439592326ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 429}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OBJECT OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Object of this Ordinance is an objective statement that guides its purpose in promoting fair and speedy resolution of disputes through arbitration without unnecessary expense."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c8bbf5a007054d5e9238f9704d8e1b9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 350}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRINCIPLES OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These principles are guiding concepts underlying the Ordinance, emphasizing freedom for parties to agree on dispute resolution methods and limiting court interference except as expressly provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c8bbf5a007054d5e9238f9704d8e1b9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 350}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRADE FACILITATION COMMISSION示范法例&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Trade Facilitation Commission 示范法例 refers to a model law that is recognized in Hong Kong with certain amendments and supplements, providing legal basis for arbitration procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trade Facilitation Commission 示范法例 refers to guidelines or examples provided by the Trade Facilitation Commission, which may include rules on interest calculations in arbitral proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7a7d382b60c68c418d8128c80396b687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c8bbf5a007054d5e9238f9704d8e1b9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 350}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OBJECT OF THIS ORDINANCE (ENGLISH VERSION)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Object of this Ordinance as stated in English aims at facilitating fair and speedy resolution of disputes through arbitration without unnecessary expense."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c8bbf5a007054d5e9238f9704d8e1b9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 350}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRINCIPLES OF THIS ORDINANCE (ENGLISH VERSION)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These principles, as outlined in the English version, emphasize parties' freedom to agree on dispute resolution methods and limit court interference except as expressly provided for by law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c8bbf5a007054d5e9238f9704d8e1b9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 350}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT INTERFERENCE IN ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court interference in arbitration is an event that may occur when a court decides to intervene in the arbitration process as expressly provided for by law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8c1c54aae15fa21fd2f3fa9a3916e793</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 722}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The UNCITRAL Model Law is referenced as providing guidance or rules for arbitration procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd3867158c784daaa4eb73ead4db9ca6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 346}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1040}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GENERAL PROVISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"General Provisions are the overarching legal principles or rules that apply across different sections of an ordinance, as noted in relation to format changes made in 2018."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea2051734d4010ecf353d49c7190a3cf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 303}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 992}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 1&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 1 of UNCITRAL Model Law is referenced here and indicates the scope of application for arbitration proceedings under this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea2051734d4010ecf353d49c7190a3cf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 303}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 992}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 1 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 1 of the UNCITRAL Model Law was previously in effect but has been superseded by Section 5 according to the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-44b140c12657294fe5c5d3a3a3fddb7b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 60}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 2 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 2 of the UNCITRAL Model Law is being replaced and its definitions are being reinterpreted within another document, indicating a significant change in legal context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-44b140c12657294fe5c5d3a3a3fddb7b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 429}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 5&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 5 has taken effect to replace Article 1 of the UNCITRAL Model Law, signifying an update or amendment in the legal framework."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 5 refers to another part of the same legislative text which is overridden by Part 10A when dealing with specific arbitration scenarios."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-358c63f61ec2ce4f0f9b4f0675b579e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44b140c12657294fe5c5d3a3a3fddb7b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 60}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 2A OF THE UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ARTICLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 2A is a specific section within the UNCITRAL Model Law that addresses international origin and general principles in legal interpretation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3694b9973d0eb7e4719ad33e81b8744f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 15}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 210}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 3 OF THE UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ARTICLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 3 is another section within the UNCITRAL Model Law that deals with receiving written communications between parties without specific agreements to the contrary."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3694b9973d0eb7e4719ad33e81b8744f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 429}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 3 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 3 details the procedures for determining when a written communication has been received in various scenarios, including personal delivery or mail."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-526d89a1459376fe55b0af078fc2a455</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 244}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 908}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WRITTEN COMMUNICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Written communication refers to any form of documented message that can be sent and recorded as per Article 3 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-526d89a1459376fe55b0af078fc2a455</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 244}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 907}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HABITUAL RESIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Habitual residence is the regular or usual place of living for an individual, used as a reference point when no other place of business exists."&lt;SEP&gt;"Habitual residence refers to a person's usual place of living and can be considered for determining receipt under certain conditions as per Article 3 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-526d89a1459376fe55b0af078fc2a455&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e027acdec4c66c21703cf2589ec26926</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 244}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 909}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAILING ADDRESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mailing address is the physical location where mail or documents are sent, used in Article 3 to determine when a written communication has been received."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-526d89a1459376fe55b0af078fc2a455</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 244}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 908}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTERED LETTER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Registered letter is a method of sending written communications that provides proof of delivery and can be used as per Article 3 of UNCITRAL Model Law for determining receipt."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-526d89a1459376fe55b0af078fc2a455</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 244}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 908}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 4&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 4 addresses the waiver of right to object in an arbitration process if a party proceeds without stating objection within a reasonable time frame."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4125722b26dc9c686c88dca771d7712f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT INTERVENTION LIMITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court intervention limits refer to restrictions on judicial interference in matters governed by specific laws, such as UNCITRAL Model Law Article 5."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4125722b26dc9c686c88dca771d7712f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 5 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 5 defines the extent of court intervention, stating that courts shall not intervene except where provided for within this law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4125722b26dc9c686c88dca771d7712f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HONG KONG INTERNATIONAL ARBITRATION CENTRE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre is a body responsible for appointing mediators and handling arbitration cases according to specific agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre is an institution responsible for appointing arbitrators when necessary, especially in cases where parties fail to reach agreements or comply with the appointed procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre is an organization responsible for appointing arbitrators in certain circumstances, as described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre is an organization tasked with executing certain functions mentioned in Articles related to arbitration assistance and supervision."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4125722b26dc9c686c88dca771d7712f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8dac8ba7cc8864d7ff7dc57b5b28604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23b1f9e25ad7b2970cb215d6bd454574&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aa40d92e810c15d1924e632ab83962f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 855}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHIEF JUDGE OF THE终审法院&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Chief Judge of the final appeal court has the authority to approve rules for the execution of specific center functions by the Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4125722b26dc9c686c88dca771d7712f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 855}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPETENT COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Competent Court is another term used within the legal framework, referring to a specific court with jurisdiction over certain arbitration-related matters."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Competent Court is the judicial authority that can enforce interim measures issued by an arbitral tribunal, as long as it complies with certain conditions outlined in Article 17I."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-20600c9214528cc8c5fe5923e8a061ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-610c6dec3dfd2d606eea19c4dfbadfa7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 809}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;時效條例 (第347章)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The 时效条例 (第347章) refers to an existing law concerning statutes of limitations that apply in both litigation and arbitration, as described in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-20600c9214528cc8c5fe5923e8a061ca</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 809}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;仲裁協議&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration Agreement is a contract between parties stipulating matters to be submitted for arbitration, referenced in the context of legal procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 'Arbitration Agreement' is a legal document where parties agree to submit disputes for arbitration in their defined contractual or non-contractual relationship. It can be an arbitration clause within the contract or as a separate agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20600c9214528cc8c5fe5923e8a061ca</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 809}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE LIMITATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 347)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Limitation Ordinance is a legal document that sets out the time limits for commencing actions in court, and it applies to arbitrations as if they were court proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-026f8c614649cf19151a207c9397cdd7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 842}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT ORDER SETTING ASIDE AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A court order setting aside an award occurs when a court decides that an arbitral decision should not stand, and this event affects the computation of limitation periods for legal actions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-026f8c614649cf19151a207c9397cdd7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 842}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERPLEADER PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interpleader proceedings refer to legal processes where multiple parties seek relief from a court regarding the same disputed matter."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d01af5189922031b9258e77aa6012d87</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 846}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIMANT(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Claimants are individuals or entities involved in interpleader proceedings, seeking resolution of disputes through arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d01af5189922031b9258e77aa6012d87</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 846}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NON-PUBLIC HEARING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Non-public hearing is a method of conducting legal proceedings where information is not disclosed publicly, and it can be ordered by the court under specific circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3977494e2da78f664ddb0fbbd085bf83</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OPEN COURT PROCEEDING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Open court proceeding refers to a legal process conducted in public, which may be ordered or stayed based on certain conditions as stated in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3977494e2da78f664ddb0fbbd085bf83</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 249}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 912}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPORTING RESTRICTIONS FOR NON-PUBLIC HEARINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Reporting restrictions are limitations placed by courts on the publication of information related to non-public hearings, ensuring confidentiality and privacy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3977494e2da78f664ddb0fbbd085bf83</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NON-PUBLIC COURT PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Non-public court procedure refers to the legal proceedings held in private, as described under section 1 of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db21b6924967f080042e677399758e3c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1189}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT'S RULING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The court's ruling is a decision made by the court on non-public court procedures, which can have significant legal implications according to Section 4 of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db21b6924967f080042e677399758e3c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1189}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL REPORTING AND PROFESSIONAL JOURNALS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal reporting and professional journals are mediums through which certain court rulings may be published as per section 4 of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db21b6924967f080042e677399758e3c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1189}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT DIRECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A court direction is made regarding the publication of information related to closed court proceedings, which may be published only if all parties agree or the court finds that publishing would not reveal any confidential matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5f33b7b9020135f31323fbae5f4463c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 309}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLOSED COURT PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Closed court proceedings are legal hearings held in private where certain information cannot be disclosed without a specific court direction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5f33b7b9020135f31323fbae5f4463c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 309}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAW REPORTS AND PROFESSIONAL PUBLICATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Law reports and professional publications refer to official documents or journals that may publish judgments if they meet the criteria set by the court."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5f33b7b9020135f31323fbae5f4463c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 309}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;10 YEARS RESTRICTION ON PUBLICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A 10-year period is imposed during which certain information, even if published in law reports and professional publications, cannot be disclosed until after this period expires."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5f33b7b9020135f31323fbae5f4463c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 309}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Arbitration Award is a formal decision made by an arbitral tribunal that resolves disputes according to contract terms and applicable trade usages, often recorded as a binding legal document."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Arbitration Award is the formal document issued by the Arbitral Tribunal based on the agreed terms of the parties, as detailed in Articles 30 and 31."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Arbitration Award refers to the decision made by arbitrators which can be subject to review or set-aside under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"An arbitration award is the decision made by an arbitrator in an arbitration proceeding, which cannot be disclosed without specific permission from the court as per the Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"An arbitration award refers to a written decision made by arbitrators in disputes, stating reasons if agreed upon by parties, and signed by majority members when multiple arbitrators are involved."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration award is a decision made by an arbitration tribunal which may be enforceable under specific ordinances or laws, including those related to Hong Kong's legal system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration award is the decision made by an arbitration tribunal on disputes between parties, which can be recognized and enforced under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration award is the final decision made by an arbitral tribunal in resolving disputes between parties through arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration award refers to the decision made by an arbitration tribunal that can be enforced under certain ordinances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f35bbfd9ee83b0701ea2384c506063d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5f33b7b9020135f31323fbae5f4463c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19092b2cdc4468b2128aef41dc2b2b67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03bb9907c4707aee4e32c05a81efe12a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aba64861ea22070188d9b7dd4c0fd47a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd8b5a6b74d6568cda4bfce7dd132460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 309}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitral Proceedings are legal processes where arbitrators make decisions, potentially involving multiple hearings or consolidations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitral Proceedings are the formal process of resolving disputes between parties as outlined in their arbitration agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitral Proceedings are the process through which disputes between parties are resolved by a neutral third party (the arbitral tribunal)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitral Proceedings refer to procedures conducted for resolving disputes through arbitration, not subject to certain sections of The Legal Practitioners Ordinance (Cap. 159)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitral Proceedings refer to the formal process of resolving disputes through arbitration. This includes both arbitral and mediation proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitral Proceedings refer to the process of resolving disputes through arbitration, which can be terminated under certain conditions as described in Article 32."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitral proceedings refer to the formal process of resolving disputes through arbitration, which can be paused or continued based on mediation activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitral proceedings refer to the process where disputes are resolved through arbitration as per an agreement between parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitral proceedings refer to the process where parties involved in a dispute submit their case for resolution through arbitration as per an existing arbitration agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ff2369343594485564382d2d30ba3755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42e0db1f27b3313444cf12ec497ffd57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5a62633bac9b2c0c6ed1e0aa83ce66e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da3d7a01706de39cd849092deef8b9b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5943028cc6f3beb70826c83454e86767&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd6c63034b5446fb90d89932614a5d4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a820d49f72ef3eeb5be9d057a9cb248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85b8cad9edd61a2498008aaa9412835f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-655dbcc67746c1c9fceca1a4e089796b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 917}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Award is a decision or judgment made by an arbitral tribunal, which resolves the dispute and provides binding instructions for the parties involved."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Award is the final decision made by an Arbitral Tribunal in resolving disputes during arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"An award is a formal decision or judgment issued by an arbitral tribunal, resolving disputes between parties in arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Award is the final decision made by an arbitrator or arbitral tribunal in a dispute, subject to certain conditions for enforcement and set-aside procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Award refers to a decision made by arbitrators, which is binding on the parties involved and resolves the dispute according to the rules set out in the arbitration agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Award refers to the decision or judgment made by an arbitral tribunal in resolving a dispute between parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Award refers to the final decision made by an arbitral tribunal in accordance with an arbitration agreement or process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Award refers to the final decision made by the arbitral tribunal, which can be confirmed, varied, or set aside by the Court."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Award is the final decision made by the arbitral tribunal in arbitration proceedings, which can be remitted for reconsideration or set aside if there's serious irregularity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5a62633bac9b2c0c6ed1e0aa83ce66e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e5ed4af08fa3d54713649e0adf6d0ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e17ae2e1dd0c38e2c8a34618b769e578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63fa361a4bbae312d93826ee30bf2182&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4373f38dac5749d35f8ccd70b8bf1d15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b2fac04904854d200ea9c9161cb98c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-655dbcc67746c1c9fceca1a4e089796b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d56571b98ba26116ef651214c379b2f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 879}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT OR OTHER JUDICIAL AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to an organization that handles legal proceedings such as courts and other judicial bodies within Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"This term generally refers to legal institutions like courts and tribunals that have the power to hear cases and make decisions in accordance with law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0cc9146e12fcb8f714add3a3f7c0771b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a252d91181bacec6fcd6f1d54297b19a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 445}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOVERNMENT BODY, REGULATORY BODY, COURT OR TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are organizations mentioned in the text where publication, disclosure or communication may be made under certain obligations by law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0cc9146e12fcb8f714add3a3f7c0771b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 838}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROFESSIONAL OR ANY OTHER ADVISER OF ANY OF THE PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to individuals who provide professional advice and can include various types of advisors for the involved parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0cc9146e12fcb8f714add3a3f7c0771b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 428}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;貿法委示範法第7條(仲裁協議的定義和形式)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to Article 7 of a Model Law on Arbitration which defines what constitutes an arbitration agreement and its forms. It is part of the legal framework for resolving disputes through arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0cc9146e12fcb8f714add3a3f7c0771b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DATA电文&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Data電文 refers to electronic means of communication as defined in the text, including any form of data transmission via digital or similar methods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0cc9146e12fcb8f714add3a3f7c0771b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OPTION I OF ARTICLE 7 OF THE UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a specific clause in an international legal document defining and specifying forms of arbitration agreements, including oral or written contracts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DATA ELECTRIC EXCHANGE (EDI)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Data Electronic Exchange, also known as EDI, refers to electronic data interchange between organizations in a standard format agreed by both parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMAIL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Email is an electronic mail service used for sending and receiving messages electronically over the internet or other networks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TELEGRAPH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A telegraph is an early form of long-distance communication that uses electrical signals to transmit written information, typically through a wire network."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FACSIMILE (FAX)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A fax machine or facsimile is used for sending and receiving documents over telephone lines in the form of scanned images."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MODEL LAW ARTICLE 7. DEFINITION AND FORM OF ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This article defines what constitutes an arbitration agreement, including various forms such as written or electronic communications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WRITTEN CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Written Contract is a formal document that outlines the terms agreed upon by parties involved in a business transaction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORAL AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Oral Agreement refers to an agreement made verbally, which may or may not be legally binding depending on local laws and practices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MUTUAL CLAIM STATEMENT AND DEFENSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are documents where parties involved in a dispute present their claims and defenses respectively, often used as evidence of the existence of an arbitration agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REFERENCE TO WRITTEN ARBITRATION CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to mentioning or referencing specific clauses related to arbitration within written contracts, which can be considered part of the formal agreement if it is acknowledged by all parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUTHORIZATION FOR RECORDING AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This involves one party authorizing another to record an agreement in writing, even if not signed by both parties, as long as such recording is done under their authorization."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STANDARD FORMAT OF ARBITRATION CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A standard format for arbitration clauses that can be included within contracts to ensure clarity and enforceability of the agreement in case of disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION THROUGH ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dispute Resolution Through Arbitration is an event where conflicting parties submit their issues to an arbitral tribunal for resolution, which can involve cost assessments and payment determinations based on the nature of the dispute and relevant legal frameworks."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process of resolving conflicts or disagreements between parties by submitting them to an arbitrator who makes a binding decision based on the evidence and arguments presented."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TELECOMMUNICATION NETWORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are networks used for transmitting information over long distances, including telephone lines which were historically used for telegraph services but now include modern digital communication systems."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STANDARDIZED COMMUNICATION FORMATS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Formats that ensure consistent and clear communication between parties in international business transactions to avoid misunderstandings or disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERNATIONAL TRADE LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the body of law governing trade relations across national borders, including rules for arbitration agreements as outlined by UNCITRAL Model Laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 886}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1199}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ELECTRONIC DATA INTERCHANGE (EDI)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A method used in business transactions where data is exchanged electronically between organizations using standardized formats and protocols to ensure accuracy and efficiency of information exchange."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMAIL COMMUNICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The use of electronic mail for communication, which has become a common form of written agreement or confirmation in modern businesses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TELEGRAPHY SERVICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Historical method of long-distance communication using electrical signals transmitted over wires to send and receive messages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FACSIMILE (FAX) MACHINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Devices used for sending and receiving documents as scanned images through telephone lines, a common form of electronic document exchange before the widespread use of email."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DATA COMMUNICATION STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Standards that define how data should be formatted and transmitted to ensure compatibility between different systems in international trade and communication networks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERNATIONAL COMMERCIAL DISPUTES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Disputes arising from commercial transactions involving parties from different countries, often resolved through arbitration as per the UNCITRAL Model Law."&lt;SEP&gt;"The industry of international commercial disputes involves organizations and professionals who handle cross-border business disagreements through arbitration or other dispute resolution mechanisms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WRITTEN COMMUNICATION AGREEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Agreements that are documented in writing, often used as proof or basis for arbitration proceedings when disputes arise between parties involved in international trade transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORAL AGREEMENT ACKNOWLEDGMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Acknowledgment of an oral agreement by one party to another, which can be considered part of a formal agreement if recognized and accepted by all parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STANDARDIZED ARBITRATION CLAUSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Clauses included in contracts that provide for arbitration as the method of dispute resolution, often standardized to ensure clarity and enforceability across different jurisdictions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TELECOMMUNICATION INFRASTRUCTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Telecommunication infrastructure includes underground telecommunication lines, submarine cable landing stations, or any other relevant facilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The network infrastructure used for transmitting information over long distances through various means including telegraphy, telephone lines, and modern digital communication systems."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c91eb1ea65f818d429644871f6909abf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DATA INTERCHANGE STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Standards that define the format and protocol of data exchange to ensure interoperability between different computer systems in international trade and business transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ELECTRONIC COMMUNICATION SYSTEMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Systems used for sending, receiving, and storing information electronically, including email, EDI, telegraphy, and fax machines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 7 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 7 of the UNCITRAL Model Law outlines the definition and form of an arbitration agreement, specifying conditions under which such agreements are considered valid and binding."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-15c5427da69a34465f87e7a3287bd026</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 243}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 903}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OPTION I OF ARTICLE 7&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Option I under Article 7 provides specific conditions and definitions related to the formation of arbitration agreements, including requirements regarding writing and electronic communications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-15c5427da69a34465f87e7a3287bd026</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 243}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 906}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ELECTRONIC COMMUNICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Electronic Communication is any communication made using data messages through various electronic means like EDI, emails, telegrams, telexes, or faxes. It underscores the flexibility and modernity of digital communications in legal contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Electronic Communication is defined here as any communication made by the parties using electronic, magnetic, optical, or similar means. It includes methods like EDI, emails, telegrams, telexes, and faxes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Electronic Communication is defined as any communication made by means of data messages such as EDI, email, telegram, telex or telecopy, which can be used for subsequent reference in forming an arbitration agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15c5427da69a34465f87e7a3287bd026</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 243}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 904}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DATA MESSAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Data Message is defined as information generated, sent, received or stored by electronic means such as EDI, email, telegram, telex, or telecopy. It emphasizes the broad range of digital communications that can be considered valid for arbitration agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Data Message refers to information generated, sent, received, or stored electronically and is a form of electronic communication that can constitute part of an arbitration agreement if recorded properly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15c5427da69a34465f87e7a3287bd026</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 243}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 906}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXCHANGE OF STATEMENTS OF CLAIM AND DEFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Exchange of Statements of Claim and Defence where one party alleges the existence of an arbitration agreement and the other does not deny it, constitutes a written form of such an agreement under Article 7(5)."&lt;SEP&gt;"An exchange of statements of claim and defence in which one party alleges the existence of an agreement while the other does not deny it also constitutes a 'written' arbitration agreement, highlighting alternative methods to establish written agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15c5427da69a34465f87e7a3287bd026</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 243}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 904}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENT CONTAINING ARBITRATION CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Document containing an arbitration clause can be considered part of the contract if referenced in another agreement, thereby constituting a valid arbitration agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-15c5427da69a34465f87e7a3287bd026</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 243}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 903}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT LITIGATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court litigation refers to the process of bringing a dispute before a court for resolution, which can be initiated by one party when an arbitration agreement exists but is contested."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-93da520a07c3f45a47c10cf01594d640</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 847}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LABOR AND MANAGEMENT TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Labor and Management Tribunal is an organization established under the Employment Disputes Resolution Ordinance (Chapter 25 of Laws of Hong Kong) with jurisdiction over certain labor-related claims or disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-93da520a07c3f45a47c10cf01594d640</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 847}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY SEIZURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property seizure refers to the act of taking possession of someone's property by law enforcement or judicial authority."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-211e080c19540ebafb0dc80d25b20e46</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 826}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 8 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 8 of the UNCITRAL Model Law outlines conditions under which parties can be referred to arbitration or when an agreement may not apply."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-524caefeb3520a83b6c8130676f95c53</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 877}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSTANTIVE CLAIM BEFORE COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A substantive claim before the court refers to the actual dispute or case being brought to judicial proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-524caefeb3520a83b6c8130676f95c53</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dispute Resolution involves the processes and methods used to resolve conflicts between parties, as described in the text related to arbitration procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dispute resolution involves methods and processes for settling conflicts or disagreements between parties without resorting to litigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dispute resolution is a broad field of social science that encompasses various methods, including arbitration, mediation, and litigation, used to resolve conflicts between parties in legal or commercial contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dispute resolution is the process of resolving conflicts between parties through various methods including arbitration and mediation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The industry related to dispute resolution involves various organizations and professionals who facilitate conflict resolution processes such as mediation or arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e027acdec4c66c21703cf2589ec26926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-524caefeb3520a83b6c8130676f95c53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edc4c9a782cb874c7fb36432df37d995</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 877}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LITIGATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Litigation refers to legal proceedings in a court of law, which is contrasted with arbitration as an alternative dispute resolution method."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-524caefeb3520a83b6c8130676f95c53</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 877}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY MEASURES BY COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Temporary Measures by Court are actions taken by a court, such as issuing orders for stays of proceedings and retaining property as security, in response to requests from one party during an arbitration process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary measures by court refers to actions taken by courts before or during arbitral proceedings, such as issuing interim orders or injunctions, which may continue even after the referral of disputes to arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a6c644c4a7067336b920f4ea718d504d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd6c63034b5446fb90d89932614a5d4a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 839}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 9 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 9 of the UNCITRAL Model Law discusses arbitration agreements and interim measures, stating that such requests do not contradict an existing agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 161}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMERGENCY ARBITRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Emergency Arbitrator is a person authorized to grant emergency relief pending a full arbitration, often seen as an interim decision-maker."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Emergency Arbitrator is a person with specific meaning given by section 22A in relation to emergency arbitrations."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Emergency Arbitrator is appointed by the parties or according to arbitral rules before the formation of an arbitral tribunal to handle urgent relief applications, providing temporary measures until a final decision is reached."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emergency Arbitrator is a person appointed temporarily to resolve urgent issues before formal arbitration proceedings begin."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emergency Arbitrator is a person appointed to handle emergency assistance applications before an arbitral tribunal is constituted, according to the arbitration rules agreed upon or adopted by the parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emergency Arbitrator is a role defined by Section 22A with its specific meaning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emergency arbitrator is defined in the context of arbitration proceedings involving a specific type of arbitrator appointed for urgent matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0813ab9a59ae553fa1d3747bf42131f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca2c3669141d3f1cd87a21d68d494cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0edcefcdaacd59cb7375b56608a714e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad963d62d75768847794433df9caf4b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 410}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1113}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART 3A OF ENFORCEMENT OF EMERGENCY RELIEF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part 3A deals with the enforcement mechanisms for emergency relief in arbitration proceedings, added by legislation as specified."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEATH OF PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The death of a party does not necessarily discharge an existing arbitration agreement; it can be enforced by or against personal representatives as per Article 22(1) of the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERSONAL REPRESENTATIVES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"In legal contexts, Personal Representatives refer to individuals who manage and enforce rights on behalf of a deceased party, ensuring continuity in arbitration agreements according to local laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENFORCEMENT BY OR AGAINST THE PERSONAL REPRESENTATIVES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the ability for either the personal representatives of a deceased party or those managing their estate to enforce an existing arbitration agreement as per Article 22(1) of the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 161}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXTINGUISHED SUBSTANTIVE RIGHT OR OBLIGATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A substantive right or obligation can be extinguished by the death of an individual according to certain legal rules; however, this does not affect existing arbitration agreements as per Article 22(1) and (2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENACTMENT OR RULE OF LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Enactment or Rule of Law refers to the formalized statutes or legal principles that govern rights and obligations, including those related to the extinction of substantive rights due to death."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2013 AMENDMENT (S. 5)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The amendment in 2013 added Part 3A dealing with emergency relief enforcement, indicating legislative changes affecting arbitration procedures and interim measures as per the provided text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 410}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1113}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMERGENCY RELIEF ENFORCEMENT MECHANISMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mechanisms for enforcing emergency relief are detailed under Part 3A of the text, providing a framework for temporary protective measures in arbitral proceedings before an arbitral tribunal is formed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMERGENCY RELIEF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Emergency Relief is a temporary measure granted by an Emergency Arbitrator to prevent harm or prejudice in arbitration proceedings, which can include maintaining status quo, issuing injunctions, preserving assets, and securing evidence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emergency Relief refers to urgent assistance provided by an emergency arbitrator before a tribunal is constituted, which can include various measures such as maintaining status quo or taking action to prevent harm to the arbitration process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emergency relief refers to urgent measures taken by the court pending the determination of a dispute."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0813ab9a59ae553fa1d3747bf42131f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3161c0abf732689fd0fb63c291711d64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad963d62d75768847794433df9caf4b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 410}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1113}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERMANENT ARBITRAL INSTITUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Permanent Arbitral Institution refers to organizations that provide arbitration services with standardized procedures for appointing emergency arbitrators and handling disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1ad963d62d75768847794433df9caf4b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT OF ORIGIN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court of Origin is the court where a party seeks enforcement of an order or relief, which can be outside Hong Kong in some cases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1ad963d62d75768847794433df9caf4b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 37}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HARM OR DAMAGE PREVENTION MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Harm or Damage Prevention Measures are actions taken to prevent current or imminent harm or damage that could affect the arbitration process, including maintaining status quo and taking preventive steps."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1ad963d62d75768847794433df9caf4b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASSET PRESERVATION METHODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Asset Preservation Methods refer to strategies used by emergency arbitrators to safeguard assets of parties involved in a dispute until an arbitral tribunal makes its decision, ensuring fairness and compliance with future rulings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1ad963d62d75768847794433df9caf4b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATHEMATICS OF ASSET PRESERVATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mathematical Aspects involve calculations and models used in determining how assets should be preserved or valued during the dispute resolution process, ensuring they remain intact until a final decision is made by an arbitral tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1ad963d62d75768847794433df9caf4b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOCIAL SCIENCES PERSPECTIVE ON ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Social Sciences Perspective examines the social implications of arbitration processes, including their impact on parties involved and broader societal norms regarding conflict resolution methods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1ad963d62d75768847794433df9caf4b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 410}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1113}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRAL PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitral process is a term used in legal contexts, referring to the arbitral tribunal's proceedings and activities related to resolving disputes through arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3161c0abf732689fd0fb63c291711d64</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HONG KONG INTERNATIONAL ARBITRATION CENTRE (HKIAC)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The HKIAC plays a crucial role in determining the number of arbitrators when parties fail to agree, ensuring fair and effective arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre (HKIAC) is the institution that decides on the number of arbitrators when parties fail to agree, in cases where Article 10(2) does not apply."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre is an organization responsible for administering arbitrations, making appointments of arbitrators, and ensuring compliance with relevant laws and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3161c0abf732689fd0fb63c291711d64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d812128591f21f04c27e6ee77e7d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 10(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ARTICLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 10(1) of the UNCITRAL Model Law states that parties are free to determine the number of arbitrators, unless otherwise agreed by the parties or specified in section 1 of Schedule 2."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2d812128591f21f04c27e6ee77e7d3c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 235}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 872}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON/ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to individuals or organizations involved in arbitration proceedings and their freedom to agree on the number of arbitrators."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2d812128591f21f04c27e6ee77e7d3c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 11(3) (A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ARTICLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"According to Article 11(3)(a), if parties fail to agree on the number of arbitrators, one party appoints an arbitrator and this appointed arbitrator together with another appointed arbitrator selects a third arbitrator in cases where there are three arbitrators."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2d812128591f21f04c27e6ee77e7d3c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 235}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 872}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 11(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ARTICLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"According to Article 11(2), parties can freely agree on the procedure for appointing one or more arbitrators, subject to certain provisions of this article."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2d812128591f21f04c27e6ee77e7d3c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SCHEDULE 2 SECTION 1&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SECTION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 1 of Schedule 2 is not applicable in cases where the number of arbitrators needs to be decided by HKIAC if parties fail to agree and section 1 does not apply, leading to a decision on whether the number should be one or three."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2d812128591f21f04c27e6ee77e7d3c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to arbitration processes where the number of arbitrators is determined based on agreements between parties or by HKIAC if necessary."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2d812128591f21f04c27e6ee77e7d3c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 235}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 872}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATOR(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An arbitrator is a person appointed by the parties involved in an arbitration agreement to resolve disputes between them."&lt;SEP&gt;"An arbitrator is a person who makes decisions in an arbitration case, and their selection process can be agreed upon by the parties or decided by HKIAC based on certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"An arbitrator or arbitrators are individuals appointed by parties involved in disputes, as per the described process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitrator is a person appointed to resolve disputes through arbitration, ensuring fair and impartial decision-making."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitrator is the role assigned to individuals appointed by parties or courts to resolve disputes through arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitrator(s) are individuals who make decisions in arbitral proceedings and sign award documents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitrators are individuals appointed to resolve disputes between parties through arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitrators are individuals appointed to resolve disputes through arbitration. The Court has the authority to appoint arbitrators for consolidated or simultaneous hearings of arbitral proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitrators are individuals appointed to resolve disputes, with specific rules on their appointment outlined in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitrators are individuals who make decisions on disputes, and their appointment can be made by mutual agreement of the parties or through a process involving the Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e8dac8ba7cc8864d7ff7dc57b5b28604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95a4de41db58b9a101c75606869df8f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e027acdec4c66c21703cf2589ec26926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4487876b424618c4533648d46889bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23b1f9e25ad7b2970cb215d6bd454574&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d812128591f21f04c27e6ee77e7d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59c7140869534366dd7270de77711ef8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad8b00bb4712fdfd27d215a729380d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3bd35452fe0a7b5e9fa7dc2c1f8074&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0cddff72aaf0d2c6f21cba88e08e8e0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 855}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE PARTIES' AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Agreement between parties regarding the number of arbitrators, which is a key aspect of the arbitration proceedings as outlined in UNCITRAL Model Law and related sections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2d812128591f21f04c27e6ee77e7d3c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 235}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 872}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 10(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ARTICLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 10(2) states that the freedom for parties to determine the number of arbitrators includes authorizing a third party or institution like HKIAC to make this determination."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2d812128591f21f04c27e6ee77e7d3c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE PARTIES' RIGHT TO AUTHORIZE THIRD PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This concept refers to the right given to parties in arbitration proceedings to authorize an external body, such as HKIAC, to decide on the number of arbitrators if they cannot agree among themselves."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c2d812128591f21f04c27e6ee77e7d3c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATORS PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Arbitrators Procedure is a method for appointing arbitrators in disputes, involving multiple steps and provisions to ensure the process runs smoothly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07932cfedca106f703c16c8c95ba919e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 856}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1194}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTIES'">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Parties' refers to the individuals or entities involved in a dispute who are required to agree on an arbitration procedure or have it designated by courts or other institutions if agreement cannot be reached."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Parties refer to entities involved in a dispute, including those requesting arbitration and those receiving such requests. They have the authority to agree or disagree with various aspects of the arbitration process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The parties are individuals or entities involved in a dispute and agree on how arbitrators will be selected or default rules apply if no agreement is reached."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-61ef9a8b87aa1cf04b46aaf871b5f39a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07932cfedca106f703c16c8c95ba919e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURTS OR OTHER INSTITUTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Courts or Other Institutions refer to bodies that can intervene and appoint arbitrators when parties fail to reach agreements, ensuring the process is fair and independent."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-07932cfedca106f703c16c8c95ba919e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 856}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1194}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE TRADE FACILITATION COMMISSION示范法&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Trade Facilitation Commission 示范法 refers to a set of guidelines or rules for arbitration procedures, which may include specific clauses and provisions related to arbitrator appointments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-23b1f9e25ad7b2970cb215d6bd454574</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 855}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT OR OTHER AUTHORITY SPECIFIED IN ARTICLE 6&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The court or other authority is an organization mentioned as a party that can take necessary measures under certain circumstances."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court or other authority is an organization responsible for appointing arbitrators if the parties fail to agree on one."&lt;SEP&gt;"This refers to a legal body that can decide on the termination of an arbitrator's mandate if requested by any party as per Article 14(2)."&lt;SEP&gt;"This refers to an external judicial body or administrative authority that can decide on challenges if they are not resolved within the arbitral tribunal, ensuring impartiality and finality of decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"This refers to the judicial body or another designated entity responsible for appointing arbitrators when parties fail to agree."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b6cff72e41603eed38553fb4f306a008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4487876b424618c4533648d46889bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea943fe3338aa88e6573bf715e772abd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4373f38dac5749d35f8ccd70b8bf1d15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad8b00bb4712fdfd27d215a729380d5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 854}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPOINTMENT PROCEDURE(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appointment procedures are methods for selecting arbitrators, which can be agreed upon by the parties or mandated by HKIAC if not agreed upon within a specified timeframe."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-95a4de41db58b9a101c75606869df8f4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 12 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 12 of the UNCITRAL Model Law outlines grounds for challenging an arbitrator's impartiality or independence, providing specific conditions under which such challenges can be made."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 238}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GROUNDS FOR CHALLENGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Grounds for challenge refers to situations where a person's impartiality or independence is questionable and can lead to challenges against them in arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The concept of 'grounds for challenge' refers to situations that may affect an arbitrator's impartiality or independence and allow parties to request their removal from the case."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 238}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JUSTIFIABLE DOUBTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Justifiable doubts refer to reasonable concerns about a person's fairness or independence, which can be scientifically analyzed in legal contexts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 875}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1195}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IMPARTIALITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Impartiality is the quality of being unbiased and fair, crucial for arbitrators who must make decisions without favoritism towards any party involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 875}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1195}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDEPENDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Independence refers to a state where an individual or entity acts freely from external influences, essential for maintaining fairness in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 875}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1195}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISCLOSURE OF CIRCUMSTANCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The act of disclosing relevant information by arbitrators is an event that ensures transparency and trust among the parties involved in the arbitration process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 856}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1193}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPOINTMENT PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Appointment Procedure refers to the process by which arbitrators are selected or appointed in accordance with legal requirements and organizational policies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 235}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 872}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Model Law is a template for legislation that provides guidelines on arbitration procedures, serving as a reference for countries developing their own laws related to international commercial disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRADE FACILITATION AND DISPUTE RESOLUTION COMMISSION (贸法委)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"贸法委 refers to the Trade Facilitation and Dispute Resolution Commission, which is involved in formulating legal frameworks such as the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTIES INVOLVED IN DISPUTE RESOLUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The social science aspect of parties involved in dispute resolution includes the dynamics and interactions among individuals or organizations seeking to resolve conflicts legally or through alternative means such as mediation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JUSTIFICATION FOR CHALLENGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Justification for Challenge is a legal ground that allows parties to request an arbitrator's removal from their case, based on specific circumstances that may affect the arbitrator's impartiality or independence."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DESIGNATED ARBITRATORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Designated Arbitrators are individuals appointed by organizations like HKIAC to resolve disputes through arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION CASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Arbitration Case is a specific dispute that is resolved through the process of arbitration, involving parties who agree to have their conflict settled by an arbitrator or panel of arbitrators."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION FRAMEWORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Dispute Resolution Framework refers to the legal and procedural guidelines used in resolving conflicts between parties, such as those provided by UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 856}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1193}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORK FOR ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Legal Framework for Arbitration is a set of rules, laws, and procedures that govern the process of resolving disputes through arbitration, ensuring fairness and consistency in international commercial transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATOR'S ROLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Role of an Arbitrator involves making impartial decisions based on evidence presented by parties involved in a dispute, ensuring fair resolution without bias or external influence."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRANSPARENCY AND TRUST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Transparency and Trust are key concepts in arbitration processes, where the disclosure of relevant information by arbitrators ensures that all parties feel confident about the fairness and integrity of the proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAIRNESS IN ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Concept of Fairness in Arbitration refers to ensuring unbiased decision-making during dispute resolution processes, which is crucial for maintaining trust among parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONFLICT RESOLUTION MECHANISMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conflict Resolution Mechanisms are tools and procedures used by organizations or individuals to resolve disputes effectively, including arbitration as one of the methods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Arbitration Process, or Adjudication Procedure, refers to the systematic method of resolving payment disputes between parties within construction contracts according to specific regulations outlined here."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration is a form of alternative dispute resolution where an arbitrator makes a binding decision on the parties' disputes, often used as an alternative to litigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Arbitration Process encompasses all steps involved in resolving disputes through arbitration, including procedural requirements and outcomes as described in Articles 25-26."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Arbitration Process is a formal method of resolving disputes outside traditional court systems, involving arbitrators who make decisions based on evidence, law, contract terms, and applicable trade usages to reach fair resolutions for all parties involved."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Arbitration Process is a structured method for resolving disputes through the appointment of arbitrators who make binding decisions based on evidence presented by parties involved."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Arbitration process refers to the procedure where disputes are resolved through arbitration, involving parties requesting interim measures and arbitral tribunals granting such measures."&lt;SEP&gt;"The arbitration process involves the steps taken from initiating an arbitration claim through to its resolution by one or more arbitrators."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e027acdec4c66c21703cf2589ec26926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a252d91181bacec6fcd6f1d54297b19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b219a4ff887909dc5fdeb24191ca220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d56571b98ba26116ef651214c379b2f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 349}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION INDUSTRY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Dispute Resolution Industry encompasses organizations, professionals, and processes dedicated to facilitating conflict resolution between individuals or entities in various sectors such as business, law, and international trade."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW PROVISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Provisions of the UNCITRAL Model Law provide specific guidelines for arbitration procedures, including appointment methods, grounds for challenge, and disclosure requirements to ensure fairness and transparency."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 349}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 12&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 12 outlines the disclosure obligations of potential arbitrators regarding circumstances that may give rise to justifiable doubts about their impartiality or independence, as well as the procedure for challenging an arbitrator once appointed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 238}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;13(4)条的规限下具有效力&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This phrase indicates that Article 13 of the UNCITRAL Model Law has effect under certain conditions, specifically as limited by paragraph (4)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 238}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第13條. 申请回避的程序&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 13 describes the procedure for applying to have an arbitrator recused, including freedom to agree on this process with other parties and a deadline of fifteen days from when one becomes aware of the composition of the arbitral tribunal or any circumstances referred to in Article 12(2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 238}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第13条的规限下具有效力&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This phrase indicates that Article 13 has effect under certain conditions, specifically as limited by paragraph (4) of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;申请仲裁员回回避的程序&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The procedure for applying to have an arbitrator recused involves freedom to agree on this process with other parties and a deadline of fifteen days from when one becomes aware of the composition of the arbitral tribunal or any circumstances referred to in Article 12(2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第6条规定的法院或其他机构&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to courts or other institutions specified under Article 6, which can be requested by a party who has received notification that their application for recusal of an arbitrator was rejected."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;当事人可自由约定申请仲裁员回避的程序&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Parties have the freedom to agree on the procedure for applying to have an arbitrator recused, but this must comply with certain provisions as outlined in Article 13(3)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;拟对仲裁员提出回避申请的当事人应在知悉仲裁庭的组成或知悉第12(2)条所指的任何情况后十五天内向仲裁庭提出书面陈述,说明提出回避申请的理由&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This describes the procedure for parties to submit a written statement within 15 days of becoming aware of the composition of the arbitral tribunal or any circumstances referred to in Article 12(2) if they wish to challenge an arbitrator."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 238}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;除非被申请回避的仲裁员辞职或对方当事人同意所提出的回避,仲裁庭应就是否回避作出决定&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This describes the decision-making process of the arbitral tribunal regarding a recusal application unless the arbitrator resigns or the opposing party agrees to the recusal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 238}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;提出回避申请的一方当事人可以在收到驳回其所提出的回避申请的决定通知后三十天内,请求第6条规定的法院或其他机构&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This describes a situation where a party can request a court or other institution specified under Article 6 to review their application for recusal if the arbitral tribunal has rejected it."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 238}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION COMMISSION DEMONSTRATION ACT OF TRADE LAW COMMITTEE (TRADE LAW COMM.) 13(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This act refers to a legal document or regulation that can be cited in challenging arbitrators and includes provisions for recusal procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d3906bbf7ee03793cf876d19cdfab509</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 863}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECUSAL REQUEST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A request for recusal is made by parties involved in arbitration proceedings, which may lead to the removal of an arbitrator under certain conditions as outlined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d3906bbf7ee03793cf876d19cdfab509</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATORS'">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitrator(s) refers to individuals appointed to resolve disputes through arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitrators are individuals who form an arbitration tribunal and make decisions in disputes, including determining places for meetings and consultations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitrators are individuals who participate in arbitration processes and can be subject to challenges or recusal requests from parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d3906bbf7ee03793cf876d19cdfab509&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPOINTMENT TERMINATION OF ARBITRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The appointment termination refers to the cessation of an arbitrator's role due to resignation, mutual agreement, a favorable decision by the arbitration tribunal without appeal, or a court ruling in favor of the challenge."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d3906bbf7ee03793cf876d19cdfab509</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT RULING ON CHALLENGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A court ruling can be made regarding challenges against arbitrators and may result in the invalidation of certain decisions as per the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d3906bbf7ee03793cf876d19cdfab509</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 13 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 13 is part of the UNCITRAL Model Law that outlines procedures for challenging an arbitrator in international arbitration cases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d8d309a2e724a8764d515c5d8417d815</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 812}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATOR CHALLENGE PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitrator challenge procedure is a legal mechanism allowing parties to contest an arbitrator's appointment or conduct in international arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d8d309a2e724a8764d515c5d8417d815</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 812}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT DECISION ON CHALLENGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court decision on challenge refers to the process where courts decide whether to uphold or reject challenges against arbitrators as outlined in Article 13 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d8d309a2e724a8764d515c5d8417d815</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 812}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHALLENGED ARBITRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Challenged Arbitrator is a member of the arbitral tribunal against whom a party has lodged a challenge for various reasons such as conflict of interest or other circumstances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Challenged arbitrator refers to an individual who has been questioned or disputed by the parties involved in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4373f38dac5749d35f8ccd70b8bf1d15</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 14 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 14 of the UNCITRAL Model Law outlines conditions under which an arbitrator's mandate may terminate or be challenged without affecting other reasons for termination."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 875}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1195}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE HAGUE RULES OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Although not explicitly mentioned, The Hague Rules of Arbitration can be inferred from the context as a legal framework that may apply to similar situations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 884}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERNATIONAL COMMERCIAL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"International Commercial Law is relevant in understanding the broader context and implications of arbitration proceedings described."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION MECHANISMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dispute resolution mechanisms refer to various methods used for resolving conflicts, including arbitration as discussed in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 884}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORKS FOR ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal frameworks for arbitration are systems and rules that govern how disputes can be resolved through arbitration processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 884}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW IMPLEMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The implementation of UNCITRAL Model Law in various jurisdictions is implied as a context within which the described legal procedures take place."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 884}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION PRACTICE AND PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration practice and procedure refer to the actual processes, rules, and methods used in arbitration proceedings as outlined by laws like UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 884}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT DECISIONS ON ARBITRATOR CHALLENGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court decisions on arbitrator challenges are instances where courts rule on whether an arbitrator should be removed or continue to serve based on the grounds of challenge presented."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 879}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARDS AND THEIR ENFORCEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration awards and their enforcement refer to the final judgments made by arbitral tribunals that can be enforced through legal mechanisms as described in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 884}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 14&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event described is a situation where an arbitrator becomes unable to perform his functions or fails to act without undue delay, leading to the termination of his mandate."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea943fe3338aa88e6573bf715e772abd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 854}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 12(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to another article in UNCITRAL Model Law that might provide additional reasons for the termination of an arbitrator's mandate but is not detailed here."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea943fe3338aa88e6573bf715e772abd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 854}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 15 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event described in this article is about appointing a substitute arbitrator when the original one’s mandate terminates under specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ea943fe3338aa88e6573bf715e772abd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 854}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 15&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 15 deals with the appointment of a substitute arbitrator when an original arbitrator's mandate terminates under specific conditions such as withdrawal or revocation by agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-25f6483a2fc8ec5293ecc7908cc08eaf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 811}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEATH OF ARBITRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The death of an arbitrator is considered in Article 29, which states that the authority of an arbitrator is personal and their mandate ends upon their death unless otherwise agreed by parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-25f6483a2fc8ec5293ecc7908cc08eaf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 811}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPOINTMENT OF UMPIRE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 30 discusses the possibility for even-numbered arbitration panels to appoint a umpire at any time after their own appointment, provided there's no agreement against it between the parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-25f6483a2fc8ec5293ecc7908cc08eaf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 811}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC ADJUDICATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Public Adjudicator is a role involved in arbitration procedures, with specific functions and rights as outlined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5d58ad3e1c6ef21463d303a3e0c4d6ff</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 232}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 849}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORIGINAL COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Original court refers to the court that can make decisions when arbitrators cannot agree on certain issues, similar to a sole arbitrator's role."&lt;SEP&gt;"Original court refers to the primary judicial authority that may have jurisdiction over certain matters, but in this context, it can also refer to a court exercising powers granted under an arbitration agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Original Court can exercise powers granted by this section if no arbitral tribunal exists, such as making decisions or orders related to claims."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Original Court is a judicial body that can make decisions on applications or appeals, issue commands regarding arbitration costs and ensure compliance with its orders."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Original Court is mentioned as an entity that can be approached by one of the parties for further action if necessary, based on certain conditions not detailed here."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Original Court refers to the primary judicial body that can make decisions and issue orders in legal proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The original court is the judicial body responsible for making decisions regarding arbitration procedures and related matters as described in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42e0db1f27b3313444cf12ec497ffd57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-882b59070dba0a27453ac53b51232f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fd04bf2888da55881f593f9613b44e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d58ad3e1c6ef21463d303a3e0c4d6ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-854d00c33e69aed0258675abc1e2d264&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06937be24d44266dd94fe85733626b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-818682a0f1950aff44c4e7f18a331608</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UMPIRE IN ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Umpire in arbitral proceedings refers to a decision-maker who can replace arbitrators for certain issues, with powers similar to those of a sole arbitrator."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06937be24d44266dd94fe85733626b9d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 864}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATORS AS THE ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitrators as the arbitral tribunal are the primary decision-makers in arbitration cases before they may be replaced by an umpire for specific matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06937be24d44266dd94fe85733626b9d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 864}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UMPIRE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Umpire is a person who may replace members of an arbitral tribunal if needed, maintaining continuity within the tribunal structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Umpire is a role within arbitral proceedings, responsible for making orders, directions, and awards when arbitrators cannot agree."&lt;SEP&gt;"Umpire refers to an arbitrator or arbiter in a dispute resolution context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8edbd1c4d3b35d7faddb32b978e73e29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aa40d92e810c15d1924e632ab83962f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-953aa58f588dab7be8bda910f0f31c38</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 857}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitrators are individuals who make orders, directions and awards in disputes but may also refer the entirety of the dispute to the umpire for arbitration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitrators are the primary decision-makers in arbitral proceedings who can be replaced by an umpire if they fail to reach agreement on certain matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3aa40d92e810c15d1924e632ab83962f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-953aa58f588dab7be8bda910f0f31c38</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 857}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UMPIRE AS ARBITRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Umpire as arbitrator refers to a situation where an umpire takes on the role of making final decisions after arbitrators cannot agree."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3aa40d92e810c15d1924e632ab83962f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE SUBMITTED TO ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dispute submitted to arbitration refers to the specific issue or conflict being resolved through arbitration procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3aa40d92e810c15d1924e632ab83962f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 869}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATORS CANNOT AGREE ON A MATTER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This phrase indicates a situation where arbitrators have differing opinions, which is studied in social sciences like law and dispute resolution theory."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3aa40d92e810c15d1924e632ab83962f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 869}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT UNDER SUBSECTION (8) DECISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A decision of the Court under subsection (8) refers to an arbitral tribunal's final ruling that cannot be appealed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3aa40d92e810c15d1924e632ab83962f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 869}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDIATOR APPOINTMENT BY HKIAC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mediator appointment by HKIAC refers to the process where the center assigns a mediator in accordance with certain conditions or applications from parties involved in disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3aa40d92e810c15d1924e632ab83962f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 855}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDIATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Mediator is a person appointed for mediation procedures and may be held legally responsible for actions or omissions related to such roles."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mediator is a person who facilitates communication between disputing parties to help them reach a mutually acceptable agreement. In this context, they are part of the broader legal process involving arbitration or mediation proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mediator is someone who facilitates communication and negotiation between disputing parties without making binding decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A role of someone appointed by parties or organizations like HKIAC for mediation, which can also involve acting as an arbitrator if no settlement is reached through mediation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mediator refers to the individual appointed for mediation proceedings, facilitating communication between parties involved in disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6afb8943a99ee7bf996b0ce17c18a04b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a820d49f72ef3eeb5be9d057a9cb248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dd6cc93acdd87603565c28f0e5d9386&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8214b3161676dee8df8d19240ebf6752</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 235}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 873}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDIATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mediation Proceedings are sessions where parties attempt to resolve their dispute through negotiation, facilitated by a neutral third party (the arbitrator in this context)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mediation Proceedings are the mediation processes referred to in sections 32(3) and 33."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mediation Proceedings refer to the processes mentioned in Sections 32(3) or 33 of the Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mediation Proceedings 指根据《律师条例》第32(3)条或第33条规定进行的调解程序。"&lt;SEP&gt;"Mediation proceedings are sessions conducted by a mediator to help disputing parties reach a mutually acceptable resolution without binding decisions being made by the arbitrator."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mediation proceedings refer to processes mentioned under sections 32 or 33, where mediation procedures are conducted by an appointed mediator."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process of resolving disputes by a neutral third party, aiming for an agreement between parties before moving to arbitration if no settlement is reached."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da3d7a01706de39cd849092deef8b9b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce0cbc87febf0559389231de15b6441b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0edcefcdaacd59cb7375b56608a714e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca2c3669141d3f1cd87a21d68d494cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a820d49f72ef3eeb5be9d057a9cb248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dd6cc93acdd87603565c28f0e5d9386</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 875}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1196}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Confidential Information is data or knowledge obtained during mediation that must be kept secret unless agreed otherwise by the parties involved, especially when those proceedings do not result in a settlement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Confidential information refers to data that must be kept secret and not disclosed without proper authorization during both mediation and arbitration processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4a820d49f72ef3eeb5be9d057a9cb248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da3d7a01706de39cd849092deef8b9b1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 875}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1196}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SETTLEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Settlement refers to an agreement reached between disputing parties. In this context, it's mentioned as something that may or may not occur during mediation before arbitral proceedings resume."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da3d7a01706de39cd849092deef8b9b1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 875}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1196}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Contract Clause refers to specific terms within an agreement, such as those related to arbitration or dispute resolution methods. These clauses are crucial in defining how disputes will be handled between parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contract Clause refers to a provision within an agreement that must meet certain standards of fairness and reasonableness, especially in relation to contractual obligations and potential liabilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b3af7b8f9d9569fddb32c031c5ec0dbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da3d7a01706de39cd849092deef8b9b1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 837}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JURISDICTION OF ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Jurisdiction of Arbitral Tribunal pertains to the authority and power of an arbitral tribunal to make decisions regarding its own competence, including disputes over arbitration agreements. It also includes rules on when objections can be raised against such jurisdiction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da3d7a01706de39cd849092deef8b9b1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 309}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRADE FACILITATION COMMISSION示范法&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Trade Facilitation Commission 示范法 refers to a set of guidelines or laws designed for arbitration processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Trade Facilitation Commission示范法 is a legal framework or set of guidelines for resolving international trade disputes through arbitration and mediation processes, providing detailed procedures and principles."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd8b5a6b74d6568cda4bfce7dd132460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da3d7a01706de39cd849092deef8b9b1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 309}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT VALIDITY DETERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Contract Validity Determination refers to the arbitral tribunal's decision on whether an agreement is legally binding. This can include decisions on contract validity despite invalid clauses or parts of a larger agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da3d7a01706de39cd849092deef8b9b1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION CLAUSE INDEPENDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Arbitration Clause Independence principle states that even if part of a contract is deemed invalid, the arbitration clause itself remains valid and enforceable as an independent agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da3d7a01706de39cd849092deef8b9b1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OBJECTION TO JURISDICTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Objection to Jurisdiction refers to challenges or disputes raised by parties regarding the arbitral tribunal's authority. According to this text, such objections cannot be made after a response has been filed and are not valid if based solely on prior involvement of an arbitrator in mediation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da3d7a01706de39cd849092deef8b9b1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Arbitration Clause is a specific provision within a contract that stipulates arbitration for resolving disputes, making it part of the legal relationship between parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration clause is a specific provision within the contract that stipulates how disputes will be resolved through arbitration rather than litigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Arbitration Clause is a legal provision that outlines the conditions and procedures for resolving disputes through arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-99f980ad8d8f30c8e25f6f9fa3f01746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efd35e44f40ed90831a05d2c28acb9a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6793dcafea3acbec1f8e9bd2a51472c1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 866}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 16&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 16 of UNCITRAL Model Law deals with the competence of arbitral tribunal to rule on its own jurisdiction and related objections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db0dce37722025939d7bba875b1ed10a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 886}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1200}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STATEMENT OF DEFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Statement of defence is a legal document submitted by a party in response to an arbitration claim, used to raise objections regarding jurisdiction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Statement of defence refers to a document submitted by one party in an arbitral proceeding, responding to claims made by another party and potentially raising objections regarding jurisdiction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db0dce37722025939d7bba875b1ed10a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99f980ad8d8f30c8e25f6f9fa3f01746</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 886}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1200}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART 6 — INTERIM MEASURES AND PRELIMINARY ORDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SECTION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This section deals with interim measures and preliminary orders in arbitration proceedings, providing guidelines on how disputes are handled when they fall within the scope of an arbitration agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d3dc78b87bb7d880e40b21eadb5c8441</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART 6&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part 6 is a section of a document, indicating it covers specific content related to interim measures and preliminary orders."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERIM MEASURES AND PRELIMINARY ORDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interim Measures and Preliminary Orders refers to the procedural guidelines or documents that outline temporary actions in legal proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIVISION 1—INTERIM MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Division 1—Interim Measures is a specific section within Part 6, detailing interim measures related to arbitration procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法第17条.仲裁庭下令採取臨時措施的權力&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This provision outlines the power of an arbitral tribunal to order provisional measures unless otherwise agreed by the parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 246}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 910}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY MEASURES (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The temporary measures as outlined in Article 17 of the Arbitration Commission示范法 include maintaining status quo, preventing harm or damage to arbitration proceedings, preserving assets for enforcement of subsequent awards, and securing evidence relevant to resolving disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The temporary measures can be enforced by an arbitral tribunal at any time before issuing a final award to ensure that they are implemented, and such measures may include actions related to maintaining status quo or preventing harm."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 246}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 911}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPULSORY ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A compulsory order is a type of provisional measure that can be issued by the arbitral tribunal under Article 17 of the Arbitration Commission示范法, but does not include certain orders as specified in Article 56."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 246}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 910}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EVIDENCE PRESERVATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Evidence preservation is a type of interim measure where parties are ordered to preserve evidence relevant and material to resolving the dispute, according to Article 17(d) of UNCITRAL Model Law."&lt;SEP&gt;"Preservation of evidence is one of the temporary measures under Article 17 of the Arbitration Commission示范法, aimed at securing relevant information that could be crucial for resolving disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-793ad550c41441bec21087b3f776d5d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 246}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 910}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESOLUTION OF DISPUTES (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The resolution of disputes through arbitration is a key aspect covered by Article 17, which outlines how provisional measures can support this process until a final decision is made."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 246}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 910}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINAL AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A final award in the context of arbitral proceedings refers to the ultimate decision or ruling issued after considering all evidence and arguments presented during arbitration."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Final Award is a document stating the decision made by arbitrators after considering reasons, dates, and places of arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d0cddff72aaf0d2c6f21cba88e08e8e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 246}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 910}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The procedure for handling disputes through arbitration, as detailed in Article 17, involves the power to order provisional measures which can be critical steps towards resolving a dispute."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 246}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 910}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The arbitral tribunal is an organization with specific powers under Article 17, including the authority to order provisional measures and make final awards in disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 246}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 910}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STATUS QUO MAINTENANCE (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maintaining the status quo as a temporary measure is one way an arbitral tribunal can ensure that parties do not change their positions before a final decision, which could affect the outcome."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREVENTIVE MEASURES (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Preventive measures are temporary actions taken by an arbitral tribunal to prevent harm or damage that might occur during arbitration proceedings before a final decision is made."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASSET PRESERVATION FOR ENFORCEMENT (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Preserving assets as a provisional measure can ensure that they are available for enforcement if an arbitral tribunal issues a final award in favor of one party, thus securing their rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EVIDENCE SECURING (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Securing evidence is crucial in arbitration proceedings as it helps ensure that relevant information can be used to resolve disputes fairly and effectively before a final decision is made."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROCEDURAL GUIDELINES (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The procedural guidelines outlined in Article 17 provide clear instructions on how arbitral tribunals can order provisional measures to support the resolution of disputes, ensuring a fair and efficient process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCESS (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The arbitration process as described in Article 17 involves various steps including ordering provisional measures that can significantly impact how parties prepare for and resolve disputes before a final award is issued."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINAL DECISION (ARTICLE 56 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The final decision or ruling in an arbitration process, as specified under Article 17 but not including certain orders mentioned in Article 56, represents the ultimate resolution to a dispute after all evidence and arguments have been considered."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISIONAL MEASURES (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Provisional measures are temporary actions that can be ordered by an arbitral tribunal under Article 17 to maintain status quo, prevent harm or damage, preserve assets for enforcement, and secure evidence relevant to resolving disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法 (MODEL LAW)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Arbitration Commission示范法 is a model law that provides guidelines on arbitration procedures, including the power of arbitral tribunals to order provisional measures under Article 17."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT DECISION MAKING PROCESS (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The decision-making process in an arbitration context as outlined by Article 17 involves ordering provisional measures that can significantly influence how disputes are resolved before a final award is issued."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 246}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 911}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL'S AUTHORITY (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The arbitral tribunal has specific authority under Article 17 to order provisional measures, which can be crucial in maintaining fairness and efficiency during arbitration proceedings before a final decision is made."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 246}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 911}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The resolution of disputes through arbitration as described by Article 17 involves various provisional measures that can support fair and efficient dispute resolution processes until a final award is issued."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 246}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 911}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INJUNCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Injunction is a type of order that can be issued under Section 35(1), indicating its legal significance in court procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Injunction is a type of order or directive that can be part of an interim measure granted under the provisions mentioned."&lt;SEP&gt;"Injunction is a type of temporary measure that can be granted by an arbitral tribunal, as specified in Article 17 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-793ad550c41441bec21087b3f776d5d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6100d8c7e7c5fa3f9af262a8c8cb68f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-964639856a5f7a7d5119569944195b09</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 813}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 56 ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 56 order refers to another form of interim measure excluded from the definition of injunction under Article 17 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-793ad550c41441bec21087b3f776d5d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STATUS QUO MAINTENANCE OR RESTORATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Status quo maintenance or restoration is a type of interim measure where a party is ordered to keep things as they are until the dispute is resolved, according to Article 17(b) of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-793ad550c41441bec21087b3f776d5d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASSET PRESERVATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Asset preservation refers to measures taken by an arbitral tribunal to safeguard assets that may be used for future award satisfaction, as mentioned in Article 17(c) of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-793ad550c41441bec21087b3f776d5d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Temporary measures are short-term actions ordered by the arbitral tribunal to maintain status quo, prevent harm or provide security for future awards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary measures refer to various actions or orders issued by an arbitral tribunal before a final award is made, including maintaining status quo, preventing harm, preserving assets, and evidence as outlined in Article 17 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-793ad550c41441bec21087b3f776d5d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f295ffb815631fda7aa87257db86215</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTY APPLICATION FOR INTERIM MEASURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A party can apply to the arbitral tribunal for an interim measure under certain conditions, as stated in Article 17(2) of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-793ad550c41441bec21087b3f776d5d3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AWARD GRANTING INTERIM MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An award granting interim measures is a decision made by the arbitral tribunal that has the same effect as the interim measure requested by a party, according to Article 17(3) of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-793ad550c41441bec21087b3f776d5d3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 17A&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17A is an article within the UNCITRAL Model Law that outlines specific conditions and requirements for granting interim measures in arbitral proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Article 17A outlines the conditions for granting interim measures, including specific requirements related to harm and likelihood of success on merits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-492db0c693c82e4a1c002b00a74ae3fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8630302d71316afe5c4d5a0aacb23fcb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTIES AGAINST WHOM THE MEASURE IS DIRECTED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON, ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Parties Against Whom the Measure Is Directed are those who may be affected by an order for a preliminary measure or interim measure in arbitration proceedings. They could include individuals or organizations involved in disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 895}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REQUESTING PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON, ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Requesting Party is the individual or entity that applies to the arbitral tribunal for measures such as damages or interim orders during an arbitration process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The requesting party can be an individual or organization that seeks to enforce a measure, highlighting their involvement in legal actions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The requesting party is an individual or entity seeking interim measures from the arbitral tribunal based on specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8630302d71316afe5c4d5a0aacb23fcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5195e3e252b673b130b3aa632c54f19f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 897}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1205}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE REQUESTING PARTY WILL SUCCEED ON THE MERITS OF THE CLAIM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This phrase indicates an event or condition where the requesting party has a reasonable possibility of winning their case based on its merits. It's used to determine if interim measures should be granted."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL CAN ISSUE PRELIMINARY ORDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitral Tribunal Can Issue Preliminary Orders refers to the authority given to arbitration bodies under Article 17B of UNCITRAL Model Law, allowing them to make decisions on interim measures without prior notice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISCLOSURE OF TEMPORARY MEASURE REQUEST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Disclosure of Temporary Measure Request is an event or condition where revealing a party's application for a temporary measure might hinder the effectiveness of that measure. The arbitral tribunal may consider this when deciding whether to issue such orders without prior notice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 17A CONDITIONS APPLY TO ANY PRELIMINARY ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conditions Specified in Article 17A Apply refers to the criteria set out for determining if a preliminary or interim measure should be granted. These are based on potential harm and likelihood of success."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 897}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1205}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIVISION 2—PRELIMINARY ORDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Division 2—Preliminary Orders is a section within UNCITRAL Model Law that outlines the procedures and conditions for issuing preliminary orders or interim measures during arbitration proceedings. It's crucial in managing disputes before final decisions are made."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 17B OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17B of UNCITRAL Model Law is a specific provision within the legal framework that details how and under what conditions preliminary orders or interim measures can be applied in arbitration. It's an important document for understanding dispute resolution procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Article 17B outlines procedures and considerations for applications for preliminary orders without prior notice to the party against whom it is directed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44743bbc15d45a8109ce653b3d495eca</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 897}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1206}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE PARTIES INVOLVED IN DISPUTES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON, ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Parties Involved in Disputes are individuals or organizations engaged in legal proceedings where they may apply for preliminary orders or interim measures to protect their interests. They can include claimants and respondents in arbitration cases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINAL DECISION IS MADE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Final Decision Is Made refers to the ultimate resolution of a dispute through arbitration after all procedural steps have been completed. It's an important milestone where the arbitral tribunal makes its final determination on the merits of the case."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HARM NOT ADEQUATELY REPARABLE BY DAMAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT, EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This phrase describes a situation where harm caused is significant and cannot be fully compensated through monetary awards. It's used to justify issuing preliminary or interim measures as an alternative form of relief."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 895}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 17A (1)(A) ESTIMATED DAMAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Estimated Damage Under Article 17A(1)(a) refers to the assessment made by the arbitral tribunal on potential harm that could result from not issuing a preliminary or interim measure. This is used in determining whether such measures should be granted."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 17B (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17B(2) of UNCITRAL Model Law addresses the application and conditions for issuing preliminary orders when there's a risk that disclosing the request might hinder its effectiveness. It outlines specific scenarios where such measures can be granted without prior notice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREVENTIVE MEASURE PURPOSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT, EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Purpose of Preventive Measure refers to actions taken by the arbitral tribunal to prevent certain behaviors or outcomes until a final decision is made in arbitration proceedings. These are temporary orders designed to protect interests and maintain fairness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE REQUEST DISCLOSURE RISK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT, EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Risk of Disclosure During Interim Measure Request refers to potential harm that could result from revealing a party's application for an interim order. The arbitral tribunal may consider this when deciding whether to grant such measures without prior notice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 37}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION BODY AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION, CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Authority of Arbitration Body refers to the powers granted to arbitration tribunals under UNCITRAL Model Law for issuing preliminary or interim orders. This is a key aspect in understanding how disputes are managed and resolved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIMANT'S SUCCESS POSSIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Possibility of Claimant’s Success refers to the likelihood that one party will win their case based on its merits. It's an important factor considered by arbitral tribunals when deciding whether interim measures should be granted."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINAL RESOLUTION DETERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Final Resolution Determination is the outcome of arbitration proceedings where the arbitral tribunal makes a final decision on the merits of the case. It's an important step in resolving disputes and concluding legal processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE EFFECTIVENESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT, EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Effectiveness of Interim Measure refers to how well such measures can prevent harm or protect interests until a final resolution is reached. The arbitral tribunal considers this when deciding whether interim orders should be granted."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE MANAGEMENT PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dispute Management Procedures are the steps and processes involved in managing disputes through arbitration, including applications for preliminary or interim measures as part of maintaining fairness and protecting interests until a final decision is made."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 17A OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17A of the UNCITRAL Model Law defines conditions for granting preliminary orders based on potential harm."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-44743bbc15d45a8109ce653b3d495eca</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 897}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1206}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRELIMINARY ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Preliminary Order is a temporary measure determined by the Arbitration Tribunal, which can be adopted or modified after notification and opportunity for statement of case."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Preliminary Order is a type of order issued by the arbitral tribunal that expires after twenty days unless modified or adopted as an interim measure. It is not subject to enforcement by a court and does not constitute an award."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Preliminary Order is an interim decision made by the Arbitral Tribunal, which can be modified, suspended, or terminated based on applications from parties or the tribunal's own initiative."&lt;SEP&gt;"A preliminary order is an order granted by the arbitral tribunal before a final decision, aimed at preventing harm and ensuring fairness during the proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"A preliminary order refers to a temporary directive issued by an arbitral tribunal in response to an application for interim measures without prior notice to the party against whom it is directed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-74be062ba4c04dd5b51c11f6d66083c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4667827d445ebb505094eb4b58494cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a8aef97985d67c64a247cd4ac0838cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7edd9fa2d61911f5177713c81f63dd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44743bbc15d45a8109ce653b3d495eca</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 897}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1206}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 17C OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17C provides specific procedures for notifying parties about applications and orders related to interim measures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-44743bbc15d45a8109ce653b3d495eca</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 897}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1206}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRADE FACILITATION COMMISSION (贸法委)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION, INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Trade Facilitation Commission is the body that developed the UNCITRAL Model Law which includes provisions on preliminary orders and interim measures in international commercial arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-44743bbc15d45a8109ce653b3d495eca</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 17C&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17C of UNCITRAL Model Law is a specific regime for preliminary orders in arbitration proceedings. It outlines the procedures and conditions under which such orders can be issued."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e76c7e2b40934f289064a0e67067836b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 896}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTIES INVOLVED IN ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Parties involved in arbitration include all individuals or organizations that are part of an arbitral proceeding. They have the opportunity to be notified about requests for interim measures and can present their case regarding any preliminary order issued."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parties refer to the individuals or entities participating in an arbitration case who can request corrections or interpretations of awards according to Article 33."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to all parties participating in the arbitration process including those requesting interim measures and those against whom such measures are requested."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b469129a05952ad01a4e34a3cd47777e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8f918840458c595eb8aa4b44f88bed0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76c7e2b40934f289064a0e67067836b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 896}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 17D&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17D of UNCITRAL Model Law provides rules for modifying, suspending or terminating interim measures or preliminary orders issued by the arbitral tribunal. It can be done upon application from any party or in exceptional circumstances with prior notice to all parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4667827d445ebb505094eb4b58494cea</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 897}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1206}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 17E&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17E of UNCITRAL Model Law deals with providing guarantees for requests of interim measures, requiring the requesting party to provide appropriate security related to such measures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4667827d445ebb505094eb4b58494cea</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 897}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1207}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 17E OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17E is an event or provision within the UNCITRAL Model Law that deals with the requirement to provide security in connection with interim measures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e379655024f7373614e8929b6e439db3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 17F OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17F is another event or provision within the UNCITRAL Model Law that addresses disclosure requirements related to temporary measures and preliminary orders."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e379655024f7373614e8929b6e439db3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 17F&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17F of UNCITRAL Model Law deals with disclosure obligations in arbitration, requiring parties to disclose material changes and ensuring ongoing disclosure until the opposing party has an opportunity to present its case."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-83690c5e64ea2f5e5e2fd1e221f812fe</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 899}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISCLOSURE OBLIGATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The concept of a disclosure obligation refers to the legal requirement for parties involved in arbitration to provide information about significant changes that may affect previously requested or granted measures."&lt;SEP&gt;"The disclosure obligation is an event where parties are required by the arbitral tribunal to disclose any material changes in circumstances relevant to interim measures or preliminary orders."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a0d3077063fc6ed9e1ac8dc5d7668e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83690c5e64ea2f5e5e2fd1e221f812fe</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 899}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 17G&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17G of UNCITRAL Model Law addresses costs and damages related to interim measures, stating that the requesting party is liable for any such costs and damages if the arbitral tribunal later determines they were unwarranted."&lt;SEP&gt;"Article 17G of the UNCITRAL Model Law deals with costs and damages related to interim measures or preliminary orders, outlining liability if such measures are later deemed inappropriate by an arbitral tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c1209a461259f70dbbf8b7173d3461&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83690c5e64ea2f5e5e2fd1e221f812fe</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COSTS AND DAMAGES LIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Costs and damages liability refers to the financial responsibility of a party who has requested an interim measure or applied for a preliminary order, should it be determined that such measures were not warranted by subsequent arbitration tribunal decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-83690c5e64ea2f5e5e2fd1e221f812fe</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIVISION 4 — RECOGNITION AND ENFORCEMENT OF INTERIM MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DIVISION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This division discusses the recognition and enforcement of interim measures in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c1209a461259f70dbbf8b7173d3461</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 17H OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW (RECOGNITION AND ENFORCEMENT)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17H, replaced by Section 61, addresses the recognition and enforcement of interim measures by arbitral tribunals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c1209a461259f70dbbf8b7173d3461</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIVISION 5 — COURT-ORDERED INTERIM MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DIVISION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This division covers court-ordered interim measures in arbitration proceedings, including their application and authority."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02c1209a461259f70dbbf8b7173d3461</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERIM MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interim Measures include temporary orders granted by the Court of First Instance in arbitration proceedings, which can be related to various types of relief sought during such processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interim measures are temporary actions taken by an arbitral tribunal to maintain the status quo or prevent harm before a final decision is made in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d2fe562ab74fde36758e6db7f158f71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d56571b98ba26116ef651214c379b2f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 291}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 978}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JUDICIAL JURISDICTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Judicial Jurisdiction refers to the legal authority of a court over certain cases or disputes, including those arising from arbitration proceedings outside Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d2fe562ab74fde36758e6db7f158f71b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 886}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1199}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT-ORDERED INTERIM MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court-ordered interim measures refer to temporary orders granted by a court in relation to arbitration proceedings, which are governed by specific provisions of the UNCITRAL Model Law."&lt;SEP&gt;"Court-ordered interim measures refer to the power of courts to issue temporary orders in arbitration proceedings, which is similar to their powers in court litigation. This does not pertain directly to a physical product or technology but rather a procedural mechanism."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06afdeae20298d16d6b6fe33975e54ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6eef98cdb7cf96d52a56e0103910d67</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 814}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 17(2) OF THE UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17(2) of the UNCITRAL Model Law is a specific provision that defines certain interim measures, which are to be given effect by Section 35(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6100d8c7e7c5fa3f9af262a8c8cb68f5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 897}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1207}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 35(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 35(1) is a legal provision that refers to the court and arbitration procedures, indicating its role in judicial interpretation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-964639856a5f7a7d5119569944195b09</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 813}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 60&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 60 refers to another specific provision, distinct from an injunction, suggesting it has unique functions within the legal framework."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-964639856a5f7a7d5119569944195b09</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART 7&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part 7 is a section title in a document, indicating its organizational structure and content focus on arbitration procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-964639856a5f7a7d5119569944195b09</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 832}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 18&quot;(">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 18 of the UNCITRAL Model Law deals with equal treatment of parties in arbitral proceedings, highlighting its role in ensuring fairness and impartiality."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-964639856a5f7a7d5119569944195b09</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 18 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 18 of the UNCITRAL Model Law outlines principles to ensure equal treatment of parties during arbitral proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddfbb014f2dc6afae82d7bc623722b27</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 19 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 19 of the UNCITRAL Model Law deals with the determination of rules for arbitration procedures, allowing parties to agree on procedural rules and providing guidelines for arbitral tribunals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Article 19 of the UNCITRAL Model Law outlines the determination of rules of procedure, allowing parties to agree on the process or providing guidance for arbitral tribunals if no agreement exists."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ddfbb014f2dc6afae82d7bc623722b27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afb67efa17f13209eb7c5173e786360c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 20 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 20 of the UNCITRAL Model Law specifies the place of arbitration, allowing parties to agree on a location or defaulting to one chosen by the arbitral tribunal based on convenience and other factors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-afb67efa17f13209eb7c5173e786360c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 857}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLACE OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Place of Arbitration refers to the location where arbitral proceedings take place, which can be agreed upon by parties or determined by the tribunal based on various factors such as convenience and practicality."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Place of Arbitration is the location where arbitral proceedings take place and decisions are deemed made from this place."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Place of Arbitration refers to a location where arbitral proceedings take place. It can be agreed upon by the parties or determined by the tribunal considering various factors such as party convenience."&lt;SEP&gt;"The place of arbitration refers to a specific geographical location where arbitration proceedings take place, which is crucial for determining if an arbitration agreement falls under international commercial arbitration laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0cddff72aaf0d2c6f21cba88e08e8e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afb67efa17f13209eb7c5173e786360c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a98fdad24b6b0148ebf6a921fbf604fc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 857}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WITNESSES'">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Witnesses refer to people whose testimonies may be heard by the arbitral tribunal during proceedings. They can provide information or evidence relevant to a case."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXPERTS'">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Experts are individuals with specialized knowledge who might be consulted by the arbitral tribunal for their opinions on matters related to the dispute at hand."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOODS'">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Goods are physical items that might be inspected by an arbitral tribunal as part of evidence gathering during proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY'">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property can refer to any form of assets or possessions, including goods and documents, which may need inspection in the context of arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTS'">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documents are written materials that might be inspected by an arbitral tribunal as part of evidence gathering during proceedings. They include various types of records relevant to a dispute."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS'">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration Proceedings refer to the formal process through which disputes are resolved, involving hearings and deliberations conducted by arbitrators based on agreements or determinations made by them."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 20&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 20 of UNCITRAL Model Law outlines rules for determining the place of arbitration when parties do not agree, considering factors such as party convenience."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 857}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMENCEMENT OF ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS'">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Commencement of Arbitral Proceedings refers to the start date and process by which arbitral proceedings are initiated based on a request for arbitration from one party to another."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 857}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 21&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 21 of the UNCITRAL Model Law defines the commencement of arbitral proceedings, specifying that unless otherwise agreed by the parties, it starts on the date a request for arbitration is received by the respondent."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9950c34a98c9cb7c295370ae17a2d5c6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 887}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 22&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 22 of the UNCITRAL Model Law addresses language in arbitral proceedings, allowing parties to agree or leaving it to the tribunal's determination, with translations required as necessary."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9950c34a98c9cb7c295370ae17a2d5c6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 887}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LANGUAGE DETERMINATION IN ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The determination of language or languages used in arbitral proceedings is a social science aspect as it involves communication standards and practices within legal frameworks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9950c34a98c9cb7c295370ae17a2d5c6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 887}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTARY EVIDENCE TRANSLATION REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Requirement for documentary evidence to be accompanied by translations into agreed-upon or determined languages, ensuring clarity and accessibility in arbitration processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9950c34a98c9cb7c295370ae17a2d5c6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 887}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPLICATION PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The application period is the time frame within which parties must submit their statements and responses in an arbitration process, as determined by mutual agreement or the arbitral tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4511c8f186e004155d32a4e03ae34f4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIMANT'S STATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A claimant's statement includes details of facts supporting a claim, points at issue, and sought relief, to be submitted within agreed timeframes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4511c8f186e004155d32a4e03ae34f4c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESPONDENT'S DEFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The respondent’s defence involves stating responses or counterpoints regarding the claims made by the claimant, typically in line with the specifics provided by the claimant."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4511c8f186e004155d32a4e03ae34f4c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documents are files submitted by parties in the arbitration process that may be relevant to their claims or defenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documents refer to written materials submitted during arbitration proceedings that are relevant and considered evidence or supporting information."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ccfc28d1a77070797c9452e760bfd7f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 783}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1181}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXPERT REPORTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Expert Reports are detailed analyses or opinions provided by experts that may be relied upon by the Arbitral Tribunal in making decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 783}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1181}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 24&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 24 of UNCITRAL Model Law outlines procedures for hearings and written proceedings during arbitration, including when to hold hearings, how documents are handled, and the role of expert reports."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 783}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1181}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRADE FACILITATION COMMISSION DEMONSTRATION LAW ARTICLE 24&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 24 of Trade Facilitation Commission's Demonstration Law provides similar procedures for arbitration proceedings but is specific to certain legal frameworks in China."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 783}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1181}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPLICATION BOOK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Application Book is a document that an applicant must submit as part of their application for arbitration."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Application Book is a specific type of document required by parties initiating arbitration, containing necessary details about their case."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39b02ac25884a8c6102243f2b93f0c03</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 856}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1193}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANSWER BOOK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Answer Book is a document that a respondent must submit in response to the application, detailing their defense or counterarguments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 856}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1193}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOODS, OTHER PROPERTY OR DOCUMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Goods, Other Property or Documents are items that may be inspected during hearings as part of evidence collection and verification processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXPERT REPORT OR EVIDENTIARY DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An expert report or evidentiary document is a type of product that may be relied upon by the arbitral tribunal when making its decision, providing specialized knowledge or evidence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Expert Report or Evidentiary Document is a detailed analysis or piece of evidence prepared by an expert for use in arbitration proceedings to support decision-making."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39b02ac25884a8c6102243f2b93f0c03</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 782}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPLICATION PROCEDURE TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Application Procedure Termination refers to the action taken by the arbitral tribunal when it decides to end the arbitration process due to insufficient application documents from one party."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANSWER BOOK NON-SUBMISSION EVENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Answer Book Non-Submission Event is an occurrence where a respondent fails to submit their answer document, potentially leading to further proceedings by the arbitral tribunal without considering this missing submission as an admission of the applicant's claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTY ABSENCE IN ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Party Absence in Arbitration refers to situations where one or both parties do not attend hearings or provide written evidence, which can still allow the arbitral tribunal to proceed with its decision based on available information."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;贸法委示范法第25条 (一方当事人的不为)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Article 25 of UNCITRAL Model Law outlines specific scenarios where a party's actions or inactions can impact the arbitration process, such as failure to submit application books or answer books."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 817}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;仲裁程序继续进行但不视为认可申请人的陈述事件&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Continuation of Arbitration Proceedings Without Acknowledging Applicant's Claims is an event where despite a respondent not submitting their answer book, the arbitral tribunal continues with proceedings without considering this as an admission of the applicant's claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 817}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;仲裁庭根据收到的证据作出裁决事件&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Decision Based on Received Evidence by Arbitration Tribunal is an event where the arbitral tribunal makes a decision based solely on evidence submitted, even if some parties did not participate fully in hearings or provide written submissions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 817}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;申请书提交不足事件&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Insufficient Application Book Submission Event refers to situations where an applicant fails to submit their application book as required by the UNCITRAL Model Law, leading to potential termination of arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 817}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 25&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 25 of UNCITRAL Model Law deals with the default behavior of parties in arbitration, specifying conditions under which an arbitral tribunal can terminate or continue proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f3cce4894f17891d1764ccd30858f11</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 862}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIMANT'S STATEMENT OF CLAIM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A statement of claim, which the claimant must submit in accordance with Article 23(1) of UNCITRAL Model Law, is a document that outlines the claims and evidence supporting the case."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f3cce4894f17891d1764ccd30858f11</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 862}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESPONDENT'S STATEMENT OF DEFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A statement of defence, which the respondent must submit in accordance with Article 23(1) of UNCITRAL Model Law, is a document that responds to the claimant’s allegations and provides counter-arguments or evidence."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f3cce4894f17891d1764ccd30858f11</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 862}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUFFICIENT CAUSE FOR NON-COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The concept of 'sufficient cause' refers to valid reasons provided by parties which can excuse non-compliance with procedural requirements during arbitration proceedings, as defined in the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f3cce4894f17891d1764ccd30858f11</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 862}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 26&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 26 of UNCITRAL Model Law outlines procedures for appointing experts to assist arbitral tribunals in specific issues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-31879101d38b1d4251cc0b47a342f1d7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 902}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXPERT(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Experts are individuals appointed by an arbitral tribunal to provide reports on specific issues and may be required to inspect relevant documents or properties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-31879101d38b1d4251cc0b47a342f1d7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 902}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EVALUATION OF ARBITRATION COSTS (ARTICLE 74)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"According to Article 74, arbitration costs including those from appointed assessors and arbitral tribunal expenses are evaluated under specific conditions as outlined in the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-31879101d38b1d4251cc0b47a342f1d7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 901}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASSESSOR(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Assessor is a person appointed by an arbitral tribunal for technical assistance during arbitration proceedings, which may be discussed further according to Article 74 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-31879101d38b1d4251cc0b47a342f1d7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 901}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXPERTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Experts are appointed by the arbitral tribunal to report on specific issues and can be questioned during hearings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-34872d5563389492bd86e96a7e9d819c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 857}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASSESSORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Assessors assist the arbitral tribunal with technical matters, which they may attend in proceedings where parties have a chance to question them."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-34872d5563389492bd86e96a7e9d819c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 892}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT ASSISTANCE IN EVIDENCE TAKING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court assistance in evidence taking refers to situations where courts are requested or ordered to assist with gathering evidence during arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-34872d5563389492bd86e96a7e9d819c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 892}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE PEOPLE'S COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The People's Court is a judicial body that can be involved in providing court assistance for evidence-taking, as mentioned under Article 27 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-34872d5563389492bd86e96a7e9d819c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 27 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 27 is a provision in the UNCITRAL Model Law that deals with court assistance in taking evidence during arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EVIDENCE ORDINANCE (CAP. 8)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Evidence Ordinance (Cap. 8) is a piece of legislation that provides rules for evidence collection and handling within Hong Kong, applicable to both criminal and civil proceedings as well as arbitral procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 56&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 56 refers to another section in the legal framework which may provide similar powers related to arbitration proceedings but is not fully detailed in this text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 828}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 81 (WARRANT OR ORDER TO BRING UP PRISONER TO GIVE EVIDENCE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 81 is a specific provision within the Evidence Ordinance that allows for the issuance of warrants or orders to bring individuals, including prisoners, to provide evidence in legal proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMERCIAL ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Commercial arbitration deals with dispute resolution in commercial contexts, involving parties from different jurisdictions and often requiring specialized legal frameworks to ensure fair and efficient resolutions of business disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT ASSISTANCE IN TAKING EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court assistance in taking evidence refers to the procedural mechanisms allowing courts to assist arbitral tribunals or parties involved in arbitration by providing necessary legal support for gathering evidence, as detailed in Article 27 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."&lt;SEP&gt;"Request for court assistance in taking evidence by an arbitral tribunal or with its approval, within the competence and according to rules on taking evidence of a competent State court."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-375bde2b853ea690587e97e345bd3671&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1203}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Proceedings refer to both criminal or civil cases where arbitral procedures may be applied."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proceedings refer to formal processes and procedures conducted within a court or arbitral tribunal setting, including those related to arbitration and evidence collection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proceedings refer to the formal process of resolving payment disputes through adjudication, involving various actions and decisions made by the adjudicator."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d879d95be32b955d798da85e699506e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac9a4105712169b0cda2b7c65d72aa76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 856}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1193}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION FEES GUARANTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration fees guarantee is a financial assurance required by an arbitral tribunal as part of the proceedings, ensuring that costs associated with arbitration are covered if necessary."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENT DISCLOSURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Document disclosure refers to the process where parties in legal or arbitration proceedings must provide relevant documents to each other for review and use during the dispute resolution process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL POWERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitral tribunal powers refer to the authority granted to arbitral tribunals under various legal frameworks, including the ability to request court assistance in taking evidence as described by Article 27 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPEAL PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appeal procedures are mechanisms within legal systems that allow parties to challenge decisions made during arbitration or other dispute resolution processes, ensuring accountability and fairness in outcomes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WARRANT OR ORDER FOR EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Warrants or orders for evidence refer to official documents issued by courts authorizing the collection of specific types of evidence necessary for legal proceedings, including those related to arbitration as described under Section 81 of the Evidence Ordinance (Cap. 8)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CRIMINAL LAW PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Criminal law procedures are formal processes and protocols established by governments to handle offenses against criminal laws, which can intersect with civil or commercial arbitration proceedings as described in Section 81 of the Evidence Ordinance (Cap. 8)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CIVIL LAW PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Civil law procedures are formal processes and protocols established by governments to handle disputes between private parties, which can intersect with criminal or commercial arbitration proceedings as described in Section 81 of the Evidence Ordinance (Cap. 8)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration costs refer to expenses incurred during an arbitration process, including legal fees, expert witness fees, and other related charges that may be managed through various procedural mechanisms as described in the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 828}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION FEES GUARANTEE MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration fees guarantee mechanisms are procedural safeguards ensuring that parties in an arbitration process have adequate financial resources to cover potential costs, often required through specific legal provisions as described by Article 27 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 828}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENT PRODUCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Document production refers to the act or practice of providing documents relevant to a case during an arbitration process, which is governed by various procedural rules and regulations such as those outlined in Section 81 of the Evidence Ordinance (Cap. 8)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASSOCIATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Association refers to a group formed under the law of a place outside Hong Kong, or one where its central management and control is exercised outside Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6127a28d22b5d9d9145842f6c4caba9c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 783}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1181}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"subsection (3)(a) is a part of the legal text, not directly fitting into any specific type but related to procedural rules."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"subsection (3)(b) is another part of the legal text, similar to subsection (3)(a), serving as procedural guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 35(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"section 35(2) is a reference within the legal document, not directly fitting into any specific type but related to procedural rules."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTIONS 39 TO 42&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"sections 39 to 42 are part of the legal text, providing details on interim measures and their application in certain scenarios."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTIES TO ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Parties to arbitral proceedings refer to the individuals or entities involved in arbitration, actively participating and presenting their cases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OATH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Oath is a procedural tool used in arbitral tribunals as described by section (8)(a) for administering oaths to witnesses and parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 62}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AFFIRMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Affirmation, similar to an oath but without religious connotations, is another procedural tool mentioned in the text for taking statements from witnesses or parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 62}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;指明款額&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"指明款額 is a term used in Chinese text, referring to a specific amount that limits the recoverable costs as decided by an arbitration tribunal according to section 57(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;指示&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"指示 refers to directives or orders given by the arbitral tribunal during proceedings, which can be active (made on its own) or reactive (given upon request of a party), as described in sections 57(2)(a) and (b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;更改指示&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"更改指示 is an event where the arbitral tribunal modifies previously given directives, which can be proactive or reactive based on section 57(2)(b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXTENSION OF TIME LIMITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Extension of Time Limits refers to the power granted to arbitration tribunals to extend deadlines as per certain criteria outlined in the text, ensuring fairness and addressing unexpected circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cfadf35d2f372b32609102a0deae476e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIMANT'S RIGHT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Claimant's right refers to the legal entitlement of a claimant in a dispute, which can be extinguished if certain steps are not taken within specified time limits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-42e0db1f27b3313444cf12ec497ffd57</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dispute resolution procedures are formal processes for resolving conflicts, particularly payment disputes under construction contracts, involving multiple steps of nomination and selection of adjudicators."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dispute resolution procedures include various methods for resolving conflicts outside of traditional court litigation, such as mediation or arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7ad6aa79a150340c8a28d98a0e6b1a24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42e0db1f27b3313444cf12ec497ffd57</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 917}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REASONABLE DELAY IN PURSUING CLAIMS IN ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event of unreasonable delay in pursuing claims during arbitration proceedings may result in the tribunal making an award dismissing a party's claim or prohibiting further proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-854d00c33e69aed0258675abc1e2d264</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 271}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSTANTIAL RISK TO FAIR RESOLUTION OF ISSUES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A substantial risk that issues in a claim will not be resolved fairly is considered unreasonable delay under subsection (4)(a)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-854d00c33e69aed0258675abc1e2d264</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 936}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SERIOUS PREJUDICE TO ANY OTHER PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Causing or likely causing serious harm to another party due to unreasonable delay falls under the definition of unreasonable delay as per subsection (4)(b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-854d00c33e69aed0258675abc1e2d264</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 258}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 936}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATHEMATICS OF REASONABLE TIME CONSTRAINTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The mathematics involved in determining reasonable time constraints for pursuing claims involves assessing the potential risks and damages associated with delays."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-854d00c33e69aed0258675abc1e2d264</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 271}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOCIAL SCIENCES OF CONFLICT RESOLUTION MECHANISMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Social sciences play a role in understanding conflict resolution mechanisms, including arbitration processes and their impact on parties' behaviors and outcomes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-854d00c33e69aed0258675abc1e2d264</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AWARD OR ORDER MADE BY THE COURT IN EXERCISE OF ITS POWER CONFERRED BY SUBSECTION (5)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a specific decision or directive issued by the Court under certain conditions, which is not subject to appeal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY&quot; OR &quot;財產&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property refers to any asset that can be subject to arbitration, including physical items and their associated issues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE&quot; OR &quot;仲裁程序&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This term describes the formal process of resolving disputes through arbitration, which may occur in Hong Kong or elsewhere."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIGH COURT&quot; OR &quot;原訟法庭&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The High Court is a judicial body with specific powers and authority over certain legal proceedings including those related to arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 162}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 60 (1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This section grants the power of the High Court to issue orders in relation to ongoing or future arbitrations, both within and outside Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 158}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 671}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 60 (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (2) defines what constitutes 'property' in an arbitration context for the purposes of issuing certain court orders."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 60 (3)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This subsection clarifies that the powers granted by this section can be exercised regardless of whether a tribunal has similar authority under other provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 160}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 673}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 60 (4)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (4) outlines circumstances where the High Court may refuse to issue certain orders, preferring arbitration for specific issues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 158}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 671}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 60 (5)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This subsection describes how court orders issued under this section can be modified or suspended by an arbitral tribunal's decision."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMAND OR INSTRUCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Command or instruction refers to directives issued during arbitral proceedings that can have enforcement implications in both local and international contexts as per the described ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LITIGATION COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Litigation Court is a judicial body that decides on preliminary legal issues in arbitration proceedings and has jurisdiction over appeals of its decisions regarding appointments and costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Litigation court is a judicial body which may grant permission for the execution of foreign arbitration commands or instructions under certain conditions, ensuring procedural fairness and legal compliance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The litigation court has the authority to grant or deny leave to appeal based on certain criteria related to legal questions and their impact."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ff2369343594485564382d2d30ba3755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fe51ca84063bb48ff26e0744002a148</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 232}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 848}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL OUTSIDE HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration tribunal outside Hong Kong refers to an arbitral body located in a jurisdiction other than Hong Kong that has primary jurisdiction over the arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RELEVANT PROPERTY SALE ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A relevant property sale order is a specific type of court decision required for the enforcement of certain commands or instructions, particularly those involving real estate assets as part of arbitral awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS OUTSIDE HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration proceedings outside Hong Kong refer to disputes resolved through arbitration in a jurisdiction other than Hong Kong, which may have implications for enforcement within the territory under specific legal frameworks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SALE OF ANY RELEVANT PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sale of any relevant property is an action that requires court approval as part of enforcing arbitral awards or commands issued outside Hong Kong, particularly in cases involving real estate assets."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD ENFORCEABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration award enforceability refers to the legal principle ensuring that arbitration decisions can be recognized and enforced under specific conditions as outlined by relevant ordinances or laws, including those related to international arbitrations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 25}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 328}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL PROCESS FACILITATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal process facilitation involves measures taken by courts to support and expedite arbitral proceedings outside Hong Kong, ensuring that the arbitration process is respected and upheld in accordance with local legal standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION COMMAND OR INSTRUCTION ENFORCEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration command or instruction enforcement refers to the procedural steps taken by courts to enforce decisions made during arbitral proceedings outside Hong Kong, ensuring that these commands are recognized and acted upon in accordance with local legal frameworks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL'S PRIMARY JURISDICTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration tribunal's primary jurisdiction refers to the authority of an arbitration body over specific disputes or cases, which may have implications for enforcement within other jurisdictions as per international and local laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL COMPLIANCE IN ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal compliance in arbitral proceedings involves ensuring that all actions taken during these processes adhere to relevant legal standards and regulations, promoting fairness and consistency across different jurisdictions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD RECOGNITION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration award recognition refers to the process by which a decision made by an arbitration tribunal is acknowledged as legally binding in another jurisdiction, potentially leading to its enforcement under specific conditions outlined by relevant ordinances or laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT'S ROLE IN ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS OUTSIDE HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The court plays a crucial role in supporting and facilitating arbitral proceedings outside Hong Kong, ensuring that these processes are respected and upheld within the legal framework of the jurisdiction where enforcement is sought."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL'S ANCILLARY POWER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration tribunal's ancillary power refers to its authority to issue commands or instructions related to arbitral proceedings, which may be necessary for ensuring the smooth execution and resolution of disputes through arbitration outside Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORK ENFORCEMENT MECHANISMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal framework enforcement mechanisms are tools and procedures designed to ensure that arbitral awards and decisions are recognized and enforced in accordance with local laws and regulations, including those related to international arbitrations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD EXECUTION PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration award execution process refers to the steps taken by courts or other bodies to enforce arbitral awards, ensuring that these decisions are carried out in accordance with legal standards and regulations, including those related to international arbitrations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT'S JURISDICTION OVER ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS OUTSIDE HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court's jurisdiction over arbitration proceedings outside Hong Kong refers to the authority of a court to oversee arbitral processes occurring in other jurisdictions, ensuring that these procedures are conducted fairly and in accordance with local legal standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD ENFORCEMENT UNDER SPECIFIC CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration award enforcement under specific conditions refers to the process by which a court grants permission for the execution of arbitral awards, ensuring that these decisions are recognized and enforced in accordance with local laws and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORK FOR ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS OUTSIDE HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal framework for arbitration proceedings outside Hong Kong encompasses the set of rules, ordinances, and procedures governing the recognition, enforcement, and execution of arbitral awards made in other jurisdictions, ensuring that these processes are respected within the legal system."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL'S ANCILLARY POWER APPLICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration tribunal's ancillary power application refers to the use of its authority to issue commands or instructions related to arbitral proceedings outside Hong Kong, ensuring that these processes are conducted fairly and in accordance with local legal standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE COURT'S DECISION ON LEAVE GRANTING/REFUSAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a decision made by the original court regarding whether to grant permission for enforcing orders or directions from an arbitral tribunal, which is not subject to appeal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ae42208132627b8d5ff98d4e7966f28e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE LEGAL PROFESSION ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Legal Profession Ordinance (Cap. 159) is a legal document that regulates certain aspects related to lawyers, notaries public, and other professionals but does not apply in the context of arbitration as per section 63."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-367745ea1d4a071f6e58849b6c7523ab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 816}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAWYERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lawyers are mentioned in relation to legal practice but not applicable under arbitration as per section 63 of the Legal Profession Ordinance (Cap. 159)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-367745ea1d4a071f6e58849b6c7523ab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 816}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTARIES PUBLIC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Notaries public are also mentioned in relation to legal practice and similarly, their activities do not apply within the context of arbitration according to section 63 of the Legal Profession Ordinance (Cap. 159)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-367745ea1d4a071f6e58849b6c7523ab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 816}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Legal Practitioners Ordinance is a legal document that regulates the practice of law in Hong Kong, specifically addressing unqualified individuals and their actions."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is the overarching legal document that contains various sections governing legal practitioners' rights and responsibilities, including provisions related to arbitration fees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85b8cad9edd61a2498008aaa9412835f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23612e5f946b89b30990ba8fe2387e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 917}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE TRADE FACILITATION AND CUSTOMS COOPERATION AGREEMENT示范法&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Trade Facilitation and Customs Cooperation Agreement示范法 is a legal framework for resolving disputes, specifically referenced in Section 28 which deals with the application of rules applicable to争议实体。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85b8cad9edd61a2498008aaa9412835f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 917}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 28 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 28 of the UNCITRAL Model Law outlines specific provisions related to the applicability of laws in arbitral proceedings and is a key part of international commercial arbitration rules."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7effd30746ff087ba04389bfb24de4c9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONFLICT OF LAWS RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conflict of Laws Rules refers to the legal principles that determine which jurisdiction's laws apply in a given situation, considered applicable by an unspecified entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conflict of laws rules are part of the legal framework used to determine which country's law applies in a situation involving multiple jurisdictions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conflict of laws rules, also known as private international law, determine which legal system or body of laws apply in a dispute involving parties from different countries."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7effd30746ff087ba04389bfb24de4c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341dbfe6e21afa768ee74c7e3db0be67</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 898}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;USAGES OF THE TRADE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Usages of the trade are industry-specific practices and norms that arbitrators consider when deciding cases involving commercial transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Usages of the trade refer to established practices and customs within an industry that are relevant when making decisions according to Article 28(4) of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7effd30746ff087ba04389bfb24de4c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341dbfe6e21afa768ee74c7e3db0be67</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EX AEQUO ET BONO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ex Aequo et Bono is a principle allowing an arbitral tribunal to decide in accordance with what they consider fair, even if not strictly applicable under the law or contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMIABLE COMPOSITEUR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Amiable Compositeur refers to a method of arbitration where parties agree on a compromise solution that is not necessarily based on legal rights but on mutual agreement for peaceful resolution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;USAGES OF TRADE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Usages of Trade refers to industry practices or customs that may influence arbitration outcomes but must be considered by arbitral tribunals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 102}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 29&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 29 of the UNCITRAL Model Law outlines rules for decision-making in multi-arbitrator proceedings, emphasizing majority rule and procedural flexibility with presiding arbitrators' authority to decide certain issues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PANEL OF ARBITRATORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Panel of Arbitrators is a group of individuals appointed to resolve disputes through arbitration, making decisions based on the terms of contracts and applicable trade usages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROCEDURE QUESTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Procedure Questions refer to issues related to how an arbitration process should be conducted, which can sometimes be decided by a presiding arbitrator with specific authorization from parties or all members of the arbitral tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRESIDING ARBITRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Presiding Arbitrator is an individual who has authority over certain procedural decisions in arbitration proceedings when authorized by the parties or all members of the arbitral tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Settlement Agreement is a specific type of agreement entered into by parties to an arbitration before the commencement of this Ordinance, which can still be enforced as if the new Ordinance had not been enacted."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Settlement Agreement is a written agreement between parties that resolves their dispute and can be treated as an arbitral award for enforcement purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Settlement Agreement is an event where disputing parties reach a mutual agreement during arbitral proceedings, leading to the termination of arbitration, mentioned in Article 30(1)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Settlement Agreement is a written agreement containing terms of settlement between parties to an arbitration, treated as an arbitral award for enforcement purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Settlement Agreement refers to a mutual agreement between disputing parties reached during arbitration, which can lead to termination of the arbitration process and recording of terms as an award."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03bb9907c4707aee4e32c05a81efe12a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e07f7e6a4e77b91de5f23262418bf4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-605f21b5a2eb897deb796a8915dad75c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a78d8505ead991a0cdc7d41a2ddb40bf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 239}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 888}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 30 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW (RECONCILIATION)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 30 of the UNCITRAL Model Law outlines procedures for reconciliation in arbitration, including terminating proceedings upon mutual agreement and documenting conditions of settlement as a binding arbitral award."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRADE PRACTICES OR CUSTOMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Trade Practices or Customs refer to industry-specific norms and customs that may influence the interpretation and application of legal principles during arbitration processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAJORITY RULE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Majority Rule is a principle in decision-making processes requiring that more than half of the members agree for an arbitral tribunal's decision to be valid or binding."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRESIDING ARBITRATOR AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The authority granted to Presiding Arbitrators includes making procedural decisions when specifically authorized by parties or all members of the arbitral tribunal, reflecting a balance between majority rule and individual arbitrator discretion in complex cases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MUTUAL AGREEMENT FOR SETTLEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mutual Agreement for Settlement is a situation where parties in an arbitration agree to resolve their dispute amicably, leading to the termination of proceedings and documentation of terms as a binding arbitral award."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BINDING ARBITRATION AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Binding Arbitration Award is a legally enforceable decision made by arbitrators that resolves disputes according to contract terms and applicable trade usages, serving as the final resolution in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 239}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 888}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATOR DECISION-MAKING PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The process of making decisions by an arbitral tribunal involves considering contract terms, applicable laws, industry practices, and mutual agreements to reach a fair and binding decision for all parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRADE USAGES APPLICABLE TO THE TRANSACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Trade Usages Applicable to the Transaction refer to specific business customs or norms relevant to a particular transaction that may influence how disputes are resolved through arbitration, emphasizing industry-specific practices and standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 102}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MUTUAL AGREEMENT IN DISPUTE RESOLUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mutual Agreement in Dispute Resolution refers to the collaborative process where disputing parties agree on a resolution during arbitration, often leading to the termination of proceedings and documentation as an arbitral award."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL MAJORITY DECISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Arbitration Tribunal Majority Decision is a decision made by more than half of the members of an arbitral tribunal in multi-arbitrator proceedings, reflecting collective judgment on disputes based on contract terms and applicable trade usages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRESIDING ARBITRATOR'S ROLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The role of a Presiding Arbitrator includes making procedural decisions when specifically authorized by parties or all members of the arbitral tribunal, highlighting individual arbitrators' authority in complex cases where majority rule may not suffice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TERMINOLOGY AND PRINCIPLES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration Terminology and Principles encompass legal concepts, procedural rules, and industry-specific norms that guide the arbitration process, ensuring fair outcomes for all parties involved in dispute resolution mechanisms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 30 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 30 of the UNCITRAL Model Law outlines procedures for settling disputes during arbitral proceedings and recording such settlements as arbitral awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a78d8505ead991a0cdc7d41a2ddb40bf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 886}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1199}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRAL AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Arbitral Award is the final decision made by an arbitration tribunal, which has legal force and status equivalent to other awards in resolving disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"An arbitral award is a decision made by an arbitrator or arbitral tribunal in resolving a dispute submitted for arbitration, which may be recognized and enforced under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitral awards are decisions made by an arbitral tribunal in accordance with the rules of arbitration, which may be set aside if certain conditions are met as described in Article 34."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-665407cfb1dd4211e1d5ff880154e6bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-368fa7e2763a0614258f01172b9c741f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a78d8505ead991a0cdc7d41a2ddb40bf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 821}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 31&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 31 of UNCITRAL Model Law outlines the form and contents of an arbitration award."&lt;SEP&gt;"Article 31 of the UNCITRAL Model Law provides provisions for corrections and interpretations of awards, as well as additional awards based on certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e07f7e6a4e77b91de5f23262418bf4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 239}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 890}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE WITH MULTIPLE ARBITRATORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration Procedure with Multiple Arbitrators refers to the process where more than one arbitrator signs off on the award, requiring a majority signature except stating reasons for any omitted signatures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e07f7e6a4e77b91de5f23262418bf4e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 239}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 890}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 31&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 31 is an event or provision within the UNCITRAL Model Law dealing with the form and contents of arbitral awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 31(4)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 31(4) is an event or provision within the UNCITRAL Model Law that mandates delivery of a copy of the arbitration award to each party after it has been signed by the majority of arbitrators."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The termination of arbitration procedures refers to the cessation of arbitral proceedings, which can be due to various reasons such as final awards or mutual agreement between parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 32&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 32 is an event or provision within the UNCITRAL Model Law dealing with the termination of arbitration procedures under specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 77&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 77 refers to a legal section that may have additional provisions affecting Article 31(4) of the UNCITRAL Model Law, though it is not explicitly detailed in this text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第32條. 程序的終止&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 32 (程序的終止) refers to a provision within The UNCITRAL Model Law dealing with the termination of arbitration procedures under specific conditions, which is stated in Chinese but its content aligns with Article 32's English version."&lt;SEP&gt;"Article 32 (程序的终止) refers to a provision within The UNCITRAL Model Law dealing with the termination of arbitration procedures under specific conditions, which is stated in Chinese but its content aligns with Article 32's English version."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第31條. 裁定的形式和内容&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 31 (裁决的形式和内容) refers to a provision within The UNCITRAL Model Law dealing with the form and contents of arbitral awards, which is stated in Chinese but its content aligns with Article 31's English version."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第31條(4)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 31(4) (裁决的形式和内容 第4款) refers to a specific provision within the UNCITRAL Model Law that mandates delivery of a copy of the arbitration award to each party after it has been signed by the majority of arbitrators, which is stated in Chinese but its content aligns with Article 31(4)'s English version."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第77條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 77 (第77條) refers to a legal section that may have additional provisions affecting the UNCITRAL Model Law, though it is not explicitly detailed in this text and its content aligns with Section 77's English version."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATOR OR ARBITRATORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitrator(s) refers to individuals appointed to resolve disputes through arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPLICATION FOR ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Application for Arbitration is a formal request by one party to initiate an arbitral proceeding, which may be withdrawn under certain conditions as stated in Article 32(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION OF ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL'S APPOINTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The termination of the arbitrators' appointment occurs when the arbitration procedure is terminated, as stated in Article 32(3)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINAL AWARD OR ARBITRATION DECISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Final Award or Arbitration Decision refers to a written and signed document that resolves disputes between parties through arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION OF ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Termination of Arbitral Proceedings is the cessation of an ongoing arbitration process, which can be due to various reasons such as final awards or mutual agreement between parties, as stated in Article 32(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL'S DECISION ON TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Arbitration Tribunal's Decision on Termination is a specific type of arbitral award that declares the end of arbitration proceedings under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION DUE TO OTHER REASONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Termination Due To Other Reasons refers to the cessation of an arbitration process for any reason not covered by Article 32(1) or (2), as stated in Article 32(c)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE TERMINATION DUE TO APPLICANT'S WITHDRAWAL WITH OPPOSITION FROM RESPONDENT AND ARBITRATOR'S APPROVAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Termination Due To Applicant's Withdrawal With Opposition From Respondent And Arbitrator's Approval refers to the cessation of arbitration proceedings when an applicant withdraws their application, but only if a respondent opposes this action and an arbitrator finds that terminating the procedure is in the interest of final resolution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Termination Of Arbitration Agreement refers to mutual agreement between parties to cease arbitration proceedings as stated in Article 32(b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION DUE TO IMPRACTICABILITY OR UNNECESSARY CONTINUATION OF THE PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Termination Due To Impracticality Or Unnecessary Continuation Of The Procedure occurs when an arbitrator determines that continuing the arbitration process is not necessary or possible, as stated in Article 32(c)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL'S DETERMINATION OF IMPRACTICABILITY OR UNNECESSARY CONTINUATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Arbitration Tribunal's Determination Of Impracticality Or Unnecessary Continuation refers to the decision made by an arbitrator that the arbitration process should be terminated due to impracticability or lack of necessity, as stated in Article 32(c)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 32&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 32 of the UNCITRAL Model Law deals with the termination conditions for arbitral proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c28925249d0e1bce05d18edbb693e21</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIMANT WITHDRAWAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The claimant's withdrawal is an event that can lead to the termination of arbitral proceedings, subject to certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c28925249d0e1bce05d18edbb693e21</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTIES AGREEMENT ON TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Agreement between parties for terminating the proceedings is a specific condition under Article 32(2)(b) of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c28925249d0e1bce05d18edbb693e21</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL'S FINDING OF UNNECESSITY OR IMPOSSIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The arbitral tribunal finding that continuation of proceedings has become unnecessary or impossible is another event leading to termination as per Article 32(2)(c)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c28925249d0e1bce05d18edbb693e21</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION OF ARBITRATORS' MANDATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The mandate of the arbitrators terminates with the end of arbitration proceedings, subject to certain provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c28925249d0e1bce05d18edbb693e21</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 33(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 33(1) of the UNCITRAL Model Law addresses corrections and interpretations of awards within a specified period after receiving the award."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c28925249d0e1bce05d18edbb693e21</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CORRECTION REQUEST BY CLAIMANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A claimant can request correction of an arbitral award for certain types of errors, such as calculation mistakes or typographical errors, within 30 days from receipt of the award."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c28925249d0e1bce05d18edbb693e21</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANOTHER DEADLINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Another deadline is set, within 30 days after receiving the award document."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb0e168b6e225c931e3274375129335c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL CORRECTION REQUEST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A party can request the arbitration tribunal to correct any calculation errors, typographical or printing errors in the award document, or similar nature within 30 days of notifying the other party."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb0e168b6e225c931e3274375129335c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXPLANATION BY ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The arbitration tribunal may provide an explanation for a specific point or part of the award document if requested and deemed reasonable within 30 days after receiving such request."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb0e168b6e225c931e3274375129335c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUTOMATIC CORRECTION BY ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The arbitration tribunal can automatically correct any errors as specified in paragraph (1)(a) within 30 days from making the decision."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb0e168b6e225c931e3274375129335c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REQUEST FOR SUPPLEMENTARY AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A party may request a supplementary award on matters that were raised during the arbitral proceedings but not included in the award document, and this can be done within 60 days of receiving the award document after notifying the other party. The arbitration tribunal should make such a decision if deemed reasonable."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb0e168b6e225c931e3274375129335c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXTENSION OF CORRECTION OR EXPLANATION PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The arbitration tribunal may extend the time limit for making corrections, explanations, or supplementary awards as necessary."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb0e168b6e225c931e3274375129335c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMENDMENT TO ARBITRAL AWARD UNDER示范法第33条&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"According to Article 33 of the Model Law on Arbitration (as per paragraph (1)), if any matters are addressed in accordance with its provisions, the arbitration tribunal has the authority to make necessary amendments or interpretations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb0e168b6e225c931e3274375129335c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MODEL LAW ON ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Model Law on Arbitration is a reference document that provides guidelines for arbitral proceedings and related corrections or explanations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb0e168b6e225c931e3274375129335c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 33 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 33 outlines specific actions related to the correction or interpretation of arbitral awards, including timelines and conditions under which these actions can be taken."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d8f918840458c595eb8aa4b44f88bed0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AWARD CORRECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Award correction refers to the process where errors in the award are corrected by the arbitral tribunal on its own initiative or at a party's request within certain periods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 893}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERPRETATION OF AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interpretation of award involves clarifying any points or parts of the award, which can be done by the arbitral tribunal as per article 33 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADDITIONAL AWARD REQUEST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Additional award request is a party's request to the arbitral tribunal for an additional award regarding claims presented in arbitration proceedings but omitted from the initial award, within thirty days of receipt of the original award."&lt;SEP&gt;"Request for additional award refers to a party's application within 30 days after receiving the initial award, seeking further clarification or supplementation of claims not included initially."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5490186775273077486362a56a5b981f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 49}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CORRECTION PERIOD EXTENSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Correction period extension allows the arbitral tribunal to extend the time limit for making corrections or interpretations if necessary."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 893}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AWARD INTERPRETATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Award interpretation involves clarifying any points or parts of the award, which can be done by the arbitral tribunal as per article 33 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 239}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 890}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COST REVIEW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cost review is a process where an arbitration award on costs may be reviewed within thirty days if the tribunal was unaware of relevant information when making the original decision."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORIGINAL AWARD DETERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Original award determination refers to the initial decision made by the arbitral tribunal regarding a dispute before any corrections or interpretations are applied."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COSTS AWARDING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Costs awarding involves the arbitration tribunal's decision on cost-related matters, which can be reviewed within 30 days of the original award if relevant information was not considered at that time."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORIGINAL DISPUTE DETERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Original dispute determination refers to the initial resolution made by the arbitral tribunal regarding a specific legal dispute before any corrections, interpretations, or additional awards are issued."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT ORDER FOR SUPPLEMENTARY RELIEF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court order for supplementary relief involves the original court's power to command supplementary relief in cases where an arbitration award is related to ongoing civil proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 240}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2017 AMENDMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The 2017 amendment refers to changes or updates made to a legal provision, specifically affecting how disputes are handled between arbitration and court procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CIVIL LAW PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Civil law procedure is the set of rules governing civil litigation processes in courts, which can be referenced when discussing supplementary relief orders from original awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 240}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SETTLEMENT OFFER INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Settlement offer information refers to any offers for settlement that may have been relevant but were not considered by the arbitral tribunal at the time of making its initial award, which can affect a party's request for an additional award."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORIGINAL ARBITRATION DECISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Original arbitration decision is the primary ruling made by the arbitral tribunal before any corrections or interpretations are applied to it."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COSTS DETERMINATION IN ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Costs determination in arbitration involves the arbitral tribunal's decision on cost-related matters within an arbitration process, subject to potential review if relevant information was not considered initially."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 239}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 889}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPPLEMENTARY RELIEF REQUEST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Supplementary relief request is a party's formal request for additional awards regarding claims presented during arbitration but omitted from the initial award, which can be made within thirty days of receiving the original award."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 239}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 889}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT CIVIL PROCEDURE LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court civil procedure law refers to legal frameworks governing court proceedings in civil matters, which may interact with or influence arbitration processes and decisions regarding supplementary relief orders."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 240}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL DECISION MAKING PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration tribunal decision-making process involves the procedures and considerations followed by an arbitral tribunal when resolving disputes and issuing awards, including potential corrections, interpretations, and additional awards based on certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SETTLEMENT OFFER CONSIDERATION IN ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Settlement offer consideration in arbitration refers to the importance of settlement offers that may have been relevant but were not considered by the arbitral tribunal at the time of making its initial award, which can affect a party's request for an additional award."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AND COURT INTERACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration and court interaction involves the relationship between arbitration processes and civil litigation procedures in courts, including how decisions made by one may influence or be influenced by the other regarding supplementary relief orders and cost determinations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 240}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL'S AUTHORITY TO CORRECT AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitral tribunal's authority to correct awards refers to the power of an arbitral tribunal to make corrections, interpretations, or additional awards based on certain conditions as outlined in relevant legal provisions such as Article 31 and others."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 893}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD REVIEW PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration award review process involves the procedures for reviewing arbitration awards, including potential corrections, interpretations, or additional awards based on certain conditions as outlined in relevant legal provisions such as Article 31 and others."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 239}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 889}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL'S INTERPRETATION OF AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitral tribunal's interpretation of awards involves the clarification or explanation provided by an arbitral tribunal regarding any points or parts of its award, which can be done as per Article 33 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 239}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 890}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION COST DETERMINATION PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration cost determination process involves the procedures for determining costs in arbitration proceedings and how these determinations may be reviewed or modified if relevant information was not considered initially."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT'S SUPPLEMENTARY RELIEF ORDER AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court's supplementary relief order authority refers to a court's power to issue orders related to supplementary relief, which can interact with arbitration processes and decisions regarding awards and cost determinations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORIGINAL TRIAL COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Original Trial Court handles appeals from arbitration decisions and decides on legal issues arising from those decisions without considering specific criteria mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Original Trial Court is a legal institution that can order remedies or relief in civil proceedings and can extend the time limit for making awards upon application."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92dbfb61aa1ae662d58ad04e46a6a1e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698354d68541c6722cada50bb05de978</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 865}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REMEDY OR RELIEF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A remedy or relief is a legal outcome that can be ordered by both the Original Trial Court and Arbitration Tribunal in civil proceedings, including specific performance of contracts not related to land."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92dbfb61aa1ae662d58ad04e46a6a1e4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 865}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAND AND INTEREST IN LAND&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Land and its interests are mentioned as exceptions where the Arbitration Tribunal does not have the power of specific performance, distinguishing them from other contracts that can be enforced by the tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92dbfb61aa1ae662d58ad04e46a6a1e4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 865}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TIME FOR MAKING AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event refers to the deadline for an arbitral tribunal to make an award, which can be extended by order of the Court."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e5ed4af08fa3d54713649e0adf6d0ad</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EFFECT OF AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event refers to the final and binding nature of an arbitral tribunal's decision under certain conditions or through specific procedures for challenging it."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e5ed4af08fa3d54713649e0adf6d0ad</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 856}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1193}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION FEES AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event is a potential decision by an arbitral tribunal to award costs related to the arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e5ed4af08fa3d54713649e0adf6d0ad</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 879}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COSTS OF ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Costs of arbitration proceedings include charges and expenditures by the arbitration tribunal, which are subject to its assessment as per section 75(5)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-caff1791e8e9f461d58d69581c8df6cd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT'S FEE SCALE AND PRACTICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court's fee scale and practices refer to the methods used by courts in assessing litigation costs, which are not followed by the arbitration tribunal when evaluating fees according to Section 75(6)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-caff1791e8e9f461d58d69581c8df6cd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OVERALL CIRCUMSTANCES REASONABLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Overall circumstances reasonable refers to a standard that must be considered for the allowance of certain requests or commands made during an arbitration process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-caff1791e8e9f461d58d69581c8df6cd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SETTLEMENT OFFER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Settlement Offer is an event where one party makes a written offer to settle the dispute concerned, which may be considered by the Arbitral Tribunal when assessing costs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 856}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1193}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 75&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 75 refers to a specific section in the legal framework governing arbitral tribunals, which outlines certain rules for assessing costs without including tribunal fees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COSTS ASSESSMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Costs Assessment is an event where the Arbitral Tribunal evaluates and determines the amount of costs to be awarded or ordered paid by parties in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 856}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1193}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE CONCERNED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Dispute Concerned refers to a specific issue or conflict between parties that has been submitted for resolution through arbitration, which may influence cost assessments and payment orders."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 894}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FEES AND EXPENSES OF THE TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fees and expenses of the tribunal refer to the costs incurred by the arbitral body in conducting proceedings, which are typically not subject to court evaluation according to section 76(6)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Fees and Expenses of the Tribunal refer to the costs incurred by the Arbitral Tribunal in conducting proceedings, including administrative fees and other related expenses that are typically excluded from direct cost awards but may be considered when assessing overall costs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 894}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WRITTEN OFFER OF SETTLEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Written Offer of Settlement is a formal proposal made by one party to another during arbitration or litigation proceedings, aimed at resolving the dispute and potentially influencing cost assessments by the tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORDER OR DIRECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Order or Direction refers to specific instructions issued by the Arbitral Tribunal in arbitral proceedings that can affect costs, such as interim measures or final determinations on payment methods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Interim Measure of Arbitration is a temporary order or direction given during arbitration to address urgent issues and may impact cost assessments by the tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COSTS ORDERED UNDER SUBSECTION (3) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Costs Ordered Under Subsection (3) refers to specific events where the Arbitral Tribunal directs that costs be paid forthwith or at a specified time, based on requests for orders or directions made by parties during arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COSTS ORDERED UNDER SUBSECTION (4) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Costs Ordered Under Subsection (4) refers to specific events where the Arbitral Tribunal directs that costs be paid forthwith or at a specified time, based on requests for orders or directions made by parties during arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COSTS ASSESSMENT WITHOUT TRIBUNAL FEES &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Costs Assessment Without Tribunal Fees is an event where the Arbitral Tribunal evaluates costs without including tribunal fees in direct awards but may consider them when assessing overall costs, as outlined in Section 75 of the legal framework."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE SUBMISSION FOR ARBITRATION &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dispute Submission for Arbitration is an event where parties submit their disputes to arbitration proceedings, which can involve cost assessments and payment determinations based on the nature of the dispute and relevant legal frameworks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COSTS ASSESSMENT BASED ON RELEVANT CIRCUMSTANCES &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Costs Assessment Based on Relevant Circumstances is an event where the Arbitral Tribunal evaluates costs considering all relevant circumstances, including offers of settlement and interim measures, which can influence cost assessments and payment orders."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE CONCERNED IN SECTION 75 &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Dispute Concerned in Section 75 refers to specific issues or conflicts between parties that are subject to the rules outlined in Section 75 of the legal framework governing arbitral tribunals, which can affect cost assessments and payment orders."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COSTS ASSESSMENT FOR PRE-ARBITRATION EXPENSES &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Costs Assessment for Pre-Arbitration Expenses is an event where the Arbitral Tribunal evaluates costs related to expenses incurred before arbitration proceedings begin, such as preparation of documents or other preparatory work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COSTS ASSESSMENT FOR POST-ARBITRATION EXPENSES &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Costs Assessment for Post-Arbitration Expenses is an event where the Arbitral Tribunal evaluates costs related to expenses incurred after arbitration proceedings have concluded, such as post-arbitration legal fees or other follow-up work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIGH COURT RULES (CHAPTER 4, ANNEX A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The High Court Rules refer to the procedural guidelines for evaluating costs in legal proceedings as specified by the court's regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 411}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1116}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Costs are financial charges or expenses that may be awarded or ordered during arbitration, including fees and expenses of the tribunal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Costs associated with arbitration include both pre-arbitration expenses and those incurred during the process, encompassing various types of expenditures related to the arbitration body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Costs in relation to an arbitration include the costs and expenses of the arbitration, such as pre-arbitration costs and fees/expenses of the arbitration body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Costs in this context refers to financial expenses related to arbitration procedures, which can be ordered paid under specific circumstances as decided by the Court."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3bd35452fe0a7b5e9fa7dc2c1f8074</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 411}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1116}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBMISSION TO ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Submission to Arbitration refers to the act of agreeing to resolve a dispute through an arbitral tribunal, as mentioned in section 78(9)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The submission to arbitration refers to the scope and terms agreed upon by parties that are subject to resolution through arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-368fa7e2763a0614258f01172b9c741f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 822}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Arbitration Agreement Clause is a provision within an arbitration agreement that dictates how costs are handled during the proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISION TO SUBMIT DISPUTES TO ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Provision to Submit Disputes to Arbitration refers to clauses in agreements that stipulate disputes should be resolved through arbitration, as mentioned in section 78(9)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIGH COURT RULES (CHAPTER 4, ANNEX A) RULE 62.28&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rule 62.28 of the High Court's regulations specifies how costs are to be assessed by a court in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TAXATION SCALES AND PRACTICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Taxation Scales and Practices refer to established methods for evaluating legal costs, which may not apply to arbitral tribunals according to section 76(6)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISION VOID IF PART OF AN AGREEMENT ON PRE-EXISTING DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Provision Void If Part Of An Agreement On Pre-Existing Dispute refers to clauses in arbitration agreements that become invalid once a dispute has arisen, as stated in section 78(9)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISION VOID IF PARTIES AGREE TO PAY THEIR OWN COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Provision Void If Parties Agree To Pay Their Own Costs is an agreement within the arbitration clause that becomes null and void once a dispute has arisen, as stated in section 78(9)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISION NOT VOID IF PART OF PRE-EXISTING AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Provision Not Void If Part Of Pre-Existing Agreement is an exception to the general rule that provisions on cost sharing are invalid once a dispute has arisen, as stated in section 78(9)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRE-ARBITRATION COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pre-Arbitration Costs refer to expenses incurred before the commencement of arbitration proceedings and may be allowed by arbitral tribunals under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT CLAUSE ON COST SHARING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Arbitration Agreement Clause On Cost Sharing is a specific provision within an arbitration agreement that dictates how costs are to be shared between parties during the proceedings, as mentioned in section 78(9)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE COMMENCEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration Procedure Commencement refers to the start of arbitral proceedings and is a significant event that triggers various legal obligations and rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT EVALUATION OF COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court Evaluation Of Costs refers to the process by which courts assess arbitration-related expenses, as mentioned in section 75(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL ASSESSMENT OF COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration Tribunal Assessment Of Costs is the evaluation and determination of costs by an arbitral tribunal according to its own practices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIGH COURT TAXATION RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"High Court Taxation Rules refer to the procedural guidelines for evaluating legal costs as specified in the High Court's regulations, which may be followed or not by arbitral tribunals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT CLAUSE ON COST SHARING AND PRE-ARBITRATION EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Arbitration Agreement Clause On Cost Sharing And Pre-Arbitration Expenses is a provision that includes both the method of cost sharing during arbitration and the allowance for costs incurred before the start of proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL'S DISCRETION ON COST ASSESSMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration Tribunal's Discretion On Cost Assessment refers to the arbitral body's authority to determine reasonable costs without necessarily following court practices, as stated in section 76(6)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT CLAUSE VOID IF COST SHARING PROVISION EXISTS AFTER DISPUTE ARISES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Arbitration Agreement Clause Void If Cost Sharing Provision Exists After Dispute Arises is a specific condition under which an arbitration agreement's cost-sharing clause becomes invalid once a dispute has arisen."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL'S OBLIGATION TO ASSESS COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration Tribunal's Obligation To Assess Costs refers to the duty of arbitral tribunals to evaluate and order costs in arbitration proceedings, as stated in section 75(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT CLAUSE ON COST SHARING FOR PRE-EXISTING DISPUTES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Arbitration Agreement Clause On Cost Sharing For Pre-Existing Disputes is a provision that applies to agreements made before the existence of any dispute, as mentioned in section 78(9)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL'S DISCRETION ON COST ASSESSMENT FOR PRE-ARBITRATION EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration Tribunal's Discretion On Cost Assessment For Pre-Arbitration Expenses refers to the arbitral body's authority to determine reasonable costs incurred before arbitration proceedings commence, as stated in section 76(7</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORDER 62 OF THE RULES OF THE HIGH COURT (CAP. 4 SUB. LEG. A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a legal document that outlines rules for arbitral proceedings and taxation, specifically mentioning rule 28(2) which deals with the taxation of costs in arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a23612e5f946b89b30990ba8fe2387e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 74(1) AND (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These sections are part of a legal framework governing arbitration procedures but not directly described further here."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a23612e5f946b89b30990ba8fe2387e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 919}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 50 (NO COSTS FOR UNQUALIFIED PERSON) OF THE LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a specific section in an ordinance that pertains to legal practitioners and states that certain individuals are not entitled to recover litigation fees, but it does not apply to arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a23612e5f946b89b30990ba8fe2387e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 919}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 74(3)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This section refers to another part of the rules or laws related to costs but is noted as being excluded from a specific context in this text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a23612e5f946b89b30990ba8fe2387e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 919}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RULE 28(2) OF ORDER 62 OF THE RULES OF THE HIGH COURT (CAP. 4 SUB. LEG. A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This rule specifies how arbitration costs should be taxed by courts, excluding tribunal fees and expenses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a23612e5f946b89b30990ba8fe2387e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 919}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 77(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This section outlines a procedure for determining arbitral tribunal fees and expenses, indicating potential disputes or conditions under which these costs might be contested or determined."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a23612e5f946b89b30990ba8fe2387e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 919}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT, LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal Practitioners Ordinance (Cap. 159) is the legislation governing lawyers in Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Legal Practitioners Ordinance (Cap. 159&lt;SEP&gt;"The Legal Practitioners Ordinance is a Hong Kong law that regulates the legal profession and includes provisions for barristers' and solicitors' registration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efd0d66399468902de54d91fb89e5a84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf0dd7c47ebdb02fb1d905b0c712a8bd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 235}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 874}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Arbitration Tribunal is an organization that handles disputes and charges fees for its services, as well as has the authority to issue decisions regarding payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Arbitration Tribunal is responsible for making determinations on applications for preliminary orders and communicating with parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e105b81cb8e7429af8bdd848fcb41de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74be062ba4c04dd5b51c11f6d66083c4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 883}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXPERT APPOINTED UNDER SECTION 26 OF THE MODEL LAW ON COMMERCIAL ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This role refers to experts appointed according to section 26 of a model law on commercial arbitration, which is part of the legal framework governing arbitrations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e105b81cb8e7429af8bdd848fcb41de5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 883}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VALUATION OFFICER APPOINTED UNDER SECTION 54(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This role involves individuals appointed as valuation officers based on specific conditions outlined in the text, who are involved in assessing charges and expenses related to arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e105b81cb8e7429af8bdd848fcb41de5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 883}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MODEL LAW ON COMMERCIAL ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Model Law on Commercial Arbitration is a set of guidelines or rules for commercial arbitrations, providing a framework for the appointment and role of experts and valuation officers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e105b81cb8e7429af8bdd848fcb41de5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 78&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 78 is referenced in relation to the liability for fees and expenses payable by parties involved in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-62de924c3226ea55de4d94d980a6b34f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 867}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXPERT APPOINTED UNDER ARTICLE 26 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW, GIVEN EFFECT TO BY SECTION 54(1)'">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An expert appointed according to Article 26 of the UNCITRAL Model Law is considered part of the arbitral tribunal and their fees are treated as those of the tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-62de924c3226ea55de4d94d980a6b34f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASSESSOR APPOINTED UNDER SECTION 54(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An assessor appointed by Section 54(2) is also involved in arbitration proceedings, with associated expenses that may be considered part of the arbitral tribunal's fees and expenses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-62de924c3226ea55de4d94d980a6b34f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCESS FOR APPEAL OR REVIEW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The availability of an arbitration process for appealing or reviewing the amount of fees or expenses demanded is a condition that prevents applications under subsection (2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-62de924c3226ea55de4d94d980a6b34f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 867}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TOTAL AMOUNT OF FEES AND EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Total amount refers to the sum of all fees and expenses involved in arbitral proceedings, which can be determined by the court."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-62de924c3226ea55de4d94d980a6b34f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 867}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRAL PROCESS FOR APPEAL OR REVIEW OF THE AMOUNT OF THE FEES OR EXPENSES DEMANDED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to procedures available for appealing or reviewing the amounts of fees or expenses claimed by arbitral tribunals, which can affect the application made under section 54(2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7aaf6f770f217f1e2eb977b5ec34ad19</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 878}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WRITTEN AGREEMENT BETWEEN A PARTY AND THE ARBITRATORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Written Agreement is an official document that fixes the total amount of fees and expenses demanded by parties to arbitration with arbitrators, potentially superseding other processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7aaf6f770f217f1e2eb977b5ec34ad19</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 830}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 26 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 26 of the UNCITRAL Model Law is a specific provision that governs certain appointments related to arbitral tribunals and their fees and expenses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7aaf6f770f217f1e2eb977b5ec34ad19</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 875}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1195}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 54(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 54(1) refers to a legal section within an unspecified legislation, detailing the appointment of arbitrators under Article 26 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7aaf6f770f217f1e2eb977b5ec34ad19</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 878}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 54(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 54(2) is another part of the same legislative framework as Section 54(1), dealing with different aspects of arbitral tribunal appointments and fees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7aaf6f770f217f1e2eb977b5ec34ad19</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 876}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT OF ARBITRATION CHARGES AND EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The payment of Arbitration Charges and Expenses refers to the legal responsibility for paying reasonable costs incurred by an arbitration tribunal, as outlined in Article 78(1) of a relevant law or regulation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7aaf6f770f217f1e2eb977b5ec34ad19</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 830}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRAL INSTITUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Arbitrational Institution is any organization vested with powers related to delivering arbitral tribunals' awards and can be included under the fees and expenses mentioned in subsections (5)-(6)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7aaf6f770f217f1e2eb977b5ec34ad19</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 876}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JUDGMENT RATE (判定利率)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Judgment Rate refers to a specific interest rate determined by the Chief Justice under section 49(1)(b) of the High Court Ordinance, used for calculating interest on awarded amounts in arbitral proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7a7d382b60c68c418d8128c80396b687</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 308}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIGH COURT ORDINANCE (CAP. 4)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"High Court Ordinance (Cap. 4) outlines the procedures and regulations related to judicial decisions, including interest rates determination by the Chief Justice."&lt;SEP&gt;"The High Court Ordinance is a legal document that includes provisions for making rules of court and defines the jurisdiction and decisions related to civil matters."&lt;SEP&gt;"The High Court Ordinance is a legal statute that includes provisions related to determining judgment rates and other financial matters in arbitration cases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd8b5a6b74d6568cda4bfce7dd132460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a7d382b60c68c418d8128c80396b687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55419da365905ce3e764775f55ac2bfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 308}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONEY AWARDED BY THE TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Money Awarded by the Tribunal is a sum determined and ordered by an arbitral tribunal in favor of one party in a dispute."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7a7d382b60c68c418d8128c80396b687</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 62}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COSTS AWARDED OR ORDERED BY AN ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Costs Awarded or Ordered by Arbitral Tribunal are expenses incurred as part of legal proceedings, which may include interest calculated at the judgment rate from specific dates."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7a7d382b60c68c418d8128c80396b687</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 235}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 872}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECOURSE AGAINST AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Recourse Against Award refers to actions taken by parties involved in an arbitral proceeding to challenge or seek enforcement of an award, often involving interest calculations based on specific dates and rates."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7a7d382b60c68c418d8128c80396b687</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 350}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPLICATION FOR SETTING ASIDE AN ARBITRAL AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event of applying for setting aside an arbitral award is a legal process where parties contest the validity of an arbitration decision."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd8b5a6b74d6568cda4bfce7dd132460</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT REVIEW OF ARBITRATION DECISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Court has the authority to review and potentially revoke arbitral awards based on specific grounds such as jurisdictional issues or public policy considerations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-946b6b4dc8815b2e45997dcb61152914</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 822}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Public Policy is a concept that influences whether enforcement of certain agreements or decisions can be refused based on the principles and values recognized by society."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public Policy is a principle or doctrine of law under which the courts will not enforce certain contracts or agreements if they violate fundamental principles of justice, morality, or good conscience."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public Policy refers to laws and regulations that reflect the collective decisions of society regarding what should be done for the common good. In this context, it can affect whether a court enforces certain awards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public Policy refers to principles of action guiding governmental decision-making and can influence whether an arbitral award should be enforced or set aside based on ethical considerations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public Policy refers to societal norms, laws, and regulations that may influence court decisions regarding arbitration outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public Policy refers to the policies established by a country that can influence court decisions regarding arbitration awards, particularly when they conflict with the terms of an arbitration agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public policy is a consideration in setting aside an arbitral award, as mentioned in Article 34(2)(b)(ii)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public policy refers to principles and practices that guide government decision-making regarding the allocation of resources and the creation of laws, regulations, and policies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public policy refers to principles and values guiding governmental decisions, which can affect whether an award is enforceable."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public policy refers to the laws or principles that a country follows in making decisions about recognizing or enforcing arbitration awards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public policy refers to the principles and values guiding government actions and decisions, which can affect legal interpretations regarding arbitration and third-party funding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public policy refers to the principles by which governments and organizations make decisions regarding enforcement of laws or agreements, especially in cases where there might be conflicts with ethical or moral considerations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public policy refers to the principles of action guiding governmental decision-making and can prevent enforcement if it would go against societal norms or interests."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feb384a29e745420d0a68b05f9a55801&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47762eabb07bb9265d79611ab6fc55f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-603a9b33a6e3900af70fd439592326ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb631b96138ab7e64e00f4b6081fb346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fdd2bff76f50fe6b943f4fd79b5f894&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63fa361a4bbae312d93826ee30bf2182&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-368fa7e2763a0614258f01172b9c741f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53aea00b88989df2a0f5c9c8eaf66aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76933a7a67fb3cee016313276af67d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aba64861ea22070188d9b7dd4c0fd47a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2047b71041716475b6c4ce04dcb74ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b2fac04904854d200ea9c9161cb98c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-946b6b4dc8815b2e45997dcb61152914</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 822}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL COMPOSITION AND PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The composition of the Arbitration Tribunal and its procedural rules must align with parties' agreements unless such agreements conflict with mandatory legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-946b6b4dc8815b2e45997dcb61152914</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 822}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 6 COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The article 6 court is specified as the one with authority to set aside arbitral awards under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The specific court mentioned in Article 6 has jurisdiction to set aside an arbitral award under certain circumstances outlined in paragraphs (2) and (3)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-368fa7e2763a0614258f01172b9c741f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b688d6d5d4487cad0a2e8714c6369fe</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 815}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTY MAKING THE APPLICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A party that can apply for setting aside an arbitral award must provide proof of specific incapacity or procedural issues according to Article 34(2) of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4b688d6d5d4487cad0a2e8714c6369fe</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 815}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATOR APPOINTMENT NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Proper Notice of Arbitrator Appointment refers to the requirement for parties to be informed about the selection process, ensuring fairness in arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proper notice of the appointment of an arbitrator is a condition for setting aside an arbitral award, as outlined in Article 34(2)(ii) of UNCITRAL Model Law."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proper notice of the appointment of an arbitrator is a condition for setting aside an arbitral award, as stated in Article 34(2)(b)(ii)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-368fa7e2763a0614258f01172b9c741f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b414ae197269a985e13f48ee92be6bda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b688d6d5d4487cad0a2e8714c6369fe</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 815}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration Award is a binding decision made by arbitrators, resolving disputes between parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59c7140869534366dd7270de77711ef8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 856}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1193}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY OF THIS STATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Public Policy refers to the principles and values that guide governmental decisions affecting society as a whole, which can influence court rulings on arbitral awards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public policy of the state refers to policies that are considered beneficial for society as a whole, guiding legal decisions on setting aside arbitral awards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public policy refers to the principles that guide governmental decisions and actions, here indicating circumstances where enforcement of an award would contravene local policies or values."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-665407cfb1dd4211e1d5ff880154e6bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f35bbfd9ee83b0701ea2384c506063d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59c7140869534366dd7270de77711ef8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 821}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 26(5)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 26(5) is a legal provision that allows the Court to set aside an arbitral award, but it's not detailed in this text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78fc62b0cd7028c5a321d5c1666b4c9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 247}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 4 OF SCHEDULE 2 (IF APPLICABLE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 4 of Schedule 2 refers to another potential ground for challenging an arbitral award if applicable, though the context is incomplete here."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78fc62b0cd7028c5a321d5c1666b4c9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 5 OF SCHEDULE 2 (IF APPLICABLE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 5 of Schedule 2 provides a right to appeal against an arbitral award on a question of law if applicable, but details are missing in this text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78fc62b0cd7028c5a321d5c1666b4c9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 34&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 34 of the UNCITRAL Model Law is mentioned as related to appeals from decisions under article 34, though specifics about its application here are not provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78fc62b0cd7028c5a321d5c1666b4c9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIVISION 1—ENFORCEMENT OF ARBITRAL AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Division 1 focuses on enforcing arbitral awards and includes provisions for recognition, enforcement, refusal, and appeal procedures related to such awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78fc62b0cd7028c5a321d5c1666b4c9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 247}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 35 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW (RECOGNITION AND ENFORCEMENT)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 35 of the UNCITRAL Model Law is stated as not having effect in this context but was intended for recognizing and enforcing arbitral awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78fc62b0cd7028c5a321d5c1666b4c9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 247}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 36 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW (GROUNDS FOR REFUSING RECOGNITION OR ENFORCEMENT)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Similarly, Article 36 of the UNCITRAL Model Law is also stated as not having effect here, but it was intended to provide grounds for refusing recognition or enforcement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78fc62b0cd7028c5a321d5c1666b4c9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 247}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRAL AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitral awards are legal decisions made by arbitration tribunals that can be enforced under certain conditions and subject to review by the Court."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-78fc62b0cd7028c5a321d5c1666b4c9b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 247}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration tribunal award refers to the decision made by an arbitral tribunal in arbitration proceedings, which can be enforced similarly to a judgment of the Court."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c57c5ae22a968acd7a8e3b02e3130cce</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OFFICIAL LANGUAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Official languages refer to the primary languages used in official capacities, which are not explicitly named but could be English and Chinese based on context."&lt;SEP&gt;"The official languages refer to the language or languages used for authentication purposes in Macao, though not specified here, they are crucial for translations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The official languages refer to the legal language standards applicable in Hong Kong, which may affect the enforceability and interpretation of Convention awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a64f61df4c2295abb6d73eef9a781326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3136488efa6b0856e563bdafbaaa1633</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 841}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD ENFORCEMENT PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The arbitration award enforcement procedure is a process described for enforcing awards outside of Hong Kong's jurisdictional scope as specified by legal regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3136488efa6b0856e563bdafbaaa1633</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 834}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REFUSAL OF ENFORCEMENT OF ARBITRAL AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event refers to situations where an arbitration award may be refused based on specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b414ae197269a985e13f48ee92be6bda</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 815}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 85&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 85 is a legal provision that outlines the circumstances under which an arbitration award can be enforced or refused."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b414ae197269a985e13f48ee92be6bda</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 815}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CAPACITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Capacity refers to the legal ability of an individual to enter into contracts or agreements, which can be affected by certain incapacities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b414ae197269a985e13f48ee92be6bda</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAW APPLICABLE TO THAT PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The law applicable to a specific party is the jurisdictional law governing their capacity and validity of agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b414ae197269a985e13f48ee92be6bda</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 815}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRAL AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitral Authority refers to the body or tribunal responsible for making decisions in arbitration proceedings, composed of arbitrators and subject to certain procedural guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitral authority is a body responsible for arbitration proceedings, whose composition must comply with certain conditions outlined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feb384a29e745420d0a68b05f9a55801&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63fa361a4bbae312d93826ee30bf2182</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 879}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2013 YEAR 7 AMENDMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The amendment in 2013 (Amendment No. 7) modified certain sections related to the enforcement procedures for Convention Awards."&lt;SEP&gt;"The amendment replaced section 12 in 2013, indicating changes in enforcement procedures for Convention awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4494c24ec2905c2010570a5a5156b75e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ba533d3bab5a376760ee4b1e5070c14</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 819}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONVENTION AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Convention awards are enforceable agreements under international conventions and can be enforced in Hong Kong courts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a64f61df4c2295abb6d73eef9a781326</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 841}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2013年第7號第11條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The amendment to the law on 11th of July, 2013, has replaced certain provisions related to enforcement procedures for Convention awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a64f61df4c2295abb6d73eef9a781326</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;87. ENFORCEMENT OF CONVENTION AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 87 outlines the enforceability and binding nature of Convention awards in Hong Kong courts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a64f61df4c2295abb6d73eef9a781326</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;88. EVIDENCE TO BE PRODUCED FOR ENFORCEMENT OF CONVENTION AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 88 details the evidence required when seeking to enforce a Convention award, including certified copies, original agreements, and translations if necessary."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a64f61df4c2295abb6d73eef9a781326</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;官方翻譯人員、經宣誓的翻譯人員、外交代表或領事代理人&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These individuals are responsible for certifying translations if a Convention award or agreement is not in one of the official languages, ensuring legal compliance and enforceability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a64f61df4c2295abb6d73eef9a781326</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2013年第7號第12條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The amendment to the law on 12th of July, 2013, has replaced certain provisions related to evidence requirements for enforcing Convention awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a64f61df4c2295abb6d73eef9a781326</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONVENTION AWARDS ENFORCEMENT EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Evidence to be produced for enforcing Convention awards includes the duly authenticated original award or a certified copy of it, the original arbitration agreement or a certified copy of it, and if necessary, a translation in either official language."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6ba533d3bab5a376760ee4b1e5070c14</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 819}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REJECTION OF ENFORCEMENT OF CONVENTION AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The rejection can occur under certain conditions as outlined in the text, such as lack of capacity to act, invalidity of the arbitration agreement based on applicable laws, improper notice or failure to present arguments, and decisions outside the scope of submitted disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6ba533d3bab5a376760ee4b1e5070c14</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 819}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATOR'S DECISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Arbitrator's Decision refers to the ruling made by an arbitrator in a dispute between parties, which may include decisions on matters submitted for arbitration as well as those outside of it."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cb631b96138ab7e64e00f4b6081fb346</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;主管當局&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The principal authorities are mentioned as entities that can be approached for applications to revoke or suspend convention decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-38b4dba8dcefb2d368c753859f749fd1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 88}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 492}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;上訴&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appeals are discussed, indicating that decisions or commands made by courts cannot be appealed against under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-38b4dba8dcefb2d368c753859f749fd1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 88}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 492}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;法律适用地的仲裁机构权威部门&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Competent authorities from the country where the arbitration took place are mentioned as entities that may set aside or suspend Convention awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-38b4dba8dcefb2d368c753859f749fd1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 232}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 849}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;裁决撤销或暂停请求&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Applications to revoke or temporarily suspend convention decisions are discussed, indicating a process for challenging arbitral awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-38b4dba8dcefb2d368c753859f749fd1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 88}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 492}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;仲裁程序的组成和程序合规性审查机构&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The composition of the arbitral authority and compliance with arbitration procedures are reviewed by relevant authorities as part of the conditions under which an award can be refused or enforced."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-38b4dba8dcefb2d368c753859f749fd1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;法律条款适用地法院&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Courts in the applicable law's jurisdiction play a role in enforcing Convention awards, especially when dealing with disputes over the validity and enforceability of such awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-38b4dba8dcefb2d368c753859f749fd1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;仲裁协议的有效性审查机构&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Authorities responsible for reviewing the validity of arbitration agreements are mentioned as entities that can affect the enforceability of arbitral awards based on certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-38b4dba8dcefb2d368c753859f749fd1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;国际公约裁决执行程序&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The process for enforcing Convention awards is described, indicating a set of procedures and legal mechanisms involved in executing such decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-38b4dba8dcefb2d368c753859f749fd1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;仲裁过程中的通知和参与机制审查机构&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Authorities responsible for reviewing proper notice given to parties and their ability to participate in arbitral proceedings are mentioned as entities that can affect the enforceability of awards based on certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-38b4dba8dcefb2d368c753859f749fd1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;法律条款适用地的主管机关&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Competent authorities from the law's applicable jurisdiction play a role in enforcing Convention awards, especially when dealing with disputes over the validity and enforceability of such awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-38b4dba8dcefb2d368c753859f749fd1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;仲裁裁决范围审查机构&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Authorities responsible for reviewing whether an arbitral award deals with differences not contemplated by or falling within the terms of submission to arbitration are mentioned as entities that can affect the enforceability of awards based on certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-38b4dba8dcefb2d368c753859f749fd1</data>
</node>
