<node id="&quot;LEGAL CAPACITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal capacity refers to a party's ability to enter into legal agreements or proceedings as recognized under applicable law, which can affect enforcement rights in arbitration cases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT VALIDITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The validity of an arbitration agreement is crucial for enforcing Macao awards and may be challenged if it violates the laws governing such agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MACAO LEGAL SYSTEM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Macao legal system includes mechanisms for enforcing international arbitration decisions, with specific requirements for evidence and conditions to enforce these awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 840}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL COMPOSITION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The arbitration tribunal is composed of arbitrators, with rules for their number and selection process as outlined in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The composition of the arbitral tribunal is a critical aspect that can affect the enforcement of Macao awards, requiring adherence to proper procedures in its formation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-61ef9a8b87aa1cf04b46aaf871b5f39a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 64}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERNATIONAL ARBITRATION PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"International arbitration processes involve complex legal and procedural requirements for enforcing decisions across different jurisdictions, as seen with Macao awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 840}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT ENFORCEMENT CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conditions under which an arbitration agreement can be enforced are detailed in the text, highlighting specific scenarios where enforcement may be refused based on legal and procedural grounds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 64}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL DISPUTE RESOLUTION MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal mechanisms for resolving disputes through international arbitration are described, emphasizing the need for proper documentation and adherence to established procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 64}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;A DISPUTE NOT ANTICIPATED BY THE ARBITRATION CLAUSE OR OUTSIDE ITS SCOPE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to a situation where the decision in an arbitration case deals with issues beyond what was expected or covered by the agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5659ee6d0cebe80b200f8882699926cf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE COMPOSITION OF THE ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL OR PROCEDURAL MATTERS, NOT IN ACCORDANCE WITH AGREEMENTS OR LOCAL LAWS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These events pertain to situations where the formation of the arbitral body or procedures do not follow agreed-upon terms or applicable local laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5659ee6d0cebe80b200f8882699926cf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENFORCEMENT REFUSAL DUE TO LACK OF BINDING EFFECT OR REVOCATION BY COMPETENT AUTHORITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event covers scenarios where enforcement is refused if a decision has not yet taken legal force, been revoked, or temporarily suspended."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5659ee6d0cebe80b200f8882699926cf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ISSUES THAT CANNOT BE RESOLVED THROUGH ARBITRATION ACCORDING TO HONG KONG LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These events refer to situations involving matters deemed unsuitable for resolution via arbitration under Hong Kong's laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5659ee6d0cebe80b200f8882699926cf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENFORCEMENT REFUSAL DUE TO VIOLATION OF PUBLIC POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event pertains to cases where enforcement is refused if it would violate the public policy of a jurisdiction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5659ee6d0cebe80b200f8882699926cf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;A DECISION THAT INCLUDES BOTH RELEVANT AND IRRELEVANT MATTERS FOR ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This product refers to an arbitral award containing decisions on issues submitted for arbitration as well as those not submitted, which can only be enforced in relation to parts concerning arbitrable matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5659ee6d0cebe80b200f8882699926cf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPLICATION FOR REVOCATION OR SUSPENSION OF ENFORCEMENT BY COMPETENT AUTHORITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These events involve applications made to the relevant authorities seeking to revoke or temporarily halt the enforcement of an arbitral award."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5659ee6d0cebe80b200f8882699926cf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAW OF MACAO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL SYSTEM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The law of Macao is a legal framework that governs arbitration agreements, award composition, and procedures for enforcing awards within the context provided in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feb384a29e745420d0a68b05f9a55801</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT DECISION OR ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A court decision or order refers to rulings made by courts regarding enforcement actions as described in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feb384a29e745420d0a68b05f9a55801</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPETENT AUTHORITY OF MACAO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A competent authority of Macao has the power to set aside or suspend an award, and can also be involved in enforcing it."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c53aea00b88989df2a0f5c9c8eaf66aa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT BEFORE WHICH ENFORCEMENT OF THE AWARD IS SOUGHT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a court where an application for the enforcement of a Macao award may be made, as described in section (5)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c53aea00b88989df2a0f5c9c8eaf66aa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Third Party Funding of Arbitration is the process where a third party funds an arbitration, see section 98G for more details."&lt;SEP&gt;"Third Party Funding of Arbitration refers to the practice where a third party funds an arbitration, and this practice is regulated by specific legal provisions in Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"Third party funding of arbitration involves financial support from external parties and is regulated by specific measures and safeguards to ensure it does not violate common law doctrines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Third party funding of arbitration involves providing financial or monetary support for an arbitration process, which can be found explicitly and implicitly within the document."&lt;SEP&gt;"Third party funding of arbitration refers to a financial arrangement where an external entity provides funds for an arbitration process, often used by parties seeking such support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Third-party funding of arbitration refers to financial support for an arbitration process from a third party, which can be communicated under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a252d91181bacec6fcd6f1d54297b19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53aea00b88989df2a0f5c9c8eaf66aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76933a7a67fb3cee016313276af67d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 416}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMON LAW DOCTRINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Common law doctrines are legal principles derived from judicial decisions, which can affect the enforceability or legality of third party funding in arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c53aea00b88989df2a0f5c9c8eaf66aa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 416}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART 10A — THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part 10A is a section added to specific legislation that addresses and regulates third-party funding for arbitration, ensuring it aligns with legal principles and provides necessary safeguards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c53aea00b88989df2a0f5c9c8eaf66aa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIVISION 1 — PURPOSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Division 1 outlines the objectives of Part 10A in terms of allowing third party funding without prohibitions from common law doctrines and providing measures to safeguard this practice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c53aea00b88989df2a0f5c9c8eaf66aa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER (出資第三者)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Third party funder refers to an entity that provides financial support for arbitration, as defined under section 98J of the relevant legislation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c53aea00b88989df2a0f5c9c8eaf66aa</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Third Party Funder is an entity or individual providing financial support for arbitration through a Funding Agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Third Party Funder refers to an entity that provides financial assistance for arbitration and includes potential funders as defined in section 98J."&lt;SEP&gt;"An individual or organization providing funding for the arbitration process under certain terms and conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Third Party Funder is an organization that provides funding for arbitration, with detailed terms and conditions including control rights over the third party's involvement in arbitration, financial responsibilities, termination clauses, and conflict of interest management procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Third party funder refers to a person or an organization who is a party to a funding agreement for the provision of arbitration funding and does not have any legal interest in the arbitration other than under this agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Third party funder refers to an entity that provides financial assistance for arbitration, which can be either explicitly mentioned or potential as defined in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Third party funder refers to an entity that provides financial support for arbitration under certain conditions and agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a177eee7ea2e82607ded8787a57461c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-319ab10afb64c747e7339427a06f0a41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5d5713c2c272a2a9c9f2f00a8d2933&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b5cecde95cc674037324a7a227c1daf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-722c61c3b51c31b6fcf0c8534507c492</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 411}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1118}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION FUNDING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration Funding refers to money or any other financial assistance related to the costs of an arbitration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration funding involves financial or monetary assistance related to the costs of arbitration as defined in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration funding is financial assistance related to the costs of an arbitration, including money and other forms of financial support."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0edcefcdaacd59cb7375b56608a714e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 411}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1116}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An arbitration body is the entity that conducts or oversees arbitration proceedings; it can be either an arbitral tribunal or a court depending on the context of the arbitration process."&lt;SEP&gt;"An arbitration body refers to a tribunal for arbitration (or court) depending on the context, an emergency arbitrator for specific proceedings, and a mediator appointed under certain clauses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration body refers to the arbitral tribunal or court in regular arbitration cases and specifically the emergency arbitrator for such proceedings. It also includes a mediator appointed under section 32 or referred to in section 33 for mediation procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration body refers to the organization or entity responsible for handling arbitrations, which receives notices regarding the end of agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The entity responsible for overseeing and conducting an arbitration, which may receive notifications regarding third-party funding agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eac62f2f1327a829e40a168eae3df71e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8df8f796c1527424030ca7952635395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5d5713c2c272a2a9c9f2f00a8d2933&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0edcefcdaacd59cb7375b56608a714e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 411}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1117}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FUNDED PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON/ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Funded Party is an individual or entity that participates in both arbitration and funding agreement as a recipient of third-party funded arbitration services."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Funded Party refers to the recipient of arbitration funding as described under section 98I."&lt;SEP&gt;"Funded Party refers to the entity receiving funding and arbitration support, required to seek independent legal advice prior to signing a funding agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Funded party is referenced but not defined in detail; it likely pertains to parties involved in arbitration that receive financial assistance as per the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a177eee7ea2e82607ded8787a57461c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-319ab10afb64c747e7339427a06f0a41</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 411}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1116}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Provision in this context refers to arrangements made by a third-party funder to provide financial assistance either directly or through intermediaries as per the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 411}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1118}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADVISORY BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Advisory Body refers to a person appointed by the Secretary for Justice according to Section 98ZT(1)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advisory body has the power to make rules with certain conditions and consultations as described."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advisory body is an organization that receives annual returns and other information from third party funders regarding their compliance with the code of practice."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advisory body refers to a person appointed by the Secretary for Justice under section 98X(1)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Advisory Body provides guidance or support to third party funders, as required by the code of practice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-24bcba17e89155ad11eeca80dd981ea9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3450bee90618bb17df6c3522ce7aa42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a96252983055863ad83c00cacd5a42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca2c3669141d3f1cd87a21d68d494cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0edcefcdaacd59cb7375b56608a714e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 413}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1119}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUTHORIZED BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Authorized Body is a person appointed by the Secretary for Justice under section 98X(2)."&lt;SEP&gt;"An authorized body appointed by the Secretary for Justice to exercise specific powers under section 98ZN."&lt;SEP&gt;"An authorized body is appointed by the Secretary for Justice according to specific criteria, responsible for exercising certain powers under relevant sections."&lt;SEP&gt;"Authorized Body refers to a person appointed by the Secretary for Justice according to Section 98ZT(2)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Authorized body refers to individuals or entities appointed by the Secretary for Justice under specific sections such as 98X(2)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Authorized Body is an institution responsible for issuing, publishing, and amending the Code of Practice related to ORFS agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Authorized Body refers to the entity responsible for issuing codes of practice, consulting public and publishing notices."&lt;SEP&gt;"The authorized body is a regulatory or official entity responsible for issuing codes of practice and making decisions based on written submissions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b83c6369ee22a5baf386b25e3605cb81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51ad58eafa2f8aa3ad189d3ab135c444&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff1392eccc9ea622ef0b3868092fcd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca2c3669141d3f1cd87a21d68d494cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c30afb3b53c21887cbdb5f0083639960&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0edcefcdaacd59cb7375b56608a714e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8d110ed10ec7ab18c6afd6141aca4b7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 413}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1120}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FUNDING AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Funding Agreement is a document or arrangement related to providing arbitration funding, see section 98H for details."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Funding Agreement is an agreement for third party funding of arbitration that must be in writing and made between a funded party and a third party funder after the commencement date of Division 3. It does not include ORFS agreements under Part 10B."&lt;SEP&gt;"A product that involves a financial arrangement where a third party funds another's legal proceedings, typically with conditions attached."&lt;SEP&gt;"Funding Agreement is a document that outlines key features, risks, and terms between funders and funded parties in relation to arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Funding Agreement is a financial arrangement that supports the funding of arbitration proceedings and ends at a specific date."&lt;SEP&gt;"Funding agreement is a document that outlines the terms and conditions for providing financial support for an arbitration process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a177eee7ea2e82607ded8787a57461c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5247edeafb01587bde32ae379e5261dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a96252983055863ad83c00cacd5a42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5d5713c2c272a2a9c9f2f00a8d2933&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-722c61c3b51c31b6fcf0c8534507c492</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 411}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1117}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POTENTIAL THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Potential Third Party Funder is a person who carries on any activity with a view to becoming a third party funder, as described under section 98J."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 411}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1118}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 98G&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 98G defines the meaning of third-party funding of arbitration in legal terms, specifying criteria such as a funding agreement, provision to funded parties by third parties, and financial benefits contingent on successful arbitrations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b5cecde95cc674037324a7a227c1daf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 412}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 98H&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 98H provides further details about the meaning of a funding agreement for third-party arbitration financing, including requirements like written agreements between funded parties and third party funders, and specific conditions regarding when such agreements can be made."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b5cecde95cc674037324a7a227c1daf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 418}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION (第三者資助仲裁)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY, CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Third Party Funding of Arbitration is a legal mechanism where an external entity provides financial support for arbitration proceedings under specified terms and conditions, often involving complex agreements that define the roles and benefits of all parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b5cecde95cc674037324a7a227c1daf</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FUNDING AGREEMENT (資助協議)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY, CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A funding agreement is a document outlining the terms and conditions for third-party financing of arbitrations, specifying requirements such as being in writing, made between funded parties and funders, and adhering to certain dates."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b5cecde95cc674037324a7a227c1daf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 412}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENT (ORFS協議)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY, CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ORFS Agreement refers to a specific type of agreement not included under the definition of funding agreements for third-party arbitration financing as per Section 98H(2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b5cecde95cc674037324a7a227c1daf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 418}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An ORFS Agreement refers to a type of agreement under Part 10B that does not include funding agreements as defined in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORFS Agreement is defined in Section 98ZB and pertains to agreements related to Result-Oriented Fee Structures."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORFS Agreement refers to a type of agreement that may affect the costs awarded in arbitration proceedings and includes conditions related to conditional fees or legal expense insurance premiums."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORFS Agreement 是一种与当事人及其律师订立的费用结构协议，包括按条件收费协议、按损害赔偿收费协议及混合式按损害赔偿收费协议。在某些情况下，它还特指适用于仲裁程序且自特定日期后生效的相关协议。"&lt;SEP&gt;"ORFS agreement is mentioned as a type of agreement that can be made between parties for arbitration purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORFS agreement refers to arbitration-related agreements, which are the subject of the practical guidelines being discussed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a177eee7ea2e82607ded8787a57461c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51ad58eafa2f8aa3ad189d3ab135c444&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3450bee90618bb17df6c3522ce7aa42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce0cbc87febf0559389231de15b6441b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca2c3669141d3f1cd87a21d68d494cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc6ead6e2679a8dfdba550b0494d664b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 409}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1111}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIVISION 3 COMMENCEMENT DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION, EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Division 3 Commencement Date marks when certain agreements and processes come into effect for arbitration funding."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a177eee7ea2e82607ded8787a57461c8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 411}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1117}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDIATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mediation refers to a dispute resolution method where a neutral third party assists in negotiating a settlement between disputing parties. It is mentioned as not being covered by this division yet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mediation refers to the process where disputes are resolved through negotiation and compromise, often facilitated by a neutral third party. It's mentioned as an area that hasn't yet applied in this context but is governed by specific legislation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-722c61c3b51c31b6fcf0c8534507c492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff1392eccc9ea622ef0b3868092fcd2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 413}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1120}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDIATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 620)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Mediation Ordinance (Cap. 620) is a piece of legislation that deals with mediation processes in Hong Kong, specifically mentioning section 7A which was referenced by L.N. 260 of 2018."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Mediation Ordinance Cap. 620 refers to a legal document that outlines provisions related to mediation processes, which is mentioned but not yet applicable in this context."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Mediation Ordinance is a piece of legislation providing the framework for mediation processes, specifically mentioned in relation to Division 5."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-aff1392eccc9ea622ef0b3868092fcd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a252d91181bacec6fcd6f1d54297b19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76933a7a67fb3cee016313276af67d0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 416}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHAMPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Champerty is an old common law offence related to the practice where a third party funds litigation in exchange for a share of any potential winnings, which has implications in legal and social science contexts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d76933a7a67fb3cee016313276af67d0</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMON BARRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A common barrator refers to someone who instigates or assists in bringing an action with improper motives, often seen as a form of litigation funding that is regulated by law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d76933a7a67fb3cee016313276af67d0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 416}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART 10A&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part 10A is a section in the legal document that does not apply to ORFS agreements for arbitration, as specified by Part 10B."&lt;SEP&gt;"Part 10A is a section of an unspecified legal document or legislation that deals with arbitration, particularly for non-Hong Kong cases. It includes rules on the application and interpretation of costs in such arbitrations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-358c63f61ec2ce4f0f9b4f0675b579e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-087a07092efc881959ad458909cb8527</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 60}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 98F&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 98F defines costs in relation to arbitrations, but its definition can be replaced under certain conditions as specified in Part 10A."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-358c63f61ec2ce4f0f9b4f0675b579e4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 60}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAWYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Lawyer is defined as a person registered in the solicitor register under Section 29 of Cap. 159, a person registered in the lawyer register under Section 5 of Cap. 159, or a qualified practitioner from outside Hong Kong's jurisdiction as defined by Section 2(1) of Cap. 159."&lt;SEP&gt;"A lawyer in this context refers to an individual providing legal services who must notify relevant parties about the existence of an ORFS agreement for arbitration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lawyer is a professional mentioned in the context of handling ORFS agreements and providing legal services."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lawyer is a professional mentioned in the text who communicates with clients or other professionals regarding ORFS agreements for arbitration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lawyers are individuals who can represent parties in arbitrations, but their role is limited by certain provisions as outlined in Part 10A."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-358c63f61ec2ce4f0f9b4f0675b579e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc6ead6e2679a8dfdba550b0494d664b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de0dbf6f53e54d631a68b2a604874d6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4158bcd358cce62e9937de8896e1ba0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-454f67393ac66e31ad436e5012345559</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 443}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL PRACTICE FIRM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal practice firms or law offices that employ lawyers or have them as members play a significant role in the interpretation and application of rules related to arbitration under Part 10A."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-358c63f61ec2ce4f0f9b4f0675b579e4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 60}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAWYER (律師)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON, PROFESSION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lawyer refers to a person enrolled on the roll of barristers or solicitors in Hong Kong or qualified to practice law elsewhere."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lawyer refers to a person registered on the barristers' roll or solicitors' roll under the Legal Practitioners Ordinance in Hong Kong, including foreign lawyers qualified to practice law outside of Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf0dd7c47ebdb02fb1d905b0c712a8bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTY (一方)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION, ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Party means an entity involved in arbitration as defined by section 98I of relevant legislation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0dd7c47ebdb02fb1d905b0c712a8bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENTS FOR ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ORFS Agreements for Arbitration are legal contracts related to arbitration services. These agreements are specifically noted as not being prohibited by certain common law offenses or torts in the context of this text."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORFS agreements for arbitration are specific contracts or arrangements related to funding in an arbitration context as defined by Part 10B of relevant legislation."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORFS agreements for arbitration are specific types of contracts or arrangements related to funding arbitrations under certain regulations or frameworks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-087a07092efc881959ad458909cb8527&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf0dd7c47ebdb02fb1d905b0c712a8bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98e9907f4439e46ca077ec9da34b8a1f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 60}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART 10A NOT APPLICABLE TO LAWYERS ACTING FOR PARTIES IN ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, REGULATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This part does not apply when a lawyer acts on behalf of any party involved in the arbitration process according to legal practice guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0dd7c47ebdb02fb1d905b0c712a8bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART 10B&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part 10B deals with the framework for fees related to arbitration, ensuring certain legal protections are in place for these agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Part 10B is a section of an unspecified document or law, applicable in relation to arbitrations outside Hong Kong as if they were within it."&lt;SEP&gt;"Part 10B refers to specific sections within relevant legislation that deal with ORFS agreements for arbitration and their applicability or non-applicability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce27b5b185900927943da2e18ee8c5d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf0dd7c47ebdb02fb1d905b0c712a8bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ec40a32e838182a39a402688664a335</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 417}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;香港以外的司法管轄區 (JURISDICTION OUTSIDE HONG KONG)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION, JURISDICTION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Jurisdictions other than Hong Kong refer to areas governed by different laws and regulations from those in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0dd7c47ebdb02fb1d905b0c712a8bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;外地律師 (FOREIGN LAWYER)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON, PROFESSION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Foreign lawyers are individuals qualified to practice law outside of Hong Kong but recognized under the Legal Practitioners Ordinance for certain legal activities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0dd7c47ebdb02fb1d905b0c712a8bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第10B部 (PART 10B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY, LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part 10B is a section within relevant legislation that deals with ORFS agreements in an arbitration context and their applicability or non-applicability to lawyers involved in such processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0dd7c47ebdb02fb1d905b0c712a8bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORFS (OVERSEAS RULES FOR FUNDING OF SECURITIES)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY, REGULATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ORFS refers to a set of rules governing the funding of securities transactions involving overseas jurisdictions as defined by relevant legislation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0dd7c47ebdb02fb1d905b0c712a8bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第10A部 (PART 10A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY, LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part 10A is another section within relevant legislation that deals with specific agreements and their applicability in arbitration contexts but excludes certain types of legal practices from its scope."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0dd7c47ebdb02fb1d905b0c712a8bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;工作或屬該事務所的成員 (WORKS FOR OR A MEMBER OF THE LEGAL PRACTICE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE, PROFESSION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This phrase refers to lawyers who are employed by or part of a legal firm and includes their roles in providing services related to arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0dd7c47ebdb02fb1d905b0c712a8bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;法律執業者條例 (LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY, REGULATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Legal Practitioners Ordinance is the primary legislation governing lawyers' registration and practice in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0dd7c47ebdb02fb1d905b0c712a8bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第98I條 (SECTION 98I)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, REGULATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 98I defines parties involved in arbitration for legal purposes as per relevant laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0dd7c47ebdb02fb1d905b0c712a8bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;登記於根據《法律執業者條例》(第159章)第29條所備存的大律師登記冊上 (ENROLLED ON THE ROLL OF BARRISTERS KEPT UNDER SECTION 29)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON, PROFESSION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to individuals registered as barristers in Hong Kong according to specific sections of the Legal Practitioners Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf0dd7c47ebdb02fb1d905b0c712a8bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;根據該條例第5條所備存的律師登記冊上 (ENROLLED ON THE ROLL OF SOLICITORS KEPT UNDER SECTION 5)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON, PROFESSION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to individuals registered as solicitors in Hong Kong according to specific sections of the Legal Practitioners Ordinance."</data>
