  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the communication or disclosure of information related to seeking third-party funding for arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNICATE (傳達)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Communicate includes publish or disclose, indicating a process or method of sharing information."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROFESSIONAL ADVISER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A professional adviser is someone who provides advice in connection with the third party funding of arbitration and may receive further communications as per legal obligations or agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISCLOSURE OF INFORMATION FOR THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION (披露第三者資助仲裁)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event involves disclosing certain details related to a third-party funding agreement, such as the identity of the financier, within specific timeframes and to designated parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION INSTITUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An arbitration institution is a professional body responsible for resolving disputes through arbitration proceedings; it receives notifications regarding ORFS agreements from lawyers."&lt;SEP&gt;"An arbitration institution is an organization involved in resolving disputes through arbitration processes, which may receive notifications regarding third party funding agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration institution refers to organizations that provide services for conducting arbitrations, such as appointing arbitrators or managing the arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to the place or organization where arbitration takes place, receiving relevant notices as per regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de0dbf6f53e54d631a68b2a604874d6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5d5713c2c272a2a9c9f2f00a8d2933&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e027acdec4c66c21703cf2589ec26926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 415}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRD PARTY (第三者)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The term 'third party' refers to entities or individuals other than the parties directly involved in a dispute or agreement, often playing roles such as financiers or advisors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISCLOSURE OF FINANCIER'S IDENTITY (披露第三者的姓名或名稱)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event involves disclosing the name or title of the third party who is providing financial support for arbitration proceedings within a specified timeframe and to specific parties involved in the arbitration process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT (資助協議)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An arbitration agreement, also known as a funding agreement, is an arrangement where a third party agrees to fund or partially finance an arbitration process, which must be disclosed under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTIFICATION OF ARBITRATION AGREEMENT (通知仲裁的資助協議)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event involves sending written notifications about the existence and details of an arbitration funding agreement within a specific timeframe to all parties involved in the arbitration process, as well as the arbitration institution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL PROCEEDINGS BEFORE COURT OR OTHER JUDICIAL AUTHORITY (法律程序前的法院或其他司法機構)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to legal actions that may take place in courts or other judicial bodies outside of Hong Kong, where further communications related to third-party funding might be made."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOVERNMENT BODY (政府部門)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A government body is an entity within the jurisdiction mentioned, which could include regulatory authorities that may require disclosures under certain legal obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATORY BODY (監管機構)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A regulatory body is a specific type of organization responsible for overseeing and enforcing regulations related to arbitration funding or other financial activities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROFESSIONAL ADVISER'S ADVICE ON THIRD PARTY FUNDING (專業顧問就第三者資助提供的意見)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event involves seeking professional advice from an advisor regarding the process of obtaining third-party funding for arbitration, which may be communicated to such advisors under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION INSTITUTION'S ROLE IN NOTIFICATIONS (仲裁機構在通知中的角色)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An arbitration institution plays a crucial role in receiving and processing notifications related to third party funding agreements as part of its functions in managing the arbitration process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL OBLIGATION (法律義務)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A legal obligation refers to the requirement under certain laws or regulations that parties involved must disclose specific information, such as the identity of a financier, within specified timeframes and contexts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCESS (仲裁程序)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Arbitration Process is the formal mechanism for resolving disputes through arbitration as per agreed-upon terms in an arbitration agreement, involving arbitrators who make binding decisions based on evidence and arguments presented by parties involved."&lt;SEP&gt;"The arbitration process is a method for resolving disputes through binding decisions made by an arbitrator or panel of arbitrators, which may involve communications related to third-party funding agreements as part of the overall proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-efd35e44f40ed90831a05d2c28acb9a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 26}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION (爭端解決)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dispute resolution refers to the broader industry and practice of resolving conflicts through various methods including arbitration, where communication about third party funding is a key aspect."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 26}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCIAL SUPPORT FOR ARBITRATION (仲裁的財務支援)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financial support for arbitration involves providing funds or resources to cover costs associated with the arbitration process, which can be communicated under specific legal and procedural conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRD PARTY FINANCIER (第三者資助方)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A third-party financier is an individual or entity that provides financial assistance for an arbitration process, often requiring disclosure of their identity as per regulatory requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD (仲裁裁決)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An arbitration award refers to the final decision made by arbitrators in a dispute resolution process, which may be subject to further communications or enforcement actions related to third-party funding agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL RIGHT OR INTEREST (法律權利或利益)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A legal right or interest is any entitlement protected under law that can justify the communication of information for purposes such as protecting or pursuing it, including in relation to arbitration and third party funding."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROFESSIONAL ADVISER'S ROLE IN COMMUNICATIONS (專業顧問在通訊中的角色)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A professional adviser plays a crucial role in providing guidance on the communication of information related to third-party funding agreements for arbitration, ensuring compliance with legal and ethical standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATORY REQUIREMENT (監管要求)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Regulatory requirements are laws or guidelines that govern how certain communications must be made, such as disclosures about third party financiers in the context of arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT OR TRIBUNAL (法院或法庭)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A court or tribunal is a judicial body where legal disputes can be resolved and where further communications related to third-party funding might take place, particularly if such communications are made for enforcement purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL PROCEEDINGS (法律程序)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal proceedings refer to formal actions taken in courts or other judicial bodies to resolve disputes, which may include the communication of information about third party financiers as part of broader legal strategies and procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION INSTITUTION'S ROLE IN FUNDING AGREEMENTS (仲裁機構在資助協議中的角色)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An arbitration institution plays a significant role in managing and overseeing the process of third-party funding for arbitrations, ensuring compliance with relevant laws and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fecad4beaf00010bb9b31611ad456e88</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISCLOSURE ABOUT THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to the disclosure requirement for third-party funding in an arbitration process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd5d5713c2c272a2a9c9f2f00a8d2933</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 411}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1117}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISCLOSURE ABOUT END OF THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to the disclosure requirement for when a third-party funding agreement ends in an arbitration process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd5d5713c2c272a2a9c9f2f00a8d2933</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 414}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FUNDING AGREEMENT (ENDS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A product that involves the termination or completion of a financial arrangement where a third party funds another's legal proceedings, typically with conditions attached."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd5d5713c2c272a2a9c9f2f00a8d2933</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 414}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COUNSELING INSTITUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Counseling Institution is an organization appointed by the Secretary for Justice to oversee and review the implementation of certain provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5247edeafb01587bde32ae379e5261dc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUTHORIZED ORGANIZATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Authorized Organization is another type of institution that can be appointed by the Secretary for Justice, distinct from a Counseling Institution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5247edeafb01587bde32ae379e5261dc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 871}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;JUDICIAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Judicial Proceedings refer to formal court proceedings that may be initiated against individuals who fail to comply with specific regulations or agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5247edeafb01587bde32ae379e5261dc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 871}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MISCELLANEOUS DIVISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Miscellaneous Division refers to additional provisions or clauses that are not specifically categorized under other sections but provide supplementary information or rules."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5247edeafb01587bde32ae379e5261dc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 24}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 316}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1005}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIVISION 5 NON-COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Non-compliance with Division 5 is an event where individuals fail to adhere to specific regulations, which may affect legal proceedings but does not automatically lead to liability unless relevant to a court decision."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5247edeafb01587bde32ae379e5261dc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAW DEPARTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Law Department, also known as the Secretary for Justice, is responsible for appointing advisory bodies and authorized institutions in relation to legal matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce27b5b185900927943da2e18ee8c5d0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 417}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSULTATIVE BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A consultative body appointed by the Secretary for Justice to monitor and review the implementation and exercise of certain powers under section 98ZM."&lt;SEP&gt;"A consultative body may be appointed by the Secretary for Justice to monitor and review the operation of certain parts or sections."&lt;SEP&gt;"Consultative body refers to an advisory group that can make rules under certain conditions as stated in section 98ZM."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6183d5dd90a32799bbb3d1b3a01652ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce27b5b185900927943da2e18ee8c5d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b83c6369ee22a5baf386b25e3605cb81</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 417}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUTHORIZED INSTITUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An authorized institution can be appointed by the Secretary for Justice to exercise specific powers under section 98P."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce27b5b185900927943da2e18ee8c5d0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 417}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OUTCOME RELATED FEE STRUCTURE AGREEMENT FOR ARBITRATION (ORFS AGREEMENT)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The ORFS agreement is a document that outlines fee structures related to arbitration and addresses issues such as enforceability and measures to ensure fairness in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce27b5b185900927943da2e18ee8c5d0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 417}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENT FOR ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An ORFS agreement for arbitration is a contract between a client and their lawyer, detailing the terms and notification obligations related to arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"An ORFS agreement for arbitration is a legal instrument that allows for arbitration, not prohibited by common law doctrines of maintenance, champerty and barratry."&lt;SEP&gt;"An ORFS agreement for arbitration is a specific type of agreement made between a client and their lawyer for an arbitration process, effective from the day Divisions 3, 4, and 7 come into operation. It does not include funding agreements as defined in Part 10A."&lt;SEP&gt;"An ORFS agreement for arbitration is a specific type of agreement that involves arbitration and must be disclosed according to certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORFS Agreement for Arbitration is a type of agreement that can be entered into between parties and their lawyers to cover costs in arbitration, involving concepts like conditional fee agreements and legal expenses insurance premiums."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORFS agreement for arbitration refers to an agreement made between parties and their lawyers for resolving disputes through arbitration, involving communication of information under specific conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORFS agreement for arbitration refers to an agreement used in arbitration processes and is void or unenforceable under certain conditions related to personal injuries claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6183d5dd90a32799bbb3d1b3a01652ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eac62f2f1327a829e40a168eae3df71e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8df8f796c1527424030ca7952635395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2799d5a0031a68f64f3cd87dbc0dabae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de0dbf6f53e54d631a68b2a604874d6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4158bcd358cce62e9937de8896e1ba0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5edce5a2ca2140e309b11b70c29b15f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 442}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FUNDING AGREEMENT WITHIN THE MEANING OF PART 10A&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Funding agreements are financial products or arrangements that do not fall under the scope of Part 10B's provisions regarding arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8df8f796c1527424030ca7952635395</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION (ARBITRATION)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration refers to a legal process where disputes are resolved by an arbitrator, including court procedures, emergency arbitrator proceedings, and mediation processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8df8f796c1527424030ca7952635395</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 442}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL EXPENSES INSURANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal Expenses Insurance is a type of coverage that pays for legal costs and other related expenses incurred by clients during litigation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal Expenses Insurance 是一种保险合同，为客户提供部分或全部因某事项产生的法律费用、败诉成本或杂费报销。"&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal expenses insurance is a type of insurance policy designed to cover certain legal costs, including litigation fees and disbursements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8df8f796c1527424030ca7952635395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce0cbc87febf0559389231de15b6441b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 409}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1110}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONEY OR MONEY'S WORTH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Money or Money's Worth 包括任何形式的资金、资产、证券、有形或无形财产或服务，以及任何可能产生财务价值的其他考虑因素。"&lt;SEP&gt;"Money or money's worth refers to any form of financial value, whether in the form of cash, assets, collateral, tangible property, intangible property, services, debts, or anything that can be quantified into monetary terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce0cbc87febf0559389231de15b6441b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8df8f796c1527424030ca7952635395</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 409}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1110}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART 10B NOT APPLICABLE TO FUNDING AGREEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The application of Part 10B does not extend to funding agreements as defined under Part 10A, indicating a specific legal distinction in the context of arbitration and financial arrangements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b8df8f796c1527424030ca7952635395</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FEE OR REIMBURSEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fee or Reimbursement refers to the process of paying for expenses incurred, which can be any form of money, assets, collateral, tangible or intangible property or services."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-454f67393ac66e31ad436e5012345559</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 444}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDITIONAL FEE AGREEMENT (CFA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Conditional Fee Agreement is an agreement where legal fees are paid only if the case is successful, as mentioned under Section 98ZC."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-454f67393ac66e31ad436e5012345559</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 444}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DAMAGES-BASED AGREEMENT (DBA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Damages-Based Agreement is a type of fee arrangement where lawyers' fees are linked to the amount of damages recovered for their clients, as detailed in Section 98ZD."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-454f67393ac66e31ad436e5012345559</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 444}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCIAL BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financial Benefit refers to any form of money or its equivalent value except for certain types of payments related to legal costs and expenses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-454f67393ac66e31ad436e5012345559</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 444}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HYBRID DAMAGES-BASED AGREEMENT (HDBA)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Hybrid Damages-Based Agreement is a combination of traditional fee structures with damages-based agreements, as described in Section 98ZE."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-454f67393ac66e31ad436e5012345559</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 444}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE LAW PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Law Practitioners Ordinance Cap. 159 refers to the legal framework governing lawyers and their practices in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-454f67393ac66e31ad436e5012345559</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 443}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Expenses refer to costs incurred by a lawyer or directly by the client's party, including insurance premiums for legal expenses insurance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-454f67393ac66e31ad436e5012345559</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 444}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLIENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Client is an individual or party that must provide written notice about the completion of an ORFS agreement for arbitration within 15 days after its end."&lt;SEP&gt;"For a lawyer, a Client includes anyone who hires or is about to hire the lawyer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The client is a party involved in the arbitration process, required by law to enter into and adhere to an ORFS agreement with their lawyer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de0dbf6f53e54d631a68b2a604874d6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eac62f2f1327a829e40a168eae3df71e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-454f67393ac66e31ad436e5012345559</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 443}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESULT ORIENTED CHARGING FRAMEWORK (ORFS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ORFS refers to a framework for charging based on the outcome of legal services, as detailed under relevant sections of the Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ca2c3669141d3f1cd87a21d68d494cf5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 409}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1111}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL OR COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The arbitral tribunal or court refers to the body responsible for resolving disputes through arbitration or judicial proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 410}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1113}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLIENT (當事人)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Client refers to a person who retains or employs a lawyer, including those potentially liable for legal costs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CODE OF PRACTICE (實務守則)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT, LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Code of Practice is the set of guidelines issued by relevant authorities and updated from time to time for lawyers' professional conduct."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDITIONAL FEE AGREEMENT (按條件收費協議)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT, LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conditional Fee Agreement allows a lawyer's fees to be paid out of any damages awarded in a case."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DAMAGES-BASED AGREEMENT (按損害賠償收費協議)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT, LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Damages-Based Agreement is an arrangement where legal costs are linked to the amount recovered from a claim."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMERGENCY ARBITRATOR (緊急仲裁員)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Emergency Arbitrator is appointed temporarily to handle urgent issues before formal arbitration proceedings start."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXPENSES (開支)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT, LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Expenses include disbursements made by a lawyer or client and legal expenses insurance premiums paid by the client."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCIAL BENEFIT (財務利益)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT, ECONOMICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financial Benefit refers to any monetary gain but excludes certain types of awards related to costs and expenses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HYBRID DAMAGES-BASED AGREEMENT (混合式按損害賠償收費協議)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT, LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hybrid Damages-Based Agreement combines elements of both conditional fee agreements and damages-based agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 29 OF CAP. 159 (《第159章》第29條)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT, LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 29 of the Legal Practitioners Ordinance defines barristers enrolled on its roll."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 235}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 874}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 5 OF CAP. 159 (《第159章》第5條)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT, LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 5 of the Legal Practitioners Ordinance defines solicitors enrolled on its roll."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 235}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 874}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOREIGN LAWYER AS DEFINED BY SECTION 2(1) OF CAP. 159 (《第159章》第2條(一))&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT, LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Foreign Lawyer is a term used in the Legal Practitioners Ordinance to refer to individuals qualified to practice law outside Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 235}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 874}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 32 OR SECTION 33 (《第159章》第32或第33條)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT, LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sections 32 and 33 of the Legal Practitioners Ordinance pertain to mediation proceedings and appointments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 235}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 873}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 98ZN (《第159章》第98ZN條)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT, LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 98ZN of the Legal Practitioners Ordinance relates to codes of practice for lawyers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 235}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 874}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 98ZT (《第159章》第98ZT條)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT, LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 98ZT of the Legal Practitioners Ordinance deals with appointments by the Secretary for Justice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 235}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 874}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 98ZE (《第159章》第98ZE條)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT, LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 98ZE of the Legal Practitioners Ordinance concerns hybrid damages-based agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 235}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 874}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;律師&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"律師是为客户提供法律服务的专业人士，在此文本中负责发出关于ORFS協議的通知。"&lt;SEP&gt;"律師是指根据《律师条例》第29条注册的出庭律师，或根据《律师条例》第5条注册的执业律师，或者具备其他司法辖区法律资格的人士。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de0dbf6f53e54d631a68b2a604874d6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce0cbc87febf0559389231de15b6441b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 409}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1110}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;出庭律师&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"出庭律师是指根据《律师条例》第29条注册的律师。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce0cbc87febf0559389231de15b6441b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;执业律师&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"执业律师是指根据《律师条例》第5条注册的律师。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce0cbc87febf0559389231de15b6441b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;仲裁&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"仲裁是一种争议解决方式，可能涉及ORFS协议的应用。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce0cbc87febf0559389231de15b6441b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;资助协议&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"资助协议不是指与仲裁相关的ORFS协议的一部分，具体定义见《律师条例》第10A部。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce0cbc87febf0559389231de15b6441b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDITIONAL FEE AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Conditional Fee Agreement (success fee as defined by section 98ZC(2)) is a type of agreement where the success fee applies if the ORFS agreement for arbitration is in place, indicating financial terms based on outcome."&lt;SEP&gt;"A conditional fee agreement is a type of ORFS agreement where lawyers agree to charge success fees only if the client achieves a successful outcome in their case."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conditional Fee Agreement is an agreement between a client and their lawyer where payment of success fee occurs only if there's a successful outcome for the client."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2799d5a0031a68f64f3cd87dbc0dabae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5edce5a2ca2140e309b11b70c29b15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80dd0247f7607a0ca7c4bc8e5c16d806</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 33}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DAMAGES-BASED AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A damages-based agreement is a legal contract where the lawyer agrees to be paid only if and based on the financial benefit obtained by the client in the matter. It involves two types: standard DBAs and hybrid DBAs."&lt;SEP&gt;"A damages-based agreement is another form of ORFS agreement related to arbitration processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2799d5a0031a68f64f3cd87dbc0dabae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98e9907f4439e46ca077ec9da34b8a1f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 409}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1112}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HYBRID DAMAGES-BASED AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A hybrid damages-based agreement combines elements of a conditional fee and a damages-based agreement in the context of arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"A hybrid damages-based agreement is a legal contract combining elements of both standard damages-based agreements (DBAs) where payment is made only if there's financial benefit to the client, and traditional lawyer fees that may or may not be discounted."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2799d5a0031a68f64f3cd87dbc0dabae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98e9907f4439e46ca077ec9da34b8a1f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 409}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1112}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUCCESS FEE (SUCCESS FEE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS,SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Success fees refer to additional charges calculated based on the outcome of legal matters, where lawyers only charge if their client achieves success. The amount is determined by comparing what would have been charged had there been no ORFS agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2799d5a0031a68f64f3cd87dbc0dabae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 33}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUCCESSFUL OUTCOME (SUCCESSFUL OUTCOME)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A successful outcome in a legal context refers to the result that meets the agreed-upon criteria for success between a client and their lawyer, which can include various positive results from a case."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2799d5a0031a68f64f3cd87dbc0dabae</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 409}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1112}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUCCESS FEE (成功收費)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Success Fee refers to a calculated payment based on what a lawyer would have charged under normal circumstances, but is contingent upon a successful outcome in the matter."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-80dd0247f7607a0ca7c4bc8e5c16d806</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 33}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUCCESSFUL OUTCOME (成果)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Successful Outcome describes any result of the matter that meets the agreed-upon description of success between client and their lawyer, including financial benefits obtained by the client."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-80dd0247f7607a0ca7c4bc8e5c16d806</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 33}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DAMAGES-BASED AGREEMENT (DBA費用)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Damages-Based Agreement is an agreement where a lawyer charges only if the client obtains a financial benefit in the matter."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-80dd0247f7607a0ca7c4bc8e5c16d806</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 33}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DBA FEES (DBA费用)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"DBA Fees are calculated based on the financial benefits obtained by the client within the matter, as per the damages-based agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-80dd0247f7607a0ca7c4bc8e5c16d806</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 33}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORFS協議&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ORFS agreement is a type of contract or document related to arbitration, with specified conditions and rules."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORFS协议是一种用于仲裁的特定类型的技术或工具，具体条款和规则未在给定文本中详细说明。"&lt;SEP&gt;"ORFS協議是一种用于仲裁的协议，涉及当事人与律师之间的条款和通知义务。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de0dbf6f53e54d631a68b2a604874d6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bdc18a88b44e3aeac65b0b72ead47ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ec40a32e838182a39a402688664a335</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 408}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1109}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;普通法的助証罪&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The common law offence of maintenance refers to the illegal practice of providing financial support for a lawsuit, including champerty which is specifically mentioned as not applying in relation to ORFS agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8bdc18a88b44e3aeac65b0b72ead47ac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 408}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1109}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;唆訟者罪&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The common law offence of being a common barrator refers to engaging in litigation for improper motives or interests, also specified as not applicable to ORFS agreements for arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8bdc18a88b44e3aeac65b0b72ead47ac</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 408}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1109}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;包攬訴訟的侵權法律責任&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The tort of maintenance (including the tort of champerty) is mentioned and stated not to apply in relation to ORFS agreements for arbitration. This refers to a specific type of legal responsibility related to providing financial support or engaging in litigation improperly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8bdc18a88b44e3aeac65b0b72ead47ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第98ZF條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 98ZF specifies that common law offences such as maintenance and being a common barrator do not apply to ORFS agreements for arbitration, indicating the specific rules governing these legal issues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8bdc18a88b44e3aeac65b0b72ead47ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第98ZG條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 98ZG states that the tort of maintenance does not apply in relation to ORFS agreements for arbitration, further detailing the exceptions and applicability of certain laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8bdc18a88b44e3aeac65b0b72ead47ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第98ZH條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 98ZH clarifies that other rules of law regarding contracts being contrary to public policy or illegal are unaffected by Sections 98ZF and 98ZG, providing a broader context for legal considerations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8bdc18a88b44e3aeac65b0b72ead47ac</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第10B部&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part 10B applies in relation to non-Hong Kong arbitration, indicating specific rules or procedures that come into effect when the place of arbitration is outside Hong Kong."</data>
