<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION SUBCONTRACT AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL AGREEMENT, CONTRACT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Construction Subcontract Agreement is a contract under which part of the work specified by a main construction contract (main contract) is subcontracted to another party. It may also include an arbitration agreement as per Section 101."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8ad741dbed5c956a0e2be863adf9b077</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TABLE 2&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Table 2 refers to an unspecified document containing terms that may apply under specific conditions in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ca57b579105e713a9a47fbe85dd981f6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HONG KONG CONSTRUCTION SUBCONTRACTING CASES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hong Kong Construction Subcontracting Cases refers to scenarios where construction operations are subcontracted within the context of Hong Kong's building industry, involving various agreements and provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f0a5fd141643101c1f971cefdaf4f9ef</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION OPERATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction Operations is a term defined in the Building Industry Council Ordinance (Chapter 587) that encompasses all activities related to constructing buildings or structures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f0a5fd141643101c1f971cefdaf4f9ef</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 800}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBCONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Subcontract refers to agreements that are part of a Main Private Contract, further detailing the terms for carrying out construction work or providing related goods and services."&lt;SEP&gt;"A subcontract is another form of agreement that falls under the context of total private contracts and their related disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of contract mentioned but not detailed further. "&lt;SEP&gt;"Subcontract is a construction contract entered into for carrying out work under another construction contract or supplying related goods and services, regardless of whether parties involved are also part of the main contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subcontract refers to an agreement where part of the construction operations are subcontracted from one party to another, often involving multiple layers of contracts and agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f0a5fd141643101c1f971cefdaf4f9ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f53c86b3a5549c4a064860e12f41a1b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04158b577f867f33b0abd25893c009fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66157f73d78c8a042051d0b5db5e4492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e089cfc832db9c43bb24baa7baf3ed42</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 800}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OPT-IN PROVISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Opt-in Provisions are clauses within agreements, such as those found in Schedule 2 of this text, which automatically apply to certain cases under specific conditions without the need for explicit consent from all parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f0a5fd141643101c1f971cefdaf4f9ef</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION INDUSTRY COUNCIL ORDINANCE (CAP. 587)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Construction Industry Council Ordinance is a legal document governing certain aspects of the construction industry in Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Construction Industry Council Ordinance is a legal document that defines terms such as 'construction contract' and 'construction operations', providing context for the application of arbitration agreements in construction projects."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e40e8a615669f7f3c43f8171f5d7b57</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 100(A) OR (B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 100(a) or (b) refers to specific conditions under which certain provisions apply regarding subcontracting and arbitration agreements within the context of a construction contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (2), (3), (4)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsections (2), (3), and (4) are legal clauses that provide detailed rules for applying arbitration agreements in specific scenarios, reflecting regulatory frameworks in social science contexts such as law and policy-making."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NATURAL PERSON WHO IS ORDINARILY RESIDENT OUTSIDE HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A natural person who is typically a human individual residing outside of Hong Kong, relevant to the conditions under which certain provisions apply regarding arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BODY CORPORATE—INCORPORATED UNDER THE LAW OF A PLACE OUTSIDE HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Body Corporate refers to an entity incorporated in a jurisdiction other than Hong Kong, impacting the application of arbitration agreements and subcontracting operations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASSOCIATION—FORMED UNDER THE LAW OF A PLACE OUTSIDE HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Association formed according to laws from regions outside Hong Kong, relevant for conditions affecting arbitration agreements and subcontracting operations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CENTRAL MANAGEMENT AND CONTROL EXERCISED OUTSIDE HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Central Management and Control refers to the governance structure of an entity or association that operates primarily outside Hong Kong, impacting legal provisions such as those related to arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FURTHER SUBCONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Further Subcontract is a secondary agreement within the context of construction contracts where operations are further divided and sublet, often involving additional arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SCHEDULE 2 APPLY TO A SUBCONTRACTING PARTIES' ARBITRATION AGREEMENT UNDER SUBSECTION (1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The application of Schedule 2 provisions in relation to arbitration agreements as stipulated by subsections within the context of construction contracts and legal frameworks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION CONTRACT (建造合約) HAS THE MEANING GIVEN TO IT BY SECTION 2(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY,INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction Contract is defined legally with specific meanings under Hong Kong's Construction Industry Council Ordinance, impacting arbitration agreements in construction projects."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION OPERATIONS (建造工程) HAS THE MEANING GIVEN TO IT BY SCHEDULE 1 TO THE CONSTRUCTION INDUSTRY COUNCIL ORDINANCE (CAP. 587)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction Operations are defined with specific meanings under Hong Kong's Construction Industry Council Ordinance, providing context for legal and regulatory frameworks in construction projects."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2015年第11號第4條修訂&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The revision of the 4th article from the 11th number of the 2015 regulation, indicating changes or updates to legal provisions affecting arbitration agreements and subcontracting operations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RELEVANT OPERATION THAT IS SUBCONTRACTED UNDER THE SUBCONTRACT IS FURTHER SUBCONTRACTED TO ANOTHER PERSON UNDER A FURTHER CONSTRUCTION CONTRACT (FURTHER SUBCONTRACT)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Further Subcontract refers to secondary subcontracts within primary construction contracts, often involving additional legal agreements and arbitration provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISIONS IN SCHEDULE 2 APPLY TO THE ARBITRATION AGREEMENT SO INCLUDED IN THAT FURTHER SUBCONTRACT AS IF THAT FURTHER SUBCONTRACT WERE A SUBCONTRACT UNDER SUBSECTION (1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Provisions from Schedule 2 are applied to arbitration agreements within secondary subcontracts, reflecting complex legal frameworks and their application."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 102&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 102 refers to specific conditions or provisions that may affect the applicability of certain clauses in construction contracts and related arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION CONTRACT (建造合約)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A legally enforceable agreement for carrying out or supplying goods and services related to construction work, not including development contracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Construction Contract is a legal document defining terms such as 'construction operations', impacting the application of arbitration agreements within specific contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Construction contract refers to the document related to which a determination has been made, as stated under section 48(2)(ii) of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bf52072b8dd02eb0cf0d0e08e22d0cd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 452}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION OPERATIONS (建造工程)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction Operations are defined in legal documents and impact various aspects including subcontracting and arbitration agreements, reflecting industry-specific regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 452}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RELEVANT OPERATION WHICH IS TO BE PERFORMED OUTSIDE HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Relevant Operation refers to tasks or activities that will take place outside of Hong Kong, impacting the application of certain legal provisions such as those related to arbitration and subcontracting operations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERSON TO WHOM THE WHOLE OR ANY PART OF THE RELEVANT OPERATION IS SUBCONTRACTED UNDER THE SUBCONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION,PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Person refers to individuals or entities who are contracted for specific parts of a construction project, impacting legal agreements such as those related to arbitration and operations performed outside Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSTANTIAL PART OF THE RELEVANT OPERATION WHICH IS SUBCONTRACTED UNDER THE SUBCONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Substantial Part refers to significant portions or activities within a construction contract that are sublet, often involving complex legal agreements such as those related to arbitration and operations performed outside Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (1) HAS EFFECT SUBJECT TO SUBSECTION (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (1) is modified by Subsection (2), indicating the interplay between different clauses in legal documents affecting arbitration agreements and subcontracting operations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERSON TO WHOM THE WHOLE OR ANY PART OF THE RELEVANT OPERATION THAT IS SUBCONTRACTED UNDER THE SUBCONTRACT HAS NO PLACE OF BUSINESS IN HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION,PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Person refers to entities without a physical presence in Hong Kong, impacting legal provisions such as those related to arbitration and operations performed outside Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSECTION (1) DOES NOT APPLY IF—&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsection (1) is subject to certain conditions that may exempt it from application, reflecting the complexity of legal frameworks in construction contracts and arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBCONTRACTING PARTIES' ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY,SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subcontracting Parties' Arbitration Agreement refers to specific clauses within subcontracts for resolving disputes through arbitration, impacting various aspects including operations performed outside Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 100 AND 101&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sections 100 and 101 are provisions within the ordinance that may or may not apply based on specific conditions, indicating technical rules for arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e40e8a615669f7f3c43f8171f5d7b57</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 99&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 99 is a provision in the ordinance whose operation is not affected by certain opt-in clauses as specified under Section 102 (b)(ii)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e40e8a615669f7f3c43f8171f5d7b57</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 196}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART 11A&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY/LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part 11A is a section of an ordinance that deals with arbitrations relating to intellectual property rights."&lt;SEP&gt;"Part 11A is a section or part of the legislation that can be applied if all relevant parties agree, providing specific rules for certain arbitrations and related proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ca44dbb10a88be455b8df250e7a7b82b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da8c2939156a68d994838f2e9bd0f166</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 881}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1198}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IPR DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An IPR dispute refers to conflicts or inconsistencies in the application of provisions related to intellectual property rights within this part."&lt;SEP&gt;"IPR dispute refers to an intellectual property rights-related disagreement that may be resolved through arbitration."&lt;SEP&gt;"IPR dispute refers to disputes over intellectual property rights, including enforceability, infringement, validity, ownership, scope, duration and other aspects of IPRs, as well as disputes related to transactions involving IPRs and compensation for IPRs."&lt;SEP&gt;"IPR dispute refers to disputes related to intellectual property rights, which are subject to specific provisions in Hong Kong law regarding arbitration and public policy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-75abbf9735ce9959e08a7259663fa08d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98b6711af3c5bbaf4412b6b0eda86915&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da8c2939156a68d994838f2e9bd0f166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d9d91db74534ffd661699611c1087da</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 439}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KNOWLEDGE产权 (知识产权)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Intellectual Property Rights, abbreviated as IPR, refer to various types of intangible assets such as patents, trademarks, copyrights, and others that are protected under specific laws or regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da8c2939156a68d994838f2e9bd0f166</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 440}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PATENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A patent is a form of intellectual property protection granted by the government for an invention, giving its owner the right to exclude others from making, using, selling, offering for sale, importing, or otherwise exploiting the patented technology without permission."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da8c2939156a68d994838f2e9bd0f166</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 439}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GEOGRAPHICAL INDICATION (地理标志)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A geographical indication is a sign used on products that have a specific geographical origin and possess qualities or a reputation due to that origin."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da8c2939156a68d994838f2e9bd0f166</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 439}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DESIGN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An industrial design refers to the appearance of an object, which can be two-dimensional (such as drawings) or three-dimensional (such as objects). It is often associated with aesthetic aspects but also includes functional elements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da8c2939156a68d994838f2e9bd0f166</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 439}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COPYRIGHT OR RELATED RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Copyright protects original works of authorship including literary, musical, and artistic works. Related rights protect the economic and moral interests of performers, producers of phonograms, and broadcasting organizations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da8c2939156a68d994838f2e9bd0f166</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 439}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOMAIN NAME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A domain name is a unique label that identifies an Internet resource such as a website or network service."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da8c2939156a68d994838f2e9bd0f166</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 439}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTEGRATED CIRCUIT LAYOUT DESIGN (集成电路布图设计)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An integrated circuit layout design, also known as mask work, refers to the artistic and technical arrangement of elements in an integrated circuit. It is protected by copyright-like laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da8c2939156a68d994838f2e9bd0f166</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 439}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLANT VARIETY RIGHT (植物新品种权)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A plant variety right protects new varieties of plants that have been developed through breeding or other means."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da8c2939156a68d994838f2e9bd0f166</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 439}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION, BUSINESS SECRETS, INDUSTRIAL KNOWLEDGE RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These refer to the rights associated with confidential information and business secrets. They protect trade secrets and proprietary knowledge within a company."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da8c2939156a68d994838f2e9bd0f166</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 439}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACTION FOR COUNTERFEITING (假冒诉讼)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An action for counterfeiting is a legal proceeding brought against someone who has infringed upon intellectual property by producing or selling counterfeit goods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da8c2939156a68d994838f2e9bd0f166</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 439}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PART 11A OF THE ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to Part 11A, which was added in 2017 and deals with arbitrations related to intellectual property rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da8c2939156a68d994838f2e9bd0f166</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 440}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 103B (IPR)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 103B defines Intellectual Property Rights as a broad category of legal protections for various types of creations, including patents, trademarks, copyrights, etc."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da8c2939156a68d994838f2e9bd0f166</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 103C (IPR DISPUTE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This section provides the definition and context for intellectual property disputes within Part 11A."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-da8c2939156a68d994838f2e9bd0f166</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PASSING OFF OR SIMILAR ACTION AGAINST UNFAIR COMPETITION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Passing off or similar action against unfair competition is a legal remedy to protect goodwill by litigation when facing an act of unfair competition."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c7a6213a2f876bebd1fa609680c4fd8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY RIGHT (IPR)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An intellectual property right includes various types such as patents, trademarks, geographical indications, designs, copyrights, domain names, layout-designs of integrated circuits, plant variety rights, and confidential information. It pertains to the protection through registration or other means."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c7a6213a2f876bebd1fa609680c4fd8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGISTRATION (註冊)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Registration in relation to an intellectual property right includes both the process of granting such a right and its application for registration if protectible by law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c7a6213a2f876bebd1fa609680c4fd8</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERPRETATION: IPR DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event involves the clarification or definition of what constitutes an Intellectual Property Rights (IPR) dispute according to legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98b6711af3c5bbaf4412b6b0eda86915</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 881}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1197}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIFIED ENTITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Specified Entity refers to any organization under Hong Kong law or other places' laws, including courts, tribunals, and individuals holding political or administrative positions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-49949a92adb17e5dadd770d704b72f8e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1192}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IPR DISPUTES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"IPR Disputes are knowledge property rights controversies that can be resolved through arbitration between the parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-49949a92adb17e5dadd770d704b72f8e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1192}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 70 OF THE ARBITRATION ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 70 of the Arbitration Ordinance grants arbitral tribunals powers to award remedies or assistance in resolving IPR disputes between parties, subject to their agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-49949a92adb17e5dadd770d704b72f8e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OPTION I OF ARTICLE 7(1) OF THE UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a specific option in an international legal framework for arbitration, related to intellectual property rights (IPR) disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39620e4541eb49ae7a7ea14a2cf664bb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 232}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 850}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIFIED ENTITY (指明實體)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A term defined within the text, referring to any entity under Hong Kong or other laws which may have exclusive jurisdiction over certain legal matters but does not preclude arbitration for IPR disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Specified entity includes the Government and any body listed in Schedule 3, as well as subsidiaries of such bodies according to section 4 of Schedule 1 to the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39620e4541eb49ae7a7ea14a2cf664bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f53c86b3a5549c4a064860e12f41a1b1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 801}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KNOWLEDGE PROPERTY RIGHT DISPUTE (IPR DISPUTE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Intellectual Property Rights Dispute refers to any disagreement or conflict involving patents, trademarks, copyrights, etc., which can be submitted for arbitration as per the legal framework provided by UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39620e4541eb49ae7a7ea14a2cf664bb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 232}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 850}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THIRD PARTY LICENSEE (第三方特許持有人)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Third Party Licensee refers to an entity that is a licensee of the IP under a license granted by a party to the arbitral proceedings, but not a party to the arbitral proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Third Party Licensee refers to someone or some entity that has been granted permission by an intellectual property owner to use their IP under certain conditions, and is not automatically considered a claimant in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39620e4541eb49ae7a7ea14a2cf664bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b2687bf72645c6f4d1292a242f8ee55</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 62}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 70 OF THE UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This section refers to specific provisions within the model law that allow arbitral tribunals to award remedies or relief related to intellectual property rights disputes, subject to any agreements between parties involved in such disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39620e4541eb49ae7a7ea14a2cf664bb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 232}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 849}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 103E OF THE UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This section pertains to the enforceability of arbitral awards concerning IPR disputes within an arbitration process, specifically addressing third-party licensees and their rights or liabilities in such proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39620e4541eb49ae7a7ea14a2cf664bb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 232}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 849}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY (IP)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Intellectual Property refers to creations of the mind for which a patent, copyright, trademark, or trade secret provides protection."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b2687bf72645c6f4d1292a242f8ee55</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 62}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXCLUSIVE LICENSEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Exclusive Licensee is an entity that holds exclusive rights under a license granted by a party to the arbitral proceedings and is not a party to the arbitration proceeding."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b2687bf72645c6f4d1292a242f8ee55</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 62}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NON-EXCLUSIVE LICENSEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Non-Exclusive Licensee is an entity that holds non-exclusive rights under a license granted by a party to the arbitral proceedings and is not a party to the arbitration proceeding."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b2687bf72645c6f4d1292a242f8ee55</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 62}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTY TO THE ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON, ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Party to Arbitration Proceedings refers to entities involved in the arbitration process as either claimants or respondents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b2687bf72645c6f4d1292a242f8ee55</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 62}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTIONS 86(2)(A), 89(3)(A), 95(3)(A) AND 98D(3)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These sections pertain to the settlement of matters by arbitration, stating that such matters are not incapable of resolution solely because they relate to intellectual property rights disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e876339a2824bdfc9f79a847c9528353</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTIONS 86(2)(B), 89(3)(B), 95(3)(B) AND 98D(3)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These sections address the enforcement of arbitration awards, indicating that enforcing such awards does not violate Hong Kong's public policy merely because they relate to intellectual property rights disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e876339a2824bdfc9f79a847c9528353</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AWARD (裁決)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Award or 裁決 refers to a decision made in arbitral proceedings, which can include declaratory awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d9d91db74534ffd661699611c1087da</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 436}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PATENTS ORDINANCE (CAP. 514) &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Patents Ordinance is a legal document that governs patents and their validity in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2d9d91db74534ffd661699611c1087da</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 436}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHORT-TERM PATENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Short-term patent refers to a type of patent as defined in the Patent Ordinance (PO), which may be subject to specific enforcement procedures outlined within the ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A short-term patent is a type of intellectual property right defined by section 2(1) of the Patents Ordinance (Cap. 514), which has specific characteristics distinguishing it from other types of patents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Short-term patent refers to a type of intellectual property with limited protection period, which can be enforced through arbitration proceedings as described under the Patents Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7dab1df7b5bb64669485d4dce1155fb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d9d91db74534ffd661699611c1087da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8322a8472d188ae5550ad46529f8b37b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 885}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE PATENT ORDINANCE (PO)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Patent Ordinance (PO) is a legal framework governing patents, including short-term patents, and outlines procedures for enforcing rights associated with these patents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7dab1df7b5bb64669485d4dce1155fb1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 885}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENFORCEMENT OF PATENT RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ACTIVITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The enforcement of patent rights involves actions taken by a patent proprietor to protect their intellectual property as defined in the Patent Ordinance (PO), including commencing arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7dab1df7b5bb64669485d4dce1155fb1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 885}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PATENTS ORDINANCE (CAP. 514)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Patents Ordinance (Cap. 514) is a legal document that defines terms such as 'short-term patent' and outlines procedures related to patents in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8322a8472d188ae5550ad46529f8b37b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 885}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ABBREVIATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"PO stands for the Patents Ordinance, which governs matters related to patents in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8322a8472d188ae5550ad46529f8b37b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 885}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATOR OR MEDIATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An arbitrator or mediator refers to individuals who are responsible for resolving disputes through arbitration, as described in the Patents Ordinance (Cap. 514)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8322a8472d188ae5550ad46529f8b37b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 64}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL OR MEDIATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Arbitral tribunal or mediator refers to the body responsible for arbitration and mediation processes. They are liable for their actions in exercising arbitral functions or mediating roles, provided these acts were done dishonestly."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitral tribunal or mediator are organizations responsible for arbitral functions or mediation procedures in dispute resolution processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6ad0ff0d84a37cbf46865a76db573d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc6d15568c3f749767f8090588c63f24</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 916}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE OR AGENT OF THE TRIBUNAL OR MEDIATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employees or agents working under an Arbitral tribunal or mediator can be held legally responsible if they act dishonestly while performing tasks related to arbitration or mediation processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6ad0ff0d84a37cbf46865a76db573d6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 916}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDIATOR (調解員)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Mediator is a person appointed according to section 32, or referred in section 33. They are involved in the process of resolving disputes through mediation and can be held legally responsible for their actions if proven dishonest."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6ad0ff0d84a37cbf46865a76db573d6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 916}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMISSIONER AND MANAGER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Commissioner and Manager are individuals who may be held legally responsible for certain actions or omissions in the context of arbitration or mediation procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner and Manager refer to individuals who appoint arbitrators or mediators and exercise administrative functions related to arbitration or mediation processes. They are only liable in law for certain acts done or omitted dishonestly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c6ad0ff0d84a37cbf46865a76db573d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6afb8943a99ee7bf996b0ce17c18a04b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 860}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE FUNCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Administrative Functions refer to tasks that are procedural in nature, often involving the management of arbitration or mediation processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6afb8943a99ee7bf996b0ce17c18a04b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 860}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEDIATION PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Mediation Procedure is another form of dispute resolution where parties attempt to reach a mutually acceptable agreement with the help of a mediator."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mediation procedures refer to the structured processes and methods used by mediators to facilitate communication between parties, aiming for mutual agreement. This technology involves specific techniques and protocols."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6afb8943a99ee7bf996b0ce17c18a04b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8214b3161676dee8df8d19240ebf6752</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 860}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An arbitration court is an organization where disputes are resolved through binding arbitration rather than litigation in a traditional courtroom setting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8214b3161676dee8df8d19240ebf6752</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 860}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE OR AGENT OF A PERSON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Employee or agent refers to individuals working under an organization who may be liable for actions related to court proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fc6d15568c3f749767f8090588c63f24</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 916}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE HIGH COURT ORDINANCE (CAP. 4)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The High Court Ordinance is the legal framework that includes rules and regulations governing court procedures, specifically mentioned in section 54 of the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fc6d15568c3f749767f8090588c63f24</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 250}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 916}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RULES OF THE HIGH COURT (CAP. 4 SUB. LEG. A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rules of the High Court are procedural guidelines or regulations established by an organization, in this case, the High Court, for conducting court proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-55419da365905ce3e764775f55ac2bfa</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 308}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPEAL, SAVINGS AND TRANSITIONAL PROVISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to a set of provisions dealing with the repeal of certain laws and the transition period for their effects."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b10b221b86861987d9e97938597f2b49</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;E.R. 3 OF 2015&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"E.R. 3 of 2015 is an editorial amendment record indicating changes made in that year."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b10b221b86861987d9e97938597f2b49</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OMITTED AS SPENT—E.R. 3 OF 2015&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This indicates a provision has been omitted due to its expiration according to the specified amendment record."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b10b221b86861987d9e97938597f2b49</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EFFECT OF REPEAL ON SUBSIDIARY LEGISLATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a legal concept or technology dealing with how repealed laws affect ongoing regulations and their continued validity under new ones."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b10b221b86861987d9e97938597f2b49</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSIDIARY LEGISLATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subsidiary Legislation refers to supporting documents or regulations made under the authority of an ordinance, continuing in force as long as they are not inconsistent with the main legislation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b10b221b86861987d9e97938597f2b49</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2015年第3號編輯修訂紀錄&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a record of editorial amendments from 2015, indicating changes or updates to laws and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b10b221b86861987d9e97938597f2b49</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;附表3第1部&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part 1 of Schedule 3 contains savings and transitional arrangements applicable on the commencement of this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b10b221b86861987d9e97938597f2b49</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;附表3第2部&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part 2 of Schedule 3 contains savings and transitional arrangements related to the coming into force of a specific amendment ordinance in 2015."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b10b221b86861987d9e97938597f2b49</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;附表3第3部&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Part 3 of Schedule 3 deals with savings and transitional provisions concerning another amendment ordinance from 2017."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b10b221b86861987d9e97938597f2b49</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 2017&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Arbitration (Amendment) Ordinance 2017 is an event that introduced savings and transitional arrangements related to the commencement of this ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4ff4d9a4c70f60d81fee6914d6220ad</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 2015&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Arbitration (Amendment) Ordinance 2015 is an event that introduced savings and transitional arrangements related to its own commencement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4ff4d9a4c70f60d81fee6914d6220ad</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2017年仲裁(修訂)條例 (第5號)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The 2017 Year Arbitration Amendment Ordinance No. 5 is an event that introduced savings and transitional arrangements related to its own commencement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4ff4d9a4c70f60d81fee6914d6220ad</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;生效日期:2015年7月17日&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The effective date of the ordinance or amendment is July 17, 2015."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4ff4d9a4c70f60d81fee6914d6220ad</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第14部 (PART 14)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"第14部 refers to a specific part in an ordinance or document that deals with certain provisions but does not belong to any other specified types."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4ff4d9a4c70f60d81fee6914d6220ad</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;《貿易法委員會國際商事仲裁示範法》&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The UNCITRAL Model Law on International Commercial Arbitration is a product, specifically a legal framework adopted by the United Nations Commission on International Trade Law in 1985 and amended later."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4ff4d9a4c70f60d81fee6914d6220ad</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 70}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNITED NATIONS COMMISSION ON INTERNATIONAL TRADE LAW (UNCITRAL)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The United Nations Commission on International Trade Law (UNCITRAL) is an organization that develops and promotes legislation in the field of international trade law, including the UNCITRAL Model Law on International Commercial Arbitration."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United Nations Commission on International Trade Law is an organization that developed and updated the UNCITRAL Model Law on International Commercial Arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b88d5ece94b64060cd9c9c3ca51a624&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4ff4d9a4c70f60d81fee6914d6220ad</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 70}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2006年7月7日&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"On July 7, 2006, the United Nations Commission on International Trade Law amended the UNCITRAL Model Law on International Commercial Arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b88d5ece94b64060cd9c9c3ca51a624</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 70}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第一章. 总则&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CHAPTER"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Chapter I of the UNCITRAL Model Law on International Commercial Arbitration contains general provisions that define its scope and application in international commercial arbitration cases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b88d5ece94b64060cd9c9c3ca51a624</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 70}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;适用范围* (第1条)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 1(1) defines the applicability of the law to international commercial arbitration, subject to any agreements between countries with effect within their territories."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b88d5ece94b64060cd9c9c3ca51a624</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;仲裁地点在本国内的情况&quot; (第1条2款)">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"According to Article 1(2), the provisions apply only when the place of arbitration is within the country's territory."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b88d5ece94b64060cd9c9c3ca51a624</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;国际仲裁的情形&quot; (第1条3款)">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 1(3) outlines conditions under which an arbitration can be considered international, such as parties having their business locations in different countries or other specified circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b88d5ece94b64060cd9c9c3ca51a624</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;营业地点&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Business location refers to the place where a party conducts its commercial activities and is used for determining jurisdictional aspects of disputes under Article 1(3) and (4)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b88d5ece94b64060cd9c9c3ca51a624</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;惯常住所&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Place of habitual residence, as mentioned in Article 1(5), serves as an alternative to business location when a party does not have one."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b88d5ece94b64060cd9c9c3ca51a624</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;本法&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This term refers generally to the UNCITRAL Model Law on International Commercial Arbitration and its provisions discussed throughout the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b88d5ece94b64060cd9c9c3ca51a624</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;国际商事仲裁&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"International commercial arbitration, as defined in Article 1(1), is a method of resolving disputes between parties from different countries through an independent third party."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6b88d5ece94b64060cd9c9c3ca51a624</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2006年第三十九届会议&quot;">
