</node>
<node id="&quot;MANDATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mandate refers to the authority and responsibility given to an arbitrator, which can be terminated under specific conditions as outlined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98d869f809c494e89028b24de4ba24f6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 875}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1195}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 13&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 13 is an event that leads to the termination of an arbitrator's mandate."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a15346ce9b7bc33ce02e54674e507b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 14&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 14 is another event that can lead to the termination of an arbitrator's mandate."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a15346ce9b7bc33ce02e54674e507b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATOR'S WITHDRAWAL FROM OFFICE FOR ANY OTHER REASON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The arbitrator's voluntary resignation or being removed due to reasons not specified in Article 13 or 14 constitutes a separate event leading to the termination of their mandate."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a15346ce9b7bc33ce02e54674e507b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REVOCATION OF HIS MANDATE BY AGREEMENT OF THE PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The revocation of an arbitrator's mandate through mutual agreement between the parties is another event that can lead to its termination."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a15346ce9b7bc33ce02e54674e507b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 15. APPOINTMENT OF SUBSTITUTE ARBITRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 15 describes the process for appointing a substitute arbitrator when the original one’s mandate terminates under various circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a15346ce9b7bc33ce02e54674e507b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHAPTER IV. JURISDICTION OF THE ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Chapter IV is a section in an arbitration document that discusses the jurisdiction of the arbitral tribunal, providing details on its authority and limitations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a15346ce9b7bc33ce02e54674e507b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 16. POWER TO DETERMINE ITS OWN JURISDICTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 16 outlines the power of the arbitral tribunal to decide on its own jurisdiction, including disputes over the existence or validity of an arbitration agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3a15346ce9b7bc33ce02e54674e507b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT SPECIFIED IN ARTICLE 6&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The court specified in Article 6 is another organization that can decide matters related to jurisdiction if requested by a party."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f295ffb815631fda7aa87257db86215</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 380}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1079}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRELIMINARY QUESTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A preliminary question is an issue that needs to be decided before proceeding with the main dispute resolution process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f295ffb815631fda7aa87257db86215</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 380}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1079}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATOR(S) APPOINTED BY A PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitrators appointed by a party are individuals chosen by one of the parties involved in the arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f295ffb815631fda7aa87257db86215</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTIES TO THE ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Parties to the arbitral proceedings refer to all entities involved, including those who have appointed or participated in appointing an arbitrator and those defending their statements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f295ffb815631fda7aa87257db86215</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINAL AWARD ON DISPUTES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A final award on disputes is a decision made by the arbitral tribunal after considering all evidence and arguments presented during arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f295ffb815631fda7aa87257db86215</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 380}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1079}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMISSION MEETING IN 2006&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION, EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Commission meeting in 2006 refers to an official gathering of the commission that took place in 2006 for passing certain resolutions or amendments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f295ffb815631fda7aa87257db86215</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 34&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES, MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 34 is a reference to specific legal provisions related to arbitration and provisional measures which provide detailed rules on these matters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0f295ffb815631fda7aa87257db86215</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STATUS QUO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Status quo is a condition of things that existed before a new development took place; in this context, it means maintaining the current state until the dispute is finally decided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d56571b98ba26116ef651214c379b2f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 291}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 978}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DETERMINATION OF THE DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The determination of the dispute refers to the final decision made by an arbitral tribunal after considering all evidence and arguments presented during arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d56571b98ba26116ef651214c379b2f2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 879}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 17(2)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17(2)(a) refers to the conditions under which certain temporary measures can be ordered, involving potential harm that cannot be adequately compensated by damages."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8630302d71316afe5c4d5a0aacb23fcb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 17(2)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17(2)(b) pertains to another condition for ordering such measures, focusing on the likelihood of success in the claim based on the case details."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8630302d71316afe5c4d5a0aacb23fcb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 17(2)(C)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17(2)(c) is part of a series of conditions under which temporary measures can be ordered, involving similar considerations as (a) and (b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8630302d71316afe5c4d5a0aacb23fcb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 17(2)(D)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17(2)(d) refers to another condition or measure that may apply in certain circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8630302d71316afe5c4d5a0aacb23fcb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 17B&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17B deals with applications for preliminary orders and the conditions under which such orders can be issued by the arbitral tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8630302d71316afe5c4d5a0aacb23fcb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 36&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION, EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 36 is referenced as a note at the end of the text, indicating it contains additional information related to interim measures or similar topics."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8630302d71316afe5c4d5a0aacb23fcb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTIES INVOLVED IN THE DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON, ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Parties involved refer to individuals or organizations participating in a dispute, including those requesting interim measures and those against whom such measures are directed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7edd9fa2d61911f5177713c81f63dd22</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE REQUESTED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT, TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An interim measure is a temporary order intended to preserve the status quo until a final decision can be made, often involving actions that prevent or facilitate certain behaviors by parties involved in a dispute."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7edd9fa2d61911f5177713c81f63dd22</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE REQUEST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT, PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Interim Measure Request is part of the application process for preliminary orders, communicated to all parties involved in the arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-74be062ba4c04dd5b51c11f6d66083c4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 897}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1206}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 17C&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY, LEGAL DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 17C outlines specific procedures and conditions related to preliminary orders within an arbitral tribunal context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-74be062ba4c04dd5b51c11f6d66083c4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 789}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 37&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 37 is a referenced location in the text that provides additional information or context for Article 17A mentioned earlier."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 37 specifies exceptions to the rules outlined in Section 35, particularly regarding evidence admissibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d30ea89e5165c3d71c14d8648bf53596&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74be062ba4c04dd5b51c11f6d66083c4</data>
