</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRAL PROCEEDING CONDUCT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The conduct of arbitral proceedings involves ensuring equal treatment for all parties and providing them with a full opportunity to present their case."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd9db0a37334cbb0b10298bc47259fa1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTIES EQUALITY TREATMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Equality treatment refers to the principle that each party in an arbitration should be treated equally, as stated in Article 18."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd9db0a37334cbb0b10298bc47259fa1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROCEDURE AGREEMENT FREEDOM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The freedom of parties to agree on procedures for arbitral proceedings is a key aspect discussed in Articles 19(1) and (2), allowing flexibility while ensuring compliance with the law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd9db0a37334cbb0b10298bc47259fa1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION LOCATION DETERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Determining the location of arbitration, either through mutual agreement or by the arbitral tribunal considering various factors such as convenience, is a significant aspect discussed in Article 20(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd9db0a37334cbb0b10298bc47259fa1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 19(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 19(2) is a provision in the text that discusses the applicability of certain sections and refers to section 47."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e8e0d2ae5a1dc045b65776863de6e9a9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 22(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 22(1) addresses the freedom of parties to agree on the language used in arbitration procedures or its determination by an arbitral tribunal if no agreement is reached."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e8e0d2ae5a1dc045b65776863de6e9a9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTARY EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documentary Evidence refers to written or recorded information submitted as part of arbitral proceedings, which may require translation into agreed-upon languages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentary Evidence refers to written or recorded material that can be used as evidence, such as documents, files, and other tangible items mentioned in Article 26(b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf8d77c0073f8253192bb2eb6ce56e99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEARINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hearings are events where evidence is presented orally, either at the request of a party or as part of the arbitral tribunal's decision-making process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hearings refer to sessions where evidence is presented, and oral arguments take place during the arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ccfc28d1a77070797c9452e760bfd7f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39b02ac25884a8c6102243f2b93f0c03</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 782}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTS AND OTHER MATERIALS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documents and other materials refer to written records and additional information used in arbitration proceedings for making decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39b02ac25884a8c6102243f2b93f0c03</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 856}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1193}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 52&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 52 refers to another part of the document that provides additional information related to the procedures and requirements for arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39b02ac25884a8c6102243f2b93f0c03</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSPECTION MEETING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Inspection Meeting is an event where the arbitral tribunal inspects goods or documents for evidence purposes as part of the proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39b02ac25884a8c6102243f2b93f0c03</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUFFICIENT REASON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sufficient Reason refers to a rationale that justifies certain actions in arbitration, such as requesting hearings or submitting materials."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39b02ac25884a8c6102243f2b93f0c03</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION OF ARBITRATION PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Termination of Arbitration Procedure is an event where the arbitral tribunal decides to end the proceedings under specific conditions, like when a party fails to submit required documents without valid reasons."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-39b02ac25884a8c6102243f2b93f0c03</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXPERT WITNESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Expert Witness is an individual or group designated by the Arbitral Tribunal to provide reports on specific issues relevant to the arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 23(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 23(1) refers to a procedural step in the arbitration process where parties are required to submit statements of claim or defence, as mentioned in Articles 25 and 26."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEARING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Hearing is a formal session where parties present their cases before the Arbitral Tribunal, but may not attend or provide evidence as stated in Article 25(c)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUFFICIENT CAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sufficient Cause refers to a valid reason for failing to comply with procedural requirements, as mentioned in Article 25(a) and (c)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 783}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1181}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROCEDURAL STEP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Procedural Steps are the formal actions required by parties during arbitration proceedings, such as submitting statements of claim or defence."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STATEMENT OF CLAIM/DEFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Statements of Claim or Defence are formal documents submitted by parties outlining their positions in the dispute. They must be communicated according to Article 23(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 245}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGREEMENT BETWEEN PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Agreement Between Parties refers to any mutual understanding or contract that may affect procedural steps during arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXPERT REPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Expert Reports are detailed analyses provided by designated experts on specific issues relevant to the dispute, as mentioned in Article 26(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENT INSPECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Document Inspection is a procedural step where parties may be required to provide or allow access to documents for examination, as stated in Article 26(b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORAL REPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Oral Report refers to verbal presentations made by experts during arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WRITTEN REPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Written Report is a detailed document provided by an expert witness, outlining their findings and opinions on specific issues relevant to the dispute."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROCEDURAL REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Procedural Requirements are formal actions that parties must take during the arbitration process to ensure fair proceedings, such as submitting statements or appearing for hearings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENT SUBMISSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Document Submission refers to the act of providing documents or evidence as part of the procedural requirements during arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 245}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEARING ATTENDANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hearing Attendance is a procedural step where parties are required to appear in person for formal sessions, but may not attend due to various reasons as mentioned in Article 25(c)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 245}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXPERT DESIGNATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Expert Designation process involves the Arbitral Tribunal selecting one or more experts to provide reports on specific issues relevant to the dispute."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 245}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION RULES AND PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration Rules and Procedures are formal guidelines that govern how disputes are resolved through arbitration, including steps like document submission and expert designation as mentioned in Articles 25-26."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROCEDURAL FAILURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Procedural Failure is a breach of the required procedural steps during arbitration proceedings, such as failing to submit statements or appear for hearings without sufficient cause."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION MECHANISM RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rules and Procedures related to Dispute Resolution Mechanisms are formal guidelines that govern how disputes can be resolved through methods like arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTARY EVIDENCE SUBMISSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The submission of Documentary Evidence is a procedural step where parties may provide written or recorded material as evidence during the arbitration process, but may fail to do so without sufficient cause as mentioned in Article 25(c)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION OUTCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Arbitration Outcome refers to the final decision made by the Arbitral Tribunal based on the evidence and arguments presented during the proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROCEDURAL COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Compliance with Procedural Requirements is adherence to formal steps required in arbitration, such as submitting statements or appearing for hearings without sufficient cause leading to potential consequences as mentioned in Article 25(a) and (c)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION METHODOLOGY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Methodologies related to Dispute Resolution are the processes and procedures used by parties and arbitral tribunals to resolve disputes, including arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXPERT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Expert is an individual appointed by the Arbitration Tribunal to report on specific issues related to the dispute."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-edc4c9a782cb874c7fb36432df37d995</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 870}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT OF THIS STATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Court of this State refers to a domestic court that can assist in taking evidence as requested by the Arbitration Tribunal or parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-edc4c9a782cb874c7fb36432df37d995</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 868}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROCEDURE TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Procedure Termination is an event marking the end of arbitration procedures, possibly involving the issuance of a decision."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-edc4c9a782cb874c7fb36432df37d995</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DECISION MAKING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The process of Decision Making involves the Arbitration Tribunal making determinations based on expert reports and evidence provided by parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-edc4c9a782cb874c7fb36432df37d995</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 54&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 54 is a reference to specific rules or guidelines related to expert appointments in arbitration procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-edc4c9a782cb874c7fb36432df37d995</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 870}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 55&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 55 refers to the rules for court assistance in taking evidence, as mentioned in Article 27 of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-edc4c9a782cb874c7fb36432df37d995</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 868}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHAPTER VI. MAKING AWARDS AND TERMINATION OF PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Chapter VI is a section that deals with making awards and terminating arbitration procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-edc4c9a782cb874c7fb36432df37d995</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPETENT COURT OF THIS STATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A location where a competent court can provide assistance in taking evidence as requested by an arbitral tribunal or with its approval."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-375bde2b853ea690587e97e345bd3671</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 158}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 672}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAKING OF AWARD AND TERMINATION OF PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The process of concluding arbitration proceedings, including making an award and terminating the dispute resolution process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-375bde2b853ea690587e97e345bd3671</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHAPTER VI.  MAKING OF AWARD AND TERMINATION OF PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to a specific chapter in a document or legal text that deals with the conclusion of arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-375bde2b853ea690587e97e345bd3671</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 28. RULES APPLICABLE TO SUBSTANCE OF DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An event where rules governing disputes are determined, considering parties' choices and applicable laws as per their agreement or default provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-375bde2b853ea690587e97e345bd3671</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1203}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL SYSTEM OF A GIVEN STATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The legal system refers to the set of rules and principles that govern the interpretation of laws, unless otherwise specified."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-341dbfe6e21afa768ee74c7e3db0be67</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 898}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EX AEQUO ET BONO OR AMIABLE COMPOSITEUR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ex aequo et bono or amiable compositeur is an arbitration method where decisions are made based on fairness and good conscience, only if explicitly authorized by the parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-341dbfe6e21afa768ee74c7e3db0be67</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DECISION-MAKING BY PANEL OF ARBITRATORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The decision-making process in arbitral proceedings involves making decisions by a majority vote among multiple arbitrators unless otherwise agreed upon by the parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-341dbfe6e21afa768ee74c7e3db0be67</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROCEDURE PROBLEMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Procedure issues are specific to arbitration processes and can be decided by a presiding arbitrator with authorization from all members of the tribunal or the parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-341dbfe6e21afa768ee74c7e3db0be67</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTIES REACHING A SETTLEMENT IN AN ARBITRATION CASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Parties can reach a settlement during arbitration which leads to termination of proceedings and recording the terms of agreement in an arbitral award."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-341dbfe6e21afa768ee74c7e3db0be67</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 886}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1201}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARDS BASED ON SETTLEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration awards resulting from settlements are formal documents that record the conditions agreed upon by parties, having equal status and effect as other arbitration decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-341dbfe6e21afa768ee74c7e3db0be67</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 886}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1201}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WRITTEN AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Written Award is a document that must be signed by one or more arbitrators, detailing the reasons for the decision unless otherwise agreed upon by the parties, according to Article 31(2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03bb9907c4707aee4e32c05a81efe12a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION LOCATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Arbitration Location refers to the place where arbitration takes place and is determined based on specific criteria as mentioned in Article 20(1), which affects the validity of the award."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-03bb9907c4707aee4e32c05a81efe12a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 856}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1193}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTIES INVOLVED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Parties Involved include applicants, respondents, or other entities participating in arbitration procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d0cddff72aaf0d2c6f21cba88e08e8e0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 855}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGREED TERMS AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Agreed Terms Award is a decision based on agreed terms between parties, without stating reasons as per agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d0cddff72aaf0d2c6f21cba88e08e8e0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 855}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION OF ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Termination of Arbitration Proceedings occurs when the final award or arbitrator's termination order ends the arbitral process under specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d0cddff72aaf0d2c6f21cba88e08e8e0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 855}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL MANDATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Mandate of Arbitration Tribunal refers to its authority or role, which terminates with the end of arbitral proceedings as stated in Article 32(3), subject to specific provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5943028cc6f3beb70826c83454e86767</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 49}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CORRECTION AND INTERPRETATION OF AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Correction and Interpretation of Award is an event where parties can request corrections or explanations for their arbitration awards, according to the terms set out in Article 33(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5943028cc6f3beb70826c83454e86767</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 49}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD CORRECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration Award Correction refers to the process by which errors in the arbitral award are corrected within a specified timeframe as outlined in Article 33(1)(a)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Correction of an arbitration award is the process where the arbitral tribunal makes changes based on justified requests from parties involved in the proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5943028cc6f3beb70826c83454e86767&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5490186775273077486362a56a5b981f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 49}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERPRETATION OF ARBITRATION AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interpretation of Arbitration Award is an event where parties can seek clarification on specific points or parts of their awards, provided the request is deemed reasonable by the tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5943028cc6f3beb70826c83454e86767</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AWARD CORRECTION REQUEST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An event where one party requests correction of errors in an award within 30 days after receiving it."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d17ccb7c45bbf013a4a9b072f210aedd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERPRETATION REQUEST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An event where a party requests the Arbitration Tribunal to provide interpretation on specific points or parts of the award, also within 30 days after receiving the award."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d17ccb7c45bbf013a4a9b072f210aedd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPPLEMENTARY AWARD REQUEST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A request made by one party for an additional award regarding matters not included in the original award but raised during arbitration proceedings, which must be submitted to the Arbitration Tribunal within 60 days of receiving the initial award."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d17ccb7c45bbf013a4a9b072f210aedd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CORRECTION AND INTERPRETATION PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The period is set at 30 days for parties to request corrections or interpretations from the Arbitration Tribunal after receiving an award, which can be extended if necessary."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d17ccb7c45bbf013a4a9b072f210aedd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPPLEMENTARY AWARD EXTENSION PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The extension period for making a supplementary award, also within 60 days of receiving the initial award, is not quantified but implies flexibility in timing based on necessity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d17ccb7c45bbf013a4a9b072f210aedd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 7.01-69&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT,MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These articles refer to sections or rules within a legal framework governing arbitration and its outcomes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5490186775273077486362a56a5b981f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 49}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 34.01-2(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This article outlines the procedure for requesting corrections and interpretations from the arbitral tribunal regarding arbitration awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5490186775273077486362a56a5b981f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 34.01-2(2)(A)(I)-(II)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These clauses specify conditions under which an arbitration award can be revoked by a court, involving issues of capacity and proper notification procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5490186775273077486362a56a5b981f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT REVIEW OF ARBITRATION AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court Review of Arbitration Awards is an event where courts review and potentially overturn arbitral awards based on specific grounds such as invalidity or public policy violations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f2047b71041716475b6c4ce04dcb74ab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT FINDING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court findings are instances where a court determines certain conditions for setting aside an arbitral award based on agreement or public policy considerations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f35bbfd9ee83b0701ea2384c506063d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 821}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THREE MONTHS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Three months is the time limit within which an application to set aside an arbitral award can be made after receiving the award or after a request has been disposed of by the arbitral tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f35bbfd9ee83b0701ea2384c506063d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SETTING ASIDE PROCEEDINGS SUSPENSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Setting aside proceedings suspension refers to the temporary halt in legal actions for setting aside an arbitral award, allowing time for the arbitral tribunal to take action that might eliminate grounds for setting it aside."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f35bbfd9ee83b0701ea2384c506063d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT APPLICATION TO SET ASIDE AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court application to set aside award refers to a legal process where a party requests a court to annul or void an arbitral award based on specific grounds such as non-compliance with agreement terms or public policy considerations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f35bbfd9ee83b0701ea2384c506063d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 309}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION裁决&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration裁决 refers to the final decision made by an arbitration tribunal in resolving disputes, which is recognized and enforceable internationally according to international law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f35bbfd9ee83b0701ea2384c506063d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;管轄法院&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"管轄法院 refers to a court with jurisdiction over matters related to arbitral awards, responsible for recognizing and enforcing such decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f35bbfd9ee83b0701ea2384c506063d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;书面申请&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"书面申请 means the formal application submitted by one party requesting recognition or enforcement of an arbitration award according to legal procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f35bbfd9ee83b0701ea2384c506063d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;裁决书正本或其副本&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"裁决书正本或其副本 refers to the original copy or a duplicate of the arbitral award document, which is required for application purposes as per legal regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f35bbfd9ee83b0701ea2384c506063d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;正式语文&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"正式语文 means official languages used in documents and proceedings, ensuring clarity and compliance with legal standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f35bbfd9ee83b0701ea2384c506063d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 309}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 35&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 35 is an event in the recognition and enforcement of arbitral awards, detailing conditions for their acceptance by competent courts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-70d6872db724ae32c205d96d7e3c902f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 821}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 36&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Article 36 is an event concerning reasons for refusing recognition or enforcement of arbitral awards, outlining specific conditions under which such actions can be denied."&lt;SEP&gt;"Article 36 outlines grounds for refusing recognition or enforcement of an arbitral award, detailing specific conditions under which such awards may be refused."&lt;SEP&gt;"Article 36 refers to a specific article within a legal document, which does not have effect as per the note provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-665407cfb1dd4211e1d5ff880154e6bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e279133cb6f847782cd0ab6a19c0d64f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70d6872db724ae32c205d96d7e3c902f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 821}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE PARTY RELYING ON AN AWARD OR APPLYING FOR ITS ENFORCEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the individual or entity that seeks to enforce an arbitration award, providing necessary documents and evidence if required by the court."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-70d6872db724ae32c205d96d7e3c902f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;7TH CLAUSE OF THE ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The 7th clause is part of an arbitration agreement that may pertain to conditions under which it becomes invalid or unenforceable due to certain circumstances such as incapacity, lack of proper notification, etc."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-70d6872db724ae32c205d96d7e3c902f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPROPRIATE NOTICE FOR APPOINTING ARBITRATORS AND THE ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appropriate Notice is a document required in arbitration procedures that ensures all parties are informed about the appointment of arbitrators and subsequent hearings to allow them to present their case effectively."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-70d6872db724ae32c205d96d7e3c902f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT OF THE PLACE WHERE THE ARBITRAL AWARD IS MADE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This location is where the court can potentially revoke or suspend enforcement of an arbitration award if it deems necessary."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-aba64861ea22070188d9b7dd4c0fd47a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 822}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;主張承認或執行裁決的一方當事人&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"指申请执行仲裁裁决的一方当事人，通常为胜诉一方。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-637d9e3dd1440e4117d86911ea5a7841</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 88}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 492}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;對方當事人&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"对方当事人是指被申请人，即需要提供担保的另一方。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-637d9e3dd1440e4117d86911ea5a7841</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 88}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 492}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;商事性質的關係&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"指与商业活动相关的各种关系和交易类型，包括但不限于贸易、代理、租赁等。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-637d9e3dd1440e4117d86911ea5a7841</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;空中、海上、鐵路或公路的客貨載運&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"涉及运输技术的应用，如航空、海运、铁路及公路货物运输的技术和服务。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-637d9e3dd1440e4117d86911ea5a7841</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第36條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"指关于拒绝执行临时措施的具体条款规定，是法律文本中的一个事件或规则。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-637d9e3dd1440e4117d86911ea5a7841</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 88}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 492}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;仲裁裁決&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"仲裁裁决是指通过仲裁程序作出的具有约束力的决定，通常涉及商业纠纷解决。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-637d9e3dd1440e4117d86911ea5a7841</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;投資&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"投资指的是与资金相关的商业活动和技术应用，包括但不限于资本注入、股权交易等。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-637d9e3dd1440e4117d86911ea5a7841</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 836}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLE 36. GROUNDS FOR REFUSING RECOGNITION OR ENFORCEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is a specific article in the legal text that outlines conditions under which an arbitral award may be refused recognition or enforcement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-637d9e3dd1440e4117d86911ea5a7841</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 836}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT OF THE COUNTRY IN WHICH, OR UNDER THE LAW OF WHICH, THAT AWARD WAS MADE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This phrase specifies a court within the jurisdiction where the arbitral award was issued, emphasizing legal authority and recognition scope."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-665407cfb1dd4211e1d5ff880154e6bb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 821}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRADE FACILITATION AND ARBITRATION COMMISSION (贸法委)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Trade Facilitation and Arbitration Commission (贸法委) is implied in references to its model law and provisions related to arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4ea69c357721dd337ab1f2ad1b4f0333</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 303}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 992}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOLE ARBITRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Sole arbitrator is a specific role mentioned for resolving disputes when the number of arbitrators is not agreed upon, indicating an individual decision-maker in arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"A sole arbitrator is a single individual appointed to resolve disputes between parties who have agreed on arbitration but failed to agree on the number of arbitrators."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4ea69c357721dd337ab1f2ad1b4f0333&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-818682a0f1950aff44c4e7f18a331608</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 231}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 835}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1191}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRANSACTION(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Transaction refers to a commercial exchange, which can be part of the basis for consolidating multiple arbitration procedures if they arise out of the same series of transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ee3bd35452fe0a7b5e9fa7dc2c1f8074</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 886}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1199}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COSTS OF ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Costs of Arbitral Proceedings are financial aspects related to the legal process, which can be ordered by an arbitrator tribunal under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ff2369343594485564382d2d30ba3755</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 232}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 848}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL ISSUE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal Issue refers to questions or problems arising during the course of arbitral proceedings, which may be decided by the court."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ff2369343594485564382d2d30ba3755</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 232}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 848}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRELIMINARY QUESTION OF LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Preliminary question of law is a specific issue that needs to be decided by the Court during arbitral proceedings, potentially affecting costs and outcomes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-76cb33f1b7685e188783adaf8e60f8f5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 180}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 724}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DECISION OF PRELIMINARY QUESTION OF LAW BY COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Decision of preliminary question of law by Court involves the Court deciding on legal issues arising in arbitration without fully resolving the dispute."&lt;SEP&gt;"The decision involves the court deciding on legal questions arising during arbitration without fully resolving the dispute, potentially impacting costs savings for parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-76cb33f1b7685e188783adaf8e60f8f5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPEAL FROM A DECISION OF THE COURT UNDER SUBSECTION (1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Appeal from a decision of the Court refers to challenging the court's decision regarding preliminary questions of law through higher courts like the Court of Appeal."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-76cb33f1b7685e188783adaf8e60f8f5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SERIOUS MISCONDUCT EVENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Serious misconduct event is an incident that can be grounds for questioning arbitration awards, affecting the fairness and integrity of arbitral proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-76cb33f1b7685e188783adaf8e60f8f5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPLICATION UNDER SUBSECTION (1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An application refers to a request made to the court regarding preliminary questions of law in arbitral proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-76cb33f1b7685e188783adaf8e60f8f5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;QUESTIONING ARBITRATION AWARDS BASED ON SERIOUS MISCONDUCT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event involves parties challenging arbitration awards due to alleged severe improprieties, affecting the validity and fairness of the arbitration process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-76cb33f1b7685e188783adaf8e60f8f5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SERIOUS MISCONDUCT EVENT FOR QUESTIONING ARBITRATION AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Serious misconduct event is an incident that can be grounds for questioning arbitration awards, impacting their legitimacy and integrity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-76cb33f1b7685e188783adaf8e60f8f5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DECISION OF PRELIMINARY QUESTION OF LAW BY COURT (REPEATED)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The decision involves the court deciding on legal questions arising during arbitration without fully resolving the dispute, potentially impacting costs savings for parties involved (repeated)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-76cb33f1b7685e188783adaf8e60f8f5</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SERIOUS IMPROPRIETY EVENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Serious Impropriety Event refers to any improper event that could cause significant unfairness to the applicant and includes various types of misconduct as listed in subsection (2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8d82bf83563624acdc014bb3783db688</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERPRETATION OF UNCERTAIN OR AMBIGUOUS AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The interpretation of uncertain or ambiguous awards is a process where the arbitral tribunal provides clarification, which can be questioned if there's serious impropriety."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8d82bf83563624acdc014bb3783db688</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FRAUDULENT MEANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Obtaining an award through fraudulent means constitutes a Serious Impropriety Event and may lead to questioning of the arbitration award by the original court."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8d82bf83563624acdc014bb3783db688</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 831}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY VIOLATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A violation of public policy is considered a Serious Impropriety Event that can affect the validity or enforceability of an arbitral award."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8d82bf83563624acdc014bb3783db688</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 831}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSTANTIAL INJUSTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Substantial injustice refers to significant unfairness or inequity resulting from an irregularity, which could justify challenging an arbitration award."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5a62633bac9b2c0c6ed1e0aa83ce66e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SERIOUS IRREGULARITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Serious Irregularity refers to significant procedural or substantive issues that can affect the fairness and validity of an arbitral award, potentially leading to its revocation or reconsideration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5a62633bac9b2c0c6ed1e0aa83ce66e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;3 MONTHS LIMIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The 3-Month Limit is a timeframe within which arbitration decisions may be returned for reconsideration by the tribunal after being sent back from the Court, unless extended or shortened as per court instructions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5a62633bac9b2c0c6ed1e0aa83ce66e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REVOCATION POWER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Court has the power to revoke an arbitral award in certain circumstances where it deems that revoking the decision is appropriate and justifiable based on serious irregularities affecting the tribunal, proceedings, or the final decision."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5a62633bac9b2c0c6ed1e0aa83ce66e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPEAL AGAINST DECISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The process of appealing a court's decision regarding arbitration awards involves obtaining permission from either the Court itself or the Appellate Court to challenge the ruling on grounds such as procedural irregularities affecting the fairness and validity of an arbitral award."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5a62633bac9b2c0c6ed1e0aa83ce66e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 856}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1193}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPLICATION FOR APPEAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Application for Appeal is a formal request submitted by parties seeking permission from the court or appellate tribunal to challenge a decision related to arbitration awards, particularly when serious irregularities are alleged that could impact the fairness and validity of those decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5a62633bac9b2c0c6ed1e0aa83ce66e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPLICABILITY CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The applicability clause ensures that provisions regarding challenging arbitral awards on grounds of serious irregularity also apply to specific types of applications or appeals, maintaining consistency in legal procedures and standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5a62633bac9b2c0c6ed1e0aa83ce66e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 879}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FRAUD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fraud refers to actions that are illegal and unethical, potentially leading to an award being contrary to public policy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2b2fac04904854d200ea9c9161cb98c1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPEAL AGAINST ARBITRAL AWARD ON QUESTION OF LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appealing against an arbitral award on a question of law is an event where parties can challenge legal aspects of the decision made during arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5540da5689ed24920444d2c678531763</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 6(4)(C)(I) OR (II)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These refer to specific criteria that are not considered when deciding questions of law under subsection (3), indicating a legal framework for arbitration appeals."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e17ae2e1dd0c38e2c8a34618b769e578</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAVE OF THE COURT OR THE COURT OF APPEAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leave from either the original Court or the higher Court is required for further appeal, highlighting the hierarchical structure in dispute resolution processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e17ae2e1dd0c38e2c8a34618b769e578</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPEAL DECISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An appeal decision is a ruling made by the litigation court regarding whether an appeal can be brought, which cannot be appealed without specific conditions being met."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fe51ca84063bb48ff26e0744002a148</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 232}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 848}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEAVE TO APPEAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Leave to appeal is an event where permission must be granted by the Court for parties to challenge arbitral awards, highlighting its importance in legal disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c9174a61c7bf0b325fa1fb34e7b741c0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPLICANT OR APPELLANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Applicant or Appellant can be a natural person usually residing outside Hong Kong or an organization established under laws other than those of Hong Kong, which may have its central management and control exercised elsewhere."&lt;SEP&gt;"Applicant or appellant refers to individuals or entities seeking relief from a court regarding arbitral awards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2da7991e9473f6c5aadfd4a87f21c511&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-882b59070dba0a27453ac53b51232f89</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 241}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 891}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;法人團體&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"法人團體是指根据香港以外地方的法律成立并由其中央管理及控制在该地行使的实体。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d0a46c25800fae1ea9c732dab0043f67</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;組織&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"组织指的是根据香港以外的地方的法律组成的实体，或者其中央管理与控制是在香港以外的地方行使的。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d0a46c25800fae1ea9c732dab0043f67</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;原訟法庭&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"原訟法庭是指在处理申请或上诉时具有管辖权并作出相关命令和指示的地方法院。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d0a46c25800fae1ea9c732dab0043f67</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;上訴法庭&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"上诉法庭指的是有权批予附表第4、5或6条所指的上诉许可，并施加与第(4)或(6)款所指的命令具同等或类似效力条件的地方高等法院。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d0a46c25800fae1ea9c732dab0043f67</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;仲裁裁决&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"仲裁裁决是指由仲裁庭作出并需支付款项的决定，通常涉及商业纠纷解决过程中的法律裁定。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d0a46c25800fae1ea9c732dab0043f67</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SCHEDULE 3&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Schedule 3 is a part of an ordinance that contains provisions related to savings and transitional matters."&lt;SEP&gt;"Schedule 3 is an appendix containing specific details or conditions that may be relevant for certain applications, though it has been omitted in this context due to its expiration date."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f43eb8e125ae108a081ead56528fd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d95ad1d2c3e1a79bcbb97aba7400ea9</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMENCEMENT OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Commencement of the Ordinance refers to its effective date, which triggers certain provisions as stated in Section 1(2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f43eb8e125ae108a081ead56528fd1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNITED NATIONS COMMISSION ON INTERNATIONAL TRADE LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The United Nations Commission on International Trade Law refers to a body that provides model laws for arbitration, specifically mentioned in Section 1(1)(a)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f43eb8e125ae108a081ead56528fd1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OLD ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Old Ordinance is an existing legal document or ordinance referred to throughout the text, providing context and basis for current provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-51f43eb8e125ae108a081ead56528fd1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 232}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 849}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPEALED ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Repealed Ordinance is an organization or legislation that was in effect before this new ordinance and governs certain aspects of arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0e013fee151f1254a38965f636a0159</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 346}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1040}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration procedures refer to the methods and processes involved in resolving disputes through arbitration, as governed by various ordinances or laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0e013fee151f1254a38965f636a0159</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 229}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 810}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPOINTED ARBITRATORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appointed Arbitrators are individuals who have been designated to arbitrate disputes according to certain legal frameworks before this ordinance's enactment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0e013fee151f1254a38965f636a0159</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 31}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 346}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1040}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPOINTMENT ADVISORY BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Appointment Advisory Board is a body established under rule 3 of the Arbitration (Appointment of Arbitrators and Umpires) Rules, which provides advice for appointments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Appointment Advisory Board is an organization established under the Arbitration (Appointment of Arbitrators and Umpires) Rules, which continues to have effect after the commencement of this Ordinance as if it had not been enacted."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-83a6ab35c70f5935f2a22cd6ce3b6e03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-605f21b5a2eb897deb796a8915dad75c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 239}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 888}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION(APPOINTMENT OF ARBITRATORS AND UMPIRES)RULES(CAP. 341 SUB. LEG. B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The rules refer to a set of regulations for appointing arbitrators and umpires, now known as Cap. 609 sub. leg. B."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-605f21b5a2eb897deb796a8915dad75c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 239}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 888}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION (APPOINTMENT OF ARBITRATORS AND UMPIRES) RULES (CAP. 341 SUB. LEG. B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Arbitration (Appointment of Arbitrators and Umpires) Rules is a set of legal rules governing the appointment process, now known as Cap. 609 sub. leg. B."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-83a6ab35c70f5935f2a22cd6ce3b6e03</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 239}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 888}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2015年第11號第7條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The enactment of section 7 in Ordinance No. 11 of 2015 added Part 2 to the document, dealing with savings and transitional provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-83a6ab35c70f5935f2a22cd6ce3b6e03</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 331}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;貿法委示範法 (UNCITRAL MODEL LAW)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The UNCITRAL Model Law is a set of model laws for international arbitration that provides legal framework for arbitral proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-83a6ab35c70f5935f2a22cd6ce3b6e03</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 331}]</data>
</node>
