</node>
<node id="&quot;NOMINATING BODY (提名團體)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An organization whose name is listed on a register established by law for managing certain construction contracts and disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1bf52072b8dd02eb0cf0d0e08e22d0cd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 454}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYING PARTY (付款方)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The party responsible for making payments under the terms of a contract, as defined in section 18(1) but not further detailed here."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1bf52072b8dd02eb0cf0d0e08e22d0cd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 454}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT CLAIM (付款申索)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A claim made by one party to another for payment due under a construction contract, referenced but not fully described in the provided text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1bf52072b8dd02eb0cf0d0e08e22d0cd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 454}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYING PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Paying Party is another entity under the construction contract who may be liable to make payments and must receive claims according to regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paying Party is the entity responsible for responding to and potentially paying according to the terms of a payment claim."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paying party is an entity that accepts delivery of goods and services and agrees to make payment according to terms specified in the contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Paying Party is the party required to respond with a payment response, acknowledging any admitted amount by the deadline of the progress payment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Paying Party refers to the entity or individual responsible for making payments in a business transaction. They are expected to respond appropriately to payment claims and provide necessary details."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Paying Party refers to the entity responsible for making payments under a contract, who must adhere to specific deadlines when responding to payment claims."&lt;SEP&gt;"The party required to make payments as per the contract or court order."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0af4d7e54b59f5f639294394f679c069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d4be77f953bdd4a222130461f58fb29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3978c9d363a5060a5f5dafe37f64fe66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98b9cc96db8e2ffdc374754939531431&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b7d543744ae8aafbe46746751935e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89690e148d95bff497042548ed9e3555&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20e283bddbd3e4e77e96ddc072a75876</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 776}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT DEADLINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT/MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Payment Deadline is the date by which the Respondent must pay the Adjudicated Amount in full as per the Construction Contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"The date by which a payment is required to be made; specific dates are defined differently based on the context of progress payments or adjudicated amounts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-20e283bddbd3e4e77e96ddc072a75876&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d229505b95cc3e576d9ad034318c66d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 217}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 770}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1179}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A formal agreement involving public works as defined in section 4(1)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public contract is an organization type entity referring to large-scale agreements that are subject to specific regulations outlined in the ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public contract is defined based on the ownership structure; if one or more owners are specified entities (government bodies or certain organizations), it qualifies as a public contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public contract refers to construction contracts where at least one party is a specified entity such as the Government or a body specified in Schedule 3."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public contracts are agreements between public entities and contractors for construction work that meet certain value criteria after a specific date."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66cbfdf286322347be702ca6a2680df3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-307d5bb8387dc47aa9c0f172efe39d0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f53c86b3a5549c4a064860e12f41a1b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daaffb786a24be963871c47c40b85efb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20e283bddbd3e4e77e96ddc072a75876</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 801}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESIDENTIAL UNIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION/PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A separate unit within a building constructed for human habitation but excluding certain specified premises as defined in Schedule 1."&lt;SEP&gt;"An existing residential unit with specific conditions for occupation as per the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-20e283bddbd3e4e77e96ddc072a75876&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04158b577f867f33b0abd25893c009fb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 777}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECRETARY FOR DEVELOPMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON/ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A government official responsible for development matters as per section 68."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Secretary for a department related to development, mentioned in the context of a title or role."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-20e283bddbd3e4e77e96ddc072a75876&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04158b577f867f33b0abd25893c009fb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 801}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELECTED BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An organization chosen by either a respondent or claimant to serve in adjudication proceedings under sections 27(3)(a) and (4)(a)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Selected Body refers to the entity chosen by a Nominating Body in an Adjudication Proceeding, responsible for resolving Payment Disputes as per construction contract terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Selected Body, once notified by the claimant, becomes responsible for arbitrating disputes as per subsection (3) and must comply with regulations outlined in section 27(5)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b219a4ff887909dc5fdeb24191ca220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20e283bddbd3e4e77e96ddc072a75876&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19b1bce23dbf161109b02b0e7ddc678</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 221}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 794}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIRECTOR OF LANDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON/ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Director responsible for land matters, issuing letters and certificates as per the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04158b577f867f33b0abd25893c009fb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 780}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTING WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Work involving construction, installation or erection of specified structures; replacement, expansion, renovation, alteration, maintenance, demolition, reconstruction, and addition of existing specified structures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04158b577f867f33b0abd25893c009fb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAIN PART OR ACCESSORY PARTS OF THE STRUCTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Parts of a building that can be modified through various works such as construction features, utility installations, landscaping, external or internal surface painting or decoration. "</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04158b577f867f33b0abd25893c009fb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARCHITECTURAL FEATURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Architectural features are part of the construction process that involves making distinctive design elements in buildings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8e519122ccc2d577ad6723a71d0f9b7b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 796}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1183}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UTILITIES AND SERVICES INSTALLATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Utilities and services installation includes electrical, mechanical, building services, electronic, radio broadcasting, and telecommunication installations as defined by local regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Utilities and services installation includes electrical, mechanical, building services, electronic, radio, broadcasting, and telecommunication installations as part of infrastructure setup in a project."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8e519122ccc2d577ad6723a71d0f9b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daaffb786a24be963871c47c40b85efb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 796}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1184}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LANDSCAPING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Landscaping refers to the construction or renovation of outdoor spaces including gardens, parks, and other areas for aesthetic purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8e519122ccc2d577ad6723a71d0f9b7b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 796}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1183}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAINTING OR DECORATING EXTERNAL OR INTERNAL SURFACES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This involves applying paint or decorative materials on both exterior and interior surfaces of structures as part of the construction process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8e519122ccc2d577ad6723a71d0f9b7b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 796}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1184}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE CLEARANCE, SITE INVESTIGATION, EXCAVATION, FILLING, TUNNELLING AND BORING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These activities are preparatory works carried out before actual construction begins to prepare the ground for building projects."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8e519122ccc2d577ad6723a71d0f9b7b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 796}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1183}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCESS ROADS AND SCAFFOLDING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Access roads provide pathways into or around a site while scaffolding supports workers during construction, both essential parts of the construction process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8e519122ccc2d577ad6723a71d0f9b7b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 796}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1184}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE RESTORATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Site restoration involves cleaning up after a construction project is completed, ensuring the site returns to its original state or meets new standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8e519122ccc2d577ad6723a71d0f9b7b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 796}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1184}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC CONTRACTS AND GENERAL PRIVATE CONTRACTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refers to agreements between public entities and contractors for various projects including construction work as defined in legal frameworks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8e519122ccc2d577ad6723a71d0f9b7b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TUNNELLING AND BORING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tunnelling and boring refers to specific engineering techniques used in site construction, including filling, tunnelling, and boring activities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-daaffb786a24be963871c47c40b85efb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 803}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAIN PRIVATE CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Main Private Contract is described as an agreement entered into on or after the commencement date with a minimum contract value specified in Schedule 4, which must adhere to specific regulations regarding its scope of work and subcontracting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Main private contract refers to construction contracts where none of the owners are specified entities, indicating a purely private contractual arrangement without government involvement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Main private contract refers to construction contracts where none of the parties are specified entities, meaning they do not include the Government or bodies specified in Schedule 3."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f53c86b3a5549c4a064860e12f41a1b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66157f73d78c8a042051d0b5db5e4492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daaffb786a24be963871c47c40b85efb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 801}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION CONTRACT (CONTRACT A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction contract refers to agreements between owners and contractors in a building project. It can be either public or private based on the criteria mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f53c86b3a5549c4a064860e12f41a1b1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 800}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANOTHER CONSTRUCTION CONTRACT (CONTRACT B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Another construction contract is another agreement for carrying out work under which subcontracts may arise, depending on its nature as specified by the conditions of Contract A."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f53c86b3a5549c4a064860e12f41a1b1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 800}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT A&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contract A is a subcontract related to construction work or supplying related goods and services under Contract B."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fed725f04c7bcd4c7d2f5a1a4787af6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT B&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONTRACT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contract B is the main contract for carrying out construction work, with which Contract A may be associated as a subcontract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fed725f04c7bcd4c7d2f5a1a4787af6d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSULTANCY SERVICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Consultancy Services are advisory services related to project planning, management, design, procurement, contract administration, asset management, maintenance supervision, surveying or quantity surveying."&lt;SEP&gt;"Consultancy services include project planning, project management, design, procurement, contract administration, asset management, asset maintenance, site supervision, surveying or quantity surveying."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-307d5bb8387dc47aa9c0f172efe39d0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fed725f04c7bcd4c7d2f5a1a4787af6d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 797}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBCONTRACT OF THE PUBLIC CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subcontracts related to public contracts involve services or goods provided by third parties in connection with the main construction project."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-307d5bb8387dc47aa9c0f172efe39d0d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 801}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TOTAL PRIVATE CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Total private contract is an organization type entity referring to large-scale agreements between private parties that are subject to specific regulations outlined in the ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Total private contract refers to a specific type of agreement mentioned as part of the legal framework discussed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66cbfdf286322347be702ca6a2680df3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e089cfc832db9c43bb24baa7baf3ed42</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 303}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 992}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBCONTRACT OF A TOTAL PRIVATE CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subcontract of a total private contract refers to a product or service agreement entered into as part of larger private contracts, governed by similar legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66cbfdf286322347be702ca6a2680df3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 18}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 251}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 921}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARCHITECTURAL OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Architectural Officer is a person responsible for approving and supervising construction work to ensure compliance with regulations, particularly those related to new constructions or significant modifications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66157f73d78c8a042051d0b5db5e4492</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUILDING ORDINANCE (CAP. 123)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Building Ordinance (Cap. 123) outlines the rules and procedures governing building activities in Hong Kong, including requirements for obtaining approvals from architectural officers before commencing work on certain projects."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66157f73d78c8a042051d0b5db5e4492</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUILDING AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Building Authority is an organization that requires approval for certain construction work to commence or be carried out, as stated in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-06e739d62dd19f34a46b38a2c7902502</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 435}]</data>
