<node id="&quot;DIVISION 1—INTERPRETATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SECTION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Division 1—Interpretation is a section in Part 2 that provides definitions for key terms used throughout the ordinance, such as 'supplied' and 'billing date'."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-62cc8e230a5d660ff292c1740f8b1b1e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 227}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPPLIED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Supplied refers to the provision of goods or services under a contract, including both actual supply and promised future supply."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-62cc8e230a5d660ff292c1740f8b1b1e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 227}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BILLING DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Billing Date is defined as the last day of a calendar month for progress payments in construction contracts, unless specified otherwise by the contract terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Billing Date is the date when an invoice or bill related to progress payment is issued, which can affect the determination of deadlines and conditions under certain circumstances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Billing Date marks the start or end period for serving claims and making payments in construction contracts, crucial for compliance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-41b7d543744ae8aafbe46746751935e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c90a7be5c9755cdde83e35c88dd2f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62cc8e230a5d660ff292c1740f8b1b1e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 227}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROGRESS PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Progress Payments refer to the payments made during construction work or for related goods and services under a contract, based on the value of the work done or supplied."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-889afebd54a7251f29bdb7f6b9bc2a85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 774}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CARRYING OUT CONSTRUCTION WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Carrying Out Construction Work refers to the process of executing construction tasks as stipulated in a contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-889afebd54a7251f29bdb7f6b9bc2a85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 774}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPPLYING RELATED GOODS AND SERVICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ACTIVITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Supplying Related Goods and Services involves providing goods or services related to the construction work under a contract, which can also entitle one to progress payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-889afebd54a7251f29bdb7f6b9bc2a85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 774}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT PRICE OR RATE FOR THE CONSTRUCTION WORK OR RELATED GOODS AND SERVICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contract price or rate refers to the monetary value agreed upon in the contract for specific work, materials, or services provided under a construction agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3978c9d363a5060a5f5dafe37f64fe66</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 774}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFECT OR NON-CONFORMANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Defect or non-conformance refers to any part of a construction work or related goods/services that does not meet contractual requirements, potentially leading to deductions from progress payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3978c9d363a5060a5f5dafe37f64fe66</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 774}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFECT RECTIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Defect Rectification involves correcting issues found in the construction work that do not meet contractual requirements but are accepted by the paying party."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c90a7be5c9755cdde83e35c88dd2f63</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIMINUTION IN VALUE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Diminution in Value refers to a reduction in the value of constructed goods or services due to defects or non-conformance, impacting payment calculations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c90a7be5c9755cdde83e35c88dd2f63</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT CLAIM FOR PROGRESS PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Payment Claim for Progress Payment is a formal request made by one party (usually the contractor) to another (the owner/developer) for partial payments during construction work based on completed milestones."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1c90a7be5c9755cdde83e35c88dd2f63</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 227}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROGRESS PAYMENT PROVISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Progress Payment Provisions are the clauses in a construction contract that detail how progress payments will be made, including their frequency, amount, and due dates."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ad2f770d3edd7fc8b6985f3040077779</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION CONTRACTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction Contracts refer to agreements between parties regarding the construction work, detailing payment terms for progress payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ad2f770d3edd7fc8b6985f3040077779</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT RESPONSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Payment Response is a document issued by the paying party acknowledging any admitted amount and stating whether it will be paid or not within the deadline."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Payment Response is an official reply from the paying party acknowledging and addressing the details of the payment claim, often required within specific timeframes as per contractual agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Payment Response is a document sent by one party acknowledging and responding to a payment claim, often required within specified deadlines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Payment Response is a document that must be in writing and includes details such as the amount to be paid, differences between claimed and admitted amounts, and calculation methods. It serves as a formal acknowledgment of a payment claim."&lt;SEP&gt;"Payment Response is an acknowledgment or rejection of received payment claim from paying party, required for compliance with construction contract terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Payment Response refers to the required action by which the party receiving a payment claim must acknowledge receipt within a specified date."&lt;SEP&gt;"The payment response, served under section 19, acknowledges or disputes part or full amount claimed and must be provided within specified deadlines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ad2f770d3edd7fc8b6985f3040077779&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d4be77f953bdd4a222130461f58fb29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b7d543744ae8aafbe46746751935e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98b9cc96db8e2ffdc374754939531431&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89690e148d95bff497042548ed9e3555&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc61c3e9d0b909249e0a6492fb80f00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bca656554298bd4af2405476efe73616</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 775}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIVISION 3 — CERTAIN PROVISIONS IN CONSTRUCTION CONTRACTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This division refers to specific provisions related to construction contracts, including progress payments and conditions for their implementation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ad2f770d3edd7fc8b6985f3040077779</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 226}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 20&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 20 is another reference in the legal document, likely setting deadlines or conditions related to responses to payment claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ad2f770d3edd7fc8b6985f3040077779</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 226}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT CLAIM EVENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Payment Claim Event is an occurrence where one party requests payment based on completed work or milestones within a construction project."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ad2f770d3edd7fc8b6985f3040077779</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 796}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1183}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDITIONAL PAYMENT PROVISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conditional Payment Provisions are legal clauses that determine when payments must be made based on certain conditions, often involving third parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bca656554298bd4af2405476efe73616</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 774}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDITIONAL PAYMENT PROVISION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A conditional payment provision in a construction contract is unenforceable between the parties to the contract and has no effect in relation to any payment for— (a) construction work carried out under the contract; or (b) related goods and services supplied under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MONEY OWING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Money owing means money owed for—(a) construction work carried out under the contract; or (b) related goods and services supplied under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 802}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTY A&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Party A is a party in an adjudication process, specified as the one who responds to or replies to another party's submission or evidence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Party A refers to one party in the contract who has liability to pay money owing to another party (Party B)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Party A specifies in an adjudication response that certain submissions, responses, documents, or evidence given by another party are of interest under specific circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712f0363a7a1263779f6581a9b8b41b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bba63535f02791b0eaca5f64d5b8ed57</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 788}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTY B&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Party B is a party in the contract that receives payment from Party A."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 783}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1181}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTY C&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Party C is a further party who may make payments to Party A, which conditions or affects the liability of Party A towards Party B."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIVISION 4 —— PAYMENT CLAIMS AND PAYMENT RESPONSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This division deals with provisions related to payment claims and responses in the context of construction contracts, outlining how claims should be made and when they are considered valid."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 26}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT CLAIM (IN RELATION TO AN INTERIM PROGRESS PAYMENT)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Payment Claim concerning an interim progress payment is a formal claim by someone with the right or claim to receive such payments under a construction contract, where another party has legal responsibility to pay these amounts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Payer in this context refers to the party responsible for paying interim progress payments as per the terms of a construction contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION PROJECT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Construction Project is an ongoing project involving building or constructing structures, where payment claims and responses are relevant."&lt;SEP&gt;"Construction Project refers to the work or activities related to building structures, which may involve disputes and require adjudication for resolving payment issues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8719074a70eff81632691da24dedfc0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 788}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERIM PROGRESS PAYMENT (期進度款)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Interim Progress Payment refers to payments made during the construction process for work completed up until a certain point in time."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIM DELIVERY DATE (發單日)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Claim Delivery Date is the date by which payment claims must be delivered to be considered valid under the terms of a construction contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RELATED GOODS AND SERVICES (相關物料及服務)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Related Goods and Services are items and services directly related to the construction work carried out under a construction contract, for which payment claims can be made."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 802}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FURTHER PARTY (進一步付款方)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Further Party is an entity that may make payments to the party responsible for making progress payments in a construction contract, affecting their liability towards another party."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 225}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OPERATION OF OTHER CONTRACTS OR AGREEMENTS (其他合同或協議的實施)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Operation of Other Contracts or Agreements refers to conditions under which payment obligations may be contingent upon the execution or operation of other agreements related to a construction contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL RESPONSIBILITY (法律責任)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal Responsibility is the obligation imposed by law on parties involved in a construction contract, including their duties and liabilities regarding payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENT (期進度款)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Interim Payment refers to partial or full payment made during the course of a construction project for work completed up until that point."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION CONTRACT (建造合同)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Construction Contract is an agreement between parties involved in building projects, outlining terms and conditions related to payments, obligations, and other aspects of the project."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT RESPONSE (付款回應)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Payment Response refers to actions taken by a party responsible for making progress payments as a response to claims made under a construction contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 225}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERIM PROGRESS CLAIM (期進度款的申索)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Interim Progress Claim is the formal claim made by someone with rights or claims regarding interim payments during the course of a construction project, where another party has legal responsibility to pay these amounts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION PROJECT PAYMENT TERMS (建造項目付款條款)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction Project Payment Terms refer to the specific conditions and provisions related to payments for work done during a construction project as stipulated in the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION WORK COMPLETION DATE (施工完成日期)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Construction Work Completion Date refers to the date by which all work under a contract is expected or required to be completed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 225}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT OBLIGATION (付款義務)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Payment Obligation is the legal duty of one party in a construction contract to make payments as per agreed terms, including progress and final payments for work performed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 225}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION CONTRACT TERMS (建造合同條款)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction Contract Terms refer to specific provisions within a construction agreement that detail payment obligations, conditions, and other aspects of the project."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 26}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT DATE (付款日期)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Payment Date is the date on which money becomes payable under a contract for work or services provided in a construction context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 225}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;A PERSON WHO IS OR WHO CLAIMS TO BE ENTITLED TO A PROGRESS PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to an individual or entity that may have the legal right to receive a progress payment, possibly involving potential legal responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd1eddc6f0faa7cf197a030cc7a29b94</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 217}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 770}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1179}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTING WORKS OR RELATED GOODS AND SERVICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Constructing works or related goods and services refer to the construction activities and associated items involved in the project that are subject to payment claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd1eddc6f0faa7cf197a030cc7a29b94</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 217}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 770}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1179}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL ENTITLEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal entitlement refers to the right or authority of an individual or entity to receive certain payments under contractual agreements and laws."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd1eddc6f0faa7cf197a030cc7a29b94</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 217}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 770}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1179}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIMING PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON/ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Claiming Party refers to a person or organization entitled to progress payment under the construction contract, required to serve a claim for payment in writing with specific details."&lt;SEP&gt;"Claiming Party refers to the entity or individual who makes a payment claim against another party."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Claiming Party is an entity that has the right to delay work or supply according to certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Claiming Party is the entity or individual who has provided goods or services and is seeking payment, thus sending out a payment claim."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Claiming Party refers to an entity that has served a payment claim for progress payment under section 18 and may delay work or supply based on certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d4be77f953bdd4a222130461f58fb29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b7d543744ae8aafbe46746751935e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98b9cc96db8e2ffdc374754939531431&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89690e148d95bff497042548ed9e3555&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a39eb07c8451fb1542c2fcc4877cecdf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 775}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION WORK OR RELATED GOODS AND SERVICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction Work or Related Goods and Services are identified in payment claims, detailing what the progress payment relates to."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-41b7d543744ae8aafbe46746751935e3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 217}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 770}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1179}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 44 DETERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL DOCUMENT/STANDARD"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 44 Determination is a binding decision by relevant authority which cannot be included in the payment claims according to regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-41b7d543744ae8aafbe46746751935e3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 217}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 770}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1179}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT RESPONSE PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Payment Response Period refers to the timeframe within which a paying party must respond to a payment claim as per contractual agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98b9cc96db8e2ffdc374754939531431</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 774}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIMED AMOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS/FINANCIAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Claimed Amount refers to the total value requested by the claiming party in a payment claim. It is the amount they believe should be paid for the work done or services provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Claimed Amount refers to the total amount of money claimed by the claimant in relation to payment disputes, which must be detailed in their notification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98b9cc96db8e2ffdc374754939531431&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b219a4ff887909dc5fdeb24191ca220</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 223}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CERTIFICATE OR VALUATION DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY,PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Certificate or Valuation Document is an official document issued according to a construction contract that provides an assessment of the value of work completed. It can serve as evidence in payment claims and responses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98b9cc96db8e2ffdc374754939531431</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUILDING CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Building Contract refers to specific types of contracts related to construction projects, which often include clauses for handling payment disputes through formal processes such as issuing certificates or valuations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98b9cc96db8e2ffdc374754939531431</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT CLAIM PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Payment Claim Process is a structured method used in business transactions where one party formally requests payment from another. It involves sending and responding to claims within specified timeframes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98b9cc96db8e2ffdc374754939531431</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTUAL OBLIGATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES,LAW"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contractual Obligations refer to the legal responsibilities and duties that parties agree upon in a contract, including obligations related to payment claims and responses. These are governed by laws and regulations ensuring fair business practices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98b9cc96db8e2ffdc374754939531431</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT DISPUTE RESOLUTION MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY/LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Payment Dispute Resolution Mechanism is the process or set of procedures designed to resolve disputes over payments, often outlined in contracts and involving steps such as issuing certificates or valuations."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mechanism for resolving payment disputes through adjudication proceedings where an adjudicator determines a dispute based on specific conditions and requirements outlined in sections 36 and 37 of the relevant legislation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-98b9cc96db8e2ffdc374754939531431&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 808}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT RESPONSE DEADLINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Payment Response Deadline is the latest date by which a paying party must serve a payment response, as defined in subsections (1) and (2)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Payment Response Deadline is the specific date by which a paying party must respond to a payment claim, either within the 30-day period or on another agreed-upon date."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Payment Response Deadline is defined by section 24(a) as the day following the occurrence of a specific event, such as those mentioned in subsections (2)(a) or (c)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d4be77f953bdd4a222130461f58fb29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0af4d7e54b59f5f639294394f679c069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f04c9983bdf92638bbe090b65a4a327a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 776}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;30-DAY PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The 30-day period refers to a standard timeframe for responding to a payment claim after it has been served under section 18 (30-day period)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0af4d7e54b59f5f639294394f679c069</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 217}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 770}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1179}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SET OFF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Set Off is a legal concept allowing one party to reduce or offset an amount owed by another in response to a claim. In this context, it refers to the paying party's inability to use set off as a defense after failing to respond within the payment response deadline."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0af4d7e54b59f5f639294394f679c069</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 776}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;工作日&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workday refers to days that are not public holidays, Saturdays, or black暴雨警告日或烈風警告日 as defined in the Interpretation and General Provisions Ordinance (Chapter 1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce595edca85b7cf2be310394d2ac094c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;方、一方 (PARTY)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Party means a party involved in adjudication proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce595edca85b7cf2be310394d2ac094c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;裁定 (DETERMINATION)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Determination is an outcome made by an adjudicator according to section 42."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce595edca85b7cf2be310394d2ac094c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;解決爭議程序 (DISPUTE RESOLUTION PROCEEDINGS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dispute Resolution Proceedings include arbitration procedures, which are part of the legal framework for resolving disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce595edca85b7cf2be310394d2ac094c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;審裁回應 (ADJUDICATION RESPONSE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjudication Response is a specific document or action required by section 31(1) in the adjudication process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce595edca85b7cf2be310394d2ac094c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;審裁陳詞 (ADJUDICATION SUBMISSION)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjudication Submission, as defined under section 30(1), refers to documents submitted for consideration during the adjudication proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce595edca85b7cf2be310394d2ac094c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;審裁答覆 (REPLY TO AN ADJUDICATION RESPONSE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Reply to Adjudication Response is a specific document or action required by section 32(1) in response to another party's submission in the adjudication process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce595edca85b7cf2be310394d2ac094c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;第54條&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 54 of the relevant legal text provides rules for interpreting costs related to adjudication procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ce595edca85b7cf2be310394d2ac094c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT OF FIRST INSTANCE OR THE DISTRICT COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Court of First Instance or the District Court is a legal organization mentioned in section 30(1) and 42, involved in adjudication proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-16c32b6c243652a8ef2eb45cb49c1e90</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 788}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BLACK RAINSTORM WARNING DAY OR GALE WARNING DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Black rainstorm warning days or gale warning days, as defined by section 71(2) of the Interpretation and General Clauses Ordinance (Cap. 1), are specific events that do not count as working days."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-16c32b6c243652a8ef2eb45cb49c1e90</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 798}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;付款方&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"付款方 refers to a party involved in payment disputes, specifically mentioned in relation to sending payment responses or making payments under section 19 and 23 of the regulation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-16c32b6c243652a8ef2eb45cb49c1e90</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;付款回應期限終結&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The end of the period within which a response to a payment claim must be made, as specified in sections 19 and 23, is an event that triggers certain legal actions or consequences."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-16c32b6c243652a8ef2eb45cb49c1e90</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;申索處理程序&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"申索处理程序是一种用于分析和决定支付额外款项法律责任以及评估额外款项金额的过程。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de0ad9b54c9ee91ca2e3599ed5448d03</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;額外款項&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"額外款項是指在某建造合約中，超出原定合同范围的额外费用或补偿。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de0ad9b54c9ee91ca2e3599ed5448d03</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;付款爭議&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"付款争议是由于支付回应未按时送达或者金额不符等原因产生的争议事件。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de0ad9b54c9ee91ca2e3599ed5448d03</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;建造合約&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"建造合約是一种产品，涉及建筑工程和合约条款。"&lt;SEP&gt;"建造合约是一种涉及工程项目的合同，规定了双方的权利和义务以及额外款项的处理程序等细节。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-de0ad9b54c9ee91ca2e3599ed5448d03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fb320dd06f32faf0b373f1098dd9a0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAIM HANDLING PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Claim Handling Procedure is a defined process used to analyze and determine the liability for, and assess the amount of, any additional payments as per the contract terms. It includes procedures outlined in sections 24(4)(a) and (b)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The claim handling procedure is a process designed to analyze and determine legal responsibility for additional payments, as well as evaluate the amount of such payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f04c9983bdf92638bbe090b65a4a327a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc61c3e9d0b909249e0a6492fb80f00</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 217}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 771}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADDITIONAL PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Additional Payment refers to any payment specified within a construction contract related to expenditures or losses incurred due to delays, disruptions, variations, or other specific events as defined by the contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"An additional payment refers to an amount specified in a construction contract for expenditures or losses incurred by one party due to delays or interruptions in construction work or supply of related goods and services."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f04c9983bdf92638bbe090b65a4a327a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc61c3e9d0b909249e0a6492fb80f00</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 217}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 771}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT CLAIM FOR ADDITIONAL PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Payment Claim for Additional Payment refers to a formal request made under section 18 when an additional payment is required due to variations or delays in construction work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f04c9983bdf92638bbe090b65a4a327a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 217}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 771}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATION PROCEEDINGS FOR PAYMENT DISPUTES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjudication Proceedings are formal processes initiated by claiming parties within 28 days of a payment dispute arising, as per section 24(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f04c9983bdf92638bbe090b65a4a327a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 788}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;A CLAIMING PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A claiming party refers to the party that can initiate adjudication proceedings for payment disputes within a specified period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4a8b59b4e3e2ba05d0864cc47510c7b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 783}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1181}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATION NOTIFICATION (NOTICE OF ADJUDICATION)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT,TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The adjudication notification is a document used by claimants to initiate payment dispute adjudications. It must include specific details such as the parties' names or titles and addresses, nature and description of the payment dispute, claimed amount, recognized amounts, and any nominated bodies involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e4a8b59b4e3e2ba05d0864cc47510c7b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;提名团体&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Nomination body refers to the group that appoints the arbitrator."&lt;SEP&gt;"提名团体是指在合同中被指定处理付款争议的一方或多方。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3f9946a33c62725ccbba5bb541cff6fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fb320dd06f32faf0b373f1098dd9a0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;审裁通知&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"审裁通知是用于启动仲裁程序的正式文件，在特定条件下可以重新发送以继续或重启争议解决过程。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb320dd06f32faf0b373f1098dd9a0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;答辯人&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON,ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"答辯人在合同纠纷中被指名回应对方提出的主张，通常为合約另一方当事人。"</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3fb320dd06f32faf0b373f1098dd9a0a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATION NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjudication Notice is a specific type of document that must be served according to certain rules outlined in the Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Adjudication Notice is a document served on the Respondent and Claimant initiating adjudication proceedings for a payment dispute."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Adjudication Notice is a document used in dispute resolution procedures, particularly for payment disputes in construction contracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Adjudication Notice is a formal document used for initiating adjudication proceedings in resolving payment disputes as per the Construction Contract terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Adjudication Notice, or written notice of adjudication, serves to formally initiate proceedings for resolving payment disputes between parties in construction contracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"An adjudication notice is a document initiating a dispute resolution process, which claimants need to address in their submissions."&lt;SEP&gt;"An adjudication notice is a document that may be served according to the rules outlined in this text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Adjudication Notice is the document served on Party A which sets out the conditions for consideration and submission within a specified period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-33f6ad83e6dad4d9e791254952be2f44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1611b0ccefada6387970ed4d17809f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4537b3223942fe128431f147e0b27414&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80d3eaf058257b6baf9891597fa09fa7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b219a4ff887909dc5fdeb24191ca220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19b1bce23dbf161109b02b0e7ddc678&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bba63535f02791b0eaca5f64d5b8ed57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b53857aed1787aca531dea0f456e8ca5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 781}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELECTED ARBITRATOR(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON/ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Selected Arbitrator or body is chosen from the nominated bodies for resolving disputes, required to act according to regulations set forth in section 27(5)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b219a4ff887909dc5fdeb24191ca220</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 221}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 794}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREVAILING ADJUDICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Prevailing Adjudication refers to a previous arbitration process that has concluded and whose decisions can influence subsequent adjudications as per the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b219a4ff887909dc5fdeb24191ca220</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 221}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 794}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEW ADJUDICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A New Adjudication is initiated after the conclusion of an earlier one, following specific procedures outlined in sections 25(1) to (4)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b219a4ff887909dc5fdeb24191ca220</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 781}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SELECTED GROUP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Selected Group refers to a body or group selected for arbitration purposes within construction contracts as per section 27(2), which can be either the nominated bodies or those chosen from them."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b219a4ff887909dc5fdeb24191ca220</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREVIOUS HEARING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Previous Hearing, also referred to in this context as '先前審裁', is a prior adjudication process that has concluded and whose decisions may impact subsequent proceedings according to section 25(8)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b219a4ff887909dc5fdeb24191ca220</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 223}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAID AMOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS/FINANCIAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Paid Amount refers to any payments already made related to the disputed amount and must be detailed for clarity in adjudication proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b219a4ff887909dc5fdeb24191ca220</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 223}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;28-DAY PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TIME PERIOD"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A 28-day Period is a timeframe within which claimants can initiate new adjudications following the conclusion of previous ones, as per section 25(1)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b219a4ff887909dc5fdeb24191ca220</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 781}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;8 WORKING DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TIME PERIOD"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An 8 Working Day period refers to the time frame in which selected bodies must be notified after a dispute has been formally initiated by claimants."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0b219a4ff887909dc5fdeb24191ca220</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 781}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 27&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 27 outlines procedures for selecting Nominating Bodies in Construction Contracts and their roles in resolving Payment Disputes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b19b1bce23dbf161109b02b0e7ddc678</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 41(A), (E), (F) OR (G)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are specific grounds under which Adjudication Proceedings can be terminated, leading to potential new proceedings as per legal provisions outlined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b19b1bce23dbf161109b02b0e7ddc678</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 804}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1185}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;28 DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A period of 28 days is mentioned for Claimants to initiate new adjudications after certain events or terminations of previous ones."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b19b1bce23dbf161109b02b0e7ddc678</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 804}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1185}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATION RULES OF THE BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjudication rules are procedures or guidelines set by the organization for appointing and managing adjudicators during dispute resolution processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7ad6aa79a150340c8a28d98a0e6b1a24</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 788}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOMINATION GROUP(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Nomination groups refer to organizations that can be selected as bodies responsible for nominating adjudicators in disputes, especially payment controversies under construction contracts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7ad6aa79a150340c8a28d98a0e6b1a24</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 791}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPOINTMENT PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The appointment process involves selecting an adjudicator from nominated groups according to specific rules set by organizations related to construction contracts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7ad6aa79a150340c8a28d98a0e6b1a24</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOCIAL SCIENCES (DISPUTE RESOLUTION THEORIES)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The concepts of nomination, appointment, and selection procedures reflect social science theories on conflict management and mediation within legal frameworks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7ad6aa79a150340c8a28d98a0e6b1a24</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOMINATION BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Nomination Body is an entity selected by the claimant to nominate and appoint an adjudicator for a payment dispute. It must follow specific rules and procedures outlined in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nomination body refers to a group that may be involved in the process of disclosing or providing data as per specific conditions mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nomination body appoints the adjudicator and receives notice of resignation, playing a role in the appointment process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-145b271e55786ea72d8690e6e1f2ebf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b68681ecca6bd68067e789107e9bdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-336d2be2a1671f4a9c20d61c824c7555</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 787}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONFLICT OF INTEREST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conflict of Interest is a situation where an individual has personal interests that might interfere with their ability to act impartially in the role of an Adjudicator, making them ineligible for appointment as per regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conflict of interest is a situation where an individual's personal interests might interfere with the ability to act impartially in their official capacity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-40b68681ecca6bd68067e789107e9bdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59f65136a37f2183ac96641ebb7819e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 788}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDEPENDENCE AND IMPARTIALITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Independence and Impartiality are key concepts ensuring fairness and objectivity in the decision-making process of an Adjudicator."&lt;SEP&gt;"Independence and Impartiality are key principles required from individuals appointed as Adjudicators. They must not have conflicts that could affect their judgment or be seen to lack impartiality in the decision-making process related to payment disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Independence and impartiality refer to qualities required from adjudicators ensuring they can make fair decisions without bias or self-interest, which may be questioned when a new representative is proposed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-40b68681ecca6bd68067e789107e9bdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-169c5c3921ad759a4d5a8b8e69511b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59f65136a37f2183ac96641ebb7819e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 788}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONFLICTS OF INTEREST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conflicts of Interest refer to situations that may affect an individual's independence or impartiality in their capacity as an adjudicator."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-169c5c3921ad759a4d5a8b8e69511b19</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 788}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATION SUBMISSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjudication submission refers to the written documents provided by parties involved in an adjudication proceeding, detailing their positions and supporting evidence."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Adjudication Submission refers to a written document containing arguments, evidence, and supporting documents submitted by either the Claimant or Respondent for consideration by the Adjudicator."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47220fb088d5ae56db9b03a4c12e8f14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b53857aed1787aca531dea0f456e8ca5</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 783}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1182}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATION RESPONSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Adjudication Response is a written submission made by the Respondent in reply to the Adjudication Submission, containing their arguments and evidence relevant to the case."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Adjudication Response refers to the initial response or document sent by one party in an adjudication process, which may include claims, evidence, or counterarguments."&lt;SEP&gt;"An adjudication response is a document submitted by respondents as part of the dispute resolution process, responding to the claimant's submissions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-47220fb088d5ae56db9b03a4c12e8f14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b53857aed1787aca531dea0f456e8ca5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ddfde50b478473b5624659f6cfdd546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 783}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1182}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WRITTEN SUBMISSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Written Submission is a formal written argument or evidence provided by parties involved in an adjudication process as part of their responses to the initial response or document."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2ddfde50b478473b5624659f6cfdd546</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 788}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATOR'S JURISDICTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The term 'adjudicator's jurisdiction' refers to the authority of an adjudicator in determining payment disputes and related matters, as outlined by specific sections and rules."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3e060ad7c0dcaf66b5c6e6d5a4b6243</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 804}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1186}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT EVIDENCE RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Court Evidence Rules refer to the regulations governing what evidence can be accepted in a court of law, which may not apply directly to adjudication proceedings but provide context for admissible information."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3e060ad7c0dcaf66b5c6e6d5a4b6243</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 804}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1186}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 35&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 35 outlines the powers and responsibilities of an adjudicator, providing specific actions they can take during adjudication proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d30ea89e5165c3d71c14d8648bf53596</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 788}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FURTHER WRITTEN SUBMISSIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Further Written Submissions are documents or written arguments requested by the adjudicator, which can be submitted by parties involved in the dispute."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d30ea89e5165c3d71c14d8648bf53596</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 789}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTS AND EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documents and evidence refer to any relevant materials that an adjudicator may consider during proceedings, regardless of their admissibility in a court of law."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d30ea89e5165c3d71c14d8648bf53596</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 789}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDEPENDENT EXPERT REPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Independent Expert Report is a report from a neutral third party appointed by the adjudicator for specific issues related to the dispute."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d30ea89e5165c3d71c14d8648bf53596</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 789}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDEPENDENT EXPERT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Independent Expert is a person appointed by an Adjudicator to investigate specific matters or provide reports in construction projects, ensuring unbiased analysis of relevant information."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Independent Expert may be appointed for specific tasks such as inspections or evaluations related to construction sites, works, or other things."&lt;SEP&gt;"Independent expert may be appointed by the adjudicator for specific inquiries or reports on matters related to the dispute."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d879d95be32b955d798da85e699506e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8719074a70eff81632691da24dedfc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ea4a40e2dfeb073559acd2aab072a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 804}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1185}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATOR'S POWER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The power of the adjudicator includes determining payment disputes based on documents, evidence, and information available to them when a party fails to meet specific obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 808}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 31 ADJUDICATION RESPONSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 31 is part of legislation that requires the respondent to serve an adjudication response within a specified period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 32 REPLY TO ADJUDICATION RESPONSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 32 is part of legislation that allows the claimant to reply to an adjudication response, potentially affecting the adjudicator's determination process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATOR'S REQUEST OR DIRECTION UNDER SECTION 35&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The request or direction made by the adjudicator under section 35 is a tool for parties involved in payment disputes to comply with during proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT DISPUTE DETERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The determination of a payment dispute based on documents, evidence, and information available to the adjudicator when certain failures occur as described by sections 36 and 37."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTY'S SUBMISSION (OTHER THAN ADJUDICATION SUBMISSION)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES/BEHAVIORAL SCIENCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A party's submission other than an adjudication submission within a specified period, which can affect the adjudicator’s decision-making process as described in section 36."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATOR'S CONSIDERATION OF MAILED DOCUMENTS/EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The consideration by the adjudicator of documents or evidence that are mailed and received after a specific deadline, potentially affecting their determination under certain conditions as stated in sections 37(1) and (2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 807}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTY'S SUBMISSION CONTAINING SPECIFIC INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES/BEHAVIORAL SCIENCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A party’s submission containing information that is not known to the other party at a specific time, potentially affecting their ability to respond fairly as described in section 37(2)(a) and (b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FAIR CONSIDERATION OF INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES/BEHAVIORAL SCIENCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The fair consideration by all parties involved in the dispute of information that is not known at a specific time, potentially affecting their ability to respond fairly as described in section 37(2)(c)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATOR'S DETERMINATION BASED ON AVAILABLE INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The adjudicator’s determination based on the documents, evidence, and information available when a party fails to meet specific obligations, as stated in sections 36(1) and (2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 808}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 37 CONSIDERATION OF SPECIFIC MAILED DOCUMENTS/EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/LEGISLATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The consideration by the adjudicator of documents or evidence that are mailed after a specific deadline, potentially affecting their determination under certain conditions as stated in section 37(2)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 807}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATOR'S DETERMINATION ON PAYMENT DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The final determination made by the adjudicator regarding payment disputes based on available documents and evidence when specific failures occur, as described in sections 36 and 37."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 31 ADJUDICATION RESPONSE FAILURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES/BEHAVIORAL SCIENCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The failure of a party to serve an adjudication response within the specified period under section 31, potentially affecting the determination process as described in sections 36 and 37."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 808}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 32 REPLY FAILURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES/BEHAVIORAL SCIENCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The failure of a party to reply to an adjudication response within the specified period under section 32, potentially affecting the determination process as described in sections 36 and 37."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 808}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 35 REQUEST OR DIRECTION FAILURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES/BEHAVIORAL SCIENCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The failure of a party to comply with requests or directions made by the adjudicator under section 35, potentially affecting the determination process as described in sections 36 and 37."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 808}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATOR'S ROLE IN DISPUTE RESOLUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON/ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The role of the adjudicator in resolving payment disputes through proceedings where they determine a dispute based on specific conditions and requirements outlined in sections 36 and 37 of the relevant legislation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENT SUBMISSION DEADLINE FAILURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES/BEHAVIORAL SCIENCE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A failure by any party to submit documents or evidence within the specified deadline, potentially affecting the determination process as described in sections 36 and 37."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATOR'S CONSIDERATION OF UNAWARE INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY/SOCIOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The adjudicator’s consideration of information that a party was unaware at a specific time, which may affect their ability to respond fairly as described in section 37(2)(a) and (b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 807}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATOR'S CONSIDERATION OF UNFAIRLY IGNORED INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY/SOCIOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The adjudicator’s consideration of information that a party could not have reasonably considered due to lack of knowledge or access, which may affect their ability to respond fairly as described in section 37(2)(c)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 807}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATOR'S DETERMINATION ON UNAWARE INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The adjudicator’s determination based on information that a party was unaware at the time, potentially affecting their decision-making process as described in sections 36 and 37."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 807}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTY A'S RESPONSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Party A’s Response includes circumstances where submissions, responses, documents, or evidence are disregarded if they were unknown at the time of service or should have been served earlier and would not allow for fair consideration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bba63535f02791b0eaca5f64d5b8ed57</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 788}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 30(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 30(2) refers to a specific section in legislation that defines certain periods related to adjudication submissions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-712f0363a7a1263779f6581a9b8b41b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 31(2)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 31(2)(a) is another reference within the legislative text, defining relevant timeframes for responses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-712f0363a7a1263779f6581a9b8b41b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 32(2)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 32(2)(a) further specifies periods related to replies in adjudication processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-712f0363a7a1263779f6581a9b8b41b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 35(1)(G)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 35(1)(g) is referenced for the period specified by an adjudicator for any additional written submissions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-712f0363a7a1263779f6581a9b8b41b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIFIED PERIOD (指明期間)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The term 'specified period' refers to a defined timeframe in legal contexts, such as those mentioned in sections 30(2), 31(2)(a) or (b), and 32(2)(a) or (b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-712f0363a7a1263779f6581a9b8b41b4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REPRESENTATIVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A representative is any person chosen by a party to act on their behalf during the adjudication process, as long as they are deemed appropriate."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-712f0363a7a1263779f6581a9b8b41b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 788}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;A PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A party refers to a participant in the adjudication proceedings, which may propose changes or substitutions of representatives."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59f65136a37f2183ac96641ebb7819e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPOSED NEW REPRESENTATIVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The proposed new representative is an individual chosen by a party for representation during adjudication proceedings but whose selection could be challenged due to potential conflicts of interest or doubts about independence and impartiality."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59f65136a37f2183ac96641ebb7819e2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATOR'S RESIGNATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjudicator's resignation is an event where an adjudicator steps down from their position due to perceived conflicts of interest or doubts about independence and impartiality."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59f65136a37f2183ac96641ebb7819e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 245}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONFLICT WITH A PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conflict with a party refers to situations where the interests of the adjudicator may be seen as conflicting with those of one of the parties involved in the dispute, potentially affecting their ability to remain fair and unbiased."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59f65136a37f2183ac96641ebb7819e2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 245}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dispute Resolution Procedures encompass the methods and processes used to resolve conflicts between parties involved in financial or contractual disagreements without resorting to legal action."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dispute resolution procedures include various mechanisms for resolving conflicts outside the traditional judicial system, such as arbitration and mediation, which can involve confidentiality requirements and data disclosure under specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-71987cb00c98805ab9ed06eb948af233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-336d2be2a1671f4a9c20d61c824c7555</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 783}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1181}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATOR'S DETERMINATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event refers to the process where an adjudicator makes a determination on a payment dispute, including the proportion of costs and the amount to be paid."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d296364c6fb1e176227c199c33f148d6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 221}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 793}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMINATION OF ADJUDICATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event describes situations leading to the termination of adjudication proceedings such as failure in nomination, non-compliance with service deadlines, withdrawal notice, full payment by respondent, resignation or inability/ineligibility of the adjudicator."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d296364c6fb1e176227c199c33f148d6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 221}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 793}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;有关审裁程序因第41条所列的理由而终止&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to the termination of a hearing due to reasons listed under Article 41."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3f9946a33c62725ccbba5bb541cff6fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;该审裁员根据第33条规定决定自己没有管轄权裁定有关付款争议&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event describes a situation where an arbitrator determines they lack jurisdiction over a payment dispute as per Article 33."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3f9946a33c62725ccbba5bb541cff6fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;有关审裁程序获支付任何费用或开支,该审裁员无须根据第(1)(B)款作出裁定&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event indicates that if the arbitrator has no authority to be paid for expenses related to a hearing as per Article 56, they do not need to make an assessment under clause (1)(b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3f9946a33c62725ccbba5bb541cff6fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;根据该合同完成建造工作或完成为建造工作供应相关货物及服务的工期获延长多少日&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to the determination of how many days a construction period or supply service completion period is extended as per Article 3."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3f9946a33c62725ccbba5bb541cff6fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;须就有关付款争议而支付的总款额(包括第(3)(B)款所指的款项及审裁程序费用)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event describes the total amount to be paid for a payment dispute, including expenses as per Article 3 and arbitration fees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3f9946a33c62725ccbba5bb541cff6fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;须支付的利息(如有的话)的款项(不不论以实际金额表示或藉参照任何比率表示)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to the determination of interest amounts (if any), whether expressed in actual amount or by reference to a ratio, as per Article 4."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3f9946a33c62725ccbba5bb541cff6fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;有关审裁员须在以下期间内作出裁定并送达裁定&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event describes the timeframe within which an arbitrator must make and deliver their decision, starting from the day of appointment plus 55 working days or a longer period agreed by both parties as per Article 5."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3f9946a33c62725ccbba5bb541cff6fc</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 42(7)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 42(7) is used for serving a determination on parties, which affects payment deadlines as specified in other sections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b49150680872ebc6da3ccdee23b5d249</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 788}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DETERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Determination is an event where a dispute, particularly related to payment, is resolved through legal or agreed means."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Determination is the outcome or decision made by an adjudicator during the adjudication proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-79816614535478a4c5093238ccf5e99a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c883642e952f5d5b217f2a11baae78f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 806}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TYPOGRAPHICAL ERROR CORRECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The process of correcting typographical errors and similar natured mistakes in determinations by Adjudicators."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c883642e952f5d5b217f2a11baae78f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 806}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION WORK VALUE CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Calculating the value of construction work is a product or outcome that can be determined through adjudication processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c883642e952f5d5b217f2a11baae78f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 224}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 806}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 42(1)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL PROVISION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 42(1)(a) is a specific clause that determines the value of construction works or related goods and services under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2c72baaf42bcfd44fb0bf40d018847b9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 218}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 774}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIVISION 6—SETTING ASIDE OR ENFORCEMENT OF DETERMINATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DIVISION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Division 6 deals with procedures for setting aside or enforcing determinations, including applications to revoke previous decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2c72baaf42bcfd44fb0bf40d018847b9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 783}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1181}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SET ASIDE APPLICATION (撤銷申請)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Set aside application is an event where a party in the adjudication process can apply to revoke a determination made during that procedure."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATOR (審裁員)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjudicator is a person who makes determinations during adjudication procedures, mentioned in sections 48(b), 48(c), and 48(d)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FRAUD OR BRIBERY (欺詐或賄賂)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fraud and bribery are social science concepts that can lead to an invalid determination if used improperly, as described in section 48(2)(a) of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NATURAL JUSTICE PRINCIPLE (自然公正原則)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Natural justice is a concept involving fairness and due process, which may be violated during adjudication procedures leading to an invalid determination, according to section 48(2)(b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIVISION 6 OF THE TEXT DOCUMENT (第6分部)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Division 6 is a part of the legal framework or document that defines and regulates set aside applications for determinations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECTION 42(7) OF THE TEXT DOCUMENT (第42(7)條)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 42(7) refers to a specific clause in the legal document, which is used as a reference point for when set aside applications can be filed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPEAL PERMISSION (上訴許可)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Appeal permission is an event that may or may not occur after a court decision on a set aside application. If granted, it allows further legal challenges to the determination as described in section 48(6) of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GUARANTEE (保證)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Guarantee is an object that may be required by law when filing a set aside application. It involves depositing part of the arbitration award with the court as security, according to section 48(5) of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATION PROCEDURE (審裁程序)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjudication procedure is an industry-specific term referring to a process where determinations are made by adjudicators in disputes or cases. It involves parties, procedures, and legal outcomes as described throughout the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORK OF SET ASIDE APPLICATIONS (撤銷申請的法律框架)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal framework refers to the comprehensive system of laws and regulations governing how set aside applications are filed, heard, and decided upon. It includes sections 47-48 as described in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD (經審裁款額)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Arbitration award is a product or outcome of an adjudication process that may be subject to set aside applications, and it involves financial obligations between parties involved. It's mentioned in section 48(5) as something that needs to be paid before filing certain documents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;14-DAY PERIOD (14日)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"14-day period is a mathematical concept representing the time limit within which set aside applications can be filed, according to section 48(3) of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SWORN STATEMENT (誓章)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sworn statement is an object or document that must support set aside applications as described in section 48(4)(b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NATURAL JUSTICE PRINCIPLE VIOLATION (嚴重違反自然公正原則的情況)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Natural justice principle violation refers to a social science concept where the fairness and due process are significantly compromised during an adjudication procedure, leading to potential invalidation of determinations as described in section 48(2)(b)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXCEEDING JURISDICTION (超越其管轄權的作為)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Exceeding jurisdiction is a social science concept where an adjudicator acts beyond their authority, which can invalidate determinations as described in section 48(2)(d)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL CHALLENGE (法律挑戰)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal challenge refers to the process of appealing or challenging court decisions on set aside applications. It is mentioned indirectly through appeal permission, which can be granted by courts as described in section 48(6)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DETERMINATION (裁定)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Determination is a product resulting from an adjudication process that may be subject to set aside applications. It's the core of the legal framework discussed throughout sections 47-48."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT DECISION ON SET ASIDE APPLICATION (撤銷申請的法院決定)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Court decision is a significant event in the process where courts decide whether to approve or reject set aside applications, as described in section 48(6) of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATOR'S INDEPENDENCE AND IMPARTIALITY (獨立或公正地行事)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjudicator's independence and impartiality are social science concepts that ensure fair proceedings. Violations can lead to determinations being set aside as described in section 48(2)(c)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL OBLIGATION (法律責任)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal obligation is a concept involving the duty of parties involved in an adjudication process, particularly regarding payment obligations. It's mentioned in relation to guarantees and arbitration awards as described in section 48(5)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEGAL DOCUMENT (文件)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Legal documents are products that serve as evidence or support for set aside applications, including determinations, construction contracts, and sworn statements. They play a crucial role throughout the legal framework described in sections 47-48."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATION PROCESS (審裁程序)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjudication process is an industry-specific term referring to the entire procedure where determinations are made and can be subject to set aside applications. It involves multiple steps, parties, and legal outcomes as described in sections 47-48."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a4515c46a290954f33bec2c90fbb156f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTIES TO ADJUDICATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Parties to Adjudication Proceedings are entities involved in the proceedings and can apply for setting aside a determination made by an adjudicator."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-143b0fa3beba6c5913ea9659f090c4b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 785}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AFFIDAVIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Affidavit is a written statement under oath that supports an application for setting aside determinations and provides details about the grounds of the application."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-143b0fa3beba6c5913ea9659f090c4b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIGH COURT (CIVIL JURISDICTION)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The High Court in its civil jurisdiction can be compared to how it enforces adjudicated amounts, similar to the enforcement methods used by the Court mentioned earlier."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-143b0fa3beba6c5913ea9659f090c4b2</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SET ASIDE APPLICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Set Aside Application is a legal action filed within 14 days of receiving an adjudication determination, seeking its撤销 or modification based on specific grounds such as fraud, denial of natural justice, lack of independence and impartiality, or acting beyond jurisdiction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Set aside application is an event in which someone challenges the validity of a judicial decision, specifically related to determinations made during adjudication proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f87d18cc47acf07db6f5458960b21f19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-143b0fa3beba6c5913ea9659f090c4b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NATURAL JUSTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Natural Justice refers to the fundamental principles that must be respected in legal proceedings, including fairness and due process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-143b0fa3beba6c5913ea9659f090c4b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 788}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENFORCEMENT OF ADJUDICATION DETERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The enforcement of adjudication determinations is a method by which these amounts are legally collected or enforced, similar to how High Court judgments are executed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-143b0fa3beba6c5913ea9659f090c4b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT PERIOD FOR ADJUDICATED AMOUNTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Payment Period for Adjudicated Amounts refers to the deadline after which one can apply for enforcement of the adjudication determination if not paid within that timeframe."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-143b0fa3beba6c5913ea9659f090c4b2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 785}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIGH COURT IN ITS CIVIL JURISDICTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"High Court in its civil jurisdiction is a specific court within the organization of High Court that handles civil matters, including enforcing determinations as if they were judgments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f87d18cc47acf07db6f5458960b21f19</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENFORCEMENT APPLICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Enforcement application is a formal request submitted by parties involved in adjudication proceedings for enforcement of a determination as if it were a judgment from the High Court."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f87d18cc47acf07db6f5458960b21f19</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 230}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 818}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rules refer to legal guidelines or regulations that can be established by the High Court Chief Judge to facilitate the enforcement process described in these sections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f87d18cc47acf07db6f5458960b21f19</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 879}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIVISION 7—GENERAL AND MISCELLANEOUS MATTERS RELATING TO ADJUDICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DIVISION"</data>
