<node id="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">The Seller refers to an entity involved in business operations who engages in selling goods under specific contractual terms. This seller may take on various roles, such as an agent endorsing a bill of lading or a consignor responsible for paying the price directly. The seller is typically required to fulfill certain conditions and obligations outlined in the contract, including delivering goods according to agreed-upon specifications and ensuring their quality and suitability for use.

The Seller can be either an individual or a business entity that provides goods or services under contractual agreements. They are subject to legal responsibilities if they fail to meet these obligations, which may result in legal actions by buyers seeking damages due to non-delivery or refusal of payment. The seller must also manage the risk and ownership transfer conditions until delivery is made or there's fault in delayed delivery.

In some cases, the Seller retains rights over goods before sale, such as reserving disposal rights until certain conditions are met. They may deliver more than agreed upon quantities during transit but remain responsible for ensuring safe transport of these goods to the buyer. The seller must be prepared to transfer possession and ownership of the goods in exchange for payment.

The term "Seller" encompasses a wide range of business entities that sell specific goods or services under contractual terms, including those involved in auctions where they may bid on their own items subject to legal restrictions. In summary, the Seller is an essential party in sales contracts who must adhere to specified conditions and obligations while managing risks associated with ownership transfer until delivery occurs.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e4c0453b8451785120b5b76a2526cab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6898f338d8c873d727625cb55234a222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-097842d27813c438fcbfa56e8eef5ca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69fc897b8b9dfae677db802b05a78337&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-183ae686da520342fd44ebd9847a6fdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34bc94419b349addb3ca3738887910de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09f76424c00042dab76ada9f73a18154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2828dcd3a1acc333b703677e12c2630&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3304fe02529acf61f5b7a297e0a498dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2262a3a4061aab5ab97a1077b67a5057&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e575d442f08ac69ffbe5033c6d10569&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8e3424a8a5275e58cb410e4ea0f205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19b288c9efaa7bb08b81764887c880c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-019dad10da4fa0e0f55e19465cb7641c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-535dface6286d8bede9ae8225e2d5326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32292d53bc2adbfdb992bdf0fe946e4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c25cd0589b8a4d3c22c97ec5d8feb564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fed27e8241086925853de29390c3f116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c93fa5b9277d567b2558365e758a282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08fbcc9c2ce9e3d4f773cc495db19495</data>
