<node id="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">A Claimant is an entity that initiates legal actions or claims against another party within an arbitration proceeding. This can encompass various roles and scenarios such as making formal claims regarding progress payments under construction contracts, submitting a claim for the value of construction work or related goods and services, initiating adjudication proceedings by serving an Adjudication Notice, providing written submissions in response to an Adjudication Notice, or stating facts and seeking relief or remedy. The Claimant is typically required to provide security as stipulated by the arbitral tribunal under certain conditions and may be involved in submitting evidence or claims for resolution through legal means.

The Claimant can also refer to a party that initiates arbitration proceedings by making a claim against another party (the Respondent) regarding specific issues such as payment disputes. This entity is responsible for initiating nomination processes, selecting Nomination Bodies to handle payment disputes, and serving adjudication submissions within the specified period or withdrawing from the proceedings if necessary.

In summary, a Claimant in an arbitration context is an individual or organization that initiates legal actions by making claims against another party, often involving construction contracts, payment disputes, and other forms of contractual obligations. The process typically requires adherence to specific procedural requirements and may involve providing security as mandated by the arbitral tribunal.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-85d99713e2d7a58da6c720456f882ba7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1611b0ccefada6387970ed4d17809f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af79dae94b8a0756fefbbf0f811ebd51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ad6aa79a150340c8a28d98a0e6b1a24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c72baaf42bcfd44fb0bf40d018847b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ddfde50b478473b5624659f6cfdd546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5943028cc6f3beb70826c83454e86767&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71987cb00c98805ab9ed06eb948af233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6127a28d22b5d9d9145842f6c4caba9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b219a4ff887909dc5fdeb24191ca220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19b1bce23dbf161109b02b0e7ddc678&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d296364c6fb1e176227c199c33f148d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b53857aed1787aca531dea0f456e8ca5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccfc28d1a77070797c9452e760bfd7f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-145b271e55786ea72d8690e6e1f2ebf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b68681ecca6bd68067e789107e9bdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d229505b95cc3e576d9ad034318c66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47220fb088d5ae56db9b03a4c12e8f14</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 783}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1181}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">Construction Work encompasses a wide range of activities related to building or altering structures, including the construction, installation, erection, reconstruction, repair, maintenance (including re-decorating and external cleaning), renewal, removal, alteration, improvement, dismantling, or demolition of specified structures. This term is primarily used in contractual agreements for projects that require approval from an architectural officer under specific conditions outlined in the Building Ordinance (Cap. 123). Construction Work also involves preparatory works and related activities such as machinery use, transportation, disposal, feasibility studies, consultancy, engineering testing, and various goods and services like materials, plant equipment, manpower resources.

Construction work is subject to noise control regulations and may require permits for certain activities. The term "construction work" can be broadly defined in legal documents or contracts to include the building of specified structures as well as related preparatory works and maintenance activities. It covers a comprehensive range of physical tasks and processes involved in constructing, altering, or maintaining buildings and other structures.

The provided descriptions collectively highlight that construction work is a multifaceted activity involving not only the actual building process but also associated goods and services, contractual agreements, regulatory requirements (such as noise control laws), and various preparatory works.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-307d5bb8387dc47aa9c0f172efe39d0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad2f770d3edd7fc8b6985f3040077779&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d64bf6870cd28991e3919d0bb4b5dfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3df2a801b8139ee63d424aaec7ccaaa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f04c9983bdf92638bbe090b65a4a327a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fae8b17287c09754a8180334dba81fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c80a5edef13387c70f1ddbc0ac7e4acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d107bfd5d6737d06b2fc1d377e10585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66157f73d78c8a042051d0b5db5e4492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e519122ccc2d577ad6723a71d0f9b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f2283841f29f58e1152dc9a3680675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d7aa41ab04a649aeb83e8611a7626ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fed725f04c7bcd4c7d2f5a1a4787af6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2eccadbd7c68a667581159c35e652034</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 796}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1183}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"WAGES" refers to monetary compensation paid by employers to employees for their work performed under specific employment contracts and agreements. This includes various forms of payments such as regular wages, performance bonuses, commissions, transportation allowances, overtime pay, and benefits like maternity leave, paternity leave, rest days, sick leaves, holidays, and annual leave. Wages are subject to certain legal limitations regarding payment timing and amount, and they can be claimed back or deducted under specific conditions outlined in labor laws.

WAGES encompass the regular earnings an employee would receive if they continued working, which is often used for comparison with current or potential future earnings during periods of incapacity such as leaves and sickness days. They are a fundamental economic concept within labor relations and social sciences related to labor economics and employment law. WAGES can be calculated on a daily average basis in certain contexts and are subject to specific regulations regarding payment timing, amount, and conditions under which they may be claimed or deducted.

In summary, "WAGES" is the monetary compensation due to employees for their work performed, including various types of leave and absences as specified by labor laws. This comprehensive definition covers all forms of payments made in exchange for an employee's labor, subject to specific legal obligations and conditions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5001d950d1e5de5921648ae860af7539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a160d4a92860e123b37153b47528d3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6ee37a79b0dc57f162b791dd8b859ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7243d6ae166cfdb764a13e61a193cccf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aafe272a6fc4c9f42a82af975bc57303&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bad177b227e380cc066abb25e6c2cf7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bfdf4a9968aec09594f73a07cdf18d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79b86e6b5d2c9cc7cc776e8be6a979bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-918c0eabaec10917e5775ff91d8fc75a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1093ec98fdeda43f43128129d5d24cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb1b0eee63da6475bd592efac352092a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-323c200d08170c4d996dbd247312e21a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602a52838c03cef3777006bf2a44b72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af77be8b003511c35b7551f4285bb427&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d93d92eb00cb1e06709b542dad7efdd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df8fc6081be757641b05c1766ffacd20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14526d01cdd531d1142f16c1d5e43367&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e3b8e5ac9feac4c8c89dafe20af1c65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07f949d11fd1c1d8a909fd36ccac57d6</data>
