<node id="&quot;COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"COMPENSATION" is a comprehensive financial benefit or reparation designed for various scenarios involving loss, injury, incapacity, or death related to employment. According to relevant regulations and legal provisions such as Sections 6-10, 10A, 16I(3), 36MA of the Ordinance (Cap. 91) and other specific sections mentioned in the document, compensation includes funeral expenses, medical fees, wages or salaries, financial support for loss of earning capacity due to injury or incapacity, and payments related to occupational diseases.

Compensation is typically provided by employers or Principal Contractors/Sub-Contractors as a form of reparation under legal obligations. It can be claimed by employees who suffer personal injuries during employment-related accidents, become incapacitated, die from an occupational disease, or have their family members affected in certain conditions. The entitlement to compensation may depend on compliance with medical examinations and documentation.

In cases where the employee is injured due to a work-related accident, compensation aims to provide financial support for losses incurred, including loss of earning capacity. Additionally, it can be extended to seafarers who suffer injuries during their employment or family members of deceased employees based on income and age at the time of death. The specific conditions under which these compensations are provided may vary according to the Ordinance's detailed provisions.

Overall, "COMPENSATION" is a financial benefit that serves as reparation for various types of loss or damage suffered by employees during their work-related activities, ensuring they receive appropriate support in accordance with legal and regulatory frameworks.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bf83ce681b3c9c2ca889e6e5ad2a0c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd0b12255f92625b40e8341bf78636d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-062631c2ee8edb363f6cc234fa986a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21a9118870da5f24590e5c8c51628539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1c30b39b26dc22df210f2ea63b93552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e7d6d62033f777323f252b1d52645d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f08187ad728064351e188904ac02ad6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d80227f925bf1b081dc41765e6e6934&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3060c6c2405e1ec77fec151e62494218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44ee098d72c3cfdd3e201662ed838d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd33f100307534902fe4100976fabc93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2792d26b948960fecf0ee999232dc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80bd6fbaafa695488034148c221f9cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bec8c023e7d401bc65410e4d6428ec7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8bab0fa8e650dc6d58da85c05c8bf94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3b44850af90a02b11f7716520e896fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1faa1664ffe65d577dff74396c2e0ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd3149c252f1ac5ec61e07c2fc936cbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f42f51d2c6e983618042024d83fb403&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1683d49752acaec3491f38a426aac742&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f281684938925901a68a287ea35fbc44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679d548673cb77dcfe447573286cf62e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54addea578982eb79d7f3048cf09c6a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be12459eb42b5303144e2a38dc8cf0c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-338f6b52974bc08baebc662da42c4477</data>
