<node id="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">MATERNITY LEAVE is a period of absence granted to female employees for the purpose of giving birth and recovering after childbirth. This leave is typically provided by employers as part of broader employment benefits and is legally protected against termination during this time. Maternity Leave can be divided into two main phases: one related to pregnancy (often starting 4 weeks before the expected date of confinement) and another following childbirth, which may last up to 14 weeks or more depending on specific legal provisions such as section 12AA.

During maternity leave, employees are entitled to various benefits including wages or compensation. These leaves can be continuous periods with associated medical certificates required for verification. Maternity Leave is not included in the notice period for termination and does not result in a loss of wages according to relevant labor laws and regulations such as BAA (Basic Appropriation Authority) guidelines.

The leave encompasses both pregnancy-related absences and post-delivery recovery, ensuring that female employees have sufficient time to recover physically and bond with their newborns. Maternity Leave is recognized under specific ordinances and labor laws in Hong Kong, providing a comprehensive framework for the rights of pregnant women during this critical period.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5001d950d1e5de5921648ae860af7539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f355da3b0eddd390953ffae58fee2099&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9112f21c7d8a89e9880b92acfce9ecd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb4129e436da0578c032f036f81bf719&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fef56ddac89c58276c95d49a4ad2fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea6b2c9739d4904eac9e0c6be6072cb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-911f250d278d47d4c7dfd5e35d124637&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c1776c3e340075487202946fbb11cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7550fdff3623ae221e2d156f6ce5cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5aaa252a172d6b006af917dc91a91759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8d3158e721c74f203da21b92ec49085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bef47a255f1eda2d15380bce3341cd94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505a565a05fcfbf53c86377d50356a49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d14b62c50b2a0a92ac73c8ef0642fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c72195a1e02c5898f4f5f3e8dd2e1df3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d6f22e03ef794b224e1918ddd3fee77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 98}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 510}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">The Authority is a regulatory body with multiple functions, primarily focused on managing construction noise permits and overseeing activities that generate noise. This organization has the power to issue directions, enforce regulations, serve notices for measurements or inspections, and make decisions regarding appeals based on specific criteria. The Authority can also grant exemptions, apply standards related to noise emissions from motor vehicles, and determine if a noise violation has occurred.

According to Section 3(1) of the relevant regulation, the Authority is appointed as the noise control supervisor responsible for overseeing noise-related activities at construction sites. It operates under guidelines provided by Technical Memoranda and uses these documents when conducting measurements or assessments of noise compliance with abatement notices. The Authority can require products for testing and has the power to serve notices on individuals regarding such tests.

The organization is also tasked with issuing, amending, and canceling construction noise permits based on specific criteria. It serves as a governing body responsible for handling complaints and information related to offenses against the Ordinance. Additionally, it may be subject to financial charges on general revenue if involved in appeals or other regulatory processes.

In summary, the Authority is an organization with comprehensive powers over noise-related activities, including issuing permits, enforcing regulations, conducting inspections, serving notices, making decisions regarding appeals, and handling complaints related to violations of noise control laws.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-aad6b1b45211aa087c009dc4e318a023&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9af0d61962337f7b194e565a06d8c298&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bda701f7b69fa34380775a0f86642cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbe588d5c34575494b1af01bf122cae8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35333cbaccd9be2f64c80f729f9d5ffb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a63521ff775998da1314db4dd547a7d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac0836d4d9cd8980aca2b9281cb718a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8555cdc45377153d4e3dfbeaa45b31ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5997efc3513d7a18a8e6ffade96f199b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddee27cc5f92142cd2814225d68af96b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d107bfd5d6737d06b2fc1d377e10585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3645bfc30781435fa7015192a9be351c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ed6bb61c777b6fe07e21fb258ca9224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf98c13106216ee2990969e11aafbee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0c6e4486519ef84f7ca9a05c6e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a461efee858ab690fe058321b8a0025&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72a00cd6e89601305d8b400d5eef9c21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d7aa41ab04a649aeb83e8611a7626ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56e97ce586530c13a293f392668859be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1740b8b8c7e777efdccf16fb8d3a59de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c46d2bc84b41a7759d92a2cdbd5b2891&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cbc913a82bac150b6a4b08953fa04d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ae14afda9d52be1864e9090474b79d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a89fc961d4c4ccbebf98c5fc224109</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 290}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 967}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1211}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">A severance payment refers to a financial compensation provided by employers upon termination of employment. This compensation can take various forms and conditions based on specific legal requirements and procedural guidelines outlined in relevant ordinances or amendments, such as Clause 31B(1). Typically, the amount is calculated according to specific sections of the law, often considering factors like length of service (with a base calculation of 18 days' wages from the last 30 working days or two-thirds of $22,500, whichever is smaller) and may be subject to reductions based on certain conditions involving gratuities or benefits. Severance payments can also apply in cases where an employee's contract is terminated by the employer without cause or after a reasonable notice period has expired.

In some instances, severance payment might include provisions for personal representatives of deceased employers, potentially affecting the calculation of gratuities and benefits based on years of service. The termination could be due to layoffs, redundancy, dismissal, or other specific conditions as stipulated in legal sections. Severance payments are designed to provide financial support during transitions out of employment but may not always be applicable under certain specified circumstances.

Overall, severance payment is a comprehensive term encompassing various forms and conditions of compensation provided by employers upon termination of an employee's contract due to layoffs, redundancy, or dismissal, subject to specific legal requirements and potential reductions based on gratuities or benefits.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e17f3710da650d1e14713613a2dff129&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5d2b28a0cc543e1f646cbc0388c9eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9546d09d8137ba2697ee36074c84b498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60278fe3510d3896a76c8ed45d034e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28b2163160f25fa57988c0b4d0c740cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11d596f17d04a1402f9a7eda05284076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622dec92f9d3c73f201fbdc4fab3be5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ca736f121ac163d07969e939b811f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8e2655c247e96affa05132d650c897b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da53ed52a17c537de0b1301ebe9c9aa8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c24d050bd3e4419e71408fc656cab32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16880dc0f6b710adfcdbea0c6c5c09ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2138132720286ddae5a4634e3cd8c8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-398cf2cb1ea6408a6d67cec4cb083e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f00bfbc74cd988e98040394204cccd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d94d21b562915559fff6272dbbdb3b70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a40a9600dcdabbcf7b1de20226238a1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd899e03ecc067de0edd74af6740db7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4803dc099d05bf6f05b27d07f8429783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbef4b639390d1d66289078a98204ee1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 166}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 690}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1168}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">A long service payment is a financial benefit provided by employers to employees based on their years of continuous employment. This compensation can be given upon death, retirement, or termination and may vary depending on specific conditions outlined in legal requirements or agreements. The payment can take various forms such as cash, bank transfer, or through an authorized agent.

The long service payment is typically a sum due to the employee for recognizing their extended period of service with the employer. It can be subject to deductions under certain circumstances and may affect total entitlements when an employee dies. In some cases, it can also trigger benefits for beneficiaries like family members (Person B) in specific situations.

The long service payment is often provided after a minimum employment duration, usually five years or more, but the exact period varies based on local laws and company policies. It may be reduced by certain qualifying items as specified in legal texts or rulings from relevant authorities. The compensation can also serve as part of an employee's retirement planning.

In some contexts, long service payment is a type of severance benefit awarded to employees with continuous employment exceeding five years, subject to specific conditions and reductions due to gratuities and other benefits related to the deceased’s employment if applicable. It may be divided into pre-transition and post-transition portions based on legal requirements or agreements.

The long service payment can also refer to a financial compensation provided under certain conditions when an employee has died, leaving behind entitlements such as gratuities or employer-funded benefits. This benefit is often stipulated in specific sections of employment laws, such as Section 76 from 1985 and Part VB of the Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 1990.

In summary, a long service payment is a financial compensation provided by employers to employees based on their years of continuous employment. It can be given upon death, retirement, or termination under specific conditions outlined in legal requirements or agreements.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-233de206d4d440690ca3d19bf8ddb77c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1bbd2f99a9b879945f0bc0e8afde73b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9d410c88421aeae56a47aedb79d008e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9335a6eed209eaa686a730c45ba54a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27ca5e1e28067ca3c2334e15e6221974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0b522ee3e92b516e9befd9d3479f215&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdbd130fa51f2bbf4428aee9c45795cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c7aef455ebf5c49827835bcb4e365e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2193ccb19ec3e792d874a92951eae0f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad13daf2441a168160e4226aa7ac493d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d634411e44f3153b1f3217349599619c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db531f9fed0b652cc40ad79eb2a48c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38034baf57d26ec704e02e12e81cdf6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aa1d2d981153f366e07b9a78ba0c7ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a3bfa1b02f074277b3b1a27f3afcb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ea74deaae12a605f5ea78eff9b6bb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0b8e9edfab8c32d5cea9270e6f74ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e5131fef8ae89d5a0f48b17c1599d19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc7d719876b6f50011d4a77def5a2428&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c317132f5543388aa4ec358d54fbcf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b785a6d2d7fe1aa9d111846965f88378&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54addea578982eb79d7f3048cf09c6a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2419e9b08cdfdf99b66599d9de26ba7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9abcb1aa4ccb5d467cb0175ca3011bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96ecd392e516343d8ffd40e3611e0e8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dabef41d299eda51d77087c2ca170398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b66ec28db0dbcb16e24e4d4df0ef35a2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 164}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 680}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">An Arbitration Tribunal is an organization or group of individuals appointed to resolve disputes through arbitration proceedings. This body consists of arbitrators who make binding decisions in disputes following established rules and procedures. The tribunal has the authority to hear applications from parties involved, determine the place of arbitration when necessary, rule on costs and fees related to its operations, issue arbitral awards, and provide remedies or relief based on the evidence presented.

The Arbitration Tribunal can be directed by a court to take specific actions regarding relevant property and may have powers over procedural matters such as language use and handling documentary evidence. It has the authority to make decisions during arbitration proceedings, including recusal determinations, corrections of errors, interpretations of awards, and supplementary awards based on party requests.

The tribunal is distinct from judicial courts but operates under certain conditions agreed upon by parties involved in disputes. Its decisions can be reconsidered under specific circumstances or influenced by serious impropriety events. The Arbitration Tribunal also has the power to make judgments with detailed reasoning, potentially requiring further elaboration if ordered by an original court.

In summary, the Arbitration Tribunal is a comprehensive entity responsible for resolving disputes through arbitration proceedings, making binding decisions, and handling various procedural aspects of arbitral cases according to agreed rules and conditions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d8f918840458c595eb8aa4b44f88bed0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac9a4105712169b0cda2b7c65d72aa76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62de924c3226ea55de4d94d980a6b34f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d17ccb7c45bbf013a4a9b072f210aedd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d99713e2d7a58da6c720456f882ba7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92dbfb61aa1ae662d58ad04e46a6a1e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698354d68541c6722cada50bb05de978&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540da5689ed24920444d2c678531763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afb67efa17f13209eb7c5173e786360c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4373f38dac5749d35f8ccd70b8bf1d15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7aaf6f770f217f1e2eb977b5ec34ad19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6793dcafea3acbec1f8e9bd2a51472c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3161c0abf732689fd0fb63c291711d64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6afb8943a99ee7bf996b0ce17c18a04b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5943028cc6f3beb70826c83454e86767&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-882b59070dba0a27453ac53b51232f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fd04bf2888da55881f593f9613b44e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caff1791e8e9f461d58d69581c8df6cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad963d62d75768847794433df9caf4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aa40d92e810c15d1924e632ab83962f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff2369343594485564382d2d30ba3755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5247edeafb01587bde32ae379e5261dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19092b2cdc4468b2128aef41dc2b2b67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aba64861ea22070188d9b7dd4c0fd47a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3906bbf7ee03793cf876d19cdfab509&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2047b71041716475b6c4ce04dcb74ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d82bf83563624acdc014bb3783db688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf8d77c0073f8253192bb2eb6ce56e99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7effd30746ff087ba04389bfb24de4c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccfc28d1a77070797c9452e760bfd7f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edc4c9a782cb874c7fb36432df37d995&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f3cce4894f17891d1764ccd30858f11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-854d00c33e69aed0258675abc1e2d264&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 234}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 861}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ANNUAL LEAVE" refers to a type of paid leave provided by employers as part of employment benefits. This leave allows employees to take time off for personal or family reasons and is typically granted after certain periods of continuous employment, with the duration calculated according to specific regulations or conditions such as service length or relevant closure days. Annual Leave can be taken or carried forward at the employee's discretion and does not result in a loss of wages if unused before employment ends. It is distinct from statutory holidays but may include provisions for use during paternity leave under certain circumstances. According to labor laws, annual leave should not be included in the notice period as per section 41D. Annual Leave is also mentioned alongside maternity leave and is part of an employee's benefits package, provided each year as a component of wages according to regulations such as BAA.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fee7842314099c25edf5106ebd221850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9e62e9c51234e7e58e65ee8d9b2c47e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8e2655c247e96affa05132d650c897b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d14b62c50b2a0a92ac73c8ef0642fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74bf264f43f2a8be1c1c6d9a90273b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7dbc6cb0d2646456eacee5097d668ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63d3371d1b762c2013adc08da9c549f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bef47a255f1eda2d15380bce3341cd94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c54e7deea495212bab465e4af100b7ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c72195a1e02c5898f4f5f3e8dd2e1df3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fef56ddac89c58276c95d49a4ad2fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1ba134cba7bc0ad2b2ef34e757e78d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8a8ba58e2f04dd4f35b5bed0e044673</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 501}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">Parties refer to individuals or entities involved in arbitral proceedings. These parties can include legal or business organizations and may be directly involved in disputes or agreements, particularly within the context of construction contracts and related legal processes. They are jointly and severally liable for paying reasonable fees, expenses, and other costs associated with arbitration proceedings. Parties have the right to agree on various aspects such as language use, document submission, appointment procedures for arbitrators, and challenge mechanisms based on serious irregularities affecting the tribunal or decision itself.

Parties can apply for preliminary orders, request expert assistance, make offers of settlement, and be subject to requests or directions from the arbitral tribunal. They may also agree on appointing experts or assessors, terminate an arbitrator's mandate, and request court intervention when necessary. According to Article 28 of the UNCITRAL Model Law, parties can apply for corrections, interpretations, or supplementary awards from the Arbitration Tribunal.

The number of arbitrators involved in arbitration proceedings may be determined by the parties according to their agreement under Article 10(1) and Article 26 of the UNCITRAL Model Law. Parties are free to agree on the functions of an umpire and whether it attends arbitral proceedings, as well as agreeing or requesting for experts.

In summary, parties involved in arbitration proceedings have significant rights and obligations, including agreement-making powers over various aspects of the process, compliance with tribunal decisions, and potential challenges based on agreed procedures. They are also responsible for costs related to the adjudication proceedings according to their relative success and other factors.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-74be062ba4c04dd5b51c11f6d66083c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95a4de41db58b9a101c75606869df8f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a8aef97985d67c64a247cd4ac0838cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d17ccb7c45bbf013a4a9b072f210aedd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4487876b424618c4533648d46889bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8edbd1c4d3b35d7faddb32b978e73e29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea943fe3338aa88e6573bf715e772abd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4373f38dac5749d35f8ccd70b8bf1d15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39b02ac25884a8c6102243f2b93f0c03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34872d5563389492bd86e96a7e9d819c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6cff72e41603eed38553fb4f306a008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341dbfe6e21afa768ee74c7e3db0be67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03bb9907c4707aee4e32c05a81efe12a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0165ce281c7667854e6df58da6d1a76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3161c0abf732689fd0fb63c291711d64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e5ed4af08fa3d54713649e0adf6d0ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59c7140869534366dd7270de77711ef8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-963f917b5a00c96d5b43bd1832480a19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-953aa58f588dab7be8bda910f0f31c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d879d95be32b955d798da85e699506e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f6ad83e6dad4d9e791254952be2f44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31879101d38b1d4251cc0b47a342f1d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d82bf83563624acdc014bb3783db688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf8d77c0073f8253192bb2eb6ce56e99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7effd30746ff087ba04389bfb24de4c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5a62633bac9b2c0c6ed1e0aa83ce66e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8dac8ba7cc8864d7ff7dc57b5b28604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edc4c9a782cb874c7fb36432df37d995&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad8b00bb4712fdfd27d215a729380d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b2fac04904854d200ea9c9161cb98c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c56a21239b5d0bf5cb22840251170eef</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 233}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 856}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1193}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECRETARY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">The Secretary, a key administrative official under the Ordinance, plays multiple roles within various contexts. The Secretary can be held personally responsible if they consent to or neglect an offense committed by a body corporate. In this capacity, the Secretary is presumed to have neglected offenses involving management of the body corporate at the time of their commission.

The Secretary's responsibilities extend across several domains including construction and related administrative matters as well as labor regulations. They are involved in appointing members for committees that assess medical needs related to prosthetic organs and surgical instruments under specific conditions, issuing Technical Memoranda on noise from various sources, establishing designated areas, managing body corporate registrations and appeals, amending schedules by gazette notices, ensuring public inspection of documents like Technical Memoranda regarding construction noise management, receiving notifications about employee deaths, directing functions of the nominating body or requesting relevant documentation, making decisions related to body corporate registrations and appeals, and extending periods for claiming redundancy payments if agreed upon.

The Secretary is also an official who has certain immunities as described in the text, such as not being civilly liable for acts done in good faith. They are designated by the Ordinance to receive documents, information, and perform other directed functions from the Nominating Body. Additionally, they have authority over administrative decision-making through Gazette notices, including amendments related to intruder alarm systems and care expenses agreements between employers and employees.

In summary, the Secretary is a multifaceted official with significant responsibilities in construction management, labor regulations, noise control, body corporate administration, employee welfare, and regulatory compliance.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-feeece6356508f661dcb4d399a15acfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb72900ee9c54337fb981f2f7d6cc6a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33baa15beb160832b6e2302162f04d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86b556980892b37b85caf641b152672a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-691e0bbfff602acd26ed9f7e9579a105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e18098fcb5747dd72313d5ee7912acb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac0836d4d9cd8980aca2b9281cb718a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c560e10db0daa7f51fa59f7a6b462aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db5cb02beaa944fb9a1df344fab4d2a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-401cd3cc83efdeb7f12cba3a9d1233da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0777124042c66cc9558d8401a55e7156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89bbff8bbf3f0985059cdccf2a6fe747&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-effb99400ad285817b5c201e84a15ab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-178a551bcbbb140ed32885ff11a760d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86dd5816dd56bd7bc4f23ec93e31f0f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ace38a89f19c657876dcff9d5f230c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72a00cd6e89601305d8b400d5eef9c21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8df740cc032fb332ff71c24c0e55c9c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622e9afcf96894f3c8695345444428d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a89fc961d4c4ccbebf98c5fc224109&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1901c04f5d127d84848a2cd1cbc4a1bd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 373}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1073}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;工資&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"工資" refers to the monetary remuneration paid by an employer to employees for their labor. This includes various forms of compensation such as wages, salaries, and allowances like travel allowances, attendance bonuses, commissions, overtime pay, tips, service charges, etc., provided in any form or manner and typically payable in currency. However, it excludes certain items: (a) the value of accommodation, education, food, fuel, lighting, medical care, or water supplied by employers; (b) contributions to retirement plans made by employers themselves; (c) discretionary free commissions that are only available at the employer's discretion; (d) attendance allowances or presence bonuses that are also of a free nature and subject to the employer’s discretion; (e) occasional travel allowances with non-regular characteristics; (f) expenses incurred for compensating actual costs due to work-related nature; (g) values of travel benefits; (h) one-time year-end bonus payments, or parts thereof, according to Part IIB provisions; and (i) bonuses that are either free in nature or only available at the employer’s discretion upon termination of employment.

"Wages" are payments made by employers to employees for their work. These can be influenced by various factors such as working days and leave periods, including specific situations like maternity leave and rest days. Wages also refer to the compensation received by an employee in a single workday, encompassing allowances and bonuses that may vary based on employment terms.

In summary, "工資" is defined broadly as monetary remuneration for labor provided by employers to employees under various conditions, with specific exclusions outlined above.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd681eafea885afa3c9b815543ffaba0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8625c1304f36a12d07cc0b6f8faf08b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab559340de48ae6d55e82984ae48a4f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bf34bf4406f6219987d03f2fb1fb1f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a82f354bd72ecc759d4ab4ed34bac3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14678de8548f803294fa05856c13dfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-285c049da04e797b33870a3a643d86c9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 479}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1132}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESPONDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">A Respondent is a party involved in arbitration proceedings and disputes related to payment under various circumstances. The term "Respondent" generally refers to the entity against whom claims or counterclaims are made by the Claimant. This can include situations where the Respondent has failed to pay an adjudicated amount by the specified deadline, opposes claims regarding the valuation of works, or is involved in a payment dispute that requires resolution through arbitration proceedings.

The Respondent must respond with their own submission in writing and may object to certain actions such as the withdrawal of the claimant's request for termination of proceedings. They are required to provide documents or materials according to the rules of arbitration and can be either the paying party against whom adjudication proceedings are initiated, or an opposing party who receives notice of these proceedings.

In cases where a Respondent fails to serve an adjudication response within the specified period, they may face consequences such as delayed performance of contractual obligations. The term encompasses both individuals and organizations that receive claims from Claimants in payment disputes under construction contracts or other financial agreements.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e5c0a23f28a68cdcea8ea323f65ec01d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1611b0ccefada6387970ed4d17809f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39b02ac25884a8c6102243f2b93f0c03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ad6aa79a150340c8a28d98a0e6b1a24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c72baaf42bcfd44fb0bf40d018847b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6edcec90a44956192e9747946f6d5481&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ddfde50b478473b5624659f6cfdd546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20e283bddbd3e4e77e96ddc072a75876&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5943028cc6f3beb70826c83454e86767&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71987cb00c98805ab9ed06eb948af233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b219a4ff887909dc5fdeb24191ca220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d296364c6fb1e176227c199c33f148d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b53857aed1787aca531dea0f456e8ca5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccfc28d1a77070797c9452e760bfd7f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04158b577f867f33b0abd25893c009fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-145b271e55786ea72d8690e6e1f2ebf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6028b01799478cec839282a4d1179b1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b68681ecca6bd68067e789107e9bdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d229505b95cc3e576d9ad034318c66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47220fb088d5ae56db9b03a4c12e8f14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4a8b59b4e3e2ba05d0864cc47510c7b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 219}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 783}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1181}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUDICATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">An Adjudicator is a neutral third party appointed or nominated by a body, typically for resolving payment disputes related to construction contracts. This individual is responsible for making binding decisions based on submitted evidence and arguments from both claimant and respondent parties involved in the dispute. The Adjudicator must adhere to specific rules of appointment and disclosure, including declaring any conflicts of interest or potential doubts regarding their independence and impartiality.

The role involves determining payment disputes according to established criteria, such as relative success and unreasonable actions by the parties involved. An Adjudicator has certain immunities, like not being compelled to give evidence, but they must act independently and impartially within their jurisdiction. They are entitled to be paid for work done and incurred expenses.

The Adjudicator is required to consider submissions only if served within a specified period as defined by the text's specific sections. Their decisions can include determining that one party is liable to pay an amount, specifying a payment period, and making determinations regarding the value of construction work or related goods and services. They may also have the authority to correct errors in their determinations.

In certain circumstances, such as conflicts of interest or doubts about independence and impartiality, the Adjudicator can resign from their position. The process involves following specific rules set by the appointing body and adhering to principles of natural justice.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e5c0a23f28a68cdcea8ea323f65ec01d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c883642e952f5d5b217f2a11baae78f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1611b0ccefada6387970ed4d17809f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4f0cfcab0e9f6d5a958dc7286fe8aad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8719074a70eff81632691da24dedfc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-304365a41d317ba2bf7cdd71b9dcffa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1901c04f5d127d84848a2cd1cbc4a1bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ea4a40e2dfeb073559acd2aab072a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ad6aa79a150340c8a28d98a0e6b1a24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c72baaf42bcfd44fb0bf40d018847b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ddfde50b478473b5624659f6cfdd546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71987cb00c98805ab9ed06eb948af233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bba63535f02791b0eaca5f64d5b8ed57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d879d95be32b955d798da85e699506e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b49150680872ebc6da3ccdee23b5d249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f6ad83e6dad4d9e791254952be2f44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4537b3223942fe128431f147e0b27414&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ace38a89f19c657876dcff9d5f230c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e089cfc832db9c43bb24baa7baf3ed42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b53857aed1787aca531dea0f456e8ca5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16c32b6c243652a8ef2eb45cb49c1e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59f65136a37f2183ac96641ebb7819e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-145b271e55786ea72d8690e6e1f2ebf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b68681ecca6bd68067e789107e9bdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-143b0fa3beba6c5913ea9659f090c4b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712f0363a7a1263779f6581a9b8b41b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-336d2be2a1671f4a9c20d61c824c7555&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-169c5c3921ad759a4d5a8b8e69511b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d30ea89e5165c3d71c14d8648bf53596&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47220fb088d5ae56db9b03a4c12e8f14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c56a21239b5d0bf5cb22840251170eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4a8b59b4e3e2ba05d0864cc47510c7b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 788}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">Arbitration Proceedings are formal dispute resolution mechanisms where parties resolve their conflicts through arbitration. These proceedings involve the appointment of arbitrators or arbitral tribunals to make decisions based on evidence, law, contract terms, and applicable trade usages. Arbitration Proceedings can be conducted within or outside Hong Kong and typically serve as an alternative to traditional court procedures, offering a more flexible and confidential process that may lead to enforceable awards in various jurisdictions.

The entire arbitration process includes multiple stages such as hearings, document submissions, expert reports, decision-making by the arbitral tribunal, and record-keeping. Disputes can be resolved through arbitration according to agreements or specific legal frameworks like the UNCITRAL Model Law, which outlines procedures for commencing proceedings, language usage, and confidentiality.

Arbitration Proceedings may involve consolidating multiple cases for simultaneous hearing based on certain conditions as determined by the court. The outcomes of these proceedings are generally binding but can be confidential unless all parties agree otherwise or a court deems it necessary to disclose information. Arbitration is particularly relevant in contexts such as enforcing rights under short-term patents according to the Patent Ordinance (PO) and resolving disputes related to enforceable awards.

In summary, arbitration proceedings encompass formal processes where disputes are resolved through an arbitral tribunal, ensuring fairness while avoiding unnecessary delays or expenses. These proceedings can be consolidated for multiple cases and may involve various stages including hearings, document submissions, expert reports, decision-making by the arbitral tribunal, record-keeping, and potentially awarding of costs and supplementary relief requests.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f295ffb815631fda7aa87257db86215&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8322a8472d188ae5550ad46529f8b37b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dab1df7b5bb64669485d4dce1155fb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afb67efa17f13209eb7c5173e786360c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4373f38dac5749d35f8ccd70b8bf1d15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0cddff72aaf0d2c6f21cba88e08e8e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-818682a0f1950aff44c4e7f18a331608&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5f33b7b9020135f31323fbae5f4463c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341dbfe6e21afa768ee74c7e3db0be67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03bb9907c4707aee4e32c05a81efe12a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9950c34a98c9cb7c295370ae17a2d5c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-963f917b5a00c96d5b43bd1832480a19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a78d8505ead991a0cdc7d41a2ddb40bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfadf35d2f372b32609102a0deae476e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd1eddc6f0faa7cf197a030cc7a29b94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61ef9a8b87aa1cf04b46aaf871b5f39a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddfbb014f2dc6afae82d7bc623722b27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf8d77c0073f8253192bb2eb6ce56e99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3bd35452fe0a7b5e9fa7dc2c1f8074&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e105b81cb8e7429af8bdd848fcb41de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2fe562ab74fde36758e6db7f158f71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae42208132627b8d5ff98d4e7966f28e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db0dce37722025939d7bba875b1ed10a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 237}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 886}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1199}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIRECTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">The Director is a key individual within an organization who plays multiple roles as outlined by various descriptions. In the context of managing and overseeing corporate activities, particularly those involving body corporations, the Director refers to someone involved in management and potentially responsible for consenting or neglecting offenses committed by the company. This role can extend to specific responsibilities such as appointing boards for evaluating prosthetic devices, issuing certificates related to necessary medical treatments, recognizing schemes of medical treatment, making applications to courts regarding claims, and taking legal actions against insurers under certain conditions.

In a healthcare context, particularly within organizations dealing with prostheses and surgical appliances in Hong Kong, the Director is an official who oversees various processes including approving the supply and fitting of such devices, handling disputes related to costs, and managing insurance claims. The role involves making decisions that can be appealed to regional courts and includes responsibilities like sending payment requests to employers, ensuring the necessary steps for the provision and maintenance of prostheses or surgical appliances, and overseeing legal procedures.

The Director is also described as a person with authority over certain organizational functions such as recognizing employer-operated medical plans under specific ordinances and issuing licenses and certificates for employment agencies. This multifaceted role underscores the significant responsibilities held by Directors in both corporate governance and healthcare management contexts within Hong Kong.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-966009ce5701084bfffbbea532d598a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-919e8934f076d1a9c5aea1486aa3f1c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a67530e0a9df975682238097b18b864&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baa998ea27b6baa036c2807f3cddf020&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a63521ff775998da1314db4dd547a7d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c560e10db0daa7f51fa59f7a6b462aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33fb429edfbad9e4130f4746d5db62bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54b3bbd8ad212745f60d65d18d1915a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72e470440b916fe7d89e88eb4a51cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d861619a56054d36c585396a6494755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5980c15d89bdf2ef4857f80a2f6b149c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fee7842314099c25edf5106ebd221850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77530b0513e9222b2220609d22541c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-607cc87ad2d00618b2e8b6ad160e563d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-effb99400ad285817b5c201e84a15ab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e6419607ae811f4fc50b4b883814d09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf8f4dc35687742a08f334ea70c92fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-786468d759a9a7b3ea39a79ba530682c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e69f47e10b2e6f7fc8c8517ea228736e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8df740cc032fb332ff71c24c0e55c9c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e2e52d53aa59764f7b51002074a7ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39a2bf80964aaaae8baf6e4ab980412a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4af496fc2b1c26e3d6bca76a4b99c25f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db7c4caf2703152da21b6fa8c5646ce3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 41}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 370}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 1066}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">A Court is an institution within the judicial system of a country responsible for hearing and deciding legal cases, including those related to arbitration agreements. It plays a crucial role in enforcing labor laws and resolving disputes over compensation, particularly in employment-related matters. The court has jurisdiction over various aspects such as setting aside arbitral awards under specific conditions (Article 34), determining the amount of compensation based on necessary attention costs, and making decisions regarding reinstatement or re-engagement orders.

The Court can order the disclosure or giving of any information deemed necessary for justice, including financial data from convicted individuals. It also has authority to extend time limits for award-making processes and rule on appeals related to awards. The court handles applications for recognition and enforcement of arbitral awards according to Article 35 provisions, as well as setting aside determinations made by adjudicators under section 48.

In cases involving employee accidents or travel conditions, the Court can interpret laws and make decisions regarding compensation claims. It also has the power to adjourn its decision and order the provision of security in certain applications, direct specific performance in contract disputes, determine damages for breach of contract, and issue orders related to reinstatement or re-engagement.

The court is involved in enforcing Convention Awards through legal actions and can make decisions on orders regarding periodical payments based on an employee's capacity for work affected by accidents. It also has the authority to review and potentially set aside determinations made by adjudicators under specific circumstances, as outlined in legal provisions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-62de924c3226ea55de4d94d980a6b34f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68ef0e8f1f38a0c8885d599e4ee4a20e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63fa361a4bbae312d93826ee30bf2182&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb0545d506978169e320db3a0cda4273&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-038abcb26f772c8f77b5ead3c3b7177c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8edbd1c4d3b35d7faddb32b978e73e29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540da5689ed24920444d2c678531763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-932bd52b3e4a92915c346a0ad3c1fd7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd8b5a6b74d6568cda4bfce7dd132460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3060c6c2405e1ec77fec151e62494218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6793dcafea3acbec1f8e9bd2a51472c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f8e345be219d3fc366dc62469796daf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02219b95b2d6273001fc2088c7c1d25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33fb429edfbad9e4130f4746d5db62bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0777124042c66cc9558d8401a55e7156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72e470440b916fe7d89e88eb4a51cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92743ab978843e283d6914a0d34ee3ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5997b47960ac46dfe44d6417d759c76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b49150680872ebc6da3ccdee23b5d249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779a6ebdcf1cc3fbd67a4dc22862c59e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aba64861ea22070188d9b7dd4c0fd47a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3906bbf7ee03793cf876d19cdfab509&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d82bf83563624acdc014bb3783db688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2200d76e6cc5397e7868136950dfb19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc2894a439737cb35869b760804ff684&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51d1d77716a000d59a4c18879a262e96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d19ac100c430c329d42230a7654f3c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff1392eccc9ea622ef0b3868092fcd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b57ac243904d2f7c387b12d47bb079b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-655dbcc67746c1c9fceca1a4e089796b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07f949d11fd1c1d8a909fd36ccac57d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-338f6b52974bc08baebc662da42c4477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01f73d3a0eb5a63d428e456a11dad9c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aae626926134b8ac6b7cded959f0e21a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c883642e952f5d5b217f2a11baae78f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fef0fb53d56f3928c358832b44a6a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd