<node id="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">A Public Officer is an individual serving in a government role, typically authorized by the Commissioner or Supervision to perform specific functions under an Ordinance. These officers are responsible for conducting inspections of Employment Agencies without requiring a warrant at any reasonable time and enforcing regulations related to employment agencies, including gathering information from them as needed. They may also be tasked with making inquiries into accidents in employment or breaches of statutory duties concerning workplace safety.

Public Officers hold positions that allow them to exercise powers conferred by Section 25 and other sections of the Ordinance, such as conducting inspections and entering premises for this purpose. These individuals are protected from personal legal liability for actions taken in good faith within their official capacities under the Ordinance, provided they believe the act was required or authorized by law.

Public Officers can seek assistance from others to discharge their functions according to section 25(1)(a) of the Ordinance and must comply with directions given by the Chief Executive. They are also responsible for making decisions related to employment regulations and issuing documents as part of their duties, which may include activities such as permitting or prohibiting noise during their official responsibilities.

In summary, a Public Officer is an individual authorized by the Commissioner or Supervision to perform specific tasks under the Ordinance, including inspections, inquiries into workplace accidents, enforcing regulations on Employment Agencies, and making decisions related to employment. They are protected from personal legal liability for actions taken in good faith within their duties but must adhere to certain confidentiality obligations regarding sensitive information.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cbf739f28af13fb255489857524eaf50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e43310bb8a059a1a014c1ba9a611877f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e37def8625e820a47ed5130364eb70d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e804bc54b158b7b2826228aa81b5372e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bba134fe326f216878a32b9c716807cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-057cc616cb8b855799f3fcacf937e222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbe588d5c34575494b1af01bf122cae8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee0cf79121cc26199f0bf5c4d14a8ce8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f02d6ddba7929fb360049bae6cab88e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fd592d376d0854e1e9f902478b9ced3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e25506f50e901e7cebe325e56cdc3f67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b297641c5fc96a9b02649fb896184fdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5742863cc938d9f9470985855601b925&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5218a05714fc8de44f54bb46fbf020e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddc943ee0b925d64ce2ff3b4b8fcc772&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da2837c3b5e351b2e1c63635e1c0a663&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ae14afda9d52be1864e9090474b79d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-029d1e15c5db53ebcfd1168d7ac7bbab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9a1fa46128d33dc86ff9326b722ce67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60c17dd78d73fb0b81ce0ba9e3153396&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1901c04f5d127d84848a2cd1cbc4a1bd</data>
