<node id="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">Arbitration is a method for resolving disputes outside traditional court systems. It encompasses various forms including proceedings before an emergency arbitrator, mediation processes, and court procedures where parties agree to have their case decided by one or more impartial third-party arbitrators. Arbitrations can be administered either through permanent arbitral institutions or independently, involving complex rules and agreements that govern the process.

The primary objective of arbitration is for disputing parties to resolve their differences without going through conventional judicial proceedings. The decision made by the appointed arbitrator(s) is binding on both sides once agreed upon. This method offers a flexible alternative to litigation, often with specific procedural frameworks such as those outlined in the UNCITRAL Model Law and local ordinances like the Evidence Ordinance.

While arbitration can be used for resolving disputes over intellectual property rights (IPR), it generally applies to any type of dispute where parties wish to avoid court proceedings. The process allows both ongoing and concluded arbitrations, with decisions made by an impartial third party or tribunal that cannot be enforced without mutual consent from the involved parties.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-95a4de41db58b9a101c75606869df8f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e027acdec4c66c21703cf2589ec26926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-603a9b33a6e3900af70fd439592326ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca2c3669141d3f1cd87a21d68d494cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca44dbb10a88be455b8df250e7a7b82b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af79dae94b8a0756fefbbf0f811ebd51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a177eee7ea2e82607ded8787a57461c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59c7140869534366dd7270de77711ef8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-953aa58f588dab7be8bda910f0f31c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98b6711af3c5bbaf4412b6b0eda86915&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea2051734d4010ecf353d49c7190a3cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca4a2a9fbbaee42187b60b84f640f8f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5247edeafb01587bde32ae379e5261dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c4488b1327869fe2b0410a202e25b48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f6ad83e6dad4d9e791254952be2f44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-524caefeb3520a83b6c8130676f95c53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0edcefcdaacd59cb7375b56608a714e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47762eabb07bb9265d79611ab6fc55f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-722c61c3b51c31b6fcf0c8534507c492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1901c04f5d127d84848a2cd1cbc4a1bd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 236}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 881}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 1197}]</data>
