<node id="&quot;PAYMENT DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">A Payment Dispute is a controversy over money, particularly in the context of contracts or services, including those related to construction projects. These disputes arise when there is disagreement between parties regarding payment terms or amounts and require formal resolution through adjudication procedures. The process can be initiated by serving a payment claim, receiving a response disputing the full amount, admitting an insufficient amount, failing to pay the admitted amount by deadline, or missing the response deadline. Adjudicators play a crucial role in resolving such disputes, with certain immunities during this process.

Payment Disputes are typically addressed within 28 days of their occurrence and can be settled either through written agreement between parties or via court procedures as outlined in section 44. The adjudication proceedings may also involve the resolution of disagreements over payments related to fees or expenses associated with the adjudication itself, which can be handled through various legal mechanisms including court actions and jurisdictional determinations.

In summary, a Payment Dispute is an event where parties are in disagreement over financial matters within the context of contracts and extensions of time. These disputes often pertain specifically to construction projects but can also apply more broadly to other contractual agreements involving payments.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1611b0ccefada6387970ed4d17809f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4f0cfcab0e9f6d5a958dc7286fe8aad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8719074a70eff81632691da24dedfc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-304365a41d317ba2bf7cdd71b9dcffa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b49150680872ebc6da3ccdee23b5d249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4537b3223942fe128431f147e0b27414&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3e060ad7c0dcaf66b5c6e6d5a4b6243&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e089cfc832db9c43bb24baa7baf3ed42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b219a4ff887909dc5fdeb24191ca220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19b1bce23dbf161109b02b0e7ddc678&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59f65136a37f2183ac96641ebb7819e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4a8b59b4e3e2ba05d0864cc47510c7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f04c9983bdf92638bbe090b65a4a327a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40b68681ecca6bd68067e789107e9bdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc61c3e9d0b909249e0a6492fb80f00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712f0363a7a1263779f6581a9b8b41b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-336d2be2a1671f4a9c20d61c824c7555&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-169c5c3921ad759a4d5a8b8e69511b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1901c04f5d127d84848a2cd1cbc4a1bd</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 16}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 220}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 788}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">僱員 refers to individuals who are hired by employers for work, receiving wages in return. In legal and administrative contexts, a 僱員 is an employee who has entered into an employment agreement with their employer under the terms of an employment contract. This person is entitled to various benefits including annual leave, compensation according to legal provisions if they suffer temporary incapacity or are injured at work, and other rights such as protection against unjustified termination under certain conditions.

僱員 can be further described in several ways:
- They may qualify for long service payments based on their years of service.
- They could be requested by employers to see registered doctors, dentists, or traditional Chinese medicine practitioners for health checks or consultations.
- Their employment status might change due to the death of the employer and they could potentially be rehired under specific conditions.
- In labor disputes and compensation matters, 僱員 refers specifically to employees who have rights protected by Employment Protection laws.

僱員 is a term used in various contexts such as work injury claims, health checks, employment contracts, termination notices, and other legal provisions. They are individuals hired for wages or salaries under the direction and control of their employers, performing tasks within defined job roles and receiving benefits like leaves and compensations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-233de206d4d440690ca3d19bf8ddb77c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-435a72f0a09b4a0be544ae91d6f3f83f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44e57b1615ed5c8b1f49eb6a6ecd4472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92d63fd21b0cce3b9e5c075238ab83af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad03aa80581d9d78c4971adade589820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb9dffd6c5cc9c95fa591e60b3b6694&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c031adb2191e2fdd70a1cfb2171a003&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a5734a3528df7505e20e5f0156116bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06d9351b59c3c08e06761abd48f7ff73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dff2dac44cda710c0a41dfe3af3e572&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9d7bf328eb68da98c29ac72b529085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede40d11dd383fafe8000e746a4c43b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7243d6ae166cfdb764a13e61a193cccf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed2004c9e59e7e54ef6756f3c59d039a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6957d2ae600df45cdcfeef087031ad45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae344452d3fef20d9a84a14e26b325a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b965639f18b2c29c5f672b6067f9d701&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c777bc9929cfa20260878316c3ec4ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56d9a950f8e72e839cb27b535da95ff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7430d09345738519e0c07e81b09c47d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56cceac4667a58d36b3976e9f95e0382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b88142ce6c5ae26fdcafd8cc6d03845&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e4b1d219d95c2446efb2aa90f70f687&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-269d623b6606eba8ac3002fec6213eae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27f6c661ada2a6aa0e1f1b94665b64df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14678de8548f803294fa05856c13dfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d9155ba523e4b47345476918c5dd94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-285c049da04e797b33870a3a643d86c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c2430bc80d4a39f49af281f4bcdadcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c82c895f7b30d4831c428126a0af9486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-193cb7d25870869b93d954860d0aaace&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19284fbf4d548ad004ef52e2b76eaa7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad6d0a2eed4fbaf59a6253fe84df6ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b4ba9b3e2ec8a01b740be7e7f709ed8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-688810e0abd091776de88edcaaba1bb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be5f720af1dc189f9088eb832b2b0cfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f5c32e3a6975f5012a9f880a409dd60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af77be8b003511c35b7551f4285bb427&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a5821c406f8b08deabbe52c126132b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57fe6a1a322921301e20ac79c773cc67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7afd3d77979ccf6bd91ad9b535aba7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86c763b37e9e3638b9a073d36c6b4de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ef856c5e83d9e91d386bd822201a8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63d24225c9fe2991b4b3b7b5c007e031&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8f159cb841c798f1b18dd22fda97160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75ec5cbcc26a69d2fa91ff3cd7cec100</data>
