<node id="&quot;EMPLOYEE CAN WITHOUT GIVING NOTIFICATION OR SUBSTITUTE NOTIFICATION MONEY TERMINMINATE THE EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT — (A) EMPLOYEE REASONABLY FEARS THAT HIS BODY WILL BE SUBJECTED TO VIOLENCE OR DISEASE HARM, AND THERE IS NO EXPLICIT OR IMPLIED TERM IN THE EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT INDICATING SUCH A SITUATION; (AA) EMPLOYEE — (I) HAS BEEN EMPLOYED FOR AT LEAST 5 YEARS UNDER THE TERMS OF THE CONTRACT; AND (II) RECEIVES A CERTIFICATE FROM A REGISTERED DOCTOR OR TRADITIONAL CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER AS SPECIFIED BY THE SECRETARY ACCORDING TO SECTION 49, STATING THAT HE IS PERMANENTLY UNSUITABLE FOR HIS POSITION DUE TO REASONS STATED IN THE CERTIFICATE.&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-b266f7ca95da19a8651bff75bd855a0c</data>
  <data key="d1">"The employer may terminate the contract without notice if an employee reasonably fears that his body will be subjected to violence or disease harm and there is no explicit or implied term in the employment contract indicating such a situation, or if he has been employed for at least 5 years under the terms of the contract and receives a certificate from a registered doctor stating that he is permanently unsuitable for his position due to reasons stated in the certificate."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE FACT THAT AN EMPLOYEE TAKES PART IN A STRIKE DOES NOT ENTITLE HIS EMPLOYER TO TERMINATE UNDER SUBSECTION (1) THE EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT.&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-b266f7ca95da19a8651bff75bd855a0c</data>
  <data key="d1">"The fact that an employee takes part in a strike does not entitle his employer to terminate under subsection (1) the employee's contract of employment, but it is still within the scope of termination without notice by the employer for other reasons."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
