<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;SCHEDULE 1 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ON INTERNATIONAL COMMERCIAL ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Schedule of the UNCITRAL Model Law can be referenced in Hong Kong's legal framework for arbitration rules."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;INTERNATIONAL COMMERCIAL ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"International commercial arbitration can be conducted in Hong Kong according to its legal framework."&lt;SEP&gt;"International commercial arbitration can take place in Hong Kong, involving parties from different countries or jurisdictions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 53 AND SECTION 68 OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sections of the ordinance apply to specific aspects of arbitration in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 53 OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section of the ordinance applies to specific aspects of arbitration in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSION ON UNCITRAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commission on UNCITRAL develops model laws and rules for international commercial arbitration, which can be referenced in Hong Kong's legal framework."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;CONCILIATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Conciliation can be part of the dispute resolution process in Hong Kong, including before or after arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration proceedings can take place in Hong Kong, involving parties from different countries or jurisdictions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration proceedings may take place in or outside Hong Kong and are subject to the legal framework provided by UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6eef98cdb7cf96d52a56e0103910d67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;PLAINTIFF&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Plaintiffs can initiate arbitration proceedings in Hong Kong, involving parties from different countries or jurisdictions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">20.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitral tribunals can be established in Hong Kong to resolve disputes under arbitration agreements, involving parties from different countries or jurisdictions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitral tribunals may be involved with proceedings that could have implications or enforcement within Hong Kong, depending on certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entities from outside HONG KONG may be subject to specific conditions when dealing with ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL awards and appeals."&lt;SEP&gt;"The concept of BODY CORPORATE and ASSOCIATION, which are related to the jurisdiction outside Hong Kong, is relevant in the context of ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL's powers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2da7991e9473f6c5aadfd4a87f21c511&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6127a28d22b5d9d9145842f6c4caba9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6100d8c7e7c5fa3f9af262a8c8cb68f5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;THIS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"This Ordinance applies to arbitrations where the place of arbitration is in Hong Kong, indicating a direct geographical and legal relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd3867158c784daaa4eb73ead4db9ca6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 1 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 1 of the UNCITRAL Model Law refers to Hong Kong in certain contexts, such as defining 'this State' and 'State'."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-44b140c12657294fe5c5d3a3a3fddb7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 2 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 2 of the UNCITRAL Model Law also references Hong Kong within its definitions and rules of interpretation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-44b140c12657294fe5c5d3a3a3fddb7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 5&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 5's effect is defined in relation to Article 1 of the UNCITRAL Model Law, which indirectly involves Hong Kong through legal terminology."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-44b140c12657294fe5c5d3a3a3fddb7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 3 OF THE UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 3 applies to Hong Kong and sets out procedures for handling written communications within the context of this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3694b9973d0eb7e4719ad33e81b8744f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">40.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration proceedings and ORDINANCE are mentioned in the context of HONG KONG."&lt;SEP&gt;"Certain conditions in the rules apply specifically to entities ordinarily resident outside HONG KONG."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Court enforces Convention Awards within the jurisdiction of Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court has jurisdiction over enforcement actions within Hong Kong as described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court's legal proceedings can be conducted in Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"The enforcement of emergency relief is subject to the laws and procedures in Hong Kong as governed by the Court."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a64f61df4c2295abb6d73eef9a781326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0813ab9a59ae553fa1d3747bf42131f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19092b2cdc4468b2128aef41dc2b2b67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2da7991e9473f6c5aadfd4a87f21c511&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4494c24ec2905c2010570a5a5156b75e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-655dbcc67746c1c9fceca1a4e089796b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitral proceedings can take place in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-655dbcc67746c1c9fceca1a4e089796b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot; COURT OR OTHER JUDICIAL AUTHORITY &quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal proceedings can take place before a court or other judicial authority in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0cc9146e12fcb8f714add3a3f7c0771b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;COURT-ORDERED INTERIM MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Interim measures can be granted by courts in relation to arbitral proceedings that may take place outside Hong Kong, affecting legal procedures and outcomes there."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6eef98cdb7cf96d52a56e0103910d67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The legal framework of Hong Kong includes provisions for court assistance in taking evidence as per the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration proceedings are mentioned specifically in relation to HONG KONG."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19092b2cdc4468b2128aef41dc2b2b67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration awards can be enforced both within and outside of Hong Kong under specific legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c57c5ae22a968acd7a8e3b02e3130cce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD ENFORCEMENT PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text specifies that the enforcement procedure for arbitral awards in Hong Kong is detailed, including requirements for producing certain documents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3136488efa6b0856e563bdafbaaa1633</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of PUBLIC POLICY in HONG KONG influences the enforcement decisions made by COURTS regarding AWARDS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-63fa361a4bbae312d93826ee30bf2182</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The enforcement of an AWARD may be refused by a COURT based on HONG KONG's PUBLIC POLICY."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-63fa361a4bbae312d93826ee30bf2182</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;CONVENTION AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Convention Awards are enforceable in Hong Kong according to the provisions of this text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4494c24ec2905c2010570a5a5156b75e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;OFFICIAL翻譯人員、經宣誓的翻譯人員、外交代表或領事代理人&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"These entities play a role in providing official translations required by Hong Kong law when enforcing Convention Awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a64f61df4c2295abb6d73eef9a781326</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;THE NEW YORK CONVENTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The New York Convention can have implications for Hong Kong, especially in matters of arbitration and enforcement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-603a9b33a6e3900af70fd439592326ba</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;CANTONAL GOVERNMENT'S LEGAL DEPARTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Legal Department of the Cantonal Government operates within and serves Hong Kong's legal system."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-603a9b33a6e3900af70fd439592326ba</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;MAINLAND AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mainland awards are enforceable in Hong Kong, either by action or under Section 84."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bcca397988541ca9ac3822ff7a363627</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;MACAO AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Macao awards can be enforced in Hong Kong, making them relevant to legal proceedings there."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ec95a82e50ec8c3adae1748b384fca48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;ENFORCEMENT PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal proceedings in Hong Kong can enforce or rely on Macao awards, indicating a connection between them through enforcement processes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ec95a82e50ec8c3adae1748b384fca48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;PART 10A&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Part 10A partially applies for non-Hong Kong arbitrations, treating them as if the place of arbitration were in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-358c63f61ec2ce4f0f9b4f0675b579e4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL PRACTICE FIRM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal practice firms are involved in providing services related to arbitrations governed by Hong Kong laws, including those under Part 10A."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-358c63f61ec2ce4f0f9b4f0675b579e4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;LAWYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Lawyers registered under Hong Kong laws, including those practicing within legal practice firms, are relevant entities when dealing with arbitrations governed by Hong Kong laws, including those under Part 10A."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-358c63f61ec2ce4f0f9b4f0675b579e4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OR TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text mentions that legal proceedings before a court or other judicial authority can take place in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4158bcd358cce62e9937de8896e1ba0b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration agreements are mentioned as part of the legal process for resolving IPR disputes in Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"The agreement's applicability is conditional on the parties' place of residence or business, and operations performed within Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d9d91db74534ffd661699611c1087da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;CONSTRUCTION INDUSTRY COUNCIL ORDINANCE (CAP. 587)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ordinance defines key terms like 'construction contract' and 'construction operations,' relevant to the legal framework in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c552b5974a2cb841d6608ab71d886584</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;IPR DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The IPR dispute is defined and regulated in the context of Hong Kong's legal framework."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text discusses the legal framework in Hong Kong related to Intellectual Property Rights (IPR) disputes under arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-98b6711af3c5bbaf4412b6b0eda86915&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d9d91db74534ffd661699611c1087da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIFIED ENTITY (指明實體)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Hong Kong law defines what constitutes a specified entity, which includes courts, tribunals, and other administrative or executive offices under the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-39620e4541eb49ae7a7ea14a2cf664bb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;AWARD (裁決)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text refers to awards made in or outside Hong Kong, which are a key component of arbitration proceedings under the Patents Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2d9d91db74534ffd661699611c1087da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;APPLICANT OR APPELLANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Applicants or appellants who are usually not resident in Hong Kong may face restrictions on having their applications or appeals secured for cost, showing geographical and legal jurisdictional considerations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-882b59070dba0a27453ac53b51232f89</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;SAVINGS AND TRANSITIONAL PROVISIONS RELATING TO ARBITRATION (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 2017&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Savings and Transitional Provisions Relating to Arbitration (Amendment) Ordinance 2017 applies in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-773d781fb9041ec95db87fc55340cd49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 2015 (11 OF 2015)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Arbitration (Amendment) Ordinance 2015 applies in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-773d781fb9041ec95db87fc55340cd49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;THE PRE-AMENDED ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The pre-amended Ordinance applies to arbitrations and related proceedings in Hong Kong before the new section's commencement date."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca44dbb10a88be455b8df250e7a7b82b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;THE ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Ordinance applies to contracts and subcontracts in Hong Kong, establishing its jurisdictional scope."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-66157f73d78c8a042051d0b5db5e4492</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;BUILDING AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Building Authority is a governing body relevant to laws and ordinances in Hong Kong regarding construction contracts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06e739d62dd19f34a46b38a2c7902502</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;BUILDINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 123)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Buildings Ordinance (Cap. 123) is a law applicable within the jurisdiction of Hong Kong, governing certain aspects of building work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06e739d62dd19f34a46b38a2c7902502</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT ORDINANCE (CAP. 57)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employment Ordinance (Cap. 57) is relevant to employment matters in Hong Kong which can intersect with construction contracts involving workers' roles and identities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06e739d62dd19f34a46b38a2c7902502</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;THE BUILDING MANAGEMENT ORDINANCE (CAP. 344)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Building Management Ordinance applies to buildings in Hong Kong as defined by the ordinance itself."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a44f4fabcd33aba35991913cf5f1f2da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;U.K.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text discusses contracts involving places of business in different countries, including Hong Kong and U.K., indicating potential legal interactions between them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8271f6bc492f9ae5ef71b7e98a92bd06</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;EXEMPTED SUPPLY CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Exempted supply contracts can involve places of business in Hong Kong and other countries, indicating a legal relationship between the two."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8271f6bc492f9ae5ef71b7e98a92bd06</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;SUPPLY CONTRACTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Supply contracts can involve places outside Hong Kong and may include delivery to or from Hong Kong, indicating a relationship between the two entities in terms of legal interactions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8271f6bc492f9ae5ef71b7e98a92bd06</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;OFFER AND ACCEPTANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Offer and Acceptance can be constituted in or outside of HONG KONG, depending on the context described in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-057148e20c6e00b2ee6dee748e6c75ff</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;CHOICE OF LAW CLAUSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text discusses how the law of Hong Kong can be chosen as the proper law for a contract, indicating its relevance to choice of law clauses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-70bc29e417a48ee998a460c753e36328</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;18. 其他有關法例的保留條文&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text specifically mentions that certain contract clauses are preserved by laws applicable in Hong Kong, highlighting its relevance to legal provisions within this section."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-70bc29e417a48ee998a460c753e36328</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSIONER FOR LABOUR, HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner for Labour oversees and enforces compliance with labor conditions by contractors."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f19199388ebb0416790d9140af888a4f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPEOPLE&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maintenance Surveyors issue passes for workpeople and ensure their compliance with site regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f19199388ebb0416790d9140af888a4f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPEOPLE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contractors employ workpeople to carry out the works as per the contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f19199388ebb0416790d9140af888a4f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (B)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sub-clause B outlines the Contractor’s obligation to assist in conducting necessary tests and provide samples as required by surveyors."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (C)&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sub-clause C defines responsibilities of the Maintenance Surveyor regarding testing, including costs and further actions if requirements are not met."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE [GCCBWT] 45&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sub-clause GCCBWT 45 ensures that the Contractor allows access by surveyors to all relevant areas of work, including workshops and storage places for materials supplied."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 46 (1)&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clause 46(1) outlines the requirement for the Contractor to allow the Maintenance Surveyor or his representative access and opportunity to examine work before covering it up."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 47 (2)&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clause 47(2) mandates that the Contractor must notify the Maintenance Surveyor for examination of work, ensuring his representative's timely presence when necessary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS COMPLETION TIME&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is responsible for completing Works within specified times, as stated in Works Orders or a reasonable time if not stated."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS COMPLETION TIME&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer sets expectations for Works completion times through issued Works Orders, impacting the Contractor’s schedule."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NORMAL WORKING HOURS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR is restricted from working outside NORMAL WORKING HOURS without permission, except in emergencies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS WORKING&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR can order CONTINUOUS WORKING at any time of the day or night."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXTENSION OF TIME FOR COMPLETION&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR may be granted EXTENSIONS OF TIME for COMPLETION if delays are reported to the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR within 42 days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXTENSION OF TIME FOR COMPLETION&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has the authority to grant or deny EXTENSIONS OF TIME for COMPLETION based on reported delays."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCLEMENT WEATHER CONDITIONS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Inclement weather conditions can be cited by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR as a cause for delay in work progress."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STORM SIGNAL NO. 8 OR ABOVE&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The presence of storm signal no. 8 or above can be cited by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR as a cause for delay in work progress."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 5, CLAUSE 63, CLAUSE 57 (2) (A) TO (D), CLAUSE 63&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clauses can be cited by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR as a cause for delay in work progress."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UTILITY UNDERTAKING, DULY CONSTITUTED AUTHORITY&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Utility undertakings or other authorities can be cited by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR as a cause for delay in work progress if they fail to commence or carry out their duties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE, PORTION OF SITE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SITE and its portions are where the CONTRACTOR must complete the WORKS ORDER tasks, and delays can be caused by lack of occupation as per MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR instructions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 57 (2)(A) TO (D)&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor uses Clause 57 (2)(A) to (D) as a basis for determining whether the Contractor is entitled to an extension of time due to certain circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f5f6be589350c8e73f0a57d60397f9eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR (CLAUSE)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clause within MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR requires CONTRACTOR to provide detailed information about delays and progress in writing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-671cf14fabde451a853f4cb49e6a812f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE OFFICES&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR is responsible for maintaining SITE OFFICES until all outstanding work is completed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0c2d16f0534b8f7a9f0c286e3e24591</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE OFFICES&quot;" target="&quot;CONSTRUCTION WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Construction includes the building and maintenance of site offices as an integral or ancillary part of a specified structure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8e519122ccc2d577ad6723a71d0f9b7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE OFFICES&quot;" target="&quot;UTILITIES AND SERVICES INSTALLATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Site offices can be used for managing various aspects of a project, including utilities installation but are not directly related in terms of their primary function."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8e519122ccc2d577ad6723a71d0f9b7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE OFFICES&quot;" target="&quot;TUNNELLING AND BORING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both Tunnelling and boring are involved in the construction of site offices, which includes their maintenance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-daaffb786a24be963871c47c40b85efb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUSPENSION ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;SUSPENSION LASTING MORE THAN 90 DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Suspension Order that lasts more than 90 days can have significant financial implications for the Contractor, potentially leading to additional expenditure claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 59(2)&quot;" target="&quot;GROUND REINSTATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clause 59(2) excludes certain works related to ground reinstatement from being considered in Certificates of Completion."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY REINSTATEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER is responsible for any damage or injury arising from the CONTRACTOR's failure to comply with obligations related to temporary reinstatements during the MAINTENANCE PERIOD."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERMANENT REINSTATEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"At the end of the MAINTENANCE PERIOD, if permanent reinstatement is required by an authority or other party, the CONTRACTOR must ensure temporary reinstatements are made good until such time."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERMANENT REINSTATEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR advises on when permanent reinstatement should be carried out by the appropriate authority or another party, rather than the CONTRACTOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFECT, IMPERFECTION OR FAULT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR is responsible for investigating and rectifying any DEFECTS, IMPERFECTIONS, or FAULTS in the work they perform under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c58277d66887ed610fbaec73a4e8d85b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VARIATION ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR must comply with any Variation Order issued by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR and is responsible for executing such changes at their own expense."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-62865738eafa658463c1c26212a98b20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFICATION OR SCHEDULE OF RATES&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Specification or Schedule of Rates provides the baseline for rates that can be varied through orders from the Maintenance Surveyor, and any variations must be agreed upon based on these documents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d72604c877ec1b265cace0cc38e4690d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFICATION OR SCHEDULE OF RATES&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor uses the Specification or Schedule of Rates as a reference for work and materials, especially when variations are made from these documents to determine new rates through agreement with the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d72604c877ec1b265cace0cc38e4690d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VARIATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is responsible for executing work as per variation orders issued by the Maintenance Surveyor, which may include additions, omissions, substitutions, or alterations in quality and form of work specified in the Schedule of Rates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d72604c877ec1b265cace0cc38e4690d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DAYWORK BASIS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor can order works to be carried out on a daywork basis, determining payment rates which must be agreed upon with the Contractor or set by the surveyor if not already included in the contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d72604c877ec1b265cace0cc38e4690d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DRAWINGS, SPECIFICATION, DETAILS OR LEVELS FROM THE MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor needs instructions from the Maintenance Surveyor regarding necessary drawings and specifications to proceed with work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DRAWINGS, SPECIFICATION, DETAILS OR LEVELS FROM THE MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"These documents guide contractors on how to perform their tasks accurately as per project requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S OPINION ON REIMBURSEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor has discretion in determining if and how expenditures should be reimbursed, impacting financial claims under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISTURBANCE OF THE PROGRESS OF THE WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;WRITTEN APPLICATION BY THE CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor can apply to the Maintenance Surveyor for reimbursement if progress is disturbed due to specific reasons outlined in the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTOR’S PROPOSED DAYWORK ACTIVITIES&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor verifies proposed daywork activities to ensure they align with project requirements and contractual obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REIMBURSEMENT OF EXPENDITURES&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor can apply for reimbursement based on daywork activities and other specific conditions outlined in the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT 51&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Works Order modifications are based on Contract 51 provisions for work execution timeline adjustments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT 51&quot;" target="&quot;UTILITY UNDERTAKING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Utility undertakings not engaged by Employer can cause delays affecting Works completion timeline as per Contract 51."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT 51&quot;" target="&quot;INGRESS/EGRESS CHANGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Changes to ingress or egress can affect work execution timeline as per Contract 51 provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM NOTICE PERIOD (28 DAYS)&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor must be notified within the claim notice period if a Contractor intends to claim additional payment or higher rates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM NOTICE PERIOD (28 DAYS)&quot;" target="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (2) CLAUSE 64, SUB-CLAUSE (2) CLAUSE 65&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sub-clauses of Clauses 64 and 65 specify the notice period for claims regarding higher rates or additional payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM NOTICE PERIOD (28 DAYS)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTUAL CLAIMS PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contractual claims procedure includes notice periods for claiming additional payments or higher rates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM NOTICE PERIOD (28 DAYS)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTUAL CLAIM HANDLING PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contractual claim handling procedures include notice periods for claims regarding additional payments and higher rates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DRAWINGS, SPECIFICATIONS, DETAILS OR LEVELS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"These documents provide guidance on how the Contractor should perform their tasks accurately."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INGRESS/EGRESS CHANGES&quot;" target="&quot;WORK INGRESS/EGRESS MODIFICATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Work ingress or egress modifications can affect changes to ingress or egress as per contract conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT, SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIM PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"General and Special Conditions of Contract govern the claim process including notice periods and documentation requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTEMPORARY RECORDS&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIM DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contemporary records are necessary to support any claim, as per documentation requirements outlined in the contract conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTEMPORARY RECORDS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contemporary records are kept by the Contractor to support claims, which must be reviewed and approved by the Maintenance Surveyor for accuracy."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM PROCESS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTUAL OBLIGATIONS AND PROVISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contractual obligations and provisions define the claim process, including notice periods and documentation requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM PROCESS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTUAL OBLIGATIONS AND RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contractual obligations and rights govern the claim process, including notice periods and documentation requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UTILITY UNDERTAKING NOT ENGAGED BY EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;WORK METHODOLOGY CHANGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Utility undertakings not engaged by Employer can cause changes in work methodology affecting project execution."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS COMPLETION TIMELINE&quot;" target="&quot;MATERIAL DELIVERY DELAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Material delivery delays can affect Works completion timeline as per contract conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS COMPLETION TIMELINE&quot;" target="&quot;WORK EXECUTION TIMELINE ADJUSTMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Work execution timeline adjustments can affect the overall Works completion timeline as per contract conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTUAL CLAIMS PROCEDURE&quot;" target="&quot;WORK EXECUTION IMPACT FACTORS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Impact factors on work execution can trigger the claim procedure as per contract conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORK ORDER MODIFICATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;WORK EXECUTION IMPACT FACTORS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Work order modifications can impact work execution factors such as sequence, method, and timing of construction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTUAL COMPLIANCE&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIM DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Compliance with contractual conditions requires proper documentation for claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIM NOTIFICATION PERIODS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Notification periods for claims require proper documentation to support any claims made by the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT also define claim provisions that apply to specific situations or clauses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has a role in processing and considering CLAIMS from the CONTRACTOR."&lt;SEP&gt;"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has the authority to consider and process CLAIMS from the CONTRACTOR within specified timeframes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM&quot;" target="&quot;COURT ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A claim can lead to a Court Order if an employer fails to comply with certain subsections."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a2e37a06f23a289862428e2457ce5863</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM&quot;" target="&quot;REASONABLE EXCUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of reasonable excuse is relevant in determining whether an employer's failure to comply constitutes an offense."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a2e37a06f23a289862428e2457ce5863</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM&quot;" target="&quot;RIGHT TO SUE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The right to sue is directly related to claims, which are a key aspect in employment protection laws and practices."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1edc8d1eae523643c8ff13994558a8c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration tribunal may make a decision or order regarding claims, and can dismiss a claim due to unreasonable delay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-854d00c33e69aed0258675abc1e2d264</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM&quot;" target="&quot;REASONABLE DELAY IN PURSUING CLAIMS IN ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A claim may be dismissed if there is a reasonable delay in pursuing it, which could lead to unfair resolution of issues or serious prejudice to other parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-854d00c33e69aed0258675abc1e2d264</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSTANTIAL RISK TO FAIR RESOLUTION OF ISSUES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Unreasonable delay can give rise to substantial risk that the claim's issues will not be resolved fairly, affecting the fairness and resolution of disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-854d00c33e69aed0258675abc1e2d264</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM&quot;" target="&quot;SERIOUS PREJUDICE TO ANY OTHER PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A reasonable delay in pursuing a claim may cause serious prejudice to other parties involved in the dispute."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-854d00c33e69aed0258675abc1e2d264</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition of arbitration includes the freedom for parties to determine a claim, which is relevant when considering counter-claims as well."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c4488b1327869fe2b0410a202e25b48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Courts are bodies of the judicial system and can be involved in handling claims as per Article 2(c)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c4488b1327869fe2b0410a202e25b48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR may instruct on NOTICE requirements and record-keeping for CLAIMS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Occupational Safety Officer is responsible for receiving and handling notices regarding workplace accidents and occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers must issue notices regarding workplace accidents to Occupational Safety Officers within 24 hours after they occur."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;RESPONSIBLE PERSON&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Responsible Person must exhibit notices as required by Occupational Safety Officer at the Workplace."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-58cf55b6baed9ac9a3c4052538486aa3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;DISPLAY PERIOD REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Notices must be displayed for at least 12 months unless otherwise specified by Occupational Safety Officer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-58cf55b6baed9ac9a3c4052538486aa3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"EMPLOYEES are entitled to receive notices from SMALL CLAIMS TRIBUNAL FOR WAGES regarding wage claims."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EMPLOYEE must receive and act upon NOTICE within 14 days, serving copies to relevant parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-14526d01cdd531d1142f16c1d5e43367&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f7e01a5307e145a0563e90666073bf5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;SMALL CLAIMS TRIBUNAL FOR WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"NOTICES from SMALL CLAIMS TRIBUNAL FOR WAGES are used to inform parties of wage claims and legal actions regarding unpaid wages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1f7e01a5307e145a0563e90666073bf5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Notices serve as the formal mechanism for requesting wages from employers under the law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af77be8b003511c35b7551f4285bb427</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTROL OF EXEMPTION CLAUSES ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ordinance provides context for understanding notices in legal documents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e6f1b0342117fba0657cd9deb544e402</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT TERM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contract terms and notices in guarantees do not affect the exclusion or limitation of liability for certain losses due to defects during consumer use."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2333b3d2deec0b227d514b0090b44838</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;LOSS OR DAMAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Notices within or operating by reference to guarantees cannot exclude liability for loss or damage arising from defects while goods are being used by consumers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2333b3d2deec0b227d514b0090b44838</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RECORDS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR is responsible for maintaining RECORDS to support any claims made under the contract clauses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FIRST INTERIM ACCOUNT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR receives a FIRST INTERIM ACCOUNT from the CONTRACTOR detailing the sum claimed and grounds for it."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FURTHER UP-TO-DATE ACCOUNTS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR provides FURTHER UP-TO-DATE ACCOUNTS to update claims as necessary, per MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR's instructions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FURTHER UP-TO-DATE ACCOUNTS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Further up-to-date accounts detailing accumulated totals of claims need approval from the Maintenance Surveyor to ensure they are accurate."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR(S)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer can make direct payments to Nominated Sub-contractors if certain conditions are met, establishing a financial and legal connection between them."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employer has the right to order work or materials from Nominated Sub-contractors and can instruct the Contractor to enter into subcontracts with them using specific forms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR(S)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor has obligations towards Nominated Sub-contractors that can be assigned by the Employer after the Maintenance Period, suggesting a contractual and operational connection."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contractor is required to enter into a sub-contract with the Nominated Sub-contractor as instructed by the Maintenance Surveyor, and must use the standard form of sub-contract provided by the Employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR (CLAUSE 69)&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor has significant supervisory roles in the project, including instructing contractors on sub-contracts with different terms from standard forms and making decisions that impact payment and project continuation."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STANDARD FORM OF SUB-CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor can instruct the Contractor to enter into a sub-contract with different terms from those specified in the Standard Form, affecting how obligations are discharged under the Contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S INSTRUCTION&quot;" target="&quot;SUB-CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maintenance Surveyor's Instruction can lead to entering into a sub-contract with a Nominated Sub-contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUB-CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S INSTRUCTION UNDER CLAUSE 68(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maintenance Surveyor's Instruction under Clause 68(2) can result in a sub-contract being entered into with a Nominated Sub-contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUB-CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S INSTRUCTION UNDER CLAUSE 69(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maintenance Surveyor's Instruction under Clause 69(2) can lead to the Contractor entering into a sub-contract with a Nominated Sub-contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUB-CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;HIRE OR HIRE-PURCHASE AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sub-contractors may be involved in hire or hire-purchase agreements for constructional plant usage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTOR'S OBJECTION&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor may raise objections against the nomination of a Nominated Sub-contractor, which must be addressed by the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;QUOTATIONS, INVOICES, VOUCHERS AND RECEIPTS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is required to provide these documents related to expenditure in respect of Nominated Sub-contractors as instructed by the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;QUOTATIONS, INVOICES, VOUCHERS AND RECEIPTS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"These documents provide financial details related to expenditures in respect of Nominated Sub-contractors and require the Maintenance Surveyor's approval for payment."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTORS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is responsible for paying Nominated Sub-contractors as directed by Maintenance Surveyor certificates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1373b3be58ae445e60a533999b71823</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTORS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Certificates issued by the Maintenance Surveyor determine payments due to Nominated Sub-contractors."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1373b3be58ae445e60a533999b71823</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTORS&quot;" target="&quot;MAIN NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The main nominated sub-contractor contracts work with other nominated sub-contractors, who employ employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-79b86e6b5d2c9cc7cc776e8be6a979bb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The certificate issued by the Maintenance Surveyor certifies payments due, impacting financial claims under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT AND TEMPORARY BUILDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor owns constructional plant and temporary buildings that vest in the Employer upon site arrival, showing an ownership transfer during project execution."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT AND TEMPORARY BUILDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Constructional Plant and Temporary Buildings owned by the Contractor become property of the Employer when brought onto the Site, establishing a property rights relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERIALS FOR INCORPORATION IN WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor owns materials for incorporation in works that vest in the Employer upon delivery to the site, indicating an ownership transfer during project execution."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERIALS FOR INCORPORATION IN WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Materials owned by the Contractor become property of the Employer when delivered to the Site and can only be removed with consent or upon surplus determination, showing a property rights relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY BUILDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR is responsible for removing TEMPORARY BUILDINGS from the SITE after COMPLETION unless otherwise specified by CLAUSE 74."&lt;SEP&gt;"The TEMPORARY BUILDINGS are part of the WORKS and their use is subject to agreement with the EMPLOYER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SURPLUS MATERIALS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SURPLUS MATERIALS revert to the ownership of the EMPLOYER, and the CONTRACTOR is responsible for their removal or disposal as per CLAUSE 74."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HIRE OR HIRE-PURCHASE AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Works Order can be linked to hire or hire-purchase agreement for constructional plant use in completing works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOSS OF OR DAMAGE TO CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;" target="&quot;SUBMISSIONS* FOR PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Submissions for payment may include claims related to loss or damage of constructional plant, impacting the cost recovery process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBMISSIONS* FOR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Submissions for payment are subject to checking and correction by the Maintenance Surveyor before being processed."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIMENSION BOOK(S)&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"DIMENSION BOOK(S) are required for each WORKS ORDER, providing necessary details for measurement and valuation of work executed under that order."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-12ff1f20b792fbc8d1bdd961c49e1244</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIMENSION BOOK(S)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR is responsible for supplying DIMENSION BOOK(S), which are set out by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR and must include supporting documents as required."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-77cf568578b8488d566bb45f92f61c0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIMENSION BOOK(S)&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR determines the manner in which DIMENSION BOOK(S) are set out and may require supporting documents for payment claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-77cf568578b8488d566bb45f92f61c0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIMENSION BOOK(S)&quot;" target="&quot;APPENDIX TO THE FORM OF TENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Dimension Books must be submitted as per the schedule set out in the Appendix to the Form of Tender upon substantial completion."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CERTIFICATES FOR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Certificates for payment are based on the completion of WORKS ORDERS, ensuring accurate billing and payments to the CONTRACTOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-12ff1f20b792fbc8d1bdd961c49e1244</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CERTIFICATES FOR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Certificates issued by the Maintenance Surveyor certify the correct value of completed works, impacting payments under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPENDIX TO THE FORM OF TENDER&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Works Orders, sorted by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR according to their claimed value as stated in the APPENDIX TO THE FORM OF TENDER, will be batched for payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-77cf568578b8488d566bb45f92f61c0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS ORDERS&quot;" target="&quot;COMPLAINT CHITS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both Works Orders and Complaint Chits are subject to batched sampling checks by the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8130c8086938f6df2d05cdf9fb7e405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS ORDERS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR is involved in certifying costs for WORKS ORDERS issued to the CONTRACTOR, impacting financial settlements between parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS ORDERS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The WORKS ORDERS issued prior to re-entry may affect the payment due to the CONTRACTOR if completion is delayed, potentially leading to additional payments for excess work or liquidated damages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5e827172d85d4fce202f234f783e044</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPENDIX TO FORM OF TENDER&quot;" target="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Appendix to Form of Tender specifies conditions under which Interim Payments can be made and their maximum percentage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8130c8086938f6df2d05cdf9fb7e405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor has the authority to certify and make interim payments based on work completed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Interim Payments are made in relation to Works Orders exceeding a certain value as specified by the Form of Tender Appendix."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF COMPENSATION ASSESSMENT FOR FATAL CASE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">25.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Interim payments are deducted from the compensation payable under section 6A to the person to whom interim payments have been paid, and also affect the final assessment of compensation for fatal cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interim payments are deducted from the total compensation amount before apportionment according to the Certificate of Compensation Assessment for Fatal Case."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interim payments will cease 7 days before the date compensation under section 6(1) is due in accordance with a Certificate of Compensation Assessment for Fatal Case, as per subsection (7)(a)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9a6dfc79f4a9de7dba162e137dcffd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-330946d46297f253a2618e1b8da8fb4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0a0053e7177c68e160847406a3692d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 6B(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 6B(1) relates to the application for interim payments, specifically mentioning spouses as recipients of such payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9a6dfc79f4a9de7dba162e137dcffd4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 7&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Interim payments are deducted from compensation payable under section 7, indicating a relationship in terms of financial adjustments and calculations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9a6dfc79f4a9de7dba162e137dcffd4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 9&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 9 is involved in the calculation or adjustment of interim payments, as it's part of the total amount that cannot exceed 45% after deductions from sections 7, 9, and 13(3)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9a6dfc79f4a9de7dba162e137dcffd4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 13(3)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 13(3) is also part of the total amount that cannot exceed 45% after deductions from sections 7, 9, and 13(3), affecting interim payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9a6dfc79f4a9de7dba162e137dcffd4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 6A&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Interim payments are deducted from compensation payable under section 6A to the person to whom interim payments have been paid."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9a6dfc79f4a9de7dba162e137dcffd4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is required to deduct INTERIM PAYMENTS from the total compensation amount when making final payments based on a Certificate of Compensation Assessment for Fatal Case or Review Certificate of Compensation Assessment for Fatal Case."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer is responsible for making and deducting interim payments as per the specified conditions in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9a6dfc79f4a9de7dba162e137dcffd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f817e1f2a5b13a0586c36573c6eea5b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT PERIOD EXPIRY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Interim Payments are subject to surcharge calculation upon the Expiry of the Payment Period, indicating a direct relationship between these two entities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d03bb282f99bcf0993cd32ec58e1edb6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF INTERIM PAYMENT OR REVIEW CERTIFICATE OF INTERIM PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The INTERIM PAYMENTS are related to the payments made under a Certificate of Interim Payment or Review Certificate of Interim Payment, which is distinct from the main compensation assessment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f817e1f2a5b13a0586c36573c6eea5b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORM OF TENDER&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Works Orders are referenced within the Form of Tender, particularly regarding payment thresholds and values."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 79A&quot;" target="&quot;CLAUSE 80A&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clause 79A determines applicability of Clause 80A for claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-affc5866b16d32a569c7ab46b9093e2a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 79B&quot;" target="&quot;CLAUSE 80B&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clause 79B determines applicability of Clause 80B for claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-affc5866b16d32a569c7ab46b9093e2a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG SUPREME COURT&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT ON CERTIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Hong Kong Supreme Court's Rules determine interest rates and payment procedures in case of overpayment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-affc5866b16d32a569c7ab46b9093e2a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE LAWS OF HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Laws of Hong Kong define the rights and obligations of the Employer, including their power to deduct payments from the Contractor for overpayment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE LAWS OF HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Laws of Hong Kong outline the responsibilities and protections afforded to the Contractor in terms of payment and work approval."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENT CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer can issue an Interim Payment Certificate which may be corrected or modified by the Maintenance Surveyor and is not deemed to constitute approval of work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENT CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An Interim Payment Certificate is issued in relation to a Works Order under the Contract but does not constitute approval of work or protect the Contractor from over-measurement or overpayment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 49&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CLAUSE 49 defines conditions under which the EMPLOYER can take action against the CONTRACTOR regarding commencement of works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 48&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CLAUSE 48 outlines actions by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR that can lead to consequences for the CONTRACTOR if not followed properly."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 48&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR certifies work completion for payment under CLAUSE 48 regarding permanent work condemnation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d02dce26d755dbc2a1f010f8cd0550db</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 48&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIAL RISKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Special risks affect the interpretation and application of CLAUSE 48, particularly concerning permanent work condemnation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d02dce26d755dbc2a1f010f8cd0550db</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 72 AND 73&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Under CLAUSE 72 AND 73, unused or partially used MATERIALS become property of the EMPLOYER if the CONTRACTOR is expelled from the SITE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 62&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The provisions of CLAUSE 62 apply for attendance by the CONTRACTOR for measurement and agreement of records, which are relevant to their obligations under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 62&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CLAUSE 62 provides rights and procedures for the EMPLOYER in relation to measurements and agreements with the CONTRACTOR regarding work completion."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERIALS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR may have agreements or contracts related to MATERIALS that are subject to assignment as per CLAUSE 59."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERIALS&quot;" target="&quot;PERCUSSIVE PILING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Materials are used in connection with or for any operation referred to in paragraph (a), including percussive piling."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ead066fe98080d41598700f44491db70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERIALS&quot;" target="&quot;PILE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Materials are used in connection with or for the sinking or forming of a pile in the ground by various means including hammering and jacking."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ead066fe98080d41598700f44491db70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERIALS&quot;" target="&quot;PILING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Materials are used in connection with or for various piling operations including driving piles into the ground using different methods such as hammering and jacking."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ead066fe98080d41598700f44491db70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERIALS&quot;" target="&quot;INTRUDER ALARM SYSTEM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Materials are used for installing and maintaining an intruder alarm system, which is part of security operations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ead066fe98080d41598700f44491db70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERIALS&quot;" target="&quot;DESIGNATED AREA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Materials are used in various activities taking place in a designated area, including piling or other ground works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ead066fe98080d41598700f44491db70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERIALS&quot;" target="&quot;FUNCTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Materials are used in the execution of various functions such as operations referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ead066fe98080d41598700f44491db70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKMEN&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The WORKMEN, employed by the EMPLOYER, will complete works after the removal of the CONTRACTOR and their costs must be accounted for before payment can be made to the CONTRACTOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKMEN&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR can authorize WORKMEN from other contractors to carry out necessary works if the CONTRACTOR fails to comply with instructions within a reasonable time."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5e827172d85d4fce202f234f783e044</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 59&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CLAUSE 59 defines conditions for assigning agreements or contracts, impacting the financial obligations of the CONTRACTOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 59&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CLAUSE 59 outlines conditions under which the EMPLOYER may require assignment of agreements, impacting financial obligations and payment terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 59&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR plays a role in certifying costs and expenses related to work carried out under CLAUSE 59, impacting financial settlements between the CONTRACTOR and EMPLOYER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE PERIODS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE PERIODS are relevant to determining when payments can be made to the CONTRACTOR after their removal from a project site."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE PERIODS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE PERIODS are critical for determining when payments can be made to the CONTRACTOR after their removal from a project site, as defined by the EMPLOYER's obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIAL RISKS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is required to use best endeavours to complete execution of works during certain specified 'special risks' events. The Employer can terminate the contract in such cases but must pay for completed work and preliminary items."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d995518579c80996691b5d1b66c19ea3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIAL RISKS&quot;" target="&quot;CLAUSE 72&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The occurrence of special risks impacts how property is deemed to be of the EMPLOYER under CLAUSE 72 for claims and indemnification purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d02dce26d755dbc2a1f010f8cd0550db</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIAL RISKS&quot;" target="&quot;WAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Special Risks include events such as war that can cause destruction or damage, leading to disputes between EMPLOYER and CONTRACTOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5fa9c6366e076e445101d83858797035</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 72&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR also plays a role in determining the property deemed to be of the EMPLOYER under CLAUSE 72 for claims and indemnification purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d02dce26d755dbc2a1f010f8cd0550db</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAR&quot;" target="&quot;DISPUTE SETTLEMENT MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Dispute Settlement Mechanisms are invoked in cases of WAR and other special risks, providing a framework for resolving conflicts between EMPLOYER and CONTRACTOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5fa9c6366e076e445101d83858797035</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISPUTE SETTLEMENT MECHANISM&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT TERMINATION/BREACH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"In the event of contract termination or breach due to special risks like WAR, DISPUTE SETTLEMENT MECHANISMS are used for resolution between EMPLOYER and CONTRACTOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5fa9c6366e076e445101d83858797035</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISPUTE SETTLEMENT MECHANISM&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor resolves conflicts between the Employer and Contractor through written decisions, ensuring project continuity."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S DECISION&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT TERMINATION/BREACH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR's decisions can lead to contract termination or breach, affecting the DISPUTE SETTLEMENT MECHANISM."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5fa9c6366e076e445101d83858797035</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S DECISION&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Decisions made by the Maintenance Surveyor are binding and impact payment and project continuation."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Any dispute involving the CONTRACTOR and MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR can be referred to an ARBITRATOR for resolution under the Lands and Works Model Arbitration Rules."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR's decisions in disputes with the CONTRACTOR can be challenged through arbitration, as per Clause 93(2)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor may be involved in disputes or differences, with an Arbitrator hearing evidence from witnesses including the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;LANDS AND WORKS MODEL ARBITRATION RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Lands and Works Model Arbitration Rules govern how arbitrations are conducted in disputes involving the CONTRACTOR and MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Disputes involving the EMPLOYER can be referred to an ARBITRATOR, as per Clause 94(1)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL can include one or more arbitrators, including an umpire."&lt;SEP&gt;"An arbitrator is a member of the arbitral tribunal, which can be either sole or composed of multiple members."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af79dae94b8a0756fefbbf0f811ebd51</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ARBITRATION involves arbitrators who make decisions in disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitrator conducts the arbitration process and resolves disputes between parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af79dae94b8a0756fefbbf0f811ebd51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSION (貿法委)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Commission may provide guidelines and rules for arbitrators to follow."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitration agreement involves arbitrators who will resolve disputes between parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"An arbitrator is appointed to resolve disputes under an arbitration agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">23.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties are involved in the process where an arbitrator is appointed or challenged based on grounds of impartiality and independence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parties can freely agree on arbitrator(s), and if no agreement is reached, courts or other institutions may intervene to make such appointments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The parties have the right to challenge an arbitrator for grounds that give rise to justifiable doubts about their impartiality or independence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0165ce281c7667854e6df58da6d1a76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-963f917b5a00c96d5b43bd1832480a19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;JUSTIFIABLE DOUBTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitrator must disclose any circumstances that could give rise to justifiable doubts about their impartiality or independence, ensuring transparency and trust in the arbitration process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;IMPARTIALITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of impartiality is central to an arbitrator's role and must be maintained throughout the arbitral process, as any doubts can lead to challenges by parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;INDEPENDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Independence is another key aspect of an arbitrator's role that needs to be disclosed and upheld; failure in this area could result in a challenge from the parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;THE COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Court has authority over arbitrators, including the power to set aside an award if a challenged arbitrator is upheld."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;COURT DECISIONS ON ARBITRATOR CHALLENGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Court decisions on arbitrator challenges can lead to the termination of an arbitrator's mandate or set aside their award if challenged successfully."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">31.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitrator's decision is part of the award that can be challenged or set aside by the Court under certain circumstances as per UNCITRAL Model Law Article 14."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ARBITRATOR is responsible for making the AWARD based on the arbitration process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63fa361a4bbae312d93826ee30bf2182</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 14 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 14 of the UNCITRAL Model Law provides rules for situations where an arbitrator may be unable to act or has been challenged, potentially leading to their mandate termination and award set-aside."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 14&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 14 outlines conditions under which an arbitrator’s mandate can terminate due to inability or failure to act promptly, impacting their role directly."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea943fe3338aa88e6573bf715e772abd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 15 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 15 addresses the appointment of a substitute arbitrator when the original one’s mandate terminates, directly affecting the arbitrator's position and responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea943fe3338aa88e6573bf715e772abd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC ADJUDICATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Public Adjudicator and Arbitrator roles are related in that the former can take on some of the functions of an arbitrator, especially when arbitration members cannot agree."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5d58ad3e1c6ef21463d303a3e0c4d6ff</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ORIGINAL COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Original Court can intervene in arbitration procedures, particularly when arbitrators cannot reach an agreement, through appointing or being notified of decisions made by Public Adjudicators."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5d58ad3e1c6ef21463d303a3e0c4d6ff</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;MEDIATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">23.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitrator can act as a mediator and must stay arbitral proceedings to facilitate mediation proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"An arbitrator can act as a mediator, and mediation proceedings must be stayed when the arbitrator acts in this capacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"An arbitrator may be appointed from a mediator in mediation proceedings, should no settlement acceptable to parties be reached."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4a820d49f72ef3eeb5be9d057a9cb248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dd6cc93acdd87603565c28f0e5d9386&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da3d7a01706de39cd849092deef8b9b1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitrator is involved in arbitral proceedings which may be suspended if they also act as mediators."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS require the appointment of an ARBITRATOR by the COURT or through mutual agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4a820d49f72ef3eeb5be9d057a9cb248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff2369343594485564382d2d30ba3755</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitrator who acts as a mediator is required to handle and treat any confidential information obtained from one party as such, ensuring confidentiality."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitrators handling confidential information during mediation must disclose it before resuming arbitral proceedings if no settlement is reached."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4a820d49f72ef3eeb5be9d057a9cb248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da3d7a01706de39cd849092deef8b9b1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT has the power to order recovery of fees from an ARBITRATOR under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-367745ea1d4a071f6e58849b6c7523ab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL MODEL LAW provides grounds for the termination of an ARBITRATOR's mandate, which can lead to fee-related orders by the COURT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-367745ea1d4a071f6e58849b6c7523ab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;THE ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Arbitration Tribunal has authority over arbitrators, including their remuneration and expenses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e105b81cb8e7429af8bdd848fcb41de5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 54(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 54(1) appoints an arbitrator who is to be treated as fees and expenses of the arbitral tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7aaf6f770f217f1e2eb977b5ec34ad19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 54(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 54(2) also appoints assessors, which are considered part of the arbitration process for appeal or review."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7aaf6f770f217f1e2eb977b5ec34ad19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 26 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 26 of the UNCITRAL Model Law is relevant to the appointment of an arbitrator."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7aaf6f770f217f1e2eb977b5ec34ad19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;法院&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"法院在特定情况下可命令提供保证以应对仲裁程序中的不当行为或通知问题。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-38b4dba8dcefb2d368c753859f749fd1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OR OTHER INSTITUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Courts or other institutions have the authority to appoint arbitrators when parties fail to agree on one."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0165ce281c7667854e6df58da6d1a76</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitrator should disclose any circumstances likely to raise questions of impartiality or independence during the arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-963f917b5a00c96d5b43bd1832480a19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A PARTY may request a decision from the ARBITRATOR or COURT OR OTHER INSTITUTION about the termination of the arbitrator’s mandate if there is controversy."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-98d869f809c494e89028b24de4ba24f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;MANDATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MANDATE of an ARBITRATOR can be terminated due to various reasons, including inability to act or resignation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-98d869f809c494e89028b24de4ba24f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;LITIGATION COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The LITIGATION COURT has the authority to appoint an ARBITRATOR for certain arbitration procedures if parties cannot agree on a choice of arbitrator."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ff2369343594485564382d2d30ba3755</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Works Order can be referred to arbitration if either party is dissatisfied with a Maintenance Surveyor's decision, subject to the provisions of the Arbitration Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-522c43aa0cb7d424d1da1c5b00c65777</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;609&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRATION ORDINANCE is codified under Cap 609."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4f6f1173170ce4ac811fedab280f3b4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 79 AND CLAUSE 81&quot;" target="&quot;NOTICE PERIOD (14 DAYS)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clauses 79 and 81 specify conditions for payment that trigger a Notice Period of 14 days if not met by the Employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3df24d7cf0a0114d43ffbcf5d5c71fd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 79 AND CLAUSE 81&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Failure to pay as per Clauses 79 and 81 within the specified period allows for Contract Termination by the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3df24d7cf0a0114d43ffbcf5d5c71fd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE PERIOD (14 DAYS)&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Notice Period of 14 days, if not honored by the Employer, leads to the possibility of Contract Termination by the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3df24d7cf0a0114d43ffbcf5d5c71fd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TERMINATION OF CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;PROBATIONARY EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Probationary employment conditions allow either party to terminate the contract without notice or payment in lieu during the first month, subject to certain provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Termination conditions differ based on whether the employment is probationary or not, affecting the notice period requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f355da3b0eddd390953ffae58fee2099</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">86.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER provides information to the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR through Contract documents which are not to be divulged outside of contract purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employer engages utility undertakings and supplies materials that can affect the progress of works, impacting the Maintenance Surveyor's role."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employer has a role in approving forms of assignment by the Contractor. The Maintenance Surveyor must act with the consent of the Employer for certain actions to be valid."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employer is involved in receiving interim payments certified by the Maintenance Surveyor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR acts on behalf of the EMPLOYER to enforce removal or sale of CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, TEMPORARY BUILDINGS, and SURPLUS MATERIALS."&lt;SEP&gt;"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR advises on work that may be necessary, particularly in cases where permanent reinstatement is required by an authority or other party."&lt;SEP&gt;"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR certifies payments to the CONTRACTOR and passes certificates to the EMPLOYER for final payment approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has discretion to decide who conducts investigations of defects and can instruct the EMPLOYER's own or other contractors for this purpose if needed."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor acts on behalf of both the Employer's interests in overseeing the Works and ensuring proper execution during the Maintenance Period."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor certifies payments due to Nominated Sub-contractors which the Employer must honor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor is distinct from the Employer and serves as a separate point of contact for notices under the Contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor is responsible for evaluating claims made by the Contractor, and these evaluations can affect the Employer's liability."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor's decisions are final and binding upon the Employer unless either party requires arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a5353a0b04268f3f2bf8419dceec4f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c58277d66887ed610fbaec73a4e8d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3df24d7cf0a0114d43ffbcf5d5c71fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fb1308c02d44b7ab0dcb7b386e3c410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d204e5d2ccca14fb7f49bf493cc0bdb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1373b3be58ae445e60a533999b71823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522c43aa0cb7d424d1da1c5b00c65777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ff1f20b792fbc8d1bdd961c49e1244</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT ON CERTIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer makes payments based on certificates issued by the Maintenance Surveyor and may deduct overpayments from future payments or issue demand notes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-affc5866b16d32a569c7ab46b9093e2a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">225.0</data>
  <data key="d5">The CONTRACTOR and EMPLOYER have a comprehensive contractual relationship involving financial, operational, and legal agreements related to construction projects. Both parties are bound by specific obligations defined in their contract, with the EMPLOYER having significant authority over the CONTRACTOR's actions regarding works execution.

Both entities can refer disputes to arbitration if they are dissatisfied with decisions made by a Maintenance Surveyor or if no decision is given within 90 days. The CONTRACTOR and EMPLOYER have financial agreements where payments for completed work, preliminary items, and costs incurred are based on interim payment certificates submitted by the CONTRACTOR.

The EMPLOYER becomes the owner of materials delivered to the site upon completion and has rights over surplus materials after project completion. Conversely, the CONTRACTOR is obligated to complete Works Orders within a prescribed time frame; failure to do so may result in liquidated damages being imposed by the EMPLOYER.

Financial responsibilities are shared between both parties: The EMPLOYER can make payments on behalf of the CONTRACTOR if wages are not paid as required and has the authority to deduct certain amounts from payments due to the CONTRACTOR under various provisions. Additionally, the EMPLOYER indemnifies the CONTRACTOR against special risks while also being potentially liable for claims made by the CONTRACTOR.

The CONTRACTOR is responsible for completing works orders and may face liquidated damages if not completed within the prescribed time frame; they are obligated to submit statements to the EMPLOYER and receive payments based on interim payment certificates. The EMPLOYER has the authority to have work carried out by the CONTRACTOR or directly pay nominated sub-contractors, with rights over plant provision and approval of forms.

The relationship between both parties is governed by clauses that define information exchange, obligations, security deposits for due performance, and potential termination conditions based on special risks. The EMPLOYER can make deductions from payments to the CONTRACTOR if there are overpayments or other causes as defined under Hong Kong laws.</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d02dce26d755dbc2a1f010f8cd0550db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599efa27c5ee543ca385bb3d944e13fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ce0f4a340a17df1f53274ac940867b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d995518579c80996691b5d1b66c19ea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87f722c8522f822c2e90eb078db141b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3df24d7cf0a0114d43ffbcf5d5c71fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522c43aa0cb7d424d1da1c5b00c65777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba22dc0a0fc19429a484bb41c261d34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef86c4247fdecc339b1414a3fdd5966&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f19199388ebb0416790d9140af888a4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-affc5866b16d32a569c7ab46b9093e2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c58277d66887ed610fbaec73a4e8d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1373b3be58ae445e60a533999b71823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-534e9d84651f98c51ccc8c24e68050b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5353a0b04268f3f2bf8419dceec4f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa9c6366e076e445101d83858797035&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5e827172d85d4fce202f234f783e044</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot; (僱員)">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYEE works under a contract of service or apprenticeship with an employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d8a5d1112f976dfc9d2cfe7182bd06d2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;OUTWORKER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The OUTWORKER's work is related to the EMPLOYER through the process of receiving items or materials for processing but no direct relationship with INSURANCE POLICIES is mentioned."&lt;SEP&gt;"The OUTWORKER's work process involves receiving items from employers to be processed at their own premises, which can indirectly relate to the employer-employee dynamic but no direct relationship with insurance policies is mentioned in this text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-700cb0251acd9df09975828a3d0f4f1d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;COHABITEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A COHABITEE's status as a person living with an employee can affect the employer in terms of insurance coverage but no direct relationship is explicitly stated for OUTWORKERS or EARNINGS."&lt;SEP&gt;"A COHABITEE's status as a person living with an employee does not directly relate to the employer in terms of insurance policies or employment, but they are considered employees for certain purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-700cb0251acd9df09975828a3d0f4f1d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;INSURANCE POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">37.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer may become liable to pay sums in respect of injuries to employees, which the insurer must then cover according to the terms of the policy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EMPLOYER's role includes being insured against liability for injuries to employees, including COHABITEES under certain conditions as described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer is liable to pay an amount paid by the insurer that exceeds the policy coverage, as per the terms of the insurance policy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer may be liable to pay amounts paid by the insurer if certain conditions are met, according to the law."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text mentions that where personal injury occurs during employment and involves a COHABITEE who would be an employee under specific conditions, the insurance policy applies as if they were an actual employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a384314fa98b789ae4d76d79c9eae831&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-700cb0251acd9df09975828a3d0f4f1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca74ec0b128bebdd8deb74d88fe33613&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab8247f4347839df18b680f569571c3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;ACCIDENT INSURANCE BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Accident insurance business covers the legal responsibility for injuries to employees during work hours, which involves employers. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7266eb6e2df511d14420717ab492d463</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;DAMAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Damages refer to compensation that can be claimed by injured employees from their employer due to workplace accidents. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7266eb6e2df511d14420717ab492d463</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF APPRENTICESHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer can be involved in the contract of apprenticeship, as it includes individuals who may employ or temporarily lend an apprentice to another party."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-033087b2f1fb0d32b2faddaa41f6e432</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PRINCIPAL CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer might also act as a principal contractor when managing projects involving employees."&lt;SEP&gt;"The principal contractor is involved when an employer is a sub-contractor, and both are required to provide details under certain sections. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-033087b2f1fb0d32b2faddaa41f6e432&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca6a3d09e67d65c6e2efdbaf610d6291</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION FOR INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are legally responsible for compensating employees injured at work according to relevant regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-607a2fda7757f874bbb128bc111c8ee6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;DETERMINATION BY COMMISSIONER OF CLAIMS FOR COMPENSATION IN FATAL CASES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer's consent is required and must be signed to proceed with the claim determination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2914073de37bf0e7df21cb9ca18483a2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">108.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner also involves employers in the determination process of medical expenses under Section 10A through issued certificates."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner also involves in determining the amount of medical expenses to be paid by the employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner can determine claims for funeral and medical attendance expenses with the employer's consent, which is a key part of their interaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner can issue notices to employers requiring them to produce documents for inspection."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner can order an employer to cease making interim payments if satisfied that a determination was based on false or misleading information, as per subsection (6)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner can serve a Suspension Notice on an Employer who is responsible for certain activities or premises."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner can serve an improvement notice on the Employer if they are believed to be in violation of workplace regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner determines reimbursement amounts and sets payment periods for expenses, which are then paid by the Employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner has the authority to consent or issue certificates that affect an employer's ability to terminate contracts of service or apprenticeship."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner has the authority to review determinations made by or objections from employers under Section 6B(1)(a). The Commissioner can confirm, vary, or initiate a review of such determinations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner sends a notice to the Employer advising of the decision regarding compensation claims."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner's approval is necessary for any agreement made under this section to be binding on the Employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner's decision on a claim can be influenced by the Employer's consent or lack thereof, as well as disputes related to familial connections involving the Employee."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employer is required to make interim and monthly payments as determined by the Commissioner."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employer must comply with subsection (4) or (8), failing which they commit an offence and are liable to a fine at level 6. The Commissioner issues certificates that affect the Employer's obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7788fe09e12252d0bb714e4f775b4322&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbcb1ef289ad456f0c48fcfc25edb43d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c974ea5d752dd73a9522c1e2701db94a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04fef0fb53d56f3928c358832b44a6a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eff0ca72356f89bbfc64201ec755179c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68ef0e8f1f38a0c8885d599e4ee4a20e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-330946d46297f253a2618e1b8da8fb4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfb4e2ef783a3573d88736c7ce485115&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bb18157fba38057f130a7b17e656fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a66ccff5f4b1f0435e3a62cb416f252b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aaf035b8724e14296be4849afc0b0d7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d76ba7381f3e95da332b4d2d5206d84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbb962605c6a7e5085bf69519da702fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af832cb4743d5ddf0c8ea32cb2fd5d71</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIM DETERMINATION PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer's consent and actions can affect whether the Claim Determination Process proceeds as well as its outcome."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-eff0ca72356f89bbfc64201ec755179c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SPOUSE OF DECEASED EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer may receive temporary payment from the Commissioner for the Spouse of Deceased Employee based on their application."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04fef0fb53d56f3928c358832b44a6a5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF COMPENSATION ASSESSMENT FOR FATAL CASE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">23.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers can make objections based on the Certificate of Compensation Assessment for Fatal Case, which is issued after a determination under Section 6B(1)(a)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EMPLOYER is responsible for making payments based on the CERTIFICATE OF COMPENSATION ASSESSMENT FOR FATAL CASE."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employer must pay according to the assessment in the Certificate of Compensation Assessment for Fatal Case, which affects interim and monthly payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f817e1f2a5b13a0586c36573c6eea5b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bb18157fba38057f130a7b17e656fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a66ccff5f4b1f0435e3a62cb416f252b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;INITIAL PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is responsible for making both initial and monthly payments under a Certificate of Interim Payment or Review Certificate of Interim Payment, pending any review process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-330946d46297f253a2618e1b8da8fb4b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SIXTH SCHEDULE SHOWN OPPOSITE SECTION 6C(8)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer must pay additional surcharges to the spouse if they fail without reasonable excuse to make interim payments, based on the Sixth Schedule shown opposite section 6C(8)(a), as per subsection (8)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer must pay surcharges based on the Sixth Schedule shown opposite section 6C(8)(a), as per subsection (8)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-330946d46297f253a2618e1b8da8fb4b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SPOUSE NAMED IN THE CERTIFICATE OF INTERIM PAYMENT OR REVIEW CERTIFICATE OF INTERIM PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is responsible for making payments to the spouse named in the certificate of interim payment or review, including initial and monthly payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-330946d46297f253a2618e1b8da8fb4b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPORARY PAYMENT CERTIFICATE OR TEMPORARY REVIEW CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer is required to pay according to the Temporary Payment Certificate or Temporary Review Certificate (as applicable). Failure to do so may result in additional fees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-54b3bbd8ad212745f60d65d18d1915a8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;ANYONE APPOINTED BY THE EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer appoints the anyone appointed by the employer, establishing a relationship of authority and responsibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-089f9cdfce12f678cda7d05b231183ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is responsible for paying according to the compensation certificate after deductions are made."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-089f9cdfce12f678cda7d05b231183ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is responsible for making compensation payments within the specified payment period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf9822f57c8a8c75b294d17dfa49f864</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;REVIEW CERTIFICATE OF COMPENSATION ASSESSMENT FOR FATAL CASE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER must also consider and act upon the REVIEW CERTIFICATE OF COMPENSATION ASSESSMENT FOR FATAL CASE if applicable."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f817e1f2a5b13a0586c36573c6eea5b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SIXTH SCHEDULE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SIXTH SCHEDULE provides details about surcharges that may be applied by the EMPLOYER upon failure to make timely payments as per the CERTIFICATE OF COMPENSATION ASSESSMENT FOR FATAL CASE or REVIEW CERTIFICATE OF COMPENSATION ASSESSMENT FOR FATAL CASE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f817e1f2a5b13a0586c36573c6eea5b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SURCHARGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER must pay a SURCHARGE if they fail to make timely payments as per the CERTIFICATE OF COMPENSATION ASSESSMENT FOR FATAL CASE or REVIEW CERTIFICATE OF COMPENSATION ASSESSMENT FOR FATAL CASE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f817e1f2a5b13a0586c36573c6eea5b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;3 MONTHS AFTER THE EXPIRY OF THE PAYMENT PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER is required to pay an additional surcharge after 3 months if the initial surcharge was not paid within the payment period as per the CERTIFICATE OF COMPENSATION ASSESSMENT FOR FATAL CASE or REVIEW CERTIFICATE OF COMPENSATION ASSESSMENT FOR FATAL CASE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f817e1f2a5b13a0586c36573c6eea5b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;FUNERAL EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"EMPLOYER may have paid FUNERAL EXPENSES and must give written consent for the COMMISSIONER to make a determination regarding these expenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employer is responsible for reimbursing Funeral Expenses as per Commissioner's determinations and schedules."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8b99b710a13a074eee4b0551f5e725be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aaf035b8724e14296be4849afc0b0d7a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;MEDICAL ATTENDANCE EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similar to FUNERAL EXPENSES, EMPLOYER might be responsible for MEDICAL ATTENDANCE EXPENSES and must provide written consent for the COMMISSIONER's determination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8b99b710a13a074eee4b0551f5e725be</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;MEDICAL ATTENDANCE ON THE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer must reimburse Medical Attendance on the Employee, following the Commissioner’s guidelines and schedules."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-aaf035b8724e14296be4849afc0b0d7a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;FUNERAL AND MEDICAL EXPENSES AUDIT CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The FUNERAL AND MEDICAL EXPENSES AUDIT CERTIFICATE can be converted into a court order when applied for by the EMPLOYER, and it includes amounts to be paid as per the certificate."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fa74d0f00f96c28e36e2d2dc5c9e2eda</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PROVINCIAL GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PROVINCIAL GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT oversees and regulates matters related to the FUNERAL AND MEDICAL EXPENSES AUDIT CERTIFICATE, which can be applied for by the EMPLOYER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fa74d0f00f96c28e36e2d2dc5c9e2eda</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;LEVEL 5 FINE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer who fails to provide required particulars or provides false information is liable for a fine at level 5. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca6a3d09e67d65c6e2efdbaf610d6291</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;FUNERAL EXPENSES AND MEDICAL TREATMENT FEES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer may be liable for funeral expenses and medical treatment fees in the case of a deceased employee. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca6a3d09e67d65c6e2efdbaf610d6291</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;INJURED EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">24.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is notified by the injured employee about their attendance as required by the Commissioner or Assessment Board."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer is responsible for the cost of supplying and fitting a prosthesis or surgical appliance to an injured employee as per section 36B."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer must sign an agreement with the injured employee regarding care expenses, which may be approved by the Director and involve compensation over a period not exceeding 2 years."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6e62d63292a05cf6bb5e6be00c591105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0777124042c66cc9558d8401a55e7156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab861803e98b52f9a42ed6d058e8b49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SECRETARY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">11.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER is required to notify the SECRETARY of an employee's death within a specified timeframe."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text does not directly mention any relationship between employer and secretary; however, it implies that an agreement may be signed with the injured employee which could indirectly involve a secretary in administrative tasks."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0777124042c66cc9558d8401a55e7156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86b556980892b37b85caf641b152672a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE REQUIRING ATTENTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer is involved in entering into agreements for the employee's permanent incapacity with the approval of the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-21c14cf842653359f26af3af94b35c1f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PERIODICAL PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is responsible for making periodical payments during incapacity periods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-70e316f848fd5f9f0f6efb5f28f0e45b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">73.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Court may determine the amount of CONTRIBUTION from an EMPLOYEE to an EMPLOYER in case of disagreement over COMPENSATION."&lt;SEP&gt;"COURT has authority over EMPLOYER in making awards for terminal payments if no reinstatement or re-engagement is made."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employers are liable to fines if they contravene the provisions related to claims for compensation in the Court."&lt;SEP&gt;"If an employer fails to pay compensation, it can be recovered by the employee through the COURT as a civil debt either in SMALL CLAIMS TRIBUNAL or DISTRICT COURT."&lt;SEP&gt;"If found not liable, the employer is ordered to receive a refund from the deposit by the court. The court also decides on disputes involving payments and necessary costs for prosthesis or surgical appliance."&lt;SEP&gt;"If the employer disputes his liability, the dispute must be resolved by a court, which can issue appropriate orders regarding the deposited amount."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT can review and decide on applications made by either the EMPLOYER or the EMPLOYEE regarding periodical payments, with certain conditions applied."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT may make orders with respect to repayment of sums where proceedings apply under subsection (3)." "&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT may受理compensation applications even if EMPLOYER did not receive NOTICE OF ACCIDENT in some cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court has the authority to resolve disputes regarding employer liability for prostheses or surgical appliance costs, potentially ordering payments from the employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court's jurisdiction can be submitted by an employer carrying on business outside Hong KONG, affecting the application of this Ordinance to employees within HONG KONG."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3b44850af90a02b11f7716520e896fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f8e345be219d3fc366dc62469796daf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1ed02e78cf2ee9e321f22dbe3ba84b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33fb429edfbad9e4130f4746d5db62bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f5fe723dc66b1a35b256f0fbcfd9642&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6087ed3d45150a001bf9f66572bde4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baa998ea27b6baa036c2807f3cddf020&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72e470440b916fe7d89e88eb4a51cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-338f6b52974bc08baebc662da42c4477</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;MEDICAL EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are liable to pay medical expenses unless certain conditions are met, such as provision of adequate free medical treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employers are responsible for paying the determined amount of medical expenses according to the Commissioner's determination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-150ac34f962a55c7a622046976949d60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbcb1ef289ad456f0c48fcfc25edb43d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SMALL CLAIMS TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Small Claims Tribunal handles disputes over medical expenses where amounts are within its jurisdiction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af55493786feba6de502e98ed832cde8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;DISTRICT COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"District Court deals with larger claims for medical expenses not handled by the Small Claims Tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af55493786feba6de502e98ed832cde8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SMALL CLAIMS TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (CAP. 338)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"This ordinance provides the legal framework for Small Claims Tribunal proceedings involving medical expenses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af55493786feba6de502e98ed832cde8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;DISTRICT COURT ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The District Court Ordinance sets out procedures and jurisdiction for larger claims, including those related to work-related injuries abroad."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af55493786feba6de502e98ed832cde8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;ACCIDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">30.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An Employer experiences or is informed about an Accident that might affect their employee's capacity and requires reporting."&lt;SEP&gt;"An accident can lead to a situation where an employer may apply for changes in periodical payment based on employee incapacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employers are liable for certain medical expenses related to accidents that occur outside Hong Kong, as defined by this ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer is required to report an accident that results in the death of, or total/partial incapacity of, an employee within a specified period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-80bd6fbaafa695488034148c221f9cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f45f6c1c93d50d9cf7dd1bef9a6ec44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d8e006856fc24f02eba931eaf4c63a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea6d20dfaa02a409f86af6c45c243e0a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">19.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Registered Chinese Medicine Practitioner may also be named by the Employer for conducting medical examinations if required."&lt;SEP&gt;"An EMPLOYER is not legally responsible for paying for subsequent doses of medicine based on a prescription unless certain conditions are met. However, if an employee fails to comply with the requirement to provide a prescription and receipt, the employer may no longer be liable for such costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EMPLOYER has the authority to request that an EMPLOYEE undergo a medical examination with a REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER if necessary, and the employer will not bear any costs associated with such treatment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-60357a5d0f946dc1e998d1bea10860b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1faa1664ffe65d577dff74396c2e0ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a9f135881cefdec226e999451dec41e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED DOCTOR/DENTIST&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYER is not legally responsible for paying for medicine based on a prescription issued by a REGISTERED DOCTOR/DENTIST unless certain conditions are met. However, if an employee fails to comply with the requirement to provide a prescription and receipt, the employer may no longer be liable for such costs."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0a9f135881cefdec226e999451dec41e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The accident occurs on the employer's premises or where an employee is working under the employer's supervision."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e5b9b6bd7c435d5501f5beca435a1caa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;NOTICE OF ACCIDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"EMPLOYER is required to receive NOTICE OF ACCIDENT from EMPLOYEE as soon as practicable after an accident occurs, before the employee leaves employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e6087ed3d45150a001bf9f66572bde4b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">38.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are responsible for compensating employees affected by occupational diseases as per the Employment Ordinance 16 of 2006 S. 19, unless there is a refusal in writing to undergo medical examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employers are responsible for providing compensation if they last employed the employee before the occurrence of an occupational disease that leads to loss of work capacity or death."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EMPLOYER is responsible for paying COMPENSATION to the employee in case of personal injury by accident arising out of employment, unless an AGREEMENT reduces or removes this responsibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EMPLOYER is responsible for providing COMPENSATION to the EMPLOYEE, but this right can be temporarily suspended if the employee does not accept a medical examination as required. The compensation may also depend on whether there are reasonable grounds for refusing the examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer may be required to provide compensation for the personal injuries of employees as per legal obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer must notify the Commissioner about accidents even if they do not result in compensation liability to ensure compliance with regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8bab0fa8e650dc6d58da85c05c8bf94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3b44850af90a02b11f7716520e896fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1faa1664ffe65d577dff74396c2e0ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e7d6d62033f777323f252b1d52645d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80bd6fbaafa695488034148c221f9cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1683d49752acaec3491f38a426aac742</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;NOTICE TO EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The notice to the employer is required to be given by the employer when an employee dies under specified circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f922ec3eb4453fd0e3ed3576f92a000e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE DEATH NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The death of an employee must be brought to the attention of the employer within 7 days for proper documentation and potential compensation claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f922ec3eb4453fd0e3ed3576f92a000e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;FAMILY MEMBERS NOTIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If the employer is notified, they are responsible for informing family members about potential compensation rights after an employee's death."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f922ec3eb4453fd0e3ed3576f92a000e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE DEATH NOTIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is required to notify family members of an employee's death and provide information about compensation rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3f3f1d97c7e20d014b257a54d818ab74</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION CLAIM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers can make claims for compensation on behalf of employees if requested by the employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3f3f1d97c7e20d014b257a54d818ab74</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL OBLIGATION TO NOTIFY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are legally obligated to inform family members of an employee's death and provide information about their rights regarding compensation if they fail to do so, they may face fines."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3f3f1d97c7e20d014b257a54d818ab74</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Ordinance defines the rights and responsibilities of the Employer in relation to accident notifications and employee health checks."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ordinance sets the rules for an employer's actions regarding contract termination and notice of termination in specific circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7788fe09e12252d0bb714e4f775b4322&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82b5f0bd8d67dc0cdec98d7b6bf55ef9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;ACCIDENT NOTIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer is required to act within a certain timeframe after receiving an Accident Notification from the Employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-82b5f0bd8d67dc0cdec98d7b6bf55ef9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PRIVATE REGISTERED DOCTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER has the authority to request that an EMPLOYEE undergo a medical examination with their PRIVATE REGISTERED DOCTOR if necessary, and the employer will not bear any costs associated with such treatment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a1faa1664ffe65d577dff74396c2e0ae</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED DENTIST&quot;">
  <data key="d4">11.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similarly, a Registered Dentist can be designated by the Employer to perform necessary dental examinations on Employees as needed."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EMPLOYER has the authority to request that an EMPLOYEE undergo a medical examination with a REGISTERED DENTIST if necessary, and the employer will not bear any costs associated with such treatment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-60357a5d0f946dc1e998d1bea10860b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1faa1664ffe65d577dff74396c2e0ae</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED DOCTOR, REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER, OR REGISTERED DENTIST&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers have the authority to ensure employees receive necessary medical treatment from registered professionals as per regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-41bbb00ceaa0cfa991f173d4f0741862</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION CLAIM FOR EMPLOYEE'S DEATH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers may be involved in compensation claims if an employee dies due to lack of proper treatment or examination as required by law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-41bbb00ceaa0cfa991f173d4f0741862</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;MEDICAL EXAMINATION AND TREATMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer has the right to require an Employee to undergo a medical examination within 7 days after receiving notice of an accident."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-60357a5d0f946dc1e998d1bea10860b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Registered Medical Practitioner may be named by the Employer to conduct examinations of Employees under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer names the registered medical practitioner or Chinese medicine practitioner for conducting medical examinations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-60357a5d0f946dc1e998d1bea10860b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea6b2c9739d4904eac9e0c6be6072cb9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER, REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER OR REGISTERED DENTIST&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer can require an employee to submit themselves for treatment by a registered medical practitioner without expense to the employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3060c6c2405e1ec77fec151e62494218</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;AMENDED 44 OF 1980 S. 15; 16 OF 2006 S. 16&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The amended provisions affect the employer's responsibilities in relation to compensation and injury."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer's role is defined under the amended provisions, affecting their responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3060c6c2405e1ec77fec151e62494218</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is responsible for paying compensation as stated in the certificate issued by the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c5bdac67e9c03ff3905f24c9ae12c304</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;DIRECTOR (處長)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both employer and director are involved in compliance with sections related to compensation payments. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffbe5c02e6f3e1420b13f54196f78358</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;16B. CANCELLATION OF INJURIES CLAIM CERTIFICATE BY THE COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is an applicant who may request the cancellation of a certificate under this section."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2eba7d646d2449192a3db7213315460a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;16CA. DETERMINATION OF COMPENSATION BY AGREEMENT IN CERTAIN CASES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer has the authority to enter into agreements with employees regarding compensation for injuries."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0d861619a56054d36c585396a6494755</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;16CB. CANCELLATION OF AGREEMENTS BY DIRECTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer is one of the parties involved when an agreement is cancelled by the Director."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0d861619a56054d36c585396a6494755</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF SERVICE OR APPRENTICESHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer is bound by the contract of service or apprenticeship with employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0d861619a56054d36c585396a6494755</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF ASSESSMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are recipients of the certificate of assessment, which affects their relationship with employees under assessments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d3ba6e4c8e42988a064ffe8e2ff8f96e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;REVIEW OF ASSESSMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers have the right to object to assessments and trigger a review of assessments by submitting their objection in writing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d3ba6e4c8e42988a064ffe8e2ff8f96e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;OBJECTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An OBJECTOR can also be an EMPLOYER, depending on the context of the objection."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0aa6a1ecbb96f241ec693e9b7796d393</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIAL ASSESSMENT BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Special Assessment Board issues a certificate to the employer after reviewing claims. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da37f195f3ad2a893b50923a13911e53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES OR SALARY IN RESPECT OF SUCH ABSENCE FROM WORK OR THE WAGES OR SALARY HE WOULD HAVE EARNED IF HE HAD WORKED DURING SUCH PERIOD.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is required to pay the employee's wages or salary during a leave of absence for an examination, or what they would have earned if working."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ab861803e98b52f9a42ed6d058e8b49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;FINE AT LEVEL 5&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer who contravenes the requirement to grant leave of absence and pay wages during such period commits an offence and is liable to a fine at level 5."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ab861803e98b52f9a42ed6d058e8b49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIM FOR COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employee may apply for enforcing his claim for compensation against the employer through the court."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d285e5cc0dd5b45c7925c806f32ec724</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTRATION DOCTOR, TRADITIONAL CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER, DENTIST&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is involved in claims that might necessitate the involvement of a registered medical professional to support an application for compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d285e5cc0dd5b45c7925c806f32ec724</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;16 OF 2006 S. 18&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Amendments to section 16 of Ordinance No. 55 of 1969 are made by this provision, affecting the process for ending or diminishing periodical payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea6d20dfaa02a409f86af6c45c243e0a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;THIRD PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both the employer and third party can be liable for compensation, as indicated by the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5264a8fa197e6ad59c59c71f8b3763e7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PLAINTIFF&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer is liable to pay compensation if found responsible in a case brought by the Plaintiff, as per provisions within the Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-71e61f5794135dfe2a1a6e5ae434940c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SEAFARER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SEAFARER is employed by an EMPLOYER who may submit or agree to submit to the jurisdiction of the COURT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-49920e3fc93948bee580896f50d6da6a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;MASTER OF THE SHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MASTER OF THE SHIP can act on behalf of the EMPLOYER in giving notice for accidents occurring on board, especially if the accident and incapacity started while onboard."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-49920e3fc93948bee580896f50d6da6a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL DISEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer's workplace may be the cause of an occupational disease, which can lead to a claim for compensation if it results in loss of work capacity or death."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8bab0fa8e650dc6d58da85c05c8bf94</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PROSTHESIS OR SURGICAL APPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are liable to pay for the cost of supplying and fitting prosthesis or surgical appliance as per regulations set by the BOARD and Director."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer may be responsible for paying costs related to prostheses or surgical appliances provided to employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5980c15d89bdf2ef4857f80a2f6b149c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72e470440b916fe7d89e88eb4a51cf95</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;36B&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 36B outlines the employer's liability in paying for medical treatment costs, including prostheses or surgical appliances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5980c15d89bdf2ef4857f80a2f6b149c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;DIRECTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">31.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The DIRECTOR can make a request for payment of costs related to prosthesis or surgical appliance to the EMPLOYER, who must pay unless there is a dispute."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Director has the authority to enter, inspect, and check places of employment where employees are known or reasonably believed to be working."&lt;SEP&gt;"The director can apply to the court against an employer who fails to pay within the specified period under 36E(1)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer must pay the amount of cost to the Director unless disputes arise, and the Director holds the deposited amount until the dispute is resolved."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-786468d759a9a7b3ea39a79ba530682c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33fb429edfbad9e4130f4746d5db62bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72e470440b916fe7d89e88eb4a51cf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-919e8934f076d1a9c5aea1486aa3f1c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 36E&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER must pay within one month unless there is a dispute over the claim, as per SECTION 36E. If in dispute, they must either pay into an account or notify the reasons for disagreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-786468d759a9a7b3ea39a79ba530682c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;36D REQUEST FOR PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 36D request for payment is sent to the employer, who must either pay within a specified period or dispute it."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-33fb429edfbad9e4130f4746d5db62bd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;36E(1) SPECIFIED PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"This specifies the time limit in which an employer must respond to and possibly pay 36D request for payment. If not paid, disputes may arise."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-33fb429edfbad9e4130f4746d5db62bd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 36M(2)(C)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is responsible for paying the amount assessed by the Board according to SECTION 36M(2)(C). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bdcbcb18d7b9887f495f81165f5fb4fc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Board assesses and determines claims, which are then handled by the employer according to SECTION 36M(2)(C). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bdcbcb18d7b9887f495f81165f5fb4fc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;INSURER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">36.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"In case of excess payment beyond the covered amount under the policy, the insurer can seek reimbursement from the employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer must obtain a policy of insurance from an insurer to cover liabilities as specified in the Fourth Schedule."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer's actions (such as providing false information or committing offenses) can impact the insurer according to the insurance policies."&lt;SEP&gt;"The insurer and employer have a relationship where the employer may be required to pay amounts paid by the insurer, depending on specific legal conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Where an amount is paid by the INSURER, which would not be payable under the policy of insurance but for this section, the EMPLOYER is liable to pay that amount to the INSURER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8df740cc032fb332ff71c24c0e55c9c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09e282cd999f281d4422d40832df059c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9b169ef4b1de04369879d234076f1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a384314fa98b789ae4d76d79c9eae831&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca74ec0b128bebdd8deb74d88fe33613</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;NOTICE OF INSURANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers must display notices as per the requirements set out in policies issued by the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04f9381ba412450dd157e86dc940f7ae</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CHINESE LANGUAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text mentions the employer in relation to Chinese languages and insurance policies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7f9b169ef4b1de04369879d234076f1c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OR TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers may be involved in legal proceedings before courts or tribunals, which can affect their liability for insurance payments under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employer has legal responsibilities that may be adjudicated by the Court or Tribunal in relation to Insurance Policies and Legal Proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ff7a7ad14c10761bcb15431ef57d8f8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a384314fa98b789ae4d76d79c9eae831</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;COURT/TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers and employees can bring claims before a court or tribunal for compensation in cases involving workplace injuries."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ab8247f4347839df18b680f569571c3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;POLICY OF INSURANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer is covered by the policy of insurance, which provides protection for claims related to employment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employers are required to produce policies of insurance as specified in the notice from the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-740adc792b975b3e69e6b1a7c25c776a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfb4e2ef783a3573d88736c7ce485115</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSIDIARY COMPANY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsidiary Company is an employer that can have legal responsibilities towards its employees as stated in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-740adc792b975b3e69e6b1a7c25c776a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;COVER NOTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers may be asked to provide cover notes related to policies of insurance for inspection by the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bfb4e2ef783a3573d88736c7ce485115</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;THE COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner can issue notices to employers requiring them to produce documents and comply with certain requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5ead5337f34ae6c6d3adbc5b06e2bc74</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are required to produce certain documents upon receiving a Commissioner's notice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5ead5337f34ae6c6d3adbc5b06e2bc74</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SUSPENSION NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYER may receive a SUSPENSION NOTICE if workplace practices do not meet regulatory standards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employers may receive suspension notices as part of the process for addressing incidents involving bodily injuries or safety violations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126e18663d810ba6b83365ff30027a71</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;FUNCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers have functions that include hiring and managing employees as well as maintaining premises safely."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7249fad978915b4915d01ecac03019f3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPIER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">27.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An Employer and Occupier can both be the recipients of a Suspension Notice, depending on their roles regarding the premises."&lt;SEP&gt;"An employer can also be considered an occupier of the workplace, depending on their level of control and responsibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"The OCCUPIER includes a person who has any degree of control over PREMISES, which can be an employer in certain contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer may also be considered an occupier of the workplace, thus having responsibilities related to safety and health."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0a0ae0d06f82179e57847e5fde58901&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbb962605c6a7e5085bf69519da702fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3717bfa1a0a429ae82cff6583f9ffc97</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER is designated by the employer to ensure occupational safety and health compliance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Work is defined as work performed by an employee, and the EMPLOYER is responsible for workplace safety and practices."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-126e18663d810ba6b83365ff30027a71</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SELF-EMPLOYED PERSON&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer can also be a self-employed person in certain contexts or scenarios described by this ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3717bfa1a0a429ae82cff6583f9ffc97</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;INDEPENDENT CONTRACTORS AND SELF-EMPLOYED PERSONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Independent contractors and self-employed persons are considered employers in certain capacities under the Ordinance, which affects their responsibilities towards employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cbf739f28af13fb255489857524eaf50</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are related to Workplaces where their employees work and accidents may occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employers have responsibilities towards the safety and health of employees at work locations they control or occupy."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cbf739f28af13fb255489857524eaf50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;REGULATIONS ON EMPLOYEE SAFETY AND HEALTH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers must comply with regulations on employee safety and health to ensure the safety and health at work of their employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9e5937ed8f53f94669beb412edc19a99</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SAFETY AND HEALTH AT WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are responsible for ensuring the safety and health at work of their employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8903577fbeb26a0f144927da3a1efb7c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;OFFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers can commit offences if they contravene specific provisions or fail to comply with certain requirements as outlined in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employers who fail to comply with subsections 1-4 can commit an offence and face penalties as specified."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8903577fbeb26a0f144927da3a1efb7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33a64188afa193f5265ae78f3b8acbe6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEES AT WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees are required to cooperate with the employer for safety and health regulations compliance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0a0ae0d06f82179e57847e5fde58901</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENTS AND OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are required to report workplace accidents and occupational diseases as per the regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers must comply with Occupational Safety Regulations when reporting workplace incidents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers must ensure legal compliance in their reporting of workplace incidents as per the regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE INCIDENT REPORTING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers must follow the Workplace Incident Reporting Guidelines when reporting incidents as per regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY COMPLIANCE PROGRAMS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers must participate in Occupational Safety Compliance Programs as per regulations for managing workplace accidents and occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;FINE LEVEL 4&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers can be fined at level 4 for offenses under this section."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e7881ceecf94346279b299fee8d79193</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;FINE LEVEL 6&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are subject to fines up to level 6 for certain offenses under the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e7881ceecf94346279b299fee8d79193</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CHARGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are liable to commit an offense by imposing or authorizing charges on employees under the statutory requirement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-77530b0513e9222b2220609d22541c30</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;INTIMIDATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Intimidation can be used as a method of preventing aid from being given, which is related to employer's actions towards their employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-77530b0513e9222b2220609d22541c30</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;LOCK-OUT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Lock-out pertains to actions taken by an Employer, specifically regarding workforce management and industrial relations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2a67530e0a9df975682238097b18b864</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Businesses are entities that employ employers who manage their workforce."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2a67530e0a9df975682238097b18b864</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">32.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYER is a party to a CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT who agrees to employ another person as an employee."&lt;SEP&gt;"An employer and an employee are bound by their contract, which can be terminated upon the employee's death as per Part VA."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EMPLOYER and CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT define the terms under which employment is provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer establishes a contract with the employee, which can be terminated by the employer under certain circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-398cf2cb1ea6408a6d67cec4cb083e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a783557f86fea333101af802aa41e0a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2f5d9b3d656df85c08982a8986732f4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT (僱主供款豁免職業退休計劃利益)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYER-funded EXEMPT ORS benefit is a type of employer-provided retirement plan benefit."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (PRESCRIBED PORTION) EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT (僱主供款(訂明部分)豁免職業退休計劃利益)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYER-funded PRESCRIBED PORTION EXEMPT ORS benefit is a specific type of employer-provided retirement plan benefit that qualifies for exemption."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CRIMINAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer can suspend an employee pending criminal proceedings, and such suspension may be extended until these proceedings are concluded."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-098ca6bfb60006d76569bead63917ebd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL BONUS PAYMENT DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER is responsible for determining when annual bonuses will be paid based on the employee's performance and calculated earnings over a specified period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9fff8612fdefb52ed816a2d4502b87bc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTINUOUS CONTRACT EMPLOYEE may receive an END OF YEAR PAYMENT from the EMPLOYER based on terms in their CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-adfd6c1ac1062c58ce3404e61a7b9509</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 11F PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER is responsible for making the SECTION 11F PAYMENT according to the CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-adfd6c1ac1062c58ce3404e61a7b9509</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;BONUS PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer's policies can affect the bonus period during which employees are considered for part-year bonuses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02218e873b9a55b35f3e34874d7090d6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">30.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"EMPLOYER's actions are regulated by laws concerning MATERNITY LEAVE for female employees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employers are required to grant maternity leave according to the regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EMPLOYER is responsible for receiving notices and managing MATERNITY LEAVE according to legal requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer provides Maternity Leave to female employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7d6f22e03ef794b224e1918ddd3fee77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7550fdff3623ae221e2d156f6ce5cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505a565a05fcfbf53c86377d50356a49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;MEDICAL CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER may require a MEDICAL CERTIFICATE from the FEMALE EMPLOYEE for various reasons, including confirming the expected or actual date of confinement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EMPLOYER receives MEDICAL CERTIFICATES from FEMALE EMPLOYEES as part of the process for confirming pregnancies and approving MATERNITY LEAVE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9112f21c7d8a89e9880b92acfce9ecd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505a565a05fcfbf53c86377d50356a49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The FEMALE EMPLOYEE is entitled to maternity leave pay from the EMPLOYER under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The FEMALE EMPLOYEE must notify her EMPLOYER about her intention and date of confinement related to maternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-681c7e69874ff6c2cdf180f0fb0d44f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9112f21c7d8a89e9880b92acfce9ecd6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PAID MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are responsible for providing paid maternity leave to female employees as per the Employment Ordinance (Cap. 27). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">33.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYER is responsible for paying Maternity Leave Pay as per the ordinance and regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"EMPLOYER is responsible for providing MATERNITY LEAVE PAY to the FEMALE EMPLOYEE as per legal requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employers must pay maternity leave pay in accordance with section 14 and as specified by Commissioner."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer is responsible for paying maternity leave pay to the female employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7d6f22e03ef794b224e1918ddd3fee77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78df2b99fcbe4aa2c71fdce1f79d338c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5001d950d1e5de5921648ae860af7539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7550fdff3623ae221e2d156f6ce5cf2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">40.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer is responsible for paying wages to employees including those related to different kinds of leaves."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employers are responsible for paying wages as per labor laws and regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EMPLOYER is responsible for paying WAGES to the EMPLOYEE as per legal restrictions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court may order an employer who is found guilty to pay outstanding wages that are due."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer pays Wages to employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-602a52838c03cef3777006bf2a44b72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-918c0eabaec10917e5775ff91d8fc75a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d93d92eb00cb1e06709b542dad7efdd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07f949d11fd1c1d8a909fd36ccac57d6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employees' Compensation Ordinance governs the compensation of employees, including those related to termination and maternity leave pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4646eb80519916bd0464a8b522d48735</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PREGNANT EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is responsible for the work allocation of a pregnant employee and must accommodate her as per legal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c53400793123be7f8846d77b56748e48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PHYSICIAN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer may arrange for the pregnant employee to undergo a medical examination by a physician, with the cost borne by the employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c53400793123be7f8846d77b56748e48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;DIRECTOR OF THE DEPARTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer may refer cases involving pregnant employees to the Director of the Department for further action, including seeking additional medical opinions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c53400793123be7f8846d77b56748e48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer can terminate employment under certain conditions related to the employee's health status as determined by medical examinations and Commissioner's rulings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea6b2c9739d4904eac9e0c6be6072cb9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are required to provide sickness allowance under certain conditions, though not directly related to maternity leave."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EMPLOYER is responsible for paying SICKNESS ALLOWANCE to the EMPLOYEE as per the regulations mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c7550fdff3623ae221e2d156f6ce5cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c96e8be9052d451fbf9a64ace39448d4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is responsible for paying the employee during paternity leave as per the terms and conditions of employment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer provides Paternity Leave to male employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c54e7deea495212bab465e4af100b7ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;WRITTEN STATEMENT SIGNED BY EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The written statement signed by an employee is provided to the employer for verification purposes regarding paternity."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6320bd8af6a47ec4d774b02d5588447a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;BIRTH CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer requires the birth certificate to verify paternity claims made by employees regarding children born outside of Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6320bd8af6a47ec4d774b02d5588447a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;REQUISITE DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer requires documents from the employee for paternity leave, specifically under 15J or 15K clauses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SERVICE LEAVE COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is responsible for compensating employees who take service leave, including paid parental leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer is required to pay the Paternity Leave Pay as per regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9f8f154dd34baff54c016b669ab2da5c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;LEAVE DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"On the Leave Day, the Employer must pay the Paternity Leave Pay if certain conditions are met."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9f8f154dd34baff54c016b669ab2da5c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 15L&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer must pay Paternity Leave Pay according to Section 15L guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9f8f154dd34baff54c016b669ab2da5c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;MACHINE BREAKDOWN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER may require work on a REST DAY in case of MACHINE BREAKDOWNS, subject to providing an alternate rest day. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-393f577c90dd494cee38d1bc9bc80592</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;UNFORESEEN EMERGENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER may require the EMPLOYEE to work on a rest day due to an unforeseen emergency, which is similar in nature to a machinery or plant breakdown."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6511dbd5eb2121ae41cf477a6c2b2884</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;ANTI-UNION DISCRIMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal protections ensure that employers cannot discriminate against employees based on union membership, affecting the relationship between EMPLOYER and EMPLOYEE in terms of labor rights and benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6511dbd5eb2121ae41cf477a6c2b2884</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT ON TERMINATION (SECTION 25)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer has responsibilities in paying due amounts to employees upon termination according to SECTION 25."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0b0b8e9edfab8c32d5cea9270e6f74ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 32, 1974&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer's responsibilities are regulated under SECTION 32, 1974 in relation to termination of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0b0b8e9edfab8c32d5cea9270e6f74ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT OR AGREEMENT IN CONSIDERATION OF A CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employment contract or agreement in consideration of an employment contract is a form of contractual relationship between employer and employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a2d24bb03fc40b38ed1a8c0cbcdbd963</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">25.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are involved in the process of paying or disputing severance payments for employees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employers have the legal obligation to provide severance payment when dismissing employees by reason of redundancy or layoff."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer is required to make and document the severance payment as per legal obligations, including providing a written statement of how it was calculated."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4803dc099d05bf6f05b27d07f8429783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d94d21b562915559fff6272dbbdb3b70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;LAYOFF&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer can lay off an employee, which is a form of dismissal under the U.K. law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9546d09d8137ba2697ee36074c84b498</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;AN EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The AN EMPLOYEE can be dismissed without entitlement to a severance payment if the EMPLOYER terminates his contract based on certain conditions outlined in section 9. (Amended 51 of 2000 s. 3)"&lt;SEP&gt;"The AN EMPLOYEE can be subject to dismissal by the EMPLOYER, and conditions for remedies are defined based on offers from the employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d536cf1eacc47eb2d3812dd2faa34e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e5f55eef00b5211e8c9c5c06c4bde96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER's offer of renewal or re-engagement must be made at least 7 days before the RELEVANT DATE to affect an AN EMPLOYEE's entitlement to severance payment under sections (2) and (3)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d536cf1eacc47eb2d3812dd2faa34e3c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;REST DAY OR HOLIDAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If the RELEVANT DATE falls on a REST DAY or HOLIDAY, it is construed as the next day for purposes of subsections (2)(b) and (3)(c)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d536cf1eacc47eb2d3812dd2faa34e3c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;ASSOCIATED COMPANIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer can be an associated company that includes or excludes other related companies for employment terms as per the defined relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-01e8dd2cd7216b43532ed7037814b54b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;DISMISSAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer is responsible for dismissing employees, which may involve termination under certain conditions as outlined in the ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The dismissal of an employee is influenced by the employer's status, which may include multiple associated companies affecting the decision-making process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01e8dd2cd7216b43532ed7037814b54b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION BY THE EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer has the authority to terminate the employment contract, which can be done for various reasons including redundancy."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a783557f86fea333101af802aa41e0a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;REDUNDANCY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer's decision to terminate employment contracts based on redundancy criteria is a specific form of termination by the employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a783557f86fea333101af802aa41e0a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;BANK WITHIN THE MEANING OF SECTION 2 OF THE BANKING ORDINANCE (CAP. 155)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer may make payment into an account in the employee's name with any bank within the meaning of section 2 of the Banking Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-88b2609f36389403179e27bcc11b4123</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CHEQUE, MONEY ORDER OR POSTAL ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Payments can be made by cheque, money order or postal order to the employee as per the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-88b2609f36389403179e27bcc11b4123</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;BANKING ORDINANCE (CAP. 155)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The BANKING ORDINANCE (CAP. 155) defines what constitutes a bank for payment purposes as per the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-88b2609f36389403179e27bcc11b4123</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD OR LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If there's a decision from MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD or Labour Tribunal specifying the severance payment amount, it overrides the employer’s obligation to provide written particulars directly to the employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d94d21b562915559fff6272dbbdb3b70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;MEDICAL EXAMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is responsible for arranging and paying for a medical examination to determine the employee's fitness."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bc7d719876b6f50011d4a77def5a2428</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CONTINUOUS EMPLOYMENT YEAR NUMBER (5 YEARS) FOR LONG SERVICE PAYMENT ELIGIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The continuous employment year number is used to determine eligibility for long service payment based on the employee's work history with the same employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bc7d719876b6f50011d4a77def5a2428</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;APPLICATION FORM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer requires an application form to be submitted by a qualified beneficiary within 30 days after the death of the employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0b3d407961e6ed952b04345f5d32a45</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is responsible for paying the long service payment to an entitled employee or spouse within specified timeframes unless reasonable excuse exists."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e9d410c88421aeae56a47aedb79d008e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;HOUSEHOLD BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer's role extends to managing the 'household business' when an employee works within or related to a private household, as per legal definitions and applications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e9d410c88421aeae56a47aedb79d008e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;DOMESTIC SERVANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The DOMESTIC SERVANT is employed by the EMPLOYER in a private household business context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dae8f763a371efa17099b990f69f8b4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;LONG-TERM SERVICE MONEY ENTITLEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER may be obligated to provide LONG-TERM SERVICE money if a DOMESTIC SERVANT's employment is terminated under certain conditions, though this entitlement can be waived based on the employee's behavior."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dae8f763a371efa17099b990f69f8b4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION NOTICE OR GARDEN LEAVE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER has the authority to give a TERMINATION NOTICE or request GARDEN LEAVE PAYMENT in certain circumstances, impacting DOMESTIC SERVANT employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dae8f763a371efa17099b990f69f8b4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;RENEWAL OR RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer makes the decision and offers of renewal or re-engagement to employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ff6ba65a2b6882ca144f894790a0cc18</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT RENEWAL OR RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer can renew or re-engage an employee under a new contract, which affects the termination of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PERSON ENTITLED TO THE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER is required to provide a written statement of long service payment to the PERSON ENTITLED TO THE PAYMENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-312b267feca3c2a25982c678db5c0527</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;WRITTEN STATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER must provide the correct WRITTEN STATEMENT as per legal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-312b267feca3c2a25982c678db5c0527</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 6&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER's notice of termination in accordance with SECTION 6 affects an employee’s entitlement to remedies after dismissal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9e5f55eef00b5211e8c9c5c06c4bde96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;15(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer must not violate section 15(1), which is related to the termination of employees, as per the FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 59 OF LAWS OF HONG KONG)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-22d580b5b472939d182c05bf201c52ef</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;21B(2)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer must not violate section 21B(2)(b), which is related to the termination of employees, as per the FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 59 OF LAWS OF HONG KONG)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-22d580b5b472939d182c05bf201c52ef</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;33(4B)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer must not violate section 33(4B), which is related to the termination of employees, as per the FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 59 OF LAWS OF HONG KONG)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-22d580b5b472939d182c05bf201c52ef</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;72B(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer must not violate section 72B(1), which is related to the termination of employees, as per the FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 59 OF LAWS OF HONG KONG)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-22d580b5b472939d182c05bf201c52ef</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 59 OF LAWS OF HONG KONG)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"This ordinance provides specific rules that the EMPLOYER must follow, including sections related to termination of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-22d580b5b472939d182c05bf201c52ef</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OR LABOUR AND INDUSTRIAL RELATIONS TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT OR LABOUR AND INDUSTRIAL RELATIONS TRIBUNAL must give the EMPLOYER an opportunity to present its arguments regarding reinstatement or re-employment orders."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-994a5726bf785617e7fce7f56d8f7b24</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OR LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">25.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT OR LABOUR TRIBUNAL makes decisions involving EMPLOYERS, including conciliation and reinstatement orders."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT OR LABOUR TRIBUNAL may order the EMPLOYER to pay compensation as it deems just and appropriate in the circumstances."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court or Labour Tribunal can treat unreasonable variation of terms as unreasonable dismissal by the employer and order terminal payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-236ae534fe116485f7714d0a24fe4030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03e96febd7377c249ee658b10e9575db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4254cc0d21afce88f6eb9b8c9366f7cc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LABOUR TRIBUNAL can order EMPLOYER to pay terminal payments if no reinstatement or re-engagement is made."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 32M, SECTION 32O&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER may be required to pay compensation as determined by sections 32M or 32O if an employee is terminated."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4254cc0d21afce88f6eb9b8c9366f7cc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OR LABOUR RELATIONS BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT OR LABOUR RELATIONS BOARD makes decisions regarding the employer's actions towards an employee, such as reinstatement or re-employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d4769919f14cc0f877d3fa0c4e17e775</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;APPLICATION FOR RELIEF&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER's actions may lead to an APPLICATION FOR RELIEF being filed with the COURT OR LABOUR RELATIONS BOARD."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d4769919f14cc0f877d3fa0c4e17e775</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;ABSENCE FROM WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYER can make deductions from WAGES due to ABSENCE FROM WORK, provided certain conditions are met."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-918c0eabaec10917e5775ff91d8fc75a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;DAMAGE TO OR LOSS OF GOODS, EQUIPMENT OR PROPERTY BELONGING TO OR IN THE POSSESSION OR CONTROL OF THE EMPLOYER OR EXPRESSLY ENTRUSTED TO AN EMPLOYEE FOR CUSTODY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYER can make deductions from WAGES for DAMAGE or LOSS directly attributable to the EMPLOYEE's neglect."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-918c0eabaec10917e5775ff91d8fc75a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;LOSS OF MONEY FOR WHICH AN EMPLOYEE IS REQUIRED TO ACCOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYER can make deductions from WAGES due to LOSS OF MONEY accounted by the EMPLOYEE, if such loss is directly attributable to his neglect or default."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-918c0eabaec10917e5775ff91d8fc75a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;WAGE PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are responsible for making wage payments within a specified wage period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fdc4a39840a667a7878ee99d632412a5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer is a party to the employment contract which outlines responsibilities including payment of wages for various leaves taken by employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d93d92eb00cb1e06709b542dad7efdd1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;RECOGNIZED SCHEME OF MEDICAL TREATMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer operates a recognized medical treatment scheme, which is subject to approval and potential withdrawal by the Director."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4af496fc2b1c26e3d6bca76a4b99c25f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;REST DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer grants Rest Days to employees for rest and relaxation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SICKNESS DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is responsible for managing Sickness Day policies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;HOLIDAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer provides Holidays to employees as part of the employment agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">24.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer must ensure the provision of ANNUAL LEAVE for employees according to labor laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer determines when annual leave will be granted and must provide at least 14 days' notice, unless agreed otherwise."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employer grants Annual Leave to employees for vacation time."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1ba134cba7bc0ad2b2ef34e757e78d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74bf264f43f2a8be1c1c6d9a90273b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;LEAVE AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Leave Agreements are made between the Employer and Employees regarding leave policies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPORARY INCAPACITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer manages compensation for Temporary Incapacity due to illness or injury."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE DEDUCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are responsible for deducting Sickness Allowance as per agreement terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer can terminate the Employment Contract with an employee under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dea1924fb64e67aeda866266fbf06fab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 39(2), (2A), (3) OR (4)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer must substitute a rest day or holiday if it falls within the period of annual leave, as per section 39."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e1ba134cba7bc0ad2b2ef34e757e78d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;COMMON HOLIDAY YEAR SELECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer has the option to choose a 12-month period as the holiday year for all employees, according to the law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a7a96ed62715f51c591ee8559b48c831</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;NOTICE PERIOD OF 1 MONTH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer must give a one-month notice in writing or publicly post it for at least one month before deciding on the holiday year."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a7a96ed62715f51c591ee8559b48c831</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;OPTION FOR COMMON LEAVE YEAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer has the option to use a common Leave Year for all Employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer determines and implements leave policies for Employees, including annual leave entitlements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8f51952a48de0746c8700f0d84b90238</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY RATE CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The calculation of annual leave pay rate involves wages paid by an employer, including payments for various types of leaves and absences."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5cf406b3b427b0e2efe01c3ec1bb9db4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer has the obligation to pay EMPLOYEE's ANNUAL LEAVE PAY upon cessation of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4b74bf264f43f2a8be1c1c6d9a90273b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY ON CESSATION OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is responsible for paying the annual leave compensation to the employee upon cessation of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3f562ef17ff451340f1810793e3d7491</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT IN LIEFU OF UNUSED ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are responsible for making the payment in lieu of unused annual leave to employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3f562ef17ff451340f1810793e3d7491</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE SHUTDOWN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer intends to close down business or part thereof for granting annual leave, which involves giving notice and identifying employees affected by this shutdown."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bc3b1c37f3356b594664179bc904382f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CLOSURE NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is responsible for exhibiting a closure notice in the workplace."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c46e076b844c67b6ef12faaaccec1c4b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY RECORD KEEPING REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER is required to keep records of annual leave pay for each employee as per the regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-341592011806c965a734bf17f63882db</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;MAIN NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer can be considered as the main nominated sub-contractor for certain work segments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL OBLIGATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers have legal obligations regarding wage payments and information provision according to the clauses mentioned in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL FINE FOR NON-COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers may face legal fines if they fail to comply with the obligations defined in 43J clause and other related clauses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL COMPLIANCE MONITORING MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers must comply with legal obligations and be subject to monitoring through compliance mechanisms as outlined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTING RELATIONSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers engage in a subcontracting relationship with main nominated sub-contractors for specific work segments as outlined by contractual agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SUPERIOR NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"When a superior nominated sub-contractor pays an employee under section 43G, it creates a debt due to the employer of that employee, linking all three parties financially."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-be3c1325ae6d7ddc996c9ba2b65c0d1d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED POST&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer's address is one of the possible delivery methods for notifications as per section 43L(1)(b). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-93a1fe97f228ec755ced3c31d6506c86</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL, MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are the subjects of claims and adjudications made by employees through these bodies as per section 43M. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-93a1fe97f228ec755ced3c31d6506c86</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PERSON ENTERING EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer must inform the person entering employment before they start their job, ensuring all necessary details are provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6cdefd54629d3267d124166ba92131ae</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is responsible for ensuring workplace conditions comply with the contract and legal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1093ec98fdeda43f43128129d5d24cf9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;RATE OF WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are required to keep records including the rate of wages for their employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f15fe91e28bec496f95bc0e2d20ab50c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;OVERTIME RATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers must record details related to overtime rates as part of employee earnings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f15fe91e28bec496f95bc0e2d20ab50c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;ALLOWANCES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Allowances are included in the conditions that employers need to document for their employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f15fe91e28bec496f95bc0e2d20ab50c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;OVERTIME EARNINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers must keep records of overtime earnings earned by employees as required under the regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f15fe91e28bec496f95bc0e2d20ab50c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;DEDUCTIONS FROM WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are obligated to document any deductions made from employee wages along with reasons for such deductions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f15fe91e28bec496f95bc0e2d20ab50c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS PREMISES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are required to keep work and employment records at their business premises or where employees are employed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fe986d49a20cfdf5d43e02699374c050</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;WAGE RECORD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer is required to maintain WAGE RECORDS that include information about wages paid during each wage period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3e6409377b6b4bbb92085773b4d5b79e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT RECORD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer must keep an EMPLOYMENT RECORD covering the employee's employment history for the preceding 12 months, which includes wage and employment details."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3e6409377b6b4bbb92085773b4d5b79e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PLACE OF BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The wage records must be kept at the employer's PLACE OF BUSINESS or where the employee is employed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d8e07a1a35f0f2dbd1d061a1e93c29e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;MINIMUM WAGE ORDINANCE (CAP. 608)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Records of employees who are within the meaning of MINIMUM WAGE ORDINANCE must include details if their wages fall below specified amounts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d8e07a1a35f0f2dbd1d061a1e93c29e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE, SICK LEAVE, MATERNITY LEAVE, PATERNITY LEAVE AND HOLIDAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Records should cover periods of leave and related payments for EMPLOYEE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d8e07a1a35f0f2dbd1d061a1e93c29e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT (PART IIA)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Records must include details on END OF YEAR PAYMENTS due to employees under Part IIA."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d8e07a1a35f0f2dbd1d061a1e93c29e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;NOTICE PERIOD FOR TERMINATION OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The records should also cover the NOTICE PERIOD required for termination of employment contracts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d8e07a1a35f0f2dbd1d061a1e93c29e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is subject to the provisions of SECTION 31, which defines their criminal responsibility if they violate its terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8cbf72b50ae34f7ab9f1b18ab52fd7f3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 72(1)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers may violate SECTION 72(1)(b), which is a material particular or withholding information, making them liable for fines and imprisonment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ad689dd49be1734c5e08c5a4e747265</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 23, 24, 25&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers may violate sections 23, 24, or 25 regarding payment of wages, making them liable for fines and imprisonment under SECTION 63C."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ad689dd49be1734c5e08c5a4e747265</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 47(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers may violate SECTION 47(1), making them liable for fines and imprisonment under relevant laws."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ad689dd49be1734c5e08c5a4e747265</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;FINE AT LEVEL 3&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers can face a fine at level 3 for violating certain sections as per the law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ad689dd49be1734c5e08c5a4e747265</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SUMMONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A summons can be served to an employer at the place of employment mentioned in the summons."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ad2c9fb7be1050f82eb2460f4de56e54</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED OFFICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is associated with the registered office where summonses for companies are sent in certain circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ad2c9fb7be1050f82eb2460f4de56e54</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;BODY CORPORATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers who are also body corporates may have similar legal responsibilities as described above."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c560e10db0daa7f51fa59f7a6b462aa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;FINE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer convicted of an offence under the Ordinance shall pay a fine in addition to other penalties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-07f949d11fd1c1d8a909fd36ccac57d6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PLACE OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
