  <data key="d6">chunk-919e8934f076d1a9c5aea1486aa3f1c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;INDUSTRIAL EMPLOYMENT (HOLIDAYS WITH PAY AND SICKNESS ALLOWANCE) ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers operate according to the provisions of the Industrial Employment (Holidays with Pay and Sickness Allowance) Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-919e8934f076d1a9c5aea1486aa3f1c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers are not allowed to disclose information about a visit made in consequence of receiving a complaint to the employer or its agents/servants."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-029d1e15c5db53ebcfd1168d7ac7bbab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;附表2 - PROCEDURE FOR APPREHENSION OF ABSCONDING EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are involved in procedures related to absconding employers as defined by the second schedule."&lt;SEP&gt;"附表2 defines the procedure for apprehending an absconding employer, directly impacting the relationship between employers and employees in cases of non-payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd0362fbf5661d142ff4aeefe27aea79</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;REGIONAL COURT JUDGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The REGIONAL COURT JUDGE has the authority to order the EMPLOYER's imprisonment if they fail to comply with a command."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffe2fc373a4f6caf645c752f135c7582</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;GUARANTOR OF GUARANTEE DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The actions of the EMPLOYER may lead to applications from the GUARANTOR OF GUARANTEE DOCUMENT for relief regarding their obligations under a GUARANantee DOCUMENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffe2fc373a4f6caf645c752f135c7582</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;DEBT RECOVERY PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The DEBT RECOVERY PROCEDURES can affect whether an EMPLOYER is released from detention or must comply with commands by the REGIONAL COURT JUDGE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffe2fc373a4f6caf645c752f135c7582</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;DISTRICT JUDGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The District Judge can issue a warrant for the Employer if they believe the Employer is about to leave Hong Kong with intent to evade debt."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-eb63fc0b243ea63257ead6ec4cad1834</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;DEBT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer has an outstanding Debt that they may try to evade, leading to actions from the District Judge."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-eb63fc0b243ea63257ead6ec4cad1834</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SURETY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer can apply for discharge of bond with sureties, and their compliance affects this process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-86f4348a1c4677448f8348eacdd112bb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;WARRANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If an employer complies or secures payment as per the order, a warrant is discharged."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-86f4348a1c4677448f8348eacdd112bb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employment Ordinance also applies to employers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-67218fecb16f152219fae29882c0cc1d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;APPLICANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">19.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Applicants are making claims against employers under the Employment Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The applicant applies for a warrant against an employer who owes wages or other moneys to employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78c6c93b249203abfbdb5ba16af8eb78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67218fecb16f152219fae29882c0cc1d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER has employees who may be affected by their death or other conditions specified in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af8bb2bf50613f2cddc9c821004e6e7d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PERSONAL REPRESENTATIVE OF THE DECEASED EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer can be construed as including a personal representative of the deceased employer in certain contexts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1c5d2b28a0cc543e1f646cbc0388c9eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;DEATH OF EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The death of an employee can trigger provisions related to their contract termination as per Part VA."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2f5d9b3d656df85c08982a8986732f4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PART VA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Part VA of this Ordinance applies when an employer terminates a contract due to an employee's death before notice expires."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2f5d9b3d656df85c08982a8986732f4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PART VIA OF THIS ORDINANCE ON EMPLOYMENT PROTECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Part VIA applies to the employer's termination notice and offers, affecting their obligations after an employee's death."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9ed372c34a6ff55010cb2f16481f447c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;NINTH SCHEDULE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER is subject to the regulations outlined in NINTH SCHEDULE regarding record-keeping of hours worked by employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1896582b740b6a3f00c9bfa592f3ab2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;THE 2020 AMENDMENT ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"EMPLOYER's actions in terminating employment contracts are subject to THE 2020 AMENDMENT ORDINANCE, particularly for situations involving female employees and the amendment date."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7d6f22e03ef794b224e1918ddd3fee77</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;ORS BENEFITS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ORS benefits refer to employer-funded basic portion benefits according to the context provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a23958c5eb862b357e8540d3c4c5afd6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;STRONGLY FUNDED PENSION SCHEMES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers fund the STRONGLY FUNDED PENSION SCHEMES as indicated in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a23958c5eb862b357e8540d3c4c5afd6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">552.0</data>
  <data key="d5">In this context, both "EMPLOYEE" and "EMPLOYER" are central entities in an employment relationship governed by a contract of employment as defined by relevant ordinances. The EMPLOYER is responsible for engaging the specified EMPLOYEE, maintaining records related to their employment, paying wages including various leaves, providing medical expenses coverage, arranging pre-employment health checks (with costs borne by the employer), and ensuring workplace safety under statutory duties. The EMPLOYER can terminate or renew the contract of employment with certain conditions, offer re-engagement, and make deductions from an employee's earnings if necessary.

The EMPLOYEE works under terms set by their employer, including fixed-term contracts that may be renewed/re-engaged based on specific provisions. They are entitled to severance pay as per legal requirements and can seek compensation for medical expenses related to work-related accidents or injuries. The relationship between the EMPLOYER and EMPLOYEE is subject to labor laws that govern rights and obligations, with both parties involved in potential reinstatement or re-employment orders decided by a court or Labour Relations Board.

The employment contract may be terminated during probation or at other times as per regulations, and the employer must maintain records of employee wage and employment history for 12 months. The EMPLOYER is also required to provide statutory holidays, recognize entitlements under various leave categories (including paternity leave), and ensure that medical examination reports are provided upon request without reasonable excuse.

Both entities can be involved in transactions requiring consent from the Commissioner or other legal authorities, with the employer bearing responsibility for ensuring safe working conditions and paying compensation as per the terms of employment. The EMPLOYER must comply with statutory duties concerning workplace safety, including provisions related to young workers and children's employment, while also being liable for medical expenses incurred by employees during work-related accidents.

In cases where an employee provides evidence or information regarding enforcing ordinances or dealing with accidents, the employer is prohibited from terminating, threatening termination, or discriminating against them. The EMPLOYER can offer substitute holidays within 30 days and may require employees to work on rest days under certain conditions, subject to voluntary agreement between both parties.

The relationship between the EMPLOYEE and EMPLOYER involves potential reinstatement or re-employment orders decided by a court or Labour Relations Board, with both entities involved in transactions that require approval from the Commissioner. The employer must provide written statements of severance payment upon termination and maintain records related to employee employment, including sick leave details.

Overall, this comprehensive description highlights the complex interplay between EMPLOYER and EMPLOYEE responsibilities under labor laws and contractual agreements, emphasizing their roles in maintaining a safe workplace environment, providing necessary benefits, and adhering to legal obligations.</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-44e57b1615ed5c8b1f49eb6a6ecd4472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-607a2fda7757f874bbb128bc111c8ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba7e2407b8844aba128e42ffefa2f5d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff6ba65a2b6882ca144f894790a0cc18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-786c67dfb1439b58fce397c3168c9e29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68ef0e8f1f38a0c8885d599e4ee4a20e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d8e006856fc24f02eba931eaf4c63a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79cc5ddf4e6de2a7921e786b0c812fc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e37def8625e820a47ed5130364eb70d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30cbd8927d8b6504c1eddb029a57bc60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f5fe723dc66b1a35b256f0fbcfd9642&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1896582b740b6a3f00c9bfa592f3ab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9546d09d8137ba2697ee36074c84b498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fff8612fdefb52ed816a2d4502b87bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2d24bb03fc40b38ed1a8c0cbcdbd963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e7d6d62033f777323f252b1d52645d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea6b2c9739d4904eac9e0c6be6072cb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a5a03e3846825046c524fcfca7051d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f08187ad728064351e188904ac02ad6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b965639f18b2c29c5f672b6067f9d701&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6409377b6b4bbb92085773b4d5b79e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8a8ba58e2f04dd4f35b5bed0e044673&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4881be1a6d6d318bb1047aad7c99da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06b0b35c8989b71abf93d8af04dd8d7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f17d41b36a40e80f45f0f635b4ad7eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994a5726bf785617e7fce7f56d8f7b24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4769919f14cc0f877d3fa0c4e17e775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caf4b3f0aa7e762095c32496aac13d2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd33f100307534902fe4100976fabc93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8e07a1a35f0f2dbd1d061a1e93c29e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f8e345be219d3fc366dc62469796daf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5c7df56b94c0c429230f0546be40142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a215b7541a9d5eb966c5aa9ffed5374&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-393f577c90dd494cee38d1bc9bc80592&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66cccec6ac7d06fb5417245d5fe5f3b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ddecf99bc0bca06387d96224afeaf4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8714cccfc72c7380caa9903fb713cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f729e4dc4d8c13592d31110960bc5996&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e72191ab4edd091f82585ac0b7be851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02218e873b9a55b35f3e34874d7090d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6511dbd5eb2121ae41cf477a6c2b2884&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af55493786feba6de502e98ed832cde8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-398cf2cb1ea6408a6d67cec4cb083e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd0362fbf5661d142ff4aeefe27aea79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c974ea5d752dd73a9522c1e2701db94a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-150ac34f962a55c7a622046976949d60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1ed02e78cf2ee9e321f22dbe3ba84b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1faa1664ffe65d577dff74396c2e0ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d94d21b562915559fff6272dbbdb3b70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5742863cc938d9f9470985855601b925&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602a52838c03cef3777006bf2a44b72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-266c63bff8f647150f70f543690f359f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af043de8381bfd2d54ddf7a99fe8b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7249fad978915b4915d01ecac03019f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f10185e6fc563260f4e1f20ab8c394fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e976980f19e9ab89febaf65027fa503e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccf624f83121089caf9f8fb044043303&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b2609f36389403179e27bcc11b4123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d19ac100c430c329d42230a7654f3c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0aa6a1ecbb96f241ec693e9b7796d393&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d580b5b472939d182c05bf201c52ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ed372c34a6ff55010cb2f16481f447c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bf6feb0461285dd636b630f26952415&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be12459eb42b5303144e2a38dc8cf0c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3acaae72bbbda2c87c57f32876a632e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d76ba7381f3e95da332b4d2d5206d84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098ca6bfb60006d76569bead63917ebd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cf406b3b427b0e2efe01c3ec1bb9db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-338f6b52974bc08baebc662da42c4477</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;" target="&quot;PERSON NAMED AS SUCH IN ARTICLES OF AGREEMENT OR APPOINTED BY EMPLOYER AND NOTIFIED TO CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Maintenance Surveyor is either named in the contract or appointed by the Employer with written notification to the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">55.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR evaluates whether a WORKS ORDER has been substantially completed and issues a Certificate of Completion, determining any liquidated damages for delay if the work is not finished on time."&lt;SEP&gt;"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has the authority to issue orders and permissions related to WORKS ORDERS."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor considers extensions related to the completion of tasks specified in the Works Order."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor has authority to make corrections and modifications in any previous certificate issued by them, withholding certificates if not satisfied with work execution."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor issues and certifies payment for works orders that comply with the contract terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor issues written orders (Works Orders) to the Contractor detailing work or services to be executed under the Contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"Works Orders are issued by the Maintenance Surveyor to direct and sanction specific works, including Emergency Work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2f5b22ce699e51609625c61aad79755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87f722c8522f822c2e90eb078db141b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1ba1c6b232e9a68005845d332fa7552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f6be589350c8e73f0a57d60397f9eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;" target="&quot;EMERGENCY WORKS ORDERED&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor can order Emergency Works from time to time which fall under the broader scope of the Works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2f5b22ce699e51609625c61aad79755</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">327.0</data>
  <data key="d5">The CONTRACTOR and MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR are key entities in a construction project, each with distinct roles and responsibilities. The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has significant authority over the CONTRACTOR's work, including issuing instructions, approving works, certifying costs, and overseeing compliance with contractual standards.

The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR is responsible for measuring and certifying payments to the CONTRACTOR based on completed work. They can withhold or grant permission regarding the use of constructional plant by the CONTRACTOR on site. The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR also has authority over interim payment certificates, corrections, modifications, and variations in works orders. They issue notices and authorize actions that the CONTRACTOR must follow diligently; any disputes with these decisions can only be contested through arbitration within 90 days.

The CONTRACTOR is responsible for executing work under a WORKS ORDER as per MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR's satisfaction and instructions, including responding to maintenance requirements during and after the Maintenance Period. The CONTRACTOR must submit bills, dimension books, claims for interim payments, notifications about delays or probable extent of causes, worker injuries, and intentions to claim additional payment within 28 days.

The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has authority over the removal of constructional plant, temporary buildings, and surplus materials from the site after completion. They can instruct the CONTRACTOR on sub-contracts and related matters, including handling objections from the Contractor. The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR also evaluates claims submitted by the CONTRACTOR within a specified timeframe.

Both parties share liability in cases where their respective acts or neglect contribute to damages, loss, or injury during work execution. The CONTRACTOR must notify the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR about delays and probable extent when causes are apparent, as well as intentions to claim additional payment within 28 days of an event becoming apparent.

In summary, the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR plays a crucial role in overseeing the work executed by the CONTRACTOR, ensuring compliance with contractual standards, approving works, certifying costs and expenses, issuing certificates for payments, and handling claims. The CONTRACTOR must adhere to these instructions and notifications while executing their responsibilities under the WORKS ORDER.</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-599efa27c5ee543ca385bb3d944e13fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ce0f4a340a17df1f53274ac940867b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b57445949baa2153e0f9f67f999456b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d204e5d2ccca14fb7f49bf493cc0bdb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2d562d8afcd917deebad02c95fa56d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522c43aa0cb7d424d1da1c5b00c65777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba22dc0a0fc19429a484bb41c261d34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-affc5866b16d32a569c7ab46b9093e2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c58277d66887ed610fbaec73a4e8d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fb1308c02d44b7ab0dcb7b386e3c410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c2d16f0534b8f7a9f0c286e3e24591&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1373b3be58ae445e60a533999b71823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-534e9d84651f98c51ccc8c24e68050b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8ac9b93ec382ad9a1bb20e1b7960a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8130c8086938f6df2d05cdf9fb7e405c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f6be589350c8e73f0a57d60397f9eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5353a0b04268f3f2bf8419dceec4f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa9c6366e076e445101d83858797035&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d72604c877ec1b265cace0cc38e4690d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5e827172d85d4fce202f234f783e044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1ba1c6b232e9a68005845d332fa7552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ff1f20b792fbc8d1bdd961c49e1244&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671cf14fabde451a853f4cb49e6a812f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62865738eafa658463c1c26212a98b20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">74.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONSTRUCTOR is responsible for carrying out the WORKS ORDER as specified in the contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"The CONTRACTOR must complete WORKS ORDERS within specified times, with provisions for extensions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contractor is responsible for completing tasks detailed in the Works Order and can seek extensions based on specific conditions outlined in Clause 57."&lt;SEP&gt;"The WORKS ORDER details tasks for which the CONTRACTOR must provide updates on potential delays to the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR."&lt;SEP&gt;"The WORKS ORDER is a document that specifies tasks for the CONTRACTOR under the Contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"The WORKS ORDER is related to the claims process, as it defines the scope of work for which claims can be made."&lt;SEP&gt;"The WORKS ORDER serves as a written order from the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR, directing the CONSTRUCTOR on specific works to be executed."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Works Order is a document that directs the Contractor what needs to be done, with specific timeframes and requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"WORKS ORDER directs the CONSTRUCTOR on specific parts of the Works, which must be executed according to Maintenance Surveyor’s directions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Works Orders document specific tasks or work items assigned to the Contractor, guiding their execution and payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e2d562d8afcd917deebad02c95fa56d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b57445949baa2153e0f9f67f999456b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c2d16f0534b8f7a9f0c286e3e24591&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8ac9b93ec382ad9a1bb20e1b7960a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671cf14fabde451a853f4cb49e6a812f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f6be589350c8e73f0a57d60397f9eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;PERSON WHOSE TENDER HAS BEEN ACCEPTED BY THE EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Contractor is an individual or company that accepts a tender from the Employer to execute Works under the Contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;CLAUSE 48 OR CLAUSE 49&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor must comply with clauses related to work commencement and progress, which are critical for avoiding Forfeiture as per Clause 87."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9ba22dc0a0fc19429a484bb41c261d34</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">31.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COMMISSIONER can engage persons to assist OFFICERS in carrying out duties related to the FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (Cap. 59), which involves YOUNG PERSON OR CHILDREN and MAGISTRATES."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner can examine persons found within the meaning of this ordinance and seize evidence related to offenses against it."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner has powers to examine persons within the context of this ordinance's meaning, including those found in industrial undertakings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner has the authority to issue notices and orders under the FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (Cap. 59). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-106089b31da6304da0bc926c63d44161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-057cc616cb8b855799f3fcacf937e222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70cdeeb8eece52f9eaa0ef190c0b61e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;CORONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 14)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The two ordinances are related in that they both deal with the administration and enforcement by appointed officers, particularly concerning labor matters."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92c85875b0985afcab2ef9a7ace52829</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">25.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational Safety Officers are appointed under this Ordinance, which outlines their roles and responsibilities. "&lt;SEP&gt;"The FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (Cap. 59) is the legal basis for appointing OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER under section 19."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ordinance governs the actions of occupational safety officers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a3c3394a6b72977677a8a437b4151b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea83763b873f6b32742c132cbac8d568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7881ceecf94346279b299fee8d79193</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;INSPECTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Inspectors are defined by the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance, which also outlines their transition to Occupational Safety Officers. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a3c3394a6b72977677a8a437b4151b9d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
