  <data key="d6">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;NOTICE PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Notice periods for termination of employment contracts are defined by the ordinance, impacting dismissal procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSEQUENT EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT RENEWAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Renewal of employment contracts is a process that can affect the interpretation and application of dismissal under the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;RE-EMPLOYMENT UNDER A NEW CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Re-employment under a new contract can impact the conditions of dismissal as per Section 32A(1)(a) and (c)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE BONUS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Long service bonuses are not directly related to dismissal but can be affected by the terms of employment contracts, which are regulated under the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Severance pay is a term that can be impacted by dismissal procedures as defined in Sections of the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;WRONGFUL DISMISSAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Wrongful dismissals are a concept that can be addressed under the provisions of the ordinance, particularly in relation to Sections 6 and 32A(1)(a)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL PROTECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal protection for employees is provided by the ordinance, which includes provisions related to wrongful dismissal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;CONCILIATION AND ARBITRATION SERVICES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Conciliation and arbitration services are mechanisms for resolving disputes, including those related to dismissal under the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;LABOR LAW ENFORCEMENT AGENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Labor Law Enforcement Agency is responsible for enforcing compliance with the provisions of the ordinance, including those related to dismissal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;CONCILIATION SERVICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Conciliation services are part of the dispute resolution mechanisms under the ordinance, which can be relevant to addressing wrongful dismissals."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration processes are part of the dispute resolution mechanisms under the ordinance, which can be relevant to addressing wrongful dismissals."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;CONCILIATION AND ARBITRATION MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The conciliation and arbitration mechanisms are part of the dispute resolution processes under the ordinance, which can be relevant to addressing wrongful dismissals."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;LABOR DISPUTE RESOLUTION PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Labor dispute resolution processes are part of the mechanisms under the ordinance, which can be relevant to addressing wrongful dismissals."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;CONCILIATION SERVICE PROVIDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Conciliation service providers are entities that offer services under the mechanisms of the ordinance, which can be relevant to addressing wrongful dismissals."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OR LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court or Labour Tribunal may consider dismissals in contravention of this ordinance when making an award of compensation, as per SECTION 32P(1)(b). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-852d5344329889ebbea0dad97630dd26</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;PREMISES OR PLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Premises or places within the meaning of this ordinance include industrial undertakings where inspections and examinations can be conducted."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-057cc616cb8b855799f3fcacf937e222</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;YOUNG PERSON OR CHILD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (Cap. 59) regulates the employment of YOUNG PERSON OR CHILDREN in industrial undertakings, requiring declarations and examinations from them regarding their working conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-106089b31da6304da0bc926c63d44161</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;LABOUR DEPARTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance provides the legal framework for the Labour Department to advise on matters related to industrial undertakings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b297641c5fc96a9b02649fb896184fdd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;AMENDED 56 OF 2000&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"AMENDED 56 OF 2000 refers to the FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (Cap. 59) for specific provisions and definitions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23a60b107acb436d1472e4d6fcca723b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;" target="&quot;INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKING is subject to the FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (Cap. 59) as defined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23a60b107acb436d1472e4d6fcca723b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SHIPPING AND PORT CONTROL ORDINANCE (CAP. 313)&quot;" target="&quot;HONG KONG SHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition and application for HONG KONG SHIPS are also covered by the SHIPPING AND PORT CONTROL ORDINANCE (Cap. 313)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f4d76a0b22237a0d626c699347fd4848</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE CONTROL ORDINANCE (CAP. 400)&quot;" target="&quot;NOISE CONTROL SUPERVISOR APPOINTED UNDER CAP. 400&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Noise Control Supervisor appointed under the NOISE CONTROL ORDINANCE (CAP. 400) sends out notifications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6d5c1db270105c42831679d46cdf6fb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE CONTROL ORDINANCE (CAP. 400)&quot;" target="&quot;NOISE CONTROL AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The NOISE CONTROL AUTHORITY operates under the Noise Control Ordinance (Cap. 400), which is the legal framework for their actions and authority to take proceedings against body corporate directors or officers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-606c291ea5ee675ad86390a5e98aaec1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE CONTROL ORDINANCE (CAP. 400)&quot;" target="&quot;DIRECTOR OR OFFICER OF BODY CORPORATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Directors or officers of a body corporate are subject to the Noise Control Ordinance (Cap. 400), as their actions can lead to offenses under this ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-606c291ea5ee675ad86390a5e98aaec1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE CONTROL ORDINANCE (CAP. 400)&quot;" target="&quot;BODY CORPORATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">19.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Body Corporate is regulated by the Noise Control Ordinance (Cap. 400), which sets out rules and penalties for violations related to noise control within their premises or operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Body Corporate is subject to the provisions of the Noise Control Ordinance, which can lead to proceedings against it for offenses committed by its Directors or Officers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-606c291ea5ee675ad86390a5e98aaec1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd34572cc7a7c12a47fc15cbaf1c545c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE CONTROL ORDINANCE (CAP. 400)&quot;" target="&quot;NOISE CONTROL AUTHORITY/PUBLIC OFFICER AUTHORIZED UNDER SECTION 3(3) OF THE NOISE CONTROL ORDINANCE (CAP. 400)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Noise Control Ordinance grants authority to the Noise Control Authority or Public Officer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bd34572cc7a7c12a47fc15cbaf1c545c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE CONTROL ORDINANCE (CAP. 400)&quot;" target="&quot;DIRECTOR(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Directors are subject to the provisions of the Noise Control Ordinance, which can lead to proceedings against them for offenses committed by the Body Corporate they manage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bd34572cc7a7c12a47fc15cbaf1c545c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE CONTROL ORDINANCE (CAP. 400)&quot;" target="&quot;OFFICER(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Officers are subject to the provisions of the Noise Control Ordinance, which can lead to proceedings against them for offenses committed by the Body Corporate they manage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bd34572cc7a7c12a47fc15cbaf1c545c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE OF GOODS ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;1893 C. 71 U.K.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Sale of Goods Ordinance is based on the legal framework established by 1893 c. 71 U.K."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-79dd10ef156d0f9f22ec627b97b0e737</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE OF GOODS ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;1 AUGUST 1896&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Sale of Goods Ordinance underwent format changes on August 1, 1896."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-79dd10ef156d0f9f22ec627b97b0e737</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE OF GOODS ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;1924年第5號第6條修訂&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Sale of Goods Ordinance was amended by the revision in 1924 s. 6."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-79dd10ef156d0f9f22ec627b97b0e737</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;原告人&quot;" target="&quot;被告人&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"原告人包括提出反申索的被告人。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc8969679580d96d1a44b2258d943923</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;原告人&quot;" target="&quot;訴訟&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"诉讼包括诉讼案、反诉和抵销，涉及到原告人的权益保护。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc8969679580d96d1a44b2258d943923</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;售賣合約&quot;" target="&quot;買方&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"买方指购货或同意购货的人，在销售合同中是另一重要角色。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc8969679580d96d1a44b2258d943923</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;售賣合約&quot;" target="&quot;錯失&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"错失指错误的行为或不履行，在销售合同中可能会涉及违约责任。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc8969679580d96d1a44b2258d943923</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;產權&quot;" target="&quot;貨品的所有權文件&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"产权指货物的一般所有权，而货品的所有权文件是证明这种权利的文档。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc8969679580d96d1a44b2258d943923</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;貨品品質&quot;" target="&quot;售卖合約&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"货品质包括货物的状态或状况，在销售合同中可能涉及质量条款。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc8969679580d96d1a44b2258d943923</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;期貨&quot;" target="&quot;售卖&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"期货是指在订立销售合约后才制造或取得的货物，与一般的售卖不同。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc8969679580d96d1a44b2258d943923</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;業務&quot;" target="&quot;卖方&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"业务包括专业，也包括公共机构、公共主管当局等的活动，与卖方可能有关联。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc8969679580d96d1a44b2258d943923</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;賣方&quot;" target="&quot;與承運人訂立的合約&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"合同要求或授權賣方向買方發貨，因此賣方需要與承運人簽訂相關協議。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c162b772c9e897f69948d67d21519288</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;賣方&quot;" target="&quot;貨品&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"賣方負責發送和保障貨品的安全運輸至目的地。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c162b772c9e897f69948d67d21519288</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FAULT&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SELLER can be involved in FAULT by making mistakes or failing to fulfill responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1e575d442f08ac69ffbe5033c6d10569</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IN GOOD FAITH&quot;" target="&quot;INSOLVENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A person is considered INSOLVENT when they are unable to repay debts, even if not declared bankrupt and acting IN GOOD FAITH."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1e575d442f08ac69ffbe5033c6d10569</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INSOLVENT&quot;" target="&quot;MERCHANTABLE QUALITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"MERCHANTABLE QUALITY refers to a product that is free from defects and meets certain standards, which can affect how an INSOLVENT party handles goods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1e575d442f08ac69ffbe5033c6d10569</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INSOLVENT&quot;" target="&quot;通常業務運作中已停止償還債項&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A person who has stopped repaying debts in their usual business operations is considered INSOLVENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1e575d442f08ac69ffbe5033c6d10569</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DELIVERABLE STATE&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SELLER's goods must be in DELIVERABLE STATE for the buyer to receive them according to contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1e575d442f08ac69ffbe5033c6d10569</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DELIVERABLE STATE&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIFIC GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Specific goods must be in a deliverable state, meaning they are fit for delivery under the contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0e4c0453b8451785120b5b76a2526cab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MERCHANTABLE QUALITY&quot;" target="&quot;QUALITY OF GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Goods of merchantable quality meet certain standards and expectations regarding their fitness, appearance, safety, defects, and durability as defined by common practices in sales."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0e4c0453b8451785120b5b76a2526cab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MERCHANTABLE QUALITY&quot;" target="&quot;IMPLIED CONDITION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Implied condition ensures that goods must have merchantable quality unless otherwise specified in point (a). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5228b6166ae5f3bb9be72928713eb4f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MERCHANTABLE QUALITY&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 16&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 16 specifies that there is an implied condition that the goods are of merchantable quality when sold by a business, except as noted for specific defects or buyer's knowledge."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abd61364920843014789da67b81b39a5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MERCHANTABLE QUALITY&quot;" target="&quot;GOODS SUPPLIED UNDER A CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Goods supplied under a contract of sale are expected to be of merchantable quality, except as specified conditions apply."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ACTION (訴訟)&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'action' is defined in the Ordinance to include suit, counterclaim, and set-off."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e80ca1cb58b86bd99a385c76452eb8d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ACTION (訴訟)&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS (業務)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business activities can be part of an action as per the definition provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e80ca1cb58b86bd99a385c76452eb8d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ACTION (訴訟)&quot;" target="&quot;FAULT (錯失)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fault is defined as wrongful act or default, and can be part of an action in the context provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e80ca1cb58b86bd99a385c76452eb8d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ACTION (訴訟)&quot;" target="&quot;PLAINTIFF (原告人)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'plaintiff' includes a defendant counterclaiming, indicating that plaintiffs are involved in actions as per the Ordinance's definition."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e80ca1cb58b86bd99a385c76452eb8d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ACTION (訴訟)&quot;" target="&quot;SALE (售賣)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sale is defined broadly in the Ordinance and includes agreements to sell, which could form part of an action."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e80ca1cb58b86bd99a385c76452eb8d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS (業務)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 54, SECTION 52, SECTION 3 OF 8 OF 2018 S. 3 (第54條、第52條及第8號法律公告第三章)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Businesses are subject to specific sections of the law that regulate their operations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4a12f68db2756f89b8999b59583f0a9b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUYER (買方)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE (售賣合約)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A buyer is defined in the context to mean a person who buys or agrees to buy goods, which are covered under a contract of sale."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e80ca1cb58b86bd99a385c76452eb8d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE (售賣合約)&quot;" target="&quot;FUTURE GOODS (期貨)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Future goods are goods to be manufactured or acquired by the seller after the making of a contract of sale, thus falling under the broader definition of 'sale'."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e80ca1cb58b86bd99a385c76452eb8d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE (售賣合約)&quot;" target="&quot;GOODS (貨、貨品)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Goods are defined as chattels personal other than things in action and money, which can be part of a contract of sale."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e80ca1cb58b86bd99a385c76452eb8d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE (售賣合約)&quot;" target="&quot;QUALITY OF GOODS (貨品品質)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The quality of goods can be a factor considered under a contract of sale as it pertains to their state or condition."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e80ca1cb58b86bd99a385c76452eb8d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DELIVERY (交、交付)&quot;" target="&quot;DOCUMENT OF TITLE TO GOODS (貨品的所有權文件)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Delivery involves transferring possession and can be evidenced by documents such as bills of lading or warehouse keeper's certificates, which are examples of a document of title to goods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e80ca1cb58b86bd99a385c76452eb8d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS (貨、貨品)&quot;" target="&quot;PROPERTY (產權)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Property is defined to include general property in goods, which relates directly to the broader term 'goods'."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e80ca1cb58b86bd99a385c76452eb8d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PLAINTIFF&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The plaintiff can include a defendant counterclaiming against the seller in legal proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0e4c0453b8451785120b5b76a2526cab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFIC GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Specific goods are identified and agreed upon at the time of sale, forming part of the contract between buyer and seller."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0e4c0453b8451785120b5b76a2526cab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFIC GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SPECIFIC GOODS are delivered by the SELLER and/or CARRIER to the BUYER, with property transfer contingent on conditions set forth in the CONTRACT or RESERVATION OF RIGHT OF DISPOSAL."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-08fbcc9c2ce9e3d4f773cc495db19495</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WARRANTY&quot;" target="&quot;QUALITY OF GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A warranty is an agreement regarding the quality of goods sold under a contract, which includes their state or condition."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0e4c0453b8451785120b5b76a2526cab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WARRANTY&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The warranty terms within the contract define claims for damages but not rejection rights upon breach by the seller."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6898f338d8c873d727625cb55234a222</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WARRANTY&quot;" target="&quot;IMPOSSIBILITY OR OTHER LEGAL EXCUSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal excuses such as impossibility may excuse the fulfillment of warranty terms in certain cases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6898f338d8c873d727625cb55234a222</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WARRANTY&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SELLER breaches Warranties, leading to potential disputes or claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-69fc897b8b9dfae677db802b05a78337</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WARRANTY&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The BUYER has the right to claim against BREACH OF WARRANTY from the SELLER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-69fc897b8b9dfae677db802b05a78337</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WARRANTY&quot;" target="&quot;DAMAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"BREACH OF WARRANTY can lead to claims for DAMAGES from the BUYER against the SELLER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-69fc897b8b9dfae677db802b05a78337</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE&quot;" target="&quot;GOOD FAITH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sales are conducted in good faith when they are done honestly and not negligently, ensuring fair transactions between parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0e4c0453b8451785120b5b76a2526cab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"When the property in goods is transferred from seller to buyer, a Contract of sale becomes a Sale."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a93975688247d3b9e7a757c9ac99d011</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOOD FAITH&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 2A OF THE UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 2A emphasizes the importance of good faith in interpreting the law, reflecting its principles."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3694b9973d0eb7e4719ad33e81b8744f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INSOLVENCY&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A seller can be deemed insolvent if unable to pay debts as they become due or have ceased paying debts in the ordinary course of business."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0e4c0453b8451785120b5b76a2526cab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INSOLVENCY&quot;" target="&quot;UNPAID SELLER'S LIEN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Insolvency is a specific condition under which an unpaid seller can exercise their lien over goods sold on credit or without stipulated payment terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"UNPAID SELLER'S LIEN can be exercised when the buyer becomes insolvent."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-83a8d937e2b926da0d7047a5288d8ae8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS OF ANY KIND ARE OF MERCHANTABLE QUALITY WITHIN THE MEANING OF THIS ORDINANCE IF THEY ARE—&quot;" target="&quot;REPLACED 85 OF 1994 S. 2&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition of merchantable quality in the ordinance is updated by replacing section 85 of 1994 s. 2."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a1f612e80bc33b548b5b253bf3e3dac0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS OF ANY KIND ARE OF MERCHANTABLE QUALITY WITHIN THE MEANING OF THIS ORDINANCE IF THEY ARE—&quot;" target="&quot;AMENDED E.R. 4 OF 2018&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition of merchantable quality in the ordinance is further amended by E.R. 4 of 2018."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a1f612e80bc33b548b5b253bf3e3dac0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPLACED 85 OF 1994 S. 2&quot;" target="&quot;PURCHASER NOT DEALING AS CONSUMER (NOT DEALS AS CONSUMER)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition for not dealing as a consumer is established by replacing section 85 of 1994 s. 2."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a1f612e80bc33b548b5b253bf3e3dac0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPLACED 85 OF 1994 S. 2&quot;" target="&quot;AMENDED E.R. 4 OF 2018&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 85 of 1994 s. 2 is replaced and then amended by E.R. 4 of 2018."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a1f612e80bc33b548b5b253bf3e3dac0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AMENDED E.R. 4 OF 2018&quot;" target="&quot;PURCHASER NOT DEALING AS CONSUMER (NOT DEALS AS CONSUMER)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition for not dealing as a consumer is further amended by E.R. 4 of 2018."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a1f612e80bc33b548b5b253bf3e3dac0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AMENDED E.R. 4 OF 2018&quot;" target="&quot;SELLING CONTRACT PARTY DEALING AS CONSUMER (DEALS AS CONSUMER)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition for dealing as a consumer is amended by E.R. 4 of 2018."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a1f612e80bc33b548b5b253bf3e3dac0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SELLING CONTRACT PARTY DEALING AS CONSUMER (DEALS AS CONSUMER)&quot;" target="&quot;CONSUMER TRANSACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A party dealing as a consumer falls under the category of consumer transactions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a1f612e80bc33b548b5b253bf3e3dac0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;A PARTY TO A CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;ANOTHER PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A PARTY TO A CONTRACT OF SALE" "deals as consumer in relation to ANOTHER PARTY under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOTHER PARTY can be a party to the same CONTRACT OF SALE, either as buyer or seller depending on context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;A PARTY TO A CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;CONSUMER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A PARTY TO A CONTRACT OF SALE may deal as a CONSUMER if the conditions specified in the text are met."&lt;SEP&gt;"An entity is identified as a CONSUMER within the context of being a party to a specific contract involving goods for private use or consumption."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;A PARTY TO A CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;AUCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An AUCTION is a specific type of SELLING CONTRACT, and thus an A PARTY TO A CONTRACT OF SALE can be involved in auctions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;A PARTY TO A CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An entity is identified as A PARTY TO A CONTRACT OF SALE within the context of a specific contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;A PARTY TO A CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business entities often engage as parties to a CONTRACT OF SALE, participating in commercial transactions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANOTHER PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ANOTHER PARTY is involved in the Contract of Sale as either buyer or seller depending on context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANOTHER PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;GOODS PASSING UNDER OR IN PURSUANCE OF THE CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ANOTHER PARTY may be involved with GOODS passing under or in pursuance of a contract, depending on their role as buyer or seller."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOTHER PARTY may have a role with GOODS passing under or in pursuance of the contract, depending on their position as buyer or seller."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANOTHER PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;SELLING CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ANOTHER PARTY can be a party to SELLING CONTRACTS, particularly when engaging in commercial activities as buyer or seller."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANOTHER PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business entities often interact with ANOTHER PARTY through various contracts and transactions involving goods or services."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS PASSING UNDER OR IN PURSUANCE OF THE CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The GOODS passing under or in pursuance of the CONTRACT OF SALE are central to defining and executing such contracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"The goods passing under or in pursuance of the contract are central to defining a Contract of Sale, especially when determining if a party deals as consumer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS PASSING UNDER OR IN PURSUANCE OF THE CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">24.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business entities often engage with GOODS passing under or in pursuance of contracts, especially when these goods involve commercial transactions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS PASSING UNDER OR IN PURSUANCE OF THE CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;CONSUMER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Consumers can be involved in the process of GOODS passing under or in pursuance of a contract, particularly when purchasing goods for personal use or consumption."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;SELLING CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A SELLING CONTRACT is a specific type of CONTRACT OF SALE that involves the transfer of property rights for consideration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business entities often engage in CONTRACT OF SALES as part of their commercial activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;SALE AND AGREEMENT TO SELL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'Sale and agreement to sell' refers to the broader concept of a contract of sale, which is defined in legal terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a93975688247d3b9e7a757c9ac99d011</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;FORMALITIES OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Formalities of contract are discussed in relation to contracts of sale, indicating their interconnection."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c537dc0fa7ed6ca01860ee51729f49a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;现货或期货&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The subject-matter of a contract of sale can include both spot goods and futures, which are defined as such."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c537dc0fa7ed6ca01860ee51729f49a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;有事件&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Events that may or may not occur can affect the ability to obtain goods in a contract of sale."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c537dc0fa7ed6ca01860ee51729f49a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;FACIE CALENDAR MONTH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'facie calendar month' is related to the context of contract of sale, indicating it might be used in legal or contractual documents dealing with timeframes for sales agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-777ee0ce7b06539972a14723dda21238</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;CONDITION TO BE TREATED AS WARRANTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Conditions within a contract of sale can potentially be treated as warranty clauses under certain circumstances, affecting the rights and obligations between buyer and seller."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-777ee0ce7b06539972a14723dda21238</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;CONDITION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Conditions in a contract of sale determine whether breaches are considered repudiations or warranties, and affect ownership liabilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6898f338d8c873d727625cb55234a222</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;REPUDIATED CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A condition in a sale contract can be treated as repudiation if breached, affecting ownership liabilities and buyer's actions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6898f338d8c873d727625cb55234a222</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;QUALITY OR FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The quality or fitness for a particular purpose is implied in a contract of sale unless specifically excluded."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;PARTICULAR PURPOSE FOR WHICH GOODS ARE BEING BOUGHT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The goods supplied under a contract of sale must reasonably fit for any particular purpose known to the buyer unless it is unreasonable for him to rely on the seller's skill or judgment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;SALE BY SAMPLE AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A sale by sample agreement is a specific type of contract of sale where there's an implied term about the correspondence between the goods and the sample."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7899f94c0b8fd41924e069cd239cc724</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;ANTECEDENT NEGOTIATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Antecedent negotiations may precede the formation of a contract of sale, including a sale by sample agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7899f94c0b8fd41924e069cd239cc724</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;QUALITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Quality and fitness for a particular purpose are implied conditions in contracts of sale, which include Sale by Sample Agreement specifically mentioned in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7899f94c0b8fd41924e069cd239cc724</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Under a contract of sale, the seller can maintain an action against the buyer for payment if they wrongfully neglect or refuse to pay according to terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c8e3424a8a5275e58cb410e4ea0f205</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The buyer's wrongful neglect or refusal to accept and pay for goods under a contract of sale allows the seller to sue them for damages due to non-acceptance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c8e3424a8a5275e58cb410e4ea0f205</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSUMER&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">25.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A CONSUMER is defined by their relationship with BUSINESS entities through contracts and transactions involving goods for private use or consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Business entities often interact with CONSUMERS through various contracts and transactions involving goods for private use or consumption."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSUMER&quot;" target="&quot;SELLING CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A CONSUMER can enter into SELLING CONTRACTS when purchasing goods for private use or consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Consumers can be involved in SELLING CONTRACTS when purchasing goods for personal use or consumption."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSUMER&quot;" target="&quot;DAMAGES FOR NEGLIGENCE OR BREACH OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Consumers do not need to compensate for the legal liabilities caused by others due to negligence or breach of contract, unless the contractual term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9caec393d81747f82a0bc36401fbbd53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSUMER&quot;" target="&quot;SALE OF GOODS ORDINANCE (CAP. 26)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Sale of Goods Ordinance (Cap. 26) defines the rights and liabilities of consumers in transactions involving goods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-872dd343c6e35c900d1e080217da3c6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSUMER&quot;" target="&quot;LIABILITY FOR BREACH OF OBLIGATION ARISING BY IMPLICATION OF LAW FROM THE NATURE OF THE CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Liability cannot be excluded or restricted against a person dealing as consumer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0093428c9e5c24b975d1827e057247c3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSUMER&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Consumer status is a key factor in determining the enforceability of arbitration agreements under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6a2e2728ed9206072fd11eab3f6ceb87</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSUMER&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitration agreement cannot be enforced against a consumer unless they give written consent after the differences have arisen or if they themselves have recourse to arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca4a2a9fbbaee42187b60b84f640f8f3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;" target="&quot;SELLING CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business entities are often parties to SELLING CONTRACTS, which can be part of their commercial activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Registered Chinese Medicine Practitioners operate within the broader scope of businesses providing healthcare services."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2a67530e0a9df975682238097b18b864</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business activities can involve contracts of employment as part of the operations or services provided by individuals or entities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fee7842314099c25edf5106ebd221850</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner for Labour oversees businesses and employment contracts, establishing an administrative relationship between them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fee7842314099c25edf5106ebd221850</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;" target="&quot;DANGEROUS DRUG&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Businesses may be involved in handling or selling dangerous drugs as part of their operations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fee7842314099c25edf5106ebd221850</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;" target="&quot;INDUSTRY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Industry and business operations are mentioned as contexts where employee absence due to strikes or lock-outs can be considered continuous employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-65134d6c88195bfcc2ac0100392eb0d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees are employed by a business, which may be taken over by its personal representative after the death of the deceased employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-85644a914cfa94d353943cc7d1724450</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPIERS' LIABILITY ORDINANCE (CAP. 314)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business includes public authorities, which may be subject to the general prudence obligations under the Occupiers' Liability Ordinance (Cap. 314), indicating a relationship between business and this ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-405702086caa260fb0fa6bf8fac677c3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;" target="&quot;SALE OF GOODS ORDINANCE (CAP. 26)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business is relevant to the Sale of Goods Ordinance (Cap. 26) as it pertains to contractual obligations, which are part of business operations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-405702086caa260fb0fa6bf8fac677c3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;" target="&quot;NEGLIGENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business operations can involve negligence as it pertains to the duties owed during business processes and interactions, thus linking these two concepts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-405702086caa260fb0fa6bf8fac677c3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPIERS LIABILITY ORDINANCE (CAP. 314)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of BUSINESS is relevant in the context of OCCUPiers Liability Ordinance as it defines obligations and duties related to business operations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ac6eb040e98e92757cf6e4d3f0473e64</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS&quot;" target="&quot;NEGLIGENCE (疏忽)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business activities, as defined by the Occupiers Liability Ordinance and Sale of Goods Ordinance, are subject to negligence claims under common law duties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Negligence can arise from business operations, as defined by the Occupiers Liability Ordinance and Sale of Goods Ordinance, impacting business liability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ac6eb040e98e92757cf6e4d3f0473e64</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUCTION&quot;" target="&quot;SELLING CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An AUCTION can be a form of SELLING CONTRACT, particularly when goods are sold competitively without regard to consumer status."&lt;SEP&gt;"An AUCTION is a specific type of SELLING CONTRACT, where the process involves competitive bidding to determine ownership of goods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d1ee5f65c2724b0bbf3ca9462ea1100b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUCTION&quot;" target="&quot;BIDDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A bidder can retract their bid before the hammer falls during an auction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-32292d53bc2adbfdb992bdf0fe946e4a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUCTION&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The seller is not allowed to bid at the auction, except where a right to bid is expressly reserved by or on behalf of the seller."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-32292d53bc2adbfdb992bdf0fe946e4a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUCTION&quot;" target="&quot;AUCTIONEER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The auctioneer announces the completion of an auction and may take bids from bidders but cannot bid for the seller."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-32292d53bc2adbfdb992bdf0fe946e4a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUCTION&quot;" target="&quot;BANKRUPTCY RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Bankruptcy rules continue to apply to the sale contract even if it is conducted by auction, and may affect the validity of the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-32292d53bc2adbfdb992bdf0fe946e4a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUCTION&quot;" target="&quot;COMMON LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Common law rules, including commercial law, continue to apply to the sale contract unless explicitly contradicted by this regulation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-32292d53bc2adbfdb992bdf0fe946e4a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE AND AGREEMENT TO SELL&quot;" target="&quot;AGREEMENT TO SELL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Sale and agreement to sell becomes an Agreement to sell when certain conditions are met or time elapses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a93975688247d3b9e7a757c9ac99d011</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CAPACITY TO BUY AND SELL&quot;" target="&quot;NECESSARIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The capacity to buy and sell is regulated by the law concerning necessaries for infants or minors."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c537dc0fa7ed6ca01860ee51729f49a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INFANT OR MINOR&quot;" target="&quot;NECESSARIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Infants or minors are required to pay reasonable prices for necessaries even if they lack full contractual capacity."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a93975688247d3b9e7a757c9ac99d011</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXISTING OR FUTURE GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTINGENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of future goods depends on a contingency which may or may not happen."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da0594a6faf073110e696a64d93f3508</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXISTING OR FUTURE GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT FOR SALE OF SPECIFIC GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Future goods are part of the broader category of contracts for sale, including both existing and future goods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da0594a6faf073110e696a64d93f3508</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXISTING OR FUTURE GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;RISK TRANSFER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Risk transfer plays a role in determining the status and effectiveness of contracts involving existing or future goods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da0594a6faf073110e696a64d93f3508</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS WHICH HAVE PERISHED&quot;" target="&quot;RISK TRANSFER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The validity of a contract for specific goods is affected by risk transfer when those goods perish before being sold."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da0594a6faf073110e696a64d93f3508</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RISK TRANSFER&quot;" target="&quot;AGREEMENT TO SELL SPECIFIC GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The agreement to sell specific goods becomes void if the goods perish before risk is transferred to the buyer due to no fault of either party."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7fbaa0d66e947840f2ec3483b78cc0fb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE PRICE&quot;" target="&quot;THIRD-PARTY VALUATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Third-party valuation can be used to determine a reasonable price in certain circumstances, but it's not always required or applicable."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7fbaa0d66e947840f2ec3483b78cc0fb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;SALE CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Third parties can be involved in the valuation process, which is related to the sale contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e2828dcd3a1acc333b703677e12c2630</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Third parties can be involved in legal procedures for compensation, as mentioned in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5264a8fa197e6ad59c59c71f8b3763e7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If an employee recovers damages against a third party, it affects compensation payable from the employer." "&lt;SEP&gt;"The EMPLOYEE can claim compensation from both the EMPLOYER and the THIRD PARTY for injuries caused by circumstances creating a legal liability in the THIRD PARTY to pay damages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8e72191ab4edd091f82585ac0b7be851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f8e345be219d3fc366dc62469796daf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OF FIRST INSTANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The third party can be sued in the COURT OF FIRST INSTANCE or DISTRICT COURT as per the provisions mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8e72191ab4edd091f82585ac0b7be851</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;DISTRICT COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similar to the COURTS of first instance, the THIRD PARTY can also face proceedings in the DISTRICT COURT based on jurisdiction limits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8e72191ab4edd091f82585ac0b7be851</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;INDEMNITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Indemnity rights are limited against a third party from whom an employee or legal representative may have recovered compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ddbe221813d2b91715360a8a16979bab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;COMMERCE ACTIVITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Commercial Activity leads to SALE CONTRACTS, which define the terms of risk and property transfer between SELLER and BUYER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENT TERMS&quot;" target="&quot;CALENDAR MONTH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Calendar months are relevant to payment terms as they define the time period for payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e2828dcd3a1acc333b703677e12c2630</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONDITIONS AND WARRANTIES CLAUSE&quot;" target="&quot;TIME STIPULATIONS CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both clauses deal with stipulations in a contract, specifically regarding conditions and timing of obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e2828dcd3a1acc333b703677e12c2630</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPUDIATED CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;OWNERSHIP LIABILITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Ownership liabilities are directly impacted by whether a contract is repudiated due to breaches, affecting legal actions and remedies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6898f338d8c873d727625cb55234a222</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OWNERSHIP LIABILITIES&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The seller is responsible for ensuring the goods have no undisclosed encumbrances before transfer of ownership, impacting potential legal excuses or warranty claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6898f338d8c873d727625cb55234a222</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OWNERSHIP LIABILITIES&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Buyer's acceptance of goods can limit their right to reject due to breaches by seller, affecting overall ownership liabilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6898f338d8c873d727625cb55234a222</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">33.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SELLER has control over the GOODS until specific terms of the contract or conditions are fulfilled."&lt;SEP&gt;"The SELLER is responsible for delivering GOODS as per the agreed quantity and quality in the contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"The seller delivers the goods to the buyer, which is a prerequisite for any acceptance or rejection by the buyer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The seller has a right to sell the goods and is responsible for any existing encumbrances that may affect their transfer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-535dface6286d8bede9ae8225e2d5326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34bc94419b349addb3ca3738887910de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09f76424c00042dab76ada9f73a18154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;SALE UNDER VOIDABLE TITLE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Goods can be sold under a voidable title, which affects the buyer's acquisition of ownership."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-097842d27813c438fcbfa56e8eef5ca4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER OR BUYER IN POSSESSION AFTER SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The seller or buyer in possession after sale continues to have control over the goods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2262a3a4061aab5ab97a1077b67a5057</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;COMMERCIAL AGENT (MERCANTILE AGENT)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A commercial agent can act on behalf of a seller or buyer regarding the goods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2262a3a4061aab5ab97a1077b67a5057</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;DOCUMENTS OF TITLE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Documents of title are related to the ownership and transfer of goods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2262a3a4061aab5ab97a1077b67a5057</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">40.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"BUYER purchases or receives GOODS, which may be subject to warranty conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Buyer may receive or reject goods, ending or continuing the duration of transit."&lt;SEP&gt;"The BUYER has the right to accept or reject the delivered GOODS based on their agreement with the SELLER."&lt;SEP&gt;"The BUYER is responsible for taking delivery of the GOODS, and if they neglect or refuse, they must bear legal responsibility for any losses incurred by the SELLER."&lt;SEP&gt;"The buyer accepts or rejects the delivered goods based on their examination and conformity with the contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-019dad10da4fa0e0f55e19465cb7641c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-535dface6286d8bede9ae8225e2d5326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69fc897b8b9dfae677db802b05a78337&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09f76424c00042dab76ada9f73a18154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3304fe02529acf61f5b7a297e0a498dd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER'S RIGHT OF STOPPING GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"This right allows the seller to resume possession of the goods during transportation if the buyer is insolvent."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a3460a8b3f83d1862f966932908fad7a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;DURATION OF TRANSIT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The duration of transit is directly related to the state and movement of goods during transportation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3304fe02529acf61f5b7a297e0a498dd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;SHIP CHARTERED BY THE BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ship chartered by the buyer is directly involved in transporting or holding goods, impacting duration of transit."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3304fe02529acf61f5b7a297e0a498dd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;AGENT OF THE BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Agent's actions in accepting or rejecting delivery can affect duration of transit for goods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3304fe02529acf61f5b7a297e0a498dd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;PLACE OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Goods may be inspected at the Place of Arbitration as part of arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;SALE OF GOODS ORDINANCE (CAP. 26)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"SALE OF GOODS ORDINANCE provides the definition for 'goods', which is relevant in understanding the context of BUSINESS activities involving goods transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The term 'goods' is defined by the Sale of Goods Ordinance (Cap. 26), indicating a direct relationship between them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ac6eb040e98e92757cf6e4d3f0473e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-405702086caa260fb0fa6bf8fac677c3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTY TRANSFER&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The buyer will have peaceful possession of the goods, subject to certain conditions regarding third-party claims or undisclosed encumbrances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTY TRANSFER&quot;" target="&quot;SALE BY SAMPLE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of 'sale by sample' implies an implied condition that the goods must correspond with the sample in quality and be free from defects, which directly relates to the transfer of property rights as discussed under Article 18 and beyond."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-57cd738c9ff0713f532a9b12760d5197</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IMPLIED CONDITION&quot;" target="&quot;TITLE GUARANTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"There is an implied condition that any existing encumbrances known by the seller but not disclosed to the buyer must be disclosed before property transfer, affecting title guarantee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IMPLIED CONDITION&quot;" target="&quot;SALE BY DESCRIPTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sale by description implies that goods must correspond with the description, which is a key condition in such sales."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5228b6166ae5f3bb9be72928713eb4f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SELLER'S RIGHTS&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER'S PEACEABLE POSSESSION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The seller's rights are crucial in ensuring the buyer can peacefully possess goods without interference from undisclosed encumbrances or third parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY CLAIMS&quot;" target="&quot;IMPLIED WARRANTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Third party claims, if not disclosed before property transfer, may affect the implied warranty of non-interference with peaceful possession by the buyer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTUAL INTENT&quot;" target="&quot;IMPLIED WARRANTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The contractual intent to sell only certain ownership rights implies an obligation for no interference in the buyer's peaceful possession unless based on disclosed encumbrances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IMPLIED WARRANTY&quot;" target="&quot;PROPERTY PASSING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The passing of property must be free from undisclosed encumbrances to uphold the implied warranty of non-interference with peaceful possession by the buyer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISCLOSURE REQUIREMENT&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL OBLIGATIONS OF SELLERS AND BUYERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both sellers and buyers have legal obligations, including disclosure requirements that affect their rights and responsibilities in property transfer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-65a567d66064fd14c157884db0005f2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISCLOSURE REQUIREMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATOR INDEPENDENCE AND IMPARTIALITY CONSIDERATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Disclosure requirements are in place to ensure transparency and prevent conflicts of interest, which is a key consideration for arbitrator independence and impartiality."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6cff72e41603eed38553fb4f306a008</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISCLOSURE REQUIREMENT&quot;" target="&quot;INDEPENDENCE AND IMPARTIALITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"There is a requirement for disclosure to ensure the independence and impartiality of the adjudicator regarding potential conflicts of interest."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-40b68681ecca6bd68067e789107e9bdc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IMPLIED CONDITION ON THE PART OF THE SELLER&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE WITH INTENTION TO TRANSFER ONLY SUCH TITLE AS A THIRD PERSON HAS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The implied condition on the part of the seller is relevant in a contract where there's an intention to transfer only such title as a third person may have."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7fc73f93b207fb939f0a65e3152d73dd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IMPLIED CONDITION ON THE PART OF THE SELLER&quot;" target="&quot;CHARGE OR ENCUMBRANCE DISCLOSURE REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The implied condition on the part of the seller, regarding his right to sell goods, is indirectly related to the disclosure requirement for charges or encumbrances since both are aspects of contract integrity and transparency."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7fc73f93b207fb939f0a65e3152d73dd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IMPLIED WARRANTY ON THE GOODS BEING FREE FROM CHARGE OR ENCUMBRANCE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE WITH INTENTION TO TRANSFER ONLY SUCH TITLE AS A THIRD PERSON HAS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The implied warranty that the goods are free from charge or encumbrance is relevant in a contract where there's an intention to transfer only such title as a third person may have, especially regarding disclosure requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7fc73f93b207fb939f0a65e3152d73dd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IMPLIED WARRANTY ON THE GOODS BEING FREE FROM CHARGE OR ENCUMBRANCE&quot;" target="&quot;CHARGE OR ENCUMBRANCE DISCLOSURE REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The implied warranty that the goods are free from charge or encumbrance is directly related to the requirement for disclosure of such charges or encumbrances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7fc73f93b207fb939f0a65e3152d73dd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE WITH INTENTION TO TRANSFER ONLY SUCH TITLE AS A THIRD PERSON HAS&quot;" target="&quot;CHARGE OR ENCUMBRANCE DISCLOSURE REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"In a contract where the seller intends to transfer only such title as a third person may have, there is an implied warranty that all known charges or encumbrances are disclosed before the contract is made."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7fc73f93b207fb939f0a65e3152d73dd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE BY DESCRIPTION&quot;" target="&quot;SAMPLE SALE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sales can be made both by description and sample; if they do not match, it does not suffice even if the bulk matches the sample."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5228b6166ae5f3bb9be72928713eb4f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE BY DESCRIPTION&quot;" target="&quot;QUALITY AND FITNESS FOR PURPOSE GUARANTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sale by description implies a guarantee of fitness for the purpose, but this is subject to conditions as stated."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5228b6166ae5f3bb9be72928713eb4f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE BY DESCRIPTION&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIFIC PURPOSE SUITABILITY GUARANTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sales made with specific purposes imply guarantees regarding suitability for those purposes, though these are limited by certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5228b6166ae5f3bb9be72928713eb4f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS OPERATION&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTUAL SUPPLY OF GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business Operation involves the Contractual Supply of Goods as a core activity."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-183ae686da520342fd44ebd9847a6fdf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS OPERATION&quot;" target="&quot;ECONOMIC HARDSHIP DUE TO COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Compliance with permit conditions may cause ECONOMIC HARDSHIP to the APPELLANT's BUSINESS OPERATIONS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c94f4e8cb6c69c21ed7b5db12f709e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTUAL SUPPLY OF GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIFIC PURPOSE GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contractual Supply of Goods may include goods with a specific purpose as part of the contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-183ae686da520342fd44ebd9847a6fdf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFIC PURPOSE GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The BUYER purchases Specific Purpose Goods for specific purposes, implying an implicit condition on suitability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-183ae686da520342fd44ebd9847a6fdf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 16&quot;" target="&quot;IMPLIED CONDITION OR WARRANTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 16 provides for circumstances and extent of implied conditions or warranties regarding quality or fitness for a particular purpose in goods supplied under a contract of sale."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abd61364920843014789da67b81b39a5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IMPLIED CONDITION OR WARRANTY&quot;" target="&quot;DEFECTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The section mentions exceptions to implied conditions where defects are specifically drawn to the buyer’s attention before the contract is made."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abd61364920843014789da67b81b39a5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IMPLIED CONDITION OR WARRANTY&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER’S KNOWLEDGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"There is an exception for implied conditions or warranties if the buyer's knowledge of specific defects exists prior to the contract being made."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abd61364920843014789da67b81b39a5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFECTS&quot;" target="&quot;CONSUMER USE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">11.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Consumer use of the goods can lead to identification and claims regarding defects, which in turn affect guarantee provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Defects occurring during consumer use are a key factor in determining the applicability of guarantee provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2333b3d2deec0b227d514b0090b44838</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFECTS SPECIFICALLY DRAWN TO THE BUYER'S ATTENTION BEFORE THE CONTRACT IS MADE&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER EXAMINES THE GOODS BEFORE THE CONTRACT IS MADE AND DEFECTS WHICH THAT EXAMINATION OUGHT TO REVEAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Defects specifically drawn to the buyer's attention or defects that should be revealed through examination are excluded from implied conditions of merchantable quality."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFECTS SPECIFICALLY DRAWN TO THE BUYER'S ATTENTION BEFORE THE CONTRACT IS MADE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT FOR SALE BY SAMPLE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"In a contract for sale by sample, defects that would be apparent on reasonable examination of the sample are excluded from implied conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;USAGE&quot;" target="&quot;SALE BY A PERSON WHO IN THE COURSE OF A BUSINESS IS ACTING AS AGENT FOR ANOTHER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Usage can imply conditions of quality or fitness for a particular purpose in sales by agents acting in business courses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE BY A PERSON WHO IN THE COURSE OF A BUSINESS IS ACTING AS AGENT FOR ANOTHER&quot;" target="&quot;PRINCIPAL IN THE COURSE OF A BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A principal in the course of a business is involved when an agent acts on their behalf, and implied conditions apply to such sales."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PURCHASE PRICE OR PART OF IT IS PAYABLE BY INSTALMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;ANTECEDENT NEGOTIATIONS (事先商议)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"In installment payments, antecedent negotiations can affect the application of implied conditions in a contract of sale."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50fde94b2a9530049fb2ca036b2e0622</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE BY SAMPLE AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ANTECEDENT NEGOTIATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">3.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Antecedent negotiations are not directly related to Sale by Sample Agreement as defined in the text, but both deal with contractual agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7899f94c0b8fd41924e069cd239cc724</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE BY SAMPLE AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;QUALITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sale by sample agreement implies quality and fitness for a particular purpose, specifically that the bulk shall correspond with the sample in quality."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7899f94c0b8fd41924e069cd239cc724</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANTECEDENT NEGOTIATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;QUALITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Antecedent negotiations can influence or lead to conditions regarding quality and fitness for a particular purpose in contracts of sale, but they are not directly implied by Sale by Sample Agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7899f94c0b8fd41924e069cd239cc724</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;確定意向的規則&quot;" target="&quot;規則1&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"規則1是確定意向的規則之一，用以處理不附帶條件的合約的情況。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c6c550597a3052a5b04c9cf13a1394b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;確定意向的規則&quot;" target="&quot;規則2&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"規則2也是確定意向的規則之一，適用於賣方需要對貨品進行某些處理後才轉移產權的情況。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c6c550597a3052a5b04c9cf13a1394b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;確定意向的規則&quot;" target="&quot;規則3&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"規則3同樣是確定意向的規則的一部分，用以處理賣方需稱量、量度等特定動作後才能轉移產權的情形。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c6c550597a3052a5b04c9cf13a1394b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;確定意向的規則&quot;" target="&quot;規則4&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"規則4也是確定意向的規則之一，適用於按有待同意或'售賣或退回'原則交付貨品的情況。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c6c550597a3052a5b04c9cf13a1394b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;移給買方&quot;" target="&quot;合理時間&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"合理時間定義了貨品產權轉移的期限，若無明確期限則為一段合理時間。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4919d9417efe70a24558dc1ea463f973</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;合理時間&quot;" target="&quot;規則5. (1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"規則5. (1) 中提到合理時間是確定貨品產權轉移期限的一個因素。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4919d9417efe70a24558dc1ea463f973</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;合理時間&quot;" target="&quot;規則5. (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"規則5. (2) 也涉及到合理時間的概念，用於界定某些情況下的產權轉移。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4919d9417efe70a24558dc1ea463f973</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;規則5. (1)&quot;" target="&quot;規則5. (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"兩條規則都涉及貨品產權的轉移條件和方式，但細節有所不同。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4919d9417efe70a24558dc1ea463f973</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;規則5. (1)&quot;" target="&quot; RULE 1.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"規則5. (1) 和 RULE 1 都描述了在特定情況下貨品產權如何轉移到買方的條件和方式，兩者有相似性。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4919d9417efe70a24558dc1ea463f973</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;規則5. (2)&quot;" target="&quot;RULE 2.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"規則5. (2) 和 RULE 2 都描述了在特定情況下貨品產權如何轉移到買方的條件和方式，兩者有相似性。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4919d9417efe70a24558dc1ea463f973</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RULE 2.&quot;" target="&quot; RULE 1.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"兩條規則都涉及貨品產權的轉移問題，但具体内容和应用场景有所不同。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4919d9417efe70a24558dc1ea463f973</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RULE 2&quot;" target="&quot;UNASCERTAINED OR FUTURE GOODS BY DESCRIPTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rule 2 discusses conditions under which property in unascertained or future goods by description passes to the buyer, implying a relationship with Rule 5(1). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e602b76f9699cca512b4176568443c48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RULE 3&quot;" target="&quot;APPROPRIATION OF GOODS TO THE CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both rules deal with when property in specific goods passed to the buyer after certain actions are taken. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e602b76f9699cca512b4176568443c48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RULE 4&quot;" target="&quot;APPROPRIATION OF GOODS TO THE CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rule 4 discusses conditions under which property passes to the buyer upon approval or acceptance, relating to appropriation of goods for sale or return terms. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e602b76f9699cca512b4176568443c48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RULE 5 (1)&quot;" target="&quot;UNASCERTAINED OR FUTURE GOODS BY DESCRIPTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rule 5(1) directly addresses unascertained or future goods by description and their property passing, making a clear relationship with the entity name. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e602b76f9699cca512b4176568443c48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RULE 5 (1)&quot;" target="&quot; RULE 4 &quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rule 4 discusses approval or acceptance, while Rule 5(1) talks about unconditional appropriation of future goods by description. Both relate to property passing conditions. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e602b76f9699cca512b4176568443c48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RULE 5 (2)&quot;" target="&quot;APPROPRIATION OF GOODS TO THE CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similar to Rule 4, this part discusses appropriation of goods for the contract, relating to when property passes to the buyer. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e602b76f9699cca512b4176568443c48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNASCERTAINED OR FUTURE GOODS BY DESCRIPTION&quot;" target="&quot;保留貨品處置權&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Chinese term '保留貨品處置權' refers to retaining rights over unascertained or future goods, indicating a relationship with Rule 5(1). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e602b76f9699cca512b4176568443c48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CARRIER&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SELLER may deliver SPECIFIC GOODS to a CARRIER for transmission to the BUYER, depending on contractual arrangements and rights reserved by the SELLER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-08fbcc9c2ce9e3d4f773cc495db19495</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CARRIER&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CARRIER is responsible for transmitting GOODS from the SELLER or BAILEE to the BUYER according to the CONTRACT's stipulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-08fbcc9c2ce9e3d4f773cc495db19495</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CARRIER&quot;" target="&quot;BILL OF LADING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CARRIER is responsible for transmitting GOODS according to the instructions on the BILL OF LADING and may be involved in transferring ownership contingent on conditions set forth by the SELLER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-08fbcc9c2ce9e3d4f773cc495db19495</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CARRIER&quot;" target="&quot;DURATION OF TRANSIT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The carrier's actions determine when the duration of transit ends based on delivery or refusal of goods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3304fe02529acf61f5b7a297e0a498dd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BAILEE&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SELLER can also deliver SPECIFIC GOODS to a BAILEE (not necessarily named by the BUYER), for transmission to the BUYER, contingent on contractual terms and rights reserved by the SELLER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-08fbcc9c2ce9e3d4f773cc495db19495</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BAILEE&quot;" target="&quot;UNPAID SELLER'S LIEN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similar to being an agent, the UNPAID SELLER'S LIEN also applies when the seller is a bailee for the buyer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-83a8d937e2b926da0d7047a5288d8ae8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RESERVATION OF RIGHT OF DISPOSAL&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The RESERVATION OF RIGHT OF DISPOSAL affects property transfer from SELLER to BUYER, as it determines whether the delivery of GOODS by CARRIER or BAILEE transfers ownership."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-08fbcc9c2ce9e3d4f773cc495db19495</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BILL OF LADING&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The BILL OF LADING is used in shipping and can indicate that the SELLER retains disposal rights over SPECIFIC GOODS until certain conditions are met, even after delivery to a CARRIER or BAILEE for transmission."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-08fbcc9c2ce9e3d4f773cc495db19495</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BILL OF LADING&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SELLER may use the BILL OF LADING as evidence of their right to dispose of SPECIFIC GOODS under the terms of the CONTRACT, even after delivery to a CARRIER or BAILEE for transmission."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-08fbcc9c2ce9e3d4f773cc495db19495</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTY IN THE GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Property in the goods has passed to the seller, allowing them legal standing to claim payment under a contract of sale or damages if not accepted by buyer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c8e3424a8a5275e58cb410e4ea0f205</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTY IN THE GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The buyer's wrongful neglect or refusal to accept and pay for goods where property in the goods has passed allows the seller to sue them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c8e3424a8a5275e58cb410e4ea0f205</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;風險表面與產權同時轉移&quot;" target="&quot;RISK &quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Risk and property transfer are linked; when property transfers, risk typically follows. However, there can be exceptions based on contract terms or fault of the parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34bc94419b349addb3ca3738887910de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;貨品&quot;" target="&quot;-BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"買方在特定條件下可以拒絕承認承運人的交付，並要求賠償損失。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c162b772c9e897f69948d67d21519288</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTY IN THE GOODS (CHINESE)&quot;" target="&quot;RISK &quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Property in the GOODS transfers to BUYER when certain conditions are met, but RISK shifts from SELLER to BUYER upon this transfer. Otherwise, RISK remains with SELLER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34bc94419b349addb3ca3738887910de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTY IN THE GOODS (CHINESE)&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"BUYER gains property rights in the GOODS upon fulfillment of seller's conditions, at which point RISK shifts to BUYER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34bc94419b349addb3ca3738887910de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTY&quot;" target="&quot;RISK ASSUMPTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Property transfer determines who bears RISK for the GOODS; delay faults can shift this responsibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTY&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL AUTHORITY TO SELL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal authority over property determines who can sell GOODS; this is subject to ownership rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTY&quot;" target="&quot;PLACE OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Property can also be examined or inspected at the Place of Arbitration during arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTY&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Property is relevant for arbitral proceedings as defined by the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SELLER'S AUTHORITY TO SELL&quot;" target="&quot;OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The authority to sell goods is contingent upon whether the SELLER has OWNER's consent or not, and if the owner acts in a way that precludes denial of such authority."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OWNER&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIMING PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CLAIMING PARTY notifies the OWNER of their intention to delay construction or supply, indicating communication between parties involved in the contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"The claiming party must notify the owner of their intention to delay work or supply under section 59(2)(c)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-89690e148d95bff497042548ed9e3555&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a39eb07c8451fb1542c2fcc4877cecdf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OWNER&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The owner is notified of the claimant's intention to delay carrying out the construction work or supplying related goods and services under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7d229505b95cc3e576d9ad034318c66d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;PERIODICAL PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Court Orders can alter the intervals at which Periodical Payments are made, but not exceeding 1 month."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bad177b227e380cc066abb25e6c2cf7d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT ON TERMINATION (SECTION 25)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Payment on termination can be subject to court orders as mentioned in the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0b0b8e9edfab8c32d5cea9270e6f74ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 32&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court order may be relevant in deductions under SECTION 32, indicating a potential interaction between the two sections."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c9335a6eed209eaa686a730c45ba54a5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;EMERGENCY ARBITRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Emergency relief granted by an emergency arbitrator can be enforced as if it were a court order."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1ad963d62d75768847794433df9caf4b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SURFACE OWNERSHIP&quot;" target="&quot;TRUE OWNERSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Surface Ownership may differ from True Ownership, affecting the legal authority and risk assumption in sales transactions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL AUTHORITY TO SELL&quot;" target="&quot;TITLE TRANSFER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal Authority to Sell is necessary for a valid TITLE TRANSFER of GOODS; this affects RISK ASSUMPTION."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RISK ASSUMPTION&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL REGULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal Regulations govern how RISKS are assumed in commercial transactions; they can affect who bears responsibility for delayed delivery faults."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RISK ASSUMPTION&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal Compliance is crucial for proper RISK ASSUMPTION in commercial transactions; it ensures that all parties adhere to legal standards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMERCE LAW&quot;" target="&quot;COMMERCIAL TRANSACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Compliance with COMMERCE LAW ensures the validity and legality of COMMERCIAL TRANSACTIONS involving GOODS, including risk transfer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-651eb52af9704a88467e396e9e0d7166</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL PROVISION&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE DISMISSAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal provisions, such as Sections 9, 10, 31R, 31RA, and 31T of the relevant acts, define conditions under which an employee can be dismissed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL COMPLIANCE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENTS AND OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal compliance is a key aspect of managing and reporting workplace accidents and occupational diseases as per the regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal compliance is required for reporting and managing workplace accidents and occupational diseases as per the regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL COMPLIANCE&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational Safety Officers ensure legal compliance in their oversight of workplace accidents and occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL COMPLIANCE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE RIGHTS AND PROTECTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal compliance ensures that employees' rights and protections are upheld, including provisions for dismissal and re-engagement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL COMPLIANCE&quot;" target="&quot;LABOR REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Labor regulations ensure compliance with laws and standards for employers and employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-adbe757d90ad335b39fd280c5f650025</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL COMPLIANCE&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT DISPUTE RESOLUTION MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both LEGAL COMPLIANCE and PAYMENT DISPUTE RESOLUTION MECHANISM are critical in ensuring that payment disputes are handled appropriately, adhering to legal standards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-98b9cc96db8e2ffdc374754939531431</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORS ORDINANCE (CAP. 48)&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The FACTORS ORDINANCE (Cap. 48) is an enabling legislation that allows the apparent owner of goods to dispose of them as if he were the true owner, which may affect the provisions of this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-097842d27813c438fcbfa56e8eef5ca4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SHOP OR MARKET&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC MARKET&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both SHOP OR MARKET and PUBLIC MARKET refer to places where goods are sold, but the latter specifically refers to a public setting in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-097842d27813c438fcbfa56e8eef5ca4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SHOP OR MARKET&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Buys made in SHOP OR MARKET are subject to this Ordinance and related laws regarding ownership acquisition."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-097842d27813c438fcbfa56e8eef5ca4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT OF COMPETENT JURISDICTION&quot;" target="&quot;VOIDABLE TITLE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A court of competent jurisdiction may validate or invalidate titles that are voidable according to this Ordinance and related laws."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-097842d27813c438fcbfa56e8eef5ca4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC MARKET&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER'S VOIDABLE TITLE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sales in a PUBLIC MARKET can be affected by the SELLER's voidable title, as buyers must act in good faith without notice of such defects."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-097842d27813c438fcbfa56e8eef5ca4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VOIDABLE TITLE&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SELLER may have a voidable title, which affects the buyer's ability to acquire good title for goods sold."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-097842d27813c438fcbfa56e8eef5ca4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PLEDGE OR OTHER DISPOSALS&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER'S DEFECTIVE TITLE KNOWLEDGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text discusses the impact of a seller's defective title knowledge on pledges or other disposals, indicating that ignorance of such defects by the buyer can affect legal outcomes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a502d54239df6738cd72e46d8d4377e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SELLER OR BUYER IN POSSESSION AFTER SALE&quot;" target="&quot;DOCUMENTS OF TITLE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The seller or buyer in possession after sale also has documents of title related to the goods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2262a3a4061aab5ab97a1077b67a5057</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SELLER OR BUYER IN POSSESSION AFTER SALE&quot;" target="&quot;COMMERCIAL AGENT (MERCANTILE AGENT)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The actions of a commercial agent acting for a seller or buyer in possession after sale are considered as if authorized by the owner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2262a3a4061aab5ab97a1077b67a5057</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SELLER OR BUYER IN POSSESSION AFTER SALE&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A person who buys goods from another can be treated similarly to a seller or buyer in possession after sale under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2262a3a4061aab5ab97a1077b67a5057</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SELLER OR BUYER IN POSSESSION AFTER SALE&quot;" target="&quot;LIEN OR OTHER RIGHT OF THE ORIGINAL SELLER IN RESPECT OF THE GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The rights of the original seller can affect the actions of a seller or buyer in possession after sale regarding the goods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2262a3a4061aab5ab97a1077b67a5057</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MERCANTILE AGENT (商業代理人)&quot;" target="&quot;GOODS OR DOCUMENTS OF TITLE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Documents or title deeds are considered as if a mercantile agent is in possession with owner's consent under good faith and without notice of any lien or other right."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MERCANTILE AGENT (商業代理人)&quot;" target="&quot;FACTORS ORDANCE (CAP. 48)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'mercantile agent' in Factors Ordinance has the same meaning as defined by Cap. 48."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS OR DOCUMENTS OF TITLE&quot;" target="&quot;OWNERSHIP TRANSFER (所有权转移)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Documents of title can be transferred to a person who receives them in good faith and without notice, thus transferring ownership."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS OR DOCUMENTS OF TITLE&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER ACCEPTANCE RESPONSIBILITY (买家接受责任)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The buyer's acceptance responsibility is tied to receiving goods or documents of title in good faith and without notice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS OR DOCUMENTS OF TITLE&quot;" target="&quot;SALE CONTRACT (售賣合同)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Goods or documents of title are part of the sale contract and its terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE AGREEMENT (售賣合約)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT PERFORMANCE (合同履行)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The sale agreement terms dictate the performance of contract, including delivery and payment obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE AGREEMENT (售賣合約)&quot;" target="&quot;HONG KONG LEGISLATION (香港立法)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sale agreements are governed by Hong Kong legislation including the Factors Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DELIVERY OF GOODS (交付貨品)&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT FOR GOODS (支付貨價)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Payment for goods is a concurrent condition with the delivery of goods as per their agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DELIVERY OF GOODS (交付貨品)&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The seller is responsible for delivering goods as per their agreement with the buyer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DELIVERY OF GOODS (交付貨品)&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Buyers are responsible for accepting and paying for the delivery of goods in accordance with sale agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;POSSESSION TRANSFER (管有交予)&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Buyer's acceptance responsibility includes receiving possession transfer from seller as per agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERFORMANCE OF CONTRACT (合同的履行)&quot;" target="&quot;SALE AGREEMENT TERMS (售賣合約條款)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The terms and conditions agreed upon in a sale agreement are crucial for contract performance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE AGREEMENT TERMS (售賣合約條款)&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">36.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Buyers are bound by the sale agreement terms, including acceptance and payment obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Buyers are bound by the terms and conditions agreed in the sale contract, including payment responsibilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Buyers are obligated to adhere to the terms and conditions agreed in the sale contract, including acceptance responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE AGREEMENT TERMS (售賣合約條款)&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sellers must adhere to the terms of sale agreements for delivery and payment obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OWNERSHIP TRANSFER (所有权转移)&quot;" target="&quot;GOOD FAITH TRANSFER (善意转让)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Ownership transfer is valid if the transfer is made in good faith without notice of any lien or other right by the original seller."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OWNER CONSENT (所有人同意)&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Seller's delivery readiness is subject to owner consent as per good faith transfer rules."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENT OBLIGATION (付款义务)&quot;" target="&quot;GOODS DELIVERY PREPARATION (货物交付准备)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both payment obligation and goods delivery preparation are necessary conditions for completing a sale agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENT OBLIGATION (付款义务)&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Buyers have a duty to pay according to the agreed terms in the sale agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS DELIVERY PREPARATION (货物交付准备)&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sellers must prepare for goods delivery as part of their obligations under the sale agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUYER ACCEPTANCE RESPONSIBILITY (买家接受责任)&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER'S DELIVERY READINESS (卖方交付准备度)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The seller must be ready to deliver and the buyer must accept, both are essential for contract performance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENT FOR GOODS PROCESS (货物付款流程)&quot;" target="&quot;CONCURRENT CONDITIONS (同时履行的条件)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Payment and delivery of goods must be performed simultaneously as per the concurrent condition clause."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENT FOR GOODS PROCESS (货物付款流程)&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">24.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sellers must prepare for payment processes as part of delivering goods according to their agreement terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sellers must prepare for the payment process as part of delivering goods according to their agreement with buyers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The seller must prepare for the payment process as part of delivering goods according to their agreement terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DELIVERY RULES&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER'S PLACE OF BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The rules establish the seller's place of business as a key reference point for determining where deliveries should take place, especially when no other agreement is specified between buyer and seller."&lt;SEP&gt;"The rules specify that unless otherwise agreed, the seller's place of business is the default location for delivering goods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-048787341fb4d01340940003ad08182c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DELIVERY RULES&quot;" target="&quot;THIRD PARTY POSSESSION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The rules address scenarios where goods are in third-party possession and outline conditions under which such possessions do not interfere with the seller's responsibilities regarding delivery."&lt;SEP&gt;"The rules provide clarity on how to handle situations where goods are under third-party control during transactions, ensuring that these circumstances do not nullify or alter standard delivery procedures unless specifically agreed upon by all parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-048787341fb4d01340940003ad08182c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SELLER'S PLACE OF BUSINESS&quot;" target="&quot;THIRD PARTY POSSESSION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">11.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If goods are in third-party possession and not delivered to the buyer by the seller, this does not affect the seller's obligation related to their place of business for delivery unless specifically acknowledged by the third party."&lt;SEP&gt;"While the seller’s place of business is typically used for deliveries, if goods are in third-party possession, this does not change the fundamental rules governing delivery and ownership transfer unless explicitly acknowledged by the third party."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-048787341fb4d01340940003ad08182c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SELLER'S PLACE OF BUSINESS&quot;" target="&quot;THIRD PERSON&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The place of delivery is the seller's place of business if he has one; otherwise, his residence. This implies that a third person might hold goods on behalf of the seller."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d46459d50da26f6edb3bcb2bd876ab7d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE TIME&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER'S EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Expenses related to putting the goods into deliverable state must be borne by the seller within a reasonable time, which is determined based on facts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d46459d50da26f6edb3bcb2bd876ab7d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE TIME&quot;" target="&quot;CONTROL OF EXEMPTION CLAUSES ORDINANCE (CAP. 71)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Control of Exemption Clauses Ordinance does not define what constitutes a reasonable time in legal disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5c4b0005d3a0274c239ac28577960774</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE TIME&quot;" target="&quot;RIGHT, ETC., CAN BE ENFORCED THROUGH LITIGATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rights and responsibilities can be enforced through litigation, including the determination of what is considered a reasonable time."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5c4b0005d3a0274c239ac28577960774</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE TIME&quot;" target="&quot;HONG KONG IDENTITY CARD NUMBER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Records containing Hong Kong Identity Card numbers are to be kept for a reasonable time, typically 12 months after each accounting period ends."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-067e7bd64c7c5b9cd0bc7a9d57842457</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE TIME&quot;" target="&quot;ACCOUNTING PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Accounting periods are relevant for determining the reasonable time within which records should be kept."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-067e7bd64c7c5b9cd0bc7a9d57842457</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE TIME&quot;" target="&quot;NON-RESIDENT APPLICANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Non-resident applicants' records must be kept for a reasonable time as per the regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-067e7bd64c7c5b9cd0bc7a9d57842457</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE TIME&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner can enter and inspect places of business at any reasonable time without a warrant."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ee0cf79121cc26199f0bf5c4d14a8ce8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE TIME&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers authorized by the Commissioner can also enter and inspect places of business at any reasonable time without a warrant."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ee0cf79121cc26199f0bf5c4d14a8ce8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE TIME&quot;" target="&quot;INSPECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Inspections can occur at any reasonable time without a warrant or hand order, indicating flexibility in inspection procedures during normal business hours."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ee0cf79121cc26199f0bf5c4d14a8ce8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE TIME&quot;" target="&quot;SIN行&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both 'reasonable time' applies to inspections during investigations, indicating a common context where these terms are used."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-409891bfe2bfb21a0731ddceffe7a7d6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE TIME&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT AGENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Reasonable time is specified for inspections of employment agencies' places of business."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-409891bfe2bfb21a0731ddceffe7a7d6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE TIME&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER AUTHORIZED BY HIM IN THAT BEHALF OR ANY POLICE OFFICER NOT BELOW THE RANK OF INSPECTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers and police have the authority to enter premises at any reasonable time for investigations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-409891bfe2bfb21a0731ddceffe7a7d6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SELLER'S EXPENSES&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT RATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The expenses for putting the goods into a deliverable state must be borne by the seller unless otherwise agreed upon in terms of the contract rate."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d46459d50da26f6edb3bcb2bd876ab7d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUYER'S REFUSAL OF GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER'S OVER-DELIVERY HANDLING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If the seller over-delivers, the buyer can accept part or all of the goods and pay according to the contract rate; otherwise, they may refuse delivery."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d46459d50da26f6edb3bcb2bd876ab7d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT RATE&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If the BUYER accepts the delivery, they must pay for it at the CONTRACT RATE specified in the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-09f76424c00042dab76ada9f73a18154</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;USAGE OF TRADE&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SELLER's actions are subject to any industry usage of trade or special agreements with the BUYER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-09f76424c00042dab76ada9f73a18154</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERIODIC DELIVERY&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The BUYER may not be required to accept goods delivered in installments unless specifically agreed upon in the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-09f76424c00042dab76ada9f73a18154</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DELIVERY BY INSTALMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;交付承運人&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both terms refer to the process of delivering goods in installments and involve similar legal considerations regarding contract breaches."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d7711a5fb09f26ba7ae910773ed7d5cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RISK OF DETERIORATION&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If the seller fails to notify the buyer for insurance, the risk of deterioration during sea transit is on the buyer."&lt;SEP&gt;"In the absence of agreement, the risk of deterioration during sea transit remains on the seller until proper notice is given to the buyer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The risk of deterioration during sea transit falls on the buyer, not the seller unless otherwise agreed upon."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19b288c9efaa7bb08b81764887c880c5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEA TRANSIT&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">22.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"During sea transit, the buyer bears the risk of goods deteriorating if the seller fails to notify them in time for insurance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The buyer must take any risk of deterioration necessarily incident to the course of transit unless otherwise agreed upon by both parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"The buyer's acceptance or rejection of goods after examination can affect their responsibility for risks incurred during transit."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19b288c9efaa7bb08b81764887c880c5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISTANT PLACE DELIVERY RISK&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If the seller agrees to deliver at a distant place and bear the risk, it shifts from the buyer but is still subject to transit risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"If the seller agrees to deliver at a distant place, they initially bear the risk but this can be transferred based on agreement terms and conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"When goods are delivered at a distant place, the seller bears the initial risk but this can be transferred based on agreement terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19b288c9efaa7bb08b81764887c880c5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RIGHT OF EXAMINING GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">27.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The buyer has the right to examine goods upon delivery to ensure they meet contractual specifications."&lt;SEP&gt;"The buyer's right of examining goods is essential for verifying compliance with contractual agreements before acceptance or rejection."&lt;SEP&gt;"The buyer's right to examine goods is crucial for ensuring compliance with contractual agreements and acceptance of delivered items."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19b288c9efaa7bb08b81764887c880c5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ACCEPTANCE&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The buyer's actions and communications determine whether they accept or reject the delivered goods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-535dface6286d8bede9ae8225e2d5326</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXAMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;SELLER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The seller is indirectly related to the examination process as it involves delivering goods that may be examined by the buyer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-535dface6286d8bede9ae8225e2d5326</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXAMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;BUYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The buyer's opportunity for reasonable inspection of goods affects their acceptance or rejection based on conformity with contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-535dface6286d8bede9ae8225e2d5326</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)&quot;" target="&quot;REPLACED 85 OF 1994 S. 6&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text of SUBSECTION (1) is part of the legal framework that has been replaced by a specific section, indicating its historical context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)&quot;" target="&quot;INSURANCE POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The amount required by SUBSECTION (1) is ascertained based on the number of employees covered under the insurance policy."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-37d1a5d83703c47f3bc06048ecc6e08a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)&quot;" target="&quot;AN EMPLOYER WHO CONTRAVENES SUBSECTION (1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer who contravenes the obligations under Subsection (1) commits an offense."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8565a0dde3a6e724288267c5d06fe0dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)&quot;" target="&quot;47 OF 1995 S. 4&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (1) is added by Section 4 of Act No. 47 of 1995."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8565a0dde3a6e724288267c5d06fe0dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (1) specifies that employers must ensure workplace conditions are safe and without risks to health."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8903577fbeb26a0f144927da3a1efb7c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31D(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The application of SUBSECTION (1) is related to the circumstances mentioned in SECTION 31D(2), where the employee's contract is not renewed or re-engaged."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d33baa15beb160832b6e2302162f04d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)&quot;" target="&quot;REDUNDANCY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (1) leads to a situation of redundancy as defined by the non-renewal and non-reengagement of an employee's contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d33baa15beb160832b6e2302162f04d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (2)(a) addresses false statements made by employers, which is related to the requirements set out in subsection (1). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-82a3bfa1b02f074277b3b1a27f3afcb2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (3) provides a remedy for non-compliance with the statement requirement of subsection (1). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-82a3bfa1b02f074277b3b1a27f3afcb2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)&quot;" target="&quot;第(2)款&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The relationship between SUBSECTION (1) and 第(2)款 is that the former sets a general rule which the latter specifies or modifies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6401943df7f64de20cb83d590f559418</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)&quot;" target="&quot;第40条&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"According to SUBSECTION (1), no payment of holiday pay payable under section 40, or other sum, shall be made in lieu of the grant of a holiday. This indicates that there is a relationship between them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6401943df7f64de20cb83d590f559418</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)&quot;" target="&quot;第39(2)、(2A)或(3)条&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The rule set by SUBSECTION (1) also applies to the holidays granted as an alternative holiday or substituted holiday under section 39(2), (2A) or (3)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6401943df7f64de20cb83d590f559418</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (5)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 5's application is conditional on the conditions specified in Section 1."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-13ee9a92c0574802dd2767b6923aabc1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OR A MAGISTRATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Courts or magistrates may order the disclosure of information related to complaints as mentioned in SUBSECTION (1). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f10185e6fc563260f4e1f20ab8c394fc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)&quot;" target="&quot;ENFORCEMENT BY OR AGAINST THE PERSONAL REPRESENTATIVES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (1) states how enforcement can occur by or against a party's personal representatives after their death."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)&quot;" target="&quot;REPLACED 85 OF 1994 S. 6&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text of SUBSECTION (2) is part of the legal framework that has been replaced by a specific section, indicating its historical context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)&quot;" target="&quot;THE SAID ACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The action referred to in SUBSECTION (2) is the one where no damages shall be recoverable."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5368f346dbcfde8d0b6c8190b98be08d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)&quot;" target="&quot;STATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (2) excludes employment by or under the State from certain provisions, indicating a relationship with STATE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2f93037749b5c82c21a4dffe24495861</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer who contravenes SUBSECTION (1) commits an offence under SUBSECTION (2), impacting employee's employment liability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-37d1a5d83703c47f3bc06048ecc6e08a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)&quot;" target="&quot;AN EMPLOYER WHO CONTRAVENES SUBSECTION (1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (2) elaborates on the penalties for contravening Subsection (1)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8565a0dde3a6e724288267c5d06fe0dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)&quot;" target="&quot;SAFETY AND HEALTH AT WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (2) elaborates on the specific duties of employers in ensuring safety and health at work, including plant maintenance, information provision, and workplace conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8903577fbeb26a0f144927da3a1efb7c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The date specified for the purpose of subsection (2) can be related to termination of employment, as per SUBSECTION (2B)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9dc495e2347a322a5aaa3ff390e7601c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"subsection (2)'s content provides a parallel scenario to subsection (3), but for partnerships rather than corporations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-13ee9a92c0574802dd2767b6923aabc1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)&quot;" target="&quot;PART X&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (2) provides details on how employers can comply with Part X by keeping specific records and forms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f15fe91e28bec496f95bc0e2d20ab50c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (5)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The conditions for unreasonable delay under SUBSECTION (2) are related to the existence of an arbitral tribunal as specified in SUBSECTION (5). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 60 (1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The commands under SECTION 60(1) are related to the conditions for unreasonable delay as specified in SUBSECTION (2). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 60 (4)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The reasons for refusing commands under SECTION 60(4) are related to the conditions of unreasonable delay as stated in SUBSECTION (2). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)&quot;" target="&quot;REPLACED 85 OF 1994 S. 6&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text of SUBSECTION (3) is part of the legal framework that has been replaced by a specific section, indicating its historical context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)&quot;" target="&quot;ISSUE OF THE CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The issue of the certificate is directly related to the receipt and processing of an objection made by either the employer, employee, or ECAFB according to subsection (3). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9d232c4c17f319179e61e9fe9f748ce7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)&quot;" target="&quot;1992 S. 9&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (3) was amended by section 9 of Act 63 of 1992."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-baa998ea27b6baa036c2807f3cddf020</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)&quot;" target="&quot;76 OF 1982 S. 14&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (3) was added by section 14 of Act 76 of 1982."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-baa998ea27b6baa036c2807f3cddf020</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)&quot;" target="&quot;36 OF 1996 S. 13&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 13 of Act 36 of 1996 repealed subsection (3)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-baa998ea27b6baa036c2807f3cddf020</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)&quot;" target="&quot;36 OF 1996 S. 14&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 14 of Act 36 of 1996 repealed the provisions related to subsection (3)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-baa998ea27b6baa036c2807f3cddf020</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)&quot;" target="&quot;36 OF 1996 S. 15&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 15 of Act 36 of 1996 also repealed the provisions related to subsection (3)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-baa998ea27b6baa036c2807f3cddf020</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)&quot;" target="&quot;WORKING ENVIRONMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (3) addresses the employer's responsibility for maintaining a safe working environment, which is part of safety and health at work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8903577fbeb26a0f144927da3a1efb7c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 15F&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (3) provides the period for leave entitlement under SECTION 15F."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7f18d7b28f469093dbda2666fad1b8f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)&quot;" target="&quot;LEAVE PERIOD FOR CONFINEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (3) defines the leave period for each confinement of a child born after specific dates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7f18d7b28f469093dbda2666fad1b8f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OR A MAGISTRATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Courts or magistrates may also order the disclosure of secrets or processes as stated in SUBSECTION (3). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f10185e6fc563260f4e1f20ab8c394fc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (3) involves the reduction of long service payment in relation to certain gratuities or benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b785a6d2d7fe1aa9d111846965f88378</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (4)&quot;" target="&quot;REPLACED 85 OF 1994 S. 6&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text of SUBSECTION (4) is part of the legal framework that has been replaced by a specific section, indicating its historical context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (4)&quot;" target="&quot;DETERMINATION BY COMMISSIONER OF CLAIMS FOR COMPENSATION IN FATAL CASES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The family members under Subsection (4) can apply for the determination of claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2914073de37bf0e7df21cb9ca18483a2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (4)&quot;" target="&quot;THE SAID ACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (4) further elaborates the action mentioned in SUBSECTION (2)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5368f346dbcfde8d0b6c8190b98be08d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (4)&quot;" target="&quot;1982年第76号第21条&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (4) is based on Article 21 of Act No.76, 1982."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5368f346dbcfde8d0b6c8190b98be08d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (4)&quot;" target="&quot;1945 C. 28 S. 2(2) U.K.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (4) is based on Section 2 of Act No.28, 1945."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5368f346dbcfde8d0b6c8190b98be08d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (4)&quot;" target="&quot;NOISE ABATEMENT NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (4) allows The Authority to cancel or vary requirements in a noise abatement notice by serving another notice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (4)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31C(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (4) provides the framework for how Section 31C(2)'s provisions apply when a new owner makes an offer to renew or re-engage employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92eb9fce002800330c9f680d468f081b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (4)&quot;" target="&quot;U.K. LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (4)'s provisions are part of U.K. law that governs how contract renewals and re-engagements should be handled in certain scenarios involving a new owner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92eb9fce002800330c9f680d468f081b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (5)&quot;" target="&quot;REPLACED 85 OF 1994 S. 6&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text of SUBSECTION (5) is part of the legal framework that has been replaced by a specific section, indicating its historical context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (5)&quot;" target="&quot;ANY PRODUCT UNDER SECTION 25(1)(E)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Any product under Section 25(1)(e) is subject to the offences defined in Subsection (5). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-37eade578e866e449433b5cf2ef5311c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (5)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 60 (3)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The powers granted by SECTION 60(3) can be exercised by the HIGH COURT even if an arbitral tribunal exists, similar to what is specified in SUBSECTION (5). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (6)&quot;" target="&quot;REPLACED 85 OF 1994 S. 6&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text of SUBSECTION (6) is part of the legal framework that has been replaced by a specific section, indicating its historical context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (6)&quot;" target="&quot;CERTIFICATE ISSUED UNDER SUBSECTION (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"According to subsection (6), any certificates issued under subsection (2) that are cancelled will no longer be valid. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9d232c4c17f319179e61e9fe9f748ce7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (6)&quot;" target="&quot;NOISE ABATEMENT NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (6) defines the offence for failing to comply with a requirement in a noise abatement notice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (6)&quot;" target="&quot;FINE OF $20,000 PER DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An offender under Subsection (6) is liable to a fine of $20,000 for each day the offence continues."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ae1515a72d04834906dde05638fab9b4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (6)&quot;" target="&quot;HIGH COURT&quot; OR &quot;原訟法庭&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The HIGH COURT has special powers concerning arbitration procedures as stated in SECTION 60(1). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPLACED 85 OF 1994 S. 6&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (3) (CHINESE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Chinese translation of SUBSECTION (3) is part of the legal framework that has been replaced by a specific section, indicating its historical context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPLACED 85 OF 1994 S. 6&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (1) (CHINESE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Chinese translation of SUBSECTION (1) is part of the legal framework that has been replaced by a specific section, indicating its historical context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cb527550097d8ae04c63a6dbcf448664</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
