  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERMANENT PARTIAL INCAPACITY&quot;" target="&quot;FIRST SCHEDULE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The compensation for permanent partial incapacity depends on the injury as listed in the First Schedule."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-062631c2ee8edb363f6cc234fa986a1a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERMANENT PARTIAL INCAPACITY&quot;" target="&quot;LOSS OF EARNING CAPACITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Permanent partial incapacity involves a loss of earning capacity, which is assessed differently from permanent total incapacity."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2d80227f925bf1b081dc41765e6e6934</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FIRST SCHEDULE&quot;" target="&quot;49 OF 1985 S. 3&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The amendment by 49 OF 1985 S. 3 refers to injuries specified in FIRST SCHEDULE, establishing a relationship between them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-430e5976cb2d37cf2cc19b50c8f851c3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FIRST SCHEDULE&quot;" target="&quot;LOSS OF EARNING CAPACITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"First Schedule provides specific percentages for certain injuries that affect loss of earning capacity less than 100%."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-779a6ebdcf1cc3fbd67a4dc22862c59e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FIRST SCHEDULE&quot;" target="&quot;S. 9&quot;|">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"S. 9" is part of the FIRST SCHEDULE, which outlines specific injury percentages for compensation purposes.</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f16e9e25a3dbce715e72ac73a5f618f3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FIRST SCHEDULE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The provisions in the First Schedule determine whether a contract is considered continuous for the purposes defined by this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e976980f19e9ab89febaf65027fa503e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FIRST SCHEDULE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 2020&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of continuous employment in First Schedule is relevant to understanding 'continuous contract' under the Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 2020."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3639cabcc91a09d2612cb06c302addd4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOSS OF EARNING CAPACITY&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Compensation is related to loss of earning capacity, especially when permanent partial incapacity results from specified injuries."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-062631c2ee8edb363f6cc234fa986a1a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOSS OF EARNING CAPACITY&quot;" target="&quot;FIRST SCHEDULE (AMENDED 76 OF 1982 S. 6)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Loss of earning capacity is calculated based on injuries specified in the First Schedule for permanent total incapacity."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2d80227f925bf1b081dc41765e6e6934</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOSS OF EARNING CAPACITY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S QUALIFICATIONS AND EXPERIENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employee's qualifications and experience are considered when assessing the percentage of loss of earning capacity in cases not specified by the First Schedule."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2d80227f925bf1b081dc41765e6e6934</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOSS OF EARNING CAPACITY&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Court is involved in assessing the loss of earning capacity when necessary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-779a6ebdcf1cc3fbd67a4dc22862c59e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
