<edge source="&quot;CARPAL TUNNEL SYNDROME&quot;" target="&quot;LEGIONNAIRES' DISEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While both are occupational health issues, they arise from different types of exposures and work-related activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7306865e35ebfb2e70b787c62738f5ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANTHRAX&quot;" target="&quot;FARMER'S LUNG&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While both are occupational diseases, they arise from different exposures: Anthrax from contact with infected animals, Farmer's Lung from inhaling dust of mouldy hay or other produce."&lt;SEP&gt;"While both can be caused by occupational exposure, Anthrax is more commonly associated with animal handling while Farmer's Lung involves inhalation of moldy hay dust."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da23b5f81dd13162b08cf24c13ec97da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65ba7ca0b25e8b8db22e6c1edfd463f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANTHRAX&quot;" target="&quot;GLANDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">11.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both conditions can be contracted through direct contact with infected animals; however, they are caused by different pathogens (Glanders is caused by *Burkholderia mallei* and Anthrax by *Bacillus anthracis*)."&lt;SEP&gt;"While both can be caused by occupational exposure to potentially contaminated environments, Anthrax is more commonly associated with animal handling while Glanders involves contact with equine animals and their carcasses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da23b5f81dd13162b08cf24c13ec97da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65ba7ca0b25e8b8db22e6c1edfd463f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANTHRAX&quot;" target="&quot;LEPTOSPIRA INFECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both conditions can be contracted through contact with infected animals or their products, though they are caused by different pathogens (Leptospirosis is caused by *Leptospira* species and Anthrax by *Bacillus anthracis*)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da23b5f81dd13162b08cf24c13ec97da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANTHRAX&quot;" target="&quot;INFECTION BY ORGANISMS OF THE GENUS BRUCELLA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both conditions can be contracted through contact with infected animals or their products, though they arise from different pathogens (Anthrax is caused by *Bacillus anthracis* and Brucellosis by organisms of the genus *Brucella*)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da23b5f81dd13162b08cf24c13ec97da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GLANDERS&quot;" target="&quot;FARMER'S LUNG&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both conditions are related to occupational exposures but in different contexts: Glanders from contact with equine animals, and Farmer's Lung from inhaling moldy vegetable produce dust."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b65ba7ca0b25e8b8db22e6c1edfd463f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GLANDERS&quot;" target="&quot;INFECTION BY LEPTOSPIRA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both conditions are related as they can both be caused by occupational exposure to potentially contaminated environments, but Infection by Leptospirosis is more commonly associated with work in infested places and handling animals or their products while Glanders involves contact with equine animals."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b65ba7ca0b25e8b8db22e6c1edfd463f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INFECTION BY LEPTOSPIRA&quot;" target="&quot;FARMER'S LUNG&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While both can be caused by occupational exposure to potentially contaminated environments, Farmer's Lung involves inhaling moldy hay dust and Infection by Leptospirosis is more commonly associated with work in infested places and handling animals or their products."&lt;SEP&gt;"While both can be caused by occupational exposure to potentially contaminated environments, Infection by Leptospirosis is more commonly associated with work in infested places and handling animals or their products while Farmer's Lung involves inhaling moldy hay dust."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b65ba7ca0b25e8b8db22e6c1edfd463f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FARMER'S LUNG&quot;" target="&quot;INFECTION BY ORGANISMS OF THE GENUS BRUCELLA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both conditions can be contracted through exposure to infected animals or their products, though they affect different parts of the respiratory system and are caused by different pathogens."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da23b5f81dd13162b08cf24c13ec97da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FARMER'S LUNG&quot;" target="&quot;LEPTOSPIRA INFECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both conditions can be contracted through exposure to infected animals or their products, though they affect different parts of the respiratory system and are caused by different pathogens."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da23b5f81dd13162b08cf24c13ec97da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FARMER'S LUNG&quot;" target="&quot;AGRICULTURE, HORTICULTURE OR FORESTRY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Farmer's lung is associated with activities in agriculture, horticulture or forestry."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1413ab0c72d29c4bf80b03987aaff3dd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FARMER'S LUNG&quot;" target="&quot;LOADING OR UNLOADING OR HANDLING IN STORAGE THE HAY OR PRODUCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Farmer's lung can be caused by handling hay or produce during loading or unloading operations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1413ab0c72d29c4bf80b03987aaff3dd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FARMER'S LUNG&quot;" target="&quot;HANDLING BAGASSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Bagasse handling may also lead to farmer's lung symptoms due to dust exposure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1413ab0c72d29c4bf80b03987aaff3dd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOT WATER SERVICE SYSTEMS&quot;|" target="&quot;STREPTOCOCCUS SUIS&quot;|">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational contact with pigs infected by STREPTOCOCCUS SUIS does not directly involve hot water service systems, but similar maintenance roles might overlap."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f4b9235f66c4fbb5045cd3777eb4910c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOT WATER SERVICE SYSTEMS&quot;|" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL CONTACT WITH BIRDS INFECTED BY CHLAMYDIA PSITTACI&quot;|">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational contact with birds infected by chlamydia psittaci does not directly involve hot water service systems, but similar maintenance roles might overlap."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f4b9235f66c4fbb5045cd3777eb4910c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STREPTOCOCCUS SUIS&quot;|" target="&quot;COOLING SYSTEMS USING FRESH WATER&quot;|">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational contact with pigs infected by STREPTOCOCCUS SUIS involves cooling systems that use fresh water."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f4b9235f66c4fbb5045cd3777eb4910c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AVIAN CHLAMYDIOSIS&quot;|" target="&quot;POULTRY HANDLING&quot;|">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Any occupation involving contact with birds infected with chlamydia psittaci is related to poultry handling."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f4b9235f66c4fbb5045cd3777eb4910c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGIONNAIRES' DISEASE&quot;|" target="&quot;COOLING SYSTEMS USING FRESH WATER&quot;|">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legionnaires' disease can be contracted from cooling systems that use fresh water, creating a direct relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f4b9235f66c4fbb5045cd3777eb4910c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVERE ACUTE RESPIRATORY SYNDROME (SARS)&quot;|" target="&quot;MEDICAL TREATMENT OR NURSING STAFF ENGAGED IN SARS CARE&quot;|">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Medical treatment or nursing staff engaged in SARS care are directly involved with SARS-infected individuals."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f4b9235f66c4fbb5045cd3777eb4910c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
