  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Byssinosis is caused by exposure to raw cotton dust, which is an occupational hazard."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd51a907a14f6acfa42e02c3a1fc0efa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL ASTHMA&quot;" target="&quot;ISOCYANATES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational asthma can be triggered by exposure to isocyanates, a type of chemical agent."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd51a907a14f6acfa42e02c3a1fc0efa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL ASTHMA&quot;" target="&quot;PLATINUM SALTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Exposure to platinum salts may also lead to occupational asthma."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd51a907a14f6acfa42e02c3a1fc0efa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL ASTHMA&quot;" target="&quot;FUMES ARISING FROM THE USE OF ROSIN AS A SOLDERING FLUX&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The use of rosin as a soldering flux can produce fumes that cause occupational asthma."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd51a907a14f6acfa42e02c3a1fc0efa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL ASTHMA&quot;" target="&quot;FORMALDEHYDE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Formaldehyde exposure is another risk factor for developing occupational asthma."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd51a907a14f6acfa42e02c3a1fc0efa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL ASTHMA&quot;" target="&quot;PROTEOLYTIC ENZYMES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Proteolytic enzymes can be a cause of occupational asthma in certain work environments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd51a907a14f6acfa42e02c3a1fc0efa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL ASTHMA&quot;" target="&quot;ANIMALS OR INSECTS USED FOR RESEARCH OR EDUCATION IN LABORATORIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Animals or insects used for research may expose workers to allergens that can cause occupational asthma."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd51a907a14f6acfa42e02c3a1fc0efa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL ASTHMA&quot;" target="&quot;DUSTS ARISING FROM THE SOWING, CULTIVATION, HARVESTING, DRYING, HANDLING, MILLING, TRANSPORT OR STORAGE OF BARLEY, OATS, RYE, WHEAT OR MAIZE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
