<edge source="&quot;SPOUSES OR COHABITEES&quot;" target="&quot;CHILDREN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If both spouses or cohabitees and children are eligible, they each receive 50% of the total compensation split equally among them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf83ce681b3c9c2ca889e6e5ad2a0c3b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPOUSES OR COHABITEES&quot;" target="&quot;PARENTS OR GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"In cases where both spouses or cohabitees and parents or grandparents are eligible, a portion (45%) of the compensation is split among all spouses or cohabitees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf83ce681b3c9c2ca889e6e5ad2a0c3b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPOUSES OR COHABITEES&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION DISTRIBUTION RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The rules specify how compensation is distributed among spouses or cohabitees, depending on whether children and/or parents/grandparents are also eligible members of the family."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4cada5f5bf4ec8ceba652ad11f10a00</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPOUSES OR COHABITEES&quot;" target="&quot;FAMILY MEMBERS ELIGIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Spouses or cohabitees are explicitly listed as eligible family members in the rules, alongside children, parents, and grandparents. Their inclusion affects how compensation is distributed among all eligible family members."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4cada5f5bf4ec8ceba652ad11f10a00</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPOUSES OR COHABITEES&quot;" target="&quot;CAP 282 RTF (14-05-26)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The document 'Cap 282 RTF (14-05-2026)' outlines the distribution of compensation among spouses or cohabitees, along with other family members. The rules specify different percentages and allocation methods for various combinations of eligible family members."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4cada5f5bf4ec8ceba652ad11f10a00</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPOUSES OR COHABITEES&quot;" target="&quot;OTHER MEMBERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"95% and 75% of compensation are paid to spouses or cohabitees, while the remaining percentages go to other members."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1938a0bb46ac68b6b87f8f976a10b061</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPOUSES OR COHABITEES&quot;" target="&quot;PARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Spouses or cohabitees receive a larger share (95% and 75%) compared to parents, who only get their portion if no other eligible members are present."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1938a0bb46ac68b6b87f8f976a10b061</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPOUSES OR COHABITEES&quot;" target="&quot;GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Spouses or cohabitees receive a larger share (95% and 75%) compared to grandparents, who only get their portion if no other eligible members are present."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1938a0bb46ac68b6b87f8f976a10b061</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPOUSES OR COHABITEES&quot;" target="&quot;CAP 282 RTF (14-05-2026)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The document outlines how spouses or cohabitees are compensated based on family composition."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-44ee098d72c3cfdd3e201662ed838d22</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILDREN&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Children receive a significant portion of the compensation, varying from 75% to 95% depending on family composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Compensation is distributed equally among eligible children if they are the only family members."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf83ce681b3c9c2ca889e6e5ad2a0c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44ee098d72c3cfdd3e201662ed838d22</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILDREN&quot;" target="&quot;PARENTS OR GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"When children and parents or grandparents are both eligible for compensation, 45% goes to each group (children and then parents/grandparents)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf83ce681b3c9c2ca889e6e5ad2a0c3b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILDREN&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION DISTRIBUTION RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">20.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Children can receive up to 95% of the compensation when there are no spouses, cohabitants, grandparents or great-grandparents involved."&lt;SEP&gt;"If children are the sole eligible family members and other relatives like parents, grandparents, etc., do not qualify, then only a small portion (5%) is distributed among them."&lt;SEP&gt;"The rules detail that 45% of the compensation will be distributed equally among all children if they are part of the eligible family members, alongside spouses or cohabitees and/or parents/grandparents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4cada5f5bf4ec8ceba652ad11f10a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498a60e85a08494b75272ed277c81a05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e900da43d00f655414f15ad83d97a3a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILDREN&quot;" target="&quot;FAMILY MEMBERS ELIGIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Children are identified as one of the categories of family members who can be eligible for distribution under the rules, alongside spouses or cohabitees and parents/grandparents. Their presence influences how compensation is allocated among all eligible family members."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4cada5f5bf4ec8ceba652ad11f10a00</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILDREN&quot;" target="&quot;CAP 282 RTF (14-05-26)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The document 'Cap 282 RTF (14-05-2026)' includes children as one of the categories for compensation distribution, alongside spouses or cohabitees and parents/grandparents. The rules provide specific percentages and allocation methods based on family member eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4cada5f5bf4ec8ceba652ad11f10a00</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILDREN&quot;" target="&quot;OTHER MEMBERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"45% of compensation is paid directly to children, with any remaining amount going to other members if no parents or grandparents are present."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1938a0bb46ac68b6b87f8f976a10b061</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILDREN&quot;" target="&quot;PARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">24.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Children directly receive compensation before parents, indicating the priority of children in distribution. If neither exists, then 'other members' receive it."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parents and their children can both be considered as eligible family members under the rules but receive different shares of compensation depending on other relatives' eligibility status."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parents share a higher percentage of the compensation when there are no spouses, cohabitants, grandparents or great-grandparents involved."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1e900da43d00f655414f15ad83d97a3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498a60e85a08494b75272ed277c81a05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1938a0bb46ac68b6b87f8f976a10b061</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILDREN&quot;" target="&quot;GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If no parents are present and only grandparents exist, they share 5% with other members; otherwise, children get their portion first before any distribution to others."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1938a0bb46ac68b6b87f8f976a10b061</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILDREN&quot;" target="&quot;CAP 282 RTF (14-05-2026)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The document details the compensation distribution for children in various scenarios involving different family members."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-44ee098d72c3cfdd3e201662ed838d22</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILDREN&quot;" target="&quot;PARENTS OR GRANDPARENTS, OR ANY COMBINATION THEREOF&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Children receive 75% of the compensation in equal amounts when parents or grandparents are present; otherwise, they get a smaller share."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILDREN&quot;" target="&quot;SPOUSES OR COHABITANTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Spouses or cohabitants and children are both groups that can receive compensation, with different percentages depending on other family members' presence."&lt;SEP&gt;"The rules outline scenarios in which only spouses or cohabitants are eligible family members along with children, indicating a different distribution pattern for compensation among these groups."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1e900da43d00f655414f15ad83d97a3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498a60e85a08494b75272ed277c81a05</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILDREN&quot;" target="&quot;OTHER FAMILY MEMBERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">30.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Children are to receive 75% of the compensation on average when there are no specific qualified family members mentioned besides children, spouses/cohabitants, parents and grandparents (including great-grandparents)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Children can be considered as part of the group that receives 75% or more of the compensation from other family members under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Other family members are to receive 95% of the compensation on average from the children."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a3729eccee563b08b3baf022dfb8e0b5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILDREN&quot;" target="&quot;PARENTS, GRANDPARENTS, GREAT-GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">22.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Children are to receive 75% of the compensation on average when there are no specific qualified family members mentioned besides children and spouses/cohabitants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parents and grandparents (including great-grandparents) can be considered as part of the qualified family members alongside children."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a3729eccee563b08b3baf022dfb8e0b5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENTS&quot;" target="&quot;GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"20% is split between parents and grandparents based on their presence; if neither parent nor grandparent exists, 5% goes to each. Otherwise, 70% of the 20% goes to parents and 30% to grandparents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1938a0bb46ac68b6b87f8f976a10b061</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENTS&quot;" target="&quot;OTHER MEMBERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Other members receive the remaining compensation after spouses or cohabitees, parents, and children have been paid. If no one else is present, they share 5% with other eligible members."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1938a0bb46ac68b6b87f8f976a10b061</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENTS&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION DISTRIBUTION RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The compensation distribution rules specify that in the absence of grandparents and great-grandparents, parents will receive an equal share."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-498a60e85a08494b75272ed277c81a05</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENTS&quot;" target="&quot;GRANDPARENTS AND GREAT-GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">11.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"In certain conditions where only parents are eligible but not their children or spouses/cohabitants, the distribution rules suggest that compensation can be shared between them and grandparents/great-grandparents."&lt;SEP&gt;"The rules indicate that in the absence of parents, compensation can be given to grandparents and great-grandparents equally."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-498a60e85a08494b75272ed277c81a05</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENTS&quot;" target="&quot;GRANDPARENTS OR GREAT-GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The compensation distribution rules specify that 20% of the remaining 30% is given to grandparents or great-grandparents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1e900da43d00f655414f15ad83d97a3a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENTS&quot;" target="&quot;OTHER FAMILY MEMBERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Other family members receive a smaller share, and parents may get more if they are the only eligible recipients besides children."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1e900da43d00f655414f15ad83d97a3a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENTS&quot;" target="&quot;95TH PERCENTILE'S 70%&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The first 70% of the 95th percentile is allocated to parents in any other situation where they are present."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23ec65cd13e12d5661e764484d0e10bd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OTHER FAMILY MEMBERS&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION DISTRIBUTION RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Other family members receive their share from the remaining 5% according to the rules."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1e900da43d00f655414f15ad83d97a3a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OTHER FAMILY MEMBERS&quot;" target="&quot;PARENTS, GRANDPARENTS, GREAT-GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">30.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Other family members are to receive 5% of the compensation on average when there are no other specific qualified family members mentioned."&lt;SEP&gt;"Other family members can be considered as part of the group that receives 5% or more of the compensation from parents and grandparents (including great-grandparents) under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parents and grandparents (including great-grandparents) are to receive 20% of the compensation on average when there are no specific qualified family members mentioned besides children, spouses/cohabitants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parents and grandparents (including great-grandparents) can be considered as part of the group that receives 20% or more of the compensation from other family members under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a3729eccee563b08b3baf022dfb8e0b5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OTHER FAMILY MEMBERS&quot;" target="&quot;REMAINING 5%&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The last 5% is distributed evenly among other family members regardless of their relation to the subject."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23ec65cd13e12d5661e764484d0e10bd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL PROVISIONS&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS OWNERSHIP CHANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal provisions such as 32A(1)(C), 32B(3), and 32C(1,2) apply to situations involving BUSINESS OWNERSHIP CHANGE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9ddecf99bc0bca06387d96224afeaf4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL PROVISIONS&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC HOLIDAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal provisions define public holidays, including statutory and alternative holidays in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-adbe757d90ad335b39fd280c5f650025</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CAP 282 RTF (14-05-2026)&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION DISTRIBUTION RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The rules are defined by the document 'Cap 282 RTF (14-05-2026)', which provides specific guidelines on how compensation is distributed among eligible family members based on their categories and combinations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4cada5f5bf4ec8ceba652ad11f10a00</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CAP 282 RTF (14-05-2026)&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The document specifies the distribution rules for compensation based on family members."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-44ee098d72c3cfdd3e201662ed838d22</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CAP 282 RTF (14-05-2026)&quot;" target="&quot;PARENTS OR GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The document specifies how parents or grandparents are compensated depending on the presence of other family members."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-44ee098d72c3cfdd3e201662ed838d22</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPENSATION DISTRIBUTION RULES&quot;" target="&quot;PARENTS OR GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The rules outline how compensation is shared among parents or grandparents when they are part of the eligible family members, alongside spouses or cohabitees and/or children. The distribution varies based on whether only parents/grandparents or both parents and grandparents are present."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4cada5f5bf4ec8ceba652ad11f10a00</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPENSATION DISTRIBUTION RULES&quot;" target="&quot;GRANDPARENTS AND GREAT-GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"In the absence of parents, grandparents and great-grandparents are to be compensated equally according to certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-498a60e85a08494b75272ed277c81a05</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPENSATION DISTRIBUTION RULES&quot;" target="&quot;SPOUSES OR COHABITANTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"When only spouses or cohabitants are eligible family members, they receive 95% of the compensation on average."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-498a60e85a08494b75272ed277c81a05</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPENSATION DISTRIBUTION RULES&quot;" target="&quot;GRANDPARENTS OR GREAT-GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The rules specify that 30% of the remaining 20% is given to grandparents or great-grandparents when there are no other family members involved."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1e900da43d00f655414f15ad83d97a3a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENTS OR GRANDPARENTS&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Compensation distribution varies based on whether parents or grandparents, or both, are the only eligible family members. If no grandparents, compensation is split equally among all parents; if no parents, it's split among all grandparents; otherwise, 70% to parents and 30% to grandparents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parents or grandparents can receive up to 20% of the compensation in specific cases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf83ce681b3c9c2ca889e6e5ad2a0c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44ee098d72c3cfdd3e201662ed838d22</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENTS OR GRANDPARENTS&quot;" target="&quot;FAMILY MEMBERS ELIGIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parents or grandparents are categorized as potential eligible family members in the rules, alongside spouses or cohabitees and children. Their eligibility impacts how compensation is distributed among all eligible family members."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4cada5f5bf4ec8ceba652ad11f10a00</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENTS OR GRANDPARENTS&quot;" target="&quot;CAP 282 RTF (14-05-26)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The document 'Cap 282 RTF (14-05-2026)' categorizes parents or grandparents as eligible family members for compensation distribution, along with spouses or cohabitees and children. The rules detail the allocation methods based on different combinations of these categories."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4cada5f5bf4ec8ceba652ad11f10a00</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FAMILY COMPENSATION GUIDELINES&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Family compensation guidelines determine how to distribute compensation among different family members based on their eligibility status."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf83ce681b3c9c2ca889e6e5ad2a0c3b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FAMILY MEMBERS ELIGIBILITY&quot;" target="&quot;CAP 282 RTF (14-05-26)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The document 'Cap 282 RTF (14-05-2026)' defines the categories of family members who are eligible for compensation distribution, including spouses or cohabitees, children, and parents/grandparents. The rules provide specific guidelines on how to allocate compensation among these groups."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4cada5f5bf4ec8ceba652ad11f10a00</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRANDPARENTS&quot;" target="&quot;OTHER MEMBERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If no one else is present, 'other members' share the remaining compensation equally with grandparents; otherwise, their portion comes last after all others have been paid."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1938a0bb46ac68b6b87f8f976a10b061</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENTS OR GRANDPARENTS, OR ANY COMBINATION THEREOF&quot;" target="&quot;OTHER MEMBERS WHO ARE NOT SPOUSES OR COHABITEES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Other members receive 20% or 5% of the compensation in equal amounts when parents or grandparents are present; otherwise, they get a smaller share."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENTS OR GRANDPARENTS, OR ANY COMBINATION THEREOF&quot;" target="&quot;FAMILY MEMBERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Family members are categorized into parents or grandparents, or any combination thereof for compensation distribution purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENTS OR GRANDPARENTS, OR ANY COMBINATION THEREOF&quot;" target="&quot;合資格家庭成員為或合資格家庭成員包括&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Qualified family members are categorized into parents or grandparents, or any combination thereof for compensation distribution purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENTS OR GRANDPARENTS, OR ANY COMBINATION THEREOF&quot;" target="&quot;其他成员 WHO ARE NOT SPOUSES OR COHABITEES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parents or grandparents and other members receive different shares of the compensation based on their roles within the family structure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVENTH SCHEDULE ADDED 52 OF 2000 S. 28&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Seventh Schedule added provisions for distributing compensation to different types of family members based on their roles and presence within the family structure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FAMILY MEMBERS&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Compensation is distributed among family members based on their roles and presence within the family structure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;配偶或同居者或其任何組合&quot;" target="&quot;子女&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Spouses or cohabitees and their combinations receive a smaller share of the compensation compared to children when present in the family structure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;子女&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Children receive a specific share of the compensation based on their status within the family structure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;子女&quot;" target="&quot;其他成员 WHO ARE NOT SPOUSES OR COHABITEES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Children and other non-spouse/non-cohabitant family members share a specific distribution of compensation in equal amounts when present in the family structure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;子女&quot;" target="&quot;配偶或同居者&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"补偿分配中涉及配偶或同居者和子女的共同利益，需要根据具体家庭成员组合进行不同比例的分配。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7253ecdaec265b8c66bb47e704e4a24a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;子女&quot;" target="&quot;父母、祖父母、外祖父母&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据具体的家庭成员组合情况，补偿会在子女和其他亲属之间进行分配。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7253ecdaec265b8c66bb47e704e4a24a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;合資格家庭成員為或合資格家庭成員包括&quot;" target="&quot;其他成员 WHO ARE NOT SPOUSES OR COHABITEES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Qualified family members, including parents or grandparents and other members, receive different shares of the compensation based on their roles within the family structure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b731a4c21596438fbc5093b43e75897f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRANDPARENTS OR GREAT-GRANDPARENTS&quot;" target="&quot;NO PARENTS SITUATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"In the situation where there are no parents, grandparents or great-grandparents receive an average allocation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23ec65cd13e12d5661e764484d0e10bd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRANDPARENTS OR GREAT-GRANDPARENTS&quot;" target="&quot;95TH PERCENTILE'S 30%&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The remaining 30% of the 95th percentile is allocated to grandparents or great-grandparents in any other situation where they are present."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23ec65cd13e12d5661e764484d0e10bd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE CONTROL ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;NOISE CONTROL AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Noise Control Ordinance establishes the Noise Control Authority, defining its powers and duties in relation to noise control."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5d00b09a8462e6600243e76883c57569</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE CONTROL AUTHORITY&quot;" target="&quot;CHIEF EXECUTIVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Chief Executive appoints the Noise Control Authority as per the regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ce50382ff024b176dc7ebf19fb5b68d4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE CONTROL AUTHORITY&quot;" target="&quot;GAZETTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Appointments of the Noise Control Authority must be notified in the Gazzette."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ce50382ff024b176dc7ebf19fb5b68d4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE CONTROL AUTHORITY&quot;" target="&quot;SECRETARY FOR ENVIRONMENT AND ECOLOGY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Secretary for Environment and Ecology's role may be indirectly related to Noise Control Authority through environmental policies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ce50382ff024b176dc7ebf19fb5b68d4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE CONTROL AUTHORITY&quot;" target="&quot;DIRECTOR OR OFFICER OF BODY CORPORATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The NOISE CONTROL AUTHORITY has advised that proceedings have been instituted against a director or officer of the body corporate for an offense under the Noise Control Ordinance (Cap. 400). This indicates legal action is being taken due to their management role."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-606c291ea5ee675ad86390a5e98aaec1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPEAL BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;NOISE CONTROL ORDINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The NOISE CONTROL ORDINANCE mentions that an Appeal Board is formed under Section 21 for related matters."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5d00b09a8462e6600243e76883c57569</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPEAL BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;CHIEF EXECUTIVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CHIEF EXECUTIVE appoints members of the APPEAL BOARD and can also appoint the Chairman."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chief Executive has the authority to appoint members of the Appeal Board by notice in the Gazette."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c65da5be1610c7210df4b6d277a43ffa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c6fd01455af1494e4efe451e7933dd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPEAL BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;NOISE PERMIT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An APPEAL BOARD can be appealed against decisions related to the issuance, limitation conditions, or revocation of a NOISE PERMIT."&lt;SEP&gt;"An APPEAL BOARD may be involved in disputes or challenges related to NOISE PERMITS, ensuring fair resolution processes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-56e97ce586530c13a293f392668859be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7741f07cb911e2c57e64574afd3fe8e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPEAL BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;APPEALS AGAINST REFUSAL OF AUTHORITY TO ISSUE CONSTRUCTION NOISE PERMIT, ETC.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Appeal Board handles appeals against refusal or cancellation of construction noise permits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-35333cbaccd9be2f64c80f729f9d5ffb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPEAL BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Appeals are made under the terms of this Ordinance regarding construction noise permits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-35333cbaccd9be2f64c80f729f9d5ffb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPEAL BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;TECHNICAL MEMORANDA ISSUED UNDER SECTION 10(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Technical Memoranda issued under Section 10(1) can be a ground for appealing to the Appeal Board regarding service of notices under Sections 13 or 16."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0a461efee858ab690fe058321b8a0025</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPEAL BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">25.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Any sum awarded by the APPEAL BOARD under subsection (6)(e) is enforceable and charged on the general revenue controlled by the AUTHORITY."&lt;SEP&gt;"The APPEAL BOARD can give directions to the AUTHORITY regarding functions relevant to appeals, indicating an oversight relationship."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Authority's actions, specifically those involving sections 13 and 16, are subject to appeal to the Appeal Board."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf98c13106216ee2990969e11aafbee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ed6bb61c777b6fe07e21fb258ca9224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a461efee858ab690fe058321b8a0025</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPEAL BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;DISTRICT JUDGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Chairman of the APPEAL BOARD is appointed from a qualified person as per section 5 of DISTRICT COURT ORDINANCE (Cap. 336). This indicates an indirect relationship through appointment qualifications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c65da5be1610c7210df4b6d277a43ffa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPEAL BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;GAZETTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Appointments to the APPEAL BOARD are notified in the GAZETTE, indicating an official publication channel for such appointments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c65da5be1610c7210df4b6d277a43ffa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPEAL BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;CHAIRMAN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Chairman has the authority to appoint members of the Appeal Board and can act on their behalf if they are unable to perform their functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chairman is a key member of the APPEAL BOARD and has significant influence over its composition and decisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf98c13106216ee2990969e11aafbee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60c17dd78d73fb0b81ce0ba9e3153396</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPEAL BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OF LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Appeals under this Part cannot question the contents of any Technical Memorandum, indicating a relationship with legal proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf98c13106216ee2990969e11aafbee7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPEAL BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;THE PURPOSES OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The purposes of the Ordinance include ensuring workplace safety and health, which relates to the role of APPEAL BOARD in handling related matters under the Administrative Review Board Ordinance (Cap. 442). The APPEAL BOARD is not directly mentioned but its context implies it may be involved in reviewing or overseeing compliance with these purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61cee1a453a83b87002df2318ef0eb78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPEAL BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition of workplace under the ordinance includes various types of work locations, which could potentially fall under the jurisdiction of APPEAL BOARD for regulatory oversight and review. However, no direct relationship is explicitly stated in the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61cee1a453a83b87002df2318ef0eb78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPEAL BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The APPEAL BOARD can hear appeals against decisions made by the COMMISSIONER regarding workplace accidents or occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bc8d52a1038b5b838fbe9231f59cfc74</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPEAL BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER may appeal to the APPEAL BOARD against a decision of the COMMISSIONER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bc8d52a1038b5b838fbe9231f59cfc74</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHIEF EXECUTIVE&quot;" target="&quot;CHAIRMAN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Chief Executive can appoint a person qualified as a District Judge under section 5 of the District Court Ordinance (Cap. 336) to act as Chairman if the original Chairman is unable to perform his functions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHIEF EXECUTIVE&quot;" target="&quot;THE FACTORY AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 59)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Regulations made by the Chief Executive can affect the implementation of this ordinance, particularly regarding inquiries and transitional provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-aa88f4f6c68bdcdf602f197a3d1b3c60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHIEF EXECUTIVE&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner can authorize public officers or classes thereof, and while the Chief Executive has broader powers to give directions, there is no explicit relationship between them in this context regarding apprenticeship or public officers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a5218a05714fc8de44f54bb46fbf020e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHIEF EXECUTIVE&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public Officers must comply with any instructions given by the Chief Executive when exercising their duties under this Ordinance. This indicates a hierarchical relationship where Public Officers are subject to directives from the Chief Executive."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a5218a05714fc8de44f54bb46fbf020e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHIEF EXECUTIVE&quot;" target="&quot;EXECUTIVE COUNCIL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Chief Executive and the Executive Council are key bodies that make decisions on matters including arbitration and enforcement policies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-603a9b33a6e3900af70fd439592326ba</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC PLACE&quot;" target="&quot;CHAIRMAN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Chairman is a role that can be appointed for managing or overseeing public places, as defined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-14c6fd01455af1494e4efe451e7933dd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC PLACE&quot;" target="&quot;MUSICAL INSTRUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public places can also host the operation of MUSICAL INSTRUMENTs, such as those used for entertainment or events."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3a0b3234913f2437002d1d69a535cc59</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC PLACE&quot;" target="&quot;LOUD-SPEAKER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LOUD-SPEAKERS are commonly found in PUBLIC PLACES to amplify sound and attract attention."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3a0b3234913f2437002d1d69a535cc59</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC PLACE&quot;" target="&quot;GAME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public places can be venues for playing GAMES or engaging in pastimes, which might involve noise."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3a0b3234913f2437002d1d69a535cc59</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC PLACE&quot;" target="&quot;TRADE OR BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"TRADE OR BUSINESS activities are also possible in PUBLIC PLACES and could generate noise annoyance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3a0b3234913f2437002d1d69a535cc59</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC PLACE&quot;" target="&quot;NOISE ABATEMENT NOTICES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public Place is one of the types of premises from which NOISE ABATEMENT NOTICES can be issued, along with construction sites and other non-domestic places."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1740b8b8c7e777efdccf16fb8d3a59de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC PLACE&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public places can be areas where court proceedings or related activities might take place."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC PLACE&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPIER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An OCCUPIER can control a PUBLIC PLACE, which includes various types of premises such as public streets or gardens."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC PLACE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition of WORKPLACE excludes certain public places from being classified as workplaces."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-126e18663d810ba6b83365ff30027a71</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHAIRMAN&quot;" target="&quot;ANNOYANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CHAIRMAN oversees matters that could involve ANNOYANCE as defined by a reasonable person."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4d107bfd5d6737d06b2fc1d377e10585</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHAIRMAN&quot;" target="&quot;TECHNICAL MEMORANDUM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CHAIRMAN has the authority to decide on matters related to Technical Memorandums issued under section 9(1) or 10(1)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf98c13106216ee2990969e11aafbee7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHAIRMAN&quot;" target="&quot;APPOINTING AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Chairman has the authority to appoint individuals, including District Judges and panel members, for various roles within the legal system."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHAIRMAN&quot;" target="&quot;PANEL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Chairman can determine forms or matters of practice and procedure, including appointing panel members for specific roles within the legal system."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78ade03ea05b85190f660e01dfba1ccc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHAIRMAN&quot;" target="&quot;SUPERVISION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The supervision mentioned may refer to oversight over the actions of the Chairman, ensuring proper conduct during appointments and hearings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-60c17dd78d73fb0b81ce0ba9e3153396</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PILING&quot;" target="&quot;PLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Piling engineering refers to work on any place, whether land-based or water-based, which involves sinking piles into the ground."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-14c6fd01455af1494e4efe451e7933dd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PILING&quot;" target="&quot;MACHINERY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Machinery is involved in piling operations, which includes driving piles into the ground using various methods such as hammering."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ead066fe98080d41598700f44491db70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PILING&quot;" target="&quot;PLANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Plant equipment can be used for piling activities that involve sinking or forming a pile by hammering, jacking, screwing, augering, boring, jetting, vibrating, casting, or other means."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ead066fe98080d41598700f44491db70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PILING&quot;" target="&quot;TOOLS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Tools are essential for operating machinery and plant during various piling operations including driving piles into the ground using different methods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ead066fe98080d41598700f44491db70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PILING&quot;" target="&quot;GEAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Gear is part of the equipment necessary for conducting piling activities, which can include hammering or other means to sink a pile in the ground."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ead066fe98080d41598700f44491db70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PILING&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Authority's decision can affect piling activities due to public interest considerations."::</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2d7aa41ab04a649aeb83e8611a7626ae</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PLACE&quot;" target="&quot;DOMESTIC USE PREMISES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Domestic use premises are a subset of places as defined in the text, indicating that they fall under the broader category of 'place'."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-14c6fd01455af1494e4efe451e7933dd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PLACE&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORIZED OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An AUTHORIZED OFFICER may enter and search a PLACE if they reasonably believe an OFFENCE AGAINST THIS ORDINANCE has been committed there."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8024a8a38a1cf4faa9e3a31112f97d7c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;局長 (SECRETARY)&quot;" target="&quot;侵擾者警報系統 (INTRUDER ALARM SYSTEM)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">38.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Secretary has the authority to regulate and oversee systems like the Intruder Alarm System, which is related to security measures."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Secretary may have policies and regulations related to Intruder Alarm Systems for security purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Secretary oversees the regulation and implementation of systems like Intruder Alarm Systems for security purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Secretary oversees the regulation of Intruder Alarm Systems as part of broader security management activities, including those related to vehicles."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Secretary oversees the regulation of Intruder Alarm Systems as part of broader security management activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;局長 (SECRETARY)&quot;" target="&quot;建築工程 (CONSTRUCTION WORK)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Secretary may have oversight over construction work as part of broader environmental and ecological management activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Secretary may oversee or regulate construction work as part of environmental and ecological management activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;局長 (SECRETARY)&quot;" target="&quot;地方 (PLACE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Secretary's authority extends to places where construction work may be carried out or where security measures like alarm systems are installed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;局長 (SECRETARY)&quot;" target="&quot;侵擾者 (INTRUDER)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Secretary may have policies and regulations related to intruders, including those who might trigger an Intruder Alarm System."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;局長 (SECRETARY)&quot;" target="&quot;車輛 (VEHICLE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Secretary may have jurisdiction over vehicles, especially in terms of security measures like Intruder Alarm Systems that can be installed on them."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Secretary may have policies and regulations related to vehicles as part of broader environmental management activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;局長 (SECRETARY)&quot;" target="&quot;住用處所 (DOMESTIC PREMISES)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Secretary may have policies and regulations related to domestic premises as part of broader environmental management activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;地方 (PLACE)&quot;" target="&quot;建築工程 (CONSTRUCTION WORK)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Construction work can be carried out in any place, whether on land or water, as defined by PLACE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;地方 (PLACE)&quot;" target="&quot;住用處所 (DOMESTIC PREMISES)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Domestic premises are a type of place where regulations related to PLACE apply, indicating their interrelated definitions and uses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Domestic premises are a type of place where the definition and regulations related to PLACE apply."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;地方 (PLACE)&quot;" target="&quot;車輛 (VEHICLE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">20.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Vehicles can be parked or used in places defined by PLACE, indicating their interrelated use spaces and regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vehicles can be parked or used in places, which are defined by PLACE, indicating their interrelated use spaces."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;地方 (PLACE)&quot;" target="&quot;侵擾者警報系統 (INTRUDER ALARM SYSTEM)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An Intruder Alarm System can be installed in any place, including those defined by PLACE for security purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Places, including domestic premises, can be equipped with Intruder Alarm Systems for security purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;住用處所 (DOMESTIC PREMISES)&quot;" target="&quot;侵擾者警報系統 (INTRUDER ALARM SYSTEM)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Domestic premises may be equipped with an Intruder Alarm System for security purposes in the residence area."&lt;SEP&gt;"Domestic premises may have an Intruder Alarm System for security purposes, indicating their relationship in terms of safety and protection."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;車輛 (VEHICLE)&quot;" target="&quot;侵擾者警報系統 (INTRUDER ALARM SYSTEM)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Vehicle can also trigger an Intruder Alarm System if it is protected by such a system, indicating their interrelated security functions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;車輛 (VEHICLE)&quot;" target="&quot;侵擾者 (INTRUDER)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An intruder can potentially interact with a vehicle, triggering an Intruder Alarm System if the vehicle is protected by one."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;侵擾者警報系統 (INTRUDER ALARM SYSTEM)&quot;" target="&quot;建築工程 (CONSTRUCTION WORK)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Construction work can involve the installation of an Intruder Alarm System for enhanced security during or after construction activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Construction work can involve the installation or integration of Intruder Alarm Systems for security purposes during or after construction activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6176dec80c975b170f3c3eef027274cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;建築工程&quot;" target="&quot;建築地盤&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"建築地盤是指進行建築工程的地方。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fcb1392a3c356025d7c364794c01ff7a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;建築工程&quot;" target="&quot;建築噪音許可證&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"建築工程需要獲得建築噪音許可證以合法施工。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fcb1392a3c356025d7c364794c01ff7a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;建築工程&quot;" target="&quot;指定範圍&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"指定範圍與進行建築工程相關，可能涉及特定操作或區域。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fcb1392a3c356025d7c364794c01ff7a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;建築噪音許可證&quot;" target="&quot;撞擊式打樁工程&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"進行撞擊式打樁工程需要持有有效的建築噪音許可證，否則屬犯罪。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75a63fc1bac46279a18763a5809259bb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;建築噪音許可證&quot;" target="&quot;非公眾假日&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"在非公眾假日的限制時間內，需持有有效的建築噪音許可證才能進行相關工程活動。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75a63fc1bac46279a18763a5809259bb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;建築噪音許可證&quot;" target="&quot;公眾假日&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"在公眾假日或晚上7時後，不得進行撞擊式打樁工程，除非有特別規定。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75a63fc1bac46279a18763a5809259bb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;建築噪音許可證&quot;" target="&quot;技術備忘錄&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據技術備忘錄指引發出建築噪音許可證,且其內容可能影響許可證的發放。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9053b5bb875d947585293b13bbe5f25e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;登記車主&quot;" target="&quot;煩擾&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"雖然文本未直接提及登記車主和煩擾之間的關係，但可以推測在某些情況下，登記車主可能會因建築工程產生的噪音或其他因素而感到煩擾。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fcb1392a3c356025d7c364794c01ff7a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE PERMIT&quot;" target="&quot;DESIGNATED AREA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The NOISE PERMIT is relevant to the use within the DESIGNATED AREA, which is defined as per specific regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-56e97ce586530c13a293f392668859be</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE PERMIT&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The REGISTERED OWNER's information might be required for obtaining or managing a NOISE PERMIT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-56e97ce586530c13a293f392668859be</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE PERMIT&quot;" target="&quot;PILE DRIVING ENGINEERING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PILE DRIVING ENGINEERING requires a NOISE PERMIT to be conducted between 7 AM and 7 PM on non-public holidays."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7741f07cb911e2c57e64574afd3fe8e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DESIGNATED AREA&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The AUTHORITY oversees the use within the DESIGNATED AREA to ensure compliance with regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-56e97ce586530c13a293f392668859be</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DESIGNATED AREA&quot;" target="&quot;CONSTRUCTION SITE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A DESIGNED AREA may include a CONSTRUCTION SITE as part of its scope."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4d107bfd5d6737d06b2fc1d377e10585</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DESIGNATED AREA&quot;" target="&quot;MACHINERY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Machinery can be deployed in a designated area as part of various operational activities including piling or other ground works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ead066fe98080d41598700f44491db70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DESIGNATED AREA&quot;" target="&quot;PLANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Plant equipment might not directly relate to the designation but could support operations within such areas."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ead066fe98080d41598700f44491db70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DESIGNATED AREA&quot;" target="&quot;TOOLS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Tools are used for various activities in a designated area, including piling or other ground works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ead066fe98080d41598700f44491db70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DESIGNATED AREA&quot;" target="&quot;GEAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Gear might be part of the equipment necessary for operations within a designated area such as piling or other ground works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ead066fe98080d41598700f44491db70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DESIGNATED AREA&quot;" target="&quot;SECRETARY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Secretary has the authority to establish a designated area through gazette notifications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-86dd5816dd56bd7bc4f23ec93e31f0f2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DESIGNATED AREA&quot;" target="&quot;BUILDING SITE NOISE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Noise regulation technical memoranda apply to designated areas concerning construction site noises."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-86dd5816dd56bd7bc4f23ec93e31f0f2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERCUSSIVE PILING&quot;" target="&quot;PILE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"PERCUSSIVE PILING is a specific type of work that involves using PILEs, which are structures driven into the ground."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-56e97ce586530c13a293f392668859be</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
