  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE includes a 5th clause that defines time limits for laying information regarding offences."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ddee27cc5f92142cd2814225d68af96b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE (CAP. 227)&quot;" target="&quot;6TH CLAUSE (OF THE ORDINANCE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE includes a 6th clause that defines time limits for laying information regarding offences."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ddee27cc5f92142cd2814225d68af96b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE (CAP. 227)&quot;" target="&quot;7TH CLAUSE (OF THE ORDINANCE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE includes a 7th clause that defines time limits for laying information regarding offences."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ddee27cc5f92142cd2814225d68af96b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE (CAP. 227)&quot;" target="&quot;13TH CLAUSE (OF THE ORDINANCE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE includes a 13th clause that defines the appointment of public officers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ddee27cc5f92142cd2814225d68af96b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE (CAP. 227)&quot;" target="&quot;17TH CLAUSE (OF THE ORDINANCE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE includes a 17th clause that defines the appointment of public officers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ddee27cc5f92142cd2814225d68af96b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE (CAP. 227)&quot;" target="&quot;PROSECUTION OF OFFENCES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PROSECUTION OF OFFENCES is governed by provisions in the MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE, particularly regarding summary trials and prosecution limits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-20f049d1d30f5c16c93c8bc30a7dab75</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE (CAP. 227)&quot;" target="&quot;CRIMINAL PROCEEDINGS (SUMMARY)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE provides rules for CRIMINAL PROCEEDINGS that are triable summarily, including the role of magistrates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-20f049d1d30f5c16c93c8bc30a7dab75</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE (CAP. 227)&quot;" target="&quot;9 MONTHS DEADLINE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE includes provisions related to deadlines for prosecuting offences that are triable summarily, such as the 9-month limit."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-20f049d1d30f5c16c93c8bc30a7dab75</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECRETARY FOR JUSTICE&quot;" target="&quot;PROSECUTION OF OFFENCES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SECRETARY FOR JUSTICE has functions related to prosecuting offences under this Ordinance but is not limited by these provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The SECRETARY FOR JUSTICE has powers in relation to PROSECUTION OF OFFENCES, as stated in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-20f049d1d30f5c16c93c8bc30a7dab75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddee27cc5f92142cd2814225d68af96b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECRETARY FOR JUSTICE&quot;" target="&quot;CRIMINAL PROCEEDINGS (SUMMARY)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SECRETARY FOR JUSTICE has functions under the MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE related to criminal proceedings that are triable summarily, though not limited by these provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-20f049d1d30f5c16c93c8bc30a7dab75</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECRETARY FOR JUSTICE&quot;" target="&quot;9 MONTHS DEADLINE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"There is no direct relationship specified between the SECRETARY FOR JUSTICE and the 9-month deadline for prosecutions; however, their functions under the MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE may indirectly relate to this."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-20f049d1d30f5c16c93c8bc30a7dab75</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECRETARY FOR JUSTICE&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While the Secretary for Justice retains powers over criminal prosecutions, the Commissioner's role is specifically defined within the Labour Department context, showing an inter-agency relationship but with distinct responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-de69b2333ff7d9bb2dd79e072a634503</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECRETARY FOR JUSTICE&quot;" target="&quot;PROSECUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Secretary for Justice retains the power to prosecute criminal offences, independent of section 63A(1)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-beb3c1a7d6211fc1cac75a7aeaaff11f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECRETARY FOR JUSTICE&quot;" target="&quot;MISCELLANEOUS DIVISION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Secretary for Justice is responsible for appointing bodies to oversee certain divisions, including Division 6 (Miscellaneous), as indicated by the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5247edeafb01587bde32ae379e5261dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECRETARY FOR JUSTICE&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORIZED BODY (獲授權機構)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'authorized body' is defined as a person appointed by the Secretary for Justice under section 98ZT(2), establishing their relationship through this definition."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECRETARY FOR JUSTICE&quot;" target="&quot;ADVISORY BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Advisory Body consults with the Secretary for Justice to make rules, showing an advisory relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d3450bee90618bb17df6c3522ce7aa42</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECRETARY FOR JUSTICE&quot;" target="&quot;PART 98ZM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Secretary for Justice has the power to monitor and review Part 98ZM, as well as appoint an authorized body under section 98ZN."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51ad58eafa2f8aa3ad189d3ab135c444</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROSECUTION&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court can consider financial information provided by the prosecution in determining the scale of operation for a convicted person."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fabbc3eeb929a4a143a6817fd7b457aa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROSECUTION&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner's consent is required before any prosecution can be commenced under the relevant sections of the Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-beb3c1a7d6211fc1cac75a7aeaaff11f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROSECUTION&quot;" target="&quot;LABOUR DEPARTMENT OFFICERS AUTHORIZED BY COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Labour Department officers authorized by the Commissioner are responsible for commencing and conducting prosecutions as per section 63A(1)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-beb3c1a7d6211fc1cac75a7aeaaff11f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;4TH, 5TH, 6TH, 7TH, 13TH OR 17TH CLAUSE OF THE ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;PROCEEDINGS FOR OFFENCES AGAINST THIS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"These clauses define the procedures for proceedings against offences under this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ddee27cc5f92142cd2814225d68af96b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROSECUTION OF OFFENCES&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER can bring and conduct prosecutions for certain offences against the PROSECUTION OF OFFENCES Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-20f049d1d30f5c16c93c8bc30a7dab75</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROSECUTION OF OFFENCES&quot;" target="&quot;CRIMINAL PROCEEDINGS (SUMMARY)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CRIMINAL PROCEEDINGS (SUMMARY) are relevant to how offences under the PROSECUTION OF OFFENCES Ordinance can be tried summarily."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-20f049d1d30f5c16c93c8bc30a7dab75</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROSECUTION OF OFFENCES&quot;" target="&quot;9 MONTHS DEADLINE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"There is a 9-month deadline for prosecuting offences under this Ordinance, as specified in the related provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-20f049d1d30f5c16c93c8bc30a7dab75</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;4TH CLAUSE (OF THE ORDINANCE)&quot;" target="&quot;5TH CLAUSE (OF THE ORDINANCE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both 4th and 5th clauses are part of the MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE, defining time limits for laying information."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ddee27cc5f92142cd2814225d68af96b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;6TH CLAUSE (OF THE ORDINANCE)&quot;" target="&quot;7TH CLAUSE (OF THE ORDINANCE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both 6th and 7th clauses are part of the MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE, defining time limits for laying information."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ddee27cc5f92142cd2814225d68af96b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;13TH CLAUSE (OF THE ORDINANCE)&quot;" target="&quot;17TH CLAUSE (OF THE ORDINANCE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both 13th and 17th clauses are part of the MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE, defining appointments of public officers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ddee27cc5f92142cd2814225d68af96b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROVISION WITHIN AN ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL DEFENSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal defenses can be based on provisions within an ordinance as stated in clause 33."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ddee27cc5f92142cd2814225d68af96b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFENCE TO PROCEEDINGS UNDER SECTION 4, 5, 6, 7, 13 OR 17&quot;" target="&quot;PROCEEDINGS FOR AN OFFENCE UNDER SECTION 4, 5, 6, 7, 13 OR 17&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The defence to proceedings under section 4-17 is applicable in the context of offences defined by these sections."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd0ab37b084efd20396f2b25c97ab3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFENCE TO PROCEEDINGS UNDER SECTION 4, 5, 6, 7, 13 OR 17 (CONTINUED)&quot;" target="&quot;CIRCUMSTANCES CONSTITUTING OR LEADING TO THE COMMISSION OF THE OFFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The defence to proceedings under section 4-17 is based on the circumstances constituting or leading to the commission of an offence defined by these sections."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd0ab37b084efd20396f2b25c97ab3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFENCE TO PROCEEDINGS UNDER SECTION 4, 5, 6, 7, 13 OR 17 (CONTINUED)&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORIZATION UNDER ANY LICENCE, PERMIT OR EXEMPTION GRANTED UNDER ANY OTHER ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The defence to proceedings under section 4-17 includes the authorization granted by any other ordinance as a valid circumstance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd0ab37b084efd20396f2b25c97ab3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREVENTION OF INJURY TO ANY PERSON OR THE SAVING OF THE LIFE OF ANY PERSON&quot;" target="&quot;DEFENCE TO PROCEEDINGS (CONTINUED)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The defence to proceedings under section 4-17 includes the prevention of injury or saving a life as valid circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd0ab37b084efd20396f2b25c97ab3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CIRCUMSTANCES PLACING THE PROPERTY IN DANGER OF BEING DAMAGED COULD NOT REASONABLY HAVE BEEN FORESEEN BY THE PERSON CHARGED WITH THE OFFENCE&quot;" target="&quot;DEFENCE TO PROCEEDINGS (CONTINUED)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The defence to proceedings under section 4-17 includes the circumstances where property damage could not be reasonably foreseen by the person charged with the offence as valid circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd0ab37b084efd20396f2b25c97ab3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREVENTION OF SERIOUS INTERRUPTION OR DISRUPTION TO ANY PUBLIC TRANSPORT SYSTEM&quot;" target="&quot;DEFENCE TO PROCEEDINGS (CONTINUED)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The defence to proceedings under section 4-17 includes the prevention of serious disruption or interruption to public transport systems as valid circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd0ab37b084efd20396f2b25c97ab3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFENCE TO PROCEEDINGS (CONTINUED)&quot;" target="&quot;CIRCUMSTANCES PLACING THE PROPERTY IN DANGER OF BEING DAMAGED COULD NOT REASONABLY HAVE BEEN FORESEEN BY THE PERSON CHARGED WITH THE OFFENCE (CONTINUED)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The defence to proceedings under section 4-17 includes the continued circumstances where property damage could not be reasonably foreseen by the person charged with the offence as valid circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd0ab37b084efd20396f2b25c97ab3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFENCE TO PROCEEDINGS (CONCLUSION)&quot;" target="&quot;PREVENTION OF SERIOUS INTERRUPTION OR DISRUPTION TO ANY PUBLIC TRANSPORT SYSTEM (CONTINUED)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The defence to proceedings under section 4-17 includes the continued prevention of serious disruption or interruption to public transport systems as valid circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd0ab37b084efd20396f2b25c97ab3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFENCE TO PROCEEDINGS (CONCLUSION)&quot;" target="&quot;CIRCUMSTANCES PLACING THE PROPERTY IN DANGER OF BEING DAMAGED COULD NOT REASONABLY HAVE BEEN FORESEEN BY THE PERSON CHARGED WITH THE OFFENCE (FINAL)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The defence to proceedings under section 4-17 includes the final circumstances where property damage could not be reasonably foreseen by the person charged with the offence as valid circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd0ab37b084efd20396f2b25c97ab3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFENCE TO PROCEEDINGS (CONCLUSION)&quot;" target="&quot;PREVENTION OF SERIOUS INTERRUPTION OR DISRUPTION TO ANY PUBLIC TRANSPORT SYSTEM (FINAL)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The defence to proceedings under section 4-17 includes the final prevention of serious disruption or interruption to public transport systems as valid circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd0ab37b084efd20396f2b25c97ab3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFENCE TO PROCEEDINGS (CONCLUSION)&quot;" target="&quot;CIRCUMSTANCES PLACING THE PROPERTY IN DANGER OF BEING DAMAGED COULD NOT REASONABLY HAVE BEEN FORESEEN BY THE PERSON CHARGED WITH THE OFFENCE (FINAL CONCLUSION)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The defence to proceedings under section 4-17 includes the final conclusion that circumstances where property damage could not be reasonably foreseen by the person charged with the offence are valid as a defence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd0ab37b084efd20396f2b25c97ab3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFENCE TO PROCEEDINGS (CONCLUSION)&quot;" target="&quot;PREVENTION OF SERIOUS INTERRUPTION OR DISRUPTION TO ANY PUBLIC TRANSPORT SYSTEM (FINAL CONCLUSION)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The defence to proceedings under section 4-17 includes the final conclusion that prevention of serious disruption or interruption to public transport systems are valid as a defence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd0ab37b084efd20396f2b25c97ab3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE DOCUMENT IS SUCH LICENCE OR NOTICE (FINAL)&quot;" target="&quot;DEFENCE TO PROCEEDINGS UNDER SECTION 4, 5, 6, 7, 13 OR 17 (FINAL)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The final defence to proceedings under section 4-17 includes the document being such a licence or notice as valid evidence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd0ab37b084efd20396f2b25c97ab3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE CIRCUMSTANCES PLACING THE PROPERTY IN DANGER OF BEING DAMAGED COULD NOT REASONABLY HAVE BEEN FORESEEN BY THE PERSON CHARGED WITH THE OFFENCE (FINAL)&quot;" target="&quot;DEFENCE TO PROCEEDINGS UNDER SECTION 4, 5, 6, 7, 13 OR 17 (FINAL)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The final defence to proceedings under section 4-17 includes the circumstances where property damage could not be reasonably foreseen by the person charged with the offence as valid evidence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd0ab37b084efd20396f2b25c97ab3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE CIRCUMSTANCES WHICH WOULD OTHERWISE CAUSE SUCH AN INTERRUPTION OR DISRUPTION COULD NOT REASONABLY HAVE BEEN FORESEEN BY THE PERSON CHARGED WITH THE OFFENCE (FINAL)&quot;" target="&quot;DEFENCE TO PROCEEDINGS UNDER SECTION 4, 5, 6, 7, 13 OR 17 (FINAL)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The final defence to proceedings under section 4-17 includes the circumstances where serious disruption or interruption could not be reasonably foreseen by the person charged with the offence as valid evidence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd0ab37b084efd20396f2b25c97ab3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE DOCUMENT IS SUCH LICENCE OR NOTICE (FINAL CONCLUSION)&quot;" target="&quot;DEFENCE TO PROCEEDINGS UNDER SECTION 4, 5, 6, 7, 13 OR 17 (FINAL)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The final conclusion of the defence to proceedings under section 4-17 includes the document being such a licence or notice as valid evidence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd0ab37b084efd20396f2b25c97ab3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE SECRETARY AND EXECUTIVE COUNCIL&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ORDINANCE can be exempted from certain provisions by a decree published in the GAZETTE with the approval of ADMINISTRATIVE SECRETARY AND EXECUTIVE COUNCIL."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0aa33b76129ff2291e92c06beb87f12a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE SECRETARY AND EXECUTIVE COUNCIL&quot;" target="&quot;GAZETTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The GAZETTE is used to publish decrees for exempting provisions under the ORDINANCE with ADMINISTRATIVE SECRETARY AND EXECUTIVE COUNCIL's approval."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0aa33b76129ff2291e92c06beb87f12a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;35. EXEMPTIONS FROM PROVISIONS OF THE ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;GAZETTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The GAZETTE is used for publishing orders that may exempt certain areas, places, premises or activities from the Ordinance provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e7a153c57e6b577c1b46cd329273673a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;35. EXEMPTIONS FROM PROVISIONS OF THE ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;AREA, PLACE, PREMISES OR ACTIVITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Exemptions can be made for specific AREA, PLACE, PREMISES or ACTIVITY from the Ordinance provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e7a153c57e6b577c1b46cd329273673a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;35. EXEMPTIONS FROM PROVISIONS OF THE ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;2 OF 1994 S. 8&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The order under section 35 can be amended by the addition of specific provisions like those in 2 of 1994 s. 8."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e7a153c57e6b577c1b46cd329273673a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;35. EXEMPTIONS FROM PROVISIONS OF THE ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;E.R. 2 OF 2021&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The order under section 35 can be edited by the record in E.R. 2 of 2021."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e7a153c57e6b577c1b46cd329273673a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;35. EXEMPTIONS FROM PROVISIONS OF THE ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;AMENDED 21 OF 2024 S. 78&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The order under section 35 can be amended by the addition of specific provisions like those in Amended 21 of 2024 s. 78."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e7a153c57e6b577c1b46cd329273673a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AREA, PLACE, PREMISES OR ACTIVITY&quot;" target="&quot;$10,000 FOR EACH DAY DURING WHICH THE OFFENCE CONTINUES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Area, place, premises or activity can be fined $10,000 per day for continuing offences."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e7a153c57e6b577c1b46cd329273673a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MTR CORPORATION LIMITED&quot;" target="&quot;OCEAN PARK CORPORATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both companies operate in Hong Kong's tourism and entertainment sector, potentially collaborating on events or promotions that benefit from public transport access."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7a31b81a1625e550531d4c12b4182702</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AIRCRAFT NOISE&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 13B&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"SECTION 13B does not apply to aircraft noise as specified by the Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-471ea86899263b19957a8682c15503f9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 13B&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 13B does not apply to the Government or any public officer making noises during duty hours, indicating a relationship through exemption from certain provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dbe588d5c34575494b1af01bf122cae8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;特區政府&quot;" target="&quot;政務司司長&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"政務司司長負責調查監督提交的報告，并采取措施防止違規行為再次發生。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-87b463683890ea692cb1904bcc74ba11</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;POLITICAL SECRETARY&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Political Secretary is part of the Authority that can determine actions against violations or potential recurrence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dbe588d5c34575494b1af01bf122cae8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 4, 5, 6, 7, 13, 13A, 14, 15, 16 OR 17&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers can make noises during their duties without facing criminal liability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dbe588d5c34575494b1af01bf122cae8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 4, 5, 6, 7, 13, 13A, 14, 15, 16 OR 17&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Authority can decide on actions against violations of noise regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dbe588d5c34575494b1af01bf122cae8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers are part of the Government Department and carry out duties related to noise control."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ae14afda9d52be1864e9090474b79d7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT&quot;" target="&quot;NOISE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Government Department officials are responsible for managing and controlling noise as part of their duties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ae14afda9d52be1864e9090474b79d7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTIFICATION&quot;" target="&quot;NOISE CONTROL OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"NOISE CONTROL OFFICER is responsible for issuing notifications according to the Noise Control Ordinance (Chapter 400)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a63521ff775998da1314db4dd547a7d9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTIFICATION&quot;" target="&quot;NOISE CONTROL ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 400)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The NOISE CONTROL ORDINANCE (Chapter 400) governs the issuance and service of notifications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a63521ff775998da1314db4dd547a7d9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTIFICATION&quot;" target="&quot;OMITTED AS SPENT (已失時效而略去)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Notices that are omitted as spent do not apply to current notifications and thus no longer serve their purpose for the GOVERNMENT or DEPARTMENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a63521ff775998da1314db4dd547a7d9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIRECTOR OR SENIOR PERSONNEL OF AN ORGANIZATION&quot;" target="&quot;PREMISES OR PLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Notifications can be served on the owner, tenant, occupier or person in charge of any PREMISES OR PLACE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a63521ff775998da1314db4dd547a7d9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREMISES OR PLACE&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers have the power to enter, inspect, and examine any premises or place where they believe persons are employed at all reasonable times."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-057cc616cb8b855799f3fcacf937e222</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE CORPORATION&quot; MENTIONED IN (A)" target="&quot;DIRECTOR(S) ASSOCIATED WITH THE MANAGEMENT OF THE CORPORATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Directors associated with The Corporation's management are involved in the notification process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6d5c1db270105c42831679d46cdf6fb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE CORPORATION&quot; MENTIONED IN (A)" target="&quot;SENIOR PERSONNEL AUTHORIZED BY DIRECTORS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Senior personnel authorized by directors of The Corporation receive notifications regarding noise violations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6d5c1db270105c42831679d46cdf6fb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE PERSON MENTIONED IN (IV) UNDER SECTION 28B(1)(B)&quot;" target="&quot;NOISE VIOLATION NOTIFICATION&quot; MENTIONED IN SECTION 28B(1)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The person mentioned in Section 28B(1)(b)(iv) receives the noise violation notification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6d5c1db270105c42831679d46cdf6fb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL PROCEEDINGS AGAINST THE CORPORATION FOR NOISE VIOLATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;NOISE VIOLATION NOTIFICATION&quot; MENTIONED IN SECTION 28B(1)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal proceedings against the corporation for noise violations are based on notifications of noise violations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6d5c1db270105c42831679d46cdf6fb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE VIOLATION NOTIFICATION&quot; MENTIONED IN SECTION 28B(1)(B)&quot;" target="&quot;THE PREMISES, PUBLIC PLACES, CONSTRUCTION SITES, OR OTHER LOCATIONS MENTIONED IN SECTION 28B(1)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The premises, public places, construction sites, or other locations mentioned in the notification are subject to legal proceedings for noise violations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6d5c1db270105c42831679d46cdf6fb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE CONTROL REGULATION&quot; MENTIONED IN SECTION 28A AND 28B&quot;" target="&quot;THE CORPORATION'S MANAGEMENT&quot; MENTIONED THROUGHOUT &quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Noise Control Regulation mentioned in Section 28A and 28B applies to The Corporation's management."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6d5c1db270105c42831679d46cdf6fb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL ACTIONS AGAINST INDIVIDUALS ASSOCIATED WITH THE CORPORATION'S MANAGEMENT&quot; MENTIONED IN SECTION 28B(1)(C)&quot;" target="&quot;THE NOISE CONTROL REGULATION&quot; AS A WHOLE &quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal actions against individuals associated with The Corporation's management are based on the Noise Control Regulation as a whole."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6d5c1db270105c42831679d46cdf6fb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE CONTROL AUTHORITY/PUBLIC OFFICER AUTHORIZED UNDER SECTION 3(3) OF THE NOISE CONTROL ORDINANCE (CAP. 400)&quot;" target="&quot;DIRECTOR(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Noise Control Authority or Public Officer has the authority to serve notices and take proceedings against Directors for offenses under the Noise Control Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bd34572cc7a7c12a47fc15cbaf1c545c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOISE CONTROL AUTHORITY/PUBLIC OFFICER AUTHORIZED UNDER SECTION 3(3) OF THE NOISE CONTROL ORDINANCE (CAP. 400)&quot;" target="&quot;OFFICER(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Noise Control Authority or Public Officer has the authority to serve notices and take proceedings against Officers for offenses under the Noise Control Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bd34572cc7a7c12a47fc15cbaf1c545c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIRECTOR(S)&quot;" target="&quot;OFFICER(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Directors can delegate their management authority to Officers, who then act on behalf of the Directors in managing the Body Corporate."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bd34572cc7a7c12a47fc15cbaf1c545c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY AND HEALTH ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Occupational Safety and Health Ordinance aims to amend the FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-eb7fcd5200d5f794a363f07e5ee2dc70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY AND HEALTH ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE APPEALS BOARD ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Occupational Safety and Health Ordinance also intends to amend the ADMINISTRATIVE APPEALS BOARD ORDINANCE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-eb7fcd5200d5f794a363f07e5ee2dc70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;INQUIRY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The inquiry is conducted under the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance, even after certain sections have been repealed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ead21a291080deb8a3da710d2fd2a7fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SHORT TITLE&quot;" target="&quot;PURPOSE OF THE ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SHORT TITLE provides a name by which the ordinance may be cited, while its PURPOSE outlines the objectives of ensuring employee safety and health at work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-eb7fcd5200d5f794a363f07e5ee2dc70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE PURPOSES OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The purposes of this Ordinance directly relate to workplace safety and health measures as defined by the term 'workplace' in the ordinance. The objectives are to ensure a safe and healthy environment for employees at their workplaces."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61cee1a453a83b87002df2318ef0eb78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE PURPOSES OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The purposes of this Ordinance include improving safety standards, which aligns with the issuance of workplace codes of practice as mentioned in section 40(1). These codes are a means to achieve some of the stated objectives."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61cee1a453a83b87002df2318ef0eb78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPIER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The occupier of a workplace is someone who has some degree of control over the premises, which may include those mentioned in the code of practice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;SERIOUS BODILY INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition of SERIOUS BODILY INJURY impacts how risks arising out of activities at WORK are managed and documented in a workplace code of practice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-126e18663d810ba6b83365ff30027a71</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;SUSPENSION NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A SUSPENSION NOTICE is a regulation that may impact workplace practices and codes of practice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-126e18663d810ba6b83365ff30027a71</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;COURTROOM PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Workplace code of practice may be used as evidence and influence legal proceedings, including courtroom procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A workplace code of practice can serve as relevant evidence in legal proceedings involving disputes over the applicability of laws or regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;SAFETY FACILITIES FOR INJURIES FROM ACCIDENTS AT WORK LOCATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Safety facilities for injuries from accidents at work locations are mentioned as a provision that can be regulated by the Chief Secretary through subsidiary legislation, which is relevant to workplace code of practice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-71e44b452a884e51f90079ec8a9ac88f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;HAZARDS AND POTENTIAL HAZARDS IN WORK LOCATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Hazards and potential hazards in work locations are also provisions that can be regulated by the Chief Secretary through subsidiary legislation, which is relevant to workplace code of practice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-71e44b452a884e51f90079ec8a9ac88f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC ANALYST&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSTANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A public analyst, such as a government chemist, may analyze substances in their work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC ANALYST&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATION SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A PUBLIC ANALYST, such as a Government Chemist or Pathologist, may provide analysis for occupational safety issues but is not directly an OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC ANALYST&quot;" target="&quot;SAMPLE ANALYSIS PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public Analyst is involved in analyzing one part of the sample provided by the Occupational Safety Officer according to the Sample Analysis Procedure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b491d14ac4486a01edd1dfafab97ca07</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC ANALYST&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE OF EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A public analyst may be requested by an occupational safety officer to analyze a sample of evidence provided under section 22."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4c1ae5b0a8aff1b3116e95deba9e3ee</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC ANALYST&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An Occupational Safety Officer must give one part of the sample to a Public Analyst for analysis as per subsection (3). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ce083c97323a19a9162d045f2002c1d4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DANGEROUS OCCURRENCE&quot;" target="&quot;RECORD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Dangerous occurrences must be recorded according to workplace codes of practice for safety and legal compliance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DANGEROUS OCCURRENCE&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational Safety Officer must be informed of any DANGEROUS OCCURRENCE at the workplace by the OCCUPIER OF RELEVANT PREMISES."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3d781ae6a3974dcd155b4f5b736d6161</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPIER&quot;" target="&quot;PLANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupiers of a workplace have control over the use and maintenance of plant equipment within their premises."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPIER&quot;" target="&quot;STRICT LIABILITY OFFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The occupier may be held responsible for strict liability offences as they are the person in control of the premises where such incidents might occur."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bec6b7a4bfd3c0c262594492fc624e7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPIER&quot;" target="&quot;WORK-RELATED DANGER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The occupier of the workplace bears responsibility for dangers that may arise there."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bec6b7a4bfd3c0c262594492fc624e7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPIER&quot;" target="&quot;INDEPENDENT CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Independent contractors may also fall under the definition of occupiers, depending on their obligations and responsibilities as stated in the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3717bfa1a0a429ae82cff6583f9ffc97</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPIER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEES AT WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'occupier' is not explicitly mentioned, but it can be inferred that employees may also need to consider the safety of others who might be affected by their actions in a shared workspace."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0a0ae0d06f82179e57847e5fde58901</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPIER&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner can also serve a Suspension Notice on an Occupier of the premises where workplace safety risks are identified."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner can also serve an improvement notice on the Occupier, who is responsible for premises where a workplace is located."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbb962605c6a7e5085bf69519da702fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPIER&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS LIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupier is responsible for business liabilities related to their use and management of premises."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3af7b8f9d9569fddb32c031c5ec0dbc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PLANT&quot;" target="&quot;BODILY INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Plant can cause bodily injury if not used or maintained properly, especially in dangerous occurrences."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IDENTITY CARD&quot;" target="&quot;PERSON RESPONSIBLE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The person responsible for a workplace may need to verify identity cards of employees and visitors as part of their duties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0e2a533c6d1827b9ef6feae269cab454</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IDENTITY CARD&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees may need identity cards for verification in their employment, which is a common requirement by employers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7249fad978915b4915d01ecac03019f3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IDENTITY CARD&quot;" target="&quot;FUNCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"FUNCTION is related to the power and duty that may involve using or requiring an IDENTITY CARD for identification purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IDENTITY CARD&quot;" target="&quot;RECORD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A RECORD includes information recorded in electronic form which could pertain to an IDENTITY CARD for documentation purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IDENTITY CARD&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The officer may request an identity card from a person suspected to have committed an offense against this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4c1ae5b0a8aff1b3116e95deba9e3ee</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BODILY INJURY&quot;" target="&quot;SERIOUS BODILY INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Serious bodily injury is a more severe form of bodily injury that requires hospital or clinic treatment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSTANCE&quot;" target="&quot;RECORD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Substances can be recorded for documentation purposes in relation to incidents or inspections."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSTANCE&quot;" target="&quot;RISKS ARISING OUT OF ACTIVITIES AT WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Substances, whether natural or artificial, can pose RISKS that need to be addressed under the Workplace Code of Practice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-126e18663d810ba6b83365ff30027a71</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RECORD&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employee records may be created or maintained to document incidents involving bodily injury or safety issues."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSON RESPONSIBLE&quot;" target="&quot;FUNCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The person responsible for a workplace has certain functions and duties related to occupational safety and health."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSON RESPONSIBLE&quot;" target="&quot;OFFENCE OF STRICT LIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PERSON RESPONSIBLE is involved in workplace offenses where strict liability applies, making them accountable for certain actions without needing to prove intent or knowledge."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOMESTIC SERVANT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A domestic servant is considered an employee in the context of employment laws, including those concerning bodily injury."&lt;SEP&gt;"DOMESTIC SERVANT is not considered an EMPLOYEE under the Employment Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Domestic servants, while not included in the definition of employees, may still be involved in employment-related activities or disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7249fad978915b4915d01ecac03019f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46d0d7db59a8dee1e09d7d4424293375</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOMESTIC SERVANT&quot;" target="&quot;SPOUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'spouse' is defined in the context of marriage, which could include domestic servants like gardeners or drivers as part of a household staff."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8b40910fef9ba5e880f9a32ae794f8b2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOMESTIC SERVANT&quot;" target="&quot;CEASE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Domestic servants are part of household staff that could have their employment status changed by ceasing operations or services."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8b40910fef9ba5e880f9a32ae794f8b2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOMESTIC SERVANT&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Domestic servants are covered by the U.K. law regarding severance payment under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9546d09d8137ba2697ee36074c84b498</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOMESTIC SERVANT&quot;" target="&quot;PRIVATE HOUSEHOLD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"DOMESTIC SERVANTS are employed within PRIVATE HOUSEHOLDS as part of their operations and maintenance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Domestic servants work in or for a private household, often under the management of the deceased employer's personal representative posthumously."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0a79efc9c7d5b3c5051c209e7d8238e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae8f763a371efa17099b990f69f8b4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOMESTIC SERVANT&quot;" target="&quot;PERSONAL REPRESENTATIVE OF THE DECEASED EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The personal representative manages domestic servants who were employed by the deceased employer and continues their employment after death."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0a79efc9c7d5b3c5051c209e7d8238e8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IMPROVEMENT NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;SERIOUS BODILY INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An improvement notice might be issued in response to a serious bodily injury incident to ensure corrective actions are taken."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IMPROVEMENT NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE VIOLATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An Improvement Notice must be served when there are violations of workplace regulations or ordinances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IMPROVEMENT NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An improvement notice is directed at an EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER who has contravened the FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (Cap. 59). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-70cdeeb8eece52f9eaa0ef190c0b61e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IMPROVEMENT NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner issues improvement notices to address contraventions under the FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (Cap. 59). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-70cdeeb8eece52f9eaa0ef190c0b61e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUSPENSION NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner determines the application for review of a suspension notice and informs the applicant about the decision."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner has the authority to issue Suspension Notices."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fbb962605c6a7e5085bf69519da702fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8247282749bd85cb6d48e946a81b3c1e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUSPENSION NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;IMMINENT RISK OF DEATH OR SERIOUS BODILY INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Suspension notices are issued when there is an imminent risk of death or serious bodily injury on the premises."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05baa7711eb26dcfef62e1a9f005bfc8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FUNCTION&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational Safety Officers have specific functions related to ensuring workplace safety and preventing bodily injury."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FUNCTION&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commission's functions include developing and promoting international trade law, which can involve defining terms such as 'function' in relevant conventions or laws."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6028b01799478cec839282a4d1179b1b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SERIOUS BODILY INJURY&quot;" target="&quot;OFFENCE OF STRICT LIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Serious bodily injuries may lead to offences of strict liability if they result from a breach of regulations or duties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SERIOUS BODILY INJURY&quot;" target="&quot;WORK-RELATED DANGER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Serious bodily injury can occur in a workplace setting, which is related to work-related dangers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bec6b7a4bfd3c0c262594492fc624e7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SERIOUS BODILY INJURY&quot;" target="&quot;TIME AT WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Serious bodily injuries can occur during time at work, linking these two concepts closely."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bec6b7a4bfd3c0c262594492fc624e7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SERIOUS BODILY INJURY&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENTS AND OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Serious bodily injury can be a result of workplace accidents and is covered under the regulations for occupational health and safety."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SERIOUS BODILY INJURY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees may suffer serious bodily injury as a result of workplace accidents or unsafe working conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TIME AT WORK&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Time at work is defined within a workplace, indicating their direct connection and context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bec6b7a4bfd3c0c262594492fc624e7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RISKS ARISING OUT OF ACTIVITIES AT WORK&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition of WORKPLACE includes any place where employees work, which must comply with RISKS arising from activities at work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-126e18663d810ba6b83365ff30027a71</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INDEPENDENT CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;SELF-EMPLOYED PERSON&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both terms refer to similar roles but are used in different contexts within this ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3717bfa1a0a429ae82cff6583f9ffc97</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INDEPENDENT CONTRACTORS AND SELF-EMPLOYED PERSONS&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">3.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers are mentioned in relation to their capacity as such, but there's no direct relationship between independent contractors and self-employed persons and public officer roles within the context of this ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cbf739f28af13fb255489857524eaf50</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPIER OF PREMISES&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The OCCUPIER OF PREMISES is responsible for ensuring the safety and health of EMPLOYEES working at those premises."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9a215b7541a9d5eb966c5aa9ffed5374</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPIER OF PREMISES&quot;" target="&quot;IMPRISONMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The OCCUPIER OF PREMISES might be imprisoned for failing to ensure employee safety and health, especially if they act negligently or intentionally."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9a215b7541a9d5eb966c5aa9ffed5374</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPIER OF PREMISES&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The occupier of premises must ensure the safety and health measures for employees, which involves cooperation with employers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0812f6740fa10908c6c96dfb7b577a49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPIER OF PREMISES&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S ROLE IN WORKPLACE SAFETY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupiers must ensure workplace safety measures are followed by employees as part of their role."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0812f6740fa10908c6c96dfb7b577a49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPIER OF PREMISES&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRAVENTION OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupiers of premises may be requested to provide information that could indicate a contravention of the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;TOTAL CONTRACTOR OR PREVIOUS SUBCONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Total contractors or previous subcontractors can claim wages directly from the employee’s employer if they have paid the employee as per section 43C. This involves either sharing the debt with a prior subcontractor or deducting payments due to subsequent subcontractors for work done by the same employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05508a87b3ed23ef299b7e04a0fe44c9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEANS OF ACCESS TO AND EGRESS FROM THE PREMISES&quot;" target="&quot;SAFETY MEASURES FOR ACCESS ROUTES AND EGRESS POINTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The means of access should be safe and without risks to health, which is a safety measure for the routes and egress points."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0812f6740fa10908c6c96dfb7b577a49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S WORKPLACE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY AND HEALTH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees' workplace must ensure that it is as far as reasonably practicable, safe and without risks to health."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0812f6740fa10908c6c96dfb7b577a49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY AND HEALTH MEASURES&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPIER'S RESPONSIBILITY FOR SAFETY MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupiers have a responsibility to ensure workplace safety and health measures are in place."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0812f6740fa10908c6c96dfb7b577a49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-EMPLOYEE COOPERATION&quot;" target="&quot;COOPERATION WITH EMPLOYERS ON SAFETY MATTERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers and employees must cooperate on safety matters, including the implementation of safety measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0812f6740fa10908c6c96dfb7b577a49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGULATIONS FOR WORKPLACE SAFETY AND HEALTH&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY COMPLIANCE MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Regulations for workplace safety and health are to be complied with by employers and employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0812f6740fa10908c6c96dfb7b577a49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FINES AND IMPRISONMENT FOR NON-COMPLIANCE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY AND HEALTH REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Non-compliance with workplace safety and health regulations can result in fines or imprisonment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0812f6740fa10908c6c96dfb7b577a49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S RESPONSIBILITY FOR OTHERS' SAFETY&quot;" target="&quot;SAFETY AND HEALTH PROVISIONS UNDER THE LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees have a duty of care towards colleagues, which is covered under the safety and health provisions in law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0812f6740fa10908c6c96dfb7b577a49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SAFETY AND HEALTH PROVISIONS UNDER THE LAW&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S ROLE IN REPORTING HAZARDS OR UNSAFE CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees have a role in reporting hazards or unsafe conditions, which are covered under the law's provisions for workplace safety and health."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0812f6740fa10908c6c96dfb7b577a49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPIER'S ROLE IN ENSURING PREMISES ARE SAFE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S DUTY OF CARE TOWARDS COLLEAGUES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupiers must ensure premises are safe, including ensuring employees care for their colleagues' safety."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0812f6740fa10908c6c96dfb7b577a49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY COMPLIANCE PROCEDURES&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE-EMPLOYER COOPERATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Cooperation between employers and employees is necessary to comply with workplace safety procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0812f6740fa10908c6c96dfb7b577a49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE-EMPLOYER COMMUNICATION ON WORKPLACE SAFETY&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPIER'S DUTY OF CARE TOWARDS EMPLOYEES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupiers must ensure employees' safety, which involves communication on workplace safety matters with employers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0812f6740fa10908c6c96dfb7b577a49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEES AT WORK&quot;" target="&quot;SAFETY AND HEALTH REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees must comply with safety and health regulations while at work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0a0ae0d06f82179e57847e5fde58901</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SAFETY AND HEALTH REGULATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Safety and health regulations are enforced through ordinances or other legal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0a0ae0d06f82179e57847e5fde58901</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE GROUNDS FOR NON-COMPLIANCE&quot;" target="&quot;400,000 HKD AND 12 MONTHS IMPRISONMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A failure to comply with an Improvement Notice can result in criminal charges and penalties if there are reasonable grounds for non-compliance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE REGULATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPIER'S RESPONSIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The occupier is responsible for ensuring compliance with workplace regulations, which may include receiving an improvement notice if non-compliance is found."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IMPROVEMENT NOTICE PROCEDURE&quot;" target="&quot;REGULATORY ENFORCEMENT MECHANISMS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The process of serving an improvement notice is one mechanism used by regulatory bodies to enforce compliance with workplace regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT LAW&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINAL PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of TERMINAL PAYMENTS falls under EMPLOYMENT LAW and its calculation methods are governed by relevant provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a1958590510250b6ab53b0fe3e4cc53e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT LAW&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT REGULATION AMENDMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"EMPLOYMENT LAW can be amended through EMPLOYMENT REGULATION AMENDMENTS, such as the 2014 amendment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL HEALTH AND SAFETY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER'S COMPLIANCE OBLIGATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers have obligations under occupational health and safety laws that can be enforced through the issuance of improvement notices."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE INSPECTION&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational Safety Officers conduct workplace inspections as part of their job responsibilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Occupational safety officers may assist in workplace inspections as described in section 21(3)(a), and their actions are protected by the ordinance from personal liability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e25506f50e901e7cebe325e56cdc3f67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7f5c7774940469ec261850f6dbd6b83</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE INSPECTION&quot;" target="&quot;FACTORY AND INDUSTRIAL OPERATIONS ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 59,)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Factory and Industrial Operations Ordinance governs workplace inspections as described in section 21(3)(a), providing legal framework for public officers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e25506f50e901e7cebe325e56cdc3f67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGULATORY ENFORCEMENT MECHANISMS&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE INSPECTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Inspections, including those related to workplace violations, are part of the broader enforcement mechanisms used by regulatory bodies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92398049cd93d8f432b90b9d7cf63d15</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER&quot;" target="&quot;IMPROVEMENT NOTICE COMPLIANCE FAILURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER who fails to comply with an IMPROVEMENT NOTICE commits an offence under the FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (Cap. 59). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-70cdeeb8eece52f9eaa0ef190c0b61e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPORARY SUSPENSION ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A TEMPORARY SUSPENSION ORDER can be issued against an EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER who has contravened the FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (Cap. 59). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-70cdeeb8eece52f9eaa0ef190c0b61e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner has the authority to issue and amend suspension notices concerning employers or occupiers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05baa7711eb26dcfef62e1a9f005bfc8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER&quot;" target="&quot;FURTHER FINE OF $100,000 AND TO IMPRISONMENT FOR 12 MONTHS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers or occupiers who contravene a suspension notice are liable to further fines and imprisonment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05baa7711eb26dcfef62e1a9f005bfc8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPORARY STOP NOTICE REVIEW RIGHTS OF EMPLOYERS AND OCCUPIERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers or occupiers have the right to apply for review of temporary stop notices issued by the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05baa7711eb26dcfef62e1a9f005bfc8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER&quot;" target="&quot;RIGHT OF EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER TO HAVE SUSPENSION NOTICE REVIEWED&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer or occupier has the right to apply for review of a suspension notice within 28 days after being served with it."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8247282749bd85cb6d48e946a81b3c1e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER&quot;" target="&quot;RIGHT OF EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER TO APPEAL AGAINST DECISION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer or occupier can appeal against the Commissioner's decision to an Appeal Commission within 28 days after receiving written notice of the decision."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8247282749bd85cb6d48e946a81b3c1e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER&quot;" target="&quot;NOTIFICATION OF SUSPENSION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER receives a NOTIFICATION OF SUSPENSION from the COMMISSIONER, which they may appeal against to the APPEAL BOARD."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bc8d52a1038b5b838fbe9231f59cfc74</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IMPROVEMENT NOTICE COMPLIANCE FAILURE&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner can revoke or amend an IMPROVEMENT NOTICE if the EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER fails to comply with it. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-70cdeeb8eece52f9eaa0ef190c0b61e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IMPROVEMENT NOTICE COMPLIANCE FAILURE&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPORARY SUSPENSION ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A TEMPORARY SUSPENSION ORDER may be issued as a result of IMPROVEMENT NOTICE COMPLIANCE FAILURE by the EMPLOYER OR OCCUPIER. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-70cdeeb8eece52f9eaa0ef190c0b61e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY SUSPENSION ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner has the authority to issue a TEMPORARY SUSPENSION ORDER under the FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (Cap. 59). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-70cdeeb8eece52f9eaa0ef190c0b61e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主或佔用人&quot;" target="&quot;WITH SUBSECTION (1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"With subsection (1) intentionally, knowingly or recklessly commits an offence and is liable on conviction to a fine of $150,000 and to imprisonment for 6 months. describes the liability of employers or occupiers who violate certain regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-177e6ff0318fdbf5027a1eb0367239e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主或佔用人&quot;" target="&quot;處長&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Director can issue an improvement notice to employers or occupants if they are found in violation of specific regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"處長可以因應情況修訂或暂停实施暂時停工通知书，以及撤銷该通知书。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-177e6ff0318fdbf5027a1eb0367239e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4dd58ad4c9957f63fe03ad87123a328</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主或佔用人&quot;" target="&quot;暫時停工通知書&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"暫時停工通知書必須送達給僱主或佔用人，指示其不得進行某些活動或使用特定處所、作業裝置或物質。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f4dd58ad4c9957f63fe03ad87123a328</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;暫時停工通知書&quot;" target="&quot;處長&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"處長有權發出暫時停工通知書並決定其內容和生效日期。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f4dd58ad4c9957f63fe03ad87123a328</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY STOP NOTICE REVIEW RIGHTS OF EMPLOYERS AND OCCUPIERS&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER'S DECISION NOTIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner must notify employers or occupiers of their decisions regarding the review applications for temporary stop notices."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05baa7711eb26dcfef62e1a9f005bfc8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPLICATION FOR REVIEW OF TEMPORARY STOP NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;14 DAYS PERIOD AFTER RECEIVING THE APPLICATION FOR REVIEW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The application for review must be submitted within 28 days after receiving a temporary stop notice, and the Commissioner's decision is required to be made within 14 days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05baa7711eb26dcfef62e1a9f005bfc8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DECISION&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPORARY WORK STOPPAGE NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Decision may result in revocation, confirmation, or variation of a temporary work stoppage notice based on the review application by Employer or Occupier."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8247282749bd85cb6d48e946a81b3c1e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATHEMATICS (TIME FRAMES)&quot;" target="&quot;SOCIAL SCIENCES (REGULATION AND COMPLIANCE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The regulation and compliance involve time frames such as 14 days for decision-making, which are quantified in mathematical terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8247282749bd85cb6d48e946a81b3c1e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATHEMATICS (TIME FRAMES)&quot;" target="&quot;SOCIAL SCIENCES (DISPUTE RESOLUTION THEORIES)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both MATHEMATICS (TIME FRAMES) and SOCIAL SCIENCES (DISPUTE RESOLUTION THEORIES) are relevant to the DISPUTE RESOLUTION PROCEDURE, though in different aspects."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7ad6aa79a150340c8a28d98a0e6b1a24</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENTS OR OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COMMISSIONER makes decisions related to WORKPLACE ACCIDENTS or OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES that can be appealed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bc8d52a1038b5b838fbe9231f59cfc74</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENTS OR OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES&quot;" target="&quot;WORK LOCATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Workplace accidents or occupational diseases occur at WORK LOCATION and are subject to regulations and decisions by the COMMISSIONER and APPEAL BOARD."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bc8d52a1038b5b838fbe9231f59cfc74</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENTS AND OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES&quot;" target="&quot;INDUSTRIAL ACTIVITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Industrial activities details must be provided in the report of a workplace accident as per regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENTS AND OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY DEPARTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Occupational Safety Department oversees and manages reports related to workplace accidents and occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENTS AND OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY TRAINING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational safety training is required to prevent and manage workplace accidents and occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENTS AND OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational safety measures are implemented to prevent and manage workplace accidents and occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENTS AND OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT INJURY REPORTING REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employment injury reporting requirements are part of the regulations for managing workplace accidents and occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENTS AND OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES&quot;" target="&quot;INDUSTRIAL ACTIVITIES DETAILS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Industrial activities details are required to be provided when reporting incidents related to workplace accidents or occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENTS AND OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE INCIDENT DOCUMENTATION STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Workplace incident documentation standards are required to be followed when reporting incidents related to workplace accidents or occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENTS AND OCCUPATIONAL DISEASES&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY COMPLIANCE AUDITS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational safety compliance audits are conducted to ensure proper management and reporting of incidents related to workplace accidents or occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOST WORK CAPACITY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees may suffer lost work capacity due to workplace accidents or occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INDUSTRIAL ACTIVITIES&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Industrial Activities are conducted in the Workplace, which can lead to accidents requiring notification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE INCIDENT REPORTING SYSTEM&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational Safety Officers use the Workplace Incident Reporting System to document and manage reports from employers regarding accidents and diseases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT INJURY REPORTING REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational Safety Officers oversee the Employment Injury Reporting Requirements as part of their duties in managing workplace accidents and occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE INCIDENT MANAGEMENT SYSTEM&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational Safety Officers use the Workplace Incident Management System to manage reports from employers regarding incidents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY TRAINING PROGRAMS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees may participate in Occupational Safety Training Programs as part of their training and safety measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSON RESPONSIBLE FOR WORKPLACE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER'S MAIN BUSINESS ADDRESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Person Responsible for the Workplace is associated with the Employer's Main Business Address where incidents may happen."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e87bb6b8feb2f7d365e7f2290bc5e29c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSON RESPONSIBLE FOR WORKPLACE&quot;" target="&quot;PENALTY FOR NON-COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Person Responsible for Workplace may face penalties for non-compliance with safety regulations, as outlined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e87bb6b8feb2f7d365e7f2290bc5e29c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE INJURED&quot;" target="&quot;DEATH REPORT AFTER INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Death Report After Injury is generated if the injured employee dies after the accident."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e87bb6b8feb2f7d365e7f2290bc5e29c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE INJURED&quot;" target="&quot;INCAPACITATED (喪失工作能力)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Incapacitated is a condition that can result from an Employee Injured due to an Accident."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e87bb6b8feb2f7d365e7f2290bc5e29c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPIER OF THE PREMISES&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Occupier of the Premises is responsible for workplace activities, including accident reporting."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ACCIDENT NOTIFICATION REQUIREMENT&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Accident Notification Requirements dictate the actions Occupational Safety Officers must take upon receiving reports."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMERCIAL ACTIVITIES&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Commercial Activities may occur at Workplaces and contribute to accident scenarios needing reporting."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OTHER ACTIVITIES&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Other Types of Activities can take place in the Workplace, potentially leading to accidents that need notification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IDENTITY CARD NUMBER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Identity Card Numbers are required for reporting details about Employees involved in accidents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AGE (IF KNOWN)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Age Information is collected and reported for Employees who have been victims of accidents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEATH NOTIFICATION REQUIREMENT&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Death Notification Requirements mandate that Occupational Safety Officers be informed when an Employee dies after an accident."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCAPACITATION REPORTING REQUIREMENT&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Incapacitation Reporting Requirements require Occupational Safety Officers to be notified if Employees are incapacitated due to accidents at Workplaces."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;POLICE STATION&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An Occupational Safety Officer is involved in reporting incidents to the nearest Police Station when required."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cbbad1d728178af8a023898a237d258a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DANGEROUS ACCIDENT&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Dangerous Accident, as defined by the ordinance, must be reported from a Workplace according to specific regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cbbad1d728178af8a023898a237d258a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DANGEROUS ACCIDENT&quot;" target="&quot;INCAPACITATED (喪失工作能力)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Dangerous Accident can result in a victim being Incapacitated, either permanently or temporarily from working."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cbbad1d728178af8a023898a237d258a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DANGEROUS ACCIDENT&quot;" target="&quot;SCHEDULE 5&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Schedule 5 has effect and may contain provisions related to dangerous accidents mentioned in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5ca77e785253c5f3aca0053cf386383c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DANGEROUS ACCIDENT&quot;" target="&quot;SCHEDULE 1&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similar to Schedule 5, Schedule 1 might also have relevant content regarding dangerous accidents as it is part of a document dealing with such matters."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5ca77e785253c5f3aca0053cf386383c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPIER OF RELEVANT PREMISES&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The OCCUPIER OF RELEVANT PREMISES is responsible for the WORKPLACE where dangerous occurrences may happen."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3d781ae6a3974dcd155b4f5b736d6161</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTY DAMAGE OR DESTRUCTION&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The report to Occupational Safety Officer must include particulars of damage to, or destruction of, property (property damage or destruction). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3d781ae6a3974dcd155b4f5b736d6161</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CIRCUMSTANCES OF OCCURRENCE&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The report to Occupational Safety Officer must contain the circumstances of the occurrence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3d781ae6a3974dcd155b4f5b736d6161</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOCTOR&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER OR FORMER EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Doctors are required to report occupational diseases found or suspected in employees or former employees to the Chief Officer, who may be an employer or a former employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3d781ae6a3974dcd155b4f5b736d6161</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOCTOR&quot;" target="&quot;SCHEDULE 2 DISEASES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Schedule 2 DISEASES must be reported if found or suspected by a DOCTOR during an examination of employees or former employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3d781ae6a3974dcd155b4f5b736d6161</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOCTOR&quot;" target="&quot;SCHEDULE 3 EXPOSURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Exposures mentioned in Schedule 3 may cause occupational diseases and should be considered when reporting to the Chief Officer by a DOCTOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3d781ae6a3974dcd155b4f5b736d6161</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENT OR DANGEROUS OCCURRENCE&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner arranges for inquiries related to Workplace Accidents or Dangerous Occurrences."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19f640b139895da0133f304114aeb8fc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE ACCIDENT OR DANGEROUS OCCURRENCE&quot;" target="&quot;INQUIRY INTO WORKPLACE ACCIDENT OR DANGEROUS OCCURRENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Workplace Accidents or Dangerous Occurrences trigger Inquiries to determine their causes and circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19f640b139895da0133f304114aeb8fc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INQUIRY INTO WORKPLACE ACCIDENT OR DANGEROUS OCCURRENCE&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational Safety Officers are responsible for conducting Inquiries into Workplace Accidents or Dangerous Occurrences as designated by the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19f640b139895da0133f304114aeb8fc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOR BUREAU&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Occupational Safety Officer conducts inquiries under the supervision of the Labor Bureau."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOR BUREAU&quot;" target="&quot;WITNESSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Witnesses are questioned by officials from the Labor Bureau during investigations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOR BUREAU&quot;" target="&quot;CIVIL LEGAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Labor Bureau officials may refer cases involving workplace incidents to civil legal proceedings if necessary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WITNESSES&quot;" target="&quot;FORMAL INQUIRY INTO WORKPLACE ACCIDENT OR DANGEROUS OCCURRENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Witnesses are required to attend and give evidence in formal inquiries, similar to their obligations in civil proceedings before a court."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1dbb46e60da08be769a0481277a08538</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WITNESSES&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Witnesses are required by the Commissioner or his deputy commissioner during formal inquiries into workplace accidents or dangerous occurrences."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1dbb46e60da08be769a0481277a08538</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WITNESSES&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATORS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitrators may hear witnesses as part of their proceedings to resolve disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WITNESSES&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitral tribunal can administer oaths and examine witnesses, indicating a direct relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CIVIL LEGAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;PROVISIONS FOR INQUIRY TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Provisions for Inquiry Termination address situations where an inquiry may be terminated due to unavailability or refusal of witnesses in civil legal proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CIVIL LEGAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;PROVIDING FALSE INFORMATION DURING INQUIRY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Providing false information during inquiry is a crime in civil legal proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5074da09c4f82109b976a4c8a7a052fb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CIVIL LEGAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Civil legal proceedings may be involved when disputes arise regarding wages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-602a52838c03cef3777006bf2a44b72e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CIVIL LEGAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;LABOR LAWS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Labor laws can lead to civil legal proceedings when there is a violation or dispute over the terms of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-602a52838c03cef3777006bf2a44b72e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INVESTIGATION OF ACCIDENTS OR DANGEROUS OCCURRENCES&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE INCIDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Investigations into accidents or dangerous occurrences are conducted for workplace incidents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE OF TERMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;REASONS FOR NON-ATTENDANCE OR REFUSAL TO PROVIDE EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The reasons for non-attendance or refusal to provide evidence can lead to the termination of an inquiry, which must be notified in writing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE OF TERMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT OBLIGATIONS UPON TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Notice of termination triggers specific payment obligations as outlined in SECTION 7."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE OF TERMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The relevant date is the reference point for when notice of termination takes effect."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a40a9600dcdabbcf7b1de20226238a1e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE OF TERMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;REST DAY OR HOLIDAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"References to relevant dates should be construed as the next day after a rest day or holiday if applicable."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a40a9600dcdabbcf7b1de20226238a1e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE OF TERMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;92-62-5 AMENDMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Amendments like the 92-62-5 Amendment modify how notice of termination is handled, particularly in cases involving rest days or holidays."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a40a9600dcdabbcf7b1de20226238a1e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROVISIONS FOR INQUIRY INITIATION AND CONDUCT&quot;" target="&quot;CIVIL LEGAL EVIDENCE RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Provisions for Inquiry Conduct Without Constraints allow the Occupational Safety Officer to gather evidence that may not be admissible in civil legal proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROVIDING FALSE INFORMATION DURING INQUIRY&quot;" target="&quot;WITNESS PROTECTION DURING INQUIRY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Providing false information during inquiry is not protected under witness protection during the inquiry process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5074da09c4f82109b976a4c8a7a052fb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROVIDING FALSE INFORMATION DURING INQUIRY&quot;" target="&quot;CRIMINAL LEGAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Providing false information during inquiry is a crime also in criminal legal proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5074da09c4f82109b976a4c8a7a052fb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORMAL INQUIRY INTO WORKPLACE ACCIDENT OR DANGEROUS OCCURRENCE&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner has the authority to arrange and conduct formal inquiries into workplace accidents or dangerous occurrences."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1dbb46e60da08be769a0481277a08538</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORMAL INQUIRY INTO WORKPLACE ACCIDENT OR DANGEROUS OCCURRENCE&quot;" target="&quot;CIVIL PROCEEDINGS BEFORE A COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Witnesses have the same rights and privileges as witnesses in civil proceedings when giving evidence in formal inquiries into workplace accidents or dangerous occurrences."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1dbb46e60da08be769a0481277a08538</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CIVIL PROCEEDINGS BEFORE A COURT&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner's actions during a formal inquiry, such as directing attendance of witnesses, are not bound by the rules of evidence and can be compared to procedures in civil proceedings before a court."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1dbb46e60da08be769a0481277a08538</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CORONIAL INQUEST&quot;" target="&quot;INQUIRY UNDER SECTION 17&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An inquiry under Section 17 does not influence or impact a coronial inquest."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4d187f5859fc0e151b7a45dda2b23c53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CORONIAL INQUEST&quot;" target="&quot;CRIMES ORDINANCE (CAP. 200)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both coronial inquests and inquiries under the Crimes Ordinance provide certain rights and protections for witnesses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4d187f5859fc0e151b7a45dda2b23c53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HEALTH OFFICER&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">21.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both the Commissioner and Health Officer have roles in exercising or performing certain functions under Ordinances, though their specific duties differ."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health Officers are also considered Occupational Safety Officers by virtue of their role, as designated by the Commissioner. "&lt;SEP&gt;"The COMMISSIONER authorizes HEALTH OFFICERS in writing to exercise and perform the functions of an occupational safety officer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a3c3394a6b72977677a8a437b4151b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea83763b873f6b32742c132cbac8d568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7f5c7774940469ec261850f6dbd6b83</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HEALTH OFFICER&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICERS and HEALTH OFFICERS are included in the list of persons who can be appointed as occupational safety officers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea83763b873f6b32742c132cbac8d568</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HEALTH OFFICER&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Health Officers are involved in the enforcement and execution of Ordinances, similar to Occupational Safety Officers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f7f5c7774940469ec261850f6dbd6b83</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUTHORITY CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An AUTHORITY CERTIFICATE is issued by the COMMISSIONER to each OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER as proof of their authority to perform functions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea83763b873f6b32742c132cbac8d568</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUTHORITY CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;EXERCISE OR PERFORMANCE OF FUNCTIONS BY OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"HOLDING AN AUTHORITY CERTIFICATE allows OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICERS to exercise and perform their functions legally."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea83763b873f6b32742c132cbac8d568</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREMISES OCCUPIER OR APPARENT MANAGER&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Occupational Safety Officer must inform the Premises Occupier or Apparent Manager of their right to request sample division into three parts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b491d14ac4486a01edd1dfafab97ca07</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 22 PREMISES ENTRY&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An occupational safety officer has the power to enter premises under Section 22."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed932e3526aee6a4abf0328b0cfd58ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 22 PREMISES ENTRY&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The entry under Section 22 allows occupational safety officers to seize articles believed to be evidence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed932e3526aee6a4abf0328b0cfd58ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 22 PREMISES ENTRY&quot;" target="&quot;PLANT EXAMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Entering premises under Section 22 enables the conduct of plant examinations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed932e3526aee6a4abf0328b0cfd58ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 22 PREMISES ENTRY&quot;" target="&quot;ATMOSPHERIC TESTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The entry under Section 22 permits conducting atmospheric tests to determine environmental conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed932e3526aee6a4abf0328b0cfd58ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE EVIDENCE&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational safety officers can seize articles believed to be evidence of a contravention of this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed932e3526aee6a4abf0328b0cfd58ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE EVIDENCE&quot;" target="&quot;PLANT EXAMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Seizing articles as evidence may involve examining plants for relevant information or context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed932e3526aee6a4abf0328b0cfd58ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE EVIDENCE&quot;" target="&quot;ATMOSPHERIC TESTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Evaluating article evidence might require understanding the atmospheric conditions in which it was found."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed932e3526aee6a4abf0328b0cfd58ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PLANT EXAMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational safety officers can conduct tests or examinations of any plant found on the premises."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed932e3526aee6a4abf0328b0cfd58ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PLANT EXAMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;ATMOSPHERIC TESTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Examinations of plants and tests to determine atmospheric conditions are both part of a comprehensive safety inspection process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed932e3526aee6a4abf0328b0cfd58ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ATMOSPHERIC TESTS&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational safety officers can perform atmospheric tests to determine conditions in the environment of the premises."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed932e3526aee6a4abf0328b0cfd58ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 22&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 22 grants the authority for an occupational safety officer to enter premises for inspection purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4c1ae5b0a8aff1b3116e95deba9e3ee</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE OF EVIDENCE&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An occupational safety officer may seize articles that are believed to be evidence of a contravention under section 22."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4c1ae5b0a8aff1b3116e95deba9e3ee</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PLANT OR SUBSTANCE&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The officer can conduct tests or examinations on plant or substances found in the premises for safety and health purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4c1ae5b0a8aff1b3116e95deba9e3ee</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ATMOSPHERIC CONDITION&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The officer may test atmospheric conditions to determine environmental hazards at the premises."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4c1ae5b0a8aff1b3116e95deba9e3ee</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE OR AGENT OF OCCUPIER&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An occupational safety officer can require employees or agents of the occupier for assistance in performing their functions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4c1ae5b0a8aff1b3116e95deba9e3ee</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RECORDS RELATING TO SAFETY OR HEALTH&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An occupational safety officer can require the production of records related to employee safety and health for inspection."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4c1ae5b0a8aff1b3116e95deba9e3ee</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SAMPLE DIVISION&quot;" target="&quot;RECORD RETENTION BY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Sample Division process involves retaining parts of the sample by an Occupational Safety Officer, as described in subsections (3) and (6). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ce083c97323a19a9162d045f2002c1d4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMERCIAL USE OFFENCE&quot;" target="&quot;RECORD RETENTION BY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An Occupational Safety Officer may retain records for commercial purposes as per subsection (6), but such retention is subject to legal proceedings and offences against the Ordinance, indicating a potential conflict. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ce083c97323a19a9162d045f2002c1d4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRAVENTION OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The occupational safety officer is responsible for determining whether a contravention has occurred or is occurring under the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6fab369635d3856df5fe750567a820e8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REQUEST MADE TO A PERSON UNDER SUBSECTION (1)&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPYER OF PREMISES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupiers of premises may receive requests for information under subsection 1."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OFFENCE AND LIABILITY ON CONVICTION TO A FINE AT LEVEL 6&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPYER OF PREMISES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupiers of premises may be liable for offences related to providing false or misleading information under subsection (2)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE EXCUSE FOR REFUSING COMPLIANCE WITH A REQUEST&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPYER OF PREMISES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupiers of premises cannot claim a reasonable excuse if the provision of information might tend to incriminate them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMING INFORMATION PROVIDED MAY TEND TO INCRIMINATE THE PERSON&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPYER OF PREMISES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupiers of premises can claim that providing certain information may tend to incriminate them, but this does not provide a reasonable excuse for non-compliance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;POWER CONFERRED BY THIS SECTION&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPYER OF PREMISES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The power conferred by the section applies to occupiers of premises who may be requested to comply with certain information requests."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;職業安全主任&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Workplace owners must display specified notices as required by occupational safety officers under section 25."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;負責人&quot;" target="&quot;告示&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The person responsible for the workplace is required to display certain notices at the workplace according to section 25."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;告示&quot;" target="&quot;本條例的實施&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Notices displayed must relate to the implementation of this ordinance as per subsection (1)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5cb675ac0cac90a784b227b042225f64</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RESPONSIBLE PERSON&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An Occupational Safety Officer may require a Responsible Person to exhibit notices at the Workplace."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-58cf55b6baed9ac9a3c4052538486aa3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMERCIAL ACTIVITY&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Workplace activities include commercial or industrial operations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-58cf55b6baed9ac9a3c4052538486aa3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INDUSTRIAL ACTIVITY&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Industrial activity is one of the types of activities that can be carried out in a Workplace."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-58cf55b6baed9ac9a3c4052538486aa3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AMENDED 5 OF 2023 S. 76&quot;" target="&quot;2023年第5號第77條修訂&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both legal amendments refer to similar provisions regarding Occupational Safety Officers and Workplaces, indicating they are related in terms of regulatory changes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fe4c625e0d88b6c7ccc901d0d7b85932</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AMENDED 5 OF 2023 S. 76&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The amendment directly impacts the responsibilities and offenses associated with Occupational Safety Officers as outlined in section 76."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fe4c625e0d88b6c7ccc901d0d7b85932</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2023年第5號第77條修訂&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The revision affects the duties and potential legal actions against those who obstruct an Occupational Safety Officer, as described by this regulation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fe4c625e0d88b6c7ccc901d0d7b85932</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICERS&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers and Occupational Safety Officers work together in a coordinated manner as described by the Ordinance amendments, ensuring that their roles are legally protected during joint operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public officers are involved in assisting Occupational Safety Officers, and their actions can be protected under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0cd5c7a6a9ef486d89da782949b23d31</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICERS&quot;" target="&quot;AMENDED 5 OF 2023 S. 77&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers are protected by the amended sections, which provide specific legal provisions for their actions in relation to Occupational Safety Officers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0cd5c7a6a9ef486d89da782949b23d31</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICERS&quot;" target="&quot;AMENDED 5 OF 2023 S. 78&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Amended Section 78 of 2023 further clarifies the legal protections afforded to public officers, including those assisting Occupational Safety Officers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0cd5c7a6a9ef486d89da782949b23d31</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICERS&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"PUBLIC OFFICERS are appointed or authorized by the COMMISSIONER to carry out functions and duties under the ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COMMISSIONER has functions, duties, and powers defined under the ordinance that are carried out by PUBLIC OFFICERS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23a60b107acb436d1472e4d6fcca723b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;21(3)(A)&quot;" target="&quot;AMENDED 5 OF 2023 S. 77&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 21(3)(A) of the Ordinance is amended by Section 77 of Amended 5 of 2023, providing legal protection for certain actions taken by public officers assisting Occupational Safety Officers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0cd5c7a6a9ef486d89da782949b23d31</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;21(3)(A)&quot;" target="&quot;AMENDED 5 OF 2023 S. 78&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 21(3)(A) of the Ordinance is also amended by Section 78 of Amended 5 of 2023, which further defines the legal protection for public officers and those assisting Occupational Safety Officers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0cd5c7a6a9ef486d89da782949b23d31</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AMENDED 5 OF 2023 S. 77&quot;" target="&quot;AMENDED 5 OF 2023 S. 78&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both Sections of Amended 5 of 2023 are related as they both amend the original Ordinance, providing legal protections for different scenarios involving Occupational Safety Officers and public officers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0cd5c7a6a9ef486d89da782949b23d31</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AMENDED 5 OF 2023 S. 77&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The amended sections provide specific legal protections to Occupational Safety Officers, ensuring their functions are supported by the law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0cd5c7a6a9ef486d89da782949b23d31</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AMENDED 5 OF 2023 S. 78&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similarly, Amended Section 78 of 2023 provides legal protections to Occupational Safety Officers and those assisting them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0cd5c7a6a9ef486d89da782949b23d31</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISCLOSURE OF COMPLAINT DETAILS&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers are not liable for disclosing complaint details if they believe it is required or authorized by the ordinance, but they can still be criminally responsible under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e25506f50e901e7cebe325e56cdc3f67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISCLOSURE OF COMPLAINT DETAILS&quot;" target="&quot;COMPLAINANT'S IDENTITY PROTECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Complainant's identity protection is a concern when disclosing complaint details as described in section 29(1), and public officers must protect this information."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e25506f50e901e7cebe325e56cdc3f67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISCLOSURE OF COMPLAINT DETAILS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER'S LIABILITY FOR EMPLOYEE DISCLOSURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers may be liable if their employees disclose complaint details without proper authorization, as described in section 29(2)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e25506f50e901e7cebe325e56cdc3f67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;A PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;" target="&quot;COMPLAINT INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers are prohibited from disclosing complaint information without lawful authority, which includes details related to complaints under this Ordinance or the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (Cap. 59)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6d5bf4b80d4916179a3f7d858e7175b4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPLAINT&quot;" target="&quot;COMPLAINT INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Complaint information pertains directly to complaints that may involve violations of laws such as the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (Cap. 59)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6d5bf4b80d4916179a3f7d858e7175b4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPLAINT&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers handle and manage complaints under this ordinance, ensuring that certain details remain confidential unless legally required to be disclosed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public officers must not disclose the name or identity of a person who has made a complaint, except with consent or as required by law for enforcement purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-029d1e15c5db53ebcfd1168d7ac7bbab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEVEL 4 FINE&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A public officer who commits an offence under section 29 is liable for a fine at level 4 if convicted."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da2837c3b5e351b2e1c63635e1c0a663</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEVEL 4 FINE&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A court can order a fine at level 4 for offences related to the administration of the Ordinance or other relevant laws."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da2837c3b5e351b2e1c63635e1c0a663</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHARGE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE EMPLOYEE AID&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Charges imposed by employers may affect the provision of workplace employee aid."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-77530b0513e9222b2220609d22541c30</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTNER&quot;" target="&quot;DIRECTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Directors and partners share similar legal responsibilities in their respective companies or business entities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-77530b0513e9222b2220609d22541c30</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPATION SAFETY INSPECTOR&quot;" target="&quot;SECRETARY OF CIRCUIT COURT JUDGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An Occupation Safety Inspector can initiate prosecution, and a Circuit Court Judge may preside over such cases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-feeece6356508f661dcb4d399a15acfe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CRIMINAL PROCEEDINGS (SUMMARY)&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER can bring prosecutions for offences that are triable summarily under the CRIMINAL PROCEEDINGS provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-20f049d1d30f5c16c93c8bc30a7dab75</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CRIMINAL PROCEEDINGS (SUMMARY)&quot;" target="&quot;9 MONTHS DEADLINE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Criminal proceedings that are triable summarily must be prosecuted within a 9-month deadline, according to the relevant provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-20f049d1d30f5c16c93c8bc30a7dab75</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;9 MONTHS DEADLINE&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 9-month deadline applies to prosecutions brought by an OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER for offences against this Ordinance, as specified in the related provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-20f049d1d30f5c16c93c8bc30a7dab75</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE (CAP. 227)&quot;" target="&quot;SUMMARY OFFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Magistrates Ordinance (Cap. 227) is superseded by the new prosecution deadline for summary offences."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd366107b74e436e9991d1102531645e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE MAGISTRATES ORDINANCE (CAP. 227)&quot;" target="&quot;PROSECUTION DEADLINE (9 MONTHS)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Magistrates Ordinance (Cap. 227)'s time limit is replaced by a new prosecution deadline of 9 months for summary offences."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd366107b74e436e9991d1102531645e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUMMARY OFFENCE&quot;" target="&quot;INDICTABLE OFFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Summary offence and indictable offence are both types of offences that can be prosecuted under the ordinance, but with different procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd366107b74e436e9991d1102531645e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUMMARY OFFENCE&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPIER OF PREMISES WHERE A SPECIFIED WORKPLACE IS LOCATED&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The occupier of premises where a specified workplace is located may receive summons for summary offences without their name being explicitly mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd366107b74e436e9991d1102531645e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-EMPLOYEE RELATIONSHIP&quot;" target="&quot;EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Evidence of employer-employee relationship is provided in the text, showing how such relationships can be proven in legal proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2d0bd5cc3392e5c0de523f5bb0536a64</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-EMPLOYEE RELATIONSHIP&quot;" target="&quot;ALTERNATIVE HOLIDAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Alternative holidays are part of the relationship between employers and employees regarding leave arrangements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-adbe757d90ad335b39fd280c5f650025</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-EMPLOYEE RELATIONSHIP&quot;" target="&quot;LABOR LAW REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Labor Law Regulations govern the relationship between employers and employees, including leave arrangements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-adbe757d90ad335b39fd280c5f650025</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ONUS ON DEFENDANT TO PROVE CERTAIN MATTERS&quot;" target="&quot;COURT'S ORDER FOR FINANCIAL DATA SUBMISSION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are related to the burden of proof and court orders in legal proceedings, specifically regarding financial data submission."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-85bf5f4c0ed4aaf7faca3a4817c0b647</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ONUS ON DEFENDANT TO PROVE CERTAIN MATTERS&quot;" target="&quot;PERSON NOT LIABLE TO BE PROSECUTED TWICE FOR SAME ACT OR OMISSION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both relate to legal principles in different contexts: burden of proof vs. non-duplication of prosecution."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-85bf5f4c0ed4aaf7faca3a4817c0b647</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSON NOT LIABLE TO BE PROSECUTED TWICE FOR SAME ACT OR OMISSION&quot;" target="&quot;COURT'S ORDER FOR FINANCIAL DATA SUBMISSION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are related to the principles of legal proceedings and court orders, but in different contexts: non-duplication of prosecution vs. financial data submission."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-85bf5f4c0ed4aaf7faca3a4817c0b647</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAX ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 112)&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"TAX ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 112) is a provision referenced by the COURT for tax-related reporting requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2783fda0cba2d6f90774b999de29ee5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ACCOUNTING AND FINANCIAL REPORTING BUREAU ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 588)&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ACCOUNTING AND FINANCIAL REPORTING BUREAU ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 588) defines the role of PROFESSIONAL ACCOUNTANT in financial reporting."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2783fda0cba2d6f90774b999de29ee5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROFESSIONAL ACCOUNTANT&quot;" target="&quot;CONVICTED PERSON&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Professional accountants are involved in auditing financial data submitted by CONVICTED PERSONS as per relevant ORDINANCE requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2783fda0cba2d6f90774b999de29ee5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONVICTED PERSON&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT commands and holds a convicted person accountable for submitting business turnover data as per relevant ORDINANCE provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2783fda0cba2d6f90774b999de29ee5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONVICTED PERSON&quot;" target="&quot;TURNOVER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A CONVICTED PERSON is required to submit information related to their business TURNOVER in accordance with the COURT's commands and ORDINANCES."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2783fda0cba2d6f90774b999de29ee5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONVICTED PERSON&quot;" target="&quot;FINANCIAL YEAR (財務年)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A convicted person's financial year is relevant to their turnover and other financial data that might affect sentencing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f5997b47960ac46dfe44d6417d759c76</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;被定罪人士&quot;" target="&quot;營業額&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"營業額與被定罪人士在香港進行的主要業務活動所得相關，用於確定其業務規模。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19a5c38f633f907e9f2b2434dc908877</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;被定罪人士&quot;" target="&quot;年份&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"年份指被定罪人士的財務年度或某公曆年，用於覆蓋犯罪行為發生之年的營業額信息。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19a5c38f633f907e9f2b2434dc908877</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TURNOVER (營業額)&quot;" target="&quot;FINANCIAL YEAR (財務年)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Turnover is related to the financial year of a convicted person, as it refers to revenue arising in that specific period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f5997b47960ac46dfe44d6417d759c76</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TURNOVER (營業額)&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court considers the turnover of a convicted person when determining appropriate fines, as it reflects operational scale."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f5997b47960ac46dfe44d6417d759c76</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;YEAR (年份)&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE CODES AND SUBSIDIARY LEGISLATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Year is relevant for defining the financial and legal context within which operations take place, especially concerning workplace codes and subsidiary legislation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f5997b47960ac46dfe44d6417d759c76</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FINE (罰款)&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court plays a role in determining the fine amount based on various financial information provided or obtained by it."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f5997b47960ac46dfe44d6417d759c76</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CIRCULATION OF INFORMATION&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC ACCESS TO DOCUMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Labour Department must publish workplace codes in both Chinese and English for public access, ensuring that the information is accessible to affected individuals."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fabbc3eeb929a4a143a6817fd7b457aa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE CODES OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;GAZETTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Workplace codes of practice are published in the GAZETTE when they are issued, amended, or revoked."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1833f1af069fda07edd900b2ad5d51e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE CODES OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL SYSTEM PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Workplace codes of practice can be relevant in legal system procedures involving disputes over their applicability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT AGENCY LICENSEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Code of Practice issued under section 62A(1) must be complied with by the licensee, failure which may result in license denial or revocation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d30f0221d62ed77d081c1e001cb1f4e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 62A(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 62A(1) governs the issuance and compliance with a Code of Practice, which is crucial for licensees' operations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d30f0221d62ed77d081c1e001cb1f4e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION FUNDING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Code of Practice may govern how Arbitration Funding should be handled and provided. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;DIVISION 4—CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Division 4 details the Code of Practice, providing guidelines and standards for third-party funders in relation to arbitrations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-087a07092efc881959ad458909cb8527</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Code of Practice sets out practices and standards for Third Party Funders, including requirements related to promotional material, funding agreements, independent legal advice, advisory body details, capital adequacy, and procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a96252983055863ad83c00cacd5a42b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;ADVISORY BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The advisory body receives annual returns and other information from third party funders regarding their compliance with the code of practice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-24bcba17e89155ad11eeca80dd981ea9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORIZED BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">25.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The AUTHORIZED BODY is responsible for issuing, publishing, and potentially amending or revoking the CODE OF PRACTICE."&lt;SEP&gt;"The AUTHORIZED BODY is responsible for preparing, consulting on, and publishing the CODE OF PRACTICE."&lt;SEP&gt;"The authorized body is responsible for issuing the code of practice after considering written submissions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c30afb3b53c21887cbdb5f0083639960&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8d110ed10ec7ab18c6afd6141aca4b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff1392eccc9ea622ef0b3868092fcd2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC CONSULTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"PUBLIC CONSULTATION is a process used by the AUTHORIZED BODY to gather input before finalizing the CODE OF PRACTICE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c30afb3b53c21887cbdb5f0083639960</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;GAZETTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">23.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The GAZETTE is the official publication where the CODE OF PRACTICE must be published, marking its implementation date."&lt;SEP&gt;"The GAZETTE is where the finalized CODE OF PRACTICE will be published, making it official and effective."&lt;SEP&gt;"The code of practice comes into operation upon publication in the Gazette."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c30afb3b53c21887cbdb5f0083639960&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8d110ed10ec7ab18c6afd6141aca4b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff1392eccc9ea622ef0b3868092fcd2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitral tribunals also have the authority to admit the code of practice as evidence and consider it in their decisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-aff1392eccc9ea622ef0b3868092fcd2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;MEDIATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While not specifically mentioned in relation to mediation, the code of practice may still be relevant or applicable as it pertains to procedural guidelines that could indirectly affect mediations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-aff1392eccc9ea622ef0b3868092fcd2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CODE OF PRACTICE sets out practices and standards expected to be followed by lawyers in connection with ORFS agreements for arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f8d110ed10ec7ab18c6afd6141aca4b7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;" target="&quot;COURTS OR ARBITRATION TRIBUNALS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"COURTS OR ARBITRATION TRIBUNALS may consider matters related to compliance or non-compliance with the CODE OF PRACTICE when deciding certain issues."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f8d110ed10ec7ab18c6afd6141aca4b7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURTROOM PROCEDURES&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL PROCEEDINGS INVOLVING DISPUTES OVER APPLICABILITY OF LAWS OR REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Courtroom procedures are involved when there are legal proceedings related to the applicability of laws or regulations, including workplace codes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CIVIL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;CRIMINAL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both civil and criminal laws may apply when workplace safety or health issues arise, depending on the nature of the violation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CIVIL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE HYGIENE GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Workplace hygiene guidelines can be enforced under civil law if violated, leading to legal proceedings or penalties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORK ENVIRONMENT SAFETY AND HEALTH GUIDELINES&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL SYSTEM PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Work environment safety and health guidelines are relevant in legal system procedures to ensure compliance with laws and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY GUIDELINES&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Workplace safety guidelines can be used as evidence in legal proceedings related to workplace incidents and violations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL EVIDENCE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE ERGONOMICS STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Ergonomics standards may serve as evidence in workplace injury cases and other legal disputes related to work environment conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE HEALTH GUIDELINES&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL PROCEEDINGS INVOLVING DISPUTES OVER APPLICABILITY OF LAWS OR REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Workplace health guidelines may influence the outcome of disputes over the applicability of laws or regulations in legal proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL SYSTEM PROCEDURES&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal system procedures must ensure that workplace safety measures are followed to prevent accidents and violations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY REGULATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;FIRE PREVENTION MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fire Prevention Measures are part of the regulations aimed at preventing fires in the workplace."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6b74f875ef514e4d7940f5dbe0d7910e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY REGULATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;HYGIENE MAINTENANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Hygiene Maintenance is required to ensure that workplaces maintain a clean and healthy condition as per safety regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6b74f875ef514e4d7940f5dbe0d7910e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY REGULATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;HAZARDOUS SUBSTANCES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Safety Regulations control the storage, use, or prohibition of hazardous substances in the workplace."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6b74f875ef514e4d7940f5dbe0d7910e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY REGULATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;MACHINERY OPERATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Regulations govern the operation and usage of machinery to ensure safety at the workplace."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6b74f875ef514e4d7940f5dbe0d7910e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY REGULATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;PHYSICAL EXAMINATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Physical Examinations are mandated by Safety Regulations for employees working in the workplace."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6b74f875ef514e4d7940f5dbe0d7910e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY REGULATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;REPORTING DETAILS ABOUT THE WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Reporting Details about the Workplace is required as per safety regulations to ensure proper documentation and communication of changes or issues."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6b74f875ef514e4d7940f5dbe0d7910e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY REGULATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;RISK ASSESSMENT FOR WORKPLACE ACTIVITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Risk Assessment for workplace activities is a key component of Safety Regulations to evaluate potential hazards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6b74f875ef514e4d7940f5dbe0d7910e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY REGULATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;INDUSTRIAL RELATIONS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Workplace Safety Regulations are part of the broader Industrial Relations Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2fd592d376d0854e1e9f902478b9ced3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHIEF SECRETARY&quot;" target="&quot;SAFETY FACILITIES FOR INJURIES FROM ACCIDENTS AT WORK LOCATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Chief Secretary can regulate safety facilities for injuries from accidents at work locations through subsidiary legislation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-71e44b452a884e51f90079ec8a9ac88f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHIEF SECRETARY&quot;" target="&quot;HAZARDS AND POTENTIAL HAZARDS IN WORK LOCATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Chief Secretary can also regulate hazards and potential hazards in work locations through subsidiary legislation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-71e44b452a884e51f90079ec8a9ac88f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;立法会&quot;" target="&quot;规例&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"规例需要获得立法会的批准才能生效。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f30bd1959d14cc825d9dc1909b7819e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYERS AND EMPLOYEES&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPIERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers and employees are subject to regulations concerning their responsibilities in ensuring workplace safety and health."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d004c27b0c530c46d0712f3eb4a62419</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPIERS&quot;" target="&quot;ADDITIONAL RESPONSIBILITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupiers have additional responsibilities as per the regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d004c27b0c530c46d0712f3eb4a62419</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGULATIONS (CONTINUED)&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE SAFETY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Continued regulations address aspects of workplace safety."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d004c27b0c530c46d0712f3eb4a62419</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGULATIONS (FINAL)&quot;" target="&quot;COMPLIANCE AND OVERSIGHT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Final regulations provide a framework for compliance and oversight mechanisms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d004c27b0c530c46d0712f3eb4a62419</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEES&quot;" target="&quot;SAFETY AND HEALTH STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees' safety and health are protected under the workplace safety and health standards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1a519085f972ab451b135f99083dc3b5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEES&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner oversees the safety or health of employees through risk assessments, biochemical tests, biological tests, medical examinations, and other measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2cd54f63250a5891c0ad271003ffd081</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEES&quot;" target="&quot;BIOCHEMICAL TESTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees are required to undergo biochemical tests when there is a risk of absorbing any substance at their workplace, as mandated by the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2cd54f63250a5891c0ad271003ffd081</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEES&quot;" target="&quot;BIOLOGICAL TESTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similar to biochemical tests, employees may also be subjected to biological tests if they are exposed to substances that pose risks to their health or safety."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2cd54f63250a5891c0ad271003ffd081</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEES&quot;" target="&quot;MEDICAL EXAMINATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Medical examinations are part of the measures prescribed by the Commissioner for detecting and investigating cases where employees have been affected by workplace activities involving substances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2cd54f63250a5891c0ad271003ffd081</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEES&quot;" target="&quot;UNNAMED ORGANIZATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The unnamed organization is related to employees, as it involves wage payments and employment contracts according to the context provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a38f5270b24602bceb3522785e4ed41d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SAFETY AND HEALTH STANDARDS&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Workplaces are subject to safety and health standards prescribed by regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1a519085f972ab451b135f99083dc3b5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACES&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner is responsible for receiving notifications and records from persons who are responsible for workplaces regarding changes in particulars and specified activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2cd54f63250a5891c0ad271003ffd081</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACES&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSTANCES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Workplaces involve activities that may lead to the absorption of substances which require testing and investigation by the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2cd54f63250a5891c0ad271003ffd081</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPLACES&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational safety officers, under the Commissioner's guidance, assess risks at workplaces and provide information to employers or other relevant parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2cd54f63250a5891c0ad271003ffd081</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STRICT LIABILITY&quot;" target="&quot;DEFENDANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Defendants may commit an offence with knowledge, intentionally, or recklessly under regulations dealing with strict liability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-990bd24369be2bc2f9bdd440773f2e19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STRICT LIABILITY&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner has authority over regulations that define strict liability offences."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-990bd24369be2bc2f9bdd440773f2e19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
