<edge source="&quot;DANGEROUS DRUG&quot;" target="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'dangerous drug' is defined in the Dangerous Drugs Ordinance (Cap. 134), which may be relevant to legal actions or terminations on certain dates as specified by the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a66612db010d80c91ad3aa4fb718df84</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;PAID SICKNESS DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The RELEVANT DATE is relevant to the calculation or determination of PAID SICKNESS DAY entitlements and allowances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d908f80036493cf02a5dd6da247a2a7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The RELEVANT DATE can be significant for determining when PATERNITY LEAVE PAY should commence or cease."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d908f80036493cf02a5dd6da247a2a7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;REST DAY OR HOLIDAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The RELEVANT DATE may be extended to the following day if it coincides with a REST DAY or HOLIDAY, as per section 4."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d536cf1eacc47eb2d3812dd2faa34e3c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;DISMISSAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Dismissing an employee can occur on or after the relevant date, which may fall on a rest day or holiday."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a40a9600dcdabbcf7b1de20226238a1e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIM FOR REDUNDANCY PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The claim for redundancy payment is subject to a relevant date within three months from which it can be made or extended with approval by the Secretary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d33baa15beb160832b6e2302162f04d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner has the authority to agree on an extended period related to the RELEVANT DATE for claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4803dc099d05bf6f05b27d07f8429783</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD REGISTRAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The claims must be filed within the period of 3 months beginning with the RELEVANT DATE or an extended period agreed by the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4803dc099d05bf6f05b27d07f8429783</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL REGISTRAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similar to the Minor Employment Claims Adjudication Board, claims must be filed within the same time frame starting from the RELEVANT DATE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4803dc099d05bf6f05b27d07f8429783</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The relevant date is significant as it marks the deadline by which an employee must accept or reject renewal/re-engagement offers, impacting their employment status."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ff6ba65a2b6882ca144f894790a0cc18</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31T(1)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 31T(1)(B) references the relevant date in determining whether a contract for a fixed term can be terminated due to an employee's refusal of renewal/re-engagement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ff6ba65a2b6882ca144f894790a0cc18</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;AN EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The RELEVANT DATE is a critical factor in determining whether an employee can claim remedies after being dismissed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9e5f55eef00b5211e8c9c5c06c4bde96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'relevant date' is used in relation to the termination of employment, defining its meaning under specific sections."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d06ee4edd39803f9b252b767c726ef91</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;VARIATION OF CONTRACT TERMS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'relevant date' also applies to when contract terms are varied, specifying the effective date of such changes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d06ee4edd39803f9b252b767c726ef91</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;THE RELEVANT DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The relevant date is a key term used in sections 32I and 32J to determine the time frame for claims and jurisdiction respectively."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-adb3767092cbae0c3a6518107e6865b5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELEVANT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;PERSONAL REPRESENTATIVE OF A DECEASED EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Personal representative of a deceased employee's claim is related to the relevant date for determining periods such as 3 months or 6 months."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da53ed52a17c537de0b1301ebe9c9aa8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;侍產假&quot;" target="&quot;侍產假薪酬&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"侍產假薪酬是根据侍產假而需支付的薪酬。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efb469411694660c1a6d57f27eeccd3d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;侍產假&quot;" target="&quot;长期服务金&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"文本未明确说明长期服务金与侍產假之间的关系。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efb469411694660c1a6d57f27eeccd3d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;侍產假薪酬&quot;" target="&quot;僱主&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據第IIIA部須支付的任何侍產假薪酬是終止僱傭金的一部分。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c82c895f7b30d4831c428126a0af9486</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;侍產假薪酬&quot;" target="&quot;資,可從該僱員的工資中扣回&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"在特定情況下，可以从僱员的工资中扣除已支付的侍产假薪酬。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f67917e32c7b3686da62a23f718318d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;儿童&quot;" target="&quot;法定假日&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"儿童可能在法定假日内受到保护或享有权利，但文本中没有直接关系描述。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efb469411694660c1a6d57f27eeccd3d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;另有定假日&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"另有定假日是相对于法定假日的一种额外规定或补充。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e7cedd297868cbefbc6ffea9f8b7a8f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;第39(4)條規定給予僱員的假日&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"第39(4)條規定给予的假日属于法定假日的一种类型或补充形式。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e7cedd297868cbefbc6ffea9f8b7a8f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;農曆年初一&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"農曆年初一是法定假日之一，具体日期根据星期日调整。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6dc88cb5a70d0e4c2d56e0663d5e01f1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;農曆年初二&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"農曆年初二是法定假日之一，具体日期根据星期日调整。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6dc88cb5a70d0e4c2d56e0663d5e01f1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;農曆年初三&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"農曆年初三是法定假日之一，具体日期根据星期日调整。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6dc88cb5a70d0e4c2d56e0663d5e01f1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;清明節&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"清明節是法定假日之一。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6dc88cb5a70d0e4c2d56e0663d5e01f1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;勞動節&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"勞動節是法定假日之一，具体日期为5月1日。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6dc88cb5a70d0e4c2d56e0663d5e01f1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;端午節&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"端午節是法定假日之一。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6dc88cb5a70d0e4c2d56e0663d5e01f1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;中秋节翌日&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"中秋节翌日是法定假日之一，具体日期根据星期日调整。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6dc88cb5a70d0e4c2d56e0663d5e01f1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;重陽節&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"重陽節是法定假日之一。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6dc88cb5a70d0e4c2d56e0663d5e01f1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;冬節或聖誕節&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"冬節或聖誕节是法定假日之一，具体日期由僱主选择。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6dc88cb5a70d0e4c2d56e0663d5e01f1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;1月1日&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"1月1日是法定假日之一。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6dc88cb5a70d0e4c2d56e0663d5e01f1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;香港特別行政區成立紀念日&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"香港特别行政区成立纪念日是法定假日之一，具体日期为7月1日。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6dc88cb5a70d0e4c2d56e0663d5e01f1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;國慶日&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"国庆日是法定假日之一，具体日期为10月1日。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6dc88cb5a70d0e4c2d56e0663d5e01f1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;佛誕&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"佛誕被列為法定假日之一。"&lt;SEP&gt;"佛诞是法定假日之一，具体日期为农历四月八日。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6dc88cb5a70d0e4c2d56e0663d5e01f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d9186420295a7ef185edec447e7f6b0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;聖誕節後第一個周日&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"圣诞节后第一个周日是法定假日之一。"&lt;SEP&gt;"聖誕節後第一個周日也被視為一個法定假日。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6dc88cb5a70d0e4c2d56e0663d5e01f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d9186420295a7ef185edec447e7f6b0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;复活節&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"复活节是法定假日之一，具体日期根据宗教传统确定。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6dc88cb5a70d0e4c2d56e0663d5e01f1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;復活節星期一&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"復活節星期一被定為法定假日之一。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6d9186420295a7ef185edec447e7f6b0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;休息日&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"法定假日和休息日在某些情况下可以互相替代或区分对待。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7430d09345738519e0c07e81b09c47d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;青年僱員(工業)規例 (第57章,附屬法例C)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"《青年僱員(工業)規例》涉及特定日期的假期安排，可能影响某些法定假日的规定。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7430d09345738519e0c07e81b09c47d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定假日&quot;" target="&quot;《僱用青年(工業)規例》 (第57章,附屬法例C)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"该条例涉及特定日期的假期安排，可能影响某些法定假日的规定。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7430d09345738519e0c07e81b09c47d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;长期服务金&quot;" target="&quot;PART VB&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Long Service Payments are defined under Part VB of the relevant document, indicating their inclusion and importance within this section."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-985c71a2aa2037adf4ce25fd3c8c12de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;长期服务金&quot;" target="&quot;连续性合约受雇的员工&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees under continuous contracts have rights related to long service payments as per the legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-985c71a2aa2037adf4ce25fd3c8c12de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;长期服务金&quot;" target="&quot;雇佣合約&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据雇佣合同的实施，雇员有权获得按服务年资支付的酬金或权益。因此，在某些情况下需要从这些酬金中扣除长期服务金。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efde970dacc8f16ccdb4b94374b28042</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;长期服务金&quot;" target="&quot;职业退休计划利益&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"在雇佣合同时，如果雇员有资格获取指定的职业退休计划利益，则可能需要从中扣除长期服务金。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efde970dacc8f16ccdb4b94374b28042</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;长期服务金&quot;" target="&quot;强积金计划权益&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"在强制性公积金计划中，如果有雇主供款（自愿）的强积金计划权益属于该雇员时，在某些情况下需要从这些权益中扣除长期服务金。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efde970dacc8f16ccdb4b94374b28042</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;长期服务金&quot;" target="&quot;附表11第5條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"附表11第5条提供了关于如何在特定条件下从酬金或利益中扣除长期服务金的具体规定和说明。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efde970dacc8f16ccdb4b94374b28042</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;长期服务金&quot;" target="&quot;附表7表A第1栏所指明的期间内&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"在特定时期内，长期服务金的金额不能超过附表7表A第1栏中指定时期的上限。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-39ff31ef4fdbcf84c8c1f1a297094829</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;长期服务金&quot;" target="&quot;雇员权益&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"雇员权益包括根据本部获付的一笔长期服务金。这两者都与员工的工作年限和离职时的利益相关联，但它们是不同的福利形式。长期服务金是在特定条件下支付给员工的一种补偿。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3af8cb7f383ac57c1ab02ce86bc0393f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;长期服务金&quot;" target="&quot;第31RA条&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据第31RA条,有关僱主须向甲方支付长期服务金。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7fb9bafd0cba5b9cfa67282f7c70bf83</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;长期服务金&quot;" target="&quot;雇员死亡&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"长期服务金的支付条件之一是某指明僱員死亡。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7fb9bafd0cba5b9cfa67282f7c70bf83</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;长期服务金&quot;" target="&quot;有关僱员服务期&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"长期服务金基于有关僱员的服务期计算得出。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7fb9bafd0cba5b9cfa67282f7c70bf83</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;青年&quot;" target="&quot;後嗣&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"後嗣包括已故僱員的子女，但未對青年身份進行直接關係描述。"&lt;SEP&gt;"青年和後嗣都涉及到个人状态或身份，但没有直接联系。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efb469411694660c1a6d57f27eeccd3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e03073aa0f6abdf5280f21aa17a6bbf7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;長期服務金&quot;" target="&quot;指明僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"指明僱員有權領取長期服務金。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e03073aa0f6abdf5280f21aa17a6bbf7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;長期服務金&quot;" target="&quot;甲方&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"甲方负责支付长期服务金给符合条件的一方。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f522c2b4fb2af18c29efee69dde9f663</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;長期服務金&quot;" target="&quot;乙方&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"乙方在特定条件下有权获得长期服务金,包括因雇员死亡而产生的各种权益和利益。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f522c2b4fb2af18c29efee69dde9f663</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;長期服務金&quot;" target="&quot;強積金計劃權益&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"強積金計劃權益與長期服務金之間存在扣除關係,在計算長期服務金時需要考慮相關的強積金計劃權益。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-90c0794da631cfd39500d26a03a02ecf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;長期服務金&quot;" target="&quot;酬金或利益或權益&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"酬金或利益或權益影響長期服務金的計算方式和扣除範圍,根據其對僱員服務期的影響進行調整。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-90c0794da631cfd39500d26a03a02ecf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;《婚姻制度改革條例》(第178章)&quot;" target="&quot;指明僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"該條例可能影響哪些人可被视为指明僱員的後嗣，但直接關係不強烈。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e03073aa0f6abdf5280f21aa17a6bbf7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WEEK&quot;" target="&quot;HOLIDAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Holidays can be scheduled within the context of weeks, indicating a relationship between these two concepts in terms of time management and planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"While weeks are mentioned separately, holidays can be considered within the framework of weekly cycles and may overlap with certain week periods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8b40910fef9ba5e880f9a32ae794f8b2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WEEK&quot;" target="&quot;PRE-AMENDMENT WEEK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A PRE-AMENDMENT WEEK is a specific type of week where the employee's work hours are counted differently for determining continuous employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7d9929bbede2eb72d013426b56ad4e6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WEEK&quot;" target="&quot;3 WEEKS NEXT PRECEDING THAT WEEK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 3 weeks next preceding that week play a crucial role in counting an employee’s working hours to determine if they have been continuously employed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7d9929bbede2eb72d013426b56ad4e6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WEEK&quot;" target="&quot;WEEK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Weeks are used as units of time in calculating continuous employment, with specific rules applying based on whether they fall within certain categories like PRE-AMENDMENT WEEK or 3 WEEKS NEXT PRECEDING THAT WEEK."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7d9929bbede2eb72d013426b56ad4e6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MISCARRIAGE&quot;" target="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Miscarriage is a form of sickness that could qualify for sickness allowance under relevant employment laws."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8b40910fef9ba5e880f9a32ae794f8b2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;" target="&quot;SICKNESS DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A sick day, which includes days off due to illness or injury, can be compensated through the provision of sickness allowance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8b40910fef9ba5e880f9a32ae794f8b2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"COURT can award SICKNESS ALLOWANCE as a form of terminal payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">32.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYEE can receive SICKNESS ALLOWANCE if their record of sickness days is lost or destroyed by the employer, as per section 33."&lt;SEP&gt;"An employee can receive sickness allowance if they meet specific conditions, such as absence lasting 4 or more consecutive days and falling on or after a specified date."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employees may be entitled to sickness allowance based on continuous employment and recent work history as per the text provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EMPLOYEE may be entitled to receive SICKNESS ALLOWANCE from the EMPLOYER when taking sickness days due to various reasons such as pregnancy, miscarriage or illness."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42671f6db02a812e702214c1753dfc91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdc4a39840a667a7878ee99d632412a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c96e8be9052d451fbf9a64ace39448d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f729e4dc4d8c13592d31110960bc5996</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A registered medical practitioner can issue an appropriate medical certificate, which is necessary to claim sickness allowance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c9af043de8381bfd2d54ddf7a99fe8b0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A registered Chinese medicine practitioner can also issue a valid certificate for claiming sickness allowance under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c9af043de8381bfd2d54ddf7a99fe8b0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPORARY INCAPACITY FOR WHICH COMPENSATION IS PAYABLE UNDER SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Temporary incapacity for which compensation is payable under the Employees' Compensation Ordinance directly leads to eligibility for sickness allowance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary incapacity leading to compensation is directly related to the eligibility for sickness allowance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e5e29cfe8eddddf302f5a14076a67a7d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The payment of Sickness Allowance is related to Wages, as it continues even when the employment contract is not terminated."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-323c200d08170c4d996dbd247312e21a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sickness Allowance's payment depends on the status and termination of the CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-323c200d08170c4d996dbd247312e21a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;" target="&quot;PAID SICK LEAVE DAYS TO BE DEDUCTED&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The payment of PAID SICK LEAVE DAYS TO BE DEDUCTED may be related to the receipt or non-receipt of Sickness Allowance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-323c200d08170c4d996dbd247312e21a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;" target="&quot;DISABILITY BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While not directly stated, both are forms of financial support for employees in different circumstances and could potentially overlap in some cases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-323c200d08170c4d996dbd247312e21a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 33(2A)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 33(2A) specifies a category for recording accumulated paid sickness days under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f5c7df56b94c0c429230f0546be40142</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 33(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 33(2) details the accumulation of paid sick leave, which is recorded in accordance with Section 33(2A)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f5c7df56b94c0c429230f0546be40142</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;" target="&quot;36 DAYS LIMITATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The total number of recorded paid sick leave cannot exceed 36 days at any time according to the regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f5c7df56b94c0c429230f0546be40142</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are types of allowances that can be paid by the employer to employees under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-98d46f6e07563bbf79e567c647ecf4fc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE&quot;" target="&quot;2008年1月13日(第16條)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"This date is mentioned alongside sickness allowance in the context of its application under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-98d46f6e07563bbf79e567c647ecf4fc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS DAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE TERMINATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sickness days are disregarded in the calculation of wages for termination compensation purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS DAY&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similar to maternity leave and rest days, wages include sickness day payments, indicating a consistent treatment in the context of compensations for different types of leaves."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS DAY&quot;" target="&quot;DISEASE津貼&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A sickness day entitles an employee to disease allowance under the employment regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e6ca8ea4c3347749e50a0bfdf049de28</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS DAY&quot;" target="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT FOR A PERIOD OF 1 MONTH OR MORE IMMEDIATELY PRECEDING A SICKNESS DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The continuous contract is a prerequisite for entitlement to sickness day benefits as per the employment ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e6ca8ea4c3347749e50a0bfdf049de28</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS DAY&quot;" target="&quot;BAA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"BAA specifies that an employer cannot terminate a contract during or after a sickness day unless certain conditions are met."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0fef56ddac89c58276c95d49a4ad2fde</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS DAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employees' Compensation Ordinance covers sickness days related to injuries or occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b89f7731524d41ce9b762132c808abd5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS DAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employee may take a sick day due to health reasons and is entitled to receive sickness allowance under specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c9af043de8381bfd2d54ddf7a99fe8b0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS DAY&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES EARNED BY THE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sickness day days are included in the wage calculations for determining holiday pay rates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9d14b62c50b2a0a92ac73c8ef0642fe9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CEASE&quot;" target="&quot;CAP. 599 REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Cap. 599 requirement involves restrictions on movement, which could lead to a cessation (停止) in certain activities or businesses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fee7842314099c25edf5106ebd221850</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Wages encompass holiday pay as well, further illustrating that these are all components of an employee's total compensation package."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Paternity leave can overlap with holidays, allowing for flexibility in scheduling."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c54e7deea495212bab465e4af100b7ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT PERIOD WITHOUT FULL WAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employment period without full wage includes holidays where no work is provided to the employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similar to REST DAY, a CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT ending on a HOLIDAY can avoid being considered dismissal under the same conditions as REST DAY."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ccf624f83121089caf9f8fb044043303</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;BAA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Holiday is included as a type of leave under BAA for wage calculation purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0fef56ddac89c58276c95d49a4ad2fde</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similar to REST DAY, holidays that fall within a period of annual leave are also counted as part of the annual leave, with substitution rules applied."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b63d3371d1b762c2013adc08da9c549f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;REST DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both REST DAY and HOLIDAY have similar rules for substitution within a period of ANNUAL LEAVE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b63d3371d1b762c2013adc08da9c549f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法定节假日薪酬&quot;" target="&quot;產假薪酬&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"法定节假日薪酬和产假薪酬都是针对特定假期（如法定假日、产假）支付给员工的报酬，但适用范围不同。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e7cedd297868cbefbc6ffea9f8b7a8f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;強制性公積金計劃&quot;" target="&quot;僱主供款職業退休計劃利益&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are types of employer-funded benefits, indicating a relationship in the context of employee benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-233de206d4d440690ca3d19bf8ddb77c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;產假&quot;" target="&quot;終止僱傭合約&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据第(2B)款的规定，在不损害第41D条的条件下，女性雇员根据第12条规定有权享有的产假不应计算在终止雇佣合同所需的通知期内。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75ec5cbcc26a69d2fa91ff3cd7cec100</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;產假&quot;" target="&quot;女性僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">19.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"女性僱員在分娩後可能放產假，需通知雇主並提供相關文件以支持申請。&lt;br/&gt;"&lt;SEP&gt;"女性僱員有權享有產假。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb31bef1e8dd24810a075920d4fb5602&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb1fa32929a7020d65f293e8c9d7dd58</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;產假薪酬&quot;" target="&quot;工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"产假薪酬是根据《雇员补偿条例》(第282章)中规定的，基于员工开始产假前的最近12个月内的平均工资计算得出。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;產假薪酬&quot;" target="&quot;女性僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"女性雇员在放取产假期间可以获得相应的产假薪酬。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;產假薪酬&quot;" target="&quot;第7條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"第7條规定了产假期间的薪酬待遇。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;產假薪酬&quot;" target="&quot;終止僱傭&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"兩者都是根據特定條件計算支付給某僱員的款項，與其工作調離和僱傭終止有關。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd5d9d61caba55ae3f9dfd2940ae47cd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;《第599章》規定&quot;" target="&quot;處長 (COMMISSIONER)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"处长负责执行或解释与《第599章》规定相关的条款和政策。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e7cedd297868cbefbc6ffea9f8b7a8f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;處長 (COMMISSIONER)&quot;" target="&quot;閉廠 (LOCK-OUT)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"处长有权决定是否实施闭厂措施，因此两者之间存在职权关系。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e7cedd297868cbefbc6ffea9f8b7a8f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOCK-OUT&quot;" target="&quot;STRIKE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both LOCK-OUT and STRIKE are defined in the Trade Unions Ordinance (Cap. 332), indicating their legal context within labor disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd0362fbf5661d142ff4aeefe27aea79</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOCK-OUT&quot;" target="&quot;TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term LOCK-OUT is defined by the TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (Cap. 332). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd0362fbf5661d142ff4aeefe27aea79</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LABOUR TRIBUNAL may request a report from COMMISSIONER to assist in making decisions regarding employment claims."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner is related to the Labour Tribunal as both are part of labor-related administrative bodies in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a2200d76e6cc5397e7868136950dfb19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a67530e0a9df975682238097b18b864</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Labour Tribunal may involve Registered Medical Practitioners in certain cases related to workplace health and safety issues."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2a67530e0a9df975682238097b18b864</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTRAR OF THE MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are regulators involved in employment claims, with the Minor Employment Claims Adjudication Board and Labour Tribunal handling different aspects of such claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c9277263fe4be5c215993320cc63c410</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIM FOR REMEDIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Claims for remedies are processed by the Labour Tribunal, which has jurisdiction over such matters under sections 32I and 32J."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-adb3767092cbae0c3a6518107e6865b5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTRAR OF THE LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Registrar of the Labour Tribunal is responsible for handling claims filed with the Labour Tribunal as per the Labour Tribunal Ordinance (Cap. 25). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a68f0496b4d3967e4dee08ee2a743063</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;LAWS OF HONG KONG: THE LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (CAP. 25)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Labour Tribunal is established under the Labour Tribunal Ordinance (Cap. 25), which outlines its jurisdiction and procedures for handling claims."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Labour Tribunal's operations are governed and defined by the Labour Tribunal Ordinance (Cap. 25). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a68f0496b4d3967e4dee08ee2a743063</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;JUSTICE PRESIDENT OF THE LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Justice President of the Labour Tribunal has judicial authority over cases submitted to the tribunal as per section 32J(1). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a68f0496b4d3967e4dee08ee2a743063</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT RELATIONS AMENDMENT REGULATION 1 OF 2013&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employment Relations Amendment Regulation 1 of 2013 amends the procedures for claims submitted to the Labour Tribunal, affecting its jurisdiction and handling processes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a68f0496b4d3967e4dee08ee2a743063</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">45.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both COURT and LABOUR TRIBUNAL are involved in determining claims related to employment contracts and dismissals under section 32L."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both COURT and LABOUR TRIBUNAL are mentioned in the text as entities responsible for making decisions regarding employment disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both COURT and LABOUR TRIBUNAL have decision-making powers in employment disputes, potentially overlapping with each other's jurisdiction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both COURT and LABOUR TRIBUNAL have similar decision-making powers regarding employment claims."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both COURT and LABOUR TRIBUNAL have the authority to make awards for terminal payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both the COURT and LABOUR TRIBUNAL are involved in adjudicating claims under employment-related ordinances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d580b5b472939d182c05bf201c52ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cec848f1858ebf48439b7f8f5961be4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee588c56ed96e2cbc4dc5b9474b0fa9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2200d76e6cc5397e7868136950dfb19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc2894a439737cb35869b760804ff684</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LABOUR TRIBUNAL considers the circumstances of an employee's contract when making determinations about dismissal or variation of terms as per section 32L."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc2894a439737cb35869b760804ff684</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;32M&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 32M provides remedies to Labour TRIBUNAL regarding unjustified dismissals or changes in employment contracts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-22d580b5b472939d182c05bf201c52ef</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;ORDER FOR REENGAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The LABOUR TRIBUNAL may decide to issue an ORDER FOR REENGAGEMENT based on the circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ee588c56ed96e2cbc4dc5b9474b0fa9a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;REINSTATEMENT ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LABOUR TRIBUNAL can make an order for REINSTATEMENT of the employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a2200d76e6cc5397e7868136950dfb19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;RE-ENGAGEMENT ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LABOUR TRIBUNAL can also make an order for RE-ENGAGEMENT if reinstatement is not suitable."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a2200d76e6cc5397e7868136950dfb19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE DISMISSAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LABOUR TRIBUNAL decides on the appropriate action after considering dismissal cases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a2200d76e6cc5397e7868136950dfb19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LABOUR TRIBUNAL can award terminal payments directly to the EMPLOYEE."&lt;SEP&gt;"The LABOUR TRIBUNAL can make an order for REINSTATEMENT ORDER based on the circumstances of the case involving the EMPLOYEE and the EMPLOYER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f17d41b36a40e80f45f0f635b4ad7eb7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;REINSTATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LABOUR TRIBUNAL may make an order for REINSTATEMENT if appropriate."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LABOUR TRIBUNAL may make an order for RE-ENGAGEMENT if appropriate."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LABOUR TRIBUNAL may include END OF YEAR PAYMENT as part of terminal payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LABOUR TRIBUNAL may include PATERNITY LEAVE PAY in the awards for terminal payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LABOUR TRIBUNAL may include LONG SERVICE PAYMENT in the awards for terminal payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;HOLIDAY PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LABOUR TRIBUNAL may include HOLIDAY PAY in the awards for terminal payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OR LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both COURT and LABOUR TRIBUNAL have the authority to make awards of compensation in cases involving employment termination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4254cc0d21afce88f6eb9b8c9366f7cc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;OCTOBER 29, 2010&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Labour Tribunal's operations are applicable from this specific date according to the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7f6302661df10aad972a6e63a05f0aa6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Labour Tribunal may be involved in disputes covered by an arbitration agreement, especially those involving claims within its jurisdiction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e7564251214dafe0ef47139543601d3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (VOLUNTARY) MPFS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED NON-EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are employer-funded benefits, with the latter specifically related to voluntary contributions in a provident fund scheme."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e70ac051c2f0b62b1c78481493c78790</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (VOLUNTARY) MPFS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;MANDATORY PROVIDENT FUND SCHEMES ORDINANCE (CAP. 485)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ordinance defines the framework within which voluntary contributions to provident fund schemes are made, directly impacting employer-funded benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e70ac051c2f0b62b1c78481493c78790</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (VOLUNTARY) MPFS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The long service payment is related to employer-funded benefits, as both are mentioned in the context of employee's years of service."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2193ccb19ec3e792d874a92951eae0f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED MPFS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;MANDATORY PROVIDENT FUND SCHEME (MPFS)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'employer-funded (voluntary) MPFS benefit' refers to a specific type of benefit under the Mandatory Provident Fund Scheme."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e7d4bbfd9a7f73f2810843d3a9e9fa2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED MPFS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;POST-TRANSITION PORTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer-funded MPFS benefit is related to the post-transition portion as it pertains to payments attributable to employment after the transition date."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0dd3aa2554b81fa47ed2eec0f056d25</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED MPFS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;PRE-TRANSITION PORTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer-funded MPFS benefit is also linked to the pre-transition portion, concerning payments related to employment before the transition date."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0dd3aa2554b81fa47ed2eec0f056d25</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED MPFS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;MODIFIED (經變通)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Modified impacts employer-funded benefits by altering their calculation methods, especially in relation to transitional employment periods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0dd3aa2554b81fa47ed2eec0f056d25</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED NON-EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;FOURTH ORDINANCE (NO.4)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'employer-funded non-exempt ORS benefit' is defined under the Fourth Ordinance, No. 4."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e7d4bbfd9a7f73f2810843d3a9e9fa2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED NON-EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (PRESCRIBED PORTION) EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are types of employer-funded benefits related to occupational retirement plans but differ in their exempt status."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e70ac051c2f0b62b1c78481493c78790</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED NON-EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;ISSUE (後嗣)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'issue' is used in the context of beneficiaries, which could include individuals like children who might be eligible for certain benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e70ac051c2f0b62b1c78481493c78790</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED SPECIFIED ORS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;FOURTH ORDINANCE (NO.4)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'employer-funded (specified) ORS benefit' is defined under the Fourth Ordinance, No. 4."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e7d4bbfd9a7f73f2810843d3a9e9fa2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED PRESCRIBED PORTION EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;FOURTH ORDINANCE (NO.4)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'employer-funded (prescribed portion) exempt ORS benefit' is defined under the Fourth Ordinance, No. 4."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e7d4bbfd9a7f73f2810843d3a9e9fa2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;FOURTH ORDINANCE (NO.4)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'employer-funded exempt ORS benefit' is defined under the Fourth Ordinance, No. 4."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e7d4bbfd9a7f73f2810843d3a9e9fa2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer-funded exempt ORS benefit is related to the contract of employment as it involves payments based on service years upon retirement, death, loss of capacity or termination of service."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-28b2163160f25fa57988c0b4d0c740cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED ORS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;MANDATORY PROVIDENT FUND SCHEME (MPFS)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'employer-funded ORS benefit' refers to a type of benefit under the Mandatory Provident Fund Scheme, which includes both exempt and non-exempt benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5e7d4bbfd9a7f73f2810843d3a9e9fa2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED ORS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;REFERENCE AMOUNT A&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The reference amount is used in calculating employer-funded (prescribed portion) exempt ORS benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e43ce81a5e24ba44cc5896e9318ba422</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED ORS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S FINAL AVERAGE MONTHLY RELEVANT INCOME B&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employee's final average monthly relevant income is a key factor in determining the amount of employer-funded (prescribed portion) exempt ORS benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e43ce81a5e24ba44cc5896e9318ba422</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED ORS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 4(3)(B)&lt;CAP. 485&gt;&lt;PERSON, ORGANIZATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The exemption from certain provisions under Cap. 485 can affect the calculation of employer-funded (prescribed portion) exempt ORS benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e43ce81a5e24ba44cc5896e9318ba422</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RECOGNIZED SCHEME OF MEDICAL TREATMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The recognized scheme of medical treatment may be related to the employee's benefits under an employment contract but is not directly defined in this text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-28b2163160f25fa57988c0b4d0c740cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RECOGNIZED SCHEME OF MEDICAL TREATMENT&quot;" target="&quot;PAID SICKNESS DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of PAID SICKNESS DAY is related to a recognized scheme of medical treatment, as both are part of employee benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d908f80036493cf02a5dd6da247a2a7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RECOGNIZED SCHEME OF MEDICAL TREATMENT&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A recognized scheme of medical treatment may involve services from a registered Chinese medicine practitioner, as both are part of healthcare provision."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both types of registered practitioners are involved in the operations of recognized medical treatment schemes for issuing relevant healthcare documentation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fcd2a26e931b9fa624c25b0caadbcdb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908f80036493cf02a5dd6da247a2a7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RECOGNIZED SCHEME OF MEDICAL TREATMENT&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A recognized scheme of medical treatment could involve services from various types of practitioners, including registered medical practitioners."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d908f80036493cf02a5dd6da247a2a7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RECOGNIZED SCHEME OF MEDICAL TREATMENT&quot;" target="&quot;APPROPRIATE MEDICAL CERTIFICATE (適當的醫生證明書)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The appropriate medical certificate must be issued according to the recognized scheme of medical treatment for an employee's sickness allowance claim."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c9af043de8381bfd2d54ddf7a99fe8b0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RECOGNIZED SCHEME OF MEDICAL TREATMENT&quot;" target="&quot;DIRECTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Director has the authority to recognize or withdraw recognition of a medical treatment scheme operated by an employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4af496fc2b1c26e3d6bca76a4b99c25f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STRIKE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Strikes are actions taken by employees, indicating their relationship through collective action and labor rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-28b2163160f25fa57988c0b4d0c740cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STRIKE&quot;" target="&quot;TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term STRIKE is also defined in the TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (Cap. 332), indicating their legal context within labor disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd0362fbf5661d142ff4aeefe27aea79</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL RETIREMENT SCHEME&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational retirement scheme is part of the benefits that may be included in a contract of employment for long-term service rewards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-28b2163160f25fa57988c0b4d0c740cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;職業退休計劃&quot;" target="&quot;轉制日&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"雖然文本中未直接提及職業退休計劃與轉制日之間的關係，但二者均涉及僱傭及退休計劃法例中的條款，可能在某一特定時點（如轉制日）有所調整或適用。因此可以推測存在一定的相關性。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b97ce5993df5b6616c6c24d7afbaa008</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;職業退休計劃&quot;" target="&quot;續訂&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"文本中未直接提及職業退休計劃與續訂之間的關係，但二者均涉及僱傭及退休計劃法例中的條款，可能在某一特定情況下（如續訂合約）有所調整或適用。因此可以推測存在一定的相關性。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b97ce5993df5b6616c6c24d7afbaa008</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;轉制日&quot;" target="&quot;續訂&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"文本中未直接提及轉制日與續訂之間的關係，但二者均涉及僱傭及退休計劃法例中的條款，在某一特定時點（如轉制日）可能影響續訂合約的適用。因此可以推測存在一定的相關性。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b97ce5993df5b6616c6c24d7afbaa008</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;續訂&quot;" target="&quot;書面向要約續訂合約&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"續訂合同可以通過書面形式的要約進行，具體條款需滿足特定條件。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cad6d0a2eed4fbaf59a6253fe84df6ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;疾病津貼&quot;" target="&quot;超时工作薪酬&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据文本，疾病的津贴与计算超时工作的薪酬有关联。具体来说，在某些情况下，如第VII部付给的任何疾病津贴的第一个工作日可能会影响超时工作薪酬的计算方式。但是没有直接说明两者之间的关系强度。因此暂时无法给出一个具体的分数。可以进一步分析以确定其确切的关系强度。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d7b8e86ee38adbfe875f0b9f94a17519</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;疾病津貼&quot;" target="&quot;假日薪酬&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据文本，虽然疾病津贴和假日薪酬都涉及第VIII部的条款，但它们之间没有直接关系描述。因此无法给出具体分数。可以进一步分析以确定其确切的关系强度。“"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d7b8e86ee38adbfe875f0b9f94a17519</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;疾病津貼&quot;" target="&quot;終止該合約&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"即使僱傭合約已告終止,僱主仍須按僱員根據第(4)款有權獲得疾病津貼的病假日總數,將疾病津貼付給該僱員。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61c622614f8a7b3173a59e39171f674c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;疾病津貼&quot;" target="&quot;第33(2A)條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据第33(2A)条所累积者为有薪病假日的一部分，用于计算疾病津贴。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ede40d11dd383fafe8000e746a4c43b7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;疾病津貼&quot;" target="&quot;復工&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"复工会影响疾病的津贴，因为根据规定，病假日过后复工的僱員需要在记录内指明缺勤日子并签署相关文件。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ede40d11dd383fafe8000e746a4c43b7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;疾病津貼&quot;" target="&quot;罪行及罰則&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"未付给雇员根据第33条应得的任何疾病津贴将构成犯罪。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f7b047f9f55a2ab249abdbcd1a65d36</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;假日薪酬&quot;" target="&quot;超时工作薪酬&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据文本，假日薪酬与超时工作的薪酬都涉及到第VIII部的条款，并且在某些情况下可能会影响计算方式。例如，在特定日期前12个月内的平均款额可能会被用来比较。”但是没有直接说明两者之间的关系强度。因此暂时无法给出一个具体的分数。可以进一步分析以确定其确切的关系强度。“"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d7b8e86ee38adbfe875f0b9f94a17519</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;假日薪酬&quot;" target="&quot;僱主&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據第VIII部須支付的任何假日薪酬是終止僱傭金的一部分。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c82c895f7b30d4831c428126a0af9486</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;A&quot;" target="&quot;B&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The formula for A depends on B, indicating a direct mathematical relationship between the two variables."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9c100a1957a664aeaa3ecb305d4386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;A&quot;" target="&quot;C&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The calculation of A also involves C, showing that both B and C are factors in determining A's value."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9c100a1957a664aeaa3ecb305d4386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;A&quot;" target="&quot;ORS BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ORS benefit amount A depends on B and C, indicating a direct relationship between them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2ebf8163b69d6052462eecc2153a2260</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;A&quot;" target="&quot;OPERATION DATE: 1 MAY 2025.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The operation date defines when these regulations and calculations will take effect."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2ebf8163b69d6052462eecc2153a2260</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;B&quot;" target="&quot;C&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"B represents the employee's final average monthly relevant income which is influenced by years of service represented by C."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2ebf8163b69d6052462eecc2153a2260</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主供款豁免職業退休計劃利益&quot;" target="&quot;《強制性公積金計劃條例》(第485章)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The exemption of employer contributions to occupational pension benefits is defined by the Mandatory Provident Fund Schemes Ordinance (Cap. 485), specifically mentioning conditions for such exemptions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9c100a1957a664aeaa3ecb305d4386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主供款豁免職業退休計劃利益&quot;" target="&quot;職業退休计划&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer contributions to occupational pension benefits are part of the broader concept of a retirement plan, with specific rules and definitions provided by laws like the Mandatory Provident Fund Schemes Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9c100a1957a664aeaa3ecb305d4386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主供款豁免職業退休計劃利益&quot;" target="&quot;僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The exemption applies to employees who meet certain conditions as defined in the law, affecting their occupational pension benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9c100a1957a664aeaa3ecb305d4386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ALTERNATIVE HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'alternative holiday' is defined as a type of leave, which can be contrasted with the more general concept of annual leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fee7842314099c25edf5106ebd221850</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ALTERNATIVE HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;REST DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rest days and alternative holidays both fall under the category of non-working days for employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0aed3ae0b98488b1b913e6b49db19fee</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ALTERNATIVE HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees under a continuous contract also enjoy alternative holidays, enhancing their benefits package."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0aed3ae0b98488b1b913e6b49db19fee</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ALTERNATIVE HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The statutory holiday can be replaced by an alternative holiday within 60 days following the statutory holiday."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4bf6feb0461285dd636b630f26952415</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ANNUAL LEAVE PAY is related to the compensation for ANNUAL LEAVE, ensuring payment upon taking or after the leave period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Annual leave pay is required to be paid in respect of a period of annual leave, indicating an economic relationship between these two concepts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fee7842314099c25edf5106ebd221850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7dbc6cb0d2646456eacee5097d668ff</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"COURT can award ANNUAL LEAVE PAY as a form of terminal payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;NOTIONAL LEAVE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Notional leave pay is calculated based on the annual leave pay that would have been due under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed2004c9e59e7e54ef6756f3c59d039a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 41C&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 41C provides a method for calculating annual leave pay in specific circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed2004c9e59e7e54ef6756f3c59d039a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;PRO RATA PORTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PRO RATA PORTION affects how ANNUAL LEAVE PAY is calculated and distributed among employees based on their specific leave periods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e7dbc6cb0d2646456eacee5097d668ff</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Annual leave pay calculation is related to temporary incapacity for which compensation may be payable under the Employees' Compensation Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employee is entitled to annual leave pay under certain conditions as specified in subsections (3) and (4). "&lt;SEP&gt;"The employee is entitled to receive ANNUAL LEAVE PAY as per employment terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c46e076b844c67b6ef12faaaccec1c4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74bf264f43f2a8be1c1c6d9a90273b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CESSER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Upon EMPLOYMENT CESSER, the employee may be entitled to receive ANNUAL LEAVE PAY as per legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4b74bf264f43f2a8be1c1c6d9a90273b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CAP. 599 REQUIREMENT&quot;" target="&quot;32K COMPLIANCE ABSENCE NOT REASONABLE CAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The clause specifies that compliance absence due to Cap. 599 requirement is not a reasonable cause for dismissal, directly referencing the Cap. 599 requirement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e6297aac0b94f77cc5b93128ce6315ec</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CAP. 599 REQUIREMENT&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL CONTRAVENTION CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The legal contravention clause may relate to situations where compliance with Cap. 599 could lead to a legal issue, thus potentially impacting employment terms or conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e6297aac0b94f77cc5b93128ce6315ec</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CAP. 599 REQUIREMENT&quot;" target="&quot;THE REDUNDANCY CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While the redundancy clause deals with business operational requirements, it indirectly relates to Cap. 599 as both are part of employment termination policies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e6297aac0b94f77cc5b93128ce6315ec</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CAP. 599 REQUIREMENT&quot;" target="&quot;SERIOUS AND WILFUL MISCONDUCT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employee's serious and wilful misconduct may subject them to the Cap. 599 requirement on absence days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-778e7c7afca4e1466ce3da77bd8ff90a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CAP. 599 REQUIREMENT&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 63(4)(E)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The requirement under CAP. 599 does not count towards annual leave unless it commences after the start of the period for which leave should have been granted."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b63d3371d1b762c2013adc08da9c549f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CAP. 599 REQUIREMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 2025&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ordinance mentions compliance with Cap. 599 requirement as a reason for absence from work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8b48e83da24f4750fe34f6e53c34ac0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILD&quot;" target="&quot;CONFINEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">20.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Confinement is defined as the delivery of a child, directly relating these two terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Confinement is the delivery of a child, directly linking these two terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fee7842314099c25edf5106ebd221850</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONFINEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Confinement determines the start date of maternity leave and its duration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8d3158e721c74f203da21b92ec49085</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONFINEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 12AA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 12AA is directly related to determining the actual date of confinement, which impacts eligibility for maternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8d3158e721c74f203da21b92ec49085</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DANGEROUS DRUG (危險藥物)&quot;" target="&quot;DIRECTOR (署長)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The DIRECTOR of Health oversees the regulation of DANGEROUS DRUGS under the Dangerous Drugs Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOMESTIC SERVANT (家庭傭工)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A DOMESTIC SERVANT is a type of EMPLOYEE, specifically one who works in domestic service."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED ORS BENEFIT (僱主供款職業退休計劃利益)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYER-funded ORS benefit is a type of employer-provided retirement plan benefit, applicable to all employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;HOLIDAY PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Statutory holidays can be part of holiday pay as defined by relevant labor laws and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e70ac051c2f0b62b1c78481493c78790</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;REST DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If the statutory holiday coincides with a rest day or is on a day when young people are not allowed to work due to regulations, an alternative non-statutory and non-rest day will be granted."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rest days are in addition to statutory holidays, which employees can also enjoy."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0aed3ae0b98488b1b913e6b49db19fee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bf6feb0461285dd636b630f26952415</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Continuous contract employees have rights to statutory holidays as part of their employment terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0aed3ae0b98488b1b913e6b49db19fee</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;NORMAL WORKING DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Statutory holiday does not count towards normal working days when assessing lay-off status."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2138132720286ddae5a4634e3cd8c8f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Neither STATUTORY HOLIDAY nor ANNUAL LEAVE are considered normal working days when determining layoff status."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8e2655c247e96affa05132d650c897b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;法定假日*&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"STATUTORY HOLIDAYS are defined and regulated by the laws mentioned in Part VIII, such as those related to Chinese New Year days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f729e4dc4d8c13592d31110960bc5996</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSTITUTED HOLIDAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A substituted holiday may replace a statutory holiday, provided it falls within 30 days of such statutory holiday."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4bf6feb0461285dd636b630f26952415</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;ANOTHER STATUTORY HOLIDAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"When two statutory holidays fall on the same date, the employee gets their next available non-holiday day off."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4bf6feb0461285dd636b630f26952415</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MANDATORY PROVIDENT FUND SCHEMES ORDINANCE (CAP. 485)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRIBUTIONS TO OCCUPATIONAL RETIREMENT SCHEME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contributions are mentioned in relation to both the occupational retirement scheme and the Mandatory Provident Fund Schemes Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da3daa00f8a571e7a58b273ea6df48ea</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL (勞資審裁處)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE establishes the Labour Tribunal as defined in the LABOUR TRIBUNAL (勞資審裁處). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b1423caf4f652f620d2ab84148c99789</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT (長期服務金)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Long service payment, a concept related to employee benefits, is not directly defined in the LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE but could be relevant under its jurisdiction. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b1423caf4f652f620d2ab84148c99789</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE (產假)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maternity leave, while not directly mentioned in the LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE, is a related concept often covered under labor laws. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b1423caf4f652f620d2ab84148c99789</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;LOCK-OUT (閉廠)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The lock-out is defined by section 2 of the TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (Cap. 332). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b1423caf4f652f620d2ab84148c99789</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MANDATORY PROVIDENT FUND SCHEMES ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;MANDATORY PROVIDENT FUND SCHEME (強制性公積金計劃)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The mandatory provident fund scheme is defined by the MANDATORY PROVIDENT FUND SCHEMES ORDINANCE (Cap. 485). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b1423caf4f652f620d2ab84148c99789</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MANDATORY PROVIDENT FUND SCHEMES ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;CAP. 485&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'mandatory provident fund scheme' is defined under the Mandatory Provident Fund Schemes Ordinance, Cap. 485."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-765d51e319fa417bcf02401654532054</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
