</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE TERMINATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similar to maternity leave, paternity leave is considered in the calculation of termination compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"PATERNITY LEAVE" is detailed in Part IIIA of the Employment Regulations, showing how it's structured within the broader context of employment laws."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-885c65878619106b2d2b302114a64bb2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employment contract is a prerequisite for an employee to be eligible for Paternity Leave as per the regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity leave is a benefit covered under the employment contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-885c65878619106b2d2b302114a64bb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;NOTIFICATION REQUIREMENTS FOR PATERNITY LEAVE (15F)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The notification requirements for paternity leave are detailed in section 15F of the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bb89bd87e81559e9820333c42f3f0c6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;REST DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Paternity Leave can be taken on a day immediately after a Rest Day, even if it would normally fall within another type of leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a8a8ba58e2f04dd4f35b5bed0e044673</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;HOLIDAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Paternity Leave can also be taken the next day following a Holiday or Annual Leave period when they coincide."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a8a8ba58e2f04dd4f35b5bed0e044673</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">20.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Paternity leave can extend into annual leave periods, providing extended time off."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paternity leave may coincide with annual leave periods, providing additional time off."&lt;SEP&gt;"Similar to Rest Days and Holidays, Paternity Leave may follow an Annual Leave period if conditions are met."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c54e7deea495212bab465e4af100b7ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8a8ba58e2f04dd4f35b5bed0e044673</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;REST DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Paternity leave can be taken on a rest day, with entitlement to take it on the next working day if necessary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c54e7deea495212bab465e4af100b7ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;BIRTH CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The birth certificate is needed to prove the paternity for leave purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bab24c47d69b1c9fe7a8b2d862514c83</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;WRITTEN STATEMENT FROM EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employee's written statement may be required as proof of entitlement to paternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bab24c47d69b1c9fe7a8b2d862514c83</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employee takes paternity leave as part of their employment relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;REQUISITE DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Paternity leave documents are required within 12 months after the first day of taking paternity leave or 6 months after cessation of employment, whichever expires first."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 15L&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 15L mandates the payment of paternity leave pay for employees who are entitled to it."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0aed3ae0b98488b1b913e6b49db19fee</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Paternity leave is granted according to a continuous contract between an employee and employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0aed3ae0b98488b1b913e6b49db19fee</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;BAA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Paternity leave is included under BAA as a type of leave affecting wage calculations and employment contracts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0fef56ddac89c58276c95d49a4ad2fde</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES EARNED BY THE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Paternity leave days are included in the wage calculations for determining holiday pay rates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9d14b62c50b2a0a92ac73c8ef0642fe9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 15E(3)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Paternity leave entitlement is governed by the provisions of SECTION 15E(3)(B), as in force before and after the amendment date."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-570e52321eeb26a637fff48779e8695d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 15G(4)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Paternity leave entitlement is also influenced by the provisions of SECTION 15G(4)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-570e52321eeb26a637fff48779e8695d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">23.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employee has a right to receive Paternity Leave Pay from the Employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employee is entitled to paternity leave pay, which may require providing proof of paternity through the mentioned documents."&lt;SEP&gt;"The payment of paternity leave pay is directly related to an employee who has taken paternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9f8f154dd34baff54c016b669ab2da5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6320bd8af6a47ec4d774b02d5588447a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4881be1a6d6d318bb1047aad7c99da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;REQUISITE DOCUMENT (所需文件)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Requisite document is required for the entitlement to paternity leave pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2f4881be1a6d6d318bb1047aad7c99da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES OR ANY OTHER SUM PAYABLE UNDER SECTION 23, 24 OR 25&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similarly to maternity leave pay, this is another form of compensation that could be awarded by the tribunal for a different reason."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6d4bd265e2aa3d3a8af55fbca1b13963</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;END OF YEAR PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"These two forms of payment, like maternity leave pay, could potentially be awarded by the tribunal as part of resolving disputes over wages or other sums."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6d4bd265e2aa3d3a8af55fbca1b13963</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are types of compensation that might be awarded in a tribunal case for different reasons related to employment rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6d4bd265e2aa3d3a8af55fbca1b13963</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT WITHOUT NOTICE OR PAYMENT IN LIEU&quot;" target="&quot;DATE ON WHICH TERMINATION TAKES EFFECT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The date on which termination takes effect is determined by the employment without notice or payment in lieu."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT WITHOUT NOTICE OR PAYMENT IN LIEU&quot;" target="&quot;SPOUSE (配偶)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">3.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employment status of an employee can be affected by the spouse's actions or circumstances, though not directly stated in this text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DATE ON WHICH TERMINATION TAKES EFFECT&quot;" target="&quot;FIXED TERM EXPIRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fixed term expiration directly leads to the date of termination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RETIREMENT AT SPECIFIED AGE&quot;" target="&quot;DATE OF RETIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The specified age for retirement determines the exact date when an employee retires."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE DEATH&quot;" target="&quot;DATE OF EMPLOYEE'S DEATH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employee death results in a specific date of termination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE DEATH&quot;" target="&quot;31RA CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The clause applies when an employee dies, relating directly to compensation for death benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-54addea578982eb79d7f3048cf09c6a2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE DEATH&quot;" target="&quot;31YA CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 31YA Clause is directly related to employee death, as it outlines specific scenarios involving such events."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-54addea578982eb79d7f3048cf09c6a2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE DEATH&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Compensation is directly related to employee death, as it involves payments and benefits in such cases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-54addea578982eb79d7f3048cf09c6a2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE DEATH&quot;" target="&quot;GRATUITY OR BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYEE DEATH triggers the entitlement for a GRATUITY OR BENEFIT under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gratuity or benefit is related to situations where an employee has died, potentially affecting its calculation in relation to long service payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dabef41d299eda51d77087c2ca170398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b66ec28db0dbcb16e24e4d4df0ef35a2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE DEATH&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The death of an employee can lead to the payment of LONG SERVICE PAYMENTS based on their length of service."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b66ec28db0dbcb16e24e4d4df0ef35a2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE DEATH&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT (SECTION 31RA)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The death of an employee triggers the requirement for a long service payment under Section 31RA."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a21b404a5b0d354defe8dd03eb692b6b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE DEATH&quot;" target="&quot;GRATUITIES BASED ON LENGTH OF SERVICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The death of an employee can result in Person A becoming entitled to gratuities based on length of service."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a21b404a5b0d354defe8dd03eb692b6b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE DEATH&quot;" target="&quot;ORS BENEFITS (EMPLOYER-FUNDED SPECIFIED)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The death of an employee may lead to Person B being eligible for employer-funded specified ORS benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a21b404a5b0d354defe8dd03eb692b6b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE DEATH&quot;" target="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS (EMPLOYER-FUNDED VOLUNTARY)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The death of an employee might result in Person B becoming entitled to employer-funded voluntary MPFS benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a21b404a5b0d354defe8dd03eb692b6b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DATE OF TERMINATION OTHER THAN ORDINANCE PROVISIONS&quot;" target="&quot;RENEWAL (續訂)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Renewal and other terminations are related as both involve changes to the employment contract's duration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT (遣散費)&quot;" target="&quot;REST DAY (休息日)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rest days do not directly relate to severance payment, but they are part of employee benefits and can indirectly influence termination processes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT (遣散費)&quot;" target="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY (法定假日)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Statutory holidays are part of employment benefits and can indirectly influence severance payment policies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS DAY (病假日)&quot;" target="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE (疾病津貼)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sickness allowance is provided for sickness days, indicating a direct relationship between the two concepts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPOUSE (配偶)&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of SPOUSE is relevant to the calculation of WAGES, as it may affect eligibility or distribution in certain scenarios."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPOUSE (配偶)&quot;" target="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY (法定假日)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While not directly related, both concepts pertain to employment conditions and benefits that may intersect in certain scenarios."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPOUSE (配偶)&quot;" target="&quot;TRANSITION DATE (轉制日)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The TRANSITION DATE may affect policies related to SPOUSE benefits or eligibility under new legislation."&lt;SEP&gt;"While not directly related, both concepts pertain to employment conditions that may intersect in certain scenarios; TRANSITION DATE could affect policies for SPOUSE benefits or eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPOUSE (配偶)&quot;" target="&quot;TIPS AND SERVICE CHARGES (小費及服務費)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">3.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While not directly related, both concepts pertain to employment conditions that may intersect in certain scenarios; SPOUSE benefits and TIPS are components of compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPOUSE (配偶)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSTITUTED HOLIDAY (代替假日)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">3.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While not directly related, both concepts pertain to employment conditions that may intersect in certain scenarios; SPOUSE benefits could be affected by work done during SUBSTITUTED HOLIDAYS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPOUSE (配偶)&quot;" target="&quot;TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While not directly related, both concepts pertain to employment conditions that may intersect in certain scenarios; SPOUSE benefits could be affected by the legal frameworks set by the TRADE UNION ORDINANCE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY (法定假日)&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIFIED EMPLOYEE (指明僱員)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Specified employees may have specific rights related to statutory holidays as defined by law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6555c73e9baef9f5e0a5b77ea0dcb72b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY (法定假日)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSTITUTED HOLIDAY (代替假日)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are types of holidays within employment context, with STATUTORY HOLIDAY being officially specified and SUBSTITUTED HOLIDAY granted under specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY (法定假日)&quot;" target="&quot;TIPS AND SERVICE CHARGES (小費及服務費)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are components of WAGES, with TIPS and SERVICE CHARGES being part of the broader context of employment terms that may intersect during STATUTORY HOLIDAYS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both are part of employment terms but serve different purposes; STATUTORY HOLIDAYS are official holidays, while TIPS and SERVICE CHARGES are components of wages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY (法定假日)&quot;" target="&quot;WAGE PERIOD (工資期)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are part of the broader context of employment terms, with STATUTORY HOLIDAYS affecting WAGE PERIODs during which wages may be payable or not."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY (法定假日)&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition of WAGES includes components like TIPS and SERVICE CHARGES, which may be affected by STATUTORY HOLIDAYS in terms of work done or not."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STRIKE (罷工)&quot;" target="&quot;TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition of STRIKE is provided by the TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE, indicating its legal framework and implications under this ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STRIKE (罷工)&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A STRIKE can impact WAGES as it affects the work done or to be done under an employee's contract of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSTITUTED HOLIDAY (代替假日)&quot;" target="&quot;WAGE PERIOD (工資期)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both concepts are related to employment terms, with SUBSTITUTED HOLIDAY affecting the WAGE PERIOD during which wages may be payable or not."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSTITUTED HOLIDAY (代替假日)&quot;" target="&quot;TIPS AND SERVICE CHARGES (小費及服務費)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are part of the broader context of employment terms and conditions, though they serve different purposes in wage calculation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSTITUTED HOLIDAY (代替假日)&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of SUBSTITUTED HOLIDAY is related to the calculation and distribution of WAGES, as it affects work done during holidays."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TIPS AND SERVICE CHARGES (小費及服務費)&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"TIPS AND SERVICE CHARGES are components of WAGES, as defined in the text, making them directly related to employee compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRANSITION DATE (轉制日)&quot;" target="&quot;WAGE PERIOD (工資期)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The TRANSITION DATE could affect how WAGE PERIODs are calculated or managed under new legislation, impacting the distribution of wages during different periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"The TRANSITION DATE may affect how WAGE PERIODs are calculated or managed under new legislation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGE PERIOD (工資期)&quot;" target="&quot;TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The TRADE UNION ORDINANCE sets legal frameworks for WAGE PERIODs, affecting how wages are calculated and paid during different periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"The definition of WAGE PERIOD is influenced by the TRADE UNION ORDINANCE, as it sets legal frameworks for wage calculation and payment periods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGE PERIOD (工資期)&quot;" target="&quot;MINIMUM WAGE ORDINANCE (CAP. 608)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Wage period is defined as having the same meaning as in the Minimum Wage Ordinance (Cap. 608). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-45d3d232b5b9df510faacc808489eadb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;" target="&quot;TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition of WAGES is influenced by the TRADE UNION ORDINANCE, as it sets legal frameworks for employee rights and compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-999568dd0ce8caf693ec39180ae820e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'wages' is defined in the Ordinance to include overtime pay under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e220e0c7587651abe976f081881efeb5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;" target="&quot;LEAVE TAKEN BY THE EMPLOYEE WITH THE AGREEMENT OF HIS EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Leaves taken with employer agreement are included in wages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;" target="&quot;NORMAL WORKING DAY ON WHICH THE EMPLOYEE IS NOT PROVIDED WITH WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Days without work but still counted as working days for wage calculation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPORARY INCAPACITY FOR WHICH COMPENSATION IS PAYABLE UNDER SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Compensation for temporary incapacity is included in wages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 12(3)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"WAGES includes any sum paid by an employer, as defined in SECTION 12(3), which is relevant to the calculation of maternity leave pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-681c7e69874ff6c2cdf180f0fb0d44f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Wages include payments for days taken as maternity leave, indicating a direct financial relationship between the two concepts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;" target="&quot;REST DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Wages also cover rest day payments, showing that both are part of an employee's compensation package."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Annual leave payments are included in the definition of wages, reinforcing their financial relationship and importance to employees' remuneration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;" target="&quot;LEAVE TAKEN WITH AGREEMENT OF EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Leaves taken with employer's agreement are considered part of an employee's compensation package as wages, indicating a direct financial relationship between the two concepts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;" target="&quot;NORMAL WORKING DAY WITHOUT WORK PROVIDED&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Even on days without work provided, normal working day payments are included in wages, showing that these are integral parts of an employee's compensation package."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPORARY INCAPACITY FOR COMPENSATION UNDER SECTION 10 OF EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Temporary incapacity due to work-related injuries or illnesses is compensated as part of wages, indicating a direct financial relationship between the two concepts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES (工資)&quot;" target="&quot;MINIMUM WAGE ORDINANCE (CAP. 608)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Wages is defined as having the same meaning as in the Minimum Wage Ordinance (Cap. 608). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-45d3d232b5b9df510faacc808489eadb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;" target="&quot;WORKER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The WORKER has the right to form or apply for registration of a trade union according to the provisions of the TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (Cap. 332)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bb269a993727b98b029449c2f2612dff</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;" target="&quot;PENALTY FOR PREVENTING UNION ACTIVITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PENALTY FOR PREVENTING UNION ACTIVITIES is defined by the TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (Cap. 332), which outlines fines for employers who prevent or deter workers from exercising their union rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bb269a993727b98b029449c2f2612dff</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;" target="&quot;21C. 以受要約人並非職工會會員作為僱傭要約的條件&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The provision '21C. 以受要約人並非職工會會員作為僱傭要約的條件' is related to the TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (Cap. 332) as it involves conditions that may affect workers and their union membership."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bb269a993727b98b029449c2f2612dff</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;" target="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (CAP. 25)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Labour Tribunal Ordinance and the Trade Unions Ordinance both contribute to labour rights, with one focusing on dispute resolution and the other on trade unions and their activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06d23d2b54047f6e0d92f6798bcab7c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;" target="&quot;APPRENTICESHIP ORDINANCE (CAP. 47)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Apprenticeship Ordinance and the Trade Unions Ordinance both contribute to labour rights, with one focusing on apprenticeships and the other on trade unions and their activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06d23d2b54047f6e0d92f6798bcab7c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRADE UNIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;" target="&quot;LABOUR RELATIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 55)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Labour Relations Ordinance and the Trade Unions Ordinance both contribute to labour rights, with one focusing on broader relations and the other on trade unions and their activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06d23d2b54047f6e0d92f6798bcab7c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;星期&quot;" target="&quot;工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"工資的计算可能涉及每周的工作时间，特别是对于按周支付或计时的工资部分。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a82f354bd72ecc759d4ab4ed34bac3db</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TERMINATION OF A CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT UNDER PART IIA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are part of the broader employment benefits and can be calculated separately for payment purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT UNDER PART IIA&quot;" target="&quot;WEEK (星期)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The week period is used in calculating end-of-year payments for employees, as defined by the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY UNDER PART III&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT UNDER PART VA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While both relate to employee benefits, they serve different purposes: maternity leave is a right during pregnancy, while severance pay occurs upon termination of employment. However, their calculation methods share some similarities in terms of wage averaging."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY UNDER PART III&quot;" target="&quot;YOUNG PERSON (青年)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">3.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Young persons are not directly related to maternity leave pay, but both terms appear within the context of employment benefits and could be part of a broader discussion on employee rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY UNDER PART III&quot;" target="&quot;WEEK (星期)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The week period is a standard timeframe that could be relevant to defining maternity leave pay periods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE PAY UNDER PART IIIA&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT UNDER PART VB&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are types of leave or payment related to the length of service but serve different purposes: paternity for new fathers, and long service as a recognition of extended employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE PAY UNDER PART IIIA&quot;" target="&quot;YOUNG PERSON (青年)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">3.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Young persons are not directly related to paternity leave pay, but both terms appear within the context of employment benefits and could be part of a broader discussion on employee rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE PAY UNDER PART IIIA&quot;" target="&quot;WEEK (星期)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The week period is used in the definition of paternity leave, which can affect how paternity leave payments are calculated."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT UNDER PART VA&quot;" target="&quot;YOUNG PERSON (青年)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">3.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Young persons are not directly related to severance payment, but both terms appear within the context of employment benefits and could be part of a broader discussion on employee rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT UNDER PART VA&quot;" target="&quot;WEEK (星期)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">3.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While not directly related to severance payment calculation, the week period could be a standard timeframe used in broader employment benefit calculations that include severance pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT UNDER PART VB&quot;" target="&quot;YOUNG PERSON (青年)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">3.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Young persons are not directly related to long service payment, but both terms appear within the context of employment benefits and could be part of a broader discussion on employee rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT UNDER PART VB&quot;" target="&quot;WEEK (星期)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The week period is relevant for defining long service payments as it sets a standard timeframe, which can affect the calculation of such benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE UNDER PART VII&quot;" target="&quot;HOLIDAY PAY UNDER PART VIII&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are forms of leave pay that provide financial support to employees during specific periods (sickness or holidays), but they serve different purposes and have distinct calculation methods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE UNDER PART VII&quot;" target="&quot;YOUNG PERSON (青年)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">3.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Young persons are not directly related to sickness allowance, but both terms appear within the context of employment benefits and could be part of a broader discussion on employee rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SICKNESS ALLOWANCE UNDER PART VII&quot;" target="&quot;WEEK (星期)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The week period could be used in calculating sickness allowances, providing a standard timeframe for benefit periods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOLIDAY PAY UNDER PART VIII&quot;" target="&quot;YOUNG PERSON (青年)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">3.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Young persons are not directly related to holiday pay, but both terms appear within the context of employment benefits and could be part of a broader discussion on employee rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOLIDAY PAY UNDER PART VIII&quot;" target="&quot;WEEK (星期)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The week period is relevant to defining holiday pay as it sets the standard timeframe within which such benefits are calculated."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY UNDER PART VIIIA&quot;" target="&quot;WEEK (星期)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">11.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Annual leave is calculated based on the week period, which defines a standard timeframe for such calculations. The term 'week' here refers to the specific definition provided in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The week period could be used in calculating annual leave payments, providing a standard timeframe for benefit periods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE PAY UNDER PART VIIIA&quot;" target="&quot;YOUNG PERSON (青年)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">3.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Young persons are not directly related to annual leave pay, but both terms appear within the context of employment benefits and could be part of a broader discussion on employee rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c735c0e7a26c8bc956ca3d3db04358ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (2B)&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (2B) specifically addresses the date for termination of employment as per subsection (2)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9dc495e2347a322a5aaa3ff390e7601c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TERMINATION OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;TRANSFER FROM HEAVY, HAZARDOUS OR HARMFUL WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A transfer from heavy, hazardous or harmful work can be related to termination of employment in terms of wage calculations and benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-47f5ddfc5b519fcf524c4d9bd233c4e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISMISSAL&quot;" target="&quot;LAY OFF WITHIN THE MEANING OF SECTION 31E&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are mentioned in the context of possible terminations or layoffs within the meaning of specific sections."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both dismissal and lay off are forms of termination of employment mentioned in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9dc495e2347a322a5aaa3ff390e7601c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISMISSAL&quot;" target="&quot;9TH REGULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Dismissal is governed by regulations, including the 9th Regulation which defines conditions under which an employee can be considered dismissed without notice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a40a9600dcdabbcf7b1de20226238a1e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISMISSAL&quot;" target="&quot;10TH REGULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 10th Regulation also plays a role in defining dismissal scenarios and conditions for employees not to receive severance payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a40a9600dcdabbcf7b1de20226238a1e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISMISSAL&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">22.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employee's dismissal is considered under the context of their association with multiple employers, including any associated companies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dismissing an employee can be done in contravention of the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (Cap. 59), specifically Section 6."&lt;SEP&gt;"The DISMISSAL of an EMPLOYEE is the subject of legal challenges and awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3deed786d6a1376b3e79e218144b7d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc0e662ccd81354d4e411a146aa85d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01e8dd2cd7216b43532ed7037814b54b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISMISSAL&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Long service payment may not be applicable as a result of dismissal according to certain conditions outlined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bdbd130fa51f2bbf4428aee9c45795cb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISMISSAL&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 32K&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Dismissal is considered without a valid reason unless shown otherwise under SECTION 32K."&lt;SEP&gt;"SECTION 32K defines conditions under which variations in contract terms by an employer are not considered as dismissal without a valid reason."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-66cccec6ac7d06fb5417245d5fe5f3b9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISMISSAL&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OR LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT OR LABOUR TRIBUNAL can make decisions regarding DISMISSAL under certain sections of the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2cc0e662ccd81354d4e411a146aa85d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISMISSAL&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 32A(1)(C)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"SECTION 32A(1)(C) defines circumstances under which DISMISSAL can be challenged by the COURT OR LABOUR TRIBUNAL."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2cc0e662ccd81354d4e411a146aa85d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISMISSAL&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 15(1), 21B(2)(B), 33(4B) OR 72B(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Dismissing an employee must not contravene these sections to be valid."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2cc0e662ccd81354d4e411a146aa85d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISMISSAL&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 6 OF THE FACTORIES AND INDUSTRIAL UNDERTAKINGS ORDINANCE (CAP. 59)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The DISMISSAL of an employee cannot violate the provisions in this section."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2cc0e662ccd81354d4e411a146aa85d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISMISSAL&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 48 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Dismissing an employee must not contravene the compensation obligations under this section."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2cc0e662ccd81354d4e411a146aa85d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TERMINATION HIS CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT IN CIRCUMSTANCES SPECIFIED IN SECTION 10(AA) OR 31R(1)(B)&quot;" target="&quot;DEATH IN CIRCUMSTANCES SPECIFIED IN SECTION 31RA(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are related to the termination of employment, with one being a voluntary action and the other an involuntary event."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both are specified as circumstances leading to the termination of employment, though one is related to death and the other to contract termination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9dc495e2347a322a5aaa3ff390e7601c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31E&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 10(AA)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both sections are part of the same Ordinance and deal with contract termination conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e43ce81a5e24ba44cc5896e9318ba422</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31E&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31R(1)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"All three sections (31E, 10(aa), 31R(1)(b)) are part of the same Ordinance and deal with contract termination conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e43ce81a5e24ba44cc5896e9318ba422</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31E&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31RA(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"All three sections (31E, 10(aa), 31R(1)(b)) are part of the same Ordinance and deal with contract termination conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e43ce81a5e24ba44cc5896e9318ba422</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 10(AA)&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據第10(aa)條，僱主可能需支付長期服務金給符合條件的僱員。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f9abcb1aa4ccb5d467cb0175ca3011bc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31R(1)(B)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 6&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Termination with notice according to SECTION 6 does not affect entitlement under section 31R(1)(b). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e3a3f0edfa08a61dbd46b52c9f94d56a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31R(1)(B)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31T(1)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Dismissal under section 31T(1)(B) affects the employee's right to a long service payment by reason of dismissal. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e3a3f0edfa08a61dbd46b52c9f94d56a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31R(1)(B)&quot;" target="&quot;4 OF 2022 S. 7&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Amendments affecting the conditions for terminating employment are detailed in s. 7 of 2022."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6c8faaa89696bb97daf5c16e2354ab6f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31RA(1)&quot;" target="&quot;REFERENCE AMOUNT A&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 31RA(1) is part of a broader set of provisions that may indirectly impact the reference amount calculation through contract termination conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e43ce81a5e24ba44cc5896e9318ba422</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 4(3)(B)&lt;CAP. 485&gt;&lt;PERSON, ORGANIZATION&quot;" target="&quot;REFERENCE AMOUNT A&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The reference amount is calculated based on an employee's final average monthly relevant income as defined in the ordinance (Cap. 485)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e43ce81a5e24ba44cc5896e9318ba422</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 5(1)&lt;CAP. 485&gt;&lt;PERSON, ORGANIZATION&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S FINAL AVERAGE MONTHLY RELEVANT INCOME B&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 5 of Cap. 485 defines the conditions under which an employee can be exempt from certain provisions, impacting their final average monthly relevant income calculation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e43ce81a5e24ba44cc5896e9318ba422</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REFERENCE AMOUNT A&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S FINAL AVERAGE MONTHLY RELEVANT INCOME B&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The reference amount calculation depends directly on the employee's final average monthly relevant income."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e43ce81a5e24ba44cc5896e9318ba422</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;MANDATORY PROVIDENT FUND SCHEMES (EXEMPTION) REGULATION (CAP. 485 SUB. LEG. B)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ORS benefit regulation defines the relevant schemes and their impact on calculating A."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2ebf8163b69d6052462eecc2153a2260</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;SCHEDULE 2 TO THE MANDATORY PROVIDENT FUND SCHEMES (EXEMPTION) REGULATION (CAP. 485 SUB. LEG. B)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Schedule 2 provides the definition of final average monthly relevant income, which is crucial for calculating A."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2ebf8163b69d6052462eecc2153a2260</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;ONUS OF PROOF THEREOF&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The onus of proof regarding the continuous contract affects how ORS benefits are calculated, as it involves disputes over employment status."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2ebf8163b69d6052462eecc2153a2260</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (BASIC PORTION) EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer-funded (basic portion) exempt ORS benefit is a specific type of ORS benefit."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-570e52321eeb26a637fff48779e8695d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT (連續性合約)&quot;" target="&quot;ONUS OF PROOF THEREOF&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Continuous contract and its onus of proof are directly related in legal disputes regarding employee status."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2ebf8163b69d6052462eecc2153a2260</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;ONUS OF PROOF&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The onus of proving that a contract is not a continuous contract lies with the employer in disputes regarding its status."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e976980f19e9ab89febaf65027fa503e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;APPLICABILITY SCOPE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The applicability scope defines which employment contracts fall under the provisions for continuous contracts as defined in this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e976980f19e9ab89febaf65027fa503e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ordinance defines continuous contracts as those that are deemed to be for 1 month and renewable from month to month unless otherwise agreed in writing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e804bc54b158b7b2826228aa81b5372e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;MONTHLY RENEWAL CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Continuous contracts are calculated based on the proportion of monthly salaries within their agreed duration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e804bc54b158b7b2826228aa81b5372e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Continuous contracts provide the basis for entitlement to maternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8d3158e721c74f203da21b92ec49085</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;NOTIFICATION REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Continuous employment under a contract is related to notification requirements for paid maternity leave according to the Employment Ordinance (Cap. 27)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;40 WEEKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The continuous contract must be of at least 40 weeks for an employee to qualify for paternity leave pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c54e7deea495212bab465e4af100b7ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSTITUTED HOLIDAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Continuous contracts include rights to substituted holidays as part of the employment agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0aed3ae0b98488b1b913e6b49db19fee</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;REPEALED 76 OF 1985 S. 4&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The repealed section may have had implications on the definition or enforcement of continuous employment contracts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d9809ad52a0fec55dacd101bbfec86fa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;LAYOFF&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A continuous contract for a period of not less than 24 months ending with the relevant date can lead to layoff."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employee under a continuous contract for at least 24 months is entitled to severance payment if dismissed by reason of redundancy or laid off."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Continuous contract is a type of employment agreement with specific terms and conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;LABOR LAWS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Labor laws govern the terms and conditions, including continuous contracts and their rights and responsibilities for both employers and employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;TRANSITION DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The continuous contract's effect is modified based on the transition date."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da3daa00f8a571e7a58b273ea6df48ea</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;PARTS VA AND VB&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The continuous contract determines if Parts VA and VB apply to an employee's situation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da3daa00f8a571e7a58b273ea6df48ea</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees are entitled to ANNUAL LEAVE after working under a CONTINUOUS CONTRACT for at least 12 months."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A CONTINUOUS CONTRACT defines the EMPLOYMENT PERIOD during which an employee can accumulate rights such as ANNUAL LEAVE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f7ea07c8002a487f595524992c8604b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 2025 (27 OF 2025)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 2025 defines the conditions for a 'continuous contract' which is central to determining employment status under this ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7d9929bbede2eb72d013426b56ad4e6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPLICABILITY SCOPE&quot;" target="&quot;IV-A PART&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"IV-A Part specifies exclusions from the applicability of certain sections, including those related to continuous contract status and onus of proof."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e976980f19e9ab89febaf65027fa503e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPLICABILITY SCOPE&quot;" target="&quot;SEAFARER AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Seafarers' agreements, defined in Chapter 478, are excluded from the applicability of certain sections under this Ordinance as per IV-A Part (2)(c)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e976980f19e9ab89febaf65027fa503e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPLICABILITY SCOPE&quot;" target="&quot;APPRENTICESHIP TRAINING CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Apprenticeship training contracts registered under Chapter 47, are excluded from the applicability of certain sections under this Ordinance as per IV-A Part (2A)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e976980f19e9ab89febaf65027fa503e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOUSEHOLD MEMBER OF EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Household members of employers are excluded from the scope of employment contracts regulated by this Ordinance as per IV-A Part (2)(b)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e976980f19e9ab89febaf65027fa503e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPRENTICESHIP ORDINANCE (CAP. 47)&quot;" target="&quot;APPRENTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Apprenticeship Ordinance specifically deals with apprentices, and their contracts of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-786c67dfb1439b58fce397c3168c9e29</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPRENTICESHIP ORDINANCE (CAP. 47)&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner has the authority to authorize public officers, which is not directly related to apprenticeship under Cap. 47 but pertains to broader administrative functions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a5218a05714fc8de44f54bb46fbf020e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPRENTICESHIP ORDINANCE (CAP. 47)&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">3.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public Officers are mentioned in the context of this Ordinance, though they do not have direct authority over apprenticeship contracts under Cap. 47."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a5218a05714fc8de44f54bb46fbf020e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPRENTICESHIP ORDINANCE (CAP. 47)&quot;" target="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (CAP. 25)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ordinances are part of the legal framework for labour and employment in Hong Kong, though they address different aspects such as disputes resolution versus apprenticeship programs."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06d23d2b54047f6e0d92f6798bcab7c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPRENTICESHIP ORDINANCE (CAP. 47)&quot;" target="&quot;LABOUR RELATIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 55)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ordinances address different aspects of labour relations, with the Apprenticeship Ordinance focusing on apprenticeships and the Labour Relations Ordinance addressing broader labour rights and collective bargaining."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06d23d2b54047f6e0d92f6798bcab7c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPRENTICESHIP ORDINANCE (CAP. 47)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTS FOR EMPLOYMENT OUTSIDE HONG KONG ORDINANCE (CAP. 78)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Apprenticeship Ordinance deals with local apprenticeships, while the Contracts for Employment Outside Hong Kong Ordinance addresses employment contracts outside of Hong Kong, both contributing to a comprehensive legal framework for labour issues."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06d23d2b54047f6e0d92f6798bcab7c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPRENTICESHIP ORDINANCE (CAP. 47)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ordinances are part of the broader legal system addressing employee rights, though they focus on different aspects such as apprenticeships versus compensation for injuries or illnesses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06d23d2b54047f6e0d92f6798bcab7c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPRENTICESHIP ORDINANCE (CAP. 47)&quot;" target="&quot;PNEUMOCONIOSIS AND MESOTHELIOMA (COMPENSATION) ORDINANCE (CAP. 360)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ordinances are part of the legal framework addressing employee rights and compensation, though they focus on different health issues such as apprenticeships versus specific occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06d23d2b54047f6e0d92f6798bcab7c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPRENTICESHIP ORDINANCE (CAP. 47)&quot;" target="&quot;MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD ORDINANCE (CAP. 453)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ordinances are part of the legal framework for labour disputes, with one focusing on general tribunal processes and the other specifically on minor employment claims adjudication."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06d23d2b54047f6e0d92f6798bcab7c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTS FOR EMPLOYMENT OUTSIDE HONG KONG ORDINANCE (CAP. 78)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"This ordinance defines employees for the purpose of contracts outside Hong Kong, which is an exception to the main Ordinance's application."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-786c67dfb1439b58fce397c3168c9e29</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTS FOR EMPLOYMENT OUTSIDE HONG KONG ORDINANCE (CAP. 78)&quot;" target="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (CAP. 25)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Labour Tribunal Ordinance covers disputes within Hong Kong, while the Contracts for Employment Outside Hong Kong Ordinance addresses employment contracts outside of Hong Kong, both contributing to a comprehensive legal framework for labour issues."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06d23d2b54047f6e0d92f6798bcab7c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTS FOR EMPLOYMENT OUTSIDE HONG KONG ORDINANCE (CAP. 78)&quot;" target="&quot;LABOUR RELATIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 55)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ordinances address different aspects of labour relations, with the Labour Relations Ordinance addressing broader labour rights and collective bargaining while the Contracts for Employment Outside Hong Kong Ordinance addresses employment contracts outside of Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06d23d2b54047f6e0d92f6798bcab7c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPRENTICE&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Apprentices are covered by a separate ordinance and have specific protections as outlined in section 2A of the main Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-786c67dfb1439b58fce397c3168c9e29</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;5(3) PROVISION&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 5(3) of the Ordinance has specific provisions that are excluded from certain applications as stated in other sections."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-786c67dfb1439b58fce397c3168c9e29</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;5(3) PROVISION&quot;" target="&quot;4 APRIL 1965&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The date marks an important exclusion for section 5(3), which does not apply to contracts made before this date."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-786c67dfb1439b58fce397c3168c9e29</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC SERVANT&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public servants are excluded from certain provisions of the main Ordinance, indicating a separate category within employment laws in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-786c67dfb1439b58fce397c3168c9e29</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHIEF EXECUTIVE'S DIRECTIONS&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers must comply with the Chief Executive's directions when exercising their powers under this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e804bc54b158b7b2826228aa81b5372e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DURATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;WORK DAY CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The duration agreement affects the calculation of work days for employees under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e804bc54b158b7b2826228aa81b5372e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;6-MONTH CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ordinance states that even if a contract is for more than one month, it should still be treated as a monthly renewable contract unless proven otherwise or specified in writing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e804bc54b158b7b2826228aa81b5372e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORMAT CHANGES (2015)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT TYPES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Format changes in 2015 affect how employment contract types, such as continuous contracts, are interpreted and applied."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e804bc54b158b7b2826228aa81b5372e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT AGREEMENT RENEWAL CONDITIONS&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers must adhere to the conditions for renewing employment agreements, which are outlined in this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e804bc54b158b7b2826228aa81b5372e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL DOCUMENT COMPLIANCE&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER'S DUTIES AND COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers must comply with legal document compliance when exercising their duties and functions as defined by this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e804bc54b158b7b2826228aa81b5372e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT RENEWAL MECHANISM&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT RENEWAL PROVISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employment contract renewal provisions dictate the mechanism for renewing contracts, especially continuous ones."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e804bc54b158b7b2826228aa81b5372e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL COMPLIANCE AND INTERPRETATION&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT DURATION REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal compliance and interpretation are crucial in understanding employment contract duration regulations as defined by this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e804bc54b158b7b2826228aa81b5372e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DURATION OF CONTRACTS OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;MANUAL WORKER CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The duration of contracts for manual workers is specified to be at least 6 months or the equivalent in working days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e3ced50112879a7d02f59ebfc4fcfea2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DURATION OF CONTRACTS OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES PER MONTH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Wages per month are calculated based on the agreed duration of the contract, particularly when it's deemed a monthly renewable contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e3ced50112879a7d02f59ebfc4fcfea2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MANUAL WORKER CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT TERMINATION NOTICE PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Manual worker contracts have specific provisions regarding notice periods for termination, which differ from general employment contracts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e3ced50112879a7d02f59ebfc4fcfea2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES PER MONTH&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT TERMINATION NOTICE PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The calculation of wages per month is relevant when determining the notice period for contract termination in certain cases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e3ced50112879a7d02f59ebfc4fcfea2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;通知期&quot;" target="&quot;7天&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"对于其他情况的通知期不得少于七天；如果该合同是根据第5条规定并可以逐月续约，则订明终止合同所需的通知期为议定期限，但不得少于七天。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75ec5cbcc26a69d2fa91ff3cd7cec100</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;通知期&quot;" target="&quot;第44號&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"由1971年第44号第2条修订了关于通知期的规定。对于根据第5条规定并可以逐月续约的合同，如果没有规定终止合同时的通知期，则不得少于一个月；如果该合同订明了终止合同时所需的通知期，则为议定期限，但不得少于七天。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75ec5cbcc26a69d2fa91ff3cd7cec100</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;通知期&quot;" target="&quot;第41D條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据第(2A)款的规定，在不损害第41D条的条件下，雇员根据第41AA条规定有权享有的年假不应计算在终止雇佣合同所需的通知期内。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75ec5cbcc26a69d2fa91ff3cd7cec100</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;通知期&quot;" target="&quot;第12條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据第(2B)款的规定，在不损害第41D条的条件下，女性雇员根据第12条规定有权享有的产假不应计算在终止雇佣合同所需的通知期内。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75ec5cbcc26a69d2fa91ff3cd7cec100</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;通知期&quot;" target="&quot;第6條終止合約的通知&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"按照第6条规定给予适当通知后，终止合同的一方需在通知期内遵守规定。否则将承担相应的责任和后果。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd681eafea885afa3c9b815543ffaba0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;通知期&quot;" target="&quot;第7條計算該僱員所賺取的工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"在通知期内，按照第7条规定计算该雇员所赚取的工资是确定终止合同一方需支付款项的重要依据之一。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd681eafea885afa3c9b815543ffaba0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;通知期&quot;" target="&quot;的通知期&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"如雇员与雇主双方议定较短的通知期，则不在此限，表明了通知期可以灵活调整。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-652fc2f400d124ee9e24d4406d85cc0f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;試用性質&quot;" target="&quot;僱傭合約&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"如果劳动合同明确规定为试用性质，则可以在首个月内随时终止该合同，无需给予通知或代通知金。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75ec5cbcc26a69d2fa91ff3cd7cec100</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱傭合約&quot;" target="&quot;首個月內隨時終止該合約,無須給予通知或代通知金&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"任何一方可以在该雇用的首个月中随时终止该合同，无需给予通知或代通知金。这适用于明确规定为试用性质的劳动合同。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75ec5cbcc26a69d2fa91ff3cd7cec100</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱傭合約&quot;" target="&quot;部分年終酬金&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"部分年終酬金的支付與僱傭合約相關,根据合同条款确定或推定。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3b7546d4e6b089b21f7a1b413d4f879c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱傭合約&quot;" target="&quot;酬金期&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"僱傭合約中指明了部分年終酬金的支付日期或推定方式,与酬金期间相关联。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3b7546d4e6b089b21f7a1b413d4f879c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱傭合約&quot;" target="&quot;工資及其他款項&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據僱員的僱傭合約應付予僱員的任何工資及其他款項是終止僱傭金的一部分。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c82c895f7b30d4831c428126a0af9486</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱傭合約&quot;" target="&quot;疾病假&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"即使僱傭合約已告終止,僱主仍須按僱員根據第(4)款有權獲得疾病的病假日總數,將疾病津貼付給該僱員。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61c622614f8a7b3173a59e39171f674c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱傭合約&quot;" target="&quot;41EA. 禁止將某些條文列入僱傭合約的規定&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"雇员合同中不得包含影响第41E(2)条适用性的条款，否则无效。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-285c049da04e797b33870a3a643d86c9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱傭合約&quot;" target="&quot;工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"工资支付规则和标准在雇佣合同中有明确规定。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-285c049da04e797b33870a3a643d86c9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱傭合約&quot;" target="&quot;YAA. 在某些情況下,酬金或利益或權益須扣除長期服務金的款額&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employment contract is relevant to YAA as it defines conditions under which gratuities or benefits can affect long service payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-233de206d4d440690ca3d19bf8ddb77c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱傭合約&quot;" target="&quot;按服務年資支付的酬金&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employment contract specifies the conditions for entitlement to long service payments based on years of service."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-233de206d4d440690ca3d19bf8ddb77c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱傭合約&quot;" target="&quot;服務年資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"僱傭合同的执行与服务年限相关,影响长期服务金计算的基础。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7fb9bafd0cba5b9cfa67282f7c70bf83</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;終止僱傭合約&quot;" target="&quot;第41AA條有權享有的年假&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据第(2A)款的规定，在不损害第41D条的条件下，雇员根据第41AA条规定有权享有的年假不应计算在终止雇佣合同所需的通知期内。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75ec5cbcc26a69d2fa91ff3cd7cec100</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;終止僱傭合約&quot;" target="&quot;第41D條的規定&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据(2A)和(2B)款的规定，在不损害第41D条的情况下，年假和产假不应计算在终止雇佣合同所需的通知期内。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75ec5cbcc26a69d2fa91ff3cd7cec100</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;終止僱傭合約&quot;" target="&quot;第31L(1)條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據第31L(1)條規定，已故僱主死亡視為終止原僱傭關係，但某些情況下僱員不受影響。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cad6d0a2eed4fbaf59a6253fe84df6ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;終止僱傭合約&quot;" target="&quot;4個星期內生效(視屬何情況而定)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據第31L(1)條規定，在某些情況下，續訂或重新聘用合同在四個星期内生效不視為解僱。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cad6d0a2eed4fbaf59a6253fe84df6ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;終止僱傭合約&quot;" target="&quot;僱主死亡&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"已故僱主的死亡視同終止原僱傭關係，但某些情況下可續訂或重新聘用以避免解僱。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cad6d0a2eed4fbaf59a6253fe84df6ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;女性僱員&quot;" target="&quot;預計分娩日期&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據預計分娩日期可以確定產假的一部分開始時間。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-eb1fa32929a7020d65f293e8c9d7dd58</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;女性僱員&quot;" target="&quot;連續性合约&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據连续性合约受僱的女性员工有权享有产假。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-eb1fa32929a7020d65f293e8c9d7dd58</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;女性僱員&quot;" target="&quot;醫生證明書&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"女性僱員需要出示醫生證明書來確認懷孕狀態。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb31bef1e8dd24810a075920d4fb5602</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;女性僱員&quot;" target="&quot;僱主&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"两者之间存在雇佣关系，并且涉及产假、假期等福利待遇的具体条款和支付方式。"&lt;SEP&gt;"女性僱員"与"僱主"之间存在雇佣关系，涉及薪酬和假期安排。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTIFICATION PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT can be terminated through NOTIFICATION PERIOD as specified by law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8e6874393fbe0406a4a2ae55efe312e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTIFICATION PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;7 DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A minimum of 7 days is required for the NOTIFICATION PERIOD according to certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8e6874393fbe0406a4a2ae55efe312e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTIFICATION PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;MONTH (MONTH)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MONTH period is defined in relation to the NOTIFICATION PERIOD, starting from either the date of employment or notification issuance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8e6874393fbe0406a4a2ae55efe312e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TERMINATION BY NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Termination by NOTICE can occur under specific conditions outlined for CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8e6874393fbe0406a4a2ae55efe312e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TERMINATION OF CONTRACT BY NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The termination of a contract can be initiated through notice given to another party under a Contract of Employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c72195a1e02c5898f4f5f3e8dd2e1df3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TERMINATION OF CONTRACT BY NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Annual leave is excluded from the length of notice required to terminate a contract under Subsection (2A)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c72195a1e02c5898f4f5f3e8dd2e1df3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TERMINATION OF CONTRACT BY NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maternity leave is also excluded from the length of notice required to terminate a contract under Subsection (2B)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c72195a1e02c5898f4f5f3e8dd2e1df3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (2), (2A), (2B), (3) AND (3A)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 15, SECTION 33, SECTION 41D, SECTION 41AA, SECTION 41, SECTION 48 OF 1984, SECTION 53 OF 1990, AND SECTION 55 OF 1987&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsections provide specific details on the notice period for terminating a Contract of Employment as governed by these sections."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c72195a1e02c5898f4f5f3e8dd2e1df3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The notice period for terminating a contract of employment can vary based on probationary status and specific agreements within the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f355da3b0eddd390953ffae58fee2099</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES (月)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of a 'month' is defined for purposes related to both notice periods and wage calculations within contracts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f355da3b0eddd390953ffae58fee2099</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Notice period is a critical component of employment contract terms affecting termination procedures and obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;AN EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An AN EMPLOYEE who leaves the service before the expiration of NOTICE PERIOD without consent or payment may not be entitled to remedies under this Part."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9e5f55eef00b5211e8c9c5c06c4bde96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYEE leaves service before the expiration of the NOTICE PERIOD unless with prior consent or payment in lieu as per sections 7 and 6."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9ddecf99bc0bca06387d96224afeaf4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES (月)&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maternity leave is included in the definition of wages, as it pertains to payments made during such a period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f355da3b0eddd390953ffae58fee2099</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEAVE WITH THE AGREEMENT OF HIS EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"工資还包括雇主同意的情况下，员工休假所得的补偿。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8625c1304f36a12d07cc0b6f8faf08b2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NORMAL WORKING DAY ON WHICH THE EMPLOYEE IS NOT PROVIDED WITH WORK&quot;" target="&quot;工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"正常工作日未提供工作的工资计算在内。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8625c1304f36a12d07cc0b6f8faf08b2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DAY OF ABSENCE FROM WORK DUE TO TEMPORARY INCAPACITY FOR WHICH COMPENSATION IS PAYABLE UNDER SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"因暂时丧失工作能力而休假的工资补偿计算在内。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8625c1304f36a12d07cc0b6f8faf08b2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DAY OF ABSENCE FROM WORK DUE TO TEMPORARY INCAPACITY FOR WHICH COMPENSATION IS PAYABLE UNDER SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;AVERAGE MONTHLY WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Days of absence due to temporary incapacity are included in the average monthly wage calculation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0a63ef432e83e1ac4184a66b9247423f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DAY OF ABSENCE FROM WORK DUE TO TEMPORARY INCAPACITY FOR WHICH COMPENSATION IS PAYABLE UNDER SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE, PATERNITY LEAVE, REST DAY, SICKNESS DAY, HOLIDAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE TAKEN BY THE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both types of leave are included in the calculation of average monthly wages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0a63ef432e83e1ac4184a66b9247423f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DAY OF ABSENCE FROM WORK DUE TO TEMPORARY INCAPACITY FOR WHICH COMPENSATION IS PAYABLE UNDER SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;LEAVE TAKEN BY THE EMPLOYEE WITH THE AGREEMENT OF THE EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both types of leave are included in the calculation of average monthly wages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0a63ef432e83e1ac4184a66b9247423f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DAY OF ABSENCE FROM WORK DUE TO TEMPORARY INCAPACITY FOR WHICH COMPENSATION IS PAYABLE UNDER SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;NORMAL WORKING DAY ON WHICH THE EMPLOYEE IS NOT PROVIDED WITH WORK BY THE EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both types of leave are included in the calculation of average monthly wages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0a63ef432e83e1ac4184a66b9247423f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TERMINATION WITHOUT NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"劳动合同的一方可以在任何时间通过同意支付另一方一定金额来无通知终止合同。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8625c1304f36a12d07cc0b6f8faf08b2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TERMINATION WITHOUT NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;FRAUDULENT OR DISLOYAL BEHAVIOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Termination without notice can be lawful due to fraudulent or disloyal behavior as per SECTION 11(2)(a)(iii)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 6&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE TERMINATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The termination agreement is based on provisions outlined in SECTION 6 regarding notice periods and compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 6&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 6.2(1A)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"SECTION 6.2(1A) is a subsection of SECTION 6, and its effect extends beyond the years of service for which severance payment was made."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8cb52dd4a9b2981de387c70ee06f029</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 6&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31J&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"SECTION 31J provides context for changes in business ownership and its effect on employment contracts, which is relevant to SECTION 6's amendments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8cb52dd4a9b2981de387c70ee06f029</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 15&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 33&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sections 15 and 33 provide exceptions or conditions that affect the general rule stated in SECTION 6."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 15&quot;" target="&quot;DIVISION 3 — CERTAIN PROVISIONS IN CONSTRUCTION CONTRACTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 15 limits the latest date by which progress payments are required to be paid, as part of Division 3 in construction contracts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ad2f770d3edd7fc8b6985f3040077779</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 33&quot;" target="&quot;PROCEEDINGS TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"SECTION 33 can affect the PROCEEDINGS TERMINATION by determining jurisdiction over a payment dispute."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f4f0cfcab0e9f6d5a958dc7286fe8aad</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 33&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 33 determines jurisdiction to decide PAYMENT DISPUTES, impacting ADJUDICATOR's fees and expenses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e089cfc832db9c43bb24baa7baf3ed42</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE TERMINATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The agreement takes into account maternity leave, which is a factor when calculating termination compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE TERMINATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;REST DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rest days are excluded from wage calculations when determining termination compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE TERMINATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;HOLIDAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Holiday or annual leave is not included when calculating wages for termination compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE TERMINATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPORARY INCAPACITY COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Temporary incapacity, if compensated under the Employees' Compensation Ordinance (Cap. 282), does not affect wage calculations for termination compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE TERMINATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ordinance provides the basis for temporary incapacity compensation, which is excluded from wage calculations in termination agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-390c9cace3f2a3a2e290c01be307700f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT PERIOD WITHOUT FULL WAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employment period without full wage includes rest days where no work is provided to the employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSTITUTED HOLIDAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Substituted holidays are also considered in addition to rest days, ensuring employee benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0aed3ae0b98488b1b913e6b49db19fee</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMERGENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"EMERGENCIES can override the REST DAY if necessary due to machine breakdown or unforeseen accidents. The employer must provide an alternative rest day within 30 days."&lt;SEP&gt;"EMERGENCIES can override the REST DAY if necessary due to machine breakdown or unforeseen accidents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-393f577c90dd494cee38d1bc9bc80592</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY&quot;" target="&quot;MACHINERY OR PLANT BREAKDOWN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An unforeseen machinery or plant breakdown can override an employee's right to their rest day as per legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6511dbd5eb2121ae41cf477a6c2b2884</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL BONUS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal provisions ensure that if an employee works on their rest day for any reason, they are entitled to receive an annual bonus as part of compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6511dbd5eb2121ae41cf477a6c2b2884</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A contract of employment may end on a REST DAY without being considered dismissal if renewed or re-engaged immediately after."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ccf624f83121089caf9f8fb044043303</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY&quot;" target="&quot;NORMAL WORKING DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rest day is excluded from the count of normal working days for determining if an employee has been laid off."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2138132720286ddae5a4634e3cd8c8f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY&quot;" target="&quot;BAA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rest day is part of the types of leaves considered in calculating wages according to BAA."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0fef56ddac89c58276c95d49a4ad2fde</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES EARNED BY THE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rest day days are included in the wage calculations for determining holiday pay rates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9d14b62c50b2a0a92ac73c8ef0642fe9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A rest day falling within a period of annual leave is counted as part of the annual leave, and another rest day or holiday will be substituted."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b63d3371d1b762c2013adc08da9c549f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY&quot;" target="&quot;NORMAL WORKING DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rest day refers to days when no work is provided on normal working days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY&quot;" target="&quot;HOLIDAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Holiday or annual leave and rest day both refer to days when no work is provided on normal working days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees are entitled to rest days which employers must grant, failing which an offence is committed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-33a64188afa193f5265ae78f3b8acbe6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOLIDAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Holiday or annual leave is related to temporary incapacity for which compensation may be payable under the Employees' Compensation Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOLIDAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;NORMAL WORKING DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Holiday or annual leave is a type of day when no work is provided on normal working days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOLIDAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Holiday or annual leave can be a benefit covered under the employment contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HOLIDAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT STOP DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Holiday or annual leave can be taken up to and including the employment stop date."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (1) OF SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (1) is part of Section 10, defining the conditions for temporary incapacity compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-40165e3c59ec939d934c64dcd17fd402</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (1B) OF SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (1B) provides clarification for the calculation of wages under Subsection (1)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-40165e3c59ec939d934c64dcd17fd402</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (1C) OF SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (1C) further clarifies the application of Subsection (1B)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-40165e3c59ec939d934c64dcd17fd402</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (1D) OF SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (1D) provides an alternative method for calculating wages when the standard method is impracticable under Subsection (1)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-40165e3c59ec939d934c64dcd17fd402</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 6 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (1) OF SECTION 6 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (1) is part of Section 6, defining the term 'wages'."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-40165e3c59ec939d934c64dcd17fd402</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 6 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (4) OF SECTION 6 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (4) provides an exception to the general definition of 'wages' under Subsection (1)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-40165e3c59ec939d934c64dcd17fd402</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 6 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (1A), (1B), (1C), AND (1D) OF SECTION 6 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsections (1A)-(1D) provide detailed definitions and clarifications for the term 'wages'."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-40165e3c59ec939d934c64dcd17fd402</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (4) OF SECTION 6 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (1A), (1B), (1C), AND (1D) OF SECTION 6 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (4) interacts with Subsections (1A)-(1D) to provide a comprehensive definition of 'wages'."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-40165e3c59ec939d934c64dcd17fd402</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OVERTIME PAY OF A CONSTANT CHARACTER OR THE MONTHLY AVERAGE OF WHICH OVER A PERIOD OF 12 MONTHS (OR IF NOT APPLICABLE, SUCH SHORTER PERIOD OF EMPLOYMENT) IMMEDIATELY PRECEDING THE DATE ON WHICH THE TERMINATION TAKES EFFECT IS EQUIVALENT TO OR EXCEEDS 20% OF HIS MONTHLY AVERAGE WAGES DURING THE SAME PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"This overtime pay is included in the definition of 'wages' as per the Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e220e0c7587651abe976f081881efeb5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱傭合約的任何一方&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ordinance applies to both parties of an employment contract regarding notice and termination rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e220e0c7587651abe976f081881efeb5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第6(2)、(3)或(3A)條的規定&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"These provisions are part of the Ordinance that governs notice requirements for certain terminations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e220e0c7587651abe976f081881efeb5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;代通知金&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ordinance includes provisions related to 'payment in lieu of notice' as a form of compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e220e0c7587651abe976f081881efeb5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;代通知金&quot;" target="&quot;僱主&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"在沒有給予妥當通知而解僱的情況下,根據第II部須支付的任何代通知金是終止僱傭金的一部份。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c82c895f7b30d4831c428126a0af9486</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;代通知金&quot;" target="&quot;原僱主&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"原僱主可以使用代通知金终止与雇员的雇佣合同,但不影响连续性计算规则。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-edb26226d8073f24c3695c26d7ad7c24</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第9、10或11(2)條&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"These clauses are part of the Ordinance that deal with termination without notice or payment in lieu."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e220e0c7587651abe976f081881efeb5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;不當地終止合約的損害賠償&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ordinance includes provisions for compensation when a contract is terminated improperly, as per section 8A."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e220e0c7587651abe976f081881efeb5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第6條&quot;" target="&quot;終止合約的一方&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"按照第6條给予适当通知的终止合同一方需要支付款项。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd681eafea885afa3c9b815543ffaba0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第7條&quot;" target="&quot;對方&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据第7条计算该雇员所赚取的工资，对方有权获得相应的补偿款额。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd681eafea885afa3c9b815543ffaba0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;終止合約的一方&quot;" target="&quot;對方&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"终止合同一方需向另一方支付款项以弥补因未按照第6或7条规定而提前终止合同造成的损失。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd681eafea885afa3c9b815543ffaba0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;終止合約的一方&quot;" target="&quot;工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据第7条计算的工资金额是终止合同一方需要支付给对方的补偿款额的一部分。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd681eafea885afa3c9b815543ffaba0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;對方&quot;" target="&quot;終止合約日期&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"终止合同的一方需根据合同终止日期计算应支付给对方的款项金额。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd681eafea885afa3c9b815543ffaba0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第9條&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"第9条补充或修订了关于雇佣合约的相关条款，适用于劳动合同的解除。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd681eafea885afa3c9b815543ffaba0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第9條&quot;" target="&quot;終止該合約&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據第9條,可以終止僱傭合約。除非相反證明成立,否則須視僱主為並非按照第9條終止該合約。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61c622614f8a7b3173a59e39171f674c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2007年第7號第4條&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"2007年修订的条款补充或修改了雇佣合约的相关内容，适用于劳动合同解除的情况。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd681eafea885afa3c9b815543ffaba0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;1975年第14號第2條&quot;" target="&quot;DAMAGES FOR WRONGFUL TERMINATION OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"1975年的规定增补了错误终止合同损害赔偿的内容，与后来的规定有联系。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd681eafea885afa3c9b815543ffaba0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 11(2)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 11(2) outlines specific scenarios affecting the employment contract's termination without proper notice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPER NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;NOTICE GIVEN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Proper Notice is a prerequisite for calculating sums and payments due upon termination as per SECTION 6."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE GIVEN&quot;" target="&quot;DAILY AVERAGE OR MONTHLY AVERAGE OF WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Daily or monthly wage averages are calculated based on the notice given, impacting termination payments as per SECTION 7."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DATE OF TERMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT OBLIGATIONS UPON TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The date of termination affects the calculation of payment obligations under SECTION 7."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TERMINATION OF THE CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employment Contract defines the conditions under which it can be terminated, including notice periods and payment obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TERMINATION OF THE CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;1965 C. 62 S. 13 U.K.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The contract's termination is governed by the legal provision specified in 1965 c. 62 s. 13 U.K."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE PARTICIPATION IN STRIKE&quot;" target="&quot;UNLAWFUL TERMINATION DUE TO STRIKE PARTICIPATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employee participation in a strike is not grounds for unlawful termination according to SECTION 9(2)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPEATED NEGLIGENCE&quot;" target="&quot;OTHER LAWFUL REASONS FOR TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Repeated negligence is one of the other lawful reasons for termination under common law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AMENDMENT OF SECTIONS&quot;" target="&quot;STATUTORY LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sections are subject to amendment according to statutory laws, impacting their interpretation and application in employment relations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-04cd6ed43a9db3f3a7e91d2bf134ecfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AN EMPLOYER MAY TERMINATE A CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT WITHOUT NOTICE OR PAYMENT IN LIEU&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE, IN RELATION TO HIS EMPLOYMENT— (I) WILFULLY DISOBEYS A LAWFUL AND REASONABLE ORDER; (II) MISCONDUCTS HIMSELF, SUCH CONDUCT BEING INCONSISTENT WITH THE DUE AND FAITHFUL DISCHARGE OF HIS DUTIES; (III) IS GUILTY OF FRAUD OR DISHONESTY; OR (IV) IS HABITUALLY NEGLECTFUL IN HIS DUTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer may terminate the contract without notice if an employee wilfully disobeys a lawful and reasonable order, misconducts himself, is guilty of fraud or dishonesty, or is habitually neglectful in his duties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b266f7ca95da19a8651bff75bd855a0c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AN EMPLOYER MAY TERMINATE A CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT WITHOUT NOTICE OR PAYMENT IN LIEU&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE CAN WITHOUT GIVING NOTIFICATION OR SUBSTITUTE NOTIFICATION MONEY TERMINMINATE THE EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT — (A) EMPLOYEE REASONABLY FEARS THAT HIS BODY WILL BE SUBJECTED TO VIOLENCE OR DISEASE HARM, AND THERE IS NO EXPLICIT OR IMPLIED TERM IN THE EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT INDICATING SUCH A SITUATION; (AA) EMPLOYEE — (I) HAS BEEN EMPLOYED FOR AT LEAST 5 YEARS UNDER THE TERMS OF THE CONTRACT; AND (II) RECEIVES A CERTIFICATE FROM A REGISTERED DOCTOR OR TRADITIONAL CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER AS SPECIFIED BY THE SECRETARY ACCORDING TO SECTION 49, STATING THAT HE IS PERMANENTLY UNSUITABLE FOR HIS POSITION DUE TO REASONS STATED IN THE CERTIFICATE.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer may terminate the contract without notice if an employee reasonably fears that his body will be subjected to violence or disease harm and there is no explicit or implied term in the employment contract indicating such a situation, or if he has been employed for at least 5 years under the terms of the contract and receives a certificate from a registered doctor stating that he is permanently unsuitable for his position due to reasons stated in the certificate."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b266f7ca95da19a8651bff75bd855a0c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE, IN RELATION TO HIS EMPLOYMENT— (I) WILFULLY DISOBEYS A LAWFUL AND REASONABLE ORDER; (II) MISCONDUCTS HIMSELF, SUCH CONDUCT BEING INCONSISTENT WITH THE DUE AND FAITHFUL DISCHARGE OF HIS DUTIES; (III) IS GUILTY OF FRAUD OR DISHONESTY; OR (IV) IS HABITUALLY NEGLECTFUL IN HIS DUTIES&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF CONTRACT WITHOUT NOTICE BY EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer may terminate the contract without notice if an employee wilfully disobeys a lawful and reasonable order, misconducts himself, is guilty of fraud or dishonesty, or is habitually neglectful in his duties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b266f7ca95da19a8651bff75bd855a0c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE FACT THAT AN EMPLOYEE TAKES PART IN A STRIKE DOES NOT ENTITLE HIS EMPLOYER TO TERMINATE UNDER SUBSECTION (1) THE EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT.&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF CONTRACT WITHOUT NOTICE BY EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer may not terminate the contract without notice if an employee takes part in a strike, even though it is under subsection (1)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b266f7ca95da19a8651bff75bd855a0c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE CAN WITHOUT GIVING NOTIFICATION OR SUBSTITUTE NOTIFICATION MONEY TERMINATE THE EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT — (A) EMPLOYEE REASONABLY FEARS THAT HIS BODY WILL BE SUBJECTED TO VIOLENCE OR DISEASE HARM, AND THERE IS NO EXPLICIT OR IMPLIED TERM IN THE EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT INDICATING SUCH A SITUATION; (AA) EMPLOYEE — (I) HAS BEEN EMPLOYED FOR AT LEAST 5 YEARS UNDER THE TERMS OF THE CONTRACT; AND (II) RECEIVES A CERTIFICATE FROM A REGISTERED DOCTOR OR TRADITIONAL CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER AS SPECIFIED BY THE SECRETARY ACCORDING TO SECTION 49, STATING THAT HE IS PERMANENTLY UNSUITABLE FOR HIS POSITION DUE TO REASONS STATED IN THE CERTIFICATE.&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF CONTRACT WITHOUT NOTICE BY EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer may terminate the contract without notice if an employee reasonably fears that his body will be subjected to violence or disease harm and there is no explicit or implied term in the employment contract indicating such a situation, or if he has been employed for at least 5 years under the terms of the contract and receives a certificate from a registered doctor stating that he is permanently unsuitable for his position due to reasons stated in the certificate."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b266f7ca95da19a8651bff75bd855a0c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TERMINATION OF CONTRACT WITHOUT NOTICE BY EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;THE FACT THAT AN EMPLOYEE TAKES PART IN A STRIKE DOES NOT ENTITLE HIS EMPLOYER TO TERMINATE UNDER SUBSECTION (1) THE EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT.&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The fact that an employee takes part in a strike does not entitle his employer to terminate under subsection (1) the employee's contract of employment, but it is still within the scope of termination without notice by the employer for other reasons."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b266f7ca95da19a8651bff75bd855a0c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PHYSICAL DANGER BY VIOLENCE OR DISEASE&quot;" target="&quot;ILL-TREATMENT BY EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both physical danger and ill-treatment can serve as grounds for terminating a contract of employment without notice, indicating overlapping reasons for termination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-515a3738f6ebf19e3d7fa78e01d28be6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PHYSICAL DANGER BY VIOLENCE OR DISEASE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Physical danger or disease can be a reason to terminate the contract of employment without prior notice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-515a3738f6ebf19e3d7fa78e01d28be6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ILL-TREATMENT BY EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Ill-treatment by an employer is another valid ground for terminating a contract of employment without notice, paralleling physical danger or disease as reasons for termination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-515a3738f6ebf19e3d7fa78e01d28be6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 7 TERMINATION CLAUSE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT TERMINATION WITHOUT NOTICE OR PAYMENT IN LIEU OF NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The clause specifies conditions for terminating an employment contract without notice or payment in lieu of notice based on common law principles."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2554ffe0d55bbe29aef6808731a595f2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 23 WAGES PAYMENT CLAUSE&quot;" target="&quot;14-DAY SUSPENSION CLAUSE FOR EMPLOYERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 23's provisions about wage payments can indirectly influence the suspension clause by setting a timeframe for payment, which may affect an employer’s decision to suspend."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2554ffe0d55bbe29aef6808731a595f2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第9條終止�ORDINATES合約&quot;" target="&quot;SUSPENSION FROM EMPLOYMENT IN CERTAIN CASES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"兩者都涉及僱傭合同中的暫停和終止問題,前者是暫停措施,後者則是終止原因。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-be5f720af1dc189f9088eb832b2b0cfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第9條終止�ORDINATES合約&quot;" target="&quot;僱主&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據特定原因,僱主可以終止僱傭合約,這可能導致僱員被暫停僱用或其他相關措施。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-be5f720af1dc189f9088eb832b2b0cfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;刑事检控&quot;" target="&quot;SUSPENSION FROM EMPLOYMENT IN CERTAIN CASES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"僱員因僱傭引起的事宜遭刑事檢控時,可能導致其被暫停僱用。這兩者都與僱傭合同的特殊情況有關。"&lt;SEP&gt;"僱員因僱傭引起的事宜遭刑事檢控時,可能導致其被暫停僱用。這關係到合同中的特殊情況和法律程序的結果。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-be5f720af1dc189f9088eb832b2b0cfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUSPENSION FROM EMPLOYMENT IN CERTAIN CASES&quot;" target="&quot;第9條終止僱傭合約&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"兩者都涉及僱傭合同的終止或暫停,前者是終止原因,後者則是暫停措施。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-be5f720af1dc189f9088eb832b2b0cfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUSPENSION FROM EMPLOYMENT IN CERTAIN CASES&quot;" target="&quot;僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"某些特定情況下,僱主可以根據僱傭合約暫停僱用僱員。這關係到僱員的行為和合同終止的可能性。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-be5f720af1dc189f9088eb832b2b0cfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUSPENSION FROM EMPLOYMENT IN CERTAIN CASES&quot;" target="&quot;僱主&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"僱主有權在特定情況下無需通知或支付代通知金而暫停僱用僱員,這關係到僱傭合同的特殊條款。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-be5f720af1dc189f9088eb832b2b0cfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LAY-OFF&quot;" target="&quot;NORMAL WORKING DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Normal working days are excluded from the count when determining if an employee is laid off due to reasons other than those specified in 1A, such as lock-out by employer or statutory holidays."&lt;SEP&gt;"The number of normal working days is a factor in determining the maximum period for which an employee can be laid off, as specified by law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-098ca6bfb60006d76569bead63917ebd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2138132720286ddae5a4634e3cd8c8f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LAY-OFF&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Lay-off can result in no severance payment, but this does not break the continuity of employment contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2138132720286ddae5a4634e3cd8c8f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NORMAL WORKING DAYS&quot;" target="&quot;LOCK-OUT BY EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Lock-out by employer does not count towards normal working days when determining lay-off status."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2138132720286ddae5a4634e3cd8c8f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NORMAL WORKING DAYS&quot;" target="&quot;DAY OF ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Day of annual leave is excluded from the count of normal working days for determining if an employee has been laid off."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2138132720286ddae5a4634e3cd8c8f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;PROPORTION OF THE END OF YEAR PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'proportion of the end of year payment' is defined based on calculations related to 'end of year payment'."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb1b0eee63da6475bd592efac352092a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;LUNAR YEAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of 'lunar year' provides context for when an 'end of year payment' might be made, typically at the end of a lunar calendar year."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb1b0eee63da6475bd592efac352092a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both terms are related as they both pertain to financial compensation, with wages including various types of payments such as end-of-year payments under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb1b0eee63da6475bd592efac352092a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;THIRTEENTH MONTH PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"THIRTEenth month payment is a type of END OF YEAR PAYMENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;FOURTEENTH MONTH PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"FOURTEENTh month payment is another variant of END OF YEAR PAYMENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;DOUBLE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"DOUBLE PAY can be considered as a form of END OF YEAR PAYMENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;END OF YEAR BONUS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"END OF YEAR BONUS is also an example of END OF YEAR PAYMENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;GRATUITOUS NATURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"END OF YEAR PAYMENT does not include payments of a gratuitous nature."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;DISCRETIONARY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"END OF YEAR PAYMENT is not payable at the discretion of the employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The END OF YEAR PAYMENT is determined by the terms of the CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT."&lt;SEP&gt;"The end of year payment's due date is specified in the contract of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-adfd6c1ac1062c58ce3404e61a7b9509&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43b4560ca9a773332d0b2bf256551f4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;SAME EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An end-of-year payment is tied to continuous employment under the same employer for a full payment period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a1bb383ea19375cfe6d50e66dce88dd1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;PROFIT CALCULATION DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The end-of-year payment may be calculated based on a profit calculation date if specified in the employment contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a1bb383ea19375cfe6d50e66dce88dd1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;PROFITS OF THE EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">11.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer's profits affect the calculation and timing of certain end of year payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"For some end of year payments, their calculation depends on the employer's profits ascertained at a certain time."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-43b4560ca9a773332d0b2bf256551f4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYEE is guaranteed payment at the end of the year regardless of whether or not they worked on their rest days due to unforeseen circumstances or voluntary work requests."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6511dbd5eb2121ae41cf477a6c2b2884</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LUNAR YEAR&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL END-OF-YEAR PAYMENT AMOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ANNUAL END-OF-YEAR PAYMENT AMOUNT is determined by a LUNAR YEAR if no other payment period is specified in the CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-adfd6c1ac1062c58ce3404e61a7b9509</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANNUAL BONUS PAYMENT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ANNUAL BONUS PAYMENT DATE depends on the employee's earnings in the 12 months prior to this date or a shorter period if employed for less than 12 months."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9fff8612fdefb52ed816a2d4502b87bc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANNUAL BONUS PAYMENT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE, PATERNITY LEAVE, REST DAY, SICK LEAVE, HOLIDAY, ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The calculation of the annual bonus payment date excludes periods during which an employee may be on leave such as maternity or sick leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9fff8612fdefb52ed816a2d4502b87bc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANNUAL BONUS PAYMENT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION FOR TEMPORARY LOSS OF WORK CAPACITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The compensation for temporary loss of work capacity is not considered in the calculation of the annual bonus payment date, ensuring that only actual earnings are used."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9fff8612fdefb52ed816a2d4502b87bc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE, PATERNITY LEAVE, REST DAY, SICK LEAVE, HOLIDAY, ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"These types of leave are not included in the calculation for determining an employee's monthly average earnings used to calculate annual bonuses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9fff8612fdefb52ed816a2d4502b87bc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE, PATERNITY LEAVE, REST DAY, SICK LEAVE, HOLIDAY, ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION FOR TEMPORARY LOSS OF WORK CAPACITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both types of leave and compensation for temporary loss of work capacity are excluded from the calculation to determine an employee's monthly average earnings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9fff8612fdefb52ed816a2d4502b87bc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPENSATION FOR TEMPORARY LOSS OF WORK CAPACITY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If an EMPLOYEE temporarily loses work capacity and is entitled to compensation under the Employment Ordinance, this period will not be included in calculating their monthly average earnings for bonus purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9fff8612fdefb52ed816a2d4502b87bc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRTEENTH MONTH PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;FOURTEENTH MONTH PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"FOURTEENTh month payment and THIRTEenth month payment are both types of END OF YEAR PAYMENTS, often used interchangeably or together."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRTEENTH MONTH PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;END OF YEAR BONUS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are types of annual payments or bonuses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FOURTEENTH MONTH PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;END OF YEAR BONUS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are types of annual payments or bonuses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOUBLE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;END OF YEAR BONUS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Double pay and end of year bonus both refer to additional compensation during the year."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR BONUS&quot;" target="&quot;PROPORTION OF THE END OF YEAR PAYMENT (部分年終酬金)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Proportion of end of year payment and bonus are related as both involve annual compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR BONUS&quot;" target="&quot;FULL MONTH'S WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Full month's wages are used as a reference point for calculating end of year bonuses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;12-MONTH PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;SAME INDUSTRY OR OCCUPATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 12-month period for calculating wages can refer to employees in the same industry or occupation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;12-MONTH PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;SAME REGION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 12-month period for calculation purposes may also consider employees from the same region."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c797912e21fe0e0cd4f06c78e6887b28</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LUNAR NEW YEAR'S DAY&quot;" target="&quot;CHINESE LUNAR YEAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Lunar New Year's Day is part of the Chinese lunar year."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LUNAR NEW YEAR'S DAY&quot;" target="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Lunar New Year's Day is a statutory holiday as defined by the relevant statutes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a1f7138b70fc0e22900e2a496ae78b23</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENT PERIOD (酬金期)&quot;" target="&quot;12 MONTHS IMMEDIATELY BEFORE THE DAY ON WHICH THE END OF YEAR PAYMENT BECOMES DUE TO THE EMPLOYEE UNDER SECTION 11E(1) OR (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The payment period is defined based on the 12 months before the due day for end of year payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENT PERIOD (酬金期)&quot;" target="&quot;IF THE EMPLOYEE HAS BEEN EMPLOYED BY THE EMPLOYER CONCERNED FOR A PERIOD SHORTER THAN 12 MONTHS IMMEDIATELY BEFORE THE DUE DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The payment period is adjusted if the employee has been employed for less than 12 months."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dbffac9fe29b467d2e151a6c12685697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEAVE TAKEN BY THE EMPLOYEE WITH THE AGREEMENT OF HIS EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPORARY INCAPACITY FOR WHICH COMPENSATION IS PAYABLE UNDER SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both can lead to a reduction in wages during normal working periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leaves taken with the agreement of the employer are not considered in calculating sickness allowance for temporary incapacity."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-84eda1f018d06824b6b2e9602213349f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5e29cfe8eddddf302f5a14076a67a7d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEAVE TAKEN BY THE EMPLOYEE WITH THE AGREEMENT OF HIS EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;NORMAL WORKING DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Normal working days are considered in calculating wages, but leaves taken with employer's agreement are disregarded."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e5e29cfe8eddddf302f5a14076a67a7d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEAVE TAKEN BY THE EMPLOYEE WITH THE AGREEMENT OF HIS EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE, PATERNITY LEAVE, REST DAY, SICKNESS DAY, HOLIDAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE TAKEN BY THE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"These leaves are both reasons for not being paid full wages during a normal working period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-84eda1f018d06824b6b2e9602213349f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEAVE TAKEN BY THE EMPLOYEE WITH THE AGREEMENT OF HIS EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;DAILY AVERAGE OF THE WAGES EARNED BY AN EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The daily wage calculation is affected when these leaves are considered."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-84eda1f018d06824b6b2e9602213349f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY INCAPACITY FOR WHICH COMPENSATION IS PAYABLE UNDER SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE, PATERNITY LEAVE, REST DAY, SICKNESS DAY, HOLIDAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE TAKEN BY THE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are reasons for not being paid full wages during a normal working period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-84eda1f018d06824b6b2e9602213349f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY INCAPACITY FOR WHICH COMPENSATION IS PAYABLE UNDER SECTION 10 OF THE EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;SAME TRADE OR OCCUPATION AND AT THE SAME WORK IN THE SAME DISTRICT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The wage calculation may refer to a person with similar employment status when calculating daily wages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-84eda1f018d06824b6b2e9602213349f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;工資 (WAGES)&quot;" target="&quot;第40条&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"According to the text, wages include the payments made by employers for a day on which an employee is entitled to take holiday."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6401943df7f64de20cb83d590f559418</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;工資 (WAGES)&quot;" target="&quot;第39(2)、(2A)或(3)条&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text mentions that wages include payments for holidays granted as an alternative holiday or substituted holiday under section 39(2), (2A) or (3)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6401943df7f64de20cb83d590f559418</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;工資 (WAGES)&quot;" target="&quot;第(2)款&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"According to the text, wages include payments for holidays granted as an alternative holiday or substituted holiday under section 39(2), (2A) or (3)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6401943df7f64de20cb83d590f559418</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE, PATERNITY LEAVE, REST DAY, SICKNESS DAY, HOLIDAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The compensation ordinance specifies that wages for certain leaves are not to be included in the monthly average wage calculation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-96a39d49ad205c3ba703c46117f4dff9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;SAME WORK, SAME TRADE OR OCCUPATION, SAME DISTRICT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">2.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The compensation ordinance provides a fallback method for calculating wages by referencing another person in the same work, trade or occupation within the same district."&lt;SEP&gt;"The compensation ordinance provides a method to calculate wages when direct data is not available through the use of comparable employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-96a39d49ad205c3ba703c46117f4dff9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;MONTHLY AVERAGE WAGE CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The compensation ordinance governs the rules for calculating the monthly average wage, including exclusions for specific leave periods and other conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-96a39d49ad205c3ba703c46117f4dff9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE, PATERNITY LEAVE, REST DAY, SICKNESS DAY, HOLIDAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT PERIOD CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">2.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Leaves and days are excluded from employment period calculations to ensure accurate wage averaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employment period calculation is adjusted to exclude certain leave periods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-96a39d49ad205c3ba703c46117f4dff9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE, PATERNITY LEAVE, REST DAY, SICKNESS DAY, HOLIDAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;MONTHLY AVERAGE WAGE CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The monthly average calculation disregards wages earned during certain leaves and days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-96a39d49ad205c3ba703c46117f4dff9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE, PATERNITY LEAVE, REST DAY, SICKNESS DAY, HOLIDAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;LEAVE WITH EMPLOYER AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are types of leave that can affect the calculation of average monthly wages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd469871354ff220088ed4c17affde45</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE, PATERNITY LEAVE, REST DAY, SICKNESS DAY, HOLIDAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPORARY INCAPACITY COMPENSATION UNDER EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are reasons for leave that can affect the calculation of average monthly wages and entitlements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd469871354ff220088ed4c17affde45</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT PERIOD CALCULATION&quot;" target="&quot;MONTHLY AVERAGE WAGE CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">2.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employment period calculations are foundational for determining the monthly average wage, especially when leaves and other conditions affect the total working days."&lt;SEP&gt;"In calculating the monthly average, periods of leave and other specified conditions must first determine the employment period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-96a39d49ad205c3ba703c46117f4dff9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MONTHLY AVERAGE WAGE CALCULATION&quot;" target="&quot;SAME WORK, SAME TRADE OR OCCUPATION, SAME DISTRICT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If it is impractical to calculate based on an employee's own wages, a comparison can be made with another person in the same work, trade or occupation within the same district."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-96a39d49ad205c3ba703c46117f4dff9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;推定每年酬金或年度花紅不屬賞贈性質和不是僅由僱主酌情付給的&quot; &quot;" target="&quot;THE AMOUNT MAY BE CALCULATED BY REFERENCE TO THE WAGES EARNED BY A PERSON WHO WAS EMPLOYED AT THE SAME WORK BY THE SAME EMPLOYER DURING THE PERIOD OF 12 MONTHS IMMEDIATELY BEFORE THE DUE DAY, OR, IF THERE IS NO SUCH PERSON, BY A PERSON WHO WAS EMPLOYED IN THE SAME TRADE OR OCCUPATION AND AT THE SAME WORK IN THE SAME DISTRICT DURING THE PERIOD OF 12 MONTHS IMMEDIATELY BEFORE THE DUE DAY&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"This clause provides the basis for calculating the amount, which is relevant to the presumption that annual payments or bonuses are not gratuitous and not at the employer's discretion unless otherwise stated in a contract." "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf0741b5ccf934d17c6a23c8ca19677d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;推定每年酬金或年度花紅不屬賞贈性質和不是僅由僱主酌情付給的&quot; &quot;" target="&quot;第(1)款不適用於在本條的生效日期前訂立的任何僱傭合約&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The presumption of non-gratuitous nature and employer's discretion does not apply to employment contracts made before the effective date as stated in subsection (2)." "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf0741b5ccf934d17c6a23c8ca19677d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;推定每年酬金或年度花紅不屬賞贈性質和不是僅由僱主酌情付給的&quot; &quot;" target="&quot;IT SHALL BE PRESUMED THAT AN ANNUAL PAYMENT OR ANNUAL BONUS IS NOT OF A GRATUITOUS NATURE AND IS NOT PAYABLE ONLY AT THE DISCRETION OF THE EMPLOYER UNLESS THERE IS A WRITTEN TERM OR CONDITION IN THE CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT TO THE CONTRARY&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"These two statements are essentially the same, both asserting that annual payments or bonuses are not gratuitous and not at employer's discretion unless otherwise stated in a contract." "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf0741b5ccf934d17c6a23c8ca19677d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第(1)款不適用於在本條的生效日期前訂立的任何僱傭合約&quot; &quot;" target="&quot;編輯附註:生效日期: 1997年6月27日&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The editorial note provides the effective date for subsection (2), which is relevant to its applicability as stated in subsection (1)." "&lt;SEP&gt;"The effective date of subsection (2) is specified in the editorial note, indicating when it comes into force." "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf0741b5ccf934d17c6a23c8ca19677d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;本部適用於該僱員&quot; &quot;" target="&quot;除有任何相反的協議及除第(2)款另有規定外,根據連續性合約受僱的僱員&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"This clause specifies the applicability of section 11B to employees under continuous contracts who are entitled to annual bonuses based on their employment contract terms." "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf0741b5ccf934d17c6a23c8ca19677d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL END-OF-YEAR PAYMENT AMOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ANNUAL END-OF-YEAR PAYMENT AMOUNT may be relevant to CONTINUOUS CONTRACT EMPLOYEE as it pertains to their employment terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-adfd6c1ac1062c58ce3404e61a7b9509</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;MAIN PROVISIONS FOR EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1983&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ordinance provides provisions for continuous contract employees, detailing their rights and benefits such as sick leave entitlements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-aca44109366b72f73416de7630e4bed5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AGREEMENT TO CONTRARY&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 11F PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Any AGREEMENT TO CONTRARY regarding SECTION 11F PAYMENT will be void according to subsection (2)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-adfd6c1ac1062c58ce3404e61a7b9509</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPORTION OF END-YEAR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PROPORTION OF END-YEAR PAYMENT may depend on the terms of the CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-adfd6c1ac1062c58ce3404e61a7b9509</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SAME EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;12 MONTHS IMMEDIATELY BEFORE THE DATE OF TERMINATION OF THE EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The same employer's wages are considered for the calculation of average monthly wage during a specific period before termination. If no such person exists, another similar employment can be used as reference."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART-YEAR BONUS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The part-year bonus is determined based on the employment contract terms and conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02218e873b9a55b35f3e34874d7090d6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART-YEAR BONUS&quot;" target="&quot;PROBATION PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"During a probation period, certain months are excluded from calculating the part-year bonus according to regulation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02218e873b9a55b35f3e34874d7090d6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROBATION PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employment contract may include terms for a probationary period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02218e873b9a55b35f3e34874d7090d6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROBATION PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;BONUS PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The bonus period may exclude a probationary period when calculating part-year bonuses according to regulation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02218e873b9a55b35f3e34874d7090d6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROBATION PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employee may be in a probationary period, affecting their eligibility and calculation of part-year bonuses according to regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02218e873b9a55b35f3e34874d7090d6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROBATION PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;PREGNANT EMPLOYEE'S EMPLOYMENT TERMINATION PROHIBITION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The prohibition includes exceptions related to the probation period of pregnant employees, showing an interaction between employment termination and probationary status."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5aaa252a172d6b006af917dc91a91759</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;1997 YEAR 74TH AMENDMENT&quot;" target="&quot;2001 YEAR 7TH AMENDMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both amendments modify the rules for employment contracts and part-year bonuses, with the latter amending specific clauses of the former."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02218e873b9a55b35f3e34874d7090d6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;部分年終酬金&quot;" target="&quot;酬金期&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"部分年終酬金与酬金期间相关,其计算依据为该期间内的服务时间比例。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3b7546d4e6b089b21f7a1b413d4f879c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT CALCULATION&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S PERIOD OF SERVICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The period of service is used in calculating the end-of-year payment. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d88cda6d2e850ba77bbd055819688849</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;END OF YEAR PAYMENT CALCULATION&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT PERIOD END DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The payment period end date influences when the proportion of the end-of-year payment becomes due. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d88cda6d2e850ba77bbd055819688849</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENT PERIOD END DATE&quot;" target="&quot;7 DAYS PAYMENT DEADLINE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Payments are to be made no later than 7 days after the specified day on the payment period end date. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d88cda6d2e850ba77bbd055819688849</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREGNANT EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A pregnant employee is entitled to maternity leave as per the provisions mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb4129e436da0578c032f036f81bf719</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREGNANT EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;14-WEEK CONTINUOUS PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A pregnant employee is eligible for a 14-week continuous period as part of her maternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb4129e436da0578c032f036f81bf719</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREGNANT EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;EXPECTED DATE OF CONFINEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The expected date of confinement influences when a pregnant employee can start her maternity leave, subject to employer agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bef47a255f1eda2d15380bce3341cd94</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREGNANT EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;MEDICAL CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A pregnant employee can provide a medical certificate to request accommodation from work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c53400793123be7f8846d77b56748e48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;14-WEEK CONTINUOUS PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maternity leave includes a 14-week continuous period from the date of confirmation of pregnancy."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb4129e436da0578c032f036f81bf719</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART III&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Part III deals with Maternity Protection, which includes provisions related to maternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb4129e436da0578c032f036f81bf719</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART III&quot;" target="&quot;ENTITLEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Entitlement includes maternity leave pay or sum payable under Part III."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1c30b39b26dc22df210f2ea63b93552</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;確實分娩日期&quot;" target="&quot;產假開始日期&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"產假的開始日期可以是預計分娩日期翌日或確切分娩日期,具體情況而定。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-eb1fa32929a7020d65f293e8c9d7dd58</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;產假開始日期&quot;" target="&quot;1997年第73號第3條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"1997年第73号第3条规定了产假开始的具体条件和时间。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-eb1fa32929a7020d65f293e8c9d7dd58</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;產假開始日期&quot;" target="&quot;2020年第13號第4條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"2020年第13号第4条规定了产假开始的替代计算方式。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-eb1fa32929a7020d65f293e8c9d7dd58</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;醫生證明書&quot;" target="&quot;懷孕或分娩引致疾病或無工作能力的另一期間&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"醫生證明書用於確認女性僱員因懷孕或分娩而導致無工作能力的情況。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-eb1fa32929a7020d65f293e8c9d7dd58</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;醫生證明書&quot;" target="&quot;註冊醫生、註冊中醫或註冊牙醫&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"簽發醫生證明書的人必須是註冊醫生、註冊中醫或註冊牙醫。他們認為僱員在某日因疾病或損傷而過去、目前或將來不適宜工作。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61c622614f8a7b3173a59e39171f674c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;1997年第73號第3條&quot;" target="&quot;1987年第55號第3條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"1997年的法例取代了1987年的部分規定。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb31bef1e8dd24810a075920d4fb5602</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">44.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A FEMALE EMPLOYEE is eligible to take MATERNITY LEAVE based on her pregnancy confirmation and intention communicated to the employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A FEMALE EMPLOYEE takes MATERNITY LEAVE, which affects her wages and compensation during that period."&lt;SEP&gt;"FEMALE EMPLOYEE has rights to MATERNITY LEAVE as per legal provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Female employees are entitled to maternity leave under a continuous contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"The FEMALE EMPLOYEE can take MATERNITY LEAVE under specific conditions outlined in the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5001d950d1e5de5921648ae860af7539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9112f21c7d8a89e9880b92acfce9ecd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505a565a05fcfbf53c86377d50356a49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d6f22e03ef794b224e1918ddd3fee77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8d3158e721c74f203da21b92ec49085</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 12AA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The actual date of confinement is determined under Section 12AA, which affects eligibility for maternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8d3158e721c74f203da21b92ec49085</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;MEDICAL CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A FEMALE EMPLOYEE must present a MEDICAL CERTIFICATE confirming her pregnancy before taking maternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-505a565a05fcfbf53c86377d50356a49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;PREGNANCY CONFIRMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PREGNANCY CONFIRMATION is necessary for a FEMALE EMPLOYEE to initiate the process of applying for MATERNITY LEAVE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-505a565a05fcfbf53c86377d50356a49</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Female employees have rights to receive wages during their maternity leave, subject to certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">25.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"FEMALE EMPLOYEE is entitled to receive MATERNITY LEAVE PAY according to the law."&lt;SEP&gt;"Female employees are entitled to maternity leave pay for 14 weeks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maternity Leave Pay is specifically related to the wages of a female employee during her maternity leave period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7d6f22e03ef794b224e1918ddd3fee77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4646eb80519916bd0464a8b522d48735&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5001d950d1e5de5921648ae860af7539</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEES COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employees' Compensation Ordinance applies to FEMALE EMPLOYEE specifically for certain leave periods, including maternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5001d950d1e5de5921648ae860af7539</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;SCHEDULE 1A&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Schedule 1A specifies the amount of maternity leave pay that an employer must provide."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78df2b99fcbe4aa2c71fdce1f79d338c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE IS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'employee' includes female employees who are protected by this legislation against unfair termination during pregnancy."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Female employees are subject to the terms of employment contract termination, including compensation for such terminations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4646eb80519916bd0464a8b522d48735</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE SICK LEAVE ENTITLEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The female employee is entitled to sick leave benefits under specific conditions, such as pregnancy and childbirth."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-635fb659aa7fe54dd44ec966f454cd08</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;33(5B) CLAUSE OF EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 2022&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 33(5B) clause of the Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 2022 concerns provisions for female employees regarding paid maternity check-up attendance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-60efa76430de6c8c3995f39eeee4cc13</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;PAID MATERNITY CHECK-UP ATTENDANCE CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PAID MATERNITY CHECK-UP ATTENDANCE CERTIFICATE is issued to FEMALE EMPLOYEES for their medical appointments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-60efa76430de6c8c3995f39eeee4cc13</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;THE 2020 AMENDMENT ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The FEMALE EMPLOYEE is subject to the provisions of THE 2020 AMENDMENT ORDINANCE regarding maternity leave and employment contract termination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7d6f22e03ef794b224e1918ddd3fee77</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 12AA&quot;" target="&quot;NOTICE UNDER SECTION 12(4) OR (5)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The female employee must give NOTICE under SECTION 12(4) or (5) as per the conditions set in SECTION 12AA."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-681c7e69874ff6c2cdf180f0fb0d44f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDICAL CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A MEDICAL CERTIFICATE is required to support a request for MATERNITY LEAVE, as specified by the employer's requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9112f21c7d8a89e9880b92acfce9ecd6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDICAL CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;15AA. PROHIBITION OF ASSIGNMENT OF HEAVY, HAZARDOUS OR HARMFUL WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"醫學證明在本條款中扮演關鍵角色，用於確認懷孕員工是否適合從事某些工作。這表明了對醫學意見的尊重和依賴。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8c6299301f5a875ef57ec9769c28d05e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDICAL CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A medical certificate from authorities serves as proof of the delivery and death status of the child, relevant to establishing paternity."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6320bd8af6a47ec4d774b02d5588447a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDICAL CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A medical certificate can be issued by a registered medical practitioner for employee fitness and sickness days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b89f7731524d41ce9b762132c808abd5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDICAL CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A medical certificate can be issued by a registered Chinese medicine practitioner for employee fitness and sickness days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b89f7731524d41ce9b762132c808abd5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDICAL CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;UNFIT FOR WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A medical certificate specifies the number of days an employee is unfit for work due to sickness or injury."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42671f6db02a812e702214c1753dfc91</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY OR HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rest days or holidays falling during maternity leave are counted as part of it, not giving rise to additional entitlements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bef47a255f1eda2d15380bce3341cd94</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY OR HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31T(1)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 31T defines circumstances where employment can be terminated, including on rest days or holidays."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6c8faaa89696bb97daf5c16e2354ab6f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY OR HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31T(2)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The termination of contracts due to rest day or holiday is covered under section 31T(2)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6c8faaa89696bb97daf5c16e2354ab6f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY OR HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31T OF 1988 S. 52&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rest days and holidays are considered in determining when a contract ends for purposes of dismissal under Section 31T."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY OR HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;AN EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If the RELEVANT DATE falls on a REST DAY OR HOLIDAY, it is considered as the next working day for certain provisions to take effect."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9e5f55eef00b5211e8c9c5c06c4bde96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAY OR HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A rest day or holiday within an annual leave period counts as part of the annual leave and another substitute is provided if necessary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e1ba134cba7bc0ad2b2ef34e757e78d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer agreement determines the payment for maternity leave and holiday pay in case no paid maternity leave is provided during holidays."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bef47a255f1eda2d15380bce3341cd94</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 12(2)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"According to SECTION 12(2)(A), an employer must provide MATERNITY LEAVE PAY for a female employee who meets specific criteria."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-681c7e69874ff6c2cdf180f0fb0d44f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;DAILY AVERAGE OF THE WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The daily average of the wages is used as a basis for calculating maternity leave pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5b551a4a483944d6cf3179909e4812f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 12(6), (7)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sections 12(6) and (7) are conditions that may affect the calculation or payment of maternity leave pay under Section 3A, 3B, and 3C."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5b551a4a483944d6cf3179909e4812f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 3E&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 3E provides an exception to the general rule for calculating maternity leave pay in Sections 3A, 3B, and 3C."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5b551a4a483944d6cf3179909e4812f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEES COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employees' Compensation Ordinance provides compensation that may overlap with Maternity Leave Pay, particularly for temporary incapacity."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5001d950d1e5de5921648ae860af7539</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maternity Leave Pay involves calculations based on Wages, particularly in determining daily averages and maximum amounts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5001d950d1e5de5921648ae860af7539</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;DISTRICT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maternity Leave Pay calculations may reference a person's employment in the same DISTRICT for determining daily wages averages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5001d950d1e5de5921648ae860af7539</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;LATTER PERIOD OF MATERNITY LEAVE (產假末段期間)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The amount of maternity leave pay may be reduced during the latter period of maternity leave, after applying subsection (3E)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78df2b99fcbe4aa2c71fdce1f79d338c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maternity leave pay is considered in calculating the compensation for employment contract termination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4646eb80519916bd0464a8b522d48735</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employees' Compensation Ordinance includes provisions related to maternity leave pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4646eb80519916bd0464a8b522d48735</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;MONTHLY AVERAGE OF WAGES EARNED BY THE EMPLOYEE DURING A PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The monthly average of wages earned by the employee is relevant to calculating maternity leave pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-47f5ddfc5b519fcf524c4d9bd233c4e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;SIN行&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maternity leave pay is relevant to the legal obligations described under '罪行' (Offences), specifically regarding payment requirements for maternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-47f5ddfc5b519fcf524c4d9bd233c4e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;产假&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maternity leave pay and 产假 are both related to the rights of female employees during pregnancy and childbirth, with legal obligations described under '罪行' (Offences)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-47f5ddfc5b519fcf524c4d9bd233c4e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner specifies the format for recording and paying maternity leave pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c7550fdff3623ae221e2d156f6ce5cf2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;15(2)条的規定&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 15(2) specifies conditions for paying maternity leave, impacting employers' obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c7550fdff3623ae221e2d156f6ce5cf2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;第15AA(2)條的規定&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner's determination under section 15AA(2) affects the payment of maternity leave according to specific rules."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c7550fdff3623ae221e2d156f6ce5cf2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"MATERNITY LEAVE PAY" is defined under the Employment Regulations, indicating its legal framework and restrictions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-885c65878619106b2d2b302114a64bb2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"COURT can award MATERNITY LEAVE PAY as a form of terminal payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES OR ANY OTHER SUM PAYABLE UNDER SECTION 23, 24 OR 25&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"These are both forms of compensation that might be awarded by the tribunal for different reasons."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6d4bd265e2aa3d3a8af55fbca1b13963</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;END OF YEAR PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are types of payments that might be part of an award in a tribunal case and can relate to employment rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6d4bd265e2aa3d3a8af55fbca1b13963</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;HOLIDAY PAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"All three are forms of pay or allowance related to employment contracts and employee benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-98d46f6e07563bbf79e567c647ecf4fc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;2007年第7號第17條增補&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The amendment in 2007 specifically mentions maternity leave pay as one of the types affected by this change."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-98d46f6e07563bbf79e567c647ecf4fc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;2020年第13號第13條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 2020年第13號第13條 (Amendment of Schedule 1A) defines the maximum amount for MATERNITY LEAVE PAY."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd0362fbf5661d142ff4aeefe27aea79</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;附表1A - MAXIMUM AMOUNT OF MATERNITY LEAVE PAY FOR LATTER PERIOD OF MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"附表1A specifies the maximum amount of MATERNITY LEAVE PAY for the latter period, directly related to the legal definition in 2020年第13號第13條."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd0362fbf5661d142ff4aeefe27aea79</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;THE 2020 AMENDMENT ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"MATERNITY LEAVE PAY is governed by THE 2020 AMENDMENT ORDINANCE, particularly for situations where the confinement occurs on or after the amendment date."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7d6f22e03ef794b224e1918ddd3fee77</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEES' LEAVE TYPES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The agreement covers the leave types that employees can take, such as maternity leave and sick leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd2478b6eecc304c9feadaf2ffde1109</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The agreement is related to the compensation ordinance which provides details on how compensation should be calculated for certain leaves or absences."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd2478b6eecc304c9feadaf2ffde1109</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;DAILY AVERAGE EARNINGS CALCULATION METHODOLOGY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The agreement and its related methodologies ensure that employers have clear guidelines on how to handle employee absences due to leave types, ensuring fair compensation practices."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd2478b6eecc304c9feadaf2ffde1109</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXPECTED DATE OF CONFINEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;DOCTORS' CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A doctor's certificate is required for determining the expected date of confinement and planning the commencement of maternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bef47a255f1eda2d15380bce3341cd94</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOCTORS' CERTIFICATES&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"DOCTORS' CERTIFICATES are required for various aspects related to MATERNITY LEAVE as per the regulations mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-911f250d278d47d4c7dfd5e35d124637</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MIDWIFE&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 8 REGISTRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Midwives are required to register under section 8 of the Midwives Registration Ordinance (Cap. 162). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MIDWIFE&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both registered medical practitioners and midwives can issue certain types of medical certificates, indicating a related professional capability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MIDWIFE&quot;" target="&quot;MIDWIVES REGISTRATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 162)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"This ordinance regulates the registration and status of midwives, who may also issue certain documents required by other ordinances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f11184ac38e9ff98017a8ef0f47064dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MIDWIFE&quot;" target="&quot;BIRTH CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A midwife, while primarily regulated by CAP. 162, may also be involved in issuing documents related to births under CAP. 174."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f11184ac38e9ff98017a8ef0f47064dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MIDWIFE&quot;" target="&quot;MEDICAL PROFESSIONAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both registered doctors and midwives fall under the broader category of medical professionals, though no direct relationship is specified between them. They may collaborate in providing care within a healthcare setting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Midwives, as a type of medical professional, offer specific healthcare services related to pregnancy and childbirth."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fcd2a26e931b9fa624c25b0caadbcdb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f158408c588106f3a0fd30a322902be</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MIDWIFE&quot;" target="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF ATTENDANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Midwives may be involved in issuing certificates related to pregnancy examinations, particularly when they conduct such exams as registered professionals."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fcd2a26e931b9fa624c25b0caadbcdb5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 12(4) OR (6)&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A medical certificate for the purposes of section 12(4) or (6) can be issued by a registered medical practitioner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;休息日&quot;" target="&quot;工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"正常工作日内不放休息日亦不会工作的日子通常无须支付工资。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;休息日&quot;" target="&quot;产假&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"两者都是休假类型，但计算每日平均款额时会被排除在外。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;休息日&quot;" target="&quot;罪行及罰則&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"未给雇员提供根据IV部应享有的休息日将构成犯罪。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f7b047f9f55a2ab249abdbcd1a65d36</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;病假日&quot;" target="&quot;工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"在员工因病请假的日子，雇主无需支付工资。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;病假日&quot;" target="&quot;产假&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"两者都是休假类型，但计算每日平均款额时会被排除在外。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;年假&quot;" target="&quot;工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"正常工作日内不放年假亦不会工作的日子通常无须支付工资。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;年假&quot;" target="&quot;产假&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"两者都是休假类型，但计算每日平均款额时会被排除在外。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;年假&quot;" target="&quot;僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"僱員有权在紧接与年假有关的假期年后12个月内享受并放取年假。"&lt;SEP&gt;"僱員有权选择放有薪年假或获得相应的补偿金。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-652fc2f400d124ee9e24d4406d85cc0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c777bc9929cfa20260878316c3ec4ad</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;年假&quot;" target="&quot;疾病或损伤&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据第(7)，在年假期间内，由于疾病或损伤以致完全丧失工作能力的期间不得计算为年假的一部分，除非该期间在年假期开始后方开始。这表明了年假不包括因病缺勤的时间。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-652fc2f400d124ee9e24d4406d85cc0f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;年假&quot;" target="&quot;僱主&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"僱主在未给予僱员年假期间继续雇佣该僱员,需支付补偿金或提供有薪假期。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c777bc9929cfa20260878316c3ec4ad</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;正常工作日&quot;" target="&quot;放取任何產假、休息日、病假日、假日或年假&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"女性僱員"可以选择不进行正常的工作，而是选择休假或者请假。</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;正常工作日&quot;" target="&quot;因正常工作日不獲其僱主提供工作&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"如果在正常的工作日内没有获得雇主提供的工作，则可能影响薪酬计算。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;正常工作日&quot;" target="&quot;《雇员补偿条例》(第282章)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据该条例，在任何正常工作日内未获雇主提供工作的期间以及因暂时丧失工作能力而缺勤的期间，工資不计算在内。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ab559340de48ae6d55e82984ae48a4f0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;正常工作日&quot;" target="&quot;工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"在正常工作日内提供给员工的工资是固定的，而在请假期间则不计入其中。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ab559340de48ae6d55e82984ae48a4f0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;正常工作日&quot;" target="&quot;平均工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"在正常工作日未獲付全部工資的情況下,不計入平均工資的計算中。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f8f159cb841c798f1b18dd22fda97160</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;正常工作日&quot;" target="&quot;《僱員補償條例》(第282章)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">3.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據該條例,僱員在正常工作日未獲付全部工資的情況下可獲得補償。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f8f159cb841c798f1b18dd22fda97160</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;正常工作日&quot;" target="&quot;僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">僱員在某些正常工作日不獲其僱主提供工作的期間可能會影響其薪酬計算方式。</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c14678de8548f803294fa05856c13dfc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;正常工作日&quot;" target="&quot;休息日、病假日、假日或年假&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"休息日、病假日、假日或年假和正常工作日在计算每日平均款额时不计入其中。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6957d2ae600df45cdcfeef087031ad45</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;正常工作日&quot;" target="&quot;暫時喪失工作能力而缺勤的日子&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"正常工作日与暂时丧失工作能力而缺勤的日子都不计算在内,以避免重复。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6957d2ae600df45cdcfeef087031ad45</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;緊接其產假開始日期之前的12個月期間&quot;" target="&quot;《僱員補償條例》(第282章)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据条例，产假薪酬是基于员工开始产假前的最近12个月内的平均工资计算得出。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;較短的期間&quot;" target="&quot;《僱員補償條例》(第282章)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"如果雇员在紧接其产假开始日期之前受雇于有关雇主一段短于12个月的时间，那么产假薪酬将基于该较短期间内的平均工资计算得出。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;不放產假亦不會工作&quot;" target="&quot;僱主通常無須就該日支付工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"如果员工在某天即使不放产假也不会工作的日子，雇主通常无需为其支付工资。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主通常無須就該日支付工資&quot;" target="&quot;放取任何產假、侍產假、休息日、病假日、假日或年假&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"这些假期通常是不计薪的，除非有特别规定。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-de9d7bf328eb68da98c29ac72b529085</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;产假&quot;" target="&quot;假日&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"两者都是休假类型，但计算每日平均款额时会被排除在外。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;产假薪酬&quot;" target="&quot;工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"产假期间的薪酬不计入正常工作日所赚取工资的一分数中，因此与工资有关联。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;产假薪酬&quot;" target="&quot;《僱員補償條例》(第282章)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"该条例详细规定了产假薪酬的计算方式和排除条款。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;12個月或較短的期間&quot;" target="&quot;同一僱主從事同樣工作的人&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"在同一期间内，相同工作的员工工资计算方法可能影响产假薪酬的确定。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;12個月或較短的期間&quot;" target="&quot;《僱員補償條例》(第282章)第10條會獲付補償&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"在计算补偿金额时，会考虑女性僱員在过去一年内所赚取工资的情况。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;正常工作日所賺取的數額的一個分數&quot;" target="&quot;《僱員補償條例》(第282章)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据条例规定，在计算每日平均款额时，某些期间内的工资不计入其中。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-56bc001544d5c8018d61bd84bcb83283</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;附表1A中的指明的款额&quot;" target="&quot;第3E条&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"第3E条规定了产假薪酬最高额度参照附表1A中明确规定的数额。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-752073f001b8e7d22967a0f26dd04e44</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;附表1A中的指明的款额&quot;" target="&quot;2007年第7号第6条增补&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"2007年对第7号第6条的修订增加了参考附表1A中明确规定的数额来计算产假薪酬。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-752073f001b8e7d22967a0f26dd04e44</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;附表1A中的指明的款额&quot;" target="&quot;2020年第13号第6条修訂&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"2020年对第13号第6条的修订进一步明确了参考附表1A中明确规定的数额来计算产假薪酬。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-752073f001b8e7d22967a0f26dd04e44</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;附表1A中的指明的款额&quot;" target="&quot;雇傭合約或任何其他協議&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"附表1A中明确规定的数额可能作为雇佣合同或其他协议条款的一部分来计算产假薪酬的具体金额。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-752073f001b8e7d22967a0f26dd04e44</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;1997年第73号第6条修訂&quot;" target="&quot;雇傭合約或任何其他協議&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"雇佣合同或其他协议中的条款可能影响根据修订后的第73号第6条规定应支付的产假薪酬的具体计算方式和金额。特别是关于未得雇主同意而在产假期间为另一雇主工作的情况下的权利丧失问题。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-752073f001b8e7d22967a0f26dd04e44</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2007年第7号第6条增补&quot;" target="&quot;雇傭合約或任何其他協議&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"雇佣合同或其他协议中的条款可能影响根据修订后的第7号第6条规定应支付的产假薪酬的具体计算方式和金额。特别是关于扣除已获款项的规定。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-752073f001b8e7d22967a0f26dd04e44</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2020年第13号第6条修訂&quot;" target="&quot;雇傭合約或任何其他協議&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"雇佣合同或其他协议中的条款可能影响根据修订后的第13号第6条规定应支付的产假薪酬的具体计算方式和金额。特别是关于扣除已获款项的规定。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-752073f001b8e7d22967a0f26dd04e44</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;雇傭合約或任何其他協議&quot;" target="&quot;第7号第6条修訂&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"雇佣合同或其他协议中的条款可能影响根据修订后的第7号第6条规定应支付的产假薪酬的具体计算方式和金额。"&lt;SEP&gt;"雇佣合同或其他协议中的条款可能影响根据修订后的第7号第6条规定应支付的产假薪酬的具体计算方式和金额，特别是关于扣除已获款项的规定。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-752073f001b8e7d22967a0f26dd04e44</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 12(2)(A)&quot;" target="&quot;40 WEEKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The condition of having been employed for at least 40 weeks is specified in SECTION 12(2)(A) to qualify for maternity leave pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-681c7e69874ff6c2cdf180f0fb0d44f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE UNDER SECTION 12(4) OR (5)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 12(6) OR (7)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Compliance with requirements by the employer under SECTION 12(6) or (7) is a condition for giving NOTICE under SECTION 12(4) or (5)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-681c7e69874ff6c2cdf180f0fb0d44f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DAILY AVERAGE OF THE WAGES&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employees' Compensation Ordinance defines the daily average of wages, which is used in calculating various types of leave pay including maternity leave pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5b551a4a483944d6cf3179909e4812f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 12(4), (5)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 3A, 3B, 3C&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sections 12(4) and (5) are prerequisites or conditions that may affect the application of Sections 3A, 3B, and 3C."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5b551a4a483944d6cf3179909e4812f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRADE OR OCCUPATION&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Wages are calculated based on the TRADE or OCCUPATION of an employee, including those related to maternity leave pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5001d950d1e5de5921648ae860af7539</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LATTER PERIOD OF MATERNITY LEAVE (產假末段期間)&quot;" target="&quot;懷孕僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"This term refers to the period of maternity leave after the first 10 weeks for a female employee who has given birth."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78df2b99fcbe4aa2c71fdce1f79d338c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;懷孕僱員&quot;" target="&quot;FINE AT LEVEL 6 (違規罰款)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If an employer contravenes subsections related to pregnant employees, they may be subject to a fine at level 6. The same employee's situation is relevant in determining the offense and penalty."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;暫時喪失工作能力以致缺勤&quot;" target="&quot;《僱員補償條例》(第282章)第10條會獲付補償&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据《僱員補償條例》，因暂时丧失工作能力而缺勤的女性僱員可以获得补偿。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;補償&quot;" target="&quot;法院繳存&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據本條例須付的任何其他補償,需向法院繳存。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a6ff3e19762d07ee36fb89575db50a74</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;補償&quot;" target="&quot;僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據《僱員補償條例》(第282章),僱員在某些情況下可獲付補償。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23f4f40202843bfce44e444942fa422e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;《僱員補償條例》(第282章)第10條會獲付補償&quot;" target="&quot;放取任何產假、侍產假、休息日、病假日、假日或年假&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據第10條,僱員在這些假期中因未獲付給工資或全部工資的期間可獲得補償。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c12a66b5fa9d29ed0b0dc7f747de3d29</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主同意下放取任何假期&quot;" target="&quot;放取任何假期&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"只有在僱主同意的情况下，女性僱員才能放取任何假期。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主同意下放取任何假期&quot;" target="&quot;每日病假津貼額&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"这种情况下不会影响计算每日病假津贴的方式，除非是因生病或受伤缺勤。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-de9d7bf328eb68da98c29ac72b529085</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;14星期的產假薪酬&quot;" target="&quot;《僱員補償條例》(第282章)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据《僱員補償條例》，女性僱員可以得到14个星期的产假薪酬。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9615e656723ee75837b02f754231cbdc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;放取任何假期&quot;" target="&quot;12個月期間&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"在過去一年內,僱員可能因休假而未獲付給工資或全部工資的期間不計入每日平均款額計算中。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c12a66b5fa9d29ed0b0dc7f747de3d29</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;放取任何假期&quot;" target="&quot;產假、侍產假、休息日、病假日、假日或年假&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"這些假期均被視為僱員因休假而未獲付給工資或全部工資的期間之一。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c12a66b5fa9d29ed0b0dc7f747de3d29</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;放取任何假期&quot;" target="&quot;《僱員補償條例》(第282章)第10條會獲付補償,&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據第10條,在休假期間僱員可能獲得補償。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c12a66b5fa9d29ed0b0dc7f747de3d29</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;产假、休息日、病假日、假日或年假&quot;" target="&quot;女性员工&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"女性员工可以享受这些假期，但某些情况下工資可能不计算在内。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ab559340de48ae6d55e82984ae48a4f0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;产假、休息日、病假日、假日或年假&quot;" target="&quot;工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"这些假期的存在可能影响实际发放给女性员工的工资数额，特别是在某些特殊情况下工资可能会被扣除一部分或者全部。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ab559340de48ae6d55e82984ae48a4f0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREGNANT EMPLOYEE'S EMPLOYMENT TERMINATION PROHIBITION&quot;" target="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The prohibition against terminating a pregnant employee's continuous contract of employment is directly related to the definition and protection of such contracts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5aaa252a172d6b006af917dc91a91759</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREGNANT EMPLOYEE'S EMPLOYMENT TERMINATION PROHIBITION&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The prohibition includes provisions regarding maternity leave, indicating a direct relationship between the two concepts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5aaa252a172d6b006af917dc91a91759</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 9 TERMINATION PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Continuous contract of employment is subject to specific termination procedures outlined in Section 9, establishing a clear regulatory framework for both parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5aaa252a172d6b006af917dc91a91759</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;TRANSITION DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The transition date is a critical point that affects the validity of employment under a continuous contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bb3d86d7a750daf3fdfd492ec75be8b0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;THE 2022 YEAR EMPLOYMENT AND PENSIONS ORDINANCE (AMENDMENT ARRANGEMENTS) ORDINANCE (NO.4, 2022)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 2022 amendment ordinance affects the interpretation and application of a continuous contract of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bb3d86d7a750daf3fdfd492ec75be8b0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER WHO TERMINATES CONTINUOUS CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT OF A PREGNANT EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)(A) OR (B)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer who terminates a pregnant employee's contract of employment is subject to the conditions specified in Subsection (1)(a) or (b). If not proven otherwise, termination without proper grounds contravenes these subsections."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER WHO TERMINATES CONTINUOUS CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT OF A PREGNANT EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;SUM WHICH WOULD HAVE BEEN PAYABLE IF CONTRACT HAD BEEN TERMINATED BY EMPLOYER UNDER SECTION 7&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If an employer terminates a pregnant employee's contract without proper grounds, they must pay the sum that would have been payable if terminated under Section 7."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5d10f3a9af779ebd8f5d93a83026e213</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NORMAL WORKING DAY WITHOUT WORK PROVIDED&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPORARY LOSS OF WORK CAPACITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both situations involve days where the employee is not provided with work, but for different reasons: one due to temporary loss of capacity and the other as a normal rest day."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT TERMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;CHANGE OF OWNERSHIP OF BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text discusses the impact on employment contracts when there is a change in business ownership, specifically regarding how terminations are handled post-ownership change."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0276e1b514303ef83e330aacbd8bcf95</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT TERMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;THE 2020 AMENDMENT ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT TERMINATION is governed by THE 2020 AMENDMENT ORDINANCE, particularly for situations involving female employees and the amendment date."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7d6f22e03ef794b224e1918ddd3fee77</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)(B)&quot;" target="&quot;WITHDRAWAL OF CONSENT BY EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The withdrawal of consent before determination prevents further action on the claim."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2914073de37bf0e7df21cb9ca18483a2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)(B)&quot;" target="&quot;MONTHLY AVERAGE OF THE WAGES EARNED BY A FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The calculation of the monthly average wage for a female employee is based on subsection (2)(b). If impracticable, it can be calculated by reference to wages earned in similar circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MONTHLY AVERAGE OF THE WAGES EARNED BY A FEMALE EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;12 MONTHS IMMEDIATELY BEFORE THE DATE OF TERMINATION OF THE EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The calculation of the monthly average wage is based on a period immediately before termination. If no such person exists, another similar employment can be used as reference."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;12 MONTHS IMMEDIATELY BEFORE THE DATE OF TERMINATION OF THE EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT (FOR NO SUCH PERSON)&quot;" target="&quot;SAME TRADE OR OCCUPATION AND AT THE SAME WORK IN THE SAME DISTRICT DURING THE PERIOD OF 12 MONTHS IMMEDIATELY BEFORE THE DATE OF TERMINATION OF THE EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If no person from the same employer exists, wages of a similar trade or occupation in the same district during the period can be used for calculation. If no such person exists, another similar employment can be used as reference."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;粗重、危險或有害的工作 (禁派)&quot;" target="&quot;懷孕僱員 (不派有害工作)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Pregnant employees are protected from being assigned harmful work, which is explicitly prohibited. The same category of work applies to all pregnant employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;懷孕僱員 (請求)&quot;" target="&quot;懷孕僱員 (不派有害工作)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A pregnant employee can request not to be assigned harmful work, which relates directly to their protection during pregnancy. The same employee's situation is relevant in determining the offense and penalty."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;懷孕僱員 (請求)&quot;" target="&quot;懷孕期間的工作保護&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The request for a pregnant employee not to be assigned harmful work falls under the broader category of protection during pregnancy. The same employee's situation is relevant in determining the offense and penalty."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;懷孕僱員 (請求)&quot;" target="&quot;醫生證明書 (醫療文件)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A doctor's certificate supporting a pregnant employee's request for not being assigned harmful work is crucial evidence. The same document supports similar requests by other employees during pregnancy."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;懷孕僱員 (請求)&quot;" target="&quot;14天期限 (时间限制)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A 14-day period is specified for employers to comply with requests from pregnant employees not to be assigned harmful work. The same time frame applies in similar situations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;懷孕僱員 (請求)&quot;" target="&quot;同一職業或行業&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Pregnant employees' requests for not being assigned harmful work apply across similar trades or occupations. The same category of employment is relevant in determining the offense and penalty."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;懷孕僱員 (請求)&quot;" target="&quot;同一工作 (同等工作 - 比较对象)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Pregnant employees' requests for not being assigned harmful work are compared with similar jobs to ensure fair treatment. The same category of employment is relevant in determining the offense and penalty."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;懷孕僱員 (請求)&quot;" target="&quot;同一工作 (同等工作)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Pregnant employees' requests for not being assigned harmful work are compared with similar jobs to ensure fair treatment. The same category of employment is relevant in determining the offense and penalty."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;懷孕僱員 (請求)&quot;" target="&quot;身體檢查的結果&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A doctor's certificate supporting a pregnant employee's request for not being assigned harmful work may include medical examination results. The same document supports similar requests by other employees during pregnancy."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;懷孕僱員 (不派有害工作)&quot;" target="&quot;懷孕期間的工作保護&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The prohibition against assigning harmful work to pregnant employees falls under broader protection measures during pregnancy. The same employee's situation is relevant in determining the offense and penalty."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;懷孕僱員 (不派有害工作)&quot;" target="&quot;同一地區&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The prohibition against assigning harmful work to pregnant employees is specific to the region where they are employed, ensuring protection within a defined area."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;懷孕僱員 (不派有害工作)&quot;" target="&quot;同一職業或行業&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The prohibition against assigning harmful work to pregnant employees applies across similar trades or occupations, ensuring protection within a defined industry. The same category of employment is relevant in determining the offense and penalty."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;懷孕僱員 (不派有害工作)&quot;" target="&quot;同一工作 (同等工作 - 比较对象)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The prohibition against assigning harmful work to pregnant employees applies across similar jobs, ensuring fair treatment. The same category of employment is relevant in determining the offense and penalty."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;懷孕僱員 (不派有害工作)&quot;" target="&quot;同一工作 (同等工作)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The prohibition against assigning harmful work to pregnant employees applies across similar jobs, ensuring fair treatment. The same category of employment is relevant in determining the offense and penalty."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dcef1d93167679643a824fa74e4d13d1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;轉介&quot;" target="&quot;處長&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"處長處理來自僱主的轉介，並基於此做出決定。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd5d9d61caba55ae3f9dfd2940ae47cd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MONTHLY AVERAGE OF WAGES EARNED BY THE EMPLOYEE DURING A PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;TRANSFER FROM HEAVY, HAZARDOUS OR HARMFUL WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The monthly average of wages earned by the employee is relevant to determining the period before a transfer from heavy, hazardous or harmful work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-47f5ddfc5b519fcf524c4d9bd233c4e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SIN行&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER AUTHORIZED BY HIM IN THAT BEHALF OR ANY POLICE OFFICER NOT BELOW THE RANK OF INSPECTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers and police of a certain rank can investigate suspected offences, similar to the Commissioner's authority over employment agencies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-409891bfe2bfb21a0731ddceffe7a7d6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;疾病津贴&quot;" target="&quot;第33(2)條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据第33(2)条按月所累积者也是有薪病假日的一部分，与第33(2A)条共同构成疾病津贴的基础。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ede40d11dd383fafe8000e746a4c43b7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;罪行&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 15M(4)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Violating the provisions of SECTION 15M(4) is considered a crime, punishable by a fine."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9f8f154dd34baff54c016b669ab2da5c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;罪行&quot;" target="&quot;第5級罰款&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The crime defined in 罪行 can be punished with a 第5級罰款 as per legal regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9f8f154dd34baff54c016b669ab2da5c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OFFENCES&quot;" target="&quot;ANY EMPLOYER WHO&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Any employer who fails to comply with certain provisions, such as providing maternity leave or paying disease benefits, is described under 'OFFENCES' and faces legal consequences."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-47f5ddfc5b519fcf524c4d9bd233c4e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FEMALE EMPLOYEES&quot;" target="&quot;RECORD OF MATERNITY LEAVE TAKEN BY AND MATERNITY LEAVE PAY PAID TO HIS FEMALE EMPLOYEES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Female employees are involved in the records of their own maternity leave and pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c7550fdff3623ae221e2d156f6ce5cf2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RECORD OF MATERNITY LEAVE TAKEN BY AND MATERNITY LEAVE PAY PAID TO HIS FEMALE EMPLOYEES&quot;" target="&quot;处长指明的格式保存一份紀錄&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner specifies the format for recording maternity leave and pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c7550fdff3623ae221e2d156f6ce5cf2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILD (嬰兒)&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY (AND PATERNITY) LEAVE POLICIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'child' defines eligibility for leave policies that include both maternity and paternity leaves, indicating its central role in these policies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-885c65878619106b2d2b302114a64bb2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERPRETATION OF PART IIIA&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONDITIONS FOR PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The interpretation of Part IIIA clarifies conditions under which employees can take paternity leave, directly impacting employment conditions for such leaves."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-885c65878619106b2d2b302114a64bb2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONDITIONS FOR PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY (AND PATERNITY) LEAVE POLICIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both policies are interrelated as they both pertain to the rights and conditions of leave, specifically paternity leave in this case."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-885c65878619106b2d2b302114a64bb2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT REGULATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;DATA PRIVACY LAWS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both sets of regulations deal with managing and protecting personal information, particularly concerning employees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both sets of regulations interact, with employment regulations guiding how data is managed under the framework set by data privacy laws."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9a1fa46128d33dc86ff9326b722ce67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT REGULATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">25.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers are key in enforcing and implementing employment regulations, including those related to employee information management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public officers are responsible for enforcing employment regulations that include managing restrictions on employee data as per Section 33(5)(ab)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public officers are responsible for enforcing employment regulations, including those related to managing and restricting employee information as per Section 33(5)(ab)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9a1fa46128d33dc86ff9326b722ce67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT REGULATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 33(5)(AB)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employment regulations, including those in Section 33(5)(ab), provide the legal framework for managing restrictions on employee data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employment regulations, such as those in Section 33(5)(ab), govern how employee information is managed and restricted."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9a1fa46128d33dc86ff9326b722ce67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE ENTITLEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The entitlement to paternity leave is dependent upon the employee being employed under a continuous contract immediately before taking leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9ac80e2aa870b9e5660e938d7493cead</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE ENTITLEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 15F(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 15F(1) specifies the conditions and dates for employer notification related to paternity leave entitlement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9ac80e2aa870b9e5660e938d7493cead</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE ENTITLEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;27 FEBRUARY 2015&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The date of February 27, 2015, is significant as it marks the transition for calculating paternity leave duration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9ac80e2aa870b9e5660e938d7493cead</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 15F(1)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER NOTIFICATION DATE(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer notification dates are specified in Section 15F(1), which affects when an employee can take paternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9ac80e2aa870b9e5660e938d7493cead</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 15F(1)&quot;" target="&quot;THE 2020 AMENDMENT ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The notification process under SECTION 15F(1), especially before the amendment date, impacts the application of sections related to paternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a591cb80e52490f9bbe6ac81407040cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) (NO. 3) ORDINANCE 2018&quot;" target="&quot;COMMENCEMENT DATE: 18 JANUARY 2019.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ordinance commences on the specified date, affecting its provisions and applicability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7f18d7b28f469093dbda2666fad1b8f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTIFICATION REQUIREMENTS FOR PATERNITY LEAVE (15F)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER NOTIFICATION REQUIREMENT (15F(A)(I))&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer notification requirement is a part of the overall notification requirements for paternity leave as specified in section 15F."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bb89bd87e81559e9820333c42f3f0c6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTIFICATION REQUIREMENTS FOR PATERNITY LEAVE (15F)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER NOTIFICATION REQUIREMENT (15F(A)(II))&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer notification requirement is a part of the overall notification requirements for paternity leave as specified in section 15F."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bb89bd87e81559e9820333c42f3f0c6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTIFICATION REQUIREMENTS FOR PATERNITY LEAVE (15F)&quot;" target="&quot;WRITTEN STATEMENT REQUIREMENT (15F(2))&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The written statement requirement is a part of the overall notification requirements for paternity leave as specified in section 15F."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bb89bd87e81559e9820333c42f3f0c6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTIFICATION REQUIREMENTS FOR PATERNITY LEAVE (15F)&quot;" target="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE NOT AFFECTED BY OTHER HOLIDAYS (15G)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The notification requirements for paternity leave do not affect the status of paternity leave as specified in section 15G."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bb89bd87e81559e9820333c42f3f0c6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER NOTIFICATION REQUIREMENT (15F(A)(I))&quot;" target="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE NOT AFFECTED BY OTHER HOLIDAYS (15G)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer notification requirement for paternity leave does not affect the status of paternity leave as specified in section 15G."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bb89bd87e81559e9820333c42f3f0c6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER NOTIFICATION REQUIREMENT (15F(A)(II))&quot;" target="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE NOT AFFECTED BY OTHER HOLIDAYS (15G)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer notification requirement for paternity leave does not affect the status of paternity leave as specified in section 15G."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bb89bd87e81559e9820333c42f3f0c6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WRITTEN STATEMENT REQUIREMENT (15F(2))&quot;" target="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE NOT AFFECTED BY OTHER HOLIDAYS (15G)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The written statement requirement for paternity leave does not affect the status of paternity leave as specified in section 15G."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bb89bd87e81559e9820333c42f3f0c6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REST DAYS&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rest Days and Annual Leave are separate types of leave that can be managed independently but may overlap in scheduling."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a8a8ba58e2f04dd4f35b5bed0e044673</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE COMPENSATION&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'wages' includes payments made for maternity leave, indicating a direct relationship between wages and maternity leave compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-df8fc6081be757641b05c1766ffacd20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT PERIOD WITHOUT FULL WAGE&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employment period without full wage includes periods when employees take maternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT PERIOD WITHOUT FULL WAGE&quot;" target="&quot;SICK LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employment period without full wage covers periods when employees are on sick leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT PERIOD WITHOUT FULL WAGE&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employment period without full wage covers annual leave periods when employees are not working."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY LOSS OF WORK CAPACITY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT INJURY COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employment Injury Compensation Ordinance covers compensation for temporary loss of work capacity, which is a reason why the employee might not be provided with work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DAILY AVERAGE WAGE CALCULATION&quot;" target="&quot;SAME EMPLOYER SAME JOB EMPLOYEES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Same employer same job employees are used as a reference for calculating daily average wage when direct data is unavailable."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DAILY AVERAGE WAGE CALCULATION&quot;" target="&quot;SAME REGION SAME INDUSTRY OR PROFESSION SAME JOB EMPLOYEES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Same region, same industry or profession same job employees are used as a reference for calculating daily average wage when direct data is unavailable."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT OR OTHER AGREEMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employment contracts or other agreements may include provisions regarding maternity leave payments, affecting the employment period without full wage calculation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-58bf119693ea1dc0090d8170647861d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFIED DATE&quot;" target="&quot;RATE OF PATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SPECIFIED DATE is crucial for determining the Rate of Paternity Leave Pay, as it marks the beginning or exact date of paternity leave taken by an employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f6ee37a79b0dc57f162b791dd8b859ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFIED DATE&quot;" target="&quot;AVERAGE DAILY WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SPECIFIED DATE is relevant in calculating AVERAGE DAILY WAGES, as it defines the period over which wages should be averaged for paternity leave pay calculations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f6ee37a79b0dc57f162b791dd8b859ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFIED DATE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 2022&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SPECIFIED DATE is the day on which the Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 2022 is published in the GAZETTE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-60efa76430de6c8c3995f39eeee4cc13</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFIED DATE&quot;" target="&quot;FORMER PROVISION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SPECIFIED DATE refers to the effective date of the FORMER PROVISION before it was amended by the 2018 Employment (Amendment) Ordinance No. 2 (Cap. 57, Laws of Hong Kong). The relationship is based on the definition provided in paragraph (a)(i) and (ii) of the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a43725922c10caf8be455ef54288f1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFIED DATE&quot;" target="&quot;MATERIAL DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SPECIFIED DATE can also refer to the MATERIAL DATE for certain situations, such as when an employee's employment is terminated before they are notified by their employer. The relationship is based on paragraph (a)(i) of the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3a43725922c10caf8be455ef54288f1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE PAY RATE&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Wages are used to calculate the PATERNITY LEAVE PAY RATE based on average daily wages during a specified period before the SPECIFIED DATE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f6ee37a79b0dc57f162b791dd8b859ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AVERAGE DAILY WAGES&quot;" target="&quot;RATE OF PATERNITY LEAVE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The AVERAGE DAILY WAGES over a 12-month period (or shorter if employed for less time) are used to determine the RATE OF PATERNITY LEAVE PAY."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f6ee37a79b0dc57f162b791dd8b859ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AVERAGE DAILY WAGES&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIFIED PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The specified period is used to calculate the average daily wages for determining the amount of severance pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-515212436640c28d5f467b8b10ac11d7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AVERAGE DAILY WAGES CALCULATION&quot;" target="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE, REST DAY, SICKNESS DAY, HOLIDAY OR ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Paternity leave is excluded from the calculation of average daily wages as per the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61c50955c5e42baad9d032d0022c3d46</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AVERAGE DAILY WAGES CALCULATION&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Temporary incapacity for which compensation is payable under section 10 of the Employees' Compensation Ordinance does not affect average daily wages calculation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61c50955c5e42baad9d032d0022c3d46</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BIRTH CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The birth certificate is required for a mother to take maternity leave, specifically when the baby is born in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2c1776c3e340075487202946fbb11cb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BIRTH CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;DOCTOR'S CERTIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both documents are related to maternity leave, with the birth certificate being primary when applicable and doctor's certification as a secondary requirement if necessary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2c1776c3e340075487202946fbb11cb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BIRTH CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;BIRTHS AND DEATHS REGISTRATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 174)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Births and Deaths Registration Ordinance issues birth certificates which are necessary for paternity leave pay documentation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f11184ac38e9ff98017a8ef0f47064dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BIRTH CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A registered medical practitioner can issue a birth certificate, which is essential for various legal and administrative purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bab24c47d69b1c9fe7a8b2d862514c83</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BIRTH CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;DEATH CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both documents are related as they pertain to vital events such as birth and death, though for different purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bab24c47d69b1c9fe7a8b2d862514c83</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BIRTH CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The birth certificate issued by authorities is a document that can prove an employee's paternity."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6320bd8af6a47ec4d774b02d5588447a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOCTOR'S CERTIFICATION&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Doctor's certification is needed as an alternative document if the baby has died and there is no birth certificate available for maternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2c1776c3e340075487202946fbb11cb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MIDWIVES REGISTRATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 162)&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A midwife registered under section 8 of this ordinance can issue a medical certificate for paternity leave."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Midwives Registration Ordinance governs the registration of midwives, which indirectly relates to registered medical practitioners involved in births."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bab24c47d69b1c9fe7a8b2d862514c83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11184ac38e9ff98017a8ef0f47064dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MIDWIVES REGISTRATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 162)&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Registered Chinese medicine practitioners are mentioned alongside midwives under the Midwives Registration Ordinance, indicating a related regulatory framework."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-73492d2774f700c9b55459d33fea445f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATERNITY LEAVE PAY: BIRTH IN HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A registered medical practitioner can issue a certificate required for paternity leave in respect of the birth of a child in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f11184ac38e9ff98017a8ef0f47064dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEATH CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A death certificate may be required as a proof in certain circumstances, such as when an infant dies after birth."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bab24c47d69b1c9fe7a8b2d862514c83</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDICAL CERTIFICATE OR DOCUMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employee must provide a medical certificate or document to confirm the birth and status of the child."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SERVICE LEAVE COMPENSATION&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Service leave compensation is provided to employees who take paternity leave as per company policies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REQUISITE DOCUMENT&quot;" target="&quot;12 MONTHS AFTER THE FIRST DAY ON WHICH THE EMPLOYEE TAKES PATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Requisite documents must be provided within 12 months after the first day of taking paternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REQUISITE DOCUMENT&quot;" target="&quot;6 MONTHS AFTER CESSATION OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If employment is terminated, requisite documents are to be submitted within 6 months from cessation of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REQUISITE DOCUMENT&quot;" target="&quot;7 DAYS AFTER CESSATION OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Requisite documents must be submitted within 7 days after cessation of employment if the employee has stopped working before providing necessary papers for paternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REQUISITE DOCUMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT RELATIONSHIP TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Relevant documents must be submitted within a specific period after the termination of employment to claim service leave compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;15J OR 15K CLAUSE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The clauses define the requirements for providing documents related to paternity leave and compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAID PARENTAL LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Paid parental leave is a form of service leave with specific conditions as outlined in legal or company policies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENT DAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Payment for service leave compensation is made on specific days as per company policies and legal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-91aa7eac66ae8e5baa6d84dcf3293f81</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REQUISITE DOCUMENT (所需文件)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 15J OR 15K&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Requisite document is defined under Section 15J or 15K for entitlement to paternity leave pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2f4881be1a6d6d318bb1047aad7c99da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CESSATION (停止受僱)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The cessation of employment affects the payment and deduction process related to paternity leave pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2f4881be1a6d6d318bb1047aad7c99da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEAVE DAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employee is entitled to receive payment on the Leave Day as per regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9f8f154dd34baff54c016b669ab2da5c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;E.R. 3 OF 2017&quot;" target="&quot;格式變更&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Format changes are recorded in E.R. 3 of 2017, indicating updates or amendments to the document's format."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-985c71a2aa2037adf4ce25fd3c8c12de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;E.R. 3 OF 2017&quot;" target="&quot;PART IXA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"E.R. 3 OF 2017 is part of the legal framework that leads to PART IXA, which addresses liability for wages of sub-contractor's and nominated sub-contractor's employees; it also indicates a format change."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-768a2ada446405fddb705e41250aee16</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EVERY EMPLOYEE WHO HAS BEEN EMPLOYED BY THE SAME EMPLOYER UNDER A CONTINUOUS CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;GRANT OF REST DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Every employee under continuous contract is entitled to at least 1 rest day in every period of 7 days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8eeab579ddc2235f2e1503e95ddb7809</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATUTORY HOLIDAY, OR ALTERNATIVE HOLIDAY OR SUBSTITUTED HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;GRANT OF REST DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rest days are granted in addition to statutory holidays or alternative/substituted holidays."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8eeab579ddc2235f2e1503e95ddb7809</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRANT OF REST DAYS&quot;" target="&quot;僱主指定的休息日&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are responsible for granting rest days to employees as part of their continuous contract obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8eeab579ddc2235f2e1503e95ddb7809</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRANT OF REST DAYS&quot;" target="&quot;APPOINTMENT OF REST DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The process of appointing rest days is integral to ensuring that employees receive the required rest as part of their continuous contract obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8eeab579ddc2235f2e1503e95ddb7809</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;1976年第71號第4條修訂&quot;" target="&quot;APPOINTMENT OF REST DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 4th revision of the 71st regulation of 1976 amended the appointment process for rest days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8eeab579ddc2235f2e1503e95ddb7809</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;每月开始之前以口頭或書面通知各僱員在該月份的休息日&quot;" target="&quot;APPOINTMENT OF REST DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers must inform employees about the designated rest days before each month starts, either orally or in writing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8eeab579ddc2235f2e1503e95ddb7809</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;固定在每7天期间的某一天&quot;" target="&quot;APPOINTMENT OF REST DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rest days can be fixed on a specific day within every 7-day period, which simplifies their scheduling and management."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8eeab579ddc2235f2e1503e95ddb7809</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MACHINE BREAKDOWN&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYEE may be required to work on a REST DAY in case of MACHINE BREAKDOWNS, with an alternative rest day provided by the employer. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-393f577c90dd494cee38d1bc9bc80592</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANTI-UNION DISCRIMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;TRADE UNION ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of anti-union discrimination is central to the provisions in the Trade Union Ordinance, which aim to protect employees from such discrimination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca5d1bd01d9d5e548435eca4ad5a23d9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORK REQUEST&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer can request an employee to work voluntarily or under certain conditions such as machinery breakdowns or unforeseen emergencies, impacting their rest day entitlements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6511dbd5eb2121ae41cf477a6c2b2884</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROTECTION AGAINST ANTI-UNION DISCRIMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 21C&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 21C is a specific provision under the Protection Against Anti-Union Discrimination that applies to individuals receiving or about to receive an employment offer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca5d1bd01d9d5e548435eca4ad5a23d9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART IVA&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT OFFER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The application of Part IVA, particularly Section 21C, pertains directly to employment offers and the rights associated with them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca5d1bd01d9d5e548435eca4ad5a23d9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 21B(1)(A)&quot;" target="&quot;TRADE UNION ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 21B(1)(A) refers to the right of employees to become members or officers of a trade union as per the Trade Union Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca5d1bd01d9d5e548435eca4ad5a23d9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 21B(1)(B)&quot;" target="&quot;TRADE UNION ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 21B(1)(B) refers to employees' rights to participate in trade union activities as per the Trade Union Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca5d1bd01d9d5e548435eca4ad5a23d9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 21B(1)(C)&quot;" target="&quot;TRADE UNION ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 21B(1)(C) refers to employees' rights to organize or apply for registration of a trade union as per the Trade Union Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca5d1bd01d9d5e548435eca4ad5a23d9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 21B(2)(A)&quot;" target="&quot;TRADE UNION ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 21B(2)(A) refers to employers or their representatives' actions that prevent employees from exercising rights as per the Trade Union Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca5d1bd01d9d5e548435eca4ad5a23d9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 21B(2)(B)&quot;" target="&quot;TRADE UNION ORDINANCE (CAP. 332)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 21B(2)(B) refers to employers or their representatives' actions that discriminate against employees for exercising rights as per the Trade Union Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca5d1bd01d9d5e548435eca4ad5a23d9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGISTRATION OF A TRADE UNION&quot;" target="&quot;PREVENTS OR DETERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The act of preventing or deterring can be related to the registration process of a trade union as it may hinder its formation or application for registration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf200a1925a9d223f09c260af5f8d034</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGISTRATION OF A TRADE UNION&quot;" target="&quot;OFFEREE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The offer to the offeree includes conditions that prohibit them from associating with others for forming or applying for registration of a trade union."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1a6c178897818a8c58b6d17f59790314</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREVENTS OR DETERS&quot;" target="&quot;WORK CONDITIONS AND RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Preventing or deterring can impact an employee's ability to exercise their rights related to work conditions, such as forming a union or participating in its activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf200a1925a9d223f09c260af5f8d034</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORK CONDITIONS AND RIGHTS&quot;" target="&quot;1971 C. 72 S. 5(1)、(2) &amp; (5) U.K.&quot; &quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The legal provisions from the mentioned statute are relevant to work conditions and rights, as they define terms like 'work time' and outline employee rights in relation to trade unions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf200a1925a9d223f09c260af5f8d034</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKER&quot;" target="&quot;PENALTY FOR PREVENTING UNION ACTIVITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The WORKER is protected by the PENALTY FOR PREVENTING UNION ACTIVITIES, which ensures that any employer who prevents or deters a worker from exercising their union rights will be guilty of an offence and liable to fines."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bb269a993727b98b029449c2f2612dff</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OFFEREE&quot;" target="&quot;MEMBER OR OFFICER OF SUCH A TRADE UNION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The offer to the offeree includes conditions that restrict their membership or office in a trade union."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1a6c178897818a8c58b6d17f59790314</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;1997年第135號第3條&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT OF WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The repealed section 3 of the 1997 Regulation is related to 'Payment of Wages' as it was part of the original document structure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5cfb2ca67c6dde30f8772d15dd059180</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;1997年第135號第3條&quot;" target="&quot;PART V&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 3 of the 1997 Regulation, although repealed, was originally under Part V."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5cfb2ca67c6dde30f8772d15dd059180</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENT OF WAGES&quot;" target="&quot;FORMAT CHANGES—2017年第3號編輯修訂紀錄&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Payment of Wages section is related to format changes as it may be affected by the 2017 amendments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5cfb2ca67c6dde30f8772d15dd059180</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENT ON COMPLETION OF EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT WITHIN 7 DAYS FROM CONTRACT END&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both payment methods refer to the same concept of paying employees within a certain period after their contract ends, with 'Payment on Completion' being more immediate and 'Within 7 Days' providing an upper limit for delayed payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ba1c077a9bcf3aa46c5e476bb87f889</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 76, 1985&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT ON TERMINATION (SECTION 25)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"SECTION 76, 1985" adds provisions related to "Payment on termination", specifically mentioning long service payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0b0b8e9edfab8c32d5cea9270e6f74ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 103, 1995&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"SECTION 103, 1995" modifies the rights and obligations of employees in certain circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0b0b8e9edfab8c32d5cea9270e6f74ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 7, 2001&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Long service payment is mentioned under SECTION 7, 2001 as one of the components to be paid on termination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0b0b8e9edfab8c32d5cea9270e6f74ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGE PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employee's wage period is a factor in calculating the payment on termination as per the text provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"The wage period is relevant to employee wages and deductions as per the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0b0b8e9edfab8c32d5cea9270e6f74ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdc4a39840a667a7878ee99d632412a5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGE PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;DEDUCTIONS IN RESPECT OF ABSENCE FROM WORK OR ANY DEDUCTION PURSUANT TO AN ATTACHMENT ORDER MADE UNDER SECTION 20(1) OF THE GUARDIANSHIP OF MINORS ORDINANCE (CAP. 13), SECTION 9A(1) OF THE SEPARATION AND MAINTENANCE ORDERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 16)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Deductions related to absence from work or attachment orders are tied to the wage period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d4260c7d330eaf337c4690f784c02608</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGE PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner's approval is required for certain wage deductions in a single wage period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fdc4a39840a667a7878ee99d632412a5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 310&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Long service payment is mentioned but not directly linked to SECTION 310, suggesting it might be governed by different provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0b0b8e9edfab8c32d5cea9270e6f74ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 32&quot;" target="&quot;OFFENCE UNDER THIS SECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Violating SECTION 32 leads to an OFFENCE under this section, which may involve fines and imprisonment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c62e4d3b32ca7459c870b08308d480ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 32&quot;" target="&quot;OFFENCE UNDER SECTION 72A(3)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Violating SECTION 32 can lead to an OFFENCE under SECTION 72A(3)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c62e4d3b32ca7459c870b08308d480ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 44 OF 1971 S. 4&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Long service payment is mentioned as an additional sum due to the employee, related to SECTION 44 of 1971 s. 4."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c9335a6eed209eaa686a730c45ba54a5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 23, 24 AND 25&quot;" target="&quot;INTEREST ON LATE PAYMENT OF WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"These sections are directly relevant in calculating interest on late payment of wages as per subsection (1)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c9335a6eed209eaa686a730c45ba54a5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTEREST ON LATE PAYMENT OF WAGES&quot;" target="&quot;生效日期:1997年6月27日。&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The effective date is relevant to when interest on late payment of wages starts, as per subsection (3)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c9335a6eed209eaa686a730c45ba54a5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FINAL COURT JUDGE&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 50 OF THE LAW OF THE REGIONAL COURT (第336章)第50条&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The final court judge's determination is crucial for the interest rate on late payment of wages as per SECTION 25(2)(A)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c9335a6eed209eaa686a730c45ba54a5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;50條以憲報公告釐定的利率&quot;" target="&quot;生效日期:1997年6月27日.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The effective date for the interest rates defined by Article 50 is specified as June 27, 1997."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c744977e34a4740a08449eedd5ecccdd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;50條以憲報公告釐定的利率&quot;" target="&quot;不須就本條的生效日期之前的任何期間支付利息.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Interest does not need to be paid for any period before the effective date of Article 50 as defined in the gazette notice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c744977e34a4740a08449eedd5ecccdd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;50條以憲報公告釐定的利率&quot;" target="&quot;26. 支付工資的方式及地點&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The interest rates defined by Article 50 are related to wage payments, which involve various payment methods and locations as specified in the Wage Payment Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The wage payment methods and locations specified in Article 26 are related to the interest rates defined by Article 50, as both fall under the same legal framework."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c744977e34a4740a08449eedd5ecccdd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;50條以憲報公告釐定的利率&quot;" target="&quot;25A. INTEREST ON LATE PAYMENT OF WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 25A regarding interest for late wage payments is directly influenced by the interest rates defined in Article 50 as per the gazette notice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c744977e34a4740a08449eedd5ecccdd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;50條以憲報公告釐定的利率&quot;" target="&quot;編輯附註:&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 50's defined interest rates are related to the editorial notes that provide additional context and information about its implementation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c744977e34a4740a08449eedd5ecccdd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;POSTAL ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;BANKING ORDINANCE (CAP. 155)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Banking Ordinance (Cap. 155) defines the context in which postal orders can be used as a method of payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;POSTAL ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;CHEQUE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are methods by which wages may be paid according to the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;POSTAL ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;MONEY ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"They both serve as alternative payment methods mentioned in the context of wage payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BANKING ORDINANCE (CAP. 155)&quot;" target="&quot;BANK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Banking Ordinance defines what constitutes a bank, which is relevant to how wages can be paid into an account."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BANKING ORDINANCE (CAP. 155)&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Banking Ordinance defines the bank accounts into which severance payments can be made."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-11d596f17d04a1402f9a7eda05284076</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BANKING ORDINANCE (CAP. 155)&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Payments can be made into an account in the name of the entitled person with any bank as per the Banking Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3aa1d2d981153f366e07b9a78ba0c7ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BANKING ORDINANCE (CAP. 155)&quot;" target="&quot;DISCLOSURE RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Banking Ordinance defines banks that can receive disclosures under specific conditions, as part of the disclosure rules."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-79816614535478a4c5093238ccf5e99a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BANKING ORDINANCE (CAP. 155)&quot;" target="&quot;MONEY LENDERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 163)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ordinances are related to financial regulations and may overlap in their application, particularly concerning licensed money lenders for reasonable commercial purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-31ad535185a1489332f643fec100e338</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHEQUE&quot;" target="&quot;MONEY ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"They both serve as alternative payment methods mentioned in the context of wage payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DULY APPOINTED AGENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text mentions that wages can be paid to an employee's duly appointed agent, indicating a relationship between these two entities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DULY APPOINTED AGENT&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A long service payment may also be made to a duly appointed agent when the recipient consents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3aa1d2d981153f366e07b9a78ba0c7ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENTERTAINMENT VENUE&quot;" target="&quot;FIXED ODDS BETTING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Entertainment venues are explicitly mentioned as places where fixed odds betting cannot take place according to the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENTERTAINMENT VENUE&quot;" target="&quot;VENUE SELLING INTOXICATING LIQUOR OR DANGEROUS DRUGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both types of venues are explicitly mentioned as places where wages should not be paid, indicating a similar context in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FIXED ODDS BETTING&quot;" target="&quot;PARI-MUTUEL BETTING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"They both fall under the category of gambling activities that cannot take place at certain venues according to the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VENUE SELLING INTOXICATING LIQUOR OR DANGEROUS DRUGS&quot;" target="&quot;RETAIL STORE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are types of locations where wages should not be paid, as mentioned in the context provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af3fa69740e6c0d13188b3cd0b0d9a52</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BETTING DUTY ORDINANCE (CAP. 108)&quot;" target="&quot;INTOXICATING LIQUOR OR ANY DANGEROUS DRUG&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Betting Duty Ordinance (Cap. 108) regulates the sale of intoxicating liquor or any dangerous drug, which is mentioned in relation to cash-sweeps and fixed odds betting."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23e0ef850c878d1bb32d1dab35a67bc7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BETTING DUTY ORDINANCE (CAP. 108)&quot;" target="&quot;PLACE OF AMUSEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Betting Duty Ordinance (Cap. 108) mentions places of amusement as a location where wages should not be paid."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23e0ef850c878d1bb32d1dab35a67bc7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BETTING DUTY ORDINANCE (CAP. 108)&quot;" target="&quot;CASH-SWEEP, FIXED ODDS BETTING OR PARI-MUTUEL BETTING ORGANIZED OR CONDUCTED WITH PERMISSION UNDER THE BETTING DUTY ORDINANCE (CAP. 108)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The betting activity is regulated under the Betting Duty Ordinance (Cap. 108)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a2d24bb03fc40b38ed1a8c0cbcdbd963</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SHOP OR STORE FOR THE RETAIL SALE OF MERCHANDISE&quot;" target="&quot;INTOXICATING LIQUOR OR ANY DANGEROUS DRUG&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Intoxicating liquor or any dangerous drug is sold in shops or stores for the retail sale of merchandise, as mentioned in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23e0ef850c878d1bb32d1dab35a67bc7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTOXICATING LIQUOR OR ANY DANGEROUS DRUG&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees are not allowed to receive intoxicating liquor or dangerous drug as remuneration for their services."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23e0ef850c878d1bb32d1dab35a67bc7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FOOD, ACCOMMODATION OR OTHER ALLOWANCES OR PRIVILEGES&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Food, accommodation, or other allowances or privileges are provided to employees according to their contract of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23e0ef850c878d1bb32d1dab35a67bc7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTOXICATING LIQUOR, DANGEROUS DRUG, TICKET OR OTHER SUBSTITUTE FOR TICKET&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Intoxicating liquor, dangerous drug, ticket or other substitute for ticket cannot be used as remuneration according to the contract of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23e0ef850c878d1bb32d1dab35a67bc7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT OR AGREEMENT IN CONSIDERATION OF A CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;REASONABLE GROUNDS TO BELIEVE IN THE ABILITY TO PAY WAGES AT DUE DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The contract of employment or agreement in consideration of an employment contract must be made with reasonable grounds to believe the employer can pay wages at due date."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a2d24bb03fc40b38ed1a8c0cbcdbd963</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT OR AGREEMENT IN CONSIDERATION OF A CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT, RENEWAL, OR CONTINUATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employment contracts, renewals, or continuations are forms of agreements in consideration of an employment contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a2d24bb03fc40b38ed1a8c0cbcdbd963</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AGREEMENT AS TO MANNER OF SPENDING&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The agreement as to manner of spending pertains directly to the employee's use of wages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a2d24bb03fc40b38ed1a8c0cbcdbd963</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AGREEMENT AS TO MANNER OF SPENDING&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER OPENING SHOPS FOR SALE OF COMMODITIES TO EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer's opening of shops for sale of commodities may involve agreements as to the manner in which employees spend their wages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a2d24bb03fc40b38ed1a8c0cbcdbd963</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE GROUNDS TO BELIEVE IN THE ABILITY TO PAY WAGES AT DUE DATE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER OPENING SHOPS FOR SALE OF COMMODITIES TO EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employer opening shops for sale of commodities to employees should have reasonable grounds to believe in the ability to pay wages at due date."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a2d24bb03fc40b38ed1a8c0cbcdbd963</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE GROUNDS TO BELIEVE IN THE ABILITY TO PAY WAGES AT DUE DATE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT, RENEWAL, OR CONTINUATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Renewal or continuation of employment contracts must be made with reasonable grounds to believe the employer can pay wages at due date."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a2d24bb03fc40b38ed1a8c0cbcdbd963</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE GROUNDS TO BELIEVE IN THE ABILITY TO PAY WAGES AT DUE DATE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees have a stake in the employer's ability to pay wages at due date as part of their contractual obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a2d24bb03fc40b38ed1a8c0cbcdbd963</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER NOT TO ENTER INTO CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT WITHOUT REASONABLE BELIEF THAT HE CAN PAY WAGES&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT AS EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer must have a reasonable belief that they can pay wages before entering into, renewing or continuing an employment contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d9809ad52a0fec55dacd101bbfec86fa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER NOT TO ENTER INTO CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT WITHOUT REASONABLE BELIEF THAT HE CAN PAY WAGES&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer's ability to pay wages is related to the entitlement of employees to severance payments, as both are concerned with the financial stability of the employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d9809ad52a0fec55dacd101bbfec86fa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT AS EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PART VA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both concepts deal with employment contracts and their terms, specifically regarding continuous contracts and severance pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d9809ad52a0fec55dacd101bbfec86fa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT AS EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employment contracts are foundational to understanding severance payments, as they determine eligibility and terms for such payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d9809ad52a0fec55dacd101bbfec86fa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART VA&quot;" target="&quot;ENTITLEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Entitlement includes severance payment payable under Part VA."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1c30b39b26dc22df210f2ea63b93552</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART VA&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31G&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Part VA is modified through Section 31G as indicated in the text, showing a direct relationship between these two entities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0dd3aa2554b81fa47ed2eec0f056d25</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REDUNDANCY&quot;" target="&quot;LAYOFF&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Layoff can be due to business operation stopping, job demand reduction, or other reasons related to redundancy."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REDUNDANCY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees who are dismissed due to redundancy have the right to severance payment according to U.K. law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9546d09d8137ba2697ee36074c84b498</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LAYOFF&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees can be laid off as part of business operation stopping or job demand reduction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LAYOFF&quot;" target="&quot;PRIVATE HOUSEHOLD WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees working in private households can be laid off, which is considered a form of business operation stopping for such businesses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LAYOFF&quot;" target="&quot;FAMILY EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Family employees working in private households are also subject to layoff as part of the business operations of these households."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LAYOFF&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Layoff does not result in a severance payment unless specific conditions are met, as stated by the contract of employment continuity clause."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8e2655c247e96affa05132d650c897b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LAYOFF&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The continuity of an employee's contract is not broken due to layoff if no severance payment has been made."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8e2655c247e96affa05132d650c897b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;LICENSEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A LICENSEE must not enter into an EMPLOYMENT AGREEMENT without written permission from the COMMISSIONER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf1cb5b59a9e111ec611acd3b69ca0ea</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ASSOCIATE OF A LICENSEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An ASSOCIATE OF A LICENSEE is also subject to the regulations regarding EMPLOYMENT AGREEMENTs, similar to those of a LICENSEE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bf1cb5b59a9e111ec611acd3b69ca0ea</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS OPERATION STOPPING&quot;" target="&quot;JOB DEMAND REDUCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business operation stopping can lead to a reduction in job demand, which may result in layoffs or other employment adjustments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL OBLIGATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers have legal obligations to provide severance payment when dismissing employees by reason of redundancy or layoff."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea2f0f182df099225a628487d487158f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;U.K.&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The U.K. law provides for the right to severance payment under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9546d09d8137ba2697ee36074c84b498</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;U.K.&quot;" target="&quot;1965 C. 62 SS. 1 &amp; 19(1) U.K.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 1965 Act provides foundational provisions for employment rights, including severance payments in the U.K."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9546d09d8137ba2697ee36074c84b498</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;U.K.&quot;" target="&quot;2000年第51號第3條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 2000 amendment to the law addresses certain exemptions related to termination of employment under specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9546d09d8137ba2697ee36074c84b498</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;U.K.&quot;" target="&quot;1965 C. 62 S. 3 U.K.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"This legal provision is from the United Kingdom's legislation (Act of 1965, Chapter 62, Section 3). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dfd284d26c8ac23ba53544b4fe799168</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;U.K.&quot;" target="&quot;1990年第41號第8條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Chinese translation refers to a section in U.K. law that was revised by this provision (Amended by the Act of 1990, Chapter 41, Article 8). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dfd284d26c8ac23ba53544b4fe799168</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;U.K.&quot;" target="&quot;1993年第61號第4條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Chinese translation refers to a section in U.K. law that was revised by this provision (Amended by the Act of 1993, Chapter 61, Article 4). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dfd284d26c8ac23ba53544b4fe799168</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;U.K.&quot;" target="&quot;PART VB&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The legal part 'Part VB' is added to the U.K. legislation context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-985c71a2aa2037adf4ce25fd3c8c12de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;U.K.&quot;" target="&quot;REASONABLENESS TEST&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The U.K. law (1977 c. 50) defines the 'reasonable standard' test, which is relevant to both REASONABLENESS TEST and CONTRACT TERM."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-723308f570a274e7e8ac1a555c11b81b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;U.K.&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT TERM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The U.K. law (1977 c. 50 s. 7) sets out specific terms regarding the exclusion or restriction of liability in relation to certain contract rights, impacting CONTRACT TERM directly."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-723308f570a274e7e8ac1a555c11b81b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;U.K.&quot;" target="&quot;LIABILITY EXCLUSION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The U.K. law (1977 c. 50 s. 7) provides rules on how liability can be excluded or restricted by reference to any such term, which is relevant to LIABILITY EXCLUSION."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-723308f570a274e7e8ac1a555c11b81b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;U.K.&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE OF GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text mentions U.K. as one of the possible locations for parties involved in contracts of sale of goods, showing a related entity within international contract law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8271f6bc492f9ae5ef71b7e98a92bd06</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;U.K.&quot;" target="&quot;SUPPLY CONTRACTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Supply contracts can involve parties from different countries or territories, including U.K., showing potential relationships between entities involved in such cross-border agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8271f6bc492f9ae5ef71b7e98a92bd06</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31G&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 31G of the U.K. law specifies how severance payment should be calculated for certain employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9546d09d8137ba2697ee36074c84b498</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31G&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS CESSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business cessation can lead to an employee being laid off or dismissed, triggering Section 31G for severance payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9546d09d8137ba2697ee36074c84b498</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT TERMINATION CLAUSE&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The clause regarding the termination of employment contract does not entitle the employee to severance pay if terminated due to certain behaviors."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-18f452820ec690c39e359260ee75e592</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT TERMINATION CLAUSE&quot;" target="&quot;SUITABLE EMPLOYMENT OFFER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Suitable employment offers can arise from the renewal or new contract terms after an employee's termination, depending on the circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-18f452820ec690c39e359260ee75e592</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVERANCE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;LESS FAVORABLE EMPLOYMENT OFFER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If an employee rejects a less favorable employment offer, they may not be entitled to severance pay according to certain clauses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-18f452820ec690c39e359260ee75e592</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVERANCE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;1965 C. 62 S. 16 U.K.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Severance pay calculation methods reference the UK legislation, indicating a legal basis for similar provisions in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3acaae72bbbda2c87c57f32876a632e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVERANCE PAY&quot;" target="&quot;31G. 遣散費的款額&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 31G details the calculation methods for severance pay, providing specific criteria and amounts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3acaae72bbbda2c87c57f32876a632e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT RENEWAL OFFER&quot;" target="&quot;NEW EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employment renewal offer can lead to a new employment contract, depending on the terms and conditions agreed upon by both parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-18f452820ec690c39e359260ee75e592</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT RENEWAL OFFER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employment contract renewal offer directly affects the employee’s status and potential entitlement to a long-term service bonus."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1bb14977455cfee69d96555a42dffb40</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT RENEWAL OFFER&quot;" target="&quot;FORMER OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The offer for employment contract renewal is related to the former owner, as it involves their employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1cb0098fa2f01839bce9b10d85c36181</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT RENEWAL OFFER&quot;" target="&quot;NEW OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The new owner is indirectly related to employment contract renewal offers, as they may inherit such obligations from the previous business state."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1cb0098fa2f01839bce9b10d85c36181</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TERMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employee may face TERMINATION, which can result in the loss of rights to SEVERANCE PAYMENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-398cf2cb1ea6408a6d67cec4cb083e74</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TERMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Termination of an employee's contract may result in entitlement to SEVERANCE PAYMENT, depending on circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-398cf2cb1ea6408a6d67cec4cb083e74</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE OR PAYMENT IN LIEU&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT can specify conditions for NOTICE OR PAYMENT IN LIEIU upon termination of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-398cf2cb1ea6408a6d67cec4cb083e74</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;51 OF 2000 S. 3&quot;" target="&quot;AMENDED 75 OF 1997 S. 2&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both amendments (51 of 2000 s. 3 and 75 of 1997 s. 2) interact with SECTION 9 to provide conditions for the dismissal without entitlement to severance payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d536cf1eacc47eb2d3812dd2faa34e3c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;7 DAYS BEFORE THE RELEVANT DATE&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31T(1)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The relevant period before termination under section 31T(1)(B) affects the employee's right to a long service payment by reason of dismissal. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e3a3f0edfa08a61dbd46b52c9f94d56a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;1990年第41號第8條&quot;" target="&quot;1993年第61號第4條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both provisions are from U.K. law and have been revised to each other."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dfd284d26c8ac23ba53544b4fe799168</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT CONTINUITY&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The continuity of an employee's contract is maintained even if there has been a lay-off without severance payment being made."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2138132720286ddae5a4634e3cd8c8f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELEVANT DATE (有關日期)&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Relevant date refers to the expiration of a period related to the right for severance payment in case of layoff."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8e2655c247e96affa05132d650c897b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELEVANT DATE (有關日期)&quot;" target="&quot;1965 C. 62 S. 5(1) U.K.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The relevant date is defined by reference to a specific section from the UK legislation, indicating its importance in determining severance payment rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8e2655c247e96affa05132d650c897b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXCLUDED CLASSES OF EMPLOYEES&quot;" target="&quot;GOVERNMENT OTHER THAN THE HONG KONG GOVERNMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees of government entities other than Hong Kong are also excluded from certain employee categories, such as those employed by the Hong Kong Government or family workers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8e2655c247e96affa05132d650c897b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;31F. EXCLUDED CLASSES OF EMPLOYEES&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Certain classes of employees are excluded from severance pay benefits as specified by law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3acaae72bbbda2c87c57f32876a632e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;$22,500&quot;" target="&quot;31G. AMOUNT OF SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"$22,500 is a reference point in calculating severance payments for monthly rated employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bacfa097f6ad79f65b09995405789b70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;$22,500&quot;" target="&quot;MONTHLY RATED EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"For monthly rated employees, $22,500 is a key reference amount in calculating their severance payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bacfa097f6ad79f65b09995405789b70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;$22,500&quot;" target="&quot;SEVENTH SCHEDULE TABLE A&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The table specifies amounts related to severance payments for monthly rated employees, including $22,500 as a reference point."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bacfa097f6ad79f65b09995405789b70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;$22,500&quot;" target="&quot;僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"$22,500 是计算遣散费时的一个固定数值，与雇员的最后一个月工资或18日工资本金进行比较。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7ef856c5e83d9e91d386bd822201a8b7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;18 DAYS'" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The calculation for SEVERANCE PAYMENT can also be based on 18 days' wage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f00bfbc74cd988e98040394204cccd2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;18 DAYS'" target="&quot;12 MONTHS'">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The calculation based on 18 days' wage can be an alternative to the one based on 12 months' average salary for calculating SEVERANCE PAYMENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f00bfbc74cd988e98040394204cccd2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;12 MONTHS'" target="&quot;$22,500'S 12 TIMES'">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"$22,500 multiplied by 12 is the maximum limit for calculating SEVERANCE PAYMENT over a period of 12 months."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f00bfbc74cd988e98040394204cccd2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;$22,500'S 12 TIMES'" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The calculation for SEVERANCE PAYMENT can be based on $22,500 multiplied by 12."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f00bfbc74cd988e98040394204cccd2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVENTH SCHEDULE TABLE A&quot;" target="&quot;TABLE A IN THE SEVENTH SCHEDULE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both refer to Table A in the Seventh Schedule, which is a key document for calculating severance payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bacfa097f6ad79f65b09995405789b70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVENTH SCHEDULE TABLE A&quot;" target="&quot;APPLICABLE CEILING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Seventh Schedule Table A defines the maximum allowable severance payment amount based on specific periods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e42d72d79a5857b9a938418db1f215c6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVENTH SCHEDULE TABLE A&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The long service payment amount is subject to ceilings defined in Table A of the Seventh Schedule."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e2ea74deaae12a605f5ea78eff9b6bb9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TABLE A IN THE SEVENTH SCHEDULE&quot;" target="&quot;PRO RATA AS RESPECTS AN INCOMPLETE YEAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are components of the Seventh Schedule Table A in severance payment calculations for incomplete years."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bacfa097f6ad79f65b09995405789b70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2022年第4號第4條&quot;" target="&quot;1990年第41號第9條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 2022 amendment repealed provisions from the 1990 legislation, indicating a historical relationship between them in terms of severance payment calculations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bacfa097f6ad79f65b09995405789b70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;31G. AMOUNT OF SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;MONTHLY RATED EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The calculation for monthly rated employees is specified under the amount of severance payment clause."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bacfa097f6ad79f65b09995405789b70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;31G. AMOUNT OF SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;18 DAYS' WAGES BASED ON ANY 18 DAYS CHOSEN BY THE EMPLOYEE AND OCCURING DURING HIS LAST 30 NORMAL WORKING DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both methods are used to calculate severance payments, depending on the type of employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bacfa097f6ad79f65b09995405789b70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;31G. AMOUNT OF SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;PRO RATA AS RESPECTS AN INCOMPLETE YEAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The pro rata calculation applies when dealing with incomplete years under the severance payment clause."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bacfa097f6ad79f65b09995405789b70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MONTHLY RATED EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;30 NORMAL WORKING DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"For a monthly rated employee, both pre-transition and post-transition employment periods are calculated based on full months or chosen 18 days within 30 normal working days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8c7aef455ebf5c49827835bcb4e365e9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRO RATA AS RESPECTS AN INCOMPLETE YEAR&quot;" target="&quot;18 DAYS' WAGES BASED ON ANY 18 DAYS CHOSEN BY THE EMPLOYEE AND OCCURING DURING HIS LAST 30 NORMAL WORKING DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both methods are part of the severance payment calculation process, applicable in different scenarios."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bacfa097f6ad79f65b09995405789b70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPEALED 4 OF 2022 S. 4&quot;" target="&quot;51 OF 2000 S. 4&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The entity '51 OF 2000 S. 4' is related to the repealed section of 'REPEALED 4 OF 2022 S. 4', indicating that it was superseded by a new law."&lt;SEP&gt;"The entity 'REPEALED 4 OF 2022 S. 4' is related to the repealed section of '51 OF 2000 S. 4', indicating that it replaced or superseded a previous law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0898f084c7eaa0fec2a37dbafdfbf647</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPEALED 4 OF 2022 S. 4&quot;" target="&quot;41 OF 1990 S. 9&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The entity '41 OF 1990 S. 9' is related to the replaced section of 'REPEALED 4 OF 2022 S. 4', suggesting a historical context where laws were amended or repealed."&lt;SEP&gt;"The entity 'REPEALED 4 OF 2022 S. 4' is related to the replaced section of '41 OF 1990 S. 9', suggesting a historical context where laws were amended or repealed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0898f084c7eaa0fec2a37dbafdfbf647</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;51 OF 2000 S. 4&quot;" target="&quot;LONG-TERM SERVICE BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Repealed by a later enactment affecting the same topic as LONG-TERM SERVICE BENEFIT, indicating potential overlap or relevance to the benefit's definition."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-24fa2abbabb20643bcca00d03c443b72</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Severance payment is reduced by the aggregate amount of ORS benefits that are employer-funded (voluntary) and related to the employee's years of service."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ORS benefits are held in mandatory provident fund schemes and may be reduced by a part of the severance payment if they are attributable to the same years of service."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-60278fe3510d3896a76c8ed45d034e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd899e03ecc067de0edd74af6740db7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ORS benefits are employer-funded and can be affected by the terms in the employee's contract of employment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The contract of employment may lead to the payment of ORS benefits as a result of an employee's service."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employee's contract of employment determines whether ORS benefits are paid to or in respect of the employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5c317132f5543388aa4ec358d54fbcf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16880dc0f6b710adfcdbea0c6c5c09ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60278fe3510d3896a76c8ed45d034e51</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">33.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Certain ORS benefits are considered qualifying items for reducing the post- and pre-transition portions of the long service payment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Long service payment is related to ORS benefits as both are employer-funded and based on length of service."&lt;SEP&gt;"Long service payment may be reduced by the aggregate amount of employer-funded ORS benefits that relate to the employee's years of service."&lt;SEP&gt;"ORS benefits are qualifying items that can reduce the amount of long service payment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The long service payment may be affected by ORS benefits paid to an employee under their contract of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-233de206d4d440690ca3d19bf8ddb77c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad13daf2441a168160e4226aa7ac493d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c317132f5543388aa4ec358d54fbcf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d634411e44f3153b1f3217349599619c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dabef41d299eda51d77087c2ca170398</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;31YAA. GRATUITY OR BENEFIT TO BE REDUCED BY AMOUNT OF LONG SERVICE PAYMENT IN CERTAIN CASES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"该条款涉及雇主资助的(指定)ORS福利,并规定了其与长期服务金的关系。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3db531f9fed0b652cc40ad79eb2a48c6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;GRATUITIES BASED ON LENGTH OF SERVICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ORS and gratuities are related to the length of service, with ORS specifically mentioned as a type of gratuity."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-16880dc0f6b710adfcdbea0c6c5c09ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees have rights related to ORS benefits as per their employment contracts, specifically basic portion benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a23958c5eb862b357e8540d3c4c5afd6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;MODIFICATIONS TO PART VB&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The modifications to Part VB include changes related to ORS (Other Retirement Savings) benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-622dec92f9d3c73f201fbdc4fab3be5f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">11.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ORS and MPFS benefits are employer-funded under the employment contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both ORS and MPFS benefits can be qualifying items for reducing long service payment, indicating a relationship in the context of employee benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-233de206d4d440690ca3d19bf8ddb77c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e5131fef8ae89d5a0f48b17c1599d19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;DEATH BENEFIT PROVISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The death benefit provisions may affect the ORS benefits in certain circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c87228f0b6f2f82336ca7700cb45e5d8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (4)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (4)(a) includes gratuities or benefits that are employer-funded ORS benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b785a6d2d7fe1aa9d111846965f88378</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)(B)(I)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (1)(b)(i) refers to gratuities that are employer-funded ORS benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b785a6d2d7fe1aa9d111846965f88378</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)(B)(II)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (1)(b)(ii) includes employer-funded ORS benefits as qualifying items for Subsections (2) and (3)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b785a6d2d7fe1aa9d111846965f88378</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;PERSON B&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Person B becomes entitled to ORS benefits upon the death of an employee due to a contract-based agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d634411e44f3153b1f3217349599619c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 21, SUBS. NO. 4 OF 2022&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ORS benefits' payment and reduction are regulated by the same legal section mentioned above."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d634411e44f3153b1f3217349599619c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;ADMINISTRATOR OF AN OCCUPATIONAL RETIREMENT SCHEME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The administrator of an occupational retirement scheme pays ORS benefits to PERSON B based on certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d634411e44f3153b1f3217349599619c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">24.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"MPFS benefits can be used in calculating severance payments, particularly those that are mandatory and funded by employers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Severance payment is reduced by the aggregate amount of MPFS benefits that are employer-funded (specified) and related to the employee's years of service."&lt;SEP&gt;"The MPFS benefits, being employer-funded and held in mandatory provident fund schemes, may be reduced by a part of the severance payment if they are attributable to the same years of service."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-16880dc0f6b710adfcdbea0c6c5c09ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60278fe3510d3896a76c8ed45d034e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd899e03ecc067de0edd74af6740db7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The contract of employment may involve MPFS benefits being held or paid through mandatory provident fund schemes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employee's contract of employment determines whether MPFS benefits are held in mandatory provident fund schemes for the employee, or have been paid to or in respect of the employee."&lt;SEP&gt;"The operation of an employee's contract of employment may lead to MPFS benefits being held or paid under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5c317132f5543388aa4ec358d54fbcf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16880dc0f6b710adfcdbea0c6c5c09ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60278fe3510d3896a76c8ed45d034e51</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">24.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Long service payment is linked with MPFS benefits, as they share similar funding sources and conditions for entitlement."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPFS benefits are also qualifying items that can affect the long service payment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Some MPFS benefits serve as qualifying items that can reduce the post- and pre-transition portions of the long service payment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The long service payment might be impacted if MPFS benefits are held in mandatory provident fund schemes for the employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5c317132f5543388aa4ec358d54fbcf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dabef41d299eda51d77087c2ca170398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d634411e44f3153b1f3217349599619c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-233de206d4d440690ca3d19bf8ddb77c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;MANDATORY PROVIDENT FUND SCHEMES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">22.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"MPFS benefits are held in mandatory provident fund schemes or paid directly to the employee."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPFS benefits are held in mandatory provident fund schemes, which are governed by the terms and conditions of these schemes."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPFS benefits are held or paid through mandatory provident fund schemes, indicating a direct relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5c317132f5543388aa4ec358d54fbcf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16880dc0f6b710adfcdbea0c6c5c09ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad13daf2441a168160e4226aa7ac493d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;31YAA. GRATUITY OR BENEFIT TO BE REDUCED BY AMOUNT OF LONG SERVICE PAYMENT IN CERTAIN CASES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"该条款涉及雇主资助的(自愿)MPFS福利,并规定了其与长期服务金的关系。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3db531f9fed0b652cc40ad79eb2a48c6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;STRONGLY FUNDED PENSION SCHEMES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"MPFS benefits are a type of pension schemes, specifically employer-funded (mandatory) MPFS benefits as mentioned in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a23958c5eb862b357e8540d3c4c5afd6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employee has a right to receive MPFS benefits due to the implementation of their employment contract,"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a23958c5eb862b357e8540d3c4c5afd6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;MODIFICATIONS TO PART VB&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similarly, the modifications to Part VB also involve adjustments to MPFS (Modified Provident Fund Scheme) benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-622dec92f9d3c73f201fbdc4fab3be5f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;LONG-TERM SERVICE FUND&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Long-term service fund provisions could impact MPFS benefits, particularly regarding deductions and eligibility conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c87228f0b6f2f82336ca7700cb45e5d8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (4)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (4)(a) includes gratuities or benefits that are employer-funded MPFS benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b785a6d2d7fe1aa9d111846965f88378</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (1)(B)(III)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsection (1)(b)(iii) covers employer-funded MPFS benefits, which are relevant to gratuities or benefits under Subsections (2) and (3)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b785a6d2d7fe1aa9d111846965f88378</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;PERSON B&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similar to ORS benefits, Person B is also eligible for MPFS benefits after the death of an employee under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d634411e44f3153b1f3217349599619c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 21, SUBS. NO. 4 OF 2022&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The rules for MPFS benefits also follow from Section 21, Subsection No. 4 of 2022."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d634411e44f3153b1f3217349599619c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;APPROVED TRUSTEE OF A MANDATORY PROVIDENT FUND SCHEME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An approved trustee of a mandatory provident fund scheme provides MPFS benefits to PERSON B under specific circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d634411e44f3153b1f3217349599619c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRATUITIES&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Severance payment is reduced by the aggregate amount of gratuities based on length of service."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-60278fe3510d3896a76c8ed45d034e51</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRATUITIES&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Gratuities based on length of service may be paid due to the operation of an employee's contract of employment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The operation of the employee's contract of employment determines whether gratuities based on length of service are paid to the employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5c317132f5543388aa4ec358d54fbcf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60278fe3510d3896a76c8ed45d034e51</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRATUITIES&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31IA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'gratuity' is defined in the context where it may be reduced by a severance payment if attributable to the same years of service."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c24d050bd3e4419e71408fc656cab32</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRATUITIES&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">24.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Gratuities may be used for a reduction under subsection (2) of the long service payment if they relate to the employee's years of service and have not been previously reduced."&lt;SEP&gt;"Long service payment may be reduced by the aggregate amount of gratuities that relate to the employee's years of service."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Long Service Payment may be reduced by gratuities based on the employee's length of service due to their death."&lt;SEP&gt;"The long service payment may be reduced by the amount of gratuities in certain cases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5c317132f5543388aa4ec358d54fbcf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38034baf57d26ec704e02e12e81cdf6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad13daf2441a168160e4226aa7ac493d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;NEW OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The new owner can offer to renew or re-engage the employee under a new contract, which is directly related to their contractual relationship with the employee."&lt;SEP&gt;"The new owner may renew or re-engage employees under their terms, potentially substituting themselves for the previous owner in employment contracts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-781090deea1d567c616cff8f0c0ae1ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92eb9fce002800330c9f680d468f081b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;PREVIOUS OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The previous owner has the authority to terminate the employee's contract of employment according to section 6 or 7."&lt;SEP&gt;"The previous owner's role in offering renewal or re-engagement of employment is contrasted and compared with that of the new owner, indicating a direct historical context for the current situation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-781090deea1d567c616cff8f0c0ae1ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92eb9fce002800330c9f680d468f081b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;RENEWAL OR RE-ENGAGEMENT BY THE PREVIOUS OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PREVIOUS OWNER can renew or re-engage under a new contract of employment with the substitution of the new owner for the previous owner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;OFFER TO RENEW OR RE-ENGAGE UNDER A NEW CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The OFFER TO RENEW OR RE-ENGAGE is made by the new or previous owner to continue the employment contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;REFUSAL OF OFFER BY THE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The REFUSAL OF OFFER indicates a decision from the employee not to accept the renewal or re-engagement offer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"COURT also takes into account the employee's contract in determining valid reasons for dismissal or variation under section 32K, similar to LABOUR TRIBUNAL as per section 32L."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc2894a439737cb35869b760804ff684</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;32K&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 32K refers to the terms of an employee's contract that can be varied or dismissed based on certain conditions, impacting the length of qualifying service as per section 32L."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc2894a439737cb35869b760804ff684</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;32L&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 32L specifies how the circumstances of an employee's contract are considered in determining claims related to dismissal or variation, impacting rights and benefits under this Ordinance as per section 32K."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dc2894a439737cb35869b760804ff684</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;COMMENCEMENT DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commencement Date determines when the Employment (Amendment) Ordinance applies to Employee's Contract of Employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a365e751a6908c5178b1168febad9bcd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;31ZEA SECTION&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 31ZEA provides additional context for severance payment reductions, specifically mentioning ORS benefits and MPFS benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-60278fe3510d3896a76c8ed45d034e51</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;31ZEA SECTION&quot;" target="&quot;SCHEDULE 11, SECTION 5&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 31ZEA refers to Schedule 11, Section 5 for additional information or related provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5c317132f5543388aa4ec358d54fbcf1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;31ZEA SECTION&quot;" target="&quot;GRATUITIES BASED ON LENGTH OF SERVICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both sections deal with gratuities based on length of service, indicating their interrelation in the context of employee benefits and payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0b522ee3e92b516e9befd9d3479f215</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SCHEDULE 11, SECTION 3&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Schedule 11, Section 3 provides further details on the conditions under which gratuities are considered in severance payment reductions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-60278fe3510d3896a76c8ed45d034e51</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SCHEDULE 11, SECTION 3&quot;" target="&quot;REVISED STATUTE 2022 NO. 4 ARTICLE 5&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Schedule 11, Section 3 is also referenced in the note of Article 5, suggesting a related provision or context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-399bbc7d38c1ce5fe769283b5a7baa4d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SCHEDULE 11, SECTION 3&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31ZEA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both provisions are mentioned together in the notes, implying they might be part of the same legal framework or context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-399bbc7d38c1ce5fe769283b5a7baa4d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2022 YEAR 4 REGULATION, SECTION 5&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 5 of Regulation 4 of 2022 replaces and updates the rules for reducing severance payments by gratuities and benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-60278fe3510d3896a76c8ed45d034e51</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REVISED STATUTE 2022 NO. 4 ARTICLE 5&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31ZEA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 31ZEA is referenced in the note of Article 5, indicating a related provision."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-399bbc7d38c1ce5fe769283b5a7baa4d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31ZEA&quot;" target="&quot;SCHEDULE 11.31ZEA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"SECTION 31ZEA is mentioned in SCHEDULE 11.31ZEA, indicating a related section within the schedule."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8cb52dd4a9b2981de387c70ee06f029</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31ZEA&quot;" target="&quot;APPENDIX 11 SECTION 5&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 31ZEA and Appendix 11 Section 5 are referenced together, indicating a related context in the legal framework."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a21b404a5b0d354defe8dd03eb692b6b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31IA&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (SPECIFIED) ORS BENEFITS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'employer-funded (specified) ORS benefits' is defined in the context where it may be reduced by a severance payment if attributable to the same years of service."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c24d050bd3e4419e71408fc656cab32</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31IA&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (VOLUNTARY) MPFS BENEFITS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'employer-funded (voluntary) MPFS benefits' is defined in the context where it may be reduced by a severance payment if attributable to the same years of service."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c24d050bd3e4419e71408fc656cab32</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31IA&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The section discusses how a 'severance payment' can reduce other benefits and gratuities if they are related to the same period of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c24d050bd3e4419e71408fc656cab32</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31IA&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1990&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 1990 is the legislative context for Section 31IA, providing its legal basis and scope."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-772d5b97625d81ec1623236fca58771c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (SPECIFIED) ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The long service payment may be reduced by employer-funded (specified) ORS benefits that relate to the employee’s years of service."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0b522ee3e92b516e9befd9d3479f215</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (SPECIFIED) ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;SCHEDULE 11 SECTION 5&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 5 of Schedule 11 specifies conditions for employer-funded (specified) ORS benefits, which are related to the employee’s years of service."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0b522ee3e92b516e9befd9d3479f215</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (VOLUNTARY) MPFS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The long service payment may also consider employer-funded (voluntary) MPFS benefits, which are related to the employee’s years of service."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0b522ee3e92b516e9befd9d3479f215</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31J&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31C(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both sections are related as they both deal with the continuity of employment after a change in business ownership, and SECTION 31C(2) is referenced within SECTION 31J."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8cb52dd4a9b2981de387c70ee06f029</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31D(2)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31C(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both sections are related as they deal with the continuity of employment after a change in business ownership; SECTION 31D(2) is specifically mentioned to have effect even if replaced by new provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8cb52dd4a9b2981de387c70ee06f029</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31D(2)&quot;" target="&quot;NEW OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"New owner may use Section 31D(2) to renew employment contracts, maintaining the continuity of the previous owner’s actions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-be5c7596bb8e4301da4cc603ef1a2b55</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RUI XIN&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT RENEWAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"RUI XIN is involved in the process of renewing employment contracts with employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6eb34df6176f74b437e7db047dc2d759</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT RENEWAL&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS OWNERSHIP CHANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The change in business ownership may affect the terms and conditions related to employment contract renewal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6eb34df6176f74b437e7db047dc2d759</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS OWNERSHIP CHANGE&quot;" target="&quot;PERSON A, PERSON B&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business ownership change can lead to situations where Person B (likely a beneficiary or successor) may be involved due to legal implications post-ownership transfer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2193ccb19ec3e792d874a92951eae0f7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS OWNERSHIP CHANGE&quot;" target="&quot;32A(1)(C)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"32A(1)(C) refers to circumstances where an employee is dismissed due to business ownership change."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9ddecf99bc0bca06387d96224afeaf4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS OWNERSHIP CHANGE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT of an employee may be affected by BUSINESS OWNERSHIP CHANGE as per legal provisions like 32D(1,2)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9ddecf99bc0bca06387d96224afeaf4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS OWNERSHIP CHANGE&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL TERMS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal terms and provisions are relevant to understanding BUSINESS OWNERSHIP CHANGE, including its impact on employees' contracts as per 32D(1-3)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9ddecf99bc0bca06387d96224afeaf4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS OWNERSHIP CHANGE&quot;" target="&quot;FORMER OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business ownership change directly affects the status of the former owner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1cb0098fa2f01839bce9b10d85c36181</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS OWNERSHIP CHANGE&quot;" target="&quot;NEW OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"New ownership of Rongxin involves changes in business operations and potentially employee contracts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1cb0098fa2f01839bce9b10d85c36181</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHANGE OF OWNERSHIP OF BUSINESS&quot;" target="&quot;PREVIOUS OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">24.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PREVIOUS OWNER is involved before the business ownership change, terminating the employment contract according to section 6 or 7."&lt;SEP&gt;"The change of ownership involves the previous owner who terminates the employee's contract before the business is owned by a new entity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The concept of change in ownership involves the previous owner who terminates the employee's contract according to section 6 or 7."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-781090deea1d567c616cff8f0c0ae1ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be5c7596bb8e4301da4cc603ef1a2b55</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHANGE OF OWNERSHIP OF BUSINESS&quot;" target="&quot;NEW OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">27.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"New Owner is introduced as someone who takes over business ownership post-change and may renew an employee’s contract under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"New owner takes over after the ownership changes, potentially renewing or re-engaging employees under different terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The NEW OWNER takes over after the business ownership change and can renew or re-engage under a new contract of employment with the substitution of the new owner for the previous owner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-781090deea1d567c616cff8f0c0ae1ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be5c7596bb8e4301da4cc603ef1a2b55</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHANGE OF OWNERSHIP OF BUSINESS&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 6 OR 7&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 6 and 7 provide conditions under which a change in business ownership can lead to termination of an employee’s contract by the previous owner."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sections 6 and 7 are used by the PREVIOUS OWNER to terminate an employment contract during business ownership change."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-781090deea1d567c616cff8f0c0ae1ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd0ed9e34d0172cc5c8b4ab3e5316192</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREVIOUS OWNER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The previous owner terminates the employee's contract as part of the business ownership change."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-be5c7596bb8e4301da4cc603ef1a2b55</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREVIOUS OWNER&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 6 OR 7&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Previous owner uses Section 6 or 7 to terminate employee's contract during ownership change."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-be5c7596bb8e4301da4cc603ef1a2b55</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREVIOUS OWNER&quot;" target="&quot;NEW OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The transition from the previous owner to the new owner is central to understanding how offers are made and responded to, as per SECTION 32C(1) and (2). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8bab69b3c78835240d5782d563ec35c1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEW OWNER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"New owner may renew or re-engage employees after taking over the business, potentially affecting their employment status."&lt;SEP&gt;"The NEW OWNER can enter into a new employment contract with the EMPLOYEE or renew their existing one after taking over business ownership."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9ddecf99bc0bca06387d96224afeaf4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be5c7596bb8e4301da4cc603ef1a2b55</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEW OWNER&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS CHANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A business change can lead to a new owner who may offer contract renewals or re-engagements, thus linking these concepts closely in terms of legal and operational contexts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92eb9fce002800330c9f680d468f081b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEW OWNER&quot;" target="&quot;FORMER OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A new owner may continue or renew an employee's contract after taking over from the former owner, treating it as if the original employer had done so."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0276e1b514303ef83e330aacbd8bcf95</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEW OWNER&quot;" target="&quot;PREDECESSOR OWNER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PREDECESSOR OWNER's business ownership changes, leading to the NEW OWNER becoming the new owner of part or all of the business."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9ddecf99bc0bca06387d96224afeaf4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEW OWNER&quot;" target="&quot;RONGXIN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"New owner takes over from the former owner after the business ownership change."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1cb0098fa2f01839bce9b10d85c36181</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31C(2) OR (3)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employee's refusal to accept new terms from the new owner triggers Section 31C(2) or (3), impacting their employment status."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-be5c7596bb8e4301da4cc603ef1a2b55</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT RENEWAL&quot;" target="&quot;RE-ENGAGEMENT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are related as they pertain to the new owner's actions towards renewing or re-engaging an employee, but with different contractual implications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92eb9fce002800330c9f680d468f081b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;相聯公司&quot;" target="&quot;31K&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 31K refers to the concept of associated companies, which is relevant when discussing employment contracts within such structures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92eb9fce002800330c9f680d468f081b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;相聯公司&quot;" target="&quot;附屬公司&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Affiliated companies are considered as related entities under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;相聯公司&quot;" target="&quot;附屬公司 (SUBSIDIARY)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據《公司條例》(第622章), 一間公司的附屬公司也被視為相聯公司。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bc7050cecd4e7d8b17b6622358415e8f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;相聯公司 (1)&quot;" target="&quot;僱主&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer refers to a company or its associated companies as mentioned in section 31K(1)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;前擁有人&quot;" target="&quot;新擁有人&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The transfer of ownership between former and new owners does not affect the implementation of Section 31J."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第31B(2)條&quot;" target="&quot;解僱&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Termination is considered under specific conditions outlined in Article 31B(2)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;解僱&quot;" target="&quot;休假日&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"解僱的情況下,根據第VIII部須支付的任何假日薪酬是終止僱傭金的一部分。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c82c895f7b30d4831c428126a0af9486</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;解僱&quot;" target="&quot;續訂或新訂合約(視屬何情況而定)的條文與緊接僱主死亡前的有效合約的相應條文無異&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據第4款規定，如果續訂或重新聘用合同條款與原有效合同完全一致，則不視為解僱。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cad6d0a2eed4fbaf59a6253fe84df6ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;解僱&quot;" target="&quot;僱主死亡&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"已故僱主死亡可能導致僱員被視為遭解僱，但某些情況下續訂或重新聘用可避免此結果。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cad6d0a2eed4fbaf59a6253fe84df6ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主的變更&quot;" target="&quot;僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employee's employment period continues uninterrupted despite changes in the employer, if both are associated companies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7411d1f85f0eff7988eea8a8452a906d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSOCIATED COMPANIES&quot;" target="&quot;COMPANY (第622章)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'associated companies' as defined in Article 15 of Chapter 622 refers to companies that are related through ownership or control, impacting employment terms and conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-01e8dd2cd7216b43532ed7037814b54b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSOCIATED COMPANIES&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSIDIARY (第15條)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A subsidiary is considered an associated company under the definition provided in Chapter 622 Article 15, affecting employee re-engagement and dismissal policies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-01e8dd2cd7216b43532ed7037814b54b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSOCIATED COMPANIES&quot;" target="&quot;RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Re-engagement policies can involve or exclude associated companies based on employment continuity and conditions as defined by related entities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-01e8dd2cd7216b43532ed7037814b54b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSOCIATED COMPANIES&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSIDIARY (附屬公司)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A subsidiary is considered an associated company of another if it shares the same ultimate parent company."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2351949864b29078618f803ef4d2c6cb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSOCIATED COMPANIES&quot;" target="&quot;IMPLIED OR CONSTRUCTIVE TERMINATION OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of implied or constructive termination can apply in situations involving associated companies, especially when considering the continuity of employment across such entities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2351949864b29078618f803ef4d2c6cb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSOCIATED COMPANIES&quot;" target="&quot;THE EMPLOYER (COMPANY)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer can be an associated company that includes its subsidiaries in the context of employment contracts and renewals under certain sections, as per The Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2c28e990fb442886ba69eb65de9d2282</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSOCIATED COMPANIES&quot;" target="&quot;THE COMPANIES ORDINANCE (CAP. 622)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'associated companies' is defined in the context of The Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622), providing a legal framework for understanding associated company relationships and their implications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2c28e990fb442886ba69eb65de9d2282</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ENGAGEMENT OF THE EMPLOYEE BY A SUCCESSOR OR ASSOCIATED COMPANY OF THE ORIGINAL EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The engagement is treated as re-engagement with the original employer under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-420f23bd6d18962ea805d721d98c3ed6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ENGAGEMENT OF THE EMPLOYEE BY A SUCCESSOR OR ASSOCIATED COMPANY OF THE ORIGINAL EMPLOYER IS TREATED AS RE-ENGAGEMENT IN COMPLIANCE WITH THE PRINCIPAL ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The engagement must be treated as re-engagement under specific terms and conditions outlined in the agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-420f23bd6d18962ea805d721d98c3ed6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSIDIARY (附屬公司)&quot;" target="&quot;PARENT COMPANY (母公司)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A subsidiary company has a parent company as defined by the Companies Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSIDIARY (附屬公司)&quot;" target="&quot;COMPANIES ORDINANCE (第622章)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subsidiary is defined under the Companies Ordinance for specific legal purposes related to company relationships and terminations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2351949864b29078618f803ef4d2c6cb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSOCIATED COMPANIES (相聯公司)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT RELATIONSHIP DYNAMICS (僱傭關係動態)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employment relationship dynamics are affected when an employee moves between associated companies, maintaining continuity of service."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTUAL TERMINATION (合同终止)&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL RULES (法律規則)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal rules govern how contract terminations are handled, including those involving subsidiaries."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TERMINATION OF CONTRACT (合同終止)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSIDIARY COMPANY (附屬公司)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A subsidiary company can be involved in the termination of contracts as per legal rules and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT RELATIONSHIP (僱傭關係)&quot;" target="&quot;RENEWAL OF CONTRACT (續約)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employment relationships can involve the renewal of contracts as a part of ongoing employment continuity."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HIRE (聘用)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTINUITY (僱傭關係連續性)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The act of hiring is related to maintaining continuous employment relations over time."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT RENEWAL (僱傭合約續訂)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTUAL AGREEMENT (合同協議)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Renewal of employment contracts is a form of contractual agreement between parties involved in the employment relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTUAL AGREEMENT (合同協議)&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL REGULATION (法律規範)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contractual agreements are subject to legal regulations and rules, ensuring their validity and enforceability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2adc43ad09777ee724aaeaf83575ad0a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTUAL AGREEMENT (合同協議)&quot;" target="&quot;DIVISION 4 —— PAYMENT CLAIMS AND PAYMENT RESPONSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contractual Agreements, including Division 4, define and govern payment claims and responses in construction contracts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-104729af58e2197afbd033252a8317e6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL REGULATION (法律規範)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCESS (仲裁程序)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal regulations govern the process of arbitration, ensuring its fairness and effectiveness."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efd35e44f40ed90831a05d2c28acb9a5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISMISSAL BY REASON OF REDUNDANCY&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If a contract of employment is not renewed and an employee is not re-engaged due to circumstances wholly or mainly attributable to one or more specified conditions, the termination can be considered dismissal by reason of redundancy."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a783557f86fea333101af802aa41e0a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31B(2)(A)&quot;" target="&quot;DEATH OF EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 31B(2)(A) is relevant to situations involving the death of an employer as per Section 31M."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d33baa15beb160832b6e2302162f04d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEATH OF EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT TERMINATION DUE TO EMPLOYER'S ACT/EVENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The death of the employer is an event that can terminate an employment contract, as per legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-96ecd392e516343d8ffd40e3611e0e8f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEATH OF EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PERSONAL REPRESENTATIVE OF THE DECEASED EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The personal representative of the deceased employer is involved in handling matters related to the death of the employer, such as business ownership transfer and employment contract renewal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fbef4b639390d1d66289078a98204ee1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEATH OF EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT RENEWAL/RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The death of the employer can lead to changes in employment contracts through re-engagement or renewal by a personal representative, which affects employee status and rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fbef4b639390d1d66289078a98204ee1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEATH OF EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"In cases where an employee is dismissed due to the death of their employer, they may not be entitled to severance payment if re-engaged or renewed within 4 weeks by a personal representative."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fbef4b639390d1d66289078a98204ee1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEATH OF EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PERSONAL REPRESENTATIVE OF DECEASED EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The death of the employer involves references to actions by personal representatives, such as renewal or re-engagement and offers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c826449cd8715ca847fb4ea3433d8bf1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEATH OF EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT PROTECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Death of an employer affects employment protection claims that can be pursued by the employee against the personal representative of the deceased employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c826449cd8715ca847fb4ea3433d8bf1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REDUNDANCY PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;SECRETARY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Redundancy payments are regulated and potentially influenced by decisions of the Secretary regarding claims and extensions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d33baa15beb160832b6e2302162f04d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGISTRAR OF THE MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD ORDINANCE (CAP. 453)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Registrar is responsible for handling claims related to minor employment disputes, including those involving severance payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Registrar operates under the Minor Employment Claims Adjudication Board Ordinance, which outlines his responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-11d596f17d04a1402f9a7eda05284076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9277263fe4be5c215993320cc63c410</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGISTRAR OF THE MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;BANKRUPTCY ORDINANCE (CAP. 6)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">3.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Although not directly related, both roles involve regulatory functions within the legal and financial systems of Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c9277263fe4be5c215993320cc63c410</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD ORDINANCE (CAP. 453)&quot;" target="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (CAP. 25)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ordinances are part of the legal framework for labour disputes, with one focusing on general tribunal processes and the other specifically on minor employment claims adjudication."&lt;SEP&gt;"These ordinances govern the procedures for handling employment claims, with CAP. 453 focusing on minor cases and CAP. 25 covering a broader range of labor disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06d23d2b54047f6e0d92f6798bcab7c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9277263fe4be5c215993320cc63c410</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD ORDINANCE (CAP. 453)&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Claims for severance payment can be made to the Registrar of the Minor Employment Claims Adjudication Board under this ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-11d596f17d04a1402f9a7eda05284076</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD ORDINANCE (CAP. 453)&quot;" target="&quot;LABOUR RELATIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 55)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ordinances are part of the legal framework for labour disputes, with one focusing on broader relations and the other specifically on minor employment claims adjudication."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06d23d2b54047f6e0d92f6798bcab7c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (CAP. 25)&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTRAR OF THE LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">25.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Labour Tribunal Registrar operates under the Labour Tribunal Ordinance, handling claims as specified in this ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Registrar of the Labour Tribunal is an official body established under the Labour Tribunal Ordinance that handles claims and disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Registrar processes claims under the Labour Tribunal Ordinance, which can include matters concerning severance payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-11d596f17d04a1402f9a7eda05284076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9277263fe4be5c215993320cc63c410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adb3767092cbae0c3a6518107e6865b5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (CAP. 25)&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Labour Tribunal Ordinance allows claims for severance payments to be filed with the Registrar of the Labour Tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-11d596f17d04a1402f9a7eda05284076</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (CAP. 25)&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COMMISSIONER's reports are based on information obtained in connection with conciliations held under the LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (Cap. 25)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner plays a role in approving extensions for filing claims as per section 32I of the Labour Tribunal Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-236ae534fe116485f7714d0a24fe4030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adb3767092cbae0c3a6518107e6865b5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (CAP. 25)&quot;" target="&quot;32J. JURISDICTION OF LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Labour Tribunal Ordinance (Cap. 25) establishes the jurisdiction for claims made by employees under this Part."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1517e5d276f14e1b4ebe83fe9ad0d435</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (CAP. 25)&quot;" target="&quot;32K. 解僱或更改僱傭合約條款的理由&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Labour Tribunal Ordinance (Cap. 25) provides the reasons for which an employer may lawfully terminate employment or amend contract terms under this Part."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1517e5d276f14e1b4ebe83fe9ad0d435</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (CAP. 25)&quot;" target="&quot;CONCILIATION HELD UNDER THE LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONCILIATION HELD UNDER THE LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE is a process governed by the LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (Cap. 25)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-236ae534fe116485f7714d0a24fe4030</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (CAP. 25)&quot;" target="&quot;REINSTATEMENT ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The REINSTATEMENT ORDER is an order made under the LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (Cap. 25), specifying terms for reinstating employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-236ae534fe116485f7714d0a24fe4030</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (CAP. 25)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYEE's rights and entitlements under the LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (Cap. 25) are considered in reinstatement orders."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-236ae534fe116485f7714d0a24fe4030</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (CAP. 25)&quot;" target="&quot;LABOUR RELATIONS ORDINANCE (CAP. 55)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ordinances deal with labour relations, one focusing on dispute resolution and the other on broader labour rights and collective bargaining."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06d23d2b54047f6e0d92f6798bcab7c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (CAP. 25)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ordinances are part of the broader legal system addressing employee rights, though they focus on different aspects such as dispute resolution versus compensation for injuries or illnesses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06d23d2b54047f6e0d92f6798bcab7c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL ORDINANCE (CAP. 25)&quot;" target="&quot;PNEUMOCONIOSIS AND MESOTHELIOMA (COMPENSATION) ORDINANCE (CAP. 360)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ordinances are part of the legal framework addressing employee rights and compensation, though they focus on different health issues such as disputes resolution versus specific occupational diseases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06d23d2b54047f6e0d92f6798bcab7c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGISTRAR OF THE LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;BANKING INDUSTRY (UNDER THE BANKING ORDANACE CAP.155)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">2.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similarly, these roles are part of broader regulatory frameworks but do not have a direct relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c9277263fe4be5c215993320cc63c410</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGISTRAR OF THE LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;《勞資審裁處條例》(第25章)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Registrar of the Labour Tribunal is an official body established under The Labour Tribunal Ordinance (Cap. 25)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-adb3767092cbae0c3a6518107e6865b5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGISTRAR OF THE LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT RELATIONS AMENDMENT REGULATION 1 OF 2013&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employment Relations Amendment Regulation 1 of 2013 impacts the procedures and jurisdiction handled by the Registrar of the Labour Tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a68f0496b4d3967e4dee08ee2a743063</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGISTRAR OF THE LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;JUSTICE PRESIDENT OF THE LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Justice President of the Labour Tribunal has authority over the Registrar in terms of judicial decisions and procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a68f0496b4d3967e4dee08ee2a743063</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BANK WITHIN THE MEANING OF SECTION 2 OF THE BANKING ORDINANCE (CAP. 155)&quot;" target="&quot;CHEQUE, MONEY ORDER OR POSTAL ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Payments can be made by cheque, money order or postal order into an account with a bank within the meaning of section 2 of the Banking Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-88b2609f36389403179e27bcc11b4123</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BANK WITHIN THE MEANING OF SECTION 2 OF THE BANKING ORDINANCE (CAP. 155)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 2 OF THE BANKING ORDINANCE (CAP. 155)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition of a bank within the meaning of section 2 is provided by the BANKING ORDINANCE (CAP. 155)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-88b2609f36389403179e27bcc11b4123</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHEQUE, MONEY ORDER OR POSTAL ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Cheque, money order or postal order are alternative methods for making long service payments when the recipient consents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3aa1d2d981153f366e07b9a78ba0c7ce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SMALL AMOUNT DISPUTE RESOLUTION OFFICE OR LABOUR RELATIONS BOARD&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAY DETAIL STATEMENT 31P&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SEVERANCE PAY DETAIL STATEMENT 31P may be based on a decision from the SMALL AMOUNT DISPUTE RESOLUTION OFFICE or LABOUR RELATIONS BOARD."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-88b2609f36389403179e27bcc11b4123</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVERANCE PAY DETAIL STATEMENT 31P&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYEE is required to receive a SEVERANCE PAY DETAIL STATEMENT 31P when being paid severance pay, unless it's based on an arbitration decision."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-88b2609f36389403179e27bcc11b4123</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD OR LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYEE can seek a decision from MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD or Labour Tribunal regarding severance payment disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Minor Employment Claims Adjudication Board or Labour Tribunal can make awards in favour of the employee regarding wage claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a544f1422493c38b567ef610eadf02d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d94d21b562915559fff6272dbbdb3b70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD OR LABOUR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD or Labour Tribunal may direct payment of WAGES if an employee files a claim."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9a160d4a92860e123b37153b47528d3e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)(A)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER GIVING CONSENT TO DETERMINE CLAIM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If the employer does not give written consent, the Commissioner cannot proceed with determining the claim."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2914073de37bf0e7df21cb9ca18483a2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (2)(A)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (4)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both subsections deal with penalties for false statements, but subsection 4(A) specifies different levels based on prior convictions. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-82a3bfa1b02f074277b3b1a27f3afcb2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (4)(A)&quot;" target="&quot;31YC条款&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 31YC clause refers to the application of subsections related to gratuities, benefits, and long service payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b785a6d2d7fe1aa9d111846965f88378</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART VB&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Part VB includes provisions related to long service payments. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-82a3bfa1b02f074277b3b1a27f3afcb2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART VB&quot;" target="&quot;1985年第76號第8條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 1985 legislation (No. 76 Article 8) adds Part VB to the legal framework."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-985c71a2aa2037adf4ce25fd3c8c12de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART VB&quot;" target="&quot;ENTITLEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Entitlement involves long service payment payable under Part VB."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1c30b39b26dc22df210f2ea63b93552</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART VB&quot;" target="&quot;MODIFICATIONS TO PART VB&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Modifications to Part VB are directly related as it specifies changes or amendments made to Part VB."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-622dec92f9d3c73f201fbdc4fab3be5f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;1997年第74号第10条修订&quot;" target="&quot;长期服务金条款修改&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 1997 amendment (No. 74 Article 10 revision) modifies certain clauses related to long service payments, specifically regarding termination conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-985c71a2aa2037adf4ce25fd3c8c12de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;1993年第61号第5条修订&quot;" target="&quot;长期服务金条款修改&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 1993 amendment (No. 61 Article 5 revision) also modifies the terms for long service payments, particularly concerning employment duration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-985c71a2aa2037adf4ce25fd3c8c12de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;1995年第65号第2条修订&quot;" target="&quot;长期服务金条款修改&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 1995 amendment (No. 65 Article 2 revision) further modifies the terms for long service payments, specifically regarding age and employment duration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-985c71a2aa2037adf4ce25fd3c8c12de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;1991年第105号第2条修订&quot;" target="&quot;长期服务金条款修改&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 1991 amendment (No. 105 Article 2 revision) revises the terms for long service payments, particularly concerning termination conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-985c71a2aa2037adf4ce25fd3c8c12de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;1997年第74号第10条废除&quot;" target="&quot;长期服务金条款修改&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 1997 amendment (No. 74 Article 10 abolition) removes certain clauses related to long service payments, indicating a change in the legal framework."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-985c71a2aa2037adf4ce25fd3c8c12de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2006年第16号第6条代替&quot;" target="&quot;长期服务金条款修改&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 2006 amendment (No. 16 Article 6 replacement) replaces certain clauses related to long service payments, indicating an update in the legal provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-985c71a2aa2037adf4ce25fd3c8c12de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;註冊醫生或註冊中醫&quot;" target="&quot;僱主&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"僱主指名註冊醫生或註冊中醫進行身體檢查,以評估僱員是否適合工作。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-20a95471afd1aaf3812ba594d6c8b0d4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;醫學專家&quot;" target="&quot;處長&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"處長在諮詢其認為所需的醫學專家後作出決定。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f9abcb1aa4ccb5d467cb0175ca3011bc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 10(AA)(II)&quot;" target="&quot;REVISED BY LEGISLATION (1991, 2006, 1997)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 10(aa)(ii) was revised by legislation in 1991, 2006, and 1997."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bc7d719876b6f50011d4a77def5a2428</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A continuous employment contract is a factor in determining eligibility for long service payment based on the employee's work history with the same employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bc7d719876b6f50011d4a77def5a2428</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS EMPLOYMENT YEAR NUMBER (5 YEARS) FOR DEATH ENTITLEMENT CALCULATION&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner uses the continuous employment year number to calculate entitlement for long service payment in case of an employee's death, if certain conditions are met."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bc7d719876b6f50011d4a77def5a2428</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG-TERM SERVICE BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S SPOUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The long-term service benefit is payable to the employee's spouse if the employee dies and leaves no children or parents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0b3d407961e6ed952b04345f5d32a45</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG-TERM SERVICE BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S CHILDREN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The long-term service benefit is payable to the employee's children if the employee dies without leaving a spouse or parents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0b3d407961e6ed952b04345f5d32a45</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG-TERM SERVICE BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S PARENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The long-term service benefit is payable to the employee's parents if the employee dies without leaving a spouse, children, or any other beneficiaries mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0b3d407961e6ed952b04345f5d32a45</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG-TERM SERVICE BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL REPRESENTATIVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If there are no surviving spouse, children, or parents, the legal representative can claim the long-term service benefit on behalf of the deceased employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0b3d407961e6ed952b04345f5d32a45</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG-TERM SERVICE BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;4 OF 2022 S. 9&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 4 of the 2022 legislation may impact long-term service benefits, though specific details are not provided in this text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-24fa2abbabb20643bcca00d03c443b72</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG-TERM SERVICE BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;31Y&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 31Y provides conditions under which long-term service benefits may be adjusted based on certain payments and contributions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-24fa2abbabb20643bcca00d03c443b72</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG-TERM SERVICE BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;RETIREMENT AGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Long-term service benefit can be affected by the employee's retirement age and conditions of employment under continuous contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da3daa00f8a571e7a58b273ea6df48ea</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S SPOUSE&quot;" target="&quot;PROOF OF RELATIONSHIP DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A proof of relationship document is required for the spouse to claim the long-term service benefit as evidence of their marital status with the deceased employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0b3d407961e6ed952b04345f5d32a45</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S CHILDREN&quot;" target="&quot;PROOF OF RELATIONSHIP DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Proof of relationship documents are needed by children to prove their parent-child relationship and thus qualify for the long-term service benefit."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0b3d407961e6ed952b04345f5d32a45</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S PARENTS&quot;" target="&quot;PROOF OF RELATIONSHIP DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parents need proof of relationship documentation to establish their filial relationship with the deceased employee in order to claim the long-term service benefit."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0b3d407961e6ed952b04345f5d32a45</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;PROOF OF RELATIONSHIP DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A legal representative must provide a proof of relationship document to substantiate their right to receive the long-term service benefit on behalf of another person."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0b3d407961e6ed952b04345f5d32a45</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER AND MANAGER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal Representative acts on behalf of Commissioner and Manager in legal matters related to arbitration or mediation procedures, establishing a professional relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6afb8943a99ee7bf996b0ce17c18a04b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;《雇员补偿条例》(第282章)&quot;" target="&quot;女性员工&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据该条例的规定，女性员工享受产假、休息日等假期时，某些情况下工资可能不会被计算在内。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ab559340de48ae6d55e82984ae48a4f0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;长期服务金分配&quot;" target="&quot;《雇员补偿条例》(第282章)补给款项&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"长期服务金的分配与根据《雇员补偿条例》发放的补充款项相关，二者共同构成对员工权益的保障。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8a3ec4e0b16148270927aaef6bc6cb14</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;长期服务金分配&quot;" target="&quot;死亡原因无关性&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"无论死因如何，雇主都必须按照规定支付长期服务金给死者家属或有权领取的人士。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8a3ec4e0b16148270927aaef6bc6cb14</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ISSUE OF THE EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT TO WHICH HE IS ENTITLED—WHERE THE PERSON SO ENTITLED IS A SPOUSE, NOT LATER THAN 7 DAYS AFTER THE RECEIPT OF THE APPLICATION; OR WHERE THE PERSON SO ENTITLED IS AN ISSUE OR PARENT, WITHIN SUCH TIME AS MAY BE AGREED UPON BY THE EMPLOYER AND THE APPLICANT.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The issue is the secondary recipient of long service payment if no spouse exists."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARENT OF THE EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT TO WHICH HE IS ENTITLED—WHERE THE PERSON SO ENTITLED IS A SPOUSE, NOT LATER THAN 7 DAYS AFTER THE RECEIPT OF THE APPLICATION; OR WHERE THE PERSON SO ENTITLED IS AN ISSUE OR PARENT, WITHIN SUCH TIME AS MAY BE AGREED UPON BY THE EMPLOYER AND THE APPLICANT.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The parent is the tertiary recipient of long service payment if no spouse or issue exists."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSONAL REPRESENTATIVE OF THE EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT TO WHICH HE IS ENTITLED—WHERE THE PERSON SO ENTITLED IS A SPOUSE, NOT LATER THAN 7 DAYS AFTER THE RECEIPT OF THE APPLICATION; OR WHERE THE PERSON SO ENTITLED IS AN ISSUE OR PARENT, WITHIN SUCH TIME AS MAY BE AGREED UPON BY THE EMPLOYER AND THE APPLICANT.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The personal representative is the quaternary recipient of long service payment if no spouse, issue or parent exists."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RELEVANT EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT CALCULATED IN ACCORDANCE WITH SECTION 31V(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is responsible for calculating and paying the long service payment as per section 31V(1)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPLICATION IN THE FORM SPECIFIED BY THE COMMISSIONER UNDER SECTION 49&quot;" target="&quot;30 DAYS BEGINNING ON THE DAY NEXT FOLLOWING THE DATE OF DEATH OF THE EMPLOYEE OR WITHIN SUCH EXTENDED PERIOD AS THE COMMISSIONER MAY ALLOW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The application must be submitted within the specified period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MINOR&quot;" target="&quot;WHERE A MINOR'S APPLICATION UNDER SUBSECTION (2) SHALL BE MADE BY THE GUARDIAN OF THAT PERSON.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A minor's application is made by their guardian."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GUARDIAN OF THAT PERSON&quot;" target="&quot;WHERE A MINOR'S APPLICATION UNDER SUBSECTION (2) SHALL BE MADE BY THE GUARDIAN OF THAT PERSON.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The guardian makes the application on behalf of a minor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE DIES AND HE HAD BEEN AT THE TIME OF HIS DEATH EMPLOYED UNDER A CONTINUOUS CONTRACT FOR NOT LESS THAN 5 YEARS OF SERVICE ON THE DATE OF HIS DEATH&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employee is entitled to a long service payment if he dies after at least 5 years of continuous employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GUARDIAN&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A guardian may apply for long service payment on behalf of a minor employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e9d410c88421aeae56a47aedb79d008e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRIVATE HOUSEHOLD&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of private household is relevant in determining who qualifies for a long service payment under specific circumstances (e.g., family servant)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e9d410c88421aeae56a47aedb79d008e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRIVATE HOUSEHOLD&quot;" target="&quot;LONG-TERM SERVICE MONEY ENTITLEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"DOMESTIC SERVANTS employed within PRIVATE HOUSEHOLDS may be entitled to LONG-TERM SERVICE money upon termination of their contract, depending on the circumstances and agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dae8f763a371efa17099b990f69f8b4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRIVATE HOUSEHOLD&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contracts of employment for domestic servants in private households are managed by the personal representative following the death of the original employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0a79efc9c7d5b3c5051c209e7d8238e8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FAMILY SERVANT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term family servant is used in relation to employees who work specifically for private households under certain conditions (e.g., long service payment eligibility)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e9d410c88421aeae56a47aedb79d008e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG-TERM SERVICE MONEY ENTITLEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE BEHAVIOR LEADING TO TERMINATION WITHOUT NOTICE OR GARDEN LEAVE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Certain behaviors of an EMPLOYEE may lead to termination without notice or garden leave payment, thereby affecting their right to receive LONG-TERM SERVICE money."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dae8f763a371efa17099b990f69f8b4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG-TERM SERVICE BONUS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employee's eligibility for the long-term service bonus is conditional upon their reasonable acceptance of an employment contract renewal offer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1bb14977455cfee69d96555a42dffb40</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG-TERM SERVICE BONUS&quot;" target="&quot;31Y, 31YAA, 31YA, 31YB AND 31YC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sections 31Y and related clauses define the conditions under which long-term service bonuses may be subject to deductions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3950c75e15e51a9aa6482b52fbd5f985</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31T(1)(B)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT FOR A FIXED TERM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 31T(1)(B) pertains to the termination of a contract for a fixed term under specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ff6ba65a2b6882ca144f894790a0cc18</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENEWAL OR RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The renewal or re-engagement offer applies to an employed employee, potentially affecting their employment status."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ff6ba65a2b6882ca144f894790a0cc18</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENEWAL OR RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A contract of employment may be renewed or re-engaged by a personal representative after the death of the original employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e17f3710da650d1e14713613a2dff129</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENEWAL OR RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employee is not entitled to severance payment if they are offered renewal or re-engagement within 4 weeks post-death."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e17f3710da650d1e14713613a2dff129</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENEWAL OR RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;UNREASONABLY REFUSED OFFER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An unreasonably refused offer for renewal or re-engagement can affect entitlement to severance payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e17f3710da650d1e14713613a2dff129</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31R(1)(A)(II)&quot;" target="&quot;4 OF 2022 S. 7&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Amendments to the termination conditions under section 31R are specified in s. 7 of 2022."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6c8faaa89696bb97daf5c16e2354ab6f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE DISMISSAL&quot;" target="&quot;REINSTATEMENT OR RE-ENGAGEMENT OF EMPLOYEE BY EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"EMPLOYEE DISMISSAL can lead to the need for REINSTATEMENT or RE-ENGAGEMENT by the employer, as determined by LABOUR TRIBUNAL."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a2200d76e6cc5397e7868136950dfb19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 9 OF 1992 S. 62&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE TERMINATION WITHOUT NOTICE OR PAYMENT IN LIEU&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 9 of the relevant act defines conditions for employee termination without notice or payment in lieu, impacting dismissal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31R AND 31RA OF 1988 S. 52&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE-EMPLOYER RELATIONSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sections 31R and 31RA of the relevant act provide specific conditions for employee-employer relationships, particularly regarding contract expiration without renewal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RE-ENGAGEMENT UNDER NEW CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31T OF 1988 S. 52&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Re-engagement under a new contract can prevent the application of Section 31T for certain employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31T OF 1988 S. 52&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER'S CONDUCT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer's conduct can lead to dismissal if it allows an employee to terminate the contract without notice or payment in lieu under Section 10."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31U OF 1988 S. 52&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL INTERPRETATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal interpretation is necessary to understand exceptions defined in Section 31U, which excludes specific types of employees from the application of certain provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TERMINATION OF EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;DECEASED EMPLOYER'S LIABILITY FOR SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The termination of employment contract can lead to a severance payment, which may be liable for by the deceased employer or their personal representative."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1c5d2b28a0cc543e1f646cbc0388c9eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENEWAL OF CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;DEATH OF EMPLOYER OR EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Renewal of contract provisions may be affected by the death of an employer, as it involves continuity with a new executor or administrator."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1edc8d1eae523643c8ff13994558a8c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL TERMINOLOGY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE-EMPLOYER RELATIONSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal terminology used in sections and subsections defines key aspects of employee-employer relationships, including dismissal conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d45ab396b6bdde518be28a76d42d6670</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT RENEWAL OR RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;31V. LONG-TERM SERVICE ALLOWANCE AMOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The calculation of long-term service allowance amounts is relevant to the context of employment contract renewals and re-engagements, as it may be a factor in such processes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-590222e3ba7f541e965c6d035076bb63</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT RENEWAL OR RE-ENGAGEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;DOMESTIC SERVANT IN A PRIVATE HOUSEHOLD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Domestic servants in private households may be subject to different conditions regarding employment contract renewals or re-engagements, as their status is not covered by the general provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-590222e3ba7f541e965c6d035076bb63</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;31U. EXCLUDED CLASSES OF EMPLOYEES&quot;" target="&quot;DOMESTIC SERVANT IN A PRIVATE HOUSEHOLD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Domestic servants in private households are specifically excluded from certain employment categories, including those defined under 31U."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-590222e3ba7f541e965c6d035076bb63</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG-SERVICE BONUS AMOUNT&quot;" target="&quot;SCHEDULE 7, TABLE A&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The maximum limit of the long-service bonus amount is capped by values specified in Schedule 7, Table A for certain periods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-71d97616e0cc4be82907beda7e2485f1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第(1)款的規定&quot;" target="&quot;緊接有關日期前12個月期間的平均工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"第(1)款的規定允許僱員選擇採用緊接有關日期前12個月期間的平均工資進行計算。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffc24d2a5dd5790adbf4c552e1c4717c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第(1)款的規定&quot;" target="&quot;每月平均工資的三分之二,或$22,500的三分之二,以款額較小者為準&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"這種計算方法是根據第(1)款的規定，適用於按月計薪僱員。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffc24d2a5dd5790adbf4c552e1c4717c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;緊接有關日期前12個月期間的平均工資&quot;" target="&quot;$22,500的12倍&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"兩者都是基於同一時間段（緊接有關日期前12個月）的總工資，但計算方式和適用對象不同。前者是按日計薪僱員的日均工资，後者則是限制了最高總工資額度。"&lt;SEP&gt;"兩者都是基於同一時間段（緊接有關日期前12個月）的總工資，但計算方式和適用對象不同。前者是限制了最高總工資額度，後者則是按日計薪僱員的日均工资。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffc24d2a5dd5790adbf4c552e1c4717c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;緊接有關日期前12個月期間的平均工資&quot;" target="&quot;附註 —— 請亦參閱第31ZEA條及附表11第4條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"附註提供了相關法規和附加說明，幫助理解基於同一時間段（緊接有關日期前12個月）的總工資計算方式。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffc24d2a5dd5790adbf4c552e1c4717c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;每月平均工資的三分之二,或$22,500的三分之二,以款額較小者為準&quot;" target="&quot;每日平均工資的18倍&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"兩種計算方式都是基於同一個時間段（緊接有關日期前12個月）的工資，但適用對象不同。前者是按月計薪僱員，後者則是其他情況下的僱員。"&lt;SEP&gt;"兩種計算方式都是基於同一個時間段（緊接有關日期前12個月）的總工資，但適用對象和結果不同。前者是按月計薪僱員的日均工资，後者則是其他情況下的僱員日均工资。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffc24d2a5dd5790adbf4c552e1c4717c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;每月平均工資的三分之二,或$22,500的三分之二,以款額較小者為準&quot;" target="&quot;附註 —— 請亦參閱第31ZEA條及附表11第4條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"這種計算方法是根據相關法規和附加說明，適用於按月計薪僱員。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffc24d2a5dd5790adbf4c552e1c4717c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;每日平均工資的18倍&quot;" target="&quot;$22,500的12倍&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"兩種計算方式都是基於同一個時間段（緊接有關日期前12個月）的總工資，但適用對象和結果不同。前者是按日計薪僱員的日均工资，後者則是限制了最高總工資額度的情況下的日均工资。"&lt;SEP&gt;"兩種計算方式都是基於同一個時間段（緊接有關日期前12個月）的總工資，但適用條件和結果不同。前者是按日計薪僱員，後者則是限制了最高總工資額度。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffc24d2a5dd5790adbf4c552e1c4717c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;每日平均工資的18倍&quot;" target="&quot;附註 —— 請亦參閱第31ZEA條及附表11第4條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"這種計算方法是根據相關法規和附加說明，適用於其他情況下的僱員。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffc24d2a5dd5790adbf4c552e1c4717c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;$22,500的12倍&quot;" target="&quot;附註 —— 請亦參閱第31ZEA條及附表11第4條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"這種計算方法是根據相關法規和附加說明，適用於限制了最高總工資額度的情況。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffc24d2a5dd5790adbf4c552e1c4717c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第(1A)(B)款所指的每日平均工資&quot;" target="&quot;附註 —— 請亦參閱第31ZEA條及附表11第4條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"附註提供了相關法規和附加說明，幫助理解第(1A)(B)款中涉及的日均工资計算方式。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffc24d2a5dd5790adbf4c552e1c4717c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
