  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employment Ordinance defines the legal context for strikes, which are mentioned in relation to employee absence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-65134d6c88195bfcc2ac0100392eb0d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE EMPLOYMENT ORDINANCE (CAP. 599)&quot;" target="&quot;LOCK-OUTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employment Ordinance also covers lock-outs, defining them as a reason for employee absence under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-65134d6c88195bfcc2ac0100392eb0d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STRIKES&quot;" target="&quot;LOCK-OUTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both strikes and lock-outs are reasons given in the ordinance for which an employee's work hours may not be counted towards their employment period continuity."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-65134d6c88195bfcc2ac0100392eb0d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OPERATION&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT PERIOD CONTINUITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The operation of businesses, including transfers between entities, affects the continuity of an employee's employment period according to the Employment Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-65134d6c88195bfcc2ac0100392eb0d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT PERIOD CONTINUITY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of employment period continuity is related to how contracts and periods of service are treated under the Employment Ordinance, especially in cases involving strikes or lock-outs."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-65134d6c88195bfcc2ac0100392eb0d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
