  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The maximum amount of wages earned by the employee during the period is $270,000 from October 1, 1998 to September 30, 1999."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dba340f7980f6229a5082026062a8004</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1995&quot;" target="=&quot;$290,000&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The maximum amount of wages earned by the employee during the period is $290,000 from October 1, 1999 to September 30, 2000."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dba340f7980f6229a5082026062a8004</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1995&quot;" target="=&quot;$310,000&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The maximum amount of wages earned by the employee during the period is $310,000 from October 1, 2000 to September 30, 2001."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dba340f7980f6229a5082026062a8004</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1995&quot;" target="=&quot;$330,000&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The maximum amount of wages earned by the employee during the period is $330,000 from October 1, 2001 to September 30, 2002."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dba340f7980f6229a5082026062a8004</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1995&quot;" target="=&quot;$350,000&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The maximum amount of wages earned by the employee during the period is $350,000 from October 1, 2002 to September 30, 2003."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dba340f7980f6229a5082026062a8004</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1995&quot;" target="=&quot;$370,000&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The maximum amount of wages earned by the employee during the period is $370,000 from October 1, 2003 or later."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dba340f7980f6229a5082026062a8004</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1995 (5 OF 1995)&quot;" target="&quot;1 OCTOBER 2003 OR LATER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 1995 comes into effect on or after October 1, 2003."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dba340f7980f6229a5082026062a8004</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱傭保障 (EMPLOYMENT PROTECTION)&quot;" target="&quot;死亡的雇主或雇員 (DEATH OF EMPLOYER OR EMPLOYEE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employment protection laws and regulations address the situation of death in employment relationships, particularly concerning rights and claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1edc8d1eae523643c8ff13994558a8c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;死亡的雇主或雇員 (DEATH OF EMPLOYER OR EMPLOYEE)&quot;" target="&quot;已故僱主的遺產代理人 (EXECUTOR OF THE DECEASED EMPLOYER'S ESTATE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The death of an employer leads to the involvement of their executor in handling employment-related matters and claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1edc8d1eae523643c8ff13994558a8c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;死亡的雇主或雇員 (DEATH OF EMPLOYER OR EMPLOYEE)&quot;" target="&quot;續訂合約 (RENEWAL OF CONTRACT)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">21.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Renewal of contracts can be affected by the death of an employer, as it involves continuity with a new executor or administrator."&lt;SEP&gt;"Renewal of contracts may be affected by the death of an employer, as it involves continuity with a new executor or administrator."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1edc8d1eae523643c8ff13994558a8c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;死亡的雇主或雇員 (DEATH OF EMPLOYER OR EMPLOYEE)&quot;" target="&quot;再次聘用 (RE-EMPLOYMENT)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Re-employment can be influenced by the circumstances surrounding the death of an employee or their employer, especially in terms of continuity and rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1edc8d1eae523643c8ff13994558a8c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;死亡的雇主或雇員 (DEATH OF EMPLOYER OR EMPLOYEE)&quot;" target="&quot;訴訟權根據本條例第VIA部產生 (RIGHT TO SUE ARISING UNDER THE VIA SECTION)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The right to sue arising under the Via section can be impacted by the death of an employer or employee, as it involves claims and legal proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1edc8d1eae523643c8ff13994558a8c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主的死亡 (DEATH OF EMPLOYER)&quot;" target="&quot;續訂合約 (RENEWAL OF CONTRACT)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The death of an employer can affect contract renewal processes, especially when handled by their estate administrator or executor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1edc8d1eae523643c8ff13994558a8c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;訴訟權 (RIGHT TO SUE)&quot;" target="&quot;申索 (CLAIM)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The right to sue is directly related to claims in legal proceedings and employment protection laws."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1edc8d1eae523643c8ff13994558a8c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ON OR AFTER 1 OCTOBER 2003 (FROM AND AFTER DATE)&quot;" target="&quot;$210,000 TO $390,000 (FINANCIAL PROVISIONS)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Financial provisions for the period starting from October 1, 2003 are defined by specific amounts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1edc8d1eae523643c8ff13994558a8c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MONTHLY $17,600&quot; (MONETARY CAP ON KEEPING RECORDS OF HOURS WORKED)" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MONETARY CAP on keeping records of hours worked affects the rights and obligations between an EMPLOYEE and their employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1896582b740b6a3f00c9bfa592f3ab2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE 2020 AMENDMENT ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;AMEMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 2020&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The two refer to the same legislative document, both named differently."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ff0ea76e10ba3baf0af94d0d3cc4f19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE 2020 AMENDMENT ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"MATERNITY LEAVE is governed by THE 2020 AMENDMENT ORDINANCE, particularly for situations where the confinement occurs on or after the amendment date."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7d6f22e03ef794b224e1918ddd3fee77</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE 2020 AMENDMENT ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 15(2)(C)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The amendment date for SECTION 15(2)(C) is a key factor in its application, as it determines whether the section applies to certain contraventions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a591cb80e52490f9bbe6ac81407040cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE 2020 AMENDMENT ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 15E(3)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The amendment date for SECTION 15E(3)(B) affects its application, particularly in relation to male employees and their infants."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a591cb80e52490f9bbe6ac81407040cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE 2020 AMENDMENT ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 15G(4)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similar to SECTION 15E(3)(B), the amendment date for SECTION 15G(4) influences its application in relation to male employees and their infants."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a591cb80e52490f9bbe6ac81407040cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRANSITIONAL PROVISIONS&quot;" target="&quot;AMEMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 2020&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 2020 includes provisions for transitional arrangements, which are detailed in the Transitions Provisions section."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ff0ea76e10ba3baf0af94d0d3cc4f19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 15E(3)(B)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 15G(4)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both sections are part of a broader set of transitional provisions dealing with male employees and their infants' rights regarding paternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a591cb80e52490f9bbe6ac81407040cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 15E(3)(B)&quot;" target="&quot;2020 AMENDMENT ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 2020 Amendment Ordinance modifies the provisions of SECTION 15E(3)(B), affecting paternity leave entitlement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-570e52321eeb26a637fff48779e8695d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 15G(4)&quot;" target="&quot;2020 AMENDMENT ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similarly, the 2020 Amendment Ordinance modifies the provisions of SECTION 15G(4)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-570e52321eeb26a637fff48779e8695d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2020 AMENDMENT ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;AMENDMENT DATE: 11 DECEMBER 2020&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The amendment date is when the 2020 Amendment Ordinance took effect, impacting provisions like SECTION 15E(3)(B) and SECTION 15G(4)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-570e52321eeb26a637fff48779e8695d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (BASIC PORTION) EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIFIED EMPLOYEES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Specified employees are the recipients of employer-funded (basic portion) exempt ORS benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-570e52321eeb26a637fff48779e8695d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (BASIC PORTION) EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;POST-TRANSITION EMPLOYMENT PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer-funded (basic portion) exempt ORS benefit is not attributed to the post-transition employment period."&lt;SEP&gt;"The post-transition employment period is not relevant to the calculation of the basic portion exempt ORS benefit."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6fc0a2ceb4811e0cf7dd2fae3da572f2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;雇主供款(基本部分)豁免职业退休计划利益&quot;" target="&quot;整段僱傭期&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"雇主供款(基本部分)豁免职业退休计划利益与整段僱傭期相关，因为该定义涉及特定雇员的整个受僱期间。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a953fb93e9985711bb86cdb5e869de50</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主供款(强制性)强积金计划权益&quot;" target="&quot;转制前部分&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"僱主供款(强制性)强积金计划权益与转制前部分相关，因为该定义涉及可归因于特定雇员的受僱期间。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a953fb93e9985711bb86cdb5e869de50</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主供款强积金计划权益&quot;" target="&quot;整段僱傭期&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"僱主供款强积金计划权益与整段僱傭期相关，因为该定义涉及雇员的整个受僱期间。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a953fb93e9985711bb86cdb5e869de50</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;整段僱傭期&quot;" target="&quot;转制前僱傭期&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"整段僱傭期包括了转制前僱傭期和转制后部分，两者共同构成了雇员的整个受僱期间。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a953fb93e9985711bb86cdb5e869de50</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;整段僱傭期&quot;" target="&quot;转制後部分&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"整段僱傭期包括了转制後部分，后者是雇员在不同时间段内的权益或福利的一部分。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a953fb93e9985711bb86cdb5e869de50</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;转制前部分&quot;" target="&quot;转制后部分&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"转制前部分和转制后部分都是指明雇员在不同时间段内的权益或福利，两者共同构成了整段僱傭期的不同阶段。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a953fb93e9985711bb86cdb5e869de50</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;转制前僱傭期&quot;" target="&quot;转制后部分&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"转制前僱傭期与转制后部分相关，因为它们是雇员在不同时间段内的受僱期间，共同构成了整段僱傭期。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a953fb93e9985711bb86cdb5e869de50</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (MANDATORY) MPFS BENEFIT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (MANDATORY) MPFS BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"These two terms refer to the same concept, with 'employer-funded (mandatory) MPFS benefit' being a specific type of employer-funded benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6fc0a2ceb4811e0cf7dd2fae3da572f2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;POST-TRANSITION EMPLOYMENT PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;POST-TRANSITION PORTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Post-Transition Employment Period directly influences Post-Transition Portion as it defines the timeframe for calculating post-transition benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0dd3aa2554b81fa47ed2eec0f056d25</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;POST-TRANSITION EMPLOYMENT PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;MODIFIED (經變通)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of Modified is directly related as it modifies the definition or calculation involving Post-Transition Employment Period, reflecting changes through Part 2 and 3 of this Schedule."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0dd3aa2554b81fa47ed2eec0f056d25</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;POST-TRANSITION EMPLOYMENT PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;PRE-TRANSITION EMPLOYMENT PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both periods are part of the employment timeline under the Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 1990, contributing to the calculation of long service payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8c7aef455ebf5c49827835bcb4e365e9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;POST-TRANSITION EMPLOYMENT PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similarly, the post-transition employment period also contributes to determining the amount of long service payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8c7aef455ebf5c49827835bcb4e365e9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;POST-TRANSITION PORTION&quot;" target="&quot;WHOLE EMPLOYMENT PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Whole Employment Period encompasses both pre and post-transitional periods; thus, it indirectly relates to the Post-Transition Portion through its definition of total employment time."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0dd3aa2554b81fa47ed2eec0f056d25</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRE-TRANSITION EMPLOYMENT PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;PRE-TRANSITION PORTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Pre-Transition Employment Period is crucial in determining Pre-Transition Portion, which calculates payments based on pre-transition employment duration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0dd3aa2554b81fa47ed2eec0f056d25</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRE-TRANSITION EMPLOYMENT PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;MODIFIED (經變通)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similarly to above relationship, Modified affects Pre-Transition Employment Period as it modifies the definition or calculation involving pre-transitional periods through Part 2 and 3 of this Schedule."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0dd3aa2554b81fa47ed2eec0f056d25</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRE-TRANSITION EMPLOYMENT PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The pre-transition employment period is a key factor in calculating the amount of long service payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8c7aef455ebf5c49827835bcb4e365e9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRE-TRANSITION PORTION&quot;" target="&quot;WHOLE EMPLOYMENT PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similar to above relationship, Whole Employment Period includes both pre and post-transitional periods making it relevant in defining Pre-Transition Portion."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0dd3aa2554b81fa47ed2eec0f056d25</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT CALCULATION FORMULA&quot;" target="&quot;PRE-TRANSITION EMPLOYMENT PERIOD CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The formula calculates an amount for pre-transition employment by considering years of service and pro rata months or days, with a cap at two-thirds of $22,500."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e42d72d79a5857b9a938418db1f215c6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT CALCULATION FORMULA&quot;" target="&quot;POST-TRANSITION EMPLOYMENT PERIOD CALCULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The formula calculates an amount for post-transition employment by considering years of service and pro rata months or days, with a cap at two-thirds of $22,500."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e42d72d79a5857b9a938418db1f215c6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVENTH SCHEDULE, TABLE A&quot;" target="&quot;APPLICABLE CEILING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The applicable ceiling is specified in Table A of the Seventh Schedule."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-baf74cd15c802dc378f719fad8fcf7e9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPLICABLE CEILING&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S AVERAGE MONTHLY WAGES DURING THE SPECIFIED PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employee's average monthly wages can influence the calculation of the severance payment which is capped by the applicable ceiling."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-baf74cd15c802dc378f719fad8fcf7e9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPLICABLE CEILING&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S AVERAGE DAILY WAGES DURING THE SPECIFIED PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employee's average daily wages are used in calculations that can affect whether the severance payment exceeds the applicable ceiling."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-baf74cd15c802dc378f719fad8fcf7e9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRE-TRANSITION PORTION OF THE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;POST-TRANSITION PORTION OF THE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If the pre-transition portion exceeds the applicable ceiling, the post-transition portion will be reduced to zero."&lt;SEP&gt;"In cases where pre-transition portion exceeds applicable ceiling, post-transition portion may be reduced or set to zero."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-baf74cd15c802dc378f719fad8fcf7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ea74deaae12a605f5ea78eff9b6bb9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S AVERAGE MONTHLY WAGES DURING THE SPECIFIED PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The average monthly wages are used as a basis for calculating the pre-transition portion of the long service payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e2ea74deaae12a605f5ea78eff9b6bb9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE'S AVERAGE DAILY WAGES DURING THE SPECIFIED PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The average daily wages are used to calculate the post-transition portion if necessary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e2ea74deaae12a605f5ea78eff9b6bb9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFIED PERIOD&quot;" target="[&quot;$22,500&quot;]">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The specified period is linked to the average monthly or daily salary calculation which involves $22,500."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-985ae67540622887dd136da808df6b3c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFIED PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;12 MONTHS PRIOR TO THE TRANSFER DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The period referred to as 'specified period' is defined based on either 12 months prior to the transfer date or the entire pre-transfer employment period, whichever applies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8af6b4dc2fe01fb4922af5ea08198c20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFIED PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;1980-01-01&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"For employees whose continuous contract of employment involves non-manual work and their average monthly wage exceeded $15,000 in the 12 months prior to the effective date of the 'Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 1990', the specified period does not include any service before January 1, 1980."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8af6b4dc2fe01fb4922af5ea08198c20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFIED PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1990&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 'specified period' is calculated based on a timeframe that may be influenced by the effective date of the 'Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 1990', particularly for employees with high average monthly wages prior to its implementation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8af6b4dc2fe01fb4922af5ea08198c20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFIED PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;PARTY A&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Party A's response can affect whether certain submissions are considered by the Adjudicator based on the time they were served."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bba63535f02791b0eaca5f64d5b8ed57</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;12 MONTHS IMMEDIATELY PRECEDING THE TRANSITION DATE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1990 (41 OF 1990)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The period of 12 months immediately preceding the transition date is relevant to the Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 1990."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-515212436640c28d5f467b8b10ac11d7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1990 (41 OF 1990)&quot;" target="&quot;JANUARY 1980&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The commencement date of the Employment (Amendment) Ordinance is after January 1980, which affects pre-transition employment periods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-515212436640c28d5f467b8b10ac11d7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;遣散費的款額&quot;" target="&quot;指明僱員有權獲得的遣散費款額&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both terms refer to the amount of severance pay that a specified employee is entitled to receive according to the law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-515212436640c28d5f467b8b10ac11d7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;A. 該僱員的轉制前僱傭期不少於一個月&quot;" target="&quot;B. 該僱員的轉制前僱傭期不足一個月&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"These two conditions describe different durations of pre-privatization employment, leading to distinct severance payment calculations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a330a959a6c15ba83519889d549f1e3a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;A. 該僱員的轉制前僱傭期不少於30個正常工作日&quot;" target="&quot;B. 該僱員的轉制前僱傭期不足30個正常工作日&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"These two conditions describe different durations of pre-privatization workdays, leading to distinct severance payment calculations based on selected 18 working days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a330a959a6c15ba83519889d549f1e3a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱員的轉制後僱傭期年數(不足一年的部分按比例計算)&quot;" target="&quot;屬該僱員的整段僱傭期的最後一個月全月工資的三分之二,或$22,500的三分之二,以款額較小者為準&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The post-privatization employment period and the severance pay based on the last month's salary are related as they both contribute to calculating the final severance payment amount."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a330a959a6c15ba83519889d549f1e3a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱員的轉制後僱傭期年數(不足一年的部分按比例計算)&quot;" target="&quot;由該僱員選取的18日(須從在整段僱傭期內該僱員最後工作的30個正常工作日中選取任何18日)為依據的18日工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The post-privatization employment period and the severance pay based on selected 18 working days are related as they both contribute to calculating the final severance payment amount. They serve different criteria for determining the payment amount."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a330a959a6c15ba83519889d549f1e3a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;屬該僱員的整段僱傭期的最後一個月全月工資的三分之二,或$22,500的三分之二,以款額較小者為準&quot;" target="&quot;由該僱員選取的18日(須從在整段僱傭期內該僱員最後工作的30個正常工作日中選取任何18日)為依據的18日工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both conditions refer to severance pay based on the last month's salary or a selected 18 working days, with $22,500 as a reference amount."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a330a959a6c15ba83519889d549f1e3a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;屬該僱員的整段僱傭期的最後一個月全月工資的三分之二,或$22,500的三分之二,以款額較小者為準&quot;" target="&quot;由該僱員選取的18日(須從在整段僱傭期內該僱員最先工作的30個正常工作日中選取任何18日)為依據的18日工資&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both conditions refer to severance pay based on the first 30 working days or the last month's salary, with $22,500 as a reference amount. They are alternatives for different scenarios of employment duration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a330a959a6c15ba83519889d549f1e3a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;18日工資&quot;" target="&quot;僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"18日工資是根据雇员在整段雇佣期内最后工作的30个正常工作日内选取任意连续18天的工资计算得出，用于与$22,500进行比较。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7ef856c5e83d9e91d386bd822201a8b7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;附表7表A第1欄所指明的期間內&quot;" target="&quot;僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"该期间内遣散费款额不得超过附表7表A第2栏相应位置列出的金额（适用款额上限）。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7ef856c5e83d9e91d386bd822201a8b7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;適用款額上限&quot;" target="&quot;遣散費轉制前部分&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"在指明期间内，如果遣散费超过适用款额上限，则遣散费转制前部分需被扣减至相等于适用款额上限的金额。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7ef856c5e83d9e91d386bd822201a8b7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;適用款額上限&quot;" target="&quot;遣散費轉制後部分&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"在指明期间内，如果遣散费超过适用款额上限，则遣散费转制后部分需被扣减至零。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7ef856c5e83d9e91d386bd822201a8b7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;遣散費轉制前部分&quot;" target="&quot;僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"僱員可能獲得遣散費轉制前部分,其計算基於服務年資和相關權益。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-27f6c661ada2a6aa0e1f1b94665b64df</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;遣散費轉制前部分&quot;" target="&quot;酬金或利益或權益&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"支付給僱員的遣散費轉制前部分涉及相關的酬金、利益或權益。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-27f6c661ada2a6aa0e1f1b94665b64df</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;遣散費轉制後部分&quot;" target="&quot;僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"僱員也可能獲得遣散費轉制後部分,其計算基於相同原則但適用不同扣除項目。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-27f6c661ada2a6aa0e1f1b94665b64df</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;遣散費轉制後部分&quot;" target="&quot;酬金或利益或權益&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"支付給僱員的遣散費轉制後部分也涉及相關的酬金、利益或權益,但適用不同的扣除項目。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-27f6c661ada2a6aa0e1f1b94665b64df</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;指明期間的平均工資&quot;" target="&quot;僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"雇员可以选择使用指明期间内的平均工资来计算遣散费用，以替代最后一个月全月工资或18日工资与$22,500进行比较。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7ef856c5e83d9e91d386bd822201a8b7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1990&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 31I&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 1990 is the legislative context for Section 31I, providing its legal basis and scope."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-772d5b97625d81ec1623236fca58771c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1990&quot;" target="&quot;12 MONTHS PRIOR TO THE TRANSFER DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The period '12 months prior to the transfer date' is relevant for calculating wages under the 'Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 1990', especially in determining average monthly earnings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8af6b4dc2fe01fb4922af5ea08198c20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1990&quot;" target="&quot;1980-01-01&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The date 'January 1, 1980' is a critical reference point for determining the inclusion of service periods in calculations under the 'Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 1990', particularly concerning high-wage employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8af6b4dc2fe01fb4922af5ea08198c20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1990&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 1990 defines the calculation method for long service payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8c7aef455ebf5c49827835bcb4e365e9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1990&quot;" target="&quot;LONG-TERM SERVICE ALLOWANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 1990 modifies the calculation method for Long-Term Service Allowance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4c5336f48f2648be18accb456b032c71</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 1990&quot;" target="&quot;31Y, 31YAA, 31YA, 31YB, 31YC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employment (Amendment) Ordinance 1990 amends Sections 31Y, 31YAA, 31YA, 31YB and 31YC to define the calculation methods for certain allowances including Long-Term Service Allowance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4c5336f48f2648be18accb456b032c71</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;約的施行&quot;" target="&quot;僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"約的施行涉及支付酬金或利益予僱員。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-27f6c661ada2a6aa0e1f1b94665b64df</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;酬金或利益或權益&quot;" target="&quot;強積金計劃權益&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"強積金計劃權益可能會被視為一種酬金或利益或權益的一部分,在某些情況下需要考慮其影響。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-90c0794da631cfd39500d26a03a02ecf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS (EMPLOYER-FUNDED ORS BENEFITS)&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SEVERANCE PAYMENT may be reduced if employer-funded ORS benefits have been paid to the employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6ca736f121ac163d07969e939b811f0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS (EMPLOYER-FUNDED ORS BENEFITS)&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT REDUCTION CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Conditions for reducing SEVERANCE PAYMENT include employer-funded ORS benefits having been paid to the employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6ca736f121ac163d07969e939b811f0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS (EMPLOYER-FUNDED ORS BENEFITS)&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Long Service Payment may be reduced by employer-funded ORS benefits due to the employee's death."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-38034baf57d26ec704e02e12e81cdf6a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS (EMPLOYER-FUNDED ORS BENEFITS)&quot;" target="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS (MANDATORY PROVIDENT FUND SCHEMES BENEFITS)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both types of benefits are related as they both pertain to employer-funded retirement or financial benefits for employees."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-38034baf57d26ec704e02e12e81cdf6a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS (EMPLOYER-FUNDED MPFS BENEFITS)&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SEVERANCE PAYMENT may be reduced if employer-funded MPFS benefits are being held or have been paid to the employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6ca736f121ac163d07969e939b811f0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS (EMPLOYER-FUNDED MPFS BENEFITS)&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT REDUCTION CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Conditions for reducing SEVERANCE PAYMENT include employer-funded MPFS benefits being held or having been paid to the employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6ca736f121ac163d07969e939b811f0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STRONGLY FUNDED PENSION SCHEMES&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Strongly funded pension schemes are related to employees who have rights based on their employment contract, as stated in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a23958c5eb862b357e8540d3c4c5afd6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;遣散费&quot;" target="&quot;服务期终止补偿金&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"遣散费和终止补偿金都是与员工离职相关的经济补偿，尽管名称不同但性质相似。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a23958c5eb862b357e8540d3c4c5afd6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRATUITY&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Gratuities based on length of service might be reduced by both pre-transition and post-transition portions of the severance payment, depending on their attribution to the same years of service."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3cd899e03ecc067de0edd74af6740db7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GRATUITY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The gratuity is paid to the employee based on years of service, which may be reduced by the long service payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-27ca5e1e28067ca3c2334e15e6221974</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31V&quot;" target="&quot;LONG-SERVICE LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'long-term service leave' is implied in the context of Section 31V which deals with long-service payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-622dec92f9d3c73f201fbdc4fab3be5f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 31V&quot;" target="&quot;MODIFICATIONS TO PART VB&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Modifications to Part VB involve changes specifically in Section 31V."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9661724896688b8cd0643c1a0b2fa146</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG-SERVICE LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Severance payment and long-service leave both deal with employee benefits, though they serve different purposes in the context of employment termination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-622dec92f9d3c73f201fbdc4fab3be5f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;适用额度上限&quot;" target="&quot;长期服务金款额&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"长期服务金款额不得超过适用额度上限所规定的数值。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-39ff31ef4fdbcf84c8c1f1a297094829</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;适用款额上限&quot;" target="&quot;长期服务金款额上限&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"长期服务金的计算会受到适用款额上限的影响，若非因特定情况则会被扣减至不超过该上限。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23d51c29b119b65758639275d4ba4446</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;适用款额上限&quot;" target="&quot;长期服务金转制前部分的款额&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"长期服务金在特定情况下的款项需要被扣减至不超过适用款额上限。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23d51c29b119b65758639275d4ba4446</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;指明期间平均工资&quot;" target="&quot;长期服务金款额上限&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"指明期间平均工资用于计算长期服务金的具体数额，特别是在某些情况下会影响适用款额上限的确定。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23d51c29b119b65758639275d4ba4446</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;31Y, 31YAA, 31YA, 31YB, 31YC&quot;" target="&quot;LONG-TERM SERVICE ALLOWANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sections 31Y, 31YAA, 31YA, 31YB and 31YC are related to the calculation of Long-Term Service Allowance as they provide specific rules for its computation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4c5336f48f2648be18accb456b032c71</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;31Y, 31YAA, 31YA, 31YB AND 31YC&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The clauses involve employee compensation in the form of long-term service bonuses and related benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3950c75e15e51a9aa6482b52fbd5f985</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;31Y, 31YAA, 31YA, 31YB AND 31YC&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL PENSION PLAN BENEFIT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The clauses relate to occupational pension plan benefits that may be subject to deductions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3950c75e15e51a9aa6482b52fbd5f985</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;31Y, 31YAA, 31YA, 31YB AND 31YC&quot;" target="&quot;MANDATORY PROVIDENT FUND CONTRIBUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The clauses involve mandatory provident fund contributions which can affect the calculation of long-term service bonuses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3950c75e15e51a9aa6482b52fbd5f985</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;YAA. 在某些情況下,酬金或利益或權益須扣除長期服務金的款額&quot;" target="&quot;僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"YAA applies to employees who have certain conditions met regarding gratuities or benefits and their relation to long service payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-233de206d4d440690ca3d19bf8ddb77c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主供款職業退休計劃利益&quot;" target="&quot;強積金計劃權益&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are types of employer-funded benefits, indicating a relationship in the context of employee retirement and financial planning."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-233de206d4d440690ca3d19bf8ddb77c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主供款職業退休計劃利益&quot;" target="&quot;酬金&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"酬金与僱主供款職業退休計劃利益都属于第(1)(a)(i)款提述的合資格项目，两者相关联。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf0d42aa8ddf0d9c1bf8ce8c4d98678b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;雇主供款職業退休計劃利益&quot;" target="&quot;僱主供款(基本部分)豁免職業退休計劃利益&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"雇主供款職業退休計劃利益与僱主供款(基本部分)豁免職業退休計劃利益相关，都属于第(1)(a)(ii)款提述的合資格项目。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf0d42aa8ddf0d9c1bf8ce8c4d98678b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;酬金&quot;" target="&quot;僱主供款強積金計劃權益&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"酬金与僱主供款強積金計劃權益都属于第(1)(a)(iii)款提述的合資格项目，两者相关联。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf0d42aa8ddf0d9c1bf8ce8c4d98678b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主供款(強制性)強積金計劃權益&quot;" target="&quot;雇主供款強積金計劃權益&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"雇主供款強積金計劃權益与僱主供款(強制性)強積金計劃權益相关，都属于第(1)(a)(iii)款提述的合資格项目。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf0d42aa8ddf0d9c1bf8ce8c4d98678b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employee-funded ORS benefits are eligible for reduction if attributable to the same years of service as the long service payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-27ca5e1e28067ca3c2334e15e6221974</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED ORS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIFIED EMPLOYEE'S DEATH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The death of the specified employee leads Person B to become eligible for employer-funded ORS benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f087949a68abbda398ef78592fe5cb12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED MPFS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employee-funded MPFS benefits may also be reduced based on the same criteria applicable to ORS benefits and gratuities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-27ca5e1e28067ca3c2334e15e6221974</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED MPFS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;DEATH BENEFIT PROVISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Death benefit provisions may interact with employer-funded MPFS benefits in terms of payment and deduction rules."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c87228f0b6f2f82336ca7700cb45e5d8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED MPFS BENEFITS&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIFIED EMPLOYEE'S DEATH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similarly, the death of the specified employee results in Person B becoming entitled to employer-funded MPFS benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f087949a68abbda398ef78592fe5cb12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS (MANDATORY PROVIDENT FUND SCHEMES BENEFITS)&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Long Service Payment may also be reduced by MPFS benefits held in mandatory provident fund schemes due to the employee's death."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-38034baf57d26ec704e02e12e81cdf6a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFIED EMPLOYEE'S DEATH EVENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT LOCATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The death event triggers entitlements based on the employee's contract of employment location."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5c7b30bfc298801ee1a93516d9613cb8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFIED EMPLOYEE'S DEATH EVENT&quot;" target="&quot;ORS BENEFITS PRODUCT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Death results in eligibility for ORS benefits as per the employee’s contract of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5c7b30bfc298801ee1a93516d9613cb8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFIED EMPLOYEE'S DEATH EVENT&quot;" target="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS PRODUCT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The death event leads to entitlements for MPFS benefits due to the operation of the contract of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5c7b30bfc298801ee1a93516d9613cb8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORS BENEFITS PRODUCT&quot;" target="&quot;MPFS BENEFITS PRODUCT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ORS and MPFS benefits are employer-funded and relate to death events triggering entitlements for gratuities or benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5c7b30bfc298801ee1a93516d9613cb8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT TECHNOLOGY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT LOCATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Long service payment technology is related to the employee's contract of employment location, as it pertains to payments based on years of service."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5c7b30bfc298801ee1a93516d9613cb8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第31YB条&quot;" target="&quot;扣减后的款额&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据第31YB条的规定,某些款项可能被扣除后支付给乙方。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7fb9bafd0cba5b9cfa67282f7c70bf83</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主供款&quot;" target="&quot;支付有关长期服务金所基于的有关僱員服務期&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"僱主供款与僱员的服务年限相关,是计算长期服务金的基础之一。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7fb9bafd0cba5b9cfa67282f7c70bf83</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFIED EMPLOYEE'S DEATH&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT UNDER SECTION 31RA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The death of the specified employee triggers the long service payment under section 31RA to be paid to Person A."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f087949a68abbda398ef78592fe5cb12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 21, SUBS. NO. 4 OF 2022&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The long service payment's eligibility and reduction are governed by Section 21, Subsection No. 4 of 2022."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d634411e44f3153b1f3217349599619c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREVENTION AND CONTROL OF DISEASE REGULATION&quot;" target="&quot;CAP. 599J&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Prevention and Control of Disease Regulation (Cap. 599) is the broader regulation that includes specific sections which are referenced in Cap. 599J."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-80287c114e819e413bb60b4185c561ea</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREVENTION AND CONTROL OF DISEASE REGULATION&quot;" target="&quot;QUARANTINE OR ISOLATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Prevention and Control of Disease Regulation (Cap. 599) includes provisions for quarantine or isolation, which are referenced in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-80287c114e819e413bb60b4185c561ea</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPULSORY TESTING NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;CAP. 599J&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Compulsory Testing Notice is published under Cap. 599J (Prevention and Control of Disease (Compulsory Testing for Certain Persons) Regulation), which enforces certain requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-80287c114e819e413bb60b4185c561ea</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPULSORY TESTING NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;QUARANTINE OR ISOLATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both compulsory testing notices and quarantine/isolation are part of the broader regulatory framework, with interactions between them as described in Cap. 599J."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-80287c114e819e413bb60b4185c561ea</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGULATION (CAP. 599 SUB. LEG. J)&quot;" target="&quot;PREVENTION AND CONTROL OF DISEASE (COMPULSORY TESTING FOR CERTAIN PERSONS) REGULATION (CAP. 599J)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Prevention and Control of Disease Regulation is a sub-legislation under the main regulation CAP. 599."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a94f998530eebc251b3752a280893508</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREVENTION AND CONTROL OF DISEASE (COMPULSORY TESTING FOR CERTAIN PERSONS) REGULATION (CAP. 599J)&quot;" target="&quot;COMPULSORY TESTING NOTICE PUBLISHED UNDER SECTION 10(1) OF CAP. 599J&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A compulsory testing notice published under Section 10(1) of the Prevention and Control of Disease Regulation is a specific implementation measure for certain persons."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a94f998530eebc251b3752a280893508</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREVENTION AND CONTROL OF DISEASE (COMPULSORY TESTING FOR CERTAIN PERSONS) REGULATION (CAP. 599J)&quot;" target="&quot;COMPULSORY TESTING ORDER MADE UNDER SECTION 14(2) OF CAP. 599J&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A compulsory testing order made under Section 14(2) of the Prevention and Control of Disease Regulation is another specific implementation measure for certain persons."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a94f998530eebc251b3752a280893508</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREVENTION AND CONTROL OF DISEASE (COMPULSORY TESTING FOR CERTAIN PERSONS) REGULATION (CAP. 599J)&quot;" target="&quot;RESTRICTED PREMISES DEFINED UNDER SECTION 19A OF CAP. 599J&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Restricted premises defined under Section 19A of the Prevention and Control of Disease Regulation are specific locations subject to certain regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a94f998530eebc251b3752a280893508</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 33(5)(AB)&quot;" target="&quot;PRESCRIBED INFORMATION (PRESCRIBED INFORMATION)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 33(5)(ab) specifies the prescribed information, which includes details about employees and their restrictions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a94f998530eebc251b3752a280893508</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 33(5)(AB)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE INFORMATION MANAGEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employee Information Management involves the handling of restrictions as specified in Section 33(5)(ab)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The information managed includes the name and identifying details of employees, as well as types and durations of restrictions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9a1fa46128d33dc86ff9326b722ce67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 33(5)(AB)&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">23.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers are involved in the implementation of restrictions as specified by Section 33(5)(ab)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public officers are responsible for implementing and enforcing Section 33(5)(ab) related to employee information management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public officers are responsible for implementing and enforcing Section 33(5)(ab) related to managing restrictions on employee data."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9a1fa46128d33dc86ff9326b722ce67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 33(5)(AB)&quot;" target="&quot;DATA PRIVACY LAWS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">33.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Data privacy laws intersect with Section 33(5)(ab), ensuring that the handling of employee data complies with legal standards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Data privacy laws provide the framework within which the restrictions in Section 33(5)(ab) must operate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 33(5)(ab)'s implementation must comply with data privacy laws ensuring the protection of personal information."&lt;SEP&gt;"The restrictions specified by Section 33(5)(ab) must comply with data privacy laws ensuring the protection of personal employee information."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9a1fa46128d33dc86ff9326b722ce67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE INFORMATION MANAGEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;DATA PRIVACY LAWS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Data privacy laws govern how employee information should be managed and protected, aligning with employment regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Data privacy laws provide the legal framework within which employee information management must operate."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9a1fa46128d33dc86ff9326b722ce67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE INFORMATION MANAGEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 57 RTF&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 57 RTF provides means for managing employee information as per employment regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9a1fa46128d33dc86ff9326b722ce67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE INFORMATION MANAGEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">25.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers are involved in managing and enforcing policies related to employee information, as per employment regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public officers are involved in the management and enforcement of policies related to employee information, as per employment regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public officers are key figures in managing and enforcing employee information as per employment regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9a1fa46128d33dc86ff9326b722ce67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DATA PRIVACY LAWS&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers must ensure that their actions comply with data privacy laws when handling and restricting employee information."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b9a1fa46128d33dc86ff9326b722ce67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A PARTY is involved in an ARBITRATION AGREEMENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4f6f1173170ce4ac811fedab280f3b4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration tribunal has the authority to make awards or orders on its own initiative or upon application of any other party concerning parties involved in disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-854d00c33e69aed0258675abc1e2d264</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;HEARING ATTENDANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Any party failing to appear at a hearing can still have the arbitral tribunal continue with the proceedings and make an award based on available evidence. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;DOCUMENT SUBMISSION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties are required to submit documentary evidence, failure of which may not prevent the arbitration process from continuing as per Article 25(c). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;STATEMENT OF CLAIM/DEFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties are required to submit a statement of claim or defence, failure in which can lead to specific consequences outlined in Article 25(a) and (b). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;EXPERT DESIGNATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A party can request or agree for an expert designation as per Article 26(1). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8e9a7aaa471f2d1e4f0d2af386c0f6d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties are involved in the arbitration process that leads to an arbitration award."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-aba64861ea22070188d9b7dd4c0fd47a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;ADJUDICATOR'S RESIGNATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If the independence or impartiality of an adjudicator is questioned, they may resign from their position during adjudication proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-59f65136a37f2183ac96641ebb7819e2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;ADJUDICATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ADJUDICATOR determines that a PARTY has legal responsibility to pay another PARTY an adjudicated amount."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b49150680872ebc6da3ccdee23b5d249</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If the determination is set aside by the COURT, it will no longer be binding on the PARTIES."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b49150680872ebc6da3ccdee23b5d249</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;ADJUDICATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The party's actions and success in ADJUDICATION PROCEEDINGS can influence the proportion of costs they pay."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f4f0cfcab0e9f6d5a958dc7286fe8aad</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 41(E), (F) AND (G)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"PARTY's actions can lead to the termination of proceedings under SECTION 41(E), (F) and (G)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f4f0cfcab0e9f6d5a958dc7286fe8aad</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINLAND&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The claimant can be from the Mainland, which refers to China excluding Hong Kong, Macau, and Taiwan."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINLAND AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA ARBITRATION LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINLAND AWARD refers to a decision made under the PEOPLES REPUBLIC OF CHINA ARBITRATION LAW."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4f6f1173170ce4ac811fedab280f3b4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINLAND AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mainland award is based on an arbitration agreement under Chinese law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINLAND AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD ENFORCEMENT PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mainland awards are specifically named in the text as a category distinct from Convention, Hong Kong, or Macao awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3136488efa6b0856e563bdafbaaa1633</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINLAND AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mainland awards can be enforced in Hong Kong through actions brought before the Court."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bcca397988541ca9ac3822ff7a363627</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OMITTED AS SPENT—E.R. 2 OF 2014&quot;" target="&quot;2014年第2號編輯修訂紀錄&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The revision record E.R. 2 of 2014 has been omitted as spent."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4f6f1173170ce4ac811fedab280f3b4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2021年第1號第3條&quot;" target="&quot;PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA ARBITRATION LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 2021年第1號第3條 amends the definition of MAINLAND AWARD under the PEOPLES REPUBLIC OF CHINA ARBITRATION LAW."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4f6f1173170ce4ac811fedab280f3b4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORMAT CHANGES— E.R. 1 OF 2018&quot;" target="&quot;2014年第2號編輯修訂紀錄&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The revision record E.R. 2 of 2014 is related to the format changes in E.R. 1 of 2018."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4f6f1173170ce4ac811fedab280f3b4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT PROCEDURE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ARBITRATION PROCEDURE and COURT PROCEDURE are covered in the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4f6f1173170ce4ac811fedab280f3b4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION DECISION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An ARBITRATION AGREEMENT leads to an ARBITRATION DECISION."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4f6f1173170ce4ac811fedab280f3b4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION DECISION&quot;" target="&quot;COURT REVIEW OF ARBITRATION DECISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court can review and potentially overturn an arbitration decision under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-946b6b4dc8815b2e45997dcb61152914</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION DECISION&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitration decision can be invalidated if it conflicts with public policy as determined by a court."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-946b6b4dc8815b2e45997dcb61152914</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA ARBITRATION LAW&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRATION LAW is related to the PEOPLES REPUBLIC OF CHINA ARBITRATION LAW as they both deal with arbitration matters."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4f6f1173170ce4ac811fedab280f3b4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE AND COURT PROCEDURE&quot;" target="&quot;REVISED DEFINITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definitions are revised to include both arbitration and court procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4f6f1173170ce4ac811fedab280f3b4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONVENTION AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;NEW YORK CONVENTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Convention award refers to awards made in a country that is a party to the New York Convention, which deals with recognition and enforcement of foreign arbitral awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONVENTION AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD ENFORCEMENT PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Conventions are a specific type of award mentioned separately from other types like Mainland and Macao awards under the enforcement procedure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3136488efa6b0856e563bdafbaaa1633</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONVENTION AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court can enforce a Convention Award, either through actions brought under this division or using methods applicable to other awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4494c24ec2905c2010570a5a5156b75e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONVENTION AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;2013 YEAR 7 AMENDMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Amendments made in 2013, specifically amendment number 7, affect how Convention Awards are enforced and referenced within Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4494c24ec2905c2010570a5a5156b75e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONVENTION AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;国际公约裁决撤销或暂停请求的主管机关&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"涉及公約裁決撤銷或暫時中止的申请应由特定主管當局处理，法院在某些情况下可以介入。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-38b4dba8dcefb2d368c753859f749fd1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONVENTION AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Convention award may be refused enforcement if it goes against public policy."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-603a9b33a6e3900af70fd439592326ba</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISPUTE&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A claimant may arise from disputes between parties in arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Claimant is a party in dispute, making claims or counter-claims during an arbitration proceeding."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISPUTE&quot;" target="&quot;MEDIATION (調解)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mediation can be used to resolve disputes before or during an arbitration process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HKIAC&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The HKIAC can intervene and appoint mediators or arbitrators based on the terms of arbitration agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre (HKIAC) handles arbitration agreements and arbitrations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2dd6cc93acdd87603565c28f0e5d9386&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HKIAC&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"HKIAC may make rules in accordance with UNCITRAL Model Law, particularly sections 23(3), 24 or 32(1)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-678280ae191a89f40bc665d65f091cbb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HKIAC&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 10(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The HKIAC's decision-making authority is defined by Article 10(1) of the UNCITRAL Model Law regarding the number of arbitrators."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2d812128591f21f04c27e6ee77e7d3c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HKIAC&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 11(3) (A)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 11(3)(a) of the HKIAC's decision-making process is based on whether parties agree or not, and involves the appointment of arbitrators by one party followed by a third arbitration appointee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2d812128591f21f04c27e6ee77e7d3c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HKIAC&quot;" target="&quot;THE PARTIES' AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The number of arbitrators in an arbitration proceeding can be decided by the HKIAC if parties fail to agree, as per Article 10(3) and 11(3)(a)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2d812128591f21f04c27e6ee77e7d3c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HKIAC&quot;" target="&quot;THE ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The HKIAC is involved in determining the number of arbitrators for arbitration proceedings when parties cannot agree, as per Article 10(3)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2d812128591f21f04c27e6ee77e7d3c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HKIAC&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATOR(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The HKIAC can appoint arbitrators, either independently or based on party agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-95a4de41db58b9a101c75606869df8f4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HKIAC&quot;" target="&quot;APPOINTMENT PROCEDURE(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The HKIAC follows specific procedures for making appointments when required by the Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-95a4de41db58b9a101c75606869df8f4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HKIAC&quot;" target="&quot;APPOINTMENT PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The HKIAC is involved in the appointment procedure for arbitrators under this Ordinance, ensuring that appointments are made with agreement of all parties where applicable."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HKIAC&quot;" target="&quot;MEDIATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The HKIAC has the authority to appoint a mediator if the initial appointed person refuses or fails to make the appointment as per arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2dd6cc93acdd87603565c28f0e5d9386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEW YORK CONVENTION&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Courts, such as the High Court Original Trial Division, may deal with matters related to the New York Convention on recognition of foreign arbitral awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEW YORK CONVENTION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION LAW OF THE PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both laws deal with arbitration, though the New York Convention focuses on international enforcement while the Chinese law is domestic."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEW YORK CONVENTION&quot;" target="&quot;STATE OR TERRITORY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Any State or territory declared by The Chief Executive in Council can become a party to the New York Convention."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed6ba602b145c3cd359dd6dda74e3b40</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSION&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commission developed the UNCITRAL Model Law, providing guidance for international commercial arbitration."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commission, UNICTRAL, has developed and promulgated the UNCITRAL Model Law on International Commercial Arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6028b01799478cec839282a4d1179b1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration agreement definition was adopted by the Commission."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSION&quot;" target="&quot;WRITING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The requirement that an arbitration agreement be in writing is defined and enforced by the Commission."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSION&quot;" target="&quot;ELECTRONIC COMMUNICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition of electronic communication as part of an arbitration agreement was established by the Commission."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSION&quot;" target="&quot;REFERENCE TO DOCUMENT CONTAINING ARBITRATION CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A reference to a document containing an arbitration clause is considered an arbitration agreement in writing according to the Commission's definition."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSION&quot;" target="&quot;EXCHANGE OF STATEMENTS OF CLAIM AND DEFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An exchange of statements of claim and defence can constitute an arbitration agreement if one party alleges its existence and the other does not deny it, as defined by the Commission."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSION&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 7. DEFINITION OF ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The article defining the arbitration agreement was adopted by the Commission."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSION&quot;" target="&quot;第7條.  仲裁協議的定義&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 7 defining the arbitration agreement was adopted by the Commission."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSION&quot;" target="&quot;INTERIM MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commission has adopted rules regarding interim measures in its thirty-ninth session, providing a framework for their implementation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d56571b98ba26116ef651214c379b2f2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONVENTION&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law is a legal framework that can be referenced under the Convention on the Recognition and Enforcement of Foreign Arbitral Awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6028b01799478cec839282a4d1179b1b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONVENTION&quot;" target="&quot;RESPONDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Respondents are parties who may be subject to claims in arbitrations governed by the Convention on the Recognition and Enforcement of Foreign Arbitral Awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6028b01799478cec839282a4d1179b1b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MACAO&quot;" target="&quot;MAINLAND CHINA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Macao is part of China but distinct from Mainland China and Taiwan."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MACAO&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Macao has its own set of arbitration rules that may differ from those in other jurisdictions like Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MACAO&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitral tribunal may be established in Macao to resolve disputes under an arbitration agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MACAO&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIM OR COUNTER-CLAIM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Macao's legal framework may involve claims and counterclaims similar to those found in other jurisdictions like Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MACAO AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Macao Award is a type of arbitration award that can refer to principles outlined in UNCITRAL Model Law, especially concerning recognition and enforcement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6028b01799478cec839282a4d1179b1b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MACAO AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD ENFORCEMENT PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Macao awards are also explicitly mentioned alongside other types of awards under the enforcement procedure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3136488efa6b0856e563bdafbaaa1633</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MACAO AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 2000 (2 OF 2000)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Macao Award is enforceable under the provisions related to the Arbitration (Amendment) Ordinance 2000 (2 of 2000)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7a8178e8eb442ffa0ed10eccd55c6223</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MACAO AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;DIVISION 4—ENFORCEMENT OF MACAO AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Division 4 specifically deals with the enforcement mechanisms for Macao Awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7a8178e8eb442ffa0ed10eccd55c6223</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MACAO AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ENFORCEMENT PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Enforcement of Macao awards involves legal procedures and actions as described by the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ec95a82e50ec8c3adae1748b384fca48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MACAO AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL DISPUTE RESOLUTION MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Macao awards are part of the legal dispute resolution mechanism in Macao's legal system."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MACAO AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The enforcement of a Macao award may be refused if it is contrary to public policy."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c53aea00b88989df2a0f5c9c8eaf66aa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MACAO AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;HONG KONG LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Under Hong Kong law, the enforcement of a Macao award can be set aside or suspended by relevant authorities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c53aea00b88989df2a0f5c9c8eaf66aa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE&quot;" target="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE OF PROTECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Interim Measure of Protection falls under the broader category of Interim Measures as defined by legal frameworks like the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6028b01799478cec839282a4d1179b1b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE&quot;" target="&quot;REQUESTING PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The requesting party can apply for interim measures, which are subject to conditions set by the arbitral tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE&quot;" target="&quot;PRELIMINARY ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A preliminary order may be modified or replaced by an interim measure issued by the arbitral tribunal after notifying the parties and giving them a chance to present their case."&lt;SEP&gt;"An interim measure can be requested together with an application for a preliminary order under Article 17B of the UNCITRAL Model Law to prevent parties from frustrating the purpose of such measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9a8aef97985d67c64a247cd4ac0838cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44743bbc15d45a8109ce653b3d495eca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">39.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Interim measures apply as if they were orders under subsection (1)(d), related through arbitral proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL can make orders related to interim measures as specified in sections 39 to 42 of relevant laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL may order INTERIM MEASURES during the arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL's orders include interim measures."&lt;SEP&gt;"The arbitral tribunal has authority to issue interim measures that may adopt or modify preliminary orders after notice to the affected party."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4667827d445ebb505094eb4b58494cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae42208132627b8d5ff98d4e7966f28e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6127a28d22b5d9d9145842f6c4caba9c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 17E&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal can require a party to provide appropriate security in relation to interim measures under Article 17E of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4667827d445ebb505094eb4b58494cea</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 17(2) OF THE UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Interim measures are defined and interpreted according to Article 17(2) of the UNCITRAL Model Law, which includes injunctions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6100d8c7e7c5fa3f9af262a8c8cb68f5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE&quot;" target="&quot;INJUNCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An interim measure can include an injunction as specified in Article 17(2) of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6100d8c7e7c5fa3f9af262a8c8cb68f5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE&quot;" target="&quot;THIRD PARTY RIGHTS PROTECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"INTERIM MEASURES can protect THIRD PARTY RIGHTS, as mentioned in Article 17H(3)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-610c6dec3dfd2d606eea19c4dfbadfa7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE OF PROTECTION&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 9 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 9 of the UNCITRAL Model Law allows for interim measures to be requested and granted, which are not incompatible with an arbitration agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE OF PROTECTION&quot;" target="&quot;EMERGENCY ARBITRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An emergency arbitrator can issue interim measures as part of their role in handling urgent relief applications before the arbitral tribunal is constituted."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE OLD ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Old Ordinance (repealed Ordinance 341章) is superseded by the UNCITRAL Model Law, which provides a modern legal framework for arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6028b01799478cec839282a4d1179b1b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONVENTION AWARD (公約裁決)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Convention award is a specific type of arbitral award made under the New York Convention."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT (原訟法庭)&quot;" target="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE (臨時措施)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Court can grant interim measures, which are temporary protective actions in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HKIAC (香港國際仲裁中心)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"HKIAC is an institution that administers and conducts arbitrations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE (臨時措施)&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Interim measures can protect the rights of claimants during arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MACAO AWARD (澳門裁決)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Macao award is a specific type of arbitral award made in Macao, following its local arbitration law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINLAND (內地)&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mainland refers to the part of China excluding Hong Kong and Macao where claimants are based or operate from."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINLAND AWARD (內地裁決)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mainland award is a specific type of arbitral award made in accordance with Chinese arbitration law on the Mainland."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM OR COUNTER-CLAIM&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitration agreement typically involves claims or counterclaims between parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION RULES&quot;" target="&quot;EMERGENCY ARBITRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Emergency Arbitrators operate under specific rules that govern their authority and the nature of any emergency relief they can grant."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EMERGENCY ARBITRATOR is appointed based on the arbitration rules agreed or adopted by parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0813ab9a59ae553fa1d3747bf42131f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad963d62d75768847794433df9caf4b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION RULES&quot;" target="&quot;SOCIAL SCIENCES PERSPECTIVE ON ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The social sciences perspective can provide insights into the rules and practices of arbitration, enhancing understanding and application."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1ad963d62d75768847794433df9caf4b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION RULES&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Court's enforcement powers are guided by the arbitration rules, which define the scope and manner in which emergency relief may be granted."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0813ab9a59ae553fa1d3747bf42131f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFENCE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitration agreement may involve defenses raised by parties against claims or counterclaims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 68 OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Another section of the ordinance that pertains specifically to arbitration matters."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDING&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law includes provisions for arbitration proceedings, which can involve court-ordered interim measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6eef98cdb7cf96d52a56e0103910d67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDING&quot;" target="&quot;OATH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Oaths can be administered during arbitration proceedings, showing a procedural relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDING&quot;" target="&quot;AFFIRMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Affirmations are also used in arbitration proceedings alongside oaths."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDING&quot;" target="&quot;MONEY AWARDED BY THE TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Money can be awarded in ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS by an ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7a7d382b60c68c418d8128c80396b687</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDING&quot;" target="&quot;THIRD PARTY LICENSEE (第三方特許持有人)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The THIRD PARTY LICENSEE is involved in the ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS, specifically regarding INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5b2687bf72645c6f4d1292a242f8ee55</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDING&quot;" target="&quot;INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY (IP)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS deal with disputes related to INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5b2687bf72645c6f4d1292a242f8ee55</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERNATIONAL COMMERCIAL ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION THROUGH ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"International Commercial Arbitration is a form of dispute resolution through arbitration, as defined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERNATIONAL COMMERCIAL ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ON INTERNATIONAL COMMERCIAL ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law provides legal framework for International Commercial Arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-603a9b33a6e3900af70fd439592326ba</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OBJECT OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law is referenced in relation to the object of this ordinance, indicating a connection through legal frameworks or principles."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c8bbf5a007054d5e9238f9704d8e1b9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OBJECT OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;TRADE FACILITATION COMMISSION示范法例&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both documents focus on facilitating trade and resolving disputes efficiently, suggesting they are related through their objectives of enhancing commercial practices."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c8bbf5a007054d5e9238f9704d8e1b9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRINCIPLES OF THIS ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;OBJECT OF THIS ORDINANCE (ENGLISH VERSION)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both versions of the principles are consistent in their emphasis on fair arbitration and freedom for parties to resolve disputes, suggesting a strong relationship through shared legal objectives."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c8bbf5a007054d5e9238f9704d8e1b9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRADE FACILITATION COMMISSION示范法例&quot;" target="&quot;OBJECT OF THIS ORDINANCE (ENGLISH VERSION)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both documents aim at facilitating trade and dispute resolution in their respective contexts, suggesting an underlying common goal of promoting fair and efficient arbitration processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both documents aim at facilitating trade and resolving disputes efficiently, indicating a connection in their overarching goals of promoting fair commercial practices."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c8bbf5a007054d5e9238f9704d8e1b9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRADE FACILITATION COMMISSION示范法例&quot;" target="&quot;PRINCIPLES OF THIS ORDINANCE (ENGLISH VERSION)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">23.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The principles mentioned for this Ordinance align with the spirit of trade facilitation, indicating a shared objective in promoting fair and efficient dispute resolution."&lt;SEP&gt;"The principles stated align with the spirit of facilitating trade and resolving disputes, suggesting a relationship through shared legal or operational goals."&lt;SEP&gt;"The principles stated in the English version align with the spirit of facilitating trade and resolving disputes, indicating a connection through shared legal or operational goals."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c8bbf5a007054d5e9238f9704d8e1b9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRADE FACILITATION COMMISSION示范法例&quot;" target="&quot;RECOURSE AGAINST AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"RECOURSE AGAINST AWARD is related to the legal framework, including the TRADE FACILITATION COMMISSION 示范法例."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7a7d382b60c68c418d8128c80396b687</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GENERAL PROVISIONS&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"General Provisions provide context and rules for interpreting ORDINANCE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea2051734d4010ecf353d49c7190a3cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 1&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law Article 1 defines the scope of application which is referenced in ORDINANCE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea2051734d4010ecf353d49c7190a3cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 1 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 5&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 5 replaces Article 1 of the UNCITRAL Model Law and has effect as a substitute."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-44b140c12657294fe5c5d3a3a3fddb7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 2 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 5&quot;">
  <data key="d4">3.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"There is no direct relationship between Section 5 and Article 2 of the UNCITRAL Model Law based on the provided text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-44b140c12657294fe5c5d3a3a3fddb7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 5&quot;" target="&quot;PART 10A&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 5's applicability is limited for Part 10A in certain conditions regarding non-Hong Kong arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-358c63f61ec2ce4f0f9b4f0675b579e4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 5&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 98F&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 5's applicability is modified by Section 98F when Part 10A applies to non-Hong Kong arbitrations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-358c63f61ec2ce4f0f9b4f0675b579e4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 5&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL PRACTICE FIRM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal practice firms are indirectly related to the applicability of Section 5 in relation to non-Hong Kong arbitrations covered by Part 10A."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-358c63f61ec2ce4f0f9b4f0675b579e4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 3 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 3 is part of the UNCITRAL Model Law, providing specific rules on receipt of written communications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-526d89a1459376fe55b0af078fc2a455</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 3 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;WRITTEN COMMUNICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 3 defines how written communication is deemed to have been received under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-526d89a1459376fe55b0af078fc2a455</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 3 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;HABITUAL RESIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"According to Article 3, a written communication is deemed received at an individual's habitual residence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-526d89a1459376fe55b0af078fc2a455</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 3 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;MAILING ADDRESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 3 includes mailing address as one of the valid locations for receiving written communications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-526d89a1459376fe55b0af078fc2a455</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 3 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED LETTER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Registered letter is mentioned in Article 3 as a method to provide proof of delivery attempt."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-526d89a1459376fe55b0af078fc2a455</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WRITTEN COMMUNICATION&quot;" target="&quot;ADDRESSEE'S LAST-KNOWN PLACE OF BUSINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A written communication can be deemed received at the addressee's last-known place of business if other addresses cannot be found after a reasonable inquiry."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-35abbe99a6e0f69accfed39ff1b9fa2a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WRITTEN COMMUNICATION&quot;" target="&quot;ADDRESSEE'S HABITUAL RESIDENCE OR MAILING ADDRESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A written communication can also be deemed received at the addressee's habitual residence or mailing address, provided it is delivered personally or to his place of business."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-35abbe99a6e0f69accfed39ff1b9fa2a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WRITTEN COMMUNICATION&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED LETTER OR ANY OTHER MEANS WHICH PROVIDES A RECORD OF ATTEMPT TO DELIVER IT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A written communication can also be deemed received if delivered by registered letter or another method that records the delivery attempt, even without personal delivery at known addresses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-35abbe99a6e0f69accfed39ff1b9fa2a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 4&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 4 is a part of the UNCITRAL Model Law, detailing the waiver of right to object in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4125722b26dc9c686c88dca771d7712f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT INTERVENTION LIMITS&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of court intervention limits is discussed in Article 5 of the UNCITRAL Model Law, specifying when courts can intervene in arbitral matters."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4125722b26dc9c686c88dca771d7712f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 5 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 5 is explicitly stated as a part of the UNCITRAL Model Law, defining the extent of court intervention in arbitration matters."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4125722b26dc9c686c88dca771d7712f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG INTERNATIONAL ARBITRATION CENTRE&quot;" target="&quot;CHIEF JUDGE OF THE终审法院&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Chief Judge of the Final Court's approval is required for the Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre to execute certain functions as per Article 13(3) and other provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4125722b26dc9c686c88dca771d7712f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG INTERNATIONAL ARBITRATION CENTRE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATOR(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre is responsible for appointing arbitrators when necessary, either directly or through the parties involved."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre is responsible for appointing arbitrators when the number of arbitrators is odd and more than 3, or upon request if parties fail to agree on appointments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e8dac8ba7cc8864d7ff7dc57b5b28604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23b1f9e25ad7b2970cb215d6bd454574</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG INTERNATIONAL ARBITRATION CENTRE&quot;" target="&quot;THE TRADE FACILITATION COMMISSION示范法&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre may be involved in the appointment process according to The Trade Facilitation Commission's示范法, particularly when there are multiple arbitrators."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23b1f9e25ad7b2970cb215d6bd454574</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG INTERNATIONAL ARBITRATION CENTRE&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre works with the Parties to resolve disputes and ensure proper arbitration procedures are followed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e8dac8ba7cc8864d7ff7dc57b5b28604</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG INTERNATIONAL ARBITRATION CENTRE&quot;" target="&quot;MEDIATOR APPOINTMENT BY HKIAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The HONG KONG INTERNATIONAL ARBITRATION CENTRE can appoint a MEDIATOR by the application of any party when arbitrators cannot agree on certain matters."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3aa40d92e810c15d1924e632ab83962f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPETENT COURT&quot;" target="&quot; COURT &quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Competent courts referred to in articles of the UNCITRAL Model Law have their functions defined and executed by the Court."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-20600c9214528cc8c5fe5923e8a061ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPETENT COURT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL issues interim measures that must be recognized and enforced by the COMPETENT COURT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-610c6dec3dfd2d606eea19c4dfbadfa7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;時效條例 (第347章)&quot;" target="&quot; COURT &quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Time Bar Ordinance applies to arbitration as it does to court litigation, defining procedural limits for legal proceedings including arbitrations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-20600c9214528cc8c5fe5923e8a061ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;仲裁協議&quot;" target="&quot; COURT &quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration agreements are subject to the Court's functions and procedures defined by the UNCITRAL Model Law regarding time bars and other related matters."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-20600c9214528cc8c5fe5923e8a061ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE LIMITATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 347)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Limitation Ordinance applies to arbitrations as it would apply to actions in the court, and terms within arbitration agreements do not affect its application."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-026f8c614649cf19151a207c9397cdd7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE LIMITATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 347)&quot;" target="&quot;COURT ORDER SETTING ASIDE AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A court order setting aside an award must be excluded in computing the time prescribed by a limitation enactment for the commencement of proceedings with respect to matters submitted to arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-026f8c614649cf19151a207c9397cdd7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT ORDER SETTING ASIDE AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Terms within arbitration agreements do not prevent court orders from setting aside awards, which affects the computation of time limits for legal procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-026f8c614649cf19151a207c9397cdd7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERPLEADER PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIMANT(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CLAIMANT(S) participate in INTERPLEADER PROCEEDINGS where disputes may arise between them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d01af5189922031b9258e77aa6012d87</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMANT(S)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ARBITRATION AGREEMENT is relevant to CLAIMANT(S) involved in interpleader proceedings and their disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d01af5189922031b9258e77aa6012d87</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NON-PUBLIC HEARING&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court can order legal proceedings to be heard in a non-public hearing, showing control over such hearings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3977494e2da78f664ddb0fbbd085bf83</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REPORTING RESTRICTIONS FOR NON-PUBLIC HEARINGS&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court has the authority to impose reporting restrictions for non-public hearings, indicating a regulatory role over such hearings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3977494e2da78f664ddb0fbbd085bf83</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NON-PUBLIC COURT PROCEDURE&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court handles non-public court procedures as defined by the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-db21b6924967f080042e677399758e3c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NON-PUBLIC COURT PROCEDURE&quot;" target="&quot;COURT'S RULING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rulings are made by the court regarding non-public court procedures, which can affect their handling and publication."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-db21b6924967f080042e677399758e3c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT'S RULING&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court makes rulings in non-public court procedures, which can be reported under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-db21b6924967f080042e677399758e3c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT'S RULING&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL REPORTING AND PROFESSIONAL JOURNALS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Court rulings on closed court proceedings may be reported in legal reporting and professional journals if they have significant legal importance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-db21b6924967f080042e677399758e3c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL REPORTING AND PROFESSIONAL JOURNALS&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court's rulings on closed court proceedings may be published in legal reporting and professional journals if deemed of significant legal importance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-db21b6924967f080042e677399758e3c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT DIRECTION&quot;" target="&quot;CLOSED COURT PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Court directions apply to closed court proceedings, specifying what information can be published."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5f33b7b9020135f31323fbae5f4463c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT DIRECTION&quot;" target="&quot;LAW REPORTS AND PROFESSIONAL PUBLICATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Courts may direct that reports of judgments in certain cases may be published in law reports and professional publications if the judgment is considered to have major legal interest."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5f33b7b9020135f31323fbae5f4463c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT DIRECTION&quot;" target="&quot;10 YEARS RESTRICTION ON PUBLICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Court directions can include restrictions on publication for up to 10 years, especially when a party wishes to remain confidential."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5f33b7b9020135f31323fbae5f4463c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSED COURT PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;LAW REPORTS AND PROFESSIONAL PUBLICATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Closed court proceedings may lead to reports being published in law reports and professional publications if the judgment is of major legal interest."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5f33b7b9020135f31323fbae5f4463c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLOSED COURT PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;10 YEARS RESTRICTION ON PUBLICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Closed court proceedings may be subject to a 10-year restriction on publication if any party wishes to remain confidential."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5f33b7b9020135f31323fbae5f4463c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LAW REPORTS AND PROFESSIONAL PUBLICATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration awards can be reported in law reports and professional publications, provided they are of major legal interest."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5f33b7b9020135f31323fbae5f4463c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration proceedings can result in an arbitration award, which involves decisions or judgments made during these proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5f33b7b9020135f31323fbae5f4463c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT can make orders that may lead to an ARBITRATION AWARD enforceable under this Ordinance or any other Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19092b2cdc4468b2128aef41dc2b2b67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ORDINANCE governs the enforcement of ARBITRATION AWARDS that may arise from arbitration proceedings outside Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19092b2cdc4468b2128aef41dc2b2b67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;TRADE FACILITATION COMMISSION示范法&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Trade Facilitation Commission's示范法 provides a basis for arbitration awards, which can be subject to application for setting aside under the Arbitration Award. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd8b5a6b74d6568cda4bfce7dd132460</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;HIGH COURT ORDINANCE (CAP. 4)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The High Court Ordinance (Cap. 4) provides the framework within which arbitration awards can be challenged or set aside, including through applications for setting aside arbitral awards. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd8b5a6b74d6568cda4bfce7dd132460</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;HONG KONG LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Hong Kong law provides rules for enforcing or rejecting arbitration awards, including those from the Mainland."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-47762eabb07bb9265d79611ab6fc55f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL makes an AWARDS based on the settlement or case details."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03bb9907c4707aee4e32c05a81efe12a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;COURT APPLICATION TO SET ASIDE AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A court application to set aside an arbitration award can be made if certain conditions are met, such as procedural irregularities or public policy conflicts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6f35bbfd9ee83b0701ea2384c506063d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;正式语文&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral award should be in an officially accepted language for it to be recognized and enforced, as per legal requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6f35bbfd9ee83b0701ea2384c506063d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitration agreement refers to the arbitral proceedings it governs."&lt;SEP&gt;"An arbitration agreement sets the stage for arbitral proceedings when parties agree on submitting their disputes to arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd6c63034b5446fb90d89932614a5d4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-655dbcc67746c1c9fceca1a4e089796b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitral proceedings are a type of dispute resolution procedure that must be considered before initiating arbitration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dispute resolution procedures include arbitral proceedings as one method to resolve disputes before initiating arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42e0db1f27b3313444cf12ec497ffd57</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;THE LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 44 to Section 47 of the Legal Practitioners Ordinance do not apply to arbitral proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-85b8cad9edd61a2498008aaa9412835f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;THE TRADE FACILITATION AND CUSTOMS COOPERATION AGREEMENT示范法&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text does not directly establish a relationship between Arbitral Proceedings and the Trade Facilitation and Customs Cooperation Agreement, but it sets up a context where such proceedings are discussed in relation to legal frameworks."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-85b8cad9edd61a2498008aaa9412835f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS are terminated by the final award or an order of the arbitral tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5943028cc6f3beb70826c83454e86767</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;COSTS OF ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal hearing the ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS can order costs related to those proceedings under sections 74 and 75."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ff2369343594485564382d2d30ba3755</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURTS have the authority to consolidate or hear multiple ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS at the same time under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ff2369343594485564382d2d30ba3755</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS result in the issuance of an AWARD by ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5a62633bac9b2c0c6ed1e0aa83ce66e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">25.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An ARBITRATION AGREEMENT leads to an AWARD being made."&lt;SEP&gt;"An arbitral tribunal makes a final and binding award based on the arbitration agreement unless otherwise agreed by the parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"The arbitration agreement leads to an award being made in the arbitral proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7e5ed4af08fa3d54713649e0adf6d0ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-655dbcc67746c1c9fceca1a4e089796b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63fa361a4bbae312d93826ee30bf2182</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A court may be involved in enforcing or challenging an award, as mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Court decides on the award based on findings of fact in the appeal process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e17ae2e1dd0c38e2c8a34618b769e578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-655dbcc67746c1c9fceca1a4e089796b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 14 of UNCITRAL Model Law deals with situations where an award may be set aside if a challenged arbitrator is upheld by the Court."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;COURT DECISIONS ON ARBITRATOR CHALLENGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">27.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Court decisions on arbitrator challenges can affect the validity and enforcement of awards as per Article 14 of UNCITRAL Model Law."&lt;SEP&gt;"Court decisions on arbitrator challenges can affect the validity of an award, potentially leading to its set-aside if a challenged arbitrator is upheld by the Court."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW IMPLEMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The implementation of UNCITRAL Model Law provides specific rules for awards and challenges thereto as per Article 14, which can impact the validity or enforceability of an award."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION FEES AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitral tribunal can make an award regarding arbitration fees in addition to the main award."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7e5ed4af08fa3d54713649e0adf6d0ad</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRAL AUTHORITY makes the AWARD after considering the case presented by parties involved in arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-63fa361a4bbae312d93826ee30bf2182</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal may continue proceedings and make an award even when a challenge is pending."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4373f38dac5749d35f8ccd70b8bf1d15</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;DETERMINATION OF THE DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An award will finally decide the dispute and interim measures are taken prior to this determination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d56571b98ba26116ef651214c379b2f2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">27.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL issues an AWARD which may be subject to review by the COURT for irregularities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL makes the AWARD, which can be challenged by PARTIES in COURT."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Arbitral Tribunal makes an initial award which can be appealed to the Court."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5a62633bac9b2c0c6ed1e0aa83ce66e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e17ae2e1dd0c38e2c8a34618b769e578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b2fac04904854d200ea9c9161cb98c1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;APPLICABILITY CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"APPLICABILITY CLAUSE governs the validity of AWARD under certain conditions, such as SUBSTANTIAL INJUSTICE or SERIOUS IRREGULARITY."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5a62633bac9b2c0c6ed1e0aa83ce66e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PARTIES agree on procedures and terms that guide the issuance of the AWARDS, but these agreements can be challenged if there is fraud or public policy issues."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2b2fac04904854d200ea9c9161cb98c1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOVERNMENT BODY, REGULATORY BODY, COURT OR TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OR OTHER JUDICIAL AUTHORITY &quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Government bodies and regulatory authorities are included under the definition of courts or other judicial authorities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0cc9146e12fcb8f714add3a3f7c0771b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROFESSIONAL OR ANY OTHER ADVISER OF ANY OF THE PARTIES&quot;" target="&quot; COURT OR OTHER JUDICIAL AUTHORITY &quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties may disclose information to their advisers, who can be involved in legal proceedings before a court or other judicial authority."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0cc9146e12fcb8f714add3a3f7c0771b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROFESSIONAL OR ANY OTHER ADVISER OF ANY OF THE PARTIES&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties may seek advice from their advisers on matters related to arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0cc9146e12fcb8f714add3a3f7c0771b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OPTION I OF ARTICLE 7 OF THE UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition and form of the Arbitration Agreement are specified in Option I of Article 7."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DATA ELECTRIC EXCHANGE (EDI)&quot;" target="&quot;EMAIL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both EDI and Email fall under electronic communication methods as defined by the Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DATA ELECTRIC EXCHANGE (EDI)&quot;" target="&quot;TELEGRAPH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both EDI and Telegraph are forms of data transmission mentioned in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DATA ELECTRIC EXCHANGE (EDI)&quot;" target="&quot;FACSIMILE (FAX)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both EDI and Fax are methods of communication as defined by the Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DATA ELECTRIC EXCHANGE (EDI)&quot;" target="&quot;MODEL LAW ARTICLE 7. DEFINITION AND FORM OF ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition and form of arbitration agreement include EDI as a method of communication."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DATA ELECTRIC EXCHANGE (EDI)&quot;" target="&quot;EMAIL COMMUNICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both Email Communication and Data Electric Exchange are forms of electronic communication methods mentioned in the Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMAIL&quot;" target="&quot;TELEGRAPH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Email is mentioned alongside Telegraph in defining electronic communications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMAIL&quot;" target="&quot;FACSIMILE (FAX)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both Email and Fax are forms of written communication as per the Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TELEGRAPH&quot;" target="&quot;FACSIMILE (FAX)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Telegraph is mentioned in relation to Facsimile, both being methods of data transmission."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACSIMILE (FAX)&quot;" target="&quot;EMAIL COMMUNICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Email Communication is a form of written communication as defined by the Model Law, similar to Fax."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACSIMILE (FAX)&quot;" target="&quot;TELEGRAPHY SERVICES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both Telegraphy Services and Facsimile are methods of data transmission mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Telegraphy Services and Facsimile both involve data transmission, as per the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MODEL LAW ARTICLE 7. DEFINITION AND FORM OF ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;STANDARDIZED ARBITRATION CLAUSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Standardized Arbitration Clauses are defined and specified in Article 7 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MODEL LAW ARTICLE 7. DEFINITION AND FORM OF ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORIZATION FOR RECORDING AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Authorization for Recording Agreement is a concept relevant in defining arbitration agreements as per Article 7 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MODEL LAW ARTICLE 7. DEFINITION AND FORM OF ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;REFERENCE TO WRITTEN ARBITRATION CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Reference to Written Arbitration Clause is a concept defined in Article 7 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MODEL LAW ARTICLE 7. DEFINITION AND FORM OF ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;STANDARD FORMAT OF ARBITRATION CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Standard Format of Arbitration Clause is specified and defined in Article 7 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WRITTEN CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Written Contract may include arbitration agreements as per the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MUTUAL CLAIM STATEMENT AND DEFENSE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mutual Claim Statement and Defense may be part of an Arbitration Agreement, according to the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REFERENCE TO WRITTEN ARBITRATION CLAUSE&quot;" target="&quot;WRITTEN COMMUNICATION AGREEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Written Communication Agreements often include references to written arbitration clauses, according to the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STANDARD FORMAT OF ARBITRATION CLAUSE&quot;" target="&quot;ELECTRONIC DATA INTERCHANGE (EDI)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The standard format of arbitration clause may include EDI as a method for written agreements, according to the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION THROUGH ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Dispute resolution through arbitration is based on the terms of an ARBITRATION AGREEMENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TELECOMMUNICATION NETWORKS&quot;" target="&quot;TELECOMMUNICATION INFRASTRUCTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Telecommunication Networks and Telecommunication Infrastructure are related concepts involving communication systems."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STANDARDIZED COMMUNICATION FORMATS&quot;" target="&quot;DATA COMMUNICATION STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Data Communication Standards and Standardized Communication Formats both pertain to standardized ways of communication as per the Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STANDARDIZED COMMUNICATION FORMATS&quot;" target="&quot;DATA INTERCHANGE STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Data Interchange Standards are related to Standardized Communication Formats in defining communication standards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERNATIONAL TRADE LAW&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"International Trade Law may involve Arbitration Proceedings as a means of dispute resolution in international commerce."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMAIL COMMUNICATION&quot;" target="&quot;TELEGRAPHY SERVICES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both Email Communication and Telegraphy Services are forms of electronic communications mentioned in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DATA COMMUNICATION STANDARDS&quot;" target="&quot;TELECOMMUNICATION INFRASTRUCTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Telecommunication Infrastructure supports Data Communication Standards, as per the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERNATIONAL COMMERCIAL DISPUTES&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"International Commercial Disputes may be resolved through Arbitration Agreements according to the Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORAL AGREEMENT ACKNOWLEDGMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Oral Agreement Acknowledgment may be relevant in establishing an Arbitration Agreement as per the Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TELECOMMUNICATION INFRASTRUCTURE&quot;" target="&quot;ELECTRONIC COMMUNICATION SYSTEMS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Electronic Communication Systems and Telecommunication Infrastructure both pertain to the infrastructure for data transmission, as per the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a71d73fb76a414dd08c07b249777f35d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TELECOMMUNICATION INFRASTRUCTURE&quot;" target="&quot;AIRPORTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Airports often have associated telecommunications infrastructure for communication and logistics support."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c91eb1ea65f818d429644871f6909abf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TELECOMMUNICATION INFRASTRUCTURE&quot;" target="&quot;WATER SUPPLY INFRASTRUCTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Telecommunication infrastructure can support water supply management through modern communication systems."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c91eb1ea65f818d429644871f6909abf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 7 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 7 is part of the UNCITRAL Model Law, defining and forming arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15c5427da69a34465f87e7a3287bd026</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 7 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Option I of Article 7 defines what constitutes an Arbitration Agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15c5427da69a34465f87e7a3287bd026</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 7 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;EXCHANGE OF STATEMENTS OF CLAIM AND DEFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitration agreement can be formed through an exchange of statements of claim and defence as per Article 7(5)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15c5427da69a34465f87e7a3287bd026</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 7 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;DOCUMENT CONTAINING ARBITRATION CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A reference to a document containing an arbitration clause is considered part of the contract, forming an arbitration agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15c5427da69a34465f87e7a3287bd026</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OPTION I OF ARTICLE 7&quot;" target="&quot;ELECTRONIC COMMUNICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Option I includes electronic communications as a form of arbitration agreement in writing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15c5427da69a34465f87e7a3287bd026</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OPTION I OF ARTICLE 7&quot;" target="&quot;DATA MESSAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Data messages are included under the definition of Electronic Communication, which is part of Option I."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-15c5427da69a34465f87e7a3287bd026</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ELECTRONIC COMMUNICATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Electronic communication can constitute an arbitration agreement if it meets certain conditions as defined for writing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ELECTRONIC COMMUNICATION&quot;" target="&quot;WRITING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Writing includes electronic communication under the definition provided by the Commission."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ELECTRONIC COMMUNICATION&quot;" target="&quot;REFERENCE TO DOCUMENT CONTAINING ARBITRATION CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Electronic communication is considered part of an arbitration agreement when it meets certain criteria as defined for writing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ELECTRONIC COMMUNICATION&quot;" target="&quot;EXCHANGE OF STATEMENTS OF CLAIM AND DEFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An electronic exchange can form a written agreement if it satisfies the conditions set by the Commission's definition of writing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ELECTRONIC COMMUNICATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 7. DEFINITION OF ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The article includes electronic communication as part of the definition for writing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXCHANGE OF STATEMENTS OF CLAIM AND DEFENCE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An exchange of statements can form an arbitration agreement if it meets specific conditions as defined by the writing requirement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXCHANGE OF STATEMENTS OF CLAIM AND DEFENCE&quot;" target="&quot;WRITING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An exchange can be in writing if it meets the conditions set by the Commission's definition of writing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXCHANGE OF STATEMENTS OF CLAIM AND DEFENCE&quot;" target="&quot;REFERENCE TO DOCUMENT CONTAINING ARBITRATION CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A reference to an arbitration clause in a document can be considered part of an exchange that forms an agreement, according to the Commission's definition."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXCHANGE OF STATEMENTS OF CLAIM AND DEFENCE&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 7. DEFINITION OF ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The article includes exchanges of statements as part of the definition for forming an agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-370a790bb1d210c95f7d43dd74075952</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT LITIGATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRATION AGREEMENT and COURT LITIGATION are related as the text describes scenarios where a party may request arbitration after initiating court litigation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-93da520a07c3f45a47c10cf01594d640</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT LITIGATION&quot;" target="&quot;LABOR AND MANAGEMENT TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The LABOR AND MANAGEMENT TRIBUNAL is mentioned as a context where disputes might also involve COURT LITIGATION, especially when there's an arbitration agreement in place."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-93da520a07c3f45a47c10cf01594d640</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 8 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 8 of the UNCITRAL Model Law is directly applicable in court proceedings involving arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-524caefeb3520a83b6c8130676f95c53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 8 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 8 specifically addresses how courts should handle arbitration agreements and related disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-524caefeb3520a83b6c8130676f95c53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 8 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 8 of the UNCITRAL Model Law provides a framework for dispute resolution involving arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-524caefeb3520a83b6c8130676f95c53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 8 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;LITIGATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 8 of the UNCITRAL Model Law also addresses situations where litigation is involved in disputes subject to arbitration agreements, providing a balance between court and arbitral proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-524caefeb3520a83b6c8130676f95c53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSTANTIVE CLAIM BEFORE COURT&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 8 of the UNCITRAL Model Law deals with substantive claims before court in matters subject to an arbitration agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-524caefeb3520a83b6c8130676f95c53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSTANTIVE CLAIM BEFORE COURT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration agreement and substantive claims are directly related as they both pertain to legal disputes brought before a court."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e7564251214dafe0ef47139543601d3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration is one method of dispute resolution as mentioned in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e027acdec4c66c21703cf2589ec26926</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY MEASURES BY COURT&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law outlines provisions for courts to issue temporary measures in relation to arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a6c644c4a7067336b920f4ea718d504d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY MEASURES BY COURT&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court can order temporary measures such as staying proceedings or retaining property in relation to arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a6c644c4a7067336b920f4ea718d504d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY MEASURES BY COURT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration agreements and the court's issuance of interim measures are interconnected, with courts recognizing these agreements while issuing necessary temporary measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a6c644c4a7067336b920f4ea718d504d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY MEASURES BY COURT&quot;" target="&quot;COURT REFERRAL PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court referral procedure can coexist with temporary measures by the court during or before arbitral proceedings, as both serve different purposes in dispute resolution."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd6c63034b5446fb90d89932614a5d4a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 9 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;ENFORCEMENT BY OR AGAINST THE PERSONAL REPRESENTATIVES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 9 of the UNCITRAL Model Law allows arbitration agreements to be enforced by or against personal representatives after a party's death."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMERGENCY ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An emergency arbitrator can be appointed under the arbitration agreement to handle urgent relief applications before the arbitral tribunal is constituted."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMERGENCY ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;2013 AMENDMENT (S. 5)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The amendment in 2013 added Part 3A which includes provisions for appointing and using emergency arbitrators to handle urgent relief applications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMERGENCY ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Court has jurisdiction over emergency relief granted by an Emergency Arbitrator, and can enforce such relief if certain conditions are met."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0813ab9a59ae553fa1d3747bf42131f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMERGENCY ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;EMERGENCY RELIEF&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Emergency Arbitrators have the authority to grant specific types of emergency relief that can be enforced by the Court under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0813ab9a59ae553fa1d3747bf42131f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMERGENCY ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration includes proceedings before an emergency arbitrator as one of its components."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e0edcefcdaacd59cb7375b56608a714e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMERGENCY ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION FUNDING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration funding can be provided for emergency arbitrator proceedings as part of the costs associated with arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e0edcefcdaacd59cb7375b56608a714e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMERGENCY ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORIZED BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Authorized Body may appoint an Emergency Arbitrator under section 22A. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMERGENCY ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;EMERGENCY ARBITRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Emergency Arbitrator is defined in the text with a specific meaning given by Section 22A."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca2c3669141d3f1cd87a21d68d494cf5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMERGENCY ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL OR COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The terms 'arbitral tribunal or court' and 'emergency arbitrator' are defined differently based on the context, with each term referring to a specific type of dispute resolution process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMERGENCY ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 22A OF CAP. 159 (《第159章》第22A條)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'emergency arbitrator' is defined by section 22A of Cap. 159, providing the specific meaning and context for this role."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART 3A OF ENFORCEMENT OF EMERGENCY RELIEF&quot;" target="&quot;EMERGENCY RELIEF ENFORCEMENT MECHANISMS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Part 3A deals with mechanisms for enforcing emergency relief, including the role of an emergency arbitrator."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEATH OF PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;PERSONAL REPRESENTATIVES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The death of a party does not discharge an arbitration agreement, and it may still be enforced by or against the personal representatives of that party."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXTINGUISHED SUBSTANTIVE RIGHT OR OBLIGATION&quot;" target="&quot;ENACTMENT OR RULE OF LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The operation of an enactment or rule of law is not affected if a substantive right or obligation is extinguished by the death of a party, as stated in Subsection (2)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d79d6d4cb98ab3f89dde1c3946204317</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HARM OR DAMAGE PREVENTION MEASURES&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Preventive measures are actions taken to avoid harm or damage, which could relate to the work of an arbitration tribunal in resolving disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1ad963d62d75768847794433df9caf4b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSET PRESERVATION METHODS&quot;" target="&quot;MATHEMATICS OF ASSET PRESERVATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Asset preservation methods often require mathematical calculations to ensure effective asset management during disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1ad963d62d75768847794433df9caf4b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG INTERNATIONAL ARBITRATION CENTRE (HKIAC)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The HKIAC has the authority to decide the number of arbitrators when parties fail to agree, forming the Arbitration Tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3161c0abf732689fd0fb63c291711d64</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 11(2)&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 10(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 10(2) and (3) of the UNCITRAL Model Law are not applicable, while Article 11 deals with the freedom to determine the number of arbitrators including third-party authorization."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2d812128591f21f04c27e6ee77e7d3c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 11(2)&quot;" target="&quot;THE PARTIES'&lt;BR&gt;RIGHT TO AUTHORIZE THIRD PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The parties have the right under Article 11(2) to authorize a third party, such as an institution like HKIAC, to determine the number of arbitrators."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2d812128591f21f04c27e6ee77e7d3c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR(S)&quot;" target="&quot;THE TRADE FACILITATION COMMISSION示范法&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The role of arbitrators is defined by or influenced by the provisions in The Trade Facilitation Commission's示范法."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23b1f9e25ad7b2970cb215d6bd454574</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR(S)&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL MODEL LAW outlines procedures for appointing ARBITRATORS, including default methods if parties fail to agree."&lt;SEP&gt;"UNCITRAL Model Law provides guidelines for appointing arbitrators, which can be adapted or applied by entities like the Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e8dac8ba7cc8864d7ff7dc57b5b28604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad8b00bb4712fdfd27d215a729380d5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR(S)&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">33.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties are involved in appointing arbitrators and can challenge their composition or procedure if necessary."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parties are involved in the process of appointing arbitrators, either directly or through the Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parties can agree on a procedure for appointing arbitrators, and if they fail, the court or other authority may intervene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parties have a role in appointing arbitrators, either directly or through agreement with other parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"The PARTIES are free to agree on a procedure for appointing ARBITRATORS in an arbitration case."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e8dac8ba7cc8864d7ff7dc57b5b28604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95a4de41db58b9a101c75606869df8f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4487876b424618c4533648d46889bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59c7140869534366dd7270de77711ef8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad8b00bb4712fdfd27d215a729380d5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR(S)&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OR OTHER AUTHORITY SPECIFIED IN ARTICLE 6&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT or other authority has the power to intervene and appoint ARBITRATORS if necessary."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court or other authority specified in Article 6 has the power to appoint arbitrators when necessary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4487876b424618c4533648d46889bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad8b00bb4712fdfd27d215a729380d5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR(S)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitrators form the composition of arbitration tribunals, which handle disputes through arbitration processes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e027acdec4c66c21703cf2589ec26926</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR(S)&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES INVOLVED&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitrators make the award and it affects Parties Involved in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0cddff72aaf0d2c6f21cba88e08e8e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR(S)&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Termination of Arbitration Proceedings affects the role and mandate of Arbitrators."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0cddff72aaf0d2c6f21cba88e08e8e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR(S)&quot;" target="&quot;TRANSACTION(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ARBITRATORS are appointed by the COURT based on the TRANSACTION(S) involved in the ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ee3bd35452fe0a7b5e9fa7dc2c1f8074</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR(S)&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT has the authority to appoint or confirm ARBITRATORS for certain ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ee3bd35452fe0a7b5e9fa7dc2c1f8074</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATORS PROCEDURE&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The procedure for appointing arbitrators involves parties who must follow specific rules and agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-07932cfedca106f703c16c8c95ba919e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATORS PROCEDURE&quot;" target="&quot;COURTS OR OTHER INSTITUTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Courts or other institutions may be involved in designating arbitrators if the parties fail to agree on their selection."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-07932cfedca106f703c16c8c95ba919e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURTS OR OTHER INSTITUTIONS&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties can request courts or other institutions to take necessary measures when appointing arbitrators, especially if agreements are not reached."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-07932cfedca106f703c16c8c95ba919e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT OR OTHER AUTHORITY SPECIFIED IN ARTICLE 6&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">23.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If the PARTIES fail to appoint ARBITRATORS, the COURT or other authority specified can make the appointment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parties can request the court or other authority specified in Article 6 to decide on an unsuccessful challenge, which decision cannot be appealed."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court or other authority specified in Article 6 can make the appointment of arbitrators if parties fail to agree."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4487876b424618c4533648d46889bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4373f38dac5749d35f8ccd70b8bf1d15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad8b00bb4712fdfd27d215a729380d5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT OR OTHER AUTHORITY SPECIFIED IN ARTICLE 6&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"According to the UNCITRAL MODEL LAW, the COURT or other authority can be involved in appointing ARBITRATORS if agreed upon by PARTIES."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ad8b00bb4712fdfd27d215a729380d5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT OR OTHER AUTHORITY SPECIFIED IN ARTICLE 6&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 14&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Under certain conditions, the court or other authority specified in Article 6 can decide on the termination of an arbitrator's mandate as per Article 14(2), impacting their role indirectly."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea943fe3338aa88e6573bf715e772abd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT OR OTHER AUTHORITY SPECIFIED IN ARTICLE 6&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 15 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court or other authority specified in Article 6 can also be involved in the appointment process of a substitute arbitrator under Article 15(2), impacting their role indirectly."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea943fe3338aa88e6573bf715e772abd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT OR OTHER AUTHORITY SPECIFIED IN ARTICLE 6&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION WITH THREE ARBITRATORS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If the court or other authority is required, it will make the third appointment in arbitration with three arbitrators when parties fail to agree."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4487876b424618c4533648d46889bd3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT OR OTHER AUTHORITY SPECIFIED IN ARTICLE 6&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION WITH A SOLE ARBITRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If the court or other authority is required, it will appoint a sole arbitrator if parties cannot agree on one."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c4487876b424618c4533648d46889bd3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT OR OTHER AUTHORITY SPECIFIED IN ARTICLE 6&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATOR QUALIFICATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court or other authority takes into account the parties' agreed qualifications when appointing an arbitrator to ensure independence and impartiality."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6cff72e41603eed38553fb4f306a008</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPOINTMENT PROCEDURE(S)&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law provides guidelines for the appointment procedure of arbitrators."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-95a4de41db58b9a101c75606869df8f4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 12 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;GROUNDS FOR CHALLENGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 12 outlines specific circumstances under which parties can challenge the arbitrator's impartiality or independence, providing clear grounds for such challenges."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GROUNDS FOR CHALLENGE&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 12&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 12 outlines specific circumstances that can give rise to justifiable doubts about an arbitrator's impartiality or independence, which are the grounds for challenge."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GROUNDS FOR CHALLENGE&quot;" target="&quot;第13條. 申请回避的程序&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The procedures outlined in Article 13 of UNCITRAL Model Law provide specific guidelines on how to address challenges based on the same grounds as defined by Article 12."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GROUNDS FOR CHALLENGE&quot;" target="&quot;拟对仲裁员提出回避申请的当事人应在知悉仲裁庭的组成或知悉第12(2)条所指的任何情况后十五天内向仲裁庭提出书面陈述,说明提出回避申请的理由&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The specific circumstances outlined in Article 13(2) are the same as those that can give rise to justifiable doubts about an arbitrator's impartiality or independence under Article 12."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GROUNDS FOR CHALLENGE&quot;" target="&quot;除非被申请回避的仲裁员辞职或对方当事人同意所提出的回避,仲裁庭应就是否回避作出决定&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The decision on whether to grant a challenge is based on the same grounds for doubt about impartiality or independence as defined in Article 12."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GROUNDS FOR CHALLENGE&quot;" target="&quot;提出回避申请的一方当事人可以在收到驳回其所提出的回避申请的决定通知后三十天内,请求第6条规定的法院或其他机构&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The procedures for challenging a decision on an application to disqualify an arbitrator are based on the same grounds as defined in Article 12."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISCLOSURE OF CIRCUMSTANCES&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties have a role in disclosing relevant information regarding an arbitrator's impartiality or independence to ensure fairness in the arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION FRAMEWORK&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties are part of the broader dispute resolution framework, which includes arbitration procedures governed by laws like UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORK FOR ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION INDUSTRY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The industry of dispute resolution relies on robust legal frameworks such as UNCITRAL Model Law, which provide clear guidelines for arbitration procedures and challenges."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCESS&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW PROVISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Provisions from UNCITRAL Model Law provide a legal framework governing the arbitration process and related challenges to arbitrators' roles."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7caa1789fd1dbffc0a18590eb020ccfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCESS&quot;" target="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Third party funding of arbitration is related to the Arbitration Process, as it involves obtaining or seeking funds for an arbitration process from a third party."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a252d91181bacec6fcd6f1d54297b19a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCESS&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL DECISION MAKING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration process is a part of the broader framework of legal decision-making within judicial systems."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e027acdec4c66c21703cf2589ec26926</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCESS&quot;" target="&quot;HARM OR DAMAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration process may be harmed by current or imminent actions that could cause prejudice to it, which is a reason for interim measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d56571b98ba26116ef651214c379b2f2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 12&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 12 is part of the UNCITRAL Model Law and defines grounds for challenge in arbitrator appointments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;13(4)条的规限下具有效力&quot;" target="&quot;第13條. 申请回避的程序&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 13 of UNCITRAL Model Law, in its limited effect under Article 13(4), provides specific procedures for challenging arbitrators."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第13条的规限下具有效力&quot;" target="&quot;当事人可自由约定申请仲裁员回避的程序&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties can freely agree on the procedure for challenging arbitrators as long as it complies with the limitations set by Article 13(4)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第6条规定的法院或其他机构&quot;" target="&quot;申请仲裁员回避的程序&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court or other institution specified in Article 6 has the authority to handle challenges to arbitration proceedings, including those under Article 13's procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3dcbbc66e6d4a6a335d1a835c7c9c2e8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION COMMISSION DEMONSTRATION ACT OF TRADE LAW COMMITTEE (TRADE LAW COMM.) 13(2)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Arbitration Tribunal can refer to the provisions of The Trade Law Commission's Demonstration Act, specifically Article 13(2), when dealing with challenges."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d3906bbf7ee03793cf876d19cdfab509</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RECUSAL REQUEST&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitrators have the right to recuse themselves under certain circumstances as per the provisions of The Trade Law Commission's Demonstration Act, specifically Article 13(2)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d3906bbf7ee03793cf876d19cdfab509</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPOINTMENT TERMINATION OF ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Arbitration Tribunal can terminate an arbitrator’s appointment based on challenges or other conditions as per the provisions of The Trade Law Commission's Demonstration Act, specifically Article 13."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d3906bbf7ee03793cf876d19cdfab509</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT RULING ON CHALLENGE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Court can rule on a challenge to an arbitrator’s decision and potentially overturn it if the challenge is deemed valid by the court, as per Article 26."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d3906bbf7ee03793cf876d19cdfab509</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 13 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATOR CHALLENGE PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 13 outlines the procedure for challenging an arbitrator under the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d8d309a2e724a8764d515c5d8417d815</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 13 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;COURT DECISION ON CHALLENGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 13 allows for a party to request that the court decide on an unsuccessful challenge, leading to a court decision on the challenge."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d8d309a2e724a8764d515c5d8417d815</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR CHALLENGE PROCEDURE&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law provides the framework within which Article 13 operates to define the arbitrator challenge procedure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d8d309a2e724a8764d515c5d8417d815</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHALLENGED ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Arbitral Tribunal may include a Challenged Arbitrator whose mandate could be terminated based on challenges under UNCITRAL Model Law Article 13(2)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHALLENGED ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration tribunal decides on challenges to arbitrators and may continue proceedings even when a challenge is pending."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4373f38dac5749d35f8ccd70b8bf1d15</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE HAGUE RULES OF ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORKS FOR ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Hague Rules of Arbitration are part of the broader legal frameworks for arbitration that provide guidelines and procedures for resolving international commercial disputes through arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION MECHANISMS&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORKS FOR ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal frameworks for arbitration are part of the broader dispute resolution mechanisms that include various methods such as arbitration, mediation, etc., to resolve commercial disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORKS FOR ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW IMPLEMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">26.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The implementation of UNCITRAL Model Law provides a legal framework for arbitration proceedings, including challenges and awards."&lt;SEP&gt;"The implementation of UNCITRAL Model Law provides a specific legal framework for arbitration proceedings, including challenges to arbitrators and award enforcement as per Article 14."&lt;SEP&gt;"The implementation of the UNCITRAL Model Law provides a specific legal framework for arbitration proceedings, including challenges to arbitrators and award enforcement as per Article 14."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORKS FOR ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PRACTICE AND PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal frameworks for arbitration include practices and procedures that govern how disputes are resolved through arbitration, including challenges to arbitrators."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORKS FOR ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARDS AND THEIR ENFORCEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal frameworks for arbitration include provisions on how awards are made, enforced, or set aside in cases of challenges to arbitrators as per UNCITRAL Model Law Article 14."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORKS FOR ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal frameworks for arbitration provide the rules and procedures that govern arbitration proceedings, including how challenges to arbitrators are handled as per UNCITRAL Model Law Article 14."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW IMPLEMENTATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The implementation of UNCITRAL Model Law provides specific rules for arbitration proceedings, including challenges to arbitrators and award enforcement as per Article 14."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT DECISIONS ON ARBITRATOR CHALLENGES&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Court decisions on arbitrator challenges can affect the validity of arbitration proceedings, potentially leading to their termination or modification based on Article 14."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 14&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 12(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both articles deal with situations where an arbitrator's inability to act or resignation affects their mandate, but do not imply acceptance of the reasons for such actions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea943fe3338aa88e6573bf715e772abd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 14&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The parties have the right to agree on the termination of an arbitrator's mandate under Article 14(2), affecting their direct involvement in dispute resolution processes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea943fe3338aa88e6573bf715e772abd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 15 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The parties play a role in initiating the process for appointing a substitute arbitrator under Article 15(2), impacting their involvement directly."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea943fe3338aa88e6573bf715e772abd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 15&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 15 of the UNCITRAL Model Law provides rules for appointing a substitute arbitrator when an original arbitrator's mandate terminates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-25f6483a2fc8ec5293ecc7908cc08eaf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 15&quot;" target="&quot;APPOINTMENT OF UMPIRE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 30 on the Appointment of an umpire is part of a broader set of rules for UNCITRAL Model Law, similar in structure and context to Article 15 which deals with substitute arbitrators."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-25f6483a2fc8ec5293ecc7908cc08eaf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 15&quot;" target="&quot;DEATH OF ARBITRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 29 on the Death of an arbitrator indirectly relates to Article 15 as it discusses authority termination, a concept that is relevant when considering replacement or substitute appointments under Article 15."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-25f6483a2fc8ec5293ecc7908cc08eaf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEATH OF ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text related to the death of an arbitrator in the UNCITRAL Model Law discusses how such events affect the authority and appointment rules for arbitrators."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-25f6483a2fc8ec5293ecc7908cc08eaf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEATH OF ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;APPOINTMENT OF UMPIRE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While both deal with appointments, Article 30 on the Appointment of an umpire is separate from the death of an arbitrator as discussed in Article 29. However, they are related in that they pertain to different aspects of arbitration procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-25f6483a2fc8ec5293ecc7908cc08eaf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPOINTMENT OF UMPIRE&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 30 on the Appointment of an umpire is explicitly part of the UNCITRAL Model Law, making it a direct relationship within this legal framework."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-25f6483a2fc8ec5293ecc7908cc08eaf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC ADJUDICATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public Adjudicators play a role within the Arbitration Procedure by potentially acting as arbiters if necessary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5d58ad3e1c6ef21463d303a3e0c4d6ff</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORIGINAL COURT&quot;" target="&quot;UMPIRE IN ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"In certain circumstances, the ORIGINAL COURT decides on the role of UMPIRE IN ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS when arbitrators cannot agree, giving it a supervisory function."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06937be24d44266dd94fe85733626b9d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORIGINAL COURT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The original court can exercise the power granted by the arbitral tribunal if no arbitral tribunal exists at a certain time, and it cannot be appealed against such an order."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42e0db1f27b3313444cf12ec497ffd57</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORIGINAL COURT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ORIGINAL COURT has the authority to order an arbitration tribunal to provide detailed reasons for its decisions and can also command a party to secure costs, indicating a supervisory relationship."&lt;SEP&gt;"The original court can exercise powers granted by this section if no arbitral tribunal exists, including making awards or orders regarding claims and disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-854d00c33e69aed0258675abc1e2d264&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-882b59070dba0a27453ac53b51232f89</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORIGINAL COURT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Original Court has the authority to decide whether an issue should be handled by the Arbitration Tribunal or itself."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7fd04bf2888da55881f593f9613b44e9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORIGINAL COURT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Original court has jurisdiction over arbitration proceedings and can order their consolidation or simultaneous hearing, as well as manage related procedural matters."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-818682a0f1950aff44c4e7f18a331608</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UMPIRE IN ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATORS AS THE ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UMPIRE IN ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS can replace Arbitrators as the arbitral tribunal, having similar powers and functions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06937be24d44266dd94fe85733626b9d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UMPIRE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATORS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UMPIRE can replace ARBITRATORS in making orders, directions and awards when there is disagreement among arbitrators."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-953aa58f588dab7be8bda910f0f31c38</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UMPIRE&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties have the freedom to agree on whether an UMPIRE attends arbitral proceedings and their functions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-953aa58f588dab7be8bda910f0f31c38</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATORS&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT can decide that the UMPIRE replaces ARBITRATORS if they cannot agree, ensuring the dispute is resolved."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT can intervene if ARBITRATORS fail to reach agreement, appointing UMPIRE as necessary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-953aa58f588dab7be8bda910f0f31c38</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATORS&quot;" target="&quot;PLACE OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Place of Arbitration is determined by the arbitral tribunal for consultations among its members or other necessary meetings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATORS&quot;" target="&quot;EXPERTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitrators can consult experts during arbitration proceedings for advice or information."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATORS&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitrators interact with the parties to hear their opinions and resolve disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATORS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitrators conduct arbitration proceedings, including meetings and hearings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATORS&quot;" target="&quot;REPEALED ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitrators appointed under the Repealed Ordinance continue to be valid after this new ordinance takes effect, maintaining their appointments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e0e013fee151f1254a38965f636a0159</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UMPIRE AS ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UMPIRE can act as the sole ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL when arbitrators cannot agree on a matter."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3aa40d92e810c15d1924e632ab83962f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISPUTE SUBMITTED TO ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATORS CANNOT AGREE ON A MATTER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"When there is a DISPUTE submitted to arbitration, arbitrators may not be able to agree on certain matters."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3aa40d92e810c15d1924e632ab83962f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATORS CANNOT AGREE ON A MATTER&quot;" target="&quot;COURT UNDER SUBSECTION (8) DECISION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"When arbitrators cannot agree, they may refer the matter to the COURT under subsection (8) for a decision."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3aa40d92e810c15d1924e632ab83962f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT UNDER SUBSECTION (8) DECISION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT under subsection (8) decision can make decisions regarding the matter when arbitrators cannot agree, acting as an ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3aa40d92e810c15d1924e632ab83962f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDIATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL OR COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The terms 'arbitral tribunal or court' and 'mediator' refer to different roles in legal proceedings, specifically for mediation processes as defined by sections 32 or 33 of Cap. 159."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDIATOR&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 32 OR SECTION 33 (《第159章》第32或第33條)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'mediator' is defined in relation to sections 32 or 33 of Cap. 159, indicating the specific context and role within mediation proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDIATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mediator is mentioned alongside Arbitration Tribunal, suggesting a relationship through the context of dispute resolution processes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6afb8943a99ee7bf996b0ce17c18a04b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDIATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL and MEDIATOR are roles involved in dispute resolution procedures, as defined by legal terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8214b3161676dee8df8d19240ebf6752</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDIATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Confidential information obtained during mediation must be treated confidentially unless otherwise agreed by the parties or specified by law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4a820d49f72ef3eeb5be9d057a9cb248</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDIATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The agreement may specify the conditions under which mediation can be conducted after arbitration proceedings have commenced."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4a820d49f72ef3eeb5be9d057a9cb248</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDIATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;SETTLEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mediation proceedings may or may not result in a settlement, and arbitrators handle confidential information obtained from parties during these proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da3d7a01706de39cd849092deef8b9b1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDIATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both arbitration and mediation proceedings are included under the broader term 'arbitration' in legal contexts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e0edcefcdaacd59cb7375b56608a714e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDIATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORIZED BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Authorized Body may appoint a Mediator for Mediation Proceedings under sections 32 or 33. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDIATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;MEDIATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mediation Proceedings are explicitly mentioned as part of arbitration procedures under this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca2c3669141d3f1cd87a21d68d494cf5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDIATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;律師&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"律师参与调解程序，提供相关的法律服务和指导。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ce0cbc87febf0559389231de15b6441b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT CLAUSE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitration agreement includes an arbitration clause which is part of the contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da3d7a01706de39cd849092deef8b9b1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT CLAUSE&quot;" target="&quot;REASONABLE STANDARD VERIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Reasonable standard verification is relevant when determining if a contract clause meets reasonable standards as defined by law or court interpretation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3af7b8f9d9569fddb32c031c5ec0dbc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;JURISDICTION OF ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;TRADE FACILITATION COMMISSION示范法&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The jurisdiction of arbitral tribunal under The Trade Facilitation Commission示范法 influences how disputes are resolved in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da3d7a01706de39cd849092deef8b9b1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT VALIDITY DETERMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitration agreement can address the validity determination of a contract, making it an independent clause within the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da3d7a01706de39cd849092deef8b9b1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION CLAUSE INDEPENDENCE&quot;" target="&quot;OBJECTION TO JURISDICTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"No objection to jurisdiction based on prior mediation role can be made by arbitrators; arbitration clauses are considered independently of other contractual terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da3d7a01706de39cd849092deef8b9b1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION CLAUSE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTUAL OBLIGATION (合同義務)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitration clause in a contract defines the obligations related to resolving disputes by arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-efd35e44f40ed90831a05d2c28acb9a5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION CLAUSE&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While an arbitration clause may grant authority to the arbitral tribunal, there remains a possibility of court intervention if disputes arise regarding the tribunal’s jurisdiction or validity of the agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-99f980ad8d8f30c8e25f6f9fa3f01746</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 16&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 16 of UNCITRAL Model Law addresses the arbitration agreement's validity and jurisdiction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-db0dce37722025939d7bba875b1ed10a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 16&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal may rule on its own jurisdiction according to Article 16 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-db0dce37722025939d7bba875b1ed10a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 16&quot;" target="&quot;STATEMENT OF DEFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A plea that the arbitral tribunal does not have jurisdiction shall be raised not later than the submission of the statement of defence, as stated in Article 16(2)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-db0dce37722025939d7bba875b1ed10a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 16&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 16 pertains to how disputes are handled during arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-db0dce37722025939d7bba875b1ed10a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATEMENT OF DEFENCE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The statement of defence is a critical document that must be submitted before certain objections can be raised against the arbitral tribunal's jurisdiction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-99f980ad8d8f30c8e25f6f9fa3f01746</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART 6 — INTERIM MEASURES AND PRELIMINARY ORDERS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Part 6 outlines the procedures for Interim Measures and Preliminary Orders that the ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL must follow when ruling on disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL has jurisdiction over matters related to Interim Measures and Preliminary Orders as defined in Part 6."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d3dc78b87bb7d880e40b21eadb5c8441</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART 6 — INTERIM MEASURES AND PRELIMINARY ORDERS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRATION AGREEMENT is the basis for determining jurisdiction over matters related to Interim Measures and Preliminary Orders as defined in Part 6."&lt;SEP&gt;"The provisions in Part 6 are directly related to and derived from the ARBITRATION AGREEMENT, defining how disputes should be handled under its terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d3dc78b87bb7d880e40b21eadb5c8441</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART 6&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text mentions Part 6 as a section within the document structure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM MEASURES AND PRELIMINARY ORDERS&quot;" target="&quot;DIVISION 1—INTERIM MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Division 1 is specifically about interim measures, which aligns with Interim Measures and Preliminary Orders."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法第17条.仲裁庭下令採取臨時措施的權力&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPORARY MEASURES (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 17 of the Arbitration Commission's model law directly relates to temporary measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法第17条.仲裁庭下令採取臨時措施的權力&quot;" target="&quot;COMPULSORY ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text mentions compulsory order as a form of interim measure under Article 17."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法第17条.仲裁庭下令採取臨時措施的權力&quot;" target="&quot;EVIDENCE PRESERVATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Evidence preservation is mentioned in the context of interim measures, indicating a relationship between Article 17 and evidence securing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法第17条.仲裁庭下令採取臨時措施的權力&quot;" target="&quot;RESOLUTION OF DISPUTES (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 17 is about interim measures, which are related to resolving disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法第17条.仲裁庭下令採取臨時措施的權力&quot;" target="&quot;FINAL AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text discusses the final award in relation to Article 17's interim measures, indicating a relationship between them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法第17条.仲裁庭下令採取臨時措施的權力&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 17 is part of the arbitration procedure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法第17条.仲裁庭下令採取臨時措施的權力&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The tribunal's authority is discussed in relation to Article 17."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法第17条.仲裁庭下令採取臨時措施的權力&quot;" target="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 17 is about interim measures, which are related to dispute resolution."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY MEASURES (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;" target="&quot;COURT DECISION MAKING PROCESS (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court decision-making process and temporary measures are both part of the arbitration procedure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EVIDENCE PRESERVATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal may order evidence preservation as part of interim measures, according to Article 17 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-793ad550c41441bec21087b3f776d5d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FINAL AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Final Award is made after Arbitration Proceedings, which ends when a decision is reached."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0cddff72aaf0d2c6f21cba88e08e8e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FINAL AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;PLACE OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Place of Arbitration is stated in the Final Award, indicating where the decision was made."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0cddff72aaf0d2c6f21cba88e08e8e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT DECISION MAKING PROCESS (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL'S AUTHORITY (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court decision-making process and the tribunal's authority are both related to Article 17."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT DECISION MAKING PROCESS (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;" target="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court decision-making process and dispute resolution are both part of the arbitration procedure."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court decision-making process is related to dispute resolution, both being part of the arbitration procedure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT DECISION MAKING PROCESS (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;" target="&quot;EVIDENCE PRESERVATION (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court decision-making process and evidence preservation are both part of the arbitration procedure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT DECISION MAKING PROCESS (ARTICLE 17 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;" target="&quot;FINAL AWARD (ARTICLE 56 OF THE ARBITRATION COMMISSION示范法)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court decision-making process and the final award are both part of the arbitration procedure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cf9a06366580d3053fd344bef553716e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INJUNCTION&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An injunction is considered an interim measure under Article 17 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-793ad550c41441bec21087b3f776d5d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INJUNCTION&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 35(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Injunction is included under Section 35(1), but not including orders under section 60."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-964639856a5f7a7d5119569944195b09</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 56 ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal does not grant orders under section 56, which are excluded from interim measures as per the model law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-793ad550c41441bec21087b3f776d5d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATUS QUO MAINTENANCE OR RESTORATION&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Status quo maintenance or restoration is an example of a temporary measure that can be ordered by the arbitral tribunal under Article 17."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-793ad550c41441bec21087b3f776d5d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSET PRESERVATION&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Asset preservation is an example of a temporary measure that can be ordered by the arbitral tribunal under Article 17."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-793ad550c41441bec21087b3f776d5d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY MEASURES&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Temporary measures are defined and regulated by the UNCITRAL Model Law for arbitral tribunals."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-793ad550c41441bec21087b3f776d5d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTY APPLICATION FOR INTERIM MEASURE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal may grant interim measures in response to applications from parties as per Article 17 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-793ad550c41441bec21087b3f776d5d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 17A&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 17A of UNCITRAL Model Law provides specific conditions for granting interim measures, which is directly related to its legal framework."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-492db0c693c82e4a1c002b00a74ae3fa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 17A&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ARTICLE 17A provides conditions for granting interim measures which are decided upon by the ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8630302d71316afe5c4d5a0aacb23fcb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTIES AGAINST WHOM THE MEASURE IS DIRECTED&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal can issue preliminary orders that may affect parties against whom the measure is directed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTIES AGAINST WHOM THE MEASURE IS DIRECTED&quot;" target="&quot;HARM NOT ADEQUATELY REPARABLE BY DAMAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties against whom a measure is directed may face harm that cannot be adequately repaired by damages, leading to the need for interim measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REQUESTING PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 17A CONDITIONS APPLY TO ANY PRELIMINARY ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The requesting party's success on the merits of the claim is considered under Article 17A conditions when applying for preliminary orders."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REQUESTING PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The REQUESTING PARTY must satisfy the ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL that harm not adequately reparable by an award of damages is likely to result if the measure is not ordered. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8630302d71316afe5c4d5a0aacb23fcb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REQUESTING PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OF THE STATE WHERE RECOGNITION OR ENFORCEMENT IS SOUGHT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court of the State where recognition or enforcement is sought may order the requesting party to provide appropriate security if necessary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5195e3e252b673b130b3aa632c54f19f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE REQUESTING PARTY WILL SUCCEED ON THE MERITS OF THE CLAIM&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal considers the possibility that the requesting party will succeed on the merits of the claim when deciding whether to grant interim measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISCLOSURE OF TEMPORARY MEASURE REQUEST&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal can issue a preliminary order to disclose temporary measure requests if it deems necessary, considering the risk of obstructing the purpose of such measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 17B OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;PRELIMINARY ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 17B of the UNCITRAL Model Law allows for applications and conditions related to preliminary orders, with considerations on disclosure risks and party notification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-44743bbc15d45a8109ce653b3d495eca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 17B (2)&quot;" target="&quot;PREVENTIVE MEASURE PURPOSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 17B(2) is related to the conditions for granting preventive measures, which are part of dispute resolution procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FINAL RESOLUTION DETERMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal makes final resolutions based on interim and preliminary orders issued during the dispute resolution process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE EFFECTIVENESS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The effectiveness of an interim measure is determined by the arbitral tribunal, which considers various conditions and factors."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-98a7cf7df4d78e9604020dd5f5323409</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 17A OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;PRELIMINARY ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 17A of the UNCITRAL Model Law defines conditions that apply to any preliminary order, specifically regarding harm likely to result from the order being granted or not."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-44743bbc15d45a8109ce653b3d495eca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRELIMINARY ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 17C OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 17C of the UNCITRAL Model Law provides specific procedures for preliminary orders, including notification to all parties and opportunities for party statements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-44743bbc15d45a8109ce653b3d495eca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRELIMINARY ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal can issue and modify preliminary orders, which are binding on the parties but not subject to court enforcement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The arbitral tribunal grants preliminary orders based on the application from parties or its own consideration, involving interim measures requested by one party against another."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4667827d445ebb505094eb4b58494cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7edd9fa2d61911f5177713c81f63dd22</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRELIMINARY ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 17D&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 17D of UNCITRAL Model Law allows for modification, suspension, or termination of preliminary orders by the arbitral tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4667827d445ebb505094eb4b58494cea</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRELIMINARY ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE REQUEST&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Preliminary Order can lead to an Interim Measure Request, as the tribunal may need to modify or confirm a preliminary order with further measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-74be062ba4c04dd5b51c11f6d66083c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRADE FACILITATION COMMISSION (贸法委)&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Trade Facilitation Commission, also known as 貿法委, is involved in the development and application of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-44743bbc15d45a8109ce653b3d495eca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 17C&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL is responsible for making determinations and issuing preliminary orders according to Article 17C of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e76c7e2b40934f289064a0e67067836b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 17C&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES INVOLVED IN ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PARTIES INVOLVED IN ARBITRATION are subject to the provisions of Article 17C, including receiving notices and presenting their cases regarding preliminary orders."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e76c7e2b40934f289064a0e67067836b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTIES INVOLVED IN ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL interacts with PARTIES INVOLVED IN ARBITRATION to issue, notify about, and hear objections against preliminary orders."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e76c7e2b40934f289064a0e67067836b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTIES INVOLVED IN ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Parties involved in Arbitration can request the Arbitration Tribunal to make corrections or interpretations as per Article 33 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d8f918840458c595eb8aa4b44f88bed0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTIES INVOLVED IN ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE OR PRELIMINARY ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties involved in arbitration are subject to measures or orders that can affect their circumstances, including the possibility of costs and damages if such measures are later deemed inappropriate by the tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b469129a05952ad01a4e34a3cd47777e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 17E OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">" ARTICLE 17E OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW is a specific article within the broader document, UNCITRAL MODEL LAW."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e379655024f7373614e8929b6e439db3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 17F OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">" ARTICLE 17F OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW is another specific article within the broader document, UNCITRAL MODEL LAW."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e379655024f7373614e8929b6e439db3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 17F&quot;" target="&quot;DISCLOSURE OBLIGATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 17F of UNCITRAL Model Law outlines a disclosure obligation that must be met by parties involved in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-83690c5e64ea2f5e5e2fd1e221f812fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISCLOSURE OBLIGATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal may require any party promptly to disclose any material change in the circumstances on which a measure was requested or granted, and this obligation continues until the party against whom the order is directed has an opportunity to present its case."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a0d3077063fc6ed9e1ac8dc5d7668e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISCLOSURE OBLIGATION&quot;" target="&quot;PARTY REQUESTING AN INTERIM MEASURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The party requesting an interim measure may be required to disclose material changes in circumstances related to that measure, as per Article 17F(1)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a0d3077063fc6ed9e1ac8dc5d7668e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISCLOSURE OBLIGATION&quot;" target="&quot;PARTY APPLYING FOR A PRELIMINARY ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The party applying for a preliminary order has an ongoing obligation to disclose all relevant circumstances until the opposing party can present its case, as per Article 17F(2)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a0d3077063fc6ed9e1ac8dc5d7668e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISCLOSURE OBLIGATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 17F. DISCLOSURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 17F outlines specific disclosure obligations that parties must adhere to regarding changes in circumstances related to interim measures or preliminary orders."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a0d3077063fc6ed9e1ac8dc5d7668e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 17G&quot;" target="&quot;COSTS AND DAMAGES LIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 17G of UNCITRAL Model Law establishes liability for costs and damages resulting from interim measures or preliminary orders requested by a party."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-83690c5e64ea2f5e5e2fd1e221f812fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 17G&quot;" target="&quot;DIVISION 4 — RECOGNITION AND ENFORCEMENT OF INTERIM MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 17G is part of Division 4, focusing on the costs and damages related to interim measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02c1209a461259f70dbbf8b7173d3461</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 17G&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 17H OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW (RECOGNITION AND ENFORCEMENT)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both articles deal with aspects of interim measures, but Article 17G focuses on costs and damages while Article 17H is about recognition and enforcement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02c1209a461259f70dbbf8b7173d3461</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 17G&quot;" target="&quot;DIVISION 5 — COURT-ORDERED INTERIM MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While both are part of the UNCITRAL Model Law, Article 17G and Division 5 deal with different aspects of interim measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02c1209a461259f70dbbf8b7173d3461</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 17G&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 17I OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW (GROUND FOR REFUSING RECOGNITION OR ENFORCEMENT)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both articles are part of the UNCITRAL Model Law, but Article 17G deals with costs and damages while Article 17I addresses grounds for refusing recognition or enforcement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02c1209a461259f70dbbf8b7173d3461</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 17G&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 17J OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW (COURT ORDERED INTERIM MEASURES)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While both are part of the UNCITRAL Model Law, Article 17G and Article 17J deal with different aspects of interim measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02c1209a461259f70dbbf8b7173d3461</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIVISION 4 — RECOGNITION AND ENFORCEMENT OF INTERIM MEASURES&quot;" target="&quot;DIVISION 5 — COURT-ORDERED INTERIM MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both divisions are part of the UNCITRAL Model Law, but Division 4 focuses on recognition and enforcement while Division 5 deals with court-ordered interim measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02c1209a461259f70dbbf8b7173d3461</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIVISION 4 — RECOGNITION AND ENFORCEMENT OF INTERIM MEASURES&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 17H OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW (RECOGNITION AND ENFORCEMENT)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 17H is part of Division 4, which focuses on recognition and enforcement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Article 17H is part of Division 4, which focuses on the recognition and enforcement of interim measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02c1209a461259f70dbbf8b7173d3461</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIVISION 4 — RECOGNITION AND ENFORCEMENT OF INTERIM MEASURES&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 17I OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW (GROUND FOR REFUSING RECOGNITION OR ENFORCEMENT)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Division 4 and Article 17I are part of the same model law, but Division 4 focuses on recognition and enforcement while Article 17I addresses grounds for refusing such actions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02c1209a461259f70dbbf8b7173d3461</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIVISION 4 — RECOGNITION AND ENFORCEMENT OF INTERIM MEASURES&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 17J OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW (COURT ORDERED INTERIM MEASURES)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Division 4 and Article 17J are part of the same model law, but Division 4 focuses on recognition and enforcement while Article 17J deals with court-ordered interim measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02c1209a461259f70dbbf8b7173d3461</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 17H OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW (RECOGNITION AND ENFORCEMENT)&quot;" target="&quot;DIVISION 5 — COURT-ORDERED INTERIM MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 17H of the UNCITRAL Model Law is part of Division 5, dealing with court-ordered interim measures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Division 5 and Article 17H are part of the same model law, but Division 5 deals with court-ordered interim measures while Article 17H focuses on recognition and enforcement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02c1209a461259f70dbbf8b7173d3461</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 17H OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW (RECOGNITION AND ENFORCEMENT)&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 17I OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW (GROUND FOR REFUSING RECOGNITION OR ENFORCEMENT)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both articles are part of the UNCITRAL Model Law, but Article 17H deals with recognition and enforcement while Article 17I addresses grounds for refusing such recognition or enforcement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02c1209a461259f70dbbf8b7173d3461</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIVISION 5 — COURT-ORDERED INTERIM MEASURES&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 17J OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW (COURT ORDERED INTERIM MEASURES)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">24.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 17J is a specific provision within Division 5, which deals with court-ordered interim measures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Division 5 and Article 17J are part of the same model law, but Division 5 deals with court-ordered interim measures while Article 17J is a specific provision within that division."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-02c1209a461259f70dbbf8b7173d3461</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM MEASURES&quot;" target="&quot;STATUS QUO&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Interim measures include maintaining or restoring the status quo pending determination of the dispute."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d56571b98ba26116ef651214c379b2f2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;JUDICIAL JURISDICTION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration proceedings may involve judicial jurisdiction issues, especially regarding the enforcement of arbitral awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d2fe562ab74fde36758e6db7f158f71b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT-ORDERED INTERIM MEASURES&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law provides a framework for court-ordered interim measures, which are relevant to the context of arbitration proceedings outside Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6eef98cdb7cf96d52a56e0103910d67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT-ORDERED INTERIM MEASURES&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Courts can grant interim measures that might be handled by arbitral tribunals, depending on circumstances and jurisdiction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b6eef98cdb7cf96d52a56e0103910d67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT-ORDERED INTERIM MEASURES&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 17J&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 17J is the legal basis for COURT-ORDERED INTERIM MEASURES, providing specific provisions regarding such measures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06afdeae20298d16d6b6fe33975e54ea</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT-ORDERED INTERIM MEASURES&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 5. COURT-ORDERED INTERIM MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"This section explicitly details the court's power to issue interim measures related to arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06afdeae20298d16d6b6fe33975e54ea</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 35(1)&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 35(1) provides the basis for court actions, as if a reference to an arbitral tribunal were the court and references to arbitral proceedings were court proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-964639856a5f7a7d5119569944195b09</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART 7&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 18&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Part 7 deals with the conduct of arbitral proceedings, which is directly related to Article 18 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-964639856a5f7a7d5119569944195b09</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 18 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 18 of UNCITRAL Model Law defines equal treatment of parties in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ddfbb014f2dc6afae82d7bc623722b27</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 18 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 18 of the UNCITRAL Model Law ensures equal treatment during arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ddfbb014f2dc6afae82d7bc623722b27</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 19 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">" ARTICLE 19 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW is a specific article within the broader document known as UNCITRAL MODEL LAW."&lt;SEP&gt;"Article 19 of the UNCITRAL Model Law deals with the determination of rules for arbitral procedures, providing flexibility to parties and tribunals."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ddfbb014f2dc6afae82d7bc623722b27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afb67efa17f13209eb7c5173e786360c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 19 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;PLACE OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 19 of the UNCITRAL Model Law indirectly relates to the place of arbitration as it sets a framework for procedural rules that can influence where proceedings take place."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-afb67efa17f13209eb7c5173e786360c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 20 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;PLACE OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 20 explicitly deals with the determination of the place of arbitration, making this relationship direct and specific."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-afb67efa17f13209eb7c5173e786360c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PLACE OF ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;DOCUMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Documents may be reviewed and inspected at the Place of Arbitration as part of the arbitral proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PLACE OF ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 20&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 20 specifies that parties can agree on or, failing agreement, the tribunal determines the Place of Arbitration for consultations among its members, hearing witnesses, experts, and parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PLACE OF ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;THIS LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The location of arbitration plays a crucial role in defining whether an arbitration falls under this law's jurisdiction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a98fdad24b6b0148ebf6a921fbf604fc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PLACE OF ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES INVOLVED&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties Involved are involved in proceedings that take place at a specific Place of Arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d0cddff72aaf0d2c6f21cba88e08e8e0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 20&quot;" target="&quot;COMMENCEMENT OF ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS'">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 20 of the UNCITRAL Model Law provides rules for determining the place of arbitration which affects how arbitral proceedings are commenced and conducted."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMENCEMENT OF ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS'" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The commencement of arbitral proceedings is based on a request from the parties to refer their dispute to arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 21&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 22&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Articles 21 and 22 of the UNCITRAL Model Law both deal with language in arbitration proceedings, specifically Article 21 on commencement of arbitral proceedings and Article 22 on language determination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9950c34a98c9cb7c295370ae17a2d5c6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 21&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 21 defines the start date for arbitral proceedings which is a fundamental aspect of arbitration procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9950c34a98c9cb7c295370ae17a2d5c6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 22&quot;" target="&quot;LANGUAGE DETERMINATION IN ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 22 explicitly addresses language determination in arbitration, directly relating to how the language or languages used are agreed upon or determined by the tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9950c34a98c9cb7c295370ae17a2d5c6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 22&quot;" target="&quot;DOCUMENTARY EVIDENCE TRANSLATION REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 22 mandates that documentary evidence be accompanied by translations, which is a specific requirement related to language determination in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9950c34a98c9cb7c295370ae17a2d5c6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPLICATION PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law specifies that statements must be made within an agreed or determined application period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4511c8f186e004155d32a4e03ae34f4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMANT'S STATEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;RESPONDENT'S DEFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Claimant's statement and respondent's defence are interrelated as they form the core of the dispute resolution process in arbitration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Claimant's statement and respondent's defence are opposing documents submitted during arbitration proceedings, each addressing different aspects of the case."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4511c8f186e004155d32a4e03ae34f4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOCUMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CLAIMANT may submit documents relevant to their claim or defense as part of the arbitration process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The claimant may submit documents relevant to their case with their statements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ccfc28d1a77070797c9452e760bfd7f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DOCUMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;RESPONDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similar to the CLAIMANT, the RESPONDENT can submit documents as part of their defense submissions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Similarly, the respondent can also provide relevant documents in support of their defense."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ccfc28d1a77070797c9452e760bfd7f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXPERT REPORTS&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Expert reports may be relied upon by the arbitral tribunal in making decisions, which can come from either party including the claimant."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXPERT REPORTS&quot;" target="&quot;RESPONDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similarly, expert reports might also pertain to the respondent’s case and could influence the arbitral proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXPERT REPORTS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Expert reports are relevant documents that can be submitted during arbitration proceedings, affecting both parties' cases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 24&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The claimant's obligations under Article 24 of UNCITRAL Model Law include stating facts, points at issue, and relief or remedy sought."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 24&quot;" target="&quot;RESPONDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 24 also outlines the respondent’s obligation to state their defense in respect of claims made by the claimant."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRADE FACILITATION COMMISSION DEMONSTRATION LAW ARTICLE 24&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The claimant's obligations under Article 24 of the Trade Facilitation Commission Demonstration Law are similar to those in UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRADE FACILITATION COMMISSION DEMONSTRATION LAW ARTICLE 24&quot;" target="&quot;RESPONDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The respondent's obligations under Article 24 of the Trade Facilitation Commission Demonstration Law are also similar to those in UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPLICATION BOOK&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties are required to submit an Application Book as per Article 24 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANSWER BOOK&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties must also provide an Answer Book according to Article 25 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOODS, OTHER PROPERTY OR DOCUMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Arbitral Tribunal may request inspection of goods, other property or documents from parties as per Article 24(3) of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXPERT REPORT OR EVIDENTIARY DOCUMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Arbitral Tribunal may rely on expert reports or evidentiary documents in making its decision as per Article 24(3) of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXPERT REPORT OR EVIDENTIARY DOCUMENT&quot;" target="&quot;HEARINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"HEARINGS may involve EXERT REPORT OR EVIDENTIARY DOCUMENTS for inspection or presentation of evidence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-39b02ac25884a8c6102243f2b93f0c03</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXPERT REPORT OR EVIDENTIARY DOCUMENT&quot;" target="&quot;RESPONDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The RESPONDENT receives and considers EXPERT REPORT OR EVIDENTIARY DOCUMENTS provided by the APPLICANT or other sources."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-39b02ac25884a8c6102243f2b93f0c03</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPLICATION PROCEDURE TERMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Arbitral Tribunal has the authority to terminate arbitration proceedings if an applicant fails to submit a sufficient application book as per Article 25(1)(a) of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANSWER BOOK NON-SUBMISSION EVENT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Arbitral Tribunal can continue with arbitration proceedings despite non-submission of an answer book by a party as per Article 25(1)(b) of the UNCITRAL Model Law, but not based on this omission alone."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTY ABSENCE IN ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Arbitral Tribunal can continue arbitration proceedings even if a party is absent or does not provide written evidence as per Article 25(1)(c) of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;贸法委示范法第25条 (一方当事人的不为)&quot;" target="&quot;仲裁程序继续进行但不视为认可申请人的陈述事件&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"According to Article 25 of the UNCITRAL Model Law, if a respondent fails to submit an answer book, arbitration proceedings can continue without acknowledging the applicant's claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;贸法委示范法第25条 (一方当事人的不为)&quot;" target="&quot;仲裁庭根据收到的证据作出裁决事件&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"According to Article 25 of the UNCITRAL Model Law, if a party fails to submit an answer book or appear in arbitration proceedings, the arbitral tribunal can still make decisions based on received evidence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;贸法委示范法第25条 (一方当事人的不为)&quot;" target="&quot;申请书提交不足事件&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"According to Article 25 of the UNCITRAL Model Law, if an applicant fails to submit a sufficient application book, arbitration proceedings can be terminated."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;仲裁程序继续进行但不视为认可申请人的陈述事件&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law provides for the continuation of arbitration procedures without acknowledging applicants' statements if certain conditions are not met as per Article 25(1)(b)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;仲裁庭根据收到的证据作出裁决事件&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law allows the arbitral tribunal to make decisions based on evidence received, even if a party is absent or does not provide written evidence as per Article 25(1)(c)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;申请书提交不足事件&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law provides for the termination of arbitration procedures due to insufficient submission of an application book by a party as per Article 25(1)(a)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 25&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration tribunal is responsible for interpreting and applying Article 25 of UNCITRAL Model Law in cases where a party fails to comply with certain requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2f3cce4894f17891d1764ccd30858f11</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 25&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIMANT'S STATEMENT OF CLAIM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 25 specifies that if a claimant fails to communicate their statement of claim, the arbitration tribunal may terminate proceedings without showing sufficient cause."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2f3cce4894f17891d1764ccd30858f11</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 25&quot;" target="&quot;RESPONDENT'S STATEMENT OF DEFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similarly, Article 25 states that if a respondent does not provide their statement of defence as required, the tribunal can continue with the proceedings without showing sufficient cause."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2f3cce4894f17891d1764ccd30858f11</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 25&quot;" target="&quot;SUFFICIENT CAUSE FOR NON-COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 25 allows for exceptions to the strict compliance requirements, provided there is sufficient cause for non-compliance by a party."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2f3cce4894f17891d1764ccd30858f11</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMANT'S STATEMENT OF CLAIM&quot;" target="&quot;RESPONDENT'S STATEMENT OF DEFENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both the claimant's statement of claim and respondent's statement of defence are crucial documents that must be submitted for arbitration proceedings, as per Article 25 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2f3cce4894f17891d1764ccd30858f11</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMANT'S STATEMENT OF CLAIM&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration tribunal must consider and act upon the claimant's statement of claim when applying Article 25 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2f3cce4894f17891d1764ccd30858f11</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RESPONDENT'S STATEMENT OF DEFENCE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Likewise, the arbitration tribunal needs to take into account the respondent's statement of defence in its application and interpretation of Article 25 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2f3cce4894f17891d1764ccd30858f11</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUFFICIENT CAUSE FOR NON-COMPLIANCE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration tribunal can consider whether a party's non-compliance is due to sufficient cause, which affects the application and interpretation of Article 25 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2f3cce4894f17891d1764ccd30858f11</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 26&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 26 of UNCITRAL Model Law defines the role and powers of the arbitral tribunal in appointing experts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-31879101d38b1d4251cc0b47a342f1d7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 26&quot;" target="&quot;EXPERT(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The article specifies that an expert can be appointed by the arbitral tribunal to provide reports on specific issues."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-31879101d38b1d4251cc0b47a342f1d7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 26&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties have a role in agreeing or requesting experts, and providing relevant information."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-31879101d38b1d4251cc0b47a342f1d7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EVALUATION OF ARBITRATION COSTS (ARTICLE 74)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 74 deals with the evaluation of arbitration costs which are related to the arbitral tribunal's operations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-31879101d38b1d4251cc0b47a342f1d7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EVALUATION OF ARBITRATION COSTS (ARTICLE 74)&quot;" target="&quot;ASSESSOR(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Assessors can be appointed by the arbitral tribunal for evaluating arbitration costs, as per Article 74."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-31879101d38b1d4251cc0b47a342f1d7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXPERTS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Experts are appointed by the arbitral tribunal to report on specific issues, aiding in the resolution process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34872d5563389492bd86e96a7e9d819c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXPERTS&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties have a role in agreeing to or requesting experts, as well as providing relevant information and documents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34872d5563389492bd86e96a7e9d819c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSESSORS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Assessors may be appointed by the arbitral tribunal for technical matters and can attend proceedings with permission from the parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34872d5563389492bd86e96a7e9d819c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSESSORS&quot;" target="&quot;COURT ASSISTANCE IN EVIDENCE TAKING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Assessors may attend proceedings where evidence-taking assistance from the court can occur, integrating their technical expertise with legal processes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34872d5563389492bd86e96a7e9d819c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT ASSISTANCE IN EVIDENCE TAKING&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal can request court assistance for evidence taking, which is also a function of the People's Court under certain circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34872d5563389492bd86e96a7e9d819c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE PEOPLE'S COURT&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The People's Court has the authority to assist in evidence-taking at the request of the arbitral tribunal or parties and can be involved in arbitration proceedings through this mechanism."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34872d5563389492bd86e96a7e9d819c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE PEOPLE'S COURT&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The People's Court is involved in providing support for arbitral procedures as outlined by the UNCITRAL Model Law, particularly regarding evidence taking and procedural assistance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34872d5563389492bd86e96a7e9d819c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 27 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Court can assist in taking evidence as per Article 27 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 56&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Court's power to assist with taking evidence is independent from and can coexist with that of an Arbitral Tribunal under Section 56."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 56&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION FEES GUARANTEE MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 56 and Article 27 both deal with arbitration fees, though in different contexts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 81 (WARRANT OR ORDER TO BRING UP PRISONER TO GIVE EVIDENCE)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 81 applies to arbitral proceedings as if they were civil or criminal legal procedures, granting similar powers for evidence taking."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT ASSISTANCE IN TAKING EVIDENCE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Court assistance in arbitration procedure includes the power to bring up a prisoner to give evidence as per Section 81 of the Evidence Ordinance (Cap. 8)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT ASSISTANCE IN TAKING EVIDENCE&quot;" target="&quot;PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Court assistance in taking evidence applies during arbitral proceedings as per Section 81 of the Evidence Ordinance (Cap. 8)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT ASSISTANCE IN TAKING EVIDENCE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal may request court assistance in taking evidence as per Article 27."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-375bde2b853ea690587e97e345bd3671</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT ASSISTANCE IN TAKING EVIDENCE&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 28. RULES APPLICABLE TO SUBSTANCE OF DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 28 rules are relevant to the context provided in 'Court assistance in taking evidence' as both deal with arbitration procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-375bde2b853ea690587e97e345bd3671</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL has the authority to conduct PROCEEDINGS and can issue various orders related to these proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ac9a4105712169b0cda2b7c65d72aa76</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;INDEPENDENT EXPERT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An INDEPENDENT EXPERT may be appointed by the ADJUDICATOR for specific inquiries or reports related to PROCEEDINGS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d879d95be32b955d798da85e699506e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PARTIES must comply with any requests and directions made by the ADJUDICATOR during the PROCEEDINGS regarding payment disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d879d95be32b955d798da85e699506e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION COSTS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION FEES GUARANTEE MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both mechanisms deal with financial guarantees related to arbitration proceedings, though they serve different purposes within the legal framework."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSOCIATION&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CLAIMANT, being an entity like ASSOCIATION, could also face the same conditions regarding jurisdiction and security requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6127a28d22b5d9d9145842f6c4caba9c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)(A)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (3)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both subsections are related to the period within which an order has not been complied with."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 35(2)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTIONS 39 TO 42&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sections 39 to 42 apply despite section 35(2), indicating a relationship in legal context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTIES TO ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal has authority over parties in arbitral proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;指明款額&quot;" target="&quot;更改指示&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both terms are related to the indication of amounts in arbitration, with potential for changes or instructions regarding these amounts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e0829311bda6ca8e30706b5b4b72bc86</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXTENSION OF TIME LIMITS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The extension of time limits is applicable in arbitration proceedings as per the agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cfadf35d2f372b32609102a0deae476e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXTENSION OF TIME LIMITS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The extension of time limits can be made based on an arbitration agreement under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cfadf35d2f372b32609102a0deae476e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMANT'S RIGHT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration agreement can potentially affect claimant's right to be extinguished if not acted upon within specified time or period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42e0db1f27b3313444cf12ec497ffd57</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMANT'S RIGHT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal has the authority to make orders extending time or period for claimant's right, if justified by circumstances outside reasonable contemplation of parties at agreement formation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-42e0db1f27b3313444cf12ec497ffd57</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION PROCEDURE&quot;" target="&quot;CONSTRUCTION CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The DISPUTE RESOLUTION PROCEDURE is related to CONSTRUCTION CONTRACT disputes, particularly in nomination and selection processes for adjudicators."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7ad6aa79a150340c8a28d98a0e6b1a24</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLE DELAY IN PURSUING CLAIMS IN ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;MATHEMATICS OF REASONABLE TIME CONSTRAINTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mathematics can provide a framework for determining what constitutes reasonable time constraints and unreasonable delay in pursuing claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-854d00c33e69aed0258675abc1e2d264</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SOCIAL SCIENCES OF CONFLICT RESOLUTION MECHANISMS&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSTANTIAL RISK TO FAIR RESOLUTION OF ISSUES, SERIOUS PREJUDICE TO ANY OTHER PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Social sciences can offer insights into conflict resolution mechanisms that may mitigate risks to fair resolution and prevent serious prejudice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-854d00c33e69aed0258675abc1e2d264</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AWARD OR ORDER MADE BY THE COURT IN EXERCISE OF ITS POWER CONFERRED BY SUBSECTION (5)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE&quot; OR &quot;仲裁程序&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An award or order made by the Court under SUBSECTION (5) pertains to arbitration procedures. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTY&quot; OR &quot;財產&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE&quot; OR &quot;仲裁程序&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Property can be the subject of or involve issues arising from arbitration procedures. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE&quot; OR &quot;仲裁程序&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 60 (5)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An award or order made by the Court under SECTION 60(5) pertains to arbitration procedures. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75a159b6970a3e7a3135ad78ad73aee0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LITIGATION COURT&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL ISSUE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The LITIGATION COURT has jurisdiction over LEGAL ISSUES arising from arbitration procedures, including appointing arbitrators and deciding preliminary legal issues."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ff2369343594485564382d2d30ba3755</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LITIGATION COURT&quot;" target="&quot;COSTS OF ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The LITIGATION COURT can make decisions regarding COSTS OF ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS, particularly in cases where multiple proceedings are heard together."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ff2369343594485564382d2d30ba3755</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LITIGATION COURT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The LITIGATION COURT has the authority to grant or deny permission for appeals related to arbitration procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3fe51ca84063bb48ff26e0744002a148</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LITIGATION COURT&quot;" target="&quot;APPEAL DECISION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The LITIGATION COURT makes decisions on whether to allow appeals in arbitration cases, and these decisions can be appealed only under specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3fe51ca84063bb48ff26e0744002a148</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL OUTSIDE HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;COURT'S ROLE IN ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS OUTSIDE HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Court's role in arbitral proceedings outside Hong Kong is ancillary to the primary jurisdiction of the arbitration tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS OUTSIDE HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Court has jurisdiction over arbitration proceedings outside Hong Kong and can make orders related to these proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORK ENFORCEMENT MECHANISMS&quot;" target="&quot;COURT'S JURISDICTION OVER ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS OUTSIDE HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal Framework enforcement mechanisms apply when dealing with Court's jurisdiction over arbitration proceedings outside Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORK ENFORCEMENT MECHANISMS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL'S ANCILLARY POWER APPLICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal Framework enforcement mechanisms include the application of arbitration tribunal's ancillary power for specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD EXECUTION PROCESS&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL FRAMEWORK FOR ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS OUTSIDE HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The legal framework for the execution of arbitration awards provides guidelines on how such awards can be enforced in and outside Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9f1ee15f14896a24f23432269f049b12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE COURT'S DECISION ON LEAVE GRANTING/REFUSAL&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Decisions of the COURT regarding leave granting or refusal are not subject to appeal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ae42208132627b8d5ff98d4e7966f28e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE LEGAL PROFESSION ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;" target="&quot;LAWYERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The THE LEGAL PROFESSION ORDINANCE (CAP. 159) regulates the practice of LAWYERS and sets out penalties for unlicensed practice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-367745ea1d4a071f6e58849b6c7523ab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE LEGAL PROFESSION ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;" target="&quot;NOTARIES PUBLIC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The THE LEGAL PROFESSION ORDINANCE (CAP. 159) also regulates NOTARIES PUBLIC and sets out penalties for unlicensed practice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-367745ea1d4a071f6e58849b6c7523ab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE LEGAL PROFESSION ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL MODEL LAW, while related to arbitration, does not directly interact with the THE LEGAL PROFESSION ORDINANCE (CAP. 159) as it pertains to legal professionals."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-367745ea1d4a071f6e58849b6c7523ab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 74(3)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 74(3) is part of the Legal Practitioners Ordinance, which deals with specific cost-related provisions in arbitral proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a23612e5f946b89b30990ba8fe2387e1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 28 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 28 of the UNCITRAL Model Law is a specific provision within it, detailing rules applicable to substance of dispute."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7effd30746ff087ba04389bfb24de4c9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 28 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;CONFLICT OF LAWS RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 28 refers to conflict of laws rules when parties do not specify applicable law, indicating a relationship between the two concepts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7effd30746ff087ba04389bfb24de4c9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONFLICT OF LAWS RULES&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal shall decide based on the conflict of laws rules which it considers applicable."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONFLICT OF LAWS RULES&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL SYSTEM OF A GIVEN STATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The legal system of a given State is not directly referring to its conflict of laws rules unless otherwise expressed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-341dbfe6e21afa768ee74c7e3db0be67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;USAGES OF THE TRADE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration tribunal must consider usages of trade in its decision-making process as per Article 28(4), showing their interrelation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7effd30746ff087ba04389bfb24de4c9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;USAGES OF THE TRADE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal shall take into account the usages of the trade applicable to the transaction when deciding in accordance with the terms of the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-341dbfe6e21afa768ee74c7e3db0be67</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EX AEQUO ET BONO&quot;" target="&quot;AMIABLE COMPOSITEUR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Ex aequo et bono or amiable compositeur can be decided only if parties have expressly authorized it, according to Article 29 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 29&quot;" target="&quot;PANEL OF ARBITRATORS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 29 of UNCITRAL Model Law states that decisions should be made by a majority, unless otherwise agreed or for procedural questions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROCEDURE QUESTIONS&quot;" target="&quot;PRESIDING ARBITRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Questions of procedure may be decided by the presiding arbitrator if authorized by parties or all members of the arbitral tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;BINDING ARBITRATION AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration tribunal should record and decide on settlement agreements in their binding arbitration awards, according to Article 30 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 30 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Settlement agreements under Article 30 are treated as arbitration awards for enforcement purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a78d8505ead991a0cdc7d41a2ddb40bf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 31&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law Article 31 defines how a settlement agreement can be treated as an arbitral award."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1e07f7e6a4e77b91de5f23262418bf4e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Settlements are recorded in the form of an AWARDS, which is a result of negotiations between PARTIES under ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03bb9907c4707aee4e32c05a81efe12a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PARTIES reach a SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT during arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03bb9907c4707aee4e32c05a81efe12a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;APPOINTMENT ADVISORY BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The advisory board's role in appointments indirectly influences settlement agreements, as both are part of a broader legal framework for dispute resolution."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-605f21b5a2eb897deb796a8915dad75c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MUTUAL AGREEMENT FOR SETTLEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATOR DECISION-MAKING PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mutual agreement for settlement can influence the decision-making process in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL MAJORITY DECISION&quot;" target="&quot;PRESIDING ARBITRATOR'S ROLE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The presiding arbitrator's role is crucial, especially when making decisions by majority rule as per Article 29 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6bbcea8f9e587ebf99b65f0299e0286b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 30 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 30 of the UNCITRAL Model Law defines conditions for settlement in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a78d8505ead991a0cdc7d41a2ddb40bf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 30 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The article applies during arbitral proceedings when parties settle disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a78d8505ead991a0cdc7d41a2ddb40bf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 30 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Under Article 30, settlements can be recorded in the form of arbitral awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a78d8505ead991a0cdc7d41a2ddb40bf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRAL AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Courts have the authority to determine whether an arbitral award should be set aside based on specific criteria."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-368fa7e2763a0614258f01172b9c741f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRAL AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 36&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 36 outlines conditions under which an arbitral award may be refused recognition or enforced."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-665407cfb1dd4211e1d5ff880154e6bb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRAL AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitration agreement leads to the creation of an arbitral award."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-665407cfb1dd4211e1d5ff880154e6bb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 31&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE WITH MULTIPLE ARBITRATORS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 31 of the UNCITRAL Model Law outlines procedures for arbitration with multiple arbitrators, including signature requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1e07f7e6a4e77b91de5f23262418bf4e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 31&quot;" target="&quot;CORRECTION PERIOD EXTENSION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 31 applies to corrections or interpretations made under paragraphs (1) and (3), which may require an extension of time for such actions. This is further detailed in the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 31&quot;" target="&quot;AWARD INTERPRETATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 31 provides rules applicable to interpretations made by the arbitral tribunal, which can affect other processes like additional awards and cost determinations. This is detailed in Article 70 of the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 31&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 31 is a specific provision within the UNCITRAL Model Law, defining the form and content of arbitration awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 31(4)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE TERMINATION DUE TO APPLICANT'S WITHDRAWAL WITH OPPOSITION FROM RESPONDENT AND ARBITRATOR'S APPROVAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 31(4) specifies a condition under which arbitration proceedings can be terminated due to the applicant's withdrawal with opposition from the respondent and arbitrator's approval."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 31(4)&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL'S APPOINTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 31(4)'s termination of arbitration proceedings also leads to the termination of the arbitral tribunal’s appointment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 32&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 77&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 77 provides a context for Article 32, which is about the termination of arbitration procedures under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第32條. 程序的終止&quot;" target="&quot;第31條. 裁定的形式和内容&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 31 (in Chinese) and Article 32 are related as they both pertain to the arbitration process, with Article 31 defining award form and content while Article 32 deals with procedure termination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第31條(4)&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION DUE TO IMPRACTICABILITY OR UNNECESSARY CONTINUATION OF THE PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 31(4) (in Chinese) specifies a condition for the impracticability or unnecessary continuation of arbitration procedures, which is related to termination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;第77條&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 77 (in Chinese) provides context and possibly additional rules that affect the termination of arbitral proceedings as mentioned in Article 32."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-12bb43cc82c8c3529243d2a3c8279c60</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 32&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIMANT WITHDRAWAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 32 of UNCITRAL Model Law specifies that the claimant's withdrawal can lead to termination of proceedings unless the respondent objects and a legitimate interest is recognized for obtaining a final settlement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c28925249d0e1bce05d18edbb693e21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 32&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES AGREEMENT ON TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 32 of UNCITRAL Model Law explicitly states that parties can agree to terminate the proceedings, leading directly to their termination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c28925249d0e1bce05d18edbb693e21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 32&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL'S FINDING OF UNNECESSITY OR IMPOSSIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 32 of UNCITRAL Model Law outlines that the tribunal can find proceedings unnecessary or impossible, leading to their termination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c28925249d0e1bce05d18edbb693e21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 32&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF ARBITRATORS' MANDATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"According to Article 32 of UNCITRAL Model Law, when the arbitral proceedings are terminated by any means mentioned in (1), (2)(a)-(c) or (3), the mandate of the arbitrators also terminates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c28925249d0e1bce05d18edbb693e21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 32&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 33(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 32 and Article 33 are interrelated in that both deal with aspects of terminating arbitral proceedings, but Article 33 specifically addresses the correction and explanation of awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c28925249d0e1bce05d18edbb693e21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMANT WITHDRAWAL&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES AGREEMENT ON TERMINATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While claimant withdrawal can lead to termination as per Article 32, it is not mutually exclusive with parties' agreement on termination; both are valid means for ending proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c28925249d0e1bce05d18edbb693e21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMANT WITHDRAWAL&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL'S FINDING OF UNNECESSITY OR IMPOSSIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Claimant withdrawal can be one of the reasons why an arbitration tribunal might find it unnecessary or impossible to continue proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c28925249d0e1bce05d18edbb693e21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMANT WITHDRAWAL&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF ARBITRATORS' MANDATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Claimant withdrawal, as one of the reasons specified in Article 32 for terminating arbitral proceedings, also leads to the termination of arbitrators' mandate."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c28925249d0e1bce05d18edbb693e21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTIES AGREEMENT ON TERMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL'S FINDING OF UNNECESSITY OR IMPOSSIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties' agreement on termination can also be a reason for an arbitration tribunal's finding that the continuation of proceedings is unnecessary or impossible."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c28925249d0e1bce05d18edbb693e21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTIES AGREEMENT ON TERMINATION&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF ARBITRATORS' MANDATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties' agreement on termination results in the end of the arbitral proceedings and thus terminates the arbitrators' mandate as per Article 32."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c28925249d0e1bce05d18edbb693e21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL'S FINDING OF UNNECESSITY OR IMPOSSIBILITY&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF ARBITRATORS' MANDATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitration tribunal's finding that the continuation of proceedings is unnecessary or impossible leads to their termination, which in turn terminates the arbitrators' mandate."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c28925249d0e1bce05d18edbb693e21</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANOTHER DEADLINE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL CORRECTION REQUEST&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The deadline for requesting arbitration tribunal correction is set within 30 days after the award."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-eb0e168b6e225c931e3274375129335c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANOTHER DEADLINE&quot;" target="&quot;EXTENSION OF CORRECTION OR EXPLANATION PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"There may be an extension period for corrections or explanations if another deadline has been set within 30 days after the award."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-eb0e168b6e225c931e3274375129335c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXPLANATION BY ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;AUTOMATIC CORRECTION BY ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both automatic and explanation requests are methods of addressing errors in the arbitration tribunal's decision, though explanations require a request from parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-eb0e168b6e225c931e3274375129335c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REQUEST FOR SUPPLEMENTARY AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;EXTENSION OF CORRECTION OR EXPLANATION PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The period for correction or explanation can be extended if there is a supplementary award request within 30 days after the receipt of the arbitration award."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-eb0e168b6e225c931e3274375129335c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AMENDMENT TO ARBITRAL AWARD UNDER示范法第33条&quot;" target="&quot;MODEL LAW ON ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The amendment to the arbitral award under Article 33 of the Model Law on Arbitration is a specific application of that law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-eb0e168b6e225c931e3274375129335c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 33 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 33 is a specific provision within the UNCITRAL Model Law that deals with corrections and interpretations of arbitration awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d8f918840458c595eb8aa4b44f88bed0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AWARD CORRECTION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal has the authority to correct any error in the award on its own initiative within thirty days of the date of the award."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AWARD CORRECTION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL'S AUTHORITY TO CORRECT AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal has authority over award corrections, which are part of its decision-making process. This is detailed in Article 31 and further elaborated on by the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ADDITIONAL AWARD REQUEST&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A party can request an additional award within thirty days of receipt of the award, if claims presented in the arbitral proceedings were omitted from the original award. If justified, the tribunal will make such an additional award within sixty days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ADDITIONAL AWARD REQUEST&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 7.01-69&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ARTICLE 7.01-69 outlines the process for making ADDITIONAL AWARD REQUESTS, which can be made by a party within 30 days of receiving the award."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ADDITIONAL AWARD REQUEST can be made based on ARTICLE 34.01-2(2)(A)(I)-(II), which allows a party to request an additional award within 30 days of receiving the award."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5490186775273077486362a56a5b981f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CORRECTION PERIOD EXTENSION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal may extend, if necessary, the period of time within which it shall make a correction or interpretation or an additional award under paragraph (1) or (3) of this article."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CORRECTION PERIOD EXTENSION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL'S AUTHORITY TO CORRECT AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal's authority to correct awards includes extending the period of time within which such corrections can be made. This is detailed in Article 31 and further elaborated on by the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AWARD INTERPRETATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal has the power to interpret any point or part of the award, and may make other changes necessitated by such interpretation under Article 33 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AWARD INTERPRETATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL DECISION MAKING PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal's decision-making process includes interpreting awards, which can lead to additional actions like corrections or supplementary relief. This is detailed in Article 31 and further elaborated on by the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AWARD INTERPRETATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL'S INTERPRETATION OF AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal's interpretation of awards can lead to additional actions like corrections or supplementary relief. This is detailed in Article 31 and further elaborated on by the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COST REVIEW&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal may review and confirm, vary or correct the award of costs if it was not aware of any relevant information when making the original award. This can be done within 30 days from the date of the award."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COSTS AWARDING&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION COST DETERMINATION PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration cost determination process can lead to awards of costs, which are a key part of arbitration proceedings. This is governed by Article 70 and further detailed in the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT ORDER FOR SUPPLEMENTARY RELIEF&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal's decision on certain awards may lead to a court order for supplementary relief, especially when the dispute involves matters that could be subject to civil law procedures. This interaction is governed by Article 70 of the relevant legal text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT ORDER FOR SUPPLEMENTARY RELIEF&quot;" target="&quot;CIVIL LAW PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Civil law procedures may lead to court orders for supplementary relief, especially when disputes involve matters that could be subject to such legal processes. This is governed by Article 70 of the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT ORDER FOR SUPPLEMENTARY RELIEF&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AND COURT INTERACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"There can be interactions between arbitration and court procedures, leading to potential court orders for supplementary relief. This is detailed in Article 70 of the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COSTS DETERMINATION IN ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL DECISION MAKING PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal's decision-making process includes determining costs, which is a key part of arbitration proceedings. This is governed by Article 70 and further detailed in the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COSTS DETERMINATION IN ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD REVIEW PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration award review process can include cost determinations, which are a key part of arbitration proceedings. This is governed by Article 70 and further detailed in the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUPPLEMENTARY RELIEF REQUEST&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL DECISION MAKING PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal's decision-making process can lead to requests for supplementary relief, especially when disputes involve matters that could be subject to such legal processes. This is governed by Article 70 of the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUPPLEMENTARY RELIEF REQUEST&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD REVIEW PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration award review process may lead to requests for supplementary relief, especially when disputes involve matters that could be subject to such legal processes. This is governed by Article 70 of the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT CIVIL PROCEDURE LAW&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AND COURT INTERACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"There can be interactions between arbitration and court procedures, leading to potential application of civil law. This is governed by Article 70 and further detailed in the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c3ad57851ab0dc6b7960a3df34491d78</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORIGINAL TRIAL COURT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both courts have similar powers in terms of remedies and relief, with some exceptions regarding land contracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ORIGINAL TRIAL COURT can remit matters to the ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL and has jurisdiction over appeals related to arbitration awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92dbfb61aa1ae662d58ad04e46a6a1e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698354d68541c6722cada50bb05de978</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORIGINAL TRIAL COURT&quot;" target="&quot;REMEDY OR RELIEF&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The original trial court can order any remedy or relief that could be ordered by the arbitral tribunal if the dispute was subject to civil proceedings in the court."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92dbfb61aa1ae662d58ad04e46a6a1e4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REMEDY OR RELIEF&quot;" target="&quot;LAND AND INTEREST IN LAND&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Land contracts are excluded from the scope of remedies or relief that can be ordered by both courts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92dbfb61aa1ae662d58ad04e46a6a1e4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LAND AND INTEREST IN LAND&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contracts related to land and interest in land are excluded from the arbitral tribunal's power to order specific performance, as per subsection (2)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92dbfb61aa1ae662d58ad04e46a6a1e4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TIME FOR MAKING AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The time for making an award is within the power of the arbitral tribunal unless otherwise agreed by parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7e5ed4af08fa3d54713649e0adf6d0ad</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EFFECT OF AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The award is binding on all parties who are involved or through whom any party claims, as well as those claiming under them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7e5ed4af08fa3d54713649e0adf6d0ad</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COSTS OF ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL can make a decision awarding costs related to arbitration proceedings, including its own fees and expenses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-caff1791e8e9f461d58d69581c8df6cd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT'S FEE SCALE AND PRACTICES&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"When assessing the costs of arbitration (excluding its own fees), the ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL is not bound by the court's fee scale and practices."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-caff1791e8e9f461d58d69581c8df6cd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OVERALL CIRCUMSTANCES REASONABLE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL must only grant what is reasonable in light of overall circumstances when assessing costs (excluding its own fees)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-caff1791e8e9f461d58d69581c8df6cd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SETTLEMENT OFFER&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"PARTIES can make a SETTLEMENT OFFER in disputes concerning arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COSTS ASSESSMENT&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"PARTIES are involved in COSTS ASSESSMENT, which can be ordered by the ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL based on relevant circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISPUTE CONCERNED&quot;" target="&quot;FEES AND EXPENSES OF THE TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The DISPUTE CONCERNED may lead to FEES AND EXPENSES OF THE TRIBUNAL being assessed by the ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FEES AND EXPENSES OF THE TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Arbitral Tribunal is responsible for its own fees and expenses, which may be assessed separately from other costs."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WRITTEN OFFER OF SETTLEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ORDER OR DIRECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A WRITTEN OFFER OF SETTLEMENT can influence ORDER OR DIRECTION from the ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM MEASURE OF ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;COSTS ORDERED UNDER SUBSECTION (3)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The INTERIM MEASURE OF ARBITRATION may be related to COSTS ORDERED UNDER SUBSECTION (3)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COSTS ASSESSMENT WITHOUT TRIBUNAL FEES &quot;" target="&quot;DISPUTE SUBMISSION FOR ARBITRATION &quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Dispute submission for arbitration can result in COSTS ASSESSMENT WITHOUT TRIBUNAL FEES."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COSTS ASSESSMENT BASED ON RELEVANT CIRCUMSTANCES &quot;" target="&quot;FEES AND EXPENSES OF THE TRIBUNAL &quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL assesses COSTS based on relevant circumstances, including FEES AND EXPENSES."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COSTS ASSESSMENT FOR PRE-ARBITRATION EXPENSES &quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES &quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"PARTIES are involved in the assessment of PRE-ARBITRATION EXPENSES by the ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COSTS ASSESSMENT FOR POST-ARBITRATION EXPENSES &quot;" target="&quot;ORDER OR DIRECTION &quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"POST-ARBITRATION EXPENSES may be assessed as part of ORDER OR DIRECTION from the ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HIGH COURT RULES (CHAPTER 4, ANNEX A)&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"High Court Rules provide the framework within which the Court evaluates costs according to specific scales and practices."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HIGH COURT RULES (CHAPTER 4, ANNEX A)&quot;" target="&quot;COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"High Court Rules provide guidelines for evaluating costs in legal proceedings, which may apply indirectly to arbitration through similar principles of reasonableness and fairness."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COSTS&quot;" target="&quot;TIME LIMIT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The time limits mentioned are related to when parties must take steps in the arbitration process, affecting recoverable costs."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5578519b1f9afcce44c23c12fe6ac94b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COSTS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION FUNDING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">26.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration Funding directly relates to the costs associated with arbitration, including both pre-arbitration expenses and those incurred during proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration Funding is directly related to the costs of arbitration, which includes both pre-arbitration expenses and those incurred during the process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration Funding is related to Costs, as it includes the costs and expenses of arbitration. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COSTS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration Bodies are involved with costs related to arbitral proceedings, which can be funded through third-party arrangements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration Bodies incur costs related to the arbitration proceedings, which can be funded by third parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COSTS&quot;" target="&quot;FUNDED PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Funded Parties are directly involved with the costs associated with arbitration, which can be covered by third-party funding arrangements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COSTS&quot;" target="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">36.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Third Party Funders are involved in providing financial assistance that covers the costs of arbitral proceedings for various parties and entities, including those related to Funded Parties' participation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Third Party Funders are involved in providing financial assistance that covers the costs of arbitral proceedings for various parties and entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Third Party Funders are involved with providing financial assistance that covers various costs associated with arbitral proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Third Party Funders provide funding that covers the costs of arbitral proceedings for various parties and entities involved in arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COSTS&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT has the power to make consequential directions as to the payment of COSTS in consolidated ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ee3bd35452fe0a7b5e9fa7dc2c1f8074</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBMISSION TO ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The submission to arbitration is a clause that can be part of an agreement, potentially subjecting disputes to arbitral proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBMISSION TO ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Submissions to arbitration are subject to review by courts, which may determine if they meet certain criteria for setting aside awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-368fa7e2763a0614258f01172b9c741f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBMISSION TO ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Submissions to arbitration must comply with public policy, which is a criterion for setting aside awards in certain cases."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-368fa7e2763a0614258f01172b9c741f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROVISION TO SUBMIT DISPUTES TO ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The provision for submission to arbitration can be part of an agreement that includes cost-sharing clauses or provisions void if the parties agree to pay their own costs."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HIGH COURT RULES (CHAPTER 4, ANNEX A) RULE 62.28&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rule 62.28 provides specific guidance on the taxation of costs by the Court, which may influence how arbitration-related costs are assessed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TAXATION SCALES AND PRACTICES&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Arbitral Tribunal has discretion over cost assessment but is not obliged to follow the scales and practices adopted by the Court, indicating a degree of independence in this process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRE-ARBITRATION COSTS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Pre-arbitration costs may be considered by the Arbitral Tribunal in its assessment of costs, provided they are reasonable and incurred for preparation purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 74(1) AND (2)&quot;" target="&quot;RULE 28(2) OF ORDER 62 OF THE RULES OF THE HIGH COURT (CAP. 4 SUB. LEG. A)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rule 28(2) of Order 62 is a basis for determining the costs of arbitral proceedings as agreed by parties, which relates to Section 74(1) and (2)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a23612e5f946b89b30990ba8fe2387e1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 50 (NO COSTS FOR UNQUALIFIED PERSON) OF THE LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 74(3)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 50 of the Legal Practitioners Ordinance does not apply to costs ordered under Section 74(3), indicating a distinction in cost-related regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a23612e5f946b89b30990ba8fe2387e1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 50 (NO COSTS FOR UNQUALIFIED PERSON) OF THE LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;" target="&quot;THE LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINATION (CAP. 159)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 50 of the Legal Practitioners Ordinance is part of the broader Legal Practitioners Ordination, addressing specific aspects related to costs for unqualified persons."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a23612e5f946b89b30990ba8fe2387e1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 74(3)&quot;" target="&quot;RULE 28(2) OF ORDER 62 OF THE RULES OF THE HIGH COURT (CAP. 4 SUB. LEG. A)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 74(3) specifically excludes the application of Rule 28(2), creating a specific exception in cost determination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a23612e5f946b89b30990ba8fe2387e1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RULE 28(2) OF ORDER 62 OF THE RULES OF THE HIGH COURT (CAP. 4 SUB. LEG. A)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 77(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rule 28(2) of Order 62 and Section 77(1) both deal with the taxation or determination of costs in arbitral proceedings, though they address different aspects."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a23612e5f946b89b30990ba8fe2387e1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 29 OF CAP. 159 (《第159章》第29條)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'lawyer' is defined under section 29 of Cap. 159, which provides the specific criteria for who can be considered a lawyer in this context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 5 OF CAP. 159 (《第159章》第5條)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'lawyer' is also defined under section 5 of Cap. 159, providing another criterion for who can be considered a lawyer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;" target="&quot;FOREIGN LAWYER AS DEFINED BY SECTION 2(1) OF CAP. 159 (《第159章》第2條(一))&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'foreign lawyer' is defined by section 2(1) of Cap. 159, providing the specific criteria for who can be considered a foreign lawyer in this context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 32 OR SECTION 33 (《第159章》第32或第33條)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'mediator' is defined in relation to sections 32 or 33 of Cap. 159, indicating the specific context and role within mediation proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 98ZT (《第159章》第98ZT條)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'authorized body' is defined by section 98ZT of Cap. 159, establishing the specific criteria for who can be considered an authorized body."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 98ZN (《第159章》第98ZN條)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'code of practice' is defined under section 98ZN of Cap. 159, providing the specific criteria for this code."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 98ZD (《第159章》第98ZD條)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'damages-based agreement' is defined under section 98ZD of Cap. 159, providing the specific criteria for this type of agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 98ZE (《第159章》第98ZE條)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'hybrid damages-based agreement' is defined under section 98ZE of Cap. 159, providing the specific criteria for this type of agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 2(1) OF CAP. 159 (《第159章》第2條(一))&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'foreign lawyer' is defined by section 2(1) of Cap. 159, providing the specific criteria for who can be considered a foreign lawyer in this context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 98ZC (《第159章》第98ZC條)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'conditional fee agreement' is defined under section 98ZC of Cap. 159, providing the specific criteria for this type of agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f7eb0e6c37c2ef17e35db1071f66982</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;EXPERT APPOINTED UNDER SECTION 26 OF THE MODEL LAW ON COMMERCIAL ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Experts appointed under Section 26 of the Model Law on Commercial Arbitration are considered part of the arbitration proceedings and their charges are included in the tribunal's expenses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e105b81cb8e7429af8bdd848fcb41de5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;VALUATION OFFICER APPOINTED UNDER SECTION 54(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Valuation officers appointed under Section 54(2) of the Model Law on Commercial Arbitration are also considered part of the arbitration proceedings and their charges are included in the tribunal's expenses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e105b81cb8e7429af8bdd848fcb41de5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration Proceedings involve the activities, decisions, and outcomes related to cases handled by the Arbitration Tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e105b81cb8e7429af8bdd848fcb41de5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Arbitration Tribunal must notify all Parties about preliminary orders and related communications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-74be062ba4c04dd5b51c11f6d66083c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 78&quot;" target="&quot;TOTAL AMOUNT OF FEES AND EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 78 determines the amount of fees and expenses that are payable to the arbitral tribunal, which includes experts and assessors appointed under Article 26 and Section 54(2) respectively."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-62de924c3226ea55de4d94d980a6b34f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 78&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 78 is a basis for determining the fees and expenses to be paid to the arbitral tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-62de924c3226ea55de4d94d980a6b34f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSESSOR APPOINTED UNDER SECTION 54(2)&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An assessor appointed under Section 54(2) of the UNCITRAL Model Law is also considered part of the arbitration tribunal's fees and expenses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-62de924c3226ea55de4d94d980a6b34f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCESS FOR APPEAL OR REVIEW&quot;" target="&quot;TOTAL AMOUNT OF FEES AND EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration process for appeal or review can determine the amount of fees and expenses that are payable, which may differ from those initially determined by the tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-62de924c3226ea55de4d94d980a6b34f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRAL PROCESS FOR APPEAL OR REVIEW OF THE AMOUNT OF THE FEES OR EXPENSES DEMANDED&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 54(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 54(1) and (2) provide processes for appeal or review of the fees or expenses demanded."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7aaf6f770f217f1e2eb977b5ec34ad19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WRITTEN AGREEMENT BETWEEN A PARTY AND THE ARBITRATORS&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT OF ARBITRATION CHARGES AND EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A written agreement between a party and arbitrators affects how arbitration charges and expenses are determined."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7aaf6f770f217f1e2eb977b5ec34ad19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 54(1)&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 54(1) and (2) involve applications made to the Court for determination on fees or expenses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7aaf6f770f217f1e2eb977b5ec34ad19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 54(2)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL INSTITUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 54(2) applies to arbitral institutions vested with powers in relation to delivering an arbitral tribunal's award."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7aaf6f770f217f1e2eb977b5ec34ad19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENT OF ARBITRATION CHARGES AND EXPENSES&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Court plays a role in the enforcement of arbitration charges and expenses as determined by subsection (2)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7aaf6f770f217f1e2eb977b5ec34ad19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;JUDGMENT RATE (判定利率)&quot;" target="&quot;HIGH COURT ORDINANCE (CAP. 4)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The JUDGMENT RATE is determined by the Chief Justice under section 49(1)(b) of the HIGH COURT ORDINANCE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7a7d382b60c68c418d8128c80396b687</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HIGH COURT ORDINANCE (CAP. 4)&quot;" target="&quot;RULES OF THE HIGH COURT (CAP. 4 SUB. LEG. A)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The High Court Ordinance (Cap. 4) includes the power to make rules for court applications and orders, which are detailed in the Rules of the High Court (Cap. 4 sub. leg. A)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Rules of the High Court (Cap. 4 sub. leg. A) are made under the authority granted by the High Court Ordinance (Cap. 4)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-55419da365905ce3e764775f55ac2bfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPLICATION FOR SETTING ASIDE AN ARBITRAL AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Courts have jurisdiction over applications for setting aside arbitral awards as per legal provisions. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cd8b5a6b74d6568cda4bfce7dd132460</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT REVIEW OF ARBITRATION DECISIONS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL COMPOSITION AND PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The review of an arbitration decision may involve assessing the tribunal's composition and procedural adherence to legal standards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-946b6b4dc8815b2e45997dcb61152914</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL COMPOSITION AND PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public policy considerations may influence the composition and procedure of the arbitration tribunal, particularly regarding its alignment with legal standards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-946b6b4dc8815b2e45997dcb61152914</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">23.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A COURT can refuse to enforce an AWARD if it is contrary to PUBLIC POLICY."&lt;SEP&gt;"Courts must consider public policy when making decisions or orders, including those related to the enforcement of Macao awards."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT must consider PUBLIC POLICY when deciding whether to set aside or remit an AWARD, as public policy can override party agreements and tribunal decisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-feb384a29e745420d0a68b05f9a55801&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b2fac04904854d200ea9c9161cb98c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63fa361a4bbae312d93826ee30bf2182</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATOR'S DECISION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A decision that violates Public Policy can lead to refusal in enforcing an arbitration agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cb631b96138ab7e64e00f4b6081fb346</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public Policy may influence the enforceability of an Arbitration Agreement, particularly when decisions within it are challenged or deemed invalid."&lt;SEP&gt;"The arbitration agreement may be subject to review based on the public policy of a country, which can invalidate or affect its enforceability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2047b71041716475b6c4ce04dcb74ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb631b96138ab7e64e00f4b6081fb346</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY&quot;" target="&quot;ENFORCEMENT OF A MAINLAND AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public policy can be used as grounds to refuse enforcement of a Mainland award, indicating its importance in the legal framework."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9fdd2bff76f50fe6b943f4fd79b5f894</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY&quot;" target="&quot;MAINLAND AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public policy can be a ground for refusing enforcement of Mainland awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-47762eabb07bb9265d79611ab6fc55f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY&quot;" target="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Third Party Funding of Arbitration is subject to public policy considerations, indicating their relation through the lens of legality and regulation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d76933a7a67fb3cee016313276af67d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY&quot;" target="&quot;COURT REVIEW OF ARBITRATION AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Court reviews and potential撤销裁决 are influenced by considerations of public policy."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2047b71041716475b6c4ce04dcb74ab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OF THE PLACE WHERE THE ARBITRAL AWARD IS MADE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court where the arbitral award is made can revoke or suspend enforcement if it conflicts with public policy of its country."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-aba64861ea22070188d9b7dd4c0fd47a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration tribunals must ensure that their decisions do not conflict with the public policies of the countries involved."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-aba64861ea22070188d9b7dd4c0fd47a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 6 COURT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATOR APPOINTMENT NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">20.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 6 COURT has the authority to set aside an arbitral award if certain conditions are met, as per the ARBITRATOR APPOINTMENT NOTICE process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Article 6 Court's decision on arbitrator appointments can impact the process of arbitration and subsequent court review."&lt;SEP&gt;"Article 6 of the COURT is relevant to the ARBITRATOR APPOINTMENT NOTICE process in determining whether conditions for setting aside an arbitral award are met under Article 34."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-368fa7e2763a0614258f01172b9c741f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b688d6d5d4487cad0a2e8714c6369fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 6 COURT&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">25.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 6 of the COURT is relevant to Article 34 of UNCITRAL Model Law, as it pertains to conditions for setting aside an arbitral award."&lt;SEP&gt;"Article 6 of the COURT plays a role in applying UNCITRAL Model Law's provisions for setting aside arbitral awards, particularly under specific conditions outlined by Article 34."&lt;SEP&gt;"UNCITRAL MODEL LAW provides a framework that ARTICLE 6 COURT can apply when dealing with applications to set aside arbitral awards under specific conditions outlined in Article 34."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4b688d6d5d4487cad0a2e8714c6369fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 6 COURT&quot;" target="&quot;PARTY MAKING THE APPLICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">32.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 6 of the COURT has jurisdiction over applications made by the PARTY MAKING THE APPLICATION for setting aside an arbitral award under specific conditions outlined in UNCITRAL Model Law."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ARTICLE 6 COURT has jurisdiction over applications made by the PARTY MAKING THE APPLICATION for setting aside an arbitral award under specific conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The PARTY MAKING THE APPLICATION must follow the procedures set out by ARTICLE 6 of the COURT when applying to set aside an arbitral award under UNCITRAL Model Law."&lt;SEP&gt;"The PARTY MAKING THE APPLICATION must follow the procedures set out in ARTICLE 6 of the COURT when applying for setting aside an arbitral award under UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4b688d6d5d4487cad0a2e8714c6369fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 6 COURT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 6 of the COURT is involved in interpreting and enforcing arbitration agreements, including those governed by UNCITRAL Model Law's provisions for setting aside awards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Article 6 of the COURT is relevant to arbitration agreements and can apply provisions like UNCITRAL Model Law's Article 34 for setting aside arbitral awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4b688d6d5d4487cad0a2e8714c6369fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 6 COURT&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 6 Court is specified as having jurisdiction over applications for setting aside arbitral awards."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT, specifically ARTICLE 6 COURT, has jurisdiction over applications for setting aside an arbitral award under specific conditions outlined in UNCITRAL Model Law Article 34."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-368fa7e2763a0614258f01172b9c741f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b688d6d5d4487cad0a2e8714c6369fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTY MAKING THE APPLICATION&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PARTY MAKING THE APPLICATION can apply to the COURT for setting aside an arbitral award under specific circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4b688d6d5d4487cad0a2e8714c6369fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTY MAKING THE APPLICATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATOR APPOINTMENT NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PARTY MAKING THE APPLICATION must follow the ARBITRATOR APPOINTMENT NOTICE process when making an application, which is relevant to setting aside an arbitral award."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4b688d6d5d4487cad0a2e8714c6369fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTY MAKING THE APPLICATION&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PARTY MAKING THE APPLICATION must adhere to the procedures outlined in UNCITRAL Model Law, including Article 34, when applying for setting aside an arbitral award."&lt;SEP&gt;"The PARTY MAKING THE APPLICATION must adhere to the procedures outlined in UNCITRAL Model Law, including those for setting aside awards as per Article 34."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4b688d6d5d4487cad0a2e8714c6369fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTY MAKING THE APPLICATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PARTY MAKING THE APPLICATION must adhere to the procedures related to arbitration agreements, including those governed by UNCITRAL Model Law's provisions for setting aside awards as per Article 34."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4b688d6d5d4487cad0a2e8714c6369fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR APPOINTMENT NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL MODEL LAW provides a framework that includes procedures related to arbitrator appointment notices, which are relevant when setting aside an arbitral award under Article 34."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4b688d6d5d4487cad0a2e8714c6369fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR APPOINTMENT NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">20.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT is involved in interpreting and enforcing procedures related to ARBITRATOR APPOINTMENT NOTICES, which are relevant when setting aside an arbitral award under Article 34."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court's decision on whether to set aside an award can be influenced by the notice given regarding arbitrator appointments and proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-368fa7e2763a0614258f01172b9c741f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b688d6d5d4487cad0a2e8714c6369fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR APPOINTMENT NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;REFUSAL OF ENFORCEMENT OF ARBITRAL AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Proper notice of the appointment of the arbitrator can be a reason for refusal if it was not given, as per Section 85."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b414ae197269a985e13f48ee92be6bda</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD(S)&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties are involved in arbitration proceedings and can apply for setting aside an award if necessary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-59c7140869534366dd7270de77711ef8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY OF THIS STATE&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court must consider the public policy of this state when deciding on setting aside an arbitral award."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court's decision to set aside an arbitral award is subject to the public policy of this state."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-59c7140869534366dd7270de77711ef8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY OF THIS STATE&quot;" target="&quot;COURT FINDING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Court findings can be influenced by the public policy of this state, which may affect whether an award should be set aside."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6f35bbfd9ee83b0701ea2384c506063d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY OF THIS STATE&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 36&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The public policy of this state can override the enforcement of an arbitral award as per Article 36(2)(b)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-665407cfb1dd4211e1d5ff880154e6bb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC POLICY OF THIS STATE&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OF THE COUNTRY IN WHICH, OR UNDER THE LAW OF WHICH, THAT AWARD WAS MADE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court in which the arbitration took place or under whose law it was made must consider public policy when deciding on recognition or enforcement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-665407cfb1dd4211e1d5ff880154e6bb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 26(5)&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Court has jurisdiction to set aside an arbitral award under section 26(5). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78fc62b0cd7028c5a321d5c1666b4c9b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 26(5)&quot;" target="&quot;DIVISION 1—ENFORCEMENT OF ARBITRAL AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 26(5) falls under the division related to enforcement of arbitral awards. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78fc62b0cd7028c5a321d5c1666b4c9b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 4 OF SCHEDULE 2 (IF APPLICABLE)&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If applicable, the Court can challenge an arbitral award according to section 4 of Schedule 2. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78fc62b0cd7028c5a321d5c1666b4c9b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 5 OF SCHEDULE 2 (IF APPLICABLE)&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If applicable, the Court has jurisdiction to appeal against an arbitral award on a question of law under section 5 of Schedule 2. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78fc62b0cd7028c5a321d5c1666b4c9b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 34&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Court requires leave for any appeal from a decision regarding the enforcement of arbitral awards based on article 34 of UNCITRAL Model Law. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78fc62b0cd7028c5a321d5c1666b4c9b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIVISION 1—ENFORCEMENT OF ARBITRAL AWARDS&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 35 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW (RECOGNITION AND ENFORCEMENT)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 35 of the UNCITRAL Model Law is related to recognition and enforcement, which falls under Division 1 on arbitration award enforcement. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78fc62b0cd7028c5a321d5c1666b4c9b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIVISION 1—ENFORCEMENT OF ARBITRAL AWARDS&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 36 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW (GROUNDS FOR REFUSING RECOGNITION OR ENFORCEMENT)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 36 of the UNCITRAL Model Law is related to grounds for refusing recognition or enforcement, which also falls under Division 1 on arbitration award enforcement. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78fc62b0cd7028c5a321d5c1666b4c9b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIVISION 1—ENFORCEMENT OF ARBITRAL AWARDS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitral awards are enforced according to the provisions in this division. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-78fc62b0cd7028c5a321d5c1666b4c9b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Court has the authority to enforce arbitration awards, either made in or outside Hong Kong, with certain conditions and procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c57c5ae22a968acd7a8e3b02e3130cce</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OFFICIAL LANGUAGES&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text mentions that if an arbitration agreement or award is not in one of the official languages, a translation certified by certain individuals must be provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3136488efa6b0856e563bdafbaaa1633</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OFFICIAL LANGUAGES&quot;" target="&quot;CONVENTION AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Official languages are relevant to the translation requirements for Convention awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a64f61df4c2295abb6d73eef9a781326</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OFFICIAL LANGUAGES&quot;" target="&quot;MACAO AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The enforcement of Macao awards requires evidence in the official languages as specified by law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OFFICIAL LANGUAGES&quot;" target="&quot;DIPLOMATIC OR CONSULAR AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Diplomatic or consular agents can also provide certified translations for documents that need to be in an official language."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AWARD ENFORCEMENT PROCEDURE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both terms are discussed together in the text regarding enforcement and production requirements for arbitration agreements and awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3136488efa6b0856e563bdafbaaa1633</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REFUSAL OF ENFORCEMENT OF ARBITRAL AWARDS&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 85&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The refusal to enforce an arbitral award under Section 85 can be based on specific conditions outlined in that section."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b414ae197269a985e13f48ee92be6bda</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 85&quot;" target="&quot;LAW APPLICABLE TO THAT PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The law applicable to that party can influence whether an arbitral award is enforceable or not as per Section 85 conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b414ae197269a985e13f48ee92be6bda</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CAPACITY&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Capacity is a factor considered when determining if enforcement of the arbitration agreement should be refused, particularly regarding incapacity under applicable law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b414ae197269a985e13f48ee92be6bda</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRAL AUTHORITY&quot;" target="&quot;MACAO AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Macao awards are subject to arbitral authority as determined by applicable laws."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-feb384a29e745420d0a68b05f9a55801</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2013 YEAR 7 AMENDMENT&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court's enforcement methods for Convention Awards may be influenced by the amendments made in 2013 as described in this text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4494c24ec2905c2010570a5a5156b75e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2013 YEAR 7 AMENDMENT&quot;" target="&quot;CONVENTION AWARDS ENFORCEMENT EVIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The amendment of the year and section number provide specific details on evidence required for enforcing convention awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6ba533d3bab5a376760ee4b1e5070c14</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2013 YEAR 7 AMENDMENT&quot;" target="&quot;REJECTION OF ENFORCEMENT OF CONVENTION AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The amendment includes provisions that can lead to the rejection of enforcement of convention awards under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6ba533d3bab5a376760ee4b1e5070c14</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONVENTION AWARDS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitration agreement is a key component in enforcing Convention awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a64f61df4c2295abb6d73eef9a781326</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2013年第7號第11條&quot;" target="&quot;87. ENFORCEMENT OF CONVENTION AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 2013年第7號第11條 amends and replaces the enforcement provisions for Convention Awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a64f61df4c2295abb6d73eef9a781326</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;88. EVIDENCE TO BE PRODUCED FOR ENFORCEMENT OF CONVENTION AWARDS&quot;" target="&quot;2013年第7號第12條&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 2013年第7號第12條 amends and replaces the evidence requirements for enforcing Convention Awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a64f61df4c2295abb6d73eef9a781326</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR'S DECISION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Arbitrator's Decision is a key component of the Arbitration Agreement, as it deals with disputes and their resolution under the agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cb631b96138ab7e64e00f4b6081fb346</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法律适用地的仲裁机构权威部门&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"仲裁协议的有效性取决于适用法律和相关程序合规性审查机构的认定。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-38b4dba8dcefb2d368c753859f749fd1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法律适用地的仲裁机构权威部门&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"仲裁程序的有效性及合规性需通过相关审查机构进行评估和确认。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-38b4dba8dcefb2d368c753859f749fd1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;法律条款适用地法院&quot;" target="&quot;法律适用地的仲裁裁决执行机制&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"涉及仲裁裁决执行的具体措施和机制需由适用法律规定的相关机构进行审查与确认。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-38b4dba8dcefb2d368c753859f749fd1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE ARBITRAL AUTHORITY OR THE ARBITRAL PROCEDURE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral authority or procedure is central to arbitration, defining how the dispute will be resolved."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-603a9b33a6e3900af70fd439592326ba</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONVENTION ON THE RECOGNITION AND ENFORCEMENT OF FOREIGN ARBITRAL AWARDS (NEW YORK CONVENTION)&quot;" target="&quot;CANTONESE TRANSLATION OF 'THE NEW YORK CONVENTION'&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Cantonese translation is a linguistic representation of the New York Convention."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-603a9b33a6e3900af70fd439592326ba</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CANTONAL GOVERNMENT&quot;" target="&quot;CANTONESE TRANSLATION OF 'INTERNATIONAL COMMERCIAL ARBITRATION'&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Cantonese translation relates to how International Commercial Arbitration would be understood in a local context, specifically by the Cantonese-speaking population."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-603a9b33a6e3900af70fd439592326ba</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ON INTERNATIONAL COMMERCIAL ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;UNITED NATIONS COMMISSION ON INTERNATIONAL TRADE LAW (UNCITRAL)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law on International Commercial Arbitration is adopted by the United Nations Commission on International Trade Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6b88d5ece94b64060cd9c9c3ca51a624</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ON INTERNATIONAL COMMERCIAL ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;2006年7月7日&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law was revised and adopted on 7 July 2006 by the United Nations Commission on International Trade Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6b88d5ece94b64060cd9c9c3ca51a624</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ON INTERNATIONAL COMMERCIAL ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;第一章. 总则&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Chapter I of the UNCITRAL Model Law is about General Provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6b88d5ece94b64060cd9c9c3ca51a624</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE CHIEF EXECUTIVE IN COUNCIL&quot;" target="&quot;STATE OR TERRITORY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Chief Executive in Council has the authority to declare a State or territory as a party to the New York Convention through an order."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed6ba602b145c3cd359dd6dda74e3b40</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATE OR TERRITORY&quot;" target="&quot;MAINLAND AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of Mainland Awards is introduced as another context related to the enforcement within the same legal framework, but not directly linked with States or territories becoming parties to the New York Convention."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed6ba602b145c3cd359dd6dda74e3b40</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINLAND AWARDS&quot;" target="&quot;ENFORCEMENT OF A MAINLAND AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The enforcement of a Mainland Award is discussed in detail, explaining under what conditions it can or cannot be enforced."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9fdd2bff76f50fe6b943f4fd79b5f894</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINLAND AWARDS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mainland Awards are subject to arbitration rules and procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-47762eabb07bb9265d79611ab6fc55f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINLAND AWARDS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mainland Awards are subject to arbitral procedures as per the agreement or law of the Mainland."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-47762eabb07bb9265d79611ab6fc55f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINLAND AWARDS&quot;" target="&quot;COMPOSITION OF THE ARBITRAL AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The composition of the arbitral authority can affect the enforceability of Mainland awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-47762eabb07bb9265d79611ab6fc55f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINLAND AWARD ENFORCEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;2013 7TH ORDINANCE S. 14&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ordinance section details the evidence needed for enforcing a Mainland award, which is related to enforcement of such awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-235e83e8e9feff8425503a1c8b92eef0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINLAND AWARD ENFORCEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;2013 7TH ORDINANCE S. 16&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Although this section was repealed, it originally dealt with the same topic as other sections on Mainland award enforcement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-235e83e8e9feff8425503a1c8b92eef0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINLAND AWARD ENFORCEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;2013 7TH ORDINANCE S. 17&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"This ordinance revised and updated the requirements for enforcing a Mainland award, impacting related enforcement efforts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-235e83e8e9feff8425503a1c8b92eef0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINLAND AWARD ENFORCEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ENFORCEMENT OF MAINLAND AWARD EVIDENCE REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The overall topic of enforcing Mainland awards is directly addressed by these sections and their requirements for evidence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-235e83e8e9feff8425503a1c8b92eef0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2013 7TH ORDINANCE S. 16&quot;" target="&quot;ENFORCEMENT OF MAINLAND AWARD EVIDENCE REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"This repealed section was related to enforcement of Mainland awards, though it is no longer in effect."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-235e83e8e9feff8425503a1c8b92eef0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2013 7TH ORDINANCE S. 14&quot;" target="&quot;ENFORCEMENT OF MAINLAND AWARD EVIDENCE REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ordinance section specifies the evidence required for enforcing a Mainland award."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-235e83e8e9feff8425503a1c8b92eef0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2021 1ST ORDINANCE S. 4&quot;" target="&quot;ENFORCEMENT OF MAINLAND AWARD EVIDENCE REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"This ordinance was repealed and its functions were taken over by other sections dealing with Mainland awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-235e83e8e9feff8425503a1c8b92eef0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENFORCEMENT OF MAINLAND AWARD EVIDENCE REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;2013 7TH ORDINANCE S. 17&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ordinance section revised the requirements for producing evidence to enforce Mainland awards, replacing an earlier version."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-235e83e8e9feff8425503a1c8b92eef0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2013年第7號第17條修訂&quot;" target="&quot;內地裁决的强制执行可遭拒绝&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"修订内容明确了内地区域裁决在特定情况下可以被拒绝执行。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-76112f3bf347661ce2f42763f99c12c0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;仲裁程序&quot;" target="&quot;仲裁员委任&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"仲裁员的任命是仲裁程序的一部分,其合法性直接影响裁决的有效性。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-76112f3bf347661ce2f42763f99c12c0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;仲裁程序&quot;" target="&quot;内地法律&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"仲裁程序必须遵循内地法律规定以确保裁决的有效性与合法性。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-76112f3bf347661ce2f42763f99c12c0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;仲裁程序&quot;" target="&quot;答辯人&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"答辩人在仲裁程序中是被诉方,参与解决付款争议的纠纷。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3fb320dd06f32faf0b373f1098dd9a0a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENFORCEMENT OF A MAINLAND AWARD&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitration agreement's validity and the circumstances affecting its enforceability are key factors considered when enforcing a Mainland Award."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9fdd2bff76f50fe6b943f4fd79b5f894</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRAL PROCEDURE&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral procedure is based on the arbitration agreement between parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6f35bbfd9ee83b0701ea2384c506063d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG LAW&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The laws in Hong Kong, as described by HONG KONG LAW, reference and incorporate provisions from the UNCITRAL Model Law, specifically Articles 34(2)(b) of it."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75abbf9735ce9959e08a7259663fa08d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG LAW&quot;" target="&quot;IPR DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The laws in Hong Kong address issues related to IPR disputes through sections such as section 81 and 86, indicating their relevance to handling IPR disputes under the law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-75abbf9735ce9959e08a7259663fa08d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE OLD ORDINANCE IV PART&quot;" target="&quot;REJECTION OF ARBITRATION AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Old Ordinance IV Part is a ground for rejection of arbitration awards under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-47762eabb07bb9265d79611ab6fc55f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;2000 ARBITRATION (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE NO. 2&quot;" target="&quot;SEPARATION OF ARBITRAL AND UNRELATED DECISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The 2000 Arbitration Amendment Ordinance No. 2 addresses the separation of arbitral and unrelated decisions in enforcement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-47762eabb07bb9265d79611ab6fc55f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;92-95 PROVISIONS&quot;" target="&quot;REJECTION OF ARBITRATION AWARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Provisions from sections 92 to 95 provide specific conditions for rejecting arbitration awards, including those from the Mainland."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-47762eabb07bb9265d79611ab6fc55f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION (AMENDMENT) ORDINANCE 2000 (2 OF 2000)&quot;" target="&quot;DIVISION 4—ENFORCEMENT OF MACAO AWARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The amendment ordinance provides the legal basis for enforcing Macao Awards through Division 4."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7a8178e8eb442ffa0ed10eccd55c6223</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;澳门 (MACAU)&quot;" target="&quot;第4分部 —— 澳门裁决的强制执行&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The division specifically mentions the enforcement of awards from Macau, indicating a direct relationship between them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7002524f6a8a76d0aa6007df37e1ac1f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;仲裁 (ARBITRATION)&quot;" target="&quot;裁决 (AWARD/DECISION)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration leads to decisions that can be enforced or not under different clauses and amendments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7002524f6a8a76d0aa6007df37e1ac1f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;仲裁 (ARBITRATION)&quot;" target="&quot;2000年第5条生效日期 (EFFECTIVE DATE OF SECTION 5 IN 2000 NO. 5)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 5 of the Arbitration Amendment Ordinance 2000 comes into effect, impacting arbitration procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7002524f6a8a76d0aa6007df37e1ac1f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;仲裁 (ARBITRATION)&quot;" target="&quot;由2021年第1号第5条废除 (REPEALED BY 2021 NO. 1, ARTICLE 5)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">40.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The repeal of Section 5 in the Arbitration Amendment Ordinance directly impacts arbitration procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7002524f6a8a76d0aa6007df37e1ac1f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;仲裁 (ARBITRATION)&quot;" target="&quot;第4分部 —— 澳门裁决的强制执行 (DIVISION FOR ENFORCEMENT OF MACAU AWARDS)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">45.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The division specifically deals with the enforcement of Macau awards, which are a form of arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7002524f6a8a76d0aa6007df37e1ac1f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;拒绝强制执行 (REFUSAL OF ENFORCEMENT)&quot;" target="&quot;时有效的《旧有条例》第44条&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The clause is directly related to the refusal of enforcement, indicating its lack of effect on certain provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7002524f6a8a76d0aa6007df37e1ac1f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;香港特别行政区 (HONG KONG SPECIAL ADMINISTRATIVE REGION)&quot;" target="&quot;内地 (MAINLAND CHINA)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text discusses legal interactions between Hong Kong and mainland China, indicating their interrelated legal frameworks."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7002524f6a8a76d0aa6007df37e1ac1f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;内地 (MAINLAND CHINA)&quot;" target="&quot;第4分部 —— 澳门裁决的强制执行 (DIVISION FOR ENFORCEMENT OF MACAU AWARDS)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The division specifically mentions the enforcement of awards from Macau, indicating a relationship with mainland China's legal framework."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7002524f6a8a76d0aa6007df37e1ac1f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENFORCEMENT PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration proceedings are treated similarly to enforcement proceedings under certain conditions, as described in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8322a8472d188ae5550ad46529f8b37b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENFORCEMENT PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATOR OR MEDIATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While not directly stated, arbitrators or mediators may be involved in enforcement proceedings as part of their broader legal responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8322a8472d188ae5550ad46529f8b37b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MACAO AWARDS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Macao awards are based on arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-feb384a29e745420d0a68b05f9a55801</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SWORN TRANSLATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sworn translators are required to certify translations of arbitration agreements if they are not in one of the official languages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENFORCEMENT OF MACAO AWARDS&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration agreement is a key document required for the enforcement of Macao awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENFORCEMENT OF MACAO AWARDS&quot;" target="&quot;MACAO LEGAL SYSTEM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The enforcement of Macao awards is governed by the laws and procedures within the Macao legal system."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENFORCEMENT OF MACAO AWARDS&quot;" target="&quot;INTERNATIONAL ARBITRATION PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"International arbitration processes can be relevant to the enforcement mechanisms of Macao awards, especially when dealing with cross-border issues."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL CAPACITY&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT VALIDITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The validity of an arbitration agreement can depend on the legal capacity of one or more parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL COMPOSITION&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL DISPUTE RESOLUTION MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The composition of arbitration tribunals is part of the mechanism for resolving legal disputes in Macao."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL COMPOSITION&quot;" target="&quot;NUMBER OF ARBITRATORS (THREE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The composition of the arbitration tribunal includes three arbitrators as a default number unless otherwise specified by parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61ef9a8b87aa1cf04b46aaf871b5f39a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT ENFORCEMENT CONDITIONS&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL DISPUTE RESOLUTION MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Conditions for enforcing an arbitration agreement are part of the broader legal dispute resolution mechanism in place."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-74a8e51496cea628136989290d2eaf6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;A DISPUTE NOT ANTICIPATED BY THE ARBITRATION CLAUSE OR OUTSIDE ITS SCOPE&quot;" target="&quot;ENFORCEMENT REFUSAL DUE TO LACK OF BINDING EFFECT OR REVOCATION BY COMPETENT AUTHORITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Disputes not anticipated by the arbitration clause or outside its scope can result in enforcement refusal due to lack of binding effect."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5659ee6d0cebe80b200f8882699926cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE COMPOSITION OF THE ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL OR PROCEDURAL MATTERS, NOT IN ACCORDANCE WITH AGREEMENTS OR LOCAL LAWS&quot;" target="&quot;ENFORCEMENT REFUSAL DUE TO LACK OF BINDING EFFECT OR REVOCATION BY COMPETENT AUTHORITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The composition of the arbitral tribunal or procedural matters not in accordance with agreements or local laws can lead to enforcement refusal due to lack of binding effect."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5659ee6d0cebe80b200f8882699926cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENFORCEMENT REFUSAL DUE TO LACK OF BINDING EFFECT OR REVOCATION BY COMPETENT AUTHORITIES&quot;" target="&quot;有規定外 - 該裁決所處理的分歧,並非提交仲裁的條款所預期者,或該項分歧並不屬該等條款所指者; 或 (II) 該裁決包含對在提交仲裁範圍以外事宜的決定;&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The issue of enforcement refusal due to lack of binding effect or revocation by competent authorities is related to the scope and content of arbitration as defined in the agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5659ee6d0cebe80b200f8882699926cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENFORCEMENT REFUSAL DUE TO LACK OF BINDING EFFECT OR REVOCATION BY COMPETENT AUTHORITIES&quot;" target="&quot;ISSUES THAT CANNOT BE RESOLVED THROUGH ARBITRATION ACCORDING TO HONG KONG LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">24.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Issues that cannot be resolved through arbitration according to Hong Kong law can result in enforcement refusal due to lack of binding effect."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5659ee6d0cebe80b200f8882699926cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENFORCEMENT REFUSAL DUE TO LACK OF BINDING EFFECT OR REVOCATION BY COMPETENT AUTHORITIES&quot;" target="&quot;ENFORCEMENT REFUSAL DUE TO VIOLATION OF PUBLIC POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">21.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Enforcement refusal due to lack of binding effect or revocation by competent authorities can be related to violations of public policy."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5659ee6d0cebe80b200f8882699926cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENFORCEMENT REFUSAL DUE TO LACK OF BINDING EFFECT OR REVOCATION BY COMPETENT AUTHORITIES&quot;" target="&quot;A DECISION THAT INCLUDES BOTH RELEVANT AND IRRELEVANT MATTERS FOR ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A decision that includes both relevant and irrelevant matters for arbitration can lead to enforcement refusal due to lack of binding effect."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5659ee6d0cebe80b200f8882699926cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENFORCEMENT REFUSAL DUE TO LACK OF BINDING EFFECT OR REVOCATION BY COMPETENT AUTHORITIES&quot;" target="&quot;APPLICATION FOR REVOCATION OR SUSPENSION OF ENFORCEMENT BY COMPETENT AUTHORITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">27.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Application for revocation or suspension of enforcement by competent authorities is directly related to the issue of enforcement refusal due to lack of binding effect."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5659ee6d0cebe80b200f8882699926cf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LAW OF MACAO&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Courts operate under the Law of Macao, which governs their decisions and orders."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-feb384a29e745420d0a68b05f9a55801</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT DECISION OR ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Courts can make decisions or orders regarding the enforcement of arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-feb384a29e745420d0a68b05f9a55801</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPETENT AUTHORITY OF MACAO&quot;" target="&quot;COURT BEFORE WHICH ENFORCEMENT OF THE AWARD IS SOUGHT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court may adjourn proceedings for enforcing an award if it has been set aside or suspended by the competent authority of Macao."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c53aea00b88989df2a0f5c9c8eaf66aa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;COMMON LAW DOCTRINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Third party funding of arbitration is not prohibited by particular common law doctrines as per Part 10A, Division 2 Interpretation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c53aea00b88989df2a0f5c9c8eaf66aa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Third Party Funders are central in Third Party Funding of Arbitration activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Third Party Funding of Arbitration involves financial assistance to bodies or entities conducting arbitral proceedings, including courts and arbitrators."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;CHAMPTYRE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of Third Party Funding of Arbitration is not affected by the common law offences such as champerty, indicating a relationship between them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d76933a7a67fb3cee016313276af67d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;COMMON BARRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of Third Party Funding of Arbitration is not affected by the common law offence of being a common barrator, suggesting they are related in legal context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d76933a7a67fb3cee016313276af67d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;MEDIATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 620)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Mediation Ordinance does not apply to Third Party Funding of Arbitration as noted, establishing a relationship between them in legal context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d76933a7a67fb3cee016313276af67d0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART 10A — THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER (出資第三者)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Part 10A provides measures and safeguards for third party funding of arbitration as defined in the interpretation section."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c53aea00b88989df2a0f5c9c8eaf66aa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION FUNDING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Third Party Funder provides Arbitration Funding to parties involved in arbitration proceedings. "&lt;SEP&gt;"Third Party Funding of Arbitration involves providing financial assistance related to the costs of arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;" target="&quot;PROVISION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">51.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Provisions address the legal framework for Third Party Funders and include measures for safeguards related to their activities in funding arbitral proceedings without being prohibited by common law doctrines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Provisions address the legal framework for Third Party Funders in relation to funding arbitration without being prohibited by common law doctrines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Provisions address the legal framework for Third Party Funders, ensuring their activities are not prohibited by common law doctrines while providing measures and safeguards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Provisions ensure that activities of Third Party Funders are not prohibited by common law doctrines while providing measures for safeguards related to their involvement in funding arbitral proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Provisions ensure that the activities of Third Party Funders are not prohibited by common law doctrines and include measures for safeguards related to their involvement in funding arbitral proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Third Party Funders are involved in provisions that ensure their activities regarding funding arbitration are not prohibited by common law doctrines and include measures for safeguards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Third Party Funders provide financial assistance to Arbitration Bodies for conducting arbitral proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;" target="&quot;FUNDED PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">26.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The third party funder provides financial support to the funded party for arbitration, which involves various agreements and procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Third Party Funder funds the Funded Party, as per sections 98I and 98J. "&lt;SEP&gt;"Third Party Funder is the entity that provides funding to a Funded Party, as defined in sections 98I and 98J. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-319ab10afb64c747e7339427a06f0a41</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;" target="&quot;POTENTIAL THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Potential Third Party Funder is an entity that could become a Third Party Funder, as defined in section 98J. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 98G&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'third party funder' is directly related to the definition of SECTION 98G, which describes how third-party funding for arbitration works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6b5cecde95cc674037324a7a227c1daf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 98H&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Third Party Funder is a key entity in defining and participating in Funding Agreements as described by SECTION 98H."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6b5cecde95cc674037324a7a227c1daf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;" target="&quot;FUNDING AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A funding agreement involves a third party funder who provides arbitration funding to the funded party."&lt;SEP&gt;"A third party funder is a person who is a party to a funding agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-722c61c3b51c31b6fcf0c8534507c492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a177eee7ea2e82607ded8787a57461c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Third party funder is involved in providing funding for arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-722c61c3b51c31b6fcf0c8534507c492</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION SUPPORT AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"There is an agreement between the third party funder and the funded party regarding funding terms, control rights, termination conditions, etc."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-319ab10afb64c747e7339427a06f0a41</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;" target="&quot;CONFLICT OF INTEREST MANAGEMENT PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The third party funder has procedures to manage potential conflicts of interest that may arise in relation to the funded party."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-319ab10afb64c747e7339427a06f0a41</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;" target="&quot;COMPLAINT HANDLING MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The third party funder has mechanisms for handling complaints from the funded party, ensuring proper resolution and enforcement of remedies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-319ab10afb64c747e7339427a06f0a41</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;" target="&quot;DISCLOSURE ABOUT THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Third party funders are named in the disclosure about third party funding of arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd5d5713c2c272a2a9c9f2f00a8d2933</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;" target="&quot;FUNDING AGREEMENT (ENDS)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The end of a funding agreement is related to the third party funder involved in it."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd5d5713c2c272a2a9c9f2f00a8d2933</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDER&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION INSTITUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Third party funders are related to the institution where arbitrations take place through funding agreements and disclosures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd5d5713c2c272a2a9c9f2f00a8d2933</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION FUNDING&quot;" target="&quot;FUNDED PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">40.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Funded Parties receive financial assistance from Arbitration Funding, which can cover various costs associated with arbitration processes and is provided through third-party arrangements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Funded Parties receive financial assistance from Arbitration Funding, which can cover various costs associated with arbitration processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Funded Parties receive funding from Third Party Funders for their involvement in arbitration processes, which includes covering costs and expenses related to the proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Funded Parties rely on Arbitration Funding to cover costs related to arbitration proceedings, which can be provided through third-party arrangements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Funded Parties rely on Arbitration Funding, which can cover various costs associated with arbitration processes and is provided through third-party arrangements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION FUNDING&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORIZED BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Authorized Body is the entity that can provide Arbitration Funding as per section 98X(2). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION FUNDING&quot;" target="&quot;FUNDING AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Funding Agreement pertains to how Arbitration Funding will be provided, as seen in section 98H. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5b66686857ee1819605df3eb94ed7318</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION BODY&quot;" target="&quot;FUNDED PARTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">32.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration Bodies may involve or support Funded Parties who can receive financial assistance from Third Party Funders to participate in arbitration processes, covering various costs and expenses related to the proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration Bodies may involve or support Funded Parties, who can receive financial assistance from Third Party Funders to participate in arbitration processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration Bodies may involve or support Funded Parties, who can receive funding from Third Party Funders to participate in arbitration processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arbitration Bodies may receive funding from Third Party Funders to support the participation of Funded Parties in arbitration processes, including covering related expenses and costs."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION BODY&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORIZED BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An authorized body may be involved in appointing or managing an arbitration body, given their role in legal frameworks."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e0edcefcdaacd59cb7375b56608a714e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION BODY&quot;" target="&quot;DISCLOSURE ABOUT THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The disclosure must be given to the arbitration body regarding the funding agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd5d5713c2c272a2a9c9f2f00a8d2933</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION BODY&quot;" target="&quot;DISCLOSURE ABOUT END OF THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The disclosure about the end of third party funding must be given to the arbitration body if it exists."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd5d5713c2c272a2a9c9f2f00a8d2933</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION BODY&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION (ARBITRATION)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration body refers to arbitration proceedings and includes arbitrators or courts depending on the context, related to the concept of arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b8df8f796c1527424030ca7952635395</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION BODY&quot;" target="&quot;7TH SECTION NON-COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Non-compliance with section 7 may affect the arbitration body's ability to handle notices and disclosures properly."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-eac62f2f1327a829e40a168eae3df71e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FUNDED PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;PROVISION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Provisions ensure that Funded Parties are protected and have measures in place for their involvement in arbitration funding activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Provisions provide safeguards and measures for the involvement of Funded Parties in arbitration funding activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4dc28f6c483991edffbe441c62202024</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FUNDED PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;FUNDING AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A funding agreement is made between a funded party and a third party funder."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a177eee7ea2e82607ded8787a57461c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FUNDED PARTY&quot;" target="&quot;CONSULTANCY FIRM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The consultancy firm is provided by the third party funder to assist the funded party in arbitration matters."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-319ab10afb64c747e7339427a06f0a41</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ADVISORY BODY&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORIZED BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Advisory Body and Authorized Body both refer to entities appointed by the Secretary for Justice, with slightly different contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"The advisory body and authorized body are both appointed by the Secretary for Justice but serve different roles within the legal framework."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e0edcefcdaacd59cb7375b56608a714e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca2c3669141d3f1cd87a21d68d494cf5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ADVISORY BODY&quot;" target="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Third Party Funders provide the name and contact details of the Advisory Body to funded parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Third party funders must provide contact details to the advisory body and submit annual returns as required by regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a96252983055863ad83c00cacd5a42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24bcba17e89155ad11eeca80dd981ea9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ADVISORY BODY&quot;" target="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Advisory Body makes rules related to ORFS agreements, directly impacting their implementation and standards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d3450bee90618bb17df6c3522ce7aa42</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUTHORIZED BODY&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Courts can consider matters related to compliance with or non-compliance with the code of practice when deciding relevant questions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-aff1392eccc9ea622ef0b3868092fcd2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUTHORIZED BODY&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORIZED BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Authorized Body is another term for the entity appointed by the Secretary for Justice, similar to Advisory Body but with a different context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca2c3669141d3f1cd87a21d68d494cf5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUTHORIZED BODY&quot;" target="&quot;CONSULTATIVE BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both bodies are appointed by the Secretary for Justice to monitor and review different aspects of a legal process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b83c6369ee22a5baf386b25e3605cb81</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUTHORIZED BODY&quot;" target="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An authorized body appointed by the Secretary for Justice can be involved in ORFS agreements related to arbitrations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51ad58eafa2f8aa3ad189d3ab135c444</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FUNDING AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;DIVISION 3 COMMENCEMENT DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A funding agreement must be made on or after the commencement date of Division 3."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a177eee7ea2e82607ded8787a57461c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FUNDING AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;THIRD PARTY FUNDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Third Party Funders' control over arbitrations, liability for adverse costs, insurance premiums, security for costs, and other financial liabilities are detailed in Funding Agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a96252983055863ad83c00cacd5a42b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FUNDING AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;DISCLOSURE ABOUT THIRD PARTY FUNDING OF ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The disclosure must include the fact that a funding agreement has been made and the name of the third party funder."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fd5d5713c2c272a2a9c9f2f00a8d2933</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FUNDING AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The funding agreement is related to the arbitration process as it ends and notifications are required regarding its termination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5247edeafb01587bde32ae379e5261dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 98G&quot;" target="&quot;FUNDING AGREEMENT (資助協議)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"SECTION 98G defines the concept of funding agreements for third-party arbitration, which is directly related to FUNDING AGREEMENT (資助協議)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6b5cecde95cc674037324a7a227c1daf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 98H&quot;" target="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENT (ORFS協議)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"SECTION 98H explicitly states that ORFS agreements are not included in the definition of funding agreements, indicating a clear distinction between them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6b5cecde95cc674037324a7a227c1daf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An ORFS agreement is not considered as part of a funding agreement for arbitration, according to legal definitions provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a177eee7ea2e82607ded8787a57461c8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ORFS Agreement and ORFS are mentioned as related terms in the text, both referring to aspects of charging frameworks."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca2c3669141d3f1cd87a21d68d494cf5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;RESULT ORIENTED CHARGING FRAMEWORK (ORFS)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Result Oriented Charging Framework (ORFS) is defined alongside ORFS Agreement, indicating they are related terms describing the same concept in different contexts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca2c3669141d3f1cd87a21d68d494cf5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;律師&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"律师参与制定和执行与客户相关的收费结构协议，如按条件收费、损害赔偿收费等。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ce0cbc87febf0559389231de15b6441b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;CONDITIONAL FEE AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ORFS agreement is a type of conditional fee agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2799d5a0031a68f64f3cd87dbc0dabae</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;DAMAGES-BASED AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ORFS agreement includes damages-based agreements as one of its types."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2799d5a0031a68f64f3cd87dbc0dabae</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;HYBRID DAMAGES-BASED AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ORFS agreement encompasses hybrid damages-based agreements within its scope."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2799d5a0031a68f64f3cd87dbc0dabae</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;DIVISION 6—CODE OF PRACTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Division 6 — Code of Practice provides guidelines for the conduct expected in relation to ORFS agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d3450bee90618bb17df6c3522ce7aa42</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal may not order costs specified under section 98ZU if an ORFS agreement has been entered into, but can still do so in exceptional circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51ad58eafa2f8aa3ad189d3ab135c444</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDIATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">3.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While the text discusses arbitration, there's no direct relationship between arbitration and mediation as per provided context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-722c61c3b51c31b6fcf0c8534507c492</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDIATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 620)&quot;" target="&quot;L.N. 260 OF 2018&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The mediation ordinance has an editorial note referencing L.N. 260 of 2018, indicating a specific legal document related to the mediation process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-aff1392eccc9ea622ef0b3868092fcd2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MEDIATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 620)&quot;" target="&quot;DIVISION 5—OTHER MEASURES AND SAFEGUARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Division 5 has an editorial note referencing the Mediation Ordinance, indicating a connection between procedural measures and mediation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Division 5 has yet to apply in relation to a mediation mentioned in section 7A of the Mediation Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-aff1392eccc9ea622ef0b3868092fcd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a252d91181bacec6fcd6f1d54297b19a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART 10A&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 98F&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition of 'costs' under Section 98F applies to arbitrations outside Hong Kong when governed by Part 10A."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-358c63f61ec2ce4f0f9b4f0675b579e4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PART 10A&quot;" target="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENTS FOR ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Part 10A is specifically excluded from applying to ORFS agreements for arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-087a07092efc881959ad458909cb8527</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 98F&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL PRACTICE FIRM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal practice firms may be affected by the definition of 'costs' as provided in Section 98F when dealing with arbitrations governed by Hong Kong laws, including those under Part 10A."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-358c63f61ec2ce4f0f9b4f0675b579e4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LAWYER&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL PRACTICE FIRM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Lawyers working for or as members of a legal practice firm may be affected by the rules and definitions provided in Section 98F when dealing with arbitrations governed by Hong Kong laws, including those under Part 10A."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-358c63f61ec2ce4f0f9b4f0675b579e4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LAWYER&quot;" target="&quot;CLIENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A lawyer represents and is hired by the client in legal matters."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-454f67393ac66e31ad436e5012345559</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LAWYER&quot;" target="&quot;THE LAW PRACTITIONERS ORDINANCE (CAP. 159)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Law Practitioners Ordinance defines the qualifications for lawyers practicing in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-454f67393ac66e31ad436e5012345559</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LAWYER&quot;" target="&quot;ORFS協議&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ORFS协议与律师订立或寻求订立有关仲裁的内容相关,涉及资料传递规则。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fc6ead6e2679a8dfdba550b0494d664b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LAWYER&quot;" target="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENT FOR ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Lawyers are involved in the process of entering into ORFS agreements for arbitration, and they may communicate information to their professional advisers for advice related to these agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4158bcd358cce62e9937de8896e1ba0b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LAWYER&quot;" target="&quot;GOVERNMENT BODY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Lawyers are obliged by law to make communications with government bodies as part of the process for ORFS agreements for arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4158bcd358cce62e9937de8896e1ba0b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENTS FOR ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;DAMAGES-BASED AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of paying lawyers based on clients' financial benefits is relevant in both agreements, though ORFS Agreements are specifically for arbitration matters."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-98e9907f4439e46ca077ec9da34b8a1f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORFS AGREEMENTS FOR ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;HYBRID DAMAGES-BASED AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
