  <data key="d6">chunk-e027acdec4c66c21703cf2589ec26926</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATE LAW&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"State law may affect the applicability of certain disputes for arbitration, as stated in Article 5."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e027acdec4c66c21703cf2589ec26926</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERPRETATION RULE(S)&quot;" target="&quot;DEFINITION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Definitions and interpretation rules are interrelated in legal texts to ensure clarity and consistency."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e027acdec4c66c21703cf2589ec26926</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT PROCEDURES&quot;" target="&quot;UNIFORMITY IN APPLICATION AND OBSERVANCE OF GOOD FAITH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Court procedures do not apply to the principle of uniformity in application and observance of good faith, indicating their distinct nature but related context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5a9efbbf91e4535558399760b519e3ef</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LEGAL INSTITUTION&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Courts are part of legal institutions within a state's judicial system."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e027acdec4c66c21703cf2589ec26926</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COUNTER-CLAIM&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 2(f) applies the concept of claims to counter-claims in the context of arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c4488b1327869fe2b0410a202e25b48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COUNTER-CLAIM&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 32(2)(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 32(2)(a) applies the concept of defense to counter-claims, showing a relationship between these articles and their subject matter."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c4488b1327869fe2b0410a202e25b48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFENSE&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 28&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 28 is an exception where it does not apply to defenses, distinguishing its scope from other articles that do cover defense aspects."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c4488b1327869fe2b0410a202e25b48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFENSE&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 25(A)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 25(a) specifically mentions defenses, indicating its relevance to legal proceedings involving parties' rights."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c4488b1327869fe2b0410a202e25b48</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
