  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 12 is referenced as a note in Article 5, suggesting there might be related provisions or explanations between these two sections."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-867eea6bba840f054f655ce7e36c7717</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECTION 12&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 8&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 8 is related to Section 12 as they both form parts of the legal framework, though their applicability differs."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3839e768a51af918bcfdbfd8b6130d8b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT INTERVENTION&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 5&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 5 directly addresses the extent of court intervention in matters governed by this Law."&lt;SEP&gt;"Article 5 explicitly defines the extent of court intervention, stating that courts shall not intervene except where provided in this Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e496ab5c7a454a1b436e9279c911d987</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT OR OTHER AUTHORITY FOR CERTAIN FUNCTIONS OF ARBITRATION ASSISTANCE AND SUPERVISION&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 6&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 6 specifies which authorities can perform certain functions of arbitration assistance and supervision, such as those mentioned in articles 11(3), 11(4), 13(3), 14, 16(3) and 34(2)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e496ab5c7a454a1b436e9279c911d987</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WRITTEN FORM&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
