<edge source="&quot;PCCW-HKT TELEPHONE LIMITED&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC CONTRACT OR MAIN PRIVATE CONTRACT FOR PURPOSES OF SECTION 7(1)(A)(II) OR 8(1)(A)(II)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The entity is involved in public contracts or main private contracts for construction work, which may involve a contract value of $5,000,000."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a75fc2e86bd1bd49cadcd97f8d2f0419</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SMAR TONE MOBILE COMMUNICATIONS LIMITED&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC CONTRACT OR MAIN PRIVATE CONTRACT FOR PURPOSES OF SECTION 7(1)(A)(II) OR 8(1)(A)(II)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The entity is involved in public contracts or main private contracts for construction work, which may involve a contract value of $5,000,000."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a75fc2e86bd1bd49cadcd97f8d2f0419</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE UNIVERSITY OF HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC CONTRACT OR MAIN PRIVATE CONTRACT FOR PURPOSES OF SECTION 7(1)(A)(II) OR 8(1)(A)(II)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The entity is involved in public contracts or main private contracts for construction work, which may involve a contract value of $5,000,000."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a75fc2e86bd1bd49cadcd97f8d2f0419</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;URBAN RENEWAL AUTHORITY&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC CONTRACT OR MAIN PRIVATE CONTRACT FOR PURPOSES OF SECTION 7(1)(A)(II) OR 8(1)(A)(II)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The entity is involved in public contracts or main private contracts for construction work, which may involve a contract value of $5,000,000."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a75fc2e86bd1bd49cadcd97f8d2f0419</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VOCATIONAL TRAINING COUNCIL&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC CONTRACT OR MAIN PRIVATE CONTRACT FOR PURPOSES OF SECTION 7(1)(A)(II) OR 8(1)(A)(II)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The entity is involved in public contracts or main private contracts for construction work, which may involve a contract value of $5,000,000."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a75fc2e86bd1bd49cadcd97f8d2f0419</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WEST KOWLOON CULTURAL DISTRICT AUTHORITY&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC CONTRACT OR MAIN PRIVATE CONTRACT FOR PURPOSES OF SECTION 7(1)(A)(II) OR 8(1)(A)(II)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The entity is involved in public contracts or main private contracts for construction work, which may involve a contract value of $5,000,000."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a75fc2e86bd1bd49cadcd97f8d2f0419</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;$5,000,000&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC CONTRACTS OR MAIN PRIVATE CONTRACTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The specified value for public contracts or main private contracts involving construction work is $5,000,000."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9d64bf6870cd28991e3919d0bb4b5dfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;$500,000&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC CONTRACTS OR MAIN PRIVATE CONTRACTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The specified value for public contracts or main private contracts involving only the supply of related goods and services is $500,000."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9d64bf6870cd28991e3919d0bb4b5dfa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTROL OF EXEMPTION CLAUSES ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;1990年第38號法律公告&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Control of Exemption Clauses Ordinance is cited in the legal notice issued on 1 December 1990."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e6f1b0342117fba0657cd9deb544e402</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTROL OF EXEMPTION CLAUSES ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;《售賣貨品條例》(第26章)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The definition of 'goods' in the Control of Exemption Clauses Ordinance is consistent with that defined under The Sale of Goods Ordinance (Cap. 26)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e6f1b0342117fba0657cd9deb544e402</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSONNEL INJURY&quot;" target="&quot;NEGLIGENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Personnel injury can be a result of negligence, which is covered by the Control of Exemption Clauses Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e6f1b0342117fba0657cd9deb544e402</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEGLIGENCE&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPIERS' LIABILITY ORDINANCE (CAP. 314)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Negligence includes general prudence obligations under the Occupiers' Liability Ordinance (Cap. 314), showing a clear relationship between negligence and this ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-405702086caa260fb0fa6bf8fac677c3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE OF GOODS ORDINANCE (CAP. 26)&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPIERS' LIABILITY ORDINATION (CAP. 314)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both ordinances deal with legal responsibilities and obligations, though in different contexts: Occupiers' Liability Ordinance focuses on property safety while Sale of Goods Ordinance deals with contractual goods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-405702086caa260fb0fa6bf8fac677c3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SALE OF GOODS ORDINANCE (CAP. 26)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT TERM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contract terms cannot exclude or limit certain obligations under the Sale of Goods Ordinance, especially when dealing with consumers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-872dd343c6e35c900d1e080217da3c6c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEGLIGENCE (疏忽)&quot;" target="&quot;PERSONAL INJURY (人身傷害)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Personal injury is a consequence that can result from negligence in various contexts including BUSINESS operations as defined by the relevant ordinances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ac6eb040e98e92757cf6e4d3f0473e64</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS LIABILITY&quot;" target="&quot;PREMISES USED FOR BUSINESS PURPOSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business liability arises from the occupation of premises used for business purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3af7b8f9d9569fddb32c031c5ec0dbc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS LIABILITY&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTUAL OBLIGATIONS OR DUTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business liability is derived from breaches of contractual obligations or duties arising from a person's course of business or occupation of premises used for business purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3af7b8f9d9569fddb32c031c5ec0dbc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUSINESS LIABILITY&quot;" target="&quot;TORT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both contract and tort sections apply to business liabilities, indicating an overlap in the types of liability considered."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3af7b8f9d9569fddb32c031c5ec0dbc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PREMISES USED FOR BUSINESS PURPOSES&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS PURPOSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Premises used for business purposes are directly linked with the definition of business purposes in this context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b3af7b8f9d9569fddb32c031c5ec0dbc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT OR ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT TERM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT OR ARBITRATOR must consider whether a CONTRACT TERM meets certain standards of reasonableness, especially in cases involving misrepresentation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34f2388558428d5c25b0420a73f3129c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT OR ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;DISCLAIMER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT OR ARBITRATOR evaluates the fairness and appropriateness of DISCLAMERS when determining their validity without contractual effect."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34f2388558428d5c25b0420a73f3129c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT OR ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;MISREPRESENTATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 284)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT OR ARBITRATOR uses the standards set by the MISREPRESENTATION ORDINANCE to assess CONTRACT TERMS and DISCLAMERS for reasonableness."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT OR ARBITRATOR's determination of reasonableness is guided by the MISREPRESENTATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 284), particularly in relation to contract terms and notices."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51792815fbdf7d62aebbf3740d5c33b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f2388558428d5c25b0420a73f3129c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT OR ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;RESOURCE ALLOCATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"When assessing whether a party can limit their legal liability, the COURT OR ARBITRATOR considers the RESOURCE ALLOCATION of that party in managing potential risks."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34f2388558428d5c25b0420a73f3129c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT OR ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;PERSON AS AGAINST WHOM ANOTHER PERSON SEEKS TO RELY UPON THE TERM OR NOTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT OR ARBITRATOR's determination on reasonableness involves considering whether it is fair and reasonable for the PERSON to rely on a term or notice."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51792815fbdf7d62aebbf3740d5c33b8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT OR ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSECTION (2) OR (4)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court or arbitrator's decision on reasonableness may be influenced by subsections (2) or (4). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-53896ec29a47d41511a83256e25be1c7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT TERM&quot;" target="&quot;REASONABLENESS TEST&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The REASONABLENESS TEST (as defined in U.K. law 1977 c. 50 s. 7) applies specifically to CONTRACT TERMS, particularly those related to the transfer of ownership and quiet possession."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-723308f570a274e7e8ac1a555c11b81b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT TERM&quot;" target="&quot;LIABILITY EXCLUSION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACT TERMS (as defined in U.K. law 1977 c. 50 s. 7) can include provisions for the exclusion or limitation of liability, which is directly related to LIABILITY EXCLUSION."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-723308f570a274e7e8ac1a555c11b81b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MISREPRESENTATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 284)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTUAL EFFECT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MISREPRESENTATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 284) influences how terms and notices are interpreted in relation to contractual effect."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51792815fbdf7d62aebbf3740d5c33b8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSON AS AGAINST WHOM ANOTHER PERSON SEEKS TO RELY UPON THE TERM OR NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTUAL EFFECT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PERSON must consider whether it is fair and reasonable to rely on a term or notice, taking into account the contractual effect of such reliance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51792815fbdf7d62aebbf3740d5c33b8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSON CLAIMING THAT A CONTRACT TERM SATISFIES REASONABLENESS REQUIREMENT&quot;" target="&quot;RESOURCES AVAILABLE FOR MEETING LIABILITY SHOULD IT ARISE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The person claiming reasonableness must consider the resources available for meeting potential liability. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-53896ec29a47d41511a83256e25be1c7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSON CLAIMING THAT A CONTRACT TERM SATISFIES REASONABLENESS REQUIREMENT&quot;" target="&quot;INSURANCE COVERAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The person claiming reasonableness may use insurance coverage as part of their argument. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-53896ec29a47d41511a83256e25be1c7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RESOURCES AVAILABLE FOR MEETING LIABILITY SHOULD IT ARISE&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Business processes can affect the resources available for meeting potential liability. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-53896ec29a47d41511a83256e25be1c7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INSURANCE COVERAGE&quot;" target="&quot;BUSINESS PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Insurance coverage is a resource that may be part of business processes to manage risk. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-53896ec29a47d41511a83256e25be1c7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEALING AS CONSUMER&quot;" target="&quot;PARTY TO A CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A party to a contract deals as consumer if they neither make the contract in the course of business nor hold themselves out as doing so."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0aa5c7bec2bb945d36bb333255416d51</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEALING AS CONSUMER&quot;" target="&quot;CONSUMER RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties dealing as consumers have specific protections and rights under laws such as those governing sales of goods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0aa5c7bec2bb945d36bb333255416d51</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXEMPTION CLAUSE&quot;" target="&quot;LIABILITY FOR NEGLECT, BREACH OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Exemption Clauses cannot exclude or limit the liability for negligence and breach of contract as stated in section 5(1) (a), (b), and (c). Additionally, sections 7 and 12 also prevent excluding or restricting such liabilities by reference to terms and notices."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4f376b792b435eb29fed3bd6caa3e8f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXEMPTION CLAUSE&quot;" target="&quot;AVOIDANCE OF LIABILITY FOR NEGLECT, BREACH OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Exemption Clauses cannot exclude or limit the liability for negligence and breach of contract as stated in section 5(1), but they are related to how such liabilities can be managed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4f376b792b435eb29fed3bd6caa3e8f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXEMPTION CLAUSE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTROL OF EXEMPTION CLAUSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The control over exemption clauses includes managing their impact on various legal responsibilities, including those for negligence and breach of contract as stated in section 5. Varieties of Exemption Clauses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4f376b792b435eb29fed3bd6caa3e8f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIABILITY FOR NEGLECT, BREACH OF CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;NEGЛИCIENCE, BREACH OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Liability for negligence and breach of contract are directly related as they both refer to the same legal responsibility under different circumstances. Section 5 specifically addresses these liabilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4f376b792b435eb29fed3bd6caa3e8f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIABILITY FOR NEGLECT, BREACH OF CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTROL OF EXEMPTION CLAUSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Control over exemption clauses includes managing their impact on liability for negligence and breach of contract as stated in section 5. Varieties of Exemption Clauses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4f376b792b435eb29fed3bd6caa3e8f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIABILITY FOR NEGLECT, BREACH OF CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;AVOIDANCE OF LIABILITY FOR NEGLECT, BREACH OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Avoidance of liability for negligence and breach of contract is directly related as they both refer to the same legal responsibility under different circumstances. Section 5 specifically addresses these liabilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4f376b792b435eb29fed3bd6caa3e8f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEGLIGENCE LIABILITY&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT TERMS AND NOTICES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text discusses how contract terms cannot be used to exclude or limit liability for negligence except under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6f58b4ec9af40aa0f4ba64be9471ec8f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEGLIGENCE LIABILITY&quot;" target="&quot;LIABILITY FOR BREACH OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both negligence liability and liability for breach of contract are addressed within the context of contractual agreements and their limitations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6f58b4ec9af40aa0f4ba64be9471ec8f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT TERMS AND NOTICES&quot;" target="&quot;LIABILITY FOR BREACH OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contract terms and notices are discussed in relation to limiting liability, specifically mentioning breach of contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6f58b4ec9af40aa0f4ba64be9471ec8f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTING PARTIES&quot;" target="&quot;LIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The liability of contracting parties cannot be excluded or restricted when they are in breach of contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9caec393d81747f82a0bc36401fbbd53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTING PARTIES&quot;" target="&quot;REASONABLE STANDARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contract terms must satisfy the requirement of reasonableness to exclude or restrict liability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9caec393d81747f82a0bc36401fbbd53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BREACH OF CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;LIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Liability cannot be excluded when there is a breach of contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9caec393d81747f82a0bc36401fbbd53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIABILITY&quot;" target="&quot;UNJUST ENRICHMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Unjust enrichment is not directly mentioned with liability in this context. However, it can be inferred that unjust enrichment might relate to legal liabilities under certain circumstances but no explicit relationship is given."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9caec393d81747f82a0bc36401fbbd53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSUMER IDENTITY TRANSACTION&quot;" target="&quot;DAMAGES FOR NEGLIGENCE OR BREACH OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Consumer identity transactions are related to potential damages for negligence or breach of contract, but no direct relationship is explicitly stated in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9caec393d81747f82a0bc36401fbbd53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNREASONABLE INDEMNITY CLAUSES&quot;" target="&quot;LIABILITY ARISING FROM SALE OR SUPPLY OF GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both terms deal with legal responsibilities arising from contracts and goods transactions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dfdaa9554cda347b9858ba470c1dfeab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNREASONABLE INDEMNITY CLAUSES&quot;" target="&quot;CONSUMER GUARANTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The clauses are related to consumer protection, specifically in the context of unreasonable indemnity obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dfdaa9554cda347b9858ba470c1dfeab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIABILITY ARISING FROM SALE OR SUPPLY OF GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;CONSUMER GUARANTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both terms involve legal responsibilities and protections for consumers regarding goods transactions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dfdaa9554cda347b9858ba470c1dfeab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOSS OR DAMAGE&quot;" target="&quot;GUARANTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Guarantee cannot exclude or limit liability for loss or damage arising from defects during consumer use of the goods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2333b3d2deec0b227d514b0090b44838</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT TERMS EXCLUDING OR RESTRICTING LIABILITY FOR BREACH OF OBLIGATION ARISING BY IMPLICATION OF LAW FROM THE NATURE OF THE CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;LIABILITY FOR BREACH OF OBLIGATION ARISING BY IMPLICATION OF LAW FROM THE NATURE OF THE CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contract terms can exclude or restrict liability for breach of obligation arising by implication of law from the nature of the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0093428c9e5c24b975d1827e057247c3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIABILITY FOR BREACH OF OBLIGATION ARISING BY IMPLICATION OF LAW FROM THE NATURE OF THE CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;NON-CONSUMER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Liability can potentially be excluded or restricted against a non-consumer, but only if the terms are reasonable."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0093428c9e5c24b975d1827e057247c3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRANSFER OWNERSHIP OF GOODS OR GIVE POSSESSION&quot;" target="&quot;QUIET POSSESSION ASSURANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Terms cannot exclude liability for transferring ownership of goods or giving possession unless they satisfy the requirement of reasonableness."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0093428c9e5c24b975d1827e057247c3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TRANSFER OWNERSHIP OF GOODS OR GIVE POSSESSION&quot;" target="&quot;LAW OF SALE OF GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The law of sale of goods does not govern these terms, which are subject to different rules."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0093428c9e5c24b975d1827e057247c3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REASONABLENESS TEST&quot;" target="&quot;LIABILITY EXCLUSION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The REASONABLENESS TEST (as defined in U.K. law 1977 c. 50 s. 7) provides a framework for determining the validity of terms that exclude or limit liability, impacting LIABILITY EXCLUSION."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-723308f570a274e7e8ac1a555c11b81b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EVASION BY MEANS OF SECONDARY CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both concepts deal with legal strategies, one involving contract evasion and the other arbitration agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6a2e2728ed9206072fd11eab3f6ceb87</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;WRITTEN CONSENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Written consent is required for enforcing arbitration agreements, especially when dealing with consumers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6a2e2728ed9206072fd11eab3f6ceb87</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTROL DOES NOT APPLY&quot;" target="&quot;SUPPLY CONTRACT EXEMPTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A supply contract exemption refers to situations where certain provisions do not apply, including those where 'control' does not apply."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca4a2a9fbbaee42187b60b84f640f8f3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTROL DOES NOT APPLY&quot;" target="&quot;EXEMPT SUPPLY CONTRACT (IN CHINESE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A supply contract exemption refers to situations where certain provisions do not apply, including those where 'control' does not apply."&lt;SEP&gt;"The concept of control not applying is related to exempt supply contracts, as both involve legal exclusions or limitations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The concept of control not applying is related to the exemption of supply contracts, as both pertain to legal exclusions or limitations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca4a2a9fbbaee42187b60b84f640f8f3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTROL DOES NOT APPLY&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">11.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of arbitration agreements is related to the concept of control not applying, as both deal with legal enforceability and exemptions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The concept of control not applying is related to arbitration agreements as both involve legal exclusions or limitations on enforceability."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca4a2a9fbbaee42187b60b84f640f8f3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUPPLY CONTRACT EXEMPTION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both agreements deal with legal responsibilities and can coexist in certain situations without conflicting directly."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca4a2a9fbbaee42187b60b84f640f8f3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT (IN CHINESE)&quot;" target="&quot;CIRCUMSTANCES WHERE CONTROL DOES NOT APPLY (IN CHINESE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">20.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Chinese version of an Arbitration Agreement is related to the circumstances where control does not apply, as both are legal agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The circumstances where control does not apply are related to arbitration agreements, as both involve legal exclusions or limitations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca4a2a9fbbaee42187b60b84f640f8f3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT (IN CHINESE)&quot;" target="&quot;EXEMPT SUPPLY CONTRACT (IN CHINESE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both Chinese versions deal with legal agreements and exemptions, indicating a relationship through their shared context in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca4a2a9fbbaee42187b60b84f640f8f3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT (IN CHINESE)&quot;" target="&quot;SUPPLY CONTRACT EXEMPTION (IN CHINESE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both Chinese versions deal with legal agreements and can coexist in certain situations without conflicting directly, similar to the relationship between their English counterparts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both Chinese versions deal with legal agreements and exemptions, indicating a relationship through their shared context in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca4a2a9fbbaee42187b60b84f640f8f3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUPPLY CONTRACT EXEMPTION (IN CHINESE)&quot;" target="&quot;CIRCUMSTANCES WHERE CONTROL DOES NOT APPLY (IN CHINESE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Chinese version of a supply contract exemption is related to the circumstances where control does not apply, as both are legal exemptions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca4a2a9fbbaee42187b60b84f640f8f3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUPPLY CONTRACT EXEMPTION (IN CHINESE)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both agreements deal with legal responsibilities and can coexist in certain situations without conflicting directly, similar to the relationship between their Chinese counterparts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca4a2a9fbbaee42187b60b84f640f8f3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CIRCUMSTANCES WHERE CONTROL DOES NOT APPLY (IN CHINESE)&quot;" target="&quot;EXEMPT SUPPLY CONTRACT (IN CHINESE)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The circumstances where control does not apply are related to exempt supply contracts, as both involve legal exclusions or limitations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca4a2a9fbbaee42187b60b84f640f8f3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXEMPT SUPPLY CONTRACT (IN CHINESE)&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both deal with legal responsibilities and can coexist in certain situations without conflicting directly, similar to the relationship between their Chinese counterparts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca4a2a9fbbaee42187b60b84f640f8f3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT TERM EXCLUSION&quot;" target="&quot;EXEMPTED SUPPLY CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Exempted supply contracts are specifically excluded from the terms that limit liability by reference to contract terms, highlighting a distinct relationship in contractual law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8271f6bc492f9ae5ef71b7e98a92bd06</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXEMPTED SUPPLY CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE OF GOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both types of contracts are discussed within the same context and share similar characteristics related to international trade and contract law, indicating a relationship through their commonality in legal frameworks."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8271f6bc492f9ae5ef71b7e98a92bd06</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT OF SALE OF GOODS&quot;" target="&quot;SUPPLY CONTRACTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both 'Contract of Sale of Goods' and 'Supply Contracts' fall under the broader category of contracts involving goods transfer or possession, making them related entities within this context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8271f6bc492f9ae5ef71b7e98a92bd06</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OFFER AND ACCEPTANCE&quot;" target="&quot;LAW APPLICABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The LAW APPLICABILITY can be influenced by how OFFER AND ACCEPTANCE are constituted, especially when involving different jurisdictions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-057148e20c6e00b2ee6dee748e6c75ff</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHOICE OF LAW CLAUSES&quot;" target="&quot;18. 其他有關法例的保留條文&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both sections discuss aspects related to the effectiveness and limitations of contractual terms under Hong Kong's legal framework, particularly concerning the choice of law for contracts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-70bc29e417a48ee998a460c753e36328</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;具合法裁判權的主管當局&quot;" target="&quot;成文法則 (ENACTMENT)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"具合法裁判權的主管當局的概念由成文法則定义。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51d1d77716a000d59a4c18879a262e96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;具合法裁判權的主管當局&quot;" target="&quot;法定 (STATUTORY)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"具合法裁判權的主管當局行使法定裁判权或职能，与法定概念相关联。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51d1d77716a000d59a4c18879a262e96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;具合法裁判權的主管當局&quot;" target="&quot; COURT &quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"法院是具合法裁判權的主管當局的一种形式。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51d1d77716a000d59a4c18879a262e96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;具合法裁判權的主管當局&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATOR &quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"仲裁人也是具合法裁判權的主管當局的一部分。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51d1d77716a000d59a4c18879a262e96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;具合法裁判權的主管當局&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC BODY &quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"公共机构是具合法裁判權的主管當局的一种形式。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51d1d77716a000d59a4c18879a262e96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;成文法則 (ENACTMENT)&quot;" target="&quot;ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"成文法則包括任何條例和通过条例生效的法律文件。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51d1d77716a000d59a4c18879a262e96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;1977 C. 50 S. 29 U.K.&quot;" target="&quot;STATUTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Statutory terms are defined by the enactment, specifically referencing section 29 of the 1977 UK legislation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-938a5862de0ab4ab87d0bfde97f7d287</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTHING IN THIS ORDINANCE REMOVES OR RESTRICTS THE EFFECT OF, OR PREVENTS RELIANCE UPON, ANY CONTRACTUAL PROVISION WHICH—&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT TERM &quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"任何合同条款都可能受到本条例中此条文的影响。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51d1d77716a000d59a4c18879a262e96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;A) IS AUTHORIZED OR REQUIRED BY THE EXPRESS TERMS OR NECESSARY IMPLICATION OF AN ENACTMENT;&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTUAL PROVISION (合同条款)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"合同条款可以由成文法則授权或必要暗示规定。</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51d1d77716a000d59a4c18879a262e96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;B) BEING MADE WITH A VIEW TO COMPLIANCE WITH AN INTERNATIONAL AGREEMENT WHICH APPLIES TO HONG KONG, DOES NOT OPERATE MORE RESTRICTIVELY THAN IS CONTEMPLATED BY THE AGREEMENT.&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTUAL PROVISION (合同条款)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"合同条款可以为遵守适用于香港的国际协议而制定，且不比该协议原意范围更局限。</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51d1d77716a000d59a4c18879a262e96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;A CONTRACT TERM IS TO BE TAKEN FOR THE PURPOSES OF THIS ORDINANCE AS SATISFYING THE REQUIREMENT OF REASONABLENESS IF IT IS INCORPORATED OR APPROVED BY, OR INCORPORATED PURSUANT TO A DECISION OR RULING OF, A COMPETENT AUTHORITY ACTING IN THE EXERCISE OF ANY STATUTORY JURISDICTION OR FUNCTION AND IS NOT A TERM IN A CONTRACT TO WHICH THE COMPETENT AUTHORITY IS ITSELF A PARTY.&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTUAL PROVISION (合同条款)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据本条例，由具合法裁判權的主管當局批准或决定纳入的合同条款被视为满足合理性的要求。</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51d1d77716a000d59a4c18879a262e96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IN THIS SECTION—COMPETENT AUTHORITY (具合法裁判權的主管當局) MEANS ANY COURT, ARBITRATOR OR PUBLIC BODY;&quot;" target="&quot;COURT &quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"法院是具合法裁判權的主管當局的一种形式。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51d1d77716a000d59a4c18879a262e96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IN THIS SECTION—COMPETENT AUTHORITY (具合法裁判權的主管當局) MEANS ANY COURT, ARBITRATOR OR PUBLIC BODY;&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATOR &quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"仲裁人也是具合法裁判權的主管當局的一部分。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51d1d77716a000d59a4c18879a262e96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;IN THIS SECTION—COMPETENT AUTHORITY (具合法裁判權的主管當局) MEANS ANY COURT, ARBITRATOR OR PUBLIC BODY;&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC BODY &quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"公共机构是具合法裁判權的主管當局的一种形式。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51d1d77716a000d59a4c18879a262e96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;本條例的任何條文 (ANY PROVISION IN THIS ORDINANCE)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTUAL PROVISION (合同条款)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"合同条款与本条例中的任何条文相关。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51d1d77716a000d59a4c18879a262e96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;本條例 (THIS ORDINANCE)&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC BODY &quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"公共机构与本条例相关联。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-51d1d77716a000d59a4c18879a262e96</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENT AUTHORITY&quot;" target="&quot;STATUTORY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The term 'statutory' is defined as being conferred by an enactment, which involves the authority of a court or public body."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-938a5862de0ab4ab87d0bfde97f7d287</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENACTMENT&quot;" target="&quot;APPLICATION SCOPE CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The application scope clause refers to provisions that apply based on enactments and their effectivity dates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-938a5862de0ab4ab87d0bfde97f7d287</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENACTMENT&quot;" target="&quot;CONSEQUENTIAL AND OTHER AMENDMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Consequential and other amendments are a result or effect of an enactment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-938a5862de0ab4ab87d0bfde97f7d287</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
