  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Securities laws often protect intellectual property rights as part of broader corporate governance and financial reporting requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f097a1fbc056ad13d4ef38369d6c79f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY RIGHTS&quot;" target="&quot;CLEARING HOUSE PARTICIPANTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clearing house participants might be involved in transactions related to intellectual property, especially if it involves complex financial instruments or derivatives."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f097a1fbc056ad13d4ef38369d6c79f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPANY ESTABLISHMENT OR DISSOLUTION&quot;" target="&quot;SECURITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Company establishment and dissolution processes can involve securities as part of the legal framework for corporate governance and financial management."</data>
