<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employees' Compensation Ordinance applies to Workplaces and outlines the procedures for reporting accidents."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employees' Compensation Ordinance governs accident notifications and reporting at Workplaces."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cbbad1d728178af8a023898a237d258a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employees' Compensation Ordinance outlines the reporting requirements to an Occupational Safety Officer for accidents at workplaces."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cbbad1d728178af8a023898a237d258a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Long service payments are payable in addition to any compensation due under the Employees' Compensation Ordinance, Cap. 282."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e9d410c88421aeae56a47aedb79d008e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;AVERAGE MONTHLY WAGES CALCULATION METHOD A, B&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The compensation ordinance provides a method for calculating average monthly wages which can be used if the standard methods are impracticable."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-dd469871354ff220088ed4c17affde45</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employees' Compensation Ordinance covers injuries or occupational diseases that may require advice from a registered medical practitioner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b89f7731524d41ce9b762132c808abd5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEES' COMPENSATION ORDINANCE (CAP. 282)&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employees' Compensation Ordinance covers injuries or occupational diseases that may require advice from a registered Chinese medicine practitioner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b89f7731524d41ce9b762132c808abd5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">21.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitration agreement involves claimants who assert their rights or interests."&lt;SEP&gt;"The CLAIMANT is a party to the arbitration agreement which may involve making claims."&lt;SEP&gt;"The claimant enters into an arbitration agreement as part of their legal proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-03ab3758cb9962eb7aad59c32353f872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af79dae94b8a0756fefbbf0f811ebd51</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">42.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL operates based on an arbitration agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL has authority to rule on disputes arising from the ARBITRATION AGREEMENT, including jurisdiction over counter-claims and set-offs as defined in Article 2(3)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL's jurisdiction is determined by the scope of the ARBITRATION AGREEMENT as outlined in Article 2(3)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ARBITRATION AGREEMENT defines the roles and powers of the ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL in resolving disputes through arbitration."&lt;SEP&gt;"The arbitration agreement defines the jurisdiction and validity for the arbitral tribunal to rule on its competence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d3dc78b87bb7d880e40b21eadb5c8441&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af79dae94b8a0756fefbbf0f811ebd51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99f980ad8d8f30c8e25f6f9fa3f01746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9669f3137e35798edd3b5969882589dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">71.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A COURT can refuse to enforce an AWARD if it is contrary to the terms set out in the ARBITRATION AGREEMENT."&lt;SEP&gt;"Courts have the authority to recognize and enforce arbitration agreements, even when issuing interim measures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Courts have the authority to refer parties to arbitration if an action is based on an existing arbitration agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT has jurisdiction over arbitration agreements and can apply UNCITRAL Model Law's provisions, including those in Article 34 for setting aside arbitral awards."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT is involved in enforcing and interpreting arbitration agreements, including those governed by UNCITRAL Model Law Article 34."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT must direct that issues are to be determined in accordance with ARBITRATION AGREEMENT if certain conditions are met."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court can refer parties to arbitration under certain conditions as per the Arbitration Agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court has jurisdiction to review and potentially set aside an arbitral award if certain conditions are met, as outlined by the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court's decision is not subject to an appeal from arbitration agreements, indicating a hierarchical relationship between them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e7564251214dafe0ef47139543601d3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6c644c4a7067336b920f4ea718d504d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b688d6d5d4487cad0a2e8714c6369fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63fa361a4bbae312d93826ee30bf2182&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-368fa7e2763a0614258f01172b9c741f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3977494e2da78f664ddb0fbbd085bf83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-211e080c19540ebafb0dc80d25b20e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d01af5189922031b9258e77aa6012d87</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OR OTHER JUDICIAL AUTHORITY &quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration agreements are enforceable through courts or other judicial authorities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0cc9146e12fcb8f714add3a3f7c0771b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An ARBITRATION AGREEMENT is described to potentially lead into an ARBITRATION PROCEDURE, which can be initiated by one of the parties involved in a dispute."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-93da520a07c3f45a47c10cf01594d640</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">40.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Article 25 of the UNCITRAL Model Law affects how arbitration agreements are given effect to in relation to unreasonable delay in pursuing claims."&lt;SEP&gt;"Article 9 of the UNCITRAL Model Law addresses the relationship between arbitration agreements and court-issued interim measures."&lt;SEP&gt;"The UNCITRAL Model Law provides rules for arbitration agreements, which are central to dispute resolution processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"UNCITRAL MODEL LAW provides a framework for arbitration agreements and includes provisions like Article 34 that are relevant when setting aside awards."&lt;SEP&gt;"UNCITRAL Model Law provides a framework for arbitration agreements and the procedures related to them, including Article 34 on setting aside awards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a6c644c4a7067336b920f4ea718d504d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-854d00c33e69aed0258675abc1e2d264&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b688d6d5d4487cad0a2e8714c6369fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-524caefeb3520a83b6c8130676f95c53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ADMIRALTY PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"In Admiralty cases, courts may conditionally refer parties to arbitration and stay legal proceedings, involving the use of an existing arbitration agreement."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e7564251214dafe0ef47139543601d3f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;CONSTRUCTION CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration agreements are included in the terms of construction contracts as per the text provided."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca57b579105e713a9a47fbe85dd981f6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration agreement leads to the initiation of arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-818682a0f1950aff44c4e7f18a331608</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;LAWSUAL LIABILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitration agreement does not exempt or limit lawful liability as defined by laws and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0aa5c7bec2bb945d36bb333255416d51</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER&quot;" target="&quot;WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A period of absence certified by a Registered Medical Practitioner is deemed total temporary incapacity, affecting wages calculation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bad177b227e380cc066abb25e6c2cf7d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">23.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A certificate from a REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER is required to support an application for review based on changes in the condition of the employee."&lt;SEP&gt;"A registered medical practitioner conducts the medical examination of an employee."&lt;SEP&gt;"An employee may receive medical treatment from a registered medical practitioner under supervision."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af55493786feba6de502e98ed832cde8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1ed02e78cf2ee9e321f22dbe3ba84b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc7d719876b6f50011d4a77def5a2428</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER&quot;" target="&quot;DIRECTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both Registered Medical Practitioners and Directors operate within the healthcare sector, with potential interactions in regulatory bodies or professional associations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2a67530e0a9df975682238097b18b864</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Registered medical practitioners can issue certificates that affect the termination conditions of a contract of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-515a3738f6ebf19e3d7fa78e01d28be6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER&quot;" target="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner may seek further medical advice if an employee's request is referred from the employer regarding fitness for work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea6b2c9739d4904eac9e0c6be6072cb9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIAL ASSESSMENT BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">30.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both Commissioner and Special Assessment Board are involved in making decisions or assessments that can be appealed to the District Court."&lt;SEP&gt;"Similar to the relationship with the Ordinary Assessment Board, the Commissioner also forwards relevant objections to the Special Assessment Board. "&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner appoints members of the Special Assessment Board and may determine its procedure."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner is involved in issuing certificates by the Special Assessment Board. "&lt;SEP&gt;"The Special Assessment Board is appointed according to the regulations set by the Commissioner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f281684938925901a68a287ea35fbc44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da37f195f3ad2a893b50923a13911e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-038abcb26f772c8f77b5ead3c3b7177c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d232c4c17f319179e61e9fe9f748ce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f5ab2145d9ab1c03798719541af19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">89.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COMMISSIONER can require an EMPLOYEE's employer to provide records of sickness days through registered post or gazette announcements, according to section 38."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COMMISSIONER has authority to authorize agreements between EMPLOYEES and employers regarding compensation for accidents caused by old age or serious physical defects."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COMMISSIONER may order deductions from compensation payable to an EMPLOYEE or a FAMILY MEMBER if certain conditions are met."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COMMISSIONER provides reports to the COURT OR LABOUR TRIBUNAL that relate to the circumstances of claims by EMPLOYEES under the Labour Tribunal Ordinance (Cap. 25)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner also forwards approved agreements to the Employee, indicating a role in their communication and record-keeping process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner can be involved in resolving disputes through section 10B of relevant ordinances."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner determines the liability and amount of medical expenses for an employee."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner determines whether there is liability for medical expenses under Section 10A, involving applications from employees."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner has the authority to approve or refuse agreements related to employees under this section."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner is responsible for determining claims related to the Employee, particularly in fatal cases and compensation matters."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner issues certificates and gives consent related to employee compensation, impacting their employment status."&lt;SEP&gt;"Through the actions of the Employer and Employee, the Commissioner makes determinations that affect them directly regarding funeral and medical attendance expenses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7788fe09e12252d0bb714e4f775b4322&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af55493786feba6de502e98ed832cde8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caf4b3f0aa7e762095c32496aac13d2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c974ea5d752dd73a9522c1e2701db94a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d19ac100c430c329d42230a7654f3c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eff0ca72356f89bbfc64201ec755179c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68ef0e8f1f38a0c8885d599e4ee4a20e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d76ba7381f3e95da332b4d2d5206d84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-236ae534fe116485f7714d0a24fe4030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1683d49752acaec3491f38a426aac742&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbcb1ef289ad456f0c48fcfc25edb43d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f729e4dc4d8c13592d31110960bc5996</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">51.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Any agreement made under this section which has been approved by the Commissioner may be made an order of the Court upon application."&lt;SEP&gt;"In certain circumstances, the COMMISSIONER's determination under section 6B(1)(a) can affect the timing of APPLICATION FOR COMPENSATION to COURT."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT has appellate jurisdiction over determinations made by the COMMISSIONER."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner must not determine claims without the employer's consent, and the Court has authority over such determinations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner's determinations on liability and amount of medical expenses are subject to review by the Court."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner, who oversees the Labour Department, may be involved in court proceedings related to workplace injuries and safety violations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court can overturn the commissioner's decisions under certain sections, indicating a supervisory relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e6087ed3d45150a001bf9f66572bde4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bca658a6c295daa0f1b015fffbbdfb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68ef0e8f1f38a0c8885d599e4ee4a20e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-932bd52b3e4a92915c346a0ad3c1fd7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-266c63bff8f647150f70f543690f359f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2e37a06f23a289862428e2457ce5863&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbcb1ef289ad456f0c48fcfc25edb43d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;" target="&quot;SECRETARY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner makes assessments and decisions, which are influenced or carried out by the Secretary as per various sections of the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-691e0bbfff602acd26ed9f7e9579a105</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;" target="&quot;16E(8) ASSESSMENT BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner oversees and manages both Ordinary and Special Assessment Boards, including their assessments under different sections."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-21097621f6720ea0958fecf07d8dcf43</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;" target="&quot;GAZETTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">40.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner can amend the amount specified in Schedule 1A by publishing a notice in the Gazette."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner can use Gazette to publish orders for amending Schedules and other regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner may amend subsections by publishing notices in the Gazette."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner publishes notices in the GAZETTE regarding the issuance, amendment, or revocation of codes of practice."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner publishes notices regarding issuance, amendment or revocation of a code of practice in the Gazette."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-db8de87b8402a32b88814909eb8b04f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b95a210c7fca53b1bea2e9c19744745&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78df2b99fcbe4aa2c71fdce1f79d338c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1833f1af069fda07edd900b2ad5d51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbbb4670a77162b48a5d0767257af240</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">54.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational Safety Officers conduct informal inquiries into workplace accidents and report findings back to the Commissioner."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COMMISSIONER is responsible for issuing certificates of authority to OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICERS, except for himself and HEALTH OFFICERS."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner appoints and designates Occupational Safety Officers under Section 19 of the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (Cap. 59). "&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner can apply for a Magistrate's authorization, allowing an Occupational Safety Officer to enter premises with required force under specific circumstances."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner designates Occupational Safety Officers to conduct inquiries into workplace accidents and dangerous occurrences."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner issues certificates of authority to Occupational Safety Officers and can exercise functions related to them."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Occupational Safety Officer reports findings to the Commissioner in writing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a3c3394a6b72977677a8a437b4151b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05288c51fb6c9855d3f031e51b7e2be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea83763b873f6b32742c132cbac8d568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7f5c7774940469ec261850f6dbd6b83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3282c20ec28d4bb14aec7fe4e4eafbe8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19f640b139895da0133f304114aeb8fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc560479538470069d89f317f702e111</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers are authorized by the Commissioner to request information from employment agencies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public officers are designated by the Commissioner to exercise certain powers under this Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner authorizes public officers in writing to perform certain duties under this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bba134fe326f216878a32b9c716807cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fd592d376d0854e1e9f902478b9ced3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-057cc616cb8b855799f3fcacf937e222</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner specifies the format for certificates issued by medical practitioners which influence contract termination conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-515a3738f6ebf19e3d7fa78e01d28be6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner can influence whether employees are entitled to severance payments through agreements and extensions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4803dc099d05bf6f05b27d07f8429783</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSIONER&quot;" target="&quot;RELEVANT EMPLOYER, PERSONAL REPRESENTATIVE OF THE EMPLOYEE, APPLICATION IN THE FORM SPECIFIED BY THE COMMISSIONER UNDER SECTION 49&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner specifies the form for applications and can extend application periods."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a881a0688f9274757e29bce4fcc07e0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;" target="&quot;RESPONDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">80.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Although not directly involved in arbitration procedures, CLAIMANT and RESPONDENT are parties in disputes that could lead to ADJUDICATOR's resignation affecting their case outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both CLAIMANT and RESPONDENT are parties involved in a dispute resolution procedure, with the former initiating proceedings against the latter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both CLAIMANT and RESPONDENT can agree on the termination of arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both parties are involved in the payment dispute which can lead to Adjudicator's Determinations, and if a settlement is reached between them (h), it could terminate further adjudication proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The CLAIMANT and RESPONDENT are parties involved in the dispute, each required to state their defense or claim against the other."&lt;SEP&gt;"The CLAIMANT initiates adjudication proceedings for a payment dispute against the RESPONDENT."&lt;SEP&gt;"The CLAIMANT must send a written submission to the RESPONDENT as part of the process for responding to an ADJUDICATION RESPONSE."&lt;SEP&gt;"The claimant may delay carrying out the construction work if the respondent fails to pay the adjudicated amount by the payment deadline."&lt;SEP&gt;"The claimant may initiate adjudication proceedings for a payment dispute against the respondent."&lt;SEP&gt;"The claimant may send a written notice of withdrawal to the respondent, indicating their intention to terminate adjudication proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The respondent is often in opposition to the claimant in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ccfc28d1a77070797c9452e760bfd7f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ad6aa79a150340c8a28d98a0e6b1a24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-145b271e55786ea72d8690e6e1f2ebf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1611b0ccefada6387970ed4d17809f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08d5d6b1196500a57db7811d96c91750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ddfde50b478473b5624659f6cfdd546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d229505b95cc3e576d9ad034318c66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5943028cc6f3beb70826c83454e86767&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71987cb00c98805ab9ed06eb948af233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b219a4ff887909dc5fdeb24191ca220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d296364c6fb1e176227c199c33f148d6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A CLAIMANT is involved in the process of arbitration as a party making claims."&lt;SEP&gt;"Claimant is a party who makes claims or counter-claims in an arbitration process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af79dae94b8a0756fefbbf0f811ebd51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66f02a8d98963433692f49f5ef863386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The parties include the claimant in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL has powers to order CLAIMANT to provide security for arbitration costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The claimant must state facts and relief to the arbitral tribunal, which decides on the course of proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6127a28d22b5d9d9145842f6c4caba9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The claimant's statements and claims are part of the arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CLAIMANT interacts with the ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL by submitting claims and statements within agreed timeframes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The arbitration tribunal can issue orders related to the claimant, such as requiring them to provide security."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ccfc28d1a77070797c9452e760bfd7f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d99713e2d7a58da6c720456f882ba7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">18.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CLAIMANT initiates adjudication proceedings related to a PAYMENT DISpute against the RESPONDENT."&lt;SEP&gt;"The claimant initiates adjudication proceedings to resolve a payment dispute with the respondent."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c1611b0ccefada6387970ed4d17809f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b219a4ff887909dc5fdeb24191ca220</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;" target="&quot;ADJUDICATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">41.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If an adjudicator has been appointed, the claimant must notify them as well when withdrawing from adjudication proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ADJUDICATOR may receive a SET ASIDE APPLICATION from the CLAIMANT regarding previous determinations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ADJUDICATOR receives the CLAIMANT's submission and must be impartial in adjudication proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ADJUDICATOR will receive submissions from both CLAIMANT and RESPONDENT, who are involved in an adjudication process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The CLAIMANT sends a written submission to the ADJUDICATOR in response to the ADJUDICATION RESPONSE."&lt;SEP&gt;"While not directly mentioned, CLAIMANT interacts with ADJUDICATOR through the nomination process and can request withdrawal of arbitration procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b53857aed1787aca531dea0f456e8ca5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c72baaf42bcfd44fb0bf40d018847b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-145b271e55786ea72d8690e6e1f2ebf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ddfde50b478473b5624659f6cfdd546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71987cb00c98805ab9ed06eb948af233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47220fb088d5ae56db9b03a4c12e8f14</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIMANT&quot;" target="&quot;CONSTRUCTION CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CLAIMANT is involved in construction contracts whose works or related goods and services are valued by adjudicators."&lt;SEP&gt;"The claimant's rights to delay work are based on conditions set out in a construction contract, which includes obligations of both parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2c72baaf42bcfd44fb0bf40d018847b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d229505b95cc3e576d9ad034318c66d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTION WORK&quot;" target="&quot;BUILDING OR ENGINEERING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Construction work refers to the construction, establishment, installation, reconstruction, repair, maintenance (including re-decorating and external cleaning) of structures or works as specified in Schedule 5."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2fae8b17287c09754a8180334dba81fa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTION WORK&quot;" target="&quot;SUPPLIED GOODS AND SERVICES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Construction work and the supply of related goods and services are both factors in determining progress payment claims."::</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e6daadd1f16d5e396cd12e56c0d0df02</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTION WORK&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Construction work can lead to a payment dispute due to delays or disruptions affecting expenditure or loss incurred by parties involved in the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f04c9983bdf92638bbe090b65a4a327a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similar to the Registered Medical Practitioner, a period of absence certified by a Registered Chinese Medicine Practitioner affects wages calculation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bad177b227e380cc066abb25e6c2cf7d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIAL ASSESSMENT BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Special Assessment Board's certification impacts wages similarly to other medical practitioners and boards."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bad177b227e380cc066abb25e6c2cf7d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">29.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYEE receives WAGES from either the PRINCIPAL CONTRACTOR or SUPERIOR SUB-CONTRACTOR, depending on the contractual arrangement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EMPLOYEE is entitled to WAGES as per their employment contract, and these are subject to legal provisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wages are a term in the employment contract directly affecting the employee's financial well-being."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wages include various types of payments made to employees, such as those for leave days and sick days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-14526d01cdd531d1142f16c1d5e43367&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1093ec98fdeda43f43128129d5d24cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602a52838c03cef3777006bf2a44b72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bfdf4a9968aec09594f73a07cdf18d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYED PERSON&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Wages include payments made by the employer for various types of leave taken by an employed person, such as sick leave and maternity leave."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d93d92eb00cb1e06709b542dad7efdd1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES&quot;" target="&quot;僱主&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Wages refer to payments made by employers (僱主) to employees (僱員)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7243d6ae166cfdb764a13e61a193cccf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES&quot;" target="&quot;僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Wages are the income received by employees (僱員) from their employers."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7243d6ae166cfdb764a13e61a193cccf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES&quot;" target="&quot;《僱員補償條例》(第282章)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employment Ordinance (Cap. 282) provides compensation related to certain wage-related issues, such as temporary incapacity for work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7243d6ae166cfdb764a13e61a193cccf</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAGES&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court can order an employer who is found guilty to pay wages that are due, even if they were acquitted based on certain grounds."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-07f949d11fd1c1d8a909fd36ccac57d6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;TOTAL INCAPACITY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Total incapacity refers to any temporary or permanent condition that prevents an employee from working at their previous capacity after an accident."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-786e383c94a3c844d81a1afb79da985c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">42.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"COURT can award terminal payments directly to the EMPLOYEE."&lt;SEP&gt;"If there's a failure in undergoing an examination or treatment, the court will make a determination based on the circumstances."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT can also make an order for REINSTATEMENT ORDER or ORDER FOR RE-ENGAGEMENT in cases involving the EMPLOYEE and the EMPLOYER."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Court has the authority to decide how an Employee's compensation should be paid, invested, or applied for his benefit."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EMPLOYEE may bring a claim for MEDICAL EXPENSES directly to the COURT if compensation is not paid by the employer within 7 days."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court can be involved in cases where an employee dies due to an accident, determining compensation claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02219b95b2d6273001fc2088c7c1d25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f5fe723dc66b1a35b256f0fbcfd9642&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3060c6c2405e1ec77fec151e62494218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f17d41b36a40e80f45f0f635b4ad7eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92743ab978843e283d6914a0d34ee3ea</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">26.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A registered Chinese medicine practitioner can also conduct a medical examination if named by the employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"An employee may also receive medical treatment from a registered Chinese medicine practitioner under supervision."&lt;SEP&gt;"Similar to REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER, a certificate from a REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER is also required for an application based on changes in the employee's condition."&lt;SEP&gt;"The EMPLOYEE has the right to undergo medical examinations with a REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER, but they are responsible for the costs. If necessary, the employer can require treatment from such practitioner without cost to the employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bc7d719876b6f50011d4a77def5a2428&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af55493786feba6de502e98ed832cde8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c1ed02e78cf2ee9e321f22dbe3ba84b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1faa1664ffe65d577dff74396c2e0ae</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;COMPENSATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">32.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYEE can recover COMPENSATION under this Part if they are incapacitated due to occupational disease during employment."&lt;SEP&gt;"An employee can recover compensation under this Ordinance either from a sub-contractor or directly from the principal contractor, depending on their preference and circumstances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employees may be entitled to receive compensation from their employer if they suffer a loss of work capacity or die due to an occupational disease related to their employment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The outcome of the medical examination can affect whether COMPENSATION is payable, depending on the findings and the employee's attendance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-be12459eb42b5303144e2a38dc8cf0c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8bab0fa8e650dc6d58da85c05c8bf94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-338f6b52974bc08baebc662da42c4477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2852e178b14d2f1e89cf137922f29e35</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;AMENDED 44 OF 1980 S. 15; 16 OF 2006 S. 2006 S. 16&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The amendment provides specific provisions for compensation in relation to the employee's failure or disregard of instructions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3060c6c2405e1ec77fec151e62494218</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIAL ASSESSMENT BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">11.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Special Assessment Board also issues certificates to employees concerning compensation, similar to the Ordinary Assessment Board."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Special Assessment Board issues a certificate to the employee after reviewing claims. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da37f195f3ad2a893b50923a13911e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7788fe09e12252d0bb714e4f775b4322</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER'">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer is responsible for any injury sustained by the employee during employment, which could lead to liability for medical treatments including prostheses or surgical appliances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-194bd276c174598edc7fcf0c6886ead7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational Safety Officers are involved in handling notifications and reports related to Employee accidents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Occupational Safety Officers are responsible for receiving reports from employers regarding employees who have suffered serious bodily injury or lost work capacity due to workplace accidents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd461abafa09b711df723a9e8d6a7aab</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">24.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Accidents occurring at the Workplace can affect Employees, leading to notification requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employees work in and depend on the workplace's safety measures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employees work in the workplace and are protected by safety provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e7881ceecf94346279b299fee8d79193&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;DIRECTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Directors oversee and make decisions regarding the employment of employees within a business context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2a67530e0a9df975682238097b18b864</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">40.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT defines the agreement between an employer and employee, establishing their roles in each other's relationship."&lt;SEP&gt;"An employee's contract of employment can be extended or renewed by a personal representative following the death of the deceased employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The contract is central to defining the relationship between an employee and their employer under Hong Kong law."&lt;SEP&gt;"The contract of employment defines an employee's rights, including their right to annual leave."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employee is employed through an employment contract established by the employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-786c67dfb1439b58fce397c3168c9e29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a79efc9c7d5b3c5051c209e7d8238e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed2004c9e59e7e54ef6756f3c59d039a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a783557f86fea333101af802aa41e0a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED NON-EXEMPT ORS BENEFIT (僱主供款非豁免職業退休計劃利益)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYER-funded NON-EXEMPT ORS benefit is a type of employer-provided retirement plan benefit that does not qualify for exemption."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER-FUNDED (SPECIFIED) ORS BENEFIT (僱主供款(指明)職業退休計劃利益)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An EMPLOYER-funded SPECIFIED ORS benefit is a specific type of employer-provided retirement plan benefit."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8d91c94560328ac7dea66d76304a618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees are entitled to maternity leave, and its payment calculation depends on their earnings before transferring from heavy, hazardous or harmful work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ea6b2c9739d4904eac9e0c6be6072cb9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">22.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employee is not entitled to severance payment unless they leave before the expiration of notice given by their employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employees may potentially receive severance payments based on certain conditions and filings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employee is entitled to receive severance payment as per legal obligations and can seek clarification or dispute it through proper channels like MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD or Labour Tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a40a9600dcdabbcf7b1de20226238a1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4803dc099d05bf6f05b27d07f8429783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d94d21b562915559fff6272dbbdb3b70</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">32.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An eligible employee may be entitled to a long service payment if certain conditions are met, including continuous employment year number and medical examination results."&lt;SEP&gt;"An employee may be entitled to a long service payment upon certain conditions being met, such as length of employment and relationship status with the employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employee is entitled to a long service payment based on their length of service."&lt;SEP&gt;"The term 'long service payment' is related to the rights and entitlements of an employee, specifically in cases involving termination or dismissal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-27ca5e1e28067ca3c2334e15e6221974&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9d410c88421aeae56a47aedb79d008e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdbd130fa51f2bbf4428aee9c45795cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc7d719876b6f50011d4a77def5a2428</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;OWNERSHIP CHANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees are affected by changes in business ownership regarding their contracts and potential terminations or continuance of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0276e1b514303ef83e330aacbd8bcf95</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employee is entitled to annual leave after a continuous contract for at least 12 months."&lt;SEP&gt;"Employee is entitled to receive ANNUAL LEAVE as part of their employment benefits."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e1ba134cba7bc0ad2b2ef34e757e78d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74bf264f43f2a8be1c1c6d9a90273b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER WHO IS A SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The employer, being a sub-contractor, may fail to pay wages due to employees as specified in sections 23, 24 or 25. If this happens, the employer must supply information within 7 days of receiving a written request from an employee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-05508a87b3ed23ef299b7e04a0fe44c9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL, MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employees have rights to recover wages from employers through the Labour Tribunal or Minor Employment Claims Adjudication Board as stated in section 43M. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-93a1fe97f228ec755ced3c31d6506c86</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A PUBLIC OFFICER can request information from an EMPLOYEE during inquiries, which may be relevant for the enforcement of ORDINANCE or handling ACCIDENTS and STATUTORY DUTIES."&lt;SEP&gt;"A public officer investigates accidents involving employees during their employment, which relates to statutory duties and safety regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5742863cc938d9f9470985855601b925&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e37def8625e820a47ed5130364eb70d4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYEE&quot;" target="&quot;PRE-PRIVATIZATION SERVICE YEARS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The pre-privatization service years are relevant to the employee's long-term service fund amount, impacting their payment calculation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9661724896688b8cd0643c1a0b2fa146</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL SAFETY OFFICER&quot;" target="&quot;WORKPLACE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">38.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An Occupational Safety Officer has responsibilities related to ensuring safety in the Workplace."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Occupational Safety Officer may enter and inspect premises if they believe on reasonable grounds that the premises are being used as a workplace or where there is a contravention of this Ordinance, directly related to the concept of a Workplace."&lt;SEP&gt;"Occupational safety measures are relevant to activities conducted in the Workplace."&lt;SEP&gt;"Occupational safety officers are involved in workplace inspections and oversight."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Occupational Safety Officer is notified by the person responsible for the workplace regarding accidents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-58cf55b6baed9ac9a3c4052538486aa3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e245666877c34f0ac196d032b544a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3282c20ec28d4bb14aec7fe4e4eafbe8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe4c625e0d88b6c7ccc901d0d7b85932&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7881ceecf94346279b299fee8d79193</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPENSATION&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIAL ASSESSMENT BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Special Assessment Board deals with compensation matters as defined in the text, particularly related to employee compensation for special assessments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f281684938925901a68a287ea35fbc44</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPENSATION&quot;" target="&quot;CERTIFICATE ISSUED UNDER SECTION 6C(1)(B)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The certificate may be related to compensation as it is part of a legal framework that includes various forms of compensation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-124c51d196f065db08f6504baeaa703c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPENSATION&quot;" target="&quot;FUNERAL AND MEDICAL ATTENDANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Compensation includes expenses of the funeral and medical attendance, which are specific types of compensation under section 6(5)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-124c51d196f065db08f6504baeaa703c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPENSATION&quot;" target="&quot;46. 補償不能予以轉讓、押記或扣押&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 46 explicitly states that compensation cannot be transferred, charged or attached under the ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-679d548673cb77dcfe447573286cf62e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPENSATION&quot;" target="&quot;47. 從收入&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 47 provides additional context on handling income related to compensation, indicating its ongoing relevance and application."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-679d548673cb77dcfe447573286cf62e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maternity leave is granted in addition to the annual leave a female employee is entitled under this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bef47a255f1eda2d15380bce3341cd94</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUTHORITY&quot;" target="&quot;PERSON WHO USES OR CAUSES TO BE USED ANY PRODUCT PRESCRIBED FOR THE PURPOSES OF THIS PART&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Authority has the power to direct the use of prescribed products by any person who uses them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5cbc913a82bac150b6a4b08953fa04d2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUTHORITY&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers can be subject to reports from the Authority if they make noise in violation of certain sections, and must comply with any notices given by the Authority."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3ae14afda9d52be1864e9090474b79d7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Severance payment is a form of compensation provided according to the terms of the contract of employment upon termination of service."&lt;SEP&gt;"The continuity and severance payment provisions in a contract of employment are interrelated, with layoff affecting both aspects."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-28b2163160f25fa57988c0b4d0c740cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8e2655c247e96affa05132d650c897b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;$22,500'">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"$22,500 is a key component in calculating the SEVERANCE PAYMENT under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f00bfbc74cd988e98040394204cccd2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;MINOR EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS ADJUDICATION BOARD REGISTRAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Minor Employment Claims Adjudication Board handles claims related to SEVERANCE PAYMENTS through its processes and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4803dc099d05bf6f05b27d07f8429783</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;LABOUR TRIBUNAL REGISTRAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Labour Tribunal also deals with issues of SEVERANCE PAYMENTS, providing another avenue for dispute resolution."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4803dc099d05bf6f05b27d07f8429783</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEVERANCE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"COURT can award SEVERANCE PAYMENT as a form of terminal payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a47dd87b7de189aa048a8aef9b8e4899</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;DEATH OF EMPLOYEE (5+ CONTINUOUS YEARS)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"In cases where an employee has worked continuously for at least 5 years and dies, the employer may be required to pay a long service payment based on certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-bc7d719876b6f50011d4a77def5a2428</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LONG SERVICE PAYMENTS are based on the operation of the CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT and the length of service specified within it."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b66ec28db0dbcb16e24e4d4df0ef35a2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER SUPPLIED (BASIC PORTION) EXEMPT ORS BENEFITS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer-supplied basic portion exempt ORS benefits are qualifying items that can reduce long service payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-233de206d4d440690ca3d19bf8ddb77c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LONG SERVICE PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER SUPPLIED (MANDATORY) MPFS BENEFITS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer-supplied mandatory MPFS benefits are also qualifying items for reducing the long service payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-233de206d4d440690ca3d19bf8ddb77c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;PARTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">39.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties have freedom in determining the number of arbitrators, and the Arbitration Tribunal is formed based on this agreement or default rules if no agreement exists."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Parties can request the Arbitration Tribunal for corrections or interpretations, and the tribunal may extend these periods if necessary."&lt;SEP&gt;"The arbitration tribunal may appoint experts to report on specific issues and can request parties for relevant information, indicating a relationship with the parties involved."&lt;SEP&gt;"The parties have the freedom to agree on a procedure for challenging an arbitrator, and can request the tribunal's decision or seek court intervention if their challenge is not successful."&lt;SEP&gt;"The parties' choices and authorizations are key factors in how the arbitration tribunal decides disputes under Article 28 of UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3161c0abf732689fd0fb63c291711d64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d17ccb7c45bbf013a4a9b072f210aedd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4373f38dac5749d35f8ccd70b8bf1d15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edc4c9a782cb874c7fb36432df37d995&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7effd30746ff087ba04389bfb24de4c9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">76.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL's decision may be reconsidered by the COURT, and the COURT has authority over it."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Arbitration Tribunal can request the Court to rule on a challenge, and during this period, the Court may refuse to grant enforcement of any decision made by the tribunal including the challenged arbitrator."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT has jurisdiction to hear appeals against ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL awards on questions of law."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT has special powers to make orders related to arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT has the authority to remit matters back to the ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL for reconsideration."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT has the power to appoint an ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL for certain arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Court has jurisdiction to order an arbitration tribunal to deliver its award if full payment is not made, and can determine fees and expenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"The arbitral tribunal can defer a jurisdiction objection if there's a valid reason, and either party may request the court to decide on this matter within 30 days without appeal during that period."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court has the authority to recognize or enforce an arbitration award, and can also delay a decision if necessary."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court's rules and procedures apply to certain aspects of arbitration proceedings, particularly regarding evidence and procedural matters."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ff2369343594485564382d2d30ba3755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19092b2cdc4468b2128aef41dc2b2b67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6793dcafea3acbec1f8e9bd2a51472c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62de924c3226ea55de4d94d980a6b34f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d99713e2d7a58da6c720456f882ba7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aba64861ea22070188d9b7dd4c0fd47a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3906bbf7ee03793cf876d19cdfab509&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698354d68541c6722cada50bb05de978&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540da5689ed24920444d2c678531763</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law provides rules and articles that govern the arbitration tribunal's operations, including their place of meeting."&lt;SEP&gt;"The UNCITRAL Model Law provides the legal framework for the arbitration tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-41866adeb2fde4b45314b888066fc6da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7aaf6f770f217f1e2eb977b5ec34ad19</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;RESPONDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The RESPONDENT also engages with the ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL through their defense submissions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ccfc28d1a77070797c9452e760bfd7f2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRATION PROCEDURE involves the operation of an ARBITRATION TRIBUNAL, which makes decisions subject to potential review by the COURT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8d82bf83563624acdc014bb3783db688</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE&quot;" target="&quot;14 DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employee must be given at least 14 days' notice for annual leave, unless otherwise agreed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e1ba134cba7bc0ad2b2ef34e757e78d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTIES&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL MODEL LAW provides a framework for PARTIES to agree on arbitration procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"The UNCITRAL Model Law outlines procedures that Parties may agree upon to select arbitrators and resolve disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e8dac8ba7cc8864d7ff7dc57b5b28604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad8b00bb4712fdfd27d215a729380d5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTIES&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties are involved in arbitration proceedings, including the appointment of arbitrators and resolution of disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parties have the freedom to agree on the functions of an umpire and how it interacts with arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-95a4de41db58b9a101c75606869df8f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-953aa58f588dab7be8bda910f0f31c38</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTIES&quot;" target="&quot;RESPONDENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The parties also include the respondent in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTIES&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">50.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL handles disputes between PARTIES during arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL makes decisions involving the PARTIES, including when and how hearings are held."&lt;SEP&gt;"The PARTIES are jointly and severally liable to pay reasonable fees and expenses of the ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL as per subsection (1)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The arbitral tribunal gives notice to all parties and provides opportunities for them to present their cases regarding preliminary orders and interim measures."&lt;SEP&gt;"The arbitral tribunal may appoint experts and assessors with the agreement of the parties or on its own initiative to assist in determining specific issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"The arbitral tribunal shall apply the law determined by the conflict of laws rules which it considers applicable, failing any designation by the parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34872d5563389492bd86e96a7e9d819c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341dbfe6e21afa768ee74c7e3db0be67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03bb9907c4707aee4e32c05a81efe12a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a8aef97985d67c64a247cd4ac0838cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8edbd1c4d3b35d7faddb32b978e73e29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39b02ac25884a8c6102243f2b93f0c03</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTIES&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties can apply for or agree on directions regarding the arbitration procedure and its associated costs."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5578519b1f9afcce44c23c12fe6ac94b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTIES&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">21.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT can hear APPLICATION FOR APPEAL from PARTIES regarding AWARDS or SERIOUS IRREGULARITY issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Court can extend the time limit for making an award upon application from any party, affecting all involved parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"The PARTIES agree on procedures for arbitration, but the COURT can override these agreements in cases of fraud or public policy violations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5a62633bac9b2c0c6ed1e0aa83ce66e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e5ed4af08fa3d54713649e0adf6d0ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b2fac04904854d200ea9c9161cb98c1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTIES&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">27.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Parties can commence or continue arbitral proceedings even when an action is brought to court, and awards may be made during this period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parties participate in arbitration proceedings where settlements and awards are made."&lt;SEP&gt;"The parties initiate arbitration proceedings by submitting a request for dispute referral."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61ef9a8b87aa1cf04b46aaf871b5f39a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03bb9907c4707aee4e32c05a81efe12a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf8d77c0073f8253192bb2eb6ce56e99</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PARTIES&quot;" target="&quot;ADJUDICATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ADJUDICATOR has the authority to request or allow PARTIES to submit further written submissions and produce documents or evidence as required."&lt;SEP&gt;"The adjudicator determines the costs proportions that each party must pay for the adjudication proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d879d95be32b955d798da85e699506e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c56a21239b5d0bf5cb22840251170eef</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECRETARY&quot;" target="&quot;DIRECTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"All three are officers who may be held guilty for the offenses committed by their body corporate or firm."&lt;SEP&gt;"The SECRETARY's role involves commissioning a committee named '義製人體器官及外科器具委員會', which may be related to actions taken by the DIRECTOR in legal proceedings against the INSURER, though no direct relationship is explicitly stated between them."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8df740cc032fb332ff71c24c0e55c9c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c560e10db0daa7f51fa59f7a6b462aa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECRETARY&quot;" target="&quot;GAZETTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Secretary can publish notices in the Gazette to establish designated areas."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-86dd5816dd56bd7bc4f23ec93e31f0f2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECRETARY&quot;" target="&quot;CONSTRUCTION CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Secretary has authority over the issuance and enforcement related to Construction Contracts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-622e9afcf96894f3c8695345444428d3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SECRETARY&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Neither the Secretary nor public officers are civilly liable for their actions performed in good faith under this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1901c04f5d127d84848a2cd1cbc4a1bd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;工資&quot;" target="&quot;代通知金終止合約的情況&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"工資包括在特定情況下支付給員工的款項，如產假、侍產假等。這些款項可能與代通知金相關联。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1788711a60d2941c6ebfead19aecb5ee</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;工資&quot;" target="&quot;僱員放取的產假、侍產假、休息日、病假日、假日或年假&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"這些假期屬於工資的一部分，因此與工資有直接關係。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1788711a60d2941c6ebfead19aecb5ee</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;工資&quot;" target="&quot;計算&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"工資的數額在特定情況下不予計算,例如正常工作日所賺取的部分或通知日期前12個月內其他人的收入。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-23f4f40202843bfce44e444942fa422e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;工資&quot;" target="&quot;MATERNITY LEAVE, A DAY OF PATERNITY LEAVE, A REST DAY, A SICKNESS DAY, A HOLIDAY OR A DAY OF ANNUAL LEAVE TAKEN BY THE EMPLOYEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"工資包括因员工休产假、陪产假等所获得的补偿天数。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8625c1304f36a12d07cc0b6f8faf08b2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;工資&quot;" target="&quot;《僱員補償條例》(第282章)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据该条例，雇主需为员工提供产假薪酬等福利。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9cbd74be84a690a6e54b01cd6e7752ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;工資&quot;" target="&quot;僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"雇员有权获得相应的工资，特别是在涉及年假薪酬的情况下。"&lt;SEP&gt;僱員根據《僱員補償條例》(第282章)可能獲得補償，而不獲付給工資或全部工資的期間。</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c14678de8548f803294fa05856c13dfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-285c049da04e797b33870a3a643d86c9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RESPONDENT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The respondent states his defense in respect of the claims made by the claimant to the arbitral tribunal."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RESPONDENT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The respondent’s defense is also a component of the arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e802264259e33579dca823a3e718f95b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RESPONDENT&quot;" target="&quot;ADJUDICATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">43.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ADJUDICATOR also interacts with the RESPONDENT, maintaining independence and impartiality throughout the process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ADJUDICATOR may also receive a SET ASIDE APPLICATION from the RESPONDENT regarding previous determinations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ADJUDICATOR will also receive responses from the RESPONDENT regarding the claims made by the CLAIMANT."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ADJUDICATOR's power is not affected by the failure of the RESPONDENT to serve an adjudication response under section 31."&lt;SEP&gt;"The RESPONDENT is addressed by the ADJUDICATION NOTIFICATION and becomes part of the adjudication proceedings initiated by the A CLAIMING PARTY."&lt;SEP&gt;"The RESPONDENT is involved in disputes that may lead to a conflict of interest for the ADJUDICATOR, necessitating a resignation notice being sent to both parties and the NOMINATION BODY."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b53857aed1787aca531dea0f456e8ca5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c72baaf42bcfd44fb0bf40d018847b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-145b271e55786ea72d8690e6e1f2ebf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c86684c7c7960eab0e6a0b609bc00e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47220fb088d5ae56db9b03a4c12e8f14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4a8b59b4e3e2ba05d0864cc47510c7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RESPONDENT&quot;" target="&quot;CONSTRUCTION CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The RESPONDENT, like the CLAIMANT, may be a party to construction contracts with valuation issues determined by ADJUDICATORS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-2c72baaf42bcfd44fb0bf40d018847b9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ADJUDICATOR&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">67.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Adjudicators are involved in determining payment disputes and have immunity from being compelled to give evidence related to such disputes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adjudicators are responsible for resolving payment disputes within the framework of adjudication proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"An ADJUDICATOR is involved in resolving PAYMENT DISPUTES, which can create conflicts of interest."&lt;SEP&gt;"An adjudicator determines a payment dispute and has powers related to it."&lt;SEP&gt;"An adjudicator is appointed to resolve a payment dispute as per the nominating body's rules."&lt;SEP&gt;"An adjudicator is appointed to resolve the payment dispute between parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ADJUDICATOR is involved in resolving PAYMENT DISPUTES."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ADJUDICATOR is responsible for determining PAYMENT DISPUTES according to specific procedures and timelines."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-40b68681ecca6bd68067e789107e9bdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4537b3223942fe128431f147e0b27414&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4f0cfcab0e9f6d5a958dc7286fe8aad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8719074a70eff81632691da24dedfc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-304365a41d317ba2bf7cdd71b9dcffa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-169c5c3921ad759a4d5a8b8e69511b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-336d2be2a1671f4a9c20d61c824c7555&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1901c04f5d127d84848a2cd1cbc4a1bd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ADJUDICATOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARBITRATION PROCEDURE involves decisions made by the ADJUDICATOR who may need to resign based on conflicts of interest or doubts about independence/impartiality, impacting the procedure's continuation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-145b271e55786ea72d8690e6e1f2ebf4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ADJUDICATOR&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">22.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT has the authority to make determinations and can set aside a determination if certain conditions are met."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT has the authority to set aside a determination made by the ADJUDICATOR under section 48."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Court can set aside a determination under section 48, affecting the payment and fees of the ADJUDICATOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e089cfc832db9c43bb24baa7baf3ed42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-143b0fa3beba6c5913ea9659f090c4b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c883642e952f5d5b217f2a11baae78f8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">25.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law provides guidelines for arbitration proceedings, ensuring fairness and efficiency."&lt;SEP&gt;"UNCITRAL MODEL LAW provides rules for arbitration proceedings, including how evidence should be handled during such procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"UNCITRAL Model Law provides the legal framework for arbitration proceedings, including procedures for challenging arbitrators."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ddfbb014f2dc6afae82d7bc623722b27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ca78018d1b3e2ef66e8091b3209bc2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afb67efa17f13209eb7c5173e786360c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;RECOVERABLE COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration proceedings can involve limiting or specifying recoverable costs based on certain conditions and timelines."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5578519b1f9afcce44c23c12fe6ac94b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT has jurisdiction over ARBITRATION PROCEEDINGS and can order their consolidation or hearing sequence."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ee3bd35452fe0a7b5e9fa7dc2c1f8074</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIRECTOR&quot;" target="&quot;COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Director can apply to the Court for enforcing his claim regarding costs or determining disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1e6419607ae811f4fc50b4b883814d09</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIRECTOR&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A director can enter into a contract of employment, establishing an individual relationship between these terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fee7842314099c25edf5106ebd221850</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIRECTOR&quot;" target="&quot;GAZETTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Director publishes notices regarding recognition and withdrawal of schemes in the Gazette."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4af496fc2b1c26e3d6bca76a4b99c25f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIAL ASSESSMENT BOARD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Similar to the relationship with the Ordinary Assessment Board, a Special Assessment Board may be substituted by the Court."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-cb0545d506978169e320db3a0cda4273</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers are subject to court orders regarding the disclosure of sensitive information related to complaints."&lt;SEP&gt;"Public officers can be ordered by a court or authorized person in connection with the hearing of matters related to this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-029d1e15c5db53ebcfd1168d7ac7bbab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da2837c3b5e351b2e1c63635e1c0a663</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATION SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupational safety officers can be involved in matters that may require court intervention or orders related to the Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da2837c3b5e351b2e1c63635e1c0a663</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">23.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT can apply Article 34 of UNCITRAL Model Law for setting aside an arbitral award."&lt;SEP&gt;"The UNCITRAL Model Law provides the legal framework for courts to take temporary measures in arbitration proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The court's procedures are governed by the UNCITRAL Model Law, particularly Article 8."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a6c644c4a7067336b920f4ea718d504d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b688d6d5d4487cad0a2e8714c6369fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-524caefeb3520a83b6c8130676f95c53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW ARTICLE 18&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The concept of court procedures in UNCITRAL Model Law Article 18 aligns with the court's decision-making process as described by Section 35(1)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-964639856a5f7a7d5119569944195b09</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 60&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Section 60 orders are excluded from the scope of court decisions under Section 35(1). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-964639856a5f7a7d5119569944195b09</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">98.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An arbitral tribunal may seek assistance from the COURT if no existing arbitral tribunal is capable of exercising certain powers, as stated in section 7."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL can request the COURT to make an additional award if a party requests within 30 days of receiving the award, and the court may invalidate the arbitration award under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL operates independently from the COURT, as it does not follow the court's fee scales."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL operates under the supervision and certain limitations set by the COURT."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL's orders or directions are enforceable in the same manner as those of the COURT with leave, and the COURT can enter judgment on such orders or directions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT has authority over the ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL regarding award reasons and costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT has authority to oversee and potentially set aside decisions made by the ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL if serious irregularities are found."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT has the authority to decide preliminary questions of law that arise in arbitral proceedings involving ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL."&lt;SEP&gt;"The COURT has the authority to invalidate arbitration awards under certain conditions as outlined in ARTICLE 7.01-69, which refers to section 69 for further details."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Court has jurisdiction over the arbitral tribunal and can make decisions regarding appeals against arbitration awards."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Court has power over the ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL, including revocation of decisions and remanding for reconsideration."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Court has the authority to evaluate costs that are ordered by the Arbitral Tribunal under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The arbitral tribunal's decisions can be appealed to the Court, and its leave must be obtained for such appeals."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5a62633bac9b2c0c6ed1e0aa83ce66e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5490186775273077486362a56a5b981f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae42208132627b8d5ff98d4e7966f28e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e17ae2e1dd0c38e2c8a34618b769e578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b29a301d74270bec02c5b77671a3c5a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76cb33f1b7685e188783adaf8e60f8f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8edbd1c4d3b35d7faddb32b978e73e29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2da7991e9473f6c5aadfd4a87f21c511&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b2fac04904854d200ea9c9161cb98c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9174a61c7bf0b325fa1fb34e7b741c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9669f3137e35798edd3b5969882589dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The court has the power to set aside arbitration awards under certain conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-59c7140869534366dd7270de77711ef8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COURT has the authority to review and potentially challenge decisions made through ARBITRATION PROCEDURE based on SERIOUS IMPROPRIETY EVENT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8d82bf83563624acdc014bb3783db688</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COURT&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A PAYMENT DISPUTE can be resolved through written agreement between the PARTIES or by the COURT in other dispute resolution procedures."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b49150680872ebc6da3ccdee23b5d249</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION PROCEDURE&quot;" target="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitration procedure is established by the UNCITRAL Model Law, providing a framework for resolving IPR disputes through arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-39620e4541eb49ae7a7ea14a2cf664bb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot; COURT &quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law defines the functions of the court that are to be performed by the Court."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-20600c9214528cc8c5fe5923e8a061ca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The UNCITRAL Model Law includes provisions related to arbitration, including Article 8 which governs how courts should handle such matters."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-524caefeb3520a83b6c8130676f95c53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">47.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitral Tribunals have powers to request court assistance for evidence under certain conditions, similar but not identical to those in Article 27 of the UNCITRAL Model Law."&lt;SEP&gt;"The UNCITRAL Model Law defines the role and authority of the arbitral tribunal in proceedings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The UNCITRAL Model Law grants powers to the arbitral tribunal regarding interim measures."&lt;SEP&gt;"The UNCITRAL Model Law provides a framework for the appointment of experts by the arbitral tribunal, which is referenced in Article 26 and further elaborated upon here."&lt;SEP&gt;"The UNCITRAL Model Law provides the basis for the powers and procedures of the Arbitral Tribunal."&lt;SEP&gt;"The arbitral tribunal has authority over applications for preliminary orders under Article 17B of the UNCITRAL Model Law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34872d5563389492bd86e96a7e9d819c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42e43618531219d229d97ed5116bec20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-204ae6c021e3fe4bd76744d9bd61144e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-793ad550c41441bec21087b3f776d5d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4511c8f186e004155d32a4e03ae34f4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44743bbc15d45a8109ce653b3d495eca</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCITRAL MODEL LAW&quot;" target="&quot;EXPERT APPOINTED UNDER ARTICLE 26 OF UNCITRAL MODEL LAW, GIVEN EFFECT TO BY SECTION 54(1)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The expert appointed under Article 26 of the UNCITRAL Model Law is considered part of the arbitration tribunal's fees and expenses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-62de924c3226ea55de4d94d980a6b34f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYED PERSON&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An employment contract governs the relationship between an employed person and their employer, defining terms such as leave entitlements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d93d92eb00cb1e06709b542dad7efdd1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;ANNUAL LEAVE CALCULATION METHODOLOGY (2007)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The methodology of calculating annual leave pay in 2007 is governed by the terms of the employment contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f9b6eb32a58d1b44de6c2f126192d169</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUYER&quot;" target="&quot;RISK (RISK)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"BUYER assumes RISK after receiving title to the GOODS, but this can change if delivery delays are caused by SELLER or BUYER’s faults."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34bc94419b349addb3ca3738887910de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BUYER&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT FOR GOODS (支付货价)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Buyers are obligated to make payment according to the terms of sale agreements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2195e6c40b4de08d5c7076514275f85</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主&quot;" target="&quot;法定規例或其他規例&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"僱主或其代表發出的命令以及適用於其受雇從事的工作的任何法定規例或其他規例都可能影響僱員的安全和行為。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0f5b6c7d25f6395f43d3ccf96762b01c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主&quot;" target="&quot;處長&quot;">
  <data key="d4">77.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Director must give consent for terminating a contract when an employee is incapacitated, or specific conditions under 16A(2), 16CA(1), and related clauses are met."&lt;SEP&gt;"The director has the authority to assess compensation for employees based on certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"僱主可以向處長給予書面同意,也可以撤回該項同意。"&lt;SEP&gt;"僱主需向處長呈交證明書及意見，而處長會決定僱員是否有權獲得長期服務金。"&lt;SEP&gt;"僱主需在特定時間內向處長報告意外並提交相關的通知。"&lt;SEP&gt;"在某些情況下，處長需要將反對書送交僱主。"&lt;SEP&gt;"處長可以決定是否維持、裁定或者拒絕僱主轉介給他的請求。此外，處長還需要根據轉介作出相關決策。"&lt;SEP&gt;"處長根據僱主提供的意見決定僱員是否有權獲得長期服務金。"&lt;SEP&gt;"處長的同意是僱主不能在特定情況下終止僱用合約的前提。"&lt;SEP&gt;"處長要求僱主在簽立後盡快呈交根據本條訂立的協議。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ad03aa80581d9d78c4971adade589820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c031adb2191e2fdd70a1cfb2171a003&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5d9d61caba55ae3f9dfd2940ae47cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0de67114856d774592b4fb886fb31e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-688810e0abd091776de88edcaaba1bb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c689b8d0795a9c81d181c39f442bd05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9abcb1aa4ccb5d467cb0175ca3011bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae344452d3fef20d9a84a14e26b325a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b965639f18b2c29c5f672b6067f9d701&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a95471afd1aaf3812ba594d6c8b0d4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主&quot;" target="&quot;僱員的配偶&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據文本描述,僱主與其配偶都涉及臨時付款證明書及相關申請程序。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-140ad6aa8f9e18c2087a074a7e55b9b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主&quot;" target="&quot;支付費用&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根據條款，僱主需要在特定時間內支付殯葬費或醫護費。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b94648c694477d4222a0ec6ba5f496e8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主&quot;" target="&quot;附表6第1欄&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"附表6第1栏可能涉及僱主的具体条款，但具体关系需进一步明确以确定其确切性质和强度。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-430e5976cb2d37cf2cc19b50c8f851c3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主&quot;" target="&quot;雇員或家庭成員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"僱主可因一項有待解決或裁定的申索而直接向僱員或家庭成員作一筆付款。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a6ff3e19762d07ee36fb89575db50a74</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主&quot;" target="&quot;第三者&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"僱主有权利为追讨因意外而有义务支付的任何款项，针对第三者提起诉讼，不论该款项是因补偿或弥偿或凭藉在该意外发生前与雇员所订立的任何协议而有义务支付的。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d99f404dbd425b6d201f5bef0ae66380</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主&quot;" target="&quot;弥偿者&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"根据第24条可被要求支付彌償的任何人，均有权利为追讨其因该意外而有义务支付的任何款项，针对第三者提起诉讼。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d99f404dbd425b6d201f5bef0ae66380</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主&quot;" target="&quot;怀孕僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"僱主不得在特定期间内因非分娩原因终止怀孕僱員的连续性僱傭合約,除非符合第(1A)款和第9条的规定。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7f27dbcc6e99e201ae8e2112a4a41612</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主&quot;" target="&quot; REGISTERED MEDICAL PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers can engage registered medical practitioners for their recognized schemes of medical treatment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-73492d2774f700c9b55459d33fea445f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主&quot;" target="&quot;REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers can also engage registered Chinese medicine practitioners for their recognized schemes of medical treatment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-73492d2774f700c9b55459d33fea445f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主&quot;" target="&quot;年假年&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employers are responsible for determining and providing the number of annual leave days according to the provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed2004c9e59e7e54ef6756f3c59d039a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主&quot;" target="《最低工資條例》(第608章)">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">根據法例規定，僱主需遵守最低工資等要求，與法例直接相關。</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd253a6ffc2d98305e581075ce59a38</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主&quot;" target="實習學員">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">根據規定，僱主需備存顯示實習學員身份的文件或副本，兩者有直接關系。</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd253a6ffc2d98305e581075ce59a38</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主&quot;" target="工作經驗學員">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">同樣地，僱主也需要保存相關的工作經驗學員的身份證明文件等，與之有關聯性。</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ffd253a6ffc2d98305e581075ce59a38</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主&quot;" target="&quot;職責&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"僱主需遵從本條例條文,並被委以相關職責和法律責任。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c2e09be0ac839e84e94f72793a659214</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主&quot;" target="&quot;擔保人&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"擔保人與僱主之間存在債務關係，擔保人在特定情況下可以申請解除義務。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e2ef1890ed05a41bc045fd740d85a179</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱主&quot;" target="&quot;僱員&quot;">
  <data key="d4">136.0</data>
  <data key="d5">The relationship between "僱主" (employer) and "僱員" (employee) is central to the labor dynamics in this context, encompassing various aspects such as wages, leave entitlements, work details, and safety. Both parties are involved in calculating notional leave pay and annual leave benefits. Employers have a legal obligation to provide necessary information upon employee requests related to wages and work conditions.

Employers must notify employees at least one month in advance of their intention to cease operations for annual leave, which can impact the employees' rights during such periods. The employment relationship also involves potential conflicts or actions taken by employers that affect employees, as well as vice versa. For instance, employers have the right to deduct certain costs from an employee's salary and may face penalties if they violate labor laws.

Employers are prohibited from terminating contracts with temporarily disabled employees unless compensation has been provided according to specific regulations or court orders. They can also suspend employment without notice in certain situations, which is linked to contract termination factors. The employer-employee relationship extends to the assessment and payment of injury-related compensation, where employers may require employees to undergo medical examinations.

According to relevant laws, employers must approve employee absences for evaluations and pay related wages or salaries during such periods. Both parties are bound by agreements that affect free medical treatment provisions and safety measures in the workplace. Overall, this relationship is multifaceted, involving financial transactions, legal obligations, health concerns, and contract management between "僱主" and "僱員".</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-56cceac4667a58d36b3976e9f95e0382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57fe6a1a322921301e20ac79c773cc67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad03aa80581d9d78c4971adade589820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f5b6c7d25f6395f43d3ccf96762b01c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c031adb2191e2fdd70a1cfb2171a003&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dff2dac44cda710c0a41dfe3af3e572&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7243d6ae166cfdb764a13e61a193cccf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b4ba9b3e2ec8a01b740be7e7f709ed8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-688810e0abd091776de88edcaaba1bb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7afd3d77979ccf6bd91ad9b535aba7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be5f720af1dc189f9088eb832b2b0cfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed2004c9e59e7e54ef6756f3c59d039a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6957d2ae600df45cdcfeef087031ad45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af77be8b003511c35b7551f4285bb427&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b965639f18b2c29c5f672b6067f9d701&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a5821c406f8b08deabbe52c126132b5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Registered Chinese medicine practitioners can also issue certificates that impact the terms for terminating a contract of employment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-515a3738f6ebf19e3d7fa78e01d28be6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REGISTERED CHINESE MEDICINE PRACTITIONER&quot;" target="&quot;SECTION 15AA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A medical certificate for the purposes of section 15AA can be issued by a registered Chinese medicine practitioner."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5f31efedbeed7b67b60bd6e147d2e1ac</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTION CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT DISPUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A PAYMENT DISPUTE arises in relation to a CONSTRUCTION CONTRACT, which provides context for initiating adjudication procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"PAYMENT DISPUTES often arise in the context of CONSTRUCTION CONTRACTS, involving payment issues related to construction work or supplies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-304365a41d317ba2bf7cdd71b9dcffa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4a8b59b4e3e2ba05d0864cc47510c7b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC OFFICER&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATION SAFETY OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public officers are authorized by law to act as occupational safety officers under certain sections."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-da2837c3b5e351b2e1c63635e1c0a663</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Arbitration includes various proceedings such as court procedures, emergency arbitrator's proceedings, and mediation procedures under this Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ca2c3669141d3f1cd87a21d68d494cf5</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;AMOUNT OF RECOVERABLE COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitral tribunal has the authority to limit the amount of recoverable costs in arbitration proceedings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5578519b1f9afcce44c23c12fe6ac94b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;COST SHARING PROVISIONS IN ARBITRATION AGREEMENT CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Cost-sharing provisions in an Arbitration Agreement Clause can be void if they exist after a dispute arises, but may still apply to pre-existing disputes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL&quot;" target="&quot;COST ASSESSMENT FOR PRE-ARBITRATION EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Arbitral Tribunal has discretion in assessing costs incurred before the commencement of arbitration, including those for preparation purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6af742025bbb451d461d7aaec24f38e3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱員&quot;" target="&quot;申索補償人士&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"申索補償人士與僱員之間存在親屬關係的爭議。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0de67114856d774592b4fb886fb31e9f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱員&quot;" target="&quot;補償申索&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"已經有其他補償申索就同一僱員存檔。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0de67114856d774592b4fb886fb31e9f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱員&quot;" target="&quot;附表6第2欄&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"附表6第2欄涉及僱員，说明了与僱员相关的条款。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-430e5976cb2d37cf2cc19b50c8f851c3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;僱員&quot;" target="&quot;處長&quot;">
  <data key="d4">32.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Director's approval is required to terminate the employment or apprenticeship contract of an injured employee unless certain conditions are fulfilled under specific sections."&lt;SEP&gt;"The employee is subject to the assessment of compensation by the director in case of injury."&lt;SEP&gt;"處長可以書面通知受傷僱員出席接受查訊或評估。"&lt;SEP&gt;"處長有權批准或拒絕僱員接受免費醫治期間無須支付補償,以及宣讀和解釋協議以保障僱員利益。"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6c031adb2191e2fdd70a1cfb2171a003&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b965639f18b2c29c5f672b6067f9d701&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56cceac4667a58d36b3976e9f95e0382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad03aa80581d9d78c4971adade589820</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
